(in-microtheory UniversalVocabularyMt)
(disjointWith Music ComputerAccount)
(comment ArmoredVehicle "#$ArmoredVehicle is a specialization of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle and #$LandTransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$ArmoredVehicle is a land vehicle protected by armor.  This collection includes  both tracked and wheeled vehicles.")
(comment InternationalMagazineSeries "The collection of #$MagazineSeries

that deal with international matters.")
(comment DynasticFamily "A specialization of #$Family-Human.  Each instance of #$DynasticFamily is a succession of rulers of the same line of descent, or a powerful family that maintains its position for a considerable time.")
(comment FantasyMovie "An instance of #$MovieTypeByGenre commonly associated with magic,  medieval times, and imaginary worlds. Anything drawn from a completely  invented world, with some element of sorcery or inventive zoology,  can qualify, though the most common forms are ones based in  the era of princes and princesses, swords, and dragons and set  in England or France.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn ThirdRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment SubordinateRoleDenotingFunction "A great many #$OrganizationalPositions have associated with
them one or more 'subordinate' positions, often prefaced with terms
like 'deputy', 'assistant', or 'vice'.  The common characteristic of
all of these 'subordinate' roles, is that the individual who plays the
'subordinate' role in an organization is a direct subordinate of the
person who plays the 'superior' role.
#$SubordinateRoleDenotingFunction and its instances have been set up
to facilitate reification of these subordinate roles on the fly with
the aim of speeding cyclification.  Each instance of this collection
is an #$IndividualDenotingFunction which takes an
#$OrganizationalPosition as its argument and returns an instance of
#$OrganizationalPosition that is subordinate to the first.")
(comment Crocheting "In instances of #$Crocheting, a fiber (usually #$Yarn) is formed into a row of a series of loops, then back along the same row making loops through the last set of loops, and so on to form a piece of fabric.  #$Crocheting is done with a #$CrochetHook.")
(comment Navy "#$Navy is a specialization of #$BranchOfMilitaryService.  Each instance of #$Navy is a military organization (contemporary or historical) composed mainly of seaborne forces, and/or forces responsible for military operations on water and adjacent coastal areas.")
(comment LogicBomb "#$LogicBomb is the collection of #$MaliciousComputerPrograms designed to activate
    under some, specified circumstances.  If activation is determined by time then see 
    #$TimeBomb-Computer.")
(comment RegularNounFrame "This frame is used in semantic translations (not denotations) for nouns which can be used intransitively, that is, without any complements at all. In HPSG terms: [COMPS < >] Example: the use of 'friend' in 'Julie is a good friend'.")
(comment Catecholamine "#$Amines derived from tyrosine. #$Catecholamines affect the #$NervousSystem, metabolic rate, and cardiovascular system.")
(comment AbradingTeeth "The process of scraping or wearing away the surface of teeth.")
(comment ArgIsaBinaryPredicate "A specialization of both #$ArgTypeBinaryPredicate and #$ArgIsaPredicate.  Each instance of #$ArgIsaBinaryPredicate takes a #$Relation RELN as its first argument, and a #$Collection COL as its second argument, and places a constraint based on COL on at least one of the argument-places of RELN.  To be more precise, suppose that PRED is an #$ArgIsaBinaryPredicate that specifies an argument-type for the Nth argument-place of RELN.  Then a sentence of the form (PRED RELN COL) entails that a closed formula of the form (RELN ... ARGN ...) is semantically well-formed only if  ARGN is an instance of COL.")
(comment ProjectileShellTypeByStabilizationMethod "The two instances of #$ProjectileShellTypeByStabilizationMethod are  the collections of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that are either stabilized  through a rapid spin or with fins near the base.  Every  #$ProjectileShellAssembly is either one or the other.")
(comment preferredNameString "(#$preferredNameString THING STRING) means that the string STRING is a preferred name for #$Cyc to use when referring to THING. #$Cyc will always prefer a preferred name over any other kind of name, all other things being equal.")
(comment rateOfFire-Cyclic "(#$rateOfFire-Cyclic GUN RATE) indicates the number of rounds per minute that can be fired. The unit of RATE to use is #$TimesPerMinute. This predicate can be used for most #$ProjectileLaunchers that have a store of projectiles. The obvious examples are the instances of #$MachineGun that have a large store of bullets that can be fired at a rapid rate. Less obvious examples include the #$Pistols that can fire six bullets at the #$rateOfFire-Cyclic, after which one must pause for the #$reloadTime of that pistol. For certain instances of #$MissileLauncher the #$rateOfFire-Cyclic is determined by the #$reloadTime: the time it takes to reload the launcher after firing a missile, determines the rate at which one can fire missiles.")
(disjointWith Water ElectricalDevice)
(comment HeadFinalMultiWordForConstantPred "The specialization MultiWordForConstantPred that maps from head-final lexical items to Cyc constnts.")
(comment DiscoveringSomething "The collection of #$Events in which something is discovered, whether that thing is an object or a proposition.  A discovery may be unintended, or may be the result of actions taken with the intent of causing a discovery.  However, since the thing discovered was not known before the discovery, the doer of a discovery is a #$nonDeliberateActors.")
(comment documentMentions "The document ARG1 explicitly mentions ARG2.")
(comment WFFCheckerTargetMicrotheory "A collection of Microtheories.  Each instance

 of #$WFFCheckerTargetMicrotheory is a spec Mt

 of every Mt that is used in a particular

  RKF dialogue context.  The existence of this

  collection allows the wff-checking that goes on

 during natural-language parsing

 to occur at a much faster speed, by restricting

  the wff-checking to only one Mt, versus 

   every Mt in the KB.")
(comment Peta "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^15.")
(comment FullTimeWorker "An instance of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus and specialization of #$Employee. Each #$FullTimeWorker is employed full time by some agent.")
(disjointWith Water RoadSystem)
(disjointWith Midday MidnightSun)
(comment BeingHealthy "The goal of being healthy, which includes emotional well being.")
(comment SuperhumanAct "Actions which, when performed by humans, exhibit a form of 'divine efficacy', or seem to be those of a superhuman entity of extraordinary physical or mental prowess. The actions of a #$Superman, or the miracles of those in the collection #$Saint, or the actions of other instances of #$DivineBeing which are clearly beyond the ability of human beings, constitute a #$SuperhumanAct. So, #$Flying when performed by a human unaided by a flying machine can be considered a superhuman act.")
(comment assertionTruth "(assertionTruth ASSERTION TRUTH) states that

          argumentation has determined that the arguments supporting

          ASSERTION indicate that TRUTH is the truth of ASSERTION.

          TRUTH will either be #$True-JustificationTruth,

          #$False-JustificationTruth or #$Unknown-JustificationTruth. See also #$assertionStrength.")
(comment LiquidOralMedicine "Medicine which is liquid and intended to be swallowed.")
(comment off-UnderspecifiedSurface "(#$off-UnderspecifiedSurface ACT LOC) states that an abstract
locational relation holds between ACT and LOC, where LOC is an
#$SurfaceRegion-Underspecified and ACT is some action requiring an ablative
role.  Only things which can be conceptualized as surfaces are thus
allowable as the second argument to an 'off' relation. 'Off' is thus
semantically more restrictive than 'from', and implies a touching of
surfaces. Probably because of the strong relation to writing, the
notion of a topic in English is conceived of as a
#$SurfaceRegion-Underspecified (that is, one can write 'on a topic', the
debate can move 'off a topic', etc.).")
(comment pipeEndsAtCavity "(#$pipeEndsAtCavity PIPE CAV) means that PIPE is an instance of #$Pipe-GenericConduit that joins the instance of #$CavityOrContainer CAV at some instance of #$PipeEndToCavityJunction (q.v.), allowing flow or access between PIPE and CAV.")
(comment exchangeRateDuring "(#$exchangeRateDuring UM1 UM2 THING NR) means that in some market or markets NR is the average exchange rate of the #$UnitOfMoney UM1 for the #$UnitOfMoney UM2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  That is, NR UM1's can be traded for 1 UM2, and conversely.  Thus two assertions of the form (#$exchangeRateDuring UM1 UM2 THING NR1) and (#$exchangeRateDuring UM1 UM2 THING NR2), where NR1 differs from NR2, can both be true if different exchange rates prevail in different markets.  In particular, the official and the (financial) market exchange rates of a currency may not be the same.  For example the official exchange rate of the Liberian currency during October of 1995 was 1 Liberian dollar for 1 United States dollar, but the market exchange rate for the same period was 50 Liberian dollars for 1 United States dollar.  So it is the case both that (#$exchangeRateDuring #$Dollar-Liberia #$Dollar-UnitedStates (#$MonthFn #$October (#$YearFn 1995)) 1.0) and (#$exchangeRateDuring #$Dollar-Liberia #$Dollar-UnitedStates (#$MonthFn #$October (#$YearFn 1995)) 50).  (It is desirable to use the more specific predicates #$exchangeRateDuring-Official and #$exchangeRateDuring-Market, when the information to be represented is precise enough to select for one of these predicates.  However, vaguer information is still meaningful, and can be represented with this predicate.)")
(comment MLMDownline "A collection of groups of people. Each instance of #$MLMDownline is the group of people recruited by one independent representative in a multi-level marketing system, together with all the people they recruited and so on ad infinitum. The representative in such a system (cf. #$MultiLevelMarketingActivity) receives commissions not only for products he or she sells, but also for the sales activity of representatives in his or her downline, up to about seven levels.")
(comment Mega "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^6")
(comment catalyst "The predicate #$catalyst identifies the particular thing that acts as a catalyst in a particular chemical reaction.  (#$catalyst R X) means that the #$ChemicalReaction R has the particular quantity of substance X as a catalyst.  For example, every instance of #$Photosynthesis-Generic has some portion of #$Chlorophyll as a catalyst; an amount of #$Water may be a #$catalyst in some #$OxidationProcess of a #$Metal.")
(comment GourdPlant "Individual gourd plants.")
(comment numberOfActionsForActorDuring " (#$numberOfActionsForActorDuring ?IND ?SITTYPE ?ROLE ?TIMEINT ?N) indicates that ?IND plays ?ROLE in ?N instances of ?SITTYPE during ?TIMEINT.")
(comment Fairy "A #$Fairy is a small imaginary creature with magic powers,           which looks like a very small person.")
(comment SalariedWorker "An instance of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus and a specialization of #$Employee. Each instance of #$SalariedWorker is paid a salary for his or her work by his or her employer. See also #$HourlyWorker and #$CommissionedWorker.")
(comment canDoDamageOfKind "A predicate used to relate an instance of #$SomethingExisting to the

kind of damage that thing is capable of causing in the microtheoretic

context in which the assertion is made.  (#$canDoDamageOfKind THING

DAMAGETYPE) means that it is consistent in the microtheory where the

assertion is made for there to be a situation SIT such that THING

plays an intermediate causal role in bringing about SIT and

(#$kindOfDamageDone SIT DAMAGETYPE). See also #$kindOfDamageDone,

#$NoteAboutDamage.")
(comment Pasteurella "A collection of #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.
These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$Bacterium-Immotile, #$GramNegativeBacterium,
coccobacilli.  They are facultative anaerobes.  Frequently bipolar stain.  Catalase-positive, almost always oxidase-positive, and fermentative metabolism.  They are parasictic with respects to the mucous membrane of the upper respiratory tract and digestive tracts of mammals and birds, but rarely infect people.")
(comment Voyeur "Someone who enjoys #$Voyeurism; i.e. watching #$SexualBehavior, especially secretively.")
(comment AmphibiousTransportDock "The collection of military amphibious transport docks. These craft are used to transport and land 

Marines and their equipment by embarked landing craft or 

amphibious vehicles augmented by helicopters in amphibious assault.")
(comment Proline "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These
compounds are a major constituent of collagen.  Its abbreviations are
Pro and P.")
(comment Cartoon-Still "Instances of this collection involve static #$Cartoon drawings, as opposed to animated cartoons (see #$Cartoon-Animated). Examples include individual cartoon drawings, comic strips (see #$SpecifiedComicStripSeriesType), and comic books.")
(comment MechanizedEngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of instances of #$EngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty typically employing motorized tracked vehicles.")
(comment FatContent "The (proportional) amount of fat that something contains. This applies especially to

foods. ")
(comment HALOParachuteJump "The collection of High Altitude Low Opening parachute jumps.  This method of parachute jumping is used for quick insertion into an area.  Because it is generally done from very high altitudes (30,000+ ft), the jumper must carry oxygen.")
(comment Melatonin "A #$Hormone secreted by the #$PinealBody.")
(comment FitnessEquipment "This is the collection of fitness equipment. It includes fitness machines

as well as things like weights, jump-ropes, Thighmasters, etc.")
(comment RocketryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped to deal with           rocket-propelled weapons in some fashion.")
(comment Phonologist "A #$Linguist specializing in #$Phonology")
(comment SelectingBetween "A collection of events.  Each element of #$SelectingBetween is a #$SelectingSomething event in which the selection is made from a set of alternatives.  The thing that is finally selected is the #$chosenItem.")
(comment infectingSource "(#$infectingSource INFECTING SOURCE) means that during the #$InfectingEvent, INFECTING, the pathogen that later causes an #$Infection in a new host, comes from SOURCE.")
(comment assertionAssertTime "(#$assertionAssertTime ASSERTION TIME) means that ASSERTION was made at TIME where TIME specifies a particular day in YYYYMMDD syntax.  For example, 19870911 is September 11, 1987.  For more precision in assertion time, see #$assertionAssertSecond.  See also #$myCreationTime.")
(comment DoubleEagleCoin-US "The collection of all US double eagle gold coins.  The face value is $20.00.")
(comment CensusGroupOfCaucasians "The collection of persons who consider themselves to be Caucasians.  This is a rather vague ethnic designation, usually synonymous with `white person' in naive US ethnic classification schemes.")
(comment Sliding-Generic "This is the most general collection about the rubbing, sliding or skidding processes that occur between solid objects in physical contact.  #$Sliding-Generic is disjoint with #$RollingOnASurface:  In instances of #$RollingOnASurface flush surface regions of the slider and the slidee do not translate relative to each other during for the brief moment that they are in contact.  By contrast, such flush surface regions are translating relative to each other during instances of #$Sliding-Generic. Typical examples include objects sliding, slipping, or skidding.  Negative examples include balls rolling (the contact surfaces do not translate relative to one another) and water flowing in a conduit (because the #$objectMoving is not solid).  All things being equal friction involved with sliding is greater than that with rolling.  See also #$Sliding-LowFriction, a low friction kind of #$Sliding-Generic to be contrasted with it high friction sibling, #$Rubbing.")
(comment InfectionTransmissionEvent "A specialization of #$InfectingEvent.  Each instance of #$InfectionTransmissionEvent is an event in which some infection is transmitted from one host to another (where both the old and new hosts are instances of #$BiologicalLivingObject).")
(comment TravelInfoForFn "#$TravelInfoForFn takes as argument an individual and returns the collection of all #$PropositionalInformationThings which include information about travelling to, from, and around the location of the individual, as well as other travel services such as car rental and accommodations in that location. For example, (#$TravelInfoForFn (#$OlympicsFn (#$YearFn 2000))) returns the collection of all information about getting to, from, and around Sydney, Australia, as well as information about lodging and car rental services in Sydney, Australia.")
(comment nailedTo "(#$nailedTo ?obj1 ?obj2) means that a #$Nail has been hammered through ?obj1 into ?obj2.")
(comment WorldCupCompetition "The collection of all WorldCupCompetitions, the international soccer tournament held once every four years.")
(comment FictionalTVShow-CW "#$FictionalTVShow-CW is a collection of #$TVShow-CWs whose content is not intended to be wholly factual. For example, a #$MedicalTVShow like 'ER' may contain some factual information about medical practice, but the characters and story line are fictional.")
(comment Lent "The collection of all periods of Lent, starting each year on #$AshWednesday and ending at midnight between Holy Saturday and Easter. Each instance of #$Lent is 46 days long, i.e., 40 days not counting the six #$Sundays.")
(comment Urolagnia "Elements of #$Urolagnia are instances of #$Urinating in which somebody urinates on somebody else with the intent of bringing about his/her own or the  other person's #$SexualArousal.")
(comment Headwaiter "This is a job which includes greeting patrons at a
restaurant and seating them.  Sometimes called the 'maitre d'hotel' or
'host'/'hostess'.")
(comment AntineoplasticAgent "Class of drug products that inhibit or prevent the growth and reproduction of malignant cells.")
(comment Lifeseeing "The collection of events in which a person or group of persons (generally #$Tourists) observe the landscape around them as they walk, drive, or ride past it.")
(disjointWith Armor-ExtrinsicToObject Armor-IntrinsicToObject)
(comment exportThroughAmountDuring "(#$exportThroughAmountDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE PT THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE exported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT (on their way to their destination) during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PT might, in the case of oil exports, for instance, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile exports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars exported.  In the case of oil exports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil exported (by REGION through PT), or it might be an instance of #$MonetaryValue indicating the monetary value of all the oil exported.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of export of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION through PT during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil exports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day or in terms of so many dollars per day (again, indicating the monetary value of the oil).")
(comment penpals "(#$penpals PAL1 PAL2) means that PAL1 and PAL2 are penpals - they are acquainted with each other primarily through written correspondence.")
(comment HeadOfGovernment "An instance of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg, and a specialization of #$Politician.  Each instance of #$HeadOfGovernment is a person who holds a political position as the head of the government of some instance of #$Country.  See the #$sharedNotes #$GovernmentLeaderNote for an explanation of the distinction between #$HeadOfGovernment and #$HeadOfState (q.v.).")
(disjointWith ArtObject DefenseSystem)
(comment LeafPetiole "The stalk of a leaf that connects it to a stem.")
(comment BatmanMovie "The collection of Batman movies.")
(comment ShippingLaneOfRegionFn "The function used to represent collections of shipping lanes within geographical regions.  (#$ShippingLaneOfRegionFn REGION) denotes the collection of all instances of #$ShippingLane, LANE, such that (#$geographicalSubRegions REGION LANE) is the case.")
(comment Corn-SkinCondition "A subset of #$PhysiologicalFeatureOfSurface.  A corn is a small, horn-shaped area of the             skin that is thicker and much harder than other parts of the skin.")
(comment UrbanLegend "A story which is usually passed orally amongst the members of a modern day (late 20th century) community.  Unlike #$Legends they are often not considered authoritative accounts of reality.")
(comment notedAreaActivities "This predicates relates instances of #$GeographicalRegion to kinds of noteable activities that are regularly performed in the area.  The activity should distinguish the area from other areas of the same type.  One sufficient, but not necessary condition, is whether the activity type attracts tourists.  For instance, while lawn mowing (#$MowingGrass) is regularly performed in #$CityOfBuffaloNY, we wouldn't assert (#$notedAreaActivities #$CityOfBuffaloNY #$MowingGrass) as this doesn't distinguish Buffalo from other cities of comparable size or geographical location.")
(comment LiquidSolution "The collection of all #$Solutions that are instances of #$LiquidTangibleThing.")
(comment hasDiet "The #$BinaryPredicate (#$hasDiet ORG FOODTYPE) means that organisms of type ORG typically eat instances of FOODTYPE.")
(comment travelTime "(#$travelTime OBJ1 OBJ2 MOVEMENT TIME) means it would usually take the transported object TIME to get from OBJ1 to OBJ2 in an event of type MOVEMENT.")
(comment BassGuitarTablatureText "The collection of all instances of #$MusicalText that are written in #$BassGuitarTablatureNotation. #$BassGuitarTablatureNotation is a notation used to describe how a sequence of musical notes is to be played on a bass guitar.")
(comment subLocationType "(#$subLocationType LARGER-TYPE SMALLER-TYPE)  means that for every #$SpatialThing X of type LARGER-TYPE, there is a #$SpatialThing Y of type SMALLER-TYPE such that X spatially contains Y.  Examples: (#$subLocationType #$ModernHumanResidence #$Closet), (#$subLocationType #$City #$Building).  See also #$superLocationType.  Note that (#$subLocationType X Y) does not necessarily entail (#$superLocationType Y X).")
(disjointWith Canoe RowingShell)
(comment PeregrineFalcon "A globally distributed falcon, Falco peregrinus, much used in falconry because of its swift flight: several subspecies are endangered.")
(comment NuclearWeapon "A specialization of #$WeaponOfMassDestruction, #$NuclearPoweredDevice, and #$ExplosiveDevice.  Each instance of #$NuclearWeapon isa a weapon that derives its destructive power from nuclear energy.")
(comment MutualFundManager "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$MutualFundManager is a professional responsible for the investment decisions of a mutual fund (see the collection #$MutualFund).  Instances of #$MutualFundManager are generally employed by investment firms.")
(disjointWith DownwardLocation-Underspecified UpwardLocation-Underspecified)
(comment IndustrialMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic, #$IndustrialMusic started as a British

   underground movement in the late 1970s and early 1980s.  It combined a Punk attitude

   with a sort of Avant Garde aesthetic.  The music was largely electronically created,

   repetitive, often trance-like, and sometimes dissonent.  Toward the late 1980s,

   #$IndustrialMusic became on the whole more rythmic and danceable, and consequently,

   more popular.  Influential practitioners of this style include #$ThrobbingGristle-MusicGroup, #$CabaretVoltaire-MusicGroup, #$EinsturzendeNeubauten-MusicGroup, and #$NineInchNails-MusicGroup.")
(comment FlowControlStructure "The collection of all physical objects (#$PartiallyTangible) which control the flow of fluid.  Instances of this collection may be #$Artifacts (in which case they are #$FlowControlDevices) or biological structures.  Merely channeling flow is not sufficient to make something a #$FlowControlStructure; some additional feature must be able to modify the flow.  Thus #$Valves are instances of #$FlowControlStructure, but tubes (#$Pipe-GenericConduit) are not necessarily.")
(comment DetectionFn "(#$DetectionFn STUFF) is the collection of

  all events in which STUFF is detected.  For 

example, (#$DetectionFn #$Smoke) is the 

 collection of all smoke detection events.

  In such an event, some #$SmokeAlarm

 would probably play the role of #$detector

 and so would stand in the #$detects relation

 to the relevant instance of #$Smoke.")
(comment RehabilitationMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements that provide for the costs of repairing and improving a home or other building that is over a year old.")
(comment DistributiveLattice "The subcollection of #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic that contains all those lattices called 'distributive lattices' by lattice theorists.  A #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic LATICE (with the #$baseSet S, meet operation MEET and join operation JOIN) is distributive if the distribution laws hold, i.e., for each X, Y and Z in S, (MEET X (JOIN Y Z)) = (JOIN (MEET X Y) (MEET X Z)).  Note that this condition is equivalent to the condition that for each X, Y and Z in S, (JOIN X (MEET Y Z)) = (MEET (JOIN X Y) (JOIN X Z)).")
(comment StringTemplate "This is the #$ParsingTemplateCategory for what is represented in Cyc as a string.")
(comment Placenta "The collection of all placentas, mammalian #$Organs which form in (and attached to) the #$Uterus out of a combination of fetal and maternal tissues, which provide oxygen and food to the fetal blood supply, and remove waste products (including CO2).  A #$Placenta is attached to the fetus proper via the #$UmbilicalCord.")
(comment FilingTaxes "The action of providing the government with ones tax return.")
(comment Nocardiaceae-Family "A collection of #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom that includes the #$Nocardia-Genus and Rhodococcus-Genus.  Previously, both of the #$BiologicalSpecies were unclassified in terms of a #$BiologicalFamily, but instead grouped as nocardioforms.  This #$BiologicalFamily comprises the members of the #$Actinomycetales-Order that are #$AerobicBacterium and #$GramPositiveBacterium that have a wall chemotype IV and form substrate mycelium.  This #$BiologicalFamily may be merged with the #$Actinomycetaceae-Family.")
(comment CombatStoreShip "A collection. Ships intended for use in a military context to replenish supplies for other ships involved in combat.")
(comment typeForCharacter "This predicate relates a type of character token to the    abstract character that all instances of the type represent.   (#$typeForCharacter TYPE CHARACTER) means that TYPE is the    collection of all character tokens that #$tokensCharacter   CHARACTER.  For example, the #$CharacterType consisting of all    tokens of the character 'W' is the #$typeForCharacter for (you   guessed it) the character 'W'.  See also #$typeForString.")
(comment CosineFn "(#$CosineFn ANGLE) yields the cosine of that angle.")
(comment Nitroglycerine "A specialization of both #$DrugSubstance and #$HighExplosive.  #$Nitroglycerine is a type of highly explosive substance which can be mixed with a stabilizer (like sawdust, or cotton) to produce dynamite, or other explosive products.  It can also used as a pharmaceutical to alleviate some heart problems.")
(comment FairIsaacCreditScoring "The collection of all events in which the 'Fair Isaac Method' is used to evaluate the likelihood that a loan will be repaid.  It uses a formula, developed by #$FairIsaacAndCompany, based not only on the #$CreditWorthiness of the #$borrower, but also on the features of the proposed #$LoanAgreement itself.")
(comment (HighAmountFn Elasticity) "completely re-expands almost instantly after compression")
(disjointWith FillingANewPrescription FillingARefillPrescription)
(comment FinnishWord "The collection of all lexical words in Finnish; a subset of #$LexicalWord.            Different inflectional forms of a word do not count as different words.")
(comment PlanBackgroundContext "This is the collection of microtheories that serve as background contexts for planning-related applications.")
(comment State-SponsoredTerroristAgent "The collection of all #$TerroristAgents who

  receive funding or safe haven from some

   #$Country or other.")
(comment GraduateManagementAdmissionTest "The collection of #$AcademicTesting events that are designed to help graduate business schools assess the qualifications of those who seek admission to study for an MBA or into another advanced business/management program.")
(comment ClipperShip "A large, fast, multi-masted sailing ship which dominated the seas during the age of discovery and colonialization.")
(comment Anesthetic " #$Anesthetic drugs deaden feeling.  If they are general anesthetics, they may make the recipient unconscious.")
(comment behaviorCapable-PerformedBy "This predicate relates objects to the kinds of activites instances of which they are capable of being performers.  See also #$behaviorCapable.")
(disjointWith ChemicalReaction ChangeInUserRights)
(comment KeystrokeDynamicsMonitor "#$KeystrokeDynamicsMonitor is a subset of #$BiometricAuthenticationDevice.  Individuals in the collection           #$KeystrokeDynamicsMonitor measure the pattern of intervals between keystrokes in pass phrases, and attempt to match            the pattern with a stored representation of it.")
(comment cityBlockBoundedBy "(#$cityBlockBoundedBy BLOCK ST1 ST2 ST3 ST4) means that BLOCK is bounded by streets ST1 - ST4 such that if one starts on ST1 (where it borders BLOCK) and circles around BLOCK making  only right-hand turns one will travel along ST1, ST2, ST3, and ST4, in that order.  The region immediately surrounding the  block must be an #$UrbanArea that has a #$GridStreetSystem running through it.  To have this predicate correctly relate a given city block BLOCK to its bordering streets, one can fill its arg2 position with any  of the four streets that borders BLOCK, and then continue to fill in the remaining argument-places according to the order in which one would travel along the other three streets if one were circling BLOCK in a clockwise fashion (i.e. by  making only right-hand turns).  See also #$CityBlockFn and #$CityGridSectionFn.")
(comment ShelfStocker "Collection of people who put items to be sold on the shelves")
(comment in-ContCompletely "(#$in-ContCompletely OBJ CONT) means that OBJ is completely within one or more cavities in CONT.")
(comment GeneticEngineer "#$GeneticEngineer is the subset of #$Scientist that consists of           people who study #$GeneticEngineering.")
(comment ColdFrontEvent "The collection of all #$AirFrontEvents in which a large atmospheric air mass colder than the ambient air moves into a region pushing the warm air above it.  This causes precipitation and usually storms (see #$StormAsEvent).  The leading edge of the cold air mass is the the locus of the #$ColdFrontEvent.  In the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region, cold fronts generally move southward (#$South-Generally), while in the #$SouthernHemisphere-Region they normally move northward (#$North-Generally).")
(disjointWith TerrestrialDirection AnatomicalDirection)
(comment JenniCamBroadcasting "#$JenniCamBroadcasting is the collection of 'Jenni Cam' broadcasts.")
(comment addressText-NC "The predicate #$addressText-NC maps a particular element of #$ContactLocation to a non-canonical #$Address-LocationDesignator, ADDRESS. The `NC' in the name stands for `non-canonical'.   (#$addressText-NC LOCATION ADDRESS) means that the #$ContactLocation LOCATION has the non-canonicalized address ADDRESS. For example, one value  for #$addressText-NC of the #$Cycorp #$MailingLocation is `Cycorp, 3721 Executive Center Dr., Ste. 100, Austin, TX 78731-1615.'  Note that this address as printed does not conform to the US Postal Service's recommended standard for printed addresses, and so relative to this standard it is not `canonical.' Non-canonical means that  ADDRESS may not conform to the canonicalization scheme(s) used for other known addresses for LOCATION.  These other (presumed canonical) addresses should be related to LOCATION using the predicate #$addressText. It really only makes sense to use #$addressText-NC in contexts (such as the logical schemas for certain database tables) where LOCATION may have both canonical and non-canonical addresses entered for it.  In contexts where the differences between canonicalized and non-canonicalized addresses is not an issue, just use #$addressText.  See also #$ContactLocation.")
(comment InsuranceTypeByThingCovered "Elements are kinds of insurance plans, characterized by the general type of thing covered.")
(comment SpankingStory "The subset of #$EroticStory whose elements contain the propositional content of an #$EroticStory in which an instance of #$Spanking occurs.")
(comment DownwardParabolicTrajectory "A downward parabolic trajectory.")
(disjointWith BookGeneric-CW PeriodicalIssue)
(comment Spike-PersistenceDistribution "Each instance of this collection is an object consisting of parameters which together indicate the probability of an assertion or set of assertions being true.  The parameters define a spike-shaped distribution contour (graph).  The parameters are specified using the predicates #$spikeWidth, #$spikePeakValue, #$spikeNonPeakValue, and #$spikePeakLocation.")
(comment PossibleIdentificationCondition "This is the collection of all collections which can be seen as representing

criteria one might use to identify some instance of #$TemporalThing. One can

think of the non-extensional, (implicit) definitional aspects of these collections

as representing these criteria. Since #$Collections are non-extensional, they are

the sorts of things which can aptly fill #$opaqueArgument places. For example,

an agent might be looking for something she conceptualizes as a bottle of aspirin

but not as a bottle of #$AcetylsalicylicAcid. The collections defined by these

two criteria are #$coExtensional but distinct. The former but not the latter would

represent the #$PossibleIdentificationCondition employed by the agent.")
(comment cordEnd "This predicate relates a cordlike object to its ends.")
(comment Yocto "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^-24")
(comment easternRegion "(#$easternRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `eastern region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `eastern region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors  influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment ComputerModeling "This is the collection of instances where a computer program creates a #$ComputerModel of some object or phenomenon. Usually the purpose of this is to

predict the behavior of the modeled thing in circumstances which would be

difficult to produce or evaluate in the actual world. ")
(comment Howitzer-155mmTowed "The collection of towed 155mm #$Howitzers.")
(comment SubcollectionOfAboutFn "(#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn COLLECTION THING) specifies the collection of all instances of COLLECTION which are ``about'' THING.  Thus (#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn Museum Ceramic) would be the collection of all pottery museums, (#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn Publication Fishing) would be the collection of all publications about fishing and (#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn TradeUnion ComputerIndustry) would be the collection of all trade unions in the computer industry.")
(disjointWith EllipticalGalaxy SpiralGalaxy)
(comment 9-TheDigit "The numeral 9 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '9' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(comment Underwriting "The collection of #$Events in which an #$IntelligentAgent guarantees to secure another #$IntelligentAgent against risk or loss in consideration of some payment, usually in the form of a premium or interest.")
(comment Pound-GreatBritain "The USDollar is the basic unit of currency used in CYC.  The British pound is currently valued at approximately 1.5 USDollars.")
(disjointWith Gardening LoadingAProjectileWeapon)
(comment supplyCapacityFrom "(#$supplyCapacityFrom PT1 COL PT2 RATE) means that the #$Rate RATE is the greatest possible rate at which the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 could supply instances of the collection COL to the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyCapacityFrom is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(disjointWith TextileArtifact Film-SheetOrCoating)
(comment Freon "Substance used in air conditioners for heat transfer.  Gaseous at room temperature and pressure but in liquid state in cooling systems.")
(comment BiologicalTransportationProcess "The process involving living structures in which objects are transported.")
(disjointWith Microtheory CyberVulnerabilityExploit)
(comment NationalPressFn "The function #$NationalPressFn returns the group of media organizations in a particular country that report news on the national level.  (#$NationalPressFn COUNTRY) denotes the group whose #$groupMembers are elements of #$NewsOrganization and of #$NationalOrganization.  Note that this function denotes a group rather than a collection group agent.  Members of (#$NationalPressFn COUNTRY) might include a government news agency, privately owned news agencies, newspapers, radio stations, TV news organizations.")
(comment collectionSubsetsByCardinality "(#$collectionSubsetsByCardinality COL CARD COL-OF-SUBSETS) means that COL-OF-SUBSETS is the collection of all subsets of COL that have cardinality CARD.")
(comment Riddle "The collection of riddles, questions that often involve puns or ambiguity.")
(comment SteelIndustry "The collection of all steel industries, each of which is a geographically defined steel #$Industry-Localized in a certain region.  Steel industries have the primary function of producing pieces or rolls of #$Steel commercially in various forms.  This includes industries that alter the composition or form of pieces of #$Steel, but it does not include the manufacture of steel products or structures in their final forms.")
(comment nearestDifferentGenlPreds "(#$nearestDifferentGenlPreds PRED-1 PRED-2 NEAR-DIFF) relates predicates PRED-1 and PRED-2 to the nearest unsubsumed predicates NEAR-DIFF of which PRED-1 is a spec predicate but PRED-2 is not. #$nearestDifferentGenlPreds is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genlPreds hierarchy. For comparison, see #$nearestDifferentGenls.")
(comment JokeOffensiveToSome "A subset of #$Joke-CW, #$JokeOffensiveToSome is the collection of all           jokes that tend to offend some salient group of people.  Examples include all instances of the           collections (#$JokeAboutFn #$SexualBehavior) and #$RacistJoke.  Note that #$JokeOffensiveToSome is #$disjointWith #$CleanJoke.  Instances of the collection #$CleanJoke are unlikely to offend anyone, or, at least, any member of a salient group in the current #$Microtheory.")
(disjointWith LifeStageType GeopoliticalEntityTypeByBasicCategory)
(comment Mumps "A contagious viral infection of childhood (usually) which affects the salivary glands, causing difficulty and pain in swallowing.  Rarely lasts more than three days, and is vaccinatable for individuals over age one.")
(comment ChangingTable "The collection of changing tables.  A #$ChangingTable is a kind of #$Table-PieceOfFurniture which is usually found in a #$Nursery-BabysRoom.  A #$HumanAdult lays the #$HumanInfant or #$HumanToddler on the this table during a #$ChangingADiaper event.")
(comment stepInitialValue "(#$stepInitialValue STEP VALUE) means that the step-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution STEP has a starting height of VALUE.  For example, the initial value of a step used to specify a temporal persistence distribution might be (#$Percent 50), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the step distribution pertains, the initial likelihood of being true (this will be at a time before the change location specified by #$stepLocation) is 0.50.  VALUE might also be a reified value such as `moderately likely'.")
(comment TankerShip "A specialization of #$CargoShip.  Each instance of #$TankerShip is a ship that by design can transport large amounts of liquid or gas materials.")
(comment Label-IBO "The collection of all labels, namely those #$InformationBearingObjects that serve to identify the object to which they are attached.  This is the most general form of such things and includes a wide range of examples.  Easily identified subsets include #$ProductLabels and #$AddressLabels.  Other, not so obvious examples include a radio isotope that serves to identify a particular gene.  Thus an intangible projection of light onto a wall cannot serve as a label although it may contain information about something (see #$containsInformationAbout).  A borderline positive example is a magnetic strip containing information about the object to which it is attached.")
(comment Phosgene "The chemical compound COCl2.")
(comment Baton-Sports "The collection of battons that runners hand off to each other in running relay races (e.g. #$Relay-4By400Meter).")
(comment M4T6Set "The collection of sets which are necessary for the assembly of a M4T6 bridge.")
(comment Francium "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of francium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment SurfaceArea-WholeSurfaceFn "This function denotes the surface area of the entire surface of an object; it applies to 3-D objects and to 2-D objects.  If a 2-D object is deemed to have a front and back side we may want to define its surface area as twice its area.  However, if it does not, the surface area of a 2-D object and its area may be equal. The surface area of an object is the sum of the areas of all of the surfaces that define the boundary of the object on all sides, including undersides.  See also #$SurfaceArea-TopSurfaceFn, to use with lakes, tabletops, etc.")
(comment RelinquishingFn "A unary function that returns the class of events in which instances of the function argument are given up.  For example, (#$RelinquishingFn #$Anthrax-Bacterium) returns those events in which #$Anthrax-Bacterium are in some way or another given up.")
(comment ParietalLobe "The collection of all parietal lobes of #$Brains.  Each individual #$ParietalLobe is in the mid-superior region of a #$CerebralHemisphere and processes sensory input (among other things).")
(comment DissidentSanctuary "The collection of events where one state provides sanctuary for a dissident of another state.  This could be as extensive as recognizing a government in exile.")
(comment Spirochete "The collection of #$SpirillaBacterium whose shape resembles that of a #$CorkScrew and which move via #$AxialFilaments.")
(disjointWith ArmoredVehicle GolfCart)
(comment (GroupFn Person) "The collection of all groups of people. More precisely, this is the collection of each instance of #$Group such that each member of that instance (see #$groupMembers) is an instance of #$Person.")
(comment successorInRole "Used to express succession in a role (i.e. headOfStateOf Kingdom).  Notice that this predicate does not pertain only to the roles of humans, but can also show a succession in roles of animals, things, or even thoughts and ideas.")
(comment VerapamilHcl "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$CalciumChannelBlocker.  VerapamilHcl is used in treating heart disease.")
(comment Sculpting "This collection includes instances of shaping an image or representation from a (semi)solid material (such as wood, stone, or metal), often resulting in a three-dimensional work of art.")
(comment GangsterMovie "An instance of #$MovieTypeByGenre and a spec of #$CrimeMovie, #$GangsterMovies often glorify the criminal activities of gangsters and elevate them to almost hero status. These anti-heroes sometimes reach the conclusion that crime does pay but often carries moral, psychological, and physical repercussions.")
(comment CruiseLine "The collection of all cruise (water) transportation companies.  An element of #$CruiseLine is a #$TransportationCompany that operates #$OceanLiners or #$CruiseShips to transport people in exchange for money.")
(comment protectiveContains "U protectively contains v1, v2, ....  This means that if there is an object or event outside U that could harm the objects contained, these latter are protected from some sort of harm. This is not transitive as different nested containers may provide different types of protection.")
(disjointWith CoastGuardOrganization Navy)
(disjointWith DrugSubstance (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet Agent-Generic (GroupFn Agent-Generic))))
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-LogicBomb "#$AttackByComputerOperation-LogicBomb is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation and an instance of both  #$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByMethod and #$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByProgram.  Each instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation-LogicBomb is an attack upon a computer or network by in which an instance of #$LogicBombs is used.")
(comment Boating "The collection of all boating events.  #$Boating does not include #$WaterSkiing or #$Surfing because they don't occur on boats.  Also you don't steer the same way so anatomical resource requirements are stated differently.")
(comment GenitiveFrame "This frame is used in semantic translations (not denotations) for nouns in association with a genitive phrase, that is, a preceding possessive as in 'my mother' or a following 'of'-PP as in 'mother of Liz'.  Every use of the #$GenitiveFrame should contain a use of the :POSSESSOR keyword, which refers to the NP inside the genitive phrase.")
(comment Corticosterone "A #$Hormone produced by the adrenal cortex. It is important for glucose absorption and utilization of carbohydrates by body tissues.")
(comment DiggingUpARoot "The collection of events in which the root of a plant is dug out of the soil")
(comment ArgGenlPredicate "Those instance of #$ArgTypePredicate used to specify the required #$genls of an argument of a #$Relation.")
(comment RecoillessGun-Heavy "The #$RecoillessGun-Heavy is a highly mobile piece of artillery that can also fire a heavy shell.  They usually support the infantry, either as light-support field guns, or more often as anti-tank guns.")
(disjointWith Elasticity ElectricalCharge)
(comment NetworkPropagationOfMaliciousComputerProgram "The collection of all occurences of the propagation of a malicious computer program by means of a network.")
(comment FunctionValueForCondFn "(#$FunctionValueForCondFn COND FUNCTION ARG) is a term for denoting whatever results from applying FUNCTION TO ARG, given that COND is true.  Since this is a #$ReifiableFunction, one can use it to refer to and talk about the result of applying a function to an argument, given a certain condition, even if one does not know (or does not care) what the actual resulting value is, or whether the condition is provable. See also #$FunctionValueFn.")
(disjointWith ElectricalDevice PrimitiveWeapon)
(comment theCyclist "(#$theCyclist CYCLIST) specifies the current human CYCLIST logged in in the current image.")
(comment muchGreaterThanWRTScale "(#$muchGreaterThanWRTScale LARGE SMALL SCALE) says that the #$ScalarInterval LARGE is

 much greater than the #$ScalarInterval SMALL, in so far as the standard by 

which we make the comparison is SCALE.  For example, (#$muchGreaterThanWRTScale

 (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 60) (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 15) LengthOfBoat) says that 

 60 feet is much greater than 15 feet where lengths of boats are concerned.")
(comment RadioAstronomicalObservation "This not the study of radio astronomy but its practice. It is the

collection of events in which a radio telescope is used to observe astronomical objects.")
(comment Offering-CommunicationAct "A specialization of #$CommunicationAct-Single.  Each instance of #$Offering-CommunicationAct is a communication act in which somebody offers to do something, furnish something, or make something the case. See also the #$IllocutionaryForce associated with these actions, #$Offer.")
(comment ProteinStuff "The collection of things that are made of protein as main constituent, contrast with #$ProteinMolecule.")
(comment MapFn-TypeLevel "#$MapFn-TypeLevel takes as argument any #$Collection COLL and returns the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings that are maps (in any format) of some instance of COLL.  For example, (#$MapFn-TypeLevel #$NationalPark) returns the collection of all paper, computerized, and other maps of National Parks.")
(comment relevantInPlace-Everywhere "(#$relevantInPlace-Everywhere MT PLACE) means that the assertions in MT are relevant throughout the entire spatial extent of PLACE.  See also #$relevantInPlace-Somewhere.")
(comment thingOfTypeConsumed "(#$thingsOfTypeConsumed EVENT TYPE) means that instances of TYPE are consumed during EVENT.")
(disjointWith LighterThanAirCraft Spacecraft)
(disjointWith Night MidnightSun)
(comment HealthCare "A collection of events. Each element of #$HealthCare is a purposeful action in which an agent acts to maintain, preserve, or promote the health of an #$Animal. Two important subcollections are (#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn #$HealthCare #$Person) and (#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn #$HealthCare #$NonPersonAnimal).")
(comment Kryptonite "The collection of all pieces of the planet #$Krypton-ThePlanet, #$Superman's home planet before it was destroyed. In the #$Superman mythos, pieces of #$Kryptonite have bizarre effects on #$Superman, ranging from robbing him of his superpowers (green and gold) to causing his hair to grow excessively (red).")
(comment LayingABirdsEgg "#$LayingABirdsEgg is the #$Collection  of all #$Actions of
laying a bird's egg.")
(comment Planetarium "This is the collection of planetariums.")
(comment ExothermicReaction "A chemical reaction which gives off heat in the process.")
(comment SpanishMoss "A type of bromeliad that grows on trees in the southeastern U.S.")
(comment StoneStuff "A specialization of (#$SolidFn #$RockyPlanetaryStuff).  Each instance of #$StoneStuff is a piece or portion of rock or stone. Stone is widely used as a material for the construction of buildings, walls, monuments, and sculptures.")
(comment Prank "A #$Prank is a mischievous trick or practical joke.")
(comment PartTimeWorker "An instance of #$EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus and specialization of #$Employee. Each #$PartTimeWorker is employeed part time by some agent.")
(comment AmphibiousWarfareShip "The collection of ships used in amphibious warfare.")
(comment Serine "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These
compounds may be synthesized from #$Glycine and are used as a dietary
supplement, feed additive, and in culture media.  Its abbreviations
are Ser and S.")
(comment groupAccountForFile "(#$groupAccountForFile FILE GROUP) means that the owner of the #$ComputerFileCopy FILE is a member of the #$UserAccountGroup GROUP on a computational system.  The owner of the file can determine whether members of some group which he or she belongs to have read, write, execute etc. permissions on FILE (cf. #$FilePermission for a list of these different permissions).  Note: it is possible for the #$permissionMode on a file to allow group access and not owner access (see also #$ownerAccountForFile, #$worldAccountForFile).")
(comment Joke-IBT "The collection of all #$InformationBearingThings whose information content is a #$Joke-CW. A #$Joke-IBT is the #$communicationToken in any act of #$JokeTelling.")
(comment eventTypeAppropriateClothingItem "(eventTypeAppropriateClothing EVENTTYPE CLOTHING-INSTANCE) means that CLOTHING-INSTANCE is appropriate to wear to events of type EVENTTYPE.")
(comment MechanizedInfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of infantry units employing motorized tracked vehicles.")
(comment VacantHouse "Those households that are unoccupied or vacant.")
(disjointWith HAHOParachuteJump HALOParachuteJump)
(comment OilIndustry "The collection of all oil industries.  Each is an instance of #$Industry-Localized (i.e., a #$Group of #$Organizations) whose products are instances of #$PetroleumProduct.")
(comment Thyrotropin "A #$Hormone secreted by the pituitary gland which stimulates the thyroid gland.")
(comment RowingMachine "This is the collection of rowing machines, devices

used for exercise which are designed to make the user perform

muscle movements similar to those in rowing.")
(comment ScoutUnit-MilitarySpecialty "A collection of units which combine the functions of cavalry unit and  

  ground-based reconnaissance unit.")
(comment PropositionalCWText "The collection of all #$CWInfoStructures that comprise the words or other text of the associated #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Instances are not #$CharacterStrings but structures of abstract words or other memes (such as meaning elements in computer code).  Every instance of #$PropositionalCWText has one or more instances of #$TextString which corresponds it.  #$MusicalTexts are not #$PropositionalCWTexts because the #$MusicalComposition is not propositional.")
(comment dailyHighTemperature "(#$dailyHighTemperature PLACE TEMP) means that the #$Temperature TEMP is the high temperature for a day at the #$GeographicalRegion PLACE.  #$dailyHighTemperature is typically used for a specified period of time (e.g., a particular day or a specific season); it may be used with generic temperature ranges as well as precise temperatures.  Examples: using #$holdsIn, we can say that Austin's temperature for 7/20/96 is 102 degrees Fahrenheit; or we can say that for any #$SummerSeason, Austin's [typical] #$dailyHighTemperature is #$VeryHot.")
(comment enables-RemovesIncapacitatingFactors "#$enables-RemovesIncapacitatingFactors expresses the notion that
an agent is 'enabled' by an event in the following sense: the event removes
all factors that are 'incapacitating', i.e., that would render the agent
certainly incapable of performing the action in question. More accurately,
(#$enables-RemovesIncapacitatingFactors SIT AGENT ACT_TYPE) is true iff,
in the given circumstances, SIT obtains, there are no factors
that would make AGENT certainly incapable of performing an instance of
ACT_TYPE, and SIT is the cause of there being no such incapacitating
factors. Hence #$enables-RemovesIncapacitatingFactors does not imply that
the agent is capable of doing ACT_TYPE_TOKEN: it merely entails that the
probability of the agent's succeeding at tokens of ACT_TYPE is
non-zero. Example: snow plowing enables people to drive after a snowstorm
in this sense -- since a heavy snow cover on roadways #$incapacitates
driving.")
(comment transmissionFromHost "(#$transmissionFromHost INFECTING FROM) means that during
the #$InfectionTransmissionEvent, INFECTING, the origin of the pathogen
that causes an #$Infection in a new host, is FROM, and FROM is an
#$Organism-Whole that is also the #$infectionHost of an #$Infection of a
type similar to that of the infection transmitted.")
(comment MilitaryStudentTextbook-PIT "Each instance is a partial representation of the           propositional content of a particular edition of a           military student textbook.")
(comment completeWordsOfIBT "(#$completeWordsOfIBT IBT STRING) means that the complete text of IBT is STRING.")
(comment Rifling "When rifle bullets go through the air they spin about their length axis just like a spiraling #$Football-American does.  This motion for a bullet starts in a #$GunBarrel.")
(comment infectionCausedByOrganism "This predicate relates a particular instance of #$Infection to an organism which causes that infection.  (#$infectionCausedByOrganism INFECT ORG) means that the organism ORG is one of the causes of the infection INFECT.")
(comment IndustrializedCountry "A specialization of #$Country.  Each instance of #$IndustrializedCountry is a nation-state whose economy is characterized by large industries, at least some mechanization of production, and by a concentration of the work force in urban, rather than rural, areas.")
(comment AspectTenseMicrotheory "This collection is the subcollection of
#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory in which the constants defined in
#$AspectTense-LogicMt are available. That is, every instance of
#$AspectTenseMicrotheory is also a spec of
#$AspectTense-LogicMt. Assertions involving tense and aspect operators --
e.g., those obtained by HPSG parsing tensed English sentences -- should
always be stated in one or more instances of #$AspectTenseMicrotheory.")
(comment SportsStatsForFn "#$SportsStatsForFn takes as argument any thing and returns the collection of all sports statistics related to that thing. For example, in taking an instance of #$SportsEvent, it will return statistics relating to scores, team rankings, etcs. for that competition. Thus, (#$SportsStatsForFn (#$OlympicsFn (#$YearFn 1996))) returns the collection of all sports statistics for the 1996 Olympics. In taking a particular instance of #$Athlete, what is returned is the collection of statistics related to that individual, such as physical statistics, performance statistics, etc.")
(comment stapledTo "(#$stapledTo ?obj1 ?obj2) ?obj1 and ?obj2 are connected together by means of a #$Staple.")
(comment QuaternaryRelation "The collection of all fixed-arity relations of arity 4 (see #$arity).  The most notable specializations of #$QuaternaryRelation are #$QuaternaryPredicate and #$QuaternaryFunction (qq.v.).")
(comment Agrobacterium "This is the collection of bacteria which are

used as vectors to introduce genetic material into plants.")
(comment AshWednesday "The collection of all Ash Wednesdays, designated in the Christian liturgical calendar as the fortieth non-Sunday before Easter. #$AshWednesday is the first day of #$Lent.")
(comment Coprophilia "Elements of #$Coprophilia are #$Events in which somebody interacts with #$Feces with the intent of bringing about his/her own #$SexualArousal.")
(comment FoodOrDrink-Hot "This is the collection of foods and beverages usually served
warmer than room temperature.")
(comment MacrolideAntibiotic "Class of antibiotics which include erythromycin.")
(comment deviceHasArmor "(deviceHasArmor DEVICE ARMOR) means that ARMOR is a
#$DefenseSystem that is part of DEVICE. A prime example of this is the
relationship between a device such as a tank and its hull (armor).")
(comment importFromThroughAmountDuring "(#$importFromThroughAmountDuring REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2 PT THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE imported by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 from the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT (on their way from REGION2) during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PT might, in the case of oil imports, for instance, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile imports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars imported.  In the case of oil imports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil imported (by REGION1 from REGION2 through PT), or it might be an instance of #$MonetaryValue indicating the monetary value of all the oil imported.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of import of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION1 from REGION2 through PT during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil imports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day or in terms of so many dollars per day (again, indicating the monetary value of the oil).")
(comment PhoneSex "The collection of all acts of phone sex. In an instance of #$PhoneSex, two (or more) people who are #$CommunicatingByTelephone get sexual titilation or satisfaction from saying explicit sexual things to each other.")
(comment Visa-Permit "A specialization of both #$Permission and #$LegalAgreement.  Each instance of #$Visa-Permit is an authorization issued by the government of some country to one (or more) person(s), stating that s/he is allowed to enter that country and remain for a certain period of time while engaging in certain specified activities (e.g., study, travel, work).  Specializations of #$Visa-Permit include #$H1WorkVisa, #$F1WorkVisa, and #$GreenCard.")
(disjointWith DefenseSystem Vane)
(comment airSpeed "(#$airSpeed PLANE SPEED) means that the

   fastest that PLANE can travel through

    the air is SPEED.")
(comment costOfAction "(#$costOfAction ACT AGENT PROP SUBJ-ATTR) holds iff the AGENT's

evaluation of the desirability of PROP, the outcome of ACT, corresponds to

SUBJ-ATTR. In other words, #$costOfAction expresses the agent's judgment

about whether the action is worth the effort of performing it. Such a judgment is

evaluative, because it depends upon the agent's assignment of preferences to the

expected outcome of the action. Notice that, given the way

#$outcomeOfAction is defined, PROP involves a specification of all

value-relevant features of the result of ACT.")
(comment BirthEvent "The collection of events in which one animal (prototypically, a #$Mammal) gives birth to another.  The mother is the #$birthParent and the child is the #$birthChild.  Both are #$objectOfStateChange; the mother goes from being pregnant to not pregnant (therefore a #$BirthEvent is an instance of #$PregnancyEndingEvent), while the child changes from being inside the mother and relying on the mother for nutritional, respiratory, and excretory needs (called in CYC the #$Embryo life stage, although different English terms apply to different stages of in utero development in mammals and not all of these terms apply to live-born #$Fish) to the #$JuvenileAnimal life stage (see #$BiologicalStageOfDevelopment).")
(comment CelestialBody "A specialization of both #$CelestialObject and #$AstronomicalBody (qq.v.).  
Each instance of #$CelestialBody is an celestial object that is an 
individual body, as opposed to a group or system of such bodies.  In other 
words, celestial bodies are astronomical bodies that can be seen in the 
heavens from the surface of the Earth without the aid of artificial optical instruments.  Instances include #$Sun, #$MoonOfEarth, and #$PlanetMars.")
(comment ZoneOfMilitaryControl "The collection of all zones of control by military forces.  Such a zone is the maximal geographic area in which some particular #$ModernMilitaryOrganization has military superiority and domination to the point that any non-concealed hostile actions within the area can be effectively punished or prevented by the controlling forces.  In #$Battles, the forward boundary of a #$ZoneOfMilitaryControl is likely to be a strip (a #$LineOfMilitaryForces) which is the #$frontLineOfTroops of the controlling force.  The boundaries and general location of a #$ZoneOfMilitaryControl often change rapidly during military campaigns.  See also #$zoneControlled.")
(comment SpecifiedCollection "#$SpecifiedCollection is the collection of all collections that are subsets of some specified #$Set-Mathematical.")
(comment PassingThroughSecurityStation "The collection of all events in which one or more agents pass through/are checked through a security station.")
(comment backchainRequired "(#$backchainRequired PREDICATE) means that rules that conclude PREDICATE must be used in order to prove literals involving PREDICATE.  In other words, when performing inferences, all literals involving PREDICATE must be eliminated using rules since there won't be any other way to prove them.  See also #$backchainEncouraged, #$backchainDiscouraged, and #$backchainForbidden.")
(comment TeenModel "The collection of #$FashionModels who are between the ages of twelve and nineteen")
(comment ManufacturerFn "A function that returns the collection of all instances of #$ManufacturingCompany that make instances of a given collection of #$PartiallyTangibleProducts.")
(disjointWith Canoe PedalBoat)
(comment NewsFn "#$NewsFn takes as argument any thing and returns the collection of all mentions of that thing in the news.  For example, (#$NewsFn #$Dog) returns all news involving dogs, and (#$NewsFn #$JohnKennedy) returns all news about John F. Kennedy.  Note that determination of what properly belongs in such a set is time-relative -- what is currently news probably will not be news two years from now.  This function is therefore of limited use outside of applications in which it triggers some time-stamped action.")
(disjointWith RifleGrenade HandGrenade)
(comment MutualFundShare "The collection of all mutual fund shares, each of which represents a proportional interest in all of the investments held by a #$MutualFund. An owner of a certain number of shares of a #$MutualFund can sell them back to the #$InvestmentFirm that operates the #$MutualFund at a price proportional to the value of the fund's total investments, subject to fees, etc.")
(comment CordlikeObject "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$CordlikeObject is a partially tangible non-fluid object (so #$CordlikeObject is disjoint with #$FluidTangibleThing) whose length is significantly greater than either its height or width. Moreover, each instance of #$CordlikeObject has a high degree of flexibility. Notable specializations of #$CordlikeObject include the collections #$Nerve, #$Tape, and #$Cable.")
(comment OrganicMethodFn "The term `(#$OrganicMethodFn ACTIVITY)' denotes the collections of instances

of the script type ACTIVITY carried out in such a way as to make them correctly

called organic. See also to #$OrganicFn.")
(comment Region-Underspecified "The collection of regions/areas, tangible or otherwise, which are
typically conceptualized by human beings for purposes of common-sense
reasoning as spatial regions. This collection thus includes tangible
#$GeographicalRegions such as #$Ireland-TheIsland, as well as metaphoric
regions such as #$FieldOfStudy. Instances of #$Region-Underspecified
differ from non-regional #$Location-Underspecified in that they
possess some underspecified correlate of the notion of 'area' and
'spatial extent'. A #$Location-Underspecified may be a point in some
abstract, metaphorical or physical space, whereas instances of 
#$Region-Underspecified can be conceptualized as possessing area in
such a space.")
(comment GrungeRockMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic that incoporates certain aspects of 
  heavy BluesRockMusic and PunkMusic.  #$GrungeRockMusic became quite popular
  in the early-to-mid 1990s.  Influential practitioners of this style include
  Nirvana, Pearl Jam, Soundgarden, and Hole.")
(comment InflatableSexDoll "This is the collection of inflatable sex dolls. ")
(comment ReverseMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements in which the owner of a #$HumanResidence recieves money or a #$SecuredLineOfCredit (or some combination of these) taken from the equity the owner has amassed by paying a previous #$MortgageAgreement on that property.  Such mortgages are usually given to senior citizens who have totally or nearly totally repaid any existing mortgage on their residences.  The #$MortgageAccount is typically settled when the #$borrower no longer occupies that residence.  The #$borrower on a #$ReverseMortgage cannot be forced to sell the residence to repay it as long as the #$borrower occupies that residence, even if the value of the loan exceeds the value of the residence.  The #$ReverseMortgage is usually easier to obtain than other #$HomeEquityLoans.")
(comment taskEfficiency "(#$taskEfficiency EVENT EFFIC-LEVEL) means that the task TASK is completed with efficiency level, EFFIC-LEVEL.   Efficiency presumably is based on measures of rate and/or amount of input compared to amount of output or success of output.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByGramStain "A collection of collections and a partition on #$Bacterium. This collection partitions #$Bacterium into two disjoint classes, #$GramPositiveBacterium and #$GramNegativeBacterium. The 'Gram Stain' is a test to see what type of cell wall the bacteria has. The #$Bacterium are stained with a violet dye and iodine, then rinsed in alcohol, and stained again with a red dye. The #$GramPositiveBacterium retain the violet dye while the #$GramNegativeBacterium will lose it but keep the red.")
(comment ConvertedCommandShip "The collection of military converted command ships.")
(comment SineFn "(#$SineFn ANGLE) yields the sine of that angle.")
(comment informationRouter "This predicate can be used to indicate instances of #$PartiallyTangible           that act as routers in instances of #$InformationTransferEvent.           (#$informationRouter TRANS PAR_TANG) means that PAR_TANG acts as a           router in the #$InformationTransferEvent TRANS.  This means, in            particular, that PAR_TANG plays some sort of active role in           receiving and transmitting the #$infoTransferred in TRANS, e.g.           encrypting the information.")
(comment AmlodipineBesylate "A #$PharmaceuticalType which is a subcategory of #$CalciumChannelBlocker.  Amlodipine Besylate is used in treating heart disease.")
(comment (LowAmountFn Elasticity) "re-expands somewhat after compression, but not all the way back")
(comment FillingARefillPrescription "The collection of all events in which a #$DrugPrescription is refilled after having been filled previously.  This is a subset of the collection of #$FillingAPrescription which is disjoint from #$FillingANewPrescription.")
(comment territoriesControlled "(#$territoriesControlled AGENT TERRITORY) means the TERRITORY is a #$GeographicalThing under the political control of AGENT.   This refers to actual practical political control, not mere legal or unenforced territorial claims.")
(comment NorwegianWord "The collection of all lexical words in Norwegian; a subset of #$LexicalWord.            Different inflectional forms of a word do not count as different words.")
(comment CovalentBond "The collection of configurations in which two atoms are bonded due to shared electrons. Mediators of #$CovalentBonds are electrons shared by the atoms bonded.")
(comment State-SponsoredTerroristAct "A specialization of #$TerroristAct.  Each instance of #$State-SponsoredTerroristAct is a terrorist act that is sponsored in some way by an instance of #$Country.")
(comment AmericanCollegeTestingProgramAssessment "The collection of #$AcademicTesting events that are designed to test the scholastic aptitude, and thus college eligibility, of a student. Also known as ACT testing, ACT test scores are used by universities and a primary selection criterion for new student admittance.")
(comment breedsType "(#$breedsType BRDR AN-TYPE) means that the #$AnimalBreeder-Business BRDR breeds the type of animal AN-TYPE.")
(comment objectEmplaced "(#$objectEmplaced EVENT OBJ) means OBJ comes to be in some location in EVENT (an instance of #$SomethingAppearingSomewhere). OBJ may exist before EVENT, or may be created during EVENT.")
(comment agentFaxNumber "ARG2 is a fax number for the agent ARG1.")
(comment CommandoUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained to deploy and fight           'commando-style'. Commando units are typically small (6-15           persons), well-versed in the art of camouflage, and trained for rapid           deployment and hand-to-hand combat. They are often employed by           paramilitary and guerilla organizations           organizations, like the US Army, may rely on commando units for           special operations.")
(comment RetinalPatternScanner "#$RetinalPatternScanner is a subset of #$BiometricAuthenticationDevice.  Individuals in the collection           #$RetinalPatternScanner use lasers to scan the pattern of blood vessels on retinas, and attempt to match            the pattern with a stored representation of it.")
(comment actionInapplicabilityConditions "(#$actionInapplicabilityConditions GENERICPURPOSEFULACTION CYCFORMULA) asserts that an instance of the
GENERICPURPOSEFULACTION is reasonable to plan to do within a particular #$Situation if only CYCFORMULA is NOT known to
be true. Note that for some action class like ACT, it is NOT the same to assert (#$actionApplicabilityConditions ACT (not
(P ?x))) vs.  (#$actionInapplicabilityConditions ACT (P ?x)), because the former says that we must be able to PROVE (not
(P ?x)), while the latter is weaker - we should only not know that (P ?x) holds. That is, we are allowed to create plans
that have an execution of ACT if we don't know that (P ?x), but we could discover ourselves to be uninformed. Using
#$actionApplicabilityConditions, however, we could not create such plans unless we were certain that (not (P ?x)). Note
also that applicability conditions differ from preconditions - we can't try to plan to achive an applicability
condition.")
(comment OccludedFrontEvent "The collection of all #$AirFrontEvents in which a #$ColdFrontEvent overtakes a #$WarmFrontEvent and pushes under it.  Long duration heay precipitation (see #$PrecipitationProcess) is usually associated with occluded fronts.")
(comment distalToFrom "(#$distalToFrom PART-1 PART-2 REF-POINT) means that the #$PartiallyTangible (often an #$AnimalBodyRegion) PART-1 lies in a #$DistalDirection of PART-2, from the point of reference REF-POINT (an #$AnimalBodyPart -- generally, of a #$Person).  PART-1 and PART-2 are parts of the same body.  For example, (#$distalToFrom FredsThumb FredsElbow FredsTorso) expresses the fact that Fred's thumb is further away from his torso than his elbow is.  Note that PART-2 is therefore proximal to PART-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `proximal to'")
(comment MSEncarta "An electronic encyclopedia published by #$MicrosoftInc.")
(comment NoSimplerArgument "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
neither argument is simpler than the other.")
(comment nameString-NC "(#$nameString-NC TERM STRING) means that the #$ProperNameString STRING names the thing denoted by TERM in a non-canonical way. The `NC' in the name stands for `non-canonical'.  For example, one value for #$nameString-NC for the Cyc constant #$Siegel might be `NICK SIEGEL'. This name as printed does not conform to the US Postal Service's recommended standard for printed names, and so relative to this standard it is not `canonical.'  (One US Postal Service `canonical' form would be `MR NICHOLAS SIEGEL').  Similarly, `JORDAN' might be the non-canonical form of the name of a Middle Eastern country.  A canonical form (official UN English version) of the name is `HASHEMITE KINGDOM OF JORDAN'. Non-canonical means that  NAME is not known to conform to the canonicalization scheme(s) used for other names entered for OBJECT.  These other (presumed canonical) names should be related to OBJECT using the predicate #$nameString. It really only makes sense to use #$nameString-NC in contexts (such as the #$LogicalTableSchemas for certain database tables) where OBJECT may have both canonical and non-canonical names entered for it, and the distinction between canonical and non-canonical forms somehow matters.  In contexts where the differences between canonicalized and non-canonicalized names is not an issue, just use #$nameString.")
(comment UpskirtPicture "A subset of #$PornographicPictures. Each element depicts the #$Pelvis or the inner #$Thigh of an ostensibly unsuspecting #$Person..")
(comment RectilinearTrajectory "A rectilinear trajectory")
(disjointWith BookGeneric-CW Article-PCW)
(comment LookingForSomething-Definite "The collection of instances of #$LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing wherein some #$IntelligentAgent is looking for a particular thing.  The agent might have consciously in mind one or more descriptions of the thing s/he is seeking or, if not, could at least be prompted to produce such descriptions.  Some of these descriptions will express properties the seeker would take to be criterial of success in the sense that s/he could not conceive of a case in which both (i) s/he successfully finds the object and (ii) the object s/he finds lacks any of those properties. The conjunction of these criterial properties will correspond to the instance of #$PossibleIdentificationCondition that is associated with the search (see #$searchCriterion-Definite).  What makes an instance of #$LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing an instance of #$LookingForSomething-Definite is that the agent believes that exactly one object has this conjunction of criterial properties, namely the particular object s/he seeks.")
(comment ComputerModel "This is the collection of models or simulations of objects or phenomena created by computer programs. See also #$ComputerModeling and #$Simulation-Activity.")
(disjointWith FluidConduit Stream)
(comment TabletSublingual "The collection of all sublingual tablets.  These tablets are placed under the tongue to dissolve their contents with saliva solvent.")
(comment 0-TheDigit "The numeral 0 of the Arabic Number system.  This is '0' as a #$Character-Abstract rather than the physical #$WrittenCharacter or the abstract mathematical #$Number-General.")
(comment ArchitecturalPlan "The collection of architectural drawings which act as plans or specifications for building some #$ConstructionArtifact. Some of these plans may be #$Blueprints, but they need not be hardcopy objects. They could be created using a computer drafting program, for example.")
(comment Peso-DominicanRepublic "Major unit of currency of #$DominicanRepublic")
(disjointWith LoadingAProjectileWeapon Archery)
(comment Ester "A collection of substances created via reaction between an alcohol and an acid.")
(comment FruitRipeningEvent "The event in which a fruit, after becoming fully grown and differentiated, ripens.  For fleshy fruits, ripening often involves conversion of starches to sugars, changes in color, and other chemical changes.  For fruits which are not fleshy, ripening usually involves drying out.  Some dry fruits eventually break apart, sometimes explosively, releasing or expelling the seeds.")
(comment Rosacea "a chronic form of #$Acne affecting the nose, forehead, and cheeks, characterized by red pustular lesions. Also called 'acne rosacea'.")
(comment StructuralSupportStuff "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleThing. Each instance of #$StructuralSupportStuff is a hard, rigid substance of a sort that typically provides some kind of structural support.  Specializations
include #$Wood, #$BoneTheStuff, and #$StoneStuff.")
(comment exploitTargetsProgram "(#$exploitTargetsProgram EXPLOIT PROGRAM) means that EXPLOIT

is designed to enable an attacker to take advantage of some

vulnerability in PROGRAM.  The 

same exploit may enable an attacker to take advantage of a

vulnerability that exists on 

several different programs.")
(comment SetOfCardinalityFn "(#$SetOfCardinalityFn COL CARD) denotes the collection of sets of elements of COL with cardinality CARD.")
(comment SerialKiller "The collection of people who murder several people over a
period of time, usually months or even years, often exciting the
sustained interest of readers of popular press")
(comment MilitaryOperationsEventNarrativeMicrotheory "Each instance of #$MilitaryOperationsEventNarrativeMicrotheory is a microtheory describing some event or series of events which take place as part of some #$MilitaryOperations.  In contrast to #$MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory and #$MilitaryOperationsDynamicSituationMicrotheory, assertions located in a #$MilitaryOperationsEventNarrativeMicrotheory do not automatically hold for the duration of that microtheory's mtTime.")
(comment Acholeplasmataceae-Family "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalFamily in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes the #$BiologicalGenus of #$Acholeplasma-Genus, #$Anaeroplasma-Genus, and #$Phytoplasma-Genus.")
(comment AlternativeMedicineEventTypeByModality "#$AlternativeMedicineEventTypeByModality is a collection of collections. Each element of #$AlternativeMedicineEventTypeByModality is a collection of #$AlternativeMedicineHealthCareEvents that have the same healing modality. In other words, an element of #$AlternativeMedicineEventTypeByModality is a kind of alternative therapy considered as a collection of #$Events. Some elements of #$AlternativeMedicineEventTypeByModality include homeopathy, naturopathy, and #$Acupuncture. Alternative therapies considered as #$FieldOfStudy can be denoted using the function   #$AlternativeMedicalModalityFOSFn.")
(comment slotOf "binary predicate arg1 denotes a slot excplicitly associated with constant arg2.")
(disjointWith EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus GeopoliticalEntityTypeByBasicCategory)
(comment Measles "A highly contagious childhood disease characterized by red spots on the skin.  One attack confers lifelong immunity.")
(comment BiologicalWeapon-GeneticallyEngineeredVirusBased "The collection of all #$BiologicalWeapons that make use of 

#$GeneticallyEngineeredViralPathogens.")
(comment FetalAlcoholSyndrome "#$FetalAlcoholSyndrome (FAS) (also known as Fetal Alcohol Effect)           is a pattern of birth defects that results from drinking alcohol            during pregnancy. It occurs in one out of every 750 births.")
(comment MorphoStructureSchema "All morphology rules are reified as Cyc constants, and represented as instances of #$MorphoStructureSchema.")
(comment SponsorFn-Agent "#$SponsorFn-Agent takes as
argument any instance AGENT01 of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of
all agents sponsoring AGENT01 in some instance of #$Action. For example,
(#$SponsorFn-Agent #$MichaelJordan) returns the collection of all agents
sponsoring basketball star #$MichaelJordan.")
(comment stepFinalValue "(#$stepFinalValue STEP VALUE) means that the step-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution STEP has a final or post-step height of VALUE.  For example, the final value of a step used to specify a temporal persistence distribution might be (#$Percent 95), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the step distribution pertains, the likelihood of being true after the step change which occurs at #$stepLocation is 0.95.  VALUE might also be a reified value such as `very likely'.")
(comment AddressLabel "The collection of labels that convey address information.  These are typically attached to packages that are shipped or mailed, but they could also be used for identification purposes (e.g. on a gym bag).  Thus not all instances of #$AddressLabel are attached to a package of some sort.")
(comment Fiber "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleThing. Each
instance of #$Fiber is a solid substance with high tenacity and high
ratio of length to diameter.")
(comment SportsTeamTypeBySex "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$SportsTeam whose instances are all of the same gender.")
(comment alignedAlongEdge "(#$alignedAlongEdge SHEET OBJ2) means that one of the edges of a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET, #$touches OBJ2 along its length.")
(comment Facemask-Baseball "The collection of face masks that BaseballCatchers wear.")
(comment M58MineClearingLineCharge "The collection of rocket-propelled explosive line charges which are used to deliberately detonate land mines.  The line charge is 350 feet long and contains 5 pounds per linear foot of composition C-4 explosive and will clear a lane 14 meters by 100 meters.")
(comment Bonfire "A large fire built in the open, typically for celebration or as a signal")
(comment Sodium "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of sodium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment RomanceMovie "#$RomanceMovie is the collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which relates a romantic story [#$RomanceStory-Generic].")
(comment Ell "A unit of distance whose length is the same as 45 #$Inches.")
(comment RevolutionsPerMinute "The #$RateOfRotation of one revolution each minute.")
(comment PlanetaryBody "A collection of heavenly bodies.  Each element of #$PlanetaryBody is an entity spacially distinct from other heavenly bodies that does not emit radiation due to internal fusion processes.")
(comment OccipitalLobe "The collection of all occipital lobes of #$Brains.  Each individual #$OccipitalLobe is in the posterior region of a #$CerebralHemisphere and processes visual input.")
(comment ExpressingAnimosity-Formally "The collection of events where one agent formally express animosity or disdain for another.")
(comment Bacterium-Lophotrichous "The collection of #$Bacterium whose instances have tufts of flagella at one end.")
(comment InternetService "A collection of accounts. Each instance of #$InternetService is an agreement for an #$InternetServiceProvider to provide email, Web, ftp, telnet service, etc. to a client.")
(disjointWith ArmoredVehicle LawnMower)
(comment CrossingOptionType "#$CrossingOptionType is used to note the kinds of crossings which are relevant to Workarounds problems.")
(comment performanceOfAIS "(#$performanceOfAIS EVENT AIS) means that EVENT is a performance of the #$AbstractInformationStructure, AIS. For example, if  EVENT1 is a case of uttering the instance of #$TextString \"The King is dead\", TEXTGROUP1, then (#$performanceOfAIS EVENT1 TEXTGROUP1).")
(comment numberOfPrescriptionsByDocDuring "(#$numberOfPrescriptionsByDocDuring DOC DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PERIOD NUM) means that #$Prescriber DOC has had NUM prescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE filled for DRUGTYPE during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment Malnutrition-Secondary "Secondary malnutrition is caused by failure to absorb or utilize nutrients.  Cf. #$DietaryDeficiencyCondition, which is caused by not ingesting nutrients. This condition is caused by not metabolizing them.")
(comment equivalenceCollectionWRT "This predicate is a collection-based version of

#$equivalenceClassWRT, i.e. it relates a collection of things to the

subcollection of that collection each of which bear the relevant equivalence

relation to some given thing in the collection.

(#$equivalenceCollectionWRT COL EQUIVREL THING SUBCOL) means that

SUBCOL is the subset of COL whose elements bear the relation EQUIVREL to THING.")
(comment SpinningSomething "This collection includes instances of stretching, twisting and otherwise shaping a fibrous material (such as cotton, wool, or synthetic material) into thread or yarn.")
(comment MusicalMovie "An instance of #$MovieTypeByGenre,
#$MusicalMovies focus on stories in which characters communicate
 their feelings through music and dance. Rather than simply
 providing a lapse in a movie's action, song and dance fuse
 to form a whole -- and here lies the main difference between
 a musical and a movie just containing occasional musical numbers.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn SecondRib) HeadOfBone) "The head of the second rib on the left side")
(comment DeputyFn "(#$DeputyFn ROLE) returns the #$OrganizationalPosition of
being deputy to an agent playing ROLE.  If (ROLE SYSTEM PERSON) and
((DeputyFn ROLE) SYSTEM DEPUTY), then DEPUTY is PERSON's immediate
#$subordinates and is deputized to act on behalf of or as a
representative of PERSON.")
(disjointWith MarineCorps Navy)
(comment TimeBomb-Computer "#$TimeBomb-Computer is a subcollection of #$LogicBomb in which the malicious code
    is activated at a certain time.")
(comment Automobile "A specialization of #$RoadVehicle.  Each instance of #$Automobile is a four-wheeled road vehicle designed for carrying about two to eight passengers.  Notable specializations of #$Automobile include #$SportsCar, #$PickupTruck and #$Van.  This collection does _not_ include motorcycles or tractor-trailers (since both motorcycles and tractor-trailers are not four-wheeled vehicles), nor does it include buses (since buses are designed to carry more passengers than instances of #$Automobile are designed to carry).")
(comment Aldosterone "An important #$Hormone secreted by the adrenal cortex. It promotes potassium, sodium, and chloride metabolism.")
(comment PickingAFruit "The collection of events in which a single fruit (the plant structure containing the seeds of flowering plants) is picked.  Note that this includes (in most cases) picking a vegetable.")
(comment ArgGenlBinaryPredicate "Those instances of both #$BinaryPredicate and #$ArgGenlPredicate used to specify the required #$genls of an argument of a #$Relation; the arg1 is the #$Relation; the arg2 is the required #$genls #$Collection.")
(comment RecoillessGun-Portable "The #$RecoillessGun-Portable is fired from the shoulder and is often used as an anti-tank weapon.")
(disjointWith ElectricalResistance ElectricalCharge)
(comment PriorProbabilityFn "A function used for probability statements.  (#$PriorProbabilityFn PROPOSITION), applied to the #$CycLAssertion PROPOSITION, yields its a priori probability of being true, in the applicable #$Microtheory.  The result is a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true.  In most microtheories, generally, this refers to the probability that PROPOSITION, by itself, would be true if there were no further evidence in the #$Microtheory for or against it, nor knowledge of the truth of anything else other than the #$domainAssumptions of the #$Microtheory.  Contrast this with the predicate form #$priorProbability and with the functions #$DerivedProbabilityFn and #$PriorProbability-RangeFn.  A #$PriorProbabilityFn may represent an absolute objective probability, a subjective assigned probability, a quantum probability, or an assigned probability based on some internal characteristic of PROPOSITION (including possibly a statement in it of the occurrence of a number of outcomes within a large number of trials).  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.")
(comment angleOfLauncher "(#$angleOfLauncher GUN ANGLE-RANGE) indicates possible vertical angles at which a GUN can be fired. For example, (#$angleOfLauncher ?MORTAR (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure 45 90) means that ?MORTAR can be fired at angles between 45 and 90 degrees.")
(comment istDecreasesSlotValue "(#$istDecreasesSlotValue INDPROP DEPPROP SLOT) means that the value that SLOT takes in the arg2 position for DEPPROP will be less if INDPROP is provable than it will be if INDPROP is not provable.")
(disjointWith ElectricalDevice Ball)
(comment MilitaryUnitSpecialtyType "#$MilitaryUnitSpecialtyType is a collection of collections. Its instances are subsets of #$ModernMilitaryOrganization grouped by military specialization. This work is based on Peterson and Andersen (1997).")
(comment dialects "(#$dialects LANGUAGE DIALECT) means that DIALECT is a dialect of the language LANGUAGE.")
(comment Gelatin "An animal protein with many uses in food, medicine, and other areas.  With flavorings and a high water content, it's a tasty dessert; in a dry form, it can be used to coat or contain medicines.")
(comment SpinningThread "Creating thread by #$Extruding fibers from a mass and twisting them together.")
(comment ElectricalProcess "The class of electrical processes.")
(comment StateLottery "Official lotteries that are regularly held by a state or country.")
(disjointWith Glider Spacecraft)
(comment receivesTreatmentTypeForType "(#$receivesTreatmentTypeForType ORG TREAT-TYPE AIL-TYPE) means that the instance of #$Organism-Whole ORG receives a #$MedicalTreatmentEvent of type TREAT-TYPE for an instance of #$AilmentCondition of type AIL-TYPE.")
(comment AircraftCrewMember "The collection of people who work aboard an aircraft in flight and assist either in flying it or in the service or task it performs.")
(comment HumanFn "The term `(#$HumanFn THING)' denotes the collection of all human instances of

THING. For example, (#$HumanFn DNA) is the collection of all human DNA.")
(comment Antifungal "Drugs which are used to prevent or fight infections caused by fungi.")
(comment EnglishLexicalMicrotheory "The collection of all instances of #$LexicalMicrotheory whose #$languageOfLexicon is the #$EnglishLanguage.")
(comment HairShirt "The collection of shirts made of coarse animal hair, worn next to the skin as penance.")
(comment internationalMonetaryReserves "(internationalMonetaryReserves AGT AMOUNT) money means that AGT (usually a country) has international monetary reserves in the amount of AMOUNT. International monetary reserves are funds an entity has available for purchasing foreign currency.")
(comment Caper-Plant "A plant cultivated in the Mediterranean area.  Its flower buds are pickled and used as condiments.")
(comment EMailSending "A specialization of #$InformationTransferEvent-Electronic. Each instance of this collection is an #$Event in which somebody or something sends an #$EMailMessage to some #$EMailAddress.  If successful, an instance of #$EMailSending ends when the email message reaches the intended recipient's #$MailServer-Network, at which point it is likely that an instance of #$EMailReceiving will ensue. See also #$EMailCommunication -- events in which an email message is successfully sent and received.")
(disjointWith Oxide Agent-Generic)
(disjointWith Artifact GeoculturalRegion)
(comment LosingALeaf "The event in which some #$Plant loses a #$Leaf, due to lack of water, ailment, or in preparation for winter.  This does not include events in which a leaf is pulled off by some other physical object.")
(comment NCAABasketballTournament "The annual #$NationalCollegiateAthleticAssociation Basketball tournaments, both men's and women's.  Held to determine the best men's and women's teams in the country")
(comment DockLandingShip "A collection. Military dock landing ships, which are intended to .")
(comment Tyrosine "A collection of compounds and a spec of #$AminoAcid.  These
compounds are synthesized metabolically from #$Phenylalanine.  They
are a precursor of thyroid hormones, catecholamines, and melanin.  Its
abbreviations are Tyr and Y.")
(comment worldAccountForFile "(#$worldAccountForFile FILE OTHER) means the  #$LoginAccount OTHER neither belongs to the creator of FILE nor is it in the group (#$UserAccountGroup) of the creator of FILE. In other words, (#$ownerAccountForFile FILE OTHER) is not the case, nor is (#$groupAccountForFile FILE GROUP) the case for any GROUP for which (#$groupMembers GROUP OTHER) is the case.")
(comment AirAssaultInfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of offensive infantry units that are inserted into combat by air vehicles - usually helicopters - without parachute drop.")
(comment HAHOParachuteJump "The collection of High Altitude High Opening parachute jumps.  This method of parachute jumping allows the jumper to travel 15 miles or so from where he departs the plane.  Because this sort of jump is generally done from very high altitudes (30,000+ ft.), the jumper must carry oxygen.")
(comment AnySpecFn "(#$AnySpecFn COL) denotes a term which represents an arbitrary spec of COL.  This function is not a #$ReifiableFunction, since it primarily exists to support queries about properties that apply to all specs of a given collection. See #$EveryFn for a similar concept.")
(comment CutaneousAnthrax "The collection of all #$AnthraxInfections which are inoculated into the body via a #$SkinLaceration or damage to #$MucousMembranes.")
(comment Epinephrine "A #$Hormone secreted by the medulla of the adrenal glands which stimulates autonomous nerve response.")
(comment FitnessMachine-MultiPurpose "This is the collection fitness

machines which are designed to allow the user to perform

a number of different exercises on them.")
(comment SelfPropelledFieldArtilleryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for handling           motorized artillery pieces. Note that 'self-propelled' refers to the           artillery piece itself, not to the projectile fired.")
(comment Syntactician "A #$Linguist specializing in #$Syntax")
(disjointWith PropositionalAttitudeContext DeclarativeContext)
(comment transmissionToHost "(#$transmissionToHost INFECTING HOST) means that as a result of

INFECTING, an instance of #$InfectionTransmissionEvent, HOST will be the host of an infection of the type of #$Infection conveyed by

INFECTING.")
(comment BusLine "Instances of #$BusLine are organizations which, as their main function, transport people in buses.")
(comment ComputerAIS "A specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure.  Each instance of #$ComputerAIS is the abstract information structure of an abstract work whose instantiation in computer memory is intended to have meaning. Important specializations include #$ComputerFile-AIS, #$ComputerCode, and #$ComputerProgram-CWIS.")
(comment InfantryFightingVehicle-BMP-2 "#$InfantryFightingVehicle-BMP-2 is the collection BMP-2's. The BMP-2  is an infantry fighting vehicle of Russian origin, first seen publicly in 1982, but in use for some time before that.  It has been used in combat by the Russian army in Afghanistan, and apparently by armies of both Iraq and Kuwait during Desert Storm.  In addition to Russian manufacture, it is also manufactured under license by India (and known as the `Sarath') and in the former Czechoslovakia.  Russia was marketing the BMP-2 for $200,000 in 1993.  It is amphibious, floating and being propelled on the water by its tracks. BMP-2's are associated primarily with Red mechanized infantry units (rather than armored units), at least at the battalion level.  At higher levels, various types of divisions may have lower-level components of several types, so mechanized infantry (with BMP-2s) and armored (with T-64 tanks, for instance) may very well be found in the same division.")
(comment RelativeHumidity "A collection of attributes; a subcollection of #$ScalarInterval.  Instances of #$RelativeHumidity represent the extent to which the atmosphere at a location approaches total saturation with water vapor.  The relative humidity of a location is indicated with the predicate #$ambientRelativeHumidity.")
(comment titleOfWork "The title of a piece of some information bearing thing (includes subtexts like chapters).")
(comment equiv "A #$LogicalConnective that represents bi-directional implication in #$CycL.  It takes two arguments, each of which must be an instance of #$ELSentence-Assertible. (#$equiv FORMULA-1 FORMULA-2) means that FORMULA-1 is true precisely when FORMULA-2 is true; in other words, FORMULA-1 is true if and only if FORMULA-2 is true.  (An EL #$equiv formula is translated during canonicalization into an equivalent, less compact, conjunction of #$implies formulas.) See also the predicate #$sentenceEquiv.")
(comment PoliticalOrganizationsFn "#$PoliticalOrganizationsFn takes as argument any #$GeopoliticalEntity and returns the collection of all instances of #$PoliticalOrganization existing at least partially within the territory of that GeopoliticalEntity.  For instance, (#$PoliticalOrganizationsFn #$CzechRepublic) returns the collection of all PoliticalOrganizations existing within the Czech Republic, including political parties like the ODS and CSSD, political advocacy groups, and any other organizations of a principally political nature existing in that country.  Also included would be organizations like #$AmnestyInternational which are international in scope but have Czech branches.")
(comment flapHingedTo "(#$flapHingedTo ?obj1 ?obj2) means there is a region of continuous connection between ?obj1 and ?obj2 that is #$Bendable.")
(comment RickettsiaRicketsii "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom
found in wood ticks.  In order to be infectious, the tick must be
engorged with blood.  Thus, there is a 45 to 90 minute delay between
attachment and #$Infection.  This #$BiologicalSpecies is confined to the Western Hemisphere.")
(comment AlbedoFeature-Topographical "The collection of all topographical features noted for an albedo (reflectivity of light) significanly different from the surrounding regions.")
(comment MtOfIndustryTypeFn "The term (#$MtOfIndustryTypeFn INDUSTRYTYPE) denotes the

#$Microtheory containing the assertions pertaining primarily to the collection

INDUSTRYTYPE of all localized industries of a certain kind.  This function can be used for any industry type; it is not

 necessary to create a new, named 

'industry Microtheory' for an industry type when the industry type is already in the

knowledge base.  For example, (#$MtOfIndustryTypeFn

#$MetallurgyIndustry) would be the #$Microtheory for assertions relating

primarily to metallurgy, i.e. to the collection of all metallurgy industries

 worldwide.  (#$MetallurgyIndustry is the collection of all metallurgy industries, each of which is an instance of #$Industry-Localized; it is not itself an individual instance of #$Industry-Localized.)  Note that each

 instance of #$IndustryType,

 or value of the function #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn, is a collection of individual,

 regionally defined industries.  To generate the #$Microtheory for a specific individual regional industry,

 use #$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn.")
(comment OpenArea "An outdoor space, exposed to the sky, where things can move unimpeded in any direction.")
(comment productionCapacity "The predicate #$productionCapacity states a producer's 

greatest possible rate of production

for a given product. The second argument to #$productionCapacity

must be a #$ProductType that is a specialization of #$PartiallyTangibleProduct.  The third argument must be a #$Rate.

The producer, the first argument, may be an industry (as in

'The production capacity of the Algerian oil industry is 529 million barrels of petroleum

per year'), a given factory (as in 'This plant can produce up to 12,000 tires per day'),

or a region ('The maple-syrup production capacity for the state of Maine is 

1,000 gallons per month').")
(comment Carnival-Catholic "The collection of pre-#$Lent celebrations in Catholic countries, rooted in pre-Christian spring fertility rites.")
(comment FingerFood "This is the collection of foods normally eaten using the
fingers rather than utensils, that is, one's fingers directly touch
the food and this is not considered rude in the cultural context of
the eating.")
(comment MultiVitamin "Drugs which are are mixtures of vitamins.")
(comment MonetaryInflationRate "A collection of rates; a subset of #$ScalarInterval.  Each element of #$MonetaryInflationRate is the rate at which the value of money has increased in relation to the goods and services it will buy.")
(comment Bible-BookCopy "A specialization of #$BookCopy; the collection of all printed, hardcopy versions of the #$Bible.")
(comment GovernmentFn "An instance of both #$IndividualDenotingFunction and #$ReifiableFunction.  Given an instance GEOPOL of #$GeopoliticalEntity as its single argument, #$GovernmentFn returns the instance of #$RegionalGovernment (q.v.) that governs GEOPOL.  For instance, (#$GovernmentFn #$Belgium) is the government of Belgium.")
(disjointWith DefenseSystem Model-Artifact)
(comment InflatableRaft "The collection of inflatable rafts. These are

rafts made out of some sort of membrane and are inflated with air to give them buoyancy in water.")
(comment Egg-Birds "The collection of complex ovum structures produced and emitted (laid) by female birds, in which the ovum is swollen with yolk (a food reserve substance), and around which other stuff (the white and the shell) is secreted before the egg is laid.  Bird eggs have usually been fertilized before the shell forms around them; chicken eggs sold commercially for food are usually unfertilized.")
(comment BattleZone "The collection of all zones of fighting in #$Battles between two (or among three or more) military forces.  Such a zone is a geographic area in which a #$Battle is taking place, is expected, or has recently taken place.  The boundaries and general location of a #$BattleZone often change rapidly during military campaigns.  A #$BattleZone need not be contiguous, compact or gap-free.  During #$Battle, some #$ModernMilitaryOrganizations will each have a #$frontLineOfTroops (a #$LineOfMilitaryForces forming the forward boundaries of its #$ZoneOfMilitaryControl), at least partly within the #$BattleZone.")
(comment specifiedSubsetOf "(#$specifiedSubsetOf SPECIFIED SET) states that the
specified collection SPECIFIED is a subset of the given SET.  This is
usually used to map instances of #$SpecifiedCollection to a #$TheSetOf
expression which they are specified to be a subset of.")
(comment VoterRegistration "The collection of events in which a citizen of some country registers to vote.")
(comment connectedAlongInside "(#$connectedAlongInside OBJ1 TUBE) means that #$LongAndThin OBJ1 is #$connectedAlongLength to the inside of TUBE.")
(comment PhaseIIBattlespaceSource-PIT "Each instance is a source for the phase II battlespace work
being done at Cyc (winter, 1998), partially represented as a chunk of
abstract propositional information in the form of a PIT (a
#$PropositionalInformationThing).")
(comment Aleph-1 "The first infinite cardinal (sometimes called 'omega-1') that is greater than the cardinality of natural numbers, i.e., the one that was supposedly the same as the cardinality of real numbers according to the continuum hypothesis.")
(comment outranksOnScale "(#$outranksOnScale PERSON1 PERSON2 SCALE) means that the subabstraction of PERSON1 that is referenced in the context of the assertion outranks the subabstraction of PERSON2 that is referenced in the context, on same military rank scale SCALE.  This generally means that for the duration of the time interval in which the assertion is asserted to hold (via #$holdsIn, or a temporally qualified Mt) PERSON1 is authorized to issue certain sorts of orders to PERSON2, which PERSON2 is in turn required to obey.  Since an outranksOnScale assertion will almost never hold true generally of a pair of entities, it should be qualified via #$holdsIn or deliberately reified subabstractions, or else be asserted within a temporally constrained context.")
(comment infoStructureOfCWUsingCC "(#$infoStructureOfCWUsingCC CW INFO_STRUCT CC) means that INFO_STRUC is an #$AbstractInformationStructure of the #$ConceptualWork, CW, using the #$CommunicationConvention, CC.")
(comment LakeGeneva-Cruise "The events associated with taking a cruise around Lake Geneva.")
(comment hangsFrom "(#$hangsFrom OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 is suspended from OBJ2, either directly touching it (like a weight attached to a line) or through some intermediary object (like a weight suspended from the ceiling via a hook).  All of OBJ1's weight is #$supportedBy OBJ2.  Most, if not all, of OBJ1 is below OBJ2; certainly, the center of OBJ1 is below the connection point. If pushed, OBJ1 will undergo an instance of #$Swinging (q.v.).")
(comment IntendedTargetTypeFn "(#$IntendedTargetTypeFn ?WEAPONTYPE) returns the intended primary target type that instances of ?WEAPONTYPE are designed to act against, assuming this can be defined.  In cases where it cannot be defined, the function is undefined.  This is the functional counterpart of #$intendedTargetTypeOfWeaponType.")
(disjointWith OrganismClassificationType OrganismPartType)
(comment relationAllExistsSpec "(#$relationAllExistsSpec PRED COL1 COL2) means that for every instance, INS1, of COL1, there is some proper subcollection, SPECCOL2, of COL2 such that (PRED INS1 SPECCOL2).")
(comment AcademyAwardsCeremony "The collection of annual ceremonies at which awards are given to the best movies of the year.")
(disjointWith Kayak Canoe)
(comment KomodoDragon "a monitor lizard, Varanus komodoensis, of certain Indonesian islands E of Java, that grows to a length of 10 ft. (3 m): the largest lizard in the world. Now rare.")
(comment FighterPlane "The collection of aircraft whose primary mission is armed assault on airborne or surface targets.")
(comment sameYlocation "One of the primitive relative spatial location primitives.")
(comment HeavyMortarUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for handling heavy

          mortar weapons.")
(comment OrganicFn "The term `(#$OrganicFn THING-TYPE)' denotes the collection of instances of 

the type THING-TYPE which are properly called `organic'. For example, 

`(#$OrganicFn (#$FruitFn #$TomatoPlant))' denotes the collection of organic

tomatoes. Note that this function need not only take as arguments terms denoting

foodstuffs. For example, #$WoolStuff, would be an appropriate argument. Note also

that, while every product raised according to (#$OrganicMethodFn ACTIVITY), for some

ACTIVITY, will be an instance of (#$OrganicFn THING-TYPE) for some THING-TYPE, the reverse

will not be the case. Wild mushrooms, for examples, will typically be instances of

(#$OrganicFn Mushroom).")
(comment Path-Underspecified "The collection of all semantically underspecified pathways,
whether spatial (and literal) like a garden path or a footpath (e.g.,
#$Trails), or metaphoric and non-spatial, linking abstract locations
(i.e., #$Location-Underspecified) as in 'greed is the path to hell', 'money
is the path to success', etc.")
(comment RockabillyMusic "An early specialization of #$RockMusic.  Heavily influenced by both 
  #$CountryMusic and #$BluesMusic.  The main purveyor of early
  #$RockabillyMusic (during the early-to-mid 1950s) was Sun Records, based
  in Memphis, Tennessee.  Influential practitioners of this style include Elvis 
  Presley, Carl Perkins, Wanda Jackson, and Johnny Cash.")
(comment TieGame "The collection of competitions which end as a tie or draw. This means that two or more participants (could be individuals or teams) performed equally well. Examples would be a stalemate in chess; a dead heat in a track race; a tie in a basketball game. This would not include competitions where, for example, two competitors tied for the top score, but a winner was decided based on some other metric. ")
(comment exportsThrough "(#$exportsThrough REGION PRODUCT-TYPE PT) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION exports significant amounts of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT on their way to their destination.  PT might, in the case of oil exports, for example, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.")
(disjointWith FirstMortgage ReverseMortgage)
(comment Horse-Stallion "The collection of male #$Horses that have not been castrated, and so are generally capable of siring foals.")
(comment GramPositiveBacterium "The collection of all instances of #$Bacterium that are not decolorized after the process known as 'Gram Staining'. In this process the bacterial cells are rinsed with ethyl alcohol after being stained with a crystal violet dye. That the #$GramPositiveBacterium retain the stain indicates that the cells lack an outer membrane. Another feature that distinguishes them from the #$GramNegativeBacterium is that their cell walls have molecules on them known as teichoic acids which regulate the growth of the cell wall. Antibiotics to work against the #$GramPositiveBacterium are engineered to interfere with these molecules.")
(comment agentViolatesAgreement "(#$agentViolatesAgreement AGENT AGREEMENT) means that AGENT has acted so as to violate some obligation imposed on her by AGREEMENT.  More precisely, whenever (#$agentViolatesAgreement AGREEMENT AGENT) holds, there is an instance of #$Obligation which is a part of AGREEMENT such that (#$agentViolatesObligation AGENT OBLIGATION).")
(comment DestroyerTender "A collection. Military destroyer tender ships.")
(disjointWith GeographicalThing-Intangible-MovableLocation GeographicalThing-Intangible-FixedLocation)
(comment typeForString "This predicate relates a type of character-string

  token to the abstract character-string that all instances 

  of the type represent.  (#$typeForString TYPE STRING) 

  means that TYPE is the collection of all character-string

  tokens that #$tokensString STRING.  For example, the 

  #$CharacterStringType consisting of all tokens of the string 

  'hello' is the #$typeForString for (you guessed it) 'hello'.

  See also #$typeForCharacter.")
(comment M4T6Raft "A raft composed of M4T6 bays whose purpose is ferry military vehicles and equipment across water obstacles.")
(comment LearnedActivityType "This is the collection of activities which must first be learned before they can be performed--i.e., before any role which is a specPred of #$doneBy can be played.")
(comment (MediumAmountFn Elasticity) "will eventually re-expand after compression")
(comment ViralInfection "An instance of #$InfectionTypeByPathogenType, and a specialization of #$Infection.  Each instance of #$ViralInfection is an infectious disease caused by a virus (see the collection #$Virus). Some specializations of #$ViralInfection are #$Measles, #$Mumps, and #$EbolaHemorrhagicFeverInfection.")
(comment DutchWord "The collection of all lexical words in Dutch; a subset of #$LexicalWord.            Different inflectional forms of a word do not count as different words.")
(comment standardVehicleOfUnitType "(#$standardVehicleOfUnitType ?UNITTYPE ?VEHICLETYPE) means that under 'ordinary' or 'normal' conditions, we should expect to find any instances of ?UNITTYPE equipped with one or more instances of ?VEHICLETYPE.")
(comment WebPageCopy "#$WebPageCopy is the collection of all copies of instances of #$WebPage-AIS.")
(disjointWith PopularMusicBand MarchingBand)
(disjointWith PortalCovering TransportationDevice)
(comment bodilyActedOn "The predicate #$bodilyActedOn is used to describe an event in which a living organism is acted on by some external agency.  (#$bodilyActedOn EVENT ORG) means that ORG is a living organism (i.e., an #$Organism-Whole) that is being affected in EVENT.  ORG itself may be intentionally participating in EVENT (e.g., a person voluntarily getting a haircut) or not (e.g., an animal hit by a car).  Either way, the organism ORG is not an active primary `doer' of EVENT.  This predicate is appropriately used to identify actors who undergo (instances of) #$DrugTherapy or #$IncurringAnInjury.
Note an important contrast with #$bodilyDoer (q.v.):  #$bodilyActedOn is for events that merely happen to the body, as opposed to actions the body does.  Because the body of an organism is an active `doer' in its instances of #$PhysiologicalCondition, including any #$InjuryCondition (which is the physical process of a body sustaining an injury and responding by healing or deteriorating), an organism is related to events of those kinds with #$bodilyDoer rather than #$bodilyActedOn.  By contrast, organisms involved in instances of #$DrugTherapy (which refers to the effect of a drug on the patient) or #$IncurringAnInjury (which refers to the event in which an organism gets injured, rather than the process of its being in an injured and hopefully healing state) should be related to events of those types with #$bodilyActedOn.")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething RemovingSomething)
(comment FrameForVerbs "The class of #$SubcategorizationFrames which make sense for #$Verbs.")
(comment commandRankOfEchelon "(#$commandRankOfEchelon ECHELON RANK) means that units with the military echelon-attribute ECHELON are typically commanded by officers of the rank RANK.")
(comment SignatureDynamicsMonitor "#$SignatureDynamicsMonitor is a subset of #$BiometricAuthenticationDevice.  Individuals in the collection           #$SignatureDynamicsMonitor measure the pattern of movements a person makes when writing a signature or a pass            phrase, and attempt to match the pattern with a stored representation of it.")
(comment cityGridSectionBoundedBy "(#$cityGridSectionBoundedBy SECTION ST1 ST2 ST3 ST4) means that SECTION is a roughly rectangular urban region that is completely bounded by segments of each of the streets ST1 - ST4.  The relative order (but not the absolute positions) of the 2nd - 5th arguments here is  important: it should be physically possible to circle completely  SECTION once by starting along ST1 and making successive right-hand turns on ST2, ST3, ST4, and back onto ST1.  SECTION must be part of a region that has a #$GridStreetSystem running through it.  To have this predicate correctly relate a given street-bounded rectangular city section SECTION to the four streets that border it, one can fill its arg2 position with  any of the four streets, and then continue to fill in the remaining argument-places according to the order in which one would travel along the other three streets if one were circling SECTION in a clockwise fashion (i.e. by making only right-hand turns). See also #$CityGridSectionFn, #$citySectionBoundedBy, and #$cityBlockBoundedBy.")
(comment CollectionType "A collection of collections of collections.  #$CollectionType is the collection of all (and only) types of #$Collections.

More precisely, a thing COLLTYPE is an instance of #$CollectionType if and 

only if COLLTYPE is a non-empty collection all of whose instances are collections.  Example: #$PersonTypeByCulture, each of whose instances is the collection of all persons who participate in some particular human culture, is an instance of #$CollectionType.  Important specializations of #$CollectionType include #$DisjointCollectionType, #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType, and #$CollectionTypeType.")
(comment NuclearFalloutParticle "Dust particles that have been coated with radioactive by-products from atomic explosions.")
(comment Aurora-Ionospheric "The collection of all ionospheric auroras.  Instances are displays of light in the night sky within a few thousand miles of one of the magnetic poles.  These, often moving, regions of light are caused by charged solar wind particles following the #$PlanetEarth's magnetic lines of force.")
(comment TruthPreservingReformulation "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
truth is preserved.  More specifically, if logical formulas are being
reformulated, the two would be #$equiv, and if denotational terms
are being reformulated, the two would be #$equals.")
(comment postalCodeExtension "(#$postalCodeExtension LOCATION STRING) means that STRING is the extension (extra or completing bits) of the postal code for LOCATION.  For addresses in the United States, STRING would correspond to the 4-digit extension part of a complete ZIP code, represented as a character string.  Note that in other parts of the world, the extension part of the postal code (if it exists) may consist of letters, numbers, or other symbols as well (e.g., dashes, colons).  See also #$postalCodeOfAddress and #$extraFourDigitsOfZip. The latter assumes that in the context of use (the #$Microtheory in which  relevant assertions are entered), the extension part of ZIP  codes will be represented as numbers rather than as character strings.")
(comment DownloadOfFileTypeFn "A function that takes a spec of #$ComputerFile-AIS and returns the collection of all #$DownloadingAFile events in which that type of file is downloaded.")
(comment Pope "The collection of all #$Popes; each is the spiritual and temporal head of the #$RomanCatholicChurch and of the #$HolySee, political ruler of the #$VaticanCity, bishop [#$Bishop-Clerical] of Rome, Italy, Prince over all christian Princes, and vice-regent of #$JesusChrist on earth.  Each #$Pope, in modern times, is elected by the College of Cardinals in the #$SistineChapel, and rules until death.  (There are other popes, such as the #$CopticPopes, that are not included in this collection.)  Certain historical popes are now held to have been antipopes.")
(comment riskOfInfectionFromTypeToType "This predicate relates infection types, organism types and levels of risk.  (#$riskOfInfectionFromTypeToType INFTYPE INFECTEDORGTYPE ENDANGEREDORGTYPE RISKLEVEL) means that if an organism of type INFECTEDORGTYPE carries the infection, INFTYPE, the likelihood that it will infect organisms of type ENDANGEREDORGTYPE if it comes into contact with such organisms is RISKLEVEL.")
(comment CircularTrajectory "A circular trajectory")
(disjointWith BookGeneric-CW Advertisement-PCW)
(comment searchCriterion-Definite "The expression `(#$searchCriterion-Definite SEARCH CRITERION)'
means that CRITERION is the #$PossibleIdentificationCondition which
expresses the criterion of success as conceived by the seeker who is the
#$performedBy in the SEARCH. Note that different searchs might employ
exactly the same CRITERION, but each search employs exactly one. For
an explanation of why, see the comment on #$LookingForSomething-Definite.")
(comment findAnalogs "(#$findAnalogs ?Num ?Src-Mt ?Src ?Tgt-Mt ?Tgt) causes ?Tgt to become successively bound to the ?Num best analogs (according to structure-mapping metrics) for the source concept ?Src as defined source domain microtheory ?Src-Mt in the target domain ?Tgt-Mt.  That is, find the ?Tgt-Mt equivalent of ?Src as it is defined in ?Src-Mt. Example: (#$findAnalogs 4 #$DesertShieldMt  #$Iraq #$Y1Phase2-AllStagesMt ?What) should cause ?What to be bound to Iran and 3 other values. See also #$findAnalog, #$structureMaps and #$structureDiffs.")
(comment Zetta "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^21")
(comment westernRegion "(#$westernRegion SUPER SUB) means that SUB is the `western region' of SUPER.  What counts as the `western region' is contextually determined. Some of the factors  influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political  considerations.")
(comment SymptomOfAilmentFn "(#$SymptomOfAilmentFn AILMENT) is the

 collection of all symptoms of AILMENT.  Note that individual symptoms and individual ailments are collections.")
(comment TabletEffervescent "The collection of all effervescent tablets.  Effervescent tablets release gas when dissolved in a liquid.")
(comment saleToFractionDuring "(#$saleToFractionDuring PT1 PRODUCT-TYPE PT2 THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the monetary value of sales of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 to the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the monetary value of all sales of PRODUCT-TYPE by PT1 during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  PT1 might, for example, be a #$Country or a #$Business; and likewise for PT2.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that in January of 1997 Japan accounted for 35 percent of Iran's sales of crude oil, we can say (#$saleToFractionDuring #$Iran #$Petroleum-CrudeOil #$Japan (#$MonthFn January (#$YearFn 1997)) (#$Percent 35)).")
(comment SexualOrgy "A collection of parties in which a primary, intended activity is many people having sex, often with people they don't know very well.")
(comment InsertingAGunClip "The collection of instances of #$LoadingAProjectileWeapon in which the   weapon in question is a #$Gun, and    the ammunition is stored in a  #$MagazineForBullets.")
(comment CarbonDioxide-Solid "The collection of instances of #$CarbonDioxide which are in a solid state. Members of this collection are also known as 'dry ice'.--Causley, Jan. 18, 1999")
(comment AnimalCell "The collection of #$Cells that #$Animals and parts of #$Animals are made of.")
(comment MartialArtsActivity-Asian "The collection of all activities that consist of a #$Person practicing, performing, or using an Asian martial art like karate, kung fu, or taekwondo.")
(comment AB-205-Helicopter "License-built version of the U.S. Bell 205 helicopter.")
(comment SerialKilling "The collection of events, often protracted over several
years, in which a single individual murders several people
individually and in separate occasions.")
(comment EconomicSector-Localized "Each instance of the collection #$EconomicSector-Localized is a particular major economic sector of some place: a large #$Group of producers or service providers in a defined geographic area.  For instance, the United States' manufacturing sector would be an element of #$EconomicSector-Localized, and would have particular U.S. manufacturers as #$groupMembers.   The 'world agriculture sector' and 'the technology sector in the United States' refer to instances of #$EconomicSector-Localized.  'The U.S. Automobile Industry' is too specific and is an instance of a particular #$Industry-Localized.   (Similarly, the collection #$AutomobileIndustry is an instance of #$IndustryType.)   Note that the main kinds of economic sector (#$EconomicSectorTypes like #$AgriculturalEconomicSector) are #$Collections (of particular geographically defined instances of #$EconomicSector-Localized); they are not themselves individual economic sectors in this scheme.  That is, there are several instances of the collection #$ManufacturingEconomicSector, such as the German manufacturing sector, the Mexican manufacturing sector, etc.  There is also the worldwide manufacturing sector.  Thus #$ManufacturingEconomicSector is a specialization, not an instance, of #$EconomicSector-Localized.  Note that this is for major sectors of an economy, not for specific industries; see #$Industry-Localized and #$IndustryType.  See also #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn and #$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn.")
(comment hasAsHeadOfGovernment "(#$hasAsHeadOfGovernment REGION HEAD) says that HEAD is the #$HeadOfGovernment REGION.")
(comment slotOfType "binary predicate arg1 denotes a slot excplicitly associated with instances of collection arg2.")
(comment KnockKnockJoke "A subset of #$Joke-CW, #$KnockKnockJoke is the collection           of jokes of the form: A: 'Knock-knock.' B: 'Who's there?' A: 'So-and-so.'          B: 'So-and-so who?' A: 'So-and-so such-and-such'.  A's last remark is           the punchline.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat GeopoliticalEntityTypeByBasicCategory)
(comment Diphtheria "An infection where the infecting bacteria secrete a toxin in the upper respiratory tract which destroys tissue and causes a membrane to form which may collapse and cause asphyxiation.")
(comment Torpedo-MK-44 "A type of #$Torpedo with #$ActiveSonar-Device.")
(comment MotionSickness "Nausea that may occur as a result of the motion caused by riding in cars, in planes, on boats, etc.")
(comment GameOfChance "The collection of all instances of #$Game whose performance involve bets of money [#$TenderObject] or property that are based on the outcome of the game [see #$GameOfChance-Event].")
(comment spikeWidth "(#$spikeWidth SPIKE INTERVAL) means that the spike-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution SPIKE has an effective (maximum or base) width of INTERVAL units.  For example, the effective width of a spike used to specify a temporal persistence distribution might be (#$YearsDuration 20), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the spike pertains, the likelihood of being true would vary in a spike-like pattern within a 20-year temporal range.")
(comment ToLabel "The collection of #$AddressLabels attached to packages that indicate the recipient of the package.")
(comment Diphosgene "The chemical ClCO2CCl3, a #$ChokingAgentType.")
(comment M60AVLB "The collection of AVLB's that are mounted on an M60 chassis.")
(comment MagazineIssue "The collection of all #$PeriodicalIssues for periodicals which are magazines.  Copies of an instance of #$MagazineIssue are all instances #$MagazineCopy for the same #$Date.")
(comment Growing "A generic attribute that applies to an entity which is increasing
in size along some underspecified dimension (e.g. volume, length, etc.).")
(comment Zinc "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of #$Zinc.")
(comment AdventureMovie "#$AdventureMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which tells the tale of an adventure.")
(comment entailsRoleInPlanOfType "(#$entailsRoleInPlanOfType SYS-SLOT PLAN-TYPE SYS-ROLE
AGENT-ROLE) means that if an agent plays the role SYS-SLOT in a
functional system which in turn plays the role SYS-ROLE in a plan of
type PLAN-TYPE, then said agent plays the role AGENT-ROLE in said
plan.")
(comment spatialIntersectionOf "(#$spatialIntersectionOf INTER SET) means that the spatial extent of INTER, an instance of #$SpatialThing, is the intersection of the spatial extents of the elements of SET, a set of #$SpatialThings.")
(comment Motion-SolidAgainstSolid "In instances of #$Motion-SolidAgainstSolid the #$motionPathway-Complete is in contact with (#$touches) every #$objectMoving.  This collection is a #$TemporalStuffType so contact between #$objectMoving and #$motionPathway-Complete occurs throughout all #$timeSlices.  The #$objectMoving and the #$motionPathway-Complete are solid objects.  Hockey pucks sliding, rolling, and spinning on ice exemplars.  Car transportation and #$SnowSkiing are a negative examples because many of the #$objectMovings in these events do not touch the pathway e.g. the car passengers, the skiers hat etc..  Instances of #$Motion-SolidAgainstSolid are involved as #$subEvents however.  The car's wheels, and the skier's skis are the respective #$objectMovings.")
(comment surfaceAreaOfWholeObject "This predicates relates an object to the area that is its surface area; see #$SurfaceArea-WholeSurfaceFn. (It does not refer just to the top surface; see #$surfaceAreaOfTopOfObject and #$SurfaceArea-TopSurfaceFn for surface of lakes, tabletops, etc..)")
(comment economyOf "(#$economyOf A B) means that B's #$EconomicSystem is A.")
(comment USBusiness "The collection of all businesses having their official residence in the                 #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment TemporalLobe "The collection of all occipital lobes of #$Brains.  Each individual #$TemporalLobe is in the mid-inferior region of a #$CerebralHemisphere and processes auditory input (among other functions).")
(comment DemandingApology "The collection of events where one state formally demands an apology to another state for some conflict involving both parties.")
(comment Bacterium-Monotrichous "The collection of #$Bacterium whose instances have one #$Flagellum-Prokaryotic. #$Bacterium-Monotrichous are faster than #$Bacterium-Peritrichous or

#$Bacterium-Amphitrichous. #$Bacterium-Lophotrichous are of an intermediate speed.")
(comment computationalSystemAttacked "(#$computationalSystemAttacked ATTACK SYSTEM) means that in the instance of #$AttackByComputerOperation, ATTACK, the primary instance of #$ComputationalSystem attacked is SYSTEM.")
(disjointWith Wheelchair ArmoredVehicle)
(disjointWith Cell (GroupFn Tooth))
(comment ConstructionProject "The group of projects with the goal of constructing a building, road, etc.")
(comment TCWATMRVignetteMicrotheory "Each element of #$TCWATMRVignetteMicrotheory represents at

most one of the vignettes contained in

#$TeachingChildrenWithAutismToMindRead-TheBook.  Each one of the

approximately 100 vignettes in the book corresponds to a simple

scenario described with one or two english sentences as well as a hand

drawn cartoon-like picture.  Exercises about feelings or thoughts of

the characters in the scenario follow each vignette.  The vignettes

plus the exercises are intended to teach children with autism about

other people's desire, emotions, beliefs, etc.  The hope is that these

scenarios will serve as a developmentally appropriate test bed from

which to construct and validate a theory of goals and emotion which is

tractable for #$Cyc.")
(disjointWith OutdoorActivity IndoorActivity)
(comment SmokingFood "A specialization of #$PreparingFoodItem.  In each instance of #$SmokingFood, an instance of #$Food is cured by being exposed to smoke, thereby allowing the food to remain usable for a much longer period of time.")
(comment EquivalencePartitionFn "This function maps collections to the partitioning of the collection that is defined by the equivalence relation in the arg2 position.  (#$EquivalencePartitionFn COLLECTION EQUIVREL) denotes

the instance of #$DisjointSetOrCollectionType that results from partitioning COLLECTION according to the equivalence relation, EQUIVREL.  For instance, equality in modulo 6 arithmetic divides the natural numbers into six collections which are pairwise disjoint.  See #$EquivalenceClassFn for a function that returns specific elements of the #$EquivalencePartitionFn.")
(comment Whittling "This collection includes instances of material shaping by the removal of small pieces with a sharp instrument. Whittling is done by hand, rather than by a machine.")
(comment ParodyMovie "A collection of #$ComedyMovies which spoofs traditional genres or a specific film, poking fun at its conventions or plotlines. The makers of these film types expect audiences to understand the well-established cliches and archetypes that are therein ridiculed with inside jokes and broad strokes. Often using slapstick techniques, parodies offer a lowbrow, tongue-in-cheek counterpoint to the more serious revisionist approach used by movements like the French New Wave and genres like Spaghetti westerns which favor subversive tactics.")
(comment ScheduleFn-SportsAgentType "(#$ScheduleFn-SportsAgentType STYPE) returns the collection of all instances of #$Schedule that include schedule information for #$SportsCompetitions performed or organized by instances of type STYPE.  For example (#$ScheduleFn-SportsAgentType #$SoccerTeam) returns the collection of all soccer team schedules.")
(comment hasStoredInside "The objects kept in this place when they are not in use.  A few comments: This slot is meant for objects which are stored in a place different from the place they are used.  If an object is always in the same place, use #$physicallyContains (in #$ContainerGMt).  Also, this slot really applies just to the object in the hands of the end-user, not so much to the object at a store, even though stores  keep things in some place while they are waiting to sell them.")
(comment MedicalCareFn "#$MedicalCareFn takes as argument any instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType and returns the collection of all instances of #$MedicalCareEvent which may be appropriately offered in response to #$PhysiologicalConditions of that type.  For example, (#$MedicalCareFn #$Cancer) includes the collection of all instances of #$MedicalCareEvent appropriate to Cancer, including many instances of #$RadiationTherapy and #$DrugTherapy.")
(comment City "#$City is a specialization of #$GeopoliticalEntity whose territory is an instance of #$UrbanArea.  Each instance of #$City is a local organization of a human settlement which has its own government.  This includes cities, towns, suburbs, villages, hamlets, and townships, as long as they have their own governments.  A city government is usually mostly autonomous from the governments of its surrounding regions, rather than being a sub-organization of them.")
(disjointWith Event (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet Agent-Generic (GroupFn Agent-Generic))))
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-TimeBomb "#$AttackByComputerOperation-TimeBomb is the collection of all attacks in which elements of #$TimeBomb-Computer are used.")
(disjointWith Automobile Motorcycle)
(comment Salt-NaCl "Pieces of sodium chloride compound -- plain table salt.  Could be in large chunks, or dissolved, or molten...  See #$TableSalt for the granular solid used as a #$Condiment.")
(comment PickingASeed "The collection of events in which a single seed is picked")
(comment InterArgGenlPredicate "Those instances of both #$TernaryPredicate and #$ArgGenlPredicate used to specify the conditional #$genls requirement of one argument (the dependent argument) of a #$Relation given the #$genls of another argument (the independent argument).  The arg1 is the #$Relation.  The arg2 is the #$genls #$Collection of the independent argument; this defines the antecedent of the conditional constraint.  The arg3 is the #$genls #$Collection required of the dependent argument when the antecedent is satsifed (that is, when the independent argument has the arg2 #$Collection as a #$genls).")
(comment SniperRifle "The collection of highly-accurate #$Rifles that are used as anti- personnel weapons.  They usually come with a telescopic scope and should hit  a #$PointTarget at 700m.")
(disjointWith Pressure ElectricalCharge)
(comment conceptuallyCoRelated "#$conceptuallyCoRelated is a symmetric version of #$conceptuallyRelated.")
(comment istIncreasesSlotValue "(#$istIncreasesSlotValue INDPROP DEPPROP SLOT) means that the value that SLOT takes in the arg2 position for DEPPROP will be greater if INDPROP is provable than it will be if INDPROP is not provable.")
(comment complianceStatus "This predicate relates situation to their degree of compliance with respect to the rules set out in some microtheory, most likely an instance of #$SupposedToBeMicrotheory or #$Specification. (#$complianceStatus Object001 SupposedToBeMicrotheory001 #$Compliant) means that Object001 fully complies with the standards set out in Microtheory001.  This predicate can also be used to clarify the nature of flaws (see #$hasFlawAttributes et al) by specifying the specification in virtue of which a flawed things (#$NonCompliant, #$PartiallyNonCompliant) is deemed flawed.")
(comment ReferenceWork "A specialization of #$TextualPCW.  Each instance of #$ReferenceWork is a conceptual work providing a more or less non-speculative, \"fact-oriented\", comprehensive description of some knowledge domain.")
(comment Cellulose "a polysaccharide that is the main constituent of the cell walls of plants.")
(comment regionControlled "(#$regionControlled GEO REGION) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION is physically controlled by the #$GeopoliticalEntity GEO. This refers to actual practical control, not mere legal or unenforced territorial claims. For one #$GeopoliticalEntity or #$GeographicalAgent being controlled by another, use the predicate #$territoriesControlled instead.")
(comment EnergyConversionProcess "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$EnergyConversionProcess, energy is converted from one form to another.")
(comment relevantInPlace-Somewhere "(#$relevantInPlace-Somewhere MT PLACE) means that the assertions in MT are relevant at least somewhere in the spatial extent of PLACE.  See also #$relevantInPlace-Everywhere.")
(disjointWith Conveying-Stationary TransportationEvent)
(comment AntiAircraftFire "The collection of events in which relatively large projectiles, ballistic or powered, are fired (from any location -- ground, air, or sea) at aircraft.")
(comment Nietzschean-Superman "#$FriedrichNietzsche's UberMensch (literally, superman or overman),         the morally supreme being whose will to power and moral efficacy         represent what Nietzsche took to be the essential spirit of the true         'noble' man. In Nietzsche's view, an ubermench did not seek moral         approval from the masses, or from a defunct religious view such as         #$Christianity, but set his own moral agenda.")
(comment AntiFlatulent "Drugs which reduce flatulence.")
(comment languageOfLexicon "This predicate relates an instance of #$LexicalMicrotheory to the #$Language whose words it describes. For instance, (#$languageOfLexicon #$EnglishMt #$EnglishLanguage) means that #$EnglishMt describes how words are used in the #$EnglishLanguage.")
(comment IllocutionaryForce "The collection of illocutionary force attributes held by illocutionary acts.  Each instance of #$IllocutionaryForce is a specialized component of a communication; its function is to indicate how the speaker in a communication wants the agent(s) whom s/he is addressing to understand, and respond to, the situation--i.e., the state of affairs--described in that communication.  Isolating the `illocutionary force' of a communication allows us to characterize the intention of a speaker; e.g., whether s/he means to assert that the described state of affairs in fact holds; or to express a desire that such a state of affairs hold; or to command someone to make that state of affairs hold; or to offer to make the state of affairs hold.  S/he may even intend to make something true by stating it (e.g., ``I name this ship `The Intrepid'.''). 

Usually, apprehending a speaker's intention is important for understanding what s/he means and what s/he intends the hearer to do.  Although the content of an illocutionary act can be represented propositionally, they are not generally communicated so explicitly.  For example, questions in English are typically communicated by inverting subject-object word order and raising one's intonation at the end of the utterance.  (The intonation marker so strongly indicates a question that it may suffice without the inverted word order, as in `You are going tonight' uttered with a rising intonation.)  Commands in English typically have an (unexpressed) understood subject and perhaps a forceful tone.  In every culture and language there are conventional sets of commonly used illocutionary forces which would be instances of #$IllocutionaryForce for that culture; e.g., in English, they include #$Inform, #$Request, #$Offer, #$Promise, and #$Query.

Note: although in this comment #$IllocutionaryForce is explained in terms of utterances, it applies to communication generally; so `speaker' and `listener' should be broadly interpreted to mean, respectively, any #$senderOfInfo and #$recipientOfInfo.  See also #$Communicating, #$CommunicationAct-Single.  In #$CycL, illocutionary forces can be related to communication acts having some propositional content, via #$iteIllocutionaryForce, or to the microtheory containing formulas expressing the information transferred in an illocutionary act with #$componentIF.")
(comment realGDPGrowthRateDuring "(#$realGDPGrowthRateDuring GE THING NR) means that NR is the growth rate of the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE's real (adjusted for inflation) gross domestic product during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  That is, NR is the quotient of the difference between GE's gross domestic product for the temporal extent of THING and GE's gross domestic product for the time interval immediately preceding, and of the same duration as, THING (as dividend) and GE's gross domestic product for the time interval immediately preceding, and of the same duration as, THING (as divisor).  For example, to express the fact that Oman's real gross domestic product growth rate for 1997 was 5.9%, we can say (#$realGDPGrowthRateDuring #$Oman (#$YearFn 1997) .059).  See also #$grossDomesticProduct.")
(disjointWith HairShirt OverGarment)
(comment BambooPlant "Individual bamboo plants.")
(disjointWith HumanScaleObject GeoculturalRegion)
(comment Separation-Incomplete "This is the collection of events in which an object undergoes some sort of separation from itself, such as ripping or cutting, but the separation is not complete.  In the end, there is still only one object.")
(comment NCAAMensDivision1BasketballChampionshipTournament "The #$NationalCollegiateAthleticAssociation Men's tournament, held annually.")
(comment timeIntervalBetween "This predicate relates two temporally disjoint things (two instances of #$TemporalThing) to the (longest) instance of #$TimeInterval between them.  (#$timeIntervalBetween BETWEEN EARLIER LATER) means that BETWEEN is the time interval that starts immediately after EARLIER ends and ends immediately before LATER begins.  LATER, of course, must begin after EARLIER ends.")
(comment InfantryLandingShip "A collection. Ships used in a military context to bring personnel onto land.")
(comment PeptideMolecule "A collection of any group of compounds formed from two or
more #$AminoAcids by the linkage of amino groups of some of the acids
with carboxyl groups of others.")
(comment ownerAccountForFile "(#$ownerAccountForFile FILE ACCOUNT) means that the #$ComputerFileCopy FILE's owner is the person who has #$UserAccount ACCOUNT on a computational system.  By default, the owner of a file has read, write, and execute permissions (cf. #$FilePermission) on the files created using that account, and he or she can also set the permissions allowing or disallowing such permissions to the group (cf. #$UserAccountGroup) of which he or she is a member, or to non-group accounts on the system. See also #$groupAccountForFile, #$worldAccountForFile.")
(comment BlueBook-Pricing "The collection of price lists published at regular intervals for various             commodities, especially those price lists for used cars.")
(comment AirborneInfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of infantry units that are deployed by parachute drop.")
(comment levelWith "(#$levelWith OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are roughly the same vertical distance from some horizontal surface in the frame of reference.")
(disjointWith NetIncreasingFunction IrregularFunction)
(comment MusicalInstrument-AcousticElectric "Instances are instances of #$MusicalInstrument

that are acoustic -- i.e., they are designed 

to produce adequate performance sound

 without electric amplification -- yet 

are have been built with internal 

electronics, enabling them to be 'plugged in'

 to an amplifier in order to generate a 

  louder and more sculptable sound.")
(comment NetworkPacketTransfer "#$NetworkPacketTransfer is the collection of all #$Events in which a  piece of data is transmitted from one machine to another machine over a #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment InhalationalAnthraxDiseaseScript-Natural "The complex event-type charting the course of #$InhalationalAnthrax infections from onset to death.  #$InhalationalAnthrax is acquired by the inhalation of a substance, most commonly dust, infected with instances of #$Spore-DormantBacterium of the #$Anthrax-Bacterium.")
(comment CycApplication "The collection of Cyc-based applications.

          Excluded are programs which are internal or essential to the maintainence

          or operation of the #$CycKB, such as the #$CycInferenceEngine or the

          #$CycCanonicalizer.")
(comment ExtractingPetroleum "Extracting petroleum from the earth; one of the #$industryActivityTypes of an #$OilIndustry.")
(comment Amine "Organic #$Nitrogen compounds.")
(comment FitnessStepper "This is the collection fitness

machines which are designed to allow the user to perform

a number of different exercises on them.")
(disjointWith Garage-Household SubwayStation)
(comment DeclarativeContext "The collection of all contexts [#$Microtheory] which assert facts and rules about some world or facet of a world.  This is disjoint with #$PropositionalAttitudeContext which refers to groups of assertions which have the property of having some specific relationship with a sentient beings internal state (beliefs, hopes, goals, questions, etc.).  It is necessary, but not sufficient for a context to be a #$DeclarativeContext in order to derive new assertions in it.  A #$SourceMicrotheory or #$PropositionalInformationThing contains assertions that are expressly in some source.  Assertions that can be derived from those assertions are NOT expressly in such sources and so should not be derived within them, even though they may be instances of #$DeclarativeContext.")
(comment infectionTypeTransmittedDuring "(#$infectionTypeTransmittedDuring INFECTING TYPE) means that during
the #$InfectingEvent, INFECTING, the infection the victim will be the host
of is of the type TYPE.")
(comment TaxiCompany "Instances of #$TaxiCompany are organizations which, as their main function, transport people in taxis.")
(comment infoStructureOfCW "(#$infoStructureOfCW CONCEPTUALWORK STRUCTURE) means that INFOSTRUCTURE is an #$AbstractInformationStructure corresponding to the whole of CONCEPTUALWORK. For example, #$MobyDickNovel is expressed by one #$AbstractInformationStructure which is the complete sequence of words which Melville penned as well as by another #$AbstractInformationStructure which is the #$TextString of the sequence of characters with which those words were written.  Similarly, a song [#$Song-CW] may have one structure which is its lyrics [#$Lyric-WordsToSong], another being a normal musical score including notes & text, and a third being an instance of #$GuitarTablatureText.  This predicate allows us to make assertions about information structures used in a particular work without reference to any instantiation of that work.")
(comment EntireInteriorSurface-Tangible "This is the collection of complete inside surfaces of objects'
interiors.")
(comment addictedTo "This predicate specifies the relationship between an addict and the substance to which s/he is addicted.  The first argument must be an #$Animal, the second an #$ExistingStuffType and a subset of #$AddictiveSubstance.  For instance: (#$addictedTo #$OKeefe #$Caffeine).")
(comment DarkAlbedoFeature-Topographical "The collection of all topographical features noted for an albedo (reflectivity of light) significanly darker than the surrounding regions.")
(comment MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn "The term

 (#$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn REGIONINDUSTRY) denotes the

#$Microtheory or 'context' containing the assertions pertaining primarily to the the

 specific individual regional #$Industry-Localized 

REGIONINDUSTRY.  This function can be used for any regional #$Industry-Localized; it is not

 necessary to create a new, named 

'industry Microtheory' for a regional industry when the instance of #$Industry-Localized is already in the knowledge base.  For example, (#$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn

GermanMetallurgyIndustry) would be the #$Microtheory for assertions relating

primarily to the German  metallurgy industry.  Note 

that each value of the function #$MtOfIndustryOfRegionFn

 is the Microtheory for an individual regionally defined #$Industry-Localized.  This is in contrast to the function #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn, which applies to collections of individual, regionally defined industries.  To generate the microtheory for all of the industry type, i.e. the collection of all individual regional industries of a certain kind, use #$MtOfIndustryTypeFn.")
(comment FictionalTVShowTypeByTopic "#$FictionalTVShowTypeByTopic is a collection of collections. Each element of #$FictionalTVShowTypeByTopic is a collection of instances of #$FictionalTVShow-CW that are about the same topic. For example, #$LawyerTVShow is an instance of #$FictionalTVShowTypeByTopic. Another example would be (#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn #$FictionalTVShow-CW #$Doctor-Medical). This collection was created to make use of a faceting of #$FictionalTVShow-CW to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(comment hasMonopolyInMarket "The binary predicate #$hasMonopolyInMarket relates an instance of #$CommercialOrganization with the market(s) in which it enjoys a monopoly, i.e., in which it has no significant competitors.")
(comment Infantilism-Sexual "The collection of all #$SexualBehaviors where sexual pleasure is derived from acting or being treated as an infant.  People who participate in #$Infantilism-Sexual are usually adults, and will often wear diapers, carry pacifiers, and be bottle- or spoon-fed by another adult acting as a nurse or parent.")
(comment CardiotonicAgent "Class of drugs that increase muscular tone of the heart. ")
(comment associator-FunctionalRole "(#$associator-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that it
is expected that AGENT will form enduring associations of some kind
between information items in SYSTEM, in ways that facilitate other
subsystems' fulfilling their assigned roles.")
(comment GroupSex "The collection of all instances of #$SexualBehavior with three or more participants whom the behavior is #$performedBy.")
(comment BlockOfStreet "A collection of artificial paths.  An instance of
#$BlockOfStreet is a segment of an instance of #$Street-Generic
that extends from one intersection (of that street with another)
to the next (i.e. the nearest intersection -- going in either 
direction -- of that street with yet another street).  Normally,
only streets in #$UrbanAreas are divided into street blocks.")
(comment termCreationTime "(#$termCreationTime TERM TIME) means that TERM was ``first used'' at TIME (TIME specifies a particular day in YYYYMMDD syntax.). For example, if TERM is an #$CycLAssertion which first appeared  in the KB due to a #$HumanCyclist directly (aka ``locally'') asserting it, then the #$termCreationTime is the same as the #$assertionAssertTime for that assertion.  However, if TERM is an #$CycLAssertion which was only deduced and not directly asserted, then #$termCreationTime is when the assertion was deduced.  If TERM were *both* directly asserted and deduced, then #$termCreationTime is the time of earliest assertion or deduction.  The analogous is true for NATs (see #$CycLNonAtomicTerm); the #$termCreationTime of a NAT is the earliest date on which it was referenced in a local or deduced #$CycLAssertion.")
(comment enablesAgentTo-Generic "#$enablesAgentTo-Generic is a generalization of all enables-* predicates, with the exception of #$enables-ImpartsSkills. Motivation: occasionally one needs to label a broad class of events as generically `enabling', i.e., as events that enable an agent to do something in one or the other sense of enabling. This predicate should be used sparingly: When describing the enabling relation between a specific event or type of event, an agent and a specific action or type of action, one should use the specific enables-* predicate appropriate to that circumstance.")
(comment BirdsOvum "The ovum of a bird's egg, which is vary large compared to other ova due to its food content (it's swollen with food reserves.)")
(comment endToEndConnected "A #$ConnectionPredicate and specialization of #$connectedAtEnd (q.v.) that 
relates tangible paths (see #$Path-Simple) that are connected end-to-end.
(#$endToEndConnected PATH1 PATH2) means that one end of PATH1 is connected 
to one end of another PATH2, in such a way that they share no subpaths and 
that flow or transport is allowed between them.  This kind of connection is 
not a #$JunctionOfPaths since there is no third distinct path joined there.  
In pipe welding, these end-to-end connections are called butt welds or 
circumferential pipe welds.")
(comment infantMortalityRate "(#$infantMortalityRate AREA RATE) means that the infant mortality rate in the #$GeographicalRegion AREA is RATE. It is most common to express ?RATE in nr. of deaths per 1000 live births per year.")
(comment sourceOfTerm-Person "This predicate is used when we wish to indicate that a particular individual figures as a 'source' for a particular Cyc term.  Figuring as a source means that the person indicated played a nontrivial and active role in the process that brought the term into existence.  It does not entail, nor is it entailed by, being the #$myCreator of a term, and it should not be interpreted as assigning sole or primary credit for the idea to the person cited.  A term can have multiple 'sources'.")
(comment AntiAircraftGun "A collection of weapons,

a subset of #$AntiAircraftArtillery. Each instance is an

artillery piece intended to bring down enemy aircraft.")
(comment sequenceCodesForType "(#$sequenceCodesForType LIST PROTEINTYPE) means that the
nucleotide sequence LIST codes for proteins of the type PROTEINTYPE
when interpreted by ribsomal bodies in the process of DNA-to-protein
translation.")
(comment outranks-Absolute "(#$outranks-Absolute PERSON1 PERSON2) means that PERSON1 outranks PERSON2 according to some internationally accepted conception of military rankings.  Note that while (#$outranksOnScale PERSON1 PERSON2 SCALE) entails (#$outranks-Absolute PERSON1 PERSON2), the reverse isn't true: eg, a Russian colonel outranks-Absolute an American private, but does not outrank the private on a rank scale shared by both countries.  Also, note that the Russian colonel is not authorized to give orders to the American private save in very special circumstances.  Since an outranks-Absolute assertion will almost never hold true generally of a pair of entities, it should be qualified via holdsIn or deliberately reified subabstractions, or else be asserted within a temporally constrained context.")
(comment NovelByAuthorFn " (#$NovelByAuthorFn WRTR) denotes the collection of novels (#$Novel-CW) that were written by WRTR.")
(comment pathUsedExclusivelyByTransporter "(#$pathUsedExclusivelyByTransporter TRANSPORTER PATH) means that there is an expectation that any motion event in which TRANSPORTER is the #$primaryObjectMoving will occur on PATH.")
(comment covers-Baglike "(#$covers-Baglike WRAP OBJECT) means that the #$SheetOfSomeStuff WRAP covers OBJECT as a continuous sheet (so that WRAP also touches OBJECT), and is wrapped wholly around OBJECT (so that OBJECT is totally enclosed in WRAP).")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat OrganismPartType)
(comment CollegeEntranceTest "The collection of #$UniversityEntryTest events that are used to help undergraduate admissions officers decide whether to admit a student.  Such tests are designed to test a student's aptitude for college-level studies.")
(comment keGeneralizationSuggestion "(#$keGeneralizationSuggestion FORMULA GENERAL) states that GENERAL is a formula which is a plausible suggestion for a more general version of FORMULA.  If GENERAL were true, it should imply FORMULA.  See also #$kePrecisionSuggestion.")
(comment mtAgentType "(#$mtAgentType MT TYPE) means that the assertions in MT are relevant for, or pertain to, members of TYPE.  The precise type of relevance or pertinence will depend on other dimension attributes for MT, including modality.")
(comment RadioPersonality "The collection of #$Persons whose job it is to broadcast over the radio.  An individual who is an instance of #$RadioPersonality may or may not have his own #$SpecifiedRadioSeriesType.")
(disjointWith Canoe Lifeboat)
(comment ParasiticOrganism "The collection of plants and animals which are considered parasites.  Parasites gain benefit from their host organisms usually at the expense of the host.  Certain vines may be parasitic to trees. Fleas, ticks, and lice are common animal parasites.")
(comment BomberPlane "The collection of military #$Airplanes which are designed to be used in #$Bombing target sites.")
(comment SharesInFundFn "#$SharesInFundFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to represent a collection of shares in a particular mutual Fund. (#$SharesInFundFn FUND) applied to a #$MutualFund FUND returns the collection of all shares of that mutual fund. See also #$StockInFn, #$MutualFund.")
(comment xyCrossSectionShapeType "The cross section shape type in the xy plane.")
(comment EngineeringUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units specialized to provide engineering support to other military units.")
(comment Permaculture "#$Permaculture is an approach to land management that creates high-yielding, low-energy, self-perpetuating systems whereby the functions of animals,

plants, humans and the Earth are integrated to maximize their value and create sustainable human habitats. 

#$Permaculture brings together disciplines relating to food, shelter, energy, water, waste management, economics, and social sciences. It aims to

maximize a site's productivity, while maintaining ecosystems and restoring damaged land to a healthy, life-promoting state.

The term was first coined by Bill Mollison of Tasmania, Australia in 1972, by merging the terms, `permanent' and `agriculture.' Although originally

developed for small subsistence farms, the practice has expanded to apply to gardens and urban settings.")
(comment RockAndRollMusic "An early specialization of #$RockMusic.  Heavily influenced by 
  #$BluesMusic and, to a lesser extent, #$CountryMusic.
  Influential practitioners of this style include Little Richard, Chuck Berry,
  and Buddy Holly.")
(comment PoliticalEvent "A specialization of #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$PoliticalEvent is an action that has an important political character.  Many official acts by instances of #$RegionalGovernment are included in this collection -- e.g. passing legislation, instances of #$DeclaringWar -- as are actions which affect the structure or composition of govermental bodies (e.g. resigning from office).  More broadly, many events which involve candidates for office, instances of #$PoliticalOrganization, or other actors with power to affect political institutions are included -- political fundraising events, letter-writing campaigns, and so on.  Events which have only unintended political ramifications, such as a polluting event which prompts a movement for stricter environmental regulations, are not included in this collection.  An individual voting (see the collection #$Voting) in an election for public office is an instance of #$PoliticalEvent, but in other cases, it seems necessary to have participants who individually or as a group have some level of political influence. So, most instances of #$PublicProtesting are instances of #$PoliticalEvent, but perhaps a single individual holding a placard is not.  A well-known politician switching parties is a #$PoliticalEvent (even if she is in private life), but perhaps JohnDoe switching parties is not. Another borderline case: the influencing of a government official by a private lobbyist.")
(comment GramNegativeBacterium "The collection of all instances of #$Bacterium that do not retain the stain in the 'Gram Staining' process. The cell walls of the #$GramNegativeBacterium are more complex and do not contain as many peptoglycans as the #$GramPositiveBacterium. Among the #$Bacterium which are pathogens, the #$GramNegativeBacterium are much more plentiful than the #$GramPositiveBacterium.")
(comment EconomicAgreement "The broad collection of agreements which constrain one or more of the agreeing parties to perform one or more instances of #$EconomicAction.")
(comment textOfTerminalSyntaxSymbol "The predicate (#$textOfTerminalSyntaxSymbol STRING SYMBOL SYSTEM) relates a terminal #$SyntaxSpecificationSymbol SYMBOL in a #$StringGrammar SYSTEM to the specific surface string STRING associated with it.   For example, in a phrase structure grammar PSG1,  DEF-DETERMINER--->''the'' would be represented as (#$textOfTerminalSyntaxSymbol ''the'' DefiniteDeterminer PSG1).   Here DEF-DETERMINER acts as one of the #$terminalSyntaxSymbols for this grammar  (because it stands directly for surface text).")
(comment MilitaryEscortOperation "A collection of events in which military personnel accompany someone or something for security purposes; a subset of #$MilitaryOperation.")
(comment FocusedTechnologyField "A collection of instances of #$FieldOfStudy.  Each instance of #$FocusedTechnologyField is a focused area of technology, understood here as applied science.  Instances include #$ComputerAidedDesign and DigitalImaging.  Broader fields of study such as #$EngineeringField should not be included in this collection.")
(comment FastAttackCraft "The collection of military fast attack craft.")
(comment RibbonRaft "A raft composed of #$RibbonBridgeBays whose purpose is to ferry military vehicles and equipment across water obstacles.")
(comment informationRelay "This predicate can be used to indicate instances of #$PartiallyTangible           that act as transmitters in instances of #$InformationTransferEvent, but only when            they receive and transmit some piece of information, e.g. do not encrypt or otherwise           change the information.  (#$informationRelay TRANS NODE) means that the instance of           #$PartiallyTangible NODE both receives and transmits the #$infoTransferred           in the #$InformationTransferEvent TRANS but does nothing else to it.           For a predicate that represents a more active role see #$informationRouter.")
(disjointWith RecreationalActivity WorkingEvent)
(comment IllegalDrug "Drugs whose ingestion, use, sale, or manufacture is prohibited by law.")
(comment (NoAmountFn Elasticity) "does not re-expand at all after compression")
(comment ParasiticInfection "A specialization of #$Infection.  Each specialization of #$ParasiticInfection is a type of infection caused by instances of #$ParasiticOrganism (q.v.).")
(comment WorldWideWebPageCopy "#$WorldWideWebPageCopy is the collection of all copies of instances of #$WorldWideWebPage-AIS.")
(disjointWith PortableObject TrainCar)
(disjointWith Perceiving EmittingAnObject)
(comment VoiceRecognitionDevice "#$VoiceRecognitionDevice is a subset of #$BiometricAuthenticationDevice.  Individuals in the collection           #$VoiceRecognitionDevice measure the sound spectrograph pattern of a person's utterance            of a pass phrase, and attempt to match the pattern with a stored representation of it.")
(comment CityGridSectionFn "(#$CityGridSectionFn ST1 ST2 ST3 ST4) denotes the unique, roughly rectangular urban region (if any) that is completely  bounded by segments of each of the streets ST1 - ST4.  The relative order (but not the absolute positions) of the arguments here is  important: it should be physically possible to circle completely  the bounded area once by starting along ST1 and making successive  right-hand turns on ST2, ST3, ST4, and back onto ST1.  The bounded  area must be part of a region that has a #$GridStreetSystem running  through it.  To have this function return a given street-bounded  rectangular city section SECTION, one can fill its arg1 position with  any of the four streets that borders SECTION, and then continue to  fill in the remaining argument-places according to the order in which  one would travel along the other three streets if one were circling  SECTION in a clockwise fashion (i.e. by making only right-hand turns). See also #$CitySectionFn and #$CityBlockFn.")
(comment Glucosamine "The collection of amino sugars produced by the body to maintain strong and healthy bones.  As a supplement, it is designed to treat arthritis.")
(comment CycLGenericRelationFormula "A subcollection of #$CycLFormula (q.v.).  Each instance of that #$CycLGenericRelationFormula is a CycL formula that begins (immediately after the opening parenthesis) with a variable or other open expression (see #$CycLOpenExpression); i.e. it has an open expression in its \"0th\" or \"arg0\" position.  A CycL generic relation formula thus consists 

of an open expression followed by some number of terms, with the entire sequence 

enclosed in parentheses.  But note that the open expression in the formula's 

arg0 position must be such that, given the syntax and intended semantics of CycL, it could conceivably have a #$Relation -- i.e. a #$Function-Denotational or a #$TruthFunction (such as a #$Predicate or #$LogicalConnective) -- as its semantic value.  Hence the arg0 open expression might be a variable, as in the generic relation formula `(?RELATION #$Muffet #$Dog)'; or it might be an appropriate open non-atomic term (or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLNonAtomicTerm), as in 

`((#$Kappa (?ARG1) (#$knows ?ARG1 ?ARG2)) #$Muffet)'; or it might itself be 

a generic relation formula, as in `((?REL ?ARG1 #$Dog) #$Muffet)'.  On the 

other hand, `((#$BorderBetweenFn ?ARG1 ?ARG2) #$Muffet #$Dog)' is not a 

#$CycLGenericRelationFormula, since #$BorderBetweenFn only returns instances 

of #$Border, which is disjoint with #$Relation; thus the open NAT 

`(#$BorderBetweenFn ?ARG1 ?ARG2)' couldn't possibly have a #$Relation as its 

semantic value, no matter what values were assigned to the variables `?ARG1' 

and `?ARG2'.")
(comment actionPreconditions "(#$actionPreconditions ACTION SITUATION) states that some instance of the ACTION may not be executed in a situation, and get
the expected effect (#$actionEffects) unless an instance of the SITUATION holds. The SITUATION is something that is subject to further
planning, i.e. we may take other actions prior to executing this one in order to (#$AchieveFn SITUATION) (if the
situation is not itself an GenericPurposefulAction) at the time that we will undertake ACTION.")
(comment GoodWill "Emotion manifested by interest in another person (or, more rarely, in some nonhuman agent), good will towards that individual, and an inclination to favor him or her (or it).  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.")
(comment Rainbow "The collection of all #$Arcs of spectral colors appearing in a gaseous medium filled with water droplets or ice crystals appearing opposite from the light source (normally the #$Sun).")
(comment DelphiComputerProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs made by #$DelphiInternationalLtd.")
(comment ElectricalCharge "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity. Each instance of #$ElectricalCharge is an amount of net electrical charge (positive or negative) possessed by a particular instance of #$PartiallyTangible. Instances of #$ElectricalCharge may be either a fixed interval, such as the charge on one electron, or a range, such as a usable charge on a flashlight battery; see #$ScalarInterval. Also see #$UnitOfCharge for the units used by Cyc to measure electrical charges.")
(comment (DownloadOfFileTypeFn MP3File) "The collection of MP3 downloads.")
(comment epistleAddresseeText "A predicate for recording the 'to' information for an epistle in the New Testament. This information is useful in generating the various ways of referring to epistles.")
(comment fixedWRT "OBJ1 is fixed with respect to OBJ2 (it cannot be moved with respect to it, by default)")
(comment spikePeakLocation "(#$spikePeakLocation SPIKE LOCATION) means that the peak of the spike-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution SPIKE occurs at LOCATION (a specified time or place).  For example, the peak of a spike used to specify a temporal persistence distribution might be (#$YearFn 1066), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the spike pertains, the likelihood of being true would peak (be at a maximum value) during the year 1066.")
(comment LookingForSomething-AcquaintedWith "This is the subcollection of #$LookingForSomething-Definite
consisting of cases in which the reason the searcher believes there is
exactly one thing satisfying the #$searchCriterion-Definite is that s/he
believes s/he has been acquainted with the thing sought. Being acquainted
in this sense means having been in (direct) perceptual contact with the
thing and being familiar enough with it to allow future identification in
similar and normal circumstances.")
(comment negotiators "(#$negotiators NEGOTIATION AGENT) means that AGENT participates, deliberately, as a negotiating party, in the negotiating event (instance of #$Negotiating) NEGOTIATION. The intent is that #$negotiators be broad in some respects, yet narrow in others. Consider the negotiations that occurred in the Spring of 1998 with the goal of producing an agreement between Unionist and Republican factions in Northern Ireland. Assuming the existence of appropriate constants, these would be correct assertions: (#$negotiators <the negotiation> <the Unionist faction>), (#$negotiators <the negotiation> <the Republican faction>), since the two mentioned factions were the parties seeking to reach an agreement in the negotiations. It would also be correct to say (#$negotiators <the negotiations> MartinMcGuinness), since McGuinness acted as a representative of one of the negotiating factions. However, although in an informal sense the United States and its representative, George Mitchell, acted as 'negotiators', by playing the role of promoting progress in the negotiations, both the following would be incorrect assertions: (#$negotiators <the negotiations> #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica), (#$negotiators <the negotiations> GeorgeMitchell). To describe the role the US and Sen. Mitchell played in the negotiations, use #$mediators.")
(comment EndsOfChainFn "(#$EndsOfChainFn CHAIN) denotes the two ends of CHAIN.  CHAIN could be any instance of CordlikeObject, e.g. a string, or a chain or strand of DNA.")
(comment VX-NerveAgent "A #$NerveAgentType that is extremely lethal when inhaled.")
(comment CapsuleTimeRelease "The collection of all CapsuleDrugs with time-release properties.  The contents of these capsules are released into the body over measured intervals of time.")
(comment importFromQuotaDuring "(#$importFromQuotaDuring REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2 THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the import quota of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE for the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 from the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (Of course, the existence of import quotas is the exception rather than the rule.)  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of automobile imports, for example, AMOUNT might be an #$Integer indicating the number of cars that may be imported.  In the case of oil imports, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil REGION1 is allowed to import from REGION2.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of import, under the quota, of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION1 from REGION2 during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil imports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day.")
(comment Franc-France "The unit of currency in #$France.")
(comment combatForceAvailableToAgentForEvent "(combatForceAvailableToAgentForEvent AGENT EVENT N) means that N is the estimated value of the combat force of the units available to agent for carrying out EVENT. The combat force value is generally relative to some military unit which is given the value of 1. Thus, a value of .8, for instance, would mean that the unit, or units, assigned to carry out EVENT have a combat force value (see #$combatForceValueOfUnit) of .8 relative to the unit designated as the standard.")
(comment supplyRateFrom "(#$supplyRateFrom PT1 COL PT2 RATE) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 at the #$Rate RATE.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyRateFrom is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(comment Auction-Event "The collection of #$BusinessEvents in which instances of #$Product are sold to the highest bidder.  An auction lasts from a few minutes to several days and involves the gathering of potential buyers--called 'bidders'--who make offers on the products being sold.  The offers are called 'bids.'  Typically, the product is sold to the person who offers the most money for it, which person is called the 'highest bidder'.")
(comment MartialArtsSportsEvent "The collection of all sports matches in which the competitors use Asian martial arts like karate, kung fu, or taekwondo to try to defeat each other.")
(disjointWith Oxide ElementStuff)
(comment hasPhysicalAccess "(#$hasPhysicalAccess PERSON OBJ) means that person PERSON has access to the individual OBJ, such that PERSON can touch or manually manipulate OBJECT. Like #$hasAccess, this predicate is true whenever a person is capable of accessing the individual involved, regardless of whether it is permitted for him or her to do so. It can return true even if (#$not (#$isa PERSON (#$AccessorFn OBJ))). Unlike #$hasAccess, #$hasPhysicalAccess is not true when PERSON is not in close spatial proximity to OBJECT. For instance, hackers have physical access to the computers on their desks, and use them to get access to other computers to which they do not have physical access.")
(comment AB-206-Helicopter "License-built version of the U.S. Bell 206 helicopter.")
(comment Solitaire-ComputerCardGameEvent "The collection of events consisting of a soliatire game
(e.g. Klondike) being played in its entirety on a computer.")
(comment IndustryOrEconomicSectorType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$IndustryOrEconomicSectorType is a general industry or a main economic sector, by function, which is the collection of all local or geographically-defined industries and major economic sectors that perform that function.  So the worldwide funeral industry is an instance of #$IndustryOrEconomicSectorType, as is the Ohio manufacturing sector.  Every instance of #$IndustryOrEconomicSectorType can have local examples of #$Industry-Localized or #$EconomicSector-Localized as its instances.  See also its specializations #$IndustryType and #$EconomicSectorType.")
(comment AlternativeMedicinePractitioner "The collection of all #$HealthProfessionals who are practitioners of #$AlternativeMedicine. This collection is not coextensive with the collection of all #$HealthProfessionals who provide services that are instances of #$AlternativeMedicineHealthCareEvent because some practitioners act as teachers of a self-care skill, such as #$AlexanderTechnique and #$Qigong.")
(comment frameOf "constant arg1 is explicitly a term of mt arg2.")
(comment everyToEveryReln "(#$everyToEveryReln Group1 Group2 SLOT) means that for every member MEM1 of GROUP1 and every member MEM2 of GROUP2, (SLOT MEM1 MEM2) is true.  See also #$oneToManyReln and #$oneToOneReln.")
(comment PoliticalJoke "A subset of #$Joke-CW, #$PoliticalJoke is the collection of all jokes that are           about some aspect of politics.")
(comment CycLReformulatorConstant "The collection of #$CycLConstants relied on by the
#$CycLReformulator.  The reformulator mentions many of these constants
in code, and depends on their existence and correct usage in the KB
to operate properly.")
(comment Influenza "A fairly common type of respiratory viral infection.")
(comment Headache "The condition of having a headache, the internal pain which may be generalized or somewhat localized, but does not include, for example, the pain associated with a cut on your forehead.")
(comment verbSemTransTotal "(#$verbSemTransTotal VERB NUM FRAME TRANS) means that the complete translation of word sense number NUM of VERB, appearing with subcategorization frame FRAME, is TRANS.")
(comment changesQuantityByFraction "This predicate specifies the fraction by which a given quantity changes in a given time period.  (#$changesQuantityByFraction TIME THING SLOT FRACTION) means that during TIME, THING's #$QuantitySlot SLOT changes by FRACTION.  TIME is a #$TemporalThing, and Fraction is a #$ScalarInterval (which may be positive or negative).  For instance, (#$changesQuantityByFraction (#$YearFn 1980) #$SaudiArabia #$oilExport (#$Percent 10)) means that in 1980, Saudi Arabia's oil export increased by 10 percent.  See also: #$changesQuantityByAmount, #$changesQuantityInDirection.")
(comment spikePeakValue "(#$spikePeakValue SPIKE VALUE) means that the spike-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution SPIKE has a peak or maximum value of VALUE. For example, the peak value of a spike used to specify a temporal persistence distribution might be (#$Percent 95), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the spike pertains, the maximum likelihood of being true is 0.95.  VALUE might also be a reified value such as `moderately likely'.")
(comment VisualLabel "The collection of all labels that present their information content visually.  Thus a label with a barcode is an instance of #$VisualLabel, as are more common labels.  Neither radio isotope labelling nor magnetic labels are instances of #$VisualLabel")
(comment SportsTeamTypeBySex "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$SportsTeam whose instances are all of the same gender.  This is not a partition (as of 10/10/2000) because boys' teams and girls' teams are not covered.")
(comment overlappingPeople "The person denoted by ARG1 shares some possibly significant attribute with the agent denoted by ARG2.  In the extreme case, ARG1 might denote the same person as ARG2.")
(comment Facemask-Hockey "The collection of face masks that HockeyPlayers wear.")
(comment M978TankerVehicle "A type of military tanker vehicle.")
(comment MediaSeriesProduct "The collection of all #$MediaProducts that appear as a series of individual #$MediaProducts.")
(comment CovalentLinking "The collection of all instances of #$ChemicalBonding that establish a #$CovalentBond between atoms.")
(comment Germanium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Germanium.")
(comment usesPhysicalSchema "(#$usesPhysicalSchema ?PHYS-TABLE ?PHYS-SCHEMA) means that  the #$PhysicalDBTable, ?PHYS-TABLE, adheres to the #$PhysicalTableSchema,  ?PHYS-SCHEMA.  ?PHYS-SCHEMA declares what fields are present, and what  their datatypes are, but doesn't impose any semantic interpretation  on ?PHYS-TABLE.")
(comment WarMovie "#$WarMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW, each of which tells a tale about war.")
(comment webPageURL "(#$webPageURL WP PATH) means that PATH is the URL (World Wide Web Uniform Resource Locator) for the instance WP of #$WorldWideWebPage-AIS (where WP is explicitly represented as a Cyc constant for an individual #$WorldWideWebPage-AIS).")
(comment TowingFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an object gets towed Like towingOf Automobile.")
(comment WeightChangingProcess "A collection of events. Each           instance of #$WeightChangingProcess is an Event which has, as           one of its significant effects, changing the weight of           some object.  Note that a change           in weight is one of the kinds of intrinsic change           which an object can undergo, that is,           #$WeightChangingProcess is a subset of           IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.")
(comment FrontalLobe "The collection of all frontal lobes of #$Brains.  Each individual #$FrontalLobe is in the anterior region of a #$CerebralHemisphere and contains the motor cortex and is involved in what are considered to be the 'higher' brain functions.")
(comment keFacilitationRules "This predicate relates a cyc term to the rules asserted on it to help guide knowledge entry.  (#$keFacilitationRules TERM RULE) means that when creating instances, subcollections or asserting relations involving TERM (the RULE will indicate which of these are relevant), one should consider RULE.  This differs from #$salientAssertions in that the assertions do not define the term but simply guide knowledge entry related to the term.  Also see knowledge entry facilitation gafs such as those involving specializations of #$keRelevantPreds, #$keRelevantInverse, #$keGenlsRelevantPreds and #$keGenlsRelevantInverse.  These rules were designed for use in tools for rapid knowledge entry.")
(comment StatementOfNeutrality "The collection of events where one agent formally states their neutrality in dealings with another.  This can range from one countries declaration of almost permanent neutrality, like Switzerland to a statement of neutrality on a specific topic, like nuclear testing.")
(comment Bacterium-Peritrichous "The collection of #$Bacterium whose instances have many flagella which are uniformly distributed around the cell.")
(comment DecontaminationTruck-Military "The collection of military vehicles used to decontaminate areas where chemical or biological weapons or dangerous radiation levels are present.")
(disjointWith EdibleStuff (GroupFn PhysicalDevice))
(disjointWith DegenerationEvent ConstructionProject)
(comment NameServer-Network "#$NameServer-Network is the collection of #$Internet hosts running
software capable of processing DNS requests.")
(comment unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocDuring "(#$unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocDuring DOC DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PERIOD NUM) means that #$Prescriber DOC has had prescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE filled for NUM 'units' of DRUGTYPE during PERIOD.  For #$TabletDrugs, the 'unit' is a single #$Tablet, while for fluids, creams, and inhalents, the 'unit' is mg of active ingredient.   RXFILLTYPE may be FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment HistoricPeriod "The collection of significant periods of history.

  Examples include #$TheRenaissance.")
(comment CarrierAirWing "A Carrier Air Wing is the group of #$Warplanes attached to an   #$AttackAircraftCarrier. These form part of the air system of a   #$CarrierBattleGroup. This would include not only attack warplanes,  but also helicopters and surveillance aircraft.")
(comment RomanticComedyMovie "A subgenre of #$ComedyMovie that focuses on the complications arising from the search for romance, courtship or a new relationship. Humor in such films tends to be of a verbal, low-key variety or situational, as opposed to slapstick.")
(comment disembarcationSubevent "This slot is used in detailed descriptions of transportation         events in which a transportation device is used. The         disemabarcationSubEvent is the event of getting off the         transportation device.")
(comment ExitingAContainer "The collection of events in which an object exits a container")
(disjointWith Army-BranchOfService AirForce)
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-Virus "#$AttackByComputerOperation-Virus

 is the collection of all attacks on computer resources

    by programs in the collection #$ComputerVirus.")
(comment HypochlorousAcid "The collection of samples of hypochlorous acid; HClO.")
(comment WoodFn "Collection-forming function - takes a type of tree as an argument, returns the class of wood which is derived from instances of that type of tree.")
(disjointWith Volume ElectricalCharge)
(comment PriorProbability-RangeFn "A function used for probability statements.  (#$PriorProbability-RangeFn PROPOSITION), applied to the #$CycLAssertion PROPOSITION, yields a range of two real numbers between zero and one that includes the a priori probability that PROPOSITION is true, in the applicable #$Microtheory. In most microtheories, generally, this refers to the range of probability that PROPOSITION, by itself, would be true if there were no further evidence in the #$Microtheory for or against it, nor knowledge of the truth of anything else other than the #$domainAssumptions of the #$Microtheory.  Contrast this with the predicate form #$priorProbability-Range and with the functions #$DerivedProbability-RangeFn #$PriorProbabilityFn.  A #$PriorProbability-RangeFn may represent an absolute objective probability range, a subjective assigned probability range, a quantum probability range, or an assigned probability range based on some internal characteristic of PROPOSITION (including possibly a statement in it of the occurrence of a number of outcomes within a large number of trials).  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.")
(comment rotationOfLauncher "(#$rotationOfLauncher GUN ANGLE-RANGE) indicates the range of horizontal rotation at which a GUN can be fired. This is not relevant for all guns but for those that are fixed and point in some forward direction, the range of left-right rotation may be limited. For example, (#$angleOfLauncher ?CANNON (#$Degree-UnitOfAngularMeasure -45 45) means that ?CANNON can be fired between 45 degrees to the left and 45 degrees to the right with respect to its intrinsic forward direction. ")
(comment NucleotideSequenceGISFn "(#$NucleotideSequenceGISFn NUCLEOTIDE_STRAND) returns the nucleotide sequence of the #$PolynucleotideStrand NUCLEOTIDE_STRAND, in the form of an abstract information structure consisting of a list nucleotide symbols (see #$Nucleotide-GIS).  Note that the function is many one: that is, it can map more than one molecule to the same sequence of nucleotides.")
(comment BoardOfDirectors "The governing body of a corporation")
(comment Compliant "This attribute is attributed to an object or event insofar as it complies with some standard.  Typically this attibute is involved in a three way relation between itself, the status-holder and the standard according to which the status holds.  See #$complianceStatus.")
(comment Survey "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$InformationGathering.  In

every instance of #$Survey, an agent questions a number of individuals

in order to gain information about the group to which they belong.

The question(s) in the survey may be asked in individual interviews,

or may be mass-disseminated (e.g. by television or magazines) so

that members of the public can choose whether to respond.")
(comment TourPackageTypeByOption "A collection of common attributes associated with instances of #$TravelTour.")
(comment ViralHepatitis "A collection of viral infections that primarily affect the liver. #$ViralHepatitis is the common spec of #$Hepatitis and #$ViralInfection. This collection has five main specs A, B, C, D and E, corresponding to the different variant of the hepatitis virus, see #$Hepatitis-VirusType.")
(comment ServiceRelatedFn "#$ServiceRelatedFn takes as argument any #$Thing and returns the collection of all services directly related to that #$Thing. For example, (#$ServiceRelatedFn #$Judaism) returns the collection of services related to Jewish beliefs (including Temple services, Hebrew education, Bat Mitzvah planning, and Jewish dating services).")
(comment NuclearFissionProcess "Whole reaction processes, that either peter out or end with a bang. They consist of lots of individual SingleNuclearFissions.")
(comment relevantInTime-Always "(#$relevantInTime-Always MT TIME) means that the assertions in MT are relevant throughout the entire temporal extent of TIME.  See also #$relevantInTime-Sometime.")
(comment OceanLiner "#$OceanLiner is a specialization of #$PublicTransportationDevice and #$Ship.  Each instance of #$OceanLiner is a ship that is designed to comfortably transport a large number of people across an ocean .")
(comment DepthBomb "The collection of #$Bombs used especially against #$Submarines.  #$DepthBombs, also called depth charges, are dropped from #$ModernNavalShips and #$MilitaryAircraft and explode under water.")
(comment X-Man "The class of #$Mutant #$Superheroes in the Marvel universe,

including characters such as the Beast, Cyclops and Wolverine.")
(comment presupposedPredicate "If (#$presupposedPredicate PRED1 PRED2), then as a general rule 
for lists of arguments (ARG1, ARG2, ...ARGn) that meet the definitional
constraints, (#$presupposes (PRED1 ARG1 ARG2 ...ARGn) 
                            (PRED2 ARG1 ARG2 ...ARGn)).")
(comment CoughSuppressant "Drugs which are used to reduce coughing.")
(comment over-UnderspecifiedLocation "(#$over-UnderspecifiedLocation ACT LOC) states that an abstract

locational relation holds between ACT and LOC, where LOC is a

#$Location-Underspecified and ACT is some action requiring some kind of

abstract 'floor' or lower boundary. We can say 'the path went over the

mountain', 'the game went over 90 minutes' (90 minutes being an abstract

location by virtue of being an abstract container), etc.")
(comment GunSystem "The collection of all #$WeaponSystems

   whose main feature is a #$Gun.")
(comment Triglyceride "The collection of all triglycerides, also known as neutral lipids. In a triglyceride molecule, three molecules of one or more different fatty acids are linked to a glycerol molecule. Triglycerides are found in #$FattyTissue of #$Mammals and in plant #$Seeds.")
(comment PineapplePlant "A pineapple plant is a type of bromeliad which produces an edible fruit, the pineapple.")
(comment Cutting-IncompleteSeparation "This is the collection of events in which something is cut, but separation is not complete.  The end product of this is a hole/cavity in the object being cut.")
(comment NCAABasketballTournament-Women "The #$NationalCollegiateAthleticAssociation Women's tournament, held annually.")
(comment LandingCraft "The collection of watercraft or amphibious craft used in landing operations.")
(comment EukaryoticRNAType "A collection of collections. Instances are kinds of
#$RNAMolecule produced by instances of #$EukaryoticOrganism.")
(comment permissionMode "(#$permissionMode FILE MODE) means that FILE has a set of  file permissions represented by MODE, where MODE is a four-digit octal  number.  The number corresponds to a particular configuration of  permission settings.  The leftmost digit indicates whether or not the  file is SUID (4) or SGID (2).  From left to right, the remaining  digits indicate   the priviledges had by the file's owner, the files owner's group, and   others. In each case, 1 represents execute priviledge, 2 indicates  write priviledge, and 4 indicates read priviledge.  So, for example,  (#$permissionMode File001 0655) means that File001's owner can read and  write FileOO1 (but not execute it), and everyone else can read and  execute it.")
(comment AcademicTest "The collection of #$PropositionalInformationThings whose instances are usually a set of questions designed to test a student's understanding of a certain subject.  See #$AcademicTesting.")
(comment eventTypeInappropriateClothingItem "(eventTypeInappropriateClothing EVENTTYPE CLOTHING-INSTANCE) means that CLOTHING-INSTANCE is inappropriate to wear to events of type EVENTTYPE.")
(comment AmphibiousInfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of infantry units that are trained and equipped to move to their places of deployment by water vehicles.")
(comment NetIncreasingFunction "#$NetIncreasingFunction is function which shows a net increase in its value from 'start' to 'finish'.  Such functions may take on any intermediate values so long as the net change in value from 'start' to 'finish' is positive.  More formally, let x denote an element in the domain of some #$NetIncreasingFunction, F.  Thus F(x) denotes an element in the range of F.  Let x1 denote the lower bound on x.  Let x2 denote the upper bound on x.  F is an #$NetIncreasingFunction if and only if F(x1) < F(x2).  See #$NetDecreasingFunction.  See also #$MonotonicallyIncreasingFunction whose elements show an increase (technically, a non-decrease) for each successive range element.")
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument-PurelyAcoustic MusicalInstrument-AcousticElectric)
(comment KakeTemplate "The collection of all Kake templates.  A Kake template is a set of
          instructions which the #$Kake-CGIInterpreter (or really, any implementation
          of #$Kake-ProgrammingLanguage) can use to generate a valid 
          document in #$HyperTextMarkupLanguage.  A Kake template can generate
          HTML based on querying a Cyc KB and input from the user.")
(comment Dumbbell-Weight "This is the collection of dumbbells,

solid metal exercise weights with the weight ends and bar merged into

a single piece.")
(comment ServicesUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profiles center           on providing various services.")
(comment LinguisticAnalysis-Phonological "A collection of microtheories.  Each element is a microtheory representing knowledge, theory, hypotheses, evidence, and problems related to the phonological analysis of a data set taken from a language or group of languages.")
(comment VisualPatternType "The collection of all visual pattern types.  The patterns may be static or dynamic.")
(comment Separation-Complete "A specialization of #$SeparationEvent.  In each instance of #$Separation-Complete, one object is separated into two or more distinct, unconnected pieces.")
(comment TutorialLesson "The collection of all #$Lessons in which one #$Teacher instructs one #$Student.")
(comment Tet-NorthVietnam-VietnamWarEra "#$Tet-NorthVietnam-VietnamWarEra is the collection of all instances of #$Tet-LunarNewYear celebrated in #$NorthVietnam between approximately 1955 to 1975.")
(comment PornStar "Instances of #$PornStar are people whose image appears in instances of #$PornographicMaterial with some commercial success, and who voluntarily participated in its production.")
(comment DustParticle "The particles which settle on furniture and need to be dusted away, or are blown around in dust storms.")
(comment AllergicReaction "A collection of dynamic, physiological states. An instance of #$AllergicReaction is an event in which an organism which is exposed to a particular substance (e.g., pollen, mold) develops some abnormality or impairment of its physiological condition as a result of interacting with the substance. Allergic reactions to some types of substances occur widely in members of a species; e.g., #$PoisonIvyPoisoning in humans. But other allergic reactions affect only a small proportion of a species, such as human allergies to penicillin. This concept is the collection of events in which allergic reactions are `taking place', not abstract unrealized potential situations such as `John is allergic to milk.' I.e., if John were allergic to milk, and he drank some, and then proceeded to have a whopping bad allergic reaction, that latter event would be an instance of #$AllergicReaction.")
(comment ActorSlotList "The collection of lists of the form (SLOT1 SLOT2...SLOTn) in

which each element of the list is an instance of #$ActorSlot (hence a

predicate).")
(comment CleaningAnObject "A collection of events.   Each #$CleaningAnObject event is a #$Cleaning event in which some particular object is cleaned.")
(comment RickettsiaProwsecki "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom that has a life cycle limited to humans and the human louse.  These ProkaryoticCells are responible for the #$Typhus-Infection.")
(comment BrightAlbedoFeature-Topographical "The collection of all topographical features noted for an albedo (reflectivity of light) significanly brighter than the surrounding regions.")
(comment WhiteMagic "#$WhiteMagic is a kind of #$Magic such that the effects of elements of #$WhiteMagic are generally believed to be beneficial or at least to have a beneficial purpose.  Who is it that generally believes this?  This is a function of the current #$Microtheory.  In some #$Microtheorys, most people may believe in the possibility of #$Magic, but it is generally believed that no magic can have beneficial effects.  In such a #$Microtheory, the extent of #$WhiteMagic would be the empty set.  In other #$Microtheorys, general belief may be that some people perform #$WhiteMagic with beneficial intent but that these actions have no effects.  Of course, there are numerous possibilities about what 'general belief' about #$WhiteMagic would entail, and thus many correspondingly different possible #$Microtheorys. Alchemists in the european tradition were often considered capable of performing #$WhiteMagic.")
(comment FormulaArgListFn "(#$FormulaArgListFn RELATION-EXPRESSION) denotes a list of the arguments in RELATION-EXPRESSION.  For example, (#$FormulaArgListFn (#$genls #$Dog #$Animal)) denotes (#$TheList #$Dog #$Animal).  See also #$FormulaArgFn and #$FormulaArityFn.")
(comment Microphilia "Microphilia is the erotic fascination with shrinking and/or science-fictionally tiny persons, generally women.

The collection #$Microphilia contains those instances in which that fascination is manifest.")
(comment AntiAnginal "Drugs that combat angina -- severe pain in the area of the heart, caused by relative lack of oyxgen supply to those tissues.")
(comment interArgIsa1-3 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa1-3 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the first argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the third argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN INST ARG2 ARG3 ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only 
if ARG3 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic 
well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment ReactiveArmor "#$ReactiveArmor is a type of armor that is composed of
explosive modules designed to counteract the explosive #$Warhead of an
incoming #$Missile.  Unlike standard #$Armor, #$ReactiveArmor is not
stuff like, because it is made of discrete explosive packets, which if
subdivided would no longer have the properties of #$ReactiveArmor.")
(comment VersusFn "(#$VersusFn TERM1 TERM2) is a note for helping KE-ers decide whether to in which cases TERM1 should be used vs TERM2 should be used.  Of course, it should only be used when it is otherwise difficult to determine KR differences between TERM1 and TERM2.  The function term is handy because it concludes (#$sharedNotes TERM1 (#$VersusFn TERM1 TERM2)) and (#$sharedNotes TERM2 (#$VersusFn TERM1 TERM2)) by means of a forward rule.")
(comment CycLFullyGroundExpression "A #$CycLExpressionType and a specialization of #$CycLClosedExpression (q.v.).  This is the collection of all and only those CycL expressions that contain no variables, free or bound.  (An expression that contains bound variables but no free variables is sometimes called merely \"ground\"; see e.g. #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence).  Specializations of this collection are #$CycLFullyGroundAtomicSentence and #$CycLConstant.")
(comment (GroupFn MilitaryOrganization) "This is the #$Collection of all #$Groups of instances of #$MilitaryOrganization. Since #$MilitaryOrganization is a collection of groups, this collection is itself a collection of groups of groups.")
(disjointWith DefenseSystem Quarry)
(comment BlockOfStreetBetweenFn "(#$BlockOfStreetBetweenFn STREET XST1 XST2) denotes
the subpath of STREET (if any) that is an instance of 
#$BlockOfStreet and that extends from the intersection of 
STREET and XST1 to the intersection of STREET and XST2.")
(comment paDisambiguatingQuestion "A statement that the Product Advisor needs to ask the user to disambiguate

previous input.  (paDisambiguatingQuestion TEMPLATE STRING SET) means that the

formula TEMPLATE is true if one of the terms in SET is substituted for

the free variable in TEMPLATE.  In addition, a user has typed in the string

STRING, which is ambiguous over SET, and the only way to disambiguate 

is to ask the user directly.  TEMPLATE must have exactly one free variable; each

element of SET must be an instance of CycLExpression.")
(comment Egg-Chickens "The egg of a chicken, the white and yolk of which are eaten by humans and probably many other animals as food.")
(comment zoneControlled "(#$zoneControlled AGENT ZONE) means that AGENT has effective military, paramilitary or police control over the geographic area of ZONE.  This means that blatant attacks on AGENT and misbehavior are preventable by AGENT and are usually effectively deterred.  The #$zoneControlled area may have rapidly changing location and boundaries during a military campaign.  See also #$ZoneOfMilitaryControl.  For control of entire countries or territories, see #$territoriesControlled.")
(comment StockMarket "A set of transactions in which stocks are bought and sold.  THE stock market usually refers to all sales in the recent past (a week, a month, a year...) up to and including current transactions, in the US.")
(comment birthRate "(#$birthRate AREA RATE) means that the #$GeographicalRegion AREA has a birth rate of RATE. It is most common to express RATE in terms of the number of births per 1000 population per year.")
(comment Battleship "A collection. Large and heavily armored warships.")
(comment Autobiography "A collection of instances of

 #$PropositionalInformationThing.  Each instance of #$Autobiography is

 a narrative containing information about the author's

 own life.")
(disjointWith UnitOfCurrent UnitOfSpeed)
(comment OrganismPartType "The collection of all the types of #$OrganismParts.  An #$OrganismPartType  is a characterization of body parts of #$Animals, #$PlantParts, or parts of other organisms by structure and/or function.   Some instances of this collection include #$SpinalColumn, #$Eyelash, #$Petal, etc.  #$OrganismPartType is not organized along species/order/class/phylum/... taxonomic lines.")
(comment GraduateSchoolEntranceTest "The collection of #$UniversityEntryTest events that are designed to help graduate and profession school admissions officers decide whether to admit a student.")
(disjointWith Canoe Raft)
(comment F-18-Fighter "The collection of all F-18 fighter jets")
(comment AccessValidationFault "#$AccessValidationFault is an attribute of computer programs.  A program has an #$AccessValidationFault if its corresponding computer process can invoke an operation or read or write to a file outside the access domain of the user, accepts input from an unauthorized user, or fails to authenticate a user.  Note that #$AccessValidationFault is distinct from #$AuthenticationSoftwareBypassFault, which is an attribute of programs that actually do authenticate, albeit poorly.")
(comment xyCrossSectionShape "The cross section shape in the xy plane. Again it is not really the xy plane in the absolute sense but in the intrinsic axes sense.\")")
(comment PestManagement "This is the collection of activities aimed at eliminating or controlling

the local detimental effects of animals considered to be pests. The animals in question

are primarily insects, and the effects in question are mostly those on agriculture and

places of human habitation or employment.")
(comment Barrier-Underspecified "The collection of all semantically underspecified barriers, 
whether spatial (and literal) like a #$Wall-GenericBarrier, or metaphoric
(like #$NetscapeCommunicationsCorporation is to #$MicrosoftInc).")
(comment SurfMusic "A fairly early, largely instrumental specialization of #$RockMusic, associated
  with the sport of surfing.  Influential practitioners of this style include Dick Dale,
  the Chantays, and the Surfaris.  Some of the music of the Beach Boys and the Ventures 
  is #$SurfMusic.")
(comment DBKeyFunctionFn "#$DBKeyFunctionFn is a function-denoting function.  (#$DBKeyFunctionFn . fields) denotes a function which is an instance of #$DBKeyFunction; it's #$arity is equal to the number of #$LogicalFields given as arguments to #$DBKeyFunctionFn.  The fields given as arguments should together form a key for their #$LogicalTableSchema.  The function denoted by (#$DBKeyFunctionFn . fields) is applied to values for the fields used to form it, in the order the fields were used in the expression, to return an instance of #$DBKeyObj, which uniquely identifies a row of a table.")
(comment importsFrom "(#$importsFrom REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 imports significant amounts of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE from the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2.")
(comment RoleplayingGameProgram "An instance is a computer role playing game.")
(comment BacteriumInCulture "The collection of those instances of #$Bacterium that are grown in a culture.  Most species reqiure certain mediums and other conditions to obtain optimum growth.  See also #$Culture-Bacterial.")
(comment VocabularyMicrotheory "The collection of all microtheories which specify the vocabulary for some topic, but have no rules or other non-definitional assertions.")
(comment SubstituteNLTEFn "(#$SubstituteNLTEFn NEW OLD F) denotes an #$NLTemplateExpression formed by substituting NEW for every occurrence of OLD in the formula F. See also #$SubstituteFormulaFn for doing the same thing with #$ELSentence-Assertibles.")
(comment CycEasySyntaxSystem "The #$CycEasySyntaxSystem is for specifying simple syntax directly in Cyc.  Each instance will be a #$CharacterString which specifies a class of allowed #$CharacterStrings.  Therefore the #$CycEasySyntaxSystem is a #$FormalMetaGrammar.  The first use is for specifying document structure, and involves an HTML hybrid form called a #$CycEasyDocDescription.")
(comment BiographyFn "#$BiographyFn takes as argument any instance of #$Person and returns the collection of all biographies of that person.  For instance, (#$BiographyFn #$JohnKennedy) returns the collection of all biographies of John F. Kennedy.")
(comment TVShowTypeByFormat "#$TVShowTypeByFormat is a collection of collections. Each element of #$TVShowTypeByFormat is a collection of instances of #$TVShow-CW that have the same format. For example, #$TVGameShow and #$VarietyShow are elements of #$TVShowTypeByFormat. The format of a #$TVShow-CW is a way of describing the distinctive manner in which #$Narrative, and the visual and audio aspects of a #$TVShow-CW are combined. For example, #$NewsShows combine shorts bits of #$Narrative with bits of audio and video clips. #$VarietyShows mix a number of #$EntertainmentPerformances by #$Artist-Performers. This collection was created to make use of a faceting of #$TVShow-CW to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(comment FastAttackCraft-Missile "A subset of #$FastAttackCraft.  Each instance is a ship used to transport and launch #$Missiles.")
(comment subConfigurations "(#$subConfigurations MAIN SUB) means that SUB is a configuration which is a meaningful part of MAIN, i.e. an informative description of MAIN would likely include a description of SUB.  For instance, in the situation of a chain being configured as it is, the situation of two of the links being linked is a sub-situation and is related to the situation by #$subConfigurations.")
(comment GarbageCollectingViaTruck "The collection of all events in which garbage is collected and brought to a dump.  Elements involve instances of #$Garbage-Generic being collected at multiple #$fromLocations and deposited at a single #$toLocation.")
(comment Prednicarbate "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(comment Premier-HeadOfGovernment "The #$Premier-HeadOfGovernment of a country.")
(comment militaryRank-CountryAndBranchOfService "(#$militaryRank-CountryAndBranchOfService PERSON RANK
COUNTRY BOS-TYPE) means that PERSON has the military rank RANK in
COUNTRY's branch of service BOS-TYPE.")
(comment NaturalizationRecord "The collection of #$LegalDocuments that record the granting of citizenship to former non-citizens.")
(comment MotorcycleClub "The collection of all clubs [#$Club-Organization] organized for fans [#$Fan-Supporter] of some #$Person, #$Group, #$ConceptualWork, etc.")
(comment Highway "A specialization of both #$Roadway and #$PublicProperty.  Each instance of #$Highway is a major road open to public use.")
(comment typeBehaviorCapable-PerformedBy "The predicate #$typeBehaviorCapable-PerformedBy is used to describe a type of situation in which objects of a certain type can be performers (see #$performedBy) due to their intrinsic properties. See also #$typeBehaviorCapable.")
(disjointWith ConstrainingEvent EmittingAWave)
(comment DegenerationEvent "A collection of events.  In each #$DegenerationEvent, some object loses its function(s) through a process of deterioration and/or a series of discrete breakdowns.")
(disjointWith EnlistedPerson CommissionedOfficer)
(comment relationExistsSpecAll "(#$relationExistsSpecAll SLOT COL1 COL2) means that for every INS2 which is a instance of COL2, there is some SUBCOL1 which is a subcollection of COL1, such that (SLOT SUBCOL1 INS2) holds.")
(comment PhysicalForce-Electromagnetic "This is the #$PhysicalForceType which ties electrons to nuclei. Radio waves and light are

common manifestations. Recently, this force and the #$PhysicalForce-Weak have been \"unified\". The single

multi-aspect force is called the Electro-Weak Force. See #$PhysicalForce-ElectroWeak.")
(comment drugForDiseaseAvailableToOrg "`(#$drugForDiseaseAvailableToOrg ORGTYPE DRUGTYPE AILTYPE)' means that instances of DRUGTYPE (which is a type of drug effective against the disease AILTYPE) are available to the members of ORGTYPE. By available, we intend to say that instances DRUGTYPE could actually be given to the members of ORGTYPE and not that it merely exists.")
(comment SubcollectionOfUsedForTypeFn "(#$SubcollectionOfUsedForTypeFn OBJECT_TYPE TYPE) specifies the collection of all instances of OBJECT_TYPE which are ``used for'' instances of TYPE.  Thus (#$SubcollectionOfUsedForTypeFn #$Costume #$PlayPerformance) would be the collection of all #$Costumes used in plays.")
(comment MeteorShower "The collection of all events in which dozens of visible (if it is #$Night below) #$Meteors appear in the sky above some part of the Earth's surface (see #$TheSkyAboveHere) per hour.  Instances of #$MeteorShower can last from tens of minutes to #$AFewDaysDuration.")
(comment Aaddzz-AdPlacementService "the collection of all #$ServiceEvents in which #$InformationAccessTechnologiesInc places an advertisement on a website under its 'Aaddzz' service program.")
(comment TruthAlteringReformulation "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
truth is not preserved; something is lost or altered in at least
one direction of reformulation.
More specifically, if logical formulas are being
reformulated, the two would not be #$equiv, and if denotational terms
are being reformulated, the two would not be #$equals.")
(comment streetAddressText-NC "The predicate #$streetAddressText-NC maps a particular element of #$ContactLocation to a non-canonical #$StreetAddress, ADDRESS. The `NC' in the name stands for `non-canonical'.   (#$streetAddressText-NC LOCATION ADDRESS) means that the #$ContactLocation LOCATION has the non-canonicalized #$StreetAddress, ADDRESS. For example, one value  for #$streetAddressText-NC of the #$Cycorp #$MailingLocation is `3721 Executive Center Dr., Ste. 100.' Note that this street address as printed does not conform to the US Postal Service's recommended standard for printed addresses, and so relative to this standard it is not `canonical.' Non-canonical means that  ADDRESS may not conform to the canonicalization scheme(s) used for other known addresses for LOCATION.  These other (presumed canonical) street addresses should be related to LOCATION using the predicate #$streetAddressText. It really only makes sense to use #$streetAddressText-NC in contexts (such as the #$LogicalTableSchemas for certain database tables) where LOCATION may have both canonical and non-canonical street addresses entered for it.  In contexts where the differences between canonicalized and non-canonicalized street addresses is not an issue, just use #$streetAddressText.  See also #$ContactLocation.")
(comment Hertz "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction and #$UnitOfFrequency.  #$Hertz returns a unit of frequency in hertz when applied to a real number (see the collection #$SubLRealNumber) or a sequence of two real numbers.  Hertz is the basic unit of measure for elements of #$Frequency (1 Hz=1 cycle per second). (#$Hertz NUM) denotes the frequency NUM cycles per second.")
(comment RemoteStarter "A subsystem which can be added to a car to allow the car to be

started remotely using a controller which often controls the #$CarAlarm as well.")
(comment epistleNumber "A predicate for recording what number an epistle is among the group of epistles to the same addressee. This information is useful in generating the various ways of referring to epistles.")
(comment actingForces "Forces acting on a physical process")
(comment acquaintedWith-Perceptual "The expression `(#$acquaintedWith-Perceptual AGENT THING)' means
that AGENT has come into causal/perceptual contact with THING so that in
similar and favorable circumstances AGENT could re-identify THING. The
qualifications on circumstances are crucial here. Being acquainted in the
present sense does not entail that one could determine that a very
similar-looking item in the same place as the original could be determined
not to be the original item, that one could re-identify by touch in a
dark room an item one had become acquainted with primarily visually, or that
one could re-identify the item were it to be presented in a different guise.")
(comment paRelatedTopic "A predicate used to guide question-generation during a Product Advisor session. (#$paRelatedTopic TOPIC1 TOPIC2) indicates the existence of a significant conceptual link between TOPIC1 and TOPIC2, one which suggests a clarificatory question about TOPIC1.  Usually, TOPIC1 is a subject area in which the user has explicitly indicated an interest (see #$paCustomerIndicatedTopic). TOPIC2 is thus a natural follow-up/response to the user's expressed interest in TOPIC1.")
(comment Yotta "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^24")
(comment processTypeRunningOn "A predicate which relates a collection of processes with a computer.
(#$processTypeRunningOn PROCESSTYPE COMPUTER) means that there is an instance
of #$ComputerProcessRunning which is an instance of PROCESSTYPE and is
related to COMPUTER via #$processRunningOn.")
(comment BetaBlocker "A drug substance that interfers with the transmission of sympathetic nervous inhibiting stimuli at the adrenergic beta receptors .  Each #$BetaBlocker is a #$CardiovascularAgent.")
(comment assertedPredicateArg "(#$assertedPredicateArg OBJ N PREDICATE) means that a ground atomic formula (or \"GAF\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) whose initial (or \"0th\" argument-place) term denotes PREDICATE, and whose Nth argument-place term denotes OBJ, is asserted in the Cyc Knowledge Base. Note that this predicate is itself #$notAssertible (q.v.), since it must be computed from the state of the knowledge base.")
(comment PublishingWrittenMaterial "A collection of events.  In each instance of #$PublishingWrittenMaterial, a book or periodical is transformed from manuscript or typescript form to a form suitable for retail sale or public distribution.  This collection can include any kind of publishing, from manuscript copies to print media to electronic publishing.")
(comment AccountsPayableDepartment "A subset of #$AccountingDepartment; those departments responsible for making payments.")
(comment Chloroplast "A green plastid with an internal membrane system incorporating the pigment molecules that are essential to photosynthesis.")
(comment KarateActivity "The collection of all activities consisting of a #$Person practicing, performing, or using karate, a method developed in #$Japan of defending oneself without the use of weapons by striking sensitive areas on an attacker's body with the hands, elbows, knees, or feet. See also #$KarateSportsEvent.")
(disjointWith Atom Water)
(comment VulnerableToPhysicalBreachOfSecurity "#$VulnerableToPhysicalBreachOfSecurity is an attribute something has

if non-authorized persons have physical access to it.")
(comment HandheldStamids "The collection of handheld mine detection systems which will replace, in part, the #$AN-PSS-12HandHeldPortableMineDetectingSet (a metallic mine detector).  It can detect metallic and nonmetallic mines by using multiple sensors such as a metal detector and Ground Penetrating Radar.  Standoff mine detection capability will be provided through use of a Forward Looking Infrared sensor.  Mine detection, through use of data processing (using computer algorithms), is autonomous.  Handheld Stamids are to be used under conditions where #$GroundStamids and #$AirborneStandoffMinefieldDetectionSystem cannot be employed. Dismounted soldiers will use Handheld Stamids while operating along footpaths, in adverse weather, in rough terrain where ground vehicles cannot operate, under overhead cover, during covert operations or where noise discipline must be observed, and during Stability and Support Operations.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment StencilingEvent "The collection of stenciling events")
(comment ReconstructiveBreastSurgery "#$Surgery done after a mastectomy.")
(comment Acholeplasma-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment Protectorate "The physical and functional sides of a Protectorate -- a geopolitical entity that is weakly controlled by a foreign power, and (typically) strongly defended by them in case of attack")
(comment evaluateAtEL "(#$evaluateAtEL FUNCTION) means that the canonicalizer will translate each non-atomic term (see the collection #$CycLNonAtomicTerm) whose  initial (or \"0th\" argument-place) term denotes FUNCTION into the value to which the non-atomic term evaluates.  For example, if (#$evaluateAtEL #$PlusFn) holds in  a #$Microtheory MT, then the non-atomic term `(#$PlusFn 2 3 4)' will canonicalize as `9' in that MT.  Note that a non-atomic term containing a nested non-atomic term whose initial term denotes another instance of #$EvaluatableFunction (call that instance OTHER-FUNCTION) will not canonicalize in this way, unless (#$evaluateAtEL OTHER-FUNCTION) is also true in MT.  For example, `(#$PlusFn 2 (#$DifferenceFn 3 4))' will not canonicalize as `1' in MT unless    

(#$evaluateAtEL #$DifferenceFn) is also true in MT.")
(comment RacistJoke "A subset of #$StereotypeJoke, #$RacistJoke is the collection of all jokes that are about            race or ethnicity.")
(comment CycLReformulationRulePredicate "The collection of #$Predicates which may appear as the operator in a #$CycLReformulatorRule.")
(comment Apprenticeship "Learning a skill from another person, rather than a book or by trial and error for example.")
(comment MadCowDisease "#$MadCowDisease, also known as Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy           (BSE) is a deadly disease affecting cows. Cattle affected with            the disease may appear normal for several years, then begin to            stagger about and previously placid animals can become aggressive            and dangerous. At autopsy, the cow's brain looks spongy and full            of tiny holes.")
(comment TextPublishedByAgentTypeFn "#$TextPublishedByAgentTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$IntelligentAgent and returns the collection of all texts published by that type of agent.  For example, (#$TextPublishedByAgentTypeFn #$University) returns the set of all texts published by any #$University.")
(comment NetUnchangingFunction "#$NetUnchangingFunction is the set of functions which show no net change in comparing their starting value with their final value.  What qualifies as 'no net change' should be dependent on microtheory.  An example of such a function might be the price of oil as a function of time for long time periods after significant terrorist activity affecting the oil sector.  The net change for such a function in the long is zero (or 'close enough' for the current microtheory) since prices will return to normal after repairs have been made despite fluctuations.")
(comment spikeNonPeakValue "(#$spikeNonPeakValue SPIKE VALUE) means that the spike-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution SPIKE has a non-peak value of VALUE. For example, the non-peak value of a spike used to specify a temporal persistence distribution might be (#$Percent 25), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the spike pertains, the minimum likelihood of being true is 0.25.  VALUE might also be a reified value such as `slightly likely'.")
(comment PornographicMaterial "The collection of texts or images judged by some sectors of a particular community to be obscene.  This collection encompasses both of the more specific collections #$PornographicPicture and #$EroticStory.")
(comment emptiesInto "(#$emptiesInto RIV WAT) means that the instance of #$Stream RIV flows into WAT, an instance of #$BodyOfWater that is not an instance of #$Stream.  Examples: (#$emptiesInto #$AmazonRiver #$AtlanticOcean); (#$emptiesInto #$HuangHeRiver #$YellowSea).")
(comment AnatomicalVessel "The collection of all anatomical vessels in #$Animals.  Instances of this collection are tubular animal tissue which acts as a conduit for body fluids or substances passing into or out of the body.")
(comment SportsTeamTypeBySport "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$SportsTeam whose instances are all of the same sport.")
(comment PlantingAField "The collection of events in which a field is planted.")
(comment PomPom "Something cheerleaders shake while cheering")
(comment MeteorologicalRADAR "RADAR devices used to gather information about weather conditions.")
(comment Rubidium "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of rubidium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment physicalLogicalTableMap "(#$physicalLogicalTableMap ?PT ?LT) means that the #$LogicalTable ?LT is the information content of the particular #$PhysicalDBTable, ?PT.")
(comment intervalBeforeOfDuration "(#$intervalBeforeOfDuration INT TEMP-OBJ  QUANT) means that INT is the instance of #$TimeInterval that is of duration QUANT immediately preceding TEMP-OBJ .")
(comment ThrillerMovie "#$ThrillerMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW, each of which relates a thrilling story.")
(comment salientURL "(#$salientURL THING URL) means that the information contained at the #$UniformResourceLocator URL, is salient to #$Thing.  Salience is a function of the microtheory that the #$salientURL assertion is placed in.  For example, in the #$WebSearchEnhancementMt, an eCyc search which returned URL would count as a good hit for a query that disambiguates to THING.  If URL points to something which most internet saavy people would refer to as ``the homepage for'' THING, then #$homepage is a more appropriate predicate to use.  Note that URL is assumed to be a publicly accessible entity on the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource.  Thus, pointers to documents on the cycorp internal filesystem are not legitimate values for URL.  For such documents #$salientCycorpPathname is appropriate.  Where possible please use the more descriptive predicate #$salientURLPrintString rather than #$salientURL. (#$BillJ 1/20/2000)")
(comment Em "A unit of distance whose length is the same as the width of the letter M in any font.")
(comment AttachingResultFn "(#$AttachingResultFn ATTACHING) denotes the attachment situation that results from the attaching event ATTACHING.")
(comment ailmentAcquiredBy "#$ailmentAcquiredBy is the most general predicate available for identifying ways that an entity can acquire an ailment.  Thus (#$ailmentAcquiredBy ILLNESSTYPE ORGANISMTYPE EVENTTYPE) says that instances of ORGANISMTYPE can become afflicted with ILLNESSTYPE via instances of EVENTTYPE.  To identify the most common ways, use the more specific #$ailmentTypicallyAcquiredBy.")
(comment ReceivingAWave "A specialization of #$Receiving.  Each instance of #$ReceivingAWave is an event in which an instance of #$WavePropagation (q.v.) is received at some location (the location is related to the instance of #$WavePropagation by the predicate #$toLocation).  Instances of #$ReceivingAWave include a CD player receiving an infrared signal from a remote control, a person hearing a sound of distant thunder, and a radio telescope receiving signals from a celestial body.")
(comment WidthFn "(#$WidthFn OBJ) denotes the Width of OBJ.")
(comment WeightGainingProcess "A collection of events and a subset of #$WeightChangingProcess.  Each instance of          #$WeightLosingProcess is an event in which the weight of the #$objectOfStateChange           increases.")
(comment CorpusCallosum "The collection of all corpora callosa.  An individual #$CorpusCallosum is a unique part of a #$Brain which connects the two #$CerebralHemispheres.")
(comment OpeningBorders "The collection of events where one state formally acknowledges the fact that citizens from another state can enter their territory.")
(comment Bacterium-Amphitrichous "The collection of #$Bacterium whose instances have two flagella, on opposite ends.")
(comment Entertainer "#$Entertainer is a specialization of #$EntertainmentOrArtsProfessional.  Each instance of #$Entertainer is a person whose job it is to entertain people, i.e., to perform for an audience (live or via a recording) in an attempt to distract them from their worries and make them laugh, cry, smile, get excited, etc.")
(comment InternalSecurityArmoredVehicle "A collection. Internal security armored military vehicles.")
(comment CommunicationConvention "The collection of conventions used to encode and interpret things which bear information; a syntax together with a semantic mapping.  Instances include natural languages like French or English, database data formats, and computer languages or idiosyncratic systems of gestures or symbols known only by a small group of people.")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent ConstructionProject)
(comment TransportationAccommodation "The collection of all #$ServiceEvents that are recieved by #$passengers during #$TransportationEvents.  For example, the services that are recieved during an airplane flight might include being served drinks and food, being offered a newspaper, being given a blanket, headphones, etc.  The collection of all these events is represented as (#$TransportationAccommodationFn #$AirplaneTrip), which is a subset of #$TransportationAccommodation.")
(comment SatireMovie "A film in which the point is to send up or skewer an aspect of society, a type of person, and/or established, often-sacred, beliefs. A tricky, often difficult style to pull off with success, satire is as much an attitude as a movie type. These films rely on precision timing, from both actors and directors, while utilizing irony, cynicism and sarcasm as a primary tool. In the best examples of the form, deadpan humor, in which the characters take themselves and their situations very seriously, is favored while the director or screenwriter winks knowingly at the audience.")
(comment UtilityCompany "The collection of all businesses that provide access to and/or sell electricity, gas, water and/or sewer service, telephone service, garbage collection service and similar services to the public.  Many instances of #$UtilityCompany are government-regulated.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-Worm "#$AttackByComputerOperation-Worm is the collection of all attacks by programs from the collection #$ComputerWorm.")
(comment Watercraft-Surface "A specialization of #$Watercraft.  Each instance of #$Watercraft-Surface is a watercraft designed to travel across the suface of a body of water.  Note that instances of #$Watercraft-Surface need not be designed to travel _exclusively_ across the surface of a body of water, since some instances may also be designed to travel under the surface of a body of water (for example, instances of #$Submarine are designed to travel in both these ways).  Notable specializations of #$Watercraft-Surface include #$Canoe, #$Ferry, #$Motorboat, and #$OceanLiner.")
(comment Estradiol "An #$Estrogen produced in the #$Ovary-AnimalBodyPart. Found in the #$Urine of pregnant females. #$Estradiol found in the #$Urine of mares is the source of commercial forms of this #$Hormone.")
(comment Staphylococcus "The bacteria that are responsible for boils on the skin.")
(comment ProjectileShell-Blast "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is designed to achieve  target damge primarily from blast effect.  When a high explosive detonates,  it is coverted almost instantly into a gas at very high pressure and  temperature.")
(disjointWith Volatility-Physical ElectricalCharge)
(comment chanceForRoleBecauseIs "(#$chanceForRoleBecauseIs AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP VAL) means
that in the context of the assertion, the chance for AGENT playing
ROLE in a situation of type EVTTYPE is VAL because PROP is true in the
context of the assertion.")
(disjointWith AudioSystem AudioSystemComponent)
(comment complementaryNucleicAcidSequences "(#$complementaryNucleicAcidSequences SEQ1 SEQ2) means that that SEQ1

and SEQ2 are lists of nucleotides such that the nucleotides that

compose SEQ2 complement the nucleotides that compose SEQ1, and vice

versa.  Another way to think of this: given that

(#$complementaryNucleicAcidSequences SEQ1 SEQ2), if someone were to replace every

nucleotide in SEQ1 with its complementary nucleotide (i.e., the nucleotide with which it forms a complementary base pair), the result would

be SEQ2, and if someone were to replace every nucleotide in SEQ2 with

its complementary nucleotide, the result would be SEQ1.")
(comment InstanceLevelScriptMicrotheory "Microtheories of this type should detail an event by giving a list of subevents and temporal orderings of these subevents. Such microtheories should also contain a claim of what type of event the collection of subevents is supposed to be an instance of. See cyclistNotes on SubeventSequenceGraphMt for a method of conformity checking scripts with their script type in terms of temporal ordering.")
(comment itemRequested "(itemRequested ?REQUEST ?ITEM) means that ?REQUEST is a request for ?ITEM.")
(comment MaupintourVacationPackage "The collection of all instances of #$VacationPackage sold by
#$MaupintourTravelAgency.")
(comment ShippingSystemFn "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction that when applied to an instance of #$GeographicalRegion denotes the system of shipping lanes within that region.  (#$ShippingSystemFn REGION) denotes the system of shipping lanes such that each of its links is within REGION.  That is, each instance of #$ShippingLane, LANE, such that (#$linksOfCustomarySystem (#$ShippingSystemFn REGION) LANE) is true, is within REGION.  See #$CustomarySystemOfLinks and #$PathArtifactSystem.")
(comment SuperconductorResistance "An instance of #$ElectricalResistance. #$SuperconductorResistance is the level of electrical resistance found in objects which have absolutely no resistance to the passage of electricity (i.e., in objects that are instances of #$Superconductor).")
(comment Hepatitis-VirusType "A collection of collections. Instances of #$Hepatitis-VirusType
are specs of #$Virus of which instances are responsible for one of the main
specs of #$ViralHepatitis. Note that this is a spec of
#$OrganismClassificationType. The main instances are collections of
hepatitis A, B, C, D and E viri.")
(comment PerspectiveMicrotheory "The collection of Microtheories that each represent the propositional beliefs of a particular perspective.  A #$PerspectiveMicrotheory is the view of facts generally taken by someone or something in a particular role or type of role.  The propositions in a #$PerspectiveMicrotheory are true from the perspective of the thing in that role.  Examples include: #$AudiencePerspectiveMt, #$WorkerPerspectiveMt, #$RecipientOfServicePerspectiveMt, #$ProviderOfServicePerspectiveMt, #$PassengerPerspectiveMt, #$DriverPerspectiveMt, etc.")
(comment EmittingStuff "The emission process. The entity that does the emission does not change its identity because of the emission.")
(comment securedBy-Contributing "A generalization of both #$securedBy and #$supportedBy-Contributing. (#$securedBy-Contributing OBJECT HOLDER) means that HOLDER at least contributes to OBJECT's maintaining its current position.  If HOLDER were to be removed, then (everything else being equal) OBJECT would at least be held less securely overall than before.  (OBJECT might even actually move, but this is not necessary.)  Examples: a building is #$securedBy-Contributing an individual pile underneath it and a hot air balloon might be #$securedBy-Contributing each one of several ropes holding it to the ground.  If, like the house pile, HOLDER contributes to the _vertical_ support of OBJECT, consider using #$supportedBy-Contributing.  If HOLDER is _crucial_ to OBJECT's being secured, consider using #$securedBy.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice PathArtifactSystem)
(comment ClusterBomb "The collection of #$Bombs that are designed to break into a number of smaller #$Bombs creating a large area of damage at the expense of precision.")
(comment TimePointAtDistanceBeforeEndOf "(#$TimePointAtDistanceBeforeEndOf INT EVT) is the  #$TimePoint that is exactly INT prior to the ending of  EVT.  For example, (#$TimePointAtDistanceBeforeEndOf     (#$HoursDuration 1) MyFlightToConnecticut)  is the #$TimePoint that is exactly 1 hour before  my flight to Connecticut ends.")
(comment presupposes "Presupposition should be distinguished from precondition or
logical consequence.  If in normal unreflective use of natural language,
as a general rule the assertion of PROP1 and the assertion of the negation
of PROP1 both at least strongly suggest the truth of PROP2, then PROP1
presupposes PROP2. If there are any presuppositions at all, there
 is a unique PROP2 such that (#$presupposes PROP1 PROP2) and that is the
conjunction of all the presuppositions of PROP1.  A precondition for my
eating rice might be that some farmer planted the rice, but an assertion
that I did not eat the rice does not suggest anything about farmers.
Another precondition might be that I was hungry, but if I did not eat the
rice it is not suggested that I was hungry. Rather the contrary is more
nearly likely to be true.  But if I say I did not know that Fermat's
theorem has been proven, there is a presupposition that Fermat's theorem
has been proven.  That presupposition could be cancelled by the assertion
`The supposed proof is invalid.'")
(comment RanitidineHydrochloride "The chemical compound which is used to treat peptic acid problems.")
(comment underlyingAsset "The predicate used to specify what type of #$TradeableSecurity is the underlying asset for some #$OptionTransactionAgreement (option).  For example (#$underlyingAsset OPTION (#$StockInFn CORP)) means that OPTION is an option to buy or sell some amount of (#$StockInFn CORP).  The value therefore of OPTION depends upon the value of CORP's #$Stock.")
(comment Dirt "A type of soil. Instances of #$Dirt are composed of humus and disintegrated rock.")
(comment MachineGun-Portable "A collection.  Each instance is a #$Gun-Portable which can fire bullets continuously and rapidly.")
(comment Animation-AdultAudience "The collection of animated moving images that contain story-lines and visuals targetted at adult viewers.  As such, this includes (possibly among other things) cartoons with pornographic or realistically violent content.  Examples include Fritz the Cat (based on the Robert Crumb character) and #$HeavyMetal-TheMovie.")
(comment CeleryPlant "Individual celery plants")
(comment Gaseous-StateOfMatter "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible and an instance of #$MatterTypeByPhysicalState. Each instance of #$Gaseous-StateOfMatter is an object of a single chemical species in the gaseous state of matter. Objects in the gaseous state of matter are at a high enough temperature or low enough pressure for the type of matter involved that the molecules are not bonded even weakly to their neighbors, and readily break free. Gaseous objects are characterized at the macroscopic level by having diffuse boundaries (when outside of containers), no shape independent of a container, and by great expandability and compressibility. Examples of things that typically have this attribute are: the helium in a child's balloon; the oxygen in Earth's atmosphere; the water vapor in Earth's atmosphere.")
(comment SlangSpeech "Word senses of words or phrases which may be considered slang. Slang is typically informal, non-standard vocabulary. Many slang words are relatively new, or have been revived. Slang is NOT the same as #$Jargon.")
(disjointWith UnderwaterLocation GeoculturalRegion)
(comment CuttingOffAPiece "This is the collection of events in which something is cut into two distinct pieces, one of which (the #$objectOfStateChange) can be said to remain the same kind of object it was, while the other (the #$objectRemoved) is regarded as a part that is removed. Thus when a branch is pruned off a tree, the tree remains a tree afterwards, and the branch has been removed, but cutting down the tree leaves two pieces, neither of which could be called a tree, so that would not be an instance of #$CuttingOffAPiece.")
(comment NITBasketballTournament-PostSeason "The National Invitational Tournament in basketball, held every year after the regular season.")
(comment Erotica "The collection of #$InformationBearingThings whose intention is artistic and whose theme is #$SexualBehavior. This includes not only some #$ArtObjects, but also some literary works, films, and dances. What some consider #$Erotica others may consider #$PornographicMaterial.")
(comment LandingCraft-AirCushioned "The collection of air-cushioned landing craft. These craft are intended for use in transporting weapon systems, equipment, cargo, and personnelboth from ship to shore and across the beach.")
(comment BacterialRNAType "A collection of collections. Instances are kinds of #$RNAMolecule
produced by instances of #$Bacterium.")
(comment PastPerfectFn "(#$PastPerfectFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-TIME) denotes the subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances end before the starting of CONTEXT-TIME.")
(comment RequestingAction "A collection of actions, many of which are speech acts.  In each element of this collection, somebody requests that some #$Action other than to be given some object(s) be performed. The #$IllocutionaryForce associated with this action is #$Request.")
(comment commonRelation "(#$commonRelation RELN) means that RELN is a very commonly used relationship in all of the Cyc contexts which access the context in which the formula is asserted.")
(comment IFVMechanizedInfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of infantry units employing Infantry Fighting Vehicles. (See M2InfantryFightingVehicle.)")
(comment keyIngredientTypes "(#$keyIngredientTypes COMPOSITE INGREDIENT-TYPE) means that (#$ingredients COMPOSITE INGREDIENT) for some instance INGREDIENT of INGREDIENT-TYPE and that an instance of INGREDIENT-TYPE is or instances of INGREDIENT-TYPE are key or featured ingredients in COMPOSITE. A \"key\" ingredient need not be the #$mainConstituent -- water is the #$mainConstituent of most alcholic beverages, however, #$EthylAlcohol and not #$Water is a #$keyIngredientTypes.  It is not required that there be a unique #$keyIngredientTypes (one can sensibly ask the question \"what are the main ingredients in ... ?\").")
(comment Diarrhea "Abnormally frequent or liquid bowel movements.")
(comment EnlargementSurgery "Surgery whose goal is to increase the size of some body part.")
(comment HumanAttributeTesting "Collection of testing events that involve evaluation of some human attribute.  Intelligence, personality, and physical skill testing events are specs of this collection.")
(comment kakeTemplateFileName "(kakeTemplateFileName TEMPLATE NAME) means that the #$KakeTemplate TEMPLATE
          has the file name NAME.  Normally, Kake templates are stored in a standard
          directory on a file system, so the full path should not be included.  For
          example, say (kakeTemplateFileName SomeKakeTemplate 'some.kt'), not
          (kakeTemplateFileName SomeKakeTemplate '/usr/local/www/cgi-bin/kake-files/some.kt').")
(comment ProcessingRefinedOil "A #$ChemicalProcessing event.  Here, the components separated out in refining crude oil are further processed to create some #$PetroleumProduct-Refined.")
(comment GourmetGiftBasket "An instance of #$GiftBasketTypeByContent.  The collection of #$GiftBaskets that are filled with gourmet foods.")
(comment SignalInterceptionUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on           the interception of EM signals.")
(comment Tet-SouthVietnam-VietnamWarEra "#$Tet-SouthVietnam-VietnamWarEra is the collection of all instances of #$Tet-LunarNewYear celebrated in #$SouthVietnam between approximately 1955 to 1975.")
(disjointWith SportsCategoryType SpecifiedGameType)
(disjointWith PrepaidTelephoneCard SocialSecurityCard)
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType HumanCapabilityType)
(comment ChristianMoralCode "The code of conduct one normally associates

 with christian religious morality (as codified in the Ten Commandments say, and the

Golden Rule).")
(comment Sliding-LowFriction "Elements of #$Sliding-LowFriction are sliding processes (see #$Sliding-Generic) for which the friction involved is low.  By contrast, elements of #$Rubbing are sliding processes for which the friction involved is high.  The main motivation for creating this unit is to provide a denotation for the usual sense of the word `slide'.  In cases where one just intends to indicate two objects sliding past each other with no implications about relative friction level see #$Sliding-Generic.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink IBTGeneration)
(comment WindEnergy "energy of the atmosphere in motion.  Can be harnessed by windmills, turbines...")
(comment DarkLargeArea-Topographical "The collection of all large area topographical features noted for significantly lower albedo than surrounding terrain.")
(comment Auctioning "The collection of #$SalesActivity(s) in which an auctioneer offers property to the highest bidder.  In contrast, every #$Auction-Event is a #$SocialOccurrence including at least one instance of #$Auctioning as a #$subEvents.  The auctioneer is typically the #$sellingAgent, rather than the #$seller.")
(comment AcceptingAnInvitation "The collection of acknowledgements in which an invitation is accepted.")
(comment VisitingSiteFn "(#$VisitingSiteFn ATTR) denotes the collection of  visits to the tourist attraction ATTR.  See also, #$SightseeingOfFn and #$SightseeingInFn.  Note that (#$VisitingSiteFn ATTR) denotes an instance of #$TemporalObjectType while (#$SightseeingOfFn ATTR) and (#$SightseeingInFn CITY) would denote instances of #$TemporalStuffType.")
(comment SurfaceToSurfaceMissile "The collection of all missiles (instances of #$Missile) which launch from platforms on the Earth's surface (located on 

land or on water) and are intended to attack targets on the Earth's surface (located on land or water).")
(comment RadioMediaProduct "A collection of  #$ConceptualWorks created for the purposes of #$RadioBroadcasting.")
(comment (VersusFn intendedPrimaryFunction behaviorCapable) "#$primaryFunction assumes that arg1 has a primary function from the viewpoint of some sentient agent.  Almost always a set of humans.  To be agnostic about such intent, use #$behaviorCapable.  For example, one may wish to assert that #$Chute-SlopingPath is capable of being #$instrument-Generic in some #$GuidanceProcess, regardless of whether there are people around, or whether there is a god, etc..  If so, #$behaviorCapable is the predicate to use.")
(comment workStationDevice "the main device of this workstation")
(disjointWith DefenseSystem MineShaft)
(comment distanceInBlocksOfStreet "This predicate relates two things located in a 
city or town in terms of the number of blocks away they 
are from each other.  (#$distanceInBlocksOfStreet OBJ1 OBJ2 N)
means that in order to get from OBJ1 to OBJ2 by the shortest
route using city streets, one must travel a total of N 
instances of #$BlockOfStreet.  OBJ1 and OBJ2 must each be
#$onPath some instance or other of #$Street-Generic, and if
they are on different streets, those streets must be (directly
or indirectly) connected to each other within the same 
#$StreetSystem.  Since the lengths of street blocks vary 
considerably, a given distance in street blocks cannot be 
generally associated with any specific absolute distance.  
Still, this predicate is useful for rough estimates of, and 
comparisons between, distances.")
(comment WillDissolve "Has greater than #$Insoluble solubility.")
(comment oilExport "This predicate denotes the amount or rate of oil exported by a country.
Among other things, this quantity is dependent on the amount of oil that
a country produces (see #$oilProduction).")
(comment Meme "#$Memes are cognitive or behavioral patterns which may be replicated from one mind or mental substrate to another.  As genes are thought to be the instructional building blocks of life, #$Memes are said to be an analogously fundamental part of culture.  Like organisms, #$Memes are said to compete with each other for mental resources.  Examples of #$Memes include neologisms, fads, and email viruses.")
(comment Place-NonAgent "A collection of places which are not agent-like.  Some things can be both places and exhibit agency; e.g., the #$CityOfMiamiFL is a region in #$Florida-State, and it also can enter into agreements with other cities (see #$GeopoliticalEntity).  Each instance of #$Place-NonAgent is a #$Place that does NOT have any agency, e.g., #$LakeErie and #$OuterSpace.")
(comment Hypochlorite-Salt "A collection of instances of a salt or ester of hypochlorous
acid (see #$HypochlorousAcid).")
(comment Circus "An on-the-road organization of performers, including animals, lion tamers, tightrope walkers, trapeze artists, etc.")
(comment connectedAlongAlignedLengths "(#$connectedAlongAlignedLengths OBJ1 OBJ2) means that #$LongAndThin OBJ1 is connected along its length (#$connectedAlongLength) to #$LongAndThin OBJ2 and vice versa.")
(comment EukaryoticGene "The collection of #$Gene-HereditaryUnits found in #$EukaryoticCells,the cellular components of #$EukaryoticOrganisms.")
(comment PlanBackgroundContext-SitSpec "A specialization of #$PlanBackgroundContext and #$SituationSpecificationMicrotheory.  Each instance of #$PlanBackgroundContext-SitSpec is a microtheory in which a _particular_ situation relevant to some plan generation is described. Thus, the objects described in the microtheory should by and large be individuals, rather than collections. Microtheories containing descriptions of classes of objects that are relevant to plan generation should be made instances of #$PlanBackgroundContext-General, not #$PlanBackgroundContext-SitSpec.")
(comment expectedTimeToTraverse "(#$expectedTimeToTraverse VEHICLETYPE PATH DURATION) means
that it is anticipated that instances of VEHICLETYPE will take
DURATION to completely traverse PATH in the context in which this
assertion is made.")
(comment AmphibiousVehicle "The collection of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicles that can cross land as well as water. Some instances are #$Ships that have special means to go on land #$AmphibiousCargoShip whereas others are #$LandTransportationDevices that can 'swim' accross water, e.g. #$ArmoredPersonnelCarrier-M113. ")
(comment DisplayingFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which a particular class of things is displayed.")
(comment LowLevelOfCommunicability "This infection may be contagious. There is a small but existing
chance to get infected if conditions of transmission are met.")
(comment GRWrestlingSportsEvent "Greco-Roman wrestling")
(comment (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice) "A collection of events.  An instance of (#$TransportViaFn #$TransportationDevice) is a #$TransportationEvent in which the #$transporter is a #$TransportationDevice; e.g., driving a car, riding a train, sending scientific instruments to Mars on an unmanned space probe.")
(comment kePrecisionSuggestion "(#$kePrecisionSuggestion FORMULA PRECISE) states that PRECISE is a formula which is a plausible suggestion for a more precise version of FORMULA.  If PRECISE were true, it should imply FORMULA.  See also #$keGeneralizationSuggestion.")
(disjointWith Canoe Dinghy)
(comment PersonTypeByFacetedActivityType "#$PersonTypeByFacetedActivityType is a collection of collections. Each element is an instance of #$PersonTypeByActivity that itself has been faceted in at least one way. This collection, which facets #$Person,can be used to generate English questions to aid classification in a clarification dialogue. To make the interface user-friendly, the range of answers to these questions should be small. Since this collection currently (01/00) has fewer than 20 elements, it will be more useful than the faceting of #$Person by #$PersonTypeByActivity, which has over 800 instances. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(comment AircraftCarrier "The collection of large warships that are capable of transporting airplanes.  These ships have large, flat decks for take-offs and landings and serve as floating air bases for military aircraft.")
(comment xzCrossSectionShapeType "The cross section shape type in the xz plane.")
(comment ScudTEL "Military vehicles used to transport, erect and launch SCUD missiles.")
(comment PrecisionFarming "Precision farming utilizes information technologies

                        such as differential global positioning systems (DGPS) and

                        geographic information system software (GIS) to

                        gather, store, view, and analyze vast amounts of data

                        - which can then be converted into usable

                        knowledge to make better farm management

                        decisions for crop production.")
(comment PsychedelicMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic whose heyday was the mid-to-late 1960s.
  Often uses reverberation, feedback, and other forms of distortion as special
  effects.  The lyrics of #$PsychedelicMusic songs often treat of altered states of
  consciousness, mysticism, love, and peace.  It later became associated with the
  #$Hippie movement.  Influential practitioners of this style include the 13th Floor
  Elevators, the Byrds, Jefferson Airplane, the (mid-period) Beatles, and (early)
  Pink Floyd.")
(comment FormulaArityFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  When applied to a #$CycLFormula FORM, #$FormulaArityFn returns the number of arguments given to the relation (an instance of #$Relation (q.v.)) appearing in the initial (\"arg0\") argument place of FORM.")
(comment Heat-FixedSmear "A collection of heat-fixed smears on slides.  These are made
by mixing cells from a pure culture with water and allowing to dry on
a slide.  The slide is then fixed by passing through a bunsen flame
twice.  The slide may now be stained and examined under a
microscope.")
(comment ExistentialQuantifier "A specialization of #$Quantifier (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ExistentialQuantifier can be used to make a certain kind of assertion regarding the existence of some thing(s) meeting a specified criterion.  For example, `(#$thereExistAtLeast 9 ?X (#$isa ?X #$Cat))' means that there exist at least nine cats.  Other instances of this collection are #$thereExists and #$thereExistExactly.  Cf. #$forAll.")
(disjointWith ProgrammingAComputer Archery)
(comment ImagesByArtistFn "#$ImagesByArtistFn takes as argument any instance of #$Artist-Visual and returns the collection of all #$VisualInformationBearingThings depicting works by that artist.  For example, (#$ImagesByArtistFn PabloPicasso) would return the collection of all VisualInformationSources, such as prints, slides, and online reproductions, depicting any work by Picasso.")
(comment CycEasyDocDescription "The collection of all Cyc 'EasyDocumentDescriptions'; each instance is a #$List of #$CharacterStrings and other things that together, in their order, specify the format of a document.  HTML forms are allowed in the list.  The system for defining these is the #$CycEasySyntaxSystem.")
(comment FastCombatStoreShip "A collection. Military fast combat store ships.")
(comment Southwest-Generally "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-General (q.v.).  From a given reference point, #$Southwest-Generally comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees (in either horizontal direction) of #$Southwest-Directly.")
(comment notablePeaksInThisGroup "important peaks in a given group of mountains")
(comment comparableRanks "(#$comparableRanks RANK1 ORGTYPE1 RANK2 ORGTYPE2) means that
RANK1 inthe rank hierarchy of ORGTYPE1 is parallel with or comparable
to RANK2 in ORGTYPE2, to the extent that whatever RANK1 authorizes a
holder of that rank to do in ORGTYPE1, RANK2 authorizes a holder of
that rank to do in ORGTYPE2.  Note that ORGTYPE1 and ORGTYPE2 must be instances of #$MilitaryOrgTypeByGeoAndBOS.")
(comment standardVehicleOfUnitTypeCount "(#$standardVehicleOfUnitTypeCount ?UNITTYPE ?VEHICLETYPE ?NUMBER) means that under 'ordinary' or 'normal' circumstances we would expect to find an instance of ?UNITTYPE equipped with exactly ?NUMBER #$TransportationDevices of type ?VEHICLETYPE.")
(comment SkinHead "The collection of all white laced (i.e. nazi ideology) skinheads.")
(comment BiologicalAttack-Anti-Animal "The collection of all #$BiologicalAttacks for which the intended, primary targets are #$NonPersonAnimals.  In the typical case, one would direct such an attack against the livestock of one's enemy, in order to cause economic devastation, hunger problems, or to spread an infectious disease indirectly to people.")
(comment Guitar-12String "Instances are instances of #$Guitar-Acoustic that have twelve strings, that is, 6 pairs of strings.  These guitars produce a lovely soft sound.")
(comment physicallyOverlaps "The predicate #$physicallyOverlaps relates two partially tangible objects. (#$physicallyOverlaps PT-1 PT-2) means that PT-1 and PT-2 share a common physical part PT-3 (that is, both (#$physicalParts PT-1 PT-3) and (#$physicalParts PT-2 PT-3) hold) .")
(comment TouchPerception "The collection of sensory-perceptual events (#$Perceivings) in which a #$PerceptualAgent perceives (acquires information) by touch.")
(comment ExtraMaritalSexualBehavior "The collection of all instances of #$SexualBehavior in which at least one of the participants is #$Married, and at least one of the other participants is not that person's #$spouse.")
(comment PhysicalForce-Weak "This is the #$PhysicalForceType which acts within atomic nuclei and is responsible for

radioactive decay. It has recently been \"unified\" with the #$PhysicalForce-Electromagnetic. This

multi-aspect force is called the Electro-Weak Force. See #$PhysicalForce-ElectroWeak.")
(comment Waterspout-Tornado "The collection of all tornados [#$TornadoAsObject] which touch down over water.  They comprise a whirling mass of rising water under a #$CumulonimbusCloud or towering #$CumulusCloud.")
(comment ReversibleReformulation "A property of reformulator rules.  A reformulator rule RULE having
the property #$ReversibleReformulation is such that:  If RULE, when 
applied in the forward direction (backward direction) to a given 
expression PRE-FORM, yields the expression POST-FORM, then RULE, 
when applied in the backward direction (forward direction) to POST-FORM, 
yields PRE-FORM.")
(comment CavityOrContainer "The collection of all cavities, containers, and hollow

objects. An instance of #$CavityOrContainer spatially subsumes a hollow space region, and might include as #$physicalParts either no enclosing walls (#$CavityInteriorRegion), just the inside surface of the walls (#$CavityWithWalls), or the complete walls (#$ContainerShapedObject).

#$Containers, such as coffee cups, buildings or stomachs, have well-defined outside walls.  Instances of #$Cavity such as caves

and rooms do not have well-defined outside walls. #$CavityOrContainer

was reified since certain properties hold true of both instances of

#$Container and of #$Cavity, and since we wish to use certain

predicates interchangeably. For example, we wish to use the same

predicate, #$pipeEndsAtCavity for talking about relationships holding

between esophagi and stomachs in addition to that which holds between

hallways and rooms.")
(comment Pressure "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Pressure is a specific measure of a force exerted on some surface.  Degrees of #$Pressure may be represented using #$GenericValueFunctions or with qualitative collections (e.g., #$BruisingPressure, #$FracturingPressure, #$ImperceptiblePressure).   Indicate the #$Pressure of a particular fluid with the predicate #$fluidPressure (q.v.); indicate atmospheric pressure with #$barometricPressure (q.v.).")
(comment AirplanePilot "Person who has been trained to fly certain kinds of aircraft, and

does so regularly on a professional basis.  Strictly speaking, a

collection of temporal subabstractions of people, where the time

interval involved in each case is the duration of professional

service.")
(comment CongenitalCondition "A specialization of #$PhysiologicalCondition.  Each instance of #$CongenitalCondition is a physiological condition that is present in an organism from the time of gestation (i.e. before birth). Instances of #$CongenitalCondition may be genetic conditions (see the specialization #$GeneticCondition) or they may be caused by the behavior of the mother during pregnancy (for example, as in a case of congenital heroin addiction).")
(comment NorthWesternRegionFn "A unary function that returns the `northwestern region' of           an instance of #$GeographicalThing. What counts as the           `northwestern region' is contextually determined. Some of the           factors influencing the determination may be local           geography, cultural identity, and political considerations.")
(comment TransferOut "A specialization of #$GeneralizedTransfer.  #$TransferOut includes all instances of #$GeneralizedTransfer in which some object plays the role of #$from-Generic, but in which there may or may not be any object playing the role of #$to-Generic.  At the start of a #$TransferOut, the object playing the role of #$transferredThing is 'located' at the object playing the role of #$from-Generic.  The collection #$TransferOut includes, among other things, all instances of the collections #$Emission, #$LosingUserRights, and #$DistributionEvent.  Negative examples of #$TransferOut include some instances of #$AppropriatingSomething (when there is no previous owner) and some instances of #$Hearing (when the sounds may come from various unspecified locations).")
(comment surfaceObject "The object along whose surface a #$Motion-SolidAgainstSolid process goes on")
(comment Step-PersistenceDistribution "Each instance of this collection is an object consisting of parameters which together indicate the probability of an assertion or set of assertions being true.  The parameters define a step-like distribution contour (graph).  The parameters are specified using the predicates #$stepLocation, #$stepInitialValue, and #$stepFinalValue.")
(comment PolarDay "The collection of all multiday periods in which the #$Sun remains visible (ignoring cloud cover) above the #$Horizon in a polar region.  Every instance of #$PolarDay necessarily includes at least one instance of #$MidnightSun.  Every #$PolarDay intersects a #$CalendarSpring and #$CalendarSummer and is #$temporallyDisjoint from any #$CalendarAutumn and #$CalendarWinter.")
(comment ClavulanatePotassium "A chemical compound which is used in injectable antibiotic products.")
(comment Translation-BackAndForth "The #$objectMoving in a #$Translation-BackAndForth periodically translates back and forth along a path. Neither end of the path is a #$toLocation or a #$fromLocation, because an instance of #$Translation-BackAndForth can begin or end at either location, or even at another location on the path between them. Examples include the movement of the weight at the bottom of a swinging pendulum, or of a shuttle bus making repeated round trips between downtown and the airport. Each 'period' of the movement must begin and end at roughly the same location, and is thus an instance of #$Translation-RoundTrip. #$Translation-RoundTrip is not, however, a subcollection of #$Translation-BackAndForth, because a single round trip is not enough to establish periodicity. For periodic rotation back and forth around an axis, see #$PeriodicReversingRotation.")
(comment exportToQuotaDuring "(#$exportToQuotaDuring REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2 THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the export quota of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE for the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 to the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (Of course, the existence of export quotas is the exception rather than the rule.)  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  In the case of oil exports, for example, AMOUNT might be a #$Volume (a number of barrels) indicating the total quantity of oil REGION1 is allowed to export to REGION2.  Alternatively, AMOUNT might be a #$Rate, characterizing the average rate of export, under the quota, of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by REGION1 to REGION2 during the temporal extent of THING.  Oil exports, for example, might be expressed in terms of so many million barrels per day.")
(comment FormalLecture-IBT "The collection of formal lectures -- i.e., teaching events in which a teacher delivers a #$Lecture-CW.")
(comment HousePlan "The collection of #$ArchitecturalPlans which act as specifications for building houses. Some of these plans may be #$Blueprints, but they need not be hardcopy objects. They could be created using a computer drafting program, for example.")
(comment combatForceRatioInEvent "(combatForceRatioInEvent EVENT AGENT1 AGENT2 N) means that force ratio of AGENT1's units to AGENT2's units is N.")
(comment suppliedWithFromThrough "(#$suppliedWithFromThrough PT1 COL PT2 PT3) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT3 (on their way from PT2 to PT1).  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$suppliedWithFromThrough is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  And PT3 might, for example, be a #$Hose, a #$Railway, a #$GeographicalRegion, or a #$BloodVessel.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(comment AccountsReceivableDepartment "A subset of #$AccountingDepartment; those departments responsible for              invoicing and receiving payments.")
(comment Photosynthesis-Plant "A collection of events in which plants convert energy captured from sunlight into usable chemical energy for their metabolic needs.")
(comment JudoActivity "The collection of all activities consisting of a #$Person practicing, performing, or using judo, a Japanese system of unarmed combat, now primarily a sport. See also #$JudoSportsEvent.")
(disjointWith Water Agent-Generic)
(comment SubLTemplate "#$SubLTemplate is the collection of objects which are SubL templates for denoting SubL constructions.  See also #$ExpandSubLFn.")
(comment Phytoplasma-Genus "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.")
(comment SpecifiedMagazineSeriesType "A collection of collections and a subset of MediaSeriesProductType. Every instance of MagazineSeriesType is a collection of InformationBearingThings - namely magazines - subsets of which are distributed via the mass media at regular intervals. In other words, every instance of MagazineSeriesType is a collection which is itself a collection of magazines of a certain type. For example, Esquire Magazine - that is, the collection of magazines called 'Esquire', of which a subset would be, say, Esquire Magazine, May 1998 edition - is an instance of #$SpecifiedMagazineSeriesType. An instance of Esquire Magazine, May 1998 edition would be an individual copy of that particular edition. See also MediaSeriesNthFn, MediaSeriesByDateFn.")
(comment nearestGenlMt "A specialization of #$genlMt.  (#$nearestGenlMt MT NEAR-MT) means that NEAR-MT is a \"nearest\" microtheory of which MT is a specialization.  That is, (#$genlMt MT NEAR-MT) holds, MT is not identical to NEAR-MT, and there is no reified #$Microtheory NEARER-MT distinct from MT and NEAR-MT such that both (#$genlMt MT NEARER-MT) and (#$genlMt NEARER-MT NEAR-MT) hold.  Note that #$nearestGenlMt is non-assertible (see #$notAssertible), since its extension at any given time depends upon (and so must be recomputed from) the current state of the #$genlMt hierarchy in the Cyc Knowledge Base.")
(comment valueOfExpression "(#$valueOfExpression VAL EXPRESSION) means that EXPRESSION evaluates to the value VAL.  Note that this predicate is not evaluatable.  However, it follows from #$evaluate, which is.  #$valueOfExpression provides a mechanism to retrieve cached statements about values of expressions.  This can't be done with #$evaluate since no lookup is done on that predicate.")
(comment RuralLaboringClassJoke "A subset of #$StereotypeJoke, #$RuralLaboringClassJoke is the collection of           all jokes that are based on stereotypes about rural working class people.")
(comment reformulationPrecondition "(#$reformulationPrecondition DIRECTION PRECONDITION RULE), asserted in

the microtheory MT, means that the #$CycLReformulator may only use

RULE in MT in the DIRECTION direction (reformulating the 'from' arg

into the 'to' arg) if PRECONDITION holds.  PRECONDITION must be a closed CycL query, which will be asked during reformulation, and either proven true or fail to be proven.")
(comment HoldingAnObject "The collection of #$StaticSituations in which some object acts to hold one or more other objects stationary in some reference frame.  For example, a nail may hold two boards together, a seat may hold a person in place, a person may hold an object with a hand tool.  Note that in another frame of reference the object need not be stationary. For example, one  of the subevents of a #$CarryingWhileLocomoting is a #$HoldingAnObject. Thus, although the object is moving it is stationary in relation to the #$transporter. ")
(comment Bassinet "The collection of beds for #$HumanInfants.  A #$Bassinet is a small, walled, often portable bed that can hold a baby usually from birth to about six months.")
(comment Schizophrenia "The collection of #$PsychologicalAilments distinguished by disturbances in thinking.  Such disturbances often involve a distortion of the usual logical relations among ideas, a separation between the intellect and the emotions so that feelings seem inappropriate to the situation, and a reduced tolerance for the stress of interpersonal relations with the result that the sufferer retreats from social intercourse into fantasy, delusions, and/or hallucinations.")
(comment verbSemTransPartialTemplate "(#$verbSemTransPartialTemplate COL FRAME TRANS) means that the partial translation of any verb denotation of a word denoting a specialization of COL, appearing with subcategorization frame FRAME, is TRANS.")
(comment rampStartLocation "(#$rampStartLocation RAMP LOCATION) means that the ramp-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution RAMP begins at LOCATION (a specified time or place).  For example, the LOCATION used to specify a temporal ramp persistence distribution might be (#$YearFn 1920), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the ramp distribution pertains, the likelihood of being true would start to change (start to go up or down in a ramp-like pattern) during the year 1920.")
(comment RoadSign "These are the signs one sees near roads spiked into the earth. Does not include changing traffic signals, such as #$TrafficLight.")
(comment Atoll "A coral island consisting of a reef surrounding a lagoon.")
(comment SensoryNerve "The collection of all solely sensory #$Nerves.  Each #$SensoryNerve is a #$Nerve that #$innervates a sensory #$Organ or the #$Skin or otherwise carries sensory information towards the #$Brain.  A #$Nerve which carries both sensory and motor #$Neurons (and thus signals) is a #$SensoryMotorNerve.")
(disjointWith SensoryNerve MotorNerve)
(comment AmateurSportsTeamTypeBySponsor "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$AmateurSportsTeam whose instances are all of the same sponsor.")
(comment objectFollowedInMovement "(#$objectFollowedInMovement MOVE OBJ) means that the #$objectMoving of MOVE is following OBJ during MOVE. ")
(comment Putter-GolfClub "a flat faced club used only to put the ball into the cup on a green of a hole on a golf course")
(comment MGBSet "The collection of sets which are necessary for the assembly of an Medium Girder Bridge.")
(comment PeriodicalIssue "The collection of all static textual #$MediaProducts that are part of a #$PeriodicalSeries.  Many copies are made of each #$PeriodicalIssue, the individual copies being instances of #$PeriodicalCopy.  Until the 1990s, the copies were made of #$Paper, while since the 1990s copies of instances of #$PeriodicalIssue were sometimes also (or solely) being distributed over #$ComputerNetworks.")
(comment Hafnium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Hafnium.")
(comment Secretary "Person who performs general secretarial support such as scheduling, typing, answering phones, travel arrangements etc.")
(comment RadioShackStore "A collection of all Radio Shack stores. ")
(comment ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory-LinearDenseTime "This is the sub-collection of

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory that contains all and only

those that take #$ReasoningWithTense-LogicMt-LinearDenseTime as

#$genlMt.")
(comment structurallySupportedBy "(#$structurallySupportedBy CORR SUPPORT-CORR) states that the analogical correspondence CORR is supported by the supporting correspondence SUPPORT-CORR.  See also #$correspondenceBetween and #$AnalogyCorrespondence for more.")
(comment WeightLosingProcess "A collection of events and a subset of #$WeightChangingProcess.  Each instance of          #$WeightLosingProcess is an event in which the weight of the #$objectOfStateChange           decreases.  This would happen, for instance, as a result of           #$DietingForWeightLoss.")
(comment PiaMater "The collection of all pia maters.  An instance of #$PiaMater is the innermost of the three #$Meninges surrounding the #$Brain, which it #$covers-Baglike.  The #$PiaMater is bathed in #$CerebroSpinalFluid and extends to the caudal end of the #$SpinalCord.")
(comment FormalApology "The collection of events where one state formally apologizes to another state for some conflict involving both parties.")
(comment ActorInPlays "The collection of people whose job it is to act in plays.")
(comment Harpoon-FishingDevice "A long, barbed spear, either thrown or fired from a gun,

used to catch extremely large fish or whales.")
(comment SupportVehicle "A collection. Vehicles meant to be used for support in a military context.")
(comment PolynucleotideMolecule "The collection of all long-chain molecules consisting of

multiply chained #$Nucleotides.  The collection can be reasonably

divided into the collection of #$DNAMolecules, which are composed of

pairs of #$Deoxyribonucleotides and which exhibit a helical structure,

and #$RNAMolecules, which composed of #$Ribonucleotides and which

exhibit a linear structure that sometimes folds up in complex tertiary

forms.")
(disjointWith LinguisticObject CommunicationConvention)
(comment DosagePhysicalStateType "Instance are the most general categories of dosage forms for drugs, corresponding roughly to the physical states of matter.")
(comment numberOfPrescriptionsDuring "(#$numberOfPrescriptionsDuring DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PERIOD NUM) means that NUM #$DrugPrescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE have been filled for DRUGTYPE during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be #$FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment omitFromIKB "Asserting #$omitFromIKB of a constant ensures that it will not make it into the IKB.  Note that asserting #$redo of a constant typically ensures that #$omitFromIKB will be asserted of a constant, because the following rule is asserted forward in the #$BaseKB : (#$implies (#$redo ?CYC-TERM ?STRING) (#$omitFromIKB ?CYC-TERM)).")
(disjointWith Movement-TranslationEvent TransportationAccommodation)
(comment Secretariat "A collection of suborganizations that are primarily responsible for implementing the policies of the various larger organizations of which each instance is a part.  Although a secretariat is generally administrative in nature, it also affects policy insofar as it is charged with implementing that policy.  Not every organization has a secretariat, but for those that do it plays a fairly standard role.")
(comment TeenMovie "A comprehensive #$MovieTypeByGenre aimed at and featuring teenagers or a group of teenagers as the protagonists.  Adolescent issues, growing pains, adventures, and psychological traumas are often the primary focus, with the antagonistic elements usually being other teens, adults, parents and/or themselves.")
(comment RNATypeByOrganismType "A collection of collections. Instances of #$RNATypeByOrganismType are those specializations of #$RNAMolecule, which are produced by organisms of a specific type such as an #$OrganismClassificationType.")
(comment BuildingContractor-Organization "The collection of all #$LocalOrganizations that engage in construction or remodeling activities.  Instances of #$BuildingContractor-Organization are smaller #$Organizations than #$ConstructionCompany and engage in construction activities on behalf of homeowners or small businesses.")
(disjointWith MarineCorps AirForce)
(disjointWith BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance (CollectionUnionFn (TheSet Agent-Generic (GroupFn Agent-Generic))))
(comment AirTransportationDevice "A specialization of #$TransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$AirTransportationDevice is a device used for transporting either people or cargo through the air.  Specializations of #$AirTransportationDevice include the collections #$Airplane, #$Helicopter, #$HotAirBalloon, and #$GroundToOrbitVehicle.")
(comment LuteinizingHormone "A #$Hormone produced in the #$PituitaryGland which promotes development of the interstitial cells of the testes and secretion of testosterone in males. In females, #$LuteinizingHormone promotes maturation of ovarian follicles.")
(comment ProjectileShell-Flechettes "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that carries flechettes.   Flechettes are fin stabilized steel projectiles similar in appearance to  arrows.")
(disjointWith Voltage ElectricalCharge)
(comment decreasedChanceForRoleBecause "(decreasedChanceForRoleBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP)
means that the chance of AGENT's playing the role ROLE in a situation
of type EVTTYPE is decreased because PROP is true in the reasoning
domain.")
(comment GeneticInformationTransferEvent "The collection of all events in which 'genetic information',
generally speaking, can be said to be transferred from one
'embodiment' to another.  This includes the central operations of DNA
replication (#$Replication-DNA), DNA-to-RNA transcription
(#$Transcription-DNAToRNA) and RNA-to-Protein translation
(#$Translation-RNAToProtein).")
(comment reloadTime "(#$reloadTime GUN TIME) indicates the time it takes to load GUN after it has been fired. This predicate can also be used for #$MissileLaunchers that must be loaded before launching another #$Missile. In case of #$Guns that contain more #$ProjectileSlug-Bullets the #$reloadTime is the time it takes to reload the gun when it is empty. ")
(comment itemRequested "(itemRequested ?REQUEST ?ITEM) means that ?REQUEST is a

request for ?ITEM.")
(comment RadiationResistance "A specialization of #$PhysicalAttribute.  Each instance of #$RadiationResistance is a specific capacity of a tangible object to resist radiation.  Degrees of #$RadiationResistance may be represented using #$GenericValueFunctions.  Indicate a particular object's #$RadiationResistance with the predicate #$resistanceToRadiation.")
(disjointWith PerspectiveMicrotheory SomethingExisting)
(comment NuclearFission-Uncontrolled "An unmediated chain reaction of many nuclear fission events.  Occurs in nuclear reactors when all graphic rods have been removed or in nuclear bombs. ")
(comment relevantInTime-Sometime "(#$relevantInTime-Sometime MT TIME) means that the assertions in MT are relevant sometime during the temporal extent of TIME.  See also #$relevantInTime-Always.")
(disjointWith HumanOccupationConstruct PathForWheeledVehicles)
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent Shortage)
(comment Sniper-Professional "The collection of all #$LawEnforcementOfficers , #$MilitaryPersons, and independent contractors whose job it is to shoot at (typically human) targets at fairly long range usually from a hidden and elevated vantage point using a #$Rifle.  In the case of #$LawEnforcementOfficers the task may sometimes be to disable instead of to kill, but for #$MilitaryPersons and independent contractors the task is primarily killing.  If the employer is not a #$RegionalGovernment, the occupation is illegal.")
(comment Erythromycin "The chemical compound which is an anti-infective.")
(comment under-UnderspecifiedLocation "(#$under-UnderspecifiedLocation ACT LOC) states that an abstract locational relation holds between ACT and LOC, where LOC is a #$Location-Underspecified and ACT is some action requiring some kind of abstract 'ceiling' or upper boundary. We can say 'the path ran under the highway', 'the game ran under 90 minutes' (90 minutes being an abstract location by virtue of being an abstract container), etc.")
(comment Frost "The stuff which forms thin sheets of solid water on the surface of cold object.")
(comment GatlingGun "the collection of mounted, multi-barrel #$MachineGuns

  that fire when the wheel to which the barrels

   are attached, turn.")
(comment LaunchPad "A device used for supporting and preparing a #$GroundToOrbitVehicle prior to launch.")
(comment caloricContent "(#$caloricContent STUFF MASS CAL) means that MASS of STUFF, if burned, releases CAL of energy. CAL will generally be stated using the unit function #$Calorie. For example, (#$caloricContent PeachPie001 (#$Gram 1) (#$Calorie 7)) means that PeachPie001 has 7 Calories per gram. To state the caloric content of a homogenous type of substance, for example to state that #$Water-Ingestible has 0 calories per gram, use (#$implies (#$isa ?WATER #$Water-Ingestible) (#$caloricContent ?WATER (#$Gram 1) (#$Calorie 0))). This predicate applies not only to food, but to anything that has any tangible part, and it is measured quantitatively and absolutely, with the arg3 representing the stored energy of the substance in kilocalories per MASS. If it can't burn, CAL will be equivalent to zero calories, regardless of the unit of mass. If it can burn, it will have a non-negative value for CAL. To specify the relative caloric content of food, use #$caloricContentOfFood, which allows qualitative values like High in addition to numeric values.")
(comment Stem "Stems of plants.  May be green or woody.")
(comment Night "#$Night is a specialization of #$QualitativeTimeOfDay, and it is the temporal complement of #$DaytimeHours.  Each instance of #$Night is #$contiguousAfter an instance of #$DaytimeHours, and vice versa.  Each instance of #$Night intersects two different #$CalendarDays.  Each instance of #$Night is #$temporallyStartedBy a #$Dusk, #$temporallyFinishedBy a #$Dawn, #$contiguousAfter a #$Sunset, and has a #$Sunrise which is #$contiguousAfter it.")
(comment ShipCaptain "Captain of ships.")
(disjointWith GeographicalHemisphere GeoculturalRegion)
(comment EnergyStuff "The most generic collection of all instances of all types of energy, either in radiating wave form or in solid matter form, that may be used to provide a source of energy.")
(comment NITBasketballTournament-Preseason "The preseason National Invitational Tournament in basketball, held every year prior to the regular season among 16 Division I teams, each from a different conference.")
(comment AdultVerification-Service "A collection of #$ServiceEvents. In each instance of #$AdultVerification-Service, the #$providerOfService verifies that the #$recipientOfService is an adult. Such verification is used by #$WorldWideWebSites that are intended exclusively for adults.")
(comment LandingCraftPersonnel "The collection of landing craft intended to transport personnel.")
(comment MechanizedInfantryMortarUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection infantry units employing motorized tracked vehicles and mortar-type weapons.")
(comment connected-LengthAlongSurface "(#$connected-LengthAlongSurface OBJ1 OBJ2) means that #$LongAndThin OBJ1 is #$connectedTo the surface of OBJ2 along (most of) the whole length of OBJ1 and #$aligned-LengthAlongSurface of OBJ2.")
(comment Fibromyalgia "#$Fibromyalgia affects the #$Muscles of the #$HumanBody, most specifically the #$ConnectiveTissue (tendons, ligaments, bursa, etc.). This #$ChronicCondition affects women more often than men. There is no viral, fungal, or bacterial cause known thus far. The American Medical Association recognized it as a legitimate medical condition in 1987 although descriptions of fibromyalgia-like conditions have been found as early as the 1800s. Symptoms include chronic pain and tiredness. Some theories suggest that the disorder could be a result of trauma (such as a car accident), severe stress during child birth, a prolonged period of emotional stress (such as grieving and depression), and/or that certain peoples' pain receptors may be more prone to the syndrome. It is no longer found to be true that inflammation occurs in the muscles affected; so, the name 'fibrositis' is no longer used.")
(comment Arthritis "Arthritis is characterized by stiffening and pain in joints.")
(comment Abnormal-Unusual "A normality attribute.  Used to describe things which are uncommon, unusual, abnormal,
         etc.  This attribute has no relation whatsoever to Cyc's default reasoning mechanism.  For
         that, see #$exceptWhen, #$exceptFor, and #$abnormal.")
(comment susceptibleToDiseaseCausedBy "(#$susceptibleToDiseaseCausedBy PATHOGENTYPE ORGTYPE) means
that typical instances of ORGTYPE are capable of contracting
infections caused by instances of PATHOGENTYPE.")
(comment AbleBodiedSeaman "Crew members who work on the deck.")
(comment ChocolateGiftBasket "An instance of #$GiftBasketTypeByContent.  The collection of #$GiftBaskets that are filled with #$Chocolate.")
(comment SignalInterceptionRadarUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on           intercepting radar signals.")
(comment WordsToPCW "The collection of all #$PropositionalCWTexts which are comprised of the words of the associated #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Instances are not #$CharacterStrings but the abstract words. #$PropositionalCWTexts which are not comprised of words (such as code for computer programs  [#$ComputerProgram-CWIS] which have other symbols) are not instances of #$WordsToPCW.")
(comment GettingToKnowSomeone "A collection of events, each instance of which involves two or more people getting to know about each other, through interpersonal interaction.")
(comment SandParticle "The particles of stone which make up sand (or #$SandMob).")
(comment Nationalism "A particularly strong feeling analogous to #$Patriotism. While it is possible to express #$Patriotism without disparaging other countries, #$Nationalism usually implies disdain of other countries.")
(comment SpecifiedGameType "Instances of #$SpecifiedGameType are types of games, specific as to the name and the rules used.  Each instance is a collection, a spec of #$GameEvent, whose instances are particular events in which the game is played from beginning to end.  For example, #$IndivPentathlonEvent is an instance of #$SpecifiedGameType, because all instances use the same set of rules, and consist of all the moves of a game until one of the players wins.  Not every instance of #$SpecifiedGameType has to consist of instances where there is a winner, because there might be games that don't have winners; the important thing is that the instances are by default played to completion (whatever that means for the particular type of game).  Also, not every spec of #$GameEvent is a #$SpecifiedGameType.  E.g., 'SolitaryGameEvent' (the class of games played by one person) would not be a #$SpecifiedGameType since that class isn't specific as to the name of the game and the rules used.")
(comment TaeBoExercising "The collection of all events of performing the 'Tae Bo' form of exercise.  #$TaeBoExercising was invented in the 1990's by an American #$BillyBlanks inspired by Asian martial arts techniques, and it was heavily promoted on American television as a commercial program.")
(comment rolesForEventType "A #$MetaPredicate and a typed-specialization (see #$typedGenlPreds) of #$requiredArg1Pred (q.v.). #$rolesForEventType's two argument-places are constrained to types of events and binary role predicates, respectively.  (#$rolesForEventType EVENTTYPE ROLE) means that for any instance EVENT of EVENTTYPE, there is some participant PLAYER that plays ROLE in EVENT.  That is, (ROLE EVENT PLAYER) holds.  For example, (#$rolesForEventType #$Perceiving #$perceivedThings) means that every perceiving involves something that is perceived.")
(comment MoralCodeOfConduct "The code of conduct one normally associates

 with moral behaviour (or, in the breech, immoral behaviour). This particular 

code is the basis for judgements regarding morality per se, not business ethics 

(e.g., where insider trading is unethical), legal ethics (e.g., where breaking a client's

confidentiality is unethical) and other ethical codes of conduct that may not

necessarily conflict with ideas of morality.")
(comment RecordedVideoProduct "#$RecordedVideoProduct is a specialization of #$PublishedMaterial, #$VideoRecordedObject, and #$PartiallyTangibleProduct.  Each instance of #$RecordedVideoProduct is a video recording which is one of a class of similar recordings with the same information content.")
(comment ChronicCondition "A collection of ailments.  An instance of #$ChronicCondition is an ailment that lingers or recurs in an organism throughout its life.  In some cases, the symptoms of a chronic condition may abate with treatment.  The condition may never go away completely.  #$Asthma is an example of a subcollection of #$ChronicCondition.")
(comment MetaPredicate "A subcollection of #$MetaRelation (q.v.).  Instances of #$MetaPredicate are used to make definitional (e.g. argument-type constraint or generalization) assertions about predicates (and only predicates).  As such, instances of #$MetaPredicate have (at least) one of their own argument-places (usually, but not always, the first or \"arg1\") constrained to be instances of #$Predicate (or some subcollection thereof).")
(comment valueEquals "(#$valueEquals X Y) means nothing more than X = Y, except that a
#$valueEquals assertion also #$evaluates NATs formed with an
#$EvaluatableFunction expression. This is not the intended behavior of
#$equals. Thus, the proper way to state that two #$Lists L001 and L002
have the same length would be
(#$valueEquals (#$LengthOfListFn L001) (#$LengthOfListFn L002)). If
#$valueEquals is replaced with #$equals in the previous assertion, one will
not get the correct inferential results, since #$equals will not evaluate
the denotation of the 2 NATs in argument position.")
(comment LawsAboutTypeFn "LawsAboutTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$Thing and returns the collection of laws pertaining to that things of that type. For example, (LawsAboutFn Automobile) returns the collection of all car-related laws.")
(comment QuintaryRelation "The collection of all fixed-arity relations of arity 5 (see #$arity).  The most notable specializations of #$QuintaryRelation are #$QuintaryPredicate and #$QuintaryFunction (qq.v.).")
(comment AerobicBacterium "The collection of all instances of #$Bacterium that metabolize oxygen.")
(comment Palus-Lunar "The collection of topographical features where each element is a a small plain on Earth's moon.")
(comment InformativeTVShowTypeByTopic "#$InformativeTVShowTypeByTopic is a collection of collections. Each element of #$InformativeTVShowTypeByTopic is a collection of instances of #$InformativeTVShow that are about the same topic. For example, #$TVShowOnHealth is an instance of #$InformativeTVShowTypeByTopic. Another example would be (#$SubcollectionOfAboutFn #$InformativeTVShow #$Doctor-Medical). This collection was created to make use of a faceting of #$InformativeTVShow to generate English questions to aid classification. See #$NoteAboutHowFacetAssertionsAreUsed.")
(comment Endorsing-CommunicationAct "A collection of specialized communications.  In each instance of #$Endorsing-CommunicationAct, some agent expresses a positive judgment about another agent or about a position, proposal, product, or course of action.  In endorsing, the expression of approval typically is made to some third party or parties, rather than to the agent(s) responsible---though that agent needn't be excluded.")
(comment RootAccount "A person

who has a #$UserAccount has access to account that enables her to access

storage space and CPU time on an instance of #$ComputationalSystem

that is running a Unix-like operating system.  People with access to a

#$RootAccount on a system have uncontrolled access to the files

on the system.")
(comment OphthalmicDrugProduct "Drug products intended to be used in the eyes.")
(comment visitsTo "This predicate relates an object, typically a tourist attraction, to the collection of tourist visits to that site.")
(comment ReconnaissanceVehicle "The collection of #$MilitaryVehicles used

 primarily for #$Reconnaissance-MilitaryOperation.")
(comment Capitate "The Capitate is the third of the #$Carpalia in Humans.")
(comment Mantilla "A collection of instances of #$Scarf, made of either silk or lace, and part of the traditional dress in Spain, Mexico, and Italy.")
(comment CountyGovernment "#$CountyGovernment is a specialization of #$LocalOrganization and #$RegionalGovernment.  Each instance of #$CountyGovernment is a local government that has jurisdiction over a single county.")
(disjointWith WorkStation DefenseSystem)
(comment TransportationPathSystemType "A collection of collections.  Instances of 
#$TransportationPathSystemType are collections of 
#$TransportationPathSystems.  Examples include #$RoadSystem,
#$StreetSystem, and #$GridStreetSystem.")
(comment holdsReciprocallyOf "#$holdsReciprocallyOf ?SET ?PRED means that for any two distinct elements of ?SET, ?PRED holds of them.  For example, the statement 'Todd and Erik are friends' can be represented as (#$holdsReciprocallyOf (#$TheSet #$ToddHughes #$ErikLarson) #$friends). This implies both (#$friends #$ToddHughes #$ErikLarson) and (#$friends #$ErikLarson #$ToddHughes).  If the example set contained a third member, then there would be 3!=6 total implications of that type, and so on.")
(comment outcomeOfAction "This predicate expresses the relation between an action (done in

a given circumstance) and its outcome. The statement (#$outcomeOfAction ACT

AG PROP) is true iff PROP expresses the value-relevant results of ACT, i.e.,

the results of the action that are relevant with respect to evaluation on

AG's part. Though we ultimately need this predicate to represent success

conditions for an action, we do not require here that AG be the actual

performer of ACT.")
(comment RinsingBody "Events in which the body or part of the body are rinsed.")
(comment binRelationExistsAllSpecsType "(#$binRelationExistsAllSpecsType PRED COL1 COL2 COL-TYPE) means

that for every subcollection of COL2 that are also instances of COL-TYPE, TYPE2,

there exists an instance of COL1, INS1, such that (PRED INS1 TYPE2) holds.")
(comment SewingByHand "The collection of instances of #$Sewing that are done strictly by hand.")
(comment officeInCountry "The predicate #$officeInCountry identifies a country in which a particular organization has one of its offices. (#$officeInCountry ORG COUNTRY) means that the #$Organization ORG has one of its offices in the #$Country COUNTRY.")
(disjointWith Circus FoodServiceOrganization)
(comment RapeStory "The subset of #$EroticStory whose elements contain the propositional content of an #$EroticStory in which an instance of #$Rape occurs.")
(comment backchainEncouraged "(#$backchainEncouraged PREDICATE) means that rules that conclude PREDICATE are most likely going to have to be used in order to prove literals involving PREDICATE.  In other words, when performing inferences about literals involving PREDICATE, rules that conclude PREDICATE should be heuristically favored. See also #$backchainRequired, #$backchainDiscouraged, and #$backchainForbidden.")
(comment IndependentMinorLeague-Baseball "the collection of all baseball minor leagues that are not sub-organizations of Minor League Baseball.")
(comment primingObject "(#$primingObject EVT PRIMER) means that PRIMER plays the role of primer in EVT. A primer helps to initiate some process or is used to initiate some process. In some ways #$primingObject is like #$catalyst except that there is no requirement that it remain unchanged during  EVT. Examples, the paint used in applying a priming coat of paint or the water used to start a water pump working.")
(comment Minister-Governmental "A specialization of both #$PublicOfficial and #$Manager.  Each instance of #$Minister-Governmental is a person who is responsible for managing the activities of some department or sub-organization of a (usually national) government.  Notable specializations of #$Minister-Governmental include #$PrimeMinister-HeadOfGovernment and #$Minister-Diplomatic.")
(disjointWith PortalCovering HumanOccupationConstruct)
(comment intendedTargetTypeOfWeaponType "Many classes of weapon are defined in part by the type of thing that instances are intended to immediately target, e.g. #$AntiPersonnelMine.  #$intendedTargetTypeOfWeaponType is intended to allow us to explicate the class of thing immediately targeted by a particular type of #$Weapon, if such a class is known. (#$intendedTargetTypeOfWeaponType WEAPON-TYPE TARGET-TYPE) means that weapons of type WEAPON-TYPE are designed to be used primarily against typical instances of TARGET-TYPE.")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType OrganismPartType)
(comment ModerateLevelOfCommunicability "There is a significative probability of acquiring an infection of
this type from an infected host when conditions of transmission are met.")
(comment MedicalCollegeAdmissionTest "The #$MedicalCollegeAdmissionTest is a test administered by the American Association of Medical Colleges to assess a student's ability to complete medical school.")
(comment (TransportViaFn Airplane) "The collection of all instances of #$TransportationEvent in which the role of #$transporter is filled by some instance of #$Airplane. This collection includes not only flying events (moving through the air, with the plane supported by the air), but also such events as taxiing, takeoff and landing.")
(comment keViewSentences "(#$keViewSentences TERM VIEW FORMULA) states that FORMULA is a CycL formula involving TERM which is known to be true, and which describes TERM as seen from a particular VIEW.")
(comment assertedTermSentences "(#$assertedTermSentences THING SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE has been asserted to the Cyc Knowledge Base (and is thus a  #$CycLAssertion) and that THING is mentioned in SENTENCE.  More precisely, and assuming the #$assertedTermSentences formula contains no free variables (and 

is thus a \"ground atomic formula\" or \"GAF\"): the CycL term immediately following the constant `#$assertedTermSentences' in the formula occurs in SENTENCE.  For example, (#$assertedTermSentences #$France (#$bordersOn #$France #$Germany)) holds.  See also #$assertedSentence and #$assertedPredicateArg for related predicates about assertions; and see #$termFormulas for a more general predicate that does not entail that SENTENCE has been asserted.")
(comment NuclearSubmarine "A specialization of both #$Submarine and #$NuclearPoweredDevice. Each instance of #$NuclearSubmarine is a submarine which uses nuclear power as its main power source (although some of the power for the submarine's systems may come from other sources).")
(comment NetworkVulnerability "#$NetworkVulnerability is an attribute of  instances of #$ComputerNetwork.  In many cases an instance of #$ComputerNetwork has a #$NetworkVulnerability because it has a vulnerable computer in the

network.")
(comment yzCrossSectionShape "The cross section shape in the yz plane. Again it is not really the yz plane in the absolute sense but in the intrinsic axes sense.\")")
(comment WorkaroundsManagementMicrotheory "A microtheory for the Battlespace Workarounds/Management project being done in collaboration with Alphatech.  If a given instance is only an instance of #$WorkaroundsManagementMicrotheory then it can be assumed that removing it from the KB will not cause problems in any other Cyc application.")
(comment SustainableAgriculture "#$SustainableAgriculture is the subcollection of

agricultural activities which are performed in the context of a concern about what may be

called the environmental ramifications of farming. In particular, this sort of agriculture

attempts to avoid soil erosion and degradation and pollution of the surrounding environment.")
(comment Immigration "The type of events in which a person moves to another country (see #$CrossingACountryBorder) with the intent of settling there more or less permanently. Such an activity may or may not be explicitly sanctioned by the laws of the host country (in which case see #$IllegalImmigration).")
(comment SurfaceRegion-Underspecified "The collection of surfaces, tangible or otherwise, which are
typically conceptualized by human beings for purposes of common-sense
reasoning as spatial surfaces. This collection thus includes tangible
Surface-Physicals such as #$Ground and #$PalmOfHand, as well as
metaphoric surfaces such as #$Mind (e.g., 'it crossed my mind that
...', 'It weighed heavily on my mind').")
(comment BluesRockMusic "A popular and long-standing specialization of #$RockMusic, #$BluesRockMusic

  consciously blended #$BluesMusic with Rock.  Most of the influential practitioners

  of this style are British, and they include the #$RollingStones, Cream, 

  and Led Zeppelin.")
(comment TrainingInFn "#$TrainingInFn takes as argument any instance of #$ExistingObjectType and returns the collection of all instances of #$Training in which that thing is (a signficant part of) what is taught. For example,(#$TrainingInFn #$VisualC) returns the collection of all instances of training in Visual C.")
(comment DuneRange "A collection of topographical features on planetary bodies.  Each element of #$DuneRange is a natural group of dunes.")
(comment commonalities "(#$commonalities CORR MAP COMMON DIFF-1 DIFF-2) states a justification for the analogy between the two objects in the #$AnalogyCorrespondence CORR for #$AnalogyMapping MAP.  COMMON indicates a justification for what is in common between the two objects.  DIFF-1 states what is different about the first object, while DIFF-2 states what is different about the second object.")
(comment EarthMovingEquipment-Military "The collection of military equipment used for mobility and countermobility support.  Instances are able to clear routes, excavate and reduce obstacles, and support bridging operations by moving earth and rubble.")
(comment Expression-Underspecified "The collection of underspecified individuals 

-- tangible or otherwise -- that are typically 

conceptualized by human beings for purposes of 

common-sense reasoning as \"expressions\" of some 

feature or feeling.  This is a spec of 

#$Agent-Underspecified for the same reason that 

instances of #$FeelingAttribute are: An 

expression -- e.g., an expression of anger -- 

can often be said to \"move\" or \"affect.\"")
(disjointWith Talking Archery)
(comment FastFrigate "The colletion of military fast frigates.")
(comment Southeast-Generally "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-General (q.v.).  From a given reference point, #$Southeast-Generally comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees (in either horizontal direction) of #$Southeast-Directly.")
(comment AuxiliaryWritingMark "The subcollection of #$TextMarking each of whose instances is a written or printed token of some instance of #$AuxiliaryWritingSymbol, such as a punctuation symbol or diacritic.")
(disjointWith NitrogenBase Nucleotide)
(comment MinisterOfState-HeadOfGovernment "The head of government of a nation.")
(comment BiologicalAttack-Anti-Personnel "The collection of all #$BiologicalAttacks for which the intended, primary targets are humans.")
(comment CommunicationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for some           mission type that centers around communications--sending,           receiving, intercepting, direction-finding, or jamming.")
(comment argAndRestGenl "A ternary #$ArgGenlPredicate (q.v.) used to 

place a specified #$genls based argument-type constraint on a given 

#$VariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places 

whose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number.

(#$argAndRestGenl RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for 

semantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument 

to RELN must be an specialization of COL.  Thus a closed formula 

(RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is an instance of COL.  See also #$argsGenl and #$argAndRestIsa.")
(disjointWith PhysicalDevice Park)
(comment PhysicalForce-Strong "This is the #$PhysicalForceType which acts within atomic nuclei and is responsible for holding them together.")
(comment GoalAction "Active action form of a #$Goal, that is, my goal is hitting Sally, not being in a state where Sally was hit by

me.")
(comment PoliticalGoal "This attribute characterizes goals which are pursued, at least in part, in the political arena.")
(comment NorthWestWind "The collection of all winds that blow from the northwest.  See #$WindProcess.")
(comment phoneNumberText-NC "The predicate #$phoneNumberText-NC maps a particular element of #$ContactLocation to a non-canonical #$PhoneNumber. The `NC' in the name stands for `non-canonical'.   (#$phoneNumberText-NC LOCATION PHONE) means that the #$ContactLocation LOCATION has the non-canonicalized #$PhoneNumber, PHONE.  For example, one value  for #$phoneNumberText-NC of the #$ContactLocation for #$Cycorp is `512-342-4000'. Note that this phone number as printed may not conform to some standard for printed phone numbers, and so relative to this standard it is not `canonical.' Non-canonical means that  PHONE may not conform to the canonicalization scheme(s) used for other known phone number entries for LOCATION.  These other (presumed canonical) phone number entries should be related to LOCATION using the predicate #$phoneNumberText. It really only makes sense to use #$phoneNumberText-NC in contexts (such as the #$LogicalTableSchemas for certain database tables) where LOCATION may have both canonical and non-canonical phone numbers entered for it.  In contexts where the differences between canonicalized and non-canonicalized phone numbers is not an issue, just use #$phoneNumberText.  See also #$ContactLocation.")
(comment UnalloyedMetal "A collection of tangible stuffs; a subcollection of #$Metal.  Every instance of #$UnalloyedMetal is a metal which is also an element, i.e., a substance of unmixed chemical type.  Thus, each subcollection of #$UnalloyedMetal is a subcollection of both #$Metal and #$ElementStuff.  Examples of #$UnalloyedMetal include #$Gold, #$Iron, #$Uranium, #$Antimony, #$Titanium, and many more.")
(comment minimize "#$minimize allows Cyc to assume that a statement is not

true unless it is known to be true.  Specifically, if for some

bindings of the variables that appear in the minimized formula the

formula with the bindings substituted in cannot be proved, then assume

the negation of the formula with the bindings substituted in.  From an

example in the KB: (#$minimize (#$disjointWith ?Collection

?Collection)) and binding ?Collection to #$Poodle means if we cannot

prove (#$disjointWith #$Poodle #$Poodle) assume (#$not (#$disjointWith

#$Poodle #$Poodle, i.e. assume every #$Collection is nonempty unless

we know otherwise.  In the case where we bind ?Collection to some

other variable ?Y and substituting in means if we cannot show

(#$disjointWith ?Y ?Y) then assume the negation, (#$not (#$forAll ?Y

(#$disjointWith ?Y ?Y))) which is equivalent to (#$thereExists ?Y

(#$not (#$disjointWith ?Y ?Y))). This is one of the predicates that

has been created to allow Cyc to do negation by failure.  Other

related predicates are #$minimizeExtent and #$minimizeExtentForArg. ")
(comment gospelName-Short "A predicate for recording the short name of a Gospel, e.g. 'Mark'. Useful for generating other, predictable, gospel names.")
(comment impactForce "The impact force in a collision")
(comment keAnalogySentences "(#$keAnalogySentences TERM SOURCE FORMULA) states that FORMULA is an analagous CycL formula involving TERM which is similar to a formula known to be true about SOURCE.")
(comment PolarNight "The collection of all multiday periods in which the #$Sun remains below the #$Horizon in a polar region.  Every #$PolarNight intersects a #$CalendarAutumn and #$CalendarWinter and is #$temporallyDisjoint from any #$CalendarSpring and #$CalendarSummer.")
(comment ObstacleSystem-Military "A structured system of artifacts intended to play the collective role of #$constrainingObject in a non-trivial subset of the collection of #$Movement-TranslationEvents such that the #$objectMoving is an instance of #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable. Collections of instances of #$ObstacleSystem-Military designed to impede the movements of certain kinds of military unit can be referenced via #$MilitarySpecialtyObstacleFn:  collections where the type is intended to impede the performance of certain tasks can be referenced via #$MilitaryTaskObstacleFn.")
(disjointWith OutdoorLocation UnderwaterLocation)
(comment NationalInfrastructureReqFn "(#$NationalInfrastructureReqFn COUNTRY) returns the collection of all products such that COUNTRY will require those products in order for its infrastructure to remain stable.  Such requisites include national highway systems and other main arteries of transportation, bridges, airports, telephone networks.  Particular countries might also feature special inclusions, eg, internet access or a canal system.  In general, a good test of whether a particular class counts as a national infrastructure requisite or not is whether it would be a plausible target of enemy action--sabotage or military attack--in wartime.")
(comment ClavulanatePotassium "The chemical compound which is an antibiotic.")
(comment MediaTransmitting "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$MediaTransferEvent and of #$Emission.  In every instance of #$MediaTransmitting, a collection of intangible #$InformationBearingThings are transmitted and received by #$CommunicationDevices.  These IBTs are NOT electrical signals, radio waves, or the like, but are constituted of sounds and/or images emitted by individual receiving devices and accessible to human senses.  Subsets of #$MediaTransmitting include #$Broadcasting (via radio or TV) and #$TVTransmitting (via cable or broadcast).")
(comment FormalLectureSeries-IBT "The collection of groups of #$FormalLecture-IBTs that, when taken together, constitute performances of #$LectureSeries-CWs.")
(comment Bookmark-WWW "A shortcut for accessing a #$WebPage-CW with a #$WorldWideWebClientProgram. Typically, from the user's point of view, a #$Bookmark-WWW takes the form of an item on a menu in the interface for a #$WorldWideWebClientProgram that, when selected, causes a particular #$WebPage-CW to be displayed. The #$Bookmark-WWW typically has as least two parts: the title of the associated web page, which is displayed to the user as the name of the #$Bookmark-WWW, and the url of the associated #$WebPage-CW, which is sent to the browser when the user selects the #$Bookmark-WWW.")
(comment Dollar-SolomonIslands "Unit of currency in the SolomonIslands")
(comment Loan-WrittenLegalAgreement "The collection of all #$LoanAgreements in which the parties sign a written contract which describes the terms of the loan.  All loans with Banks and other financial institutions are instances of this collection.")
(comment KungFuActivity "The collection of all activities consisting of a #$Person practicing, performing, or using kung fu, a Chinese martial art. As a combat skill, kung fu can be traced to the Chou dynasty (1111-255 BC) and even earlier. As physical exercise it was practiced by the Taoists in the 5th century BC. Its prescribed stances and actions are based on keen observations of human skeletal and muscular anatomy and physiology, and it employs great muscular coordination.")
(comment Pipe-GenericConduit "A specialization of #$FluidConduit; the collection of all enclosed tubular fluid conduits with openings at both ends.  #$Pipe-GenericConduit encompasses both human-made pipes as well as natural pipes, found naturally occurring in the environment or in an organism's body (like #$BloodVessels).")
(comment WordGame "All instances of any game involving the formation or alteration or discovery of words")
(comment directionOfTranslation-Avg "Predicate used to specify the 'general' direction of travel in a

#$Movement-TranslationEvent. The direction will be stated as a range

specified with a vector interval. ")
(comment CableTVNetwork "This is the collection of #$TelevisionNetworks that are were originally

broadcast only via cable television systems (they are not broadcast via 

satellite as well). These networks do not, like ABC, NBC, CBS and Fox, own

local affiliates through which they broadcast their programming locally 

using transmitting towers.")
(comment PleomorphBacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium.  In some species, the shape of cells typically varies from one to another.")
(comment Dominion "The physical and functional sides of a Protectorate -- a geopolitical entity that is nearly independent; it is still somewhat influenced by a foreign power, and (typically) weakly defended by them in case of attack")
(comment approvedCrossReference "(#$approvedCrossReference ?LTS ?IDTYPE1 ?IDTYPE2) means that the #$LogicalTableSchema ?LTS is approved as being a source of cross-reference information for the two #$UniqueIDTypes, ?IDTYPE1 and ?IDTYPE2.  For example, (#$approvedCrossReference DOCTOR-XREF-LTS #$SocialSecurityNumber #$DoctorME) means that, for the job of determining an individual's #$DoctorME if you know his or her #$SocialSecurityNumber, or vice-versa, DOCTOR-XREF-LTS is an approved table to use.")
(comment SickJoke "A subset of #$JokeOffensiveToSome, #$SickJoke is the collection           of all jokes that are about death, disease, pain or suffering.")
(comment ReformulationDirectionSpecification "The collection of directions for
#$CycLReformulatorDirectives.  There are exactly three directions:
#$ReformulationForwardDirection, #$ReformulationBackwardDirection, and
#$ReformulationNeitherDirection.  This concept of direction has
nothing to do with the forward vs. backward rule distinction in
inference.  Reformulator directives often have a 'from' argument and a
'to' argument, for example a reformulator rule could direct the
reformulator to reformulate (#$FruitFn #$AppleTree) into #$Apple.
However, this might be expressed as (#$rewriteOf #$Apple
(#$FruitFn #$AppleTree).  In this case, we would want to tell the
reformulator that the #$rewriteOf gaf has a 'backward' reformulation
direction.  See #$reformulationDirectionInMode for how these
directions are used.")
(comment ElectricalConductor "An instance of #$ExistingStuffType, and a specialization of #$ConductingMedium.  Each instance of #$ElectricalConductor is a partially tangible thing that can conduct electricity. Instances include power cords, electrical plugs, and pieces of metal.")
(comment Hernia "A condition where an organ protrudes through an opening in the tissue.  Often occurs in the bowels, the lungs and brain.")
(comment TextPublishedByAgentFn "#$TextPublishedByAgentFn takes as argument any instance of #$IntelligentAgent and returns the collection of all texts published by that agent.  For example, (#$TextPublishedByAgentFn #$LonelyPlanet) returns the set of all texts published by the Lonely Planet publishing company.")
(comment powerSet "This predicate relates an instance of #$Set-Mathematical to its power set, i.e. the set containing all and only its subsets.")
(comment oppositeFunction "(#$oppositeFunction FUNCTION OPP-FUNCTION) is used in inferences which involve quantities which are negatively related to one another.  For example, barometric pressue is inversely dependent on altitude above sea level.  Similarly, class rank in college is inversely correlated with SAT score.  Thus, the #$oppositeFunction of a geometrically increasing function would be a geometrically decreasing function.  The #$oppositeFunction of a net increasing function would be a net decreasing function.  The opposite function of a function involving no net change is a itself.")
(comment rampInitialValue "(#$rampInitialValue RAMP VALUE) means that the ramp-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution RAMP has a starting value or height of VALUE.  For example, the initial value of a ramp used to specify a temporal persistence distribution might be (#$Percent 25), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the ramp distribution pertains, the likelihood of being true at the #$rampStartLocation (ramp starting time) is 0.25. VALUE might also be a reified value such as `slightly likely'.")
(disjointWith Airport-Physical SeaportFacility)
(comment SubtopicForStringFn "This function returns the subtopic function/s which has/have            a given string as part of its/their prinstring/s.")
(comment aligned-EdgeToSurface "(#$aligned-EdgeToSurface SHEET OBJ2) means that a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET, is #$alignedAlongEdge to a surface of OBJ2.")
(comment PostalService "#$PostalService is a specialization of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization and #$ShippingOrganization.  Each instance of #$PostalService is an organization, usually government-run, usually national in scope, which has the main function of shipping letters and packages among people and organizations.")
(comment Iron-GolfClub "golf clubs with flat metal heads sloped a various angles for hitting the ball shorter distances and with higher accuracy")
(comment MilitaryLoaderVehicle "The collection of heavy wheeled military vehicles which are used to transport rubble, earth, or construction materials.")
(comment MagazineSeries "The collection of all #$PeriodicalSeries which have #$MagazineIssues as #$subWorks.")
(comment covalentlyLinkedTo "The relation existing between two molecules or other chemical
units that have been the objects of a #$CovalentLinking event.")
(comment Palladium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Palladium.")
(comment cellValue "(#$cellValue ?PT ?KEYOBJ ?LF ?VAL) states that  in the physical table ?PT, the value for the field ?LF in the tuple identified by ?KEYOBJ  is ?VAL.")
(comment MoviesDirectedByFn "#$MoviesDirectedByFn takes as argument any instances of #$Director-Movie and returns the collection of all instances of #$SpecifiedMovieType (Movies by title) directed by that director.  For example,  (#$MoviesDirectedByFn #$OrsonWelles) would return the collection of #$SpecifiedMovieTypes directed by Orson Welles.")
(comment attachingResult "This predicate relates an attaching to the resulting attachment situation.")
(comment connected-SheetsDiverge "(#$connected-SheetsDiverge SHEETSERIES) means that a members of series of #$SheetOfSomeStuff are all #$connectedAlongEdge to each other along some common connection.  The angle between the adjacent sheets may be either acute or obtuse.  The connection between the sheets may be an edge of the combined object (as in a book) or not (e.g. the pivot of a turbine).")
(comment ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory-LinearDiscreteTime "This is the sub-collection of

#$ReasoningWithTenseMicrotheory that contains all and only

those that take #$ReasoningWithTense-LogicMt-LinearDiscreteTime as

#$genlMt.")
(comment AnalogyPredicate "#$AnalogyPredicate is the collection of all Cyc predicates which constitute the vocabulary for representing analogical relationships.")
(comment xyCrossSection "This predicate relates an object to the arbitrarily thin slice of the object that defines the xy-cross section of the object as determined by the object's intrinsic axes.  For objects fixed on the surface of the earth, we will typically adopt the convention that #$xyCrossSection relates the object to a cross section of the object that is \"parallel\" to the earth's surface.  See also #$xzCrossSection, #$yzCrossSection and  #$IntrinsicAxisOfObjects.")
(comment AnatomicPathologist "The collection of doctors who study the structural changes associated with diseases.")
(disjointWith JokeOffensiveToSome CleanJoke)
(comment ArachnoidMater "The collection of all arachnoid maters.  An instance of #$ArachnoidMater is the middle of the three #$Meninges surrounding the #$Brain.  The #$ArachnoidMater #$sheetSurfaceTouches the #$DuraMater and contains #$CerebroSpinalFluid in which the #$Brain floats.")
(comment andWhile "(#$andWhile ?Form1 ?Form2) is equivalent to stating (#$and ?Form1 ?Form2), where it is implicit that ?Form2 is qualitatively different in some sense that ?Form1. The purpose of using #$andWhile is to generate more natural paraphrases for #$and situations where this tension is present.")
(comment Photoorganotroph "A collection of #$Bacterium that use organic electron donors in #$Photosynthesis-Bacterial.  Such donors include formic acid and methanol.")
(comment TroopTransportVehicle "The collection of #$MilitaryVehicles whose main purpose is the transport of military personnel.")
(comment DNAMolecule "The collection of all long-chain molecules whose components
are Deoxyribonucleotides are in pairwise structure, the overall shape of the
molecule being that of a double-helix.  #$DNAMolecules can be usefully
represented as information-encoding structures that code for the amino
acid sequences of various enzymes--and those, indirectly, for organic
phenotypes.")
(disjointWith Dream CommunicationConvention)
(comment physicalStateOfDrugType "For a type of pharmacy product, gives the physical state it is usually in when it is administered.")
(comment TransportationAccommodationFn "An instance of #$ReifiableFunction.  #$TransportationAccommodationFn takes a subset of #$TransportingPeople and returns the collection of accommodations which are provided during such an event.  For instance, (#$TransportationAccommodation (#$TravelingByMeansOfPathMediumFn #$Railway) denotes the collection of services that are generally provided during a rail travel trip.  This includes things like being served food and drink, being offered a newspaper, being given a blanket, etc.")
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization Secretariat)
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-BufferOverflow "The collection of electronic attacks by which a hacker uses a program running on the computer rather than logging in to the computer as a means of inserting malicious code.  By carefully constructing a long string of input to the target program, the hacker overflows the memory space alotted to it, resulting in the input data overwriting data in the process stack, which then executes the malicious code in the input buffer.")
(comment ProkaryoticGene-HereditaryUnit "The collection of #$Gene-HereditaryUnits found in #$ProkaryoticCells, which include #$Bacterium.")
(comment FoodProcessingEstablishment "This is the collection of companies like General Mills and Beatrice, mass food producers.")
(comment MarineCorps "A subcollection of #$BranchOfMilitaryService.  Each instance of #$MarineCorps is a military branch, modern or historical, composed mainly of soldiers (i.e. combat personnel) who serve on ships or in conjunction with naval forces, and whose purpose is to defend or attack coastal areas.")
(comment Androsterone "An androgenic steroid found in the urine. It contributes to growth and development inthe male.")
(comment Prune "The collection of individual prunes. #$Prune is to (#$FruitFn #$PlumTree) as #$Raisin is to (#$FruitFn #$GrapeVine).")
(comment ProjectileShell-Fragmentation "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is designed to  cause more damage from the the fragmentation of the shell than from the blast  itself.  Often a #$ProjectileShell-Fragmentation is exploded in the air  before hitting its target.")
(disjointWith Distance ElectricalCharge)
(comment ArtilleryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained in handling certain classes of           projectile weapon.")
(comment nearestSpecs "(#$nearestSpecs COL NEAR-SPEC) relates any  collection COL to the nearest unsubsumed collections NEAR-SPEC which are subsets of COL. This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it  must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genls hierarchy.  Moreover, it is merely the #$elInverse of #$nearestGenls.")
(comment SpreadingOntoSurface "A collection of events. In each #$SpreadingOntoSurface event, an object or stuff is spread out [see #$ShapingSomething] onto a surface so that it covers [#$covers-Generic] it.  Major specializations of #$SpreadingOntoSurface are #$SpreadingStuffOntoSurface and #$SpreadingSheetOntoSurface.")
(comment ContextOfPCWFn "(#$ContextOfPCWFn WORK) denotes the #$PropositionalInformationThing associated with WORK. The expression (#$ContextOfPCWFn WORK) serves the same role as expressions that denote the PIT of a particular physical instance of WORK (such as (#$PITOfIBTFn COPY67OFWORK)), except that  (#$ContextOfPCWFn WORK) denotes the PIT of the abstract object WORK, which a copy of WORK instantiates. For example if we think of (#$ContextOfPCWFn WORK) as the entirety of the content of WORK, (#$ContextOfPCWFn #$MobyDickNovel) denotes the entirety of the content of MobyDick, whereas (#$PITOfIBTFn Copy787OfMobyDick) denotes the entirety of the content of Copy787OfMobyDick. Note that we assert as a default rule that whatever is true in the PIT of a #$PropositionalConceptualWork is true in the PIT an instantiation of that work, but not the converse. (A copy of Moby Dick may contain an introductory critical essay, or publication information -- information not contained in #$MobyDickNovel. Thus the PIT of a copy of MobyDick may be such that more things are true in it than are true in the PIT of #$MobyDickNovel). This rule is made default to account for the fact that a copy of a book remains a copy of Moby Dick even after damage which results in a small loss of the information that it contains.")
(comment Warhead-HighExplosiveAntiTank "The collection of #$Warheads that are meant to be used against #$Tank-Vehicles and other #$ArmoredVehicles.")
(comment FissionWeapon-GunMethod "The collection of #$FissionWeapons which use a conventional explosive charge to fire one subcritical mass of Uranium-235 at another subcritical mass in a tube that is similar to a gun barrel. When the two subcritical masses collide, a supercritical mass forms that results in a #$NuclearFissionProcess.")
(comment KnowledgeEditingActivity "The collection of human activities that are considered knowledge editing activities.")
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic ScientificInstrument)
(comment BiologicalDecompositionEvent "A collection of events.  In each #$BiologicalDecompositionEvent, some living structures are decomposed.")
(comment Street-Generic "#$Street-Generic is a specialization of both #$Roadway and #$UrbanArea.  Each instance of #$Street-Generic is a #$Roadway located inside a city or town.")
(comment AirsoftGun "The collection of all guns designed for use

in #$AirsoftSkirmishes.")
(comment LaserGuidedBomb "A specialization of #$Device-RemoteControlled and #$AerialBomb.  Each instance of #$LaserGuidedBomb is a bomb that is guided by a laser beam projected from #$MilitaryAircraft onto the intended target.  #$LaserGuidedBombs were developed for precision bombing and can be used at night unlike other types of smart weapons.")
(comment Emoticon "The collection of all emoticons, conceptualized as a subset of #$CharacterString. An #$Emoticon is a sequence of ASCII characters such as :) that, when viewed sideways, graphically represents a face. #$Emoticons are prototypically used in email and #$ChatRooms to convey emotional tone otherwise difficult to represent compactly in ASCII text.")
(comment relevantSubcollection "The predicate form of #$RelevantSubcollectionFn. Convenient to
have both a predicate and a function for inference purposes. For an
example of use of this predicate, consider the fact that in a generic 
context, the relevant subcollection of bird is adult bird and thus 
 (#$relevantSubcollection Bird (AdultFn Bird)).")
(comment DiflorasoneDiacetate "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(comment with-UnderspecifiedAgent "(#$with-UnderspecifiedAgent ACT AGENT) states that an abstract
complicity relation holds between ACT and AGENT, where AGENT is an
#$Agent-Underspecified that contributes to the execution of ACT.
#$with-UnderspecifiedAgent is an underspecified semantic representation
that may be elaborated to represent either a co-agency example of 'with'
(as in 'Brutus killed Caesar with Cassius') or a metaphorical use
('Brutus killed Caesar with the republic's blessing.').")
(comment MachinePistol "The collection of #$Handguns that are

  also #$MachineGuns.  Such guns are fairly

  rare, since they are relatively useless: Once

  the trigger is pulled, the clip is more or 

  less emptied instantly.")
(comment Rafting "Transportation by way of raft.  If an event is a #$TransportationEvent such that the #$transporter is a #$Raft, then the event is an element of #$Rafting.")
(comment DialingATelephoneNumber-Electronic "The collection of all instances of DialingATelephoneNumber where the 'dialing' is actually accomplished by automatic means, e.g. a computer program.  Someinstances may not involve the direct intervention/supervision of a human user.  Both complete and partial dialings are included.  See also #$DialingATelephoneNumber.")
(comment HydrogenChlorideMolecule "The collection of HCl molecules.")
(comment Leaf "The main photosynthetic organ of most green plants, consisting of a lateral outgrowth from a stem and comprising lamina, petiole, and leaf base.")
(disjointWith Gaseous-StateOfMatter Mixture)
(comment Jargon "#$Jargon is a specialized vocabulary shared by a group of people with a common recreational, occupational, educational etc. pursuit. It is NOT the same as #$SlangSpeech.")
(disjointWith BodyOfWater GeoculturalRegion)
(comment Blending "A collection of events.  In each #$Blending event, the substance involved (one or more) is stirred so vigorously that it liquefies (if it isn't already liquid) or becomes a smoother liquid.  Where two or more substances are involved, the output is a mixture of all the substances that were #$inputs to the #$Blending.")
(comment NCAADivisionIAProgram "The collection of college sports teams that the #$NationalCollegiateAthleticAssociation has classified as Division IA.  This classification is generally relevant for football teams.")
(comment LandingCraftUtility "The collection of utility landing craft.")
(comment BacterialMessengerRNA "The specialization of #$MessengerRNA to those produced by bacteria.")
(comment QuotationFn "#$QuotationFn takes as argument any instance of #$IntelligentAgent and returns the collection of all #$Quotations attributed to that agent.  For example, (#$QuotationFn JuliusCeasar) returns the collection of quotations attributed to Julius Ceasar including the one

whose actual text [#$actualTextOfPIT] is ``Veni, vedi, vici.''")
(comment MultinationalCorporation "A subset of #$HPKB-TransnationalAgent and #$LegalCorporation. An element of #$MultinationalCorporation is a corporate entity that operates internationally and involves firms or interests from different countries.")
(comment PhysicalCollectionEvent "Events in which tangible objects are collected from various sources to a single destination via some collection network.")
(disjointWith MicroPhysicalEvent MentalSituation)
(comment StomachUlcer "An irritation or hole in the stomach lining")
(comment performsMusicType "The expression `(#$performsMusicType AGENT TYPE)' means

that AGENT performs music of type TYPE. Note that agents may perform music of

different types. Note also that this predicate allows a broader class of assertions

to be made than does #$styleOfArtist. Four-hand harpischord music, for example, is a type of music, but not

a music genre. Classification of performer and music by style (genre) is really only 

adequate, if at all, for popular music.")
(comment Emulation "A collection of #$Events; a specialization of #$ComputerProcessRunning.  In every instance of #$Emulation, one computer system performs in exactly the same way (although perhaps not at the same speed) as another system of a different type.  The emulator may consist solely of software, or be a combination of software and hardware.  See also #$EmulatorProgram, #$EmulatorHardware, #$emulatesType.")
(comment dataSender "(#$dataSender TRANSFER COMPUTER) means that COMPUTER sends the

data in the #$InformationTransferEvent TRANSFER.")
(comment FruitGiftBasket "An instance of #$GiftBasketTypeByContent.  The collection of #$GiftBaskets that are filled with #$Fruit.")
(comment SignalInterceptionRadioUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on           intercepting radio signals.")
(comment ambientVisibility "(#$ambientVisibility LOC DEGREE) indicates how clear the ambient fluid is at the location LOC.  Higher values of DEGREE mean one can see farther (than one could have at lower values).")
(disjointWith MeetingSomeoneForTheFirstTime SayingGoodbyeToSomeone)
(comment InfectionEpidemicFn "`(#$InfectionEpidemicFn INFECTIONTYPE)' denotes the collection of all epidemics consisting of infectious diseases of type INFECTIONTYPE.")
(comment IAMicrotheory "The collection of all microtheories that are part of the  information assurance (IA) project.  Instances of this collection are automatically linked to the appropriate microtheories.")
(comment Commandment "In Judeo-Christian teaching, a #$Commandment is 

a #$MoralPrecept that has the authority of #$GodOfAbrahamIsaacAndJacob behind it.

Whereas many precepts will be human interpretations of moral behaviour, Christians 

(#$ChristianPerson) and Jews (#$JewishPerson) usually consider the commandments

to come from God (#$GodOfAbrahamIsaacAndJacob).")
(comment interArgReln "A quaternary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln RELN M N BINPRED) means that a ground atomic formula (or \"GAF\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) or closed non-atomic term (or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) built from RELN is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the Mth and Nth arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ..ARGM..ARGN..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARGM ARGN) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.  See also the more specific binary #$InterArgRelnPredicates, each of which is defined for two particular argument-places of RELN (e.g. #$interArgReln1-2 and #$interArgReln4-2).")
(comment sameListLength "(#$sameListLength LIST01 LIST02) means that LIST01 and LIST02 are
lists of the same length.")
(comment WindingProcess "The collection of #$WindingProcesses by which a 1 or 2 dimensional object is wrapped around a solid object over and over.  If this is done by rotation of the spool around its axis, the more specific term, #$Reeling, should be used.  Note that this is distinct from the process of winding a watch (which is a type of #$CoilTightening), since the coil being wound already encircles the center post.")
(comment TernaryFunction "A specialization of #$FixedArityFunction and #$TernaryRelation.  An instance FUNC of #$FixedArityFunction is an instance of #$TernaryFunction if and only if FUNC has an #$arity of three.")
(comment AnaerobicBacterium "The collection of all instances of #$Bacterium which do not metabolize oxygen.")
(comment BallisticMissile-BattlefieldShortRange "A ballistic missile with a range of up to 94 miles")
(comment Pedophilia-MaleChild "This collection involves behaviors which treat male children as sexual objects of (male or female) adult desires.")
(comment NBCWeaponsUnit-Defensive "A subset of #$MilitaryOrganization.  Instances of #$NBCWeaponsUnit-Defensive are those military units specialized in defending against, or dealing with the consequences of, either nuclear, biological, or chemical weapons.")
(comment AntimalarialDrug "Drugs used to cure or ameliorate malaria.")
(comment TVMediaProduct "A collection of objects; a subset of #$MediaProduct.  Every instance of #$TVMediaProduct is a #$ConceptualWork or #$MovingImageWithSound that was created for the purposes of #$TVTransmitting.  Examples of #$TVMediaProduct are television commercials, soap operas, and sitcoms.")
(comment ShorteningEvent "In an instance of this collection, an object's length (#$lengthOfObject) is decreased by some amount.")
(comment Neckerchief "A collection of instances of #$Kerchief, folded or rolled and worn about the neck.")
(comment DiplomaticMission-ThePost "#$DiplomaticMission-ThePost is a specialization of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization.  Each instance of #$DiplomaticMission-ThePost is an official diplomatic mission (the organization --embassy or consulate -- not physical structure) of a legal government in a foreign country.")
(comment DefenseSystem "#$DefenseSystem is a specialization of both #$ProtectiveSystem and #$Artifact. Instances of #$DefenseSystem are created by agents to protect things (not necessarily the agents themselves) from harmful situations or individuals.")
(comment accessFilename "(#$accessFilename FILE NAME) means that the #$CharacterString

   NAME can be used to designate the #$ComputerFileCopy FILE.  Note that there can be multiple

   names associated with the same file.  Note also that each instance of #$ComputerFileCopy is

   uniquely stored in a single area of memory which resides on one computer or network.  The

   name referred to by this predicate is the name of the file that will be recognized by that

   computer or network.")
(comment Stimulant "Consumable substances that stimulate the fight-or-flight syndrome and speed the metabolism.")
(comment FarmTheOrganization "The collection of farms considered as functioning organizations")
(comment connectedAround "(#$connectedAround OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 is #$connectedTo OBJ2 in a circuit around OBJ2.  Portions of OBJ2 are open to the environment on both sides (three dimensionally) of OBJ1.")
(comment fastestRouteForVehicleType "A Predicate mapped in from the NWU Trafficability and
Terrain Engine.  (#$fastestRouteForVehicleType PATH VEHICLETYPE LOC1
LOC2) means that of the paths available, taking PATH will oridinarily
be the fastest route for getting a vehicle of type VEHICLETYPE from
LOC1 to LOC2.")
(comment CharacterToken-Inscribed "The collection of all inscribed tokens of individual
  abstract characters.  More precisely, #$CharacterToken-Inscribed
  is a  specialization of #$CharacterToken each of whose instances 
  is a physical marking, #$Engraving, or character-in-relief that 
  represents or realizes a particular instance of #$Character-Abstract 
  in some writing system.  Instances include character tokens that 
  are written or printed on paper, carved into stone, displayed on 
  computer monitors or LCDs, generated by skywriting, and created 
  by Brailling.  Examples such as these last two demonstrate 
  why #$CharacterToken-Inscribed is a proper generalization 
  of #$WrittenCharacter.  Inscribed characters are 
  identified (both in theory and in practice) as tokens of
  particular abstract characters largely by their shapes,
  though context and creator's intention also figure in 
  (see #$tokensCharacter).")
(comment regionalPastimes "(#$regionalPastimes REGION ACTIVITY) means that ACTIVITY is a common pastime of the inhabitants of the region REGION. This implies that a sufficient number of people engage in instances of ACTIVITY, and that they do so for entertainment or amusement, rather than as a job.")
(disjointWith CampaignManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment transferOutSubEvent "The Cyc predicate #$transferOutSubEvent indicates the initial stage of a particular #$GeneralizedTransfer in which the #$transferredThing leaves the point of origin.  For example, (#$transferOutSubEvent TRANSLOC EMISSION) means that EMISSION is the initial stage (see #$firstSubEvents) of the #$Translocation TRANSLOC.  (The #$emitter in EMISSION is a #$fromLocation of TRANSLOC.)")
(comment HighLevelOfCommunicability "There is a high probability of acquiring an infection of
this type from an infected host when conditions of transmission are met.")
(comment CentimetersPerSecond "An instance of #$UnitOfSpeed.  When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$CentimetersPerSecond returns an instance of #$Speed as its value.  For example, (#$CentimetersPerSecond 9.8) is a speed of 9.8 centimeters per second.")
(comment PlacementOfMaliciousProgram "Collection of all activities of a placement of programs which are instances of #$MaliciousComputerProgram. Note that #$PlacementOfMaliciousProgram  is a complex script that should cover actions prior to and immediately after the actual placement  of the program.  For instance, if a hacker had use methods to disguise the placement, such activity  would be part of this script.  On the other hand, probing a computational system for vulnerabilities  in order to make such a placement possible would fall under #$ProbingAComputerNetwork.")
(disjointWith Dock SeaportFacility)
(comment atmosphereChunk "The piece of atmosphere within this physical-geographic region.")
(comment AmateurProducedProductFn "#$AmateurProducedProductFn takes a #$ProductType as its argument, and returns the collection of such products produced by people who were not paid to produce the product, i.e. by amateurs.  Examples include amateur movies, pictures,...  See also #$ProfessionallyProducedProductFn.")
(disjointWith Gun Tank-Vehicle)
(comment SportFishing "Fishing done for challenge or relaxation.")
(comment BorderCheckEvent "The collection of events in which a border agent checks (handles, processes) a person or thing.  Normally takes place shortly after crossing a #$CountryBorder, though not necessarily in the same place.")
(comment Mind "The collection of all 'complete mental states' of all
sentient creatures, the intangible, emergent process that arises from
each functioning #$Brain.  In metaphorical terms, the body's container
of ideas. It is difficult to state more than this without committing
to a particular philosophical theory of mind.")
(comment FolkRockMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic whose heyday was the late 1960s to the early

  1970s.  Influenced by #$FolkMusic, #$FolkRockMusic is quieter and slower than most other

  types of Rock, and features more acoustic (i.e. non-electrified) instrumentation.

  Its lyrics focus less on rebellion, and more on peace, nature, rustic living,

  and personal growth.  Influential practitioners of this style include Joni Mitchell;

  Crosby, Stills and Nash; and James Taylor.")
(comment PipingSystem-Generic "The collection of all #$Groups of #$Pipe-GenericConduits that form an interconnected system wherein fluid (liquid or gaseous) can flow from one component to other components connected to it by #$JunctionOfPipes junctions.  Parts of a generic conduit system may be temporarily closed off; also, parts may be open to the outside environment.  Examples: the plumbing system of a house, the piping at an oil refinery, a cardiovascular system.  It may also include reservoirs, pumps, storage, valves, etc.")
(comment emissionAmountDuring "(#$emissionAmountDuring PT COL THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$Collection COL emitted by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PT might, for example, be a #$Country or a #$Business or a #$FactoryBuilding.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of emission of instances of COL by PT during the temporal extent of THING.")
(comment Interval-Bounded "A specialization of #$Interval-BoundedAbove and #$Interval-BoundedBelow.  Each instance of #$Interval-Bounded is an interval that has both upper and lower bounds.  Example: the interval comprised of real numbers from 3.5 to 4.5.  Note that #$Interval-Bounded is more general than #$IntegerExtent (q.v.) because #$Interval-Bounded includes dense, negative, imaginary and complex ranges and point values.")
(comment distributionRate "(#$distributionRate PT PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE are distributed to the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT at the #$Rate RATE.  In a general economic context, PT will often be an instance of (#$GroupFn #$IntelligentAgent).")
(comment Snowsuit "A collection of #$PlaySuits worn by infants and young children as protection against very cold weather.")
(comment nearlySimultaneousEvents "(#$nearlySimultaneousEvents EVT OTHEREVT) says that EVT and OTHEREVT occur/occured almost simultaneously, though falling short of (#$temporalBoundsIdentical EVT OTHEREVT) being true.")
(comment PurchaseDecision-PriceBased "The collection of purchase decisions in which the main or sole criterion for selection is price. Such a  process typically involves the comparison of similar items and a selection made on  the basis of which item has the lowest price.")
(comment EndosporeTest-Indirect "A collection of events in which a bacterial culture is
indirectly tested for #$Spore-DormantBacterium.  Here, the culture is
heated to 80 Degrees Celsius for 10 minutes.  This will kill the
vegetative cells in the culture, but endospores, if produced, will
survive.  Any growth following subculture to a fresh medium suggests
the presence of endospores.")
(comment PeaceKeepingOperation "The collection of events in which an armed force attempts to keep the peace in an area which has recently undergone (or which is on the brink of) an armed conflict.  Typically, the force keeping the peace (an instance of #$PeaceKeepingForces) is not directly aligned with any side in the recent or incipient conflict.")
(comment Bangalore-MineClearingKit "The collection of hand-portable mine breaching systems which consist of a torpedo and explosive-laden tubing.")
(disjointWith SteeringADeviceByHand Archery)
(comment OnlineListingsFn-IBT "#$OnlineListingsFn-IBT takes as argument any instances of #$IBTContentType and returns the collection of web pages featuring online listings of InformationBearingThings of that type.  For example (#$OnlineListingsFn-IBT #$JobClassifiedAd) returns the collection of all web pages featuring online listings of employment classifieds. (#$Vizedom 2/2/99)")
(comment BiographyOfTypeFn "#$BiographyOfTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$Person and returns the collection of all biographies of persons of that type. For instance, (#$BiographyOfTypeFn #$MovieStar) returns the collection of all biographies of movie stars.")
(comment dutiesOfAgentInJob "(#$dutiesOfAgentInJob AGT WORKERTYPE EVENT) means that agent AGT is 

obligated to perform at least some actions of type EVENT by virtue of 

being a worker of type WORKERTYPE.  The obligation may derive directly from an 

explicit provision in an instance of  #$WorkAgreement for WORKERTYPE to which AGT is bound

or it may stem from more general norms and institutions governing the behavior

of agents of type WORKERTYPE.  The fact that AGT is an instance of WORKERTYPE

must be at least one source, however, of the duty in question, in order

for (#$dutiesOfAgentInJob AGT WORKERTYPE EVENT) to be true or taken to be true

by agents within the relevant normative system.")
(comment FleetSupportShip "The collection of ships intended to be used in operations supporting some fleet.")
(comment Northwest-Generally "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-General (q.v.).  From a given reference point, #$Northwest-Generally comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees (in either horizontal direction) of #$Northwest-Directly.")
(disjointWith OralDrug FoodOrDrink)
(comment PapyrusSheet "paper-like material made from bonded leaves of the papyrus reed")
(comment NaturalGasCompany "An #$NaturalGasCompany is in the business of bringing #$NaturalGas to market.")
(comment FillingANewPrescription-Retail "The collection of all events in which a new #$DrugPrescription is filled in a #$Pharmacy which is either a #$RetailStore or a #$Department of a #$RetailStore; a subset of #$FillingANewPrescription and #$FillingAPrescription-Retail.")
(comment FollicleStimulatingHormone "A #$Hormone secreted by the hypophysis. It stimulates maturation of the ovarian follicles in females, and is important in male spermatogenesis.")
(comment Lawn "A grassy piece of land in a human-occupied areas, etc.  Lawns are usually maintained by mowing, etc.  They are often but not always around buildings.")
(comment rankAuthorizes "(#$rankAuthorizes RANK ORGTYPE-BY-EGB ACT-TYPE ROLE) means

that a person with #$rank-Military RANK in ORGTYPE-BY-EGB is

#$authorityCapableOf of playing ROLE in events of type ACT-TYPE. Also

if the second argument is represented by a NAT of the form

(#$OrgTypeByGeoAndBOSFn GEO-AG BOS) and it is true that

(#$militaryRank-CountryAndBranchOfService PERSON RANK GEO-AG BOS),

then PERSON is #$authorityCapableOf playing ROLE in events of type

ACT-TYPE.")
(comment Serape "The collection of long brightly-colored scarfs, traditionally worn by Mexican women.")
(comment crewMember "(#$crewMember OPERATE PERSON) means that the #$Person PERSON is a member of the crew needed to perform the #$TransportationEvent OPERATE appropriately. Very often the only #$crewMember is the #$driverActor (when driving an #$Automobile for instance), but there are cases when there are more #$crewMembers (when driving a large #$Ship for instance). ")
(comment BiologicalAttack-Anti-Plant "The collection of all #$BiologicalAttacks for which the intended, primary targets are plants.  In the typical case, one would direct such an attack against the staple crop of one's enemy, in order to cause economic devastation or even hunger problems.  Anti-plant attacks are unique in that one can be carried out *without* the use of #$LivingBiologicalAgents, as one can attack 

crops by releasing certain kinds of insects into an area.")
(comment Garbage-OfficeRefuse "#$Garbage-OfficeRefuse is a subset of #$Garbage-Generic.  It is a type of stuff dicarded by a business office.  It includes paper that will be recycled, such as memos and other computer printouts.")
(comment ColloidalGel "#$ColloidalGel is the collection of solid-liquid #$Colloids which
have a texture ranging from that of a #$Gel - that is to say,
semi-solid, sticky, and about as thick as a paste - to a texture
that is firm but somewhat yielding, such as a hard-boiled egg.")
(comment ArgGenlTernaryPredicate "A specialization of #$ArgTypeTernaryPredicate and #$ArgGenlPredicate.  Each instance of #$ArgGenlTernaryPredicate is used to specify that a certain collection is required to stand in the #$genls relation to anything that is acceptable in a particular argument slot of a given instance of #$Relation.  With each instance of #$ArgGenlTernaryPredicate, the first argument is the relation constrained; the second argument is the argument constrained; and the third argument is the required collection that the relation's specified argument is required to be a specialization of.")
(comment EconomicEmbargo "The collection of events in which one nation, acting as an agent, officially forbids all economic commerce with a particular country, and takes additional steps to prevent and/or intercept all relevant instances of commerce trade.  Often, but not always, embargoes are cases of punishing or imposing sanctions.  An embargo can be thought of as the most extreme possible case of imposing trade restrictions. In CycL, we take an embargo to be the combination of the legal/official edict interdicting commerce and the actual steps taken to enforce the edict, eg, the conducting of additional customs inspections in ports.")
(comment Superstring "Superstrings are the posits of a string theory which takes into account

               boson/fermion symmetry. String theory is a class of theories which posit

               that the basic subatomic entities are \"strings\" which are have only one

               dimension. One interesting feature of quantum field theories of strings is

               that they are only non-anomalous if spacetime is assumed to have 10 (or

               26) dimensions.")
(comment CycLOpenSentence "A specialization of both #$CycLOpenExpression and #$CycLSentence. The collection of CycL sentences that contain one or more free variables.  Note that those CycL sentences that are treated (in the context of representing assertions in the Cyc Knowledge Base) as implicitly containing initial universal quantifiers are in fact #$CycLOpenSentences.")
(comment vaccineUsedOn "(#$vaccineUsedOn VAC ORG) relates a type of #$Vaccine to the type of #$Organism-Whole it is intended to be used on. This means that the #$Organism-Whole ORG is what is being vaccinated.")
(comment Hashish "The psychoactive resin found in seeds, flowers, leaves, and stems of female #$HempPlants. #$Hashish is an #$IllegalDrug in the #$NaiveUSLawCOC microtheory.")
(comment WestWind "The collection of all winds that blow from the west.  See #$WindProcess.")
(comment YahooChatRoom "The collection of all #$ChatRooms sponsored and

 powered through the Yahoo! web interface.

#$YahooChatRooms are always free, but to use

  them you need a Yahoo! account (which is 

  also free).")
(comment IrreversibleReformulation "A property of reformulator rules.  A reformulator rule RULE having

the property #$IrreversibleReformulation is such that one of the following

4 conditions obtains: (1) If RULE, when 

applied in the forward direction to a given 

expression PRE-FORM, yields the expression POST-FORM, then RULE, 

when applied in the backward direction to POST-FORM, 

does not yield PRE-FORM.

(2) If RULE, when 

applied in the backward direction to a given 

expression PRE-FORM, yields the expression POST-FORM, then RULE, 

when applied in the forward direction to POST-FORM, 

does not yield PRE-FORM.

(3) Applying RULE in the forward direction is impossible.

(4) Applying RULE in the backward direction is impossible.

See also #$OneWayReformulation-Forward and #$OneWayReformulation-Backward")
(comment ArtificialMaterial "A collection of substances; a subcollection of #$Artifact.  An instance of #$ArtificialMaterial is a portion of artificial stuff that was intentionally made by some agent(s), such as #$Plastic or #$SweetNLow. Since #$ArtificialMaterials are intentionally produced, this class does not normally include materials which are merely #$byProducts or #$wasteProducts of an intentional process.  However, what is a by-product at one time or in one context may be a useful material that would count as an instance of #$ArtificialMaterial in another.")
(comment Embankment "A collection of fixed structures.  Each instance of
#$Embankment is a long raised structure of earth, gravel, etc., used
to hold back water or to carry a road or railroad.")
(comment elasticityOfCollision "The coefficient of restitution of the collision. This is the ratio of the relative velocity of 'moving away' and the relative velocity of approach. The value is between 0 and 1. If it is 1, then the collision is perfectly elastic (all momentum is conserved); if it is 0, then it is perfectly inelastic (so the objects move together after the collision).")
(comment DisengagingFromCombat "Disengagement is breaking contact with the enemy so as to allow the conduct of another mission. It involves moving to a location where the enemy can neither engage the friendly force with direct fires or observed indirect fires. Disengaging from the enemy while displacing from one position to the next is a difficult procedure.")
(comment ProgramProcessFn "A function which relates a #$ComputerProgram-CW with the collection
of all the instances of #$ComputerProcessRunning which are related to that
program via #$programOfProcess.")
(comment Amoxicillin "The chemical compound which is an antibiotic.")
(comment purchaseFromFractionDuring "(#$purchaseFromFractionDuring PT1 PRODUCT-TYPE PT2 THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the monetary value of purchases of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the monetary value of all purchases of PRODUCT-TYPE by PT1 during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  PT1 might, for example, be a #$Country or a #$Business; and likewise for PT2.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that Norway has a 25 percent share of the European natural gas market in 1998, we can say (#$purchaseFromFractionDuring #$ContinentOfEurope #$NaturalGas #$Norway (#$YearFn 1998) (#$Percent 25)).")
(comment BFVUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Specialization of motorized units with mission profiles dedicated to the deployment and use of BradleyFightingVehicles.")
(comment Dollar-EastCaribbean "The standard UnitOfCurrency in #$AntiguaAndBarbuda")
(comment Corruption-Activity "A collection of actions.  Each instance of #$Corruption-Activity is a criminal action that subverts the proper, legal, and just operation of some procedure in government or in the private sector.  Under corruption we include both offering inducements to cheat and accepting them.  Thus types of corruption include both offering and accepting bribes, and the various species of graft.")
(comment supplyRateFromThrough "(#$supplyRateFromThrough PT1 COL PT2 PT3 RATE) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT3 (on their way from PT2 to PT1) at the #$Rate RATE.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyRateFromThrough is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  And PT3 might, for example, be a #$Hose, a #$Railway, a #$GeographicalRegion, or a #$BloodVessel.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(comment OwnershipAgreement "Each instance is a #$LegalAgreement that involves ownership rights, rights to transfer ownership or other rights related to something owned.")
(comment CellEnlargementEvent "The event in which a cell newly produced by cell division enlarges.")
(comment TaekwondoActivity "The collection of all activities consisting of a #$Person practicing, performing, or using taekwondo, a Korean art of unarmed combat based on the earlier form of Korean self-defense known as tae kyon and on karate.")
(disjointWith Water ElementStuff)
(comment AntiAircraftArtillery "The collection of large anti-aircraft weapons (such as cannons).")
(comment explains-Generic "(#$explains-Generic EXP THING) says that  EXP, in some underspecified way, explains THING. This predicate is neutral with respect to whether  EXP and  THING are agents, propositions, situations, or classes  of situations.")
(comment BoforsGun "A large, double barrelled #$MachineCannon

  used to shoot down airplanes.")
(comment Nucleoid "A collection.  The #$Nucleoid is the folded structure of

#$DNAStuff within a #$Bacterium.  Analogous to the chromosome located in

the nucleus of a eukaryotic cell, however, the nucleoid floats freely

in the cell's #$Cytoplasm.")
(comment nearestGenlPreds "A #$TaxonomicSlotForPredicates and a specialization of #$genlPreds (q.v.).  (#$nearestGenlPreds PRED NEAR-PRED) means that NEAR-PRED  is a \"nearest\" generalization of PRED.  That is, (#$genlPreds PRED NEAR-PRED)  holds, PRED is not identical to NEAR-PRED, and there is no reified #$Predicate  OTHER-PRED distinct from PRED and NEAR-PRED such that both  (#$genlPreds PRED OTHER-PRED) and (#$genlPreds OTHER-PRED NEAR-PRED) hold.  Note   that #$nearestGenlPreds is non-assertible (see #$notAssertible), since its  extension at any given time depends upon (and so must be recomputed from) the  current state of the #$genlPreds hierarchy in the Cyc Knowledge Base.")
(comment StereotypeJoke "A subset of #$JokeOffensiveToSome, #$StereotypeJoke is the collection of all           jokes that are rooted in some widely held stereotype about a group of people.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForCanonicalization "(#$useReformulationRuleForCanonicalization RULE), asserted

in the microtheory MT, tells the #$CycCanonicalizer to consider RULE

at canonicalization time, and use it to help canonicalize

#$CycLExpressions in MT or a specMt thereof.")
(comment nearForRolesInEventType "This predicate relates objects according to nearness conventions associated with roles in an event type.  (#$nearForRolesInEventType OBJ1 OBJ2 ROLE1 ROLE2 EVENTTYPE)

means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are near each other with respect to the roles

ROLE1 and ROLE2 in an event of type EVENTTYPE. For instance,

(#$nearForRolesInEventType OBJ1 OBJ2 ROLE1 ROLE2 EVENTTYPE) means that

were PLAYER1 and PLAYER2 playing ROLE1 and ROLE2 respectively in an

EVENT of type EVENTTYPE they would be near each other according to the

conventions associated with those roles in that event type. (see

#$nearnessForRolesInEventType).  Note that (#$nearForRolesInEventType

OBJ1 OBJ2 ROLE1 ROLE2 EVENTTYPE) doesn't imply that OBJ1 is playing

ROLE1 and OBJ2 is playing ROLE2 in an event of type EVENTTYPE but only

that they'd be deemed to be near each other, relative to these roles,

if they were participating in an event of type EVENTTYPE.  For

instance, if Person001 is one kilometer from GasStation001 we might

assert that (#$nearForRolesInEventType PersonOO1 GasStation001

#$transportees #$toLocation #$TransportWithMotorizedLandVehicle) but

it would not necessarily be simultaneously true that (#$nearForRolesInEventType

Person001 GasStation001 #$performedBy #$toLocation

#$Walking-Generic).  Also note that while (#$nearForRolesInEventType

OBJ1 OBJ2 ROLE1 ROLE2 EVENTTYPE) doesn't imply that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are participating in an event of type EVENTTYPE it does imply that OBJ1 and OBJ2  are capable of playing ROLE1 and ROLE2 respectively in events of type EVENTTYPE.

See #$nearnessForRolesInEventType for a useful corresponding predicate.")
(comment CoronaryHeartDisease "A physiological condition in which the heart is weakened due to buildup of plaques in the arteries.  Seems to be related to the consumption/production of (saturated) fats and cholesterol.")
(comment SpikeFunction "Elements of #$SpikeFunction are functions which have a steep slope over some portion of their domain.  Thus a function which has a part which is a sharp increase, a sharp decrease, or a sharp increase followed immediately by a sharp decrease are all exemplar members of this collection.  A graph of a heartbeat over time illustrates numerous elements of #$SpikeFunction in it.  A graph of altitude as a function of position for someone walking off of a cliff is also an illustrative element of #$SpikeFunction.")
(comment rampFinalValue "(#$rampFinalValue RAMP VALUE) means that the ramp-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution RAMP has an ending value or height of VALUE.  For example, the final value of a ramp used to specify a temporal persistence distribution might be (#$Percent 95), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the ramp distribution pertains, the likelihood of being true at the #$rampEndLocation (ramp ending time) is 0.95. VALUE might also be a reified value such as `very likely'.")
(disjointWith Airport-Physical LaunchPad)
(comment OxygenatedBlood "The collection of all 'pieces' of #$Blood which are fully or mostly oxygenated.  Such blood normally exists in each #$SystemicArtery and each pulmonary vein (see #$PulmonaryVein-Generic).")
(comment causes-SitSitType "(#$causes-SitSitType CAUSING-SIT EFFECTED-SITTYPE) means that CAUSING-SIT will cause an instance of EFFECTED-SITTYPE  to come about.")
(comment Wedge-GolfClub "a kind of iron with an extreme slope primarily used to hit a golf ball out of a sand trap or short approach shots onto the green")
(comment MilitaryTankerVehicle "The collection of wheeled military vehicles which are used to transport fuel or other liquids.")
(disjointWith SkinHead RedSkin-PersonByBeliefSystem)
(comment Krypton "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of Krypton in stuffeous form.")
(comment DBKeyObj "Each #$DBKeyObj is a reified, unique identifier  for a physical tuple in a database table or other information source.")
(comment GroupOfCardinalityFn "(#$GroupOfCardinalityFn COL N) denotes the collection of all instances of (#$GroupFn COL) whose #$groupCardinality is N.")
(comment entailsCapability "(#$entailsCapability SYSTEM-SLOT EVENT-TYPE ACTOR-SLOT)
means that if an agent plays the role SYSTEM-SLOT in a
#$FunctionalSystem, it is expected that that agent has the ability to
play the role ACTOR-SLOT in events of type EVENT-TYPE throughout the
duration of the system.")
(comment genFormat-Precise "#$genFormat-Precise is similar to #$genFormat, but is intended to allow generation of more verbose and/or precise English from CycL formulas such that the resulting English can be uniquely identified with the single CycL formula from which it was produced.")
(comment isomorphicWith "(#$isomorphicWith ?Form1 ?Form2) states that the CycL formula?Form1 is structurally isomorphic with that of ?Form2; this isomorphism is highly suggestive of an analogy between the domain of ?Form1 and that of ?Form2.")
(comment Autotroph-Bacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium that use #$CarbonDioxide as their main or only source of #$Carbon.  This collection contains #$Chemolithotrophs and #$Photolithotrophs.")
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention Character-Abstract)
(comment unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsDuring "(#$unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsDuring DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PERIOD NUM) means that NUM 'units' have been filled (by all #$Prescribers) for DRUGTYPE via #$DrugPrescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be #$FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment DoughnutShop "A shop that serves doughnuts and coffee to customers and also sells fresh doughnuts by the dozen for take-out.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization BranchOfMilitaryService)
(comment Gonadotropin "#$Hormones which stimulate the gonads.")
(comment ProjectileShell-Gas "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is designed to cary gas, whether chemical or biological.")
(disjointWith AngularDistance ElectricalCharge)
(comment WarrantOfficer "The collection of all armed forces personnel with the
statuses of Petty Officer, Chief Petty Officer, Warrant Officer, or
Chief Warrant Officer.")
(comment SpreadingSheetOntoSurface "A collection of events. In each #$SpreadingSheetOntoSurface event, a #$SheetOfSomeStuff is spread out onto a surface so that it covers [#$covers-Sheetlike] it.")
(comment FissionWeapon-ImplosionMethod "The collection of #$FissionWeapons which use a series of precisely-shaped charges concentrated on a single focal point - a subcritical sphere of #$Plutonium. When set off simultaneously, the shaped charges compress the sphere of #$Plutonium into a supercritical mass and set off a #$NuclearFissionProcess.")
(comment detailedInProp "(#$detailedInProp OBJ EXP) says that OBJ is described somehow by the expression EXP")
(comment profileDBQueries "This #$QuaternaryPredicate is used to state the CycL and English (template) versions of queries used by various #$Cyc database applications and prototypes.  ARG1 is the type of object the query is about.  ARG2 is the type of information the query is asking for (the type of information the answer will consist of).  ARG3 is a CycL query expression.  ARG4 is a list consisting of a keyword followed by an English query (template) string.  The keyword may be :text or :tabular.  It indicates how the query answer should be formatted.  If the keyword is :text, the English query string should contain the Cyc variable ?subject, which denotes the object being profiled (the object the query is about).  This object will be an instance of ARG1.  If the keyword is :tabular, the English query string will be followed by two lists: a list of field (column) name strings, and a list of Cyc variables.  Each field name string corresponds to one of the variables.  The corresponding elements must occur in the same positions in their respective lists.  This arcane syntax allows the answer to be formatted as a table, if so desired.")
(comment ContiguousZoneFn "(#$ContiguousZoneFn ENT) picks out the region of the sea designated as the contiguous zone of ENT, in accordance with U.N provisions. An entity's contiguous zone must be adjacent to its territorial sea, and the territorial sea and contiguous zone of a country may not together be more than 24 nautical miles wide.")
(comment (VeryLowAmountFn SocialPower) "Powerlessness, the social effectiveness enjoyed by the the homeless, the chronically unemployed, and the mentally ill.")
(comment relevantInTypeOfPlace-Everywhere "(#$relevantInTypeOfPlace-Everywhere MT PLACE-TYPE) means that assertions in MT are relevant throughout the entire spatial extent of every instance of PLACE-TYPE.  See also #$relevantInTypeOfPlace-Somewhere.")
(comment TransportationPathSystem "A specialization of #$PathSystem instances of which are systems of spatial paths used for transportation. Examples include a country's rail system, a state's highway  system, and the system of hiking trails in a given national park.")
(comment AerialBomb "The collection of #$Bombs dropped from #$MilitaryAircraft.  Some very specialized instances are designed to explode in the air above the target.")
(comment OxiconazoleNitrate "The chemical compound which is an anti-fungal.")
(comment EmployeeStockOption "The collection of #$StockOptions owned by #$employees of the #$LegalCorporation some of whose #$Stock is the #$underlyingAsset for those options.  Such options are owned by employees who come into possession of them as a result of some transaction whose terms are available only to employees as a form of compensation.  For example, employees may receive stock options entirely free as a benefit, they may receive them as part of a 401(k) matching plan, or they may be allowed to buy the options at a discount.")
(comment exchangeRateDuring-Market "(#$exchangeRateDuring-Market UM1 UM2 THING NR) means that NR is the average market exchange rate of the #$UnitOfMoney UM1 for the #$UnitOfMoney UM2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  That is, NR UM1's can be traded for 1 UM2, and conversely, in a market that is not controlled by the #$GeopoliticalEntity whose currency UM1 is.  For example, the fact that during October of 1995 the market exchange rate between Liberian and United States dollars was 50 Liberian dollars for 1 US dollar can be expressed as (#$exchangeRateDuring-Market #$Dollar-Liberia #$Dollar-UnitedStates (#$MonthFn #$October (#$YearFn 1995)) 50).  See also #$exchangeRateDuring-Official and #$exchangeRateDuring.")
(comment TruckTractor "Vehicles used for hauling semitrailers or other freight trailers such as tankers or car carriers.")
(comment DialingATelephoneNumber-Manual "The collection of all instances of DialingATelephoneNumber where a human agent manually inputs a phone number to a phone by pressing buttons or turning a rotary dial.  Both partial and complete dialings are included.  See also #$DialingATelephoneNumber.")
(comment HydrogenFluorideMolecule "The collection of HF molecules.")
(comment PlantShoot "Shoots of plants, e.g., a stem, its leaves, flowers, etc.")
(comment Vibration-Translational "The center of mass of an #$objectMoving in a #$Vibration-Translational periodically translates back and forth due as a function of some location dependent potential.  For example, a ball bounces up and down.  When the ball is high its potential energy is high and rising kinetic energy is low and decreasing.  Eventually kinetic energy peters out and the ball comes to a stop turns around and starts heading downward.  This kind of motion applies to non-circular elements of #$Orbiting, mass spring systems, swinging pendulums.  A bus shuttling to and fro (see #$Translation-BackAndForth) is not an exemplar since there is no equilibrium position for the bus.  Note that  #$Vibration-Translational is different from vibrational movement due to shape change.  For example, if you hit a bell it vibrates by changing its shape periodically.  Its center of mass does not necessarily move back and forth.  Therefore a bell ringing which does not also rock back and forth is not an #$objectMoving in a #$Vibration-Translational.  Note that the most typical exemplars of #$Vibration-Translational (e.g. a pendulum swinging) are also elements of #$Translation-NoLocationChange.  However, not changing location is not a necessary property since, e.g. a ball bouncing its way across a stage is clearly an element of #$Vibration-Translational and does undergo location change.")
(comment NCAADivisionIAAProgram "The collection of college sports teams that the #$NationalCollegiateAthleticAssociation has classified as Division IAA.  This classification is generally relevant for football teams.  #$NCAADivisionIAAPrograms are generally not as talent-laden as #$NCAADivisionIAPrograms.")
(comment TheoryMicrotheory "The collection of all instances of #$Microtheory which contain rules about some topic, but exclude the definitions of the terms used in the rules (which should be defined in an instance of #$VocabularyMicrotheory), and also exclude reference to specific instances of #$TemporalThing (which belong in a #$DataMicrotheory) other than instances referred to in its #$mtTopics or which are otherwise mentioned in #$domainAssumptions.  Queries posed in a #$TheoryMicrotheory are answered solely considering the topic of that microtheory (or any #$genlMts). Scenario microtheories and #$ProblemSolvingCntxts are expected to draw on a large number of theory microtheories.")
(comment LandingShip "The collection of military amphibious landing ships.")
(comment EukaryoticMessengerRNA "The collection of instances of #$MessengerRNA produced by eukaryotic organisms.")
(comment FutureFn "(#$FutureFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-TIME) denotes the         subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances start after the starting of CONTEXT-TIME.")
(comment ValentinesCard "The collection of #$GreetingCards that are sold for/ and or sent on/before #$ValentinesDay each year. Such cards are often send anonymously, to express love/affection/lust for another person. People in relationships are often expected to send cards to their partners. The cards celebrate #$ValentinesDay, a religious holiday that commemorates (#$SaintFn #$Valentine-TheMartyr), though the life (and martyrdom) of this #$Saint have little to do with the idea of #$ValentinesCard . It is probable that the secular holiday arose because the feast day of (#$SaintFn #$Valentine-TheMartyr) occurs close to a pagan #$Love festival.")
(comment SkolemFunctionFn "#$SkolemFunctionFn is used by the #$CycCanonicalizer and should rarely (if ever) need to be seen by users or referenced in assertions entered at the EL level.  It is used by the canonicalizer to denote a skolem function before it is reified, when the skolem is derived from a formula asserted at the EL level that uses #$thereExists. Its arity is 3: the first argument is a list of the term variable arguments of the denoted skolem function, (term variables which are in the scope of the existential), the second argument is a variable which uniquely identifies the existentially quantified variable by which the denoted skolem will be represented in the canonical version of the formula, and the third is  a sequence variable if there is a sequence variable argument of the denoted skolem function (which there will be iff there is a sequence variable in the scope of the existential), and NIL otherwise.")
(disjointWith CohabitationUnit MultinationalCorporation)
(comment Hypertension "High blood pressure")
(comment MindControl "A collection of events in which one agent attempts to coerce the action
          of another's mind against their will.  This includes attempts using
          telepathy or ESP, but also includes, e.g., secret government experiments
          using drugs or satellites.  Borderline positive examples include administering
          truth serum during an interrogation.  Borderline negative examples include
          getting someone drunk in the hopes of facilitating sexual activity; stronger
          negative examples include persuading someone to believe something
          and coercion (using force, you can coerce someone's actions, but not their thoughts).")
(comment argGenlPreds "(#$argGenlPreds REL N PRED) means that anything given as the Nth argument to the relationship REL must be a specialization of PRED or PRED itself.")
(comment DessertGiftBasket "An instance of #$GiftBasketTypeByContent.  The collection of #$GiftBaskets that are filled with #$DessertFood.")
(comment SignalsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile involves           interception, direction-finding, or analysis of EM signals of any           kind.")
(comment enables-RemovesDisablingFactors "#$enables-RemovesDisablingFactors expresses the notion that an
agent may be 'enabled' by an event in the following sense: the event
removes all factors that are 'disabling', i.e., that would cause the agent
not to be capable of doing a given action -- put another way: all factors
that would prevent the agent from performing the action. More accurately,
(#$enables-RemovesDisablingFactors SIT AGENT ACT_TYPE) is true iff SIT
obtains, there are no factors preventing AGENT from performing an instance
of ACT_TYPE, and SIT is the cause of there being no such disabling
factors. Hence #$enables-RemovesDisablingFactors does not imply that the
agent is in fact capable of doing a token of ACT_TYPE: it merely entails
that no factor that would disable her is present. Note that in general this
is a stronger notion than merely removing incapacitating factors. Example:
giving an ax or a saw to a physically fit adult individual would typically
enable him to chop down a tree in this sense, since in typical
circumstances not having an ax would be disabling -- though perhaps not
incapacitating. Complex events such as military tasks may also be regarded
as typical examples of this concept -- e.g., in a
#$ReliefInPlace-MilitaryTask the relieved unit is enabled in this sense to
disengage and perform service support tasks.")
(comment IntelAttack-Focused "A subset of #$IntelAttack, #$IntelAttack-General is the collection           of intel attacks in which a small number of specific instances            of #$InformationBearingThing are targeted for retrieval from the           enemy by the perpetrator.")
(comment BirthdayCard "The collection of #$GreetingCards that are bought (or hand-made) and sent to a person on/before the person's #$birthDay to congratulate the person for having a #$birthDay.   People in family or romantic relationships are often expected to send such cards to their relatives or partners.  They are sometimes sent to work colleagues too.  (Different societies have different customs for #$BirthdayCards, birthday presents, etc.)")
(comment itemCopied "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$IBTCopying (a specialization of #$InformationTransferEvent) to instances of #$InformationBearingThing. (#$itemCopied COPY IBT) means that the reproduction event COPY produces a copy of the information-bearing thing IBT. This predicate is a specialization of #$informationOrigin. See also #$copyProduced, which relates copying events to the copies they produce (rather than to their sources).")
(comment nameSpelling "(#$nameSpelling NAME SPELLING) means that the #$ProperNameString SPELLING is a correct spelling of the #$Name NAME. For example, (#$nameSpelling #$Esteban-TheName \"Esteban\").")
(comment Sliding-LowFriction "A process of moving along a surface with all points of the moving obejct having the same trajectory")
(comment allergicTo "ARG1 will have an allergic reaction whenever participating in instances of situation type ARG2 with instances of ARG3.")
(comment Preposition-Duration "Prepositions which denote durations of time, for example, 'for'.")
(comment QuaternaryFunction "A specialization of both #$FixedArityFunction and #$QuaternaryRelation (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$QuaternaryFunction is a function that always takes four arguments at a time, i.e. has the arity (see #$arity) 4.")
(comment BacillusBacterium "A specialization of #$Bacterium whose instances are characterized by having cylindrical or rod-like shape.")
(comment SaintPatricksDay "Each of these is an annual #$Holiday celebrating the patron saint of Ireland. Currently, it is essentially a secular holiday as practiced in the United States of America. Traditional U.S. celebrations include parades, wearing green clothing, and sometimes even beer with green dye in it.")
(comment BallisticMissile-IntermediateRange "A ballistic missile with a range of 1,500-3,437 miles")
(comment EndorsingAProduct "The collection of events in which an agent publicly expresses a positive attitude towards some brand of product, in exchange for some (usually monetary) consideration from the product maker. The product endorsed is identified as the #$targetedProductType. Product endorsement is a specialization of #$Advertising.")
(comment NBCWeaponsUnit-Offensive "A subset of #$MilitaryOrganization.  Instances of #$NBCWeaponsUnit-Offensive are those military units specialized in attacking with either nuclear, biological, or chemical weapons.")
(comment OticDrugProduct "Drug products intended to be used in the ears.")
(comment activeDuringPeriod "(#$activeDuringPeriod PERSON PERIOD)

 says that PERSON pursued or completed many of his or her notable

 achievements during PERIOD. For example, 

(#$activeDuringPeriod #$Michelangelo #$TheRenaissance)

 says that #$Michelangelo was active during 

  #$TheRenaissance.")
(comment TVShow-IBT "A collection of objects; a subset of #$TVMediaProduct.  Every #$TVShow-IBT is a #$MovingImageWithSound, usually with some sort of #$News or #$Narrative content, and a duration of at least 20 minutes that appears on a specific #$TelevisionSet. Instances of #$TVShow-SingleCW are listed on schedules, whereas instances of #$TVShow-IBT, #$Commercial-CW, and public-service announcements are not.  Note that, e.g., 'Seinfeld' is not a #$TVShow-IBT but a #$TVSeriesProduct since it is a #$ConceptualWork.")
(comment Hamate "The Hamate is the merged fourth and fifth #$Carpalia in Humans.")
(comment Kerchief "A collection of pieces of cloth of various sizes, worn about the neck, over the head, or in the pocket of a suit coat.")
(disjointWith DiplomaticMission-ThePost RegionalGovernment)
(comment transPathSystemTypeOfRegion "This predicate relates a geographical region

such as a county, town, or the downtown area of a city

to a type of transportation path system that runs 

throughout the region.

(#$transPathSystemTypeOfRegion REGION TRANS-SYS-TYPE) 

means that there is an instance of TRANS-SYS-TYPE

that runs throughout (and possibly beyond) REGION.  

The system in question must be \"maximally spread\" 

throughout REGION, in the sense that it must not be a 

#$subPathSystems of any other transportation system 

wholly in REGION and covering a larger portion of REGION.  

For example, suppose that an instance of #$GridStreetSystem 

runs throughout the downtown area of City001, but that the 

more-inclusive street system that runs throughout City001 

as a whole is not generally grid-like.  While it would be 

true that (#$transPathSystemTypeOfRegion (#$DowntownFn City001) 

#$GridStreetSystem), it would not be true that

(#$transPathSystemTypeOfRegion City001 #$GridStreetSystem).

See also #$streetSystemOfArea.")
(comment elaborationAttribute-RST "The relation of elaboration attribute as used in Rhetorical Structure Theory.")
(comment nthDayTypeOfMonth "#$nthDayTypeOfMonth is used to say that a #$CalendarDay occurs annually on a specified nth #$DayOfWeekType during a certain month.  For example, if the #$CalendarDay always falls on the third Friday in June, one would use (#$nthDayTypeOfMonth #$CalendarDay Friday 3).  The month June needs to be specified in a separate assertion.  Notice that if the day is not a #$CalendarDay, but an #$Event or #$Holiday, the predicate #$eventTypeFallsOnNthDayTypeInMonth needs to be used instead.")
(comment argAndRestIsa "A ternary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.) used to 

place a specified #$isa based argument-type constraint on a given 

#$VariableArityRelation (q.v.) with respect to any of its argument-places 

whose ordinal position is greater than or equal to a specified number.

(#$argAndRestIsa RELN N COL) means that, as a necessary condition for 

semantic well-formedness, anything given as the Nth or greater argument 

to RELN must be an instance of COL.  Thus a closed formula

(RELN ARG1..ARG(N)..ARG(N+1)..) is well-formed only if each of ARG(N)..ARG(N+1).. is an instance of COL.  See also #$argsIsa and #$argAndRestGenl.")
(comment HorseFarm "A farm whose main activity is raising horses.")
(comment EukaryoticRNA-Molecule "The collection of #$RNAMolecules produced in #$EukaryoticCells, the cellular components of #$EukaryoticOrganisms.")
(comment ChastityBelt "A collection of tangible items.  Chastity belts are belt-like devices designed to be worn by woman and to prevent sexual intercourse while being worn.")
(comment allAssignedMilitaryOrg "(#$allAssignedMilitaryOrg SUPER SUB) means that SUB is a permanently assigned (immediate or more remote) sub-organization of SUPER #$assignedMilitaryOrg.  SUPER directly or indirectly commands SUB, supports it logistically, and with services, and either provides the money for SUB's budget or accounts for SUB within SUPER's own budget. There is financial support, service support, material support, and command subordination permanent (that is, the relationship has obtained historically and will continue to be hold for the foreseeable future).  Saying (#$allAssignedMilitaryOrg DVN-101 BAT-103) really means that the commander of DVN-101 can give operational orders to BAT-103, and that the headquarters of DVN-101 is responsible for coordinating logistic and admin support to BAT-103. Every military unit lower than division level is assigned to some unit.  See also #$allAttachedMilitaryOrg and #$allOperationalControlMilitaryOrg for contrast.")
(disjointWith BenefitsManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment Mica "Aluminum silicate based rock that characteristically splits into sheets.  Thin sheets of #$Mica are #$Translucent.")
(comment (RentingFn Automobile) "A collection of events; a subset of #$Renting.  In each instance of this collection, the object which the agent rents (i.e., the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer) is an instance of passenger car (#$Automobile).")
(comment CurrencyOfDateFn "A binary function, which takes a function belonging to the collection #$UnitOfMoney UOM1 as its first argument and a calendar time period DATE as its second argument, by means of which one can specify a #$UnitOfMoney UOM2 having the value of the currency UOM1 in DATE.  For example, ((#$CurrencyOfDateFn #$Dollar-Liberia (#$YearFn 1987)) 20) denotes $20 in 1987 Liberian dollars.  Because of inflation ((#$CurrencyOfDateFn #$Dollar-Liberia (#$YearFn 1997)) 20) is worth less than ((#$CurrencyOfDateFn #$Dollar-Liberia (#$YearFn 1987)) 20).  See also the more specific #$USDollarFn.")
(comment SystematicLevelOfCommunicability "The higher level of contagioity. If an #$Infection has this
level of contagiousness, someone in contact with an host of an instance this
type of infection is in practically contaminated automatically.")
(comment HardRockMusic "A loud, hard and bourgeoisie specialization of #$RockMusic. It is agressive, dominated by distorted guitars, sometimes organ, a simple song structure and mostly simple lyrics about the problems of everyday life. Its heyday was in the seventies with influential practitioners #$LedZeppelin-MusicGroup, DeepPurple, Judas Priest and #$AC-DC-MusicGroup. It is different from #$HeavyMetalMusic in its blues roots and a slower speed.")
(disjointWith Dock LaunchPad)
(comment soilChunk "The piece of soil within this physical-geographic region.")
(disjointWith MathematicalLanguage HumanLanguage)
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice AircraftCarrier)
(comment yzCrossSectionShapeType "The cross section shape type in the yz plane.")
(disjointWith KSTemplateMicrotheory LexicalMicrotheory)
(comment BorderCheckEvent-Thing "The subset of BorderCheckEvents in which a good or some other non-person object passes through a border checkpoint, unaccompanied by its owner, as in commercial shipping.")
(comment UnderspecifiedPredicate "The collection of predicates that capture underspecified
semantic views of complex relationships by committing neither to a
spatial/temporal/abstract/concrete/literal/metaphoric reading of the
relationship. Since such predicates are non-commital, so too are their
argument constraints. For instance, the #$arg2Isa constraint  of
#$to-UnderspecifiedLocation is #$Location-Underspecified, which is non-commital
as to a literal location (e.g., Moscow) or a metaphoric location
(e.g., Trouble, Purgatory, etc.).")
(comment BritishFolkRockMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic (but not of #$FolkRockMusic, which was largely
  American), #$BritishFolkRockMusic was mainly produced in England, and was heavily
  influenced by traditional #$FolkMusic of the #$BritishIsles-Region.  Influential 
  practitioners of this style include Fairport Convention, Pentangle, and Nick Drake.")
(comment FluidConduit "The collection of all conduits, natural or artifactual, through which fluid (instances of #$FluidTangibleThing) can flow in #$FluidFlowEvents.")
(comment DBKeyFunction "Instances are functions which, when applied to values of key fields from a particular row of a database table, return unique identifiers for that row.  #$DBKeyFunctions can be formed by applying #$DBKeyFunctionFn to the #$LogicalFields which are the key fields.")
(comment ailmentEpidemicType "This predicate relates a disease type to the collection of epidemics of that disease.  (#$ailmentEpidemicType AIL EP-COL) means that EP-COL is the collection of epidemics of the ailment AIL.")
(comment SwaddlingClothes "The collection of loose-fitting baby clothes, consisting of little more than a strip of cloth or several such strips used to wrap a baby.")
(comment GramStainTest "A collection of events in which a bacterial culture is

stained to distinguish #$GramPositiveBacterium from

#$GramNegativeBacterium.  In this test a heat-fixed smear is stained

for 1 minute with crystal violet and rinsed briefly under water.  Next

the smear is treated for 1 minute with Lugol's iodine (a solution of

iodine and potassium iodine in water) and rinsed again.

Decolorization is attempted with a solvent, for example ethonal (95%),

acetone, or iodine-acetone and immediately rinsed.  #$GramPositive

cells will be violet.  The smear is then counterstained for 30 seconds

with dilute carbolfuchsin to stain #$GramNegative cells red.")
(disjointWith Density AngularDistance)
(comment CombatEngineeringVehicle "The collection of tank-like vehicles used by military organizations to clear obstructions, prepare firing positions, fill in craters and ditches, and recover disabled vehicles.")
(comment UnderspecifiedCollectionType "A collection of collections. Each element of #$UnderspecifiedCollectionType is a collection of 
 of objects or stuffs that may bridge
any of the domains of literality and metaphoricity, space and time, or
physical and intangible. Each type of underspecified thing is intensionally
neutral with regard to such issues; the type exists to allow
underspecification to occur at the relational level, thus releasing
Natural Language (NL) semantics from the need to specify precise
semantic structures when such a responsibility is essentially post-NL
(i.e., one of real-world reasoning).  Inference rules should be used to
bridge between underspecified predicates and fully-specified
predicates. For instance,(#$contains-Underspecified #$Love
#$SiddharthaGautama) is an underspecified (and conventionally-metaphoric)
means of stating 'Siddhartha is in love'. Inference rules which encode the
common-sense relationship between abstract-states and containment are
responsible for producing the fully-specified assertion
(#$feelingTypeExperienced #$SiddharthaGautama #$Love) from this
underspecified form.  So why use the underspecified form at all? Firstly,
it conforms to human thought processes as visible through language use
(many, many empirical studies support this).  Secondly, it greatly
simplies the processes of lexical semantics and NL parsing.")
(disjointWith BiologicalEvent Archery)
(comment Pancreatitis "Inflammation of the pancreas.")
(comment actualTextOfSymbol "The predicate (#$actualTextOfSymbol SYMBOL STRING) relates a #$SyntaxSpecificationSymbol SYMBOL (in a #$CycEasyDocDescription) to the final text STRING that actually appears in the document.   In the #$FormalGrammarSpecification of the #$CycEasyDocDescription, the symbol SYMBOL will be one of its #$terminalSyntaxSymbols.  Note: The binary predicate #$actualTextOfSymbol depends on the microtheory to determine what document it applies in, whereas the ternary predicate (#$textOfTerminalSyntaxSymbol STRING SYMBOL SYSTEM) uses the 3rd argument position to specify the document.")
(comment Censuring-CommunicationAct "To harshly criticize, rebuke, or otherwise punish verbally or in writing.--BillJ, Feb. 5, 1998")
(comment GuidedMissileCruiser "The collection of #$Cruisers intended to be used for transporting and launching #$GuidedMissiles.")
(comment Northeast-Generally "An instance of #$GeographicalDirection-General (q.v.).  From a given reference point, #$Northeast-Generally comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees (in either horizontal direction) of #$Northeast-Directly.")
(comment PunctuationMark "The collection of all written symbol-marks, other than letters and numerals, giving clues as to what kind of grammatical structure is contiguous, e.g., quotation maks, periods, etc.  These are the physically written marks, not the abstract symbols they instantiate (see #$PunctuationSymbol).")
(comment FillingARefillPrescription-MailOrder "The collection of all events in which a #$DrugPrescription is refilled by a #$MailOrderPharmacy; a subset of #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder and #$FillingARefillPrescription.")
(comment expectedTenureInRank "(#$expectedTenureInRank COUNTRY BOS ECHELON RANK DURATION) means that
an agent who holds RANK in a military unit of the
branch-of-service BOS with #$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg COUNTRY and
#$echelonOfUnit ECHELON is expected to hold that RANK for
DURATION.")
(comment BiologicalAttackTypeByTargetType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$BiologicalAttackTypeByTargetType are collections of #$BiologicalAttack organized by the intended target type of the attack (e.g., attacks aimed primarily against personnel, versus livestock, versus plants).")
(comment Scavenging-Recon "#$Scavenging-Recon is a specialization of #$ResearchProject and #$StealingInformation.  It is the collection of events that involve searching through trash to acquire sensitive data (individuals in the collection #$SecurityInformation) without authorization.  Such events are often precursors to events in the collection #$AttackByComputerOperation, if they result in the discovery of, e.g., protected computer passwords. They may also lead to events in the collection #$AttackByComputerOperation more indirectly if they result in the discovery of personal information that could be used to guess a password or to perform more effectively an event in the collection #$SocialEngineering.")
(comment LandStuff "A specialization of #$NaturalTangibleStuff.  Each instance of #$LandStuff is a portion of the stuff that the ground of a planet (at or near its land surface) is made of, including rocks, boulders, sand grains, soil, mud, lava, and mixtures of those things (such as islands or whole continents).  Examples of #$LandStuff include #$ContinentOfAustralia, #$CapeCod, Zion Hill, and the lava pouring out of #$MountEtna-Volcano.")
(disjointWith PathForWheeledVehicles CityBlock)
(comment Mooning "The collection of all events in which someone uncovers their #$Buttocks and points them toward the #$Person(s) they wish to provoke (i.e. the #$communicationTarget).")
(comment PhysicalForce-ElectroWeak "A \"unification\" of the #$PhysicalForce-Electromagnetic and #$PhysicalForce-Weak forces. These latter are now seen as aspects of this single force.")
(comment Replication-DNA "The process wherein the complementary strands of a DNA double-helix unwind and separate to serve as templates for the construction of two new complementary strands, resulting in production of two identical new DNA molecules.  The process is mediated by DNA polymerases.")
(comment TetraHydroCannabinol "The collection of all portions of tetrahydrocannabinol, or THC, believed to be the primary active constituent in #$Marijuana and #$Hashish.")
(comment SouthWestWind "The collection of all winds that blow from the southwest.  See #$WindProcess.")
(comment GameboyGame "The collection of video games and versions of such that are made to run specifically on a #$Gameboy-TheProduct platform.")
(comment OneWayReformulation-Forward "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
reformulation can only be performed in the #$ReformulationForwardDirection
direction.")
(comment NucleusFn "#$NucleusFn is a Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  #$NucleusFn takes an instance of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons (q.v.) as its single argument and returns a collection of all the atomic nucleii belonging to element-stuff of that type.  Thus, (#$NucleusFn E) denotes a subcollection of #$AtomicNucleus whose elements all have the same number of protons. For example, (#$NucleusFn #$Carbon) is the collection of #$Carbon nuclei, each of which has six protons.")
(comment PreparingFinancialRecords "A specialization of #$InformationRecordingProcess and #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$PreparingFinancialRecords is an event in which financial records are prepared for some purpose.")
(comment Moat "A collection of artifacts.  Each instance of #$Moat is
a deep wide trench around a building (e.g. a castle) usually filled with water.")
(disjointWith FallingProcess LoweringAnObject)
(comment UpwardParabolicTrajectory "An upward parabolic trajectory")
(comment stepLocation "(#$stepLocation STEP LOCATION) means that the change (step, increment or decrement) of the step-shaped #$PersistenceDistribution STEP occurs at LOCATION (a specified time or place).  For example, the LOCATION used to specify a temporal step persistence distribution might be (#$YearFn 1066), meaning that for the assertion or assertions to which the step pertains, the likelihood of being true would change (go up or down, according to the shape of the step) during the year 1066.")
(comment SourceMicrotheory "A collection of microtheories.  An instance of #$SourceMicrotheory represents a source external to the #$CycKB, from which the Microtheory Contents of such a microtheory were obtained.")
(comment SubplanetaryStellarOrbiterTypeByPhysicalProperty "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$SubplanetaryStellarOrbiter whose instances are all of the same physical property.")
(comment InhalerCanisterHolder "The collection of all InhalerCanisterHolders.  An #$InhalerCanisterHolder is a plastic holder into which small aerosol canisters fit for dispensing asthma medications.   Each #$InhalerCanisterHolder is a physical part of some #$InhalerDevice.")
(comment TravelingByMeansOfFn "(#$TravelingByMeansOfFn TRANSPORTERTYPE) returns the collection of all instances of #$TransportationEvent in which the #$transporter is an instance of TRANSPORTERTYPE.")
(comment BradleyFightingVehicle "Specialized type of #$ArmoredPersonnelCarrier used regularly by the modern US Army.")
(comment Riel-Cambodia "The unitOfCurrenty used in Cambodia-AtPresent.")
(comment OfferingABribe "A collection of actions.  In each instance of #$OfferingABribe, some agent offers an inducement to another agent who has the power to do something that the first agent wants.")
(comment supplyRateThrough "(#$supplyRateThrough PT1 COL PT2 RATE) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 (on their way from their origin to PT1) at the #$Rate RATE.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyRateThrough is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and PT3 might, for example, be a #$Hose, a #$Railway, a #$GeographicalRegion, or a #$BloodVessel.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(comment PhloxFlower "The reproductive organ of a Phlox plant.")
(comment relationExistsSpecExists "(#$relationExistsSpecExists PRED COL1 COL2) means that there

exists a subcollection of COL1, SUBCOL1, such that there exists an instance

of COL2, INS2, such that (PRED SUBCOL1 INS2).")
(comment PsychicAdviser "The collection of all #$Persons who give advice in exchange for money based on purported psychic abilities.")
(disjointWith Water SubAtomicParticle)
(comment M9ArmoredCombatEarthMover "A type of ampibious military earthmoving equipment.  The vehicle hull is a welded and bolted aluminum structure with a two speed winch capable of 25,000 pound line pull.  It is equipped with a unique suspension system which allows the front of the vehicle to be raised, lowered, or tilted to permit dozing, excavating, rough grading and ditching functions.  In addition, the M9 has armor protection against small arms and artillery fragmentation, a smoke screening capability and chemical-biological protection for the operator.  The M9 is capable of 30 MPH road speed, can swim at 3 MPH (under ideal conditions) and is transportable in C130, C141, and C5A aircraft.  The M9 is capable of excavation and preparation/reduction of obstacles, preparation of bridging operations, battle positions, strong points, and protective emplacements (for command posts, air defense, communications equipment and critical supply/logistical bunkers). (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment Culture-Bacterial "The collection of all bacterial cultures.  Instances are
produced by inoculating bacterial cells to a nutritious
#$CultureMedium and incubating to allow the #$Bacterium
cells to grow and divide.  Most bacterial species have particular
mediums and conditions needed to assure optimum growth.  See also
#$BacteriumOfTypeInCultureFn.")
(comment OrientalHealthCareEvent "#$OrientalHealthCareEvent is a collection of #$AlternativeMedicineHealthCareEvents that use one of the healing modalities which are studied in the branch of #$AlternativeMedicine known as #$OrientalMedicine. These therapies include #$Acupuncture and #$Acupressure, for example.")
(comment YoMamaJoke "A subset of #$JokeOffensiveToSome, #$YoMamaJoke is the collection of all           jokes that are of the form 'Yo mama so SO-AND-SO, SUCH-AND-SUCH is the case'.")
(comment stuffInExposureEvent "This predicate relates instances of #$ExposureToSubstance to that which the object exposed (see #$objectExposed) is exposed to in the event.")
(comment Lupus "Lupus is a chronic autoimmune disease where the immune system, for unknown

    reasons, becomes hyperactive and attacks normal tissue. This attack results in inflammation and

    brings about symptoms. ")
(comment StabilizingFunction "Elements of #$StabilizingFunction are those which may take on any values in the beginning of their domain but eventually settle out to some 'normal' or at 'rest' or 'target' value.  Examples include displacement of a dampened spring oscillator as a function of time, a commodity's price as stabilizing mechanisms take over, the position of a servo feedback driven robot arm.  Homeostatic processes can be characterized by #$StabilizingFunction.")
(comment mtSubsetAbstractionLevel "(#$mtSubsetAbstractionLevel MT COLLECTION) means that when reasoning in (or with) the context MT, (instances of) classes of objects at about the level of abstraction indicated by COLLECTION should be attended to, or taken into account.  If you consider the knowledge base as a lattice of abstract concepts arranged in a hierarchical structure via the subset/superset relation (#$genls), then the further `up' the hierarchy you go from COLLECTION, the less likely it is that (instances of) these classes should be used in inferencing.  (Instances of) classes may also become less worth attending to as you go `down' the hierarchy (although it's hard to see how this could be true in a system with class-property inheritance). See also #$mtPartonomicAbstractionLevel.")
(disjointWith ExistingStuffType TransportationEventByVehicleType)
(comment FromLabel "The collection of #$AddressLabels attached to packages that indicate the sender's address.  Note: these are not required.")
(comment DeoxygenatedBlood "The collection of all 'pieces' of #$Blood which are fully or mostly deoxygenated.  Such blood normally exists in each #$SystemicVein and each pulmonary artery (see #$PulmonaryArtery-Generic).")
(comment interferesWithGoal "(#$interferesWithGoal ACT GOALFORM) means that the action ACT makes it less likely that the goal expressed in the formula GOALFORM will be achieved.")
(comment Wood-GolfClub "golf clubs with large heads on them, usually made of wood, which are used for hitting the ball very long distances with less accuracy than with an iron club")
(comment MinePlow "The collection of all devices intended to be mounted on a military vehicle and used to unearth mines.")
(comment PluralityOfLikeSubevents "The collection of all events that are groups of the same type of subevent.  Note that an event does not  qualify as an instance simply in virtue of having a number of subevents of the same type, the event must be entirely composed of these events. Also note that not all groupings of like subevents constitute an  instance, the grouping must be regarded as a single event in its own right.  A positive example would be the event of making exactly thirty copies of a particular document for a meeting, it is an event composed of instances of copying.  However, if we considered thirty random instances of making a single copy of that document, this would not constitute an instance insofar as that collection of events would likely not form a group of events that could be regarded as a single event.")
(comment determination-UnderspecifiedRelation "Underspecified determination is a relation between two types of objects: roughly the essential properties of instances of the first type depend in some way on the essential properties of instances of the second type. Similar to the metaphysical relation of supervenience.")
(comment En "A unit of distance whose length is half an #$Em.  This is the same as the width of the letter N in many variable width fonts.")
(comment senses "(senses SENSOR ITEM) means that SENSOR detects ITEM. Sensor can be a human eye, or a metal detector, or a piece of mine sweeping equipment, RADAR, etc. Contrast #$senses with #$perceives. The latter takes a #$PerceptualAgent in the first argument position. This suggests that there is cognition, or awareness involved. However, a sensor can sense the presence of something even when there is no cognition involved.")
(comment Influence "Closely related to #$Prestige, #$Influence denotes the respect one Agent commands. Other than #$Prestige, which is a quality sort of passively admired, #$Influence denotes the ability to actually get involved in decision making processes, i.e. have a respected say in these contexts.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink TransportationEvent)
(comment xzCrossSection "This predicate relates an object to the arbitrarily thin slice of the object that defines the xz-cross section of the object as determined by the object's intrinsic axes.  See also #$xzCrossSection, #$yzCrossSection and  #$IntrinsicAxisOfObjects.")
(comment Gracefulness "Performing a particular activity with physical grace. i.e. fluid body movements.  This is meant to be distinct from physical precision.")
(comment (InfectionFn Meninges) "Meningitis - an inflammation of the #$Meninges, esp. of the #$PiaMater and #$ArachnoidMater, caused by a bacterial

                  or viral infection and characterized by high fever, severe headache, and stiff neck or

                  back muscles.")
(comment mostSpecificClass "(#$mostSpecificClass ?Ins ?Col) means that the most specific collection --in terms of its depth in the hierarchy -- that ?Ins is an instance of is ?Col.")
(comment Chemolithoautotroph "A collection of #$Bacterium that are both #$Autotroph-Bacterium and #$Chemolithotrophs.")
(comment ModernFrigate "A collection. Warships which are larger than destroyers and smaller than cruisers.")
(disjointWith AwardPractice CommunicationConvention)
(comment eventTypeThreatensWithFrequency "(#$eventTypeThreatensWithFrequency EVENT-TYPE OBJ-TYPE FREQUENCY) means that events of type THREAT-TYPE threaten damage to things of type OBJ-TYPE with frequency FREQUENCY.  The purpose of this predicate is to represent type-level claims about the threats certain events pose to physical objects")
(comment SecretaryGeneral "A collection.  Each instance of #$SecretaryGeneral is the principal administrative officer of an organization.  As such, the secretary general of an organization also heads the #$Secretariat.  Since this role is primarily administrative, the secretary general is not directly responsible for making policy.")
(comment AntiSubmarineRocket "The collection of #$Missiles designed

 to destroy or inflict damage on #$Submarines.")
(comment MeatProcessingPlant "Local (one site) organizations that process dead animals to produce meat for consumption, and possibly other products.")
(comment AnalSex "The collection of events involving anal penetration of one agent with another agent's penis.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization BranchOfMilitaryService)
(comment Truck "A specialization of #$RoadVehicle.  Each instance of #$Truck is a road vehicle designed to carry both passengers and (relatively heavy) cargo.  A typical instance of #$Truck has a cab area for the driver, as well as a large cargo area separate from the cab.  The cargo area of a truck may be open (as in many instances of #$PickupTruck) or closed (as in most instances of #$SemiTrailer-Truck).  Some specializations of #$Truck are #$DumpTruck, #$FireTruck, and #$GarbageTruck.")
(comment Adrenosterone "An #$Androgen secreted by the adrenal cortex.")
(comment agentAPIConstant "(#$agentAPIConstant TERM AGENT) relates a TERM in Cyc to a sofware agent that uses some description of the term as part of it's API. Thus modifying certain constants may require changes to one or more agents (or agent communities) to match.")
(comment Nut-TheFruit "A dry hard dry fruit which has an edible kernel and a shell on the outside.")
(comment ProjectileShell-Illumination "The collection of #$ProjectileShell-Pyrotechnics that provides  illumination of enemy targets, typically for night warfare.  These warheads  usually contain a flare or magnesium flare candle as the payload, which is  expelled by a small charge and is parachuted to the ground.")
(disjointWith Temperature ElectricalCharge)
(comment increasedChanceForRoleBecause "(#$increasedChanceForRoleBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP)
means that the chance of AGENT's playing the role ROLE in a situation
of type EVTTYPE is increased because PROP is true in the reasoning
domain.")
(comment SpreadingStuffOntoSurface "A collection of events. In each #$SpreadingStuffOntoSurface event, some stuff is spread out onto a surface so that it covers [#$covers-Paintlike] it.")
(comment (IsotopeFn Uranium 238) "The collection of pieces of #$Uranium whose atoms have a mass number of 238. Uranium-238 is an isotope of #$Uranium.")
(comment correspondingSequences "(#$correspondingSequences LIST1 LIST2) means that LIST1

is a list of of deoxyribonucleotides and LIST2 is a corresponding

sequence of ribonucleotides.  The coding

sequences of ribonucleic acid molecules (see #$RNAMolecule) differ

from the coding sequences of deoxyribonucleic acid molecules (see

#$DNAMolecule) in that the nucleic acid thymine in DNA is replaced by

the ribonucleic acid uracil in RNA.  Corresponding sequences in DNA

and RNA molecules are thus coding sequences that are identical, save

that where 'T' appears in the nucleic sequence, 'U' appears in the

ribonucleic sequence.")
(comment FullNelsonLike-SexualPosition "The collection of sexual positions that are commonly referred to
as full Nelson in North America and double nelson in central European
countries. The configuration is close to a type of wrestling holds after
which it's been named.")
(comment SwimMeet-SportsEvent "The collection of all swim meets -- competitions where representatives from two or more swim teams compete in swimming races and diving competitions.")
(comment recordedSlots "The entries of unit ARG1 on slot ARG2 are recorded somewhere.")
(comment CuttingSomething "A specialization of both #$HandlingADevice and #$SeparationEvent.  Each instance of #$CuttingSomething is an event in which some piece of material stuff is cut, whether or not a complete separation of parts occurs.  Specializations of #$CuttingSomething include #$CuttingNails, #$Butchering, and #$CuttingFabric.")
(comment TransportationLicense "A license to operate some kind of transportation device.")
(comment SocialPower "The collection of attributes that describe a person's social power, `clout,' the ability to influence people and achieve one's social goals through some combination of privilege, position, personal contacts, skill, hard work, and intelligence.  Money (income, wealth) and esteem/prestige may both contribute to attaining social power and may be necessary to hold on to it, but they cannot be equated with it.  This is basically Max Weber's schema.")
(comment pigments "The components of objects or substances which provide coloration.")
(comment RoadSystem "A specialization of #$ConnectedPathSystem instances of which are systems of roads (see #$PathForWheeledVehicles). Examples include the US Interstate Highway system and any  system of all the connected roads throughout an entire city  or country.")
(comment AirDefenseSystem "A collection.  An instance of #$AirDefenseSystem is a group of sensors and weapons designed to detect, and defend against, aerial military attack, either by #$MilitaryAircraft or airborne #$Weapons.")
(comment heightToReduce "(#$heightToReduce FEATURE HEIGHT] means that the topographical feature (generally, a #$Riverbank) should be reduced in a #$ReducingASlope event by removing a 'wedge' of height HEIGHT.")
(comment BetamethasoneDiproprionate "The chemical compound which is a steroid.")
(comment JobPosition "#$JobPosition is the collection of all job positions conceived as #$StaticSituations that exist at an #$Organization. A #$JobPosition can be characterized by a set of #$duties (see also #$dutiesOfAgentInJob) that the person filling the #$JobPosition will be expected to perform. In practice, we often use instances of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg instead of specializations of #$JobPosition to represent types of job positions. See also #$JobPositionTypeFn. A #$JobPosition can be either open or filled (see #$JobOpen and #$JobFilled). A #$JobPosition is not the same as a #$WorkAgreement or a #$HasPositionRelationship. These latter two exist only when a #$JobPosition is filled by a #$Person who enters into a relation with the #$Organization that has the #$JobPosition. For each #$JobPosition, there can be only a single #$Person who fills it for a given temporal interval, although two different #$Persons may successively fill the same #$JobPosition. Use #$versionOfJobPosition to relate a #$JobPosition to a #$HasPositionRelationship.")
(comment ReceivingInformationByTelephone "The collection of all 'receivings' where what is received is information or data sent via phone line.  #$ListeningOnATelephone is one important specialization, but the collection includes all instances where data of any kind is received from a phone transmission. Instances of #$TelephoneConversation ordinarily include at least one instance of #$ReceivingInformationByTelephone as an important subevent.")
(comment HydrogenSulfideMolecule "The collection of H2S molecules.")
(comment Flower-BotanicalPart "The collection of all reproductive organs of angiosperm plants.  May or may not look like conventional 'flowers'.")
(comment nearestIsa "A #$TaxonomicSlotForAnyThing, and a specialization of #$isa (q.v.).  (#$nearestIsa OBJ COL) means that COL is a \"nearest\" collection of which OBJ is an instance.  That is, (#$isa OBJ COL) holds, OBJ is not identical to COL, and there is no reified #$Collection NEARER-COL distinct from OBJ and COL such that both (#$isa OBJ NEARER-COL) and (#$genls NEARER-COL COL) hold.  Note that #$nearestIsa is non-assertible (see #$notAssertible), since its extension at any given time depends upon (and so must be recomputed from) the current state of the #$isa and #$genls hierarchy in the Cyc Knowledge Base.")
(comment VulnerableToSYNFlood "#$VulnerableToSYNFlood is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer. A computer has this vulnerability if it is running an operating system that fails to handle excessive streams of malformed
 SYN packets.")
(comment LogisticLandingShip "A collection. Military logistic landing ships.")
(comment TransportationFromToFn "(#$TransportationFromToFn PLACE1 PLACE2) denotes the collection of instances of #$TransportationEvent which begin at PLACE1 and end at PLACE2.")
(comment TransnationalCriminalOrganization "A subcollection of #$CriminalOrganization. Instances of #$TransnationalCriminalOrganization are organized syndicates that operate illicit enterprises, such as a narcotics trafficking or fraud, on an international level, but remain based in a home country.")
(comment BoneFracture "Broken bone")
(comment EmulatorHardware "A collection of #$ComputerHardwareItems.  Every instance of #$EmulatorHardware is a device running certain instances of #$EmulatorProgram in order to emulate some other device. See also #$emulatesType.")
(comment effectiveSterilizationMeansFor "(#$effectiveSterilizationMeansFor MICROBETYPE STUFFTYPE) means that, absent evidence to the contrary, a given person can perform a killing of an instance of MICROBETYPE by means of an instance of STUFFTYPE with a high level of #$Effectiveness.")
(comment MicrotheoryDesignatingRelation "The collection of #$Relations which specify that a #$ELSentence-Assertible is to be interpreted in a given #$Microtheory.  It will be canonicalized and checked for well-formedness with respect to that microtheory. Each microtheory-designating relation has an argument which denotes a microtheory, and another argument which denotes a #$ELSentence-Assertible.  It may have other arguments as well. Use #$microtheoryDesignationArgnum and #$sentenceDesignationArgnum to specify these argument positions for each microtheory-designating relation.")
(comment MaintenancePerson "The collection of maintenance workers.")
(comment SpecialForcesUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units that are dedicated to           'special forces' operations--ie, operations carried out by           comparatively small units involving reconnaissance, sabotage,           security and 'black' ops, usually carried out behind enemy lines.")
(comment RescueVehicle "The collection of vehicles, the primary purpose

  of which is to transport rescuers to, and

   rescuers and rescuees from, rescue sites.

  This is a distinct class from #$EmergencyVehicle,

  which includes #$FireTrucks, many of which

   are not #$RescueVehicles.")
(comment IntelAttack-General "A subset of #$IntelAttack, #$IntelAttack-General is the collection           of intel attacks in which no specific instances  of            #$InformationBearingThing are targeted for retrieval from the           enemy by the perpetrator.")
(comment Pedophilia-FemaleChild "This collection involves behaviors which treat female children as sexual objects of (male or female) adult desires.")
(comment Instructions "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork. Each instance of #$Instructions is an abstract work that outlines a sequence of tasks to be performed by an agent.  Positive examples of instantiations are instructions on a food package, verbal instructions, a musical score.  Illustrative specializations include #$DirectionsToGetSomewhere and #$InvestmentGuide.")
(comment PsychologicalAilment "The collection of ailments that are classified as psychological due to their origin and/or manifestation in the mind of the sufferer rather than (or at least in addition to, and perhaps causing) manifestations in the sufferer's body. Having a brain tumor is not an instance of this collection, but imagining that you have one is an instance of #$PsychologicalAilment , and so is the deep case of depression you fall into once you believe (rightly or wrongly) that you have a brain tumor. Some subcollections of this collection are the collections #$Phobia, #$Depression-PsychologicalCondition, and #$PanicAttack.")
(comment Preposition-Duration-Atelic "Prepositions which denote durations of time, and generally modify atelic or incomplete events; for example, 'for'.")
(comment genlSlotLists "(#$genlSlotLists LIST01 LIST02) is true iff LIST01 and LIST02
have the same length and, for every N > 0 and <= the lentgh of the lists, if
N-SLOT1 is the N-th element of LIST01 and N-SLOT2 is the N-th element of
LIST02, then (#$genlPreds N-SLOT1 N-SLOT2). Note that it would make sense
to define this predicate for any #$Predicate lists whatsoever, as opposed
to just #$ActorSlotLists. At the time of this writing, #$ActorSlotList is
the only defined collection of predicate lists.")
(comment hasPartAsBorder "(#$hasPartAsBorder REGION SPATIALTHING) means that part of SPATIALTHING forms part of the border of REGION.")
(comment QuintaryFunction "A specialization of both #$QuintaryRelation and #$Function-Denotational. An instance of #$Function-Denotational FUNC is an instance of #$QuintaryFunction if and only if FUNC has an #$arity of 5.")
(comment CoccusBacterium "A specialization of #$Bacterium whose instances are characterized by having spherical shape.")
(comment SalaryAccount "An account for salary that an employee receives.")
(comment BallisticMissile-CSS8 "A short range ballistic missile produced in China.")
(comment EndorsingAPoliticalCandidate "The collection of events in which an agent publicly expresses support for some political candidate.")
(comment rootAccountForSystem "(#$rootAccountForSystem ROOT-ACCOUNT SYSTEM) means that ROOT-ACCOUNT is an account on #$ComputationalSystem SYSTEM which is used for administration and therefore has greater privileges than the user accounts on SYSTEM. Unlike #$UserAccounts, for which SYSTEM often spans an entire local area network of machines, for #$RootAccounts SYSTEM is almost always a single computer (for security reasons). For the MS Windows version of this concept, see #$administratorAccountForSystem.")
(comment Oxytocic "Class of drug products that stimulate uterine contractions.")
(comment MediaOrganization "This collection is a subset of #$CommunicationsOrganization.  Every instance of #$MediaOrganization exists for the purpose of disseminating information to the public (cf. #$MediaTransferEvent).  Examples of #$MediaOrganization include radio stations, cable-TV providers, and publishing companies.  A #$MediaOrganization may also create the #$MediaProducts it distributes.  However, an organization that merely creates #$MediaProducts, but does not distribute them, is not a #$MediaOrganization.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn TwelfthRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment Cunnilingus "The collection of events involving oral stimulation of the external female genitalia.")
(disjointWith GovernmentMilitaryOrganization DiplomaticMission-ThePost)
(comment hasProtocolStack "(hasProtocolStack ?COMP ?STACK) means that ?STACK is the instance of #$NetworkProtocolStack which is implemented on ?COMP. A #$NetworkProtocolStack is not actually a #$ComputerProgram-CW; it is more of a #$ProgramSpecification, which is why the predicate #$programFoundOnComputer is not used.")
(comment logicalCondition-RST "The relation known as logical condition in Rhetorical Structure Theory.")
(comment solubilityOfSampleInSubst "(#$solubilityOfSampleInSubst SOLUTE SOLVENT DEGREE) means that the #$PartiallyTangible individual SOLUTE can dissolve in the substance type SOLVENT with this qualitative DEGREE of #$Solubility (q.v.).")
(comment postalCodeOfAddress "The predicate #$postalCodeOfAddress relates an instance of #$ContactLocation to an instance of #$PostalCode.  (#$postalCodeOfAddress LOC PC) means that the location LOC has the #$PostalCode PC.  For example, if LOC had the address: P.O. Box 1677-B, New York, NY, 10014, PC would be the string `10014'.  See also #$ContactLocation.")
(comment GuessingGame "The collection of games in which participants compete to identify some obscurely indicated thing; includes #$Charades, twenty questions, I spy, and others")
(comment embeddedCylinderInSheet "The predicate (#$embeddedCylinderInSheet CYLINDER SHEET) means that the #$SheetOfSomeStuff SHEET surrounds all of the #$LongAndThin object CYLINDER or a section its major axis which extends through the length of SHEET.  The predicate is agnostic as to whether the cylindrical object is part of the sheet.  

If the #$LongAndThin object is a part of SHEET, it need not be an internal part.

Examples of this predicate include wires in a ribbon cable, #$Threads in a piece of #$Cloth, and lacrimal ducts in an #$Eyelid.")
(comment backchainDiscouraged "(#$backchainDiscouraged PREDICATE) means that rules that conclude PREDICATE are most likely not going to have to be used in order to prove literals involving PREDICATE.  In other words, when performing inferences about literals involving PREDICATE, rules that conclude PREDICATE should be heuristically disfavored. See also #$backchainRequired, #$backchainEncouraged, and #$backchainForbidden.")
(disjointWith KidsChatRoom SexualProductOrServiceEvent)
(comment Yaw-WhileTranslating "#$Yaw-Orientational while moving along a non-solid #$motionPathway-Complete.  The concept applies to water-, air-, and spacecraft.  For water- and aircraft, this is normally a rotation about a vertical axis.")
(comment favorableMonthForTour "(#$favorableMonthForTour TOUR MONTH) means that the instance of #$CalendarMonth MONTH is favorable for conducting the instance of #$TravelTour TRAVEL.")
(disjointWith InventoryBuyingManager Minister-Governmental)
(disjointWith PortalCovering RecordingOfWaveIBT)
(comment noIDForField "(noIDAvailable LF KEYOBJ LTS) means that for the implicit field LF of the schema LTS, on the row identified by the DBKeyObj KEYOBJ, there is no unique ID which can identify the entity binding to the implicit field LF.")
(comment occupation "This predicate relates persons to the types of occupations they have.  (#$occupation PERSON OCCTYPE) means that PERSON is an instance of the collection of persons that constitute OCCTYPE.")
(comment MilesPerHour "An instance of #$UnitOfSpeed. When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$MilesPerHour returns an instance of #$Speed as its value. For example, (#$MilesPerHour 55) is a speed of 55 miles per hour.")
(comment WeaponProductionFacility "The collection of all #$ConstructionArtifacts that serve

  as production facilities for #$Weapons.  

  Generally, a #$WeaponProductionFacility

  will consist of some property

  on which there are one or more #$FactoryBuildings.")
(comment PopRockMusic "A kind of popular music drawing upon the same musical elements and instruments as #$RockMusic, but in a much more digestable and in many ways less ambitious, less rebellious, less agressive and more commercially oriented and short lived form. #$PopRockMusic focuses on singing rather than instrumentals, the guitars are less distorted, the instrumental parts and the songs in general tend to be shorter than their rock counterparts, the tunes are catchier, and the lyrics are likely to be politically correct. Typical practioners of #$PopRockMusic include #$ABBA-MusicGroup, Ace of Base, Milli Vanilli, and New Kids on the Block.")
(comment MillenniaDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in millennia. More precisely, an expression of the form (#$MillenniaDuration NUM) denotes the (\"point-value\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM millennia in duration, and an expression of the form (#$MillenniaDuration MIN MAX) denotes the (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN millennia and at most MAX millennia in duration.")
(comment M35A2SupplyTruck "A type of military supply truck.")
(comment BorderCheckEvent-Person "The subset of BorderCheckEvents in which a person (and perhaps that person's luggage) passes through a border checkpoint.")
(comment underspecifiedLocation "(#$underspecifiedLocation ACT LOC) states that an event ACT
occurs relative to the #$Location-Underspecified LOC. This location may
be a destination (e.g., 'go to Newark' and 'go to hell') or a current
location (either 'on', 'in' or 'at'). #$underspecifiedLocation is used as 
an inferential hub for more specific (though still underspecified)
predicates such as #$to-UnderspecifiedLocation, #$at-UnderspecifiedLandmark,
#$on-UnderspecifiedSurface and #$in-UnderspecifiedContainer, to allow rules
to refer to 'locatives' in a general way.")
(comment CountryRockMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic whose heyday was the late 1960s to the early

  1970s.  Heavily influenced by CountryMusic, #$CountryRockMusic often incorporates

  instruments more commonly featured in Country than in Rock, e.g. the pedal steel type

  of #$Guitar-Electric.  Influential practitioners of this style include Gram Parsons,

  Linda Ronstadt, and the Eagles.")
(comment inputingCoupler "(#$inputingCoupler ?SIT ?COUP) means that ?COUP is one of the 2 connected couplers in the #$Coupling-Configuration ?SIT.  In addition, the flow of materials enabled by ?SIT generally and typically comes from ?COUP.  See also #$outputingCoupler.")
(comment distributionCapacity "(#$distributionCapacity PT PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that the #$Rate RATE is the greatest possible rate at which instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE could be distributed to the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT.  In a general economic context, PT will often be an instance of (#$GroupFn #$IntelligentAgent).")
(comment salaryIncome "(#$salaryIncome PERSON MONETARY_FLOW_RATE) means that #$Person has an #$occupation as an #$Employee and earns salary from this employment at the specified rate.  The rate is the official rate of payment to the employee.  It includes funds withheld for taxes, union dues, insurance, retirement, and/or other purposes.  Income from sources other than a salary are not included in this rate.  If the rate is expressed in monetary units per hour or per day, that refers to working hours (or days), so that the number is not multiplied by the number of hours (or days) in a year to obtain a monetary rate per year.  In addtion, note that this rate can vary from time to time.  Someone may have a #$salaryIncome during the day of one value, but a different value during the night when working at a second job for a different employer.")
(comment BacteriumIdentificationTestType "A collection of collections.  These are all methods of
identifying types of #$Bacterium.  It includes the various stains and
other tests performed on bacterial cultures.")
(disjointWith Density ElectricalCharge)
(comment nullMapsTo "(#$nullMapsTo ?MAPPING ?VAL) means that the #$ReifiedMapping ?MAPPING assumes that, if a field that uses this mapping is null, the represented value should be assumed to be ?VAL.")
(comment UnderspecifiedStuffType "A collection of collections. Each element of #$UnderspecifiedStuffType is a stuff-like collection  (see #$StuffType), instances of which may bridge any of the domains of literality and metaphoricity, space and time, or physical and intangible. Each type of underspecified stuff is intensionally neutral with regard to such issues; the type exists to allow underspecification to occur at the relational level, thus releasing Natural Language (NL) semantics from the need to specify precise semantic structures when such a responsibility is essentially post-NL (i.e., one of real-world reasoning).   For a more complete explanation of underspecification, please see  the #$comment on #$UnderspecifiedCollectionType.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess Archery)
(comment textConformsToGrammar "The predicate (#$textConformsToGrammar STRING GRAMMAR SYSTEM) relates a specific text STRING to a specific #$FormalGrammar-CW GRAMMAR and claims that STRING conforms to all the constraints of GRAMMAR as defined in the #$SyntaxSpecificationSystem SYSTEM.  The text STRING is therefore 'grammatical' according to the specifications in GRAMMAR, if SYSTEM is followed.   SYSTEM often will have a specific parsing program associated with it to test whether STRING really does conform to GRAMMAR.")
(comment GuidedMissileDestroyer "The collection of #$Destroyers intended to be used for transporting and launching #$GuidedMissiles.")
(comment subStringTokens "This predicate is a specialization of #$subSeries that

  relates a serial string token to other serial string tokens that 

  occur within it (see #$CharacterStringToken-Serial).  (#$subStringTokens SERIES SUBSERIES) means that 

  SUBSERIES is a sub-token-series of SERIES.  That is, all of the 

  members of SUBSERIES are members of SERIES, that SERIES and 

  SUBSERIES share the same ordering principle, and that, if the first 

  member of SUBSERIES is the Mth member of SERIES, the Nth member of 

  SUBSERIES is the (N+M-1)th member of SERIES.  So a #$subStringTokens 

  is an uninterrupted \"slice\" of the whole.  Note that any character

  token series is trivially a #$subStringTokens of itself.  See also #$concatenateStringTokens.")
(comment ArcSineFn "(#$ArcSineFn SINE) yields the angle whose sine is SINE.")
(comment SchoolDistrict "A collection of geographical regions.  An element of #$SchoolDistrict is typically a town-, township-, or city-sized area whose public schools (for grades K-12) are controlled by a single governing body, such as a Board of Education or School Board.  Minor-aged residents of the district attend schools within that district.  Typically, district schools are funded by property taxes on residents of the district.")
(comment typicalRankForPosition "(#$typicalRankForPosition RANK POSITION ECHELON COUNTRY

BOS-TYPE) means that a person who holds the #$UnitPosition POSITION in

a #$ModernMilitaryOrganization with #$echelonOfUnit ECHELON,

#$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg COUNTRY, and branch-of-service BOS-TYPE

will typically hold the rank RANK in COUNTRY's branch of service

BOS-TYPE.")
(disjointWith ElectricalDevice DoorKnocker)
(disjointWith SeparationEvent StrictlyMentalEvent)
(comment CruiseMissileUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on           'missiles' that deliver an explosive weapons package by flying as           drone aircraft, but with internally programmed, non-remote           control.")
(disjointWith PathForWheeledVehicles Downtown)
(comment FossilFuel "This is the collection of instances of #$CombustibleFuelSubstance which are either naturally created from the decay of organic matter or are refined from

such. ")
(comment PrivateCollection "The collection of all private collections of #$PartiallyTangible things owned by people or organizations.  Instances include stamp collections, doll collections, photo collections, butterfly collections.")
(comment RepeatedBoosterShotFn "#$RepeatedBoosterShotFn takes a spec of a #$Vaccine and returns the collection of #$RepeatedBoosterShots involving that type of vaccine.")
(comment SouthWind "The collection of all winds that blow from the south.  See #$WindProcess.")
(comment NeoGeoGame "The collection of video games and versions of such that are made to run specifically on a #$NeoGeoPocket-TheProduct platform.")
(comment MathematicalObject "A specialization of both #$MathematicalThing and #$IntangibleIndividual.  Each instance of #$MathematicalObject is a purely abstract mathematical thing which is also an individual (see #$Individual).  Specializations of #$MathematicalObject include #$Quantifier, #$RealNumber, #$Triangle, and #$TruthValue.  Note that instances of #$SetOrCollection are not instances of #$MathematicalObject, since they are not instances of #$Individual.")
(comment nthStreetOver "This predicate relates a street to another street that 

is a specified number of \"streets over\" from the first.

(#$nthStreetOver STREET1 STREET2 N) means that STREET1 and

STREET2 run parallel to each other in some #$GridStreetSystem,

and that, for any given perpendicular street XSTREET that 

intersects both of them, the distance between the two 

intersections is a #$distanceInBlocksOfStreet of N blocks

along XSTREET.  For example, in a typical grid system, 15th

Street is five streets over from 10th Street.  Of course, 5th

Street is also five streets over from 10th Street; so to 

identify a particular street in a given context using this 

predicate, it is generally also necessary to specify a 

direction from STREET1 to STREET2.")
(comment subTopic "(#$subTopic ARG1 ARG2) means that in some context,  ARG2 is a more specific concept belonging to the same theme or `topic' as ARG1.")
(comment Recycling "This is the collection of activities in which some item is reused or which are

part of a process culminating in reuse, the aim being to conserve some resource.")
(comment Cefadroxil "The chemical compound which is a cephalosporin. It helps urinary tract infections and skin infections as well as some types of strep and tonsillitis.")
(comment GasIndustry "The collection of all industries (instances of #$Industry-Localized, i.e., #$Groups of #$Organizations) whose products are instances of #$NaturalGas.")
(comment CombatUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Collection of all units specialized for combat.")
(comment Dollar-Australia "Unit of currency in #$Australia")
(comment LoveStory-Generic "A collection of pieces of information; a subset of #$PropositionalInformationThing.            Each element of #$LoveStory-Generic is a #$Narrative containing the            propositional content of a love story, regardless of the format or formats (play, book) in which           that love story is or can be told.")
(comment Raisin "The collection of individual raisins.")
(comment KickboxingSportsEvent "The collection of all kickboxing matches. A #$KickboxingSportsEvent is similar to a #$BoxingSportsEvent, but it allows some kinds of kicks, and in some forms blows with the knee or elbow.")
(comment DeployableUniversalCombatEarthmover "The collection of high-speed, high-mobility military bulldozers capable of conducting excavating operations in support of mobility, countermobility, survivability, and sustainment engineering missions. Its earthmoving capability will at least match the current D%B dozer. Instead of traditional steel tracks, the DEUCE will use one-piece rubber tracks to allow travel on paved surfaces.  The DEUCE will perform the same missions as the bulldozers it replaces, but will provide self-mobility between job sites, and will arrive faster.  This will represent a significant increase in total work effort.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment Premier-HeadOfState "The #$Premier-HeadOfState of a country")
(comment InformationGatheringDevice "#$InformationGathering device is the subset of #$PhysicalDevice whose instances are typically used in instances of #$InformationGathering.")
(comment nearestSpecPreds "(#$nearestSpecPreds PRED NEAR-PRED) relates any predicate PRED to the nearest unsubsumed predicates NEAR-PRED which are spec predicates of PRED. #$nearestSpecPreds is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genlPreds hierarchy. Moreover, it is merely the #$elInverse of #$nearestGenlPreds.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForSimplification "(#$useReformulationRuleForSimplification RULE) indicates

that in the mt in which this is asserted or a specMt thereof, the

#$CycLSimplifier (part of the #$CycCanonicalizer) will use RULE to

help simplify #$CycLExpressions.")
(comment Insoluble "not at all soluble")
(comment Autism "#$Autism is a pervasive developmental disorder defined by the presence            of abnormal and/or impaired development that is manifest before the age            of 3 years, and by the characteristic type of abnormal functioning in all            three areas of social interaction, communication, and restricted, repetitive           behaviour. The disorder occurs in boys three to four times more           often than in girls.")
(comment PowerSetFn "(#$PowerSetFn SET) denotes the power set (see #$powerSet) of SET: the set whose elements are all and only the subsets of SET.")
(comment quantityInfluenceFunction "(#$quantityInfluenceFunction TIME THING QUANTITY-SLOT FUNCTION-TYPE) means that during TIME the value of QUANTITY-SLOT for successive time slices of THING is subjected to some influence.  If that influence were to be expressed, e.g. in the absence of other influences, then the shape of that function would be one characteristic of elements of FUNCTION-TYPE.  Unlike #$quantityChangeFunction, #$quantityInfluenceFunction does not necessarily entail a change in the value of QUANTITY-SLOT for THING.  It can be used to directly infer #$quantityChangeFunction in the absence of other influences.  If other influences are present, the relative strengths of each influence along with the direction of each influence can be summed to infer a final #$quantityChangeFunction.  See also #$quantityInfluenceFunctionStrength.")
(disjointWith LaunchPad SeaportFacility)
(comment ArterioVenousAnastomosis "The collection of all arteovenous anastomoses.  An individual #$ArterioVenousAnastomosis is a #$BloodVessel larger than a #$Capillary which connects an #$Artery with a #$Vein.")
(comment functionCorrespondingPredicate "A #$MetaRelation that is used to state that a given function and a given predicate amount to  essentially the same relationship, modulo possible (consistent)  differences in argument-order and a specification of which argument  to the predicate corresponds to the result of the function.  (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate FUNC PRED N) means that FUNC maps  a given argument-sequence ARGS (say of length M) to the value VAL if  and only if PRED holds of a certain (M+1 length) sequence ARGS-N-VAL,  where ARGS-N-VAL has as members all of the members of ARGS and has   VAL as its Nth member.  The members of ARGS-N-VAL other than VAL must be in some fixed (but unspecified) order in relation to their ordering  in ARGS, though this need not be the same order in which they occur in  ARGS.  Thus PRED will be a #$FunctionalPredicate (q.v.), with its Nth argument-place being a \"functional\" one (see #$functionalInArgs).  For example,  (#$functionCorrespondingPredicate #$StreetCornerFn #$streetCornerOf 1) implies that (#$equals (#$StreetCornerFn XING DIRECTION) LOT) is either  equivalent to (#$streetCornerOf LOT XING DIRECTION) or  (#$streetCornerOf LOT DIRECTION XING).  (It is in fact equivalent to  the former.)  When reifying an instance of #$Function-Denotational it  is generally considered good ontological engineering practice also to  reify a (or to find an already-existing) corresponding #$Predicate, as  this allows one to describe more explicitly the relationship between  the members of the function's domain and the corresponding members of  its range (see #$relationDomain and #$relationRange).  See also the more specific #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical (for cases where the order of arguments in FUNC and PRED is the same, except for the removal of PRED's Nth argument from FUNC's argument list) and the less specific #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Generic.")
(comment Driver-GolfClub "a kind of wood golf club that is typically only used to tee off and which can be used to hit the ball farthest")
(comment MineRoller "The collection of a type of #$MineClearingEquipment which is vehicle-mounted and is used to deliberately detonate #$LandMines.")
(comment Tungsten "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of #$Tungsten.")
(comment MilitaryWMDProgram "The collection of organized research and development activities performed by military organizations for the purpose of creating a #$WeaponOfMassDestruction.")
(comment AttachmentsResultingFromTypeFn "(#$AttachmentsResultingFromTypeFn ATT-TYPE) denotes the collection of attachment situations that result from attachment events of type ATT-TYPE.")
(comment ProductDevelopment "The set of #$MarketingActivity events that fall in the stage of ProductPlanningAndDevelopment after the concept stage and before the TestMarketing stage.  During #$ProductDevelopment, a physical #$Product or prototype is created.  This is done prior to mass production in order to determine the technical and product feasability of the product.  Instances of this activity are #$performedBy #$MarketingPersons and #$TechnicalWorkers.")
(comment DescendingAlongSurface "Any process in which an object moves downward along some surface.")
(disjointWith MovieShowingAtATheater TransportationEvent)
(comment Lifeguard "People who monitor other people in swimming pools or at beaches.")
(comment Meninges "The collection of all meninges, of which there are three protectively surrounding each person's #$CentralNervousSystem.  The three #$Meninges lie within the #$Skull (for that portion which covers the #$Brain) and consist of the #$DuraMater on the outside, the #$ArachnoidMater in the middle and the #$PiaMater coating the #$Brain and #$SpinalCord.")
(comment Cutter-NavalWatercraft "The collection of military cutters.")
(comment RNAMolecule "The collection of all long-chain molecules composed of
strings of Ribonucleotides.  #$RNAMolecules perform a number of
critical functions in the intracellular environment.  Notably, they
are the medium by which the information encoded in #$DNAMolecules is
transferred outside the cellular nucleus, where it can be used in
protein manufacture.  #$RNAMolecules are also incorporated into the
ribosomal enzymes that 'read' messenger RNA molecules and manufacture
proteins..")
(disjointWith BeliefSystem CommunicationConvention)
(comment relativeImportanceOf "(#$relativeImportanceOf IND1 IND2 GENERIC-VALUE) means that the relative importance of IND1 to IND2 is GENERIC-VALUE. In other words, for an agent who owns, controls, or is otherwise responsible for IND2, IND1 is important to degree GENERIC-QUANTITY.")
(comment AntiSubmarineRocket "The collection of #$Missiles designed

 to transport a #$Torpedo as payload to the vicinity of an enemy #$Submarine.

 Once in the water, the #$Torpedo executes a search for the enemy #$Submarine.")
(comment ResumeFieldPredicate "#$ResumeFieldPredicate is a specialization of #$BinaryPredicate.   Each instance of #$ResumeFieldPredicate relates an instance of #$Resume-CoABS  to the instance of #$CharacterString that serves to fill in a particular field in that resume.  Instances of #$ResumeFieldPredicate include #$resumeField-GridAddress and #$resumeField-Capacities.")
(comment BacterialMRNAProductionProcess "A collection of #$Transcription-DNAToRNA events which take place in instances of #$Bacterium. #$BacterialMRNAProductionProcess is the process whereby #$MessengerRNA are generated from information encoded in bacterial DNA molecules.")
(comment OpticalRetailer "The collection of retail outlets that specialize in selling prescription eyewear, such as individual Lensecrafters or PearlVisionCenters.\"")
(comment NotaryPublic "The collection of instances of #$PersonWithOccupation who have a job of  legally verifying that individuals have personally signed documents.  The person who signs a document in front of a #$NotaryPublic must be personally known to the notary or show a legal #$IDDocument to the notary.")
(disjointWith LocalOrganization BranchOfMilitaryService)
(disjointWith Truck Motorcycle)
(comment Testosterone "The collection of all instances of testosterone.  The substance is a #$ReproductiveHormone, produced by the #$Testicles, which is needed for spermatogenesis and for secondary sexual characteristics in male mammals as well as for the male sex drive.  It stimulates skeletal muscle production and is important in maintining muscle mass and bone tissue in the adult male.")
(comment MilkSecretionEvent "A collection of events.  Each #$MilkSecretionEvent is done by the mammary glands of (female) #$Mammals as a natural process with the function of nourishing the female's offspring.  The secreted milk is stored in the mammary glands until it is drawn out in some fashion.")
(comment ProjectileShell-Marker "The collection of #$ProjectileShell-Pyrotechnics that uses white  phosphorous to mark the position of the enemy.")
(disjointWith IntervalOnNumberLine ElectricalCharge)
(comment UnrollingOnto "A collection of events. In each #$UnrollingOnto event, some coiled object is spread out onto a surface by unrolling it across the #$toLocation.  Once part of the #$objectMoving is in contact with the surface, it ceases motion relative to that surface.")
(comment VariableAritySkolemFunction "The subcollection of #$SkolemFunctions with variable arity. These are only created when a sequence variable is in the scope of the skolem.")
(comment (IsotopeFn Uranium 235) "The collection of pieces of #$Uranium whose atoms have a mass number of 235. Uranium-235 is an isotope of #$Uranium. Uranium-235 is often used in nuclear fission reactions. It is the only naturally occurring fissile isotope (see #$FissileMaterial).")
(comment nextSubeventTypeInScript "This predicate relates types of events and is intended to show a possible constraint on the script type, i.e. (#$nextSubeventTypeInScript STYPE1 STYPE2 STYPE3) means that if an event of SUBTYPE3 has a subevent of STYPE1 it may be followed by an event of type STYPE2, but may not necessarily be followed by such an event.")
(comment Nano "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^-9")
(comment FixedArityFunctionTypeByArity "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$FixedArityFunction whose instances are all of the same arity.")
(comment Form-StandardizedIBO "A specialization of both #$InformationBearingObject and #$StructuredInformationSource.  Each instance of #$Form-StandardizedIBO is an information-bearing object having some standard set of labelled fields; these fields are left blank for the user to fill in with certain items of information (often information pertaining to the user).  Instances of #$Form-StandardizedIBO often accompany some sort of bureaucratic procedure, which they may be used to initiate or to certify.  Specializations include the collections #$LeaseDocument, #$DepositSlip, #$InsuranceClaimForm, and #$Check-TenderObject.")
(comment Pump-Generic "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleThing.  Each instance of  #$Pump-Generic is a natural or mechanical pump, and is thus capable (see the predicate #$behaviorCapable) of pumping fluid from one spatial region to another.  Notable specializations of #$Pump-Generic include #$Heart, #$GasolinePump, and #$OilPump.")
(comment seriesMembers "This predicate relates series to their members.  

(#$seriesMembers SERIES MEMBER) means that MEMBER belongs to SERIES.")
(comment (MediumAmountFn SocialPower) "The degree of power exercised by, for example, a middle manager in a large corporation, or a city council member in a large US city.  This might mean the ability to determine how many thousands of dollars are spent and/or to affect the lives of dozens or hundreds of people.")
(comment BreakingOpenEvent "The process in which objects break open , sometimes to release a tangible such as when a seed coat ruptures to release the seedling's root (radicle).")
(comment IncendiaryDevice "A collection of devices that project fire at enemy troops.")
(comment Cefixime "The chemical compound which is an antibiotic.")
(comment orientation-Underspecified "(#$orientation-Underspecified SUBJECT ORIENTEDLOCATION) claims

that SUBJECT is in some underspecified sense oriented according to the

abstract orientation ORIENTEDLOCATION. For example,

(#$orientation-Underspecified #$MicrosoftInc

#$UpwardLocation-Underspecified) states that #$MicrosoftInc 'is up', while

(#$orientation-Underspecified #$Amazon-CommercialOrganization

#$DownwardLocation-Underspecified) claims that Amazon, the on-line

bookseller, is in some sense 'down'. Note that these formulae actually say

very little. The full meaning of the assertion is its inferred meaning,

using rules that encode what it means for a company (as opposed to a stock,

a person, an idea, etc.)  to be 'up' or 'down' (e.g., their stock price,

market share, earnings ratio, confidence, etc. might all be 'up').")
(comment nearestDifferentIsa "(#$nearestDifferentIsa OBJ-1 OBJ-2 NEAR-DIFF) means that NEAR-DIFF is a \"nearest\" collection of which OBJ-1 is an instance, but OBJ-2 is not. That is, (#$isa OBJ-1 NEAR-DIFF) holds, but (#$isa OBJ-2 NEAR-DIFF) does not, and there is no reified #$Collection OTHER-COL distinct from NEAR-DIFF such that (#$isa OBJ-1 OTHER-COL) holds, (#$isa OBJ-2 OTHER-COL) does not hold, and (#$genls OTHER-COL NEAR-DIFF) holds. Note that this predicate is #$notAssertible, since it must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$isa and #$genls hierarchy. For comparison, see #$nearestDifferentGenls.")
(comment exchangeRateDuring-Official "(#$exchangeRateDuring-Official UM1 UM2 THING NR) means that the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE whose currency UM1 is has set NR as the official exchange rate of the #$UnitOfMoney UM1 for the #$UnitOfMoney UM2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  (THING will often be a calendar time period.)  The official exchange rate will not necessarily be the same as the (financial) market exchange rate, but in at least some markets regulated by GE, NR UM1's can be traded for 1 UM2, and conversely.  (Official exchange rates are typically more stable than market exchange rates; but to the extent that there is fluctuation in the official exchange rate during the temporal extent of THING, NR should be taken to be the average official exchange rate during the temporal extent of THING.)  For example, the fact that during October of 1995 the official exchange rate between Liberian and UnitedStates dollars was 1 Liberian dollar for 1 US dollar can be expressed as (#$exchangeRateDuring-Official  #$Dollar-Liberia #$Dollar-UnitedStates (#$MonthFn #$October (#$YearFn 1995)) 1.0).  See also #$exchangeRateDuring-Market and #$exchangeRateDuring.")
(comment EventRate "#$EventRate, a subset of #$Rate, is a collection of values (or more precisely #$ScalarInterval's) for representing the rate of progress for arbitrary #$Event's. This can be seen as a generalization of #$Speed, which just applies to #$Movement-TranslationEvent's.")
(comment MortgageInsurer "The collection of insurance companies that insure mortgages.  See #$MortgageInsurance.")
(comment totalReserves "(#$totalReserves COUNTRY PRODUCT-TYPE AMOUNT) expresses the total reserves of a organization such as a #$GeopoliticalEntity for PRODUCT-TYPE. A useful example is (#$totalReserves COUNTRY #$Petroleum-CrudeOil VOLUME). The amount of oil held in reserve has an impact on the economy of the region.  This predicate refers to the amount of PRODUCT-TYPE that is proven to exist at some time. It is often the case that estimates exceed the proven reserves, and often new sources are found so the reserves increase.")
(disjointWith Configuration JobPosition)
(comment Trawler "The subcollection of Ship that contains all


trawlers, i.e., ships that drag large nets along the sea


bottom in gathering fish or other marine lives.")
(comment SendingInformationByTelephone "The collection of all events in which information is transferred via a telephone line or linkage of some kind. #$SpeakingOnATelephone is one important specialization also includes all cases where data of any kind is transferred electronically via phone line.  Instances of #$TelephoneConversation ordinarily include at least one instance of #$SendingInformationByTelephone as an important subevent.")
(comment interArgIsa3-2 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).   (#$interArgIsa3-2 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that,  when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the third argument to RELN,  a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the second argument  must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then  (RELN ARG1 ARG2 INST ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only  if ARG2 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic  well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment VulnerableToSmurfAttack "#$VulnerableToSmurfAttack is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerNetwork.  A computer network has this vulnerability if it is running an operating system that can be disabled from a smurf attack.  Practically every computer network has this vulnerablity.")
(comment Haemophilus "A collection of a #$BiologicalGenus in the #$MoneraKingdom.
These are small, pleomorphic #$GramNegativeBacterium.  These are #$Bacterium-Immotile that are #$AerobicBacterium or #$AnaerobicBacterium-Facultative.  Chemoorganotrophic and all species use carbohydrates fermentatively.  They require preformed growth factors present in blood.  These are obligate parasites in the mucous membranes of humans and certain other species.")
(comment MaterialLandingShip "A collection. Military material landing ships.")
(comment AcademicEssay "A kind of short non-fiction #$AcademicComposition in which the #$Student argues for a point of view, discusses a topic, etc.")
(comment Bargaining "The collection of events where agents negotiate over the terms of a contract, the most typical example being the negotiation of a price for an item to be purchased.")
(comment connectedPerpendicularlyTo "(#$connectedPerpendicularlyTo ?obj1 ?obj2) means that ?obj1 and ?obj2 are #$connectedTo each other such that their longest axiis are perpendicular to each other.")
(comment InjuryCondition "The state of being injured.  For getting an injury, use #$IncurringAnInjury.")
(comment CallingATranslationAgent-CommunicationAct "Collection of all instances of #$Requesting-CommunicationAct
in which an #$Agent-CoABS instance issues a broadcast requesting the
services of a translation agent.")
(comment Computing "The collection of actions in which an agent uses

some device that embodies an algorithm (e.g. a pocket calculator or a PC)

in order to compute something.  For actions in which the agent itself carries

out the steps of an algorithm directly, see #$UsingAnAlgorithm.")
(comment Period-TheSymbol "The period symbol '.', most often used used to indicate the end of a sentence, an abbrevition, a decimal point, etc.  This is the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract), not any physical instantiation.")
(comment StrategicNuclearWeaponsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units organized, equipped, and trained for           maintainance, launch, and/or response to the employment of           'strategic' nuclear packages. 'Strategic' in this context refers to           'high-yield' atomic weapons in the multi-kiloton to            multi-megaton range, usually           delivered via bomber or ballistic missile.")
(comment ColorTypeByBrightness "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Color whose instances all have a similar lightness, darkness, or brightness.")
(disjointWith SportsAction GameEvent)
(disjointWith IntelAttack-General IntelAttack-Focused)
(disjointWith TangibleStuffCompositionType OutdoorLocationTypeByWeather)
(comment ArmoredCavalryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Collection of all armored cavalry units.")
(comment holderFor "ARG1 serves as a holder for ARG2.")
(comment SpirillaBacterium "A specialization of #$Bacterium whose instances are characterized by having spiral or corkscrew shape.")
(comment BonusAccount "An account for bonus money that an employee receives.")
(comment BallisticMissile-M11 "A short range ballistic missile produced in China.")
(comment SublingualAdministration "Administering a substance, usually a drug, by placing it under one's tongue to be dissolved.")
(comment interArgIsa2-4 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa2-4 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the second argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the fourth argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN ARG1 INST ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only 
if ARG4 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic 
well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment DestinationAddressField-Packet "A #$DestinationAddressField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet that
    contains the #$IPAddress of the intended destination computer for
the #$Packet-Internet.")
(comment streetIntersectionOf "(#$streetIntersectionOf XING

STREET AVENUE) means that XING is an intersection of STREET and AVENUE.

This predicate is not functional in its first argument because (although uncommon) it is possible for two streets to intersect with each other in more than one place.  Nor is it functional in its second or third arguments.

For example, if three streets all intersect at XING, then XING is the intersection of any two of them.")
(comment Rinsing "The collection of events in which an object is cleaned by running or pouring some liquid over it.")
(comment TrappedFeeling "Unpleasant emotion associated with situations in which a person feels unduly constrained in behavior or otherwise pressured or controlled by others.  This is a #$Collection --- for an explanation of that, see #$Happiness.")
(comment ArgIsaTernaryPredicate "A specialization of both #$ArgTypeTernaryPredicate and #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ArgIsaTernaryPredicate is a ternary predicate used to place an \"#$isa\" constraint on (and thereby specify an argument-type for) one or more argument-places of a relation.  To be more precise, each instance PRED of #$ArgIsaTernaryPredicate takes a #$Relation RELN as its first argument, a #$NonNegativeInteger N as its second argument, and a #$Collection COL as its third argument.  PRED places an \"#$isa\" constraint on RELN's Nth argument-place that is based on COL, so that a ground atomic sentence (GAF) of the form (RELN ARG1..ARGN..) is semantically well-formed only if ARGN is an instance of COL. (Note that (i) if N = 0 then this same constraint is placed on _all_ of RELN's argument-places and (ii) if PRED is #$argAndRestIsa then this constraint is placed on all of RELN's argument-places whose ordinal positions are greater than or equal to the Nth.)  An important instance of #$ArgIsaTernaryPredicate is #$argIsa.")
(comment SoftballBall "The collection of #$Balls designed for use in performances of #$Softball-TheGame")
(comment KidsChatRoom "the collection of #$ChatRooms designed 

 especially for use by children only.")
(comment Cannon "The collection of #$Guns that have a large caliber, and are generally mounted on a platform of some kind.")
(comment MultirevolutionRotation "The #$Collection of all unidirectional #$MultirevolutionRotation movement processes, although one may stop and continue.  Clock hand motion is #$MultirevolutionRotation even if it is a continual series of small turns and pauses.  The angular position monotonically increases or decreases (modulo 360 degrees).  The final stopping position of the process need have no relationship with the starting position.  A sufficiently long time slice is also a #$MultirevolutionRotation.")
(comment favorableExchangeRateDuring "(#$favorableExchangeRateDuring UM1 UM2 THING) means that in some market or markets the #$UnitOfMoney UM1 has a favorable exchange rate with #$UnitOfMoney UM2 during the temporal extent of #$TemporalThing THING. Note that THING will often be a calendar time period.")
(disjointWith AssistantManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment CombineViaFn "(#$CombineViaFn METHOD LIST) returns a term which is the result of applying the #$FieldCombiningMethod METHOD to the items that are elements of LIST.  For example, (#$CombineViaFn #$Concatenate (#$TheList ''5555'' ''333'')) would return the string ''5555333''.")
(comment purposeOfSocialEvent "This predicate can be used to represent the goal in those instances of #$SocialOccurrence that exist so that participants in them can reach some particular goal. (#$purposeOfSocialEvent EVENT FORMULA) means that the goal of EVENT (as determined by at least one participant in EVENT) is represented by FORMULA. When EVENT is an instance of #$CooperationEvent, all  #$cooperatingParticipants in EVENT have the goal represented by FORMULA and are participating in EVENT because they believe doing so will help bring about that goal. This predicate is particularly useful in connection with instances of #$CooperationEvent but can also be relevant for other subcollections of #$SocialOccurrence, such as #$MilitaryExercise,  #$HelpingAnAgent or #$BusinessEvent.")
(comment axisOfRotation "(#$axisOfRotation ROT AXIS) means that in the #$Movement-Rotation ROT, the #$primaryObjectMoving rotates in a counterclockwise direction about AXIS (use the right hand rule i.e. point your thumb in the direction that AXIS points.  Curl your fingers.  The direction from your knuckles to your fingertips is the direction of rotation.  A rotation in the opposite direction is simply an axis whose direction is 180 degrees away from AXIS.  AXIS must spatially intersect some line segment between two points in the spatial extent of the #$primaryObjectMoving. That is, it must  either spatially intersect the #$primaryObjectMoving or go through a 'hole' in it. Positive examples include the earth spinning on the axis between its poles, a tire spinning around an axis through the middle of the wheel on which it is installed, and a pendulum swinging on an axis through its endpoint. Negative examples include the movement of the earth orbiting around the sun and of a child swinging on a swing. Both of these are examples of translation, not rotation.")
(comment RhythmAndBluesMusic "A specialization of #$Music 

  that first appeared in

  the United States in the mid-1940s, #$RhythmAndBluesMusic

  was an important precursor of both #$RockAndRollMusic and

  #$SoulMusic.  Early R&B was itself influenced by #$BluesMusic 

  and by big-band and swing-era #$JazzMusic.  Initially often 

  known as 'jump blues' to its fans, R&B was commonly referred

  to in the mainstream (i.e. white, middle-class) culture as 

  'race' music, due to the fact that almost all of its performers 

  were African Americans.  Compared to straight Blues, with which 

  it shares chord structures, riffs, and lyrical themes, R&B 

  tends to be louder and faster, uses more electrical instruments,

  and is often horn-driven.  Influential practitioners of R&B 

  include Louis Jordan, Big Joe Turner, Ruth Brown, Ike Turner, 

  Big Mama Thornton, Screamin' Jay Hawkins, and Ray Charles.")
(comment NorthernRegionFn "A unary function that returns the `northern region' of an instance of #$GeographicalThing.  What counts as the `northern region' is contextually determined.  Some of the factors influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political considerations.")
(comment CriticismFn "The term `(#$CriticismFn THING)' denotes the collection of #$InformationBearingThings

in which THING is criticized. THING may be an action which is criticized on

ethical grounds, a written work criticized on the basis of its content or style, or a field of study criticized for its assumptions or methodology. What is common to all of these is an element of finding fault. This constrasts with #$CriticismLiteraryFn.")
(comment ProgressiveRockMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic whose heyday was the early-to-mid1970s.
  Compared to  most #$RockMusic, #$ProgressiveRockMusic typically features longer
  compositions and more purely instrumental passages.  Influential practitioners of
  this style include Yes, King Crimson, and Soft Machine.")
(comment outputingCoupler "(#$outputingCoupler ?SIT ?COUP) means that ?COUP is one of the 2 connected couplers in the #$Coupling-Configuration ?SIT.  In addition, the flow of materials enabled by ?SIT generally and typically goes toward ?COUP.  See also #$inputingCoupler.")
(comment intervalAfterOfDuration "(#$intervalAfterOfDuration INT TEMP-OBJ  QUANT) means that INT is the #$TimeInterval of duration QUANT (an instance of #$Time-Quantity) that immediately follows (see the predicate #$contiguousAfter) the #$TemporalThing TEMP-OBJ.")
(comment fee "(#$fee THING CHARGE) means that CHARGE is a fixed amount that must be paid for THING which is determined by the type of THING.")
(comment BacteriumStainTypes "A collection of collections.  These are types of stains used
to identify types of bacterium.")
(comment sameThing "(#$sameThing OBJ1 OBJ2 COL) states that an argument for OBJ1 and OBJ2 being analogous is that they are both instances of collection COL.  See also #$commonalities and #$sameBinaryRelation for other vocabulary for expressing the justification of an analogy.")
(disjointWith Time-Quantity Density)
(comment MastersDegreeInFn "A NAT to denote collections of Masters Degrees in different fields.")
(disjointWith ShootingAGun Archery)
(comment ShipbuildingIndustry "The collection of all ship-building industries: each member of this collection           is a #$Group of #$Organizations (an instance of #$Industry-Localized)           each #$groupMembers of which is in the business of manufacturing #$Ships.")
(comment constructionStartingDate "(#$constructionStartingDate CONS DATE) means that the

construction of CONS, an instance of #$ConstructionArtifact, was started on

DATE, an instance of #$Date.")
(comment ArcCosineFn "(#$ArcCosineFn COSINE) yields the angle whose cosine is COSINE.")
(comment Coal "Carbonized vegetable matter, usually black, usually used as fuel.")
(comment SuburbanNeighborhood "residential area near a city, developed primarily as residential. Mark and Pat live in this.")
(comment PenisEnlargement-NonSurgical "A collection of #$Events in which a #$Penis of a #$MalePerson is enlarged.  When done nonsurgically, the procedure usually involves drugs and/or physical devices meant to change the size of the penis.  #$PenisEnlargement-Surgical refers to surgical procedures with the same goal.")
(comment SubcollectionOfUsedForFn "(#$SubcollectionOfUsedForFn OBJECT_TYPE INDIV) specifies the collection of all instances of OBJECT_TYPE which are intentionally used by some agent ``for'' INDIV.  Thus (#$SubcollectionOfUsedForFn #$PhysicalDevice #$Medicine-FieldOfStudy) would be the collection of all devices used in the practice of medicine and (#$SubcollectionOfUsedForFn #$PostageStamp #$France) would be the collection of all postage stamps valid for use in France.  A misuse would be (#$SubcollectionOfUsedForFn #$Enzyme #$Transcription-DNAToRNA) because the enzyme is not intentionally used by an agent.")
(comment ViralBioAgent "The collection of #$BiologicalAgents that are also #$Viruses. #$ViralBioAgent is an important instance #$BiologicalAgentType.  See also #$BacterialBioAgent and #$FungalBioAgent.")
(comment SocialEngineering "The collection #$SocialEngineering is a collection of events  that is a subset of the collection #$IntelligenceGathering.  In each instance  of #$SocialEngineering, an agent attempts to use interpersonal  techniques of persuasion to gain sensitive information critical to compromising the security of a computer or computer network.")
(disjointWith RemovingSomething InformationBearingThing)
(comment DefensiveOperationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units that deal with any dimension           of defensive operations.")
(comment PurificationProcess "This is the collection of processes in which something is purified. It is not

required that what is treated become absolutely pure, only relatively pure. In particular, the outputs of such processes may not be members of (#$PureFn X) for any X. It is also not required that these processes by the result of #$PurposefulAction.  Important subcollections would include water treatment events, industrial events in which impurities are removed from substances which are then either sold or used as materials, and the natural processes by which groundwater becomes purified.")
(comment RadioTalkShowHost "Each #$RadioTalkShowHost is a person who is a continuing presence on radio talk shows which have varying content and varying personnel. The role of the host could be to interview guests, to propose topics for listeners to call in and discuss, or to act as moderator.")
(comment feelsPotentialEmotion "(#$feelsPotentialEmotion AGENT EMOTYPE) means that there is at least some, possibly small, potential for AGENT to actually feel (see e.g. #$feelsEmotion) EMOTYPE.")
(comment admittedSentence "(#$admittedSentence SENTENCE) states that SENTENCE is a #$CycLSentence which is both syntactically and semantically well-formed with respect to argument constraints only.  For example, (#$admittedSentence (#$bordersOn #$Canada #$France)) is true in #$WorldGeographyDualistMt, but not in #$WorldGeographyMt, since #$Canada and #$France are known to be instances of #$GeographicalRegion in the former microtheory, but not in the latter microtheory.  See also #$admittedArgument.")
(comment SouthEastWind "The collection of all winds that blow from the southeast.  See #$WindProcess.")
(comment (OrganismPartTypeFn Vertebrate Eye) "The kind of eye that is typical of #$Vertebrates.")
(comment SegaDreamcastGame "The collection of video games and versions of such that are made to run specifically on a #$Dreamcast-GameSystem platform.")
(comment OneWayReformulation-Backward "A property of reformulator rules which says that in this rule,
reformulation can only be performed in the #$ReformulationBackwardDirection
direction.")
(comment WaterSurfaceTrajectory "The collection of all trajectories of movements across the surfaces of bodies of water.  Each such #$Trajectory is traced out by the motion of the object along a water surface.  A moving object with a #$WaterSurfaceTrajectory is supported by the water, but is neither fully immersed in the water nor completely in the air.  The trajectory may or may not follow designated #$WaterSurfacePaths like sea-lanes, channels, pre-designated ship routes, safe-passage mine-free paths, etc.   For a pre-designated or pre-existing #$Path-Generic across a water surface, use #$WaterSurfacePath.")
(comment Brokering "A kind of #$ServiceEvent.  In each instance, there is a
#$providerOfService who acts as an intermediary between a would-be
#$buyer and one or more instances of would-be #$seller to organize and
finalize the sales transaction.")
(comment StreetIntersectionFn "(#$StreetIntersectionFn STREET AVENUE) denotes the unique intersection (if any) of STREET and AVENUE.  If STREET

and AVENUE do not intersect, or intersect more than once, then this function is #$undefined for them.")
(comment standardActingForceTypes "The types of forces which appear in all instances of a particular type of #$MovementProcess")
(comment TemporalPersistenceDistribution "#$TemporalPersistenceDistribution is a collection of objects, each of which consists of parameters that together indicate the probability distribution (likelihood of being true) for an assertion or set of assertions over some time period.")
(comment processCode "(#$processCode PROC CODE) means that PROC is executing the #$ComputerCode CODE.")
(comment BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance "A #$Collection.  Instances are portions of substances that are harmful to people.")
(comment AlbuterolSulfate "The chemical compound which is a bronchodilator.")
(comment CoalIndustry "The collection of all industries (instances of #$Industry-Localized) (i.e., #$Groups of #$Organizations) whose products are instances of #$Coal.")
(comment TVBroadcastOfTeamEventFn "#$TVBroadcastOfTeamEventFn takes as argument any instance TEAM of #$SportsTeam or           #$SportsLeague and returns the collection of events that are TV broadcasts           of games in which TEAM participates.  For instance,            (#$BroadcastOfSportsTeamEventFn #$MinnesotaVikings) returns the collection of           all TV broadcasts of Minnesota Vikings games.")
(comment industrialGrowthRateDuring "(#$industrialGrowthRateDuring REGION INDUSTRY TIME RATE) means that the total value of goods and services produced by the #$Industry-Localized INDUSTRY within REGION grows at a rate of RATE per year. See also #$productionValueOfIndustryDuring. ")
(comment DismountedUnit-MilitarySpecialty "A Collection of military units that are trained to deploy from motorized transports and fight on foot.")
(comment Paanga-Tonga "Unit of currency in Tonga")
(comment MysteryStory-Generic "A collection of pieces of information; a subset of #$PropositionalInformationThing.            Each element of #$MysteryStory-Generic is a #$Narrative containing the propositional content           of a story that would commonly be considered a 'mystery',regardless of the format or           formats (play, book, movie) in which the story is or can be told. ")
(comment SavingsAndLoanInstitution "A subset of nationally or state-chartered financial institutions each of which takes deposits from individuals, funds mortgages, and pays dividends or interest to depositors.  It may or may not have shareholders.  Some #$SavingsAndLoanInstitutions have the word 'Bank' in their names.")
(comment GrainOfCereal "The collection of individual Grains - the harvested fruits of cereal plants like wheat, corn, etc.")
(comment KickboxingActivity "The collection of all activities consisting of a #$Person practicing, performing, or using kickboxing. This collection includes both competitive (or combative) kickboxing, and also 'aerobic kickboxing' activities such as those employed in Taebo, etc.")
(comment HeavyWheeledVehicle "Heavier weight wheeled military vehicles.")
(comment connectedAlongSurface "(#$connectedAlongSurface OBJ1 OBJ2) means that the surface of OBJ1 is #$connectedTo OBJ2 over a significant extent of OBJ2 (either area-wise or linearly).")
(comment FantasyWriter "The collection of writers who write Fantasy fiction")
(comment headOfStateOf "The HeadOfStateOf of a country, not to be confused with the HeadOfGovernmentOf if a country has both.")
(comment ManagedAccount "The subcollection of #$FinancialAccount that includes accounts that are managed by professional managers.  These are similar to #$MutualFunds, except that each account is managed separately, rather than the money being aggregated into a single account which is then managed as if it were a single account.  Examples include some stock brokerage accounts, futures accounts,...")
(comment CapabilityPredicate "This is a collection of #$TernaryPredicates which assert capabilities of different sorts, and all of which can be generalized in the same way on their second and third argument places.  See the antecedent rule.")
(comment celestialSubRegions "(#$celestialSubRegions SUPER SUB) means that SUPER and SUB are both elements of #$CelestialRegion, and the area SUB lies wholly within the region SUPER (see #$inRegion).  This is the analog of #$geographicalSubRegions on the celestial sphere.")
(comment AnorexiaNervosa "An #$EatingDisorder associated with a distorted body image that            may be caused by a mental disorder. Inadequate calorie intake            results in severe weight loss.")
(comment quantityInfluenceFunctionStrength "(#$quantityInfluenceFunctionStrength TIME THING QUANTITY-SLOT FUNCTION-TYPE STRENGTH) means that during TIME the value of QUANTITY-SLOT for successive time slices of THING is subjected to some influence.  The strength of this influence is specified by STRENGTH.  The higher the STRENGTH of a given influence, the more likely that the time course of actual changes in QUANTITY-SLOT during TIME will follow the shape that elements of FUNCTION-TYPE have.  If two influences are present, the actual time course of QUANTITY-SLOT follows resembles the shape of its corresponding FUNCTION-TYPE most.  When STRENGTH is unknown or irrelevant use #$quantityInfluenceFunction.  See #$quantityChangeFunction for making statements about the *actual* time course of some quantity.  See also #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for important pointers to related vocabulary.")
(disjointWith Airport-Physical RailroadStation)
(comment lowestPointInRegion "(#$lowestPointInRegion LOWPOINT REGION)  This is the area in which the lowestPlace is located - Asia is the region in which the #$DeadSea is the lowestPlace.  This would be expressed as (#$lowestPointInRegion #$DeadSea #$ContinentOfAsia).")
(comment subProcesses "A #$SubEventPredicate and a specialization of both #$timeSlices and #$subEvents (qq.v.). (#$subProcesses EVENT SUBPROCESS) means  that SUBPROCESS is a subevent of EVENT that consists of everything that  \"happens in\" EVENT during the #$TimeInterval that SUBPROCESS occurs.")
(comment FootballPants "#$FootballPants have pads in the knees.  Some #$FootballPants also have pads around the waist.")
(comment RibbonBridgeBay "The collection of bays which are used to assemble ribbon bridge.")
(comment SequenceOfFn "A sequentially arranged group of instances of TYPE is an
instance of (#$SequenceOfFn TYPE): the collection of sequentially arranged
groups of things of type TYPE.")
(comment Niobium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Niobium.")
(comment typePlaysFunctionalRoleInType "(#$typePlaysFunctionalRoleInType AGENTTYPE SYS-ROLE
SYSTEMTYPE) means that if SYS-INST is an instance of SYSTEMTYPE, then
there exists an instance of AGENTTYPE, AGT-INST, such that (SYS-ROLE
SYS-INST AGT-INST).")
(comment TechnicalWorker "A collection of persons; a subset of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each element of #$TechnicalWorker is a professional who works in some branch of engineering, computers, mathematics or one of the natural sciences.  Negative examples are #$MarketingPerson, #$Manager and #$Psychiatrist.")
(comment yzCrossSection "This predicate relates an object to the arbitrarily thin slice of the object  that is its yz-cross section as determined by its intrinsic axis.  See also #$xzCrossSection, #$yzCrossSection and  #$IntrinsicAxisOfObjects.")
(comment SexualHarassment "A collection of events with multiple participants.  In each #$SexualHarassment,  one or more victims is made to engage in sexual activity, is humiliated, or is otherwise disempowered.")
(comment Epithalamus "The collection of all epithalami.  An individual #$Epithalamus is a small region of the #$Diencephalon situated dorsal to the #$Thalamus and superior to the #$ThirdVentricle.  The #$Epithalamus contains and controls the #$PinealBody.")
(comment Heterotroph-Bacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium that use complex carbon compounds to fulfill their cardon requirements.  This type of #$Bacterium can not use #$CarbonDioxide, see #$Autotroph-Bacterium.")
(comment castMembers "A predicate linking a #$DramaticPerformance to its cast members. (#$castMembers SHOW ACTOR) means that ACTOR acted in SHOW.")
(comment Cruiser "The collection of warships which are relatively large and fast. Cruisers are usually smaller than battleships, but larger than destroyers.")
(comment jointlyCatastrophicSituations "(#$jointlyCatastrophicSituations AGENT SIT1 SIT2) means that the outcomes(s) of SIT1 and SIT2 are catastrophically worse to AGENT than the respective outcomes of SIT1 and SIT2 individually.  In other words, for AGENT the occurrence of both SIT1 and SIT2 is far worse than the occurrence of either one individually.")
(comment numberOfPrescriptionsByDocPayerDuring "(#$numberOfPrescriptionsByDocPayerDuring DOC DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PAYER PERIOD NUM) means that #$Prescriber DOC has had NUM prescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE filled for DRUGTYPE and payed by PAYER during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(comment VacationPackage "Each instance of #$VacationPackage is a set of travel-related services sold together, and usually includes transportation and lodging, but might also include meals, entertainment and guided activtities.")
(comment Snowboarding "The collection of all snowboarding events.  This involves one person, standing on a #$Snowboard, sliding down a snow-covered slope.")
(comment BranchOfMilitaryService "A specialization of  #$ModernMilitaryOrganization.  Each instance of #$BranchOfMilitaryService is one of the main overarching organizations in a modern military command structure.  Thus, for any given modern nation-state, its army, navy, and air force will each be instances of #$BranchOfMilitaryService.")
(comment Airplane "A subcollection of #$FixedWingAircraft, each instance of which is a heavier-than-air, self-powered flying machine (other than a cruise missile) that gets its lift while flying from #$AirplaneWings. #$Helicopters are thus excluded because their lift is created by rotors. A near-borderline (positive) case is a plane that takes-off vertically using a turbojet engine, since its initial lift is not due to its wings. In flight, however, such a plane needs its wings to stay aloft.")
(comment Androgen "Class of steroids that includes the anabolic steroids.")
(comment ProblemSolvers-TheProgramCollection "#$ProblemSolvers-TheProgramCollection is the #$Collection of all artificial #$ProblemSolvingAgents.")
(comment Mescaline "A hallucinogenic drug derived from Peyote cactus.")
(comment ProjectileShell-Pyrotechnics "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is typically employed for  signaling, illuminating, or marking targets.")
(disjointWith Elasticity ElectricalResistance)
(comment PlacingInOrientationFn "A collection denoting function describing movement into a specified #$orientation. (#$PlacingInOrientationFn ORIENTATION) denotes the collection of #$MovementEvents in which the #$objectMoving is in the specified ORIENTATION at the end of the event.  The event might be a #$Movement-TranslationEvent, like carrying a book from a shelf and laying it in a #$HorizontalOrientation on a table, or it might be a #$Movement-Rotation, like laying down a standing book without moving it to a different place.  In any case, the action is #$doneBy some participant other than the #$objectMoving.")
(comment nearestCommonSpecs "(#$nearestCommonSpecs COL-1 COL-2 NEAR-SPEC) relates collections COL-1 and COL-2 to the nearest unsubsumed collections NEAR-SPEC of which are subsets of both COL-1 and COL-2. This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it  must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genls heirarchy.  For comparison, see also #$nearestCommonIsa and #$nearestCommonGenls.")
(comment AtmosphericBoundaryLayer "Instances are boundary layers in the gaseous envelopes or #$Atmospheres of planets.  Instances usually exist between regions with different properties of temperature and pressure, and are characterized by unique boundary conditions themselves.  As a matter of convention, they are usually considered proper parts of the instances of #$AtmosphericLayer that lie directly below them.")
(disjointWith LoveCalculator CalculatorProgram)
(comment powerInGroup "(#$powerInGroup AGENT GROUP LEVEL)

specifies the level of (generic) power that AGENT has in 

GROUP, where GROUP may be an #$Organization or some less

organized sector or community, e.g. an instance

of #$EconomicSector-Localized or an academic community.")
(comment NonCompliant "This attribute is attributed to an object or event as a result of violating some standard.  Typically it is involved in a three way relation between itself, the status-holder and the standard according to which the status holds.  See #$complianceStatus.")
(comment Femto "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^-15")
(comment instructionsUsed-IBT "(#$instructionsUsed-IBT EVENT INS) means that the instructions INS are directly used in EVENT in some way.")
(comment RequestingInformation "A specialization of #$Requesting-CommunicationAct.  In each instance of #$RequestingInformation, an agent asks a question or requests some information. See also the #$IllocutionaryForce associated with this action, #$Query.")
(comment Water-Saline "A specialization of #$Water.  Each instance of #$Water-Saline is a portion of water with some substantial concentration of salt mixed into it.  An important specialization of #$Water-Saline is #$SeaWater (q.v.).")
(comment (HighAmountFn SocialPower) "The degree of social power exercised by, for example, a highly-placed executive in a large corporation, or a highly placed official in a state government -- power over millions of dollars and/or with the ability to affect hundreds or thousands of lives.")
(comment relevantInTypeOfPlace-Somewhere "(#$relevantInTypeOfPlace-Somewhere MT PLACE-TYPE) means that assertions in MT are relevant at least somewhere in every place (spatial region) of type PLACE-TYPE.  See also #$relevantInTypeOfPlace-Everywhere.")
(comment ArtistsModel "The collection of #$ProfessionalModels that earn a living posing for #$Artist-Visuals")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice NaturalTangibleStuff)
(comment CollectionTypeTypeByDisjointness "A collection of instances of #$CollectionTypeType.  #$CollectionTypeTypeByDisjointness is a collection of the three major types of #$CollectionTypes: #$CollectionType is the most general type of #$CollectionType and tells nothing about how the collections in the type are related (no disjointness restrictions).  #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType (a spec of #$CollectionType) gives some disjointness constraints, but with some exceptions.  #$DisjointCollectionType gives the most disjointness constraints--all instances of any instance of #$DisjointCollectionType must by disjoint collections.  #$CollectionTypeTypeByDisjointness is in the KB to explicitly show how #$CollectionType, #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType, and #$DisjointCollectionType are related to anyone dealing with #$CollectionTypes.  The facet assertion (#$facets-Covering #$CollectionType #$CollectionTypeTypeByDisjointness) states that any instance of #$CollectionType should be checked for possible membership in #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType or #$DisjointCollectionType.")
(comment AgentOrange "A collection.  Each instance is a portion of a #$ToxicSubstance.  #$AgentOrange is an herbicide sprayed on plants as a defoliant.  It has been used mainly in modern guerilla conflicts, notably in the #$VietnamWar.  Although #$AgentOrange is not used against troops like #$NerveGas, it is classified as a #$ChemicalWeapon because it's used to gain strategic advantage, either by reducing the amount of vegetation enemy troops can use for cover or by destroying an enemy's civilian crops.  The name is a US military code name which comes from the color of the containers used for this #$ChemicalWeapon in the #$VietnamWar.")
(comment Azithromycin "The chemical compound which is an antibiotic.")
(comment containerUsed "(#$containerUsed EVENT CONT) means that the #$objectActedOn in EVENT is contained in (#$in-ContGeneric) CONT during EVENT, and that CONT facilitates EVENT being accomplished.")
(comment HoroscopeForSignFn "A function returning the collection of all horoscopes for a given #$ZodiacSign.")
(comment PrivateMortgageInsurer "The collection of #$MortgageInsurers that are private, that is, not instances of #$GovernmentOwnedCompany.")
(comment RowingShell "A lightweight, narrow-beamed boat designed for competitive racing by crews of one or more persons rowing (and, in larger crews, a coxswain steering).")
(comment ListeningOnATelephone "The collection of all events in which a human agent listens to information that has been electronically transmitted over a phone line and which is issuing from a phone receiver in an audible form. Usually it is coming from another human agent who is performing an instance of #$SpeakingOnATelephone.")
(comment Anther "An anther is the pollen-bearing part of a flower's stamen.")
(disjointWith Mixture ElementStuff)
(comment DecadeFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance of #$NonNegativeInteger, #$DecadeFn returns an instance of #$CalendarDecade. (#$DecadeFn NUMBER) denotes the instance of #$CalendarDecade consisting of (#$YearFn (#$TimesFn NUMBER 10) ), (#$YearFn (#$PlusFn (#$TimesFn NUMBER 10) 1)) , ... , and(#$YearFn (#$PlusFn (#$TimesFn NUMBER 10) 9)).  For example, (#$DecadeFn 197) refers to the 1970s.")
(comment nearestCommonIsa "(#$nearestCommonIsa THING1 THING2 NEAR-COL) means that NEAR-COL is a \"nearest\" collection of which both THING1 and THING2 are instances.  That is, both (#$isa THING1 NEAR-COL) and (#$isa THING2 NEAR-COL) hold, and there is no reified #$Collection NEARER-COL distinct from NEAR-COL such that (#$isa THING1 NEARER-COL), (#$isa THING2 NEARER-COL) and (#$genls NEARER-COL NEAR-COL) all hold.  Note that this predicate is non-assertible (see #$notAssertible), since its extension at any given time depends upon (and so must be computed from) the current state of the #$isa and #$genls hierarchies in the Cyc Knowledge Base. See also #$nearestCommonGenls and #$nearestCommonSpecs.")
(comment VulnerableToTearDropAttack "#$VulnerableToTearDropAttack is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is running an operating system that fails to handle a deliberately malformed
 UDP (#$UserDatagramProtocol) packet.  In a Teardrop attack, a remote attacker sends one or multiple fragmented UDP packets to a host, which have the correct (according to the IP header) fragment sizes but false (according to the IP header) fragment offsets.  The result is that the destination host's memory allocation fails and the OS crashes. ")
(comment MechanizedLandingCraft "The collection of mechanized watercraft used in military landing operations.")
(comment BacterialGene-HereditaryUnit "A specialization of #$ProkaryoticGene-HereditaryUnit.  Instances are segments of #$DNAMolecules that belong to bacteria.")
(comment FuturePerfectFn "(#$FuturePerfectFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-TIME) denotes the subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances are temporally subsumed by CONTEXT-TIME.")
(comment ApprovingARequest "The collection of communication actions in which an agent approves a request.")
(comment Flirting "The collection of all events of flirtation, where the agent behaves so as to invite romantic or sexual interest in another. Examples include non-verbal communication such as smiling and batting one's eyelashes, as well as other forms of communication.")
(comment PhysicalCollectingFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an agent collects something.")
(comment ToothDecay "The phenomemon during which bacteria rot your teeth, turn them brown, give you bad breath, etc.  When you have #$ToothDecay, you get a cavity and sometimes a toothache.  Brush and floss your teeth and this won't happen.")
(comment WebcamBroadcasting "A specialization of #$InternetBroadcasting. Each instance of this collection is an event whereby a camera transmits images 'live' to a #$WorldWideWebSite.")
(comment BroadcastAddress "A #$BroadcastAddress is an #$IPAddress that services an entire network of computers.")
(comment Hoax "A hoax, in this sense, is a situation which is brought about by an instance

of #$Deceiving or an attempt to perform such an act. A situation which is a hoax always contains or embodies misleading

evidence. The creating of this evidence is either a performance of or an attempt to perform

an act of #$Deceiving.")
(comment (RefiningFn Petroleum-CrudeOil) "The #$ChemicalProcessing event whereby #$Petroleum-CrudeOil is refined; one of the #$industryActivityTypes of an #$OilIndustry.")
(comment compoundString "The predicate #$compoundString expresses the relationship between a multi-word string, a part of speech, and its denotation.  (#$compoundString WORD LIST PART TERM) means that the translation of the multi-word phrase containing both WORD and the word-strings in LIST, when the part of speech is PART, is TERM.  TERM must be an element of either #$Collection or #$Individual.  If TERM is a collection, the semantic meaning of TERM is (#$isa :noun TERM).  If TERM is an individual object, the semantic meaning of TERM is (#$equals :noun TERM).  See also #$multiWordString, #$multiWordSemTrans, and #$compoundVerbSemTrans.")
(disjointWith BeliefSystem DevisedPracticeOrWork)
(comment LinguisticAnalysis-Syntactic "A collection of microtheories.  Each element is a microtheory representing knowledge, theory, hypotheses, evidence, and problems related to the syntactic analysis of a data set taken from a language or group of languages.")
(comment MartianStuff "A collection of tangible things.  Each element in #$MartianStuff is a portion of the stuff that the ground of the planet #$PlanetMars (at or near its land surface) is made of, including rocks, boulders, sand grains, rigolith, ice, carbon dioxide ice, etc., and mixtures of those things.")
(comment ComputerVideoFile "The collection of #$ComputerImageFiles that when played by the appropriate software produce an #$InformationBearingWavePropagation with a #$MovingImage (often a #$VideoClip) as a subevent. The #$ibtGenerated during a playing of a #$ComputerVideoFile may also include a #$SoundInformationBearingThing as a subevent. Common file formats for #$ComputerVideoFiles include Quicktime, MPEG, AVI, and MOV.")
(comment TablatureNotation "The class of musical notations which consist of marks on lines where the lines designate different physical strings of a stringed instrument.  The positions of the marks indicate the musical notes (e.g. A,B,C,D,E,F,G in various octaves) by position on the string; each mark corresponds to such a note that is to be played, and it visually corresponds approximately to a physical location on the instrument.")
(disjointWith OutdoorLocationTypeByWeather TangibleStuffStateType)
(comment IBTCopying "A specialization of #$IBTGeneration-Replication.  Each instance of #$IBTCopying is an event which generates some new instance or instances of #$InformationBearingThing by copying the information and format from a source #$InformationBearingThing (see #$informationOrigin).  The new instance(s) of #$InformationBearingThing encode(s) approximately the same information in approximately the same way as the source #$InformationBearingThing.  A positive example of #$IBTCopying would be a person producing a hand-written copy of a newspaper story, where the copy is in the same language as the story, and the format of the story (e.g., the ordering of the paragraphs) is not changed.  Negative examples of #$IBTCopying would be a person producing a translation of the newspaper story, or a person producing a document in which the paragraphs of the story are extensively rearranged.  Specializations of #$IBTCopying include #$CopyingAComputerFile and #$PhotocopyingADocument. See also the predicates #$copyProduced and #$itemCopied.")
(comment defenseBudgetExpenditures "The amount of money in the total #$nationalBudgetExpenditures for defense.")
(comment Superstition "The collection of #$BeliefSystems that are not in accordance with accepted scientific beliefs or scientific methods, but are not accorded the status of #$Religion.")
(comment AnaerobicBacterium-Oxyphobic "The collection of all instances of #$AnaerobicBacterium to which oxygen is actually lethal; i.e., which not only do not metabolize oxygen, but which are actually killed by it.")
(comment BallisticMissile-Mushak160 "A short range ballistic missile produced by Iran.")
(comment FetishFn "The expression `(#$FetishFn TYPE)' denotes the spec of #$Fetishism

in which TYPE is the object of the fetish.")
(comment OphthalmicAdministration "Administering a liquid, possibly a drug, by dropping it into one's eyes.")
(comment MediaSeriesProductType "A collection of collections; a subset of #$ExistingObjectType.  Every
instance of #$MediaSeriesProductType is a collection of
#$InformationBearingThings, subsets of which are distributed via the
mass media at regular intervals.  Examples: #$TheNewYorkTimes-TheNewspaper is a
#$MediaSeriesProductType, a collection of #$NewspaperSeries of which each
edition is a subset -- a collection of the newspapers printed and
circulated on a particular day; each instance of #$TheNewYorkTimes-TheNewspaper is
a #$NewspaperCopy, a #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject. #$StarTrek-Classic is a #$MediaSeriesProductType, a #$TVSeriesProduct of which each episode is a subset -- a collection of TV shows broadcast at a particular time; each instance of
#$StarTrek-Classic is a #$TVShow-SingleCW.  See also #$MediaSeriesNthFn, #$MediaSeriesByDateFn.")
(comment EnemaAdministeringEvent "Instances of #$EnemaAdministeringEvent involve injecting a fluid (although there are references to smoke enemas, the fluid is almost always a liquid) into the intestines by way of the anus.  In some cases this is done as a medical procedure, e.g. as a kind of cleaning before pregnancy, as a means of administering a drug (see #$Enema-DosageForm), or to enable medical imaging (e.g. a 'barium enema').  In other cases it may be done for health, spiritual, or erotic reasons.")
(comment CrossingABorder "Any subEvent of a #$Movement-TranslationProcess in which a #$Border is crossed.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn EighthRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment DoNotFragmentField-Packet "A #$DoNotFragmentField-Packet is a flag in a #$Header-Packet
that, if set, indicates that the packet should not be fragmented into
smaller packets. A #$Packet-Internet with this flag set has to be
routed around small-packet #$ComputerNetworks.")
(comment blockOfStreetBetween "(#$blockOfStreetBetween BLOCK STREET XST1 XST2) means that BLOCK is a one-block long subpath of STREET that extends from the intersection of STREET and XST1 to the intersection of STREET and XST2.")
(comment FluidFlow-Translation "A specialization of both #$FluidFlowEvent and #$Movement-TranslationEvent (qq.v.). In each instance of #$FluidFlow-Translation, the moving object (see the predicate #$objectMoving) is an instance of #$FluidTangibleThing (i.e. a portion of some fluid, such as a quart of milk) rather than a discrete solid object.  At least some of the moving object leaves its original position (see the predicate #$fromLocation) and some arrives at the destination (see the predicate #$toLocation), but it is not necessary that all of the moving object go from the origin to the destination.  Instances of #$FluidFlow-Translation include rivers flowing or winds blowing or air filling one's lungs when one takes a breath.  Other instances of #$FluidFlow-Translation include flows of #$GranularFluids (q.v.), such as sand or drifting snow, that are 
composed of multiple solid particles.")
(comment CycLClosedExpression "The collection of #$CycLExpressions that contain no free variables.  (A variable VAR occurs _free_ in an expression EXPR if and only if there is an occurrence of VAR in EXPR that is not bound by a quantifier or other #$ScopingRelation (q.v.) in EXPR.)  Note that those CycL sentences that are treated (in the context of representing assertions in the Cyc Knowledge Base) as implicitly containing universal quantifiers are _not_ closed expressions (see #$CycLClosedSentence). Also cf. #$CycLOpenExpression.")
(comment HammerThrowField "The collection of fields where HammerThrowSportsEvents usually occur.")
(comment BankingGame "All instances of any gambling game in which bets are laid against the gambling house or the dealer")
(comment PokemonCharacter "#$PokemonCharacter is a collection of all characters in anything Pokemon related, including the human characters.")
(comment speedInMoveTypeOnTerrain "(#$speedInMoveTypeOnTerrain VEHICLETYPE MOVETYPE TERRAINTYPE
SPEED) means that the typical speed of vehicles of type VEHICLETYPE
when they are playing the role of #$primaryObjectMoving in translation
events of MOVETYPE on TERRAINTYPE is SPEED.")
(comment AirForceFn "(#$AirForceFn COUNTRY) denotes the particular instance of #$AirForce which belongs to (see #$officialArmedForces) COUNTRY.  Note that (#$AirForceFn COUNTRY) denotes the entire air force of COUNTRY, not a given subdivision of that air force.")
(disjointWith KidsChatRoom LesbianChatRoom)
(comment MilitaryWatercraft "#$MilitaryWatercraft is a specialization of #$Watercraft and #$Platform-Military. Each instance of #$MilitaryWatercraft is a #$Watercraft used in a military context. A few notable specializations include nuclear submarines and destroyers, but transportation devices which are not vehicles could also be instances.")
(comment PublicRelationsActivity "Activities used to create public interest in a           person, idea, product, institution, or business establishment.")
(comment sequenceCodesForSequence-Continuous "(#$sequenceCodesForSequence-Continuous NUCLEOTIDE_SEQUENCE AMINO_SEQUENCE) means that the nucleotide sequence represented by the list NUCLEOTIDE_SEQUENCE codes for the amino acid sequence represented by the list AMINO_SEQUENCE, in the sense that if NUCLEOTIDE_SEQUENCE appears in a DNA molecule, it can be translated into a #$ProteinMolecule with the amino acid sequence AMINO_SEQUENCE (see #$sequenceCodesForType) via DNA-to-RNA transcription followed by RNA-to-Protein translation, and if NUCLEOTIDE_SEQUENCE appears in an RNA molecule, it can be translated into a #$ProteinMolecule with the amino acid sequence AMINO_SEQUENCE via RNA-to-Protein Translation.")
(comment RotationAxisParallelToDirectionOfMotion "The direction of #$axisOfRotation is #$directionOfTranslation-Throughout.  This includes rifling, propeller motion, drilling, screw and bolt insertion & removal, etc.  Each point off of the axis corkscrews forward.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction PathArtifactSystem)
(comment Lecture-CW "The collection of lectures, considered

  abstractly as conceptual works.  Note that

  #$Lecture-CW is not a spec of #$TextualPCW, as

  the performances of their instances (#$FormalLecture-IBTs)

 often involve much more than a simple

  expression of propositions, e.g., 

  simple experiments.")
(disjointWith SalesManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment Receiving "A specialization of #$TransferIn.  Each instance of #$Receiving is an event in which something `comes in' to an object.  Typically, a receiving has associated with it an instance of #$Translocation (q.v.); a particular receiving and its associated translocation(s) are related by the predicate #$transferInSubEvent.  If the thing which `comes in' is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible (such as a baseball, or a SCUD missile), then its reception is an instance of the specialization #$ReceivingAnObject (q.v.).  If the translocation associated with the receiving is an instance of #$WavePropagation (such as a radio broadcast, or heat radiation from the Sun), then the receiving is an instance of the specialization #$ReceivingAWave (q.v.).")
(comment WeaponTypeByIntendedTargetTypeFn "(#$WeaponTypeByIntendedTargetTypeFn WEAPON-TYPE TARGET-TYPE) returns that specialization of WEAPON-TYPE whose instances have TARGET-TYPE as the #$intendedTargetTypeOfWeaponType.  Thus, for example, (#$WeaponTypeByIntendedTargetTypeFn BiologicalWeapon MilitaryPerson) returns the class of biological weapons designed primarily to be used against military personnel.")
(comment compositeFields "(#$compositeFields LTS LF) means that LF is a field which is not explicitly a part of the #$LogicalTableSchema LTS, but can be formed as a composite of two or more fields which are explicitly present.  Also see #$compositeFieldFormat, which is used to express how to form the composite field by combining others.")
(disjointWith Microtheory AbstractInformationStructure)
(comment objectTranslating "(#$objectTranslating MOVEMENT OBJECT) means that in MOVEMENT, OBJECT undergoes some salient translational or place-to-place motion (see #$Movement-TranslationEvent).  #$objectTranslating is stronger than its generalization #$objectMoving, since the latter is agnostic as to whether  the moving object is rotating or translating.  When considering using #$objectTranslating, one should also consider whether its specialization #$translatesFromTo applies.  If MOVEMENT is a #$Translation-SingleTrajectory,  then any #$objectTranslating in any #$timeSlices of MOVEMENT is #$onPath the #$motionPathway-Complete of MOVEMENT.")
(comment Ileum "The collection of all ilea.  Each instance of this collection is the distal section of a #$SmallIntestine.")
(comment SouthernRockMusic "A variety of #$RockMusic that draws heavily from both #$BluesMusic and #$CountryMusic, both in the music and the lyrics, but mixes those styles with the louder and harder elements of #$RockMusic. The home of #$SouthernRockMusic is the American south, and typical practitioners include The Allman Brothers Band, #$ZZTop-MusicGroup, Lynard Skynard and 38 Special.")
(disjointWith Railway SeaportFacility)
(comment SouthernRegionFn "A unary function that returns the `southern region' of an instance of #$GeographicalRegion.  What counts as the `southern region' is contextually determined.  Some of the factors influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political considerations.")
(comment SportsVersionFn "This function maps from #$ExistingObjectTypes to the versions of those types that are suitable for use in sporting activities.  The sport versions will share many of the same characteristics, but will not share the same purpose.  For example, the purpose of a #$Spear is to help its user kill animals, while a #$Javelin (i.e. (#$SportsVersionFn #$Spear) is used in distance throwing competitions).  Likewise, this function when applied to #$Guns would yield guns that are used for sport, but NOT used for killing, which is the primary purpose of most #$Guns.  Guns that are used for sport hunting (i.e. not subsistence hunting) would not be considered sports versions, because they retain the primary purpose of guns-- killing.")
(comment CycLFormula "The collection of compound CycL expressions.  Each instance of #$CycLFormula consists of a CycL expression that denotes a relation (e.g. a #$Predicate, #$Function-Denotational, or #$TruthFunction) -- or at least an expression that could be interpreted as having a relation as its semantic value (see #$CycLGenericRelationFormula) -- followed by one or more CycL terms (see #$CycLTerm), with the entire sequence enclosed in parentheses.  For example, (#$isa #$Muffet #$Poodle) and (#$BirthFn #$Muffet) are both CycL formulas.  Two important specializations of #$CycLFormula are #$CycLNonAtomicTerm (whose instances are also called \"denotational formulas\") and #$CycLSentences (whose instances are also called \"logical formulas\").  Note that this notion of \"formula\" differs somewhat from that used in formal logic, where a formula is normally defined as an (atomic or non-atomic, quantificationally closed or open) sentence.")
(disjointWith AnimalTypeByMaturity OrganismPartType)
(comment RowOfObjects "A collection whose instances are groups of similar objects that are aligned in a row.")
(comment availableMaterial "In Workarounds problems, (#$availableMaterial OBJ) means that OBJ is available for use as a resource in a solution to the problem.  Generally, #$availableMaterial will be a #$PhysicalDevice, but engineering companies are also usefully treated this way.")
(comment in-UnderspecifiedContainer "(#$in-UnderspecifiedContainer ACT CONT) states that an abstract
containment relation holds between ACT and CONT, where CONT is
the abstract container employed by the action ACT.
#$in-UnderspecifiedContainer is an underspecified semantic representation
that may be elaborated to represent either a spatial example of
containment (as captured by #$in-ContGeneric and its specific forms) or
a temporal use of containment ('in the summer' etc.) or metaphorical
containment ('in emacs', etc.)")
(comment GlamRockMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic whose heyday was the early-to-mid 1970s.
  #$GlamRockMusic performances tend to be theatrical, with the performers decked-
  out in outrageous costumes and lots of makeup.  This music is also known as Glitter.
  Influential practitioners of this style include David Bowie, T-Rex, and Sweet.")
(comment IntakingViaPortal "The subset of IntakingVia a coupler where the intaking Coupler is a Portal.")
(comment primeMinister "The #$HeadOfGovernment of a country.")
(comment HardcopyOfCWFn "A function that maps a #$ConceptualWork or #$CWInfoStructure onto the collection of hardcopy instantiations of that work. For example, (#$HardcopyOfCWFn #$MobyDickNovel) is the collection of all hardcopy books of Moby Dick. See also #$HardcopyOfInformationTypeFn for the collection of hardcopy instantiations of a type of #$ConceptualWork and #$HardcopyOfIBTTypeFn for the #$collectionIntersection between #$InformationBearingThing types and #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject.")
(comment StainingOfBacteria "The collection of events in which a bacterial culture is

stained.  Staining is used for identification and detection of

bacterium.  Dyes or other materials are applied to a thin film of

cells on a microscope slide and subsequently observed for changes.

Examples of bacterial stains are the Gram stain or the

Ziehl-Neelsen stain.")
(comment countryProductionCapable "(#$countryProductionCapable GEO-ENT PRODUCTION-TYPE) means that the government of the #$IndependentCountry GEO-ENT is #$behaviorCapable of playing the role #$directingAgent in #$ProductionEvents of type PRODUCTION-TYPE.")
(comment sameBinaryRelation "(#$sameBinaryRelation OBJ1 OBJ2 PRED JUST) states that an argument for OBJ1 and OBJ2 being analogous is that they are both related by predicate PRED to analogous objects.  The justification for the analogous objects is the expression JUST.  See also #$commonalities and #$sameThing for other vocabulary for expressing the justification of an analogy.")
(disjointWith Density Temperature)
(disjointWith FluidFlowEvent Archery)
(comment PuttingArmAroundSomeone "The collection of all events in which a person puts his or her arm around another person.  Usually this is an expression of concern or affection.")
(comment Mission-ReligiousOrganization "A collection of religious orgnizations.")
(comment upwardCompatibleProgram "(#$upwardCompatibleProgram ?OLD ?NEW) means, roughly,           that you can do everything with ?NEW that you could do with ?OLD.")
(comment Rhodococcus "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$Nocardiaceae-Family.  These are partially acid-fast #$Bacterium, that are chemoorganotrophic with an oxidative type metabolism.  They are also catalase-positive.")
(comment increasesLikelihood-PropProp "(#$increasesLikelihood-PropProp p1 p2) means that p1's becoming true would increase the likelihood that p2 will be true.  This is a defeasible relationship: not all situations in which p1 becomes true are situations in which the likelihood of p2 is increased.  Thus (#$increasesLikelihood-PropProp  (I win the lottery) (I am happy)) could be true even if the likelihood that I am happy is not increased in the situation in which I win the lottery and at the same time discover that I have cancer.  #$increasesLikelihood-PropProp can be thought of as a form of subjunctive implication, where instead of p1's subjunctively implying p2, the likelihood of p2 would be greater if p1 were true than if p1 were not true.  It is therefore definable in terms of the subjunctive operator #$subImplies together with the predicate #$likelihood.   See also #$cfImplies and #$causes-PropProp.")
(comment GunCruiser "A collection. Military gun cruiser ships.")
(comment ArcTangentFn "(#$ArcTangentFn TAN) yields the angle whose tangent is TAN.")
(comment Parchment "Thin animal hide used to write on")
(comment ChemoReceptiveSensor "Sensors that detect molecules or properties of molecules.")
(comment ExurbanNeighborhood "The collection of all residential development areas located in countryside within commute of a city.")
(comment Slave "A person who is bound to hard servitude without any meaningful compensation.")
(comment PhysicalSkillTesting "Collection of tests performed in order to evaluate a particular physical skill.")
(comment GeneticallyEngineeredViralPathogen "The collection of all instances of #$Virus

  that have been genetically engineered

   for use in #$BiologicalWeapons.")
(comment performanceOfIBT "(#$performanceOfIBT IBT EVENT) means that EVENT is a performance of the #$InformationBearingThing, IBT.  For example: (#$performanceOfIBT 2001MovieReel0353 2001MovieShowing0133538)")
(disjointWith RemovingSomething Separation-Incomplete)
(comment FaceLift "A surgical procedure in which the skin of the face is drawn taut, from an incision up along the hairline.  Face lifts are almost always done purely for cosmetic reasons. ")
(comment DirectionFindingUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped to           determine the point of origin of an EM Signal.")
(comment landmarksOfCity "(#$landmarksOfCity CITY THING) means that THING is generally considered to be a distinguishing 'landmark' of CITY in the context of the assertion, both by city residents and visitors.")
(comment TelephoneCoupling "The collection of all coupling situations in which a telephone jack is properly plugged into a physical housing or connection, thereby rendering the phone usable for purposes of telecommunication.")
(disjointWith CycLClosedSentence CycLNonAtomicTerm)
(comment EastWind "The collection of all winds that blow from the east.  See #$WindProcess.")
(comment InsultingAnOfficial "The collection of communication acts in which a participant in a #$SportsEvent insults an official presiding over that event.  Instances of #$InsultingAnOfficial can only occur while that #$SportsEvent is taking place.")
(comment SegaGenesisGame "The collection of video games and versions of such that are made to run specifically on a #$SegaGenesis-TheProduct platform.")
(comment reformulatorRule "(#$reformulatorRule EXPR-1 EXPR-2), asserted in the

microtheory MT, means that EXPR-1 may be reformulated into EXPR-2 (or

vice versa, based on meta-properties of this rule and what mode the

reformulator is in) in MT

or a specMt thereof.  Free variables in EXPR-1 and EXPR-2 are shared,

and may bind with CycL expressions which match the template. Truth

and semantics are not necessarily preserved (see #$TruthPreservingReformulation).

Use the more specific predicates #$reformulatorEquiv and #$reformulatorEquals

when applicable.")
(comment atStreetIntersection "This predicate can be used to relate an object to

a street intersection in or next to which it is located. 

(#$atStreetIntersection OBJ XING) means that OBJ is located 

out in the open either directly on XING or on one of the 

street corners (i.e. lots of land) adjacent to XING.  When 

it is necessary to indicate the particular street corner 

adjacent to XING (e.g. the northwest one) where OBJ is 

located, either use #$streetCornerOf or simply specify 

OBJ's #$GeographicalDirection from XING.")
(comment directionRelativeToAxis "The direction of ARG1 is at an angle of ARG3 with respect to ARG2.  ARG2 could be any vector (e.g. the rectilinear trajectory of another object).")
(comment TimeOfDay-PM "A specialization of #$TimeOfDay.  Each instance of #$TimeOfDay-PM is a period of time from one second after Noon to one second before Midnight on a particular calendar day (see #$CalendarDay).")
(comment distanceAboveSeaLevel "(#$distanceAboveSeaLevel REG DIST) means that the altitude above sea level of the #$GeographicalRegion REG is the #$Distance DIST.  For elements of #$Mountain, distance is measured from sea level to the peak; for elements of #$Lake, from the surface to sea level; for cities, from the center of town to sea level.  Examples: (#$distanceAboveSeaLevel #$PikesPeak-Mount (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 14110)); (#$distanceAboveSeaLevel #$MountEverest (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 29028)); (#$distanceAboveSeaLevel #$MountFuji-Volcano (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 12389)); (#$distanceAboveSeaLevel #$LakeHuron (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 580)).  To describe ``distance above sea level'' for a non-#$GeographicalRegion, see #$altitudeAboveSeaLevel.")
(comment ProcessExecutableCodeFn "Takes a #$ComputerProcessRunning and returns the unique #$ComputerCode-Binary that the process is executing.")
(disjointWith ElectromagneticRadiationTypeByWaveFrequency SoundWavePropagationType)
(comment CondensatePipeline "A collection of #$Pipelines; a subset of #$OilPipeline.  Each instance of #$CondensatePipeline is a pipeline  whose primary function is the transportation of portions of #$Petroleum-Condensate.")
(comment Thiethylperazine "The chemical compound which is an anti-emetic. It should not be administered intraveneously and should not be taken by pregnant women.  It can cause severe central nervous system depression and comatose states.")
(comment RadioBroadcasting "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$Broadcasting.  In every #$RadioBroadcasting event, an #$InformationBearingThing consisting of #$AudibleSound is converted into radio signals and transmitted by a #$BroadcastAntenna, and received by a #$ReceivingAntenna.")
(comment LyricsToMusicFn-Agent "#$LyricsToMusicFn-Agent takes

as argument any instance of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection

of all instances #$Lyric-WordsToSong which are the lyrics of some

piece of music written or performed by that musician or group of

musicians. For Example, (#$LyricsToMusicFn-Agent #$PinkFloyd-MusicGroup)

would return the collection of lyrics written or used in songs

performed by Pink Floyd.")
(comment HeavyHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Specialization of heavily armed helicopter units.")
(comment Franc-Monegasque "One of the monitary units in Monaco-AtPresent.")
(comment RomanceStory-Generic "A collection of pieces of information; a subset of #$PropositionalInformationThing.            Each element of #$RomanceStory-Generic is a #$Narrative containing the propositional           content of an idealized and adventurous story that (usually) takes place in a remote           time and place and often contains heroic events.  The story may be told in any format,           as a play, book, movie, etc.")
(comment suppliedWithFromExclusivelyThrough "(#$suppliedWithFromExclusivelyThrough PT1 COL PT2 PT3) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied with instances of the #$Collection COL from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT3 (on their way from PT2 to PT1), and that PT1 is supplied with instances of COL from PT2 only through PT3.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$suppliedWithFromExclusivelyThrough is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  And PT3 might, for example, be a #$Hose, a #$Railway, a #$GeographicalRegion, or a #$BloodVessel.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.")
(comment SecondMortgage "Each instance of #$SecondMortgage is a #$MortgageAgreement on real estate which has already been pledged as collateral for a previous mortgage.")
(comment CoffeeCherry "The fruit of a coffee bush; contains two seeds which are coffee beans.")
(comment HeraldicDevice "The collection of all #$Insignias representing an individual #$Person, family, or organization, as used in a heraldic system. The patterns of images on #$HeraldicDevices are inherited.")
(disjointWith HeavyWheeledVehicle GolfCart)
(comment IllocutionaryForceType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$IllocutionaryForceType is a subcollection of #$IllocutionaryForce.  Notable instances of #$IllocutionaryForceType include #$DirectiveIllocutionaryForce, #$CommissiveIllocutionaryForce, and #$ConstativeIllocutionaryForce.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByCatalaseProduction "A collection of collections and a method of partitioning the
collection of #$Bacterium according to #$Catalase production.  This
collection divides into the #$CatalasePositiveBacterium and
#$CatalaseNegativeBacterium.")
(comment Chairman-HeadOfState "The #$HeadOfState in a country where Chariman-HeadOfState is the highest ranking state office.")
(comment CommodityTrading "buying an object, where the object(s) bought is(are) #$CommodityProduct(s).")
(comment SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn "(#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn COLLECTION PREDICATE THING) specifies the collection of all instances INSTANCE of COLLECTION for which (PREDICATE INSTANCE THING) holds.  For example, (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn #$MoonOfAPlanet #$orbits #$PlanetMars) refers to the collection of the moons of Mars.")
(comment MusicalComposition "The collection of all composed pieces of music, whether recorded or not, extant for centuries or composed on the spot, instrumental or sung, etc.  This is not to be confused with musical performances, although musical performances normally enact instances of #$MusicalComposition.")
(comment MediumAttackHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of moderately armed military units that rely on the use of attack helicopters for closing with and engaging the enemy.")
(comment Bulimia "#$Bulimia is an #$EatingDisorder characterized by uncontrolled            episodes of overeating usually followed by self-induced vomiting.")
(disjointWith SimplifyForward SimplifyBackward)
(disjointWith RailroadStation SeaportFacility)
(comment BaseballMitt "Mitts used to catch baseballs and softballs.")
(comment RibbonBridgeEquipment "The collection of equipment used to build a ribbon bridge.")
(comment NewspaperIssue "The collection of all #$PeriodicalIssues for periodicals which are newspapers.  Copies of an instance of #$NewspaperIssue are all instances of #$NewspaperCopy for the same #$Date.")
(comment thereExistAtLeast-RelHolds "(#$thereExistAtLeast-RelHolds NUM VAR REL FORM) means that

(#$thereExistAtLeast NUM VAR FORM) and that for the NUM things of which FORM

holds we can assume that for any given pair of them, ONE, OTHER, the

relation  REL holds, i.e. (REL ONE OTHER).  For instance, suppose we wanted

to translate the sentence \"Joe has 3 friends, at least, who get along with

each other.\"  (#$thereExistAtLeast-RelHolds 3 ?PALS #$likesAsFriend (#$likesAsFriend

Joe ?PALS))")
(comment ProductPlanningAndDevelopment "The set of #$MarketingActivity events in which a product is conceived of, designed, developed and test-marketed.  Instances of this activity are #$performedBy #$MarketingPersons with help from #$TechnicalWorkers.")
(comment interArgReln4-1 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln4-1 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the fourth and first arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG4 ARG1) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(comment Harassment "A collection of events with multiple participants.  In each #$Harassment,  one or more participants repeatedly trouble, annoy, threaten or attack a victim or victims.")
(comment prefersToMaximize "(#$prefersToMaximize AGENT THING SLOT)

means that AGENT prefers (see also #$prefers) greater values of SLOT

(its second argument) when applied to THING (as the first argument of

SLOT). In a sense it means that AGENT will prefer situations whereby

SLOT of THING becomes higher, or stays the same, over situations

whereby SLOT of THING becomes less.  It need not imply that the agent

will directly pursue such maximization (in order to imply direct

pursuit, see #$goals)")
(comment FiberDistributedDataInterface "A ring-shaped fiber optic network.")
(comment AnaerobicBacterium-Facultative "A collection of #$Bacterium that are typically #$AerobicBacterium, but can still grow under anaerobic conditions, if necessary.")
(comment ActorInMovies "The collection of people whose job it is to act in movies.")
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice Cruiser)
(comment Abbreviation "A shortened version of a written word or phrase. An #$Acronym is a specific type of abbreviation.")
(comment trueRule "(#$trueRule TEMPLATE FORMULA) states that FORMULA is both true and an instantiation of the rule template TEMPLATE.")
(comment TravelTour "Instances of #$TravelTour are sets of travel-related services sold together, and usually consisting of transportation, lodging, meals and guided daytime activities.  #$TravelTour is a special kind of #$VacationPackage that is more fully scripted and complete.")
(comment AchievingNirvana "The state of a person who has destroyed the processes that lead to the cycle of birth, death, and rebirth as a conditioned being. This state is the goal of the Buddhist path and is believed to be a state of indescribable bliss, freedom from suffering, and insight into the causes of the reincarnational process.")
(comment potentialDutyOfAgent "(#$potentialDutyOfAgent AGENT ACTTYPE ROLE) means that AGENT may potentially be called upon to play ROLE in an event which satisfies the description given in the set or collection expression that is ACTTYPE in the context of the assertion. Ordinarily GAFs which use this predicate will be asserted in fairly constrained contexts in which a limited number of contingent options exist. The fact that arg3 is an instance of #$ActorSlot presupposes that the set identified in the arg2 position is a subset of #$Event.")
(comment County "A specialization of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  Each instance of #$County is a geopolitical whose territory typically has an area larger than that of a #$City, but smaller than that of a #$State-Geopolitical.")
(comment (FemaleFn EthnicGroupOfAsians) "The group of women that share  cultural features  common to Asians.")
(comment Thyroxine "A #$Hormone produced by the #$Thyroid. Used in the treatment of hypothyroidism.")
(comment NursingYoung "A collection of events in which a baby is fed by milk from the breast. Breastfeeding, suckling.")
(comment TheList "#$TheList is a function that combines its arguments into a list.  For any ITEM(1), ..., ITEM(n), each of which is an instance of #$Thing, (#$TheList ITEM(1) ... ITEM(n)) gives the instance of #$List-Extensional whose first member is ITEM (1), ..., and whose last member is ITEM(n). Note that in general ITEM(1), ..., ITEM(n) do not have to be distinct, though they do if (#$TheList ITEM(1) ... ITEM(n)) is an instance of #$ListWithoutRepetition.")
(disjointWith Elasticity Pressure)
(comment SuckingSomethingUp "A collection of events. In each instance of #$SuckingSomethingUp, the #$objectMoving is propelled along a #$motionPathway-Complete by means of suction (fluid pressure differential). The #$objectMoving need not be an instance of #$FluidTangibleThing. Examples: Sucking a liquid through a straw; a vacuum cleaner sucking objects off of a surface.")
(comment FacilitiesPerson "Someone who provides the upkeep of a professional facility - a building or site - as their job.")
(comment Meteorite "The collection of the remains of all #$Meteors that strike the surface of the Earth so long as they are larger than #$SandParticles.")
(comment VariableAritySkolemFuncN "The subcollection of #$SkolemFuncNs with variable arity. These are only created when a sequence variable is in the scope of  a bounded existential.")
(comment nucleotideSequenceSubsumes "(#$nucleotideSequenceSubsumes SEQUENCE SUBSEQUENCE) means that

the sequence of nucleotides SEQUENCE, considered as an abstract list

of nucleotides, subsumes the nucleotide sequence SUBSEQUENCE")
(comment PartiallyCompliant "This attribute is attributed to an object or event as a result of at least partially complying to some standard.  Typically it is involved in a three way relation between itself, the status-holder and the standard according to which the status holds.  See #$complianceStatus.")
(comment RemnantOfTangibleFn "The term `(#$RemnantOfTangibleFn THING)' denotes the remnants of the #$PartiallyTangible thing THING.

If THING is an ancient building, for example, its remnants would be what we also call its ruins.")
(comment IBTRecoding "A specialization of #$IBTGeneration-Replication.  Each instance of #$IBTRecoding is an event which generates a new information-bearing thing (i.e., an instance of #$InformationBearingThing) by taking information from a source information-bearing thing (see #$informationOrigin), encoding it a new way, and incorporating it into a new information-bearing thing (see #$ibtGenerated).  Instances of #$IBTRecoding may be done either by agents (e.g., people) or by non-agents (e.g., record players, or computers running translation software).  Recoding the content of a pre-existing information-bearing thing presupposes some instance of accessing it (i.e., of #$AccessingAnIBT).")
(comment ShoppingForFn "This is a function that, applied to a collection (type) of objects, contracts or services, denotes the collection of all events in which a person shops for (or searches for) one or more instances of that type, or for information on them, with the purpose of buying them or engaging them.  (#$ShoppingForFn TYPE) denotes the collection of events in which instances of the collection TYPE are sought for purchase, hire, or use, in return for some payment.")
(comment SemiconductorResistance "An instance of #$ElectricalResistance.  #$SemiconductorResistance is the level of resistance found in instances of #$SemiconductorStuff.  See also #$resistanceOfObject.")
(comment (LowAmountFn SocialPower) "What most people have as individuals: the ability to affect the spending of a few thousand dollars and/or the course of a few dozen lives.")
(disjointWith PromotionalProduct ExtractedSample)
(comment PornographicWebSite "The specialization of #$WorldWideWebSite whose instances have #$PornographicMaterial as their main content.")
(disjointWith Conveyance DrugSubstance)
(comment ProperNamePredicate-General "Elements of #$ProperNamePredicate-General are all the lexical predicates that can be used to register the information that a certain STRING is (one of the) name(s) of a certain FORT. This includes members of both #$ProperNamePredicate-Strict and #$ProperNamePredicate-Loose.")
(comment TimePointAtDistanceBeforeStartOf "(#$TimePointAtDistanceBeforeStartOf INT EVT) is the  #$TimePoint that is exactly INT prior to the start of  EVT.  For example, (#$TimePointAtDistanceBeforeStartOf     (#$HoursDuration 1) MyFlightToConnecticut)  is the #$TimePoint that is exactly 1 hour before  my flight to Connecticut begins.")
(comment Exelderm "The chemical compound which is an anti-fungal.")
(comment relativeOrientation-Underspecified "(#$relativeOrientation-Underspecified OBJ1 OBJ2 ORIENT) states

that relative to OBJ2, OBJ1 occupies the #$OrientedLocation-Underspecified

denoted by ORIENT. This predicate allows us to express relativistic notions

of orientation, such as 'sick is better than dead', 'ecstatic' is better than

'happy', etc. More usefully, it allows us to define the lexical semantics of

actions like 'to raise X' (the subabstraction of X after the raise occupies

an upwardly oriented state relative to the subabstraction of X just before

the raise). Many verbs, such as 'improve', 'increase' and 'enhance' have this

core meaning.")
(comment Inspector-Professional "The collection of instances of #$PersonWithOccupation who are charged in their job descriptions with #$Inspecting some class of thing for purposes of quality assurance.")
(comment AutonomousRegion "A collection of geopolitical entities; a sub-collection of #$CountrySubsidiary.  Each instance of #$AutonomousRegion is a sub-region of a country that enjoys more powers of political and/or economic self-determination than do normal provinces of the country.")
(comment JobPositionTypeByOccupation "A collection of collections. Each element of #$JobPositionTypeByOccupation is a collection of #$JobPositions such that the duties and responsibilities of these #$JobPositions are typically performed and borne by instances of a #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg. This collection can be used to facet #$JobPosition.")
(comment Tractor "The collection of vehicles generally used to pull different kinds of farm machinery through a field")
(comment SpeakingOnATelephone "The collection of all events in which a human agent speaks over the telephone.  Ordinarily the acoustic pattern of the speaker's utterance is translated into a series of electrical signals which are conveyed over a phone line to someone who is performing an instance of #$ListeningOnATelephone")
(comment Spore-PlantLifeStage "A (usually) haploid cell which is the product of meiosis in plants.  Spores develop into gametophytes.")
(disjointWith Mixture Liquid-StateOfMatter)
(comment PoliticalInstability "Elements of #$PoliticalInstability are situations in which the stability of the regime in power is low or when there is social unrest.  Terrorist attacks can cause political instability as can food shortages, rioting, or political crises.  The prices of certain products made in regions which are politically unstable tend to be elevated (e.g. oil from oil producing nations).  In the #$HPKBCrisisMt, these events are assumed to be severe enough to cause significant global price increases of a given commodity for major producers of that commodity.")
(comment QuittingAHabit "A collection of events. Each instance of #$QuittingAHabit is an      event in which someone quits some kind of (not necessarily bad)      habit such as smoking, using drugs, nailbiting, etc.")
(comment VulnerableToUDPPacketStorm "#$VulnerableToUDPPacketStorm is a specialization of the attribute #$NetworkVulnerability.  It is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerNetwork.  A network has this vulnerability if it is running an operating system that can be disabled by an #$AttackByComputerOperation-UDPPacketStorm.")
(comment TankLandingShip "The collection of ships intended for use in transporting and landing amphibious vehicles, tanks, combat vehicles, and equipment in amphibious assault.")
(comment DecliningAnInvitation "The collection of acknowledgements in which an invitation is declined.")
(comment Eloping "The collection of marriages performed in secret without the presence (and often without the permission) of the participants' parents.")
(comment Constipation "Abnormally delayed or infrequent passage of dry, hardened feces.")
(comment FamilyTree "A collection of PropositionalInformationThings that convey information about the history/ancestry of a particular Family-Human.")
(comment CyberTerrorist "A specialization of #$Hacker. Each instance of #$CyberTerrorist is a person whose whose intent in breaking into an instance of #$ComputationalSystem is to damage or impair the system, cause a loss of confidence in the integrity of the system, or otherwise corrupt the information content of the system in order to advance their particular worldview, ideology, or political agenda.")
(comment duties "'(#$duties AGREE EVENT)' means that under the #$WorkAgreement AGREE, events of type EVENT must be performed by the obligated agents. It is generally assumed that these duties are observed by the job-holder, though the job-holder performs the duties because, ultimately, the employer itself is obligated. Thus, for example, #$DebuggingAComputerProgram is a duty of the job (#$JobFn #$ComputerProgrammer), meaning that debugging will be carried out by a computer programmer. Nonetheless, the programmer does this because his/her company (#$MicrosoftInc, say) is obliged to perform such duties.")
(comment CarDealer "The collection of persons who negotiate with a potential buyer of a car, find out what they want, and describe what is available.")
(comment GiftBasketTypeByRecipient "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$GiftBasketTypeByContent is a collection of instances of #$GiftBaskets that are intended for similar recipients.")
(comment gameCOC "(#$gameCOC GAME RULES) means that RULES is the #$CodeOfConduct that obligates each player of any playing of GAME.")
(comment cloudCeiling "the height of the clouds above the ground here.")
(comment LinguisticAnalysis-Semantic "A collection of microtheories.  Each element is a microtheory representing knowledge, theory, hypotheses, evidence, and problems related to the semantic analysis of a data set taken from a language or group of languages.")
(comment atomicSymbol "(#$atomicSymbol ELEMENT CODE) means that CODE is the standard abbreviation for the name of ELEMENT.")
(comment currentDepthOfConveyance "(#$currentDepthOfConveyance CONV DEPTH) says    that CONV is DEPTH deep.  For example,     (#$currentDepthOfConveyance Submarine00241    (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 500)) says that     Submarine00241 is 500 feet deep.  Be sure    to temporally qualify such assertions.")
(comment EventOrganizer-Organization "The collection of #$Organizations who

  primarily engage in the organization

 and running of #$ServiceEvents, such

  as Concerts, #$Convention-Meetings and #$TradeShows.")
(comment AVIFile "The collection of computer files encoded in the AVI (Audio

Video Interleave) format. #$AVIFiles are either #$ComputerVideoFiles

or #$ComputerSoundFiles.")
(comment WatchingFn "The term `(#$WatchingFn OBJ-TYPE)' denotes the collection of recreational activities wherein a person sets out to observe objects of type OBJ-TYPE.

Often these are animal types, but other things, such as tornados and stars, can also be the focus of these activities. ")
(comment Confusion-Generic "Every element of this collection is a feeling of being confused or bewildered.")
(comment HostingForeignDelegation "The collection of events where one state accepts a delegation from another state.  This can be as simple as a state visit or as complex as nuclear disarmament negotations.")
(comment BallisticMissile-Mushak200 "A short range ballistic missile produced by Iran.")
(comment approvalStatement "#$approvalStatement is a specialization of #$ist-Information.  (#$approvalStatement INFO APPROVED) means that the #$ELSentence-Assertible APPROVED represents some or all of what the agent approves of in the content (INFO) of an approval that the agent is making.  See also #$Approval-CommunicationAct.")
(comment Coprophagia "Elements of #$Coprophagia are instances of #$Coprophilia in which somebody  ingests #$Feces with the intent of bringing about his/her own #$SexualArousal.")
(comment UrethralAdministration "Administering a liquid through one's urethra.")
(comment resourceInSystem "(#$resourceInSystem SYSTEM THING) means that THING is something which could, through a normal expenditure of energy on the part of SYSTEM, play an instrumental role in some event that would support the normal or nominal function of system.")
(comment Golfer "This is the collection of athletes who make their livings playing golf.")
(comment objectAttacked "(#$objectAttacked ATTACK OBJECT) means that OBJECT is the target of an ATTACK event.")
(comment FragmentOffsetField-Packet "A #$FragmentOffsetField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet
that indicates which fragment of the original #$Packet-Internet that the
current #$Packet-Internet represents. This is useful if fragments of
the original #$Packet-Internet arrive at the destination out-of-order;
the #$FragmentOffsetField-Packet can be used to recreate the original
#$Packet-Internet from the various fragment #$Packet-Internets.")
(comment paAskedQuestion "Predicate used to state that a question has been asked

by the #$ProductAdvisorApplication.  (#$paAskedQuestion FORMULA SET)  means that a question which

attempts to determine the truth of FORMULA has been asked, where SET contained the possible answers from which the

user could select.  (If the question was not multiple choice, then SET should be empty.)")
(comment above-Touching "A binary #$SpatialPredicate that is a
specialization of both #$above-Directly and #$touches (qq.v.).
(#$above-Touching ABOVE BELOW) means that ABOVE is located over 
BELOW and they are touching.  Examples of things related by
#$above-Touching include a person and a chair s/he is sitting on, 
a boat and the on water it floats on, and a hat and the head 
wearing it.  Note that it need _not_ be the case that every point 
of ABOVE is higher than every point of BELOW.")
(disjointWith CycLOpenExpression CycLClosedExpression)
(comment RunningTrack "A track designed for running.")
(comment PennyAntePoker "All instances of poker played for small stakes")
(comment Adoption "The collection of all events in which one or two adults formally become the official parents of a #$HumanChild who was born to someone else.  The #$Adoption is #$performedBy the new parents and their new child [see #$children] is the #$objectActedOn.")
(comment LesbianChatRoom "the collection of #$ChatRooms that #$LesbianPersons visit

  in order to meet and converse with one another.")
(comment SemiAutomaticFirearm "The collection of #$AutomaticFirearms that fire a burst of bullets per pull of the trigger.")
(comment ConstrainedRotation "#$Movement-Rotation constrained by physical contact with a solid or liquid external object along an external or internal boundary of the rotating object.  Physical contact between the rotating body and the external object continues during the rotation, although pairs of points of the two objects in contact may change.  Rigidly connected #$physicalParts of an object undergo #$ConstrainedRotation if the part to which it they are connected also undergo #$ConstrainedRotation.  #$RollingOnASurface, spinning on an axle, #$BeltedMotion, bolt insertion, etc. are all #$ConstrainedRotation s.  A borderline case would be juice whirling within a pitcher just after being stirred.  A maple seed helicoptering in its descent is not an example of #$ConstrainedRotation; neither is a whirlpool in a body of water.")
(comment transportMeansOfType "(#$transportMeansOfType MEAN-TYPE TRANSPORT-TYPE) means that
during instances of TRANSPORT-TYPE, a spec of #$TransportationEvent,
instances of MEAN-TYPE, a spec of #$TransportationDevice, are used as
transportation device.")
(disjointWith RetailDepartmentManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment Cream-Generic "#$Cream-Generic is a collection of creams. Creams are opaque, fluid, tangible stuff.  Cream can be almost as viscous as #$Honey.  An important specialization of #$Cream-Generic is dairy cream (#$Cream-Dairy).")
(comment ArchiveHoldings "The collection of all #$Holdings of documents or records kept as an archive about a given #$Organization or set of events.")
(comment NBCWeaponProductionFacility "The collection of facilities where

   instances of #$WeaponOfMassDestruction

   are built.")
(disjointWith Railway Heliport-Physical)
(comment WesternRegionFn "A unary function which returns the 'western region' of an instance of

#$GeographicalRegion.  What counts as the 'western region' is

contextually determined.  Some of the factors influencing the

determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political

considerations.")
(comment (SportsVersionFn Gun-Portable) "Guns used for sports, and not for hunting/killing.  Examples 

      include guns used in skeet shooting.")
(comment AntiShipCruiseMissile "The collection of #$CruiseMissiles that are designed to attack instances of #$ModernNavalShips.")
(comment M1939ArtilleryGun "The collection of 37mm artillery guns typically used against aircraft.")
(comment CriticismLiteraryFn "The term `(#$CriticismLiteraryFn WORK)' denotes the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings 

which constitute literary criticism of the literary work WORK. Note that such

#$InformationBearingThings are often merely analytical and do not take a critical or fault-finding view

of the work. Such instances would not be in the collection (#$CriticismFn WORK).")
(comment NewWaveMusic "A specialization of #$RockMusic whose heyday was the mid 1970s to early
  1980s. #$NewWaveMusic was influenced by #$RockAndRollMusic from the early-to-mid
  1960s and by early #$PunkMusic.  Like Punk, it was partly a reaction against the 
  self-importance of mid-1970s mainstream #$RockMusic.  Influential practitioners of
  this style include Elvis Costello, Talking Heads, Devo, and Blondie.")
(comment IntakingViaACoupler "An intake process through a coupler.  Most of these will also be #$IntakingViaPortals.")
(comment UniqueWordSenseFn "An evaluatable function. (#$UniqueWordSenseFn WORD SPEECHPART MEANING) denotes the word sense of WORD whose meaning is MEANING for speech part SPEECHPART, if such exists. Otherwise it returns the #$NonNegativeInteger one higher than the highest sense number used for #$denotation assertions involving SPEECHPART and WORD.")
(comment demandRate "(#$demandRate PT PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that the #$Rate RATE is a measure of the demand for instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT.  In a general economic context, PT will often be an instance of (#$GroupFn #$IntelligentAgent).")
(comment Commander-USArmyStaff "A collection of instances of #$MilitaryOfficer.  Each instance of
this collection is the #$organizationHead of a #$StaffOrganization-USArmy. A commander
is responsible for effectively using available resources and for planning the
employment, organizing, directing, coordinating, and controlling of military forces
for the accomplishment of assigned missions.")
(comment PathForWheeledVehicles "A specialization of #$PathArtifact.  Each instance of #$PathForWheeledVehicles is an artifact whose primary function is to serve as a path along which wheeled vehicles may move or park. Often such paths are paved, but they need not be.  Specializations of #$PathForWheeledVehicles include #$AirplaneRunway, #$ParkingLot, and #$Roadway.")
(comment AminoAcid "A collection of organic compounds that are the building

blocks for #$ProteinMolecules.  #$AminoAcids contain an amino (-NH2) and a

carboxyl (-COOH) group.  One way to partition this collection is

according to the side chains: acidic, basic, uncharged polar, and

nonpolar.  Another collection division is that of amino acids

required for protein synthesis and not synthesized by humans,

essential amino acids, and those amino acids required for protein

synthesis but are synthesized by humans, non-essential amino acids.")
(comment HardcopyOfCWFn "A function that maps a #$ConceptualWork or #$CWInfoStructure onto the collection of hardcopy instantiations of that work. For example, (#$HardcopyOfCWFn MobyDickNovel) is the collection of all hardcopy books [#$BookCopy] of Moby Dick. See also #$HardcopyOfInformationTypeFn for the collection of hardcopy instantiations of a type of #$ConceptualWork and #$HardcopyOfIBTTypeFn for the #$collectionIntersection between #$InformationBearingThing types and #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject.")
(comment SporeStainingProcess "A collection of events in which a bacterial culture is

tested for endospore formation.  A culture is grown for several days

or a week on solid medium and then a heat-fixed smear of the growth is

treated with a spore-stain, for example ethonal.  Vegetative cells are

decolorized but endospores will retain the dye.  An indirect endospore

test is also possible, see #$EndosporeTest-Indirect.")
(comment PacifyingAnAgent "A collection of actions; a subset of #$InfluencingAnAgent. In each instance of #$PacifyingAnAgent, one agent deliberately takes actions that will make a hostile agent less hostile to it, or refrains from taking actions that, if taken, will make an agent hostile to it.  This collection doesn't constrain the kinds of actions, or refrainings, that may be taken, except as to the motive and intention with which the agent performs them.  The objects of pacification are intelligent, or at least sentient, agents--including groups of intelligent or sentient agents.")
(disjointWith Density Mass)
(disjointWith ChemicalReaction Archery)
(comment ContactInfoForTypeFn "#$ContactInfoForTypeFn takes as argument any spec of Agent and returns the collection of PropositionalInformationThings about how to contact agents of that type.  For example, (#$ContactInfoForTypeFn #$Doctor-Medical) returns the collection of all information about how to contact one or more doctors.")
(comment HelicopterCarrier "The collection of #$AircraftCarriers intended for use in transporting #$Helicopters.")
(comment NucleotideBonding "A collection of events in which nucleotides are linked by #$PhosphodiesterBonds to form a #$PolynucleotideStrand. The reaction is catalyzed by a #$NucleicAcidPolymerase.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat BeliefSystemType)
(comment ArcCotangentFn "(#$ArcCotangentFn COTAN) yields the angle whose cotangent is COTAN.")
(comment Vanadium "This represents the set of all pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of vanadium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment FillingARefillPrescription-Retail "The collection of all events in which a #$DrugPrescription is refilled in a #$Pharmacy which is either a #$RetailStore or a #$Department of a #$RetailStore; a subset of #$FillingARefillPrescription and #$FillingAPrescription-Retail.")
(comment areaCrimeRate "Per capita frequency of acts of crime including burglary, rape, mugging, shooting, murder.  Generally how safe a neighborhood is for walking around. ")
(comment PersonalityTesting "Collection of tests performed in order to evaluate a person's personality.")
(comment GeneticallyEngineeredBacterialPathogen "The collection of all instances of #$Bacterium

  that have been genetically engineered

   for use in #$BiologicalAttacks.")
(disjointWith Separation-Complete Separation-Incomplete)
(comment DirectionFindingNuclearBurstUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile is to locate the point of           origin of a nuclear explosion.")
(comment mainBusinessActivityOfOrgOccursAt "This predicate is used to link #$CommercialOrganizations  to the places they conduct the majority of their  business activities.  For example,      (#$mainBusinessActivityOfOrgOccursAt JoesGarage-Organization    JoesGarage-TheBuildingOnTheCornerOf6thAndLamar) says   that Joe's Garage (the business) operates out of the  building at 6th and Lamar.  It does not mean that  *all* business activities of Joe's Garage take place  in that building -- ; e.g., every Wednesday, and employee  of Joe's Garage might take a desposit to the bank.")
(comment FTPSite "A collection of #$StructuredInformationSources. An #$FTPSite is a structured directory of downloadable computer files on some computer.")
(comment ExperiencingSecondaryEmotion "#$ExperiencingSecondaryEmotion is the collection of events which are emotional feelings about one's emotional feelings. If an agent experiences one emotion, and then feels another emotion about that first experience, then the experience of that second emotion is an element of #$ExperiencingSecondaryEmotion.  For example, if a person feels fear in response to some situation, and feels angry at oneself for the experiencing that fear, then the experience of anger would be an element of #$ExperiencingSecondaryEmotion.")
(comment NorthEastWind "The collection of all winds that blow from the northeast.  See #$WindProcess.")
(comment SonyPlaystationGame "The collection of video games and versions of such that are made to run specifically on a #$SonyPlayStation-TheProduct platform.")
(comment TheEmptySet "#$TheEmptySet is the empty (or \"null\") set: the unique set that has no elements.  Note that #$TheEmptySet is an instance of #$Set-Mathematical and thus _not_ an instance of #$Collection.")
(comment MakingLegalAgreement "A collection of events.  In each #$MakingLegalAgreement event, an instance of #$LegalAgreement is forged.")
(comment caterCornerTo "This predicate relates objects such as buildings (or

the lots on which they stand) that are located diagonally

across a street intersection from each other.

(#$caterCornerTo OBJ1 OBJ2 XING) means that OBJ1 and OBJ1

are located out in the open on diagonally-opposite street 

corners of XING.  For example, if OBJ1 is on the northwest 

corner of XING, then OBJ2 must be on the southeast corner.

See also #$atStreetIntersection and #$streetCornerOf.")
(comment standardOpposingForceTypes "Force types opposing the direction of movement for a given moving process type")
(comment objectSought-Definite "The expression `(#$objectSought-Definite SEARCH SEEKER CRITERION
OBJECT)' means that SEARCH is a #$LookingForSomething-Definite which is
#$performedBy SEEKER, and that OBJECT is the unique thing which
satisfies the #$PossibleIdentificationCondition which is the #$searchCriterion-Definite
for the search. This predicate is agent-relative
in some respects and non-agent-relative in others. Including the searchCriterion-Definite
makes is agent-relative in a certain sense. 
On the other hand, the term used to denote the OBJECT need not
be one the agent would use or even recognize as denoting the OBJECT, so
that the arg4 position of this predicate is not opaque (see
#$opaqueArgument). Nor need the SEEKER ever be in a position to recognize
that the OBJECT satisfies the CRITERION: in some cases the SEEKER may fail
to recognize that the OBJECT satisfies the CRITERION even upon coming face
to face with said object, because of the guise under which OBJECT is
presented.")
(comment ProvidingEconomicSupport "The collection of events where one agent provides some level of economic aid to another agent.")
(comment RuralArea "A geographical region outside cities or suburbs.  Ruralness is an intrinsic property of these areas, i.e. every piece of a #$RuralArea is an instance of #$RuralArea.")
(comment Labetalol "The chemical compound which is a beta blocker.  This drug helps control blood pressure in severe hypertension.")
(comment malleabilityOfObject "(#$malleabilityOfObject OBJ DEGREE) indicates that the instance of #$SolidTangibleThing OBJ has the degree of #$Malleability DEGREE.")
(comment TVBroadcasting "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$TVTransmitting.  In every #$TVBroadcasting event, an intangible #$InformationBearingThing (usually a #$MovingImageWithSound) is converted into radio signals and transmitted by a #$BroadcastAntenna and received by a #$ReceivingAntenna.  See also #$CableTVTransmitting and #$TVMediaProduct.")
(comment HelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Specialization of units that deploy by means of helicopters.")
(comment SpatiallyDistributiveBinaryPredicate "A collection of predicates.  Each element of #$SpatiallyDistributiveBinaryPredicate is a binary predicate which holds for every spatial subregion of an object to which it is applied.  Thus, for any predicate F belonging to the collection #$SpatiallyDistributiveBinaryPredicate, if (F WHOLE VALUE) is true, then for any spatial portion PART of WHOLE, it is also true that (F PART VALUE).  For example, #$temperatureOfObject, #$stateOfMatter, #$constituents.")
(comment SciFiOrFantasyStory-Generic "A collection of pieces of information; a subset of #$PropositionalInformationThing.            Each element of #$SciFiOrFantasyStory-Generic is a #$Narrative containing the            propositional content of a science fiction or fantasy story, regardless of the format or           formats (play, book) in which the story is or can be told.")
(comment ArrowrootPlant "Individual arrowroot plants; starch can be extracted from their rhizomes.")
(comment MilitaryTreaty "This is the collection of all #$Agreements in which an element of #$MilitaryEvent is governed by the treaty.")
(disjointWith CloudOfH2O Mineral)
(comment LightWheeledVehicle "Lighter weight wheeled military vehicles.")
(comment CatalasePositiveBacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium.  #$CatalasePositiveBacterium
are those that test positive in the #$CatalaseProductionTest.  Most
#$AerobicBacterium produce #$Catalase to de-toxify the hydrogen
peroxide produced during aerobic metabolism.  See also
#$CatalaseNegativeBacterium.")
(disjointWith SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType RoadVehicleType)
(comment Emperor-HeadOfState "The emperor of a country which is usually an empire.")
(comment affectedType "(#$affectedType EVENT TYPE) says that during EVENT, instances of TYPE are affected by the goings-on of EVENT.  For example, (#$affectedType #$WorldWarII #$JapanesePerson) says that some Japanese people were affected by World War II.")
(comment containsInfoStructure-IBT "(#$containsInfoStructure-IBT IBT INFO_STRUCT) means that the #$InformationBearingThing, IBT, contains (at least) the information in the #$AbstractInformationStructure, INFO_STRUCT.")
(comment appropriateAttireTypeAt "This predicate relates locations to clothing types that are appropriate clothing items at the location for the kind(s) of event(s) that usually occurs there. (#$appropriateAttireTypeAt PLACE ATTIRETYPE) means that if one is a human participating in an instance of #$HumanActivity of the sort that PLACE is usually used for, that person should wear an instance of ATTIRETYPE. The appropriateness may result from social conventions or physical factors.")
(comment EatingDisorder "A medical condition in which you do not eat normal amounts            or at normal times.")
(disjointWith TersifyBackward NoTerseArgument)
(comment PornographicMagazineSeries "The collection of #$MagazineSeries whose main content is #$PornographicMaterial")
(disjointWith RailroadStation LaunchPad)
(comment drainageArea "This is the the amount of area drained by a river or other body of water.")
(comment aligned-EdgeToEdge-Acute "(#$aligned-EdgeToEdge-Acute SHEET OBJ) means that a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET1 and SHEET2 are mutually #$alignedAlongEdge to each other.  The angle between the two sheets is acute.  In many such cases, e.g. a stack of papers, the two sheets are #$alignedAlongSurface.")
(comment Racket-SportsEquipment "various paddles or rackets, hand-held devices used in sports like tennis, badminton, ping-pong etc. to knock balls around.")
(comment RibbonBridgeRamp "The collection of ramps used to assemble a ribbon bridge.")
(comment NewspaperSeries "The collection of all #$PeriodicalSeries which have #$NewspaperIssues as #$subWorks.")
(comment Cadmium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Cadmium.")
(comment ProductPlanning "The set of #$MarketingActivity events that occur as the first subEvent within a ProductPlanningAndDevelopment event.  During #$ProductPlanning, a #$Product is conceived and considered for development. Instances of this activity are #$performedBy #$MarketingPersons.")
(disjointWith TakingCareOfSomething Harassment)
(comment ActorOnTV "The collection of people whose job it is to act in television shows. It does not include talk-show hosts and news personnel, who do not pretend to be something they are not.")
(comment PlayOpportunityCWFn "#$PlayOpportunityCWFn takes as argument any instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity and returns the collection of all opportunities (situations in which normal barriers are absent or minimized) to play that game.  For example, (#$PlayOpportunityCWFn #$Chess) returns the collection of all opportunities to play chess, and (#$PlayOpportunityCWFn #$Softball-TheGame) returns the collection of all opportunities to play softball.  See #$PlayOpportunityFn for references to collections of #$GameEvents")
(comment BattleCruiser "The collection of warships which are large and fast, with a great deal of firepower.")
(disjointWith Agent-Generic CharacterStringToken)
(disjointWith Bridge-Military Bridge-Permanent)
(comment backupFileFor "(#$backupFileFor BACKUP FILE) means that computer file BACKUP is a backup of computer file FILE.")
(comment TimesPerDay "Times per day -- unit of frequency")
(disjointWith NumericQuantifier DateDenotingFunction)
(comment countryOfCity "(#$countryOfCity COUNTRY CITY) means that the city CITY is a part (territorially and politically) of the country COUNTRY.")
(comment AchievingNirvana "This is the collection of events in which a person attains and maintains a state of mind known as \"nirvana\". In this state the person has destroyed the processes that lead to the cycle of birth, death, and rebirth as a conditioned being. This state is the goal of the Buddhist path and is believed to be a state of indescribable bliss, freedom from suffering, and insight into the causes of the reincarnational process.")
(comment ViceFn "(#$ViceFn ROLE) returns the #$OrganizationalPosition of
being the 'vice-ROLE' of an agent playing ROLE.  That is, if (ROLE
SYSTEM PERSON) and ((ViceFn ROLE) SYSTEM VICEPERSON), then VICEPERSON
is the immediate #$subordinates of PERSON who is charged with stepping
into PERSON's role in SYSTEM if PERSON is incapacitated.")
(disjointWith StructuredInformationSource Agent-Generic)
(comment (FemaleFn EthnicGroupOfAsians) "The group of women that share cultural features  common to Asians.")
(disjointWith Trailer SelfPoweredDevice)
(comment Cutin "A wax-like plant lipid impervious to most liquids and gasses encountered by plants.")
(comment SublistFromToFn "The function #$SublistFromToFn applied to a list and two numbers, as in (#$SublistFromToFn LIST X Y), picks out the sublist of LIST from position X to position Y, inclusive.  For each nonempty #$List LIST, and for each pair of positive integers M and N such that M is less than or equal to N and such that N is less than or equal to the length of LIST, (#$SublistFromToFn LIST M N) denotes the sublist SUBLIST of LIST such that the first member of SUBLIST is the Mth member of LIST and the last member of SUBLIST is the Nth member of LIST.  See #$subLists.  Note that (#$SublistFromToFn LIST M N) is not defined if LIST is #$TheEmptyList or M is greater than N or N is greater than the length of LIST.")
(disjointWith Elasticity Volume)
(comment lessThwartedFromBecause "(#$lessThwartedFromBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP) means
that there is an increased chance of AGENT's playing the role ROLE in
a situation of type EVTTYPE because PROP is true
(#$decreasedChanceForRoleBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP) and AGENT
has the #$goals (ROLE EVTTYPE AGENT).")
(comment ProcessingPayments "Event of processing requests for payment or purchases, usually performed by people in an accounting department.")
(comment bayesNetOfMicrotheory "A predicate used for probability reasoning using 'Bayesian Networks'.  (#$bayesNetOfMicrotheory BNET MT) means that the #$BayesNet BNET has been created for the #$Microtheory MT.  This means that all of the nodes in BNET are propositions (Cyc formulae) that are asserted in MT, and are linked to one another by #$bayesParent assertions in the same MT.  This predicate associates the network, a #$DirectedAcyclicGraph, with the microtheory. For every #$BayesNet there is exactly one #$Microtheory with which it is associated, but (at present) one #$Microtheory may have multiple #$BayesNets associated with it.  Some, but possibly not all, of the #$CycLAssertions in the #$Microtheory will be nodes in the #$BayesNet.")
(comment CriminalSectorFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction which returns the group of


agents (including #$Organizations) performing criminal acts in a


particular geographical region.  Roughly, this is a version of


#$EconomicSector-Localized for illegal activities. Group members of a


criminal sector include black marketeers, participants in the illegal


drug trade, and organized crime groups.")
(comment StormAsEvent "The kind of storms directly perceivable by people on the ground on Earth -- Rainstorms, windstorms, sandstorms, but not ionospheric electrical disturbances, underwater phenomena.  Storms are short-lived when experienced from the ground (#$AmbientConditionsMt).  See also #$StormAsObject.")
(comment PartiallyNonCompliant "This attribute is attributed to an object or event as a result of at least partial non-compliance to some standard.  We would use this when compliance status would admit of degree.  Typically it is involved in a three way relation between itself, the status-holder and the standard according to which the status holds.  See #$complianceStatus.")
(comment RemnantOfIntangibleFn "The term `(#$RemnantOfIntangibleFn THING)' denotes the remnants of the intangible thing THING. The remnants of an ancient civilization, for example, will be some #$PartiallyTangible things which were created by that civilization and are evidence of it.\")")
(comment IBTGeneration-Replication "A specialization of #$IBTGeneration.  Each instance of #$IBTGeneration-Replication is an event in which a new instance of #$InformationBearingThing (IBT) is created whose content is based on that of a preexisting IBT (which is the #$informationOrigin (q.v.) of the generation event).  The new IBT contains at least part of the information content of the original IBT.  It may use the same or a different way of encoding the information.")
(comment GammaRay "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation.  Each instance of #$GammaRay is an instance of electromagnetic radiation that has a wavelength (see the predicate #$wavelength) of less than  1x10^-2 angstroms (see the constant #$Angstrom).  Low power instances of #$GammaRay overlap with high power instances of #$XRay (q.v.).")
(comment (VeryHighAmountFn SocialPower) "The degree of social power exercised by those high in a national government or very high in a huge multinational corporation -- those people actually formulating plans and putting in motion policies that could determine how billions of dollars are spent and affect millions of lives.  According to popular perception, persons with ImperialPower can pretty much achieve their social goals on a national or world scale, and they are `players' at the national and world level.")
(comment Uranium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of uranium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType TransportationEventByVehicleType)
(comment ProperNamePredicate-Loose "Instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Loose are all the lexical predicates that can be used for the purpose of temporarily and rapidly registering the information that a certain STRING is (one of the) name(s) for a certain FORT. The salient feature of the predicates that are instances of #$ProperNamePredicate-Loose is that assertions made using those predicates are not guaranteed to contain all the grammatical information that would be necessary to handle morphological variants of the strings that appear in those assertions. For example, such assertions would not contain information on whether the STRING argument, can or cannot be pluralized when referring to the FORT argument. A prototypical example of such a predicate would be #$termStrings. Compare to #$ProperNamePredicate-Strict.")
(comment PlanningDomainMicrotheory "A specialization of #$Microtheory.  Each instance of #$PlanningDomainMicrotheory is a microtheory created to store knowledge relevant to performing planning activities. Such a microtheory will act as the main receptacle for any information that is relevant to the planning problem - i.e., background contexts, whether these be general or specific.")
(comment NetworkingHardware "A collection of #$ComputerHardwareItems.  Every instance of #$NetworkingHardware is a device used to connect computers together in a network.")
(comment FluticasonePropionate "The chemical compound which is used in nasal inhalant products.")
(comment highlyRelevantInEvent "This predicate relates instances of #$Event to things that are highly relevant in the event, help to define the nature of the event, but play no direct role in carrying out the actual event. For instance, in a tribute to a dead person it may be the case that (#$highlyRelevantInEvent TributeToDeadPersonA PersonA), (but see the more specialized predicate, #$eventHonors).  This predicate should apply only to things that play some central, but indirect, role in an event, i.e. note that #$actors is a  genlPreds of this predicate.  Often this predicate applies to things that motivate the event in question.  Also note that it should help to distinguish the event from other events of a slightly more general type.  For instance, a particular kind of chair might be highly relevant in a chair buying event but the capitalist system is not.  Insofar as other shopping events also involve the capitalist system, the capitalist system does not distinguish the chair buying event from other shopping events.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization County)
(comment TallShip "Type of ship predominant until the late 19th Century, wooden-hulled and tall-masted, and powered by wind pushing against their sails.")
(comment DisconnectingAPhoneLink "The collection of all events in which a telephone communication link is severed.  This may be done through an overt physical act, such as an instance of #$HangingUpATelephoneReceiver, or it may be accomplished by electronic means.")
(comment BotanicalCell "A subset of #$Cell.  #$BotanicalCell is the collection of cells which constitute the elements of #$Plant and #$PlantPart, e.g., the cells making up elements of #$BotanicalOrgan, of #$Seed, and of #$Spore-PlantLifeStage.")
(comment MilitaryWeaponTypeByFunction "A collection of collections.  Each member TYPE of #$MilitaryWeaponTypeByFunction is either a specification of #$MilitaryWeapon or a specification of #$WeaponSystem satisfying the following conditions.  (i) TYPE is distinguished from other members of #$MilitaryWeaponTypeByFunction by a main function that members of TYPE have.  Thus, e.g., #$FighterPlane is a member of #$MilitaryWeaponTypeByFunction while #$F-18-Fighter is not.  (ii) The so-called 'main function' should not be too broad or too narrow, but significant enough for comparison between different military organizations.  Thus neither #$Weapon nor #$Handgun is a member of #$MilitaryWeaponTypeByFunction.")
(comment Mining "Extracting minerals and other resources from the earth.")
(comment SomethingAppearingSomewhere "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  During each instance of #$SomethingAppearingSomewhere, an object (related to the instance of #$SomethingAppearingSomewhere by #$objectEmplaced (q.v.)) is introduced into a location or situation where it previously was not.  This location or situation (related to the instance of #$SomethingAppearingSomewhere via #$objectOfStateChange (q.v.)) is somehow intrinsically affected by the arrival of the object.  The object may be created during the coming-to-be event, it may move, either by external force or under its own power, or it may metaphorically 'enter' into a new state.  Examples of #$SomethingAppearingSomewhere include: spreading fertilizer on a lawn; mold growing on bread; Columbus' ships arriving in the New World.")
(comment VulnerableToFraggleAttack "#$VulnerableToFraggleAttack is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer. A computer has his vulnerability if it is running an operating system that can be disabled from a fraggle attack.")
(comment Destroyer "The collection of highly maneuverable, relatively small warships which are used to destroy other naval ships. Typically these ships are armed with naval guns, depth charges, and torpedoes.")
(comment CaucasusCountry "The collection of nation-states neighboring the Caucasus Mountains, including Azerbaijan, Armenia, Russia, Georgia, Turkey and Iran.")
(comment infectionHost "This predicate relates a particular case of #$Infection to the organism it is infecting.  (#$infectionHost INF ORG) means that INF is an #$Infection in which the host organism is ORG.")
(comment Goofer "#$Goofers are #$Hackers that break into #$ComputationalSystems without malicious intent, but simply for the thrill of breaking in.  #$Goofers are typically kids, although they do not have to be. They damage, corrupt or degrade service or integrity to the systems that they hack only unintentionally.")
(comment effectiveSterilizationMethodFor "(#$effectiveSterilizationMethodFor MICROBETYPE EVENTTYPE)

means that if an instance of MICROBETYPE is the #$objectActedOn by an

instance of EVENTTYPE, then there is a high #$likelihood that there

will be a #$Dying caused by the instance of EVENTTYPE of which the

instance of MICROBETYPE will be the #$bodilyDoer.")
(comment subIndustries "(#$subIndustries INDUSTRY SUBINDUSTRY) means that 

the individual (usally geographically defined) SUBINDUSTRY is one

of the subindustries of the individual INDUSTRY.  (Both must be instances of #$Industry-Localized.)  For instance, the SUBINDUSTRY may produce a specialized form of the products that INDUSTRY produces.

Thus, the Argentine beef industry is a subindustry of the Argentine livestock

industry, and the Argentine livestock industry is a subindustry of the

South American food industry.  Or the SUBINDUSTRY may perform one of the

#$industryActivityTypes of INDUSTRY, such as the (#$RefiningFn

#$Petroleum-CrudeOil) phase of the #$OilIndustry.  Note that this predicate relates two individual (geographically defined) industries (instances of #$Industry-Localized), not two kinds of industry.  To relate two kinds of industry, use #$subIndustryTypes.")
(comment microtheoryDesignationArgnum "Used to specify which argument of a given #$MicrotheoryDesignatingRelation
designates the microtheory in which to interpret some formula.")
(comment ExecutiveGiftBasket "An instance of #$GiftBasketTypeByRecipient.  An #$ExecutiveGiftBasket is a gift basket that is intended to be given to an #$Executive.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType TransportationEventByVehicleType)
(comment TourOfRegionFn "(#$TourOfRegionFn REGION) is the collection of 

#$TravelTours of REGION.  So for example (#$TourOfRegionFn #$France) is the collection of tours of France.")
(comment Nobelium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Nobelium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment enables-RemovesContraryFactors "#$enables-RemovesContraryFactors expresses the notion that an
agent may be 'enabled' by an event in the following sense: the event
removes all factors that are 'contrary', i.e., that would decrease the
likelihood of the agent's success -- put another way: all factors that
would make it less likely that the agent would succeed in performing the
action if she tried. More accurately, (#$enables-RemovesContraryFactors SIT
AGENT ACT_TYPE) is true iff SIT obtains, there are no contrary factors for
AGENT to do an instance of ACT_TYPE, and SIT is the cause of there being no
such contrary factors. Hence #$enables-RemovesContraryFactors does not
imply that the agent is in fact capable of doing an action: rather, it
entails that, given SIT, the probability of the agent's success is
increased. Example: proper bicycle maintenance enables the cyclist to
complete the race.")
(disjointWith PrecipitationParticle DustParticle)
(disjointWith OrganSubPartType OrganRegionType)
(comment Course-Collegiate "This is the collection of college courses. These are individuated by

department and course number, including section number. Thus, different sections

of English 101 taught by the English Department at University X during the same term count as distinct courses in this sense. Similarly,  courses with the same course number and section number taught through the same department and by the same professor during different terms count as different courses.   ")
(comment visuallyDepictsEvent "(#$visuallyDepictsEvent PICT EV) means that PICT is a #$VisualInformationBearingThing that depicts the #$Event EV. Compare with #$visuallyDepicts, which is used to describe situations in which what is depicted is not an #$Event but a #$SpatialThing.")
(comment Name "A specialization of #$LexicalWord. Each instance of this collection is a (proper) name -- a word by which an entity is designated and distinguished from others -- for e.g. #$Cassandra-TheName, #$Sidney-TheName. Note that this collection contains names not just for people, but for other nameable entities (such as pets, intelligent computer programs...). However, the most notable specializations of this collection are #$HumanGivenName and #$HumanSurname. For a representation of the actual string of letters which makes up any given name, see #$ProperNameString and its specializations (and see #$nameSpelling for relating the two).")
(comment Debutante "The collection of young women who are making their societal debuts.  A debut is the event in which a young woman makes her first formal appearance in society.")
(comment PersianGulfCountry "The collection of nation-states bordering the Persian Gulf.")
(comment TeamGame "The collection of all instance of #$Game whose #$competingAgents are #$Teams instead of individual #$Persons.")
(comment BallisticMissile-SCUDB "A short range ballistic missile produced in North Korea.")
(comment createdBy "The predicate #$createdBy relates something to its creator(s).  (#$createdBy THING AGENT) means that AGENT is one of the people, corporations, publishers, etc., responsible for the invention or bringing into being of THING.  This is a very general predicate, whose narrower specifications such as #$developerOfIBTType, #$ibtCreator, #$madeBy, or #$creatorOfCW, should be used if applicable instead.")
(comment MouthAndThroatAdministration "Administering a drug through application to one's mouth or throat.")
(comment TechnologyIndustry "The set of all elements of #$Industry-Localized that are in some way technologically sophisticated.  Thus, elements of #$TechnologyIndustry are groups of providers of technologically sophisticated goods or services.")
(disjointWith Account-LegalAgreement Visa-Permit)
(comment Header-Packet "An instance of #$Header-Packet is the portion of a #$Packet-Internet that 

    contains an instance of #$SourceAddressField-Packet and an instance of 

#$DestinationAddressField-Packet

    as well as other information about the #$Packet-Internet.")
(comment Fish "An instance of #$BiologicalClass, and a specialization of #$Vertebrate.  Each instance of #$Fish is a cold-blooded animal (see the collection #$Poikilotherm) with gills and fins. Each instance of #$Fish spends all or almost all of its life under water.  Note that the collection #$Fish excludes fish-shaped examples of #$Mammal, such as porpoises and whales. Specializations of #$Fish include the collections #$Salmon, #$Catfish, and #$Tuna.")
(comment Knuckle "By Knuckle, I mean the region on the outer surface of a finger, over the middle segment of the finger. ")
(comment numberOfPrescriptionsByDocTypeDuring "(#$numberOfPrescriptionsByDocTypeDuring ?DOC-TYPE ?DRUG-PROD ?PRESC-TYPE ?TIME ?NUM) means that, during the time interval ?TIME, #$MedicalCareProfessionals of type, ?DOC-TYPE, had ?NUM #$DrugPrescriptions for ?DRUG-PROD filled.")
(comment CricketField "The collection of fields where games of cricket are played.")
(comment Paralegal "Also referred to as ``legal assistant'' and ``legal executive'',           a #$Paralegal is a person with specialized training who assists lawyers.")
(comment CycLDenotationalTerm "The collection of all CycL terms that are not sentences (cf. #$CycLSentence), and thus are either #$CycLAtomicTerms (such as constants or variables) or #$CycLNonAtomicTerms (also known as \"NAT\"s).   #$CycLDenotationalTerms are so-called, not because they all have denotations (not all of them do), but because they are in a certain sense the right kind of term for having a denotation.  That is, an instance of #$CycLDenotationalTerm -- if it is semantically well-formed and closed (i.e. contains no free variables) -- might denote something in the universe of discourse.  (Even so, it will not _necessarily_ denote something, considering (e.g.) the fact that a function need not be defined for every (sequence of) thing(s) satisfying its argument type constraints; see #$PartialFunction.)  But note that neither semantic well-formedness nor being closed is a requirement for being a CycL denotational term: `(#$JuvenileFn #$isa ?X #$genls #$JuvenileFn)', for example, is a NAT and thus a denotational term.  Other examples of denotational terms are the expressions: `#$Muffet', `?X', `(#$JuvenileFn ?X)', `(#$TheSetOf ?X (#$objectHasColor ?X #$GreenColor))', and `212'.  Note also that, like most instances of #$CycLExpressionType, #$CycLDenotationalTerm is a #$quotedCollection (q.v.).")
(comment SecurityService "The collection of private law enforcement agencies that are legally empowered to enforce some laws on specific private property.  This collection includes campus police, security guards at sporting events and concerts, operators of #$ArmoredCars, etc.  It does NOT include instances of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization.")
(comment GayMaleChatRoom "the collection of #$ChatRooms that #$GayMales visit

  in order to meet and converse with one another.")
(comment SelectiveFireFirearm "The collection of #$AutomaticFirearms that can operate as either a #$FullyAutomaticFirearm or a #$SemiAutomaticFirearm.")
(comment Chitin "#$Chitin is a nitrogen-containing polysaccharide, related chemically            to cellulose, that forms a semitransparent horny substance and is           a principal constituent of the exoskeleton or outer covering of insects,            crustaceans and arachnids.")
(comment SurfaceConstrainedRotation "Rotation constrained by/at the surface of the rotating object.  Rolling along a surface, rocking, capsizing, and the motion of a trackball are such motions.  For #$SurfaceConstrainedRotation the #$axisOfRotation is parallel to the surface of the #$constrainingObject (perpendicular to the surface normal) at the region of contact.  The surface of contact between an object engaged in #$SurfaceConstrainedRotation and its #$constrainingObject moves around the rotating object, except when the object is encircled by the #$constrainingObject throughout its region of contact.")
(comment PlainTrickCardGame "The subcollection of all #$TrickTakingCardGames in which the value of the trick does not depend on what cards it contains.  The object of such games will typically be to win some number of tricks, or as many tricks as possible.  Occasionally the object is to win a specific trick (like the last one).  There are also some plain trick games where the object is to lose tricks (such as #$HeartsGame).  Other examples of #$PlainTrickCardGames are #$Spades-CardGame, #$Whist, #$Bridge-TheGame.")
(comment IBTCopying-SingleCopy "The collection of #$IBTCopying events in which an item is copied exactly one time.")
(disjointWith PurchasingManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment Paste "#$Paste is the collection of pastes.  Pastes are opaque, semi-solid, sticky,  tangible stuff.  Unlike some semi-solid stuff (like sand), pastes cannot be poured.  Pastes are thicker than creams and are the same thickness as gels.")
(disjointWith PedestrianSportsEvent (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(comment keViews "(#$keViews TERM VIEW) states that VIEW is one view for looking at TERM.  See also #$keViewSentences.")
(comment WheeledTransportationDevice "#$WheeledTransportationDevice is a specialization of #$LandTransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$WheeledTransportationDevice is a transportation device that uses only wheels (as opposed to tracks, runners, etc.).  This collection includes not only many instances of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle, but also non-self-powered devices such as #$Bicycles and #$Wagons.")
(comment EasternRegionFn "A unary function that returns the `eastern region' of an instance of #$GeographicalRegion.  What counts as the `eastern region' is contextually determined.  Some of the factors influencing the determination may be local geography, cultural identity, and political considerations.")
(comment TVTalkShowHost "Each #$TVTalkShowHost is a #$TVShowHost of a #$TVTalkShow, and is thereby a #$TalkShowHost as well.")
(comment CloseQuarterCombatWeapon "A collection of the collections of #$Weapons which are normally used in hand-to-hand combat.")
(comment contiguousAfterMt "(#$contiguousAfterMt AFTER-MT BEFORE-MT) means that the time associated with (see #$mtTime) AFTER-MT is #$contiguousAfter the time associated with BEFORE-MT.")
(comment CropCircle "This is the collection of large patterns created by tamping down

crops. Some believe these patterns are the work of non-humans, and the purpose of

these patterns is almost certainly to suggest the presence of non-human intelligent beings.")
(comment CirculationFn "(#$CirculationFn FLUID-TYPE) denotes the collection of instances of #$FluidCirculating in which the #$objectMoving is an element of FLUID-TYPE. (#$BillJ, 7/10/96)")
(comment intervalStartedBy "This predicate that relates time intervals to the temporal things that immediately precede them. (#$intervalStartedBy INT TEMP-OBJ) means that INT is the instance of #$TimeInterval that immediately follows TEMP-OBJ. The end of INT coincides with the end of all time (#$Always-TimeInterval), if time has an end. See #$IntervalStartedByFn.")
(comment consumptionRate "(#$consumptionRate PT PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT consumes instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE at the #$Rate RATE.  PT might, for example, be a #$Country or a #$Business.")
(comment SurfaceTransportationEvent "The collection of #$TransportationEvents in which the #$transporter is in contact with some surface, either land or water. The #$transporter may not be suspended in air or immersed in water.")
(comment CatalaseProductionTest "A collection of events in which bacterium is tested for the
presence of catalase.  A bacterial culture is exposed to hydrogen
peroxide.  If catalase is present, the culture will bubble with gas,
#$Oxygen.")
(comment HumanitarianAssistance "#$HumanitarianAssistance is a collection of attributes representing the levels of humanitarian aid (food, clothing, medical attention, etc.) that one group of agents may give to another.")
(comment XRay "A specialization of #$ElectromagneticRadiation.  Each instance of #$XRay is some electromagnetic radiation with a wavelength (see the predicate #$wavelength) ranging from about 1 #$Angstrom to 1x10^-3 #$Angstroms.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single Archery)
(comment Stirrup "The collection of all stirrups -- rings or loops for the feet while riding, usually connected to (part of) a saddle")
(comment SystemAdministrator "Someone who specializes in security in the silicon realm.")
(comment inheritedTermSentences "(#$inheritedTermSentences TERM GENL FORMULA) states that FORMULA can be deduced to be a true formula about TERM based on the fact that GENL is one of the generalizations of TERM.  In other words, although FORMULA is not usually asserted to be true, it is nevertheless an 'inherited' truth based on a more general truth asserted about the more general concept GENL. See also #$assertedTermSentences and #$trueSentence.")
(comment StreptococcusPneumoniae "A collection of #$Bacterium comprising a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These cells are the most common cause of pneumonia and may also cause meningitis.")
(comment HelicopterCruiser "A collection. #$Cruisers specialized for carrying #$Helicopters.")
(comment providesPlanningInformation "(#$providesPlanningInformation EVENT IBT) means that IBT contains all or part of the plan for carrying out EVENT.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat SpatiallyDisjointRegionType)
(comment ArcSecantFn "(#$ArcSecantFn SEC) yields the angle whose secant is SEC.")
(comment WritingSurfaceProduct "Kinds of objects produced to serve as a writing surfaces, surfaces on which marking are intentionally made to communicate.")
(comment Tin "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of tin.")
(comment Fairway "A kind of subregion of a golf course, where the ball is hit a long distance over a grassy stretch free of obstacles like trees.")
(comment orgFacilities "(#$orgFacilities ORG PLACE) means that PLACE is *the* physical location and complex out of which the #$Organization ORG operates and functions.")
(comment MineField-AntiPersonnel "A collection of instances of #$MineField that are specifically designed and intended to attrit enemy forces by inflicting casualties on enemy personnel.")
(comment OfficialDocumentType "A collection of all the subcollections of #$OfficialDocument whose instances are a particular and distinct type of official document -- for instance #$Passport and #$PostageStamp. It should not be asserted of subcollections of #$OfficialDocument which might not be disjoint -- for instance #$FloodReport and #$TermiteReport.")
(comment Rave-DanceParty "The collection of all rave parties, big dance parties, typically held in discoteques or outside with Techno, House and/or Hip Hop music played and Ecstasy taken.")
(comment Adamsite "A chemical agent which produces #$Nausea and #$Vomiting. When used as a weapon, it, like #$TearGas, is usually not intended to kill or permanently harm its victims, but to incapacitate them so that they can be more easily controlled.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent Perceiving)
(comment DirectionFindingRadarUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile is to locate the point of           origin of radar signals.")
(comment RecreationalDrugUse "Taking drugs to acheive some state of mind rather than for medicinal purposes.  This includes drinking alcoholic beverages and coffee, so it's not necessarily illegal.")
(comment TranceMusic "A kind of techno music that features subtly changing melodies and beats. It is fast and engaging, but not agressive.")
(comment NorthWind "The collection of all winds that blow from the north.  See #$WindProcess.")
(comment SegaSaturnGame "This is the collection of video games designed specifically to be

played on a #$SegaSaturn-TheProduct platform.")
(comment reformulatorEquiv "A #$CycLReformulationRulePredicate that relates two CycL sentences.  When asserted in a #$Microtheory MT, (#$reformulatorEquiv SENTENCE-1 SENTENCE-2) means that the #$CycLSentence SENTENCE-1 may be reformulated into the #$CycLSentence SENTENCE-2, or vice versa (based on meta-properties of this rule and what mode the reformulator is in), in any #$Microtheory SPEC-MT such that (#$genlMt SPEC-MT MT) holds.  Free variables in SENTENCE-1 and SENTENCE-2 are shared, and may bind with CycL sentences which match the template.  Note that (#$reformulatorEquiv SENTENCE-1 SENTENCE-2) does _not_ necessarily imply (#$equiv SENTENCE-1 SENTENCE-2), although this implication would hold if the reformulation is a #$TruthPreservingReformulation (q.v.).")
(comment CultMovie "The collection of movies that have an obsession-like following.  One of the most well-known instances of this collection is #$RockyHorrorPictureShow-TheMovie.  What is considered a #$CultMovie by one person may not be considered as such by another.  Hence, this is a very fuzzy collection.")
(comment speciesImmunity "An organism with this attribute belong to species not susceptible

of diseases caused by given pathogen.")
(comment StreetSystem "A specialization of #$RoadSystem instances of which
are systems of streets (see #$Street-Generic).  Examples
include any system of all the connected streets in a given
city, town, or neighborhood.")
(comment inclinationOfObject "The inclination of a surface")
(comment ProvidingPoliticalSupport "The collection of events where one agent provides some level of political aid to another agent.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay PolarDay)
(comment PalmReading "Elements of #$PalmReading are events in which the doer fortels another person's future or divines aspects of their personality by studying the shape and texture of their hands and the markings on their palms.")
(comment LandlockedGeopoliticalEntity "The set of regions which do not border on any significantly large #$BodyOfWater; regions which are completely surrounded by land. In practical terms, landlocked areas do not have easy access to an #$Ocean or #$Sea.")
(comment HavingAParticularShape "This is the collection of situations in which some object maintains a particular shape.  Such situations begin and end with an instance of #$MovementOrShapeChangeEvent.")
(comment SoundWavePropagationType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$SoundWavePropagationType is a specialization of #$Sound (q.v.).  Notable instances of #$SoundWavePropagationType include #$AudibleSound and #$UltraSound.")
(comment farRelativeTo "(farRelativeTo ?SIDE ?OBJ) means that ?SIDE is the farther away of two or more relevant objects, or the farther away of two or more parts of a relevant object, relative to ?OBJ.  See also #$nearRelativeTo.  Created for the Battlespace Workarounds effort.")
(comment Timolol "The chemical compound which is a beta blocker.  This drug is intended to be used for therapeutic treatment of hypertension.")
(comment Malleable "has greater than #$NonMalleable Malleability")
(disjointWith RadioBroadcasting TVBroadcasting)
(comment PrivatizingAnIndustry "#$PrivatizingAnIndustry is in some sense the opposite of #$NationalizingAnIndustry and refers to the selling of a company formerly owned by the government to the private sector.--Kahlert, Feb 26, 1999")
(comment EnumeratedPartType "Elements are types of parts that occur a fixed number of times (greater than 2) in the individuals that have them.  The nthInstanceOf an #$EnumeratedPartType may be a #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType (#$Vertebra) or #$SymmetricAnatomicalPartType (#$Rib-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment LightHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Specialization of lightly armed helicopter units.")
(comment Hecto "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 100")
(comment WesternStory-Generic "A collection of pieces of information; a subset of #$PropositionalInformationThing.            Each element of #$WesternStory-Generic is a #$Narrative containing the            propositional content of a story that would be considered a 'western', regardless of           the format or formats (play, book) in which the story is or can be told.")
(comment UnblockingTraffic "The collection of events in which a previously blocked path         is re-opened. Each instance of #$UnblockingTraffic is a         purposeful action done by some agent with a purpose of         reopening a certain path to traffic. For each element of         #$UnblockingTraffic, there is at least one #$objectActedOn         which is an element of #$Path-Customary (e.g., a bridge which         is broken or a road which is blocked to prevent vehicles or         people from passing through it).  See also #$pathState.")
(comment StockOption "The collection of #$Agreements that give their owners the right to buy (#$OptionToBuy) or to sell (#$OptionToSell) a particular kind of #$Stock for an agreed-upon sum up to or after a specified date (or within a specified #$TimeInterval).  If the right is not exercised during the specified time, it expires and the owner forfeits the right it conveyed.  #$EmployeeStockOptions are often given as a form of compensation to employees.")
(comment Rhizome "An elongated underground stem, sometimes swollen and serving as a storage organ.")
(comment BradleyFightingVehicle-M2 "A model of #$BradleyFightingVehicle.")
(disjointWith SubAtomicParticle Mineral)
(disjointWith TrainEngine LightWheeledVehicle)
(comment DentalSchool "Schools that grant dental degrees, whose students usually end up as dentists.")
(comment CatalaseNegativeBacterium "A collection of #$Bacterium that do not produce #$Catalase.
These cells are typically #$AnaerobicBacterium that do not produce
hydrogen peroxide during metabolism.  Catalase is the enzyme that
would decompose the hydrogen peroxide.  See also
#$CatalasePositiveBacterium.")
(comment King-HeadOfGovernment "The King of a country and the #$HeadOfGovernment of that country")
(comment originalInfoStructureOfCW "(#$originalInfoStructureOfCW CONCEPTUALWORK CW_VERSION) means that the original structured version of the #$ConceptualWork, CONCEPTUALWORK, is the #$CWInfoStructure, CW_VERSION.")
(comment hotelCableAmenities "This predicate relates an instance of #$HotelBuilding to the instances of #$TelevisionNetwork that guests are able to watch in their rooms.")
(comment bordersOn-Celestial "(#$bordersOn-Celestial REGION-1 REGION-2) means that the #$CelestialRegion REGION-1 and the #$CelestialRegion REGION-2 are physically adjacent to each other on the celestial sphere.  This is the astronomical analog of #$bordersOn.  Examples: (#$bordersOn-Celestial #$UrsaMajor-Constellation #$UrsaMinor-Constellation).")
(disjointWith ReversibleReformulation IrreversibleReformulation)
(comment mtRemovalConstraint "(#$mtRemovalConstraint MT PROP) means that the constraints specified in PROP must be satisfied in order for assertions to be deleted from MT, by a user or an application")
(comment StripTeaseShow "A kind of #$EntertainmentPerformance featuring #$Strippers.")
(disjointWith AircraftHangar Airport-Physical)
(comment Lymphocyte "A subclass of #$WhiteBloodCells, which are mononucleated, nonphagocytic, and immunologically capable, or will be at a later stage.  They are affected in a common type of #$Leukemia and in #$AIDS.")
(comment GolfClub "Those long clubs that golfers own so many of; used to hit around a little white ball.")
(comment SA-9WheeledSAMVehicle "Wheeled vehicles which transport SA-9 surface-to-air missiles.")
(comment Iron "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of iron; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(disjointWith AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent ChemicalSynthesis)
(comment typePlaysFunctionalRoleInType-Expect "(#$typePlaysFunctionalRoleInType-Expect AGENTTYPE SYS-ROLE
SYSTEMTYPE) means that if SYS-INST is an instance of SYSTEMTYPE, then
the expectation is that there exists an instance of AGENTTYPE,
AGT-INST, such that (SYS-ROLE SYS-INST AGT-INST).")
(comment MajorLeague "A collection of organizations.  An element of #$MajorLeague is a professional #$SportsLeague that is not part of [#$subOrganizations] any larger #$SportsLeague and is not ranked lower than some other league in the same sport.  Examples: #$NationalFootballLeague, #$NationalHockeyLeague, #$NationalLeague-Baseball.")
(comment ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory-SingleDateSeries "This is a subcollection of 

#$ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory.  Each instance MT of 

#$ReasoningWithMultiFutureMicrotheory-SingleDateSeries

is a spec MT of both #$ReasoningWithMultiFuture-LogicMt and 

#$ReasoningWithTense-LogicMt-SingleDateSeries.  Thus each such MT 

has access to the notions of historical possibility and necessity in

#$ReasoningWithMultiFuture-LogicMt as well as those notions of 

metric tense operators in #$ReasoningWithTense-LogicMt-SingleDateSeries.")
(comment equity-Financial "(equity-Financial ORG AMOUNT) means that AMOUNT was invested in ORG in the form of direct investment and/or retained earnings.")
(comment MetallicConductingMedium "Any metallic conductor. ")
(comment Scandal "A specialization of #$ControversialAction.  Each instance of #$Scandal is a discreditable action that causes public uproar.")
(comment ChildsGame "The collection of all games [#$Game] whose performances are typically played by children [#$HumanChild]")
(comment destructivePotentialOf "This #$BinaryPredicate is used for linking an instance of #$TemporalThing with a capacity of that thing to cause damage in a certain context, measured as a scalar #$DestructivePotential.")
(comment Enterobacter "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These
are large #$GramNegativeBacterium found in the intestinal tract of
humans and animals.  Motile by peritrichous flagella.  They will ferment lactose promptly and produces colonies similar to Klebsiella-Genus.  Most species are resistent to ampicillin and cephalosporins, but respond to carbenicillin and newer cephalosporins.")
(comment Actor-Voice "The collection of people whose job it is to use only their voice to portray a character. This includes people who provide voices for cartoon characters and actors in radio dramas, but not announcers, #$DiscJockeys, and radio talk-show hosts,")
(comment enables-PropProp "(#$enables-PropProp PROP1 PROP2) says that the fact that PROP1 'enabled' or 'allowed' the situation described in PROP2 to take place.  For example, (#$enables-PropProp \"The prison guard turned his back on the prisoners\" \"One of the prisoners escaped\") says that 'that the prison guard turned his back on the prisoners allowed one of the prisoners to escape.'")
(comment EdibleSeed "The seeds that people typically eat.")
(comment CharacterStringToken "The collection of concrete tokens of abstract    character-strings.   More precisely, #$CharacterStringToken    is a specialization of #$HumanAccessibleIBT each of whose    instances is a specific physical representation of some    particular instance of #$CharacterString.  (Note that a    character-string might consist of only a single character,   in which case a token of the string effectively represents    the character itself; thus for simplicity #$CharacterToken    has been made a specialization of #$CharacterStringToken.)   Character-string tokens exist in at least three different    basic forms: as inscriptions, sounds, or electromagnetic    encodings (see #$CharacterStringToken-Inscribed,    #$CharacterStringToken-Sounded, and #$CharacterStringToken-ElectroMagnetic).  Abstract character-strings themselves are inherently    neither inscriptional nor sonic nor electromagnetic, so the same    string can be represented by tokens of these different forms.     Character-string tokens often, but not always, consist in    spatial or temporal series of character tokens (see    #$CharacterStringToken-Serial).")
(comment unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocPayerDuring "(#$unitsOfDrugPrescriptionsByDocPayerDuring DOC DRUGTYPE RXFILLTYPE PAYER PERIOD NUM) means that #$Prescriber DOC has had NUM prescriptions of type RXFILLTYPE filled for DRUGTYPE and paid by PAYER during PERIOD.  RXFILLTYPE may be FillingAPrescription-Retail, #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder, #$FillingANewPrescription, #$FillingARefillPrescription, intersections of these, or merely #$FillingAPrescription.")
(disjointWith MathematicalFunctionOnScalars DateDenotingFunction)
(comment ChemicalObject "A specialization of #$MicroscopicScaleObject.  Each instance of #$ChemicalObject is an object whose behavior is typically described in terms of its outer cloud of #$Electrons.  Specializations of #$ChemicalObject include the collections #$Atom, #$Molecule, and #$Ion.")
(disjointWith ElectricalDevice Wagon)
(comment 3DComputerWallpaperFile "A collection of #$ComputerWallpaperFiles.  Each instance of #$3DComputerWallpaperFile represents a three-dimensional  image that is intended to be displayed as the background of the GUI of an #$OperatingSystem like #$MSWindows, or the  background of a web page.")
(comment BacterialProteinType "A type level collection. Each instance is a type of protein found in bacteria.")
(comment Bus-RoadVehicle "A specialization of #$RoadVehicle.  Each instance of #$Bus-RoadVehicle is a ground transportation vehicle designed to carry many  passengers (instances of #$Bus-RoadVehicle typically have capacities ranging from 20 to 80 passengers).  Instances of #$Bus-RoadVehicle are often used as a means of public transportation (see the constant #$PublicTransportationDevice); instances used for public transportation are usually driven by professional drivers.")
(comment Gastrin "Any of several polypeptide #$Hormones secreted by the stomach mucosa. It stimulates the secretion of gastric acid.")
(comment LengthOfListFn "The function #$LengthOfListFn, applied to a list, gives the length of the list, a non-negative integer.  Note that the length of LIST should not in general be considered the same as the cardinality of (#$SetOfListMembersFn LIST).  For example, given that LIST = (#$TheList A B C B D), (#$LengthOfListFn LIST) is 5 while the cardinality of (#$SetOfListMembersFn LIST) is 4.  When LIST is an instance of #$ListWithoutRepetition, nevertheless, the length of LIST is identical to the cardinality of (#$SetOfListMembersFn LIST).")
(disjointWith Elasticity Volatility-Physical)
(comment IncomeTax "The collection of all #$Tax-COCs that are collected on an agent's income.  Instances include #$USIncomeTax as well as income taxes levied by other govenments.")
(comment AdobeClay "The collection of clay from which adobe bricks are made. Much adobe clay is found in the Southwestern United States. #$AdobeClay has a high sand content. See also #$AdobeBrick.")
(comment isATemplateForType "(#$isATemplateForType OBJ TYPE) is true iff OBJ is a prototype or
template for the instances of TYPE. Note that OBJ may but
need not be an instance of TYPE.")
(comment ScriptGraphComplianceMicrotheory "This collection of microtheories contains microtheories that set out rules for interpreting models of script graphs (see #$ScriptGraph) and evaluating alleged instances of these scripts for compliance with this norm.")
(comment Pico "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^-12")
(comment relationMemberInstance "(#$relationMemberInstance PRED GROUP INST) states that for every MEMBER of GROUP the following is true: (PRED MEMBER INST).  This predicate enables one to make claims about the members of a group by referencing only the group itself.")
(comment Camp-Recreational "This is the collection of recreational camps. Some camps

are day camps, where campers come only during the day and go home at night. Most camps

are places in the woods where children come for a period of time, typically in the summer,

and engage in a variety of recreational activities. A number of camps are organized around

training in a particular skill, such as gymnastics, or around education in a certain field.")
(comment acknowledgementOf "(#$acknowledgementOf ACT PIT) means that ACT is an acknowledging act to signify receipt of the abstract information PIT that is being acknowledged and to indicate a response.  The ACT may be an #$Accepting-CommunicationAct or a #$Rejecting-CommunicationAct, or several others.  Some may be combinations, e.g. David may accept part of #$Wanda's order (say the part about cleaning the kitchen) but not the other part (say cleaning the bathroom).  See also #$acknowledgedAct which relates the two acts directly.")
(comment CorrosionResistance "A specialization of #$PhysicalAttribute. Each instance of #$CorrosionResistance is a specific level of resistance to corrosion had by some tangible object.  Degrees of #$CorrosionResistance may be represented using #$GenericValueFunctions.  Indicate a particular object's #$CorrosionResistance with the predicate #$resistanceToCorrosion.")
(comment ChildrensFood "The collection of foods and beverages not only normally eaten by children, but intended to be eaten by children and marketed as such. A salient example is children's breakfast cereal.")
(comment Cornish-Fowl "The breed of #$Chicken known as the Cornish.  The hens are often referred to as 'Cornish hens'.")
(comment ExplanationFn "#$ExplanationFn takes as argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the collection of all #$PropositionalInformationThings that are explanations of that thing.  For example, (#$ExplanationFn #$DemocraticPartyIdeology) returns the collection of explanations of that system of beliefs, and (#$ExplanationFn #$AnaximandersPhilosophy) returns the collection of all explanations of the philosophical views of Anaximander.")
(comment solvent "The predicate #$solvent indicates a particular liquid in a #$Solution in which the #$solute is dissolved.")
(comment ProperNamePredicate-Strict "Elements of #$ProperNamePredicate-Strict are all the lexical predicates that can be used to register the information that a certain STRING is (one of the) name(s) of a certain FORT. This only includes predicates that are used for permanent and thorough lexification. Assertions using predicates that are members of this collection contain all the grammatical information that is necessary to deal with issues such as pluralization. Compare to #$ProperNamePredicate-Loose.")
(comment TakingHostage "The collection of events in which some agent takes a person or persons hostage. This generally involves the agent taking custody of the hostage(s) by force. The hostage-taker often uses the hostage(s)'s safety to bargain for political concessions or, sometimes, for relief from prosecution for some other criminal act.  See also #$HoldingHostages.")
(comment Fugitive "The set of people who are on the run from the law, generally because of past criminal activities, though some outlaws are on the run from the law because they are thought to be criminals even though they may not have actually committed any crimes.  #$Fugitives differ from #$Outlaws, insomuch as #$Fugitives are actively trying to evade the law, while #$Outlaws need not be doing so.")
(comment CiclopiroxOlamine "The chemical compound which is an anti-fungal.")
(comment nearestDifferentGenls "(#$nearestDifferentGenls COL-1 COL-2 NEAR-DIFF) relates collections COL-1 and COL-2 to the nearest unsubsumed collections NEAR-DIFF of which COL-1 is a subset but COL-2 is not. This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it  must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genls heirarchy.  For comparison, see #$nearestDifferentIsa.")
(comment BookOfTheBible "Collection of all the books of the #$Bible.")
(comment importsFromThrough "(#$importsFromThrough REGION1 PRODUCT-TYPE REGION2 PT) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION1 imports significant amounts of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE from the #$GeographicalRegion REGION2 through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT on their way from REGION2.  PT might, in the case of oil imports, for example, be a #$GeographicalRegion or a #$Pipeline.")
(comment doctrinalRulesOfOrganization "(#$doctrinalRulesOfOrganization MILITARYORG FORMULA) means that FORMULA is a doctrinal, standard rule of combat or other action in MILITARYORG. Most often, they are meant as guidelines and goals, not as actual expectations of actions.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization Territory)
(comment TowingARoadVehicle "transportation events where some device (possibly animal?) pulls a wheeled vehicle behind it.")
(comment EstablishingAPhoneLink "The collection of all events in which a link for telephone communication of some kind is established.  Every instance of #$MakingAPhoneCall has at least one instance of #$EstablishingAPhoneLink as a subevent, since this is ordinarily the consequence of making a successful dialing connection to a phone system.  This means that even unsuccessful instances of #$MakingAPhoneCall will have instances of #$EstablishingAPhoneLink as subevents.  See #$MakingAPhoneCall, #$DialingATelephoneNumber.")
(comment atomGrouping "(#$atomGrouping EL N GROUP) relates a kind of #$ElementStuff and the integer N to the collection of groups of atoms of that element that contain exactly N atoms of EL.")
(comment Corolla "A corolla is the flower's second outermost whorl and is composed of petals; it encloses and protects the reproductive organs, and is often conspicuously colored to attract insects.")
(comment SubAtomicParticle "A specialization #$MicroscopicScaleObject and #$InanimateObject-Natural.  Each instance of #$SubAtomicParticle is a physical particle smaller than the smallest atom.  Major subcollections of #$SubAtomicParticle include #$Electron, #$Proton, and #$Neutron.")
(comment interArgIsa3-1 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).   (#$interArgIsa3-1 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that,  when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the third argument to RELN,  a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the first argument  must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then  (RELN ARG1 ARG2 INST ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only  if ARG1 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic  well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment Submarine-Military "The collection of submarines typically used by military organizations.")
(comment IPMasqueradingFault "#$IPMasqueradingFault is an attribute  of some #$LinuxOSes.  IP masquerading is one of the functions performed by the Linux kernel when it is set up on a firewall.  From Bugtraq: \"[IP masquerading] allows you to connect an internal network using private addresses to an external
 network (internet) in a fairly secure manner. All packets coming from
 the internal network and destined for the external network are rewritten
 so the source of those packets is the masquerading gateway's external
 address and the source port is the gateway's source port.  This only
 requires one external IP address to enable internet access for
 hundreds/thousands of internal machines and is therefore a popular
 method for many businesses and home users with broadband connections.\"  A kernel has the #$IPMasqueradingFault when it does not properly validate incoming packets, forwarding the packets when they are not allowed.")
(comment solubleIn "(#$solubleIn SOLUTE SOLVENT) means that the piece of #$PartiallyTangible stuff SOLUTE will ordinarily dissolve if placed into the #$LiquidTangibleThing SOLVENT.  See also #$Solubility.")
(comment VulnerableToOSCrashing "#$VulnerableToOSCrashing is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer. A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a program on a port, and that program crashes the entire
 computer in response to invalid input.")
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice Destroyer)
(comment PresentFn "(#$PresentFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-TIME) denotes the

         subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances temporally include CONTEXT-TIME.")
(comment Explaining-CommunicationAct "A specialized collection of communication acts.  In each instance of #$Explaining-CommunicationAct, some agent explains something to some other agent(s).  The information given in an act of explaining is an instance of #$Explanation.")
(disjointWith CaucasusCountry LevantCountry)
(disjointWith Bronchiole LobarBronchus)
(comment Hacker-Insider "#$Hacker-Insider is the subcollection of #$Hacker referring to those instances of #$Hacker who hack an instance of #$ComputationalSystem from inside the company or agency that is the proprietor of that system.  An insider is usually an employee of the targeted organization.")
(comment ComputerIndustry "A specialization of Industry-Localized.  Each instance of #$ComputerIndustry is a group of manufacturers and/or

entrepreneurs whose output is related in some way to the functionality

of computers.  This collection includes as instances groups which manufacture the hardware components used by computers, groups which assemble these

components into computers, groups which write computer software, and

groups which perform all three of these functions, or some subset

thereof.")
(comment Swinger "A denizen of the party-world who 'swings' in bars and 
night-clubs and casinos. Similar to the idea of #$Playboy, but a 
#$PersonTypeByActivity only from a social-activities perspective. 
While a #$Playboy often is a full-time party-goer and reveller, instances of
 #$Swinger usually have to support themselves with a non-partying #$JobFn. 
 Also, the term #$Swinger is gender-neutral.")
(comment BladderInfection "A collection of infections. Instances of #$BladderInfection are infections by bacteria that cause urination to be painful.  See #$UrinaryTractInfection.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType ControllableAutonomousActionType)
(comment TourOfRegionTypeFn "(#$TourOfRegionTypeFn COL) is the collection of 

#$TravelTours of instances of COL.  So for example (#$TourOfRegionFn #$City) is the collection of tours of cities.")
(comment Mendelevium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Mendelevium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment organizerOfEvent "(#$organizerOfEvent EVENT AGENT) means   that AGENT is the chief organizer of    EVENT.")
(disjointWith PrecipitationParticle Sawdust)
(comment StructureMicrotheory "#$StructureMicrotheory is a class of microtheories each of which defines the prototypical structure of some type of complex object.  For example, the #$HumanBodyStructureMt contains assertions that define the structure of the prototypical human body.  You can think of this kind of microtheory as a basic template.")
(comment GeneTherapy "This is a kind of therapy especially aimed at genetic

diseases wherein the genomes within cells are altered, usually by employing a virus

to emplant new genetic material.")
(comment performancesOfWorkAre "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$DevisedPracticeOrWork to specializations of #$Event.  (#$performancesOfWorkAre WORK EVENT_TYPE) means that every performance of WORK is an instance of EVENT_TYPE.  For example, (#$performancesOfWorkAre RadioCommercial001 #$RadioCommercial-IBT) means that every performance of the abstract work denoted by RadioCommercial001 is an instance of #$RadioCommercial-IBT.")
(comment ObstructionEvent "The collection of events in which an area that would otherwise be passable by someone or something is rendered unpassable with respect to that someone or thing.")
(comment KiloClassSubmarine "A kind of #$Submarine, manufactured in #$Russia.  As of April of 1998, #$Iran is known to have purchased several.")
(comment Preposition-Directional-Atelic "Prepositions which denote direction, and generally modify events in which the destination is not reached; for example, 'towards'.")
(comment eventPred "This predicate is used to construct 'non-Davidsonian'

representations of actions and events, which are of the form WALKS(Mary,

Marys-Home). In the usual 'Davidsonian' style, this would be expressed as 'there is

an event X such that X is a #$Walking-Generic, etc.'. Notice that, unlike

its Davidsonian counterpart, it makes sense to say that WALKS(Mary,

Marys-Home) is true at some times -- namely when Mary *is walking* home --

but not at others -- e.g., after she has arrived. The problem is that we

don't have such predicates as WALKS in Cyc. #$eventPred is intended to fill

this gap in a general and simple way, and without introducing a lot of

redundant duplication. Suppose EVTYPE is a subcollection of #$Event, LIST1

is a n-ary list of the form SLOT01 ... SLOT0n, where each element is an

instance of #$ActorSlot, and LIST2 is a n-ary list of things satisfying the

#$arg2Isa constraint on their respective actor slot. Then (#$eventPred

EVTYPE LIST1 LIST2) is true at a time t iff t if the 1st element of LIST2

is playing role SLOT01 in an event of type EVTYPE, the 2nd element of LIST2

is playing role SLOT02, and so on. Consider the example above: we can form

(#$eventPred #$Walking-Generic (#$TheList #$performedBy #$toLocation)

(#$TheList MARY HOME)) to represent the clause WALKS(Mary, Home) as

described in the example. The meaning of this #$ELSentence-Assertible is expressed by

the sentence 'Mary is walking home'.")
(comment FullTextOfIBTFn "#$FullTextOfIBTFn takes as argument any instance of #$InformationBearingThing and returns the collection of #$PropositionalCWTexts of that thing, including texts in different encodings (ASCII vs. EBCIDIC), computer files [#$ComputerFile-CW] of the words, and the words themselves [#$WordsToPCW].  For example, (#$FullTextOfIBTFn MartinLutherKingsSpeechAtTheLincolnMemorial) returns the collection of #$PropositionalCWTexts of the \"I Have a Dream Speech\".")
(comment suspendingFluid "The predicate #$suspendingFluid indicates the particular fluid in which particles are suspended in a particular instance of #$Suspension.  Thus, (#$suspendingFluid SUS FLU) means that FLU is among the #$constituents of the #$Suspension SUS, FLU is a fluid (i.e., liquid OR gas), and FLU is the fluid constituent which suspends the particles in SUS.  For example, in an instance of #$CloudlikeObject, the #$suspendingFluid is the portion of #$Air that is surrounding and supporting the droplets of water vapour in the cloud.  In muddy water, the #$suspendingFluid is that instance of #$Water which is supporting the particles of soil.")
(comment StrategicInterest "An attribute characterizing goals that are crucial interests of organized bodies of people, and that are regarded as such by the bodies themselves.  Some examples of bodies having goals to which the attribute #$StrategicInterest applies are businesses, labor unions, political parties, countries, and international institutions.  (However, in assertions about countries, it is preferable to use the more specific attribute #$StrategicNationalInterest.)")
(comment Firmicutes-Division "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalDivision within the $#$MoneraKingdom, the #$Firmicutes-Division are #$ProkaryoticCells with a thick and strong cell wall, such as #$Streptococcus.  These cells are #$GramPositiveBacterium, with a few exceptions.")
(comment TwoPersonGame "The collection of all #$NonTeamGames typically played by two people.")
(comment BallisticMissile-SCUDC "A short range ballistic missile produced in North Korea.")
(comment Injecting-Intravenous "Injecting a fluid, usually containing a drug, into a vein.")
(comment resourceProcessor-FunctionalRole "(#$resourceProcessor-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means

that AGENT is expected to execute some kind of processing function

with respect to some form of matter or energy that is a

resource with respect to SYSTEM.  This can involve ingestion of raw

material from which resources can be made, production of resources

from raw materials, distribution of resources, consumption of

resources, extrusion of waste material that is a byproduct of the

production of resources, and other things besides.")
(comment ASCII-Art "The fine art of drawing diagrams using the #$ASCII character set            (mainly `|', `-', `/', `', and `+'). Also known as `character            graphics' or `ASCII graphics'.")
(comment HeaderChecksumField-Packet "A #$HeaderChecksumField-Packet indicates the
checksum of only the #$Header-Packet of the #$Packet-Internet.
The checksum is used to ensure that the #$Header-Packet
was not corrupted en route to the destination.")
(comment paAnsweredQuestion "Predicate used to state that a question has been answered by a user of

the #$ProductAdvisorApplication.  (#$paAnsweredQuestion FORMULA SET)  means that a question which

attempted to determine the truth of FORMULA has been answered, where SET was the set of possible answers from which the

user could have selected.  (If the question was not multiple choice, then SET should be empty.)")
(comment Turtle "The collection of all turtles; a subset of #$Reptile.  Elements of #$Turtle are toothless reptiles with hard or else leathery enclosing shells.  Turtles may live on land or in fresh or salt water.  #$Turtle constitutes an instance of #$BiologicalOrder (also called Testudinata), which is of the #$BiologicalClass #$Reptile.")
(comment IndexicalConcept "#$IndexicalConcepts are those  whose referent essentially depends on the occasion of use and  the user, e.g., #$Now, I, Here. When I use the word 'I,' I  am referring to myself (#$OKeefe), but 'I' does not mean  #$OKeefe, but refers to whomever the user is. Similarly, #$Now denotes the moment in which it is used.")
(disjointWith TimeInterval CulturalThing)
(comment DigestionEvent "A specialization of #$BiologicalDecompositionEvent and #$TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure.  Each instance of #$DigestionEvent is a process in which a single animal converts food into substances that can be assimilated by the body.  This collection should not be confused with #$DigestingInStomach, each instance of which occurs only in an instance of #$Stomach; an instance of #$DigestionEvent spans the whole #$DigestiveSystem, from start to finish.")
(comment MissileWatercraft-Surface "The collection of military surface ships which are armed with missiles.")
(comment ConstructionSite "The collection of all places where construction artifacts are in the process of being constructed.  If the place has only finished artifacts in/on it, then it is no longer a construction site.")
(comment BaseballPitch-Fastball "The collection of all baseball pitching events in which the ball is thrown especially hard and fast.  In major league baseball, a fastball will typically reach speeds of over 70 miles/hour.")
(comment increasesVulnerabilityIn "(#$increasesVulnerabilityIn SITUATION OBJECT RESULT-TYPE) means that being in situation SITUATION increases OBJECT's vulnerability to RESULT-TYPE.  This predicate is similar to #$makesVulnerableToDegree except that, unlike #$makesVulnerableToDegree, it expresses a relative increase in OBJECT's vulnerability rather than an absolute degree of vulnerability.  It also resembles #$vulnerableIn, but there is an important difference that must be observed, namely that when using #$increasesVulnerabilityIn one assumes that certain conditions coming into effect increase vulnerability.  Therefore, it should not be used to declare vulnerabilities outright; Cyc should have to conclude that a situation increases an object's vulnerability to some result.")
(comment GenitalHerpes "A sexually transmittable disease which causes blisters on the sexual organs and has no cure.")
(comment vehicleLinearSpeedOnTerrain "(#$vehicleLinearSpeedOnTerrain VEHICLETYPE REGIONTYPE
SPEED) means that the typical speed of an instance of vehicletype
driving in a straight line course across an instance of REGIONTYPE is SPEED.")
(disjointWith KidsChatRoom GayMaleChatRoom)
(comment MilitarySpacecraft "The collection of #$Spacecraft intended to be used in a military context.")
(comment InverterLoop "A primitive type of two-phase-clocked electrical device that can store one bit of information.")
(comment RotationAxisPerpendicularToDirectionOfMotion "Axis of rotation is perpendicular to direction of travel.  Rolling, discus / Frisbee (tm) flying, and the cutting motion of rotary cutters fall in this category.  If the direction of travel is straight, the motion of each point of the object remains in a plane.")
(comment PointTrickCardGame "The subcollection of all #$TrickTakingCardGames in which the value of the trick does depend on what cards it contains.  Point trick games are so called because the cards have point values, and the result is determined not by the number of tricks taken, but by the total point value of the cards taken.  #$Tarot-CardGame is an example of a #$PointTrickCardGame.")
(comment MassReplication "This is the collection of events in which a single IBT is
copied many times.")
(comment actionSequence "(#$actionSequence (#$TheList FORM_1 FORM_2 ... FORM_n)) means that the actions described by the action formulas FORM_i were performed in the order indicated.  Each FORM_i should be an atomic formula whose predicate is an instance of #$ActionPredicate.")
(disjointWith CreditManager Minister-Governmental)
(disjointWith SeparationEvent EmittingAWave)
(comment InfectingFn "This function denotes the collection of events in which diseases

of a certain type are transmitted.  For instance, (#$InfectingFn

#$ChickenPox) denotes the collection of events in which the chickenpox virus

is transmitted from one biological living object to another.")
(disjointWith Surgery (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(comment Thimble "The collection of all #$Thimbles.  #$Thimbles are used during #$SewingByHand in order to protect the doer's fingers from the #$SewingNeedle-Hand.  Some people also collect #$Thimbles as a hobby.")
(comment Bicycle "#$Bicycle is a specialization of #$WheeledTransportationDevice, #$MountableTransporter, #$Device-UserPowered, and #$Device-UserControlled.  Each instance of #$Bicycle is a personal wheeled transport device powered by human peddling.   Most bicycles have two main wheels arranged in-line, but some tandem bicycles have more than two wheels.")
(comment LineOfObjects "The #$groupMembers of #$LineOfObjects are arranged such that #$inFrontOf-Directly applies  of one another.  The current (May 96) default is that the objects in the line, are in it for the duration of the existence of the #$LineOfObjects.  If the line is #$Straight then all objects in the line are either in front of or in back of one another.")
(comment NewAgePsychologicalTherapy "This is a loose grouping of practices which make some claim to

therapeutic benefit and are in some way alligned with views which are popularly

characterized as New Age. These may or may not be associated with something

that would appropriately be called a #$FieldOfStudy.")
(comment to-UnderspecifiedLocation "(#$to-UnderspecifiedLocation TRAJ TOLOC) states that an

abstract locational relation holds between TRAJ and TOLOC, where

TOLOC is an abstract destination.

#$to-UnderspecifiedLocation is an underspecified semantic representation

that may be elaborated to represent either a spatial example of destination (as captured by #$to-Generic and its specific forms)

or a temporal use of destinations ('from june to august' etc.) or

metaphorical destination ('road to happiness', etc.)")
(comment HeavyMetalMusic "An especially loud specialization of #$RockMusic.  #$HeavyMetalMusic features

  lenthy guitar solos, heavy  bass lines, and propulsive drumming.  Arguably, it began in 

  early seventies, but it had its Renaissance and heyday from the late 1980s to the

  mid 1990s.  Influential practitioners of this style include Black Sabbath, Motorhead,

  Metallica, and Megadeth.")
(comment TurningOffEngine "The turning off/stopping of an engine.")
(comment AdenosineTriphosphate "The collection of nucleotides created by some

#$Cells.  When a cell needs energy, it is converted from a storage

molecule, such as a #$CarbohydrateStuff, or from environmental energy

into #$AdenosineTriphosphate which is then used to power activites

in the cell.")
(comment ArrivingAtAPlace "A physical transfer in which the performer moves to a location other than that from which she started. See also #$LeavingAPlace.")
(comment countryCanProduceObject "(#$countryCanProduceObject COUNTRY OBJTYPE) means that the government of the #$IndependentCountry COUNTRY can play the role of #$directingAgent in instances of #$ProductionEvent whose outputs are objects of type OBJTYPE.")
(comment HumanSexualBehavior "The set of events in which instances of #$Person are engaged in #$SexualBehavior.")
(disjointWith ChemicalObject SubAtomicParticle)
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink Archery)
(comment SecureMailGuard "A spec of #$SecurityDevice that allows mail to be transferred electronically between the non-classified internet protocol router network (NIPRNET) (see #$NIPRNet-PathSystem) and the secret internet protocol router network (SIPRNET) (see #$SIPRNet-PathSystem). It is designed to allow Coalition users (who do not have access to SIPRNET) to exchange mail with American users (who do have access to SIPRNET) without allowing the Coalition users access to SIPRNET. The mail guard works by examining transmitted data and allowing only that in the right format to be released. It also may do security checks, word checks to look for sensitive information that should not be allowed through, and it supports content scanning, downgrade, releasability review, regrade, and sanitization.")
(comment OverrideTrojanHorse "This is a spec of #$TrojanHorseComputerProgram.  It includes instances of trojan
    horses which are called instead of some other program by the simple expedient of
    having the same name and being higher in the execution path.")
(comment HighEnduranceCutter "A collection. Military high-endurance cutter ships.")
(comment RibonucleotideBonding "A collection of events in which #$Ribonucleotides are  linked by #$PhosphodiesterBonds to form a RNA #$PolynucleotideStrand. The reaction is catalyzed by #$RNAPolymerase.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat MicrotheoryType)
(comment ArcCosecantFn "(#$ArcCosecantFn COS) yields the angle whose cosecant is COS.")
(disjointWith FourWayJunctionOfPaths ThreeWayJunctionOfPaths)
(comment perceivedThings "(#$perceivedThings PERCEPTION TANGIBLE) means that the perceiver in a #$Perceiving event PERCEPTION has some perception of (awareness of, gaining information about) some sensorially detectable event or object TANGIBLE. E.g., if you are on the sidewalk and witness a car crash, the impacting event itself is almost sure to be a #$perceivedThings, as is the car.  Whereas the blinking of one car's right turn signal, the crossing of one drivers' arms in front of their face, the right foot of the driver of the car, etc. might very well not be #$perceivedThings by the doer of PERCEPTION.  Note: we would not use this predicate to refer to `Cameron perceived the apprehension in the air when he walked in the door', as apprehension is not even partially tangible or readily available to our basic senses.  Some #$perceivedThings, e.g. the red spot on jupiter seen while glancing in a telescope, might last longer than their perception events.  Other #$perceivedThings, e.g. the flash of an explosion seen while watching a movie might last shorter than the entire perception event.")
(comment Sulfur "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of sulfur; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form -- but not necessarily.")
(comment MineField-AntiTank "Collection of instances of #$MineField designed to impede the progress of mechanized or tracked units.")
(disjointWith TemporalThing GeneticInformation)
(comment OfficialDocumentByAgentFn "This collection allows one to reify types of #$OfficialDocuments issued by a particular agent.  For example, #$Passports issued by the UnitedStates or #$CertificateOfDeposit issued by Bank One.")
(comment ThoughtExperimenting "This is the collection of instances in which a person does a thought experiment. Carrying out a thought experiment is a technique employed extensively in philosophy but also notably

in relativistic physics and quantum mechanics. The idea is to achieve insight by

imagining a particular sort of scenario and then trying to figure out what would

or should happen or how the scenario should be evaluated. A philosophical example is the Experience

Machine: would a life in which all of your apparent experiences were simulated by

a computer hooked up to your brain be as good as one in which you have the same experiences

in the normal way? If not, then hedonism, the theory that the only intrinsically valuable thing is pleasure, is incorrect. Note that there need not

be a prior conceptual work of which such an activity is an instantiation. Thought experiments can be improvised.")
(disjointWith Thinking ChemicalReaction)
(comment DirectionFindingRadioUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile is to locate the source of           radio communications.")
(comment Ayahuasca "A hallucinogenic beverage produced in the western #$AmazonRiver basin ceremoniously used by shamans.")
(comment feelingTypeExperienced "#$feelingTypeExperienced is a binary role predicate relating emotional experiences (see #$ExperiencingEmotion) to the type of feeling experienced (i.e. a spec of #$FeelingAttribute).  Often just one kind of emotion is experienced during any emotional experience.  Nonetheless multiple values on #$feelingTypeExperienced are possible in experiences of mixed emotion.  Note that predicates such as #$feelsEmotion, #$feelsTowardsEvent and others should be used in preference to this predicate.  This is because #$feelingTypeExperienced requires a term to be skolemized referring to the instance of experiencing that particular emotion whereas the other predicates do not.")
(comment Tournament "Elements are #$Competitions comprised of a number of individual #$Competitions in which competitors compete against each other. Instances of #$Tournament may be instances or #$ChampionshipCompetition or #$QualifyingTrial.")
(comment Nintendo64Game "The collection of video games and versions of such that are made to run specifically on a #$Nintendo64-TheProduct platform (or are emulations of such).")
(comment VietnamMemorial "The collection of all monuments which commemorate the #$Vietnam War.  The most famous such marker is a dramatic black slab in Washington DC")
(comment AnimeMovie "A subset of #$AnimatedMovie and a subset of #$Anime.  This is the collection of all #$Movie-CWs that use the #$Anime style.  See #$Anime for a more in-depth explanation of what anime means.")
(comment GridStreetSystem "A specialization of #$StreetSystem instances of 
which are systems consisting of (at least nearly) straight 
streets arranged in a grid-like pattern, wherein any two 
streets are (at least nearly) either parallel or perpendicular 
to each other.  It is not necessary that each street in a 
grid system intersect with every street in the system that 
is perpendicular to it.")
(comment ParabolicTrajectory "A parabolic trajectory")
(comment ExpressingFriendship "The collection of events where one agent formally express friendship for another.  This can range from one countries declaration of 'Friendly Status' for another or simply a person stating that another person is a friend.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDay PolarNight)
(comment SocialServicesEconomicSector "The collection of all localized groups of enterprises (including government enterprises) in which each such group consists of members that are primarily engaged in providing social services, and in which the group forms the major social services sector for that region.")
(comment NaturalRegion "A region which is in a natural state, not obviously affected by the activities of humankind - there are no or very minimal human structures present, and the land is not used for agriculture, mining, or other human activities which disrupt the natural plants and wildlife.")
(comment programCopyOfProcess "(#$programCopyOfProcess PROC COPY) means that COPY is the unique #$ComputerProgramCopy directly associated with PROC.  Examples: COPY was loaded from disk and is executing in memory as PROC, or COPY is the region of memory that is the 'code segment' (as opposed to the 'data segment') for PROC.")
(comment nearRelativeTo "(#$nearRelativeTo SIDE OBJ) means that SIDE is the nearer of two or more objects, or the nearer of two or more parts of a relevant object, relative to OBJ.  See also #$farRelativeTo.  Created for the Battlespace Workarounds effort.")
(comment interArgReln3-1 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln3-1 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the third and first arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 arg3 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG3 ARG1) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.  Use #$interArgReln-Inferred to conclude that (BINPRED ARG3 ARG1) holds.")
(comment Dronabinol "The chemical compound which is an anti-emetic.  It is often used with cancer patients undergoing chemotherapy.  It's synthetic THC.")
(comment defaultSpecializedType "(#$defaultSpecializedType GENERAL SPECIF) means that, in the current context and application, the default (most normal or typical) instances of the collection GENERAL are likely to be member of its intersection with the the Collection SPECIF (which my or may not be a subclass of GENERAL).   This is not a new logical construct (for any kind of default logic); rather it is to be used as a heuristic guide in specific applications.  If no other information about an individual is known other than that it is an instance of GENERAL, then assume tentatively that it is an instance of SPECIF.")
(comment NonMalleable "not at all malleable")
(comment Broadcasting "A collection of #$Events; a subset of #$MediaTransmitting.  In every #$Broadcasting event, an #$InformationBearingWavePropagation is converted into radio signals, which are transmitted by a #$BroadcastAntenna and received by a #$ReceivingAntenna.  Subsets of #$Broadcasting are #$RadioBroadcasting and #$TVBroadcasting.")
(comment FreeMarketEconomicSystem "A collection of #$EconomicSystems which feature private ownership of the means of production, and the utilization of markets to set prices and wages.")
(comment reproducer-FunctionalRole "(#$reproducer-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that AGENT is expected to

be capable of producing a new #$FunctionalSystem that has the same

functional organization and environmental role as SYSTEM.")
(comment MediumHelicopterUnit-MilitarySpecialty "Specialization of moderately armed helicopter units.")
(comment Terminal-TransferPoint "The collection of #$ConstructionArtifacts whose #$primaryFunction is to provide for a #$ChangeOfConveyance of goods or people.  Examples include: a #$PortFacility where cargo is loaded and unloaded from ships, an airport terminal where people are changing planes or changing from planes to other forms of transportation.  Negative examples include bus stops, where most people probably just walk to the bus (though some transit centers may be marginal positive examples).  A borderline case is subway stations where two or more lines meet; many passengers may be changing from one conveyance to another but many may just be walking there")
(comment taxRate "The predicate used to specify the tax rate that someone has to pay for a certain kind of tax.  (#$taxRate BEING TAX RATE) means that for #$TaxType TAX, BEING SocialBeing pays the tax rate RATE.")
(comment Aril "An outgrowth of the funiculus which some seeds have.")
(comment BradleyFightingVehicle-M3 "A model of #$BradleyFightingVehicle used by scouts and  designed to carry more TOW missiles than the model #$BradleyFightingVehicle-M2.")
(disjointWith AstronomicalObject Mineral)
(comment TelecommunicationsIndustry "The collection of all telecommunications industries: 

each member of this collection           

is a #$Group of #$Organizations 

(an instance of #$Industry-Localized)           

each #$groupMembers of which is in the business of telecommunication services.")
(comment Project "An organized endeavor with a set goal")
(comment connectedAlongLength "(#$connectedAlongLength OBJ1 OBJ2) means that #$LongAndThin OBJ1 is #$connectedTo OBJ2 along all, or almost all, of their mutual lengths.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByCarbonSource "A collection of collections that divides #$Bacterium into two main types based on their carbon sources, see #$Autotroph-Bacterium and #$Heterotroph-Bacterium.")
(comment Amir-HeadOfState "The collection of all Amirs (Emirs) of countries or emirates.  Amir is an islamic title of nobility.")
(comment FuturesOptionsTrading "buying an object, where the object(s) bought is(are) #$CommoditiesFuture(s) and/or #$OptionTransactionAgreement(s).")
(comment completeTextOfWork "(#$completeTextOfWork WORK TEXT) means that TEXT is the full text of the #$PropositionalConceptualWork WORK.")
(comment CommuteDrive "The collection of events in which one person or more commutes to work by            driving rather than taking a subway or bus.             This includes those commutes in which a #$Carpool is used.")
(comment GrowthChart "The collection of all growth charts.  A #$GrowthChart is a chart that has markings for different heights.  They are often hung in a child's bedroom or a #$Nursery-BabysRoom.  Children, with the help of their parents or guardians, use these charts to track their growth.")
(comment interArg2ResultIsa "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$isa based relationship holds between the second argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg2ResultIsa FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the second argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL. Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg2ResultIsa _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary  #$interArgResultIsa.")
(comment Scurvy "A condition arising from having a vitamin C deficiency.")
(disjointWith SimplifyForward NoSimplerArgument)
(comment lengthOfRecording "A predicate relating a #$RecordingOfWaveIBT to the length of the recording.  Does not specify the #$duration of the object (when it did or did not exist), but rather the #$Time-Quantity necessary to replay the recording at its intended playback speed.")
(comment mtQueryingConstraint "(#$mtQueryingConstraint MT PROP) means that the constraints specified in PROP must be satisfied in order for assertions that occur in MT to be used to answer a query, whether from a user, from an application, or via the inference engine.")
(comment SexualAssault "The collection of #$SexualOffenses in which somebody sexually assaults somebody else.")
(disjointWith AircraftHangar RailroadStation)
(comment permanentlyNorthOf "(#$permanentlyNorthOf NORTH SOUTH) means that the #$GeographicalThing NORTH is situated to the north of the #$GeographicalThing SOUTH, when viewed in a planetary frame of reference, typically the terrestrial frame of reference.  To compare the position of two objects, at least one of which is mobile or is an instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized but not of #$GeographicalThing, use the more general, #$northOf.  Note that SOUTH is therefore south of NORTH; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `south of'.  Example: (#$permanentlyNorthOf #$CityOfPhiladelphiaPA #$CityOfWashingtonDC); (#$permanentlyNorthOf #$35thParallel-North #$37thParallel-North).  See also #$permanentlyEastOf and #$directionBetweenObjects.  To say '(permanentlySouthOf x y)' all we need is to say (#$permanentlyNorthOf y x).  See also #$fartherNorthThan.")
(comment Pistachio-TheNut "The collection of the fruit of the #$PistachioTree.  Pistachio nuts are a valuable food commodity and are produced in southern Europe, northern Africa and the Middle East.")
(comment TheInstance "#$TheInstance is the instance sibling to #$TheSpec and used for NL Parsing instead of the ambiguous #$The. Thus, (#$TheInstance COL) represents an instance of the collection COL.")
(comment SportsSock "The collection of socks worn with AthleticShoes.  TubeSocks, for example.")
(comment SA6Missile "A type of surface-to-air missile.")
(comment Mercury "A piece of mercury; this is usually a liquid, at least here on Earth.")
(comment CollegeSportsTeam "The collection of #$SportsTeams that are affiliated with colleges or universities. College sports are generally subject to NCAA rules. College teams usually belong to a particular conference or division, such as the Big 12 Conference for college football.")
(comment ReligiousBeliefs "The collection of all religions or equivalent sets of beliefs that answer the `big questions' about creation, existence, etc.  Some instances of this are: #$AnimistReligion, #$Catholicism, #$Buddhism, etc.")
(comment projectSharedNoteToInstances "(#$projectSharedNoteToInstances NOTE COL) means that the
#$SharedNote NOTE should be attached to all instances of COL via the
predicate #$sharedNotes.")
(comment principal "The predicate used to relate an #$Agreement, such as a #$LoanAgreement or a #$Bond, to the amount originally invested by the #$creditor or the purchaser (the investor).")
(comment ArmedForcesFn "(#$ArmedForcesFn GEOPOLITICALENTITY) denotes the  armed forces of  GEOPOLITICALENTITY. This entity is usually a country,  but could be a smaller unit belonging to a political unit not thought of as  a country. For example, the Duke of Atholl presently (1999) has, what one  might refer to as, a standing army. Also, Vatican City has a Swiss guard,  which might be thought of as an army, and Vatican City is not universally  recognized as an independent country. The armed forces of a country  comprises all military organizations. This includes the navy, the infantry, the air force and the military intelligence agency.")
(comment MinorLeague "A collection of organizations.  An element of #$MinorLeague is a professional #$SportsLeague that is not part of [#$subOrganizations] any larger #$SportsLeague and is ranked lower than a #$MajorLeague in the same sport.")
(comment nonThirdSg-Present "This predicate is a generalization over the #$SpeechPartPredicates for present tense active-voice verbs that are not third-person. For the vast majority of English verbs, this is morphologically identical to the #$infinitive form.")
(comment returnOnEquity "(returnOnEquity ORG AMOUNT) means that AMOUNT was return earned on the invested capital in ORG.  The invested capital can be determined by looking for an assertion of the form (#$equity-Financial ORG EQUITY-AMOUNT) in a microtheory that has the same #$holdsIn assumptions as the #$returnOnEquity assertion.  Return on equity for some time period is calculated as net income divided by equity.")
(comment ConductingMedium "An instance of #$ExistingStuffType, and a specialization of #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$ConductingMedium is a partially tangible object that can serve as a conductor, e.g., for heat or electricity.  Specializations include #$PowerLine, #$Superconductor, and #$ElectricalWire.")
(comment interArgReln4-2 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln4-2 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the fourth and second arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG4 ARG2) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(comment StereotypicalBlondeAdultFemale "The main stereotype about instances of the collection #$StereotypicalBlondeAdultFemale is that they            are very unintelligent.")
(comment Acrobat "An #$Acrobat is someone who entertains people by doing            difficult physical actions such as walking on their hands           or balancing on a high rope, especially at a #$Circus.")
(comment ActorInMusicals "The collection of people whose job it is to sing, act, and dance in Broadway-type musicals.")
(comment ExpellingFromStatus "A collection of #$ChangeOfStatusEvents: in each instance of

#$ExpellingFromStatus, a person, group, or organization is expelled

from a status that it had previously, so that the agent in question

has the status before the expelling event and lacks the status after

the event is over.  An expulsion from status is ordinarily considered

to have 'permanent' effect.")
(comment capabilityEnablesCapability "(#$capabilityEnablesCapability SE SIT-TYPE1 ROLE1 SIT-TYPE2 ROLE2) means that SE's ability to play the role ROLE1 in situations of SIT-TYPE2 enables SE to play the role ROLE2 in situations of type SIT-TYPE2.")
(comment EnglishMuffin "A type of flat muffin baked on a griddle, and reputedly eaten by #$EnglishPersons.")
(comment CharacterStringToken-ElectroMagnetic "A specialization of both #$CharacterStringToken and 

  #$ElectroMagneticIBT each of whose instances 

  represents or realizes a particular abstract instance of 

  #$CharacterString in some language, writing system, or encoding 

  scheme.  Most electromagnetic character-string tokens are (not 

  necessarily spatially contiguous) physical series of electromagnetic 

  character tokens (see #$CharacterToken-ElectroMagnetic and 

  #$CharacterStringToken-Serial).  An electromagnetic string token 

  can literally be stored (e.g. in a computer's memory or on a 

  floppy disk) and transmitted (e.g. via wires or as radio signals) 

  using certain electronic devices.")
(comment FemaleProfessionalWrestlingEvent "A collection of #$ProfessionalWrestlingEvents involving  female wrestlers.")
(comment SupportGroupFn-Demographic "#$SupportGroupFn-Demographic takes as argument any instance TYPE of #$HumanCultureType and returns the collection of all support groups for persons who are members of TYPE.  For example, (#$SupportGroupFn-Demographic #$LesbianPerson) denotes the collection of all support groups for persons whose sexual orientation is lesbian.")
(disjointWith Automobile TruckTractor)
(comment Estrone "An #$Estrogen produced in the #$Ovary-AnimalBodyPart. Found in the #$Urine of pregnant females. May also be prepared synthetically. #$Estrone is not as active as #$Estradiol.")
(comment TheEmptyList "An instance of #$ListWithoutRepetition. #$TheEmptyList is a list that has no members (see #$listMembers).  Note that any list that has no members is identical with #$TheEmptyList; thus #$TheEmptyList is the only list whose length is 0.  Note also that #$TheEmptyList is a sublist (see #$subLists) of every list.  Note finally that #$TheEmptyList is not the same as #$TheEmptySet (q.v.).")
(disjointWith Elasticity Voltage)
(comment bayesParent "A predicate used for probability statements.  (#$bayesParent BAYES-VARIABLE1 BAYES-VARIABLE2 BAYESNET) means that the #$BayesDiscreteOutcome associated with BAYES-VARIABLE2 influences the #$BayesDiscreteOutcome associated with BAYES-VARIABLE1, and that BAYES-VARIABLE2 is an immediate 'parent node' of the BAYES-VARIABLE1 node in the Bayesian Network BAYESNET representing probabilistic influence in the applicable #$Microtheory.  That is, the second bayes variable is a direct parent of the first in the #$BayesNet.   Note that BAYES-VARIABLE1/outcome and BAYES-VARIABLE2/outcome cannot be #$conditionallyIndependent in the #$Microtheory if one is a #$bayesParent of the other.  Given the outcomes of all of a node's #$bayesParent nodes, then all of its further ancestor nodes and other non-descendant nodes are #$conditionallyIndependent of it in the applicable #$Microtheory.  To relate a node to the set of all of its parent nodes, use #$bayesParentSet.   The direction is obtained from the conditional dependence --- given the outcome of a node --- among its #$bayesParents (the 'explaining away' effect), which does not seem to apply among its Bayesian 'child' nodes.  Many Bayesian network theorists consider that the directions on the links correspond to the direction of causal influence, and hence to the direction of time. ")
(comment groupCohesion "(#$groupCohesion GROUP DEGREE) indicates that the members of the group GROUP have the degree DEGREE of loyalty to          GROUP.  Group loyalty may be based on a variety of motives.             For example, in a business the degree of #$groupCohesion may depend             upon the extent to which its employees desire the             success of the business.  In a military organization #$groupCohesion may depend              upon the extent to which its members believe in the purpose or purposes for             which the organization exists.  In a criminal organization it may depend             upon how much the members can benefit from the success of the organization's             endeavors.  Note that a particular degree of #$groupCohesion             does not imply any degree of loyalty between members of the group on an             individual level.  For example, a criminal organization may have a high degree             of #$groupCohesion but this does not imply that any one member will be loyal to             other members where the success or well-being of the organization is not             at stake. See also #$Loyalty-Status.")
(comment ThunderstormAsObject "A rainstorm with lightning.")
(comment Yaw-Orientational "Turning along an intrinsic bottom-to-top side axis.  This is normally a rotation about a vertical axis.")
(comment SubeventSequenceGraphMicrotheory "A collection of microtheories.  Each microtheory of this type gives information concerning a graph, GRAPH, that is purported to represent the sequencing rules for instances of some script type, SCRIPTTYPE.  i.e., (#$relationInstanceAll #$graphRepresents GRAPH SCRIPTTYPE).  If MT is an instance of #$SubeventSequenceGraphMicrotheory then it should define the graph(#$PathSystem), state all the nodes (#$nodeInSystem), each of which should be script-types and state links between the nodes which represent script types, instances of which may or could be in a #$followsInProgression relationship during the instances of the SCRIPTTYPE that is being constrained (if we are focussing mainly on the temporal ordering of the subevents).  For instance, suppose we define a car safety checking script type (SimpleCarSafetyCheck) and want to define the sequence of events which must occur in any such event.  Suppose that the first step is to check the tires (TireCheck, a kind of event), the second step is to check fluid levels (FluidLevelCheck, a kind of event), the third and final is to check the brakes (BrakeCheck, a kind of event).  We define a path system (e.g., #$DirectedMultigraph) and assert that it represents (see #$graphRepresents or #$graphRepresentsType) all instances of SimpleCarSafetyCheck.  It should also be asserted that the last required event-type is a sink node (#$sinkNodeInSystem) We assert that TireCheck, BrakeCheck, and FluidLevelCheck are all nodes in the path system, CarSafetyCheckGraph and create instances of #$Path-Simple to link the event-types instances of which will be in a #$followsInProgression relation and then use #$linkFromToInSystem to articulate the links.  Note that this becomes more complicated in cases in which the type of event that precedes an event has implications for the type of event that should follow.  For instance, in a gas buying event, if one pays after getting out of the car one should pump after paying.  However, if one pays after closing the tank one should get into the car after paying.  In those cases we need to use #$weightOfLink.  If a link between two nodes is n and we want events of type EVENTTYPE to follow sequences of events of this type, then EVENTTYPE should be linked to the second event type with a link of weight n.")
(comment Light "This is the collection of events consisting of the propogation of electromagnetic radiation and associated with photons, a particle which lacks rest mass. Somewhat paradoxically, light has both a wavelike and a particle-like nature.")
(comment Exa "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^18.")
(comment DecompositionEvent "The collection of events in which one or more objects decompose more or less completely.  See also the more general concept #$DecompositionProcess, in whose instances objects at least partially decompose.")
(comment relevantInTypeOfTime-Always "(#$relevantInTypeOfTime-Always MT TYPE) means that the assertions in MT are relevant throughout the entire temporal extent of instances of TYPE.  See also #$relevantInTypeOfTime-Sometime.")
(comment genlMtSpecification "(#$genlMtSpecification SET) states the assumption that every microtheory in the given SET is an additional #$genlMt of the current microtheory.  This predicate is primarily used for reasoning in hypothetical contexts about the ramifications of having more microtheories visible to the hypothetical context.")
(comment Conveying-Generic "A specialization of both #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion and #$Translation-SingleTrajectory.  In each instance of #$Conveying-Generic, some object (see #$conveyor-Generic) enables or facilitates the conveyance of another object, or objects, or stuff (see #$transportees).  The conveyor itself might or might not also be undergoing translational motion (see #$objectTranslating) during the event.  See also the various specializations of #$Conveying-Generic.")
(comment agentResourceInPlan "(#$agentResourceInPlan PLAN AGENT) means that if EXEC is an
execution of PLAN, and is #$performedBy PERFORMER, then AGENT's being
#$behaviorCapable of being the #$assistingAgent in any specialization
of #$Event of which EXEC isan instance is a precondition for EXEC
being #$successfulForAgents.")
(comment desiredValue "(#$desiredValue THING SLOT VALUE) means that it is a des ired in this context for THING to have a value for SLOT of VALUE.")
(comment HumanPreschooler "Children of the proper age to be in preschool, but not yet old enough to be in school (more or less ages 3-5 years).")
(comment Albuterol "The chemical compound which is a bronchodilator.")
(comment CognitiveAwarenessPredicate "A collection of binary predicates that reveal information about the epistemological state of the ARG1.  Examples include #$awareOf and #$knowsAbout, both of which indicate cognitive properties of the ARG1 with respect to ARG2.  A necessary condition for membership in this collection is that the predicate is non-modal.  This means that coreferential substitution into the ARG2 positions of these predicates preserves truth.  This non-modal constraint amounts to the following: if (#$knowsAbout Joe #$GeorgeWashington) holds then so does (#$knowsAbout Joe 'the first U.S. president') and (#$knowsAbout Joe 'the Valley Forge commander buried in Baltimore, Maryland.') even though Joe might not know this last piece of information.  In contrast, modal predicates, including instances of #$PropositionalAttitudeSlot, do not permit coreferential substitution.  In some cases a modal predicate may have a non-modal counterpart (e.g. #$knows and #$knowsAbout), but only the non-modal sense will be a member of this collection.")
(comment citizens "The predicate relates a #$Person to a  #$GeopoliticalEntity. (#$citizens GEOPOL PERSON) means that PERSON is a citizen of GEOPOL.")
(comment MountableTransporter "A #$MountableTransporter is a transporter that one `rides' or `rides on' but does not `ride in'.  This collection was originally created to enable the following sorts of natural language interpretations.  Anyone who is said to `ride' such an object is most likely to be the #$driverActor.  If someone `rides' a non #$MountableTransporter (e.g. a train) is most likely not a #$driverActor but a #$passengers.  Positive exemplars include horses, jet skis, motorcycles, bicycles.  Negative exemplars include cars, trains, planes.  A borderline positive example is a skateboard.  When one `rides' a skateboard one is most likely the #$driverActor, but, unlike typical #$MountableTransporters, one is also most likely not sitting.")
(comment HangingUpATelephoneReceiver "The collection of all events in which a human agent hangs up a telephone receiver.  Most instances of #$CommunicatingByTelephone where human agents are doing the communicating are terminated by instances of #$HangingUpATelephoneReceiver: an instance of #$Teleconference might be an exception.  Instances of #$HangingUpATelephoneReceiver are often instances of #$DisconnectingAPhoneLink.")
(comment AtomGroupingFn "(#$AtomGroupingFn ELEMENT N) denotes the collection of groups of atoms of ELEMENT in which there are exactly N atoms of ELEMENT.")
(comment Calyx "A calyx is the flower's outermost whorl and is composed of sepals; it encloses and protects the reproductive organs.")
(comment Bishop-Clerical "The collection of all bishops, which are christian #$Clerics, usually male, who are mostly senior leaders within hierarchically organized church denominations such as the Orthodox, Roman Catholic, Methodist, Lutheran, Anglican  or Episcopalian churches.  Every Christian bishop is consecrated by one or more other bishops, in a chain of consecrations in direct 'apostolic succession' from #$JesusChrist.  Some bishops in this succession are 'wandering bishops' (episcopes vagrantes) not associated with organized churches.  In mediaeval times, some countries were ruled by bishops.")
(comment FormalSpeech "Word senses of words or phrases which are considered formal. One usually uses formal language when speaking to people who demand respect or have a higher station than oneself; perhaps also in rituals or other situations where scripted language is called for.")
(comment logicalFieldMapping "(#$logicalFieldMapping ?LF ?MAP) means that the values of the #$LogicalField ?LF are to be interpreted according to the code mapping ?MAP.  Normally, we associate a physical field with such mappings (see #$usesMapping), but if a field is dependent, contained, or composite, no corresponding #$PhysicalField exists so this predicate must be used.")
(comment DomainSocketDenialOfServiceFault "#$DomainSocketDenialOfServiceFault is an attribute of some OS kernels.  A kernel has a #$DomainSocketDenialOfServiceFault if it allows the creation of enough successive domain sockets to create a denial of service condition on the machine running that kernel.  The denial of service could be the dropping of network connections.")
(comment SexualServitude "Also referred to as ``sexual bondage'', #$SexualServitude is an oft considered perverse kind of #$SexualBehavior which requires at least two people.  One person playing the role of master commands another person playing the role of servant to perform certain actions some of which are sexual.")
(comment BuildingCleaningChore "Not only for houses! The collection of events in which the whole or part of the interior of a building is cleaned. ")
(comment VulnerableBecauseHasPredictableTCPSequenceNumbers "An attribute of some instances of #$Computer. A computer has this vulnerability if its operating system orders its TCP sequence numbers in a manner that allows prediction.")
(comment MultiPersonNonTeamGame "The collection of all #$NonTeamGames typically played by more than two people.  The game rules generally do not specify a limit, although after some point having more participants is less practical.")
(comment Anthrax-Bacterium "A collection.  Each instance is a sample of the #$Bacterium Bacillus anthracis which is responsible for a usually fatal hemorrhagic disease of wild and domesticated livestock, especially cattle and sheep.  Humans may become infected with Anthrax via contamination of a wound or by inhaling the organism.  Anthrax infections in humans are often fatal if not treated early.")
(comment RNATypeByTranslationFunction "#$RNATypeByTranslationFunction is a collection of collections. Each instance is a collection of #$RNAMolecules that perform the same function in the process of #$Translation-RNAToProtein.")
(disjointWith CaucasusCountry MaghrebCountry)
(comment RemoteControlledDeviceFn "Given a type of #$SelfPoweredDevice, #$RemoteControlledDeviceFn returns the
          collection of all devices of that type which are remote-controlled")
(comment SteamSterilization "The collection of all procedures in which superheated steam
is applied to a #$PartiallyTangible object at high pressure for the
purpose of rendering the object #$Sterile.")
(comment SystemsAnalyst "The collection of professionals who make their living

    by analyzing the computational needs of organizations.")
(comment GiftTypeByOccasion "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$GiftTypeByOccasion is a collection of instances of #$Gifts that all have something in common that makes them appropriate for a particular occasion.")
(comment Song-Sung "The collection of all events of a song [#$Song-CW] being sung by a (normally) human voice or a playing of a recording of such an #$Event.  The voice may be accompanied by #$MusicalInstruments.")
(comment AdenineNucleotide "The collection of instances of #$Nucleotide that have an adenine base.")
(comment Lawrencium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of $Lawrencium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment increasesVulnerabilityTo "(#$increasesVulnerabilityTo THREAT-OBJ OBJECT HARM-TYPE) means that THREAT-OBJ increases OBJECT's vulnerability to HARM-TYPE.  This predicate resembles #$vulnerableTo, but there is an important difference that must be observed, namely that when using #$increasesVulnerabilityTo one assumes that certain conditions coming into effect increase vulnerability.  Therefore, it should not be used to declare vulnerabilities outright; Cyc should have to conclude that a situation increases an object's vulnerability to some result.")
(comment Terra-Planetary "The collection of all topographical features on extra-terrestrial planetary bodies of extremely large size distingished by abrupt and clearly delineated boundaries, that is generally of higher altitude than the surrounding topographical features.  Continents, large islands, bulges rising above the 'datum' of planetary bodies are all elements of this collection.  Examples include Ishtar Terra on Planet Venus and Tempa Terra on Planet Mars, etc.")
(disjointWith DrainingProcess WindProcess)
(comment AudioConceptualWork "A specialization of #$ConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$AudioConceptualWork is an abstract work designed to be instantiated in sound (see #$SoundInformationBearingThing).  Notable specializations include #$MusicalComposition and #$Album-CW.")
(comment Preposition-Duration-Telic "Prepositions which denote durations of time, and generally modify telic or complete events; for example, 'in'.")
(comment Crystallizing "the process in which a liquid is transformed to become crystalline")
(comment Calf-TheAnimal "The offspring of a cow")
(comment TwoTeamGame "The collection of all games [#$Game] whose performances are typically played by two #$Teams.")
(comment BallisticMissile-Mushak120 "A battlefield short range ballistic missile produced by Iran")
(comment DefenseCooperationAgreement-Mutual "The collection of agreements in which the all of the #$agreeingAgents agree to support each other militarily in cases where defense in needed. A defense agreement between countries, for example, might include provisions for one country to station some military personnel and equipment in another country.")
(comment possessedWeaponRange-Max "(#$possessedWeaponRange-Max AGENT WEAPON-TYPE RANGE) means that the weapons of type WEAPON-TYPE that AGENT possesses have the maximal range RANGE.  For example, suppose that AGENT possesses TYPE(1)-missiles, ..., TYPE(n)-missiles, whose maximal ranges (see weaponEffectiveRange-Max) are, respectively, RANGE(1), ..., RANGE(n). Then, if these are the only types of missiles that AGENT possesses, we have (#$possessedWeaponRange-Max AGENT #$Missile RANGE) where RANGE is the maximal one among RANGE(1), ..., RANGE(n).  Actually, RANGE is the same as (#$Maximum (#$TheSetOf TYPE (#$and (#$genls TYPE #$Missile) (#$relationInstanceExistsMany #$possesses AGENT TYPE))) (#$FunctionToArg 2 #$weaponEffectiveRange-Max)).")
(comment Injecting-Intrathecal "Injecting a fluid, usually containing a drug, into the spinal canal.")
(comment instantiatesBorderPart "This predicate is used to assert that a particular #$PartiallyTangible thing is used to demarcate part of a border.   This is the predicate we would use in order to say, eg, that the Rio Grande instantiates part of the border between the United States and Mexico, thus: (#$instantiatesBorderPart RioGrande (#$BorderBetweenFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$Mexico)).  If (#$instantiatesBorderPart ?MARKER (#$BorderBetweenFn ?REG1 ?REG2)) then there exist ?SUBREG1 and ?SUBREG2 such that ?SUBREG1 is inRegion ?REG1 and ?SUBREG2 is inRegion ?REG2 and (#$instantiatesBorderWhole ?MARKER (#$BorderBetweenFn ?SUBREG1 ?SUBREG2)).")
(comment (LeftObjectOfPairFn FirstRib) "The head of the first rib on the left side")
(comment UFO "The collection of all UFOs, unidentified flying objects frequently           reported, esp. since 1947, to have been or observed or tracked in the           sky and variously explained as being atmospheric phenomena, hallucinations,           misperceptions of actual objects, alien spacecraft, etc.")
(comment ProtectiveSystem "#$ProtectiveSystem is the collection of objects that are supposed to prevent damage. Instances of #$ProtectiveSystem will either lower something's vulnerability or lower the #$DegreeOfDamage it incurs in a situation.  Also, instances of #$ProtectiveSystem can either be part of the object protected or distinct from it.  This collection includes both natural systems (e.g., turtle shells and cacti thistles) as well as intentionally designed systems (e.g., shields and barricades).  To refer to the latter specifically, use #$DefenseSystem.")
(comment HeaderLengthField-Packet "A #$HeaderLengthField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet
that indicates how long the header is in 32-bit words. The minimum
value is 5 [20 bytes], and the maximum value is 15 [60 bytes].")
(comment Crocodile "The collection of all crocodiles.  These so-called True Crocodiles are distinct from alligators.  The collection #$Crocodile constitutes a biological suborder of the #$Crocodilians.  Cf. #$Alligator.")
(comment CulturalActivity "The collection of all #$CulturalThings that are #$PurposefulActions.")
(comment VibrationThroughAMediumSensor "A specialization of #$Sensor (q.v.).  Each instance of 
#$VibrationThroughAMediumSensor operates by detecting or
reacting to the amplitude and frequency of vibrations that 
travel to it through a physical medium.  Specializations 
of this collection include #$Ear, #$Skin, #$SONAR-Device, 
and #$Microphone.  Note that #$Eyes are _not_ 
#$VibrationThroughAMediumSensors because electromagnetic 
wave propagation does not require a physical medium (cf.
#$ElectroMagneticRadiationSensor).")
(comment Wisdom "Performing an activity wisely or with good judgment, defined in the context of that particular activity.")
(comment FlowerArrangementTypeByFlower "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$FlowerArrangementTypeByFlower is a collection of instances of #$FlowerArrangements that feature the same flower.  An instance of this collection is #$RoseBouquet.")
(comment ShotPutField "The collection of fields where ShotPutSportsEvents usually occur.")
(comment Monster "The collection of all fictional/mythical animals of strange or terrifying shape, typically but not always imagined also to be very large in comparison  with human beings.")
(disjointWith AilmentConditionTypeBySyndrome InfectionType)
(comment EstablishingRelations "A collection of events.

Each element of #$EstablishingRelations is an event in which two 

instances of #$IndependentCountry formally or informally establish some

kind of diplomatic relationship. (Note that diplomatic recognition can 

also be extended to certain types of #$PoliticalOrganization, see below).

This collection includes both formal announcements of recognition

and acts via which two countries 

establish such relationships de facto (e.g., by beginning to engage in 

officially-sanctioned trade).  In certain cases, diplomatic recognition 

can be extended to #$PoliticalOrganizations which claim to speak on behalf

of a people desiring autonomy, e.g., the #$PalestineLiberationOrganization.  See also #$EndingRelations, and the attributes #$FullDiplomaticRecognition and #$TradeRelations.")
(disjointWith GayMaleChatRoom LesbianChatRoom)
(comment MachineCannon "The collection of #$Cannons which can fire continuously.")
(comment Transistor "An electrical device used as a switch or to provide voltage or current amplification.")
(comment RotationTranslationCombined "Combined translational and rotational movement")
(comment TrickTakingCardGame "The collection of all card games in which the objective of play is to win tricks, where a trick consists of each player in turn playing one card face up on the table (a few games have multiple tricks where several cards may be played at once).  Playing the first card to a trick is called leading.  There is some rule to determine which card wins the trick (for example the highest card of the suit led or the highest trump card played).  The cards played to the trick are captured and generally placed face down in front of the winner of the trick.  Usually the winner of a trick leads to the next.  #$TrickTakingCardGame is covered by two sub-collections, #$PlainTrickCardGames and #$PointTrickCardGames.")
(comment allAttachedMilitaryOrg "(#$allAttachedMilitaryOrg SUPER SUB) means that the organization SUB has been temporarily 'attached', directly or through intermediate levels, to the organization SUPER, which has temporary command of SUB and provides most logistic and facilities support needed by SUB.  SUPER does not necessarily pay for SUB out of out of SUPER's own regular budget support of SUB may come from SUB's original (assigned) organization rather than from SUPER.  The relationship is considered temporary (even if long-term), possibly established for a major undertaking or campaign, or for a fixed period of time of months or years.  Every military unit is attached to some organization same organization to which it is assigned, unless overridden.  The #$allAttachedMilitaryOrg predicate entails logistical support and command with any number of intervening units of organization between SUPER and SUB.  See #$attachedMilitaryOrg for the non-transitive version.  See also #$allAssignedMilitaryOrg and #$allOperationalControlMilitaryOrg for contrast.")
(disjointWith IBTCopying-SingleCopy MassReplication)
(disjointWith FrontOfficeManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment containedFields "(#containedFields LTS LF) means that LF is a field which is not explicitly a part of the #$LogicalTableSchema LTS, but which is contained within a field that is explicitly present.  For example, if ''9-digit-zip'' was a field in a schema, ''5-digit-zip'' would be a #$containedFields of that schema, since it can be accessed by deconstructing the value for ''9-digit-zip''.  Also see #$compositeFieldFormat, which is used to express how to extract the contained field.")
(comment CoralReef "Tropical underwater (seawater) habitat which features a preponderance of coral and many colorful tropical fish.")
(disjointWith BlastGrenade FragmentationHandGrenade)
(comment internalSubRegions "(#$internalSubRegions REGION INTERNALREGION) means that INTERNALREGION is a subregion of REGION which does not border on anything outside of REGION.")
(comment HypnotizingSomeone "The collection of all events in which a #$Person puts a #$Person #$InAHypnoticTrance. Such events include any actions the hypnotizer does to put or keep the hypnotizee in a state of hypnosis.")
(comment FluidCirculating "A #$FluidCirculating is a moving event in which pieces of the #$objectMoving are moving, but the #$objectMoving is not necessarily undergoing rotational (see #$Movement-Rotation) or translational motion (see #$Movement-TranslationEvent) as a whole.  E.g. the parts of a whirlpool are moving with respect to one another but the whirlpool as a whole may or may not be changing its location.  Tornadoes also undergo #$FluidCirculatings.  Note that if the tornado as a whole were undergoing motion it would be necessary to either make the #$FluidCirculating event also an element of some appropriate specialization of #$MovementEvent or to reify another event (which was not a #$FluidCirculating) to describe its motion as a whole.")
(comment DomesticViolence "The collection of events in which either a current or former spouse, partner, boyfriend, girlfriend, or cohabitant physically attacks another person to whom they are related in this way.")
(comment PunterComputerProgram "The class of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used by #$AmericaOnlineInc subscribers in order to expel other subscribers from a #$ChatRoom.")
(comment Ribose "A collection of molecules. Instances of #$Ribose are molecules of
a certain kind of sugar.")
(comment HepatitisA-Infection "A collection of Infections. A spec of #$ViralHepatitis. Instances of #$HepatitisA-Infection are viral infections caused by the hepatitis A virus, see #$HepatitisA-Virus.")
(comment Sublimating "A specialization of #$StateOfMatterChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$Sublimating is an event in which a piece of tangible stuff is directly transformed from a solid state to a gaseous state.  See also the related collection #$SublimatingToSolid.")
(disjointWith Mounting-Installing Archery)
(comment ReplacementTrojanHorse "This is a spec of #$TrojanHorseComputerProgram.  It includes instances of trojan
    horses which replace some program in the system so that it behaves differently
    than it did previously.  This includes trojan horses that modify other applications
    as well as those that only mimic the appearance and functionality of another 
    program.")
(comment StreptococcusPyogenes "A collection of #$Bacterium forming a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These cells are responsible for such human infections as streptococcal pharyngitis.")
(comment LightAircraftCarrier "A collection. Military light #$AircraftCarriers.")
(comment DeoxyribonucleotideBonding "A collection of events in which #$Deoxyribonucleotides are  linked by #$PhosphodiesterBonds to form an #$DNAStrand. The reaction is catalyzed by #$DNAPolymerase.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus)
(comment Silver "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of silver.")
(comment FacilityOfOrganizationFn "This is a functional analog of the #$orgFacilities

relation: (#$FacilityOfOrganizationFn ORG) returns the

facility (#$Place) which ORG operates out of.  The function is defined only if

ORG operates out of one and only one facility: i.e., only if there is a

facility such that it is appropriate to assert

(#$orgFacilities ORG PLACE).")
(comment GeneticInformation "The information encoded in any 

 #$GeneticInformationStructure.")
(comment RockyPlanetaryStuff "The subcollection of #$LandStuff which is part of some #$RockyPlanetaryBody.")
(comment ElectronicWarfareUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on the use of           electromagnetic energy to determine, exploit, reduce, or prevent           hostile use of the EM spectrum and/or retain its use by friendly           forces.")
(disjointWith Fur (OrganismPartTypeFn PygmyHippopotamus MobOfHair-Mammal))
(comment Bristle "The collection of all bristles")
(comment GlobalWarming "Collection of global warming events.  A global warming event is a general warming of the average temperature of the Earth.")
(comment SuperNintendoGame "The collection of video games and versions of such that are made to run specifically on a #$SuperNintendo-TheProduct platform (or emulate programs made to run on such platforms).")
(comment reformulatorEquals "A #$CycLReformulationRulePredicate that relates two CycL denotational terms.  When asserted in a #$Microtheory MT, (#$reformulatorEquals TERM-1 TERM-2) means that the #$CycLDenotationalTerm TERM-1 may be reformulated into the #$CycLDenotationalTerm TERM-2, or vice-versa (based on meta-properties of this rule and what mode the reformulator is in), in any #$Microtheory SPEC-MT such that (#$genlMt SPEC-MT MT) holds.  Free variables in TERM-1 and TERM-2 are shared, and may bind with CycL terms which match the template.  Note that (#$reformulatorEquals TERM-1 TERM-2) does _not_ necessarily imply (#$equals TERM-1 TERM-2), although this implication would hold if the reformualtion is a #$TruthPreservingReformulation (q.v.).")
(comment CutaneousFormFn "A #$ReifiableFunction which returns the collection intersection of a type of #$CutaneousInfection with the input type of #$Infection.")
(comment RadialStreetSystem "A specialization of #$StreetSystem instances 

of which are systems of streets arranged in a radial 

pattern, wherein there is a central \"hub\", and any 

street in the system either (i) is straight and joins 

with the other straight streets (\"spokes\") at the

hub or (ii) is circular and centered around the hub 

and concentric with the other circular streets (\"rings\")

in the system.")
(comment TransferIn "A collection of events.  Each instance of #$TransferIn is a #$GeneralizedTransfer (q.v.) for which there is a well-defined thing that it is a transfer \"to\" (see #$to-Generic), but not necessarily a well-defined thing that it is a transfer \"from\" (see #$from-Generic).  Subcollections of #$TransferIn include #$Collecting, #$GainingUserRights, and #$AccessingAnIBT.  At the end of a #$TransferIn, the thing transferred (see #$transferredThing) is in some sense \"located\" at the #$to-Generic.  Non- examples of #$TransferIn include instances of #$AbandoningSomething (when there is no prospective owner) and of #$IBTGeneration (when the information may go to various unspecified locations).")
(comment Dusk "A specialization of #$Twilight.  Each instance of #$Dusk is a dimly-lit period of time which is #$contiguousAfter an instance of #$Sunset, and is the event which starts an instance of #$Night.")
(comment TraversingATunnel "Collection of events in which an actor moves completely through a tunnel.  Created for the Battlespace Workarounds effort.")
(comment Metoprolol "The chemical compound which is a beta blocker.  This drug is intended to be used for therapeutic treatment of hypertension and myocardial infarction.")
(comment SocialistEconomicSystem "A collection of #$EconomicSystems which feature public ownership of the means of production, and scientific central planning to set prices and wages.")
(comment Gourde-Haiti "Major unit of currency of #$Haiti")
(comment Centi "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 1/100")
(comment TaxShelter-Action "The collection of #$PurposefulActions in which an #$IntelligentAgent (either an #$Organization or a #$Person) uses one of a number of techniques to legally reduce or avoid taxes, such as #$PersonalIncomeTax.  See also #$TaxType and #$FinancialObligation.")
(comment OnionPlant "Individual onion plants.")
(comment specs "An #$ELRelation; the #$elInverse of #$genls; 

denotes that one natural kind is a specialization of another; 

that is, every instance of arg2 also #$isa arg1.")
(comment MultipleRocketLauncher-122mmMRL "The collection of 122mm multiple rocket launchers. The MRL is a Soviet-made, truck mounted rocket launcher, similar to the American Multiple Launch Rocket system (MLRS), but much older.")
(comment MissileArmedCraft "The collection of military vehicles that are equipped to carry and fire missiles.  This collection includes missile-equipped submarines, surface ships, and aircraft.")
(disjointWith Project Emission)
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity RoadVehicleType)
(comment GrandDuke-HeadOfState "The grandDuke of a country which is usually a monarchy and always a GrandDuchy.")
(comment SubcollectionOfByTypeFn "(#$SubcollectionOfByTypeFn COLLECTION AGENTTYPE) describes the collection of all instances of COLLECTION which are created by instances of AGENTTYPE (see #$createdBy).")
(comment exposureToType "(exposureToType EXPOSURE TYPE) means that during EXPOSURE, the
object exposed is exposed to substance of the TYPE.")
(comment TravelAccessory "Instances are tangible products which are intended for use during travelling.  Often they are lighter-weight, more-compact versions of products people normally use at home.")
(comment CysticFibrosis "Hereditary disorder of the endocrine glands marked by excessive mucous in the lungs and difficulty digesting due to a deficiency of pancreatic enzymes")
(disjointWith TersifyForward TersifyBackward)
(comment molecularSubComponents "(#$molecularSubComponents CHEMICAL_OBJECT MOLECULAR_COMPONENT) means that MOLECULAR_COMPONENT is a connected part of CHEMICAL_OBJECT (either an instance of #$Molecule or a larger part of a molecule).  #$molecularSubComponents is a #$typedGenlPreds of #$physicalParts, used for relating a molecule (or portion of a molecule) with molecular subcomponents that are deemed to be of interest.  Subcomponents may be polyatomic or they may be atoms, and are to be distinguished on the grounds that they are part of the molecule in question in virtue of ionic or covalent bonds.")
(comment mtPersistenceDistribution "(#$mtPersistenceDistribution MT DISTRIBUTION) means that for assertions in MT, the likelihood of being true at a particular location in space-time with the context of MT is (partly) specified by the #$PersistenceDistribution DISTRIBUTION.")
(comment SexualOffense "The collection of events in which somebody violates somebody else either physically (see #$SexualAssault) or psychologically (see #$SexualHarassment) in a sexual way.")
(comment NamedRoadway "#$NamedRoadway is a specialization of #$Street-Generic.  Each instance of #$NamedRoadway is named part (stretch or segment) of roadways.  (Not roadway the stuff.)  Instances are named pieces of roadways (or highways or streets) which have names and lengths, and (usually) intersect with other roads. ")
(comment riverEndTopography "The predicate #$riverEndTopography is used to indicate the type of topographical feature found at the end of a particular river.  (#$riverEndTopography RIVER TOPO-TYPE) means that the instance RIVER of #$River has at its ending point a topographic feature of the type TOPO-TYPE.  Examples:  the #$riverEndTopography of both the #$SaintLawrenceRiver and #$SeineRiver is an instance of #$Estuary; the #$NigerRiver, #$MekongRiver, and #$GangesRiver all have instances of #$Delta as their #$riverEndTopography; the #$AlleghenyRiver ends in another instance of #$River (viz., the #$OhioRiver.")
(comment PsychoactiveAgent "The collection of all substances which, in sufficient doses, can cause hallucinations, euphoia, delirium, hyperalertness, drowsiness, or other mental effects.  Many such substances are used recreationally and many of them are banned from recreational use in various juristictions.")
(comment FixedAritySkolemFunction "The subcollection of #$SkolemFunctions whose arity is fixed. This is the most common type of skolem function, since variable- arity skolem functions are only created when a sequence variable is in the scope of the skolem.")
(comment SA9Missile "A type of surface-to-air missile.")
(comment sequentiallyArrangedSetOf "(#$sequentiallyArrangedSetOf TYPE SEQ) holds iff SEQ is an
instance of (#$SequenceOfFn TYPE).")
(comment Xenon "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of Xenon in stuffeous form.")
(comment infectionResultsFrom "(#$infectionResultsFrom INFECTION INFECTING) means that INFECTING is the #$InfectingEvent which causes INFECTION.")
(comment EconomicIndexPredicate "A collection of measures of economic performance.  Instances include the #$consumerPriceIndex-USA and #$stockIndexValue.")
(comment perfective-Generic "This predicate is a generalization over the #$SpeechPartPredicates for past tense and past participle forms of verbs, for the vast majority of English verbs, are identical to each other. This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it will always cash out as an assertion on one of its spec-preds.")
(comment roleInGoal "(#$roleInGoal OBJ CYCFORMULA ROLE) means that the goal represented by CYCFORMULA contains an event (or implies existence of an event) in which OBJ plays the role defined by ROLE. For example, if there exists a goal (it doesn't matter who possesses the goal) that #$MicrosoftInc go bankrupt, then one could assert (#$roleInGoal #$MicrosoftInc (#$financialState #$MicrosoftInc #$LegallyBankrupt) #$maleficiary).  This predicate could be used to find all of the goals that involve a particular #$Individual, to characterize that involvement and to reason about possessors of the goal.")
(comment ColoredGlass "glass that is colored, not clear")
(comment interArgReln4-3 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln4-3 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the fourth and third arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG4 ARG3) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(comment M1A1AbramsTank "A type of tank. Since its deployment in 1983, the           M1A1Abrams has been the principal tank used by the United           States Army and Marine Corps.")
(comment COABackgroundMicrotheory-General "An instance of #$COABackgroundMicrotheory-General contains background information that is relevant to ANY COA. For example, ModernMilitaryTacticsMt is an instance of COABackgroundMicrotheory-General. Every instance of COASpecificationMicrotheory inherits the information contained in every instance of COABackgroundMicrotheory-General, by way of a genlMt link between the #$MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory associated with the COA and instances of COABackgroundMicrotheory-General.")
(comment HomeBrewing "The activity of making beer at home.")
(comment WesternCountry "The collection of industrialized Western nations, including the United States, Canada, and the nations of Western Europe.  In general, these countries have a high level of economic and technological development and some form of representative government.  For a broader collection of industrialized nations worldwide, see #$IndustrializedCountry.")
(comment EnterobacterAerogenes "A collection of#$ProkaryoticCells that have small capsules and are found free-living as well as in the intestinal tract.  They may cause
#$UrinaryTractInfections and sepsis.  They are closely related to KlebsiellaPneumoniae-Species and can be differentiated on basis of motility and urease characteristics.")
(comment CharacterStringToken-Inscribed "A specialization of #$CharacterStringToken    each of whose instances is a specific physical marking,    #$Engraving, or character-string-in-relief that represents or    realizes a particular abstract instance of #$CharacterString    in some writing system.  Most (but not all) inscribed    character-string tokens are serial, i.e. are physical series    consisting of one or more instances of #$CharacterToken-Inscribed   (see #$CharacterStringToken-Serial).  Examples of nonserial inscribed string tokens include those illegible or barely legible instances of    #$Signature that cannot be divided into discrete character    tokens.  #$CharacterStringToken-Inscribed is a proper   generalization of #$WrittenCharacterSequence, as things like    illegible signatures, skywriting, and Brailling are instances   of the former but not the latter.")
(comment effectGeneralizes "(#$effectGeneralizes SPECIFIC GENERAL) means that when the type of effect some event has on an object SPECIFIC, GENERAL is also a type of result.  For instance, poisoning is often the effect of a person being bitten by a snake, and, as a result, so is getting sick.  To use this predicate properly, one should be able to construe SPECIFIC and GENERAL as the results of some sequence of events.")
(comment TimesPerYear "A Cyc function, #$TimesPerYear is a #$UnitOfFrequency.  (#$TimesPerYear NUMBER) denotes a frequency NUMBER times per year.")
(comment RuleTemplate "Terms denoting formulas (typically without support for efficient inference) that can be (partially) instantiated as Cyc assertions (typically with support for efficient inference); see #$trueRule and #$ruleTemplateAssertion.")
(comment CraterBasin "A topographical depression comprising the portion of a crater inside the rim.")
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention Agent-Generic)
(comment HermaphroditeHuman "The collection of all people who have both male and female (or ambiguous) anatomical (sexual) characteristics.")
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice Spacecraft)
(comment Starch "A piece of starch, i.e., a piece of a substance made up of starch molecules.")
(comment CellularRespiration-Aerobic "The breakdown of glucose by oxygen into CO2 and water, which releases energy used to make ATP.  Occurs in the cells of most living things; some odd bacteria use sulfide instead of oxygen in respiration.")
(comment ProjectileShell-Smoke "The collection of #$ProjectileShell-Pyrotechnics that uses smoke to  screen troop movement.  A black powder charge ignites and expels canisters  that may be designed to emit white, yellow, red, green, or violet smoke.")
(disjointWith Elasticity AngularDistance)
(comment lessVulnerableToBecause "(#$lessVulnerableToBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP) means
that there is an decreased chance of AGENT's playing the role ROLE in
a situation of type EVTTYPE because PROP is true
(#$decreasedChanceForRoleBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP) and AGENT
has the #$goals (#$not (ROLE EVTTYPE AGENT)).")
(comment RuralAreaPopulationDensity "The population density of rural areas.")
(comment SportsStatsForTypeFn "#$SportsStatsForTypeFn takes as argument any subclass of #$TemporalThing, probably a kind of agent or event, and returns the collection of all sports statistics relating to things of that kind.  For example, (#$SportsStatsForTypeFn #$FootballTeam) returns the collection of all football team statistics.  For sports statistics about an individual thing, use #$SportsStatsForFn.")
(comment AcademicOrganization "The collection of all #$EducationalOrganizations whose educators consist of #$AcademicProfessionals. For example, #$SchoolInstitution-KThrough12, and #$HigherEducationInstitution are subcollections of #$AcademicOrganization , whereas dance studios and figure skating schools are not, even though the latter have employees who educate others. Assertions about #$AcademicOrganizations should be made in the #$AcademicLifeMt.")
(comment Smog "A mixture of smoke and fog that occurs in the atmosphere as a result of industrial society pollution processes.")
(comment Pitch-Orientational "Turning along a lateral axis perpendicular to the front to back axis of an object.  A boat may do this as it dives into the trough of a wave.  A spec, #$Pitch-WhileTranslating, applies to translating objects such as air- and spacecraft.")
(comment typeConstraintToConsider "This predicate relates things to types against which they are to be evaluated as instances.  For instance, if we are given some event, EVENT, and want to determine whether it is an instance of some event type, TYPE, we can communicate this to Cyc by asserting, within or ''within sight of'' some evaluation microtheory, that (#$typeConstraintToConsider EVENT TYPE).  We then might evaluate whether the EVENT conforms to the rules for being an instance of this TYPE.")
(comment relationInstanceMember "(#$relationInstanceMember PRED INST GROUP) states that for every MEMBER of GROUP the following is true: (PRED INST MEMBER).  This predicate enables one to make claims about the members of a group by referencing only the group itself.")
(comment Exploration "This is the collection of activities in which some region is explored. This is

not restricted to regions of Earth. It is also not restricted to the surface of

the earth: one can explore below the earth's surface for resources, and one can

 explore the depths of the ocean or the surface of Mars. Not every instance of exploration

involves a human moving to the location being explored, but every instance

does involve some sensing device (human sensory apparatus or artificial device)

gathering information about the region explored.")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject DrugSubstance)
(comment Acupressure "A collection of events.  #$Massaging with the fingers applied to those specific areas of the body used in #$Acupuncture.")
(comment ModernNavalShip "A specialization of #$Ship and #$MilitaryWatercraft.  Each specialization of #$ModernNavalShip represented in the Knowledge Base is a type of ship that has been used at some time since the beginning of the Nineteenth Century primarily for naval purposes, such as military attack and defense, reconnaisance, support, rescue, or coastal monitoring.  Most instances of #$ModernNavalShip are specifically constructed for naval purposes.")
(comment SouthEasternRegionFn "A unary function that returns the `southeastern region' of           an instance of #$GeographicalRegion. What counts as the           `southeastern region' is contextually determined. Some of the           factors influencing the determination may be local           geography, cultural identity, and political considerations.")
(comment RemnantOfTangibleTypeFn "The term `(#$RemnantOfTangibleTypeFn TYPE)' denotes the collection of remnants of things of type TYPE, where TYPE is a type of partially tangible thing.")
(comment Cefprozil "The chemical compound which is an antibiotic.")
(comment Watt "This is the basic unit of power in the metric system and the basic #$UnitOfPower in CYC.  It is a newton-meter per second or a joule per second.")
(comment ConvProdOntMicrotheory "A collection of #$Microtheorys, each instance of which contains information about which #$ProductTypes are exhibited at particular #$Convention-Meetings or #$TradeShows. For example,  #$COMDEXFall2000ProductOntologyMt is used to record assertions about the product ontology for the #$COMDEXFall2000TradeShow. Instances of #$ConvProdOntMicrotheory can also contain information about collections of #$Convention-Meetings when the instances of the collection share a brand name. For example, #$COMDEXProductOntologyGMt can be used to record information about the product ontology common to most #$COMDEXConferences.")
(comment WaterSurfacePath "The collection of pre-designated or customary #$Path-Spatials that lie along water surfaces.  A moving object following (or blocking) this path is supported by the water, but is neither fully immersed in the water nor completely in the air.  This collection includes sea-lanes, channels, pre-designated ship routes, safe-passage mine-free paths, etc.  They may or may not be marked with #$Buoys.  Certain bodies of water like #$Canals are generally #$WaterSurfacePaths or have #$WaterSurfacePaths on them.  For the pure #$Trajectory of the motion of any object on a water surface, use #$WaterSurfaceTrajectory.")
(comment PickingUpATelephoneReceiver "The collection of all events in which a human agent picks up a telephone receiver.  In instances of #$MakingAPhoneCall where human agents are involved, the initial subevent is usually an instance of #$PickingUpATelephoneReceiver.  Note that an instance of #$PickingUpATelephoneReceiver is not ordinarily an instance of #$EstablishingAPhoneLink.  Exceptions would be some military 'crash' phones.  See #$CommunicatingByTelephone, #$MakingAPhoneCall.")
(comment CompoundPistil "Gynoecium consisting of fused carpels.")
(comment Archbishop "The collection of all archbishops: #$Clerics, usually male, who are high-ranking religious and administrative leaders of hierarchically-organized churches such as the Orthodox, Roman Catholic, and Anglican churches.  Archbishops outrank (mere) bishops and abbots.  Technically, every #$Archbishop is also a #$Bishop-Clerical or abbot, and hence a #$Priest or #$Monk.")
(comment PulverizationEvent "A specialization of #$PhysicalDestructionEvent.  In each instance of #$PulverizationEvent, some instance of #$SolidTangibleThing is reduced to a large number of small particles (see the collection #$Particle) through the application of a force.")
(comment interArgIsa4-1 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa4-1 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fourth argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the first argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 INST ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only 
if ARG1 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic 
well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment SetGIDFault "#$SetGIDFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if it runs SGID and can be exploited at some point during its operation to yield its elevated group privileges to a user that is not a member of the group. An important specialization is #$SetGIDFault-bin.")
(comment HauntedThing "The collection of all places and objects which are considered to be visited regularly by the spirit of a dead person.  Instances of #$HauntedThing should be declared only in microtheories expressing the viewpoint of one or more agents.")
(comment Mist "A kind of suspension in which particles of liquid are suspended in a gas.")
(comment Packet-ICMP-ECHO "#$Packet-ICMP-ECHO is a specialization of #$Packet-Internet. It is the collection of packets sent to computers in accord with the Internet Control Message Protocol, which is part of the #$InternetProtocol.  These packets are used in pinging.  See #$Packet-ICMP-ECHO-Spoofed.")
(disjointWith TeamGame NonTeamGame)
(comment backupMediumForCount "(#$backupMediumForCount SYS NUM) means that SYS has NUM backups.")
(disjointWith WesternEuropeanCountry CaucasusCountry)
(comment TumblingMotion "Moving forward in #$ProjectileMotion while spinning along an often horizontal axis perpendicular to the direction of motion")
(comment Bruise "Contusion")
(comment VaccinationEvent "The collection of all #$MedicalCareEvents in which an

instance of #$MedicalCareProfessional administers a dose of #$Vaccine, either 

through an instance of #$HypodermicSyringe or orally, with the intention of

conferring upon the recipient immunity to infection by a certain kind

of viral pathogen.")
(comment sentenceDesignationArgnum "Used to specify which argument of a given #$MicrotheoryDesignatingRelation

designates the CycL sentence to be interpreted in a specific microtheory.")
(comment RomanticGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByOccasion.  The collection of #$Gifts that demonstrate romantic love or otherwise imply love and romance.")
(comment responsibleFor-TypeType "(#$responsibleFor-TypeType AGTTYPE EVTTYPE) says that instances of EVTTYPE are typically brought about via the involvement of instances of AGTTYPE.  For example, (#$responsibleFor-TypeType #$Person #$PollutionProcess) says that generally, people have a hand in the pollution process.")
(comment containsInfoPropositional-IBT "(#$containsInfoPropositional-IBT IBT PIT) means that the #$InformationBearingThing, IBT, contains (at least) the propositional information in the #$PropositionalInformationThing, PIT.")
(comment CytosineNucleotide "The collection of all instances of #$Nucleotide that have cytosine as a base.")
(comment Fermium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Fermium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment contextOfPCW "(#$contextOfPCW WORK CONTEXT) means that CONTEXT is the complete context of WORK.")
(comment playsIntendedRole "(playsIntendedRole SITUATION THING ROLE) means that THING participates in a SITUATION in a way that is expected, given THING's nature.")
(comment ContinentalShelfZoneFn "(#$ContinentalShelfZoneFn ?ENT) picks out the region of the sea designated as the continental shelf of ?ENT, in accordance with U.N. provisions. The continental shelf of a region is the seabed and subsoil of the submarine areas extending beyond its territorial sea. Typically, an entity can claim a continental shelf extending to the continental margin, or to a distance of 200 n.m. from its coast, when the continental shelf doesn't extend that far.")
(comment Preposition-Directional-Telic "Prepositions which denote destination, and generally modify events in which the destination is reached; for example, 'into'.")
(comment Distilling "A collection of events.  In each instance of this collection, a liquid mixture is heated up to the boiling point of at least one of its liquid #$constituents.  That constituent vaporizes and the vapor is trapped and allowed to cool, thus separating (some or most of) that constituent from the mixture.")
(comment BiologicalWeapon-Bacterial "The collection of all bacterial-based #$BiologicalWeapons.")
(comment MissileLauncher "A collection of

devices, a subset of #$ProjectileLauncher. Each instance is a 

device used for launching missiles, generally under combat

conditions.  May be a fixed construction or mobile.")
(comment explainedStatement "The predicate #$explainedStatement is used to identify the proposition to be explained in a particular instance of #$Explanation. See also #$explanatoryStatement.")
(comment HumanWalkingProcess "A #$HumanCapabilityType and a specialization of #$AnimalWalkingProcess and #$WalkingOnTwoLegs. Each instance of this collection is a walking event in which the locomotor is a #$Person. Specializations include  #$Backpacking and #$RaceWalkingEvent.")
(comment NuclearAttack "The collection of events in which a nuclear weapon is used against a #$PartiallyTangible target.--Habash, June 18, 1998")
(comment PresidentsHoliday-US "The U.S. holiday commemorating the birthdays of Abraham Lincoln and George Washington; observed on the third Monday in February.")
(comment NasalAdministration "Inhaling a vapor substance, usually a drug, through one's nose.")
(comment interArgIsa1-4 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa1-4 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the first argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the fourth argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN INST ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed only 
if ARG4 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic 
well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment natArgument "(#$natArgument NAT N TERM) means that TERM is in the Nth argument position of the non-atomic term NAT.  For example,  (#$natArgument (#$JuvenileFn #$Dog) 1 #$Dog).  Note that (#$termOfUnit NAT (FUNCTION ... ARGN ...)) implies  (#$natArgument NAT N ARGN).")
(comment CompletelyVolatile "This instance of substance will evaporate almost instantly upon exposure to air.  Intended for instances of substances more volatile than acetone (roughly).")
(comment MediaSeriesNthFn "Each regularly distributed #$MediaSeriesProduct, such as a #$PeriodicalSeries or #$TVSeriesProduct has a series of #$MediaProducts as #$subWorks, ordered by the date of ORIGINAL media distribution.  (#$MediaSeriesNthFn, MEDIA_SERIES_PRODUCT N) returns the Nth member of this series.  Thus, (#$MediaSeriesNthFn #$StarTrek-Classic 1) returns the first episode of the original 'Star Trek' #$TVSeriesProduct.  Compare with #$MediaSeriesByDateFn, which returns members of a #$MediaSeriesProduct with instantiations distributed on a given date.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn FirstRib) HeadOfBone) "The head of the first rib")
(comment resourceDistributor-FunctionalRole "(#$resourceDistributor-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means
that AGENT is expected to carry resources around SYSTEM to various
other system components.")
(comment RolePlayingGame "A collection of events. Each instance includes the entirety of playing a role playing game event.")
(comment IdentificationField-Packet "An #$IdentificationField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet
that indicates which datagram a packet belongs to. This is necessary because
a single datagram may need to be split into various packets to conform to
restrictions on the size of a packet.")
(comment paIgnoredQuestion "Predicate used to state that a question has been ignored by a user of

the #$ProductAdvisorApplication.  (#$paIgnoredQuestion FORMULA SET)  means that a question which

attempted to determine the truth of FORMULA has been ignored, where SET was the set of possible answers from which the

user could have selected.  (If the question was not multiple choice, then SET should be empty.)")
(comment Chameleon "Small to medium-sized lizard, with laterally flattened bodies ornamented with crests, horns, or spines, and bulging, independently rotating eyes.  Their skin changes color in response to stimuli such as light, temperature, and emotion.")
(comment HypochlorousAcid "A collection of instances of a weak, unstable acid, HOCl, occurring only in solution and used as a bleach (see #$Bleach), oxident, deodorant and disinfectant.")
(comment skolemizeForward "(#$skolemizeForward FUNC) tells the inference engine that terms should be generated for fully-bound uses of FUNC during forward inference.")
(comment CycLOpenExpression "A specialization of #$CycLExpression.  The collection of CycL expressions that contain one or more free variables.  A #$CycLVariable VAR occurs _free_ in an expression EXPR if and only if there is an occurrence of VAR in EXPR that is not bound by another term in EXPR that denotes a #$Quantifier or other #$ScopingRelation (q.v.).  For example, the expression `(#$isa ?X #$Cat)' is open, but `(#$thereExists ?X (#$isa ?X #$Cat))' is not.")
(comment JavelinThrowField "The collection of fields where JavelinThrowSportsEvents usually occur.")
(comment WebHosting "The collection of #$ServiceEvents in which an #$IntelligentAgent provides another the capability to maintain its own #$WebPage-CW.")
(comment CycLOpenDenotationalTerm "The collection of all open denotational terms in the CycL language.  An expression is \"open\" if it contains one or more free variables (see #$CycLOpenExpression).  A CycL term is said to be \"denotational\" if it is the right sort of term to have a denotation (or value) in the universe of discourse (see #$CycLDenotationalTerm).  Each instance of #$CycLOpenDenotationalTerm is either a #$CycLOpenNonAtomicTerm (i.e. a \"NAT\" with a free variable) or a #$CycLVariable itself.  Examples include `?X', `(#$JuvenileFn ?X)', and `(#$JuvenileFn #$isa ?X #$genls #$JuvenileFn)' (even though the latter is semantically ill-formed).")
(comment shortestRouteByRoadsBetween "A predicate mapped in from the NWU Trafficability and
Terrain Engine. (#$shortestRouteByRoadsBetween PATH LOC1 LOC2) means
that PATH is the shortest path for wheeled vehicles connecting LOC1
and LOC2, in the sense that there does not exist any other path for
wheeled vehicles connecting LOC1 and LOC2 whose length is the same
length as PATH or shorter.")
(disjointWith KidsChatRoom TeenChatRoom)
(comment CommonObjectRequestBrokerArchitecture "#$CommonObjectRequestBrokerArchitecture (CORBA) is an architecture            that enables pieces of programs, called objects, to communicate with            one another regardless of what programming language they were written            in or what operating system they are running on.")
(comment OrGate "An electrical device whose inputs and outputs are digital signals and that implements the logical-OR function.")
(comment UnidirectionalPartialRotation "Unidirectionally changing the direction of movement or orientation.  The angular position of a point on the object monotonically either increases or decreases (modulo 360 degrees).  A turn is assumed to be less than 360 degrees unless specified.  See the sibling concept, #$PeriodicReversingRotation.")
(comment predicateConnectsCollections "(#$predicateConnectsCollections PRED COL1 COL2) means that when INST1 is an instance of COL1 and (PRED INST1 INST2) or (PRED INST2 INST1) holds, then (isa INST2 COL2) holds also.")
(disjointWith ServiceManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment wetWithLiquid "(#$wetWithLiquid OBJ LIQ) means that OBJ is wet with LIQ.  This predicate can be used with liquids (like oil) to which the word 'wet' normally wouldn't apply.")
(comment StockroomWorker "Someone who works in the stockroom or supply room of a company.")
(comment Train-TransportationDevice "#$Train-TransportationDevice is a specialization of #$WheeledTransportationDevice, #$TransportationContainerProduct, and #$PublicTransportationDevice.  Each instance of a #$Train-TransportationDevice is a \"train,\" i.e.,  a transportation device that runs on #$Railways and consists of multiple #$TrainCars coupled together.")
(comment FragmentationHandGrenade "A subset of #$HandGrenade.  Instances of this collection act by hurling fragments of the grenade case at high velocity.  These fragments often harm friendly troops and civilians up to 100 yards from the detonation.")
(comment Ethanol "A portion of an alcohol whose molecules have the chemical formula C2H5OH; it's a colorless liquid with many uses including cleaning solutions, beverages, pharmaceuticals, rocket fuels, etc.")
(comment consumptionCapacity "(#$consumptionCapacity PT PRODUCT-TYPE RATE) means that the #$Rate RATE is the greatest possible rate at which instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE could be consumed by the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT.  PT might, for example, be a #$Country or a #$Business.")
(comment PhaderComputerProgram "The class of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used by #$AmericaOnlineInc subscribers in order to change the appearance (font size, style and color) of the text they type in the context of  an #$OnlineChat.")
(comment embarcationSubevent "This slot was used in detailed descriptions of transportation events in which a transportation device is used.  The emabarcationSubEvent is the event of getting into/on the transportation device.  As a specSlot of #$temporallyStartedBy, it must be the first thing one does.")
(comment Deoxyribonucleotide "A collection of molecules. #$Deoxyribonucleotides are basic molecules that

compose molecules of DNA, see #$DNAMolecule. There are four kinds of nucleotides identical except that

each contain a different nitrogen base.")
(comment PercentOfFn "(#$PercentOfFn INDIVIDUAL AMOUNT) returns the part of

INDIVIDUAL that is AMOUNT percent of it. Example: (#$PercentOfFn

#$Sally'sEveningMeal01 50) represents 50% of Sally's meal.")
(comment HepatitisB-Infection "A collection of Infections. A spec of #$ViralHepatitis. Instances of #$HepatitisB-Infection are viral infections caused by the hepatitis B virus, see #$HepatitisB-Virus.")
(comment SexualBehaviorType "Element of this #$Collection are #$Collections whose instances are #$Events that are also instances of #$SexualBehavior. Not every subset of #$SexualBehavior is an instance of this collection, as there are subsets of #$SexualBehavior that would not be commonly regarded as `types' of sexual behaviour (e.g. the collection consisting of two events, two butterflies copulating on a tree leaf and Oedipus and Jocasta indulging in incest).")
(disjointWith Reading Archery)
(comment StrepThroat "#$StrepThroat is a kind of bacterial infection (spec of #$BacterialInfection) caused by a bacterium called Group A #$Streptococcus, in which the throat is very sore.")
(comment LightCruiser "The collection of light cruiser ships.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat ContactLocationType)
(comment PrescriberType "Instances of #$PrescriberType are collections of health care workers.  These collections don't group together medical professionals by specialty, but rather identify general classes of medical professionals which may have some permission to prescribe prescription drugs.  For example, #$Doctor-MD and #$NursePractitioner are instances of #$PrescriberType, but #$Cardiologist is not.")
(comment Accepting-CommunicationAct "An acknowledgement in which the performer affirms what was communicated to them in a prior communication.")
(comment Radon "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of radon in stuffeous form.")
(comment FillingANewPrescription-MailOrder "The collection of all events in which a new #$DrugPrescription is filled by a #$MailOrderPharmacy; a subset of #$FillingAPrescription-MailOrder and #$FillingANewPrescription.")
(comment intervalEndedBy "This predicate relates time intervals to the temporal things that immediately follow them.  (#$intervalEndedBy INT TEMP-OBJ) means that INT is the instance of #$TimeInterval that immediately precedes TEMP-OBJ . The beginning of INT coincides with the beginning of all time (#$Always-TimeInterval), if time has a beginning. See #$IntervalEndedByFn.")
(comment MineField-Scatterable "Collection of instances of #$MineField such that the relevant instances of #$Mine-Weapon are emplaced by broadcast scatter.")
(disjointWith GeneticInformation GeneticInformationStructure)
(comment NitrogenMustard "The collection of all chemical substances belonging to the nitrogen mustard group.  Notable specs include HN2, which is not only a chemical warfare agent (see #$ChemicalAgentType), but is used to treat cancer.")
(comment industryActivityTypes "(industryActivityTypes INDUSTRY ACTIVITY) means that ACTIVITY is one of the defining types of activities performed by members of an #$Industry-Localized INDUSTRY. For instance, a defining activity of any OilIndustry is #$ExtractingPetroleum, and a defining activity of any agriculture industry would be #$RaisingLivingThings.")
(disjointWith NuclearEvent ChemicalReaction)
(comment ElectronicWarfareAntiCountermeasuresUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile is to           defend against threat force attempts to disrupt transmissions           utilizing the EM spectrum.")
(comment Tower "A manmade structure, higher than its diameter, generally
used for observation, storage, or electronic transmission.")
(comment CycLClosedAtomicSentence "A #$CycLExpressionType and a specialization of both #$CycLAtomicSentence and #$CycLClosedSentence (qq.v.).  This is the collection of all and only the syntactically well-formed atomic sentences in the CycL language that contain no free variables.  Syntactically, each instance of #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence consists of a CycL expression denoting a #$Predicate followed by one or more (closed) CycL terms, with the entire sequence enclosed in parentheses.  Such sentences are sometimes called \"GAFs\" (an acronym for \"ground atomic formulas\"); see also the specialization #$CycLFullyGroundAtomicSentence.")
(comment Fulcrum "The collection of all fulcrums.  The fulcrum

   is the part of the lever around which the 

   bar turns.  Without a fulcrum, all you have

   is a bar.")
(disjointWith Campaign Emission)
(disjointWith OfficialDocument CycTheCollection)
(comment Commercial-CW "The collection of all advertisements designed for broadcast on radio or TV.  #$Commercial-CW is the conceptual work.  The output of a #$RadioReceiver or #$TelevisionSet is a #$Commercial-IBT")
(comment USStatePark "A collection of parks.  An element of #$USStatePark is a park which is managed by the state government of the U.S. state in which it is located; e.g., Presque Isle Park in Erie, PA, and Point State Park in Pittsburgh.")
(comment Plasma-StateOfMatter "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible and an instance of #$MatterTypeByPhysicalState. Each instance of #$Plasma-StateOfMatter is an object in the plasma state of matter. Matter existing in this state is at sufficiently high temperatures and pressures (for the kind of matter it is) that all molecules are completely ionized and those ions move freely away from each other.  Plasmas don't exist naturally on Earth, but do exist inside stars.")
(comment WaveAbsorptionFn "#$WaveAbsorptionFn is a Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$WaveAbsorptionFn WAVETYPE) denotes the collection of events in which #$WavePropagations of the type WAVETYPE are absorbed by some medium.")
(comment StreetSystemOfAreaFn "(#$StreetSystemOfAreaFn AREA) denotes the 

unique maximal street system (if any) SYSTEM that is spread 

throughout much of (and possibly beyond) AREA.  SYSTEM's 

being \"maximally spread\" throughout AREA means that it 

must not be a proper #$subPathSystems of any other 

street system wholly in AREA and covering a larger 

portion of AREA.  (If there were such a larger system, 

presumably, _it_ would be what this function mapped AREA 

to.)  See also #$streetSystemOfArea and #$transPathSystemTypeOfRegion.")
(comment AscendingEvent "An event is an #$AscendingEvent if and only if its object (#$objectMoving) has a higher altitude (#$altitudeAboveSeaLevel) at the end of the event than it did at the beginning of the event.  Thus, some descent may occur during the ascent so long as the net affect is to increase altitude.  Climbing stairs, walking down a hill to the top of a higher hill, being lifted, and airplane taking off are exemplars of #$AscendingEvent.  Technically, a standing up or bread rising are not exemplars because the #$altitudeAboveSeaLevel of these objects is not higher at the end of the ascension.  (#$altitudeAboveSeaLevel is based on the distance between the bottom of the object and the mean sea level.)")
(comment x-Component "The projection on the x-axis of a vector")
(disjointWith War WagingAColdWar)
(comment objectSought-DefiniteDeRe "`(#$objectSought-DefiniteDeRe SEARCH SEEKER OBJECT)' means that
SEARCH is a #$LookingForSomething-Definite which is #$performedBy SEEKER
and that OBJECT is the (unique) object sought in the sense that it is the
unique object that satisfies the SEEKER's #$searchCriterion-Definite.
Often we will not know what this criterion is, so this predicate allows us
to speak of the relation between the seeker and the object sought in the
absence of such knowledge. Note that the arg3 position is not opaque. This
reflects the fact that this is a \"third-person perspective\"
predicate. The term used to denote the object sought needn't match the way
SEEKER conceives of that object.")
(comment Twilight "A specialization of #$QualitativeTimeOfDay.  #$Twilight is union of the two collections of events, #$Dawn and #$Dusk.  Each #$Twilight is an event during which the sky is indirectly illuminated by the #$Sun, either just before an instance of #$Sunrise or just after an instance of #$Sunset.")
(comment programOfProcess "(#$programOfProcess PROC CW) means that PROC is executing some instantiation of CW. Example: (#$programOfProcess ACopyOfEmacsExecutingOnMyComputer #$Emacs-TheProgram)")
(comment requestedForward "(#$requestedForward ASSRT) means that some #$Cyclist requested that the direction of the #$CycLAssertion ASSRT be turned on forward. By default, rules are required to be stated with backward direction, nonetheless it often seems that a certain rule would be more useful or effective if stated as forward. This predicate is designed to enable easier tracking of such cases.")
(comment Propranolol "The chemical compound which is a beta blocker.  This drug is intended to be used for therapeutic treatment of hypertension and migraines.")
(comment MusicalCompositionFn-Agent "#$MusicalCompositionFn-Agent takes as argument any instance of
#$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of all instances of #$MusicalText
which are the text of some piece of music written or performed by that
musician or group of musicians.  For Example,
(#$MusicalCompositionFn-Agent #$PinkFloyd-MusicGroup) would return the
collection of texts of music written or performed by Pink Floyd.")
(comment Tariff "Elements of #$Tariff are taxes imposed by a country on goods imported to the country.  Note that the members of this collection are not either monies paid and collected or payment events, but are relatively abstract intangible artifacts - the tariffs themselves.")
(comment boundary-FunctionalRole "(#$boundary-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that AGENT
is expected to hold together the components of SYSTEM, protect them
from environmental stresses, and exclude or permit entry to various
sorts of matter, energy, and information.")
(comment HumanTakingItsFirstStep "The collection of events in which a human takes their first walking step.  Usually in the first 10 to 14 months of one's life.")
(comment Tax-COC "The collection of #$GovernmentCOC's, such as  #$USIncomeTax, each of which generates a collection of #$FinancialObligations all sharing similar features such as the sort of property that is taxed, the government levying the tax, and the required method of tax collection.")
(comment YamPlant "Individual yam plants.")
(comment InstantiateFn "(#$InstantiateFn PREFIX MT SET) denotes a term which is an element of SET in MT, which is a #$SetOrCollection.  This is accomplished by creating a new #$CycLConstant with a unique name that begins with the string PREFIX.")
(disjointWith SandMob StoneStuff)
(comment TorpedoArmedCraft "The collection of military vehicles that are equipped to carry and fire torpedoes.  This collection includes both submarines and torpedo planes.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single Project)
(comment sheetSurfaceTouches "(#$sheetSurfaceTouches SHEET OBJ2) means that SHEET #$touches all over most of one surface to a surface of OBJ2.  For example, pairs of sheets in a stack would be #$sheetSurfaceTouches to each other.  This would also apply to a #$Napkin on a #$Table-PieceOfFurniture.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByAerobicity "A collection of collections and a partion on #$Bacterium. This collection partitions #$Bacterium into two disjoint classes, the #$AnaerobicBacterium and the #$AerobicBacterium.")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType RoadVehicleType)
(comment CoRegent-HeadOfState "The coRegent of a country which is always a CoRegency.")
(comment includedText "(#$includedText PIT STRING) means that the #$PropositionalInformationThing, PIT, includes the string, STRING in its representation.")
(comment hotelsAccessibleNewsLanguages "This predicate relates a hotel to the natural languages in which guests can read news, hear radio news broadcasts or watch television broadcasts of news.")
(comment ZodiacConstellation "The collection of the 12 #$Constellations which represent the 12 signs of the zodiac used in Western astrology. #$Leo-Constellation and #$Aries-Constellation are instances.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice TravelAccessory)
(comment Rabies "An acute, often fatal, disease caused by a virus transmitted from one animal to another through infected saliva, usually through a bite. Sometimes named 'Lyssa', after a Greek goddess of raging madness. Symptoms are headache, fever and malaise progressing to excitability, fear of water, delirium, convulsions and death.")
(disjointWith OneWayReformulation-Backward OneWayReformulation-Forward)
(comment RecordingOfWaveIBT "The collection of recordings (audio or video), each of which has a specific, timed length.  For example, a video of a birthday party might have a length of 60 minutes.")
(comment mtPartonomicAbstractionLevel "(#$mtPartonomicAbstractionLevel MT COLLECTION) means that when reasoning in (or with) the context MT, (instances of) classes of objects at about the level of partonomic abstraction indicated by COLLECTION should be attended to, or taken into account.  If you consider the knowledge base as a lattice of abstract concepts arranged in a hierarchical structure via the subparts/superparts relation (#$parts), then the further `up' or `down' the hierarchy you go from COLLECTION, the less likely it is that (instances of) these classes should be used in inferencing. Example: the assertions in MT might apply to wheel-and-axle assemblies, but not to bearings (part of a wheel-and-axle assembly), and not to cars (which have wheel-and-axle assemblies as parts).  See also #$mtSubsetAbstractionLevel.")
(comment TransportFacility "#$TransportFacility is a specialization of #$ConstructionArtifact and #$InfrastructureProduct.  Each instance of #$TransportFacility is a structure built and used by human beings for the purpose of transportation of people, livestock or goods, or for associated support services.")
(comment riverStartTopography "Lists the starting type of the river - mountains, gorges , glaciers etc. Use this if you want to say that the river starts in a glacier without specifying the glacier. If you mean a specific place A, use the other slot riverStartsWhere.")
(comment Pony "#$Pony is a collection, a specialization of #$Horse, each member of which is (thought to be) descended from the primitive pony of the ice age.  Each member of #$Pony is a member of a pony breed, however, only a few representative breeds are in Cyc as collections.  Modern instances of #$Pony are rarely if ever pure bred ponies, but are mixtures of various horse and pony breeds.  While some instances of #$Pony (of a specialization of #$Pony that represents a breed) are larger than some instances of #$Horse, in sports the pony is defined as any horse shorter than about 148 cm (in horse terminology about '14.2 hands').  Ponies are ridden by children or small adults.")
(comment EconomicSystem "A collection of all economic systems.  It can be the economic system of a #$GeopoliticalEntity, or the economic system in a #$GeographicalRegion.  To refer to the economic system of a particular country or a state (or a province, etc.), use #$EconomyFn.")
(comment Speediness "The qualitative speed with which an activity is performed.")
(comment SportsStick "various stick-like, hand-held devices in sports like ice hockey, lacrosse, and hurling, used, in lieu of one's hands, to manipulate a ball or puck.")
(comment SAMVehicle "The collection of military vehicles used to transport surface-to-air missiles.")
(comment Bromine "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby 

molecules) of Bromine. Bromine is a heavy, volatile, corrosive, reddish-brown nonmetallic 

substance that is liuquid under normal physical conditions.")
(comment properNounSemTrans "(#$properNounSemTrans NOUN INT FRAME TRANS) means that the translation of word sense number INT of proper noun NOUN in frame FRAME is TRANS.")
(comment consumerPriceIndex-USA "The #$consumerPriceIndex-USA or 'CPI', is an index that measures the prices of consumer goods and services and is a measure of the pace of the effectsof monetary inflation in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  The CPI is published by the US Department of Labor once a month (the number is calculated by the #$BureauOfLaborStatistics).  The CPI measures and compares, from month to month, the total cost of a statistically determined 'typical market basket' of goods and services consumed by U.S. households.  (#$consumerPriceIndex-USA DATE NUMBER) means that NUMBER is the CPI on DATE.")
(comment GeneralizedQuantifier-Conservative "If GEN is a conservative generalized quantifier, then for any

domain of discourse and any pair of collections C1, C2 defined therein,

(GEN C1 C2) is true iff (GEN C1 (#$CollectionIntersection2Fn C1 C2)) is. In

informal terms, a generalized quantifier is conservative if the elements of

C2 that are not in C1 do not affect the truth-conditions of the

quantifier: if we increased the extension of C2 with elements that are not

also in C1, we would not change the truth-value of (GEN C1 C2). Take, e.g.,

`every mailman runs': if the extension of the class of runners is augmented

by adding

runners who aren't mailmen, it makes no difference to the truth of that

sentence. Contrast with `only mailmen drive those funny trucks': if the

extension of funny-truck drivers is augmented with individuals who aren't

mailmen, then that sentence would change from true to false.")
(comment Wealthy "The quality or state of possessing #$GreatWealth.")
(disjointWith ClearGlass ColoredGlass)
(comment Humvee "The collection of 'high mobility, multi-purpose, wheeled vehicles' used by the U.S. Army.")
(comment MilitaryOperationsDynamicSituationMicrotheory "Each instance of #$MilitaryOperationsDynamicSituationMicrotheory contains situation information that is relevant to a particular class of #$MilitaryOperations -  operations involving some particular unit or units against some particular enemy unit or units, in some specific geographical region, given the current situation with respect to the units in question.  Unlike related instances of #$MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory, each #$MilitaryOperationsDynamicSituationMicrotheory contains information which is likely to change over the life of the relevant operations, such as location of units (both friendly and hostile), troop strength, and weather, if relevant. Each #$MilitaryOperationsDynamicSituationMicrotheory inherits static situation information from some instance(s) of #$MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory.")
(comment Brewing "The activity of producing beer.")
(comment BroadcastOfStructuredActivityFn "#$BroadcastOfStructuredActivityFn takes as argument any instance of #$DevisedStructuredActivity and returns the

collection of events that are broadcasts (radio or television) of instantiations of that activity. For example, (#$BroadcastOfStructuredActivityFn #$Baseball-TheGame) would return the collection of broadcasts of baseball games.")
(comment CharacterStringToken-Interpreted "The specialization of #$CharacterStringToken whose 
  instances, in addition to whatever other information 
  they might happen to contain, contain a certain piece of
  information primarily (see #$primarilyContainsInfo).  This is 
  the semantic notion got at by saying that (a particular use of) 
  a given English term or sentence has an ''overt meaning'', 
  despite the fact that other meanings might be taken from or 
  read into it.  Unlike instances of #$Message, however, 
  interpreted character-string tokens (might be but) need not 
  be produced with an explicit intention on the part of some 
  agent that it have the primary meaning that it does.")
(comment RoundDownFn "(#$RoundDownFn QUANTITY) converts QUANTITY into one where the maximum and minimum ranges have been rounded downwards to integer values.  For example, (#$RoundDownFn (#$Meter 2.5)) denotes (#$Meter 2).")
(comment RemoteExecutableExploit "The collection of #$MaliciousComputerPrograms that allow
users to affect remote computers.")
(comment BPHDrug "The collection of all #$DrugSubstances designed to counteract benign prostatic hperplasia (BPH).  One such drug is the alpha-blocker, terazosin.")
(comment BuildingTourFn "(#$BuildingTourFn ?BLDG) returns the collection of all
instances of #$TouringABuilding in which the #$objectsPerceived is
?BLDG.")
(comment ruleTemplateAssertion "(#$ruleTemplateAssertion TEMPLATE ASSERTION) states that ASSERTION is an assertion which is an instantiation of the rule template TEMPLATE.")
(comment AccountType "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$ObjectType.  Each instance of #$AccountType is a collection of financial accounts of the same type.  Instances of #$AccountType include #$SavingsAccount, #$CreditCardAccount, #$RetirementAccount, #$SocialSecurityAccount, and #$TravelExpenseAccount.")
(comment SkiResort-Attraction "A collection of objects, a spec of #$Resort-Attraction.  Each

 instance of #$SkiResort-Attraction is a place for #$SnowSkiing

 which draws visitors, typically vacationers who stay there for

 one or more nights.")
(comment CraterBasinFormedByImpact "A topographical depression comprising the portion of an impact crater inside the rim.  The basin contains breccia and may contain impact melt.")
(disjointWith BeliefSystem Agent-Generic)
(comment Watercraft-Subsurface "A specialization of #$Watercraft.  Each instance of #$Watercraft-Subsurface is a vehicle designed to travel underwater.  Note that since some instances of #$Watercraft-Subsurface are also designed to travel across the surfaces of bodies of water, the collections #$Watercraft-Subsurface and #$Watercraft-Surface (q.v.) are not disjoint.")
(comment Glucocorticoid "A class of #$Hormones which affect protein and carbohydrate metabolism.")
(comment physicalBuild "arg2 is a physical build attribute which describes arg1.")
(comment SetOfListMembersFn "The function #$SetOfListMembersFn, applied to a #$List LIST, results in the set of all members of LIST.  Note that although something may occur in LIST more than once, it of course cannot occur more than once in the set of members of LIST.  For example, suppose that LIST = (#$TheList A B A).  Then (#$SetOfListMembersFn LIST) = (#$TheSet A B).")
(comment ProjectileSlug-ArmorPiercing "The collection of #$ProjectileSlug-Bullets that contains a core of  hardened steel.  It is used against bullet-proof vests and tank armor.")
(disjointWith Elasticity Temperature)
(comment exports "(#$exports COUNTRY PRODUCT-TYPE) means that the region COUNTRY has substantial regular exports of the goods or services PRODUCT-TYPE to other countries. ")
(comment AnalogyMatch "An #$AnalogyMatch is the result of a #$matchBetween two #$AnalogyCases.  The Base description is the historical precedent or case, the target is the current situation.  The result of the comparison is a set of mappings (#$AnalogyMappings).  The comparison itself is reified because there are aspects of the comparison that are shared across multiple mappings, and it is potentially useful to talk about the existence (or lack thereof) of mappings satisfying particular properties with respect to a comparison.  For example, consider comparing Operation Desert Storm to WW2.  There are several different ways to view this comparison, each corresponding to a different mapping.  Note, #$AnalogyMatch is very much like #$AnalogyCorrespondence but the first links cases and the second links items, or statements, in cases.")
(comment puller "(#$puller ACT PULLER) means that PULLER provides physical force against the #$pullee in ACT to tend to close the gap between #$puller and #$pullee. For example, a #$Mule would be a #$puller of a barge along a #$Canal in a #$PullingAnObjectAlongWith event, a #$Fisherman would be a #$puller in reeling in a fish in a #$PullingAnObjectCloser event, and a #$Dog tied to a tree would be a #$puller in an event in which it was trying to get away from the tree, even though neither the tree nor dog moved.")
(comment bayesParentSet "A predicate used for probability statements.  (#$bayesParentSet BAYESVARIABLE SETOFBAYESVARIABLES BAYESNET) means that the #$BayesDiscreteOutcome associated with each bayes variable in the set SETOFBAYESVARIABLES influences the #$BayesDiscreteOutcome associated with BAYESVARIABLE, and that each member of SETOFBAYESVARIABLES is an immediate 'parent node' of the BAYESVARIABLE node in the Bayesian Network BAYESNET representing probabilistic influence in the applicable #$Microtheory.  That is, each #$BayesVariable in SETOFBAYESVARIABLES is a direct parent of BAYESVARIABLE in the #$BayesNet.   Note that BAYESVARIABLE and any #$BayesVariable in SETOFBAYESVARIABLES cannot be #$conditionallyIndependent in the #$Microtheory since one is a #$bayesParent of the other.  Given the outcome associations of all the members of SETOFBAYESVARIABLES (#$bayesParent nodes), then all of BAYESVARIABLE's further ancestor nodes and other non-descendant nodes are #$conditionallyIndependent of it in the applicable #$Microtheory.  To relate a node to a single one of its parent nodes, rather than the whole set, use #$bayesParent.")
(comment CycLAtomicTerm "The collection of all atomic #$CycLDenotationalTerms (q.v.).  \"Atomic\" here means not constructible  from other CycL terms via the syntax of CycL.  Thus, subcollections  of #$CycLAtomicTerm include #$CycLConstant, #$CycLVariable, and #$SubLAtomicTerm.  Note that #$CycLAtomicTerm, like most instances of #$CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\" (see #$quotedCollection).")
(disjointWith SexualProductOrServiceEvent SportsChatRoom)
(comment Roll-Orientational "Turning about the back to front axis.")
(comment Lolita "The collection of all goodlooking pubescent or pre-pubescent girls with a #$SexyPersonality well above the average for that age group. A concept derived from the main female character in #$Lolita-TheBook.")
(disjointWith ContactLocation DrugSubstance)
(comment Atto "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10^-18")
(comment BallAndSocketJoint "The ballAndSocket connection")
(comment Acupuncture "The collection of all #$ServiceEvents where #$Acupuncture, an originally Chinese practice of puncturing the body at specific points, is used to cure disease or to relieve pain.  #$Acupuncture is not a #$MedicalTreatmentEvent because it is not necessarily performed by a medical care professional.")
(comment SouthWesternRegionFn "A unary function that returns the `southwestern region' of           an instance of #$GeographicalRegion. What counts as the           `southwestern region' is contextually determined. Some of the           factors influencing the determination may be local           geography, cultural identity, and political considerations.")
(comment ArmoredVehicle-Heavy "#$ArmoredVehicle-Heavy is a specialization of #$ArmoredVehicle and #$MilitaryVehicle.  Each instance of #$ArmoredVehicle-Heavy is designed  to sustain tank, artillery, and small-arm fire while engaging in combat.  The light-armored vehicles, on the other hand, only sustain small-arm fire and shrapnel.  This collection is disjoint with #$ArmoredVehicle-Light.")
(comment Comet "The collection of all comets moving under the influence of our Sun.  In AstronomyMt this collection might also include comets outside the Solar System.")
(comment TriamcinoloneAcetonide "The chemical compound which is a cortico-steroid. Used in Azmacort.")
(comment MultiWordForConstantPred "The specialization of #$MultiWordPhrasePredicate whose instances map phrases to Cyc constants.  See also #$MultiWordForFormulaPred.")
(comment ConvVenInfoMicrotheory "A collection of #$Microtheorys, each instance of which contains information about #$Vendors promoting #$ProductTypes at a given instance of #$Convention-Meeting or #$TradeShow. In this context, a #$Vendor is an #$LegalAgent who rents  a booth or table at the #$TradeShow in order to promote a product.")
(comment (ListOfTypeFn IndependentCountry) "A specialization of #$List.  Each instance of (#$ListOfTypeFn #$IndependentCountry) is a list each of whose members (see the predicate #$listMembers) is an instance of #$IndependentCountry.  An example of such a list is (#$TheList #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$Iran #$Japan).")
(comment Gynoecium "The female component of a flower, made up of one or more carpels.")
(comment CopticPope "The collection of all #$CopticPopes; each is the spiritual leader and pope of #$CopticChristianity and vice-regent of #$JesusChrist on earth.  In recent times the #$CopticPopes have lived in #$Egypt.  See also #$Pope.")
(comment Neutrino "The collection of all neutrinos.  Neutrinos are #$SubAtomicParticle which are massless (or near massless), have a \"spin\" of +/- 1/2, lack charge, travel at (or near) the speed of light, and have an extremely low reaction cross-section.  There are three kinds of neutrinos, the electron-like, tau-like, and beta-like types, which are created in reactions in which their namesakes are also produced.  There is a theory that a single neutrino may change from one category to another, which would indicate that it must travel slower than the speed of light, and thus must have \"rest mass\".")
(comment AuthenticationSoftwareBypassFault "#$AuthenticationSoftwareBypassFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if it is possible to circumvent an authentication or certification method the program is designed to perform.  Note that #$AuthenticationSoftwareBypassFault is distinct from #$AccessValidationFault.")
(comment Lens "The collection of all lenses, natural (#$Lens-EyePart) and artifical (e.g. for #$Telescopes and #$EyeGlasses).")
(comment PerformanceOfClassicalMusicCWTypeFn "(#$PerformanceOfClassicalMusicCWTypeFn COMPTYPE) denotes the collection of all #$ClassicalMusicalPerformances that are performances of the #$ClassicalMusicalCompositionType COMPTYPE. For example,(#$PerformanceOfClassicalMusicCWTypeFn #$StringQuartetComposition-CW) denotes the collection of all performances of any #$StringQuartetComposition-CW. Use #$performanceOfWork to relate a particular performance event to the #$ConceptualWork being performed.")
(comment openPorts "A predicate relating a #$Computer with a #$TransportLayerProtocol and a #$NetworkPortNumber. (#$openPorts COMP PROTOCOL PORT) means that COMP is an instance of #$Computer and that PORT is an instance of  #$PositiveInteger between 0 and 65535 inclusive on which some process is listening for incoming of instances of #$Packet-Networks that conform to PROTOCOL.")
(comment NonTeamGame "The collection of all #$Games played by individual competitors instead of #$Teams.")
(comment statementOfPurpose "(#$statementOfPurpose THING STRING) means that the expressed purpose of THING (such as an instance of

#$Organization, #$Treaty,

#$Law or some other #$CodeOfConduct)

is STRING. This statement describes the expressed or public purpose of THING; the actual goals or purpose of THING may differ from this expressed purpose.")
(comment MessengerRNA "#$MessengerRNA is the collection of #$RNAMolecules that direct the synthesis of proteins in the process of #$Translation-RNAToProtein. They are transcribed from a portion of a #$DNAMolecule during #$Transcription-DNAToRNA.")
(comment ShouldModeFn "(#$ShouldModeFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-MT) denotes the      subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances possess the modal property denoted by \"should\", from the perspective of CONTEXT-MT.")
(comment reformulationOf "(#$reformulationOf SIMPLE-TERM COMPLEX-TERM) means that SIMPLE-TERM and COMPLEX-TERM are definitionally or intensionally equal.  Also SIMPLE-TERM is a simpler form of COMPLEX-TERM.  That is, SIMPLE-TERM contains fewer nested #$Function-Denotationals than does COMPLEX-TERM.  Unlike #$equals, #$reformulationOf is strictly a #$HumanCyclist asserted form of equality.  #$reformulationOf differs from #$rewriteOf in that its COMPLEX-TERM argument is unreified. This allows us to state equalities between existing Cyc terms and NAUTS so that at dialogue time, a compositionally determined output of one of our parsers can be mapped to Cyc terms.  See #$ncRule for examples of such NAUTS.")
(comment Refugee "The collection of #$Persons who move from one location to another because of adversity.  There is a #$TakingRefuge event, #$performedBy a #$Refugee, with a #$fromLocation and a #$toLocation.")
(comment ApplyingStuffToSurface "A collection of events. In each #$ApplyingStuffToSurface event, some stuff is applied to a surface so that it covers [#$covers-Generic] it.  This may be done in different ways, for example by dipping an object into the stuff being applied, spraying the stuff onto the surface, or #$SpreadingStuffOntoSurface.")
(comment ProperMassNoun "The collection of all proper mass nouns. Proper mass nouns are usually capitalized.")
(comment TVShow-SingleCW "The collection of all individual TV shows considered as #$ConceptualWorks.  An instance of #$TVShow-SingleCW is intended to be presented to the public in a single broadcast.  One can be either a one-time tv special or an episode [see #$episodes] of a #$TVSeriesProduct.  Every #$TVShow-SingleCW is a #$ConceptualWork, usually with some sort of #$News or #$Narrative content, whose instantiations have a duration of at least 20 minutes. Instances of #$TVShow-SingleCW are listed on schedules, whereas instances of #$TVShow-IBT, #$Commercial-CW, and public-service announcements are not.   Each instance of #$TVSeriesProduct has a (large) number of instances of #$TVShow-SingleCW as #$subWorks.  Note that, e.g., 'Seinfeld' is not a #$TVShow-SingleCW but a #$TVSeriesProduct since it refers to a series of instances of  #$TVShow-SingleCW.  Both #$TVShow-SingleCW and #$TVSeriesProduct are specializations of the generic #$TVShow-CW.")
(comment Hustler-ConArtist "The sub-genus of #$Criminal person. A #$Hustler-ConArtist is a confidence-trickster who fools people into parting with money or valuables using a variety of hoaxes or scams. These hoaxes usually require the #$Hustler-ConArtist (i.e, #$perpetrator) to first gain the trust of the hoax's #$victim.")
(comment SympathyGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByOccasion.  The collection of #$Gifts that demonstrate sympathy for the recipient.")
(comment groupQuarantined "(#$groupQuarantined QUARANTINE ORGANISMS) means that the #$Group ORGANISMS are among those (not necessarily only those) that are quarantined by QUARANTINE. ORGANISMS includes only those organisms which are in in fact confined by QUARANTINE. To describe a group as subjected to a #$Quarantine, irrespective of whether all members of that group are in fact confined, use #$groupSubjectToQuarantine. To say of a single organism that it is confined in a certain #$Quarantine, use #$organismsQuarantined. For the location of a #$Quarantine, used #$quarantineLocation.")
(comment infoStructureCC "(#$infoStructureCC AIS CC) means that the #$AbstractInformationStructure, AIS, encodes information according to the #$CommunicationConvention, CC")
(comment GuanineNucleotide "The collection of instances of #$Nucleotides that have guanine as a base.")
(comment eventTheme "(#$eventTheme EVT THEME) says that the \"theme\" of EVT is THEME.  For example, (#$eventTheme   FundRaiserDinner3457 FundRaising) says that  the \"theme\" behind FundRaiserDinner3457 is fund raising.")
(comment Einsteinium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Einsteinium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment firstRoleInEventType "(#$firstRoleInEventType INDIV TYPE ACTOR-SLOT EVENT) means that EVENT
is the very first instance of TYPE in which INDIV occupied ACTOR-SLOT.
For instance, (#$firstRoleInEventType #$Foxvog (#$MakingFn
#$CycLAssertion) #$performedBy Event001) means that Event001 was the first
time that #$Foxvog ever made a Cyc assertion.  See also #$lastRoleInEventType")
(comment COMDEXTradeShow "The collection of instances of

 #$TradeShow-Technological that

  are a part of every #$COMDEXConference.")
(comment usefulToAgent "(#$usefulToAgent THING AGT) means that 

  THING is useful to AGT.")
(disjointWith HailStone Frost)
(comment Preposition-TimePoint "Prepositions which denote points in time, for example, 'at'.")
(comment PressingFlat "the process by which an object in bulk form is flattened to become sheetlike")
(comment Firmibacteria-Class "An instance of a #$BiologicalClass in the #$Firmicutes-Division of the #$MoneraKingdom.  This class contains important human pathogens such as Bacillus anthracis.")
(comment BiologicalWeapon-BiologicalToxinBased "The collection of all #$BiologicalWeapons that make use of #$BiologicalToxins.")
(comment EconomicDiversificationGoal "The attribute characterizing goals whereby some #$Organization (often the government of a country) attempts to diversify its economy, usually by reducing reliance on some particular industrial sector, and increasing production in other sectors; or, perhaps, by fostering brand-new industries.")
(comment EvaporatesQuickly "Substance evaporates quickly, e.g. GasolineInstance422.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (RightObjectOfPairFn FirstRib) BoneShaft) "")
(comment RushHour "A #$TimeOfDayType (q.v.). Each instance of this collection is a time of day when the roads, busses, trains, etc. are most crowded, because people are travelling to or from work.")
(comment cityInState "(#$cityInState CITY STATE) means that the #$City CITY is located in the geopolitical sub-region STATE.  Note that STATE may be an instance of #$State-Geopolitical, or it may be an instance of some other specialization of #$CountrySubsidiary, such as #$Territory. For example, the #$CityOfDurhamNC is a #$cityInState of #$NorthCarolina-State; Xiamen (Amoy) is a #$cityInState of Fujian. See also #$majorCityInState.")
(comment MoreFragmentsField-Packet "A #$MoreFragmentsField-Packet is a flag in a #$Header-Packet
that, if set, indicates that more fragments of the same original
#$Packet-Internet are following the current #$Packet-Internet. A 
#$MoreFragmentsField-Packet will not be set if the #$Packet-Internet 
is the last fragment of the original packet, or if it is in a
#$Packet-Internet that never split into smaller packets.")
(comment ConventionalClassificationType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ConventionalClassificationType is a collection that corresponds to a category in some agreed-upon or conventional classification system (see #$ClassificationSystem) used by people.  In such systems, a change or reclassification is possible by a decision of an authority, or by a changed social agreement or custom, without changing the intrinsic natures of the actual objects in the category.   #$ConventionalClassificationTypes include categories in biological taxonomy, standard classifications in data dictionaries and thesauri, cultural taboo classes, military doctrinal classes, and named calendar intervals.")
(comment Woolsorter "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation and a sub-collection of #$PersonWithOccupation. Each instance of #$Woolsorter is a worker whose job involves sorting wool, usually according to the fineness, length, and color of the wool fibers.")
(comment WaterJet "The collection of all water jets.  A water jet is a forceful stream of water, usually discharged through a narrow opening or nozzle.")
(comment Nursing "The field and occupation of #$Nursing, encompassing all the skills and tasks that #$Nurses do at work.")
(comment FlowerArrangementTypeBySeason "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$FlowerArrangementTypeBySeason is a collection of instances of #$FlowerArrangements that feature flowers and colors that are appropriate for a particular season.  The collection has exactly four instances, one for each #$CalendarSeasonType.")
(comment BallisticMissile-AlHussein "Efforts to extend the standard Scud B's (#$BallisticMissile-SCUDB) range began in the early 1980s as project 144, and in August 1987 Saddam announced that it had successfully tested a longer-range Scud, the Al Hussein (#$BallisticMissile-AlHussein), over a range of more than 500 km.")
(comment authenticationSourceFor "(#$authenticationSourceFor ?SOURCE-TYPE ?DEVICE) means that the authentication device ?DEVICE uses instances of the collection ?SOURCE-TYPE for purposes of authentication.  Note that ?SOURCE-TYPE is a  collection of collections of a certain type.")
(comment BedAndBreakfast " The collection of establishments that provide accomodations (a place to sleep) and breakfast for their customers in exchange for money.  They are typically converted private residences, with the owner(s) still living in them.")
(comment decreasesVulnerabilityTo "(decreasesVulnerabilityTo SITUATION OBJECT RESULT-TYPE) means that being in situation SITUATION decreases OBJECT's vulnerability to RESULT-TYPE.  This predicate is similar to #$makesVulnerableToDegree except that, unlike #$makesVulnerableToDegree, it expresses a relative decrease in OBJECT's vulnerability rather than an absolute degree of vulnerability.  It also resembles #$vulnerableIn, but there is an important difference that must be observed, namely that when using #$decreasesVulnerabilityTo one assumes that certain conditions coming into effect descrease vulnerability.  Therefore, it should not be used to declare vulnerabilities outright; Cyc should have to conlcude that a situation decreases an object's vulnerability to some result.")
(comment Prefecture "This is a collection of major geopolitical sub-regions analogous to a #$State-UnitedStates in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(disjointWith SexualProductOrServiceEvent TeenChatRoom)
(comment SimpleLogicCell "A primitive type of electrical device whose inputs and outputs are digital signals.")
(disjointWith UnidirectionalPartialRotation PeriodicReversingRotation)
(comment itemRepeatedlyCopied "(#$itemRepeatedlyCopied MASSREP IBT) means that IBT was copied
repeatedly in MASSREP.")
(comment averageDailyHighTemperature "(#$averageDailyHighTemperature REGION TEMP TYPE) means that during instances of TYPE, the average daily high temperature in the #$GeographicalRegion REGION is TEMP. Note that TYPE will often be a type of calendar time period, such as a subset of #$CalendarMonth.")
(comment UnderwritingOfMortgage "The collection of #$Underwritings in which an #$IntelligentAgent, who is a #$creditor on the relevant #$MortgageAgreement, accepts the risk of losing the funds borrowed in that #$MortgageAgreement, in return for payment in the form of interest and a #$Lien on the property.")
(comment Gum "#$Gum is the collection of all gum.  When moist, gum is like gel in many respects.  One way in which gum is NOT like gel is that wet gum is sticky and, as such, has adhesion properties and is less malleable than gel.")
(disjointWith StoringSomething Emission)
(disjointWith Painting-Activity (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(disjointWith WheeledTransportationDevice Snowmobile)
(comment histObject "(#$histObject ACT THING) relates THING (generally a referent) to a particular ACT request made to the history-list agent.  #$histObject is used as part of the cycorp dialog agents project.")
(comment CruiseMissile "A collection whose instances are #$Missiles which travel at low elevation, dodging fire if necessary, then climb, find the target with its own sensors, and make a final high-speed diving attack.  Although grouped with #$Missiles, #$CruiseMissiles are actually unmanned drone aircraft directed in flight by remote control.")
(comment bordersOn "(#$bordersOn REGION1 REGION2) means that the #$GeographicalRegions REGION1 and REGION2 are physically adjacent to each other and do not overlap, i.e. there is a border between them.  Examples: (#$bordersOn #$CentralUSATimeZone #$MountainUSATimeZone), (#$bordersOn (#$TerritoryFn #$Nepal) (#$TerritoryFn #$Tibet)).")
(comment AlternativeBeliefFn "(#$AlternativeBeliefFn FIELD) denotes the often loosely organized set of systems of belief which constitute the alternatives to a well-accepted #$FieldOfStudy FIELD. Each such term denotes a collection of #$BeliefSystems, each member of which has the normality attribute #$Alternative.")
(comment for-UnderspecifiedLocation "(#$for-UnderspecifiedLocation ACT GOALLOC) states that an
abstract locational relation holds between ACT and GOALLOC, where
GOALLOC is a target goal conceptualized as an abstract location.
#$for-UnderspecifiedLocation is thus a specialization of #$to-UnderspecifiedLocation 
that views the target location as a goal, abstract or physical.
Consider the difference between 'shampoo for greasy hair' and 
'shampoo for shiny hair': the former sees 'greasy hair'
as a geographical goal (i.e., apply the shampoo to greasy hair)
while the latter sees 'shiny hair' as a desired goal (i.e.,
apply this shampoo if you want shiny hair). This distinction is
a subtle one, and not one that can be captured adequately at the
level of lexical semantics. Thus we provide #$for-UnderspecifiedLocation to
indicate that GOALLOC should -- when it makes good 'pragmatic' sense 
to do so -- designate a goal rather than a physical destination.")
(comment genreHeyday "(#$genreHeyday GENRE HEYDAY) means that GENRE was at the height of its
  artistic and/or sociological significance during the entire #$TimeInterval HEYDAY.
  Given the vagueness of this notion, the #$arg2Format of this predicate is NOT
  #$SingleEntry.  But this much is clear: Before the start of HEYDAY GENRE either
  did not yet exist or did exist but was not yet near its peak of influence, and
  after the end of HEYDAY GENRE is either well past its artistic peak or no longer
  exists at all.  (Note that a genre may continue to exist long after its heyday.)")
(comment pathogenCausesCondition "This predicate relates an instance of #$PhysiologicalCondition
to the type of organism that caused it.")
(comment StaffOrganization-USArmy-BrigadeAndBattalion "A collection of staff organizations of the United States Army at
the level of brigades or battalions.")
(disjointWith ExpertSystemShell ExpertSystem)
(comment PassengerAircraft "The collection of aircraft designed and/or used primarily for carrying passengers.")
(comment Adenine-Base "A collection of molecules. #$Adenine-Base is one of the four kinds of nitrogen base, #$NitrogenBaseType, that enter in the constitution of instances of #$AdenineNucleotide. Its abbreviattion is A.")
(comment HepatitisC-Infection "A collection of Infections. A spec of #$ViralHepatitis. Instances of #$HepatitisC-Infection are viral infections caused by the hepatitis C virus, #$HepatitisC-Virus.")
(comment graduationDate " (#$graduationDate PERSON DEGREETYPE DATE) indicates that PERSON received an instance of DEGREETYPE during DATE.")
(comment expresses-Underspecified "(#$expresses-Underspecified EXP THING) is used to say -- abstractly or metaphorically -- that EXP is an \"expression\" of THING.  For example,  (#$expresses-Underspecified MyDogWaggingItsTail001 Joy) can be used to say that this particular instance of tail wagging is an expression of joy.  (#$relationAllInstance #$expresses-Underspecified #$HeavyMetalMusic TeenageAngst) could be used to say that heavy metal music is an expression of teenage angst.")
(comment Librarian "The collection of persons who manage and work in libraries")
(comment DisablingACommunicationDevice "The collection of all events in which a #$CommunicationDevice is rendered incapable of performing its #$primaryFunction, which is to communicate.  Such a disabling event might by performed by an agent, done automatically via the functioning of some device (e.g. a radio frequency scrambler), or caused by sheer accident (e.g. a tree branch falling on a telephone line).  Borderline example: a television fails due to a burned-out vacuum tube.  Negative examples: turning off the power to a radio, hanging up a telephone.")
(comment Spirochaetales-Order "A collection of #$ProkaryoticCells in the #$MoneraKingdom.
It includes the #$BiologicalFamily #$Spirochaetaceae-Family and
#$Treponemataceae-Family.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are helical cells
and #$Bacterium-MotileByFlagellum. They have a unique flagellum
struture. The flagellum originates at each end of the organism and
extend down the length of the cell and overlap.  These periplasmic
flagella are between the peptidoglycan layer and outer membrane.")
(comment LightFrigate "The collection of light frigate ships.")
(comment IndividualDenotingFunction "The subcollection of #$Function-Denotational whose instances, when applied to any appropriate

(sequence of) arguments, return instances of #$Individual.  Examples include #$PerimeterFn, #$GovernmentFn, and #$CavityInteriorRegionFn. See also the collections #$CollectionDenotingFunction and #$SetDenotingFunction.")
(comment GreetingCard "A type of (usually mass-manufactured and preprinted) correspondence, usually containing a message to commemorate or observe holidays or important events in a person's life.  #$GreetingCards can be textless when sold. ")
(comment countryFaxCode "ARG2 is a country fax code number for the country ARG1.  A country has only one country fax code number.")
(comment OrganizationOfFacilityFn "This is a functional analog of the #$orgFacilities
relation: (#$OrganizationOfFacilityFn PLACE) returns the instance of
#$Organization which operates out of PLACE.  The function is defined only if
one and only one #$Organization operates out of #$Place: i.e., only if there is an #$Organization such that it is appropriate to assert
(#$orgFacilities ORG PLACE).")
(comment ChildrensWebSite "The collection of #$WorldWideWebSites that have content which is geared toward children.")
(comment inventedThing "The predicate #$inventedThing is used to relate a particular invention event to the thing that is invented in that event. (#$inventedThing INVENTING INTANGIBLE) means that INTANGIBLE doesn't exist before INVENTING but comes into existence sometime during and as a result of INVENTING.")
(comment industryProducesType "(#$industryProducesType INDUSTRY PRODUCT-SPEC) means that PRODUCT-SPEC is a type of product produced by the #$Industry-Localized INDUSTRY.")
(disjointWith StateOfMatterChangeEvent Ablation)
(comment ElectronicWarfareCountermeasuresUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission is to utilize EM           energy to interfere with threat force communications via jamming           or deception.")
(comment SlantedOrientation "(orientation OBJECT #$SlantedOrientation) means that OBJECT is neither vertical nor horizontal with respect to the current instance of #$FrameOfReference.")
(comment denotationPlaceholder "(denotationPlaceholder WORD POS SENSE CONCEPT) indicates that a suitable #$denotation or #$denotationRelatedTo for WORD in part-of-speech POS and SENSE would be CONCEPT.")
(comment objectTypeDispersed "(#$objectTypeDispersed DISPERSAL TYPE) means that the

#$AerialDispersionEvent DISPERSAL includes many #$subEvents which are

instances of #$ConveyingMaterials in which the #$primaryObjectMoving

is an instance of TYPE.")
(comment conditionalProbabilitySet "A predicate used for probability statements. (#$conditionalProbabilitySet PROPOSITION SETOFPROPOSITIONS PROBNO) means that the probability of PROPOSITION being true, given that all the propositions in SETOFPROPOSITIONS are known to be true, in the applicable #$Microtheory, is PROBNO (a real number between zero and one, where zero means certainly false and one means certainly true).  In most microtheories, generally, this #$conditionalProbabilitySet refers to the conditional probability that PROPOSITION is true given only that the propositions in SETOFPROPOSITIONS, and the #$domainAssumptions accessible in the applicable #$Microtheory, are true, without regard to any further evidence or the truth of any other assertions.  See also #$conditionalProbability, #$priorProbability, #$derivedProbability, #$conditionallyIndependent, and the function version of this predicate: #$ConditionalProbabilitySetFn.  This definition makes no presumption as to determinism versus nondeterminism, nor as to whether probability is only in the mind of some beholder.  The definition allows for any of several different systems of deriving the probability of one assertion from the probabilities of, or conditional probabilities relating, other assertions.")
(comment VaccineAgainstMicroorganismFn "#$VaccineAgainstMicroorganismFn takes a type of #$Pathogenic #$Microorganism and returns the collection of #$Vaccines effective against it. See also #$VaccinationAgainstFn and #$vaccineEffectiveAgainstMicroorgType.")
(comment fileCopies "(#$fileCopies FILE COPY) means that the #$ComputerFileCopy COPY is a copy (e.g. on disk) of the abstract information that is the #$ComputerFile-AIS FILE.")
(comment AdvertisingCampaign "The collection of all extended, organized activity by which a group tries to convince others to buy, rent, attend, vote for, some product.")
(comment barometricPressure "(#$barometricPressure GAS PRESS) means that the instance of #$GaseousTangibleThing GAS has the #$Pressure PRESS.  Typically, GAS is a piece of atmosphere; #$barometricPressure indicates the atmospheric pressure in and around that `object'.")
(comment CycTheCollection "A specialization of (#$ProgramTypeCopyFn #$IntelligentComputerProgram) and (#$ProgramTypeCopyFn #$InteractiveComputerProgram). Each instance of #$CycTheCollection is a copy (see #$programCopies) of #$CycProgram. Instances of #$CycTheCollection include all of the copies of #$CycProgram on storage media (see #$CycCopy) or running on computers (either #$CycAgent or #$CycImage) at any time in history. A notable instance of this #$CycAgent is #$Cyc, which is the agentive copy of #$CycTheCollection that one is currently running and using.")
(comment USStateGovernment "A collection of regional governments.  An element of #$USStateGovernment is a State government of one of the fifty states of the United States of America.")
(comment waveSource-Direct "The predicate #$waveSource-Direct is used to indicate that there is a wave propagation of some type directly between two points.  (#$waveSource-Direct SOURCE ENDPOINT WAVETYPE) means that there is a #$WavePropagation of type WAVETYPE between the #$fromLocation SOURCE and the #$toLocation ENDPOINT, and the propagation is direct in the sense that there are no significant diffusion or reflection subevents of that #$WavePropagation.")
(comment WaveReflectionFn "#$WaveReflectionFn is a Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$WaveReflectionFn WAVETYPE) denotes the collection of events in which #$WavePropagations of the type WAVETYPE are reflected from some object.")
(comment HealthCarePayer "Instances are agents which pay for health care goods and services, such as HMOs, PPOs, medical insurance companies, Medicaid organizations and even individual patients.")
(comment DowntownFn "(#$DowntownFn CITY) denotes the instance of
#$Downtown (if any) within CITY.")
(disjointWith CalendarSecond PolarNight)
(comment SubcollectionOfByFn "(#$SubcollectionOfByFn COLLECTION AGENT) describes the collection of all instances of COLLECTION which are created by AGENT (see #$createdBy).")
(comment ElectricPowerGrid "A specialization of #$ConstructionArtifact and #$SpatialPathSystem.  Each instance of #$ElectricPowerGrid is an electrical power supply system dedicated to satisfying the electrical power requirements of a population center which may be a #$City or a similar agglomeration of #$HumanOccupationConstructs.  Paths within instances of #$ElectricPowerGrid will ordinarily be instances of #$ElectricalConduit.  Power grids also will ordinarily include transformers (see #$TransformerSubstation), generators (see #$ElectricalGenerator), instances of #$ElectricalTerminal, and stations for monitoring the overall stability of the grid.")
(comment Atenolol "The chemical compound which is a beta blocker.  This drug is intended to be used for a non-initial therapeutic treatment of hypertension.")
(comment CoercingAnAgent "A collection of #$Actions; a specialization of #$InfluencingAnAgent.  A paradigm example of coercion is influencing an agent's behavior through a successful (implicit or explicit) threat.")
(comment GrantingMostFavoredNationStatus "The collection of events in which a country grants most favored nation trading status to another country.  That is, the first country engages not to subject the second to tariffs any higher than the lowest level applied by the first to any other country.")
(comment Franc-Swiss "The monitary unit in Switzerland and #$Liechtenstein.")
(comment Pyrotechnics-Manufacturing "This is the collection of events in which a #$PyrotechnicDevice is manufactured.

(See #$PyrotechnicDevice.)")
(disjointWith LegalCode Tax-COC)
(comment TurnipPlant "Inidividual turnip plants.")
(disjointWith Pipe-GenericConduit HumanOccupationConstruct)
(comment MortarLauncher "Cannon for firing projectiles at low muzzle speed on a high trajectory.")
(comment TableGame "All instances of games that are played on a table, including #$Billiards, #$DominoesGame, and #$TableTennisGame.")
(comment connected-EdgeToEdge "(#$connected-EdgeToEdge SHEET OBJ) means that a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET1, is #$connected-EdgeToEdge to another #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET2, such that the sheets extend away from each other.")
(comment emperor "The country who has this person as emperor")
(disjointWith FillingAPrescription FinancialInstrumentTrading)
(comment SandMob "An instances of #$TangibleStuffStateType, and a  specialization of #$Soil-Generic.  Each instance of #$SandMob is a portion of loose granular material that results from the disintegration of rocks, consisting of particles smaller than gravel but coarser than silt.")
(comment WetTShirtPicture "A subset of #$PornographicPictures.  These are pictures of women who wear wet t-shirts, which reveal the contours of their body underneath.")
(comment interArg3ResultIsa "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$isa based relationship holds between the third argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg3ResultIsa FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the third argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 ARG2 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg3ResultIsa _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultIsa.")
(comment KidneyStoneCondition "An ailment characterized by the build-up of kidney-stones in the body.")
(disjointWith TruthPreservingReformulation TruthAlteringReformulation)
(disjointWith SingleRecording-CW Album-CW)
(comment IndecentExposure "The collection of #$SexualHarassment in which somebody exposes his/her erogenous parts to somebody else.")
(comment OkraPlant "Individual okra plants.")
(comment ParanormalEvent "The collection of all events that cannot be explained by scientific means.")
(comment aligned-EdgeAlongCylinder "(#$aligned-EdgeAlongCylinder SHEET CYL) means that a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET, is #$alignedAlongEdge to the outside surface of #$LongAndThin object CYL along its length.")
(comment SkiEquipmentPackage "Skis, boots, poles.")
(comment ScissorBridgeTruck "A collection of #$MilitaryVehicles.  A scissor bridge truck transports and deploys a scissor bridge (consisting of hinged sections that can be folded together).  The reach of the bridge deployed by a scissor bridge truck (about 28 meters) is longer than that of an #$ArmoredVehicleLaunchedBridge (q.v.).")
(comment PeriodicalSeries "The collection of all static textual #$MediaSeriesProducts that come out on a regular basis.  The #$PeriodicalSeries is not created at one time, but #$PeriodicalIssue are produced on a somewhat regular basis.")
(comment Neodymium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of neodymium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.  This unit could probably just as well be called Neodymium or NeodymiumStuff")
(comment StockIndexGroup "A collection of #$Groups, each element of which is a group of #$LegalCorporations having #$Stocks that are #$PubliclyTradedSecurity(s).  A #$StockIndexGroup can have as #$groupMembers any #$LegalCorporation.  The index measure of the market price of the #$Stocks for the group is used as a measure of the market value for a particular pattern of investing.  Well-known #$StockIndexGroups are the #$StandardAndPoors500 and the #$DowJonesIndustrials.  To state the value of a #$StockIndexGroup, or 'stock index', use #$stockIndexValue.")
(comment ClearGlass "glass that is clear, not opaque or colored")
(comment causes-ThingProp "(#$causes-ThingProp THING PROP) means that THING causes the proposition PROP to become true.  THING may be an #$Agent, a #$Situation, or  a #$ELSentence-Assertible.  This is a very general predicate.  It is almost always better to use a more specialized predicate such as #$causes-PropProp, #$causes-EventEvent, or #$causes-SitProp, particularly in rules.  Nonetheless, #$causes-ThingProp can be useful if one wishes to collect all the possible causes of some proposition be they #$Situations, #$Agents, other propositions (see #$ELSentence-Assertible).  See #$NoteAboutCausalityPredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(comment HistoricTemporalThing "The collection of all events, people, objects, periods, etc. which are considered to have historical significance.  The membership in this collection depends upon time, place, and culture.")
(comment MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory "Each instance of #$MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory contains static background information that is relevant to a particular class of #$MilitaryOperations - operations involving some particular unit or units against some particular enemy unit or units, in some specific geographical region, etc. The information in each #$MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory is information that will remain the same no matter what the specifics of the course of action are. Such information typically will include geographical facts, e.g., location of mountains, rivers, etc., political facts, if they are relevant, assets available for the course of action, etc. Each #$MilitaryOperationsStaticSituationMicrotheory inherits information from ModernMilitaryTacticsMt.  For situation information which changes more frequently, see #$MilitaryOperationsDynamicSituationMicrotheory")
(comment VirtualReality "A hypothetical three-dimensional visual world created by a computer; user wears special goggles and fiber optic gloves etc., and can enter and move about in this world and interact with objects as if inside it.")
(comment EnterobacterCloacae "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$Bacterium have a natural resistence to ampicillin.  Most important tests for identification are LDC-negative, OCD- and ADH-positive.")
(comment NarrativeTVShow-CW "#$NarrativeTVShow-CW is the collection of all #$TVShow-CWs that are also #$Narratives. Thus, #$NarrativeTVShow-CWs tell a story and represent a structured sequence of events. Typically, the actors playing roles in a #$NarrativeTVShow-CW follow a script that describes the sequence of action and spoken lines. #$SoapOperas are positive examples of #$NarrativeTVShow-CW, whereas #$TVGameShows and #$LiveSportsTVShows are negative examples. #$NarrativeTVShow-CW can be characterized using the predicate #$hasAttributes and an instance of #$NarrativeGenre. Most #$NarrativeTVShow-CWs are instances of #$FictionalTVShow-CW. However, #$TVDocumentary and #$TVBiography are nonfictional #$NarrativeTVShow-CWs.")
(comment CharacterStringToken-Serial "A specialization of both #$CharacterStringToken and
  #$SeriesWithoutRepetition each of whose instances thus (1) 
  #$tokensString a certain character-string and (2) is itself a series 
  of instances of #$CharacterToken.  Most inscribed and electromagnetic 
  character-string tokens are serial (see #$CharacterStringToken-Inscribed
  and #$CharacterStringToken-ElectroMagnetic).  Conversely, most sounded 
  character-string tokens are not serial, as they cannot normally 
  be divided into discrete sounded character tokens (see
  #$CharacterStringToken-Sounded).  Inscribed 
  serial string tokens are instances of #$PhysicalSeries, and are 
  #$seriesOrderedBy instances of #$SpatialPredicate.
  Sounded serial string tokens, though rare, do ostensibly occur, 
  for example, when words are \"spelled aloud\" or when one recites 
  the alphabet; they are #$seriesOrderedBy instances of 
  #$TemporalPredicate.  An example of an inscribed character-string 
  token that is not serial is an illegible signature that cannot be 
  divided into discrete inscribed character tokens.  A given serial 
  string token T #$tokensString a particular string S just in case 
  each of the component character tokens in T #$tokensCharacter the 
  corresponding component character in S (and T and S are the 
  same length).")
(comment RemoteExecutableRootExploit "The collection of #$MaliciousComputerPrograms that allow
remote users who have not already cracked a user account to get root
access to computers.")
(comment LSD "Lysergic acid diethylamide - a hallucinogenic agent.")
(comment ruleTemplateDirection "A #$MetaKnowledgePredicate. (#$ruleTemplateDirection TEMPLATE DIRECTION) states that all assertions which are instantiations of TEMPLATE should  have a direction of DIRECTION.")
(comment KMartStore "A collection of all the local KMart stores. ")
(comment MatraMica-AirToAirMissile "A kind of 

#$AirToAirMissile currently (2000) used by 

#$France (who designed it) as well as 

  #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina.")
(disjointWith Cavity Agent-Generic)
(comment NthInListFn "An instance of both #$EvaluatableFunction and #$PartialFunction.  For each LIST in #$List with length M (i.e., (#$LengthOfListFn LIST) = M), and for each #$PositiveInteger N that is less than or equal to M, (#$NthInListFn LIST N) is the member of LIST that occurs at the Nth position of LIST.  For example, given that LIST = (#$TheList A B C D A E F), (#$NthInListFn LIST 1) = A, (#$NthInListFn LIST 2) = B, (#$NthInListFn LIST 5) = A and (#$NthInListFn LIST 7) = F.  Note that when N is greater than the length of LIST or LIST is #$TheEmptyList, then (#$NthInListFn LIST N) is undefined.")
(comment ProjectileSlug-Incendiary "The collection of #$ProjectileSlug-Bullets that contains an incendiary composition.")
(disjointWith Elasticity Density)
(comment expenseFor "The ternary predicate #$expenseFor relates an agent to an event in which the agent incurs some expense, and to the amount of the expense incurred in that event. (#$expenseFor AGENT EVENT AMOUNT) means that AGENT's expense for EVENT is AMOUNT. Note that AMOUNT can be AGENT's expense for EVENT even if AGENT has not yet paid that expense. That is, AMOUNT can be an unpaid debt that AGENT incurs in EVENT.")
(comment AnalogyMapping "An #$AnalogyMapping is a construal of a comparison between base and target #$AnalogyCases.  It consists of a set

of correspondences, and a set of candidate inferences.  The set of correspondences (see #$AnalogyCorrespondence) indicate what specific entities and statements in one description go with what others in this construal of the comparison.  The set of candidate inferences indicate the conjectures that this analogy suggests, based on the correspondences.")
(comment SportsChatRoom "the collection of #$ChatRooms in which 

 users chat about sports.")
(comment TranssexualPerson-PreOperation "A collection of #$Persons. A #$TranssexualPerson-PreOperation is a #$Person who has undergone initial treatment in order to attain the physical characteristics of the opposite sex, but who has not had the primary genital surgery operation for this.")
(comment Fog "The collection of clouds (instances of #$CloudOfH2O) that cover a #$GeographicalRegion at ground-level.")
(comment mtJustificationType "(#$mtJustificationType MT JUST) means that all assertions in MT are supported by justifications of type JUST.")
(comment Team "#$Team is a specialization of #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly and #$ActivityTypeFocusGroup.  A #$Team may be a commercial, professional team supported by a large full-time staff, or simply a #$Group of people who got together for playing a game for a single time, or something in between. Organized #$Teams which play sports at least semi-regularly are instances of the narrower concept, #$SportsTeam.")
(disjointWith Place DrugSubstance)
(comment Tablet-21DaySupply "The collection of #$TabletDrugs intended for packaging into 21-day-supply packages.")
(comment SkinAilment "The collection of all #$AilmentConditions that primarily afflict the #$Skin.")
(comment HingedJoint "The hinged connection")
(comment Moxibustion "A collection of events.  #$Moxibustion is counterirritation produced by placing on the skin and igniting a cone or cylinder of moxa, a tuft of soft combustible substance popularly used in the #$FarEastAsia-Region as a cautery or counterirritant.")
(comment MostNotableEruptionOfFn "#$MostNotableEruptionOfFn is a function. (#$MostNotableEruptionOfFn VOLCANO) denotes the best known eruption of VOLCANO.  See also #$mostNotableEruptionDate.")
(comment BuyingFn "A #$ReifiableFunction used to denote collections of events in which objects or services of a specified type are bought/sold.  (#$BuyingFn ITEM-TYPE) denotes the collection of events in which instances of the collection ITEM-TYPE are bought/sold. For example, (#$BuyingFn #$Cookie) denotes the collection of all events in which cookies are purchased.")
(comment planResourceQuantForTime "(#$planResourceQuantForTime PLAN STUFFTYPE QUANT TEMPTYPE) means that in an execution of PLAN the executing agent needs to have control of quantity QUANT of some stuff of type STUFFTYPE for the duration of an event of type TEMPTYPE in the plan execution, in order for the execution to be #$successfulForAgents.--Rode, May 26, 1999")
(comment AntiTankGuidedWeapon "The collection of guided missiles which have armor penetration capabilities and are used against tanks.")
(comment Asteroid "The collection of all chunks of rock which orbit our Sun.  In AstronomyMt this collection might also include asteroids outside the Solar System.")
(comment Budesonide "The chemical compound which is used in nasal inhalant products.")
(comment MultiWordForFormulaPred "The specialization of #$MultiWordPhrasePredicate whose instances map phrases to #$NLTemplateExpressions.  See also #$MultiWordForConstantPred.")
(comment densityOfObject "(#$densityOfObject OBJ DENS) means that the tangible thing OBJ has the #$Density DENS.")
(disjointWith MilitaryOrganization SellingOrganization)
(comment Petal "A petal is a specialized leaf; collectively a set of petals comprise a flower's corolla; they are often conspicuously colored to attract insects.")
(disjointWith PulverizationEvent LosingALeaf)
(comment DenialOfServiceFault "#$DenialOfServiceFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if the program can be forced into a denial of service mode either remotely or at the console.")
(comment Emission "A specialization of #$TransferOut.  Each instance of #$Emission is an event in which something `comes out' of a source, where the source in question causally contributes to that thing's `coming out' (e.g., the source is a #$providerOfMotiveForce).  The source of the emission is indicated with the predicate #$emitter.  If the thing which `comes out' is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible, then the event belongs to a more specific collection, #$EmittingAnObject. If an emission is the first sub-event of an instance of #$WavePropagation, then the emission belongs to the more specialized collection, #$EmittingAWave.")
(comment ChamberMusicEnsemble "#$ChamberMusicEnsemble is a collection of #$MusicPerformanceOrganizations who perform #$ChamberMusicCompositions. One notable subcollection is #$StringQuartet-MusicGroup. Since #$ChamberMusicCompositions are usually scored for between two and eight instruments, #$ChamberMusicEnsembles range in size between two and eight members.")
(comment Pseudomonadales-Order "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom that includes the #$Psuedomonadaceae-Family and #$Nitrobacteraceae-Family.")
(comment TakingRefuge "The collection of #$ChangeOfResidence events where the performer is a #$Refugee, changing residence because of adversity.")
(comment PullingAnObject "Using a force to tend to move something (#$pullee) towards the #$puller.  If the #$pullee moves, it is a case of the more specific, #$PullingAnObjectAlong (which has significant specializations #$PullingAnObjectCloser and PullingAnObjectAlongWith).  If the #$puller moves and the #$pullee does not, it is a case of #$PullingOneselfTowards.  If neither the #$puller nor #$pullee moves, it is a case of #$PullingWithoutTranslation.  If the force causes the #$pullee to stretch, it is a case of #$Pulling-Stretching.")
(comment AudioBook-CW "The collection of #$AudioConceptualWorks,

 recorded on tape or CD, which are usually #$derivedConceptualWorks

 of #$Book-CW or #$LiteraryWork-CW.  For example, an audio version 

of #$MobyDickNovel would be #$MobyDick-AudioBook; it is necessary to

show that the audio book is derived from the novel.")
(comment PunctureWound "Bullet wounds, stab wounds etc.")
(comment grievanceInDispute "(#$grievanceInDispute DISPUTE AGENT ISSUE) means that ISSUE is a grievance or complaint which is prompting AGENT to be involved in DISPUTE. 'Grievances' as understood here can be   involved in both formal and informal conflicts (lawsuits, physical confrontations, etc.).  ISSUE can be a state of affairs that AGENT wishes to change -- e.g.,

an agent's complaint in a lawsuit or contract dispute -- or a state of affairs with respect to which AGENT is seeking revenge, restitution, punishment, etc. In the case of the U.S. criminal justice system, a charge against a defendant can be considered a 'grievance' of the prosecuting agent.")
(comment Paralysis-Generic "The collection of conditions in which one loses the ability to move, have motor control over, and/or have sensation in some part of the body. Typically one should introduce or use a specialization of this collection to specify the extent of the paralysis, i.e., the body parts affected.")
(comment RefiningFn "A function that returns a specialization of #$Refining when given an instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType. (#$RefiningFn STUFF) denotes the collection of events in which STUFF is refined.")
(comment WebSearchResultPage "#$WebSearchResultPage is a subset of  #$WebPage-AIS. Each #$WebSearchResultPage consists primarily of a list of links into other web pages which was dynamically created and returned as the result of some web search. The links may or may not be related by some subject area, due to the lack of accuracy of many search engines (which is, in turn, partly due to the ambiguity of typical string-based search requests).  Many instances of #$WebSearchResultPage are created by professional search sites such as hotbot.com.")
(comment VaginalYeastInfection "An often chronic ailment whereby yeast microorganisms flourish beyond control in the vagina, often due to the absence of certain bacterial flora.")
(comment FuneralGift "An instance of #$GiftTypeByOccasion.  The collection of #$Gifts that are appropriate to bring to a #$Funeral.")
(comment quarantineLocation "(#$quarantineLocation QUARANTINE REGION) means that every individual which has been confined in accordance with QUARANTINE is found in REGION, where REGION is a region designated for such confinement, according to the standards of QUARANTINE.")
(comment infoStructureRepresentsPIT "(#$infoStructureRepresentsPIT INFO_STRUCT PIT) means that the #$AbstractInformationStructure INFO_STRUCT encodes information in the #$PropositionalInformationThing, PIT.")
(comment Curium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Curium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment isAContraryFactorFor "(#$isAContraryFactorFor FACTOR AGENT ACT_TYPE) means that in the
given circumstances FACTOR would cause AGENT's likelihood of success in
doing actions that are tokens of ACT_TYPE to be lower, i.e., the
conditional probability of AGENT's succeeding at ACT_TYPE given FACTOR is
less than it would be if FACTOR did not obtain. In other words, FACTOR
brings it about that the #$derivedProbability of the proposition expressed
by 'A would be successful at ACT_TYPE_TOKEN if she tried' is
decreased. Note that 'being a contrary factor' in this sense is relative to
the given circumstances: in the present, ordinary circumstances not having
coffee readily available might be a contrary factor for Julia to make a
successful presentation, but things might well be different in a state
of affairs where Julia has slept for 3 straight days and is fully
rested.")
(comment DictionaryFn "#$DictionaryFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. (#$DictionaryFn LANGUAGE) represents the spec of #$Dictionary whose elements are dictionaries of LANGUAGE that are written in LANGUAGE.  For example, (#$DictionaryFn #$SpanishLanguage) denotes the collection of Spanish dictionaries.  Note that the #CollectionDenotingFunction #$DictionaryFromToFn should be used to represent the collection of dictionaries that are used to translate between two languages.")
(comment MultiplayerOnlineRolePlayingGame "This is the collection of role-playing computer games which are played over the internet. All of these games have the genre attribute 

 #$RolePlayingGameGenre. An example of such a game is #$AsheronsCall-TheGame.")
(comment HailStone "A specialization of #$PrecipitationParticle.  Instances of #$HailStone are small particles emitted from clouds in instances of #$HailProcess (q.v.).  Instances of #$HailStone usually consist of several concentric layers of ice.")
(comment informationUsed "(#$informationUsed EVENT INFO) means that INFO plays an instrumental role in EVENT, serving the purpose of some agent.  For example, the \"doer\" of EVENT may use INFO to initiate or guide EVENT or one of its subevents (as when someone uses a computer program to compose a document).  Or the \"doer\" of EVENT may be guided in EVENT by INFO (as when someone follows instructions). See also the predicate #$ibtUsed, which relates instances of #$Event to instances of #$InformationBearingThing.")
(comment overlappingAddresses "ARG1 and ARG2 are variations of `the same' address. This is a specialized predicate intended primarily for database querying.")
(comment eventSequence "(#$eventSequence (#$TheList FORM_1 FORM_2 ... FORM_n)) means that the actions

described by the event formulas FORM_i were performed in the order

indicated.  Each FORM_i should be an atomic formula whose predicate is

an instance of #$EventPredicate.")
(comment LexicalAffix "A subcollection of #$WordConstituent (q.v.).  #$LexicalAffix is the collection of all natural language affixes.  A lexical affix is a \"bound\" morpheme: it cannot appear in a phrase without being \"bound to\" (i.e. concatenated with) another lexical item.  (Cf. #$LexicalWord.)  For further details, see the various specializations of #$LexicalAffix. ")
(comment Bacillales-Order "An instance of a #$BiologicalOrder in the #$Firmicutes-Division of the #$MoneraKingdom that contains the #$BiologicalFamily #$Bacillaceae-Family.")
(comment BiologicalWeapon-GeneticallyEngineeredOrganismBased "The collection of all #$BiologicalWeapons that make use of genetically engineered #$BiologicalAgents. In general, any spec of #$BiologicalWeapon-GeneticallyEngineeredOrganismBased will be a spec of some other instance of #$BiologicalWeaponTypeByAgent.")
(disjointWith MissileLauncher Tank-Vehicle)
(comment ChemicalAttack "The collection of events in which a chemical weapon is used against a #$PartiallyTangible target.")
(comment Injecting-Subcutaneous "Injecting a fluid, usually containing a drug, beneath the skin.")
(comment MiddleVoiceFrame "This frame is used for verbs which can appear in the middle voice. Middles are syntactically intransitive constructions in which the subject position in filled by the object affected by the action. The semantic agent of a middle is unspecified. For example, in the middle construction 'This material rips easily', the subject is the object affected by the ripping and the agent of the action is unspecified. This construction is syntactically parallel to other (non-middle) intransitives such as 'The man walks quickly' but the semantic role of the subject is different.")
(comment WillEvaporate "Substance will evaporate, but not quickly, e.g. WaterInDansGlass.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn FourthRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment sovereignAllegianceOfOrg "(#$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg MIL-UNIT COUNTRY) means

          that the military unit MIL-UNIT owes allegiance to COUNTRY.

          This predicate relates a military organization to whatever sovereign

          agency is ultimately responsible for its creation. The agency is

          usually an instance of #$IndependentCountry. For example, the 101st

          Airborne Division has as its #$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg the

          #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica. However, the first argument need not be

          an instance of #$IndependentCountry : military and paramilitary

          forces can be organized by corporations (e.g., the

          Freeport-MacMoRan security force in Indonesia) or even by

          individuals (e.g., the Duvaliers' Tonton Macoutes).

          #$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg is also a different concept from

          'assignment' and/or 'attachment' in a command-and-control

          structure. An American battalion might be placed under temporary

          UN command in an international action. However, the

          #$sovereignAllegianceOfOrg would remain the

          #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment OptionsField-Packet "An #$OptionsField-Packet can include various optional
information about the #$Packet-Internet and its routing information.")
(comment pathTrafficableForTransportVia "(#$pathTrafficableForTransportVia PATH O-TYPE) means that PATH is #$behaviorCapable of playing the role of #$motionPathway-Complete in all instances of #$TransportationEvent in which instances of O-TYPE play the role of #$transporter.  Furthermore, O-TYPE is #$typeBehaviorCapable of playing the role of #$transporter in all instances of #$TransportationEvent in which PATH plays the role of #$motionPathway-Complete.")
(comment ManMadeDisaster "The collection of those elements of #$DisasterEvent that are caused by humans. Positive examples are chemical spills or bombings. Negative examples include earthquakes and droughts, which are instances of #$NaturalDisaster.")
(comment reportID "(#$reportID REPORT STRING) means that STRING is a uniquifying tag used to identify and track REPORT.")
(comment IndexedInformationSource "The collection of all structured  information sources in which the information contained therein  is indexed by some set of index terms (the terms could be names, phrases, #$CharacterStrings,  #$IDNumbers or codes).   For every index term, there is one  specific part of the #$IndexedInformationSource associated with that  term.  Each instance of #$IndexedInformationSource has some format  or organizing structure of specified parts or 'chunks' imposed on the information.    (Although its indexed parts might be  be ordered in a certain sequence, in theory it could be indexed without  there being any particular sequential ordering of the parts.)  An instance of #$IndexedInformationSource  is the abstract informational content of the source, not any  particular physical object in which the information is stored.   Examples include a #$Dictionary, #$Thesaurus,  #$Database-AbstractContent, or a #$KnowledgeBase.  Some examples  that do not qualify are #$Painting-ArtForm, or a #$CharacterString  without any structuring information about it or that has no  structure beyond being a string of characters.   Thus this is not referring to unstructured text, even if it has an 'Index'.  The fact that a book has an index does not make it an #$IndexedInformationSource.")
(comment ChemicalPurity "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity. Each element of #$ChemicalPurity is a measure of the degree to which a substance consists of a single kind of #$ChemicalSubstanceType.")
(comment PlowingAField "The collection of events in which a field is plowed.")
(comment RoseBouquet "An instance of #$FlowerArrangementTypeByFlower.  An instance of #$RoseBouquet is a #$FlowerArrangement consisting primarily of #$RoseFlowers.")
(comment AuthenticationSourceType "#$AuthenticationSourceType is the collection of types of sources instances of which can be used           for authentication events.  For example, instances of #$Fingerprint are used to authenticate            a person's identity.")
(comment AcademicTesting "The collection of #$PerformanceTesting events in which some #$IntelligentAgent measures some aspect of another agent's academic achievement using a generic method to collect and analyze the relevant data.  #$AcademicTests are generic in the sense that individual such tests are not tailored to the person tested.  They typically consist of a series of questions that the student must answer.")
(comment FederalDistrict "The collection of all federal districts.  Each instance of #$FederalDistrict is a #$CountrySubsidiary which answers directly to the government of the #$Country without being part of any intermediate body.  A #$FederalDistrict usually contains the #$capitalCity of the #$Country.")
(comment TeenChatRoom "the collection of #$ChatRooms designed 

 especially for use by #$HumanTeenagers only.")
(comment ClockedLogicCell "The type of electrical device that accepts a clocked input.")
(comment PeriodicReversingRotation "The collection of events which are mobs whose granule is a turn in one direction followed by a stop, direction reversal, a reverseEvent to the initial one, a second stop, and a second direction reversal.  A single return to the starting position does not constitute a #$PeriodicReversingRotation")
(comment OccasionCard "The subcollection of #$GreetingCard consisting of

those cards which are intended for specific occasions, such as anniversaries

and birthdays, a person's being sick, moving away, graduating, etc. Cards intended for specific holidays are not #$OccasionCards

but rather #$HolidayCards.")
(comment ignore-Temporary-ForRKFTool "This predicate serves as a wrapper for rules that would normally be used as ke suggestions, see #$keFacilitationRules, but whose form results in an undesirable user prompt at present.  (ignoreAtPresentForRKFTool FORM) does not mean that FORM is incorrect or fails to state a legitimate knowledge entry expectation, however, the natural language that it results in is very awkward and therefore not worthy of demo inclusion.  This should serve as a flag for further NL work or perhaps the creation of simpler vocabulary to represent the salient content.  This predicate, once it is incorporated into tool function, should be used to hide assertions causing problems for impending demos.")
(comment BookCWsAboutFn "(#$BookCWsAboutFn TOPIC) is the collection of

 all instances of #$Book-CW about TOPIC.  Do not use this function to talk

 about physical copies of books about Topic, only to talk about books in the 

sense of #$PropositionalConceptualWork.")
(comment Socializing "This collection involves events of social interaction in a social setting. Instances usually have #$Communicating subevents, but communicating needn't be the primary subactivity. Instead, two people hanging out together drinking at a bar or dancing at a nightclub could be an instance of socializing, with or without conversation. The context of these events is a social context, therefore business meetings, commercial exchanges, interactions with the dental receptionist, etc. are not examples of #$Socializing, unless there is some non-official (i.e. social) purpose for the agents spending time together.--Causley, March 22, 1999")
(comment JetOfFluid "A straight long and thin region of fluid which is in a fluid that is moving relative to its fluid surroundings.  Thus their are water jets in whirlpools, air  jets at the exhaust of jet engines.  I guess we want to say that car exhaust usually does not jet out of the tail pipe (unless of course you are driving the Batmobile).")
(disjointWith ChangeInUserRights Emission)
(comment AdviceFn "#$AdviceFn takes as argument any spec of #$Thing and returns the collection of all tips and pieces of advice about things of that type.  For example, (#$AdviceFn #$ComputerGameProgram) returns the collection of all tips and pieces of advice about computer games, and (#$AdviceFn (#$MakingFn #$Beer)) returns the collection of all tips and pieces of advice about making beer.")
(comment holdsInPlace-Everywhere "(#$holdsInPlace-Everywhere MT PLACE) means that the assertions in MT are true throughout the entire spatial extent of PLACE.  See also #$holdsInPlace-Somewhere.")
(comment TrainCar "#$TrainCar is a specialization of #$WheeledTransportationDevice and #$TransportationContainerProduct.  Each instance of #$TrainCar is a non-motorized wheeled vehicle that runs on #$Railways (q.v.).  When instances of #$TrainCar are to be moved, they are coupled together to form trains pulled by train engines.  There are freight #$TrainCars, and passenger #$TrainCars for transporting people.")
(disjointWith CruiseMissile Spacecraft)
(comment keGenlsRelevantInverse "This is, by definition, the most general instance of a

certain kind of #$KEFacilitationPredicate.  Its specializations

include #$keGenlsStrongSuggestionInverse, #$keGenlsConsiderationInverse,

#$keGenlsWeakSuggestionInverse and, of course, any

specializations of those predicates.  #$keGenlsRelevantInverse was created

mainly for practical reasons, i.e., to use in situations where one

might want to consider the disjunction of its specializations.  See

the comments on the specializations for clearer explanations.")
(comment HollowCylindricalObject "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleThing; instances are characterized

by a cylindrical, single-walled structure and a hollow interior.

Examples include #$GunBarrels and #$Bottles.  The structure

in question must be 'long' enough to justify the appelation of 'hollow'.

Borderline non-cases might include two-dimensional ringlike structures like

wedding-rings.")
(comment MensSportsTeam "the collection of all #$SportsTeams whose members are

   #$AdultMalePersons.  This collection enables one to

   reify types of sports teams on the fly; e.g., the collection 

    of all mens basketball teams is (#$CollectionIntersection2Fn 

  #$BasketballTeam #$MensSportsTeam).")
(comment Vaccine "A preparation of killed microorganisms, living attenuated organisms, or living fully virulent organisms that is administered to produce immunity to a particular disease.")
(comment DribblingProcess "During instances of #$DribblingProcess the flow stream is irregular, although mostly continuous.")
(comment InterExchangeAccessCarrierCompany "A long distance carrier company that sells inter-exchange service to the regional telephone companies")
(comment infectingOrganismMob "This predicate relates a physiological condition to the mob of microorganisms that caused the physiological condition.  Note that this can relate to the ailment conditions associated with an infection as well as the infection itself.")
(comment StaffOrganization-USArmy-CorpsAndDivision "A collection of staff organizations of the United States Army at
the level of corps or divisions.")
(disjointWith IntelligentComputerProgram ExpertSystemShell)
(comment CommercialAirplaneTransportation "Commercial air transport of humans or cargo")
(comment Guanine-Base "A collection of molecules. #$Guanine-Base is one of the four kinds of nitrogen base [#$NitrogenBaseType] which enter in the constitution of instances of #$GuanineNucleotide. Its abbreviation is G.")
(comment percentOfIndividual "(#$percentOfIndividual PART INDIVIDUAL PERCENT) means that PART is PERCENT percent of INDIVIDUAL. Example: (#$percentOfIndividual (#$PercentOfFn ApplePie001 50) ApplePie001 (#$Percent 50)) means that  (#$PercentOfFn ApplePie001 50) is 50% of ApplePie001.")
(comment HepatitisD-Infection "A collection of Infections. A spec of #$ViralHepatitis. Instances of #$HepatitisD-Infection are viral infections caused by the hepatitis D virus, see #$HepatitisD-Virus.")
(comment TermPhrasesConstraint "The collection of all Cyc terms that can serve as the second argument to 
#$termPhrases (q.v.).")
(comment LightGuidedMissileFrigate "The collection of military light frigates intended for use in carrying and launching guided missiles.")
(comment W2-Form "In some American-related Mt, the document stating how much an employer paid an employee in a calendar year.")
(comment Polonium "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of polonium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment FaintingEvent "The collection of events in which a person loses consciousness and physically collapses.  Fainting occurs as a result of various causes, including physical shocks and strong emotions of surprise, grief, or fear.")
(comment OfficialReportType "A collection of all collections of #$OfficialReports.")
(comment LAV-25 "A collection of all-terrain, all-weather vehicles.  It is air transportable aboard C-130, C-141, C-5 and CH-53 E.  They are equipped with M242 chain gun and a 7.62mm machine gun.  When combat-ready, these vehicles have 210 ready rounds and 420 stowed rounds of 25mm ammunition, 400 ready rounds and 1200 stowed rounds of 7.62mm ammunition, and 8 ready rounds and 8 stowed rounds of smoke grenades.  These vehicles are fully amphibious with 3 minutes preperation, maximum.")
(disjointWith StateOfMatterChangeEvent AttachmentEvent)
(comment SemipreciousStone "#$GemStones which are typically used for adornment. #$SemipreciousStones are generally considered not quite as beautiful, rare, or durable as #$PreciousStones, and are usually less expensive.")
(comment ElectronicWarfareSupportUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile is to           provide logistical support to electronic warfare units.")
(comment considersAsHome "(#$considersAsHome PERSON PLACE) means that PERSON considers PLACE his or her home, regardless of whether or not PERSON happens to reside in PLACE (see #$residesInRegion) currently.  Note that a given person might simultaneously consider more than one place home in this sense.  For one thing, someone who considers a small region (e.g. a  particular #$City) home might also consider a larger surrounding  region (e.g. the #$State-Geopolitical in which the city is located)  home as well.  For another thing, some people consider two completely  separate places home: their hometown and their current place of residence, for example.")
(comment accessibleFrom "This predicate relates pairs of nearby regions or
objects that are so situated that an unaided human could 
move directly to the second from the first.  
(#$accessibleFrom HERE THERE) means that HERE and THERE 
are places -- i.e. either regions or objects (like rooms
and rooftops) that are capable of containing or supporting
a human -- such that the average human could, more or less 
directly, get from being in/on HERE to being in/on THERE
without excessive difficulty or risk, and without the use 
of special equipment.  For example, one room is accessible 
from another if the door between them is unlocked, but not if
the door is locked.  This predicate is not symmetric as, for 
example, it might be possible to jump from one rooftop to a 
lower rooftop yet not possible to climb back.")
(comment EnteringAComputerPassword "The collection of events in which an instance of #$Password-Computer is entered into a computer in order to gain            access to a #$ComputationalSystem. #$EnteringAComputerPassword and #$EnteringAUsername are the key subevents            in instances of #$LoggingInOnAComputer.")
(comment SolutionOfStrengthFn "(#$SolutionOfStrengthFn SOLVENT SOLVENT-QUANT SOLUTE
SOLUTE-QUANT) returns the collection of all #$Solutions that consist
of SOLUTE-QUANT amount of SOLUTE dissolved in SOLVENT-QUANT amount of
SOLVENT.")
(comment conceptNeeded "(#$conceptNeeded STRING) means that KR work needs to be done to create a Cyc concept corresponding to the meaning of STRING. For example, (#$conceptNeeded 'trademark') means that the concept of trademarks needs to be reified in Cyc.")
(disjointWith ZipCode DoctorME)
(comment z-component "The projection on the z-axis (vertical axis) of a vector. The magnitude is positive if the direction of the vector is downward")
(disjointWith CalendarSecond PolarDay)
(comment predicateRestrictsWhen "(predicateRestrictsWhen PRED SPECPRED COL) means than when INST is an instance of COL and bears a binary relation to X in PRED (i.e. (PRED INST X) or (PRED X INST) holds) then INST also bears this relation to X in SPECPRED.  Note that the following holds: (#$genlPreds SPECPRED PRED).")
(comment NuclearEngineer "An instance of #$PersonTypeByOccupation and a specialization of both #$Scientist and #$Engineer.  Each instance of #$NuclearEngineer is an expert in the field of nuclear engineering.  Instances of #$NuclearEngineer are often consulted when evaluating and monitoring nuclear power plants.")
(comment Pindolol "The chemical compound which is a beta blocker.  This drug is intended to be used for the management of hypertension.")
(comment PushingABabyCarriage "Moving a baby by pushing a baby carriage with it inside.")
(disjointWith SelfPoweredDevice Barge)
(comment mostFavoredNations "(#$mostFavoredNations COUNTRY1 COUNTRY2) means that the #$Country COUNTRY1 accords most favored nation trading status to the #$Country COUNTRY2.  That is, COUNTRY1 subjects COUNTRY2 to tariffs no higher than the lowest level applied by COUNTRY1 to any other country.")
(comment Line-Marking "A collection of visual marks.  Each element of #$Line-Marking is a visual mark which is relatively long and thin.")
(comment informationProcessor-FunctionalRole "(#$informationProcessor-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means
that AGENT is supposed to execute some kind of processing function
with respect to information that modifies the behavior of various
components of SYSTEM.  Information processing functions include, but
are not limited to, translating information from one form to another,
storing information, retrieving information, making decisions on the
basis of information input, and erasing information.")
(comment Dollar-NewZealand "Major unit of currency of #$NewZealand")
(comment PyrotechnicEvent "This is the collection of events in which #$PyrotechnicDevices do what they

were intended to do. A visual-aural fireworks display would be a prime example, but others

would be the use of signalling flares to signal (not to hit someone over the

head) and the setting off of cherry bombs. #$PyrotechnicEvents needn't have

both an important visual and sonic aspect but they must have one or the other. Also, fireworks can

go off accidentally, thereby creating the sort of display they were intended to create,

so not all instances of this collection occur as a direct result of purposeful action.")
(comment (Centi Meter) "This is a unit of length derived by dividing a meter by 100; see also #$UnitOfMeasureWithPrefix.")
(comment TermLoanAgreement "The collection of all #$Loan-WrittenLegalAgreements in which credit is extended by commercial banks for a fixed period not more than 10 years.  The interest rate may be fixed (so that the loan has #$loanInterestOptions #$FixedRateLoan) or tied to some index (so that it is an #$IndexedLoan) such as the prime lending rate.")
(disjointWith TimePoint (MeaningInSystemFn SENSUS-Information1997 "TIME-INTERVAL"))
(comment ephemeralTerm "(#$ephemeralTerm TERM) states that TERM is a term that only has meaning in this particular copy of the knowledge base.  A such, it can be viewed as an ephemeral concept which could likely be forgotten at some future point in time, perhaps by an explicit 'forgetting' process.  See also #$termDependsOn.")
(disjointWith ContactLocation Horizon)
(comment connected-EdgeToEdge-Acute "(#$connected-EdgeToEdge-Acute SHEET OBJ) means that a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET1, is #$connectedAlongEdge to an edge of another #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET2.  The angle between the two sheets is acute.  The connection between the sheets can be considered to be an edge of the combined object.")
(comment Rickettsiaceae-Family "This collection of #$ProkaryoticCells are small rod-shaped, coccoid and diplococcous-shaped, often pleomorphic.  They may be parasitic in humans and other vertebrates and are transmitted by arthropods (lice, fleas, and ticks) and are thus restricted in their geographical distribution to that of the infected host. It includes #$Rickettsia, #$Orientia-Genus, #$Ehrlichia-Genus.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat RoadVehicleType)
(comment FinancialInstrumentTrading "buying an object, where the object(s) bought is(are) some type of financial instrument.")
(comment SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn "(#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn COLLECTION PREDICATE THING) specifies the collection of all instances INSTANCE of COLLECTION for which (PREDICATE THING INSTANCE) holds.  For example, (#$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromFn #$Laboratory owns #$DepartmentOfEnergy-US) refers to the collection of laboratories owned by the DOE.")
(comment RadioCommercial-CW "The collection of all commercials (#$Commercial-CW) designed for broadcast as part of a radio broadcast")
(comment Compressing "The collection of events in which some #$PartiallyTangible is subjected to opposing forces which crush or compact the object, so that afterwards its volume is less than before.  Instances are not necessarily also #$DestructionEvents, although they certainly can be depending on the thing acted on.")
(comment typeGenlMt "(#$typeGenlMt MT-COL GENL-MT) states that every microtheory which is an instance of microtheory type MT-COL has GENL-MT as a generalization.  For example, (#$typeGenlMt #$Microtheory #$BaseKB).")
(disjointWith HumanNameSuffix InternationalPostalCode)
(comment EbolaHemorrhagicFeverInfection "A severe, often-fatal disease in humans and other primates, caused by the #$EbolaVirus. Has occurred in sporadic outbreaks, generally in health-care settings in #$SubSaharanAfrica, since its initial identification in 1976. There is currently no known effective treatment.")
(disjointWith TersifyForward NoTerseArgument)
(disjointWith PublicTransportationDevice Device-SingleUser)
(comment EggplantPlant "Individual eggplant plants")
(comment increasesImmediately "(#$increasesImmediately

PERIOD THING SLOT) means that the value for the predicate SLOT applied

to THING (in the first argument position) is greater immediately after

(#$STIF q.v.) PERIOD than it was immediately before (#$STIB q.v.)

PERIOD.  PERIOD may be any instance of #$TemporalThing, i.e., anything

that has a time period associated with it, whether an event, an

entity, a life stage, etc. No causal connection is implied between the

#$TemporalThing PERIOD and the increase.  See

#$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(comment FranchiseContract "A contract between a company and an individual or organization granting the rights to use the company's name, image, etc., in selling the company's products.")
(comment RoleFn "A Cyc function, specifically an instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  #$RoleFn is used to represent the role that something plays in a kind of situation.  (#$RoleFn THING SIT-TYPE) denotes the role that THING has in situations of the type SIT-TYPE.  For example, #$RoleFn could be used to denote the role played by an element of #$Minister, MIN, when participating in #$WeddingCeremony situations: (#$RoleFn MIN #$WeddingCeremony)  The denotation of any expression of the form (#$RoleFn THING SIT-TYPE) #$isa element of #$RoleReferentTheTerm.")
(comment Snowboard "The collection of all snowboards.  These are planks a few to 5 or so feet long, about a foot wide, with bindings used to attach the board to the feet.")
(comment SCUDTransloader "Military vehicles used to transport SCUD missiles.")
(comment Oxygen "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of #$Oxygen in stuff form.")
(comment Vermin "A collection of animals considered undesirable to find living in human habitation buildings or other facilities. ")
(comment GeoCitiesWebHostingService "The collection of #$WebHosting events sold by  #$YahooInc as part of their 'GeoCities' service.")
(comment countryCodeDigraph "(#$countryCodeDigraph PLACE CODE) means that CODE is an internationally recognized two-letter abbreviation for the name of PLACE.--Kathy Burns, May 14, 1998")
(comment SituationSpecificationMicrotheory "An instance of #$SituationSpecificationMicrotheory is a microtheory containing those propositions that describe (or partially describe) a particular situation. The situation may or may not be reified as an instance of #$Situation.")
(comment Foreplay "erotic caressing performed as a prelude to #$SexualCopulation")
(comment PartiallyIntangibleIndividual "A specialization of both #$Individual and #$PartiallyIntangible.  Each instance of  #$PartiallyIntangibleIndividual is an individual that has at least some intangible (i.e. immaterial) component.  The instance might be partly tangible (e.g. a copy of a book) and thus be a #$CompositeTangibleAndIntangibleObject, or it might be fully intangible (e.g. a number or an agreement) and thus be an instance of #$IntangibleIndividual.")
(comment CharacterStringToken-Sounded "A specialization of #$CharacterStringToken, 
  each of whose instances is a specific sound event that 
  represents or realizes a particular abstract instance 
  of #$CharacterString in some language or writing system.
  A sounded character-string token might be generated
  directly by a human voice, created by playing a recording 
  of a voice, or generated by purely electronic means. 
  Instances of #$CharacterStringToken-Sounded, unlike inscribed 
  or electromagnetically-encoded string tokens, normally do not
  have individual character tokens as parts, as most sounded 
  string tokens simply cannot be divided into discrete sounded 
  character tokens (see #$CharacterToken-Sounded).  E.g. a 
  spoken token of the string 'cat' -- unless it happens to be 
  literally spelled out -- does not contain a token of the 
  letter 'c' as a part.  Thus, most sounded character-string 
  tokens are not instances of #$CharacterStringToken-Serial.")
(comment FTPServer-Network "A subcollection of #$Computer, whose instances function as

FTP servers for instances of #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment Cocaine "#$Cocaine is a naturally occurring substance present in the leaves of the #$CocaPlant. Pharmacologically, #$Cocaine has two prominent actions: it is a potent #$LocalAnesthetic, and it is a powerful #$Stimulant. Psychotropically, #$Cocaine inhibits the re-uptake of dopamine in the brain, causing alertness and heightened energy, a sense of euphoria, decreased anxiety and social inhibitions, and heightened sexuality. Side-effects include addiction, anxiety, depression, irritability, extreme fatigue, and possibly paranoia. #$Cocaine has been used in South America for more than 3,000 years and in the United States since the 19th century in a variety of forms: coca leaves, coca paste, #$Cocaine-Powder, and cocaine base (e.g., freebase and #$Cocaine-Crack).")
(comment Code-AssertionDirection "An instance of #$CycLAssertionDirection (q.v.).  A CycL assertion that
has the #$Code-AssertionDirection cannot itself be used in either 
backward (ask-time) or forward (assert-time) inferences, but is instead 
implemented in the underlying code of the Cyc system.  Contrast with 
#$Backward-AssertionDirection and #$Forward-AssertionDirection.  Also 
see #$assertionDirection.")
(comment SearsStore "A collection of all the local Sears stores. ")
(comment (ProfessionalFn Skateboarder) "The collection of professional skateboarders.")
(comment eventSeriesMembers "(#$eventSeriesMembers SERIES EVENT) says that (#$subEvents SERIES EVENT) and (#$seriesMembers SERIES EVENT).  So for example, (#$eventSeriesMembers 2015WordSeries Game1Of2015WorldSeries) says that game 1 is a sub-event and member of the event that is the 2015 World Series.")
(disjointWith Agent-Generic CornerOnObject)
(disjointWith Motorboat Watercraft-Subsurface)
(comment JoinListsFn "This function attaches lists together to make longer lists. For any instances LIST(1), ..., LIST(n) of #$List, (#$JoinListsFn LIST(1) ... LIST(n)) denotes the list, i.e., the instance of #$List, that is obtained by concatenating LIST(1), ..., LIST(n) end to end in the order from 1 to n.  Note that LIST(1), ..., LIST(n) do not have to be distinct.")
(comment ProjectileSlug-Tracer "The collection of #$ProjectileSlug-Bullets that contain a lead slug and a chemical composition in the rear.  This is used at night in order to  see what target the bullet hits.")
(disjointWith Elasticity IntervalOnNumberLine)
(comment moreThwartedFromBecause "(#$moreThwartedFromBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP) means
that there is a decreased chance of AGENT's playing the role ROLE in
a situation of type EVTTYPE because PROP is true
(#$decreasedChanceForRoleBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP) and AGENT
has the #$goals (ROLE EVTTYPE AGENT).")
(comment DesolateAreaPopulationDensity "The population density of desolate areas like deserts or polar regions.")
(comment mappingOf "(#$mappingOf MAPPING MATCH) signifies that MAPPING is one #$AnalogyMapping associated with MATCH.")
(comment pullee "(#$pullee PULL PULLEE) means that PULLEE is being pulled towards the #$puller in a #$PullingAnObject event, PULL.  Neither PULLEE nor the #$puller move in a case of #$PullingWithoutTranslation.  PULLEE moves towards the #$puller in cases of #$PullingAnObjectAlong.  The #$puller moves towards PULLEE in cases of #$PullingOneselfTowards.")
(comment Haze "An aggregation of fine widely dispersed particles which subdues colors a bit.  Of all clouds, haze is the most transparent.  When it occurs, it comes in very large lumps (i.e. may cover an entire city or horizon) and envelopes the observer in the same way that Fog (qv) does.  Thus Haze is only a cloud from the #$WeatherEvent perspective.")
(comment TemporalStep-PersistenceDistribution "The collection of #$TemporalPersistenceDistributions with a step-like distribution contour (graph).")
(comment Terraforming "Terraforming is a process of planetary engineering, specifically directed at enhancing the capacity of an

 extraterrestrial planetary environment to support life. The ultimate in terraforming would be to create an

 uncontained planetary biosphere emulating all the functions of the biosphere of the Earth---one that

 would be fully habitable for human beings.")
(comment Centerfold-Generic "a collection of hardcopy still images. A #$Centerfold-Generic is a #$Photograph or other #$StillImage found in the very middle a magazine, where the staples come through. It takes up two pages (sometimes more if there's an extra fold), but both pages are on the same side of a single physical piece of paper, so you can remove it from the magazine and display it. For those centerfolds that feature physically attractive #$Persons, see #$Centerfold-PhotoOfPerson.")
(comment Tablet-28DaySupply "The collection of #$TabletDrugs intended for packaging into 28-day-supply packages.")
(comment healedInjury "The injury ARG2 is healed in Healing event ARG1.")
(comment ExclusiveEconomicZoneFn "(#$ExclusiveEconomicZoneFn ?ENT) picks out the region of the sea designated as the exclusive economic zone of ?ENT, in accordance with U.N provisions. An entity's exclusive economic zone must be adjacent to its territorial sea, and the territorial sea and exclusive economic zone of a country may not together be more than 200 nautical miles wide. In this zone, the country controlling it also controls the (living and non-living) natural resources in that region, for purposes of research, exploration, exploitation, and so on.")
(comment relevantInTypeOfTime-Sometime "(#$relevantInTypeOfTime-Sometime MT TYPE) means that the assertions in MT are relevant sometime during the temporal extent of instances of TYPE.  See also #$relevantInTypeOfTime-Always.")
(comment ManeuverUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of units that are regarded as deployable in maneuver. This includes as specializations #$MechanizedInfantryUnit-MilitarySpecialty and #$ArmoredUnit-MilitarySpecialty. Reference in RKF Year2 specs, v. 1.2.")
(comment Powerball-Lottery "The collection of Powerball lotteries.")
(disjointWith TrainCar MountableTransporter)
(comment TakingWrittenNotes "#$TakingWrittenNotes is the collection of all #$WritingANote events in which a #$Note-Document is created whose content is based on a preexisting #$InformationBearingThing. Examples include taking notes of a meeting, taking notes of a lecture, taking notes of a textbook. A negative example would be writing a note to remind oneself to go to the grocery store.")
(comment LastEruptionOfFn "#$LastEruptionOfFn is a function. (#$LastEruptionOfFn VOLCANO) denotes the most recent eruption of VOLCANO. See also #$mostNotableEruptionDate.")
(comment resourceInPlan "(#$resourceInPlan PLAN RESOURCE) means that if EXEC is an
execution of PLAN performedBy AGENT, then (#$controls AGENT RESOURCE)
is a precondition for EXEC being #$successfulForAgents.  Exactly what
#$controls will entail will vary from context to context.")
(comment TorpedoWatercraft-Surface "The collection of surface naval ships which are are equipped with torpedo tubes and are capable of firing torpedoes.")
(comment OrbitalPath "The path followed by an object revolving around another object, under the influence of gravitation.")
(comment InterracialFn "InterracialFn takes as its argument any spec of #$HumanActivity and returns a collection of interracial instances of that Activity.  For example, (#$InterracialFn #$WeddingEvent-Entire) returns all the weddings in which people of different races were married.  For something to count as interracial, one or more of the major participants in the event should be of a race different than the other major participants.")
(comment Ketoconazole "The chemical compound which is an anti-fungal.")
(comment MultiWordPhrasePredicate "A collection of #$NLSemanticPredicates.  Each instance of
#$MultiWordPhrasePredicate specifies a multi-word phrase and its
CycL translation.  The phrase consists of a sequence of strings,
beginning or ending with a head word (an instance of #$EnglishWord)
whose form can vary.  For instance, the assertion (#$compoundString
#$Chamber-TheWord (\"of\" \"commerce\") #$CountNoun
#$ChamberOfCommerce) means that the strings \"chamber of commerce\"
and \"chambers of commerce\" both denote the CycL term
#$ChamberOfCommerce.  Specializations of #$MultiWordPhrasePredicate
are: #$MultiWordForConstantPred, whose instances map
phrases to CycL constants, #$MultiWordForFormulaPred,
whose instances map phrases to #$NLTemplateExpressions and #$MultiWordForStringPred, whose instances map phrases to strings.")
(comment RadioBroadcastOfTeamEventFn "#$RadioBroadcastOfTeamEventFn takes as argument any instance of #$SportsTeam or           #$SportsLeague and returns the collection of events that are radio broadcasts           of games in which TEAM participates.  For instance,            (#$BroadcastOfSportsTeamEventFn #$MinnesotaVikings) returns the collection of           all radio broadcasts of Minnesota Vikings games.")
(comment A-TheLetter "The letter A of the alphabet.  This is 'A' or 'a' as a #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterA and #$LatinSmallLetterA.")
(comment SupremeCourt "The highest appeals court of a #$Country or #$CountrySubsidiary.")
(disjointWith ServiceEstablishment MilitaryOrganization)
(comment AtomicCompositionFn "(#$AtomicCompositionFn GROUPOFATOMTYPE1 GROUPOFATOMTYPE2 ...) denotes the type of molecules that are made up of an instance of GROUPOFATOMTYPE1, an instance of GROUPOFATOMTYPE2, etc.")
(comment Sepal "A sepal is a specialized leaf; collectively a set of sepals comprise a flower's calyx.")
(comment VectorBorneInfectionType "A collection of infections. Instances of this collection are types of infections that are commonly spread by vector organisms. Vectors are carrier of the pathogen, Anopheles mosquitoes carrying malaria bacterium, or carriers of carrier of pathogen, rats carrying fleas carrying the plague bacterium are examples. Thus infections such as malaria, #$Malaria, and plague, #$BubonicPlague, are instances of #$VectorBorneInfectionType. See #$infectionTypeHasVectorType.")
(comment portalHasCovering "A general predicate that relates portals to their coverings.  (#$portalHasCovering PORTAL COVERING) means that the #$PortalCovering COVERING covers the #$Portal PORTAL.  Cf. the more specialized predicates, #$doorwayHasCovering and #$windowHasCovering.")
(comment FormalityOfSpeech "Formality attributes apply to individual word senses of words or phrases.")
(comment uncodedContainedFields "(#$uncodedContainedFields ?LTS ?LF) means that ?LF is a field contained within some other field of ?LTS, and, once it has been extracted, the value should be used without interpretation.")
(comment VulnerableToPrivilegeEscalation "A vulnerability of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this  vulnerability if it is running a program that allows (authorized or unauthorized) users to raise their privileges on the system to a level that they are not authorized to have.")
(comment LibraryHoldings "The collection of all collections kept by a #$Library-Organization.  Each instance of #$LibraryHoldings is the complete set objects a library keeps, protects, and makes available for public use.")
(comment NuclearFusionProcess "Whole reaction processes, that either peter out or end with a bang. They consist of lots of individual nuclear fusion events.")
(comment DataSending "This is a collection of one-way information transfer events in which information
    is sent from some #$informationOrigin to some #$informationDestination.")
(comment SexualArousal "The states of SexualArousal; sexual stirrings or physical readiness for sexual activity.")
(comment Platform-Military "#$Platform-Military is a specialization of #$MilitaryHardware and #$TransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$Platform-Military is a transportation device which can carry military equipment such as #$Weapons, personnel and communications equipment. When a #$Platform-Military is armed with a #$Weapon, such as a #$Tank-Vehicle, it will result in a type of #$WeaponSystem.")
(comment connectedTo-Directly "(#$connectedTo-Directly OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are directly attached in a way that allows at most only certain types of relative motion between them.  Adjacent links in a bicycle chain, for example, can only undergo limited rotational motion in relation to each other.  OBJ1 and OBJ2 must both be #$SolidTangibleThings, must be directly touching  each other, and their mutual connectedness must _not_ obtain merely in virtue of some third object's serving as a connector between them.  For a generalization of this 

that does not imply a _direct_ connection between objects, see #$connectedTo

(which is in effect the transitive closure of #$connectedTo-Directly).")
(comment Abrasion "Scraped or abraded skin.")
(comment Paraplegia "The collection of instances of the condition in which the lower half of one's body is paralyzed.")
(comment meansOfInfoTransfer-ComputerProgram "This predicate is a more specific version of #$programUsed-Generic intended to indicate

when instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW play the role of #$programUsed-Generic

in instances of #$InformationTransferEvent and are designed to

aid in information transfer.  (#$meansOfInfoTransfer-ComputerProgram ITE COM_PROG) means that the instance COM_PROG of #$ComputerProgram-CW plays an instrumental role in the #$InformationTransferEvent ITE and that COM_PROG was created in part to be able to play such roles, e.g. (#$intendedBehaviorCapable COM_PROG #$InformationTransferEvent #$programUsed-Generic) holds.  For example, if an instance EMAIL_PROG of #$EMailServerProgram is used in some instance SEND of #$EMailSending, then we may assert (#$meansOfInfoTransfer-ComputerProgram SEND EMAIL_PROG).")
(comment HardwareMarketCategory "The market category for tools, building supplies, and the sundry kinds of items associated with them")
(comment groupSubjectToQuarantine "(#$groupSubjectToQuarantine QUARANTINE GROUP) means that the members of GROUP are precisely those organism which are supposed to be quarantined according to the standards of QUARANTINE. Note that this does not imply that the members of GROUP are in fact confined. To state that a certain group is in fact confined, according to a #$Quarantine, use #$groupQuarantined.")
(comment Californium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Californium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment ComputerProcess-ContinuouslyRunning "The subcollection of #$ComputerProcess-Generic each of whose instances 
    runs continuously on at least one CPU for the entire duration of its 
    existence.  This means that it is never temporarily swapped out or 
    timesliced.")
(disjointWith Snowflake HailStone)
(comment BumpkinJoke "A specialization of #$RuralLaboringClassJoke, #$BumpkinJoke is the collection of all jokes that are based on stereotypes about so-called \"bumpkins\".")
(comment IncurringBodilyHarm "Instances of #$IncurringBodilyHarm are events in which some #$Organism-Whole either sustains an injury, or incurs an ailment or some sort, which in some way makes the organism worse off than it would otherwise have been.")
(comment LexicalItem "A subcollection of #$LinguisticObject (q.v.).  #$LexicalItem is the collection of linguistic objects that are part of the lexicon of some natural language or other.  Instances of #$LexicalItem include words as well as constituents of words, such as affixes (see #$LexicalWord, #$WordConstituent, and #$LexicalAffix).")
(comment residentAlien "The #$Person ARG2 is a resident alien (i.e., a resident, but not a full citizen) in the #$GeopoliticalEntity ARG1.")
(comment Pericardium "The collection of all pericardia.  Each #$Vertebrate (except some #$Fish) possess one #$Pericardium, which is a membranous sac (#$Sac-Organic) enclosing the #$Heart.")
(comment Bacillaceae-Family "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalFamily within the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells all form spores and are #$BacillusBacterium.  This includes the #$BiologicalGenus #$Bacillus-Genus.  This #$BiologicalFamily is a synonymous to the Bacillus/Staphylococcus group in NCBI Taxonomy Browser.")
(comment AirToSurfaceMissile "The collection of missiles (instances of #$Missile) that are designed to launch from airborne platforms and are intended to attack targets on the ground.")
(comment explanatoryStatement "The predicate #$explanatoryStatement is used to identify the propositions used to give the explanation in a particular instance of #$Explanation.  See also #$explainedStatement.")
(comment WeaponOfMassDestructionAttack "Any MilitaryAttack in which a weapon of mass destruction is used such as NuclearAttack, BiologicalAttack, or ChemicalAttack.")
(comment EthnicGroupOfCaucasians "The collection of persons who consider themselves to be Caucasians.  This is a rather vague ethnic designation, usually synonymous with `white person' in naive US ethnic classification schemes.")
(comment RadiocarbonDating "This is the technique of dating organic materials

by checking the proportion of Carbon 14, a radioactive isotope of carbon, which has

decayed. Since the rate of decay is known, the age of the object can be fairly accurately

estimated. This technique only works for objects that are quite young relative to

the scale of geological time.")
(comment VaginalAdministration "Administering a substance through one's vagina.")
(comment wordStrings "(#$wordStrings WORD STRING) states that STRING is one of the strings for the word unit WORD in some microtheory.  In other words, some #$SpeechPartPredicate is used on WORD to relate it to STRING.  This predicate is

#$notAssertible since it is concluded from the current state of the knowledge base.")
(comment NonVolatile "Substance does not evaporate, e.g. MercuryBlob245.")
(comment mediaSeriesPeriod "(#$mediaSeriesPeriod SERIES FREQUENCY) expresses the frequency of Circulation for #$MediaProducts that are distributed via the mass media at regular intervals, such as the publication of #$PeriodicalIssues of a #$PeriodicalSeries or episodes of a #$TVSeriesProduct.  The first argument to #$mediaSeriesPeriod is a #$MediaSeriesProduct (q.v.) second is a #$Frequency.")
(comment instantiatesBorderWhole "This predicate is used to assert that a particular #$PartiallyTangible thing is used to demarcate or pick out the whole of a given #$Border and not some proper portion thereof.  More specifically, if (#$instantiatesBorderWhole ?MARKER ?BORDER) is true, then there does not exist a ?SUBBORDER such that (#$formsBorderPart ?SUBBORDER ?BORDER) and (#$not (#$instantiatesBorderWhole ?MARKER ?SUBBORDER)).  This is particularly useful when we need to make clear that a particular #$PartiallyTangible entity demarcates the entirety of a given border.")
(disjointWith InternationalOrganizationOfCountries (GroupFn OrganicMaterial))
(comment PacketLengthField-Packet "A #$PacketLengthField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet
that indicates how long the entire packet is in bytes.")
(comment Conveyance-Stationary "The subcollection of #$Conveyance that contains object that are intended for moving partially tangible things while remaining stationary. Positive examples are conveyor belts or guns. A borderline case is a #$River that is used to transport logs; that river is a #$Conveyance-Stationary because the river as a whole does not change its location (only parts of it; the water). ")
(comment BlackAndWhiteColorScheme "Something that has a #$BlackAndWhiteColorScheme will have parts that are #$BlackColor and parts that are #$WhiteColor.")
(comment Snake "The collection of all snakes; a subset of #$Reptile.  Each element of #$Snake is a limbless, scaly, vermiform reptile with a long, narrow, tapering, mostly smooth body.  Snakes in many species have poisonous and sometimes fatal bites.  Snakes live on land, in trees, in fresh water, and in the sea (sea snakes).  #$Snake constitutes a biological suborder (also called Serpentes or Ophidia).")
(disjointWith LinguisticObject Algorithm)
(comment CataloguingAnArtifact "The collection of recording-and-filing-information-about-an-artifact event.")
(comment Wreath-Decoration "The collection of all wreaths.  A #$Wreath-Decoration is a decorative object which is circular in shape and often made out of plant material.")
(comment ArmoredPersonnelCarrier-BTR50 "A type of armored personnel carrier which Iran is known to possess.")
(comment sourceAuthenticated "(#$sourceAuthenticated AUTH SOURCE) means that SOURCE is the specific instance of #$AuthenticationSource that is being used for the purpose of authentication in the specific instance of #$AuthenticationEvent AUTH.")
(comment DiscusThrowField "The collection of fields where DiscusThrowSportsEvents typically occur.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent AcademicTesting)
(comment makesMoreVulnerableThan-Situation "(#$makesMoreVulnerableThan-Situation SIT1 SIT2 OBJECT RESULT-TYPE) means that situation SIT1 increases the vulnerability of OBJ to results of type RESULT-TYPE more than situation SIT2 does. OBJECT is presumably vulnerable in both SIT1 and SIT2 to RESULT-TYPE.  Note also that this is an instance level predicate, although the last argument is a type of situation.  For restrictions on RESULT-TYPE see #$vulnerableIn.")
(comment CycLClosedDenotationalTerm "The collection of all closed denotational terms in the CycL language.  An expression is said to be \"closed\" if it contains no free variables (see #$CycLClosedExpression).  A CycL term is said to be \"denotational\" if it is the right sort of term to have a denotation (or value) in the universe of discourse (see #$CycLDenotationalTerm).  CycL sentences, while terms of CycL, are not considered denotational terms.  Each instance of #$CycLClosedDenotationalTerm is either a #$CycLClosedAtomicTerm (i.e. a #$CycLConstant or #$SubLAtomicTerm) or a #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm (i.e. a \"NAT\" with no free variables).  Examples of closed denotational terms include `#$Muffet', `(#$JuvenileFn #$Dog)', `(#$TheSetOf ?X (#$objectHasColor ?X GreenColor))', and `212'.  Note that these are also examples: `(#$BorderBetweenFn #$Canada #$Mexico)' (despite the fact that it fails actually to denote anything) and `(#$JuvenileFn #$isa #$genls #$JuvenileFn)'

(despite the fact that it is not semantically well-formed).")
(comment IntelligenceCommunityFn "For each #$Country COUNTRY, (#$IntelligenceCommunityFn COUNTRY) denotes the intelligence organization of COUNTRY that includes all organizations (or branches) in the intelligence community in COUNTRY.  For example, (#$IntelligenceCommunityFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) denotes the intelligence community in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, including FBI, CIA and others.")
(comment RegisteredInvestmentAdvisor "A specialization of #$FinancialAdvisor.  Each instance of #$RegisteredInvestmentAdvisor is a financial advisor registered with the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC).  Instances of #$RegisteredInvestmentAdvisor earn a living by giving advice to clients about investing in securities (e.g. stocks, bonds, or mutual funds).")
(comment AndGate "An electrical device whose inputs and outputs are digital signals and that implements the logical-AND function.")
(comment PartialRotation "Any rotation which has a restricted starting and ending point.  A partial rotation normally spans less than 360 degrees.")
(comment WritingBoard "A (usually rectangular) sheet of some composite material, usually framed and supported by a stand or hung on a wall, for writing messages.  Popular in business/corporate offices and school rooms.")
(comment DecliningARequest "An acknowledgement of a request in which the preformer declines the request.")
(comment averageDailyLowTemperature "(#$averageDailyLowTemperature REGION TEMP TYPE) means that during instances of TYPE, the average daily low temperature in the #$GeographicalRegion REGION is TEMP. Note that TYPE will often be a type of calendar time period, such as a subset of #$CalendarMonth.")
(comment PrerequisiteDocumentsFn "This is a function that, applied to a collection (type) of events or evidence of such an event, denotes the collection of all documents that are standard prerequisites for objects or services of the specified type.  (#$PrerequisiteDocumentsFn FOO) denotes the collation of all types of papers ordinarily needed to obtain or achieve instances of the colllection FOO.")
(disjointWith SportsCompetition Emission)
(comment NurseryLaundryHamper "A subset of #$LaundryHamper.  A #$NurseryLaundryHamper is a  hamper which belongs in a #$Nursery-BabysRoom.  These hampers are generally decorated in designs that delight infants and toddlers.")
(comment ExtractViaFn "(#$ExtractViaFn METHOD N VAL) returns a term which is the result of using the #$FieldCombiningMethod METHOD to extract the Nth item from VAL.  Numbering begins with 1 for this purpose.  For example, (#$ExtractViaFn (#$FieldLengthsFn (2 2 2)) 1 ''ABCDEF'') would return the string ''AB''.  ")
(comment ElectronicSynthesizer "The collection of music synthesizers which produce musical tones electronically, often from #$MIDIFiles. See also #$SynthesizerProgram.")
(comment RibSeries "People have two bilaterally symmetric #$RibSeries comprised of 12 ribs (#$Rib-AnimalBodyPart) each: 7 #$TrueRibs and 5 #$FalseRibs of which two are #$FloatingRibs.")
(comment TransportationDevice-Vehicle "#$TransportationDevice-Vehicle is a specialization of both #$TransportationDevice and #$SelfPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle is a transportation device that moves under its own power.  Examples include jet airplanes and automobiles; non-examples include skateboards, gliders, and rowboats.  Note that hand-pushed power lawnmowers, even though they are #$SelfPoweredDevices, are not instances of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle, since they must be pushed in order to remain in motion.")
(comment sitResultsInProp "(#$sitResultsInProp FORMULA1 FORMULA2 SIT-TYPE PRED) means that FORMULA2 becomes true when FORMULA1 becomes true, where FORMULA1 contains a clause of the form (#$thereExists ?SIT SIT-TYPE), and where ?SIT changes some assertion of the form (PRED ...).")
(comment MensSportsTeam "the collection of all #$SportsTeams whose members are #$AdultMalePersons.  This collection enables one to reify types of sports teams on the fly; e.g., the collection  of all mens basketball teams is (#$CollectionIntersection2Fn  #$BasketballTeam #$MensSportsTeam).")
(comment Quinine "An alkaloid used to make tonic and cure malaria.  Derived from the bark of the Cinchona tree.")
(comment SubLListOfSubLLists "Each #$SubLListOfSubLLists is a #$SubLList, in which each element of the list is also a #$SubLList.")
(comment CavityInteriorContent "The collection of pieces of matter that fill or occupy the space inside cavities (i.e. instances of #$CavityInteriorRegion).  Instances of #$CavityInteriorContent can be solid (like a gold filling in a tooth) or fluid (like air in a cave or water in a pot-hole).")
(comment PoliticalIssue "The collection of all #$Issues which are dealt with in the political arena.")
(disjointWith IntelligentComputerProgram ExpertSystem)
(comment Sailboat "Boats powered mainly by lift or push from wind passing over or into their sails.")
(comment (FruitFn PlumTree) "The collection of individual plums.")
(comment Cytosine-Base "A collection of molecules. #$Cytosine-Base is one of the four kinds of nitrogen
base, #$NitrogenBaseType, that enter in the constitution of instances of
Cytosine-Nucleotide. Its abbreviattion is C.")
(disjointWith FunctionDenotingFunction PredicateDenotingFunction)
(comment HepatitisE-Infection "A collection of Infections. A spec of #$ViralHepatitis. Instances of #$HepatitisE-Infection are viral infections caused by the hepatitis E virus, see #$HepatitisE-Virus.")
(comment Drummer "The collection of people who play the drums for a living.")
(comment Spirochaetaceae-Family "A collection of #$ProkaryoticCells that forms a
#$BiologicalFamily in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It includes the
#$BiologicalGenus #$Spirochaeta-Genus. These #$Cells are
chemoorganotrophic and utilize carbohydrates and/or amino acids for
carbon and energy sources.")
(comment MaterialSupportShip "A collection. Military material support ships.")
(comment subPaths "(#$subPaths PATH SUBPATH) means that any point (see #$pointOnPath) on the #$Path-Simple SUBPATH must also be on the #$Path-Simple PATH.")
(comment ProvidingFeedback "Providing feedback to some controlling agent about something they control.")
(comment Platinum "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of platinum.")
(disjointWith BiologicalLivingObject Coffee-Ground)
(disjointWith AnimalActivity Artifact-Generic)
(comment Limping "Any impaired form of locomotion due to damage to the locomotion appendage used in the locomotion.")
(comment OfficialReport "An instance of #$OfficialReport serves to communicate an analysis of selected data in a published form.  The report is often issued or generated by an institution that claims authority in the subject with which it is dealing.  For example, the US Labor Department may collect employment statistics, write an analysis, and issue it as an annual report.  Jouralistic reporting or personal reporting are not an instance of #$OfficialReport, although it may treat #$OfficialReports as evidence or news.  There is a conceptual relationship with #$OfficialDocument and #$OfficialRecord.  For example, an immigration document is the official form issued to legal immigrants; an immigration record is the record of who receives the immigration document, at what location, and at what time; an immigration report is issued by the appropriate governing body that analyzes immigration 'and other' records and may propose changes in policy.")
(disjointWith Ship Pipeline)
(comment MagneticSensor-200m "A collection of magnetic sensor devices.  These are placed across a path or track to detect vehicles as they pass.")
(comment Spraying "Directing a #$FluidTangibleThing from one place to another by expelling it with force, rather than along a #$FluidConduit. However, typically, such a conduit is used to direct the fluid to the point where the #$Spraying begins.")
(comment NoseJob "#$Surgery in which the #$objectActedOn is a #$Nose; the bone structure of the #$Nose is reshaped. Typically, a #$NoseJob is an elective procedure and would be considered #$CosmeticSurgery. However, #$NoseJobs may also be performed to reconstruct features damaged by disease or accident.")
(comment EvacuationUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profiles center           on assisting with evacuations.")
(comment CityBlock "A collection of urban regions.  Instances of #$CityBlock are usually roughly rectangular regions within cities or towns that are bounded by four streets running  approximately at right angles to each other, and such that  they do not spatially subsume any other such regions.  City  blocks are often divided into one or more instances of  #$LotOfLand, on which typically stand houses or other  buildings.")
(comment EnteringAUsername "The collection of events in which an instance of #$Username is entered into a computer in order to gain            access to a #$ComputationalSystem. #$EnteringAComputerPassword and #$EnteringAUsername are the key subevents            in instances of #$LoggingInOnAComputer.")
(comment WeatherEvent "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$WeatherEvent is a meteorological event of some duration, occurring over some spatial region.  Some weather events are almost instantaneous (for example, instances of the collection #$LightningEvent), while others are quite lengthy (for example, instances of the collection #$AnnualClimateCycle).  Spatially, weather events may cover a small locality or a large portion of a continent.")
(comment W4-Form "The document through which a person subject to United States income tax informs his/her employer how much money to take from his/her periodic wages to apply toward that tax.")
(disjointWith ZipCode HumanNameSuffix)
(disjointWith TimePoint CalendarMillennium)
(comment QuantizedType "A collection of collections. Each instance of each instance of
#$QuantizedType is a partially tangible object. Moreover, each instance of
each instance of #$QuantizedType is 'quantized' in the following sense: if
PT-1 and PT-2 are instances of the same instance of #$QuantizedType, then
PT-2 cannot be a proper physical part of PT-1, nor can PT-1 be a proper
physical part of PT-2.")
(comment y-component "The projection on the y-axis of a vector")
(comment OnlineTravelAgency "This is the collection of travel agencies who do business via the internet.

They employ #$ReservationSystems.")
(comment Dawn "A specialization of #$Twilight.  Each instance of #$Dawn is a period of time just before an instance of #$Sunrise (q.v.) during which the sky is partially and indirectly illuminated by the sun.")
(comment TroubleWithTypeReportFn "#$TroubleWithTypeReportFn takes as argument a spec of #$Thing and returns the collection of #$InformationBearingThings containing reports of trouble or problems with instances of that spec. For example, (#$TroubleWithTypeReportFn #$MSWindowsOperatingSystem) returns the collection of IBTs that are reports of problems with Microsoft Windows operating systems.")
(comment shapeSituation "This predicate relates a shape attribute to the collection of situations in which some object holds this shape.")
(comment transportedInTypes "(#$transportedInTypes ITEMTYPE MEANSTYPE) means that items of type ITEMTYPE are usually or typically transported in instances of type MEANSTYPE.  This is a relation between two #$Collections (based on common relations between their instances), not between two #$Individuals.  This predicate refers to what is commonplace, or normal; it does not claim that every instance of ITEMTYPE is transported in some instance of MEANSTYPE, nor that every instance of MEANSTYPE transports some instance of ITEMTYPE.  (For contrast, see #$relationAllExists and #$relationExistsAll.)")
(comment Acebutolol "The chemical compound which is a beta blocker.  This drug is intended to be used for therapeutic treatment of hypertension.")
(comment Eagerness "Intensely desiring something; impatiently expectant.")
(comment MinQuantValueFn "(#$MinQuantValueFn QUANTITY) returns a point value which is the minimal quantity that is subsumed by QUANTITY.  For example, (#$MinQuantValueFn (#$Meter 2 5)) returns (#$Meter 2).  See also #$MaxQuantValueFn.")
(comment CertificationOfWorkExperience "A collection of credentials.  Each element of #$CertificationOfWorkExperience is an (abstract) declaration, by an appropriate authority, that a particular person has performed a certain amount of work of some kind.  Such information might be embodied in a letter, a form, or a verbal statement issued by the authority.")
(comment Peso-Philippines "Major unit of currency of Philippines")
(comment Deka "Metric unit of measure prefix indicating 10")
(comment Contraband "The collection of all goods whose possession, production, transportation, or use is prohibited by law.  This collection depends upon the #$GovernmentCOC in effect at a given place and time for specific classes of individuals.")
(comment supplyFromCapacityDuring "(#$supplyFromCapacityDuring PT1 COL PT2 THING AMOUNT) means that that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the greatest possible amount of instances of the #$Collection COL with which the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 could be supplied from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyFromCapacityDuring is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates what would be the average rate of supply of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE to PT1 from PT2 during the temporal extent of THING if PT1 were supplied with PRODUCT-TYPE from PT2 at the limit of its capacity.")
(comment IceCoring "This is the technique of drilling into deep masses of

ice and removing long cylinders of ice from which information about the past

can be inferred. Polar ice cores contain a record of the

 past atmosphere - temperature, precipitation, gas content, chemical composition, and other properties. This can reveal a broad spectrum of information on past environmental, and

 particularly climatic, changes.")
(comment SisalPlant "Individuals of a kind of agave whose leaves yield sisal fiber.")
(comment continuouslyConnectedTo "(#$continuouslyConnectedTo OBJ1 OBJ2) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are #$PartiallyTangibles which are directly and almost seamlessly connected (e.g. they are formed from the same chunk of material, with no substantial barrier or surface or gap separating them.).")
(comment LightSurfaceToAirMissileLauncher "The collection of lightweight surface-to-air missile launchers.")
(comment NumbersPool "All instances of an illegal daily lottery")
(comment Rickettsia "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the

#$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are rods, nonmotile without

flagella.  They are #$AerobicBacterium.  They use glutamate as their

main energy source in respiration.  Glucose is not used.  These are

small #$Bacterium that are transmitted to humans by arthropods and

cause various types of diseases, such as #$TyphusFeverGroup.  Some

#$BiologicalSpecies are transmitted transovarially in the arthropod,

which serves as a vector and reservoir.")
(comment ComicStrip "The collection of all comic strips as #$ConceptualWorks - i.e., those humorous ibo's that appear in newspapers and magazines. #$DickTracy-TheComicStrip is an instance of #$ComicStrip as are individual day's episodes of Dick Tracy.")
(comment AbilityOfToTypeFn "(#$AbilityOfToTypeFn AGT TYPE) refers to AGTs ability to engage in TYPE.  For example, (#$AbilityOfToTypeFn #$MichaelJordan (#$PlayingFn #$Basketball-TheGame)) is #$MichaelJordan's ability to play basketball.")
(comment TVCommercial-CW "The collection of all commercials (#$Commercial-CW) designed for broadcast as part of a #$TVBroadcasting")
(comment NLPragmaticPredicate "The collection of all #$NLPredicates used to describe pragmatic properties of words and phrases.")
(comment DigestingInStomach " #$DigestingInStomach takes place in the stomach.  In the stomach, food is converted into absorbable form.  #$DigestingInStomach is a subEvent of #$DigestionEvent.  After a substance is broken down in the #$Stomach, it goes on to the intestine where it is absorbed into the wall of the intestine and into the bloodstream.  At this point, a #$BiologicalAbsorptionEvent subEvent of #$DigestionEvent is occurring, not a #$DigestingInStomach event.")
(disjointWith InternationalPostalCode DoctorME)
(comment Dwarfism "#$Dwarfism is the collection of #$PhysiologicalConditions in which an animal or plant is less than normal in size and lacks the capacity for normal growth. It can be caused by a variety of hereditary factors, diseases, nutrional deficiencies, etc. A person with #$Dwarfism may or may not develop normally intellectually and sexually, depending on the cause of the dwarfism.")
(disjointWith NoSimplerArgument SimplifyBackward)
(comment exampleAssertions "(#$exampleAssertions TERM ASSERTION) means that the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION provides a good example of how to use the #$CycLReifiableDenotationalTerm TERM.")
(comment mtComprehensionConstraint "(#$mtComprehensionConstraint MT PROP) means that the knowledge in MT assumes a level of user sophistication (education, intelligence, experience, etc.) specified by PROP.")
(comment SexOffender "The set of #$Criminals that are guilty of a #$SexualOffense.")
(comment Ship "#$Ship is a specialization of #$HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject, #$PoweredDevice, and #$Watercraft-Surface.  Each instance of #$Ship is a typically large and ocean-going vessel. Notable specializations of #$Ship include #$ModernNavalShip, #$CargoShip, and #$OceanLiner.")
(comment whereRiverEnds "The place, usually land rather than water, where the river ends, eg. N.Y. City for Hudson.")
(comment Headhunter-Corporate "A specialization of #$Consultant.  Each instance of this collection is a person who provides a service of finding employers for white-collar workers, especially in fields related to computer or engineering, and/or of finding individuals qualified to fill such positions.")
(comment BadmintonBirdie "The collection of objects that one hits around while playing a #$BadmintonSportsEvent.")
(comment SilkwormLauncher "Missile launchers for Silkworm missiles.")
(comment Ruthenium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Ruthenium.")
(comment stockIndexValue "This predicate is used to state the index reading for any given group of stocks at any time.  (#$stockIndexValue GROUP DATE NUMBER) means that at DATE, the index number for GROUP is NUMBER.  Note that the DATE in this context should be a specific day and time.  Index values are represented by representing the relevant group of stocks as an instance of #$StockIndexGroup and using #$stockIndexValue.")
(comment relationAllExistsMin-DifferentSpecs "(#$relationAllExistsMin-DifferentSpecs BINPRED COL1 COL2 N) means that for every instance, INS1, of COL1 there are at least N pairwise disjoint subcollections of COL2 each of which contains at least one element bearing the relation BINPRED to INS1.")
(comment Nostalgia "The collection of feelings of homesickness, a kind of wistful longing for things experienced in the past.")
(comment OnlineGameService "The collection of #$ServiceEvents  in which an #$IntelligentAgent provides another the capability to  play online games against multiple players.")
(comment Environment-Generic "The collection of environments -- i.e., #$Places that constitute one's surroundings.  One environment is distinguished from others via its #$EnvironmentalAttributes and its exact location.")
(comment nthSmallestElement "(#$nthSmallestElement X N SET FUNCTION) means that X is an element of SET that has precisely N-1 other elements with a smaller value for FUNCTION. For example, (#$nthSmallestElement #$RhodeIsland-State 1 #$State-UnitedStates (#$FunctionToArg 2 #$areaOfRegion)). Yet there may be more #$nthSmallestElements. For example, (#$nthSmallestElement ?X 3 (#$TheSet 1 2 3 -3) #$AbsoluteValueFn) is true for both 3 and -3 - when the elements in the set are ordered according to their absolute value both 3 and -3 are 3rd smallest elements. ")
(disjointWith CharacterStringToken-Sounded CharacterStringToken-ElectroMagnetic)
(comment Cocaine-Crack "#$Cocaine-Crack is produced by boiling #$Cocaine-Powder in a solution of #$BakingSoda and water, producing 'rocks' of 100-500 miligrams, each about 75-90% pure cocaine. #$Cocaine-Crack is chemically a base form of #$Cocaine, and unlike #$Cocaine-Powder, vaporizes at a low enough temperature to be smoked, but does not dissolve in water and is not readily absorbed into the body if ingested, snorted, or injected. Therefore is generally smoked in a pipe or cigarette, which produces a very rapid effect on the user. The cocaine reaches the brain within 30 seconds, and maximum physiological and psychotropic effects occur within 1-2 minutes. Another base form of #$Cocaine is freebase, which is more dangerous to produce than #$Cocaine-Crack.")
(comment TimesPerSecond "An instance of #$UnitOfFrequency. When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$TimesPerSecond returns an instance of #$Frequency as its value. For example, (#$TimesPerSecond 45) is a frequency of forty-five times per second.")
(comment TouringACity "The collection of all instances of #$SightSeeing which consist of comprehensive tours of cities, usually, but not always,

conducted by a guide.  Instances are to be distinguished by the fact that they are systematic, endeavoring to cover most of the historically salient features of some nontrivial part of the area toured.  Instances may be performed by individual tourists or by groups of the same.  See #$CityTourFn")
(comment SevenElevenStore "A collection of all the local Sears stores. ")
(comment Skateboarder "This is the collection of persons who engage in #$SkateBoarding, either professionally, or as an amateur who  is very serious about the sport.")
(comment (SurvivorSupportGroupFn Murder) "The collection of all survivor support 

groups for people who have been affected by

 a murder.  Candidates for inclusion in

  such groups include neighbors, friends, and 

family members of murder victims, but obviously

 exclude murder victims.")
(comment salientDifferenceBetweenSiblings "#$salientDifferenceBetweenSiblings COL1 COL2 COL3 BINPRED)

means that while for any given instance, INS1, of COL1 there will be an

instance, INS3, of COL3 such that (BINPRED INS1 INS3), this does not

hold for instances of COL2 that are not instances of COL1.  See also

#$salientDifferenceBetweenSiblings-Inverse and #$salientDifferenceBetween for closely related predicates.")
(comment eventDisables "If (#$eventDisables SIT1 SIT2) and there is a known
propositional precondition PRECON for SIT2, then SIT1 causes the
negation of PRECON to become true.")
(comment Crocodilian "The collection of all alligators, crocodiles, caimans and gavials; a subset of #$Reptile.  Each element of #$Crocodilian is a lizard-like aquatic or semi-aquatic reptile.  (#$Crocodilian is not, however, a subset of #$Lizard.)  Crocodilians are amphibious, carnivorous animals with many big sharp teeth and powerful bites.")
(comment FirstInListFn "The function #$FirstInListFn, applied to a list as in (#$FirstInListFn LIST), results in the first item on the list.  For each nonempty #$List, (#$FirstInListFn LIST) = (#$NthInListFn LIST 1). (#$FirstInListFn LIST) is undefined if LIST is #$TheEmptyList.")
(comment Fuse-IgnitionDevice "The #$Fuse-IgnitionDevice is the device used to ignite an  explosion.  It may be as simple as string for a stick of dynamite or as  sophisticated as a radio transmitter.")
(disjointWith ElectricalResistance Pressure)
(comment AnalogyCase "Instances of #$AnalogyCase are collections of propositions that describe some real or hypothetical scenario.")
(comment PerformingACardTrick "A skillful set of actions performed using a deck of cards that seem            like magic, done to entertain people.")
(disjointWith SexualCopulation HomosexualBehavior)
(comment PrecipitationCloud "The collection of clouds that emit #$PrecipitationParticles in instances of #$PrecipitationProcess.")
(comment (LowAmountFn Compressibility) "can be compressed somewhat")
(comment TestingASample "This collection is in contrast to #$Experimenting, although there is some overlap. This is the collection of events in which a sample of something is tested in order to determine something about it: its chemical composition, the presence of certain antibodies, the density of the sample, etc. These events are diagnostic in nature and usually not part of a process, such as those in #$Experimenting, in which a scientific hypothesis is tested.")
(comment Cyc-BasedProject "Collection whose instances represent 

projects based on Cyc.  Used to categorize and organize terms and assertions. 

An example project is #$OpenCycProject.  See also #$myCreationPurpose and

#$assertionAssertPurpose.")
(comment FantasySportsGameOfFn "#$FantasySportsGameOfFn takes any instance

    of Sport-CW and returns its corresponding #$FantasySportsGame

     version.  For example, (#$FantasySportsGameOfFn

   Baseball-TheGame) is the NAT that

    represents fantasy baseball.")
(comment Tablet-Soluble "The collection of all soluble #$TabletDrugs.")
(comment Healing "The collection of events in which a BLO repairs an injury in itself, through biological means rather than externally.  For example, a broken bone heals itself by growing new cells which connect the different pieces of bone - a doctor does NOT heal a patient.")
(comment SeparationEvent "A sub-collection of #$PhysicalEvent.  In each instance of #$SeparationEvent, an object is cut, scraped, broken, cracked or pulverized, so that part of the object is no longer attached where it once was.  Note that the part need not be completely separated from the object; it may still be attached in places.  See the specialization #$Separation-Complete for the case of complete separation.")
(comment SpecialEducationForHandicapped "A collection of education events.  Special education is often provided to mentally handicapped children with special educational needs.")
(comment SystemicHemorrhagicPathology "A collection of events in which an #$AilmentCondition has spread through the body via the #$CirculatorySystem and begins to damage to the body of the host.")
(comment Karst "This is the collection of elements of terrain known as karst.

These are terrain elements which have been formed chiefly by the dissolving of

rock, primarily carbonates such as limestone and evaporites such as salt.

Landforms which count as karst include sinkholes, caves, and natural bridges.")
(comment schoolSymbolName-Male "An instance of #$ProperNamePredicate-Loose and a specialization of #$termStrings.  (#$schoolSymbolName-Male SCHOOL STRING) means that STRING is a common way to refer to SCHOOL-affiliated #$SportsTeams, clubs, and other student organizations.  Accordingly, STRING is normally pluralized (e.g. 'the Ohio State Buckeyes').  Since the advent of co-ed higher education, some schools have found that their symbol-name is exclusionary, and so have gone on to adopt alternative, \"female\" names to apply to female-only teams, clubs, etc.  When entering lexical info for 
a school in such a situation, make sure to use both #$schoolSymbolName-Male and #$schoolSymbolName-Female.")
(comment availableToAgentTypeForEvent "(#$availableToAgentTypeForEvent AGENT-TYPE OBJECT EVENT) means that OBJECT is typically available for agents of type AGENT-TYPE to use in EVENT.  For example, (#$availableToAgentTypeForEvent #$HumanCyclist #$Cyc #$CycProject) means that Cyc is available to human cyclists for use in the Cyc project. If an instance of AGENT-TYPE is capable of using OBJECT in EVENT, nothing prevents that agent from choosing to use OBJECT in EVENT. Compare this predicate to #$availableForEvent and #$availableToAgentTypeForEventType.")
(comment sheetSurfaceConnected "(#$sheetSurfaceConnected SHEET OBJECT) means that SHEET is connected over most of one of its surfaces to a surface of OBJECT.  For example, #$sheetSurfaceConnected would hold between the two parts of a bi-layer membrane.  The sheet(s) may be flexible, but the surface connection is firm (i.e., no sliding can occur without a separation, tearing, or breaking occurring).")
(comment MultiRoleAircraft "The collection of military aircraft which are able to perform several functions.")
(disjointWith Comet Meteoroid)
(comment originallyBroadcastOnNetwork "This predicate is used to related a #$TVShow-IBT with the #$TelevisionNetwork that it was originally broadcast on.")
(comment SalmeterolXinafoate "The chemical compound which is a bronchodilator.")
(comment releases-Underspecified "(#$releases-Underspecified CONTAINER CONTENTS) states that the

abstract container CONTAINER in some underspecified (possibily

metaphoric or non-spatial) manner once but no longer contains

CONTENTS.  For instance, we might say (#$releases-Underspecified

#$Alcatraz-ThePrison #$SeanConnery) or more figuratively,

(#$releases-Underspecified #$MicrosoftInc #$MSWindows).")
(comment DiplomaticAction "The collection of all diplomatic actions.  Instances of #$DiplomaticAction are typically performed by one (or more) country(s), towards some other country(s).  Examples: establishing diplomatic relations, negotiating a peace treaty, or withdrawing the country's ambassador. Specializations of this collection include #$DiplomaticProtest, #$DiplomaticRequest, and #$DiplomaticWarning.  Note that diplomatic actions may be performed by one country towards another during a war between the two, but in general, diplomatic actions themselves are not violent.")
(comment exportRevenueFractionDuring "(#$exportRevenueFractionDuring REGION PRODUCT-TYPE THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the monetary value of exports of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE by the #$GeographicalRegion REGION during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the monetary value of REGION's exports of all goods and services during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that Oman's oil exports accounted for 80 percent of the total value of its exports in 1997, we can say (#$exportRevenueFractionDuring #$Oman #$PetroleumProduct (#$YearFn 1997) (#$Percent 80)).  See also #$exportAmountDuring.")
(comment B-TheLetter "The letter B of the alphabet.  This is 'B' (or 'b') as a #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterB and #$LatinSmallLetterB.")
(comment JobPositionTypeFn "(#$JobPositionTypeFn POS-TYPE) denotes the collection of #$JobPositions such that the duties and responsibilities of these #$JobPositions are typically performed and borne by instances of POS-TYPE. For example, (#$JobPositionTypeFn #$Electrician) denotes all #$JobPositions in which the duties and responsibilities are those typically performed and borne by #$Electricians.")
(comment MilitaryAttache "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Attache.  Each element of #$MilitaryAttache is a person who is officially appointed as a representative of a country's government and military in dealing with another government or military.  For example, the collection #$MilitaryAttache includes the U.S. military attaches in #$Japan, #$Russia, #$China-PeoplesRepublic, and other countries.  Military attaches usually work with higher officials appointed by their country.")
(comment Carpel "A carpel is the part of a flower which encloses ovules; the female spore-bearing structures.")
(comment EurostarChunnelTrain "The collection of Eurostar trains that travel through the Chunnel between London, England and Paris, France.")
(comment AtomicNucleus "A specialization of #$MicroscopicScaleObject.  Each instance of #$AtomicNucleus is an object composed of some definite number of instances of #$Proton and some definite number of instances of #$Neutron.  Each instance of #$Atom has exactly one instance of #$AtomicNucleus as a part.")
(comment CommonBridgeTransporter "A #$CommonBridgeTransporter is a HEMTT chassis with a Load Handling System installed (same as Palletized Load System (PLS)).  It is able to haul Standard Ribbon Bridge bays, Improved Ribbon Bridge bays, Bridge Erection Boat-ShallowDraft, and all fixed bridging (Heavy Dry Support Bridge, MGB and Bailey).  It is capable of transporting a 10 ton load and hauling a loaded (10 tons) PLS trailer.  It can transload and adapter to or from the trailer.  It can upload or down load adapters in one minutes.  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment BakeryMarketCategory "Market category for the kinds of baked goods typically sold in a bakery shop or bakery section of a grocery store.")
(comment eMailDestinationAddress "(#$eMailDestinationAddress MSG ADDRESS) means that MSG is being sent to  ADDRESS.  Note that one message can have several destination addresses, however  any change in these addresses still involves the creation of a new instance of  #$EMailMessage.")
(comment Pseudomonas "A collection of #$Bacterium  in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are #$GramNegativeBacterium, motile with one or several flagellum.  They are also #$AerobicBacterium, and straight or curved rods.  They occur widely in soil, water, plants, and animals.")
(comment Incest "Acts of #$SexualCopulation between persons who are closely related by blood. The legal definition includes persons who are so closely related that they are forbidden to marry. Many instances of #$Incest are also instances of #$Rape.")
(comment Spring-WaterSource "A specialization of #$LandTopographicalFeature.  Each instance of #$Spring-WaterSource is a place from which a small stream of fresh water flows.")
(comment MilitaryAmphibiousPlatform "The collection of military platforms intended to be used on land and in water. These are usually amphibious craft which can transport military equipment and personnel.")
(comment CouldModeFn "(#$CouldModeFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-MT) denotes the      subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances possess the modal property denoted by \"could\", from the perspective of CONTEXT-MT.")
(comment PfizerProductID "each is a 7-character code identifying a product.")
(comment SkinLaceration "Torn or cut skin.")
(comment ZeroArticleFrame "This subcategorization frame is for count nouns which need not take an article, as in 'in spring', or 'in prison'.")
(comment Quadriplegia "The collection of instances of the condition of quadriplegia. Legs, arms, hands and feet are paralyzed.")
(comment regulatesResource "(regulatesResource AUTHORITY RESOURCE) means that the #$ResourceManagementAuthority AUTHORITY is responsible for the  resource RESOURCE.")
(comment GreenParty-Ecological "A collection of #$Organizations.  Each instance of #$GreenParty-Ecological is a #$PoliticalParty organized around the system of #$GreenBeliefs.  Note that this collection does not include the Green Party of Libya.")
(comment GiftTypeByReligion "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$GiftTypeByReligion is a collection of instances of #$Gifts that are all associated with a particular religious faith.")
(comment organismsQuarantined "(#$organismsQuarantined QUARANTINE ORGANISM) means that ORGANISM is quarantined to a certain region, according to the standards of QUARANTINE.")
(comment Berkelium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Berkelium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment enables-RemovesUnspecifiedFactors "This predicate is a generalization of the more specific
predicates of the form 'enables-Removes????Factors'. It may be used to
assert that an event enables an agent to do something when it's clear that
the relevant sense of 'enabling' is that of 'removing generally negative
factors' but it's not equally clear whether the negative factors removed
were incapacitating, disabling or merely contrary. Please check the
documentation for this and related constants thoroughly before settling on
this predicate: assertions involving it are not likely to be helpful in
inference.")
(comment ComputerProcess-Distributed "The subcollection of #$ComputerProcess-Generic whose instances
execute in parallel on multiple CPUs.")
(comment AuxiliaryWritingSymbol "The subcollection of #$WritingSymbolCharacter whose instances are auxiliary writing symbols, including punctuation symbols, diacritic symbols, etc.  Instances are abstract linguistic objects.  Cf. #$AuxiliaryWritingMark for the collection of concrete written and printed tokens of these symbols (i.e. marks on paper and the like).")
(comment CircularWindSystem "A collection of generally circular systems of winds which whirl (see #$WhirlingOfFluid), normally while proceding along or above the Earth's surface.  This is a general term including everything from hurricanes and tornados down to dust devils.  A negative exemplar would be air moving in a spiral fashion as it comes out of the back of a jet engine.")
(comment HickJoke "A specialization of #$RuralLaboringClassJoke, #$HickJoke is the collection of all jokes that are based on stereotypes about so-called \"hicks\".")
(comment Interval-BoundedAbove "A specialization of #$ScalarInterval.  Each instance of #$Interval-BoundedAbove is an interval that has an upper bound.  Example: the interval comprised by integers less than 10.")
(comment EnglishLexicalItem "The set of items which form the lexicon of English. This
includes both free morphemes, like 'dog', and bound morphemes, like
affixes.")
(comment Baking-Hardening "A collection of events, and a subset of #$HeatingProcess.  In each #$Baking-Hardening event, a semisolid object is heated to a high temperature in order to transform it to a rigid, hardened, solid state.  Examples of this collection include: a particular event in which someone bakes cookie dough into cookies, or fires a clay pot, etc.")
(comment preconditionFor-PropSit "The predicate #$preconditionFor-PropSit is used to state a necessary precondition for a certain event or situation. (#$preconditionFor-PropSit PROP SIT) means that unless the proposition PROP is true, the #$Situation SIT won't obtain.")
(comment (AttendingFn EntertainmentEvent) "(#$AttendingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) is the collection of subevents of instances of #$EntertainmentEvent which subevents consist of the attending of some instance of #$EntertainmentEvent. So assertions about (#$AttendingFn EntertainmentEvent) should be assertions about attending an entertainment event, as opposed to performing in, or hosting, or otherwise producing an entertainment event. Note that (#$AttendingFn EntertainmentEvent) is a spec of #$RecreationalActivity, whereas its complement, (#$PerformingFn #$EntertainmentEvent), which picks out only the subevents of instances of #$EntertainmentEvent which involve the production end of an entertainment event, is a spec of #$ServiceEvent.")
(comment BiologicalWeapon-Rickettsial "The collection of all #$BiologicalWeapons that make use of rickettsial organisms.")
(comment AprilFoolsDay "A subset of #$Holiday, instances of the collection #$AprilFoolsDay are characterized by the fact that, during them, people tell instances of the collection #$AprilFoolsJoke.")
(comment Spectroscopy "This is the technique of analyzing the chemical composition

of a substance by seeing what sort of spectrum of electromagnetic radiation is emits

when stimulated.")
(comment IrrigationAdministration "Cleansing a canal, such as the bladder and colon, with water or some other liquid.")
(comment mediaSeriesTopics "This predicate characterizes the type of content shared by instances of a #$MediaSeriesProductType.  (#$mediaSeriesTopics SERIES THING) means that every instance of SERIES contains information about THING. For instance, topics of the magazine series 'Field and Stream' include #$Hunting and #$Fishing.")
(comment IntermediateVocabPredicate "The collection of instances of #$Predicate that

 are important for NL parsing by contributing to an intermediate

 vocabulary between the English to be parsed, and

 the terse CycL that will be used in inferencing.")
(comment PresentationProtocolDataUnit "#$PresentationProtocolDataUnit is the collection of discrete blocks of

data that are composed by instances of #$PresentationLayerProtocol and passed

down to a #$SessionLayerProtocol or #$TransportLayerProtocol. 

PPDUs contain data generated by an application.")
(comment BlackMagic "The collection of actions which are considered,  by the adherents of some belief system, to be religious or sacred (lit.: 'set apart').  Many such actions are also instances of #$Ritual (q.v.).")
(comment Bee "The collection of bees.")
(comment Hydrogen "The chemical element distinguished by the fact that each of its atomic nuclei has exactly one proton.")
(comment TendingBar "The actual activity of making drinks and serving them - and the peanuts - to customers at a bar.")
(comment FloralWreath "A subset of #$Wreath-Decoration.  The collection of wreaths that are made of #$CutFlowers.")
(comment ArmoredPersonnelCarrier-BTR60 "A type of armored personnel carrier which Iran is known to possess.")
(comment CycLAtomicSentence "The collection of syntactically well-formed atomic sentences in the CycL language. Each instance of #$CycLAtomicSentence consists of a CycL constant denoting a #$Predicate followed by one or more (closed or open) CycL terms, with the entire sequence enclosed in parentheses.  Thus CycL atomic sentences never contain other sentences as truth-functional components (see #$TruthFunction).  Note that \"atomic\" as used here specifically in connection with _sentences_, has a less strict meaning than it does when applied to terms generally, where it means \"not constructible from other terms via CycL syntax\" (see #$CycLAtomicTerm).")
(comment MotoCrossTrack "A dirt race track used for dirt bike racing.")
(disjointWith RecreationalActivity AcademicTesting)
(comment Bodyboarding "The collection of all bodyboarding events. Bodyboarding is a recreational water activity in which a #$Person uses a #$Bodyboard to ride water waves. Bodyboarders typically ride the #$Bodyboard in a prone position or while kneeling, in contrast to surfers who ride waves standing on a #$Surfboard.")
(comment geneticTemplateFor "(#$geneticTemplateFor TRANSFER OBJ) means that OBJ serves as a genetic template in TRANSFER. See also #$geneticTemplateFrom.")
(comment BallisticMissile-Guided "The collection of #$BallisticMissiles which can change course in flight using either remote guidance, such as radio control, or internal guidance, such as on-board heat-seeking sensors.")
(comment Inverter "An electrical device whose one input and one output are digital signals and that implements the logical NOT function.")
(disjointWith PartialRotation MultirevolutionRotation)
(comment FederalSupplyDepot "A collection of organizations; a subset of both #$StorageOrganization and #$USFederalGovernmentOrganization.  An element of #$FederalSupplyDepot is a United States Federal government supply depot.  Federal supply depots are collection, storage, and distribution organizations which supply some goods to other government organizations.  They may be located inside or outside the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment SummerJob "The collection of #$JobPositions that are for the summer months only, and  that are typically held by students.")
(comment holdsInPlace-Somewhere "(#$holdsInPlace-Somewhere MT PLACE) means that the assertions in MT are true at least somewhere in the spatial extent of PLACE.  See also #$holdsInPlace-Everywhere.")
(comment Caning "The collection of #$Canings, which involve the hitting of a person with a cane, stick, or similar object.")
(comment Wagon "#$Wagon is a specialization of #$TransportationContainerProduct, #$WheeledTransportationDevice, and #$MusclePoweredDevice. Each instance of #$Wagon is a relatively small non-motorized wheeled device (usually with two or more wheels) used for moving goods.  Instances of #$Wagon are usually human-powered or animal-powered.")
(comment termChosen "(#$termChosen TERM) is true for any closed Cyc TERM, and indicates that TERM has been chosen from the set of terms in the universe of discourse.  This predicate is primarily used on a variable so that the moment of choice of a particular term as the binding for that variable can be identified.  There should never be methods for generating bindings for non-closed #$termChosen literals.")
(comment ColdMedicine "Over-the-counter commercial products (like Contac) designed to combat the common cold.")
(comment GenreStartFn "(#$GenreStartFn GENRE) returns the #$TimePoint at which the #$IBTContentType
  GENRE--e.g. a particular artistic movement--began.")
(comment GaseousFlowAlongPipe "The collection of all flowings of #$GaseousTangibleThing (including #$Air) along some constraining #$Pipe-GenericConduit or vessel. This does not include any flow in an open #$GutterSystem .  Examples include air-flow in the #$BronchialTubes, forced air ventilation through ducts, pneumatic air hoses, etc.")
(comment CavityInterior-Generic "A subcollection of #$SpatialThing-Localized whose instances are \"cavity interiors\", which might be either the intangible space region inside a cavity's walls (see #$CavityInteriorRegion) or the (partially) tangible material that occupies this region (see #$CavityInteriorContent).")
(comment SexualAbuse "The collection of #$SexualOffenses in which there is overt or covert #$HumanSexualBehavior between two #$Persons when the following conditions exist:   (1) The balance of power and authority (meaning psychological power, economic power, role status power, etc.) between the two #$Persons is unequal, and and  (2) The two #$Persons have an established emotional connection (such as between a child and a caregiver, or a child and authority figure). Instances of #$SexualAbuse can involve two #$HumanAdults as long as the above conditions hold, for example, #$SexualBehavior between an institutional caregiver and an adult for whom he/she cares.")
(comment Coalition-International "A collection of groups of nations which are cooperating on or allied in some issue, task, or endeavor.  Although they are considered international alliances, coalitions are typically not as long-term or institutionalized as are long-standing alliances such as #$NATO.")
(comment AOLComputerProgram "The collection of #$ApplicationPrograms that are developed and/or used by users belonging to the #$AmericaOnlineInc community in order to interact somehow with the #$AmericaOnlineInc  #$WorldWideWebClientProgram.")
(comment CarryingOnFoot "Bearing something while moving on foot, causing it to move also, either with or without a container.  The object being carried does not touch the ground and is supported by the person carrying it.")
(comment Thymine-Base "A collection of molecules. #$Thymine-Base is one of the four kinds of nitrogen
base, #$NitrogenBaseType, that enter in the constitution of instances of Thymine-Nucleotide. Its abbreviattion is T.")
(comment HepatitisA-Virus "A collection of viri. Instances of #$HepatitisA-Virus are virus of the kind responsible for instances of #$HepatitisA-Infection.")
(comment Freezing "A specialization of #$StateOfMatterChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$Freezing is an event in which an object is cooled to a temperature at or below its freezing point (see the predicate #$freezingPoint), and is thereby changed from a #$Liquid-StateOfMatter to a #$Solid-StateOfMatter.")
(comment EntertainmentPerformer "#$EntertainmentPerformer is the collection of all artists/arts organizations whose performances ordinarily occur in the context of a 'running show,' like a concert tour or a broadway musical.  Instances thus include individual comedians, rock stars, particular Ballet Companies, circus performers, the Icecapades performance troupe.")
(comment SecureGatewaySystem "The collection of all instances of #$SecureGatewaySystem, a specific type of gateway used by the US military. 'Gateway' is a generic term to refer to any of a variety of security devices. In general, gateways are mechanisms to control access to services and resources within a local area network (LAN)or group of LANs, authenticate requesters, perform auditing, provide secure transmission protocols, support virtual private networks using encryption, and enforce limited virus protection capabilities.")
(comment MediumEnduranceCutter "The collection of military medium endurance cutters.")
(disjointWith LeftRiverbank RightRiverbank)
(disjointWith CleaningDevice Path-InfoTransfer)
(comment InitiatingTransaction-CommunicationAct "This collection denotes communication acts that serve as both an Offer and a Request that a transaction be made.  If the #$CommunicationAct-Single is accepted, then there is an informal agreement.")
(comment Phosphorus "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of phosphorus; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form -- but not necessarily.")
(disjointWith Mace-ArilOfNutmegSeed Mace-TheSpice)
(comment ImmediatelyLifeThreateningCondition "The collection of physiological conditions which present an immediate threat to the life of the animal that they afflict.")
(comment Toyota4WDTruck "A collection of all Toyota brand trucks with four wheel drive.")
(comment FacilityManagementUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military organizations whose purpose is to           facilitate management operations at military installations.")
(comment areaInSquareBlocks "(#$areaInSquareBlocks REGION N) means that the urban area REGION consists of N contiguous instances of  #$CityBlock.  If REGION is a proper subregion of a city block, then N should be 0.  This predicate obviously does  not correspond to an absolute measure of the area of REGION,  as city blocks can vary considerably in size.  Yet it can  be useful for rough estimates and comparisons of area.")
(disjointWith EnteringAUsername EnteringAComputerPassword)
(comment AqueousSolutionFn "(#$AqueousSolutionFn PERCENT SUBSTANCETYPE) returns the collection of all #$LiquidSolutions in which (#$LiquidFn #$Water) is the solvent, and the volume of dissolved solute is PERCENT times the volume of solvent.")
(comment vaccineEffectiveAgainstMicroorgType "This predicate relates microorganisms to the collection of vaccines (i.e., instances, not types)  that are effective against them.")
(comment WindyClimateCycle "The collection of climate cycles that are frequently windy.")
(disjointWith ZipCode ProperNameString)
(comment CalendarMillennium "An instance of #$CalendarCoveringType, and a specialization of #$Date,
each instance of #$CalendarMillennium is a millennium on
a particular calendar.")
(comment TrajectoryThroughAir "The collection of all trajectories of objects moving through air (mid-air).  Such a #$Trajectory exists as the #$trajectory-Complete for any #$Movement-TranslationEvent all of which passes through mid-air.  This includes arbitrary traces through the air.  A #$TrajectoryThroughAir may or may not follow a designated or pre-defined #$PathThroughAir.  The moving object is immersed in, and supported, if supported at all, by the air.  Thus it excludes a #$SolidSurfaceTrajectoryThroughAir and a #$WaterSurfaceTrajectory.  For a pre-designated #$Path-Generic through airspace, use #$PathThroughAir.")
(comment PrivateThirdPartyHealthCarePayer "Instances are health care plans/organizations which are private health care payers such as HMOs, PPOs, medical insurance companies, etc.")
(comment principalLandmarksOfCity "(#$principalLandmarksOfCity CITY LANDMARK) means that LANDMARK is considered to be one of the chief 'landmarks' of CITY in the context of the assertion, such that the average person with a smattering of geography can generally be counted on to think of CITY when presented with a picture of LANDMARK.  Examples include the #$EiffelTower in the #$CityOfParisFrance and #$TheAlamo in the #$CityOfSanAntonioTX.")
(comment OscillatingTrajectory "A oscillating trajectory where there is not really a net change in location.")
(disjointWith PathArtifact Facility-Construct)
(comment Ichor "an ethereal fluid taking the place of blood in the veins of the ancient Greek gods.")
(comment dateOfDisbandment "This predicate relates a multi-individual agent (see

#$MultiIndividualAgent) to the date that it stopped functioning

together as a single agent at least with respect to its previous

primary function.  After this date, it should no longer be the case

that the multi-indiviudal agent performs its primary function unless

the multi-individual agent is somehow intentionally resurrected and reunited.

However, it may be the case that the multi-individual agent is

rejuvenated, hence this isn't necessarily an ending date (although it

will be by default rule). Note that it may still be possible to talk

about the ''disbanded'' agent as an actor in an event even after it

has disbanded.  For instance, the Rolling Stones might conceivably

disband and continue to work together on fundraising for their

favourite drug rehabilitation project or as litigants in a litigation.

However, it would not be the case that a disbanded music group would

perform music as that group.")
(comment Nadolol "The chemical compound which is a beta blocker.  This drug is intended to be used for therapeutic treatment of hypertension.")
(comment codeTransducer-FunctionalRole "(#$codeTransducer-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that
AGENT is supposed to take some informational input in the form of
instances of #$InformationBearingObject and change the form in which
the information is encoded, while preserving semantic content as far
as possible.")
(comment Colon-ElSalvador "The unit of currency for ElSalvador-AtPresent.")
(disjointWith Credential TradeableSecurity)
(comment AtmosphericScience "This is the collection of scientific fields of study

whose object of study is some aspect of planetary atmospheres, especially that of our planet.")
(comment Sisal-Fiber "Quantities of fiber derived from the leaves of sisal agave.")
(comment relationExistsExistsSpec "(#$relationExistsExistsSpec PRED COL1 COL2) means that there

exists a subcollection of COL2, SUBCOL2, such that there exists an instance

of COL1, INS1, such that (PRED INS1 SUBCOL2).")
(comment HobbyVersionFn "This function takes any spec SPEC of #$Event

  and returns the collection of instances of SPEC

  performed as a hobby.  For example,

   (#$HobbyVersionFn (#$PlayingFn 

    #$Golf)) is the collection

  of golf-playing events done as a hobby.")
(comment FighterInterceptorPlane "#$The collection of military aircraft designed primarily for use against other aircraft or airborne weapons.")
(comment Rabbi "Each instance of #$Rabbi is Jewish religious leader, qualified to lead (and who typically does lead) some synagogue.")
(comment Plague-Bacterium "An instance of #$BiologicalSpecies, and a specialization of #$BacterialBioAgent.  #$Plague-Bacterium is a species (Yersinia pestis) of bacterium (see the collection #$Bacterium) that causes bubonic plague (see the collection #$BubonicPlague.")
(comment AnimatedTVShow "A collection of TVShow(s) (that is moving images with sound) which are animated. Please see the comment for TVShow for a more detailed explanation of this collection.")
(comment LyricsToMusicFn-Genre "#$LyricsToMusicFn-Genre takes as argument any instance of #$MusicTypeByGenre and returns the collection of all instances #$Lyric-WordsToSong which are the lyrics of some piece of music belonging to that genre. For Example, (#$LyricsToMusicFn-Genre #$RapMusic) would return the collection of lyrics to rap songs.")
(comment InfectionFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to a specialization PART of #$AnimalBodyPart (q.v.), #$InfectionFn returns the collection of all infections in some instance of PART.  For example, (#$InfectionFn #$Throat) is the collection of all throat infections (and hence a specialization of #$Infection).")
(comment hotelsAccessibleTVNewsLanguages "This predicate relates a hotel to the broadcast languages of the television news shows that can be accessed in guest room.")
(disjointWith ProperNameString InternationalPostalCode)
(comment interArg4ResultIsa "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$isa based relationship holds between the fourth argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg4ResultIsa FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fourth argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg4ResultIsa _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultIsa.")
(comment Dwarfism-Proportionate "The collection of #$Dwarfism cases in which the dwarf's proportions are essentially the same as a non-dwarf's. In humans, proportionate dwarfism is usually caused by hormonal deficiency and can be treated medically.")
(comment OnlineAuction "The collection of all #$Auction-Events conducted through a #$WorldWideWebSite. A description of each item up for bids is placed on the website, and bidders submit their bids electronically. The transaction is generally mediated by the operators of the website.")
(comment mtAdditionConstraint "(#$mtAdditionConstraint MT PROP) means that the constraints specified in PROP must be satisfied in order for assertions to be added to MT, by a user or an application.  If multiple #$mtAdditionConstraint gafs are asserted for a #$Microtheory, each one must be satisfied in order for assertions to be added.  See also #$domainAssumptions.")
(disjointWith Ship Device-SingleUser)
(comment whereRiverStarts "(#$whereRiverStarts RIVER START) means that START is the #$GeographicalRegion where the #$River RIVER originates.  START may be a county, state, town, mountain range, etc.  For example, (#$whereRiverStarts #$PearlRiver #$NeshobaCountyMississippi).")
(comment BlackGuillemot "The collection of all members of a species (Cepphus grylle) of Arctic #$Bird.  In summer, instances of this collection are black with white wing patches; in winter, mostly white with white wing patches.  Their  feet are red")
(comment MetricConversion "The collection of all mental events in which the subject converts a measurement to or from the metric system.")
(comment Farmer "A specialization of #$PersonWithOccupation.  Each instance of #$Farmer is a person who makes (or significantly supplements) his or her income by farming, where farming includes such activities as growing vegetables, grain, or fruit crops, dairy farming, and raising livestock (e.g., cattle, pigs, sheep, fish) for their meat or other animal products (e.g., wool).")
(comment WeaponForSports "The collection of all #$Weapons that are designed primarily for use in sports competitions and *not* for use in injuring people or animals. This collection does *not* include weapons designed for use in #$Hunting, but rather includes things like #$FencingFoils and #$Javelins.")
(comment SilkwormTEL "Military vehicles used to transport, erect and launch Silkworm missiles.")
(comment Antimony "AntimonyStuff.  A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of antimony; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment TankerCaptain "Members of this collection are captains of tanker-ships.")
(comment YahooGames "The collection of #$OnlineGameService events  provided by #$YahooInc.")
(comment formerName "(#$formerName THING NAME) means that NAME was once, but is no longer commonly in use as the name for THING. For example (#$formerName #$TheArtistFormerlyKnownAsPrince \"Prince\") indicates that the singer and composer of \"1999\" previously was named Prince.")
(comment OccupationalPhysicalEnvironmentalQuantity "The collection of #$PhysicalAttributes that generally apply to one's #$WorkEnvironment.")
(comment receivesServicesFrom "This predicate relates potential service recipients to service providers that are bound to provide services of some type to that agent.  The first argument place should be the potential recipient of service and the second argument place should contain the potential service provider.  The relationship holds while the agreement to provide the service is in place, not just while the service is being provided.  This agreement need not be a formal agreement but it should involve the service provider in a task for which he, she, it or the service provider's controller is paid, although not necessarily by the service recipient.  Hence, #$mother is not a specpred (#$specs) of this predicate but the relationship between a client and social worker or between parishioner and priest might be even if the client or parishioner does not pay for the service.  If a company, Company001, puts a lawyer, Lawyer001, on retainer, then it is true that (#$receivesServicesFrom Company001 Lawyer001) even before the lawyer has provided any services.  Usually it is preferable to use one of the specializations of this predicate. See, for instance, #$accountants, #$attorneys or #$hasWorkers. #$receivesServicesFrom is more general than #$hasWorkers as it can describe the relationship between a person and her dentist or priest and the relationship between an organization that may occassionally receive a service from an agent, e.g. a subcontractor.  If a business, Business001 has a certain accountancy firm, AccountantsRUs001, perform occasional bookkeeping work, it is not true throughout the year that (#$hasWorkers BusinessOO1 AccountsRUs001) but it may be true throughout the year that (#$receivesServicesFrom Business001 AccountantsRUs001).")
(comment conditionCharacterizedBy "(#$conditionCharacterizedBy CONDTYPE REGTYPE) means that
instances of the #$PhysiologicalCondition type CONDTYPE are
characterized, as a matter of definition, by the #$bodilyDoer of the
condition having an #$AnimalBodyRegion of type REGTYPE as a
#$physicalParts for the duration of the instance of the condition-type.")
(comment Cocaine-Powder "#$Cocaine-Powder is a white, powdery salt (cocaine hydrochloride) produced by reacting coca paste with hydrochloric acid. It is the most commonly used form of #$Cocaine. #$Cocaine-Powder cannot be taken into the body by smoking, because it vaporizes at a relatively high temperature. Users 'snort' it (inhale it into the nose), or dissolve it in water and inject it.")
(comment HallmarkOrnament "The collection of #$ChristmasTreeDecoration made by #$HallmarkCards-CommercialOrganization.")
(comment (SurvivorSupportGroupFn Suicide) "This is the collection of all support

  groups for people whose lives have been

  impacted by suicide.  Candidates for membership

   in such groups include family members, friends,

  neighbors, etc. of suicide victims, but obviously

  not suicide victims.")
(comment ComputerAuditLogFile "A specialization of #$ComputerLogFile.  Each instance of #$ComputerAuditLogFile is a file in which audit information for a network (often security-related) is stored.")
(disjointWith Watercraft-Small Watercraft-Subsurface)
(comment RestOfListFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  When applied to an instance LIST of #$List, #$RestOfListFn returns another list having as members all but the first item in LIST, in the same order.  To put it more precisely, for each instance LIST of #$List with LIST not equal to #$TheEmptyList, (#$RestOfListFn LIST) is the list obtained from LIST by taking away the first member of LIST.  If the first member of LIST is ITEM and LIST = (#$JoinListsFn (#$TheList ITEM) THE-LIST-OF-THE-REST), then (#$RestOfListFn LIST) = THE-LIST-OF-THE-REST.  Note that (#$RestOfListFn LIST) is undefined if LIST is #$TheEmptyList and that (#$RestOfListFn LIST) is #$TheEmptyList if the length of LIST is 1.")
(comment Fuse-IgnitionDevice-DelayedImpact "The collection of #$Fuse-IgnitionDevices that ignite an explosion  shortly after impact.  This is used primarily against structures or armor, so  that the warhead has time to penetrate before exploding.")
(disjointWith ElectricalResistance Volume)
(comment fertilityRate "(#$fertilityRate PLACE RATE) means that the average number of children borne by women residing in PLACE is RATE.")
(comment AnalogyCorrespondence "Instances of #$AnalogyCorrespondence represent a correspondence between some item or statement in the base #$AnalogyCase and some item or statement in the target #$AnalogyCase, with respect to a given #$AnalogyMatch. As such, it can appear in multiple mappings under the same match. However, its structural evaluation is the same for every mapping.  Note, #$AnalogyCorrespondence is very much like #$AnalogyMatch but the first links items, or statements, in cases and the second links cases.")
(comment StudyAbroad "A collection of events. Each instance of #$StudyAbroad involves           one #$Person going to a foreign country to study for a certain           duration (usually one year).")
(comment PuffyCloud "Cumulus clouds.  Puffy white clouds.  For example, the kind you see on nice days.  But not neccessarily limited to those (e.g. thunderclouds from afar may look like these.")
(comment (MediumAmountFn Compressibility) "Can be compressed to less than half its volume")
(comment Phytoremediation "This is the collection of events in which plants and trees are used to (help) clean up contaminated soil and water.")
(comment modeOfCharacterType "This predicate relates a type of character token 
  to certain specializations within that type. 
  (#$modeOfCharacterType MODE TYPE) means that MODE is a
  specialization of TYPE whose instances all realize the
  corresponding character in the same general way, e.g. as
  inscriptions, or as sounds, or as electromagnetic encodings.
  For example, if MODE is an instance of #$CharacterMode-Inscribed 
  and TYPE corresponds to the uppercase letter 'W', then MODE is 
  the collection of all inscribed tokens of 'W'.")
(comment TemperatureChangingProcess "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  In each instance of #$TemperatureChangingProcess, the temperature of some object is changed.  Specializations of #$TemperatureChangingProcess include the collections #$CookingFood and #$Freezing.")
(comment BedRail "The collection of all #$BedRails that can be attached to a #$HumanToddler's bed to keep him or her from rolling off.")
(comment Capsule-ContinuousDelivery "The collection of all continuous-delivery #$CapsuleDrugs.")
(comment NucleusEmittingASubAtomicParticle "An #$EmittingAnObject event in which a single unstable atomic nucleus loses energy by emitting a single #$SubAtomicParticle such as a AlphaParticle, BetaParticle or GammaParticle.  The nucleus (the #$emitter) undergoes a transformation from one isotope to another or from one element to another.  The higher the chance of a #$NucleusEmittingASubAtomicParticle happening, the shorter the half-life of the substance which the nucleus makes up.")
(comment DreamInterpretation "The collection of activities in which someone analyzes a #$Dream. Typically, objects or storylines found in a dream are interpreted as having some psychological or symbolic significance for the dreamer. There are many different kinds of dream interpretation, including dream analysis based on Freudian principles.")
(comment PainInFn "#$PainInFn is a Cyc function that is used to describe pain in a particular region of an animal's body.  (#$PainInFn REGION) denotes the collection of pain felt in REGIONS.")
(comment Pomona-PitzerCollegesAthleticsProgram "This is the collection of all sports teams

    who compete under the banner of 'Pomona-Pitzer.'  Members of

     such teams are students at either #$PomonaCollege

     or #$PitzerCollege -- two small colleges with no

     sports teams of their very own.")
(comment in-Among "(#$in-Among OBJ GROUP) means that the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ is physically located within the tangible #$Group GROUP.  OBJ may (but need not) be a member of GROUP.  OBJ is spatially distinct (see the predicate #$spatiallyDisjoint) from any (other) group-member of GROUP.  Examples: a bird in the branches of a tree would be #$in-Among those branches, and a zebra in its herd would be #$in-Among that herd.")
(comment reliabilityOfMicrotheory "(#$reliabilityOfMicrotheory MICROTHEORY NR) means that NR is a measure of the reliability of the assertions in the #$Microtheory MICROTHEORY.  A reliability of 1 means the content of MICROTHEORY is entirely reliable; a reliability of 0 means the content of MICROTHEORY is entirely unreliable.  For example, a microtheory the content of which is blatantly false would have a reliability of 0, as would a microtheory each assertion in which was chosen from a pair consisting of the assertion and its negation by flipping a coin.  There is, of course, a spectrum at one end of which would be guaranteed falsehoods, at the other guaranteed truths, and in the middle would be assertions equally likely true as false.  For the purposes for which this predicate is intended, however, we are interested in a spectrum which

is a proper part of the former one -- the idea is that being as likely true as false is a minimum threshold.")
(comment CoronaOfStar "The halo of hot gas visible around the main body of a #$Star such as the #$Sun. The corona is often only plainly visible when this main body is fully obscured, as for instance during a #$SolarEclipse.")
(comment Outlaw "The set of people thought to live outside the reach of the law.  Outlaws are generally criminals, though some outlaws are on the run from the law because they are thought to be criminals even though they may not have actually committed any crimes.  #$Outlaw differs from #$Fugitive, in that #$Outlaws need not be on the run from the law (for example, because the law might be afraid of them), while #$Fugitives are actively trying to avoid capture.")
(comment CefpodoximeProxetil "The chemical compound which is an antibiotic.")
(comment C-TheLetter "The letter C of the alphabet.  This is 'C' (or 'c') as a #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.  As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterC and #$LatinSmallLetterC.")
(comment UnderwritingOfLoan "The collection of #$Underwritings in which an #$IntelligentAgent, who is a #$creditor on the relevant #$LoanAgreement, accepts the risk of losing the funds borrowed in that #$LoanAgreement, in return for payment in the form of interest.")
(comment versionOfJobPosition "(#$versionOfJobPosition JOB RELATION) means that the version of #$JobPosition JOB is the #$HasPositionRelationship RELATION. An instance of #$JobPosition can have more than one version because the same #$JobPosition can be filled successively by more than one person. A different #$HasPositionRelationship is created each time a different person fills the same #$JobPosition JOB. Each of these #$HasPositionRelationships bear the relation #$versionOfJobPosition to the same #$JobPosition, although these relations hold at different time intervals. Two different people cannot bear the #$versionOfJobPosition relation to the same #$JobPosition during the same time interval. For example, suppose #$Cycorp has a #$JobPosition, OntologicalEngineer01. At t1, the position is open (see #$JobOpen). At t2, David Smith is hired to fill this position (see #$JobFilled) . At t2, a #$HasPositionRelationship, OntologicalEngineer01DS begins, the relation between David Smith and #$Cycorp. At t2, it's true that (#$versionOfJobPosition OntologicalEngineer01 OntologicalEngineer01DS). At t3, David Smith resigns. At t4, Kevin Jones is hired to fill the #$JobPosition OntologicalEngineer01, and a new #$HasPositionRelationship, OntologicalEngineer01KJ is created. At t4, it's true that (#$versionOfJobPosition OntologicalEngineer01 OntologicalEngineer01KJ). On the other hand, if David Smith and Kevin Jones were each hired by #$Cycorp at the same time as ontological engineers, there would be two #$JobPositions at #$Cycorp, and each person would bear a #$versionOfJobPosition to different instances of #$JobPosition.")
(comment CulturalAttache "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Attache.  Each element of #$CulturalAttache is a person who is officially appointed as a representative of a country's government in dealing with another government.  For example, the collection #$CulturalAttache includes the U.S. cultural attaches in #$Japan, #$Russia, #$China-PeoplesRepublic, and other countries.  Cultural attaches usually work with higher officials appointed by their country, and are attached to an embassy or mission.")
(comment Pistil "Flower gynoecium, composed of a single pistil or several fused organs.")
(comment Meteora-Monastery "The collection of monatsery that are located in the Meteora region in Greece.")
(disjointWith Propelling PullingWithoutTranslation)
(comment Proton "A specialization of #$Nucleon.  Each instance of #$Proton is a nucleon which has an #$ElectricalCharge of +1.")
(comment BridgeErectionBoat-ShallowDraft "The collection of boats designed to facilitate #$RibbonBridge and port construction, and other amphibious and waterborne operations.")
(comment BatikDyeing "The collection of cloth dyeing events whose purpose is the production of 
#$BatikCloth")
(comment IceCube "The man made stuff which you can eat without getting sick. Often not cube shaped.  Often made at home in the freezer.  Sometimes small enough to be held between two fingers, sometimes as big as a cinder block.")
(comment Manga "A style  of comic and cartoon drawing, currently (year 2000) extremely popular in Japan, and fast becoming so elsewhere. It is said that the famous Japanese painter Hokusai used the term to brand `irresponsible pictures'. Animated Manga comics are called #$Anime.")
(comment computerIP "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$Computer with instances of #$IPAddress. (#$computerIP COMP IP) means that COMP has the IP address IP. (Note that a given computer might have different IP addresses at different times.)")
(comment MessagePiggyBacking "This is the collection of events in which unauthorized information is attached to  a legitimate message which is being sent outside the security perimeter of some  network.")
(comment PseudomonasAeruginosa "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are a #$Saprophyte in humans and causes disease in humans with abnormal host defenses, for example, when mucous membranes and skin are disrupted by direct tissue damage.")
(comment fileCopyFormat "This predicate relates a copy of a file to a particular #$ComputerFileTypeByFormat. (#$fileCopyFormat FILE FORMAT) means that the #$ComputerFileCopy FILE has the #$ComputerFileTypeByFormat FORMAT.")
(comment Sea "A specialization of both #$BodyOfWater-Large and #$SeaWater.  Each instance of #$Sea is a body of salt water as large as (or larger than) a lake.  Instances of #$Sea include #$PacificOcean, #$IonianSea, #$EastChinaSea, and #$BlackSea.")
(comment chemicalBondTypeBetween "(#$chemicalBondTypeBetween BOND-TYPE CHEMICALOBJECT1 CHEMICALOBJECT2) means that a bond of type BOND-TYPE exists between CHEMICALOBJECT1 and CHEMICALOBJECT2.")
(comment recommendedTouristGift "(#$recommendedTouristGift PERSON GIFT) means that it is recommended that the instance of #$Person PERSON purchase as a gift an instance of #$ProductType GIFT.  In the context of vacation and travel itineraries, PERSON is assumed to be a #$Tourist visiting some #$GeographicalRegion.")
(comment SurgicalIncision "Deliberate cut made in skin for the purpose of medical treatment; special conditions are assumed to apply: sterile implements, controlled bleeding, repair of the wound immediately following the interior procedure.")
(comment FrameForNouns "The class of #$SubcategorizationFrames which make sense for nouns.")
(comment StarTrek-TVSeries "A collection of #$TVSeriesProducts.  The instances of #$StarTrek-TVSeries are specific Star Trek television series, each of which is has a number of episodes [#$TVShow-CW] as #$subWorks.  Each instance of #$StarTrek-TVSeries is set in the #$FictionalContext of the Star Trek universe.  Instances of #$StarTrek-TVSeries include #$StarTrek-Classic, #$StarTrek-TNG, #$StarTrek-DS9, and #$StarTrek-Voyager.")
(comment NationalDefenseGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with the military defense of a country.")
(comment MachineGun-M242 "The 25mm M242 Bushmaster cannon used on the Bradley Fighting  Vehicle and a variety of land and sea vehicles.  The Marine Corps carries  this weapon on the Light Armored Vehicle (LAV) while the Navy carries it on  many of its ocean-going vessels to deal with small attack craft. The M242  25mm Bushmaster Chain Gun, manufactured by McDonnell Douglas, has a single  barrel with an integrated dual-feed mechanism and remote ammunition selection. Either armor piercing (AP) or high explosive (HE) ammunition may be selected  with the flick of a switch. The Gunner may select from single or multiple  shot modes. The standard rate of fire is 200 rounds per minute, and has a range of 2,000 meters (depending on the ammunition used). A wide range of  ammunition has been developed for this weapon, making it capable of defeating  the majority of armored vehicles it is likely to encounter, up to and  including some main battle tanks.")
(comment spatiallyHoldsOver "if (#$spatiallyHoldsOver OBJ REG-TYPE SLOT ATT) is true, this means that if the OBJ has a part which is an instance of REG-TYPE, that part has SLOT with value ATT.")
(comment WeightLiftingGlove "This is the collection of weightlifting

gloves. Note that these are not #$Gloves, as that is currently defined.

The purpose of weight lifting gloves is to improve the grip and torsion that

one has on a weight bar.")
(comment Designer "Anyone who designs something as a job.")
(comment Americium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a RadioactiveObject of #$Americium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment lastRoleInEventType "(#$lastRoleInEventType INDIV TYPE ACTOR-SLOT EVENT TIME) means that,
as of TIME, EVENT is the last instance of TYPE in which INDIV has
occupied ACTOR-SLOT.  For instance, if (#$lastRoleInEventType
#$AbrahamLincoln #$EntertainmentPerformance #$spectators Event008
(#$YearFn 1988)), Event008 would be the final event in which Abraham
Lincoln watched an entertainment performance.  (Presumably, Event008
took place in the Ford Theater shortly before the
#$AssassinationOfPresidentLincoln.)  See also
#$firstRoleInEventType.")
(comment DictionaryFromToFn "DictionaryFromToFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. (#$DictionaryFromToFn LANGUAGE1 LANGUAGE2) represents the spec of #$Dictionary whose elements are dictionaries that translate words from LANGUAGE1 into LANGUAGE2.  For example, (#$DictionaryFromToFn #$SpanishLanguage #$EnglishLanguage) denotes the collection of dictionaries that translate Spanish words into English.  Note that the order of the arguments is important because a dictionary that translates Spanish into English need not also translate English into Spanish.  Use the #CollectionDenotingFunction #$DictionaryFn to represent the collection of dictionaries that are written in the same language about which they provide information, e.g., English language dictionaries.")
(comment ComputerProcess-Generic "The collection of events in which a 'process' is executed on a #$ComputationalSystem, using the #$ComputationalSystem's resources. 'Process' here refers to the act of a CPU or multiple CPUs executing the  instructions in a #$ComputerProgramCopy.  A process ends when it is terminated (by its own instructions, the operating system, a power outage, etc.) A #$ComputerProcess-Generic can be suspended or swapped out by the #$OperatingSystem (whereupon it temporarily ceases to exist) but when it is swapped back in, it will still be the same #$ComputerProcess-Generic. Hence, the time during which a #$ComputerProcess-Generic exists can be a discontinuous time interval. #$ComputerProcess-Generics can exist on multiple #$Computers (e.g. a single instance of #$ComputerProcess-Generic distributed over a network), but cease to exist on a #$Computer when that #$Computer is rebooted. Note that this is slightly more general than the notion of process in standard computer terminology, e.g. 'a Unix process', which corresponds more closely with #$ComputerProcess-SingleComputer.")
(comment InformativeTVShow "The collection of television shows [#$TVShow-CW] primarily intended to inform their viewers, though this does not preclude their being intended for entertainment as well. #$TVShow-CWs that are not intended to be wholly factual are instances of #$FictionalTVShow-CW, even if they are based partly in fact.")
(comment AnnualClimateCycle "A specialization of #$WeatherEvent.  Each instance of #$AnnualClimateCycle is an extended event, one year in length, which encompasses sub-events marking the changing of the seasons (see the collection #$SeasonOfYear and its specializations).  Specializations of #$AnnualClimateCycle include #$TemperateClimateCycle and #$HumidSubtropicalClimateCycle (qq.v).  See also #$ClimateCycleType and #$hasClimateType.")
(comment RedneckJoke "A specialization of #$RuralLaboringClassJoke, #$RedneckJoke is the collection of all jokes that are based on stereotypes about so-called \"rednecks\".")
(comment Interval-UnboundedBelow "A subcollection of #$ScalarIntervals that is not bounded at the bottom. It is disjoint with #$Interval-BoundedBelow.")
(comment KEFacilitationPredicate "This collection of predicates contains all predicates whose primary function is the relation of  knowledge entry principles, rules, suggestions, expectations and procedures to Cyc constants.")
(comment LexicalInfix "The set of lexical items which may attach somewhere in the
middle of a word. Not found in English.")
(comment verbSemTransTemplate "(#$verbSemTransTemplate COL FRAME TRANS) means that the translation of any verb denotation of a word denoting a specialization of COL, appearing with subcategorization frame FRAME, is TRANS.")
(comment MedicalTreatmentEvent "A subcollection of #$MedicalCareEvent.  Each instance of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent is a procedure performed by one or more medical professionals to alleviate or ameliorate a #$PhysiologicalCondition (q.v.).")
(comment listwiseArg2Type "(#$listwiseArg2Type LIST SLOTLIST) is true when for every N, 0 < N

<= (#$LengthOfListFn LIST), if SLOTn is the N-th element of SLOTLIST and

(#$arg2Isa SLOTn COLL), then the N-th element of LIST is an instance of

COLL. In other words, for every N the N-th element of LIST satisfies the

arg2 constraint for the N-th element of SLOTLIST. Example: the pair

(#$TheList #$performedBy) and (#$TheList #$Lehmann) is an element of this

relation. Note that (#$listwiseArg2Type LIST1 LIST2) presupposes that LIST1

and LIST2 are of the same length.")
(comment Drying-Paintlike "The process by which something sheetlike, like paint, dries into a solid sheetlike substance.")
(comment BacillusCereus "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$ProkaryoticCells are responsible for two types of food poisoning in humans.")
(comment AttendingFn "#$AttendingFn is a collection denoting function which takes as its argument a type of event and returns a collection of events, which collection is itself a collection of subevents of the instances of the subcollection of #$Event entered in the Arg1 position. For example, (#$AttendingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) returns the collection of events which consist of attending some entertainment event or other. Moreover, attending an entertainment event is a subevent of the entertainment event in question, which is itself an instance of #$EntertainmentEvent, so (#$AttendingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) is a collection of subevents of instances of #$EntertainmentEvent.  Another more specific example would be (#$AttendingFn #$BalletDancePerformance), which would be the collection of all instances of attending an instance of ballet. Since attending a ballet is a subevent of an instance of ballet, (#$AttendingFn #$BalletDancePerformance) is a collection of subevents of instances of #$BalletDancePerformance. Yet a third example is as follows: (#$AttendingFn #$SocialGathering) returns the collection of events in which some agent attends some instance of #$SocialGathering. In each case, '#$AttendingFn' is meant to distinguish the spectators from the performers, or the guests from the hosts.")
(comment BiologicalWeapon-Viral "The collection of all #$BiologicalWeapons that make use of viruses.")
(comment InternationalConflict "Elements of #$InternationalConflict are conflicts between two elements of #$Country.  A sufficient condition for being an element of this collection is two elements of #$Country are opponents in some conflict.  Note that there may be more than two countries as well as some non-countries that are parties to the conflict.  Wars and territorial disputes are prototypical exemplars.")
(comment Synchrotron "This is the collection of synchrotrons, which are a type of particle accelerator.")
(comment RectalAdministration "Administering a drug through one's anus.")
(comment AirCavalryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of instances of ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable that are involved in offensive operations such as #$SearchAndAttack-MilitaryOperation.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn NinthRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment ProtocolField-Packet "A #$ProtocolField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet
that indicates which #$TransportLayerProtocol process to give the
#$Packet-Internet to.")
(comment Threatening-CommunicationAct "This is the collection of acts in which one agents threatens another.  The propositional content can typically be divided into a demand and what the sender of info intends if the demand is not met. Note that this has not been made a subset of #$Intimidation-CommunicationAct, as the intention of a threat may be intimidation but the one making the threat may be unsuccesful.")
(comment SacredPractice "The collection of Events related to spiritual or sacred matters")
(comment Solid-StateOfMatter "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible and an instance of #$MatterTypeByPhysicalState. Each instance of #$Solid-StateOfMatter is a solid quantity of matter. Pieces of matter in the solid state are at a sufficiently low enough temperature or high enough pressure for the particular type of matter involved that their molecules are bonded to each other by various sorts of forces, and don't move away from their neighbors. Solid objects are characterized at the macroscopic level by definite, persistent boundaries, independent of container.")
(comment ControlPestInfestation "The collection of pest control events.")
(comment IntelligenceAgency "The collection of all government agencies [#$GovernmentAgency] which secretly collect and/
or analyze data about other governments or organizations, and/or which covertly attempt to influence political or economic events in other countries or in non-governmental organizations.")
(comment Dendrite "The collection of all dendrites (or 'dendrons'), which are branching fibers of a #$Neuron which transmit signals towards the cell body.")
(comment dateOfPublication-CW "(#$dateOfPublication-CW CW DATE) means that the work CW was published on DATE.")
(comment AntiTankWeapon-M47Dragon "The M47 DRAGON is a particular type of anti-tank guided missile.")
(comment Capacitor "An electrical device used to store electrical charge.")
(comment Roll-WhileTranslating "A collection of events.  Turning about the back to front axis (normally the direction of travel) for a #$transporter (#$AirTransportationDevice, drone plane, unmanned rocket, ...) not traveling along a solid surface.  An aircraft, ship, or spacecraft may roll in this sense of the word.")
(comment informationStorageUnit "(#$informationStorageUnit STORING STORE) means that in the information storage situation STORING, STORE is an information storage unit.")
(comment favorableMonthTypeForTour "The binary predicate #$favorableMonthTypeForTour is used to relate an instance of #$TravelTour to an instance of #$MonthOfYearType. (#$favorableMonthTypeForTour TOUR MONTH-TYPE) means that MONTH-TYPE is a favorable type of month for TOUR. Compare with #$favorableMonthForTour, which takes an instance of #$CalendarMonth, rather than a subset, as its second argument.")
(comment ProcessingALoanApplication "The collection of all events in each of which a lender processes an application for a loan (a #$LoanAgreement).  Each such event is a complex script involving various standard subevents, although practices differ from lender to lender and from locale to locale.")
(comment Hysterectomy "the surgical procedure in which the uterus is removed.")
(comment fileFTPd "(#$fileFTPd COPYING FILE) means that the instance of #$ComputerFileCopy that is the input to the #$FTPingAFile process COPYING is FILE.")
(comment strengthDescription "For #$PharmacyProductType-Level3, gives a #$CharacterString which describes the strength of the product.  The strength may be how concentrated the product is or may be the size of a dose in mass, volume, or some other measurement.")
(comment OnlineCasino "The collection of #$WorldWideWebSites that feature opportunities to gamble.")
(comment holdsInTime-Always "(#$holdsInTime-Always MT TIME) means that the assertions in MT are true throughout the entire temporal extent of TIME.  See also #$holdsInTime-Sometime.")
(comment CrossCountryBicycling "The collection of bicycling actions where the bicyclist uses a #$MountainBike on a dirt trail.  Generally, the purpose of an instance of #$CrossCountryBicycling is not to get from point A to point B.  Instead, the bicyclist performs the bicycling activity for exercise or fun.")
(disjointWith Wheelbarrow TrainCar)
(comment watershedOf "maps bodies of water to the region that is their watershed.")
(comment IntelligenceOperation-Joint "A subset of #$IntelligenceGathering, in which two or more parties are working together to perform the gathering.   These parties are often different intelligence organizations of a country, or the intelligence organizations of several countries. Examples include US-IsraelIntelligenceWorkInTheMiddleEast. ")
(comment BeetleShaped "#$BeetleShaped is the instance of #$ShapeAttribute defined by the typical shape of a beetle.")
(comment Penicillin "A well-known family of drugs used to combat bacteria.")
(comment from-UnderspecifiedLocation "(#$from-UnderspecifiedLocation THING FROMLOC) states that an abstract locational relation holds between FROMLOC and THING, where FROMLOC is an abstract origin (a #$Location-Underspecified) of THING.  #$from-UnderspecifiedLocation is an underspecified semantic representation that may be elaborated to represent either a spatial example of

origin/destination (as captured by #$from-Generic and its specific

forms) or a temporal use of destinations (e.g. \"from June to August\")

or metaphorical destination (e.g. \"fall from grace\").")
(comment Siphoning-FluidFlow "Transferring a liquid from a #$Container via a #$SiphonTube.")
(comment PleonasticForNPInfinitivePhraseFrame "This frame is used for transitive words (usually verbs or adjectives) that take exactly one complement--an infinitive phrase preceded by 'for NP'--in a pleonastic construction. In HPSG terms: [COMPS <CP[infinitive]>]. Examples: 'It is disappointing for him to not get a raise', 'It stinks for him to get fired'.")
(comment InternationalAlliance "The collection of all agreements between geopolitical agents where the parties to the agreement agree to work in concert with respect to some endeavor or set of issues.  An international alliance may be formed for a comparatively specific purpose, like the #$DesertShieldCoalition, or it may be formed with a wide range of goals in mind, like the North Atlantic Treaty Organization.  Also, alliances may be relatively brief or may be quite long-standing.  Alliances are often established through some sort of formal treaty.  Their participants are almost always instances of #$IndependentCountry acting as international agents.  A situation where one or more of the participants is an international corporation like the Lippo Group or Saudi Aramco, or some other global economic entity like the International Monetary Fund, might conceivably be a borderline case.")
(comment Spam-UnsolicitedEMail "A specialization of #$EMailMessage. Each instance of this collection is an electronic mail message sent to many different #$EMailAddresses on the #$Internet, often in an attempt to sell a product, and causing irritation to the recipients. For the acts of sending such mass-mailings, see #$MassEMailSending.")
(comment Wheelbarrow "The collection of wheelbarrows.")
(comment NucleotideType "A collection of collection. Instances of #$NucleotideType are

types of instances of the collection #$Nucleotide. There are four kinds of

these corresponding to the four kinds of nitrogen bases that enter in their

constitution. See #$Nucleotides, #$NitrogenBaseType.")
(comment HepatitisB-Virus "A collection of viri. Instances of #$HepatitisB-Virus are virus of the kind responsible for instances of #$HepatitisB-Infection.")
(comment Ohm "An instance of #$MKSUnitOfMeasure.  #$Ohm is the standard unit of electrical resistance in the MKS (meter-kilogram-second) system.  One ohm is equivalent to the resistance of a circuit in which a 1-#$Volt electrical potential difference produces a 1-#$Coulomb #$ElectricalCurrentLevel (qq.v).")
(comment Consul "A collection of persons, a subset of #$Diplomat. Each
element of #$Consul is a person who is officially appointed
by a country's government to aid and serve its citizens in a foreign
city.")
(comment Spirochaeta-Genus "A collection of #$ProkaryoticCells in a #$BiologicalGenus in

the #$MoneraKingdom.  All #$BiologicalSpecies, except Spirochaeta

plicatilis, have two periplasmic flagella.  These are

#$AnaerobicBacterium-Facultative or #$AnaerobicBacterium-Oxyphobic.

If grown under aerobic conditions, the #$AnaerobicBacterium-Facultative species

will usually produce a carotenoid pigment that will stain the colonies

yellow, orange or red.")
(comment MineCountermeasuresVessel "The collection of watercraft intended for use in mine countermeasure operations.")
(disjointWith AdultAnimal JuvenileAnimal)
(comment meansOfInfoTransfer-Artifact "This predicate is a more specific version of #$instrument-Generic intended to single out those instances of #$Artifact-Communication that play the role of #$instrument-Generic in instances of #$InformationTransferEvent and that are designed to aid in information transfer.  (#$meansOfInfoTransfer-Artifact ITE ART) means that the instance of #$Artifact-Communication ART plays an instrumental role in the  #$InformationTransferEvent ITE and that ART was created in part to be able to play such roles, e.g. (#$intendedBehaviorCapable ART #$InformationTransferEvent #$instrument-Generic) holds.  For example, if some instance TEL of  #$Telephone is used in a successful telephone call CALL, then we could represent this with (#$meansOfInfoTransfer-Artifact CALL TEL).")
(comment educationalDegrees "(#$educationalDegrees PERSON DEGREETYPE) means that PERSON has been awarded an #$EducationalDegree of type DEGREETYPE.")
(comment Nitrogen "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of #$Nitrogen in stuffeous form (could be solid, liquid, gaseous, etc.).")
(comment carriesInfectionType "The predicate (#$carriesInfectionType OBJECT INFECT_TYPE) relates a particular organism or other object to a type of infection that it carries.  (#$carriesInfectionType OBJ INFTYP) means that the individual OBJ is a carrier of the #$InfectionType INFTYP.  For example, (#$carriesInfectionType TyphoidMary #$TyphoidFever) or (#$carriesInfectionType Needle0567 #$AIDS).")
(disjointWith GraduateSchool College)
(disjointWith Travel-TripEvent UncoveringSomething)
(comment FieldArtilleryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for handling heavy           guns used for indirect fire against land-based targets.")
(comment ReducingToPowder "This is the collection of events in which some #$PartiallyTangible
thing, things, or stuff, is reduced to a powder in some manner. Often this
is accomplished by grinding, but any method of ending up with a powder
is an instance of this collection. It is required that the stuff so reduced
wasn't a powder before the reduction, i.e., grindings of a powder so as to make
it a finer powder aren't in this collection.")
(comment Password-Canonical "#$Password-Canonical is a subset of #$Password-Weak.  It includes all passwords that            manufacturers of hardware and software set up their products with.  Products usually           come with instructions on how to change such factory presets, but users often neglect            to change them, leaving open a vulnerability to a security breach.")
(comment SnowyClimateCycle "The collection of climate cycles that have frequent cases of snow in the winter.")
(comment Clavicle "The #$Clavicle, also known as the 'collarbone', is the #$Bone-BodyPart in front of body just below the neck.  It connects the #$RibCage to the forelimbs.")
(disjointWith StreetAddress ZipCode)
(comment WheelRolling "#$WheelRolling involves #$RollingOnASurface using an axle which is attached to something which is not rotating along with the wheel.  The wheel and what it is attached to move without #$Slipping along a surface.")
(comment QuantityConversionFn "(#$QuantityConversionFn UNIT QUANTITY) converts QUANTITY into an equivalent quantity expressed using UNIT as the unit of measure.  For example, (#$QuantityConversionFn #$Inch (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 2)) denotes (#$Inch 24).")
(comment objectActedOn-Gradual "The predicate #$objectActedOn-Gradual is used to relate an event to an entity acted on in a gradual (or incremental) way in that event. (#$objectActedOn-Gradual EVENT GRADUAL-OBJECT) means that in each sub-event SUB-EVENT of EVENT, there is some part PART of GRADUAL-OBJECT such that (#$objectActedOn SUB-EVENT PART), and for each part PART of GRADUAL-OBJECT, there exists some SUB-EVENT of EVENT, such that (#$objectActedOn SUB-EVENT PART).")
(comment visibleParts "The #$visibleParts of this tangible object.  Since #$colorOfObject, #$textureOfObject transfersThro visiblePartOf it is important to understand the following. Implicit in what is a visible part is a point of view.  This point of view is probably context dependent.  Thus for your average human activities the visible parts of an apple should be its stem and its skin. Or for a House the #$visibleParts would be Shutter, Roof, OutsideWalls.  Note that AppleFlesh, Seeds, and RoomInAHouse are internal parts.  Each of these parts has their own #$visibleParts.  However, internal parts are usually not #$visibleParts from the bigger object that they are part of.  Thus the color of RoomInAHouse's walls will not affect the color of the House.  This gets very complex for containers, or objects with portals in them.  Also transparent parts sometimes allow #$internalParts to be visible.  These two issues are hard and important and need to be dealt with.  For now, this ad hoc solution may deal with a large number of common sense cases.  So just annotate cases where this breaks down.  Sometimes a new microtheory may be necessary.  I.e. there may be some mT where we are constantly opening things up and taking them apart.  What is on #$visibleParts would be completely different then.  Thus for #$HumanActivitiesMt good slot values would be things that would be visible from a reasonable point of view.  We usually don't cut pencils open; it is usual to think of a house's color as being its colors visible from outside etc..")
(disjointWith Amenity Facility-Construct)
(comment Uniform-PersistenceDistribution "Each instance of this collection is an object consisting of a parameter which indicates the probability of an assertion or set of assertions being true (satisfied).  The parameter defines a uniform (constant) distribution contour (graph).  The parameter is specified using the predicate #$uniformValue.")
(comment AdultCheckWebSite "The specialization of #$WorldWideWebSite whose instances use #$AdultCheck to verify that visitors are of legal age.")
(comment dateOfResumption "This predicate relates multi-individual agents to the 
date on which they resumed the multi-individual agent's previous
primary activity.  Agents take on the attribute, #$ResumedAgency at
this time.")
(comment PractitionerFn "The term `(#$PractitionerFn FIELD)' denotes the collection of all persons who

significantly engage in or count as practitioners of the #$FieldOfStudy FIELD.")
(comment Misoprostol "The chemical compound which is used to treat peptic acid problems.")
(comment ArmoredAmphibiousTractor "The class of tractors used by expeditionary forces that are equipped with armor to make the battle-suitable and are amphibious as well to facilitate their operation in unfavorable terrain.")
(comment oilSolubility "(#$oilSolubility OBJ DEGREE) means that the particular tangible OBJ has this DEGREE of #$Solubility in #$Oil.")
(comment NthInSeriesFn "An instance of both #$PartialFunction and #$ReifiableFunction.  (#$NthInSeriesFn SERIES N) is the Nth member (see #$seriesMembers) of the #$Series SERIES, provided that N is less than or equal to the length (see #$seriesLength) of SERIES.  When N is greater than the length of SERIES, then (#$NthInSeriesFn SERIES N) is undefined.")
(comment Geochronology "Geochronology is the determination of age through the measurement

                            of exponential decay of unstable isotopes in a rock.")
(comment Jute-Fiber "Quantities of fiber derived from the stems of  the jute plant.")
(comment BattleTank-T64 "A type of battle tank.")
(comment elasticityOfObject "This predicate relates a solid thing to its degree of elasticity (that is, to its capacity to readily return to its original shape after being deformed, but not broken).  (#$elasticityOfObject OBJ DEGREE) means that the #$SolidTangibleThing OBJ has DEGREE as its degree of elasticity (where DEGREE is an instance of #$Elasticity).  Note that the higher the  degree of elasticity, the more quickly and completely the object returns to its previous shape.")
(comment FighterAttackPlane "#$The collection of aircraft designed primarily for attacking targets on land #$or sea.  

Distinct from Interceptors, designed primarily for air-to-air use.")
(comment Blitzing-Football "A football play in which defensive players attempt to break through the offensive line, usually in an attempt to tackle or pressure the quarterback before he can get rid of the ball.")
(comment CellNucleus "The part of a #$EukaryoticCell that contains most of its genetic material.  ")
(comment ResidentialTimeshareAgreement "The collection of timeshare agreements. People pay to enter such an agreement,            and it concerns some #$HumanResidence.  Being party to the agreement entitles            them to reside at that residence for a certain amount of time per year.             Usually used with vacation homes.")
(comment Association "A spec of #$Organization. Unlike many organizations, associations are characterized by voluntary membership, and by a relatively egalitarian governance structure in which all members have at least initially an equal say in associative decisions.")
(comment AbilityWithRespectToFn "(#$AbilityWithRespectToFn TYPE) is the collection of TYPE abilities -- i.e., the collection of instances of #$AgentCapacity that make sense to describe as \"relevant to\" TYPE.  For example, (#$AbilityWithRespectToFn (#$PlayingFn #$Basketball-TheGame)) is the collection of basketball-playing abilities.  (#$AbilityWithRespectToFn DribblingABasketball) is a spec, and (#$LowAmountFn (#$AbilityWithRespectToFn DribblingABasketball)) is an instance.")
(disjointWith GeneticCondition Infection)
(comment CycLNLSemanticAssertion "The collection of #$CycLAssertions whose main (i.e. arg0) operators denote #$NLSemanticPredicates.")
(comment Infantilism "the persistence in an adult of markedly childish anatomical, physiological, or psychological characteristics.")
(comment SatelliteEarthStation "The collection of #$CommunicationDevices 
located on the Earth's surface designed to transmit and receive 
#$SatelliteTransmissions to and from a #$Satellite-Device orbiting         
the Earth. While all instances of #$SatelliteEarthStation have
#$SatelliteReceivers, and thus can receive #$SatelliteTransmissions, 
some, but not all, have #$SatelliteTransmitters, which allow them to 
send signals to satellites.  It is important to note that quite a
number of things count as Earth Stations.  These include the satellite
dishes that people have attached to their houses, and anything else on
the surface of the Earth that can send and/or receive signals with 
a satellite.  For this reason, although the name might suggest otherwise,
#$SatelliteEarthStation is not a spec of #$FixedStructure. ")
(comment mtAccessConstraint "(#$mtAccessConstraint MT PROP) means that the constraints specified in PROP must be satisfied in order for assertions in MT to be accessed at all, by a user or an application")
(comment Dock "#$Dock is a specialization of #$FixedStructure, #$TransportFacility, and #$OutdoorLocation.  Each instance of #$Dock is a long flat walkway that juts out over water from shorelines.  A dock's main function is to provide a place to secure boats and to provide a place where passengers and cargo can be loaded and unloaded.")
(comment riverEndingNearby "a river which ends in this general vicinity but not exactly here")
(comment decreasesFluent "(#$decreasesFluent SET F) means that, all else equal, for any X, (F X) will be smaller than (F Y) where X and Y are in the domain of F but where X is an #$elementOf SET and Y is not.--Pittman, Nov 13, 1997")
(comment PoleVaultBar "The collection of bars that pole vaulters try to clear.")
(comment TankBlade "The collection of devices intended to be mounted on a tank and used to remove mines from a mine field.")
(comment Thorium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of thorium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.  This unit could probably just as well be called Thorium or ThoriumStuff")
(comment Divination "A specialization of #$InterpretingSignificance and #$ParanormalEvent. Each instance of this collection is an event of predicting the future or discovering the truth by means underexplained by current science -- such as #$TarotCardReading, #$Astrology, palmistry, and geomancy.")
(comment baseSet "(#$baseSet STRUCTURE SET) means that SET is the base set of #$RelationalStructure STRUCTURE.  That is, SET is the domain from which the individual elements of the structure are drawn.  Although there may be several relations involved in the relational structure, they all relate members of the base set.  As each relational structure has a unique base set, this predicate is functional.")
(comment USNavySEALTeam "This is the collection of special forces units of the United States Navy.  'SEAL' stands for 'SEa, Air, Land'.")
(comment ReformulatorDirectivePredicate "The collection of #$Predicates which can affect the
behaviour of the #$CycLReformulator or its submodules.  When
reformulator directive GAFs are asserted, they are only relevant to
the reformulator when it is reformulating expressions in the
microtheory in which the directive is asserted, or a specMt thereof.")
(disjointWith Metal Water)
(comment lifeExpectancyForGroupInRegion "(#$lifeExpectancyForGroupInRegion REGION GROUP YEARS) means that the average lifetime of a member of GROUP residing in REGION is YEARS.")
(comment EconomicAction "The class of all actions which are either  'transactions' within some economic system -- instances of #$Buying, #$Bartering, contract-signing, boycotting, etc. -- or which are in some

way 'directed at' the functioning of an economic system.  Examples of the latter include ordering an embargo on a certain country's goods or changing a tax rate.  To a first approximation, instances of #$EconomicAction must be performed by 

#$IntelligentAgents. E.g., although animal stampedes might have economic consequences, they are not instances of #$EconomicAction.  More precisely, saying that an action is 'directed at' an economic system entails that the initiator has some awareness of its economic consequences.  Even if painting my house purple results in an increased demand for purple paint, such an action is not an #$EconomicAction unless I did it in part hoping to affect the paint market in some way.")
(comment analogicalHypothesis "(#$analogicalHypothesis ?Domain ?Formula)

states that ?Formula is a prediction concerning ?Domain that arises out of

analogical reasoning. That is, the system reasons on the basis of some analogy that

?Formula may hold in a context determined by ?Domain. ?Domain may denote

a microtheory (a true context), or merely some event/scenario that hasn't been

reified as a fully-fledged microtheory. In essence, we use this predicate merely

to mark the analogical provenance of ?Formula, and to ensure that it receives

a nice, explanatory paraphrase.")
(comment Masquerading "This is the collection of events in which a person pretends to be someone or something other than himself, in some context other than that of a dramatic performance. The purpose of the pretense may be entertainment, however, as in the case of #$Masquerading on #$Halloween, or for #$MardiGras (see #$MasqueradingAtASocialGathering). On the other hand, instances of #$Masquerading also include deliberately deceitful acts such as those that a con-artist might engage in in order to defraud someone (see #$Masquerading-Deceiving). #$Masquerading is distinct from #$DramaticActing, which is the collection of events in which a person portrays someone or something other than himself in the context of a dramatic performance (i.e., in a theatre, in front of an audience...).")
(comment Panning "This is the collection of events in which small pieces of gold or other

metals are separated from sand and pebbles by agitating the mixture in

water contained in a pan-shaped object. ")
(comment typesCapabilityEnablesCapability "(#$typesCapabilityEnablesCapability SE-TYPE SIT-TYPE1 ROLE1 SIT-TYPE2 ROLE2) means that instances of SE-TYPE have the  ability to play the role ROLE1 in situations of type SIT-TYPE1 and that this ability  enables SE to play the role ROLE2 in situations of type SIT-TYPE2.")
(comment CharacterStringMode "A collection of collections.  A character-string mode is

  a collection of concrete character-string tokens that all represent

  the same abstract character-string in the same way, e.g. by being 

  handwritten rather than printed or spoken.  That is, each instance

  MODE-INST of #$CharacterStringMode is a specialization of an 

  instance TYPE-INST of #$CharacterStringType that includes all 

  elements of TYPE-INST that are realized in a particular way (such 

  as by being inscribed, or by being sounded).  For example, if 

  TYPE-INST is the collection of all tokens of the string 'cat', 

  MODE-INST might be the collection of all _spoken_ tokens of 'cat'.  

  For other examples, see the specializations 

  #$CharacterStringMode-Inscribed, 

  #$CharacterStringMode-Sounded, and 

  #$CharacterStringMode-ElectroMagnetic.  See also #$modeOfStringType for

the relation between a given string type and each of the various string modes

it subsumes.")
(comment RoundUpFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  When applied to an instance INTERVAL of #$ScalarInterval, #$RoundUpFn returns an instance ROUNDED-INTERVAL of #$ScalarInterval in which the minimum and maximum ranges of INTERVAL have been rounded upwards to integer values.  For example, (#$RoundUpFn (#$Meter 2.5 5.2)) is (#$Meter 3 6).")
(comment DeonticReasoningMicrotheory "This is a sub-collectiono of #$ModalReasoningMicrotheory.
Instances of #$DeonticReasoningMicrotheory are microtheories
accessible to deontic `to-be' operators, in which deontic reasoning via
rules concerning those operators can be carried out.  These
microtheories can also be used in deontic reasoning via microtheories,
applying rules (outside) about these microtheories.  General relations
among these microtheories, in addition to #$genlMt, include
#$mtDeonAccessible and #$mtDeonIdeal.")
(comment CollectionRuleTemplateFn "(#$CollectionRuleTemplateFn COL) denotes the rule template unique to collection COL.")
(comment SurvivorSupportGroupFn "#$SurvivorSupportGroupFn takes as argument any spec of #$Event and returns the collection of all support groups for persons who have or are currently experiencing that #$Event, or for persons who bear some special relation to someone experiencing that #$Event.")
(comment AuditTrailOverflow "This is the collection of all instances of #$SystemOverload in which the overflow occurs in the #$ComputerAuditLogFile.  This can result in an instance of #$ComputerCrashing, but more frequently it simply allows intruders to remain active in the system without leaving a record in the audit log.")
(disjointWith Watercraft-Subsurface OceanLiner)
(comment LastInListFn "The function #$LastInListFn, applied to a list as in (#$LastInListFn LIST), results in the last item on the list.  For each nonempty #$List LIST, (#$LastInListFn LIST) = (#$NthInListFn LIST (LengthOfListFn LIST)).  (#$LastInListFn LIST) is undefined if LIST is #$TheEmptyList.")
(comment Fuse-IgnitionDevice-Impact "The collection of #$Fuse-IgnitionDevice that ignite an explosion upon impact with  a target.")
(comment moreVulnerableToBecause "(#$moreVulnerableToBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP) means
that there is an increased chance of AGENT's playing the role ROLE in
a situation of type EVTTYPE because PROP is true
(#$increasedChanceForRoleBecause AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP) and AGENT
has the #$goals (#$not (ROLE EVTTYPE AGENT)).")
(comment PersonTypeByGeographicResidence "A collection of collections.  This collection exists to make it easier to refer to that dimension or facet of a person's behavior, attitudes, and beliefs (culture) which derives from, or is influenced by, the person's residence in a distinct geographical region.  This facet of culture is slightly different from that which derives from a person's rights and obligations relative to some geo-political entity. For that, see #$PersonTypeByGeoPoliticalAffiliation.")
(comment AestheticSense "Performing an activity with an artistic or aesthetic sense.")
(comment AnalogyEntityWithStructuralEvaluation "An information entity associated with an analogy that can be structurally evaluated.")
(comment CycLClosedAtomicTerm "The collection of all closed #$CycLAtomicTerms.  \"Closed\" here means not containing any free (i.e. unbound) variables.  Since a variable itself is the only type of _atomic_ term that contains a variable (and contains it _free_, moreover, as a single occurrence of a variable can't bind itself), #$CycLClosedAtomicTerm has as instances all #$CycLAtomicTerms except #$CycLVariables.  Like all CycL atomic terms, Cycl closed atomic terms are \"denotational\" (see #$CycLDenotationalTerm).  Note that this collection, like most instances of #$CycLExpressionType, is \"quoted\" (see #$quotedCollection).")
(comment BallisticMissileSubmarine "A class of submarines that have the capability of launching nuclear            ballistic missiles from underwater (cf. #$BallisticMissile-SubmarineLaunched).")
(comment IceCloud "Those very high clouds which don't block out much sunlight. Mackerel sky clouds, flat high clouds and wispy cirrus clouds are all of this type.  They often indicate that a warm front is on its way.")
(comment (NoAmountFn Compressibility) "essentially cannot be compressed")
(comment CharacterToken-ElectroMagnetic "The collection of all electromagnetically-encoded 
  tokens of individual abstract characters.  More precisely, 
  #$CharacterToken-ElectroMagnetic is a specialization of 
  #$CharacterToken each of whose instances is a specific 
  electromagnetically-realized (and usually, digitally-interpreted) 
  representation of particular instance of #$Character-Abstract 
  in some language, writing system, or encoding scheme.  
  Electromagnetically-realized character tokens are objects that 
  are literally stored (e.g. in a computer's memory or on a floppy 
  disk) and transmitted (e.g. via wires or as radio signals) with 
  the use of electronic devices.  See also 
  #$CharacterStringToken-ElectroMagnetic.")
(comment partitionedIntoViaEquivRelation "This predicate relates instances of set or collection and instances of #$EquivalenceRelation to the partitioning that results from applying the given equivalence relation to the set or collection.  (#$partitionedIntoViaEquivRelation SETORCOL ER PARTITIONING) means that each element of PARTITIONING is a subset, or subcollection of SETORCOL and any particular element of PARTITIONING contains all the members of SETORCOL that bear the relation ER to each other.")
(comment Capsule-EntericCoated "The collection of all enteric-coated #$CapsuleDrugs.  This capsules, when ingested, remain intact until they reach the intestines.")
(comment SprainingSomething "Twisting or stretching a joint so that a ligament tears or separates from bone.")
(comment IssueAboutFn "(#$IssueAboutFn ?ACTION) means the #$Issue concerning that type of action.")
(comment spatiallyIntrinsicArg "(#$spatiallyIntrinsicArg PRED N) means that the #$Predicate PRED expresses a property that is \"spatially intrinsic\" for its argument position N. In other words, if a sentence S using PRED is true for some object OBJ (in the Nth argument position), every sentence is true in which a term denoting any spatial part (via #$physicalPortions) of OBJ is substituted for OBJ in S. For    example, since (#$spatiallyIntrinsicArg #$temperatureOfObject 1) is true, if  it is true that (#$temperatureOfObject Coffee007 (#$DegreeCelsius 90)), it is true that any spatial part of \"Coffee007\" will also have that temperature.  An example of a property that is not spatially intrinsic is #$massOfObject; there are parts of any object that have less mass than the entire object.  Another example of a relation that is not spatially intrinsic, but might at first seem to be, is #$constituents.  In (#$constituents ChocolateMilk37 Milk36), it is not the case that every spatial part of ChocolateMilk37 has Milk36 among its #$constituents.  #$constituents means, rather, that every part of its first argument has some part of the second argument among its components.")
(comment PhotochemicalEnergyTransduction "event in which light energy is transformed into chemical bond energy.")
(comment StreetCornerFn "(#$StreetCornerFn XING DIRECTION) is the
lot of land (if any) that lies adjacent to, and generally to 
the DIRECTION of, XING.  A given intersection will normally 
have four street corners associated with it, corresponding 
to four directions that are approximately 90 degrees apart 
from each other.  For example, if the two streets that 
intersect at XING run north-south and east-west, respectively, 
then there will be street corners to the #$Northeast-Generally, 
#$Northwest-Generally, #$Southeast-Generally, and 
#$Southwest-Generally of XING.  See also #$streetCornerOf,
#$atStreetIntersection, and #$directionsOfPath.")
(comment SavingAFile "A collection of actions done by computers on files. In each instance of #$SavingAFile, a computer writes the contents of a file it has in its #$ComputerMemory (usually in its #$RAM) to a long-term, computer-readable storage medium like a #$ComputerDisk.")
(comment Sinkhole "A collection of topographical features.  Each instance of
#$Sinkhole is a hollow area in which drainage collects.")
(comment SportsLeagueRecordHoldersFn "#$SportsLeagueRecordHoldersFn takes any instance

 of #$SportsLeague as its argument and returns as 

 its value the collection of all record-holders 

 in that league, regardless of the sport. For example, (#$SportsLeagueRecordHoldersFn #$BigEastConference) 

 returns the collection of all Big East record holders.")
(comment weaponPayload-Max "(weaponPayload-Max ?WEAP ?MASS) means that the weapon ?WEAP can carry ?MASS amount of explosive charge.")
(comment Eclipse-CelestialEvent "The celestial event whereby one object (a planet, moon, etc.)  obscures the light from a #$Star so that a #$Shadow is cast on a third celestial object. For instance, when the #$MoonOfEarth is aligned between the #$Sun and #$PlanetEarth, the moon partially or fully obscures the view of the #$Sun from some parts of #$PlanetEarth. Eclipses could be predicted by the Ancients (e.g., the #$AncientRomanPersons) and were considered to represent divine providence.")
(comment temporalSettingOfPIT "The time(s) during which a PIT takes place.")
(comment Loracarbef "The chemical compound which is an antibiotic.")
(comment tourDayMeals "(#$tourDayMeals TOUR DAY MEALTYPE) means that on DAY, a meal
of type MEALTYPE will be provided for those taking TOUR, having
already been paid for in advance by the participants as part of the
tour package.")
(comment D-TheLetter "The letter D of the alphabet.  This is 'D' (or 'd') as a #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterD and #$LatinSmallLetterD.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization RegionalGovernment)
(comment boyfriend "(#$boyfriend PERS MALE) states that PERS and MALE are involved in a romantic relationship with each other.  They interact fairly frequently.  Such interaction may range from just talking (as in a long-distance relationship) to dating, sexual activity, or cohabitation.")
(comment Attache "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Diplomat.  Each element of #$Attache is a person who is officially appointed as a representative of a country's government in dealing with another government or an international organization.  For example, the collection #$Attache includes the U.S. attaches in #$Japan, #$Russia, #$China-PeoplesRepublic, and other countries.  Attaches usually work with higher officials appointed by their country.  Usually attaches are attached to particular diplomatic staff or mission, for example #$MilitaryAttache or #$NavalAttache.")
(comment offspringActors "(#$offspringActors EVENT ORGANISM) means that ORGANISM is an offspring created in the #$BiologicalReproductionEvent EVENT .")
(comment atomicNumber "This predicate relates an atomic number to an element.  (#$atomicNumber ELEMENT INT) means that ELEMENT, an instance of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons, has the #$PositiveInteger INT for its atomic number.  This means that any instance of (#$AtomFn ELEMENT) must have INT many protons (see #$Proton) in its atomic nucleus (see #$AtomicNucleus).  For example, (#$atomicNumber #$Carbon 6) means that every instance of (#$AtomFn #$Carbon) has six protons in its nucleus.")
(comment interArgIsa5-3 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).   (#$interArgIsa5-3 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that,  when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fifth argument to RELN,  a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the third argument  must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if ARG-INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then  (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 INST ... ARGN) is semantically well-formed  only if ARG3 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation of semantic  well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations.")
(comment AirborneStandoffMinefieldDetectionSystem "An #$AirborneStandoffMinefieldDetectionSystem (ASTAMIDS) is a system that will provide near real-time minefield information for: development of Operations Plans, gathering information used to verify or modify Operations Plans, and detecting minefields for maneuvering units so they may bypass minefields or plan breaches.  An ASTAMIDS is employed on an aerial platform to gather minefield intelligence over specific areas or along routes.  Aerial platforms may be unmanned (UAV) or manned (helicopter).  Types of minefields located are surface patterned, buried patterned, scatterable, and nuisance mines on unpaved roads. Information gathered during these missions provides indicators or minefield presence, location, and boundaries.  After detecting a mine or mines (called the initial detection), the platform is directed to conduct a survey of the area using the S=ASTAMIDS system to determine minefield boundaries.  On a UAV, this information is transmitted to a Ground Control Station where it is processed in real-time.  This processed information, containing minefield locations, is transmitted to meneuver commanders.  ASTAMIDS assists the maneuver commander by identifying minefields to assist in determining courses of action (such as bypassing mined areas or planning breaches).  (Source: Engineer Systems Handbook, 4/97)")
(comment unfilteredPorts "A predicate relating instances of #$Firewall-Network with instances of #$Computer in the firewall's network. (#$unfilteredPorts FIREWALL PROTOCOL NUM COMPUTER) means that FIREWALL lets through all packets that conform to PROTOCOL coming from outside the network bound for port number NUMBER on COMPUTER.")
(comment DataSignaling "This is the collection of all events in which information is passed from a source to a target by non-obvious means.  This is usually done to avoid some form of security monitoring.")
(comment Nitrobacteraceae-Family "A collection of diverse #$Bacterium.  These #$ProkaryoticCells have the ability to utilize amonia or nitrate as an energy source and use carbon dioxide as a source of carbon.  All except #$Nitrobacter-Genus are obligate chemolithotrophs.  All are #$AerobicBacterium.  ")
(comment positiveInterest-Prop "(#$positiveInterest-Prop AGT PROP) means that AGT has a pro-attitude towards PROP -- i.e., AGT has a positive interest in PROP being or becoming true.  #$positiveInterest-Prop is a generalization of more specific pro-attitude predicates such as #$desires, #$intends, and #$goals.  In contrast with #$desires and #$goals, #$positiveInterest-Prop is not strictly future-directed.  An agent may have a positive interest in a proposition which already holds.  Also, (#$positiveInterest-Prop AGT PROP) does not 

entail that AGT intrinsically values PROP.  AGT may only prefer PROP to the available alternatives.")
(comment InternalSecurityGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with internal matters of security, such as detecting espionage and preventing sabotage.")
(comment ComputerOperator "#$ComputerOperator is a subset of

#$DeskWorker.  Instances of the collection #$ComputerOperator

work with computers, but they do not program computers.  The collection

includes people who work with computer databases and word processors, as well as

other non-programers who interact with a computer via a keyboard.")
(comment AbdominalExerciseDevice "This is the collection of devices

designed specifically to work the abdominal muscles.")
(comment SupplyUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile is to provide           supplies to other units.")
(comment NucleotideTypeByBase "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$NucleotideTypeByBase is a collection of instances of #$Nucleotide that have an instance of #$NitrogenBaseType in common.")
(comment Protactinium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of Protactinium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment ComputerProcess-MultiComputer "The subcollection of #$ComputerProcess-Generic whose instances
    have as #$processThreads various instances of #$ComputerThread 
    running on different computers.")
(disjointWith SeasonOfYear AnnualClimateCycle)
(comment kePlausibleConsideration "(#$kePlausibleConsideration TERM FORMULA) means that FORMULA expresses information that could be useful to the KB if asserted about TERM.  Such judgements are based on generalizations about things of the same type. Note that if FORMULA is salient to term, it may be strongly or weakly suggested that FORMULA be known to be true in the system, see #$keWeakSuggestion, #$keStrongSuggestion.  As an example of how this differs from strong or weak suggestions consider a partition of a collection, call it CollectionA.   It is probably useful to consider whether new specializations of CollectionA should also be made specializations of one of the partition cells.  However, we wouldn't strongly or weakly suggest that it be made such a specialization until after we've considered whether it fits into one of the cells.")
(comment adjSemTransTemplate "(#$adjSemTransTemplate COL FRAME TRANS) means that the translation of any adjective denotation of a word denoting an instance of COL, appearing with subcategorization frame FRAME, is TRANS.")
(comment Cancer "An instance of #$DiseaseType, and a specialization of #$AilmentCondition.  Instances of #$Cancer may belong to any one of the many different types of disease that are studied and treated by oncologists.  Instances of #$Cancer are characterized by abnormal (and usually rapid) growth of cells in some organ or system of the body; these growths are then prone to dispersal (metastasis) into other body regions.  See also #$CancerFn.")
(comment OxidationProcess "A collection of events.  In each instance of this collection, some amount of #$Oxygen reacts with (`reduces') another substance and releases energy in the process.")
(comment descriptionSentences "(#$descriptionSentences TERM FORMULA) states that FORMULA is a CycL formula involving TERM which is known to be true, and which desribes TERM. #$descriptionSentences is intended to apply to all formulas which partly comprise a description of TERM, while applying to no formulas which merely pertain to TERM. A query of the form (#$descriptionSentences TERM ?X) may be thought of as querying 'WhoWhat is TERM?'")
(comment BreakingEven "The collection of #$Events in which an investing #$Person or #$Organization reaches the #$breakEvenPoint, the level whereby it neither profits nor loses.  A #$CommercialOrganization is #$BreakingEven when it reaches the sales volume level at which total revenue equals total costs.  A securities investor who purchases a #$CallOption or a #$PutOption reaches his #$breakEvenPoint (and is therefore #$BreakingEven) when the price at which he has the option to buy or to sell some stock equals the price of the stock (adjusted to account for the amount of premium he has or will pay).")
(comment SurfaceToAirMissile "The collection of missiles (instances of #$Missile) which launch from platforms on the Earth's surface (located on either land or water) and are intended to attack airborne targets.")
(disjointWith PresidentsHoliday-US ReligiousHoliday)
(comment Matter "This is the collection of all instances of matter. The notion of matter here is

that employed in physics.")
(comment OralMedicationAdministration "Ingesting a drug.")
(comment interArgIsa2-5 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).  
(#$interArgIsa2-5 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, 
when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the second argument to RELN, 
a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the fifth argument 
must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is
an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then 
(RELN ARG1 INST ARG3 ARG4 ARG5 ... ARGN) is semantically 
well-formed only if ARG5 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation 
of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct 
specializations.")
(comment OilCompany "A specialization of both #$SellingOrganization and #$CommercialOrganization.  Each instance of #$OilCompany is a commercial organization whose primary business consists in bringing petroleum products (see the collection #$PetroleumProduct) to market.")
(comment AccessingAnIBTTypeFn "This function, given a #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType, returns the collection of #$AccessingAnIBT events involving #$InformationBearingThings that are instances of this type.  For instance, (#$AccessingAnIBTTypeFn #$DimeCoin-US) would return all the events of reading text on a dime.  See #$AccessingACWFn for the collection of events of accessing instantiations of a #$ConceptualWork.")
(comment PresuppositionPredicate "The collection of predicates  that   enable a basic CycL representation of commonsense knowledge  that \"pack in\" or \"gloss over\" assumptions that, for Cyc to do  interesting reasoning over,  would generally need to be made explicit.  By  definition, instances of  #$PresuppositionPredicate are axiomatically   related to other predicates that make all or most of  the assumptions in such natural language expressions  explicit.  Consider, for example, the Cyc treatment  of statements about evidence, which (appropriately)  involves ascribing an amount of evidence that an   #$IntelligentAgent has in support of some belief (see  #$evidentialSupportForBelief).  However, in ordinary  English, people who make statements about evidence  generally do not make them in terms of agents or beliefs.  Often, they make them in terms of an amount of evidence  and some #$Individual or #$Collection (e.g., \"there  is plenty of evidence for Nessie,\" \"there is no  evidence of UFOs\").  Obviously, parsing such syntactically  and semantically different expressions using  #$evidentialSupportForBelief is problematic.  Thus we  need #$evidentialSupportForPhenomena-AgentUnspecified,  which takes an amount and a collection -- and so   allows for easy parsing of such common English   expressions -- and is understood by Cyc via axioms  to the explicit, or 'longhand' CycL involving  #$evidentialSupportForBelief.")
(disjointWith CountyGovernment CityGovernment)
(comment vulnerableInType "(#$vulnerableInType SITUATION-TYPE OBJECT RESULT-TYPE) means that when in situations of type SITUATION-TYPE, existing object OBJECT is vulnerable to hardships of type RESULT-TYPE.  The purpose of #$vulnerableInType is to represent knowledge that an object is vulnerable in an entire class of situations.  For restrictions on RESULT-TYPE please see the comment on #$vulnerableIn.  Note that this is a type-level predicate in the first argument place and that care needs to be taken in developing rules that draw #$vulnerableIn conclusions from #$vulnerableInType GAFs so that we do not overpopulate the KB with potentially questionable #$vulnerableIn judgments.")
(comment SourceAddressField-Packet "An instance of #$SourceAddressField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet that

    contains the #$IPAddress of the computer which originally sent

the #$Packet-Internet which it is a part of.")
(comment Burning-Execution "A collection of event. A spec of #$Execution-Judicial.")
(comment freezingPoint "(#$freezingPoint STUFF TEMP) means that TEMP is the temperature at which the substance STUFF changes between having the attribute #$Liquid-StateOfMatter to #$Solid-StateOfMatter (when sufficient energy is output/input to lower/raise STUFF's temperature through this point).  Note that the freezing point of most substances is context-dependent (e.g., based on pressure.)")
(comment PlantingASeed "The collection of all events in which a seed is intentionally placed in or covered with soil")
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent AcademicTesting)
(comment abutsSurface "(#$abutsSurface OBJ1 OBJ2) means that an end of #$LongAndThin OBJ1 is in contact with the surface of OBJ2.")
(comment Axon "The collection of all axons (or 'neuraxons'), which are fibers of a #$Neuron which transmit signals away from the cell body to other #$Neurons or #$MuscleTissue.")
(comment HeartRateMonitor "The collection of all #$MedicalDevices designed to monitor a patient's heart rate and make that information available to medical personnel.  If the heart beat becomes irregular or stops, it emits a warning signal so that professional intervention will be prompt.")
(comment CollegeDevelopmentalBaseballLeague "baseball leagues whose players are college students from different colleges.  The purpose of such leagues is to give promising players professional-like experience while upholding their amateur status.")
(comment ArmoredPersonnelCarrier-M113 "The #$ArmoredPersonnelCarrier-M113 is the first modern 'battle taxi' developed to transport infantry forces on the battlefield. The M113 is built of aluminum so it is strong as steel at a much lighter weight. This allows the M113 to utilize a relatively small engine to power the vehicle, as well as carry a large payload cross-country. The vehicle is light enough that it floats and is capable of 'swimming' bodies of water.")
(comment And2Gate "An electrical device whose two inputs and one output are digital signals and whose output is the logical AND of its inputs.")
(comment AxisConstrainedRotation "#$Movement-Rotation physically constrained at the axis of rotation.  The object may rotate about an #$Axle, may be attached to a rotating #$Axle which is constrained it its position, or may be rotated by a spinning device which is attached to it along the #$axisOfRotation.  The axis may be through the center of gravity (e.g. #$DrillBit, #$Propeller, #$Wheel, ...) or not (clock hand, pendulum, ...).  A #$Wheel which falls off a car and rolls down the street is NOT axis constrained, and one of two wheels connected by a fixed #$Axle rolling as a unit is a borderline negative example.")
(comment StateMedicaidAdministrationOrganization "The collection of all US state organizations which  administer that state's Medicaid program.  Medicaid is federally  funded, but administered by a separate state organization in  each of the 50 US states.")
(comment allOperationalControlMilitaryOrg "(#$allOperationalControlMilitaryOrg SUPER SUB) means that the organization SUPER has been given direct or indirect operational control (at least temporary command) of the organization SUB for at least the duration of some operation.  This predicate corresponds to the concept known in military parlance as the 'OPCON' relation.  It is a transitive subordination-relation with any number of intermediate levels of command between SUPER and SUB version see #$operationalControlMilitaryOrg. If SUB is not permanently assigned or temporarily attached to SUPER, then the operational control (OPCON) relation lasts only for the extent of the operation in question (it is even more temporary than #$attachedMilitaryOrg). Usually SUPER will not be responsible for any logistical or service support of SUB, nor for paying SUB's operating expenses out of SUPER's regular budget.  See also #$allAssignedMilitaryOrg and #$allAttachedMilitaryOrg for contrast.")
(comment RaisingLivingThings "The collection of events in which something is grown, raised: plants, crops, livestock, etc.")
(comment InformationStoring "this is the collection of situations in which information is being stored on some information bearing thing.")
(comment tourCoversWorkBy "(#$tourCoversWorkBy TOUR ARTIST) means that tourists following itinerary of TOUR, an instance of #$TravelTour, have opportunities to see artistic works created by ARTIST, an instance of #$Artist.")
(comment FluidTangibleThing "A subcollection of #$PartiallyTangible and an instance of #$TangibleStuffStateType.  Each instance of #$FluidTangibleThing is a tangible thing that can flow.  This includes gases, liquids, and \"granular fluids\" (i.e. tangible things that are #$Pourable, such as sand); see #$GaseousTangibleThing, #$LiquidTangibleThing, and #$GranularFluid.  Instances of #$FluidTangibleThing include the air in Austin, the water in #$LakeErie, a particular chunk of snow, the sand on the beach at Malibu, and the mercury in a thermometer.  Non-instances include an air molecule, a snowflake, a grain of sand, a boulder, and a hunk of bread dough.")
(comment Issue "The collection of all instances of matters of discussion, debate, or public concern.")
(comment MusicalTextFn-Agent "#$MusicalTextFn-Agent takes as argument
any instance of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of all instances of
MusicalText which are the text of some piece of music written or
performed by that musician. These #$MusicalTexts may contain the
Lyric-WordsToSong of the piece, if it has lyrics. For example,
(#$MusicalTextFn-Agent KeithRichards) returns the collection of texts of
music written or performed by Keith Richards of the #$RollingStones.")
(comment PartyGame "All instances of games designed for playing at parties or with large groups of people.")
(comment Spacecraft "#$Spacecraft is a specialization of #$TransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$Spacecraft is a transportation device either deployed entirely in outer space, or one whose trajectories leave the atmosphere of the planet it's launched from, in order to orbit the planet or to travel beyond the planet's gravitational field.  A #$Spacecraft may either be manned or unmanned.")
(comment HillRange "a range of hills, analagous to #$MountainRange.")
(comment HumanShaped "#$HumanShaped is the instance of #$ShapeAttribute defined by the typical shape of a human.")
(comment WomensSportsTeam "the collection of all #$SportsTeams whose members

    are either human female teenagers (e.g., many

  Olympic gymnastics teams), adult human females

  (e.g., many Olympic soccer teams), or some mixture

  of both (e.g., many Olympic tennis and swim teams).  This 

   collection allows one to reify types of sports teams

   on the fly; e.g., (#$CollectionIntersection2Fn

   #$BasketballTeam #$WomensSportsTeam) is the collection

  of all women's basketball teams.")
(comment Decongestant "A drug that relieves congestion (as of mucous membranes)")
(comment Permeation "The expansion and/or translation of some stuff into some area or across some barrier, e.g. an odor in a room, wetness coming through a sponge.")
(comment InternationalOrganizationOfCountries "A collection of organizations; a specialization of #$InternationalOrganization.  Each instance of #$InternationalOrganizationOfCountries is an organization whose members are countries (as represented by their goverments).  Examples include the United Nations, NATO, SEATO, OAU, the League of Arab States, and OPEC.")
(comment EducationalGameProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerGamePrograms that are intended to be both game-like and educational. That is, in addition to educational goals, instances of this collection have 'game' aspects such as accumulating points, 'dying' and having to restart, and/or winning and losing. Instances are games such as 'Darby The Dragon' or 'Elroy Goes Bugzerk'.")
(comment Trailer "A wagon, van, box, etc. designed to be pulled by an automobile, truck. etc.")
(comment IterativeEvent "#$IterativeEvent is the  collection of all #$Events that are instances of some instance of #$IterativeEventType. An instance of #$IterativeEvent is a group of repeated events. For example, consider  ClockTicking01, an iterative clock ticking event which consists of the repeated tickings of a particular clock.   ClockTicking01 is an instance of both (#$IterationOfTypeFn ClockTicking) and  (#$GroupFn ClockTicking).  Since (#$IterationOfTypeFn ClockTicking) is an instance of #$IterativeEventType,  ClockTicking01 is  an instance of #$IterativeEvent.")
(comment HepatitisC-Virus "A collection of viri. Instances of #$HepatitisC-Virus are virus of the kind responsible for instances of #$HepatitisC-Infection.")
(disjointWith FallingEvent Translation-Periodic)
(comment Electronics-Hobby "A spec of #$HobbyActivity instances of which

  involve taking apart, tinkering with, and building

   #$ElectronicDevices.")
(comment ProductsSoldByFn "#$ProductsSoldByFn takes as argument any instance of #$RetailOrganization and returns the collection of all products sold by that organization.  For example, (#$ProductsSoldByFn #$SearsTheCompany) returns the collection of all products sold by Sears.")
(comment commutativeInArgsAndRest "A variable-arity #$MetaRelation used for 

stating that a given #$PartiallyCommutativeRelation (q.v.) is \"commutative\" 

with respect to two or more argument-places, including all argument-places that 

come after the ordinally highest one that is explicitly specified.  

(#$commutativeInArgsAndRest RELN ARGNUM-1 ARGNUM-2 ... ARGNUM-N) means that 

RELN is commutative in its ARGNUM-1th, ARGNUM-2th, ..., and ARGNUM-Nth 

arguments-places, along with any of its argument-places whose ordinal positions 

are greater than the greatest of the ARGNUM-i.  Thus RELN admits unrestricted 

permutation among any of these arguments.  More precisely (and assuming without 

loss of generality that ARGNUM-N is the numerically greatest of the ARGNUM-i):  

(i) if RELN is a #$Predicate that holds of a given argument-sequence SEQ, then 

RELN also holds of any other sequence SEQ-PERMUTE obtainable from SEQ by 

permuting some or all of SEQ's ARGNUM-1th, ARGNUM-2th, ..., ARGNUM-Nth, and 

subsequent items (while leaving all of SEQ's other items unchanged).  

(ii) if RELN is a #$Function-Denotational that associates a given 

argument-sequence SEQ with the value VALUE, then RELN also associates any 

sequence SEQ-PERMUTE (as described above) with VALUE.  For example, 

(#$commutativeInArgsAndRest #$commutativeInArgsAndRest 2) 

has as a consequence that whenever a sentence of the form 

(#$commutativeInArgsAndRest RELN 2 3 5) holds, so do the corresponding 

sentences (#$commutativeInArgsAndRest RELN 2 5 3), 

(#$commutativeInArgsAndRest RELN 3 2 5), and so on.  Note that since RELN 

is an instance of #$PartiallyCommutativeRelation, it must have at 

least two argument-places that are commutative with each other and at 

least one that is _not_ commutative with any other argument-place.  See

also #$commutativeInArgs.")
(comment Minehunter-Coastal "The collection of coastal minehunter ships.")
(comment DomesticPet "#$DomesticPet is a specialization of #$DomesticatedAnimal, #$HumanOccupationConstructResident, and #$PortableObject.  Each specialization of #$DomesticPet is a type of domesticated animal kept by humans primarily for companionship.  Many members of #$DomesticPet live in the homes of their owners.")
(comment meansOfInfoTransfer "This predicate is a more specific version of #$actors intended to single out those instances of #$SomethingExisting that play some role in instances of #$InformationTransferEvent and that are designed to aid in information transfer.  It is also a generalized version of  #$meansOfInfoTransfer-Artifact and #$meansOfInfoTransfer-ComputerProgram. (#$meansOfInfoTransfer ITE THING) means that the instance THING of #$SomethingExisting plays an instrumental role in the  #$InformationTransferEvent ITE and that THING was created in part to be able to play such roles, e.g. (#$intendedBehaviorCapable THING #$InformationTransferEvent #$instrument-Generic) holds.  For example, if some instance TEL of  #$Telephone is used in a successful telephone call CALL, then we could represent this with (#$meansOfInfoTransfer CALL TEL).")
(disjointWith NonintrusiveJunction BranchingJunction)
(comment OneToManyCommunication "A CommunicationAct in which there are multiple receivers.")
(comment Nickel "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of nickel.")
(comment (BuyingFn Artifact-Generic) "This non-atomic reified term denotes the collection of buying events in which the object purchased is an instance of the collection #$Artifact-Generic.")
(comment Addiction "A physiological condition in which the bodilyInvolved organism has a need for a particular #$AddictiveSubstance.")
(comment FormalSchooling "This is the type of studying usually carried out at an educational institution following a prescribed 
course of study.")
(comment OfficialReportByAgentFn "This collection allows one to reify types of #$OfficialReports issued or generated by a particular agent.  For example, #$ImmigrationRecords issued by the #$USImmigrationAndNaturalizationService or #$AnnualBusinessReport issued by #$MicrosoftInc.")
(comment agentDeployed-BCW "(#$agentDeployed-BCW DEPLOYING AGENT) means that AGENT is a

#$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance that is deployed in the

#$DeployingAChemicalOrBiologicalAgent event DEPLOYING.")
(comment SnowShoe "The collection of snow shoes. Snow shoes aren't really shoes but rather

devices with a lattice of material designed to keep one from sinking

into deep snow.")
(comment FieldServicesUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profiles center on           services provided in the field.")
(comment SportBoating "Boating done for challenge or relaxation.")
(comment Password-Poor "#$Password-Poor is a subset of #$Password-Weak.  It includes short passwords and common passwords             such as 'PASSWORD'  and 'START', as well as passwords that are fairly easily guessed, such as            any character strings that are also English words.")
(comment calendarParts "A function that relates an instance of #$CalendarSystem to an element of some salient division of the instance. E.g., the 'Common Era' (if it were KE-ed) could be related to #$JulianCalendar by #$calendarParts. For another example: (#$calendarParts #$ElvishCalendar #$FirstAgeOfMiddleEarth).")
(comment SunnyClimateCycle "The collection of climate cycles that are primarily sunny.")
(comment Narrative "A specialization of #$PropositionalConceptualWork. Each instance of #$Narrative is an abstract work that recounts a sequence of events (in chronological order or in such a manner that their temporal order can be ascertained) involving some agent or agents.  Instances of #$Narrative may be fictional or factual and, accordingly, may involve instances of #$Person or instamces of #$FictionalCharacter.  Important specializations of #$Narrative include #$Novel-CW and #$Biography.")
(comment AvianVeterinarian "Instances are veterinarians that specialize in the care of birds.")
(comment Hardness "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity.  Each instance of #$Hardness is a level of pressure a tangible material can withstand before deforming or fragmenting.  Hardnesses may be characterized using a #$GenericValueFunction (q.v.), or relative to certain substances, e.g., #$HardAsARock.  See also the predicate #$hardnessOfObject, which relates a physical object to its level of #$Hardness.")
(comment OldTownArea "A collection of #$UrbanAreas. Instances of #$OldTownArea are
older parts within certain cities. These area are usually considered of
historical and touristic interest. See #$OldTownFn, #$oldTownOf")
(comment Clay-Wet "Natural earthy material that is plastic when wet, consisting essentially of hydrated silicates of aluminum: used for making bricks, pottery, etc.")
(disjointWith Planetarium Facility-Construct)
(comment YearFn "An instance of #$DateDenotingFunction.  #$YearFn returns an instance of #$CalendarYear when applied to an instance of #$Integer. (#$YearFn INTEGER) denotes the year INTEGER in the (extended) #$GregorianCalendar. For example, (#$YearFn 1966) denotes the year 1966. Customarily, the Gregorian calendar is used only for dates from the 1500's onward, when it was instituted, and the #$JulianCalendar for dates before that, including dates before the common era. It is possible to follow this convention in Cyc and use (#$YearBCE-JulianFn 1), (#$YearBCE-JulianFn 2), ... instead of (#$YearFn 0), (#$YearFn -1), ... .")
(disjointWith AirportOrganization TravelAgency)
(comment DesignForObjectTypeFn "#$DesignForObjectTypeFn takes as argument a spec of #$Artifact, and returns the spec of #$ObjectSpecification whose instances are designs or specifications for that type of Artifact.  For example, (#$DesignForObjectTypeFn #$RadioReceiver) returns the collection of designs for radio receivers.")
(comment MusicalComposition-Classical "The collection of #$MusicalCompositions that are considered 'classical', rather than popular. In the sphere of influence of Western Europe, instances are members of a tradition that started with the rise of counterpoint and modern conceptions of harmony around the 17th century.")
(comment GeneExpression "The collection of events in which some quantity, more than a
single molecule, of protein is synthesized \"under the guidance\" of a
particular gene, i.e., the entire process from transcription to the
point at which protein is synthesized.")
(comment CruiseMissile-AS15 "A type of cruise missile.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Egypt is possession of many of these cruise missiles and may use the missiles as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment Sport "The collection of all sports considered as abstract activities.  See #$SportsEvent for events of engaging whole units of such sports and #$AthleticActivity for activity of the type engaged in while performing sports.  Sports which are also games, are members of the collection #$SportsGame.  The activity of participating in SPORT is an instance of (#$PlayingFn SPORT).")
(comment Metoclopramide "The chemical compound which is used in ulcer medication.")
(comment CommandHelicopter "The class of helicopters used to transport the commanders of a unit. Examples are the UH-1H Command and Control Helicopter.")
(comment waterSolubility "(#$waterSolubility OBJ DEGREE) means that the tangible OBJ has this DEGREE of #$Solubility in water.  A higher value of DEGREE indicates that a substance dissolves more readily and completely than one with a lower solubility.")
(comment CensusGroupOfHispanicOrigin "Collection of people identified as having personal or family origins in Hispanic countries or regions.")
(comment PhysicalSeries "A specialization of both #$Series and #$PartiallyTangible.  Each instance of #$PhysicalSeries is a group of partially tangible objects ordered in a linear fashion, most likely according to some spatial relationship.  Instances would include a group of people in line at a ticket booth, or the vertebrae in a person's spine.")
(comment inputCodeTransducer-FunctionalRole "(#$inputCodeTransducer-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means that

AGENT is expected to take instances of #$InformationBearingObject that

originate outside of SYSTEM and change their encoding to a form

suitable for dissemination within SYSTEM.")
(comment AmateurFn "(#$AmateurFn PERSON-BY-ACTIV-TYPE) denotes the subcollection of PERSON-BY-ACTIV-TYPE consisting of those persons who perform the relevant activity without pay, i.e. as an amateur. Cf. #$ProfessionalFn.")
(comment Naira-Nigeria "The unit of currency used in Nigeria-AtPresent.")
(comment LuminescenceDating "While some charge traps in minerals are sensitive to heat, others are extremely sensitive to light. When an irradiated quartz or feldspar sample is

exposed to visible or even infrared photons, the trapped electrons are evicted from these light-sensitive deep traps. They promptly undergo

recombination, and in doing so emit photons in the visible spectrum. Careful wavelength restriction of the stimulating light, combined with strict

filtering of the photons emitted by the sample, allows detection of the recombination luminescence. The amount of light emitted is proportional to

the mineral's intrinsic sensitivity to radiation and the total amount of radiation energy absorbed. Comparisons made of the light emitted by a natural

sample and the amount of light emitted by a sample with a known added radiation dose, plus separate dosimetry measurements, allow the sample's

age since it was last exposed to a \"clock-resetting event\" to be calculated. For optical dating, also sometimes referred to as OSL (optically stimulated luminescence) dating, the clock-resetting event is the exposure to

sunlight which sediment grains undergo during transport and the process of sedimentation. Optical dating is therefore suitable for the dating of a

wide variety of unheated sedimentary deposits laid down within the last ~500,000 years.")
(comment Clove-TheFlowerBud "The stage of the flower of the clove tree at which it is harvested to be used as a spice.")
(disjointWith (MeaningInSystemFn SENSUS-Information1997 "NON-ADDRESSEE-ORIENTED-VERBAL-PROCESS") (MeaningInSystemFn SENSUS-Information1997 "ADDRESSEE-ORIENTED-VERBAL-PROCESS"))
(comment Howitzer-122mmSelfPropelled "The collection of self-propelled 122mm #$Howitzers.")
(comment Liquid-StateOfMatter "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangible and an instance of #$MatterTypeByPhysicalState. Each instance of #$Liquid-StateOfMatter is an object of a single chemical species in the liquid state of matter. Objects in the liquid state of matter are at a temperature and pressure such that the molecules of the matter move freely relative to their neighbors, but are not excited enough to break free. Liquid objects are characterized at the macroscopic level by special qualities of flow, such as being pourable and conforming to whatever container they occupy.  Instances of #$Liquid-StateOfMatter include a quantity of liquid nitrogen, the water component of a gallon of seawater, a lump of mercury at room temperature, and some molten silver about to be poured into a teapot mold.  Counterexamples include a gallon of seawater (since it has dissolved minerals) and 190 proof ethanol (since it is 5% water).")
(comment XYCrossSectionFn "This function maps three-dimensional objects to the arbitrarily thin slice of the object that defines an xy-cross section of the object as determined by the object's intrinsic axes.  See also #$xyCrossSection and #$IntrinsicAxisOfObjects.")
(comment AirborneEarlyWarningAircraft "The collection of military aircraft which are equipped with long-range radar and used in the surveillance of airspace and maritime territory.")
(comment BowlingActivity "A collection of events in which bowlers roll heavy balls toward a group of pins, intending to knock the pins down.")
(comment AcupunctureNeedle "A collection of needles designed specifically for acupuncture.")
(comment ProkaryoticRibosome "A collection.  These are tiny bodies located in prokaryotic
cells and made of protein and RNA.  These are the sites in which
proteins are synthesized for cell use.")
(comment AlternativeMedicalModalityFOSFn "(#$AlternativeMedicalModalityFOSFn MODALITY) is the subfield of #$AlternativeMedicine concerned with the instance of #$AlternativeMedicineEventTypeByModality MODALITY. For example, (#$AlternativeMedicalModalityFOSFn #$Acupuncture) denotes acupuncture as a subfield of #$AlternativeMedicine. Although many of these therapies are not studied in traditional #$AcademicDepartments, there are usually schools and training centers that offer instruction and provide a kind of certification to those who complete the training successfully. This function makes it unnecessary to create a hierarchy of alternative medicine subfields paralleling the hierarchy of alternative medical modalities and practitioners that already exists.")
(comment NewsShow "A collection of television shows [#$TVShow-CW], those primarily intended to provide #$News about current events e.g. 'NBCNews' or     'The News Hour with Jim Lehrer'.  This collection includes both #$TVSeriesProducts and individual shows [#$TVShow-SingleCW]")
(comment SkinnyDipping "The collection of events in which a #$Person frolics in a #$BodyOfWater or a #$SwimmingPool-Outdoor in the #$Nude")
(disjointWith LighterThanAirCraft FixedWingAircraft)
(comment Flexus-Planetary "A collection of topographical features.  Each element of #$Flexus-Planetary is an very low curvilinear ridge with a scalloped pattern on an extraterrestrial planetary body.")
(comment riverStartsNearWhere "a place just in the general vicinity of where the river originates, cited to give a rough idea of where that is")
(comment PigeonGuillemot "The collection of all members of a species (Cepphus columba) of Arctic #$Bird.  Breeding adults have all black feathers, while non-breeding adults have white wing patches, necks, and underparts.  Their feet are red")
(comment increasesFluent "This predicate relates a quantity-slot to a set or collection with respect to whose elements the slot tends to associate relatively large quantities.  More precisely, (#$increasesFluent SETORCOL SLOT) means that, all else being equal, for any ELEMENT and any NON-ELEMENT such that only the former is an element of SETORCOL, if (SLOT ELEMENT AMOUNT1) and (SLOT NON-ELEMENT AMOUNT2), then AMOUNT1 will be larger than AMOUNT2.")
(comment HighJumpBar "The collection of bars that high jumpers try to clear.")
(comment ThreePersonInflatableBoat "The collection of military inflatable boats which can accommodate three people.")
(comment RadioSeriesProduct "The collection of all #$BroadcastSeriesProducts which are intended for broadcast by radio.")
(comment Scandium "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of scandium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment TransvestitePerson "The collection of persons who enjoy dressing like a person            of the opposite sex.")
(comment VisaFn "An instance of #$ReifiableFunction and #$CollectionDenotingFunction. Given an element of #$IndependentCountry as its argument, #$VisaFn forms a non-atomic term used to denote the collection of visas (see the constant #$Visa-Permit) issued by that country.")
(comment MathematicalOrdering "The collection of all those #$RelationalStructures that are called 'orderings'.  A #$MathematicalOrdering is usually described as an ordered pair <S, R> where S is a set and R is a binary relation on S that is transitive, i.e., for each X, Y and Z in S, R(X Y) and R(Y Z) imply R(X Z).  We do not have to define a #$MathematicalOrdering in Cyc as an ordered pair, but it is essential that each such #$MathematicalOrdering has a unique #$baseSet and a unique ordering relation.  We use, for each #$MathematicalOrdering ORDER, (#$orderingRelations ORDER PRED) to specify a binary predicate PRED, the restriction of which to the #$baseSet S of ORDER indicates the ordering relation R on S, and we require the collections that are used to specify the arguments to PRED to be supersets of S.  In principle, there could be different predicates PRED1 and PRED2 such that when restricted to the same #$baseSet S of a #$MathematicalOrdering ORDER, they order the elements of S exactly the same way.  When we said that there is a unique ordering relation R on S, we mean to ignore the difference between PRED1 and PRED2 when they are restricted to S, and treat the results of such restrictions the same, as far as they are used to talk about ORDER.  Subcollections of #$MathematicalOrdering include #$PartialOrdering, #$PartialOrdering-Strict, #$TreeOrdering, #$TreeOrdering-Strict, #$TotalOrdering, #$TotalOrdering-Strict, #$WellOrdering and #$Lattice-LatticeTheoretic, etc.")
(comment GeneralizedQuantifierRelation "Each instance of this collection is a `relational' version of a

#$GeneralizedQuantifier. These relational variants have been introduced mostly to simplify rapid OE creation and NL parsing.")
(comment SimplifierDirectivePredicate "The collection of #$Predicates which can affect the
behaviour of the #$CycLSimplifier.  When
simplifier directive GAFs are asserted, they are only relevant to
the simplifier when it is simplifying expressions in the
microtheory in which the directive is asserted, or a specMt thereof.")
(disjointWith Metal CarbonDioxide)
(comment LifeThreateningCondition "A specialization of #$PhysiologicalCondition.  Each instance of #$LifeThreateningCondition is 
an ailment which, if left untreated, may cause the death of the organism 
afflicted by it.  Specializations include #$Poisoning and #$Rabies.")
(comment nonPlural-Generic "This predicate is a generalization over the #$SpeechPartPredicates that do not express plural number:  specifically, the spec-preds of #$singular-Generic and #$massNumber-Generic (q.v.).  This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it will always cash out as an assertion on a more specialized predicate.")
(comment ShkvalTorpedo "A type of high-speed Russian #$Torpedo with speeds of hundreds of miles per hour underwater.")
(comment MusicVideoCopy "A #$VideoRecordedObject whose playings (see #$performanceOfIBT) have an audio portion, consisting of a #$Song-Sung, and a video portion typically consisting of images of the performers dancing, singing, playing instruments, etc. Made for sale or television broadcast.")
(comment Klebsiella "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  These #$GramNegativeBacterium exhibt mucoid growth, large polysaccharide capsules, and lack motility.  These organisms are found in the gastrointestinal flora as well as free living in nature.  Usually they are characterized by prompt lactose fermentation, except for the species Serratia.  They have both a fermentative and respiratory type metabolism and are oxidase negative.  Most #$BiologicalSpecies can use citrate and glucose as a sole carbon source.  These are opportunistic pathogens that are resistent to ampicillin and carbenicillin.")
(comment MasqueradingAtASocialGathering "#$MasqueradingAtASocialGathering is the collection of instances of #$Masquerading which are done primarily for entertainment. For example, attending a #$Halloween party would constitute an instance of #$MasqueradingAtASocialGathering. #$MasqueradingAtASocialGathering stands in contrast to #$Masquerading-Deceiving, instances of which are not instances of  #$EntertainmentEvent, but are done for the purpose of defrauding others.")
(comment chemicalPurityOfObject "(#$chemicalPurityOfObject OBJ PUR) means that the tangible thing OBJ has the
#$ChemicalPurity PUR.")
(comment targetedProductType "(#$targetedProductType EVT PROD) means that PROD is the kind of product with which the #$EconomicAction EVT is concerned.  Economic actions of various kinds may involve a #$targetedProductType: boycotts (in which instances of that product type are not purchased from the agent being boycotted), embargoes (in which that product is not traded with the embargoed agent), or marketing campaigns (in which that type of product is promoted).--Nichols, Mar 25, 1998")
(comment IntermediateVocabAttribute "The collection of instances of #$AttributeValue that

 are important for NL parsing by contributing to an intermediate

 vocabulary between the English to be parsed, and

 the terse CycL that will be used in inferencing.")
(comment enables-SitSit "If (#$enables-SitSit SIT1 SIT2) and PRECON is a known

propositional precondition for SIT2, then SIT1 causes PRECON to become

true.")
(comment Hacker "A specialization of #$ComputerUser. Each instance of #$Hacker is a person who who willfully attempts to access, use, or affect an instance of #$ComputationalSystem without authorization.   Hackers may also be authorized users of a system that attempt to  use or affect the system in a manner that is not consistent with its normal operation or intended use (see #$Hacker-Insider). Hackers attack computational systems using computers -- someone who crashes their computer by beating it with a bat or pouring water on it would not be a hacker.  Hackers use the resources -- input devices, drives, programs, operations, etc. -- of a computer to hack it, or they use one computer's resources to hack another.")
(disjointWith TrackedVehicle WheeledTransportationDevice)
(comment Fuse-IgnitionDevice-Proximity "The collection of #$Fuse-IgnitionDevices that uses a sensor device to determine the presence, direction, and/or distance of the target.  The fuse will initiate after the target is detected.")
(comment Atom "A specialization of #$ChemicalObject. Each instance of #$Atom is a microscopic-scale object with exactly one atomic nucleus (see #$AtomicNucleus) and some number of electrons (see #$Electron).  A typical instance of #$Atom has no net charge, i.e., it has as many instances of #$Electron as it does of #$Proton.  For the collection of atoms that do have non-zero charges, see #$MonoatomicIon.")
(comment Emirate-Geopolitical "#$Emirate-Geopolitical is a specialization of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  Each instance of #$Emirate-Geopolitical is a geopolitical entity, or territories, each of which is ordinarily ruled by an #$Amir-HeadOfState or an Emir (Amir) who is not necessariy a #$HeadOfState of an #$IndependentCountry, but rules a subsidiary region.  See especially the #$UnitedArabEmirates.")
(comment SeveralHoursDuration "A duration of from 6 to 18 hours")
(comment correspondenceBetween "(#$correspondenceBetween CORR BASE-ITEM TARGET-ITEM) represents the hypothesis that BASE-ITEM matches TARGET-ITEM. BASE-ITEM and TARGET-ITEM can be entities, functors, or expressions of #$AnalogyCases. Mappings include a set of structurally consistent correspondences. For example, comparing WW-II to the Gulf war may produce a correspondence between Germany and Iraq.")
(comment TridentClassSubmarine "A class of nuclear powered ballistic missile submarines,            used in the #$UnitedStatesNavy.")
(comment RifledBoreWeapon "The collection of #$ProjectileLaunchers that have #$Bores with spiralled scoring.  Rifling the #$Bore increases the accuracy of the #$ProjectileWeapon.")
(comment Raindrop "The collection of drops of liquid water emitted by clouds in instances of #$RainProcess.")
(comment (HighAmountFn Compressibility) "Can be compressed almost any amount")
(comment rejectsProposal "(#$rejectsProposal REJECTING PROPOSAL) means that the communication 

act REJECTING rejects PROPOSAL which is the information content of some propoasl.")
(comment AsymmetricDigitalSubscriberLine "A variation of 'Digital Subscriber Line' designed for an upstream data flow (client-to-server) which is a fraction of the downstream data flow (server-to-client).  Typically the upstream data flow is measured in kilobits per second while the downstream data flow is measured in megabits per second (e.g. 6 megabits per second over standard phone lines). ADSL is appropriate for applications such as Video on Demand or World-Wide Web where a request from the user is far less data than the response.")
(comment Cyanosis-PhysiologicalCondition "A collection of the #$PhysiologicalConditions defined as bluish
discolorations, applied especially to such discoloration of #$Skin and
mucuous membranes due to excessive concentration of reduced hemoglobin in
the #$Blood.")
(comment MtTimeFn "(#$MtTimeFn MICROTHEORY) denotes the piece of time during which the assertions in MICROTHEORY are true.  See also #$mtTime.")
(comment structureMapAnyMt "(#$structureMapAnyMt ?Src ?Tgt ?Src-Desc ?Tgt-Desc) returns a structure-mapping of the formulae in ?Src-Mt pertaining to the source concept ?Src that are isomorphic with formulae in ?Tgt-Mt that pertain to the target domain concept ?Tgt. The mappings are condensed as formulae, so ?Src-Desc becomes bound to an and of all the matching formulae in the source domain, while ?Tgt-Desc becomes bound to an and of all the matching formulae in the target domain. See also #$structureMap, a version of this predicate in which the structure-mapping process is restricted to axioms available in specified microtheories only.")
(disjointWith (TransportViaFn AirTransportationDevice) (TransportViaFn WaterTransportationDevice))
(comment availableToAgentTypeForEventType "(#$availableToAgentTypeForEventType AGENT-TYPE OBJECT EVENT-TYPE) means that OBJECT is typically available for agents of type AGENT-TYPE to use in events of type EVENT-TYPE.  If an instance of AGENT-TYPE is capable of using OBJECT in an instance of EVENT-TYPE, nothing prevents that agent from choosing to use OBJECT in that event. Note that if OBJECT is available to an instance of AGENT-TYPE in an instance of EVENT-TYPE, that instance of AGENT-TYPE may still, for other reasons, be incapable of using OBJECT in that instance of EVENT-TYPE. Compare this predicate to #$availableForEvent and #$availableToAgentTypeForEvent.")
(comment relevantPath "In Workarounds problems, (relevantPath ?PATH) means that PATH is the path on which the interdicted will move at the end of the workaround operations. Generally, relevantPath will be an emplaced bridge or the gap containing a fording site.")
(comment SolidPlanetaryBody "A collection of heavenly bodies.  Each element of #$SolidPlanetaryBody is a planetary body composed primarily of solid substances.")
(comment WesternMovie "#$WesternMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW, each of which depicts a story that takes place in the old west.")
(comment NaftinfineHydrochloride "The chemical compound which is an anti-fungal.")
(comment E-TheLetter "The letter E of the alphabet.  This is 'E' (or 'e') as a #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterE and #$LatinSmallLetterE.")
(disjointWith EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus FamilyTypeByIncome)
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization DiplomaticMission-ThePost)
(comment parentActors "(#$parentActors EV P) means that organism P is one of the parents in the #$BiologicalReproductionEvent EV.")
(comment Electron "A specialization of #$Lepton.  Each instance of #$Electron is a subatomic particle with an #$ElectricalCharge of -1.  Each instance of #$Atom consists of a nucleus (see #$AtomicNucleus) surrounded by a cloud of negatively charged electrons.")
(comment weaponEffectiveRange-Max "(#$weaponEffectiveRange-Max WEAPON RANGE) means that RANGE
is the maximum range at which the projectile weapon WEAPON is
considered to be 'effective', ie, capable of doing significant damage
to a target.  Every projectile weapon has a maximum effective range,
at least in the terrestrial frame of reference.  Some also have a
minimum effective range--see #$weaponEffectiveRange-Min.  Where it is
desireable to have both the minimum and maximum effective range
referenced in the same GAF, use #$weaponEffectiveRange.  Also,
#$weaponEffectiveRange-Max should be distinguished from #$weaponRange,
which cites the maximum distance a projectile weapon can travel.  This
is often much greater than the #$weaponEffectiveRange-Max.")
(comment Tellurium "The element Tellurium, atomic number 52.")
(comment Nitrobacter-Genus "A collection of all #$BiologicalSpecies in the #$Nitrobacter-Genus.  They are rod or pear-shaped.  May or may not be #$MotileBacterium.  These #$ProkaryoticCells oxidize nitrite into nitrate for energy.  #$CellDivision occurs by #$BuddingCellDivision or #$BinaryFission.  These may or may not be motile.")
(comment undergroundOf "(#$undergroundOf OBJ GROUND) means that OBJ is beneath the surface of GROUND and has the #$locationState #$Underground.")
(comment MilitaryLandPlatform "#$MilitaryLandPlatform is a specialization of #$Platform-Military and #$LandTransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$MilitaryLandPlatform is used by the military to transport equipment, weapons, and/or personnel on land.")
(comment CanModeFn "(#$CanModeFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-MT) denotes the      subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances possess the modal property denoted by \"can\", from the perspective of CONTEXT-MT.")
(comment Puzzle-Generic "The collection of all puzzles, i.e., instances of #$Artifact-Generic that have a 'solution' one has to figure out, and which are intended to provide diversion or serve as a test of intellect.")
(comment Hemophilia "A sex-linked hereditary blood defect almost exclusively of males characterized by delayed clotting of the blood and consequent difficulty in controlling bleeding, even after minor injuries.")
(comment Post-NounPhraseModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which can postmodify a noun. Example: 'yesterday', as in 'the meeting yesterday'.")
(comment programCopyOfTransfer "(#$programCopyOfTransfer TRANSFER COPY) means that in the instance of #$InformationTransferEvent, TRANSFER, the instance COPY of #$ComputerProgramCopy transfers information.  This predicate would be used to assert, e.g., that a particular instantiation of #$Pine-TheProgram was used in a particular instance of #$EMailSending.")
(comment VaccinationAgainstFn "(#$VaccinationAgainstFn INFECTIONTYPE) returns the
collection of all #$VaccinationEvents such that the #$transferredThing
is an instance of (#$VaccineForFn INFECTIONTYPE) and such that the
primary purpose of the caregiver is to render the recipient
#$immuneWithRespectToPathogen w.r.t. the pathogen that causes
DISEASETYPE.")
(comment BiblicalEpicMovie "#$BiblicalEpicMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which dramatize a narrative taken from the #$Bible. An example is #$TheTenCommandments-TheMovie.")
(comment TradeGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with having access to international markets and other trading advantages.  A minimal trade goal is simply being able to trade.  Example: (#$goalCategoryForAgent (#$GovernmentFn #$China-PeoplesRepublic) (#$groupMembers #$China-PeoplesRepublic #$WorldTradeOrganization) #$TradeGoal).")
(comment ParathyroidHormone "A #$Hormone secreted by the parathyroid glands that regulates calcium and phosphorus metabolism.")
(comment VanityMirror "The collection of #$VanityMirrors. A #$VanityMirror has two #$Mirrors, one of which has a higher magnification  than the other. Usually the #$Mirrors are circular and are mounted to something thin, back to back. The mirrors revolve in such a manner that you can have either mirror facing forward. #$VanityMirrors don't require the use of a hand or a wall mounting. They are mounted in a stand which has the axle that the #$Mirrors turn on. If one were to use a #$VanityMirror, it usually sits on a table or counter in the #$BedRoom or in the #$Bathroom-Home where one's #$Makeup is applied.")
(comment SurfaceToAirMissileUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on missiles           that are fired from a ground-based weapons platform at an airborne           target.")
(comment instantiationOfAIS "(#$instantiationOfAIS IBT AIS) means that the #$InformationBearingThing, IBT, instantiates the #$AbstractInformationStructure, AIS. This is the relation between the text of a hard copy of Moby Dick and the instance of #$TextString (a spec of #$AbstractInformationStructure) which is the text of that copy. Likewise, it is the relation of a physical piece of sheet music to the intangible piece of #$MusicalText that is written on that sheet.")
(comment ProblemSolvingAgent "#$ProblemSolvingAgent are those agents capable of performing #$ProblemSolvingActions.")
(comment IntervalStartedByFn "An instance of both #$UnaryFunction and #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance TEMP-OBJ of #$TemporalThing, #$IntervalStartedByFn returns the time interval that begins when TEMP-OBJ ends, and continues until the end of time (if time has an end).")
(comment Promethium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of promethium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment DictionaryFromEnglishToFn "#$DictionaryFromEnglishToFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. (#$DictionaryFromEnglishToFn LANGUAGE) represents the spec of #$Dictionary whose elements are dictionaries that translate English words into LANGUAGE. For example, (#$DictionaryFromEnglishToFn #$SpanishLanguage) denotes the collection of dictionaries that translate English words into Spanish.")
(comment FunctionalSystem "A Cyc collection.  Each instance is a special kind of #$Group that exists in time and interacts over the course of time in ways that underpin controlled application of resources and internal information exchange and processing by the system as a whole in order to perform certain tasks--which often can themselves be considered as functional roles in a larger system.  #$FunctionalSystems have some of the characteristics of what James Grier Miller calls 'living systems'.  Instances of #$BiologicalLivingObject, #$Organization, and #$GeopoliticalEntity are all considered to be #$FunctionalSystems in the #$FunctionalRoleAnalysisMt.")
(comment ConsumerLoanAgreement "The collection of #$AuthorizedAgreements which are #$LoanAgreements made to private individuals for personal use, rather than for business.  #$ConsumerLoanAgreements include #$MortgageAgreements, #$CreditCardAccounts, #$CarLoans, #$StudentLoans, #$HomeImprovementLoans, and #$HomeEquityLoans.")
(comment ComputerProcess-SingleComputer "The subcollection of #$ComputerProcess-Generic whose instances meet
   the criteria of the word 'process' as used in standard computer parlance, i.e.
   each runs on a single computer.
   An instance of #$ComputerProcess-SingleComputer may have multiple threads,
   but all its threads must execute on the same computer as the process,
   though not necessarily the same CPU.
   An instance of #$ComputerProcess-SingleComputer
   may be suspended or temporarily swapped out, so it is not necessary that it be
   continuously running throughout its existence.  However, if the process saves 
   out its state, is killed, and the state is reloaded, there will then be a
   different instance of #$ComputerProcess-SingleComputer running on the computer.
   This is meant to agree with the sense of process used when one speaks, for 
   example, of a 'Unix process'.")
(comment TVBiography "Instances of this collection are #$TVShow-CWs that are primarily intended to present a biography as a nonfictional historical narrative. If it is intended as a semi-fictional fact-based narrative, then it is  an instance of #$TVBiography-PartlyFictional.")
(disjointWith AirFrontEvent AnnualClimateCycle)
(comment Interval-UnboundedAbove "A subcollection of #$ScalarIntervals that is not bounded at the top. It is disjoint with #$Interval-BoundedAbove.")
(comment MilitaryVeteranTypeByWar "Instances are collections of people who served in some official military organization as part of a particular war.  Note that the instances of #$MilitaryVeteranTypeByWar are not necessarily disjoint, because the same person might have served in more than one war.")
(comment NonDavidsonianPredicate "The general concept is: predicates that are used to describe eventualities -- i.e., events, states or processes -- in a 'non-Davidsonian' way, that is, without presupposing the existence of event particulars in the manner of Davidson. Currently, the only constant in this collection is #$eventPred, though it is conceivable that more may be added, perhaps by using something like #$eventPred.")
(comment DrawingAFilament "drawing a filament, like a wire or thread")
(comment totalValueOfNonCurrentAssets "The predicate that relates a #$Person or #$Organization to the total monetary value of its noncurrent assets.  Noncurrent assets include fixed assets (see #$fixedAssetOf), investments, and intangible assets (see #$intangibleAssetOf).  (#$totalValueOfNonCurrentAssets AGENT MONEY) means that MONEY is the sum of the #$valueOfFixedAssets, value of investments, and #$valueOfIntangibleAssets.")
(comment BiologicalWeaponTypeByAgent "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$BiologicalWeaponTypeByAgent are collections of #$BiologicalWeapons, arranged according to the #$BiologicalAgent used in their instances.")
(comment AirToAirMissile "The collection of missiles (instances of #$Missile) that are designed to launch from airborne platforms and are intended to attack airborne targets.")
(comment TallPhysicalBuild "The attribute of being above average height.")
(comment unfilteredPortsForNetwork "A predicate relating instances of #$Firewall-Network with port/protocol pairs and instances of #$Computer in the firewall's network. (#$unfilteredPortsForNetwork FIREWALL PROTOCOL NUM NETWORK) means that FIREWALL lets through all packets that conform to PROTOCOL coming from outside the network bound for port number NUM on any computer on NETWORK.")
(comment PhilosophyFn "The term `(#$PhilosophyFn ?THING)' denotes the #$FieldOfStudy, the subfield of

#$Philosophy, in which ?THING is the topic. ")
(comment IntrauterineAdministration "Inserting a drug or object into the uterus.")
(comment PublicPrivateConsortium "A #$PublicPrivateConsortium is a consortium of private businesses or individuals and public or governmental institutions")
(disjointWith CountyGovernment GovernmentOfCountry)
(comment TimeToLiveField-Packet "A #$TimeToLiveField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet
that indicates how many hops a #$Packet-Internet can make between
routers en route to its destination before it should be discarded.
This prevents lost #$Packet-Internets from wandering around
indefinitely.")
(comment WalkingSpeed "The range of velocity which an average person walks.")
(comment PlayPerformance "#$PlayPerformance is the collection of instances of #$EntertainmentPerformance the predominant activity of which consists of instances of #$DramaticActing-Live. Each instance of #$PlayPerformance will be a performance [#$performanceOfWork] of a #$Play-CW.")
(comment WrittenReportOnSituation "A collection of instances of #$TextualMaterial.  Each instance is a textual report composed by one agent for the benefit of another concerning a particular situation in which that other agent is believed to be interested.")
(disjointWith PurposefulAction Perceiving-Involuntary)
(comment Incorporation-Physical "The collection of events in which an object or chunk of stuff comes to include, or acquire, or be joined to another object or chunk of stuff. If the additional object can be properly said to be a part of the entity into which it is incorporated, it is probably more appropriate to use #$AttachmentEvent or one of its specs. But incorporation is more general: for instance, an egg can be incorporated into a chunk of pizza dough, or a teaspoon of cream into a cup of coffee.")
(comment MakingButter "A specialization of #$PreparingFoodItem.  Each instance of #$MakingButter is an event in which milk is churned into butter.")
(comment Shipyard "The collection of shipyards. Each #$Shipyard is a place where ships or boats are constructed or repaired. If a shipyard is meant for repair there will be equipment for hauling the ships onto the shore. ")
(disjointWith IntrinsicStateChangeEvent AcademicTesting)
(comment CycLReifiedDenotationalTerm "The collection of denotational terms in the CycL language which are
reified in the KB.  Examples include #$Muffet and (#$JuvenileFn #$Dog); a
counterexample would be (#$JuvenileFn #$Platypus) because that term is not
currently reified in the KB.  These are often called 'FORTs', which stands for
'first-order reified terms'")
(disjointWith AmateurSportsEvent ProfessionalSportsEvent)
(comment Engine-GM6V53 "The collection of General Motors Model 6V53 six-cylinder water cooled diesel engines.")
(comment AssassinatingSomeone "A specialization of #$Murder.  In each instance of #$AssassinatingSomeone, a person is killed for political reasons, and the murder has political significance.")
(comment ElectronicComponent "A collection of devices; a subset of #$ElectronicDevice.  An #$ElectronicComponent is a device  which is normally considered a part to another device (which in turn is a more meaningful entity, at least in this context.  `More meaningful' might mean that the larger device is sold, moved, named,... as a unit.)   An electronic component needs to be connected with other parts in order to perform its #$primaryFunction.")
(comment Spiraling "#$Movement-Rotation whose distance from a fixed axis is (monotonically) increasing or decreasing.")
(comment StateHealthCareAssistanceOrganization "The collection of all state organizations which provide health care assistance - financial assistance for health care.")
(comment TextualPCWStructure "The collection of all instances of #$CWStructure that are a complete abstract structure of a #$TextualPCW.")
(comment Film-Coating "The collection of all #$LiquidFilm that coat some other object.  Exemplars include wet #$Paint and patchy oil floating on water.")
(comment fileStructureFTPd "(#$fileStructureFTPd ?COPYING ?COPIED) means that the syntactic information structure that is preserved in the #$FTPingAFile process ?COPYING is ?COPIED.")
(comment differentSymbols "This variable-arity predicate (see #$VariableArityRelation), all of whose argument-places are #$quotedArguments (q.v.), is used to make non-identity statements about two or more symbols. Stated loosely, (#$differentSymbols X1 X2 ... Xn) means that each of the Xi is a symbol that is different from all of the others.  Given that the arguments are \"quoted\", however, it is more accurate to say: A ground atomic formula (or \"GAF\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence) consisting of the expression `#$differentSymbols' followed by the CycL expressions E1, ..., En (all enclosed within a pair of parentheses) is true if and only if each Ei is a different expression from all of the others.  Note that two symbols can denote the same thing (in ordinary circumstances) and still be different symbols.  As an example (using English expressions for convenience), the proper name `Bertrand Russell' and the descriptive phrase `the author of \"On Denoting\"' are two different expressions, even though they both denote the same person. Two symbols can even share the same intensional meaning and yet be different symbols; e.g. `bachelor' and `unmarried man'.  The sentence `(#$differentSymbols #$BertrandRussell #$BertrandRussell)', on the other hand, is false.  See also #$equalSymbols and #$different.")
(disjointWith Character-Abstract Issue)
(comment PremierePerformance "The collection of premiere (or opening night) performances of #$EntertainmentPerformance.")
(comment Subway "#$Subway is a specialization of #$Railway.  Each instance of #$Subway is an underground #$Railway under the surface of some city.  Some parts of subways may be in trenches, on bridges or on elevated tracks, but most of a subway is in underground tunnels.")
(comment keGenlsRelevantPreds "This is, by definition, the most general instance of a

certain kind of #$KEFacilitationPredicate.  Its specializations

include #$keGenlsStrongSuggestionPreds, #$keGenlsConsiderationPreds,

#$keGenlsWeakSuggestionPreds and, of course, any

specializations of those predicates.  #$keGenlsRelevantPreds was created

mainly for practical reasons, i.e., to use in situations where one

might want to consider the disjunction of its specializations.  See

the comments on the specializations for clearer explanations.")
(comment unitPossessesVehicleType "(#$unitPossessesVehicleType UNIT V-TYPE) means that the military unit UNIT possesses one or more vehicles of the type of V-TYPE.")
(disjointWith WomensSportsTeam MensSportsTeam)
(comment AntiToxin "drugs used to counteract the effects of toxins.")
(comment ControlStructure-Physical "The collection of all physical control structures.  An instance of #$ControlStructure-Physical is a physical object (#$PartiallyTangible) with the #$behaviorCapable of controling the behavior/functioning/properties of another physical object.  Instances of #$ControlDevice include manufactured #$ControlDevices and biological control structures.")
(comment ISNull "This denotes the value of a datum in an information source when it is empty.  For example, null cells in a relational database.")
(disjointWith ContactLocation State-Geopolitical)
(comment StrategyGameProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerGameProgram in which players must formulate somewhat sophisticated strategies for defeating opponents or overcoming obstacles. This collection has significant overlap with #$RoleplayingGameProgram and #$BoardGameProgram. Instances are game titles such as \"Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time\" or \"Diablo II\".")
(comment TruckTrailer "Typical detached semitrailer for hauling dry freight.")
(comment MakingASalesPhoneCall "Trying to sell something over the telephone.")
(disjointWith MicroscopicScaleObject GeographicalThing)
(comment HepatitisD-Virus "A collection of viri. Instances of #$HepatitisD-Virus are virus of the kind responsible for instances of #$HepatitisD-Infection.")
(comment BigBeautifulWoman "The collection of larger than average #$AdultFemalePersons, especially as an object of sexual attraction.")
(comment WaveReceptionFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction. When applied to an instance WAVETYPE of #$WavePropagationType, #$WaveReceptionFn returns the collection of all events in which an instance of WAVETYPE is received at some location (so the collection in question is a specialization of #$ReceivingAWave).  For example, (#$WaveReceptionFn #$AudibleSound) is the collection of all events in which audible sound waves are received.")
(comment CombatEngineeringVehicle-M728 "A type of combat engineering vehicle which consists of an M60 tank chassis, a hydraulically operated debris blade, a 165mm turret-mounted demolition gun with a 925-meter range, a 7.62mm machine gun, a full-width mine rake capable of clearing mines in in non-cohesive granular soils, a retractable boom and winch.  The CEV performs mobility tasks such as reduction of roadblocks and obstacles; filling craters, ditches, and short dry gaps; limited construction of combat trails; construction of obstacles; and clearing of rubble and debris.")
(comment GenericWordGender "This is the generic (non-specific) word gender whose main
intended use is as a possible argument to #$PronounFn. It can be used in
circumstances in which, for some reason, we don't want to specify the
gender of a pronoun. This attribute should not be confused with
#$Ungendered, which is a specific word gender that pronouns like `they' and
`you' have. Nor should it be confused with #$NeuterWordGender, which is a
specific #$WordGender that only `it' in its various forms has.")
(comment instanceListLength "(#$instanceListLength LIST-TYPE N) states that every list which is an instance of LIST-TYPE will contain N elements.  For example, (#$instanceListLength (#$ListOfLengthFn 2) 2), or (#$instanceListLength (#$ListOfMinimumLengthFn 2) (IntegerExtent 2 #$PlusInfinity))")
(comment Treponema "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalGenus in the
#$MoneraKingdom, these #$ProkaryoticCells are motile and spiral in
shape.  These are strictly anaerobic or microaerophilic.  They are
found in the oral cavity, intestinal tract, and genital areas of
animals.")
(comment MineLayerShip "The collection of ships intended for use in laying undersea mines.")
(comment programImplementsProtocol "(#$programImplementsProtocol PROG PROT) means that, in cases where PROG is used (as client or server) to communicate over a computer network, that communication is conducted according to the #$NetworkProtocol PROT.")
(disjointWith DomesticPet BeastOfBurden)
(comment interArgFormat3-3 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.).
(#$interArgFormat3-3 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.)
requirement for the third argument-place of PRED when PRED's third argument
is an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form 
(PRED ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ... ARGN) in which ARG3 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg3
position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG3' in the preceding
sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances for
further explanation.  Note that #$interArgFormat3-3 is one of several 
\"degenerate-case\" inter-argument format predicates, in which the 
specified condition and the corresponding format constraint both have to do 
with the _same_ argument-place of a given predicate.")
(comment transferRelay-Generic "This predicate can be used to indicate whatever acts as a relay in instances of #$GeneralizedTransfer and plays as well a primarily passive though crucial role.(for a predicate to indicate instances of #$Thing playing an active role see #$transferRouter-Generic).            (#$transferRelay-Generic TRANS THING) means that THING acts as a relay            in the #$GeneralizedTransfer TRANS but primarily in a passive capacity.            For example, suppose a trip TRANS via  airplane taking a person PER from New York to Austin makes a stop in #$CityOfOmahaNE,   where PER changes flights.  If 'CityOfOmahaNEAirport' is the instance of  #$Airport-Physical located in the #$CityOfOmahaNE, then we can say that 'CityOfOmahaNEAirport' is a relay point or node in the #$GeneralizedTransfer TRANS of PER and represent this by (#$transferRelay-Generic TRANS 'CityOfOmahaNEAirport').")
(comment Song-CW "A musical piece, usually with lyrics sung by a human voice.")
(comment exhibitedTypeInMuseum "(#$exhibitedInMuseum MUSEUM ARTIFACT-TYPE) means that some artifacts of the kind ARTIFACT-TYPE are on

exhibit in MUSEUM.")
(comment Neon "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of neon in stuffeous form.")
(comment DrugOverdose "The collection of events which occur when someone takes more of a given type of drug than is medically advisable.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn SeventhRib) Tuberosity) "")
(comment BallisticMissileLauncher "The collection of #$MissileLaunchers designed

  to fire #$BallisticMissiles.")
(comment ClosedClassWord "The collection of all words that are members of closed lexical classes such as #$Prepositions, #$Determiners, etc.")
(disjointWith CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion ProjectileMotion)
(comment EndingAnAgreement "A specialization of #$PurposefulAction and #$SocialOccurrence.  Each instance of #$EndingAnAgreement is an event in which some instance of #$Agreement comes to an end.  For example, #$EmploymentTermination is a specialization of #$EndingAnAgreement.")
(comment Wakeboard "The collection of waterboards. These are somewhat like waterskis, except

they are shorter and wider and one uses only one. They are analogous to

snowboards.")
(comment Efficiency "The ratio of input to useful output in a system or process.")
(comment Password-Strong "#$Password-Strong is a subset of #$Password-Computer.  It includes passwords that           have been created and maintained according to strict security standards.")
(comment Lottery "#$Lottery is a kind of #$Drawing-RandomSelection in which            participants buy numbered tickets to enter and those whose           ticket numbers are selected as winning numbers win prizes.")
(comment SemTransPred "The specialization of #$NLSemanticPredicate whose instances map phrases to #$NLTemplateExpressions.")
(comment EquineVeterinarian "Instances are veterinarians that specialize in the care of horses.")
(comment OldTownFn "(#$OldTownFn CITY) denotes the instance of #$OldTownArea within

CITY. See also #$oldTownOf.")
(comment Charcoal "The collection of all pieces of charcoal")
(disjointWith PartOfAnHSC Facility-Construct)
(comment (ProfessionalFn Wrestler) "The collection of #$Persons who perform wrestling for pay or as an occupation")
(comment CondensateField "The collection of regions which are naturally rich in #$NaturalGas and #$Oil; the pressure of the #$NaturalGas can be used to bring the #$Oil up to the ground.")
(comment FoldingIntoProteinShape "The event in which a chain of amino acids folds into a protein shape, the final subevent of a gene expression event.")
(comment CruiseMissile-Badar2000 "A type of cruise missile developed and produced by Iraq and Egypt.  According to the CSIS source document 'Creeping Proliferation Could Mean a Paradigm Shift

          in the Cost of War and Terrorism', Egypt and Iraq are possession of many of these cruise missiles and may use the missiles as delivery vehicles for weapons of mass destruction.")
(comment ButorphanolTartrate "The chemical compound which is an anti-migraine agent.  This drug is also used to relieve other pain and can be used as a preoperative or preanesthetic medication.")
(comment ConsultingExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes to pay consultants")
(comment ExpeditionaryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "An Expeditionary Unit is a military unit usually deployed initially when terrain that is still dangerous due to enemy presence or not fully tractable by normal units has to be taken and prepared for the main body of the forces. Thus, expeditionary units are usually equipped with tools and vehicles to prepare roads, bridges, and the like.")
(comment MakingATradeAgreement "A collection of events. Each instance of #$MakingATradeAgreement is an event in which two or more parties specify the terms of a #$TradeAgreement to which they will be #$agreeingAgents, and enter into it.")
(comment HealthCertificate "A collection of credentials.  Each element of #$HealthCertificate is the (abstract) declaration, by the appropriate authority, that a particular person (or other animal) is in good health.  Typically a health certificate is embodied in a document issued by the authority.")
(comment MessJacket "The collection of #$Jackets that are worn by military officers in the mess for formal dinners.")
(comment Dinar-Yugoslavia "The currency unit for Yugoslavia.")
(comment RadiometricDating "This is the technique of determining the

age of a sample by measuring the state of radioactive decay of some isotope.

Its accuracy depends upon the assumption that decay proceeds at a constant

rate. The best-known type of radiometic dating is Carbon-14 dating. Other

types are Potassium-Argon, Rubidium-Strontium, and Uranium-Lead dating.")
(comment JutePlant "Individual jute plants; these are grown as crops for the fiber in their stems.")
(comment Howitzer-152mmSelfPropelled "The collection of self-propelled 152mm #$Howitzers.")
(comment Sunrise "A specialization of #$QualitativeTimeOfDay.  Each instance of #$Sunrise is an event during which, at a given location, the #$Sun appears to clear the horizon as it \"rises\".  An instance of #$Sunrise occurs at a given place even if the visibility of the #$Sun is impaired due to obscuring objects such as clouds.  Every instance of #$Sunrise immediately follows (see #$contiguousAfter) some instance of #$Dawn (q.v.), and every instance of #$DaytimeHours (q.v.) is started by (see #$temporallyStartedBy) an instance of #$Sunrise.")
(comment Prestige "This attribute denotes the degree of prestige or standing that one agent has in the eyes of another.")
(comment CardGame "All instances of games played with playing cards")
(comment Organelle "This is the collection of organelles (individuals, not types).  An organelle is a specialized structure or compartment within a eukaryotic cell, which is responsible for carrying out certain isolated functions. 

Organelles include the nucleus, mitochondria, the endoplasmic reticulum, the Golgi apparatus, lysosomes, the cytoskeleton and (in plant cells only)

chloroplasts and vacuoles.")
(comment DownloadSiteFn "#$DownloadSiteFn takes as argument any spec of #$ComputerFile-AIS and returns the collection of sites at which one can download copies of files of that type electronically (see #$DownloadingAFile). For example, (#$DownloadSiteFn SoundFile) would return the collection of all sites from which any sound file can be downloaded.")
(comment SoapOpera "The collection of television shows [#$TVShow-CW] which are normally called ``soap operas''.  Sequential episodes of a #$SoapOpera continue the same #$Narrative.")
(comment HumanMother "The collection of all mothers")
(comment networksPrimaryBroadcastLanguage "This predicates relates a television network to the natural language in which most of its broadcasting is done.")
(comment JewelryBox "A box designed for, or used primarily for, storing jewelry.")
(comment interArg5ResultIsa "A ternary #$MetaRelation predicate for stating that a certain kind of complex, partly #$isa based relationship holds between the fifth argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned. (#$interArg5ResultIsa FUNC INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fifth argument to FUNC, then -- regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be -- the value (if any) of that function for those arguments is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is: if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 INST ...) = VALUE, then VALUE is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike (e.g.) the #$InterArgTypePredicates, #$interArg5ResultIsa _cannot_ be used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on functions.  See also the similar but more flexible quaternary #$interArgResultIsa.")
(comment InelasticColliding "A specialization of #$Colliding. The collection of collisions in which kinetic energy of the colliding system is not conserved. While the total energy of the system must be conserved, the kinetic energy may be converted during the collison into other forms, such as thermal energy. Compare with #$ElasticColliding.")
(comment interArgReln3-2 "A binary #$InterArgRelnPredicate (q.v.).  (#$interArgReln3-2 RELN BINPRED) means that a formula built from RELN (i.e. a \"GAF\" or \"NAT\"; see #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence and  #$CycLClosedNonAtomicTerm) is semantically well-formed only if BINPRED holds between the third and second arguments to RELN (in that order) in the GAF/NAT.  That is, a formula (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ..) is semantically well-formed only if (BINPRED ARG3 ARG2) holds.  For further explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct specializations. See also the more general quaternary predicate #$interArgReln, which has two argument-places for specifying the pair of RELN's arguments that must be related by BINPRED.")
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion Conveyance)
(comment SatelliteTransmission "The collection of events in which a #$SatelliteTransmitter, either
located on a #$Satellite-Device orbiting the Earth or on the ground at a 
#$SatelliteEarthStation, sends #$MicrowaveRadiation signals to a #$SatelliteReceiver,
located either on a #$Satellite-Device or at a #$SatelliteEarthStation.")
(comment FashionShow "The collection of #$EntertainmentPerformances in which #$FashionModels model fashion items")
(comment HempFamily "A #$BiologicalFamily of #$Plants within the #$NettleOrder, with #$taxonMembers including the #$BiologicalGenus #$Cannabis and the #$BiologicalSpecies #$HempPlant.")
(comment negativelyCorrelatedWith "(#$negativelyCorrelatedWith ?SET ?SLOT1 ?SLOT2) means that the values for ?SLOT1 and the values for ?SLOT2 are negatively correlated, when they are applied to elements of ?SET.  In other words, ?SLOT1 is low when ?SLOT2 is high (and vice versa: high when low) for an arbitrary element of ?SET. High and low are with respect to the range of all values of ?SLOT1 respectively ?SLOT2 for elements of ?SET. 

Note that #$negativelyCorrelatedWith and #$positivelyCorrelatedWith don't entail a particular directionality of the causal relationship between ?SLOT1 and ?SLOT2.  It might go either direction, or there may be no direct causal link, with instead values of ?SLOT1 and ?SLOT2 actually being independent but subject to some common causal mechanism.")
(comment PublishingCompany "A collection of organizations; a subset of #$CommercialServiceOrganization.  An element of #$PublishingCompany has as its primary function publishing information (either hardcopy or software, but not solely broadcasting) for particular customers or for the general public.  Note: this collection does not include companies that merely provide manuals as #$includedItems with other products.")
(comment SpeedSkate "The collection of all skates used for speed skating")
(comment TMMScissorBridgeTruck "A type of #$ScissorBridgeTruck.")
(comment TVSeriesProduct "The collection of all TV series considered as #$ConceptualWorks.  Each instance of #$TVSeriesProduct has a (large) number of instances of #$TVShow-SingleCW as #$subWorks.")
(comment pointOfContact-Types "(#$pointOfContact-Types AGENT_TYPE CONTLOC_TYPE BLDG_TYPE) means that instances of AGENT_TYPE ordinarily have some instance of the #$Collection BLDG_TYPE as their #$ContactLocationType CONTLOC_TYPE.")
(comment Manganese "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of manganese; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment typedGenlInverse "A #$MetaPredicate that is a specialization of

#$genlInverse.  #$typedGenlInverse is to #$genlInverse what #$typedGenlPreds 

is to #$genlPreds (qq.v.).  (#$typedGenlInverse PRED TYPED-GENL-INV-PRED) means that TYPED-GENL-INV-PRED is a more general version of the inverse of PRED that allows for more general argument types.  More precisely: (i) TYPED-GENL-INV-PRED

is a generalization of the inverse of PRED (see #$genlInverse); (ii) the 

argument-type constraints (see #$ArgTypePredicate) on PRED are at least as 

narrow as (and in most cases narrower than) the inversely-corresponding constraints on TYPED-GENL-INV-PRED, and (iii) for any pair of things <THING1, THING2> such that (TYPED-GENL-INV-PRED THING2 THING1) holds and where THING1 

and THING2 respectively satisfy the argument-type constraints on the first and second argument-places of PRED, (PRED THING1 THING2) holds.  For example, 

(#$typedGenlInverse #$pathInsideRegion #$spatiallySubsumes) implies that any

path that is spatially subsumed by a given geographical region is a path inside 

that region.")
(comment Permeability "#$Permeability is the capacity for a material to transmit fluids into or completely through its body.  It is measured by the rate  of volume at which a fluid of unit #$Viscosity passes through a unit cross section of the material under a unit #$Pressure gradient.")
(comment Bodybuilding "The collection of activities, including #$LiftingWeights, done with the intention of increasing muscle tone and size.")
(comment orderingRelation "(#$orderingRelations ORDER PRED) means that, in a #$MathematicalOrdering ORDER, there is an order-predicate PRED that forms an ordering relation on the #$baseSet of ORDER.  The predicate PRED, when restricted to the #$baseSet of the #$MathematicalOrdering ORDER, is transitive on the #$baseSet of ORDER.  Note that the predicate #$orderingRelations is not a functional predicate because we may have both (#$orderingRelations ORDER PRED1) and (#$orderingRelations ORDER PRED2).  (This is true even if, extensionally, the two predicates PRED1 and PRED2 denote only one set-theoretic binary relation associated with ORDER.)  Such an ordering relation is not necessarily a full order or even a partial order; it depends on the kind of #$MathematicalOrdering.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent Incorporation-Physical)
(disjointWith Metal SubAtomicParticle)
(comment TillingSoil "The collection of all soil tillings.  This can include turning over as little as one shovel-full of earth.")
(comment naturalHazardsInRegion "(#$naturalHazardsInRegion PLACE HAZARD) means that PLACE is prone to occurrences of HAZARD. HAZARD could be #$Earthquake, flooding, and so on.")
(comment nonSingular-Generic "This predicate is a generalization over the #$SpeechPartPredicates
that do not express singular number: the spec-preds of
#$plural-Generic and #$massNumber-Generic (q.v.).  This predicate
is #$notAssertible, since it will always cash out as an assertion
on a more specialized predicate")
(comment worksInEnvironment "(#$worksInEnvironment PERSON ENVT) says that  PERSON works in a particular instance ENVT of  #$WorkEnvironment.  An example assertion:  (#$relationAllExists #$worksInEnvironment #$Librarian  (#$SubcollectionWithAttributeFn #$WorkEnvironment    (#$VeryLowAmountFn #$NoiseLevelAttribute)))  says that every librarian works in some quiet  work environment.")
(comment (AttemptingFn Deceiving) "#$The collection of instances of #$PurposefulAction which are conducted specifically for the purpose of deceiving some agent. In the case of (#$AttemptingFn #$Deceiving), it is #$not necessary that there is someone who is actually deceived. If you wish to talk about an event in which the attempted deception is successful, then use #$Deceiving.")
(comment TrackingAnObject "This is the collection of events in which the trajectory of a moving object

is somehow kept track of. This would include both the sort of tracking involved

when radar tracks the course of an aircraft and the sort of tracking involved

when the path of a person or animal is discerned and followed.")
(comment CharacterStringMode-Inscribed "A specialization of #$CharacterStringMode each 
  instance of which is the collection of all of the inscribed 
  tokens of some particular abstract character-string.  Examples
  include the collection of all inscribed tokens (see
  #$CharacterStringToken-Inscribed) of the string 'hello'.")
(comment Morphine "a white, bitter, #$Crystalline #$Alkaloid, the most important narcotic and addictive constituent of #$Opium, obtained by extraction and crystallization and used chiefly in medicine as a pain reliever and sedative.")
(disjointWith ImpureCompound PureSubstance)
(comment ChildrensMagazineSeries "The collection of all #$MagazineSeries which are intended primarly for children.  Examples of instances of this collection are 'National Geographic World' and 'KidCity'.")
(comment eventOfPlan "(#$eventOfPlan EVENT PLANMT) means that EVENT is a
hypothetical #$Event referenced in the description of a plan that is
represented in the #$Plan microtheory PLANMT.  Ordinarily, such an
assertion will be made within PLANMT itself, and every event in the
plan that figures as a 'planned' event will have such an assertion
made of it.  The reason for having this predicate is twofold.  First,
we may wish to have dependent on PLANMT (via a #$genlMt link) a
microtheory that describes the 'real world'--e.g., a description of an
attempted execution of the plan.  In that microtheory, we will wish to
distinguish between events that occur in reality from 'hypothetical'
events that are part of the planning context: because the
#$eventOfPlan assertions will inherit to the dependent mt, we will
have a ready means of doing this.  Second, we will want to distinguish
within the planning context itself between 'hypothetical' events in
the plan and real-world events which hypothetical events in the plan
may be contingent on.  It may, in other words, be necessary at times
to give planning contexts access to non-hypothetical events are
mentioned.  Again, the #$eventOfPlan assertions will give us a ready
means for distinguishing, within the hypothetical mt, between events
which are considered to be hypothetical and events which are not.")
(comment Pioneer "The collection of all #$Persons involved in pioneering.  A #$Pioneer could be a #$Person who breaks new ground in a field (as #$StevenJobs) as well as the classical definition of a settler of the American West.")
(comment TrackedVehicle "A collection of #$LandTransportationDevices.  Each instance of #$TrackedVehicle used caterpillar-like tracks (see #$VehicleTrack-Device) instead of, or in addition to, wheels for propulsion.  Specializations include #$Tank-Vehicle and #$Bulldozer.")
(comment Fuse-IgnitionDevice-Time "The collection of #$Fuse-IgnitionDevices that ignite an explosion  after a set time duration, either by using a clock or by combustion.")
(disjointWith ElectricalResistance Voltage)
(comment hasCorrespondence "(#$hasCorrespondence MAP CORR) means that some analogy correspondence, CORR, is one of the #$AnalogyCorrespondences that comprise the #$AnalogyMapping, MAP.  CORR can be part of multiple #$AnalogyMappings.")
(comment SmoothBoreWeapon "The collection of #$ProjectileLaunchers that have #$Bores with smooth surfaces.")
(disjointWith TVFamilyShow PornographicMaterial)
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion GaseousTangibleThing)
(comment Avatar-ComputerImage "The collection of #$VisualImages that represent computer users on a network. Avatars are commonly used in #$ChatRooms or Internet-based interactive games to give computer users a more realistic experience of interacting with other users.")
(comment Pain-PhysiologicalCondition "A collection of the #$PhysiologicalConditions in which the #$bodilyDoer experiences physical pain.")
(comment BreakingEvent "Generic breaking events, in which some rigid tangible object gets broken.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-WhClauseFrame "This frame is used for words that take exactly two complements,

          the first of which is an NP and the second a wh-clause.

          In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP, S[wh-comp]>] Example: 'I asked them whether this car was new'.")
(disjointWith (TransportViaFn Spacecraft) (TransportViaFn WaterTransportationDevice))
(comment TransportAircraft "The collection of military aircraft typically used for transporting people, not equipment.")
(comment PlanetarySystem "A group of celestial bodies moving in orbit around a central star or stars.")
(comment VentureCapitalFirm "the collection of all companies whose primary business is providing venture capital to new companies")
(comment PirbuterolAcetate "The chemical compound which is a bronchodilator.")
(comment tourDayEventType "(#$tourDayEventType TOUR DAY EVENTTYPE) means that according
to the itinerary of TOUR, an event of type EVENTTYPE is supposed to
take place on the day DAY.")
(comment ductilityOfObject "(#$ductilityOfObject OBJ DEGREE) means that the instance of #$SolidTangibleThing OBJ has this DEGREE of #$Ductility (q.v.).")
(comment budgetExpenditureFractionOfGDP "(#$budgetExpenditureFractionOfGDP GE COL THING NR) means that NR is the quotient of the amount of money spent by the #$GeopoliticalEntity GE on instances of the specialization of #$SpatialThing-Localized COL during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING (as dividend) and the monetary value of GE's total domestic production of goods and services (its gross domestic product) during the temporal extent of THING (as divisor).  A country would be a typical instance of GE.  COL might be any type of thing on or for which budget expenditures are made; for example, goods, services, institutions (such as government agencies or military organizations), or debt service.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  For example, to express the fact that Oman's 1996 expenditure on the military was 13.7% of its gross domestic product for that year, we can say (#$budgetExpenditureFractionOfGDP #$Oman #$GovernmentMilitaryOrganization (#$YearFn 1996) (#$Percent 13.7)).  See also #$budgetExpenditures and #$grossDomesticProduct.")
(comment F-TheLetter "The letter F of the alphabet.  This is 'F' (or 'f') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterF and #$LatinSmallLetterF.")
(comment NavalAttache "A collection of persons; a subset of #$Attache.  Each element of #$NavalAttache is a person who is officially appointed as a representative of a country's government and navy in dealing with another government or navy.  For example, the collection #$NavalAttache includes the U.S. navy attaches in #$Japan, #$Russia, #$China-PeoplesRepublic, and other countries.  Naval attaches usually work with higher officials appointed by their country.")
(comment Androecium "The male component of a flower which is made up of several stamens, and usually surrounds the gynoecium.")
(comment ProducingMusicalSound "The collection of events in which musical sounds are generated (c.f. #$Music).  This collection includes both the production of music by agents (see #$MakingMusicalSound) and the production of music by automated means, as in the playback of a musical #$RecordedSoundProduct.")
(comment weaponEffectiveRange-Min "(#$weaponEffectiveRange-Min WEAPON RANGE) means that RANGE
is the minimum range at which the projectile weapon WEAPON is
considered to be 'effective', ie, capable of doing significant damage
to a target.  Some projectile weapons have specifiable minimum ranges,
while others do not.  It is a particularly useful concept with respect
to certain kinds of #$IndirectFireWeapon which cannot be fired higher
than a certain angle, and which therefore cannot fall inside a certain
circumference.")
(comment filtersPacketType "A predicate relating instances of #$Firewall-Network with
instances of #$Computer in the firewall's network. (#$filtersPacketType
FIREWALL PACKTYPE COMPUTER) means that FIREWALL drops all packets of
type PACKTYPE coming from outside the network bound for COMPUTER.")
(disjointWith FixedWingAircraft RotaryWingAircraft)
(comment IBTTranslating "A collection of events; a subset of #$IBTGeneration-Replication.  Each element of #$IBTTranslating is an event which generates a new IBT (i.e., an element of #$InformationBearingThing) by copying the information from a source IBT (see #$informationOrigin) into a representation using a different #$Language.  The new IBT encodes approximately the same information as the source IBT.  This concept does not include changing the #$WritingSystem (which would be transliterating) of text, nor of converting #$DatabaseDataFormats, musical notation [#$MusicalNotation-General], or other syntactic properties of non-textual language.")
(comment FixedAritySkolemFuncN "The collection of #$SkolemFuncNs (q.v.) whose arity is fixed.")
(comment Magnet "An object that possesses the property of attracting certain substances, especially iron.")
(comment DietaryDeficiencyCondition "The collection of physiological conditions brought on by consuming less of a nutrient than the body requires.")
(comment DestructionEvent "A collection of events and a specialization of #$CreationOrDestructionEvent.  In each instance of this collection at least one instance of #$SomethingExisting (the #$inputsDestroyed) ceases to exist. Examples include deleting a computer file, chopping down a tree and breaking an agreement. For cases where the item destroyed is a material thing (i.e. an instance of #$PartiallyTangible), see the more specialized #$PhysicalDestructionEvent.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperationTypeByPurpose "#$AttackByComputerOperationTypeByPurpose is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperationType.  Every instance of  this collection is a subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation whose instances are attacks that share intended consequences.  Examples include #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService

and #$AttackByComputerOperation-CorruptionOfInformation.")
(comment Murderer "The collection of all #$Criminals who have committed a #$Murder.  This does not include people who killed in self-defense, etc.  Also, a #$Murderer need not have been convicted to qualify for membership in this collection.")
(comment HistoricalNarrativeMovie "#$HistoricalNarrativeMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which dramatize a narrative taken from a #$HistoricalNarrative. Usually, the #$Screenplay departs from a completely factual narration in order to heighten the drama and audience interest. An example is #$Amistad-TheMovie.")
(comment DomesticAgricultureGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with promoting agricultural production in a country.")
(comment AddressBook "The collection of documents in which an agent records the names and contact information of agents they wish to keep in touch with.")
(comment BindingEvent "A collection of events. In each #$BindingEvent event, several loose sheets (of paper or other material) are combined into an ordered whole, which could be a book, a catalogue, or any kind of multipage document.")
(comment SurfaceToSurfaceMissileUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on missiles           that are fired from a ground-based weapons platform at a target           that is also on the ground.")
(comment objectAttached "(#$objectAttached ATTACHING OBJ) means that OBJ is the thing attached to something else in ATTACHING.  Often it is useful to think of actors in #$AttachmentEvents as \"attached\" and \"attachees\", i.e., the thing attached versus the thing to which something is attached.  For instance, if I attach a rearview mirror to my windshield, the rearview mirror seems to be the item attached while the windshield is the \"attachee\".   We use the predicate #$objectAttached to relate an attachment event to the \"thing attached\" in an attachment event.

When a much smaller object gets stuck to a larger object, the smaller object is usally deemed play the role #$objectAttached.  For instance, if a person becomes attached to a burr, the burr plays the role #$objectAttached and the person plays the role #$objectAdheredTo in the attachment event.  If two burrs become attached to each other they both play the role #$objectOfAttachment and there is no designated \"attached\" and \"attachee\".  Note that as a default rule (#$objectAttached ATTACHING SMALL) relates an attaching event to the smaller of the relevant actors in the ATTACHING, but there may be counterexamples.  For instance, a trailer may be larger than the car by which it is towed and yet be deemed to play the role #$objectAttached in the event in which the car is connected to the trailer.")
(comment LinguisticAnalysis-Morphological "A collection of microtheories.  Each element of #$LinguisticAnalysis-Morphological is a microtheory representing knowledge, theory, hypotheses, evidence, and problems related to the morphological analysis of a data set taken from a language or group of languages.")
(comment Samarium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of samarium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment RockyPlanetaryBody "A collection of heavenly bodies.  Each element of #$RockyPlanetaryBody is a planetary body composed primarily of rocky substances.")
(disjointWith ComputerProcess-MultiComputer ComputerProcess-SingleComputer)
(comment PrecipitationProcess "A specialization of #$ImmediateWeatherProcess, #$FallingEvent, and #$EmittingStuff.  Each instance of #$PrecipitationProcess is a  meteorological process in which atmospheric clouds precipitate rain, snow, or some other form of precipitation.")
(comment orthography "(#$orthography LANG WRIT) means that the #$WritingSystem WRIT is the usual mode of writing used to encode the #$Language LANG; that is, WRIT is used by most of the people who customarily engage in writing LANG. For instance, (#$orthography #$RajasthaniLanguage #$DevanagariWriting).")
(comment keStrongConsideration "(#$keStrongConsideration TERM FORMULA) means that FORMULA could be salient to TERM and, if salient, it is strongly expected that the information expressed in FORMULA be asserted about TERM.  Note that the meaning of this predicate is not simply that the suggestion be strongly considered.  Rather, it is that if the ke suggestion is salient it is strongly suggested that the appropriate information be asserted in the KB.  An example may help to clarify the distinction between #$kePlausibleConsideration and #$keStrongConsideration, a specialization.  Note that if one creates a collection it is useful to consider whether there are facetings of the collection.  However, we wouldn't make this a \"strong consideration\" insofar as some facets are worth articulating in the KB but many other ad-hoc facets are not worth asserting in the KB.")
(comment antisymTestPred "Prototypical instance of #$AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate, to
be used for testing purposes.")
(comment Rash-Object "A collection of both #$Injury-Objects and #$PhysiologicalFeatureOfSurfaces. Each instance is a group of abnormal red bumps on the skin. The rash may be localized or cover the entire surface of the body. The bumps may be quite tiny and far apart or be so close together as to form large welts or hives. The #$Rash-Object may be the result of an #$Infection or an allergic reaction.")
(comment NonDavidsonianSentence "The collection of #$ELSentence-Assertible that are governed by an

#$NonDavidsonianPredicate, hence can be used to express tensed clauses. At

present an instance of this collection is either (i) an atomic #$ELSentence-Assertible

of the form (#$eventPred TYPE LIST1 LIST2) or (ii) is of the form (CONN

P1...PN) where CONN is a #$LogicalConnective and P1, P2 are

#$NonDavidsonianSentences, or (iii) is of the form (#$aspectProgressive F)

or (#$aspectPerfect F), where F is an instance of #$ELSentence-Assertible (not

necessarily an #$NonDavidsonianSentence).")
(comment currentLevel "The level of current in the flow of electricity.")
(comment prefersToMinimize "(#$prefersToMinimize AGENT THING SLOT)

means that AGENT prefers (see also #$prefers) smaller values of SLOT

(its second argument) when applied to THING (as the first argument of

SLOT). In a sense it means that AGENT will prefer situations whereby

SLOT of THING becomes smaller, or stays the same, over situations

whereby SLOT of THING becomes greater.  It need not imply that the

agent will directly pursue such minimization (in order to imply direct

pursuit, see #$goals)")
(comment stringSubword "(#$stringSubword SUBWORD STRING) means that SUBWORD is a subword of

STRING. That is, SUBWORD is a #$substring of STRING surrounded by whitespace.")
(comment intangibleAssetOf "The predicate that relates some #$PartiallyIntangible thing (either a #$Collection or an #$Individual) to the #$Organization or #$Person of whom it is an intangible economic resource.  For example a brand name might be an #$intangibleAssetOf some #$CommercialOrganization, or an #$Event (such as a publicity event) might be an #$intangibleAssetOf some #$EducationalOrganization.")
(comment Warhead "A collection of devices, a subset of #$Weapon.  A warhead is a weapon carried in the nose cone of a missile.  Usually some kind of explosive package is involved, but the weapon may also be biological or chemical in nature.")
(comment MailServer-Network "A specialization of #$Computer.  Each instance of #$MailServer-Network is a computer that functions as a mail server for some instance of #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment AreaStudies "This is the collection of fields of study, now offered by

most colleges and universities, which deal with the culture, politics, and history of

a particular region of the world. Examples include Asian Studies, Latin American Studies, and so on.")
(comment InVitroAdministration "Administering a drug to a cell, tissue or organ which is in a test tube or glass container.")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn TenthRib) HeadOfBone) "")
(comment TypeOfServiceField-Packet "A #$TypeOfServiceField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet
that indicates the kind of service that the source computer wants for the
#$Packet-Internet. The first three bits of the field represent precdence
[0-7]. If a #$Packet-Internet's precedence is high, it should be processed
immediately. If it is low, it can be put in a queue for processing.
The next three bits are flags representing Delay, Throughput, and
Reliability. One of the flags can be chosen to indicate what service
is most important for the #$Packet-Internet. The last two bits are unused.")
(comment GeographicalDirection-General "A specialization of #$GeographicalDirection whose instances are general, as opposed to precise or \"direct\", directions.  More exactly: with respect to a specified reference point, a given general direction (e.g. #$North-Generally) is an instance of #$VectorInterval that comprises the wedge-shaped set of vectors that point within 22.5 degrees in either horizontal direction of the corresponding \"direct\" direction (viz. #$North-Directly).  The vertical direction of these vectors is in effect ignored, and can be anything strictly between 0 degrees (\"straight up\") and 180 degrees (\"straight down\").  Thus the \"wedge\" itself has a 45 degree interior horizontal angle, and none of the eight reified general directions \"overlap\".  Compare #$GeographicalDirection-Direct.")
(comment NationalRedCrossSocietyFn "(NationalRedCrossSocietyFn ?COUNTRY) denotes ?COUNTRY's national Red Cross or Red Crescent organization. (NationalRedCrossSocietyFn ?COUNTRY) will be a member of the InternationalFederationOfRedCrossAndRedCrescentSocieties.")
(comment reportTime "(#$reportTime REPORT DATE) means that DATE is the time at which REPORT was submitted by its author.")
(comment HumanResidenceArea "A specialization of #$GeographicalRegion.  Each instance of #$HumanResidenceArea is a region in which a number of people live semi-permanently (that is, for a duration of at least a year or more).  Examples include #$SanFranciscoBayArea, #$ResearchTrianglePark, research stations at the #$SouthPole, and radar posts in the Aleutians.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementActivity AcademicTesting)
(comment Amygdala "The collection of all amygdalae.  An individual #$Amygdala (or 'amygdaloid body/complex/nucleus') is a #$BasalNucleus which is a unique part of a #$TemporalLobe as well as part of the #$LimbicSystem.  An #$Amygdala is involved in the emotions of rage, aggression, and fear.")
(comment Outpatient "The collection of all #$MedicalPatients who leave after being the recipient of a #$MedicalCareEvent without spending a night in a #$MedicalCareInstitution.")
(comment MilitaryFieldManual-PIT "Each instance is a partial representation of the
propositional content of a particular edition of a military field
manual.")
(comment SubcollectionFunction "A collection of functions.  Instances of #$SubcollectionFunction are functions which take a collection as their first argument and restrictions of that function as second and possibly third argument. Examples of instances of #$SubcollectionFunction include #$SubcollectionByRegionFn and #$SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn.")
(comment Helicopter-AH64 "The #$Helicopter-AH64 Apache is the Army's primary attack helicopter. It is a quick-reacting, airborne weapon system that can fight close and deep to destroy, disrupt, or delay enemy forces. The Apache is designed to fight and survive during the day, night, and in adverse weather throughout the world. The principal mission of the Apache is the destruction of high-value targets with the HELLFIRE missile. It is also capable of employing a 30MM M230 chain gun and Hydra 70 (2.75 inch) rockets that are lethal against a wide variety of targets. The Apache has a full range of aircraft survivability equipment and has the ability to withstand hits from rounds up to 23MM in critical areas.")
(comment ReligiousEvent "A collection of human activities.  Each instance of #$ReligiousEvent is an occurrence which has religious significance.")
(comment Battery "Batteries: providers of DC electricity from chemical reactions")
(comment Flipping "Tossing with a sharp movement so as to cause to turn in the air #$PerpendicularTo the direction of motion")
(comment USStateGovernmentOrganization "A collection of government organizations.  An element of #$USStateGovernmentOrganization is an organization that is part of the state government of a particular state of the United States; e.g., PennDOT (the Pennsylvania Department of Transportation) or the Texas Employment Commission.")
(comment IBTGeneration-Original "A specialization of #$IBTGeneration.  Each instance of #$IBTGeneration-Original is an event in which some instance of #$InformationBearingThing (hereafter IBT) is generated, where the content of the IBT generated is not a copy of the content of any previously created IBT.")
(disjointWith Algorithm Issue)
(comment keStrongSuggestionInverse "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and specialization of #$keRelevantInverse that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keStrongSuggestionInverse COL BINPRED) means that for every known (i.e. Cyc-reified) instance INST of COL, it is strongly suggested that there be some reified THING such that (BINPRED THING INST) is known in the Knowledge Base.  See also #$keWeakSuggestionInverse and #$keStrongSuggestionPreds.")
(comment holdsInTime-Sometime "(#$holdsInTime-Sometime MT TIME) means that the assertions in the #$Microtheory MT are true sometime during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing TIME.  See also #$holdsInTime-Always.")
(comment GameWalkthrough-Instructions "The collection of all complete instructions for beating a computer
          game.  Walkthroughs are generally only possible for games which
          involve puzzles, like adventure games, RPGs, and puzzle games
          and therefore a set of detailed step-by-step instructions is
          appropriate.  Note that walkthroughs are more comprehensive and
          detailed than hints.  Walkthroughs are also not 'cheating': in
          computer game parlance, 'cheats' are features in a game that 
          override the standard rules of the game and are (almost always)
          hard to find and not documented in game manuals.  Walkthroughs
          do not generally make use of these cheats.")
(comment Conveyance "A collection of solid tangible objects each instance of which
is used for moving partially tangible things.  A #$Conveyance 
could be a car, ship, plane, or other vehicle for transporting 
people; it could be a conveyor belt or a grocery bag for moving 
goods; it could be a gun, a bow, or a cannon for launching 
projectiles.  Notable specializations include #$TransportationDevice,
whose instances actually move along with the things they transport, 
and #$Conveyance-Stationary, whose instances remain stationary 
while moving other things.  Note that not all conveyances are 
artifacts, as (e.g.) horses and rivers can be used to convey
things.  See #$Conveying-Generic, #$TransportationEvent, and 
#$Conveying-Stationary for the different kinds of conveying 
events.")
(comment keRelevant "This is, by definition, the most general instance of #$KEFacilitationPredicate.  It is intended as a generalization for #$keStrongSuggestion, #$keWeakSuggestion, #$keNeighborSuggestion, #$keStrongConsideration and #$kePlausibleConsideration or any other such predicates which may be suggested.  This predicate, along with #$keRelevantPreds, #$keRelevantInverse, #$keGenlsRelevantPreds, #$keGenlsRelevantInverse are designed to facilitate the implementation of rapid knowledge formation tools implementing #$KEFacilitationPredicates. One should almost always use one of its specializations.")
(comment WomensSportsTeam "the collection of all #$SportsTeams whose members are either human female teenagers (e.g., many Olympic gymnastics teams), adult human females (e.g., many Olympic soccer teams), or some mixture of both (e.g., many Olympic tennis and swim teams).  This  collection allows one to reify types of sports teams on the fly; e.g., (#$CollectionIntersection2Fn #$BasketballTeam #$WomensSportsTeam) is the collection of all women's basketball teams.")
(comment DietMedication "The collection of drugs used to aid in weight loss and in maintenance of lower body weight. These drugs may act as stimulants, or may have other modes of action, such as interfering with fat absorption.")
(comment InterposedCovering "The collection of coverings which cover an object by virtue of being interposed between the object and its environment")
(comment nullCellValue "(#$nullCellValue ?PT ?KEYOBJ ?LF) states that in the #$PhysicalDBTable ?PT, on the row identified by ?KEYOBJ, the field corresponding to the #$LogicalField ?LF is empty.")
(comment ChildSexualAbuse "The collection of #$SexualAbuses in which the victim of the abuse is an instance of #$HumanChild. #$ChildSexualAbuse is not limited to acts involving direct and invasive physical contact, but also includes inappropriate touching, #$IndecentExposure, procuring sexual activity for a child, showing #$PornographicMaterial to children, etc.")
(comment Enclave "The physical and functional sides of an Enclave -- a small geographic region which is controlled almost completely by a foreign power")
(comment combineDags "(#$combineDags ?Combined ?Schema ?Dag1 ... ?Dagn) creates a new dag by substituting into ?Schema the parts ?Dag1 .. ?Dagn at positions indicated in ?Schema by the integers 1 .. n. The new Dag is bound to the variable ?Combined.")
(comment WeatherBalloon "The collection of meteorological tools consisting of gas-filled #$Balloons connected to small boxes of #$Sensors called #$Radiosondes. These balloons are released and float to the upper atmosphere, where they record temperature, pressure, wind speed, and humidity. The balloon breaks, and the radiosonde falls back to earth, supported by a parachute.")
(comment Ribonucleotide "The collection of all RNA nucleotides.  Instances of this

collection are compounds consisting of #$Ribose, a phosphate group,

and a nitrogeneous base, either #$Adenine-Base, #$Uracil-Base,

#$Cytosine-Base, or #$Guanine-Base.  These compounds form the repeating

subunits of RNA.")
(disjointWith EdibleStuff GeographicalThing)
(comment HepatitisE-Virus "A collection of viri. Instances of #$HepatitisE-Virus are virus
of the kind responsible for instances of #$HepatitisE-Infection.")
(comment CosmeticTreatmentEvent "The collections of #$ProfessionalServicing events in which a #$Person is acted upon so that his/her #$PhysicalAttractiveness could be enhanced.")
(disjointWith Translation-Periodic Meteor)
(comment Ungendered "This is the #$WordGenderAttribute that `they' and `I', for example,
have. This is a specific word gender and is not to be confused with the
generic, non-specific word gender #$GenericWordGender. The latter is 
to be used when one wishes to avoid specifying a word gender. This should
also not be confused with #$NeuterWordGender, another specific word gender,
which `it' in its various forms has.")
(comment AFewDaysDuration "Duration of 2 to 10 days")
(comment RemoteMaintenancePortProgram "A remote maintenance port is a program on a device such as a router or a firewall  that permits remote users to log in and do maintenance, such as altering settings.")
(comment TreponemaPallidum "A collection of #$Bacterium that comprise a
#$BiologicalSpecies in the #$MoneraKingdom which cause the
#$SexuallyTransmittedInfection #$Syphilis.  They are probably
microaerophilic.")
(comment Minesweeper-Coastal "The collection of minesweepers designed to operate in coastal areas.")
(comment SignTheDisplay "A specialization of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject. Each instance of #$SignTheDisplay is a physical object typically placed where #$Persons can see it so that they can obtain (generally propositional) information from it. Signs are typically used to identify objects (e.g., street signs, name tags, species labels at zoos), to advertise goods (e.g., billboards, neon signs, posters for garage sales), and to warn of hazards (e.g., signs for road hazards or road construction, printed tape marking off a police line). #$SignTheDisplay differs from #$SymbolicObject in displaying specific information rather than symbolizing another thing, though the two collections are obviously not disjoint. See also #$signifiesTo, #$signifies.")
(comment TaxForm-CW "Forms which are meant to be filled out and returned to a a tax agency such as the IRS.")
(comment Magnesium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of magnesium.")
(comment NasalCongestion "The physiological condition of having a stuffed up nose.")
(comment WildernessPark "Parks which are mostly wild area, intended for wildlife preservation, camping, hiking, and sightseeing")
(comment (PartTypeFn (LeftObjectOfPairFn SixthRib) Tuberosity) "")
(disjointWith PrepaymentWithoutPenaltyOption PrepaymentPenalty)
(comment agentStaysViableAfterDeployment-BCW "(#$agentStaysViableAfterDeployment-BCW AGENTTYPE DURATION) means

that, other things being equal, an instance of the

#$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance type AGENTTYPE will retain the capacity to

harm living organisms for a period of DURATION following its

'deployment' in a #$DeployingAChemicalOrBiologicalAgent event")
(disjointWith EndingAnAgreement SeparationEvent)
(comment KickBoard "The collection of kickboards. These generally made

of styrofoam and their purpose is to keep one's torso afloat so that

one can move through the water just by kicking one's legs.")
(comment GroundBasedReconnaissanceUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units dedicated to carrying out           reconnaissance missions using ground-based transports and           platforms.")
(comment PrionDisease "This is the collection of all transmissible and genetic
neurodegenerative diseases of humans and animals caused by #$Prions. The
diseases are usually characterised by vacuolation in the gray matter and
result in ataxia, motor disturbances, #$Dementia, and progression to a fatal
outcome. They include Creutzfeldt-Jakob
syndrome, Gerstmann-Straussler syndrome, kuru, scrapie, fatal familial
insomnia, bovine spongiform encephalopathy, transmissible mink
encephalopathy, and chronic wasting disease of mule deer and elk. The
literature has sometimes referred to these as unconventional slow virus
diseases.")
(comment CycLAtomicAssertion "A specialization of #$CycLAtomicSentence.  An instance ATOM of #$CycLAtomicSentence is also an instance of #$CycLAtomicAssertion just in case ATOM has been explicitly asserted to the Cyc Knowledge Base (see #$CycLAssertedAssertion), or deduced in the Knowledge Base by the Cyc inference engine (see #$CycLDeducedAssertion).")
(disjointWith Password-Strong Password-Weak)
(comment Drawing-RandomSelection "An element of #$Drawing-RandomSelection  is an event in which some agent randomly selects an agent from a pool of agents. A #$Lottery is an example.  ''Drawing lots`` to see who has to endure the hardship of taking out the garbage tonight is another example.")
(comment TravelReservation "The class of #$Reservations which involve an agreement between a person and a business that travel services of a particular nature will be provided to the person at a future time and place.  Such travel services include transportation and lodging.")
(comment TableOfContents "Each element of #$TableOfContents is a #$TextString detailing the contents of some  #$ConceptualWork, usually a #$Book-CW or #$PeriodicalIssue. Each item on the list has two parts: the name of a section or chapter, and the number of the page on which that section or chapter begins. The sections or chapters are listed in order of page number. A instantiation of a #$TableOfContents generally appears near the beginning of the #$BookCopy or #$PeriodicalCopy whose contents it lists.")
(comment FelineVeterinarian "Instances are veterinarians that specialize in the care of cats.")
(comment EntireSurfaceLayer "This is the collection of surface layers which entirely cover an  object, e.g., the human skin of one person, or the peel of an orange.")
(comment MechanicalEnergy "The collection of instances of mechanical energy - the energy of things in motion <considered as a stuff>.")
(disjointWith Facility-Construct MemorialMarker)
(comment LeapYear "The collection of #$CalendarYears which are leap years; in the Julian & Gregorian calendar systems these are calendar years in which February has 29 days")
(comment (FemaleFn Wrestler) "The collection of women wrestlers.")
(comment Event-Organized "A collection of individual events.  An event is an instance of #$Event-Organized if it is planned and directed by some instance of #$Person or #$Organization.  Elements of #$MusicalPerformance, #$Trial, and #$Bombing would all be instances.  Elements of #$Earthquake and #$Breathing would not.")
(comment Depressant "Drugs which diminish a body's ability to perform its functions or activities.")
(comment TravelExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes for paying travel expenses.")
(comment tourTransportTypes "(#$tourTransportTypes TOUR TRANSTYPE) means that travel of
the type TRANSTYPE is employed on at least one 'subleg' of the tour.")
(comment ArmoredVehicle-Light "The class of vehicles that have enough armor to protect against bullets but are not comparable to a tank or something heavliy protected.")
(comment AmateurActivity "An attribute used to describe the relatively unskilled work (as in artwork), actions, performances, productions, etc, of non-professionals.  To indicate the professional status of a person, use #$AmateurFn and #$ProfessionalFn.")
(comment MacroeconomicEvent "The collection of events that are macroeconomic in nature, such as inflation, economic recessions, stock market behavior, and increases or decreases in production, trade, or employment.  Also included are decisions and policy-setting that affect macroeconomic trends.  Note, however, that most instances of #$MacroeconomicEvent are not actions by individuals but rather are of an aggregative character.")
(comment BuildingPermit-PIT "A collection of credentials; a type of #$Permission.  Each element of #$BuildingPermit-PIT is an authorization for an agent to build some particular structure as specified in the permit.  A building permit is issued typically by the local government authority over the region wherein the building is to be built, and the permit information is embodied in a physical document, a copy of which typically must be displayed at the building site.")
(comment outputCodeTransducer-FunctionalRole "(#$outputCodeTransducer-FunctionalRole SYSTEM AGENT) means

that AGENT is expected to take instances of #$InformationBearingObject

that originate within SYSTEM and change their encoding to a form

suitable for dissemination outside SYSTEM.")
(comment Dollar-Fiji "Major unvt of currency of Fiji")
(comment supplyFromThroughAmountDuring "(#$supplyFromThroughAmountDuring PT1 COL PT2 PT3 THING AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$Collection COL with which the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT1 is supplied from the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT2 through the instance of #$PartiallyTangible PT3 (on their way from PT2) during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  Like the predicate #$suppliedWith (q.v.), #$supplyFromThroughAmountDuring is very general.  In various assertions PT1 might, for instance, be a #$Cell, a #$Person, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion; and likewise for PT2.  And PT3 might, for example, be a #$Hose, a #$Railway, a #$GeographicalRegion, or a #$BloodVessel.  The range of possible supplies is similarly broad.  THING will often be a calendar time period; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of supply of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE to PT1 from PT2 through PT3 during the temporal extent of THING.")
(disjointWith Atom Molecule)
(comment BuyingBiologicalLivingObject "A subset of #$BuyingAnObject. In each instance of #$BuyingBiologicalLivingObject, an organism or part of an organism is purchased by an agent. Examples include people buying pets, zoos buying wild animals, people buying plants from a greenhouse, and so on. An example in which the purchased objects are proper parts of organisms is that of a gardener buying seeds. An event in which a dead organism or part of a dead organism is bought would not be included in this collection.")
(comment PeaPlant "Individual pea plants.")
(comment Howitzer-155mmSelfPropelled "The collection of self-propelled 155mm #$Howitzers.")
(comment XZCrossSectionFn "This function maps three-dimensional objects to the arbitrarily thin slice of the object that defines an xz-cross section of the object as determined by the object's intrinsic axes.  See also #$xzCrossSection and #$IntrinsicAxisOfObjects.")
(comment FoodChain "A collection of Groups of PartiallyTangible things.  Each instance of #$FoodChain is a group of PartiallyTangible things such that each member of the group is an instance of a food source type for some other member, and a connection between any two members can be made by tracing through some number of #$isa and #$foodSourceFor relationships.")
(comment NuclearBody "The part of a cell which contains the genetic material.  This includes the nucleus of eukaryotic cells and the nucleoid of prokaryotic cells.")
(comment MeatMixture "The collection of all mixtures which include #$Meat as the            main component.")
(comment Queen-HeadOfState "The queen of a country which is usually a monarchy and always a kingdom")
(comment TVTalkShow "A collection of television shows [#$TVShow-CW], ones normally refered to as talk shows, e.g. 'Oprah' [#$TheOprahWinfreyShow-TheTVShow].")
(comment PileFn "A unary function from types of #$PartiallyTangibles to collections of #$Piles of things of those types. (#$PileFn TYPE) denotes the 

collection of all piles consisting (exclusively or almost exclusively) of

things of TYPE.  Note that, although not all piles are arrangements of like objects (see #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects), any pile in a collection returned by this function is such an arrangement.")
(comment GeneticallyEngineeredBacterium "The collection of all instances of #$Bacterium

   that have been genetically altered.")
(comment Catatonia "A psychological ailment during which the affected person does not move his or her body.")
(comment SegmentOfLung "The collection of segments of #$Lungs (segmenta bronchopnumonalia), each being a sub-part of a lobe of a lung, separated from other segments by membranes (septa), and served by one #$SegmentalBronchus.")
(comment externalTermStrings "(#$externalTermStrings TERM STRING) states that some external system considers TERM as a possible interpretation for the string STRING.")
(comment Contortionist "The collection of #$StagePerformers that twist their bodies into position hard or impossible to reproduce for people who did not receive a specific training. #$Contortionists often perform in a #$Circus.")
(disjointWith Wall-GenericBarrier SubwayStation)
(comment meansOfDeployingAgent-BCW "(#$meansOfDeployingAgent-BCW AGENTTYPE MEANSTYPE) means that, other things being equal, a given person can perform instances of MEANSTYPE in which the #$transferredThing is a (#$MobFn AGENTTYPE) with a high degree of #$Effectiveness.")
(comment Delta "alluvial deposit at mouth of river, usually threaded by multiple channels")
(comment Owl-Barn "A collection of very common Owls found nearly worldwide. Their scientific name is Tyto albq.")
(comment positivelyCorrelatedWith "(#$positivelyCorrelatedWith ?SET ?DEP-PRED ?INDEP-PRED) means that the second arguments to ?DEP-PRED are positively correlated with those for ?INDEP-PRED, when elements of ?SET appear in the first argument position.  In other words, given the range of bindings for DEP-VAL and INDEP-VAL in (#$and (#$elementOf X ?SET)(?DEP-PRED X DEP-VAL) (?INDEP-PRED X INDEP-VAL)), whenever INDEP-VAL is high for a particular X, DEP-VAL will also be high and whenever INDEP-VAL is low, DEP-VAL will be low.  Note that #$negativelyCorrelatedWith and #$positivelyCorrelatedWith don't entail a particular directionality of the causal relationship between arg2 values for ?DEP-PRED and ?INDEP-PRED.  It might go either direction, or there may be no direct causal link, with instead arg2 values for ?DEP-PRED and ?INDEP-PRED actually being independent but subject to some common causal mechanism. ")
(comment HoneymoonTrip "The collection of all #$VacationTrips taken by newlyweds as newlyweds.")
(comment CameraOperator "A person who operates a video or moving-film camera as a job.")
(comment Ski-BoardPart "The collection of narrow strips of wood, metal, or plastic curving upward in front used especially for

gliding over snow, water, etc. A #$Ski-BoardPart is just a runner, not including any attached bindings, etc.")
(comment TransporterErectorLauncher "The collection of vehicles which transport, erect and launch missiles and rockets.")
(comment Praseodymium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of praseodymium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.  This unit could probably just as well be called Praseodymium or PraseodymiumStuff")
(comment AmateurSportsTeam "The collection of #$SportsTeams whose members are not paid for being a member of that team. This collection includes university sports teams, recreational sports teams, etc.; it could also include a team formed of players who normally are members of professional teams, but for some particular competition are playing as an amateur team. Example: the 1998 U.S. Olympic Men's Hockey team had many members who play professionally in the #$NationalHockeyLeague, but their participation on the Olympic team was not for pay, so the team is considered amateur.")
(comment PartialOrdering-Strict "The collection of all #$MathematicalOrderings ORDER in which the ordering relation R is an irreflexive and transitive relation on the #$baseSet S of ORDER, i.e., for each X in S, R(X X) does not hold, and for each X, Y and Z in S, R(X Y) and R(Y Z) imply R(X Z).  For example, if one takes the set of all people, and the relation '__ is older than ...' on this set, one gets a #$PartialOrdering-Strict, since the relation '__ is older than ...' is irreflexive and transitive on this set.  Note that the important difference between a #$PartialOrdering (q.v.) and a #$PartialOrdering-Strict is that the ordering relation of the former is reflexive, while that of the latter is irreflexive.  Note also that the ordering relation R of a #$PartialOrdering-Strict ORDER is in fact antisymmetric (i.e., for each X and Y in S, R(X Y) and R(Y X) imply X = Y) and asymmetric (i.e., for each X and Y in S, R(X Y) and R(Y X) can never be both true) on the #$baseSet S. This is because both antisymmetry and asymmetry follow from transitivity and irreflexivity.")
(disjointWith Incorporation-Physical WavePropagation)
(comment Metal "An instance of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType.  Every instance of #$Metal is a tangible object having certain characteristic physical and chemical properties.  Instances of #$Metal are good conductors of electricity and heat, and most instances of #$Metal are solids at room temperature (although all instances of #$Mercury, for example, are liquids at room temperature).  Solid instances of #$Metal have a shiny luster, and are highly malleable.  Specializations of #$Metal include #$Mercury, #$Potassium, #$Brass, #$Lead, and #$Iron.")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent Gardening)
(comment RemoveEconomicSubsidy "The collection of events where one state removes or does not renew economic subsidies to another state or itself (then viewed as a subsidy to the domestic sector).")
(comment KlebsiellaOxytoca "A collection of #$Bacterium in the #$MoneraKingdom.  They may cause hospital-acquired #$Infections.  They are part of the gastrointestinal flora.")
(comment objectOfSimulation "The expression `(#$objectOfSimulation SIM THING)' means that the simulation event

SIM is a simulation or a modelling of THING. THING can be a static object, a

dynamic object, or an event. This

sort of simulation should not be confused with the simulation of a

certain type of *experience*, for example, the experience of flying in

flight simulation video games. In the latter, there is often a certain degree

of simulation in the present sense as well, although this is just a means to

the intended effect. For more about the present notion of simulation see

the comment on #$Simulation-Activity.")
(comment RoundClosestFn "(#$RoundClosestFn QUANTITY) converts QUANTITY into one where the maximum and minimum ranges have been rounded to the closest integer values.  For example,  (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 2.41)) denotes (#$Meter 2),  (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 2.7)) denotes (#$Meter 3), and (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 1.6 4.2)) denotes  (#$Meter 2 4). If QUANTITY is exactly between two integers (that is, in the form integer+0.5), then it is rounded to the one that is even. So, (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 2.5)) denotes (#$Meter 2), and (#$RoundClosestFn (#$Meter 7.5)) denotes (#$Meter 8). See also #$RoundUpFn, #$RoundDownFn.")
(comment Meclizine "The chemical that is the main ingredient in Dramamine II, Bonine, etc. - used to treat nausea and sea-sickness.")
(comment PredicateRuleTemplateFn "(#$PredicateRuleTemplateFn PRED) denotes the rule template unique to predicate PRED.")
(comment Exhaust-InternalCombustionEngine "The collection of gases which are #$outputsCreated from an #$InternalCombustionEngine in an #$InternalCombustionProcess.  More specifically, a gas consisting of unburned hydrocarbons, carbon monoxide, oxides of nitrogen, and other noxious gases.")
(comment IMSPrescriberNumber "ID strings issued by IMS which uniquely identify a number of types of things, including: Doctors, hospitals, and zip-code regions for patients, stores, and doctors.")
(comment Imposter "#$Imposter is the subset of #$ImitationOfIndividual which includes all and only those instances of #$Person who pretend to be someone they are not.")
(comment BackupTapeManager "Someone whose job is to make sure that backup tapes are made.")
(comment Raft "A small flat kind of boat.  Rubber rafts and flat wooden rafts are the most common.")
(comment Lizard "The collection of all lizards; a subset of #$Reptile.  Each element of #$Lizard is a toothed reptile with a tail and (with some exceptions) limbs, external ears, eyes with movable lids, and without enclosing shells.  Reptiles range in size from less than an inch long to that of the large #$KomodoDragon.  The collection #$Lizard constitutes a biological suborder (also called Sauria or Lacertilia).  Colloquially, `lizard' may denote a crocodile, but compare #$Crocodilian.")
(comment AssaultRifle-M16A1 "The collection of all M16-A1 #$AssaultRifles.")
(disjointWith ElectricalResistance AngularDistance)
(comment vulnerabilityOfBecauseIs "(#$vulnerabilityOfBecauseIs AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP VAL) means that AGENT has the #$goals (#$not (ROLE EVTTYPE AGENT)) and the chance for AGENT's playing the role ROLE in a situation of type EVTTYPE in the context is VAL (#$chanceForRoleBecauseIs AGENT EVTTYPE ROLE PROP VAL).")
(comment matchBetween "#$matchBetween is used to identify an #$AnalogyMatch between two #$AnalogyCases, one being the base case and one being the target case. Its format is (#$matchBetween BASE TARGET MATCH).")
(disjointWith RifledBoreWeapon SmoothBoreWeapon)
(comment defaultSuitableProduct "(#$defaultSuitableProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that any instance of the instance of #$ProductType, PROD-TYPE, is a suitable #$Product to be purchased for the #$Person PRSN, unless PROD-TYPE is known to be not suitable (see #$contraindicatedProduct). For example,(#$defaultSuitableProduct #$TheRecipient #$PersonalDigitalAssistant) means that any instance of #$PersonalDigitalAssistant is a suitable #$Product to be purchased for #$TheRecipient. Assertions using this predicate are the weakest assertions that can be made about the suitability of a #$Product for a recipient. There need be no positive evidence in favor of PROD-TYPE being suitable for a recipient for it to be default suitable. The motivation for creating this predicate is to enable asks of the form (#$defaultSuitableProduct ?PRSN ?PROD-TYPE) to return bindings right at the beginning of a session in which a customer uses the Cyc Product Advisor interface. In the beginning of a session we have no information about the customer, so we can't do any inferencing about which #$Products are indicated.")
(comment GasGiant "The collection of all #$Planets which are composed primarily of a gaseous #$Atmosphere, which becomes denser towards the center of the planet, possibly dense enough to solidify hydrogen.")
(comment CharacterMode-Inscribed "A specialization of #$CharacterMode each instance of    which is the collection of all of the inscribed character    tokens of a some particular abstract character.  Examples    include the collection of all inscribed tokens (see   #$CharacterToken-Inscribed) of the character '&'.")
(comment decreases-Generic "(#$decreases-Generic TEMP-THING THING SLOT)            means the value of the            predicate SLOT applied to THING (in the first argument            position) will decrease over some time period after the start of            TEMP-THING. Compared with            its value immediately before TEMP-THING, the value of            SLOT applied to THING will be lower            immediately following or some time after the start of TEMP-THING.             This is the most generic of the #$SlotTrendPredicates relating to decreasing of a given #$QuantitySlot: the decrease may be causal, or may not be, and may occur immediately, or over a period of time following TEMP-THING. For GAFs, or in the consequents of rules dealing with decreased quantities, use the more specific predicates if possible. See            #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related            predicates.")
(comment ImmuneDeficiencyDisorderType "This is the collection of diseases (disease types)

the primary manifestation of which is chronic inadequate immune response. The best-known

instance is AIDS. Most immune deficiency diseases, however, are genetic. Examples

of these include X-Linked Agammaglobulinemia, Selective IgA Deficiency, and

Chronic Granulomatous Disease.")
(comment Fisting "The collection of events involving insertion of the entire fist in the #$Anus or the #$Vagina for the purpose of sexual stimulation.")
(comment Bending "A process of straining a material uniformly along a straight axis.")
(comment BeliefsContext "The collection of all contexts which contain assertions expressing the beliefs of some agent or group of agents.")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething Conveying-Generic)
(comment Stress-Feeling "Cumulative psychological or emotional disturbance caused by environmental influences. Can be relieved by #$Resting-Relaxing, #$Meditating, #$Exercising, etc.")
(comment ClindamycinHydrochloride "The chemical compound which is an anti-infective.")
(comment G-TheLetter "The letter G of the alphabet.  This is 'G' (or 'g') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterG and #$LatinSmallLetterG.")
(comment Dollar-Bahamas "Major unit of currency of #$Bahamas")
(comment FunctionValueFn "(#$FunctionValueFn FUNCTION ARG) is a term 

denoting the resulting value of applying a unary FUNCTION to ARG, whatever 

that value may be. Since #$FunctionValueFn is a #$ReifiableFunction, one can

use this to refer to and talk about the result of applying a function to 

an argument even if the actual resulting value is not known.  For example,

'the diameter of Mars is smaller than the diameter of Earth' can be expressed

as :

(#$followingValue

  (#$FunctionValueFn

     (#$FunctionToArg 2 #$diameterOfObject)

     #$PlanetMars)  

  (#$FunctionValueFn

     (#$FunctionToArg 2 #$diameterOfObject)

     #$PlanetEarth)")
(comment RNAMoleculeType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$RNAMoleculeType are

types of instances of the collection RNA.  There are four kinds of

RNA: messenger RNA, ribosomal RNA, transfer RNA, and viral RNA.")
(comment Bacterium "The collection of bacteria; a subset of #$SingleCellOrganism.   Each element of #$Bacterium is also an element of #$ProkaryoticCell and of #$Heterotroph.  Bacteria are typically incapable of processes of #$Photosynthesis-Bacterial.  The class #$Bacterium, also called the Schizomycophyta, is one of the divisions of the #$MoneraKingdom.  Many bacteria cause diseases that are instances of #$BacterialInfection in both plants and animals, but some are beneficial or even necessary for life.  Compare with the #$BlueGreenAlgae.")
(comment ElementStuffType "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType. Each instance of #$ElementStuffType is a specialization of #$ElementStuff.")
(comment interArgIsa5-4 "A ternary instance of #$InterArgIsaPredicate (q.v.).   (#$interArgIsa5-4 RELN INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that,  when an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the fifth argument to RELN,  a necessary condition for semantic well-formedness is that the fourth argument  must be an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  That is, if INST is an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL, then  (RELN ARG1 ARG2 ARG3 ARG4 INST ... ARGN) is semantically  well-formed only if ARG4 is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  For an explanation  of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its direct  specializations.")
(comment StabbingSomething "The collection of events in which a hole is formed in the #$objectActedOn using a sharp tool that penetrates deep into it.")
(comment trustsAccount "A predicate relating instances of #$ComputerAccount to each other.

(#$trustsAccount TRUSTS TRUSTED) means that the user of

TRUSTED can access resources on TRUSTS without further

authentication, but not necessarily vice versa.")
(comment Nitrospina-Genus "A collection of #$Bacteria in the #$BiologicalGenus #$Nitrospina-Genus.  These #$ProkaryoticCells reproduce by #$BinaryFission.  They are NonMotileBacterium and #$AerobicBacterium.  Also, these are obligate chemolithotrophs.")
(disjointWith LighterThanAirCraft RotaryWingAircraft)
(comment Distance-Absolute "#$Distance-Absolute is the length of a path in space extending from one point to another.  Unlike #$Distance, instances of #$Distance-Absolute do not contain directional information.  Rather #$Distance-Absolute is by definition a scalar, not a vector quantity, and is thus always positive or zero.  Instances of #$Distance may be either a fixed interval such as the height of the #$WashingtonMonumentInWashingtonDC, or a range, such as #$WithinAudibleDistance (see #$ScalarInterval for more explanation). Also see #$UnitOfDistance for the units used by Cyc to measure distances.  Distances must be #$NonNegativeScalarIntervals.  See also #$Distance, which can take on negative values.  Exemplars of #$Distance-Absolute include the distance in miles between Austin and San Antonio, or the turning radius of a Model T Automobile. Non-exemplars of #$Distance-Absolute include height above sea level. Since the Dead Sea is below sea level, its height above sea level is a negative value.  Thus #$Distance is a more appropriate argument constraint for height above sea level.")
(comment hingedTo "(#$hingedTo OBJ1 OBJ2) means that there is some hinge connecting OBJ1 and OBJ2, allowing limited rotational motion (but no other sort of relative motion) between OBJ1 and OBJ2.  The connecting hinge may be part of OBJ1, part of OBJ2, or separate from both OBJ1 and OBJ2. Note that (#$hingedTo OBJ1 OBJ2) implies that some edge of OBJ1 adjoins some edge of OBJ2.")
(comment Asphyxiation "Ailment characterized by deficiency of oxygen.  If acute asphyxiation continues more than a few minutes for most animals, they will die.")
(comment Thrashing "State of affairs in a #$GridCommunity wherein significant community activity and expenditure of effort are accompanied by no discernable result or advancement toward the community's goal.")
(comment DecreaseEvent "The collection of #$Events the focal characteristic of which is a decrease in some quantity.")
(comment Packet-UDP "The collection of all #$Packet-Internets that are also

#$UserDatagramProtocol packets.")
(comment DomesticIndustryGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with promoting and preserving domestic industries of a country.")
(comment TacticalNuclearWeaponsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military unit organized, equipped, and trained for           operations involving handling, employment, and/or containment of           'tactical' nuclear weapons           for use by individuals or small groups in combat conditions.")
(disjointWith Layer FreeSheet)
(comment Europium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of europium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment DictionaryToEnglishFromFn "#$DictionaryToEnglishFromFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. (#$DictionaryToEnglishFromFn LANGUAGE) represents the spec of #$Dictionary whose elements are dictionaries that translate words from LANGUAGE into English. For example, (#$DictionaryToEnglishFromFn #$SpanishLanguage) denotes the collection of dictionaries that translate words from Spanish into English.")
(comment USMilitaryServicePersonnel "#$USMilitaryServicePersonnel is the collection of all officers and enlisted personnel in any instance of #$UnitedStatesMilitaryOrganization.")
(disjointWith ComputerProcess-SingleCPU ComputerProcess-Distributed)
(disjointWith Language SystemOfMeasure)
(comment keSuggestionApplies "This predicate relates terms in the KB to formulas expressing KE suggestions for things of that type which do in fact apply to the term in question.  (#$keSuggestionApplies TERM FORMULA) relates TERM to some FORMULA containing a suggestion about information that should be asserted about TERM.  For instance, if some collection is partitioned it might be suggested in some formula, FORM-EX, that subsets of the collection be considered for membership in one of the partition cells.  If in fact, this suggestion applies to a given subset, SUB-EX, of the collection, i.e. if it should be made a specialization of one of the partition cells, it would be the case that (#$keSuggestionApplies COL FORM).")
(comment EnglishSuffix "The set of lexical items which may attach to the end of
an English word. Example: 'less', as in 'fearless'.")
(comment antitransTestPred "Prototypical instance of #$AntiTransitiveBinaryPredicate, to
be used for testing purposes.")
(comment RustingProcess "The oxidation of an iron-based metal; rust is formed in the process.")
(comment PoliticalSupport "#$PoliticalSupport is a collection of attributes representing the generic levels of political support that one group of agents gives to another.  Attributes in this collection represent the general committment of one agent to provide political assistance to another agent, as evidenced by pledges and/or present or previous behavior.  For example, (#$givesSupportToAgent #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$Israel (#$HighAmountFn #$PoliticalSupport)). Note that such relationships are liable to change and therefore assertions about them should have temporal qualification (see #$holdsIn).  Political support is intangible but significant, in that it may sway the opinion of third parties, and it often implies or includes economic or military support.  (See also #$MilitarySupport, #$EconomicSupport.)  To represent actual events in which support is given, see #$ShowingSupportForSomeone, #$HelpingAnAgent.")
(comment intangibleAssetsOfAgent "The predicate that relates a #$Person or #$Organization to the monetary value of its intangible assets.  Intangible assets are considered noncurrent, so the value of #$totalValueOfNonCurrentAssets depends partly upon the #$valueOfIntangibleAssets.")
(comment NuclearWarhead "The collection of #$Warheads which contain #$NuclearBombs instead of conventional #$ExplosiveDevices.")
(comment WebServer-Network "A subcollection of #$Computer, whose instances function as
web servers for instances of #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment EthnicStudies "These are fields of study rather similar to those

in #$AreaStudies, except that it is people grouped by ethnicity rather than by 

region that are studied.")
(comment OticAdministration "Administering a liquid, possibly a drug, through one's ears.")
(comment compressibilityOfObject "(#$compressibilityOfObject OBJ DEGREE) indicates how readily the tangible object OBJ can be compressed to a smaller volume.  The higher the DEGREE of compressibility, the more easily the object can be compressed to a smaller volume.  A related concept is #$elasticityOfObject.")
(comment IntrusionDetectionSystem-Network "A subcollection of #$Computer.  Instances of this collection have the primary function of looking at other nodes in the network to which they belong and \"sniffing\" for intrusions.  They fulfil this functioon in part by running copies of #$IntrusionDetectionPrograms.")
(comment LicensesPertainingToTypeFn "#$LicensesPertainingToTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$Thing and returns the collection of            #$License-LegalAgreement pertaining to that things of that type. For Example,            (#$LicensesPertainingToTypeFn #$Fishing) returns the collection of all instances of             #$License-LegalAgreement pertaining to #$Fishing.")
(comment borderSubRegions "(#$borderSubRegions REGION BORDERREGION) means that BORDERREGION is a subregion of REGION which borders on some region outside of REGION.")
(comment NewsGroupServer "A collection of #$Computers.  Instances of this collection provide access to Usenet newsgroups.  To receive postings to Usenet newsgroups, one must direct one's newsreader program to the #$DomainName or #$IPAddress of an instance of #$NewsGroupServer that is regulated by #$NetworkNewsTransferProtocol.")
(disjointWith FederalCourt RegionalGovernment)
(comment VersionField-Packet "A #$VersionField-Packet is the part of a #$Header-Packet that
indicates the version of the #$NetworkProtocol which the #$Packet-Internet
belongs to.")
(comment LiquidFlowAlongConduit "the process in which a liquid flows along a conduit, as in water through a hose or channel, milk through a straw, etc.  Does not necessarily imply this is the result of an agent's action.")
(disjointWith GeographicalDirection-Direct GeographicalDirection-General)
(comment Iguana "A group of lizard species, typified by the Green Tree Iguana, the species most commonly
kept as a pet. Most species are tropical.")
(comment Perceiving-Voluntary "A specialization of both #$Perceiving and #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$Perceiving-Voluntary is a perceptual event in which the perceiving agent does not merely passively receive sensory information, but actively filters or directs how it is perceiving.  Thus, searching for a set of lost keys would be an instance of #$Perceiving-Voluntary, as would straining to hear something, but merely hearing a balloon pop next to one would _not_.")
(comment Decapitation-Execution "A collection of event. A spec of #$Execution-Judicial.")
(comment TimeOfDay-6PM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 6PM.")
(disjointWith Cleaning AcademicTesting)
(comment typeMakesMoreVulnerableThan-Situation "(#$typeMakesMoreVulnerableThan-Situation SIT-TYPE1 SIT-TYPE2 ?OBJECT-TYPE ?RESULT-TYPE) means that when existing things of type ?OBJECT-TYPE are involved in situations of type ?SIT-TYPE1 they are more vulnerable to results of type ?RESULT-TYPE than when they are involved in situations of type ?SIT-TYPE2.  The purpose of this predicate is to enable broad, comparative knowledge representations of vulnerabilities.  For a similar, instance level predicate see #$makesMoreVulnerableThan-Situation.  Note that this is predicate is type-level across the board; it is meant to capture very broad generalizations.")
(comment BasalNucleus "The collection of all basal nuclei (or 'basal ganglia'), which are internal structures of the #$Cerebrum.  Basal nuclei include the #$CaudateNucleus, #$LentiformNucleus, and #$Amygdala in each #$CerebralHemisphere.  Basal nuclei are involved starting, stopping, and regulating intensity and smoothness of voluntary movements.  #$ParkinsonsDisease and #$HuntingtonsDisease are #$BasalNucleus diseases.")
(comment CycLRepresentedAtomicTerm "A specialization of #$CycLAtomicTerm.  An instance ATOM of #$CycLAtomicTerm is also an instance of #$CycLRepresentedAtomicTerm just in case ATOM is explicitly represented in the CycL language (as opposed to being represented in SubL, the underlying implementation language of the Cyc system).  Important specializations of #$CycLRepresentedAtomicTerm include #$CycLVariable and #$CycLConstant.")
(comment Inpatient "The collection of all #$MedicalPatients who spend at least one night in a #$Hospital for their current occasion of being a patient.")
(comment PageFn "If TEXT is a text with numbered pages and the #$PageNumberingSchema #$SimpleSequentialSchema and is not divided into subsections and is not itself a subsection of some larger text, (PageFn TEXT N) returns page number N of TEXT.  If TEXT is divided into subsections and has as its #$PageNumberingSchema the #$SimpleSequentialSchema, then (#$PageFn TEXT N) also returns page number N of TEXT.  If TEXT is divided into subsections and has as its #$PageNumberingSchema the #$SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema, then (#$PageFn TEXT N) returns page with number N, in the 'main body' of the text, disregarding the priviledged subsection or subsections. If TEXT is itself a subsection of a larger autonomous text SUPERTEXT with the #$PageNumberingSchema of #$SimpleSequentialSchema then (#$PageFn TEXT N) returns (#$PageFn SUPERTEXT N).  If TEXT is itself a subsection of a larger autonomous text SUPERTEXT with the #$PageNumberingSchema of #$RepetitionBySubsectionSchema then (#$PageFn TEXT N) returns the page with number N in TEXT's own internal numbering schema.  And if TEXT is itself a subsection of a larger autonomous text SUPERTEXT with the #$PageNumberingSchema of #$SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema, then (#$PageFn TEXT N) returns (#$PageFn SUPERTEXT N) unless TEXT is one of the 'priviledged' subsections, in which case (#$PageFn TEXT N) returns the page with number N in TEXT's own internal numbering schema.  Otherwise the function is undefined.  In any case the function returns an instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing, which means there will always be an genlMt access link between a given TEXT and (#$PageFn TEXT N) where the function is defined.")
(comment NeutralZone "A collection of regions, usually situated on borders between two political entities and jointly administered by them.")
(comment AssessingEnemyCapabilities "A collection of processes.  Each element of #$AssessingEnemyCapabilities
is an instance of #$Evaluating in which the military capabilities of
the enemy are  evaluated.")
(comment MachineGun-M2 "The M2 is a 0.50 caliber machine gun.")
(comment TechnologicalActivity "A specialization of #$HumanActivity.  In each instance of #$TechnologicalActivity, an agent uses or produces technology or transfers technological knowledge.")
(comment TwoTerminalElectricalDevice "electrical devices with two terminals")
(comment AxisConstrainedMultirevolutionRotation "Multirevolution rotation constrained by an axis to which the rotating object is attached.  The axis does not move relative to the constraining object.")
(comment USSecretaryOfState-Federal "The federal Secretary of State heads the foreign affair efforts of the State Department.")
(comment detector "(#$detector EVENT SENSOR) says that 

 in EVENT, SENSOR plays the role of #$detector.

  Moreover, via axioms, where EVENT is an 

  instance of some 

  (#$DetectionFn STUFF), 

(#$detector EVENT SENSOR) requires that

  SENSOR #$detects STUFF during

  EVENT.")
(comment FTPingAFile "The collection of all instances of #$CopyingAComputerFile where the protocol employed is File Transfer Protocol.")
(disjointWith Event Issue)
(disjointWith Ship Projectile-Device)
(comment CatShaped "#$CatShaped is the instance of #$ShapeAttribute defined by the typical shape of a domestic cat.")
(comment genlInverseWRTTypes "(#$genlInverseWRTTypes BINPRED1 BINPRED2 COL1 COL2) means that if (BINPRED1 INS1 INS2) where INS1 is an instance of COL1 and INS2 is an instance of COL2, then (BINPRED2 INS2 INS1).  See #$genlPredsWRTTypes for examples of usage.")
(comment Injecting-Medical "Taking a hypodermic syringe with needle attached, puncturing skin, injecting substance into #$objectActedOn.  This could be either an injection that takes only a few moments, or it could be an infusion where fluid is introduced into the body over a longer period of time.  When done by a medical care provider, injections are usually done to treat a patient, but could be for diagnostic reasons.")
(comment uniqueIDForType "(#$uniqueIDForType ?ID-TYPE ?COL) means that each ID in the class ?ID-TYPE uniquely identifies one instance of ?COL.  Specifically, if an instance of ?COL has an ID of type ?ID-TYPE, no other instance of ?COL has the same ID of that type.  This allows a situation where some instances of ?COL may have more than one ID of type ?ID-TYPE, and others may have none at all. ")
(comment ChildAbuse "#$ChildAbuse is a spec of #$HarmingAnAgent in which a #$HumanAdult causes a nonaccidental injury or pattern of injuries to a #$HumanChild for whom they bear caregiving responsibility. It includes nonaccidental physical injury, neglect, #$ChildSexualAbuse, and emotional abuse.")
(comment HumanlyOccupiedRegionOfTransportationDevice "Those parts of boats, trains, planes, space shuttles that people occupy.  A moving equivalent of room.  There may be reasons to make this a spec of #$RoomInAConstruction.")
(comment DNAPolymerase "A collection of #$Enzyme molecules that catalyze the

step-by-step template-directed addition of deoxyribosenucleotides to

the 3' strand of an RNA molecule primer or growing DNA molecule

chain, using a single-stranded DNA template.")
(comment FacialCosmeticTreatment "The collections of #$ProfessionalServicing events in which a #$Person is acted upon so that his/her #$PhysicalAttractiveness could be enhanced by somehow modifying the features of his/her #$FaceOfAnimal.")
(comment decileForQuantity "(#$decileForQuantity OBJ GROUP PRED N) means that the corresponding value when applying the functional binary predicate PRED to OBJ appears in the Nth decile of the result of applying PRED to each member of GROUP.")
(comment Webmaster "A #$WebMaster is a person who administers and develops a #$WorldWideWebSite.")
(comment ConnectingToAComputerNetwork "A collection of events.  In an instance of #$ConnectingToAComputerNetwork, a user gains communications access to a computer network, either locally, or via a dial-up connection.")
(comment Minesweeper-Ocean "The collection of minesweepers designed to operate in open-sea areas.")
(comment PlaintextProtocol "The collection of all instances of #$NetworkProtocol according to which communications between computers are conducted in #$Plaintext, i.e., are not #$Encrypted.")
(disjointWith TransportationCompany ConstructionCompany)
(comment fieldStudies "(#$fieldStudies FIELD THINGTYPE) means that persons working in FIELD customarily study instances of THINGTYPE.")
(comment Lead "A piece (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of lead; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(disjointWith ManipulatingFoodOrDrink ChangeOfStatusEvent)
(comment UrgentCareMedicalCondition "Physiological conditions that need immediate attention - not just those treated by paramedics and emergency rooms, but also those that can be handled by standard first aid practices.")
(comment PuttingGreen "A kind of subregion of a golf course, where the grass is clipped very short and the ball is rolled across it.")
(comment typicalFacilityOfOrgType "(#$typicalFacilityOfOrgType ORG-TYPE PLACE-TYPE) means that
under ordinary circumstances an instance of ORG-TYPE can be expected
to control one or more instances of PLACE-TYPE as organizational
facilities.")
(comment TridentBallisticMissile "The collection

of all #$BallisticMissiles designed

for use on #$TridentClassSubmarines.")
(comment MinorEmergencyClinic "A medical clinic which primarily provides care on relative short notice.  It can not handle extreme, life-threatening cases but is ideal for a small injury requiring stitches or an infection like a head cold or the flu.")
(comment WaterBoardingEvent "The collection of all waterboarding events.

  Waterboarding is similar to #$WaterSkiing except that one uses

a single #$WaterBoard instead of a pair of water skis. ")
(comment GroundToAirCommunicationsUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units whose mission profile centers on           communication from ground-based platforms to air-based           platforms.")
(comment OrganicCompound "A collection of chemical compounds containing carbon.")
(comment Password-Weak "#$Password-Weak is a subset of #$Password-Computer.  It includes passwords that           are easy to guess, such as passwords in the collections #$Password-Canonical and           #$Password-Poor.")
(disjointWith MeasuringSomething Drawing-RandomSelection)
(comment GameFn "(#$GameFn GAME) is the collection of all complete games [#$GameEvent] played of the game type, GAME.  To refer to all playings of the game, whether of not the game is completed, use the more general function, #$PlayingFn.")
(comment VideoConceptualWork "A specialization of #$VisualWork and #$PropositionalConceptualWork.  Each instance of #$VideoConceptualWork is an abstract work that is intended to be instantiated as an instance of #$MovingImage.  Important specializations include #$Movie-CW, #$TVShow-CW, and #$MusicVideo.")
(comment UnitedStatesPresident "A specialization of both #$UnitedStatesPerson and #$President-HeadOfGovernmentOrHeadOfState.  Each instance of #$UnitedStatesPresident is a person who holds the office of President of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment LargeAnimalVeterinarian "Instances are veterinarians that specialize in the care of large animals such as horses and livestock.")
(comment DescendingEvent "An event is an #$DescendingEvent if and only if its object (#$objectMoving) has a lower altitude (#$altitudeAboveSeaLevel) at the end of the event than it did at the beginning of the event.  Thus, some ascent may occur during the descent so long as the net effect is to decrease altitude.  Descending stairs, walking over a ridge on the way to a lower valley, being lowered, and airplane landings are exemplars of #$DescendingEvent.  Technically, sitting down and souffles falling are not exemplars because the #$altitudeAboveSeaLevel of these objects is not lower at the end of the event.  (#$altitudeAboveSeaLevel is based on the distance between the bottom of the object and the mean sea level.)")
(comment oldTownOf "(#$oldTownOf CITY OLDTOWN) means that OLDTOWN is the old town
area of CITY, an instance of City. See also #$OldTownArea, #$OldTownFn.")
(comment Swinging "The process of repetitive swinging with either a rigid (e.g. pendulum or metronome) or flexible (e.g. child's swing) connection to an axis not at the center of gravity.  The axis does not have to be horizontal; thus a gate can swing back and forth.  The motion, for a horizontal axis, may be above the axis as well as below.  Both the object attached to the pivot and any object 'riding' on that object are said to swing.  This does not include swinging an axe or a bat as a single swing is not periodic, and the return to the start of the swing for repeated swings is not a temporal reflection of the forward swing.   Swinging a pail around the head while it is attached to a rope is not this kind of #$Swinging since it is not a repetative reversing motion.")
(disjointWith Facility-Construct AstronomicalObservatory)
(comment Year-JulianFn "(#$Year-JulianFn N) denotes the calendar year that is Nth year after the start of the common era. For N close to 1 the difference with (#$YearFn N) is nothing, but by October 4, 1582 (Julian) the Julian calendar was off by 11 days. ")
(comment objectFound-Definite "The expression `#$objectFound-Definite(SEARCH SEEKER OBJECT)'
means that the search has succeeded. It says that SEEKER, the
#$performedBy in the SEARCH, has come across the OBJECT which was sought
and that SEEKER #$notices that OBJECT satisfies the #$searchCriterion-Definite
associated with the search. The arg3 position is an #$opaqueArgument because it is intended
to represent the way SEEKER conceptualizes OBJECT in the act of noticing
that it satisfies the search criterion.")
(comment Dementia "A mental disease resulting in impaired memory and abstract thinking.")
(comment explains-PropProp "(#$explains-PropProp SENT1 SENT2) means that the proposition expressed by SENT1 helps to explain why SENT2 holds.  In other words, SENT1 is an integral part of some plausible explanation as to why SENT2 holds. Note that SENT1 need not constitute the entirety of the explanation.")
(comment TranscriptOfEventFn "#$TranscriptOfEventFn takes as argument a particular event and returns the collection of transcripts  [#$TranscriptOfSpeech-CWIS] of that event.  There may be multiple transcripts because of different choices of punctuation, different transcribees hearing different things, or because of censoring.  For example, (#$TranscriptOfEventFn NixonHaldemanOvalOfficeConversation03061972) would return the collection of Transcripts of that particular conversation.  See comment on #$TranscriptOfEventTypeFn for examples of the difference between the three functions, #$TranscriptOfEventFn, #$TranscriptOfEventTypeFn, and #$TranscriptOfSpecifiedEventTypeFn.")
(comment SubcollectionPerformedByFn "(#$SubcollectionPerformedByFn EVENTTYPE AGENT) describes the collection of all instances of EVENTTYPE which are #$performedBy AGENT.")
(comment Sertraline "The chemical compound which is an antidepressant.")
(comment HardwareExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes to pay for hardware")
(disjointWith ArmoredVehicle-Heavy ArmoredVehicle-Light)
(comment Recession-Economic "A subset of #$MacroeconomicEvent. Each element of #$Recession-Economic is a downward turn in the business cycle, during which there is a decline in production and employment.")
(comment Franc-Madagascar "Major unit of currency of #$Madagascar")
(comment VisualArtActivity "The collection of activities that instances of #$Artist-Visual do. This includes things like #$PaintingAPicture, (#$MakingFn #$Sculpture), and #$TakingAPhotograph.")
(comment LandVehiclePathSystem "The collection of all road systems, systems of one or more #$PathForWheeledVehicles interconnected to allow a #$LandTransportationDevice (normally a #$RoadVehicle or a #$Train-TransportationDevice) to travel.  The roads or tracks in a #$LandVehiclePathSystem may be publically or privately owned or maintained.  Typically, though not always, raods in such a system are paved, and wide enough to allow passage of passenger automobiles under normal conditions.  Note that #$PathForWheeledVehicles includes #$ParkingLots, #$AirplaneRunways, and #$Railways; these could in principal be parts of a #$LandVehiclePathSystem if they are accessible to other parts.  In practice, most #$AirplaneRunways and all #$Railways are not accessible from nearby streets, so they would not be considered part of the same #$LandVehiclePathSystem.")
(comment OpiumPoppyPlant "Individual opium poppy plants.  The latex from their fruits [raw opium] is harvested and used as a narcotic.")
(comment SupportHelicopter-OH58DKW "The collection of helicopters used to provide reconnaissance and close air support duties. The OH58DKW is generally equipped with anti-tank missiles and rockets, thermal imaging equipment for providing target information to other air and ground-based units.")
(disjointWith Mob FoodChain)
(comment connectedAlongEdge "(#$connectedAlongEdge SHEET OBJ2) means that one of the edges of a #$SheetOfSomeStuff, SHEET, is #$connectedTo OBJ2.")
(comment MissileSystem-Offensive "The collection of #$WeaponSystems

   used to attack cities, armies, vehicles, etc.

   with #$Missiles.")
(comment programRunningOn "(#$programRunningOn PROGRAM SYSTEM) means that an instantiation of the instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW, PROGRAM, is running on the instance of #$ComputationalSystem, SYSTEM.")
(comment EukaryoticRibosome "A collection of small spherical organelles present in

eukaryotic cells.  These are the site of protein synthesis after the

genetic instructions have been carried there by messenger RNA.  Not to be confused with bacterial #$ProkaryoticRibosomes, which are smaller and have a lower rate of sedimentation.")
(comment EmployeeBenefits "Instances of this collection are offered by (some) employers as part of the #$CompensationPackage stipulated in hiring #$WorkAgreements.")
(comment Stack "an organized pile. Usually things in a stack are similar in sized and shaped, and lay nicely one on top of another.")
(comment TemproMandibularJointSyndrome "This syndrome effects the #$TemporoMandibularJoint, and is marked by pain in the joint and face, popping noises when the jaw is opened, and headaches.")
(comment inconsistentWithMt "(#$inconsistentWithMt SENTENCE MT) means that adding the #$ELSentence-Assertible SENTENCE to the assertions already in the #$Microtheory MT would generate a contradiction. For asserting that a given #$ELSentence-Assertible does not contradict what is known tout court, see #$consistent.")
(disjointWith LighterThanAirCraft RocketPropelledTransportationDevice)
(comment confluentWith "River u joins river v to form a river with a name different from either.  This is transitive since the implication would be that three (or more) rivers come together at that point.   An abnormal counterexample would be if a river's name reverted to the name of one of the streams, downstream and came to another confluence with a second name change.")
(comment LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing "The most general collection of events in which an agent purposefully looks or searches for something.  The thing being looked for may be a particular individual or it may be anything that satisfies a certain description (see #$NoteAboutLookingForIndividualsVsTypes).  The thing being looked for may be tangible or intangible, timeless or temporally bounded. Visual perception is not necessarily involved in all instances of #$LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing.  Examples include searching for the largest prime number less than 10 billion, Johnny looking for Santa Claus, Humans looking for intelligent life, Fred looking for any dictionary, Fred looking for Joe's dictionary, and Deep Blue searching for the best possible move.")
(comment Cockatiel "A collection of small Parrots living in the #$ContinentOfAustralia.  Their scientific name is Nymphicus hollandicus.")
(comment ScubaVest "The collection of scuba vests.")
(comment WheeledAntiTankVehicle "The collection of wheeled, armored military vehicles with the turret replaced with an anti-tank missile platform.")
(comment Cerium "A piece (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of cerium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.  This unit could probably just as well be called Cerium or CeriumStuff")
(disjointWith AmateurSportsTeam ProfessionalSportsTeam)
(comment visaType "The binary predicate #$visaType relates an instance of #$IndependentCountry to a subset of #$Visa-Permit. (#$visaType COUNTRY VISA) means that the government of  COUNTRY issues instances of VISA, where VISA is a type of #$Visa-Permit.")
(disjointWith PartialOrdering-Strict QuasiOrdering)
(disjointWith Incorporation-Physical BusinessRelationshipActivity)
(comment AnthropologicalStudy "A study of a group of people.")
(disjointWith AtomicNucleus Metal)
(disjointWith Gardening ShootingAProjectileWeapon)
(comment netMigrationRate "(#$netMigrationRate PLACE RATE) indicates the balance between the number of persons entering and leaving a region. It is most common to express RATE in terms of number per thousand people.")
(comment TerminatingProtectionistPolicies "The collection of events where one state terminates its protectionist economic policies.  This is viewed as a negative economic event since the state is terminating 'protection'.  This may be incorrect in some cases.")
(comment programCopyRunningOn "(#$programCopyRunningOn PROGRAM SYSTEM)   means that PROGRAM is an instance of #$ComputerProgramCopy, SYSTEM is an instance of   #$ComputationalSystem, and that an instance of (#$RunningVersionFn PROGRAM) is running on SYSTEM.")
(comment DiplomaticRequest "The collection of actions in which one country or international organization makes a request to another country or countries through diplomatic channels.")
(comment CharacterStringMode-Sounded "A specialization of #$CharacterStringMode each 
  instance of which is the collection of all of the sounded 
  tokens of some particular abstract character-string.  
  Examples include the collection of all sounded tokens 
  (see #$CharacterStringToken-Sounded) of the string 'hello'.")
(disjointWith MilitaryWithdrawal MilitaryInvasion)
(comment Emulsion "The collection of all instances of one liquid (or more than one) dispersed in another.  At least two of these substances are immiscible.")
(comment FalxCerebri "The collection of all falx cerebrii.  An instance of #$FalxCerebri is the part of the #$DuraMater which separates the two #$CerebralHemispheres.  It is a unique part of a #$Brain.")
(comment salientDifferenceBetweenSiblings-Inverse "(#$salientDifferenceBetweenSiblings-Inverse COL1 COL2 COL3 BINPRED) means that while for any given instance, INS1, of COL1 there will be an instance, INS3, of COL3 such that (BINPRED INS3 INS1), this does not hold for instances of COL2 that are not instances of COL1, these instances will not be related to any instance of COL3.  See also #$salientDifferenceBetweenSiblings and #$salientDifferenceBetween.")
(comment eventSupports "If there is a propositional precondition PRECON for SIT2 such
that SIT1 causes PRECON to become true, then (#$eventSupports SIT1
SIT2).")
(comment ICQSkin "The collection of custom 'skins' for #$ICQ-TheProgram.")
(disjointWith BackupTapeManager Minister-Governmental)
(comment PullingOneselfTowards "Applying force to an object (#$pullee) to tend to move it towards the #$puller, yet the #$pullee remains fixed (in the inertial reference frame) and the #$puller moves towards the #$pullee.")
(comment ReverseListFn "The function #$ReverseListFn applied to a #$List, as in (#$ReverseListFn LIST), results in the same list, but in reverse order.  For example, if LIST is (#$TheList A B C A D), then (#$ReverseListFn LIST) = (#$TheList D A C B A).")
(comment Bazooka-3point5InchM20 "The collection of all M20 #$Bazookas.")
(disjointWith ElectricalResistance Temperature)
(comment absolute-PreconditionFor-PropSit "A specialization of the predicate #$preconditionFor-PropSit needed for the external problem solver.")
(disjointWith Dock Quarry)
(comment explicitlyIndicatedProduct "(#$explicitlyIndicatedProduct PRSN PROD-TYPE) means that the customer using the CYC ProductAdvisor interface has explicitly indicated a positive interest in purchasing an instance of the instance of #$ProductType PROD-TYPE for the #$Person PRSN. For example, a positive response to a question of the form, 'Are you interested in toys?' would result in the following assertion being made in #$TheSessionMt, (#$explicitlyIndicatedProduct #$TheRecipient #$Toy). Assertions using this predicate are the strongest positive indication of the suitability of a #$ProductType for a recipient and also represent that the justification for this assertion is that the customer has told us she is interested in this #$ProductType.")
(comment TerrestrialPlanet "The collection of all #$Planets which are composed primarily of #$SolidTangibleThings.  #$TerrestrialPlanets are standardly smaller than #$GasGiants.")
(comment Locomotion-SolidSurface "The collection of all locomotion events in which the locomotor moves along, and is supported by, a #$SolidTangibleThing. Includes walking, slithering, somersaulting, etc.")
(comment CharacterMode-Sounded "A specialization of #$CharacterMode each instance of    which is the collection of all of the sounded character tokens    of a some particular abstract character.  Examples include    the collection of all sounded tokens (see #$CharacterToken-Sounded)    of the numeral '0'.")
(comment HospitalID "The collection of all #$IDStrings used to distinctively identify hospitals.")
(comment Vampire "The collection of all vampires - mythological creatures (perhaps animated corpses) that bite the necks of their human victims and drink their blood. The victims then turn into vampires themselves. Vampires can be 'killed' by driving a stake into their hearts or cremating them, sleep in coffins during the daytime and are active only at night, and have a strong aversion to sunlight and garlic.")
(comment infectionHostType "#$infectionHostType HOST TYPE means that HOST is the host of an
infection of the type TYPE. See #$infectionHost.")
(comment HumanParenting "The collection of all events in which a #$HumanAdult who has the legal authority to do so raises a #$HumanChild.")
(comment externalParts "(#$externalParts OBJ PART) means that OBJ has PART as one of its external #$physicalParts. See #$surfaceParts, an important specialization of #$externalParts, for parts which do not extend from one side to the opposite side of ARG1.")
(comment keStrongSuggestionPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate (q.v.) and specialization of #$keRelevantPreds that relates a collection to a binary predicate.  (#$keStrongSuggestionPreds COL BINPRED) means that for every known (i.e. Cyc-reified) instance INST of COL, it is strongly suggested that there be some reified THING such that (BINPRED INST THING) is known in the Knowledge Base.  See also #$keWeakSuggestionPreds and #$keStrongSuggestionInverse.")
(comment beliefs-Microtheory "(#$beliefs-Microtheory AGENT MT) means that AGENT's beliefs include all of the propositions in MT.")
(comment typesSimilarWRTTypeViaBinRel "(#$typesSimilarWRTTypeViaBinRel SIMCOL1 SIMCOL2 COL3 BINPRED) means that any two instances of SIMCOL1 and SIMCOL2, THING1 and THING2, will be such that  (#$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel THING1 THING2 COL3 BINPRED).  See the comment on #$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel for further discussion.")
(comment LocomotionEvent-Animal "A specialization of #$LocomotionEvent, #$AnimalActivity, #$SingleDoerAction, and  #$PurposefulAction.  In each instance of #$LocomotionEvent-Animal,  the object moving (see #$objectMoving) is an instance of #$Animal.   Notable specializations of #$LocomotionEvent-Animal include  #$Climbing, #$Swimming-Generic, and #$WalkingOnTwoLegs.  Other  specializations include types of events, such as single-person canoeing and  #$Skating, in which a person moves himself or herself using a  device to which s/he supplies the motive force.  Note that instances of locomotion of several animals working together; e.g., tandam bicycling, a crew team rowing a boat, running a three-legged race; are not instances of this collection.")
(comment FactoryBuiltHome "The collection of all homes that are wholly or partially made in factories. This includes everything from #$MobileHomes, which are complete when they leave the factory, to #$PreCutHomes, which are essentially home-building kits with the lumber cut to the right size.")
(comment WebHostingServiceCompany "A collection of service-providing businesses. Each #$WebHostingServiceCompany, provides to its clients a #$WebHosting service. That is, the clients' websites are kept on the #$WebHostingServiceCompany's servers.")
(comment Ondansetron "The chemical compound which is an anti-emetic.")
(comment speechPartPreds "This predicate expresses the relation between parts of speech and the corresponding syntactic predicates.  The first argument is a part of speech, i.e., a collection that is a specialization of #$SpeechPart. The second argument is a #$SpeechPartPredicate (q.v.).  For instance, (#$speechPartPreds #$CountNoun #$singular) means that the predicate #$singular only applies to words that have #$CountNoun forms.")
(comment priceChargedFor "(#$priceChargedFor PLACE PRODUCT-TYPE MONEY-RATE) means that MONEY-RATE is the price at which PRODUCT-TYPE is sold in PLACE.")
(comment H-TheLetter "The letter H of the alphabet.  This is 'H' (or 'h') as an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract (more specifically a #$RomanLetter) rather than the any physical #$WrittenCharacter or other #$CharacterToken.   As such, this individual is oblivious to the distinction between uppercase and lowercase.  See also #$LatinCapitalLetterH and #$LatinSmallLetterH.")
(comment InherentlyVulgarWord "The collection of all words that are considered vulgar, no matter in what sense they are used. These are words that most people avoid saying in front of their mothers or religious leaders, in a job interview, or on a first date, and some people avoid using altogether. These words have inherent shock value in most social settings, and heavy use of them can cause a television show or movie to be rated inappropriate for young viewers. Words like #$Ass-TheWord and #$Bitch-TheWord are not #$InherentlyVulgarWords, because they have word senses that are not vulgar.")
(comment Pound-Cyprus "Major unit of currency of Cyprus")
(comment girlfriend "(#$girlfriend PERS FEM) states that PERS and FEM are involved in a romantic relationship with each other.  They interact fairly frequently.  Such interaction may range from just talking (as in a long-distance relationship) to dating, sexual activity, or cohabitation.")
(comment Catalase "A collection of the enzyme catalase.  These iron-containing
enzymes catalyze the decompisition of hydrogen peroxide into water and
oxygen.  It is found in almost every cell, except for certain
#$AnaerobicBacterium-Oxyphobic.")
(comment ComicBookIssue "The collection of all #$MagazineIssues of #$ComicBookSeries.  Each #$ComicBookIssue is instantiated in many copies.")
(comment geopoliticalSubdivision "(#$geopoliticalSubdivision BIG SMALL) means that the #$GeopoliticalEntity SMALL is a part of the larger #$GeopoliticalEntity BIG.  The territory (see the constant #$TerritoryFn) of SMALL is a geographical sub-region (see the predicate #$geographicalSubRegions) of the territory of BIG.  The government (see the constant #$GovernmentFn) of BIG usually has some sovereignty over the government of SMALL.")
(comment MakingMusicalSound "The collection of acts of an agent producing #$Music sounds, including #$Singing, #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument, and #$Whistling-Human.  The production of music by a mechanical device not directly controlled by an agent (such as a radio speaker or a water-powered prayer wheel) is not a member of this collection, but of the more general #$ProducingMusicalSound.")
(comment PragmaticAttribute "Attributes which have to do with pragmatic aspects of language such as formality and politeness.")
(comment AH-1J-Helicopter "The #$Collection of Bell AH-1J Sea Cobra #$AttackHelicopters.")
(disjointWith BiologicalToxin LivingBiologicalAgent)
(comment RouterWithDirectedBroadcastingEnabled "The collection of all network routers which forward incoming packets whose destination address is the broadcast address on that router.")
(comment AccessingSensitiveData "This is the collection of events in which sensitive data is accessed by an  unauthorized agent usually by exploiting some hole in the security which  protects the data.")
(disjointWith EndogenousInfection ExogenousInfection)
(disjointWith Spacecraft RotaryWingAircraft)
(comment WouldModeFn "(#$WouldModeFn SCRIPTTYPE CONTEXT-MT) denotes the      subcollection of SCRIPTTYPE whose instances possess the modal property denoted by \"would\", from the perspective of CONTEXT-MT.")
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion CelestialRegion)
(comment ApplyingObjectToSurface "A collection of events. In each ApplyingObjectToSurface event, a physical object is attached to a surface.  Important subcollections of this are #$MountingOntoSurface, #$ApplyingAdhesiveBackedMaterialToSurface, and #$SpreadingSheetOntoSurface.")
(comment MuscularDystrophy "Hereditary disorder marked by the progressive degeneration of the muscles")
(comment conceptuallyRelated "This predicate is used to state the fact of a conceptual link between two things, where a very complex sentence would be required in order to describe the precise nature of this link explicitly.  Examples of such conceptually-linked couples include #$PublicTransportationDevice / #$PublicTransportationScheduleDocument and #$Dog / #$DogFood.  The rationale for having such a predicate as #$conceptuallyRelated is similar to that behind many #$RuleMacroPredicates (q.v.).  Having complex relationships represented -- possibly redundantly -- in a more compact fashion makes for faster retrieval. Because things can be conceptually related in many different ways, no explicit definition for this predicate is provided.  Note that #$conceptuallyRelated is _not_ a #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate (q.v.); but see #$conceptuallyCoRelated for a specialization of this predicate that is symmetric.")
(comment IncreaseEvent "The collection of #$Events the focal characteristic of which is a increase in some quantity.")
(comment packetsTransferred "(#$packetsTransferred TRANSFER PACKETS) means that in the

#$InformationTransferEvent TRANSFER, the #$Packet-Networks PACKETS

are transferred.")
(comment antiInfectiousDrugWithRespectTo "(#$antiInfectiousDrugWithRespectTo DRUG_TYPE ORG_TYPE) means that #$DrugSubstances of DRUG_TYPE are used to prevent or fight infections caused by organisms [#$Organism-Whole] of ORG_TYPE.")
(comment FuelSupplyGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which are concerned with producing or acquiring supplies of fuel adequate for use by a country's populace and industries.  This is an especially important goal for industrialized countries.")
(comment basicSpeechPartPred "This predicate asserts the relation between parts of speech and their

\"basic\" forms, i.e., the forms from which other regular forms are

predictable.  For instance, since the regular #$plural of a

#$CountNoun is predictable from the #$singular, it is the case that

(#$basicSpeechPartPred #$CountNoun #$singular).")
(comment InformationDesignationType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$InformationDesignationType is a
collection of attributes.  These attributes are those designations or classifications of 
information that are part of some recognized classification scheme.  For instance, the collection 
#$GovernmentInformationDesignation is an instance of #$InformationDesignationType.  
Instances of #$GovernmentInformationDesignation are attributes of information that are part of
US government's scheme of classification, eg, #$TopSecretInformation.  Other examples include 
#$CorporateInformationDesignation, #$GovernmentAffiliatedInformationDesignation, and others.")
(comment TractoredFieldArtilleryUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of all military units trained and equipped for handling artillery           pieces that must be towed into position by other equipment.")
(comment Gadolinium "The collection of all pieces (i.e., specific collection of nearby molecules) of gadolinium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment enables-StaticConduciveFactor "This predicate represents the idea that an agent may be enabled
to do something not by the occurrence of an event, but simply by finding
herself, more or less statically, in a certain situation. Example: having
residence in midtown Manhattan enables one to attend performances of the
Metropolitan Opera, in the sense of making it more likely that one would be
capable of attending such a performance than if one would be if she were,
say, in Austin. Therefore, (#$enables-StaticConduciveFactor SIT AGENT
ACT_TYPE) means that SIT makes it more likely that AGENT would succeed at
an instance of ACT_TYPE were she to attempt than it would be otherwise --
i.e., if SIT did not obtain.")
(comment USMarinePersonnel "#$USMarinePersonnel is the collection of all officers and enlisted personnel of the #$UnitedStatesMarineCorps.")
(comment ComputerProcess-SingleCPU "The subcollection of #$ComputerProcess-SingleComputers
that are executed on a single CPU.")
(comment ImmediateWeatherProcess "A specialization of #$WeatherEvent. Each instance of  #$WeatherEvent is a meteorological event of a duration shorter than a seasonal process.  A particular hurricane event, for example, might be characteristic of a seasonal process for a region; but the hurricane event itself is an instance of #$ImmediateWeatherProcess.  Another example of an instance of #$ImmediateWeatherProcess is a single #$LightningEvent.  (Cf. #$AnnualClimateCycle.)")
(comment episodes "(#$episodes CWSERIES CONCEPTUALWORK) means that CONCEPTUALWORK is one of the episodes or issues making up the #$ConceptualWorkSeries, CWSERIES.  For example, (#$episodes #$LordOfTheRings-Trilogy #$TheFellowshipOfTheRing-Novel) means that _The Fellowship of the Ring_ is an episode in the Lord of the Rings trilogy.")
(comment EnglishAffix "The set of lexical items which may be concatenated with other
morphemes in the inflectional or derivational morphology of English.")
(comment IndependentMovie "An instance of #$MovieTypeByGenre.  #$IndependentMovies are movies which are not produced by big Hollywood producers and directors, but rather by unknown or novice filmmakers.  #$IndependentMovies are often entered into competitions such as the Sundance Film Festival.")
(comment asymTestPred "Prototypical instance of #$AsymmetricBinaryPredicate, to
be used for testing purposes.")
(comment InhalationalInfectionType "A collection of collections of #$Infections. Instances of this collection are types of infections that are commonly acquired by inhalation of infective particles. Often, but not invariably, instances present clinically with symptoms affecting the #$RespiratorySystem such as #$DifficultBreathing, #$Cough-AilmentCondition, or (#$PainInFn #$Chest-BodyPart).")
(comment SmugglingFn "A unary function that returns the class of events in which instances of the function argument are smuggled.  For example, (#$SmugglingFn #$Anthrax-Bacterium) returns those events in which #$Anthrax-Bacterium are smuggled.  This function is particularly useful for type-level claims about certain kinds of events (e.g., (#$subEventTypes (#$SmugglingFn STUFF) (#$ObtainingFn STUFF))).")
(comment HeatProductionProcess "A heat production process such as condensing, freezing, or oxidation.")
(comment TVShowHost "Each #$TVShowHost is a person who is a continuing presence on television shows which have varying content and varying personnel on the show.  Typically, game shows, talk shows, music video shows, and any program that shows several short (shorter than the entire program) pieces of content will have a host.  The role of the host could be to introduce the various segments of the show, to interview guests, or to act as moderator.")
(comment Scotobacteria "A collection of #$Bacterium in a #$BiologicalClass in the #$MoneraKingdom.  It contains many human pathogens such as #$VibrioCholerae-Species.")
(comment CertificateOfDepositAccount "The collection of #$AuthorizedAgreements under which a #$FinancialCompany accepts a deposit of a certain amount of money and issues in return a #$CertificateOfDeposit, typically entitling the holder to payment of the original amount plus interest after the passage of some amount of time.")
(comment KnowledgeManagement "See the note for #$KnowledgeManagementProgram.")
(comment Aztreonam "A chemical compound which is used in injectable antibiotic products.")
(comment mediaProductTypeDuration "This predicate specifies the time interval during which types of #$MediaProducts are available.  (#$mediaProductTypeDuration PRODUCT-TYPE TIME) means that a person who is in the right place during TIME (cf. #$mediaProductTypeLocation) can access instances of PRODUCT-TYPE, which is a #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType and a collection of #$MediaProducts.  For example, the #$mediaProductTypeDuration of a daily newspaper would be one day from its publication.  The #$mediaProductTypeDuration of a radio program would be the #$duration of the broadcast.")
(comment Property "This is the collection of all things which are owned. Members of this collection may be tangible, such as real estate, or intangible, such as the rights to produce a movie based on a particular book.")
(comment StaffOrganization "The collection of all groups of military officers such that serve as the staffs of units, i.e., as advisory staff for the unit commander.")
(disjointWith GovernmentMilitaryOrganization RegionalGovernment)
(comment vulnerableTo "(#$vulnerableTo THREAT-OBJ OBJECT HARM-TYPE) means that THREAT-OBJ poses harm of type HARM-TYPE to OBJECT when the two are appropriately situated.  In other words, when THREAT-OBJ can affect OBJECT, it is likely that OBJECT will be damaged in some way.  However, OBJECT's vulnerability persists even if it never happens to be affected by THREAT-OBJ.  The point of stating blanket object-object vulnerabilities is to facilitate the representation of vulnerabilities that transcend particular situations.  However, reference to a situation is required to draw specific conclusions about increased likelihood of damage, for it is not until the objects are related in a designated situation that we can draw significant inferences about fluctuating likelihoods.")
(comment GeographicalDirection-Direct "A specialization of #$GeographicalDirection whose instances are precise, as opposed to general, directions.  For example, #$North-Directly is due north.  Compare #$GeographicalDirection-General.")
(comment AuditoryNerve "The collection of all auditory #$Nerves.  Each #$AuditoryNerve is a #$CranialNerve innervating the #$InnerEar which transmits signals concerned with hearing and balance to the #$Brain")
(comment RelationalStructure "A specialization of #$MathematicalObject.  Each instance of #$RelationalStructure
is a mathematical structure that is a composite individual consisting of (i) a base set (see #$baseSet) and (ii) one or more relations or operations on that 
set (and, optionally, one or more selected other sets, relations, functions, or individuals).  Specializations of #$RelationalStructure include 
#$MathematicalOrdering and #$Multigraph (qq.v.).  Mathematicians sometimes 
specify a given relational structure as a #$Tuple (q.v.) of sets, relations, 
functions, and/or individuals.  Note that a relational structure is not the 
same as its base set, since a pure #$SetOrCollection necessarily lacks the 
associated \"structure\".  See also #$structureRelations and #$structureFunctions.")
(comment AutomaticFirearm-BlowbackOperated "The collection of #$AutomaticFirearms that use the blowback system  for automatic loading and firing.  Before firing, the breechblock is not  actually locked to the barrel.  On firing, the strength of the spring, the  inertia of the breechblock and sometimes a simple retarding device delay the  extraction of the empty case until the barrel pressure is down to a safe  level.  Nevertheless it is gas pressure which operates the operating cycle, not recoil.")
(comment ChemicalReaction "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$PhysicalTransformationEvent.  Each instance of #$ChemicalReaction is an event in which two or more substances undergo a chemical change, i.e., some portions of the substances involved are transformed into different #$ChemicalSubstanceTypes.  The transformations are brought about by purely chemical (including biochemical) means which affect chemical bonds between atoms in the molecules of stuff, rather than by physical means, biological means, or purposeful planning, etc.  Examples of #$ChemicalReaction: instances of #$CombustionProcess; instances of #$Photosynthesis-Generic.")
(comment regionProduces "(#$regionProduces REGION PRODUCT-SPEC) means that           PRODUCT-SPEC is a type of product produced in REGION.")
(comment TimeOfDay-7AM "The collection of time intervals one hour long beginning at 7AM.")
(comment CaudateNucleus "The collection of all lentiform nuclei.  An individual #$CaudateNucleus is an arch shaped #$BasalNucleus which is connected to both the #$LentiformNucleus and #$Amygdala its #$CerebralHemisphere.")
(comment intendedSoleFunction "A specialization of 

both #$soleFunction and #$intendedPrimaryFunction (qq.v.) 

that is used to indicate the sole use a given artifact 

(see #$Artifact-Generic) was designed to serve.  

(#$intendedSoleFunction ARTIFACT SITTYPE ROLE) means that (i) the

sole function of ARTIFACT is to play ROLE in situations of 

the type SITTYPE and (ii) ARTIFACT was intended by its designer 

solely to play ROLE in SITTYPEs.  For example, the causing fluid

to move (see #$providerOfMotiveForce) in #$ConveyingMaterials 

events is arguably the intended sole function of a #$Pump-Mechanical.

If a given artifact has, or might have, more than one intended 

primary function, consider the more general predicate 

#$intendedPrimaryFunction.")
(comment AssessingEnemyCOA "A collection of processes.  Each instance of #$AssessingEnemyCOA
is an instance of #$AssessingWhatAnAgentWillDo in which what is evaluated 
is the course of action of the enemy.")
(comment maxNrOfPassengers "(#$maxNrOfPassengers VEHICLE NR) states that the number of #$passengers (not #$crewMembers) is NR. In a military context this is often referred to as 'infantry dismounts' or 'cavalry scouts' depending what type of vehicle we are considering. ")
(comment ResistorProcess "All the inheritance from 2.terminal etc has to be done properly. The bound values have been made local and ?r added. The correct thing shud be (?x ?r) and not (?x ?r ?i1 ..)")
(comment ConstrainedMultirevolutionRotation "Multirevolution rotation constrained by a physical boundary either external or internal")
(disjointWith USFederalGovernmentOrganization USStateGovernmentOrganization)
(comment PressRelease "A #$PressRelease is a #$Statement that is directly communicated to #$ThePress with the intent that #$ThePublic have access to (possibly we should strengthen `have access to' to `recieve' the information.")
(comment AmericaOnlineService "The collection of instances of #$InternetService that are provided by #$AmericaOnlineInc, as part of its 'AOL Interactive Services' product line. This service includes email, Web access, and proprietary chat rooms and other content.")
(comment PayingCasualUseFee "#$PayingCasualUseFee is the collection of events in which one agent pays a fee to another in exchange for the right to use something that the latter controls Examples: paying a parking fee, paying a bridge or highway toll, paying an admissions fee to an art museum.  #$PayingCasualUseFee covers usage that is temporary and possibly not exclusive.  For longer-term use arrangements, see #$Renting.  Note: events in #$PayingCasualUseFee are both payings and collectings (cf. #$Buying).  The agent doing the paying is the #$buyer, and the agent doing the collecting is the #$seller.  The object accessed is the #$objectPaidFor.")
(comment CollidingWithAnObstacle "A specialization of #$Colliding.  Each instance of #$CollidingWithAnObstacle is an event in which an agent collides with something theat has \"gotten in its way\".  Note that since this collection is a specialization of #$Colliding (and thus of #$ContinuousPhysicalContactSituation),  the collider and the obstacle are in physical contact throughout the duration of each instance of this event.")
(comment keGenlsWeakSuggestionPreds "A #$KEFacilitationPredicate and a specialization of #$keGenlsRelevantPreds (q.v.).  (#$keGenlsWeakSuggestionPreds COL BINPRED) means that for every specialization SPEC of COL, it is weakly suggested that there be some VALUE such that (BINPRED SPEC VALUE) is known in the KB.  See also #$keGenlsStrongSuggestionPreds.")
(comment holdsInTypeOfPlace-Everywhere "(#$holdsInTypeOfPlace-Everywhere MT PLACE-TYPE) means that assertions in MT hold throughout the entire spatial extent of every instance of PLACE-TYPE.  See also #$holdsInTypeOfPlace-Somewhere.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice RecordingOfWaveIBT)
(comment Pass-Geographical "a passage through an topographical obstruction (e.g., mountains)")
(comment GrenadeLauncher "A specialization of #$ProjectileLauncher.  Each instance of #$GrenadeLauncher is a hand-held, portable gun-like device that shoots #$RifleGrenades.")
(comment ErasingAMark "A specialization of #$PurposefulPhysicalAction, #$RemovingSomething and #$PhysicalDestructionEvent.  Each instance of #$ErasingAMark is an event in which a mark is destroyed.")
(comment MultiIndividualAgent "The collection of all #$Agent-Generics that each consist of other #$Agent-Generics operating together.  Usually the constituent agents form some kind of #$Group that itself acts as an #$Agent-Generic.  Examples: a #$LegalCorporation, a #$GeographicalAgent, a #$Neighborhood or an #$Industry-Localized.  Although it would be a positive exemplar of (#$GroupFn #$Agent-PartiallyTangible), the 'group of people whose first names all start with the letter 'B'' is a negative exemplar of #$MultiIndividualAgent. In almost all contexts, such a group will not act as an #$Agent-Generic in any way.  It is less cohesive than some of the least cohesive kinds of #$MultiIndividualAgents such as #$CrowdOfPeople.")
(comment HypotheticalContext "A #$MicrotheoryType.  Each instance of  #$HypotheticalContext consists of assertions that are posited strictly for the purpose of exploring their consequences, without alleging their actual truth.   A hypothetical context can be used to analyze hypothetical outcomes of actions or to examine the hypothetical consequences of assuming some theory to be true.  Also, various alternative choices might be asserted, each in its own hypothetical context, so their ramifications can be generated and compared.")
(comment MarketFn "An instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction and #$TernaryFunction. #$MarketFn takes as its arguments a product type, an instance of #$TimeInterval, and an instance of #$GeographicalRegion, and returns an instance of #$Market as its value. (#$MarketFn PRODUCT TIME REGION) returns the instance of #$Market for PRODUCT during TIME in REGION. For example, (#$MarketFn #$LamborghiniP400Car (#$YearFn 1999) #$Albania) denotes the market for Lamborghini P400's in Albania in 1999.")
(comment productCompetitors "(#$productCompetitors ARG1 ARG2 ARG3) means that the agents ARG1 and ARG2 are competing to be the providers/sellers of a product type ARG3. ")
(disjointWith EONodeRawMeaningDefined EONodeLevelSkipped)
(comment rents "The predicate #$rents relates an agent to something that the agent is renting.  (#$rents AGENT OBJ) means that the #$SocialBeing AGENT is renting the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ from some other agent; that is, AGENT is paying the other agent for temporary use and enjoyment of OBJ.  See also #$TemporaryUserRightsAgreement, #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights, #$Renting, #$rentingOf.")
(disjointWith EONodeRawMeaningDefined EONodeIgnored)
(disjointWith EONodeRawMeaningDefined EONodeNotHandledYet)
(disjointWith EONodeRawMeaningDefined EONodeDefined)
(disjointWith EONodeDefinedButNeedsDeeperKE EONodeRawMeaningDefined)
(comment ProductFeature "All the features of products, from dual-overhead-cams to battery-powered.  Saying a product x has a particular feature is simply shorthand for saying that a certain proposition P(x) is true.  Thus, for each instance of #$ProductFeature, we will have a rule to state (#$hasProductFeatures x F) => P(x) for each P associated with F.")
(disjointWith EONodeNeedsDeepKE EONodeRawMeaningDefined)
(disjointWith EONodeNotHandledYet EONodeIgnored)
(comment Suicide "A specialization of #$HumanActivity, #$KillingByOrganism, #$SingleDoerAction, and #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$Suicide is an event in which a person intentionally causes its own death.")
(disjointWith EONodeNotHandledYet EONodeRawMeaningDefinedButNeedsDeeperKE)
(comment SponsorFn-AgentType "#$SponsorFn-AgentType takes as argument any spec AGENTTYPE of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of all agents sponsoring any instance of AGENTTYPE in some instance of #$Action.  For example, (#$SponsorFn-AgentType #$Athlete) returns the collection of all agents sponsoring any athlete.")
(disjointWith EONodeNotHandledYet EONodeLevelSkipped)
(disjointWith EONodeNotHandledYet EONodeDefined)
(disjointWith EONodeNeedsDeepKE EONodeNotHandledYet)
(disjointWith EONodeLevelSkipped EONodeRawMeaningDefinedButNeedsDeeperKE)
(disjointWith EONodeIgnored EONodeRawMeaningDefinedButNeedsDeeperKE)
(disjointWith EONodeDefinedButNeedsDeeperKE EONodeRawMeaningDefinedButNeedsDeeperKE)
(disjointWith EONodeLevelSkipped EONodeIgnored)
(disjointWith EONodeIgnored EONodeDefined)
(disjointWith EONodeNeedsDeepKE EONodeIgnored)
(comment OrigamiFoldingEvent "The events in which a piece of paper is folded onto itself several times so as to assume a recognizable ornamental shape.")
(disjointWith EONodeNeedsDeepKE EONodeLevelSkipped)
(disjointWith EONodeLevelSkipped EONodeDefined)
(comment knowsContentsOfMt "(#$knowsContentsOfMt AGT MT) means that the #$IntelligentAgent AGT knows the propositional contents of the #$Microtheory MT.")
(comment FortTheShelterRegion "Forts are analogous to campuses, or even miniature villages.  They usually consist of a high stone wall enclosing an area with various buildings.  There is often a watchtower.  They were built to protect people from invaders.")
(comment BestAnimatedShortFilm-MotionPicture "The collection of all academy awards given in the category ")
(comment ExtremelyToxic-HodgeAndSternerScale "An instance of #$Toxicity. A type of substance is #$ExtremelyToxic-HodgeAndSternerScale if it has a toxicity rating of 1 on the Hodge and Sterner scale of toxicity classes.")
(comment DonorFn-AgentType "#$DonorFn-AgentType takes as argument any spec AGENTTYPE of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of all #$LegalAgents who donate money, goods, or services to any instance of AGENTTYPE. These donations are typically #$CharitableDonations intended to benefit the instance of AGENTTYPE who receives them. For example, (#$DonorFn-AgentType #$Museum-Organization) denotes the collection of all #$LegalAgents who donate money, goods, or services to any museum. If the money, goods, or services are donated as part of a marketing strategy designed to benefit the donating agent, then the donating agent will be an instance of (#$SponsorFn-AgentType AGENT) not (#$DonorFn-AgentType AGENT).")
(comment ModeratelyToxic-HodgeAndSternerScale "An instance of #$Toxicity. A type of substance is #$ModeratelyToxic-HodgeAndSternerScale if it has a toxicity rating of 3 on the Hodge and Sterner scale of toxicity classes.")
(comment BestOriginalScreenplay-MotionPicture "The collection of all academy awards given in the category ")
(comment HighlyToxic-HodgeAndSternerScale "An instance of #$Toxicity. A type of substance is #$HighlyToxic-HodgeAndSternerScale if it has a toxicity rating of 2 on the Hodge and Sterner scale of toxicity classes.")
(comment PracticallyNonToxic-HodgeAndSternerScale "An instance of #$Toxicity. A type of substance is #$PracticallyNonToxic-HodgeAndSternerScale if it has a toxicity rating of 5 on the Hodge and Sterner scale of toxicity classes.")
(comment Format "A collection of argument entry-formats that can be  specified for #$Predicates with respect to particular argument-places (see #$argFormat).  An argument entry-format is a kind of restriction on  a predicate regarding how many things, or the range of things, that the  predicate holds of with respect to a given one of its argument-places.  More  precisely: given any particular way of fixing the arguments in the rest of  the predicate's argument-places, the entry-format tells us something about  the number of different things, or the range of things, that can occupy the  given argument-place such that the relation holds of those arguments.  That is, supposing the given argument-place is the Nth, the entry-format tells us  something about the number or range of different sequences of arguments  of which the predicate holds and that differ from each other only in their Nth items.  For example, the format #$SingleEntry (q.v.) is used to state  that in every case there is at most only one such sequence, the format  #$SetTheFormat (q.v.) to state that there is no particular (upper or lower)  limit to the number of such sequences that applies to every case, and the  format #$IntervalEntry (q.v.) to state that the Nth items of any two such  sequences must be #$ScalarIntervals that \"intersect\" (see #$quantityIntersects). Thus, the first argument-place of #$biologicalMother has the format (see  #$arg1Format) #$SetTheFormat, since a given female animal might have any  number (including zero) of offspring; but the second argument-place of  this predicate has (see #$arg2Format) #$SingleEntry format, since any  given animal has at most (in fact, exactly) one biological mother.  And  the format of the second argument-place of #$bodyTemperature is #$IntervalEntry because, while a given creature (at a given moment in time) has a single  exact (see #$ScalarPointValue) body temperature, we want the predicate #$bodyTemperature to be flexible enough to allow us to specify this  temperature with varying degrees of precision (e.g. as \"98.6 degrees Fahrenheit\" or as \"between 98 and 99 degrees\" or as \"less than 100 degrees\").  See the various instances of #$Format for further details.  See also #$ArgFormatPredicate.  Note that, in contrast with what #$ArgTypePredicates  are used for, specifying an argument entry-format for a predicate does  _not_ impose any sort of necessary condition for semantic well-formedness.   A violation of a legitimate entry-format constraint necessarily involves  two or more statements, and at least one them must be _untrue_;  but there is no implication that any of them is malformed.")
(comment Agent-PartiallyTangible "The collection of all #$Agent-Generics that are also instances of #$PartiallyTangible.")
(disjointWith PhysicalPartOfObject Agent-PartiallyTangible)
(disjointWith FluidTangibleThing Agent-PartiallyTangible)
(disjointWith CelestialRegion Agent-PartiallyTangible)
(comment PlayingFn "(#$PlayingFn GAME) returns the collection of instances of #$PlayingAGame of type GAME performed by players or competitors.  For example, (#$PlayingFn #$Monopoly-TheGame) returns the collection of actions, including instances of #$ThrowingADie or moving a piece, performed by one or more players while playing #$Monopoly-TheGame.  Note that the game does not ever have to be completed for these actions to be part of the playing of the game.  The predicate also applies to non-game sports (see #$Sport).  To refer to a complete game being played use the more specific function, #$GameFn.")
(comment SomeFn "(#$SomeFn COL) denotes a term which represents an instance of COL which is expected to be a representative exemplar of at least one but not necessarily all elements of COL.  See also #$EveryFn, #$GenericInstanceFn and #$ArbitraryInstanceFn.")
(comment ArbitraryInstanceFn "A unary #$ReifiableFunction used to represent an arbitrary individual belonging to a given collection. (#$ArbitraryInstanceFn COLLECTION) denotes an instance of COLLECTION which is arbitrary in the sense that any properties it instantiates can be assumed to be instantiated by every member of COLLECTION. (It thus has a great deal in common with #$EveryFn, except that the latter is unreifiable). See also #$GenericInstanceFn.")
(comment legalOwnerOf "(#$legalOwnerOf OWN OBJ) means that OWN is the legal owner of OBJ.  To be the #$legalOwnerOf implies more than just full or #$ExclusiveUserRights.  If an owner lends or rents out the object then, during that time period, the owner does not have full rights to that object.")
(comment dedicatedToAgent "(#$dedicatedToAgent AGENT ACT DEDEE) states that AGENT, who is performing ACT, is dedicating ACT to the agent DEDEE.")
(comment EveryFn "(#$EveryFn COL) denotes a term which represents an instance of COL which is a representative exemplar of every instance of COL.  This function is not a #$ReifiableFunction, since it primarily exists to support queries about properties that apply to all instances of a given collection. See #$ArbitraryInstanceFn, #$GenericInstanceFn and #$AnySpecFn for similar concepts, and #$SomeFn for a related function.")
(comment TransportationOfWeaponTypeFn "(#$TransportationOfWeaponTypeFn WEAPON-TYPE) refers to the collection of all events in which an instance of WEAPON-TYPE is an #$objectMoving in some #$TransportationOfWeaponToTarget event.")
(comment EssentialAminoAcidType "A collection of collections.  An instance of an #$EssentialAminoAcidType is a collection of #$AminoAcids that can not be sythesized by the body and is necessary for life.  These amino acids are obtained from the diet.  See also #$NonessentialAminoAcidType.")
(comment GenericInstance "#$GenericInstance is the collection of all terms in the language intended to represent generic instances of particular collections (cf. #$GenericInstanceFn).")
(comment NonessentialAminoAcidType "A collection of collections.  An instance of #$NonessentialAminoAcidType is a collection of #$AminoAcids that is synthesized by the human body and is not specifically required in the diet.  See also #$EssentialAminoAcidType.")
(comment AminoAcidTypeByChemicalSpecies "This type level collection (see #$CollectionType) is a partition on #$AminoAcid: each instance (each \"cell\" in the partition) is one of the cardinal specializations of #$AminoAcid whose instances serve as building blocks of proteins: e.g., Alanine, Cysteine, Aspartic Acid, Glycine, etc.")
(comment AsMuchAsFn "(#$AsMuchAsFn PROP STUFF-TYPE) denotes the level of property PROP that all STUFF-TYPE has")
(comment GenericInstanceFn "A unary #$ReifiableFunction used to represent a generic individual belonging to a given collection. (#$GenericInstanceFn COLLECTION) denotes an instance of COLLECTION which is generic in the sense that it possesses all the qualities had by paradigmatic, typical or normal instances of that collection.  For example, (#$GenericInstanceFn #$Cat) represents a cat with whiskers and a tail, even though certain actual cats lack these anatomical parts. See also #$SomeFn and #$ArbitraryInstanceFn.")
(comment AstronomicalSatellite "The collection of all artificial satellites (#$Satellite-Device) which are designed for collecting data on celestial and astronomical phenomena.")
(comment Wolf "The collection of all wolves; a subset of #$CanineAnimal.  By default, members of #$Wolf are elements of #$WildAnimal.  Wolves are not included in the collection #$Dog.  The collection #$Wolf does not correspond to any biological taxon.  Note that members of the collection #$Wolf-Red are included in this collection as well as members of the collection #$Wolf-Gray.")
(comment HKLM-Software-Microsoft-WindowsNT-CurrentVersion-Winlogon-Directory "The #$Collection of all HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\WindowsNT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\ directories (instances of #$ExecutableRegistryKey) found on NT machines.")
(comment LegOfPieceOfFurniture "A leg of a table; one of those parts that supports the table top.")
(comment VentralRamusT8 "The collection of all T8 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT8 and #$DorsalRamusT8 branch from SpinalRootT8.  #$VentralRamusT8 supplies below the #$EighthRib.")
(comment ProsciuttoHam "The collection of prosciutto hams. Prosciutto is an Italian salt-cured ham which is usually served in very thin slices.")
(comment accountForSystem "A predicate relating instances of #$ComputerAccount with instances of #$AccountSystem.  (#$accountForSystem ACCOUNT SYSTEM) means that ACCOUNT is an account in the account system SYSTEM (which may  allow logging in to one individual computer or to many).")
(comment SheetMetal "Any kind of metal that has been formed into a sheet.")
(comment Zebrafish "A species of small fish which is used extensively in

genetics research.")
(comment LispPackage "Family of software packages incorporating Lisp.")
(comment DiningRoomChair "The sort of chair that is found at a table intended for eating.")
(comment ProximalDirection "The general direction towards the center of the body and away from the extremities, or towards some other central reference point, such as the #$Heart (for objects in the #$CirculatorySystem) or the #$Brain (for objects in the #$NervousSystem), in or near an object with #$AnimalBodyShape.  This is a #$VectorInterval comprising a roughly cone-shaped set of vectors; note that its direction is dependent both on the location and on the types of objects involved.")
(comment preface-DocumentPartOf "(#$preface-DocumentPartOf WORK PREFACE) means that the #$DocumentStructure PREFACE is contained within the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK and is a preface within that work.  Prefaces precede the body of a work, are written by the author or authors of the main propositional content of the work, and often set forth the origins or purpose of the work, the subjects covered, and the audience for which the work is intended. For prefatory textual material that is written by a person other than the author of the work in which the prefatory material is contained, see #$foreward-DocumentPartOf.")
(comment GuyanaPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Guyana, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment frontOrganizationFor "'(#$frontOrganizationFor GENCOSOLIVEOIL MAFIA)' means that the #$Organization GENCOSOLIVEOIL acts as a front organization (i.e. it secretly represents the interests of) the #$IntelligentAgent MAFIA.  #$Organizations that act as #$frontOrganizationFor can be legitimate businesses or organizations (an anonymous donor sets up a charitable organization through which his philanthropic activities are conducted) or can be organized in order to hide illegal or illegitimate activities.")
(comment CosmeticsBag "This is the collection of luggage-like

bags designed to hold cosmetics and to go into luggage.")
(comment Algonquian-WakashanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally from mid-continent northwards")
(comment Filament-LightBulb "The metal part inside of a light bulb that glows when the bulb is turned on.  Not a part of flourescent light bulbs.")
(comment ManipulatingWithFingers "Manipulating an object in a dexterous manner with at least two fingers: for instance, manipulating the pins while changing a diaper, cleaning contact lenses, buttoning a shirt....")
(comment Pork "The collection of all pig meat. This collection includes raw meat as well as cooked, smoked, and/or salted meat.  Raw pork is not ready to be eaten.")
(comment DistributionOrganization "A collection of organizations; a subset of #$ServiceOrganization.  An element of #$DistributionOrganization is an organization that distributes things (in #$DistributionEvents) as a service for (and normally paid for by) their customers.  An element of #$DistributionOrganization may be among the #$subOrganizations of a larger #$Organization.")
(disjointWith HarvesterAgriculturalImplement Wheelchair)
(disjointWith OperatingSystem OperatingSystemKernel)
(comment AirHeatingDevice "The collection of devices used to heat the air in humanly-occupied constructs. Different from ovens and hair dryers, whose primary functions are NOT to heat the air, but to heat something else.")
(comment BiologicalSubdivision "A more specific partition than Biological Division; more general than Biological Class.")
(comment NuclearExplosion "Explosion involving the release of nuclear energy via nuclear fission, nuclear fusion, or both.")
(comment CombustibleFuelSubstance "The substances usually used as fuels.")
(comment AnimalTypeByMaturity "A #$DisjointCollectionType and a 
specialization of #$LifeStageType.  #$AnimalTypeByMaturity has as its
only instances #$AdultAnimal and #$JuvenileAnimal. This collection-type 
strictly facets (see #$facets-Strict) #$Animal.")
(comment ImageFileCopy "#$ImageFileCopy is the specialization of #$ComputerFileCopy whose instances contain images as the encoded data.")
(comment PhonoCable "The kind of cable used to connect stereo components to each other.")
(comment CompletedRegistrationOfGuest "The signed contract of a hotel guest registering in that hotel")
(comment Sternum "The #$Collection of all breastbones (or #$Sternums/sterna).  An individual #$Sternum is a #$Bone-BodyPart connecting the two #$RibSeries in the front of the chest and protecting the #$Heart and other organs inside the chest region.")
(disjointWith Paper TextileArtifact)
(comment Pug-TheDog "A collection of small to medium-sized dogs with short fur and black muzzles.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup TransportationOrganization)
(comment CatLitter "Each instance of #$CatLitter is some quantity of particulate matter intended to be placed in a box on the floor (see #$LitterBox), for indoor #$DomesticCats to go to the bathroom in.  #$CatLitter has been traditionally made of absorbent clay particles, but newer versions of the product are made of other materials; some are designed to clump into balls around the waste and be flushed down the toilet.")
(comment ExtensorDigitiMinimi "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExtensorDigitiMinimi #$Muscle.  The #$ExtensorDigitiMinimi extends the #$ProximalPhalanx of the #$LittleFinger.")
(comment PlasticGroceryBag "The collection of plastic grocery bags")
(comment BiologicalLivingObject "The collection of all structures that are composed of one or more living cells (see #$Cell).  Biological living objects (or \"BLO\"s) might either be instances of #$Organism-Whole (like dogs or pine trees) or components of such whole living organisms (like noses, tails, and pine needles).  The healthy leg of a living person is a BLO (as is the person), but an amputated leg is not a BLO.  Almost every instance of #$BiologicalLivingObject is either capable of biological reproduction itself or has components which are capable of biological reproduction (such as the cells in a living arm).  Red blood cells are abnormal instances of BLO in that they cannot reproduce.")
(comment AnteriorMarginOfLung "The collection of anterior margins of #$Lungs, the front angular edges ('corners' or 'crests') of #$Lungs, each of which divides the #$CostalSurfaceOfLung from the front #$MedialSurfaceOfLung.")
(comment DessertFood "A collection of tangible stuff.  Each instance of #$DessertFood is an item of food which, in its prepared state, is customarily eaten by people as part of the #$DessertCourse of a meal.  For example, (in #$NorthAmericanCuisine,) ice cream, cake, pie.")
(comment Laundromat "A localized (one site) service organization that allows customers to rent the use of washing machines and clothes dryers.")
(comment TrojanHorseComputerProgram "The class of #$ComputerProgram-CWs which pretend to be innocent, and quite useful, but in matter of fact are malicious in intent, do not perform their overt functionality, but often sabotage the user's computer or compromise his/her system security. Examples include fake login-screens that solicit passwords from naive users, and game programs that scrub one's hard-disk.")
(comment CocaPlant "Member of species Erythroxylon coca.")
(comment LeaseDocument "A specialization of #$ContractDocument. Each instance of this collection is a document signed by the two parties in a #$RentalAgreement, signifying the agreement. The terms of the agreement are stated in the document's PIT (#$PropositionalInformationThing).")
(disjointWith Bulb-ThePlantPart Root)
(comment PolishPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Poland, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AngoraWool "A very warm wool derived from #$AngoraRabbits.")
(disjointWith Fox Wolf)
(comment Ampersand-TheSymbol "The ampersand or '&' symbol, as an abstract character (#$Character-Abstract).  It has been traditionally used in texts to mean 'and', but it has other uses in computer languages.")
(comment PlasterBoard "A board used in large sheets to cover walls and ceilings as a substitute for plaster.")
(comment outputsOfSynthesis "(#$outputsOfSynthesis SYN OUTPUT) says that

 OUTPUT was the result of the synthesis of two or more

 things in the synthesis event SYN.")
(comment PositionInputDevice "A device used for accepting positional input from a computer user.")
(comment HosingSomethingOff "The collection of events in which some object is sprayed with water using a hose, usually a #$GardenHose. The purpose is usually to clean or rinse the object off, as in hosing off a sidewalk or a dirty lawn chair.")
(comment WildAnimalFn "A function that returns collections of un-domesticated, as-found-in-nature animals. For example, (#$WildAnimalFn #$Dog) denotes the collection of all wild dogs. See also #$WildPlantBLOFn.")
(comment Peeps-TheConfection "Instances of this collection are (ostensibly) edible snacks
composed of spun sugar and dye, and usually molded in the shape of
various iconic animals related to the #$SpringSeason and the
#$EasterHoliday.")
(comment VentralRamusC6 "The collection of all C6 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC6 and #$DorsalRamusC6 branch from SpinalRootC6.  #$VentralRamusC6 supplies the #$BrachialPlexus.")
(comment Duck-Meat "Raw duck meat.")
(comment similarWRTTypeViaBinRel-Inverse "This predicate is the 'inverse' version of

#$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel, in that (#$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel-Inverse THING1 THING2 COL PRED) means that if there is an instance of COL, COLINS1 such that

(BINPRED COLINS1 THING1) then either (BINPRED COLINS1 THING2)

or there is some similar instance of COL, COLINS2, such that (BINPRED

COLINS2 THING2).")
(comment Cruise-Vacation "The collection of all #$VacationTrips by sea taken for pleasure")
(comment ComputerProgrammer "A specialization of #$ComputerUser.  Each instance of this collection is an agent (usually a #$Person) who programs computers in some capacity -- professional or otherwise. See also #$programsIn, #$ComputerLanguage.")
(comment Distiller-Device "an apparatus used for distillation")
(comment Spore-PlantLifeStageFn "(#$Spore-PlantLifeStageFn BLO_TYPE) returns the collection of all spores of instances of the class of of #$BiologicalLivingObject BLO_TYPE.")
(comment ResidentialPhoneDirectory "A sub-collection of #$TelephoneDirectory. Each #$ResidentialPhoneDirectory lists #$PhoneNumbers for #$HumanResidences. The listings are generally sorted alphabetically by the #$familyName of the head of household.")
(comment BodyOfHand "The main body of a hand, excluding the fingers")
(disjointWith HouseholdAppliance NavigationDevice)
(comment FrenchPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$France, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment TelevisionSetTypeBySize "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$TelevisionSet whose instances are all of the same size.")
(comment encryptionAlgorithms "(#$encryptionAlgorithms ENCRYPTED ALGORITHM) means that ENCRYPTED contains some information which has been encrypted according to the #$EncryptionAlgorithm ALGORITHM.")
(comment WaxedCardboardCarton "A cardboard bax with a wax coating on the interior.")
(disjointWith Braking ComingHomeFromWork)
(disjointWith Tail-BodyPart Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(comment FoodIngredientOnly "A specialization of #$EdibleStuff.  Each instance of #$FoodIngredientOnly is an edible substance that is used in making other food but isn't eaten by itself.  Instances of #$FoodIngredientOnly may or may not require some preparation.  For example, #$TableSalt, #$VegetableOil, and #$Ketchup are specializations of #$FoodIngredientOnly, since all of their instances are used only as ingredients or condiments.   In contrast, #$Egg-Chickens is not a specialization of #$FoodIngredientOnly; some of its instances serve as ingredients in cooking other dishes, but other instances are simply eaten after poaching or frying.  Types of food, such as #$Pizza, whose instances are never merely ingredients, are specializations of #$Food.")
(comment FaxMachine "The collection of all fax machines: machines used for the transmission-and-reproduction of hardcopied printed matter.")
(disjointWith IntrinsicStateChangeEvent Talking)
(comment AuricleOfHeart "Receiving chamber of the heart")
(comment ElectricalOutlet "A place to plug in a power cord; a source of electrical current; usually on a wall of a building.")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType LifeStageType)
(comment KanaCharacter "characters composed of few strokes and used in writing Japanese")
(comment Rivet "A strong solid fastening rod with a flattish head on one end.  It is put through a hole in the object(s) to be fastened, and the other end is flattened to form the connection.")
(comment ProductDisplayOrganization "The collection of #$Organizations that, though they   might sell something, primarily serve to put    items on display for the public.  Major specs    include #$Museum-Organization and #$Library-Organization.")
(disjointWith Climbing Locomotion-Air)
(disjointWith Metal Styrofoam)
(comment Quarterhorse "Instances of #$Quarterhorse are characterized by their ability to run very fast for short distances; they were particularly bred to run quarter-mile races.")
(disjointWith InsuranceProvider RepairAndMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment DoublingCube "The collection of cubical blocks with the numbers 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, and 64 marked on its faces, used in a game of Backgammon for keeping track of the increase in stakes of a game and the player who has the right to make the next double.")
(comment contaminatedWithMicroorganismType "(#$contaminatedWithMicroorganismType STUFF MICROTYPE) means that the #$PartiallyTangible STUFF is

contaminated with #$Microorganisms of the type MICROTYPE.")
(comment Pisiform "In humans the #$Pisiform bone is in the #$Carpus, articulating with the #$Triquetrum.")
(comment ToasterOven "A small electric oevn that can be used to toast bread, heat up leftovers, etc.")
(comment InferiorGlutealNerve "The collection of all inferior gluteal nerves.  The inferior gluteal nerve is formed by the #$VentralRamusL4, #$VentralRamusL5 and #$VentralRamusS1 and supplies the#$GluteusMaximus.")
(comment RomanoGeneric-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Romano-type cheese.

 These are sharp, aged, cheeses made for grating. They are made from differnt sorts of milk.")
(comment GIFFile "A collection of #$ComputerImageFiles. Each #$GIFFile is encoded in the \"Graphics Interchange Format\". #$GIFFiles are extremely common for inline images on web pages, and generally have filenames that end in \".gif\".")
(comment PhotoFlashBulbAttachment "A camera attachment that holds photo flash bulbs and controls the timing of the flash.")
(disjointWith ReferenceWork Screenplay)
(comment DescendingAorta "The collection of all descending aortas.  A #$DescendingAorta is the section of an #$Aorta following the #$AorticArch.  The #$DescendingAorta is comprised of the #$ThoracicAorta (above the diaphragm [#$Diaphragm-BodyPart]) and the #$AbdominalAorta (below the diaphragm).")
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice ComputerHardwareItem)
(comment NamibianPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Namibia, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment BabyProductMarketCategory "Includes products which are intended to be used by, for, or with #$HumanInfants or #$HumanToddlers.")
(comment HuaveLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment DiningRoomTable "A table used in the dining room for taking one's meal on.")
(comment ShippingAndReceivingDepartment "A specialization of #$Department. Each instance of this collection is an organization's centralized office for dispatching (material) items to the outside world, and also accepting them as they come in.")
(comment TelevisionTuner "Television tuners do for television signals what radio tuners do for radio broadcasts.")
(comment Sprite "The collection of instances of Sprite")
(comment smells "(#$smells AGENT OBJECT) means that AGENT perceives the physical object or event OBJECT via the sense of smell.  This implies that OBJECT releases (or involves the release of) a scent (see #$Odor) of which AGENT is sensuously aware.  In the situation described by \"Joe smells the coffee brewing\", both of the following are true: (#$smells Joe Coffee01) and (#$smells Joe CoffeeBrewingEvent09).")
(comment Vertebrae "#$The #$Vertebrae is the #$Series of individual #$Vertebra in #$The #$SpinalColumn.")
(comment SouthAsianCuisine "The collection of instances of what many Americans tend to think of as Indian food")
(disjointWith HouseholdAppliance TransportationDevice-Vehicle)
(disjointWith ChemicalReaction TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment PowerSaw "Devices that do the sawing for you! Table saws, chain saws, etc.")
(disjointWith AccessingAnIBT Conveying-Generic)
(comment StatementOfHoursAccruedForm "The collection of documents in which an employer informs its employee of how many hours towards vacation/emergency time have been used during a given time period and how many remain.")
(comment Exoskeleton "An external supportive covering of an arthropod")
(comment NovaScotiaDuckTollingRetriever "A collection of medium-sized dogs.  Members of this breed are also called           Tollers or Duck Tollers.")
(comment CongoPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of  #$Congo-Brazzaville, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment RealEstateOrganization "The collection of all Organizations that are primarily or significantly engaged in the real estate industry or whose activities focus on that industry. There are many instances of overlap between instances of #$FinancialOrganization, #$InsuranceOrganization, and #$RealEstateOrganization (e.g., #$PrivateMortgageInsurer, #$MortgageLender).")
(comment ExternalCombustionEngine "The collection of #$Engines in which the

 ignition occurs outside the chamber where

  heat is converted to mechanical energy.")
(comment MedialBasalSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all medial basal segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of right #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a right #$InferiorLobeOfLung that supplies the #$MedialBasalSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung.  It branches from the right #$InferiorLobarBronchus.  (There is no #$MedialBasalSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung in the left #$Lung.)")
(comment Receiver-AudioComponent "The receiver component of a component stereo system. Other #$AudioSystemComponents outputs feed into the #$Receiver-AudioComponent which in turn drives the #$AudioSpeakers.")
(disjointWith MakingAGesture Murder)
(comment AnteriorTibialArtery "The collection of all anterior tibial arteries.  The #$AnteriorTibialArtery connects to the #$PoplitealArtery at its proximal end and supplies the #$LowerLeg, #$Ankle and foot (#$Foot-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment Bread-Wheat "bread")
(comment DownloadOfFn "A function that takes an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW and returns the collection of all #$DownloadingAFile events in which instantiations of that program are downloaded.")
(comment Cord-Textile "Those long, thin, flexible things which are made of textile fibers.")
(disjointWith Encrypting Decrypting)
(disjointWith TextileArtifact Shaft)
(disjointWith Pollen Fruit)
(comment LatinCapitalLetterK "The capital letter 'K'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$K-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterK.")
(comment StringInstrument "The collection of #$MusicalInstruments with strings which are made to vibrate (via bowing, plucking or striking) to produce sound.")
(comment Gesture "A specialization of #$VisualInformationBearingThing. Each instance of #$Gesture is a configuration of body parts (usually animal body parts) that has some meaning to an observer with an understanding (whether explicit or instinctive) of the interpretive convention. A gesture may include some tool or prop. #$Gestures may be fleeting (e.g., a hello wave) or may last a long time (e.g., the gesture embodied in the #$StatueOfLiberty ). Note that, as defined in #$Cyc, a gesture is a meaningful configuration of body parts, NOT the #$Actions producing the arrangement. For representation of the actions, see #$MakingAGesture.")
(comment ArabidopsisThaliana "Arabidopsis Thaliana is a small flowering plant which is widely used by plant science researchers as a model organism to study plant developmental

processes. It is a member of the Brassica family, like cabbage and radish. Arabidopsis is not of major agronomic significance, but it does have several

important advantages for the researchers in many areas of plant biology - especially genetics and molecular biology. Its advantages include a small

genome size (a haploid content estimated to be between 100 and 120 Mbp of DNA which is distributed among five chromosomes), a rapid life cycle

(about 6 weeks from seed to seed), easy cultivation in restricted space, prolific seed production, and a large number of mutant lines.")
(comment ServerRoom "#$ServerRoom refers to the collection of all rooms which are occupied by computer servers.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization SpeciallyCharteredInstitution)
(comment CommunicationsSatellite "The collection of all artificial satellites (#$Satellite-Device) which are designed for facillitating communications between locations on the #$PlanetEarth by receiving radio transmissions and retransmitting them for reception on Earth.  Individual signals may come from or be transmitted to other satellites, they do not need to be solely with ground stations.")
(comment HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE-SAM-Directory "The #$Collection of all HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SAM\\ directories found on NT machines.  Instances of this collection will have an instance of #$SAMFile as their value (i.e., as their #$fileContents).")
(comment Sofa-PieceOfFurniture "A piece of furniture used for seating that can hold more than one person comfortably; usually padded and fully upholstered [covered with fabric].")
(comment VentralRamusT2 "The collection of all T2 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT2 and #$DorsalRamusT2 branch from SpinalRootT2.  #$VentralRamusT2 sometimes supplies the #$BrachialPlexus and also below the #$SecondRib.")
(comment unauthorizedUserOfAccountSystem "(#$unauthorizedUserOfAccountSystem AGENT SYSTEM) means that AGENT is not authorized to use any account on SYSTEM.  That is, if the person in charge of maintaining SYSTEM were to find out that AGENT could get access to some account on SYSTEM, she would be perturbed.")
(comment NTUserPassword "Represents the password used by #$DisgruntledEmployee to log into #$UserAccountOnCycorpLAN-WindowsNT.")
(comment SaccharomycesCerevisiae "This is the collection of yeasts (individual yeast

organisms of various types, not the collection of types of yeasts).")
(comment StorageChest "A type of container which sits on the floor, and has a hinged lid.  Can be used as both luggage and as furniture. Pirates used them to store booty, Victorian maidens used them to store things for when they got married, travelers use them to carry their belongings while travelling, and many people nowadays use them to store blankets at the foot of a bed.")
(comment OrganSubPartType "The collection of all types of functional and discernible sub-parts of animal organs, each being smaller than its containing organ but larger than typical pieces of uniform tissue or cells.  This collection includes parts types like a #$Bronchiole or #$Alveolus of the #$Lung, but not any general #$OrganRegionTypes like #$ApexOfLung which refer to general directional regions of organs.")
(comment creatorOfPartOfWork "(#$creatorOfPartOfWork WORK DOCSTRUC AGENT) means that AGENT, an instance of #$IntelligentAgent, is the creator of that part of the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK that is represented in the #$DocumentStructure DOCSTRUC.  For example, forewards (see #$foreward-DocumentPartOf) that are parts of #$StructurallySpecificWorks are written by someone other than the author of the work.  Newspapers and magazines consist of articles authored by different individuals; the agent responsible for the creation of an individual article can be indicated by #$creatorOfPartOfWork.")
(disjointWith WindPoweredDevice WindupDevice)
(comment MalawiPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Malawi, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization "#$PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization is a specialization of #$HealthcareOrganization.  Each instance of #$PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization provides prescription drugs to members of the general public.  This collection does not include drug manufacturing companies like Squibb or drug store chains like Walgreens.  Positive examples include the pharmacy within the Albertsons on Research Boulevard in Austin and a mail order prescription drug provider.")
(comment DoppKit "This is the collection of luggage-like

bags designed to hold men's toiletries and to go into luggage.

The name comes from a registered trademark for this sort of

bag.")
(comment Indo-EuropeanLanguageFamily "A #$LanguageFamilyType that is commonly spoken on all six populated continents.  It has eleven sub-families and most languages familiar to Americans are of this language family.")
(comment PowerCordExtension "If the #$PowerCord of a device use this (which is not part of the device) to cover the missing distance.")
(comment SugarFreeEdibleStuff "This is the attribute possessed by foods that contain no sugar (often merely no #$Sucrose or #$Glucose.  These foods often contain a sugar substitute such as #$Aspartame or #$Saccharin.")
(comment Department "The collection #$Department is a subset of #$Organization.  An element of #$Department is a major sub-organization of a business, government, or academic organization.  An element of #$Department is part of the organization to which it belongs, NOT a separate legal entity (such as a partly or wholly owned subsidiary company), and it performs some of the activity of that organization.  In Cyc, the collection #$Department includes generically what may be called a division, department, office, bureau, ministry, etc., within an actual organization.  Common types of departments include those represented by the subsets #$LegalDepartment, #$SecurityDepartment, #$PayrollDepartment, #$AccountingDepartment, #$HumanResourcesDepartment, #$AcademicDepartment, and CustomerServiceDepartment (and many others).")
(comment ProjectileLauncher "#$ProjectileLauncher is a specialization of #$Conveyance-Stationary and #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$ProjectileLauncher is a physical device used to launch a #$Projectile-Device. A few notable specializations are #$Slingshots, #$Guns, and #$MissileLaunchers. The launcher and projectile start out at the same location, possibly even as parts of the same object, but once the projectile is fired it leaves the launcher. ")
(disjointWith ApplicationProgram OperatingSystemKernel)
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization FinancialOrganization)
(comment Cattle "All types of animals that can be referred to as 'cattle'; includes buffalo, cows...")
(comment InternalCombustionProcess "The collection of all events in which a #$CombustionProcess is taking place inside an #$InternalCombustionEngine.")
(comment Trunk-BodyCore "#$Trunk-BodyCore is a specialization of #$ExternalAnatomicalPart and #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$Trunk-BodyCore is a body core of a vertebrate.  A #$Trunk-BodyCore is the main portion of the animal's body, generally located centrally, and one can conceive of an animal's body as a #$Trunk-BodyCore to which are connected the head and various appendages which together make up the entire body.  To refer to a human #$Trunk-BodyCore use the more specific term, #$Torso.")
(comment CellularProteinSynthesis "the final subevent of a #$GeneExpression, in which the protein is produced.")
(comment FormattingADisk "A collection of actions performed by computers. In each instance of #$FormattingADisk, a #$Computer prepares an instance of #$ComputerDisk to have data written to it under a particular file system. After the event, the disk will be recognized by computers that use the file system for which the disk was formatted as a readable, blank disk.")
(comment CrimpingTool "The tool used to fasten crimp connectors, also called crimping pliers.")
(disjointWith BorderCheckEvent SkyDiving)
(comment CompletedRegistration "The contract binding some client registering to use a service -- like hotel guests, car rental agreements, hospital registration")
(comment ContainerLid "A specialization of #$PortalCovering. Each instance of this collection is a covering used to seal some kind of #$ContainerArtifact.")
(comment SpinalColumn "The #$SpinalColumn includes every #$Vertebra and the spinal discs.

 It provides the main support of the #$Torso and #$Head-Vertebrate")
(disjointWith CookingVessel TextileArtifact)
(comment Pomeranian-TheDog "A collection of very small dogs.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment LitterBox "Each #$LitterBox is a rectangular box, 4 or 5 inches tall and on the order of a foot-and-a-half long and wide, open on the top, desgined to contain #$CatLitter so that indoor #$DomesticCats can go to the bathroom there.")
(comment Popliteus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Popliteus #$Muscle.  The #$Popliteus initiates flexion of the #$Knee by rotating the #$Tibia.")
(comment TrashBag "The collection of trash bags")
(comment InferiorMarginOfLung "The collection of inferior margins of #$Lungs: each is the bottom angular edge ('corners' or 'crests') of a #$Lung, towards the edge of the diaphragm, and which divides the #$CostalSurfaceOfLung from the #$BaseSurfaceOfLung.")
(comment Milano-ItalianCuisine "A style of #$ItalianCuisine associated with #$CityOfMilanItaly.")
(comment LocalBank "An organization which is a local customer point of contact, and which offers banking services.")
(comment CountNoun-Generic "The collection of all count nouns. This collection also includes proper count nouns like 'Rolodex', agentive count nouns like 'teacher', etc.")
(comment CottonPlant "Individual cotton plants; their seeds have long hairs on the seedcoat which are cototn fibers.")
(disjointWith OfficialDocument Currency)
(comment CerebrospinalFluid "The collection of all volumes of cerebral spinal fluid.  Each instance is a portion of fluid that circulates in an #$Animal's #$CentralNervousSystem or that has come from such a place.")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice AirTransportationDevice)
(comment ChadPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Chad, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith Jackal Dog)
(comment MinusSign-TheSymbol "The minus sign symbol as an abstract character (#$Character-Abstract) in some mathematical character set.  Used to indicate subtraction, or a negative number.  Contrast with #$Hyphen-TheSymbol.")
(comment Pipe-Plumbing "The old familiar water pipe found in the plumbing of buildings.")
(comment interArgNotGenl "(#$interArgNotGenl PRED FIRST-ARG FIRST-COL SECOND-ARG SECOND-COL) means that, when a spec of FIRST-COL appears as argument # FIRST-ARG to PRED, argument # SECOND-ARG in that assertion is constrained not to be a spec of SECOND-COL and vice versa.")
(comment DigitizingTablet "A computer device which consists of a pointer (usually a pen or a puck) and a specialized electronic surface.  When the pointer is near the surface, transmits position data relative to the surface to its host.  Pointers usually have one or more buttons the user can push.")
(comment GardenHose "The set of #$Hoses intended for use in watering lawns or similar areas.")
(comment Worm "The collection of all worms; a subset of #$Animal.  Each element of #$Worm is a long, thin, flexible, tubular or thread-like or ribbon-shaped animal (excluding eels, snakes, and limbless lizards); most worms are small or even microscopic.  The collection #$Worm includes members of numerous worm phyla (see #$BiologicalPhylum), for example,  Annelida (earthworms, etc.), Platyhelminthes (flatworms), Nematoda (nematodes), Nemertia, tapeworms, liver flukes, etc.  #$Worm also includes the vermiform larval stages of several species of #$Arthropod.  #$Worm is not a standard scientific category (see #$BiologicalTaxon).")
(comment BudweiserBeer "A premium lager, brewed and sold since 1876. Known as 'The King of Beers,' Budweiser is the largest-selling beer in the world.")
(comment VentralRamusS4 "The collection of all S4 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusS4 and #$DorsalRamusS4 branch from SpinalRootS4.  #$VentralRamusS4 supplies the #$SacralPlexus and the #$CoccygealPlexus.")
(comment CornishHen-Meat "Raw cornish hen meat.")
(comment ElectronicMusicalKeyboard "Instances are instances of #$Keyboard-MusicalInstrument which employ a standard musical keyboard, and where the musical tone produced by depressing any key is generated by an electronic rather than a purely mechanical process.")
(comment Sheetrock "Sheetrock")
(comment contactToxicityFor "(#$contactToxicityFor STUFF ORGTYPE TOXLEVEL) means that under ordinary circumstances, stuff has the #$Toxicity TOXLEVEL for instances of ORGTYPE that come into skin contact with it.")
(comment CalfMuscle "Muscle in the back of the lower leg")
(disjointWith Hat Mask)
(comment Daisy "plants in the aster order with yellow or white petals and usually a yellow center.")
(comment StVincentAndTheGrenadinesPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$StVincentAndTheGrenadines, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment MiniDiscPlayer "#$MiniDiscPlayers are devices which read and play

 music from #$MiniDiscs.")
(comment DentalDrill "A dental tool used for boring holes in objects by means of a rotating sharp-edged cylindrical bit.")
(disjointWith Trunk-TheAppendage Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(comment Salad "Different kinds of salads.  Green salad, potato salad, etc.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareOrganization DrugTestingOrganization)
(comment RollerSkate "The collection of all skates used for roller skating")
(comment Penis "The collection of all penises.  An instance of this collection is an external sex #$Organ of a male #$Mammal that is used in #$SexualCopulation and #$Urinating.")
(comment Horse-DomesticatedTypeByBreed "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$Horse-Domesticated whose instances are all of the same breed.")
(comment subStructures "'(#$subStructures WHOLE PART)' means that whatever instantiates the #$AbstractStructure WHOLE also instantiates the #$AbstractStructure PART.  For example, the #$MusicalText corresponding to the whole of a particular #$Symphony includes as one of its #$subStructures an instance of #$MusicalText that corresponds to the first movement of that #$Symphony.")
(comment TireRepairSubstance "Stuff you put in your tire to fix an air leak .")
(disjointWith LifeStageType BeliefSystemType)
(comment CyrillicLetter "characters adapted from Greek, originally devised for writing Slavic languages")
(comment WoodStain "Liquid applied to wood in order to change its color.")
(comment genFormat-ArgFixed "(#$genFormat-ArgFixed RELN ARG-NUM ARG-VALUE STRING LIST) means that when generating an English phrase from a formula whose operator is RELN and whose ARG-NUMth argument is ARG-VALUE, use STRING and LIST instead of what would be used based on the regular #$genFormat assertion.")
(disjointWith ThrowingAnObject Hitting-ProjectilePropelling)
(comment salientImagePathnamePrintString "(salientImagePathnamePrintString IMAGE PATH STRING) means that
IMAGE can be found at the location specified by #$Pathname PATH.  STRING can
be used to give a free-form description of the file IMAGE for reference.")
(comment LawnMower-TractorPulled "A collection of devices; a subset of #$LawnMower.  Each element of #$LawnMower-TractorPulled is a lawnmower which is pulled along by another vehicle (typically a #$Tractor) when it is used.  They are often used when large areas need to be mowed, e.g., a football field.")
(comment ThoroughbredHorse "The collection #$ThoroughbredHorse is not a specialization of #$Horse-WarmBlood.  Although it descended from instances of #$ArabianHorse and English ponies, it is considered pure bred.")
(comment Trapezius "#$The #$Trapezius is shaped like a triangle with its apex on #$The #$Scapula and its base on #$The #$SpinalColumn.  It can raise, lower, and rotate #$The #$Shoulder.   It consists of three parts, the Upper, Middle, and Lower Trapezius (so named because of their attachment locations of #$The #$SpinalColumn) which impart different motions to #$The #$Scapula.")
(comment WashingClothesInAMachine "Washing a load of clothes, towels, sheets, etc., in a #$ClothesWasher.")
(comment UpperSubScapularNerve "The collection of all upper subscapular nerves.  The upper subscapular nerve branches from the #$PosteriorCord-BrachialPlexus and supplies the subscapularis.")
(comment Provolone-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Provolone, a mild Italian melting cheese.")
(comment GIFFile-Animated "A collection of #$ComputerImageFiles. Each #$GIFFile-Animated contains a representation of a short sequence of images within a single #$GIFFile. When such a file is displayed, the #$ibtGenerated is a sequence of images, usually producing a simple animation effect.")
(comment PhotographicLightStand "A portable, collapsible rack for supporting lights that are used to illuminate something being photographed.")
(comment GameteFn "(#$GameteFn ORG-TYPE) denotes the class of #$Gametes which are produced for sexual reproduction by organisms of type ORG-TYPE.")
(comment hasLogo "this slot denotes the logo used to represent this unit.")
(comment ThoracicAorta "The collection of all thoracic aortas.  A #$ThoracicAorta is the section of an #$DescendingAorta following the #$AorticArch and preceding the diaphragm [#$Diaphragm-BodyPart].  The #$ThoracicAorta is continued by the #$AbdominalAorta below the diaphragm.")
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice MusicalInstrument)
(comment AntiguaAndBarbudaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$AntiguaAndBarbuda, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganismPartType AnimalTypeBySex)
(comment TotonacanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment BedCovering "The collection of stuff that is intended to cover one's bed.")
(comment programFoundOnComputer "This predicate relates computer programs to computational systems.  (#$programFoundOnComputer PROG COMP) means that a copy of PROG (see #$ComputerProgramCopy) is stored on COMP.  This predicate allows one to state that a copy of a program is on a computer without actually referring to the copy.  See also #$programCopyFoundOnComputer, which does require reference to a program copy.")
(comment HelpDeskSession "The collection of all help-desk sessions, in each of which a person manning a help desk tries to help someone by answering a question, supplying relevant documents, or referring the person to an expert.  This is usually done over the telephone or by email.  #$HelpDeskSession is a collection of individual #$Events.")
(comment CadillacAllanteCar " the Cadillac convertible Allante")
(comment TastePerception "The collection of sensory #$Perceivings in which a #$PerceptualAgent #$tastes some object, by means of the appropriate #$Sensor, and thereby acquires information about it.")
(comment CervicalVertebrae "#$The #$CervicalVertebrae is the #$Series of individual #$CervicalVertebra in #$The #$SpinalColumn.  There are seven in the human body (C1-C7).  The first two are #$The #$AtlasVertebra and #$The #$AxisVertebra.")
(comment ItalianCuisine "The collection of instances of what many Americans tend to think of as Italian food")
(disjointWith ChemicalReaction BodyMovementEvent)
(comment CarryingWhileLocomoting "A specialization of #$TransportationEvent. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some #$Animal moves by locomotion (cf. #$LocomotionProcess) while holding some physical object, so that the object also moves.  Examples include a person carrying a baby.  A negative example is a propeller plane towing a glider. Specializations of this collection include #$ServingFoodOrDrink and #$TakingOutTheGarbage. See also #$CarryingFn.")
(comment CreditCardAuthorizationForm "A collection of #$InformationBearingObjects. Each instance of #$CreditCardAuthorizationForm is an instance of #$Form-StandardizedIBO that is signed or electronically accepted when a credit card purchase is made. Such signature indicate that the account holder authorizes payment.")
(comment Horn-AnimalBodyPart "Hard protrusion from the head of an animal, usually made from bone or cartilage, or, in the case of the rhinoceros, tightly compressed hair")
(comment WelshCorgi-Cardigan "A collection of dogs.")
(comment RwandaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Rwanda, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith HealthcareOrganization RealEstateOrganization)
(comment SteamEngine "The collection of #$Engines that use steam

 to turn turbines or move pistons.")
(comment LingularBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of the lingular bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) in left #$Lungs.  This is a short #$BronchialTubeSegment intermediate between a #$LobarBronchus and a #$SegmentalBronchus.  It occurs only in the left #$SuperiorLobeOfLung and it leads down to the #$LingulaOfLeftLung.")
(comment RadioTuner "A collection of electronic devices. Each   radio tuner is capable of taking a radio signal from a radio   antenna, isolating that part of the signal corresponding to a   frequency, and passing it on to an amplifier for sound playback.")
(disjointWith DentalCareEvent EyeCareEvent)
(comment PoplitealArtery "The collection of all popliteal arteries.  The #$PoplitealArtery connects at its proximal end to the #$FemoralArtery and branches into the #$AnteriorTibialArtery and #$PosteriorTibialArtery at its distal end.")
(comment HotCereal-Uncooked "Cereals such as oatmeal or cream of wheat, in their uncooked, granular or flakelike state.  For the cooked stuff, see #$HotCereal-Cooked.")
(comment AerosolCan "Aerosol spray can dispenser")
(comment bodyTemperature "The core temperature of an animal, as opposed to the skin temperature.")
(disjointWith ProductionEvent BiologicalEvent)
(comment Thermos "Containers for keeping liquids at almost their original temperature.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterK "The lowercase letter 'k'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$K-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterK.")
(comment PercussionInstrument "Musical instruments which are struck to produce a sound.")
(comment DivisionEquisetophyta "This is the collection of horsetails (plants,

not the tails of horses).")
(comment ComputerPrinter "The collection of computer hardware that is used for producing hard copies of text or images.")
(disjointWith LegalCorporation LimitedLiabilityCompany)
(comment SpySatellite "The collection of all artificial satellites (#$Satellite-Device) which are designed for collecting data for use by a #$GovernmentIntelligenceOrganization.")
(comment OrganismTypeByHabitat "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$OrganismTypeByHabitat is a collection of organisms (i.e., a specialization of #$Organism-Whole) all of whom share the same sort of habitat.  Instances of #$OrganismTypeByHabitat include #$AquaticOrganism and #$TerrestrialOrganism.")
(comment EditingARegistry "The collection of all events in which someone edits an instance of #$WindowsRegistry on some instance of #$Computer.")
(comment Desk-PieceOfFurniture "A special type of table used to support books, paperwork, etc, and at which a person sits to read or write.")
(comment DorsalRamusT8 "The collection of all T8 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT8 and DorsalRamiT8 branch from SpinalRootT8.  DorsalRamiT8 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment VeganCuisine "A type of cuisine that excludes all meat (including fish, poultry, and seafood) and all animal products (such as eggs, honey, and milk products).")
(comment PresuppositionVocabTerm "The collection of CycL terms

 that 

 enable a basic representation of commonsense knowledge 

that \"pack in\" or \"gloss over\" assumptions that, for a machine,

 would generally need to be made explicit.  By

 definition, instances of 

#$PresuppositionVocabTerm are axiomatically 

 related to other predicates that make all or most of

 the assumptions in such natural language expressions

 explicit.  Consider, for example, the Cyc treatment

 of statements about evidence, which (appropriately)

 involves ascribing an amount of evidence that an 

 #$IntelligentAgent has in support of some belief (see

 #$evidentialSupportForBelief).  However, in ordinary

 English, people who make statements about evidence 

generally do not make them in terms of agents or beliefs.

 Often, they make them in terms of an amount of evidence

 and some #$Individual or #$Collection (e.g., \"there

 is plenty of evidence for Nessie,\" \"there is no

 evidence of UFOs\").  Obviously, representing such compacted 

forms of knowledge about evidence using 

#$evidentialSupportForBelief is problematic.  Thus we

 need #$evidentialSupportForPhenomena-AgentUnspecified,

 which takes an amount and a collection -- and so 

 allows for representation of such commonly understood claims about

 evidence, and is understood by Cyc via axioms

 to the explicit, or 'longhand' CycL involving

 #$evidentialSupportForBelief.")
(comment authenticatorForAccountSystem "(#$authenticatorForAccountSystem COMP ACCT_SYS) means that, when a user logs into ACCT_SYS from some machine, the username and password the user logs in under are checked against the password file stored on COMP.")
(comment Ascomycota-Division "This is the division of the fungus kingdom containing

yeasts.")
(comment TrafficLight "A thing which usually hangs over roads near intersections and tells cars when they must stop, go, or slow.")
(comment SportsGame "The collection of all sports (instances of #$Sport) which are also #$Games.  See #$SportsEvent for events of playing whole units of such games and #$AthleticActivity for activity of the type engaged in while performing sports.")
(comment OrganRegionType "The collection of all named or designated types of regions of #$Animal #$Organs specified by general direction or main sector, rather than by specific functional and discernible substructures of the organs (for which, see #$OrganSubPartType). Examples include the #$ApexOfLung or the left hemisphere of the eye, rather than, say, an #$Alveolus or #$Bronchiole in a #$Lung or the iris of an eye, which are #$OrganSubPartTypes.")
(disjointWith LightingDevice Engine)
(comment PeaPod "The fruit of the pea plant; contains edible seeds [peas], and is edible when immature.")
(comment VanuatuPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Vanuatu, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith RetailPharmacyNetwork PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization)
(comment WalkingShoe "The collection of shoes designed specifically

for walking.")
(comment MigratoryAnimal "A subcollection of #$Animal; the collection of animals that change their dwelling place on a periodic, typically seasonal basis.  Such behavior is usually characteristic of particular types of #$BiologicalSpecies.")
(comment AfroasiaticLanguageFamily "group of languages indigenous to the Near East and northeast Africa")
(comment Flashlight "A small portable electric lamp powered by batteries.")
(comment CraftActivity "The collection of activities that are commonly known as crafts")
(comment ProfessionallyProducedProductFn "#$ProfessionallyProducedProductFn takes a #$ProductType as its argument, and returns the collection of such products produced by people who were paid to produce the product, i.e. by professionals. Most products that can be bought in stores would be such products. See also #$AmateurProducedProductFn.")
(comment PersonalizableWebPortal "A collection of #$WebPortals that permit the user to personalize or customize the #$WebPortal for his own interests or needs.  The #$PersonalizableWebPortal often has a different homepage from the main homepage of a #$SearchEngine.  For example, #$Yahoo-SearchEngine has different homepage from 'My Yahoo', which is an instance of #$PersonalizableWebPortal.  Yet, the instances of #$PersonalizableWebPortal are not collections of individualized #$WebPortals.  For example, #$Yahoo-PersonalizableWebPortal is not a collection containing Roland's MyYahoo or Michael's MyYahoo.  Instead, to create Roland's MyYahoo one would assert that Roland's MyYahoo is a #$WebPortal and is #$derivedConceptualWork from #$PersonalizableWebPortal.")
(comment RegularOven "This is the regular kind of oven heated by electricity or natural gas, into which you can fit pans and such.")
(comment TrueFungus "A collection of fungi.  #$TrueFungus contains the subsets #$Mushroom and #$Yeast.")
(comment serviceCeiling "(#$serviceCeiling CRAFT DISTANCE) means

  that the maximum #$altitudeAboveSeaLevel that

   CRAFT can fly is DISTANCE.")
(comment Torso "A specialization of #$Trunk-BodyCore.  Each instance of #$Torso is a human body's trunk, i.e., the main portion of a human's body, to which typically are connected a head and various appendages (see #$Appendage-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment CleaningSubstance "Cleaning aids of all types.")
(comment DeletingAFile "A collection of actions done by computers on files. In each instance of #$DeletingAFile, a computer changes the directory information on a #$ComputerDisk or other long-term storage medium so that the file that is the #$objectActedOn in the event is no longer represented as being stored on that disk, etc. Furthermore, the space on the disk that was used to store the file immediately before the event is designated immediately after the event as available to be written to. Note that in an instance of #$DeletingAFile it is necessary only that the disk directory be changed. The actual encoding of the file itself may or may not be changed. Thus a deleted file is sometimes recoverable.")
(comment SpeakerWire "The wire commonly used for connecting speakers to stereo systems.")
(disjointWith BiologicalEvent SkyDiving)
(comment AccountingReport "The collection of accounting reports, that is, at the most general level, reports (usually prepared by professional accountants) which describe the financial state of a person or organization")
(comment Jaw "Lower region of the head that moves when chewing food. NOT the Jawbone.")
(disjointWith RoomInAConstruction FurniturePart)
(comment Pekingese-TheDog "A collection of small, stocky dogs.")
(comment TransportationOrganization "Each instance of #$TransportationOrganization is an #$Organization that is primarily or significantly engaged in the #$TransportationIndustry or whose activities focus on that industry (whether or not the #$Organizations actually provide transportation services).  Examples of specializations of #$TransportationOrganization include #$AutoDealership, #$RailwayOrganization and #$TaxiCompany.   Both #$UnitedAirlines and #$USDepartmentOfTransportation are instances of #$TransportationOrganizations.")
(comment ConcentrationCamp "The collection of all concentration camps.  A concentration camp is a type of camp where large numbers of political prisoners or ethnic minorities are detained, often by military or executive order.  Such camps are often used as part of a 

campaign of political #$Persecution or a #$GenocideCampaign.  For Westerners, the term most vividly recalls the concentration camps set up by Nazi Germany during the #$NaziHolocaust.")
(comment VitaminD "#$Vitamin D is a group of fat-soluble hormones, calciferol (vitamin D2), cholecalciferol (vitamin D3), together with 7-dehydrocholesterol (vitamin D1), a precursor which is found in human skin and becomes vitamin D3 when exposed to ultraviolet light.")
(comment AnteriorCompartmentMuscleSet "The #$Collection of all #$AnteriorCompartmentMuscleSet  The #$AnteriorCompartmentMuscleSet controls dorsiflexion of the #$Ankle, #$Toe extension, and eversion and inverison of the #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart.  The #$AnteriorCompartmentMuscleSet includes the Tibialis Anterior, Extensor Hallucis Longus, Extensor Digitorum Brevis, Extensor Digitorum Longus, and Peroneus (or Fibularis) Tertius.")
(comment PaperGroceryBag "The collection of paper grocery bags")
(comment PosteriorMarginOfLung "The collection of posterior margins of #$Lungs, the rear and upper angular edges ('corners' or 'crests') of #$Lungs, each of which divides the #$CostalSurfaceOfLung from the rear of the #$MedialSurfaceOfLung.")
(comment Mustard-ThePreparation "The collection of all instances of a specific type of #$Condiment.  #$Mustard-ThePreparation is a #$Paste made from powdered musterd seeds mixed with #$Wine,#$Vinegar, and/or #$Water, and various #$Spices.")
(comment MetalWorkingShop "Local (one site) organizations that work metal (bend it, mold it, refinish it) for customers for a fee.")
(comment ReformulatorIrrelevantFORT "The collection of Cyc FORTs that are not relevant to the reformulator.")
(comment hasPhysiologicalConditionType "This type-level predicate relates an animal to a type of physiological condition it has.  

(#$hasPhysiologicalConditionType ANIMAL CONDTYPE) means that ANIMAL has CONDTYPE, which is equivalent to the strictly instance-level assertion that ANIMAL is the #$bodilyDoer of an instance of CONDTYPE.  For example, (#$hasPhysiologicalConditionType Fred #$Acne) means that Fred has acne.")
(comment Urine "Liquid waste created by the kidneys as they cleanse the blood of waste")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice WaterTransportationDevice)
(comment PortuguesePerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Portugal, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment productionsOfOutputType "#$productionsOfOutputType relates a spec of #$Product to the
collection of all instances of #$ProductionEvent that have instances
of that kind of #$Product as the #$outputsCreated.")
(disjointWith Coyote-Animal Dog)
(comment Umlaut-TheSymbol "A mark consisting of two dots side by side. When placed above a vowel, it indicates that the pronunciation is different.")
(comment GutterOnARoof "A trough attached to the roof of a house, designed to catch and transport rainwater.")
(comment VirtualMemory "#$VirtualMemory is a subset of #$ComputerMemory.  It

is a collection of expansions of the apparent size of RAM accomplished by

using part of ROM as an extension of RAM.")
(comment SiphonTube "A small tube used in siphoning liquids.")
(comment DrPepper "First made and sold in Waco, Texas in 1885, Dr Pepper is the oldest major brand soft drink in the United States of America.")
(comment AcousticNoiseLevel "The collection of attributes that describe the volume of a sound.")
(comment IliohypogastricNerve "The collectionof all iliohypogastric #$Nerves.  Each #$IliohypogastricNerve is connected to a #$VentralRamusL1 and #$innervates the posterior part of the #$TransverseAbdominous and the #$InternalOblique #$Muscles.")
(comment Shoebox "The collection of boxes for packaging instances of footwear")
(comment Cat "The collection of all members of the species Felis domesticus. Most members of this collection are #$DomesticCats, but feral cats are also included in this collection.  Big cats, e.g., lions, ocelots, or tigers, are not members of this collection, although they are of its superset, #$FelidaeFamily.")
(comment BuildingInsulation "thermal insulating material used in walls and roofs of buildings to prevent undesirable heat transfers")
(comment SacredText "The collection of all texts that are sacred to adherents of a #$Religion.")
(comment GluteusMaximus "Buttock muscle")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice SomethingToWear)
(comment Nectary "The nectar gland of a flower.")
(comment FrenchPolynesiaPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$FrenchPolynesia, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment ProfessionalOrganization "The collection of all #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnlys whose membership or ownership is distinguished by the fact that all such members or owners are professionals.  For example, #$DoctorGroup and #$LawFirm are both specializations of #$ProfessionalOrganization.")
(comment DentalTool "An object intended be used to perform a #$DentalCareEvent.")
(comment HeterosexualHuman "The collection of people who are sexually attracted primarily to members of the opposite sex.")
(disjointWith Tentacle Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization ManufacturingOrganization)
(comment VersionedProgram "A specialization of #$VersionedSoftwareObject and #$ComputerProgram-CW.  The collection of all instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW which represent programs that are in the most literal sense bought, downloaded, and run on a machine.  Positive examples: (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Linux-RedHat \"6.1\") (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$WU-FTPD-TheProgram \"2.5\").  Negative examples: #$Linux-RedHat, #$WU-FTPD-TheProgram.  The latter are instances of #$UnversionedProgram.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization SellingOrganization)
(comment BeachTowel "A larger-than-standard towel, intended for sitting on at the beach or pool and drying the body after swimming.")
(disjointWith ProjectilePropelling Talking)
(comment FallopianTube "The collection of all fallopian tubes.  Individual #$FallopianTubes are #$AnatomicalVessels connecting the region around an #$Ovary-AnimalBodyPart to a #$Uterus.  Ova (see #$Ovum), #$SpermCells (after #$SexualCopulation), and early #$Embryos (after fertilization) pass through the #$FallopianTubes.")
(comment FloorTile "The collection of all instances of #$Tile that are intended to be used as #$Covering-Objects for instances of #$FloorInAConstruction.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType HumanCapabilityType)
(comment CuneiformCharacter "characters composed of wedge-shaped strokes, used in ancient writing systems, esp. of and influenced by Mesopotamia")
(comment CarpentryTool "A collection of tools.  An instance of #$CarpentryTool is any tool (not limited to hand tools) that is used in carpentry.  Examples include table saws, jigsaws, hammers, woodworking tools, etc.  By default, a carpenter would be skilled at using such tools.")
(disjointWith MicroPhysicalEvent ArmMovement)
(comment objectStability "This predicate relates an object to its degree of stability.  Degree of stability can be interpreted as an indicator as to whether the object is likely to continue in its present form for some time barring extreme kinds of events.")
(comment GrassTrimmer "A collection of powered devices used to cut hard-to-get-at areas of grass and other kinds of short plants.  An early brand of #$GrassTrimmer was Weedeater.")
(comment HunterHorse "Instances of #$HunterHorse are usually suited for hunting and jumping sports.  The breed represented by #$HunterHorse originated in England and Ireland and was bred from female instances of #$Horse-WarmBlood (mares) and Thoroughbred stallions.")
(comment PoolBall "The collection of balls used in playing pool or billiards")
(comment Seal-Animal "Includes sea-lions and earless or 'true' seals.")
(comment Anconeus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Anconeus #$Muscle.  The #$Anconeus is an extender of the #$ElbowJoint.")
(comment WashingDishes "The collection of dishwashing events.")
(comment SpinalNerve "The collection of all of #$Nerves arising from a #$SpinalCord. There are 31 such pairs in a human body.")
(comment ParmesanGeneric-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Parmesan-type cheeses.

These are aged cow's milk cheeses in the style of #$ParmigianoReggiano-Cheese.")
(comment ComputerPatchProgram "#$ComputerPatchProgram is the collection of small computer programs which are used to update programs that are already installed on a computer.")
(comment WaterWell "a well for extracting groundwater")
(comment documentsImprovement "(#$documentsImprovement OBJ1 OBJ2 ASPECT EXP) says that the improvement in some ASPECT of OBJ1 over OBJ2 is described somehow by the expression EXP")
(comment CleaningImplement "A specialization of both #$HandTool and #$CleaningDevice.  Each instance of #$CleaningImplement is a hand-held tool used for cleaning something.  Notable specializations of #$CleaningImplement include #$Mop, #$DentalPick, #$WashCloth, #$FacialTissue, and #$ShoeBrush.")
(comment JordanianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Jordan-TheNation, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment accessoryFor-Activity "This predicate is analogous to

#$accessoryFor, except that it relates products to activities for

which they are considered accessories rather than to other products.

Note that the intended interpretation is weak (compare to #$accessoryFor-Strict).

Saying that (#$accessoryFor-Activity PRODTYPE ACTTYPE) means that for

every spec of PRODTYPE there is some spec of ACTTYPE such that all instances

of the former may be used in performing any instance of the latter.")
(comment HaidaLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of western North America")
(comment WoodenSpoon "a spoon made of wood used for cooking.")
(comment PresentationProgram "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used to create slide presentations.")
(comment AcademicDepartment "A collection of sub-organizations. Each instance of #$AcademicDepartment is a major subdivision of an educational institution, with the primary purpose of research and/or teaching related to a particular academic discipline or subject-matter. See also #$SchoolInUniversity-DegreeGranting.")
(comment CanisterVacuumCleaner "The set of all canister type vacuum cleaners.  If a #$VacuumingACarpet event occurs in a #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle, the #$deviceUsed is a #$CanisterVacuumCleaner.  #$CanisterVacuumCleaners are used when the #$objectActedOn is not a carpet, too, e.g. to vacuum up sawdust in the workroom.")
(comment CadillacConvertible "a cadillac car with a removable top")
(comment DepthPerception "Seeing with two eyes, so as to perceive depth.")
(comment LumbarVertebrae "#$The #$LumbarVertebrae is the #$Series of individual #$LumbarVertebra in #$The #$SpinalColumn.  There are five in the human body (L1-L5).")
(comment JapaneseCuisine "The collection of instances of what many Americans tend to think of as Japanese food")
(comment paymentDueForAccount "The agent ARG1 owes to (is obliged to pay toward) account ARG2 the amount ARG4 by the date ARG3.  ARG3 is the payment due date.  This says nothing about whether the payment is actually made.  It is just a way of stating that there is an obligation to pay.")
(comment OrchestralStringInstrumentType "The collection of #$StringInstruments that are found in a typical #$Orchestra, i.e. the four members of the violin family: #$Violin, #$Viola, #$Cello, and #$BassViolin.")
(disjointWith Research BodyMovementEvent)
(comment ConveyFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to a specialization MATERIAL of #$PartiallyTangible, #$ConveyFn returns the collection of all events in which an instance of MATERIAL is conveyed from one location to another (so the collection in question is a specialization of #$ConveyingMaterials).  For example, (#$ConveyFn #$Petroleum-CrudeOil) is the collection of all events in which crude oil is conveyed from one location to another, whether that be via pipeline, oil tanker, or some other means. For cases where the means in question is bodily transportation by an animal, see the more specific #$CarryingFn.")
(comment CheckFromIndividualAgent "Checks written on a specific agent's bank account - either personal or corporate.")
(comment Neck-AnimalBodyPart "The part of the body that connects the head to the shoulders.")
(disjointWith WritingImplement ProjectileLauncher)
(comment CookIslandsPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$CookIslands, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization RealEstateOrganization)
(comment Boiler-Device "Instances of this collection are 

  sealed containers used to convert liquid water

 to steam.")
(comment MedialSegmentalBronchusOfMiddleLobeOfLung "The collection of all medial segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of right #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a (right) #$MiddleLobeOfLung that supplies the #$MedialSegmentOfMiddleLobeOfLung.  It branches from the (right-side only) #$MiddleLobarBronchus.  (There is no #$MedialSegmentalBronchusOfMiddleLobeOfLung in the left #$Lung.)")
(comment AcrylicPaint "Acrylic paint used primarily by artists as an alternative to #$ArtistsOilPaint.")
(comment positionHasType "(#$positionHasType REL POS-TYPE) means that the job position filled in a #$HasPositionRelationship has the job duties characteristic of #$PersonTypeByPositionInOrg POS-TYPE. See also #$JobPosition, #$jobPositionHasPositionType and #$versionOfJobPosition.")
(comment PosteriorTibialArtery "The collection of all posterior tibial arteries.  The #$PosteriorTibialArtery connects to the #$PoplitealArtery at its proximal end and to the plantar arteries at its distal end.")
(comment Onion-Bulb "Individual onions, enlarged bulbs of the onion plant.")
(comment Chigger "minute, six-legged, reddish #$Larva of the harvest #$Mite, one of various 'red bugs' widely distributed throughout the world and common in the S United States. Attaching itself by its mouthparts to the skin of its vertebrate host, the chigger injects saliva that destroys cells and may cause an intense irritation known as red-bug dermatitis. The food of the chigger consists of the cellular contents and tissue fluid of the host. Certain Asian species carry minute organisms (rickettsias) that cause scrub typhus, a disease of humans.")
(comment PriceTag "A collection of #$InformationBearingObjects. They are physical labels for a product indicating how much it costs to purchase it. Examples include the cardboard slips affixed to clothing, and the paper strips stuck on food items.  Note that \"electronic tags\" found on types of #$Products sold on the world wide web are not instances of #$PriceTag.")
(disjointWith ProductionEvent PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment LatinCapitalLetterL "The capital letter 'L'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$L-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterL.")
(comment BrassInstrument "Musical instruments into which one buzzes one's lips to produce a sound.  Traditionaly made of brass, sometimes of silver or copper, sometimes even fiberglass.")
(comment sexuallyAttractedToType "(#$sexuallyAttractedToType IND TYPE) is true if and only if the individual IND is generally sexually attracted to instances of the collection TYPE. Typically, TYPE is a collection such that any one of its members and IND are conspecific. However, see #$Fetishism, #$Sitophilia, #$Bestiality, etc., for counterexamples.")
(comment OrientalLotus "the sacred lotus of the Orient (Nelumbo nucifera), found in tropical and subtropical Asia.")
(comment ComputerMotherBoard "The collection of the main printed circuit boards in computers.")
(comment LimitedLiabilityCompany "The collection of all limited liability companies organized under the law of one of the #$State-UnitedStates.  Instances of #$LimitedLiabilityCompany are formed pursuant to statutes that are distinct from a jurisdiction's statutes governing incorporation (the #$LimitedLiabilityCompany statute may, however, refer to the state law governing #$LegalCorporations and incorporate parts of it).")
(comment TopOfTable-PieceOfFurniture "The top of a table; has a smooth surface and usually a rectangular or oval shape when viewed from above.")
(comment SupraClavicularNerve "The collection of all supraclavicular #$Nerves.  A #$SupraClavicularNerve branches on each side of the body into medial, intermediate, and lateral supraclavicular #$Nerves.  A #$SupraClavicularNerve is supplied by the #$VentralRamusC3 and #$VentralRamusC4 on its side of the body.  They supply the #$Skin on the front, top, and back of the #$Shoulder.")
(comment Licorice "A type of candy that is flavoured with an extract of the dried root of a European leguminous plant (Glycrrhiza glabra).")
(comment PresuppositionFunction "The collection of CycL functions

 that 

 enable a basic representation of pieces of commonsense knowledge 

that \"pack in\" or \"gloss over\" assumptions that, 

for a machine,

 would generally need to be made explicit.")
(comment Annelida "This is the collection of segmented worms. It includes earthworms.")
(comment SoftwarePackage "#$SoftwarePackage is the collection of programs composed of loosely coupled component programs, possibly including an #$OperatingSystem, libraries, tool sets, or \"system software\".")
(comment UtilityWire "telephone lines, power lines, cables that traffic lights hang from.  Some are underground, some are outdoors.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByMotility "A collection of collections and a partition on #$Bacterium. This collection divides #$Bacterium into disjoint groups according to motility: #$Bacterium-Immotile, #$Bacterium-MotileByFlagellum,
#$Bacterium-MotileByGliding, and #$Bacterium-MotileByAxialFilament.")
(comment MaterialSafetyDataSheetCW "This is the collection of #$PropositionalConceptualWorks the instances of members of which comprise the members of the collection #$MaterialSafetyDataSheet. It is really the members of the present collection which companies are required to create.\"")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice LightingDevice)
(comment EdibleLegumeSeed "The seed of a legume plant.")
(comment HaitianPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Haiti, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith DrugStoreChain PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization)
(comment HomeTheaterSystem "This is the collection of home theater

systems. These are basically large-screen television sets souped-up with

some sort of hi-fi sound system.")
(comment Sino-TibetanLanguageFamily "Various kinds of Chinese and its relatives")
(comment FireplaceBroom "A broom found by the fireplace.")
(comment EmbroideringEvent "The collection of craft events that result in embroidered objects. The performer uses a needle and fine yarn, and makes
decorative stitches in a piece of fabric.")
(comment Pacing "Walking with a deliberate or measured stride.  Pacing is also associated with expending nervous energy.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink Collision)
(comment WordProcessingProgram-Visual "#$WordProcessingProgram-Visual is the most significant specialization of #$WordProcessingProgram. It is the collection of computer programs whose primary function is the production, manipulation, and editing of text under the interactive direction of the user of the program who reads files displayed by the program on a monitor.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization ManufacturingOrganization)
(comment ModularPowerCord "A power cord that is removable from its electrical device, such as is frequently found on computers and their peripherals.")
(comment Limb-AnimalBodyPart "#$Limb-AnimalBodyPart is a specialization of #$Appendage-AnimalBodyPart and an instance of #$SymmetricAnatomicalPartType.  Each instance of #$Limb-AnimalBodyPart is a bilaterally symmetric #$Appendage-AnimalBodyPart that extends from the #$Trunk-BodyCore; including #$Arm, #$Leg, #$Wing-AnimalBodyPart, #$Flipper, and pectoral #$Fin.  A #$Finger, #$Toe, #$Hand, #$Tail-BodyPart, ... is not a #$Limb-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment HumanInitiatedFn "This function links collections of actions done by computers (specs of #$ProgramAction) with the collections of people getting computers to do those actions (specs of #$ProgramAction-HumanInitiated). The collection denoted by (#$HumanInitiatedFn ACTION) is the collection of events of people getting computers to perform instances of ACTION. Thus every instance of (#$HumanInitiatedFn ACTION) includes an instance of ACTION as a subevent.")
(comment CrimpConnector "A connector for conductive wires which is fastened by being smashed flat.")
(disjointWith AutoMaintenance SkyDiving)
(comment BillForServices "The bill for services rendered")
(comment TearDuct "The collection of all tear ducts.  Each #$TearDuct is a tube which allows #$LacrimalFluid to flow from a #$TearGland through an #$UpperEyelid to an #$Eye")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece FurniturePart)
(comment Papillon "A collection of small dogs.")
(comment minorityLanguageHere "The minority language of a country.  This may be a legally recognized language, but is usually not used in official documents")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment InnermostIntercostal "The #$Collection of all instances of #$InnermostIntercostal #$Muscle.  An #$InnermostIntercostal is the middle of three muscles which connect two adjacent ribs.  It elevates the ribs during inspiration and helps maintain the intercostal space.")
(comment HealthAndBeautyMarketCategory "The market category for sundry products used in caring for the physical person.")
(comment SubEventPredicate "A specialization of #$IntangibleObjectRelatingPredicate (q.v.) whose instances relate events to certain of their parts or subevents.  Each instance of #$SubEventPredicate is a specialization (via #$genls or #$genlInverse) of the predicate #$subEvents (q.v.).    Examples include #$subProcesses and #$cotemporalSubEvents.  Note that, while most currently reified subevent predicates are in fact also #$TemporalPartPredicates (q.v.), it is not necessary that a subevent predicate divide events along temporal lines.")
(comment Yogurt "Yogurt is a dairy product containing active yogurt cultures which digest the lactose and make the yogurt more easily digestible for us humans.")
(comment RentalShop "Local (one site) service organizations whose main function is to allow customers/clients to rent (the use of) objects for a fee.")
(comment textOfWork "(#$textOfWork WORK TEXT) means that TEXT is part of the full text of the #$PropositionalConceptualWork WORK.")
(comment effectiveDestructionMethodFor "(#$effectiveDestructionMethodFor ORGTYPE DESEVENT) means that if an instance of ORGTYPE, ORG, is acted on in an instance of DESEVENT, EVENT, it is likely that ORG will die in EVENT.")
(comment LegalDocument "A specialization of #$OfficialDocument. Instances of this collection not only have the force of the law behind them (as most #$OfficialDocuments do) but also either must be prepared by a #$Lawyer in order to be legitimate, or their construction is strictly specified by the rule of law governing the parties bound by them.  While #$OfficialDocuments such as #$CreditReportDocuments may have legal force in some contexts, they are not considered #$LegalDocuments because their construction is not as tightly specified by law as that of #$LegalDocuments.  Also, #$LegalDocuments are distinguished as being created expressly for legal purposes. See also #$LegalAgreement.")
(comment Brachiating "A locomotion strategy by which the performer moves while hanging from the arms.")
(comment EnforcingSomething "Enforcing or monitoring a proposition to be true. If it is violated, the performer should perform some action. This task is performed by #$FlightAttendant, LifeGuard, and #$SecurityGuard. This unit may have a slot to specify what proposition is enforced. But we are not creating it at this stage.")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice ExplosiveDevice)
(comment ChileanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Chile, or participate in its #$NationalCulture..")
(comment Gun-BreechLoading "The collection of #$Guns that are loaded from the #$Breech-GunPart. This is almost necessary for all rapid-fire weapons.")
(comment QuotationMark-Double "The symbol ''. Looks like double inverted commas. Used in pairs to attribute the enclosed text to a particular speaker.")
(comment GutterDownSpout "A vertical pipe which carries rain water from a GutterOnABuilding to the Ground.")
(comment LawnMower "The collection of lawnmowers: rider mowers and handpushed mowers, power mowers and old-fashioned hand-powered mowers. See also #$LawnMower-Power, #$LawnMower-HandPowered, #$LawnMower-Riding, #$LawnMower-HandPushed, and #$LawnMower-TractorPulled.")
(comment GeoCarTypeByModel "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$GeoCar whose instances are all of the same model.")
(comment DorsalRamusT5 "The collection of all T5 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT5 and DorsalRamiT5 branch from SpinalRootT5.  DorsalRamiT5 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment Mutton "Raw meat of sheep.")
(comment SemiconductorDevice "A specialization of #$ElectronicDevice. Each instance of  #$SemiconductorDevice is an electronic component used in computers and communications equipment.  Each instance of #$SemiconductorDevice is constructed largely from instances of some specialization of #$SemiconductorStuff such as #$Silicon or #$Germanium.")
(disjointWith BusinessEvent BodyMovementEvent)
(comment Hacking "A specialization of #$ProgrammingAComputer, comprising particularly clever or expert programming feats. Contrary to popular usage of the word \"hacking\", this constant is not intended to refer to acts of breaking into computer systems (for that, see #$PenetratingAComputerNetwork and #$AttackByComputerOperation).")
(comment Centrifuge "a device used in centrifuging to separate particles of varying density")
(comment ingestingToxicityFor "(#$ingestingToxicityFor STUFF ORGTYPE TOXLEVEL) means that under ordinary circumstances, stuff has the #$Toxicity TOXLEVEL for instances of ORGTYPE that ingest it.")
(comment JobClassifiedAd "A collection of classified ads for job opennings.")
(comment Freckle "Pigmented spot on skin")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice Weapon)
(comment SudanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Sudan, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment DentalFile "A Hand-held tool used for smoothing, shaping or surfacing teeth in the patients mouth; has a rough surface which is rubbed on the tooth and used to wear away thin layers of it's surface.")
(disjointWith Antenna-AnimalBodyPart Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(disjointWith OpticalRetailer MedicalCareOrganization)
(comment Napkin "An object made of paper or cloth, used for cleaning the face and hands during and after a meal")
(comment DevelopingAnIBO "Product development where what is developed is some type of information-bearing object.")
(comment Clitoris "A small organ at the anterior or ventral part of the vulva homologous to the penis")
(comment CarSeatCovers "The different types of coverings forthe seats in your car.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType PhysiologicalConditionType)
(comment BengaliCharacter "characters composed of major sections for consonants and added squiggles for vowels other than A")
(comment GovernmentPaidService "Specifically those services paid for fully by the government via taxes, license fees, etc., and for which the recipient of the service does not pay directly (e.g., food stamps).  By default, the #$providerOfService is a LegalGovernmentalOrganization.")
(disjointWith Climbing ArmMovement)
(disjointWith StationeryProduct SomethingToWear)
(comment Fjordhorse "The collection of all Fjordhorses, commonly caled Fjording, or Fjord, constituting a scandinavian (originally Norwegian) breed of general work-horse known for their reliability, good nature and pleasant disposition.  Fjordhorses are usually 'dun' colored (very light brown), of medium height, and often have 'primitive' markings like a dark area at the tail or vestigial stripes on the legs.")
(comment NextTermInListFn "(#$NextTermInListFn LIST TERM) returns the term in LIST that
immediately follows the first instance of TERM.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByIndustry PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment ElectricFireplace "The subcollection of #$AirHeatingDevices which are space heaters and are designed to look like a #$Fireplace, but without the chimney.")
(comment Wolf-Red "A collection of wolves, also called Swamp wolves. Their natural range is in            southeastern United States and their scientific name is            Canis rufus (or Canis niger).")
(comment PectoralisMajor "The #$Collection of all instances of #$PectoralisMajor #$Muscle.  The #$PectoralisMajor #$Muscle underlies the front of the #$Chest-BodyPart.  The #$PectoralisMajor #$Muscle connects the #$Sternum (via its Sternal Head) and #$Clavicle (via its Clavicular Head) to the #$Humerus and is used for movement of the #$Humerus.  Actions of different parts of the #$Muscle are different.")
(comment SoapCupOfDishwasher "The container in which soap is placed in a dishwasher.")
(comment CranialNerve "The collection of all cranial #$Nerves.  In an individual #$CranialNerves appear as 12 pairs of #$Nerves extending from the #$Brain.")
(comment ParmigianoReggiano-Cheese "This is an aged richly flavored cow's milk cheese

made in the Emilia-Romana region of Italy.")
(comment completeGISOfChem "(#$completeGISOfChem CHEM COMP-GIS) means that the #$GeneticInformationStructure COMP-GIS is the maximal #$GeneticInformationStructure instantiated by #$ChemicalGeneticIBT, CHEM. More precisely, it means that for all SUB_GIS distinct from GIS, CHEM instantiates SUB_GIS if and only if SUB_GIS is a #$subGIS of GIS.")
(comment ElectronicFlash "A reusable device that produces short intense flashes of light to illuminate subjects being photographed. No need for flash bulbs.  At least some electronic flashes have a brief wait for recharging before reusing.")
(comment Gonad "The collection of all gonads.  A #$Gonad is a sexual #$Organ which produces #$HaploidCells.  It is also a #$Hormone producing #$Gland, producing sex #$Steroids.  A male #$Gonad is a #$Testicle (which produces #$SpermCells and #$Androgens such as #$Testosterone) and a female #$Gonad is an #$Ovary-AnimalBodyPart (which produces egg cells [#$Ovum] and the #$Steroids #$Estrogen and #$Progesterone).  Hermaphroditic #$Animals have both types of #$Gonads.")
(disjointWith WaterTransportationDevice Tool)
(comment WildPlantBLOFn "A function that returns collections of un-cultivated, as-found-in-nature plants and plant-parts. For example, (#$WildPlantBLOFn #$CherryTree) denotes the collection of all cherry trees that are not cultivated by humans, but grow in the wild. See also #$WildAnimalFn.")
(comment NauruanPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Nauru, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment MayanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment SatinCloth "All the satin cloth in the universe.")
(comment CoordinatedBodyMovement "#$VoluntaryBodyMovement s that require some coordination between multiple movements and external events. i.e. more complex than simply #$Reaching or #$LiftingALeg. Exemplary example: #$Juggling.")
(comment SalesDepartment "A specialization of #$MarketingDepartment. Sales departments are departments within a larger organization which have as their specific function the selling of goods or services (as opposed to broader marketing duties such as market research, product design, pricing etc.)")
(comment Yard-BoatPart "A long spar tapered toward the ends to support and spread the head of a square sail, lateen, or lugsail.")
(comment MercedesConvertible "a mercedes car with a removable top")
(comment smellsOdorOfMagnitude "arg1 #$smells #$Odor arg2 which has an #$OdorMagnitude of arg3.")
(comment CoccygealVertebrae "#$The #$CoccygealVertebrae is the #$Series of individual #$CoccygealVertebra in #$The #$SpinalColumn.  The four in the adult human body are united into a single bone, the #$Coccyx.  Unification takes place many years later in women than in men.")
(comment FrenchCuisine "The collection of instances of what many Americans tend to think of as French food")
(disjointWith NuclearEvent BiologicalProcess)
(comment PaperCutter "The collection of devices for cutting paper which are composed of a blade attached at a pivot point to a flat base.")
(disjointWith TillingSoil (TransportViaFn Spacecraft))
(comment GroceryList "The collection of documents which contain a list of items to be purchased the next time the owner goes grocery shopping.")
(comment RibCage "A protective cage composed of ribs which covers the lungs and heart")
(disjointWith WritingImplement Paddle-Water)
(comment RyukyuIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$RyukyuIslandsTerritory, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith RealEstateOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment GasTurbineEngine "The collection of #$TurbineEngines that

 use the gas from a burning, liquid fuel

 to turn wheels.")
(comment SuperiorLingularSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all superior lingular segments of left #$SuperiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by a #$SuperiorLingularSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.  (These segments and bronchi do not exist in right #$Lungs.)")
(comment FurniturePart "The collection of all parts made for #$FurniturePieces.")
(comment SweetPotato-Foodstuff "Sweet potato in any of its edible forms.")
(comment fileFormat "This predicate relates a file to a particular #$ComputerFileTypeByFormat. (#$fileFormat FILE FORMAT) means that the #$ComputerFile-AIS FILE has the #$ComputerFileTypeByFormat FORMAT.")
(comment Galvanometer "A device used to measure electric current.")
(comment Imago "A collection of stages in the lives of individual organisms; a subset of #$BiologicalStageOfDevelopment.  Each element of #$Imago is a metamorphic insect during its adult stage.")
(disjointWith OfficialDocument PlayingCard)
(disjointWith Vacuuming PolishingSomething)
(comment DeckOfCards "The collection of packs of playing cards")
(comment LatinSmallLetterL "The lowercase letter 'l'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$L-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterL.")
(comment MusicalInstrument-Electronic "The collection of #$MusicalInstruments which produce sound electronically rather than physically.")
(comment SimpleWholeBodyMovement "A specialization of #$BodyMovementEvent and an instance of #$OneAtATimeProcessType (q.v.).  A collection of common bodily movements in which the whole body is involved in the movement.  Specializations of this collection include #$Jumping, #$AnimalWalkingProcess, and #$FallingDown.")
(comment interArgNotIsa2-4 "(#$interArgNotIsa2-4 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the second argument to PRED, the fourth argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(comment DivisionZygomycota "This is the division of the fungus kingdom which

contains bread molds.")
(comment SoundCard "Computer sound cards.")
(disjointWith SpeciallyCharteredInstitution LimitedLiabilityCompany)
(comment MannedSpacecraft "The collection of all manned #$Spacecraft.")
(comment BackupFn "(#$BackupFn FILECOPY) denotes the collection of all #$ComputerFileCopys which were created as backups of and hence contains all relevant information contained in FILECOPY.")
(comment Chair-PieceOfFurniture "A piece of furniture that is used primarily for seating, and can hold one person.")
(comment DorsalRamusS1 "The collection of all S1 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiS1 and DorsalRamiS1 branch from SpinalRootS1.  DorsalRamiS1 supplies the posterior gluteal skin.")
(comment LeftoverFood "A collection, all of whose instances are (or were) morsels of

food left at a meal.")
(comment passwordFileForAccountSystem "(#$passwordFileForAccountSystem FILE SYSTEM) means that FILE contains all the username-and-password combinations for all user accounts on the #$AccountSystem SYS.")
(comment hasImplementation "(#$hasImplementation IMP PROG) means that the program specifications of IMP are implemented in PROG.")
(comment BacterialCellWall "The collection of cell walls present on most #$Bacterium.  These thick outer layers protect the cell and acts as a permeability barrier to prevent certain molecules from entering the cell.")
(comment ImmigrationRecord "The collection of #$OfficialDocuments that record the admission of persons immigrating to a country.")
(comment InteriorDirection "The general direction towards the interior of the body and away from the exterior, in or near an object with #$AnimalBodyShape.  This is a #$VectorInterval comprising a roughly cone-shaped set of vectors; note that its direction is dependent on the location of the objects involved (e.g., downward near the head of a #$Person in #$UprightPosture; upward at the feet).")
(comment workPublicationDate "(#$workPublicationDate WORK DATE) means that the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK was published on #$Date DATE. An instance of #$StructurallySpecificWork can have only one publication date.")
(comment Cashew-TheSeed "The embryo of the cashew seed, which is the edible and delicious cashew nut.")
(comment MalaysianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Malaysia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith DrugTestingOrganization PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization)
(comment PhoneAnsweringMachineCombo "This is the collection of

telephone that have an answering machine built into them.")
(comment Aztec-TanoanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages spoken in western North America and #$Mexico")
(comment ElectricalHeater "A device whose function is to generate heat by consuming electricity.")
(disjointWith ProductDistributionEvent AcademicTesting)
(comment TurningAway "To rotate the body away from something, usally done in shame or embarrassment.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink InformationBearingThing)
(comment TransportationCompany-Provider "Instances of #$TransportationCompany-Provider are service organizations whose main product is the direct providing of transportation of people or goods.  Organizations that rent or loan vehicles should not be instances of this class, but instead belong in the more-general #$TransportationCompany.")
(comment genlPrograms "(#$genlPrograms SPEC GENL) means that SPEC is a more specific \"version\" of GENL.  Example: (#$genlPrograms (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Emacs-TheProgram \"20.4\") #$Emacs-TheProgram) and (#$genlPrograms #$GnuEmacs #$Emacs-TheProgram), but not (#$genlPrograms (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Emacs-TheProgram \"19\") (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Emacs-TheProgram \"20.4\") ), and not (#$genlPrograms #$Quake-TheGame #$Quake-TheGameSeries). #$softwareInVersionSeries is the right predicate for series.  See also #$versionOfSoftware.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization StorageOrganization)
(comment AssemblyLine "A collection of physical devices.  Each element of #$AssemblyLine is a complex device that consists of a sequence of processing stations. The function of an assembly line is to perform some change on its inputs. So a car is not an assembly line, even though it burns gasoline, since its function is not to burn gasoline.  Some change is performed on the inputs at each station, and then it is passed on to the next.  The outputs of one station are inputs to another, and vice versa.")
(comment implementProtectsAgainst "(#$implementProtectsAgainst PRODUCTTYPE EVENTTYPE) means
that, under ordinary circumstances, an instance of PRODUCTTYPE will
act to protect its owner against instances of EVENTTYPE.")
(comment Respiration "A specialization of #$BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary.  Each instance of #$Respiration is a process through which an instance of #$Animal acquires oxygen for its cells, and releases carbon dioxide formed by those cells into the atmosphere.")
(comment EukaryoticProteinSynthesis "The collection of protein synthesis events that are subevents of eukaryotic gene expression.")
(comment captive "ARG2 is the animal which is being held captive in the #$HeldCaptive configuration, ARG1. ")
(comment ProjectileWeapon-Fired "A very generic term for projectiles fired from firearms. It includes musket balls, cannon balls, pistol slugs, rifle cartridges, shotgun shot, and #$ArtilleryShells.  In the case of 'rifle cartridge' and #$ArtilleryShell, only part of the object becomes the projectile (see #$ProjectileShellAssembly).  The other part of such objects, which includes a casing, explosive charge, a primer, etc. stays behind or is destroyed in detonation.  In the case of 'cannon ball', 'pistol slug' or 'musket ball' the entire object is propelled from a gun due to an explosive charge behind it.")
(comment SugarcanePlant "Individual sugarcane plants; these are grown as crops for the sugar they contain.")
(comment InsulatedScrewDriver "A screwdriver with insulation protecting the user from shock.")
(disjointWith IntrinsicStateChangeEvent SkyDiving)
(comment InsurancePolicyDocument "The set of insurance policy agreement documents.  An #$InsurancePolicyDescription on the other hand, is merely a description of what may go in an #$InsurancePolicyDocument.")
(comment Biceps "The large muscle on the front of the upper arm")
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice FurniturePiece)
(comment Otterhound "A collection of large dogs with webbed feet, bred in England.")
(comment Trident-HandWeapon "A #$Trident-HandWeapon is a weapon with three points that looks            like a large fork.")
(comment RotatorsOfHip "The #$Collection of all sets of hip rotating #$Muscles.  The #$RotatorsOfHip consist of 6 #$Muscles on each side which control the lateral rotation of the #$Femur at the #$Hip. Thes muscles are the Piriformis, Gemellus Superior and Inferior, Obturator Internus and Externus, and QuadratusFemoris.")
(comment BedFrame "The part of a bed that supports the box spring and mattress.")
(comment Minimum "Computes the minimum of a unary function's values over all elements in a given set or collection.  That is, (#$Minimum SETORCOL FUNC) denotes the value of FUNC for the element ELEM of SETORCOL taken as argument (if any) such that (FUNC ELEM) is less than or equal to (FUNC OTHER) for any element OTHER of SETORCOL other than ELEM.  Note that (#$Minimum SETORCOL #$IdentityFn) denotes the minimum element of SETORCOL itself.")
(comment AbdominalCavity "The collection of AbdominalCavities, or cavities within the #$Abdomen, that each contains the digestive #$Organs (#$Stomach, intestines, #$Liver, #$Spleen, #$Pancreas, etc.).  An #$AbdominalCavity includes its walls.")
(comment ChiliConCarne "A dish made with chilies or chili powder, ground or diced #$Beef, chopped onion and pepper, and sometimes kidney beans and tomatoes.")
(comment Cafe-Organization "Limited-menu restaurants serving pastries and beverages, primarily coffee drinks.  May also serve juices, beer, or wine.  Atmosphere is informal.")
(disjointWith TextualMaterial Crucifix-ChristianSymbol)
(comment AnimalBodyPart "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyRegion.  Each instance of #$AnimalBodyPart is an anatomical part of some living animal, and thus is itself an instance of #$BiologicalLivingObject (q.v).  #$AnimalBodyPart includes both highly localized organs (for example, hearts) and physical systems composed of parts distributed throughout an animal's body (such as an animal's circulatory system and nervous system).  Note that severed limbs and removed organs are _not_ instances of this collection, since they are not _parts_ of some living animal.")
(comment Post-VerbPhraseModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which only modify verb phrases by right-attaching them. Example: 'slowly', as in 'He ate slowly.'")
(comment QatarPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Qatar, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Gun-Multibarreled "The collection of #$Guns that can fire a shot from each barrel before needing to be reloaded by hand.  A double-barrel shotgun is such an example.")
(comment Nutrient "A specialization of #$EdibleStuff.  Each instance of #$Nutrient is a substance considered necessary or beneficial in the diet of a person or animal.  If a food or a pill is sold in a package, often the nutrients in the food or pill are listed on the package label.  Specializations of #$Nutrient include #$EdibleSodium, #$ProteinStuff, #$EdibleCalcium, #$EdibleIron, and #$Vitamin.")
(comment QuotationMark-Single "The symbol '. Looks like an inverted comma. Used in pairs to attribute the enclosed text to a particular speaker.")
(comment GutterSystem "The collection of all drainage systems composed of horizontal conduits (instances of #$GutterOnARoof) connected to vertical pipes (instances of #$GutterDownSpout) for carrying rainwater safely from a building to the ground.")
(comment MultipleUserComputer "Multi-user computers.")
(comment SuperficialPeronealNerve "The collection of all superficial peroneal (or 'fibular') #$Nerves.  A #$SuperficialPeronealNerve is a branch of the #$CommonPeronealNerve on its side of the body.  It #$innervates, via branches or directly, #$Muscles in the #$LowerLeg and foot (#$Foot-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment FreshBakedGoods "Class of baked goods that are sold on the same day they are baked (typically).  They differ from other baked goods in their superior aesthetic quality, lack of preservatives, and (often) in being sold in a separate location.")
(comment AbstractProgrammingLanguage "A specialization of #$ComputerLanguage, #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage is the collection of languages invented for the purpose of composing computer programs (i.e., instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW), as opposed to merely facilitating interaction between pieces of software or indicating how to represent pieces of text. Thus, #$ComputerLanguages such as #$Lisp are instances of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage, whereas #$ComputerLanguages such as #$HypertextMarkupLanguage are not.")
(comment Condom "A piece of (usually) rubber, worn by a man during sexual intercourse to prevent pregnancy and/or transmission of sexually transmitted diseases.")
(comment Hair-Strand "An individual strand of hair")
(disjointWith Hat TransportationContainerProduct)
(comment GabonPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Gabon, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByGeographicReach PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment ToyGlider "The collection of all (#$ToyVersionFn #$Airplane)s

  that actually glide through the air.")
(comment MailBox "Boxes or containers that contain mail-type objects.")
(disjointWith Pincer Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(comment NonProfitCorporation "A specialization of both #$LegalCorporation and #$NonProfitOrganization.  Each instance of #$NonProfitCorporation is a legal corporation which is engaged in not-for-profit activities.  Typical instances of #$NonProfitCorporation have no shareholders or owners, although they are commonly governed by a board (see the collection #$BoardOfDirectors).  Most instances of #$NonProfitCorporation have official non-profit standing with a government, and thus do not pay corporate income taxes. Instances of #$NonProfitCorporation include #$PlannedParenthood, #$SierraClub, and #$HabitatForHumanity.")
(disjointWith SellingOrganization CooperativeOrganization)
(comment Hemostat "A clamp-like instrument that is used to stop bleeding.")
(comment OomycetesClass "The single #$BiologicalClass within the fungus division, Oomycota.")
(disjointWith Travel-TripEvent IBTGeneration)
(comment Breast "Mammaries of female primates.")
(comment AutomobileBonnet "The protective covering (usually leather or plastic) that fits on the front of your car to protect it from things (flying rocks, etc.).")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment ASCIICompatibleCharacter "The collection of all ASCII-compatible characters (and control codes).  Each is an instance of #$Character-Abstract rather than a specific physical character as written, printed or displayed.  Each #$ASCIICompatibleCharacter has a binary encoding in the #$ASCII Standard. (Note: all #$ASCIICompatibleCharacters are also #$UnicodeCompatibleCharacters.)")
(comment RegisteringForAService "A collection of events.  Each #$RegisteringForAService entails an act of recording one's identity (usually at least by name) and making an agreement to pay for a service to be rendered at some future time, perhaps almost immediately.  Typical examples are registering at a university, registering to attend a conference, registering for a hotel room, etc.  Payment (or some guarantee of payment) typically occurs at the time of registration, before the service is received.")
(disjointWith ArmMovement DecompositionProcess)
(disjointWith StationeryProduct AnimalContainer)
(comment AmericanWaterSpaniel "A collection of dogs.")
(comment PreviousTermInListFn "(#$PreviousTermInListFn LIST TERM) returns the term in LIST that
immediately precedes the first instance of TERM.")
(comment GasFireplace "The collection of constructions attached to a chimney that open into a room and in which the combustion of natural gas is used to generate heat.")
(comment PectoralisMinor "The #$Collection of all instances of #$PectoralisMinor #$Muscle.  The #$PectoralisMinor #$Muscle underlies the front of the #$Chest-BodyPart.  The #$PectoralisMinor #$Muscle consists of three straplike portions connecting each of ribs 3-5 with the #$Scapula.")
(comment ControlKnob "The collection of generic knobs which are turned with one's fingers to control devices")
(comment PlantarRegionFn "#$PlantarRegionFn is a function which yields the inferior region of a foot (#$Foot-AnimalBodyPart) or part of a foot.  This function should not be used with any other type of argument.")
(comment Mozzarella-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of

all types of mozzarella, including fresh mozzarella as well as the firmer

sort familiar from pizzas. The most famous variety is Mozzarella di Bufalo, an

Italian cheese made from water buffalo milk. (Italy is not particularly

known for its water buffalo.)")
(comment Deoxyribonucleotide-GIS "The collection of all abstract nucleotides [#$Nucleotide-GIS] which are instantiated by instances of #$Deoxyribonucleotide.")
(comment AirPropeller "The type of propeller found on airplanes, and sometimes on other propeller-driven vehicles.")
(comment gameteOfOrgType "(#$gameteOfOrgType GAM-TYPE ORG-TYPE) means that GAM-TYPE is the type of gamete produced by the type of eukaryotic organism ORG-TYPE.")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject TextualMaterial)
(comment Withers "#$Withers is the collection of the withers of instances of #$EquineAnimal.  The withers of an instance of #$Horse (or other #$EquineAnimal) is the area that forms the border between the animal's back and neck.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice-Vehicle Tool)
(comment FlowerFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction for referring to a type of flower.")
(comment AndorranPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Andorra, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment TsimshianLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment CoatHanger "A shoulder-shaped frame with a hook at the top, usually of wire, wood or plastic, for draping and handing an articale of clothing when not in use.")
(comment BoardGameProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerGamePrograms that are simulated versions of board games like chess or Risk. Instances are games such as 'Chessmaster 6000' or 'Mastermind'.")
(comment MarketingDepartment "A specialization of #$FinanceDepartment. Each instance of #$MarketingDepartment consists of employees who are responsible for an organization's marketing activities, which typically include tasks such as market research, #$Advertising, product design and pricing and of course, sales (for which, see the more specific #$SalesDepartment).")
(comment PlumbingTool "A collection of objects; a subset of #$Tool.  An instance of #$PlumbingTool is any tool used in installing or repairing parts of plumbing systems (pipes, faucets, drains, etc.) --- such tools include wrenches, plungers, etc.")
(comment BMWConvertible "a BMW car with a removable top")
(comment hears "(#$hears AGT OBJ) means that the #$PerceptualAgent AGT perceives sounds emananating from or as the result of OBJ.  Events such as the shooting of a gun and tangible objects such as telephones are things which can emit audible sound and thus be perceived auditorily. ")
(comment Tuberosity "A #$Tuberosity is a portion of a #$Bone-BodyPart that slightly protrudes from the bone and is labeled a 'tuberosity' or 'tubercle'.  It is normally a place for attachment of #$MuscleTissue or a #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment AutomobileTypeByBodyStyle "A collection of collections, each element of #$AutomobileTypeByBodyStyle is a collection of instances of #$Automobile which share a particular body style, e.g., sedan, hatchback.")
(disjointWith StateOfMatterChangeEvent BodyMovementEvent)
(comment RotaryCutter "The collection of cutting devices with a circular blade attached to a handle.  The user holds and pushes on the handle causing the blade to roll over and cut the sheetlike object.  Pizza cutters and fabric rotary cutters, not power saws.")
(comment PolicyDocument "The collection of all documents in which a set of policies (of a corporation, governmental body, or some other organization or agent) are explicitly stated.")
(comment Rib-AnimalBodyPart "Part of a rib cage")
(comment permittedActType "'(#$permittedActType GRANT ACT-TYPE)' means that ACT-TYPE is the type of #$Action permission for which is granted in the #$GrantingPermission GRANT.")
(disjointWith FoodUtensil WritingImplement)
(comment CorsicanPerson "A person who is an #$Corsica #$citizens, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup RealEstateOrganization)
(comment TurbojetEngine "The collection of all #$JetEngines 

   that, at high speeds, compress air

  taken in as a ramjet and increases exhaust

   velocities with an afterburner.")
(comment PosteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all posterior segments of right #$SuperiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by a #$PosteriorSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.  (On the left side the apical and posterior segments of the #$SuperiorLobeOfLung are usually combined in the #$ApicoposteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.)")
(comment ManualDrill "A hand tool used for boring holes in objects by means of a rotating sharp-edged cylindrical bit.")
(comment PeronealArtery "The collection of all peroneal arteries.  The #$PeronealArtery connects to the #$PosteriorTibialArtery at its proximal end.  The #$PeronealArtery runs alongside (#$alignedAlongLength) the #$PeronealVein in the #$Leg.")
(comment Caper-TheCondiment "The chopped and pickled flower buds of the #$Caper-Plant.")
(comment MUDRealm "This is the collection of MUDs, which may be thought of as virtual worlds located in cyberspace. The term is derived from an acronym for \"Multi-User Dungeon\", but

has since been generalized to apply to any well-detailed virtual environment in which

people, playing characters, can interact. The term is now sometimes taken as an acronym for \"Multi-User Domain\". It is also sometimes used to refer to

 games that are played in such domains (see #$MUDGame), though some #$MUDRealms exist for purposes other than

playing a game. #$MultiplayerOnlineRolePlayingGames are played in #$MUDRealms.")
(comment Arachnid "A group of arthopods having segmented body, no antenna, and four pairs of legs. Spiders are the best known subset.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice InformationStorageMedia)
(disjointWith DangerousTangibleThing CrimpingTool)
(comment PlayingCard "the collection of playing cards, each of which is one of a pack of cards used in playing card games")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterM "The capital letter 'M'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$M-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterM.")
(comment RustproofingPaint "Paint that you usually put on metal to prevent it from rusting.")
(disjointWith MakingFacialExpression SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment DivisionPsilotophyta "This is the collection of whisk ferns.")
(comment HardwareBusInternalOptimizedForTask "Members of this collection are hardware buses that are internal to a 

  computer system but have been optimized for a specific functionality that

  allows a high level of through-put, usually with bypassing some of the other

  components.")
(comment Committee-Organization "The collection of all committees formally organized to accomplish particular purposes.  Instances of #$Committee-Organization usually operate in accordance with rules or procedures.  #$Committee-Organizations are groups of individuals and are usually named.  Each instance of #$Committee-Organization consists of at least two individual #$CommitteeMembers and may, in instances of #$Committee-Organization having many #$CommitteeMembers, include a #$CommitteeChairman.")
(comment WebDesign "A collection of events. In each instance of #$WebDesign, a service provider designs and develops material for a client's #$WorldWideWebSite. This material can include not only html pages, but also images, sound files, video, applets, cgi scripts, etc. Note that #$WebDesign is a spec of #$ServiceEvent, so it must be done for someone else. Designing your own website doesn't count.")
(comment BicycleTire "Every unit should have an english.")
(comment MedialCord-BrachialPlexus "The collection of all medial cords of the brachial plexus.  The medial cord is formed by the anterior division of the #$InferiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus.  Nerves formed from the medial cord are the #$UlnarNerve, the #$MedialPectoralNerve, the MedialCutaneousOfTheForearm and the #$MedianNerve.")
(comment Fondue "#$Fondues are usually made of melted #$Cheese mixed with a little #$Wine which is then eaten by dipping cube-shaped pieces of #$Bread in the #$Mixture. Specific cookware and utensils can be bought for making #$Fondue recipes: a type of pot to heat the ingredients that are to be melted and long fork-like spears used for spearing and dipping the #$Bread, #$Meat, fruit, or other items. Besides the traditional #$Cheese #$Fondue, there are many other types, such as #$Chocolate #$Fondues into which one typically dips #$EdibleFruits.")
(comment SecretDataFile "Who knows what secrets lie within?  Hmmm?")
(comment ComputerVirus "#$ComputerVirus is the collection of all

#$MaliciousComputerPrograms whose copies attach to instances of 

#$ComputerProgramCopy.

An instance of #$ComputerVirus is activated when the #$ComputerProgramCopy it

is attached to is run on a computer. An instance of #$ComputerVirus 

may be transmitted over a #$ComputerNetwork

or via a #$ComputerDisk to other computers.")
(comment PaperProductCore "Denotes the collection of generic paper product cores for stuff like paper towel, aluminum foil, plastic wrap, gift wrap, etc.")
(comment ReproductiveFission "A collection of events in which a #$Cell splits into approximately identical organisms, each becoming a new independant organism.  After the DNA replication, the cell wall and plasma membrane grow inward and constrict the cell to divide it in two.  This is a common form of asexual reproduction in #$ProkaryoticCells.")
(comment CelebrityCenterfold "The collection of all instances of #$Centerfold-Generic that depict #$StunninglyBeautiful (generally scantily clad or #$Nude) #$Persons. In many microtheories, many instances of #$Centerfold-PhotoOfPerson are #$PornographicMaterial.")
(comment ExteriorDirection "The general direction away from the interior of the body and toward the exterior, in or near an object with #$AnimalBodyShape.  This is a #$VectorInterval comprising a roughly cone-shaped set of vectors; note that its direction is dependent on the location of the objects involved (e.g., upward near the head of a #$Person in #$UprightPosture; downward at the feet).")
(comment publicationDate-IBO "(#$publicationDate-IBO IBO DATE) means that the #$InformationBearingObject IBO was published on #$Date DATE.  Use of the predicate implies that a particular #$InformationBearingObject has been published, that is, that it is of a type that can be distributed to the public or an identifiable subset of the public consisting of more than a few members.  There is no requirement of printing or physical distribution, however.   To have a publication date implies that an #$InformationBearingObject has been made available to, or accessible by, the public or a portion of the public.  Publication date is not the same as creation date.  An #$InformationBearingObject that has been created, but not made available to anyone except its creator, has not been published and has no #$publicationDate-IBO.")
(disjointWith Water Brush)
(comment Mace-ArilOfNutmegSeed "The bright red aril on the outside of nutmeg seed, which is used as a spice (mace).")
(comment UruguayanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Uruguay, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith PharmaceuticsAndTherapeuticsCommittee PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization)
(comment TelevisionSet-DirectView "The collection of television sets

which have the usual electron-gun picture tube as opposed to

a rear or front projection system.")
(comment AustroasiaticLanguageFamily "Languages of Indo-China")
(comment Lantern "The set of lighting devices which consist of a transparent or translucent case enclosing a light and protecting it from wind, rain, etc.; often used outdoors on patios or for camping trips.")
(comment JumpingUpAndDown "Repeatedly springing vertically into the air through rapid extension of the legs.")
(comment focalActivityType "(#$focalActivityType ORG ACT-TYPE) means that ACT-TYPE is the type of activity which is the main focus of ORG.  For example, basketball [(#$PlayingFn #$Basketball-TheGame)] is the focal activity of the NBA (#$NationalBasketballAssociation) and of each instance of #$BasketballTeam.")
(disjointWith BabyWalker Tricycle)
(comment ComputerProgramModule-CW "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are not intended to operate by themselves, but do contain procedures that can be utilized by other #$ComputerProgram-CWs.  Positive examples: DLLs, the #$CycCanonicalizer, #$PlugInPrograms. Negative examples: #$CycKB.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization CriminalOrganization)
(comment ToothbrushHolder "The collection of cup-shaped containers intended to hold toothbrushes and toothpaste tubes when they are not in use.  This collection is not intended to cover the single-toothbrush containers used for travel.")
(comment PeronosporalesOrder "A biological order within the fungus kingdom which is one of the orders within the division Oomycota (water molds)")
(comment maxDepthForConveyance "(#$maxDepthForConveyance CRAFT DEPTH) says

 that the deepest underwater that CRAFT can

  safely go is DEPTH.")
(disjointWith Respiration PregnancyEndingEvent)
(comment TrueRib "A #$TrueRib is connected to the lage.")
(comment Family-SocialEntity "A specialization of #$Group.  Each instance of #$Family-SocialEntity is a group of people or of other animals related by birth and mating.  The kinship relation between group-members of an instance of #$Family-SocialEntity  is closer than simply being members of the same species.  Instances of #$Family-SocialEntity may (but need not) function together as an #$Organization (q.v.).  See also the specialization #$Family-Human.")
(comment ProjectileShellAssembly "This collection includes #$ProjectileWeapons whose parts include a casing (#$ProjectileCasing) which contains a projectile (e.g. #$ProjectileSlug-Bullet) or projectiles (#$Shotgun shot). The casing itself is discarded after the projectile is launched.  Positive examples include #$ArtilleryShells, rifle cartridges, and pistol cartridges.  Negative examples include musket balls and cannon balls.")
(comment Vegetable-Plant "A specialization of #$Plant-NonWoody: a collection of plants that play a special role in human nutrition.  Each instance of #$Vegetable-Plant is a plant that produces the edible things that we normally call `vegetables' (which can include fruits, seeds, stalks, leaves, or other parts, or even the whole plant). For that which we normally call `cereals', however, see #$CerealPlant.  #$Vegetable-Plants grow and produce the vegetables that are eaten; vegetable plants are not necessarily also instances of #$Food.  See #$Vegetable-Food for the collection of vegetables--plants or (more usually) plant parts--that are eaten by humans.")
(comment ProgramAction "A collection of actions performed by computers. Instances include displaying text and images on a monitor, making sounds, input and output actions, and manipulation of external objects. #$ProgramAction does not include actions of humans or other external agents to initiate the action of the computer.")
(comment ElectriciansTool "A device used in wiring or other tasks commonly performed by an electrician.")
(disjointWith BaseballFielding SkyDiving)
(comment reproductionOf "ARG1 is a copy of the #$InformationBearingThing ARG2.")
(comment Triceps "The large muscle that runs along the back of the upper arm")
(disjointWith GameBoard FurniturePiece)
(comment OldEnglishSheepdog "A collection of medium-sized dogs with thick, shaggy coats.")
(comment Baronet "The collection of all baronets, or male persons who hold hereditary baronetcy titles, the lowest in the system of nobility of the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland, or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf.")
(disjointWith ManufacturingOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment RubberStampDevice "An instance is a small piece of rubber with a handle, used for            printing dates or names on paper.")
(comment TransverseThoracis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$TransverseThoracis #$Muscle.  The #$TransverseThoracis #$Muscle connects the #$Sternum with the ribs, serving to narrow the chest during #$Exhaling.")
(comment Ceramic "The substance which is basically fired clay such as porcelain.")
(comment Sewing "The action of stitching by hand or by machine.")
(comment Diner "A kind of generally less-expensive, no-frills restaurant.")
(comment VideoDriver "A #$ComputerProgram-CW that acts as an interface between an instance of #$VideoController and an instance of #$OperatingSystem. The #$VideoDriver usually presents a standard interface to the operating system, allowing the #$VideoController to be manipulated in a standard way.")
(disjointWith PublishedMaterial Currency)
(comment WhiteMatter "The collection of all instances of white matter tissue, considered as an #$OrganicStuff.  #$WhiteMatter is nervous tissue consisting of myelinated #$Axons with no cell bodies, as opposed to #$GrayMatter which is nervous tissue where the bodies of #$Neurons are concentrated.")
(comment Tool "A specialization of both #$PhysicalDevice and #$Device-UserControlled (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$Tool is a  device that is used by people to manipulate or alter other objects  or the immediate environment in some way.  (Thus it does not include  #$PomPoms, e.g.)  #$Tools are typically controlled by their user  during use and can be used more than once (so #$Tool is disjoint  with #$Device-OneTimeUse).  #$Tool includes devices used in many  different activities, as shown by this sampling its subcollections: #$WoodworkingTool, #$PlumbingTool, some (but not all) kinds of  #$MedicalDevices, #$CleaningImplement, and #$WritingImplement.")
(comment Pre-VerbPhraseModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which only modify verb phrases by left-attaching them. Example: 'quickly', as in 'He quickly went inside.'")
(comment ChinesePerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$China-PeoplesRepublic, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Macron-TheSymbol "A mark that looks like a dash. When placed above a vowel, it often indicates that the vowel should be lengthened.")
(comment ElectricalGenerator "The collection of electrical generators -- devices that convert mechanical energy to electricity (ususally by means of magnets)")
(comment Lying-Physical "The collection of all actions in which an animal capable of an upright posture assumes a posture in which the body is stretched out flat against a horizontal surface, such as the ground or a bed.")
(comment ROM "Read only memory.")
(comment BladedWeapon-NonProjectile "The collection of all hand held #$Weapons with blades (see #$BladeOfADevice).  This includes as subsets #$Swords, #$Daggers, and bayonets.  Weapons such as the knives attached to the wheels of Ben Hur's chariot are not included in this collection because they are not hand held.")
(comment CherryKoolAid "#$KoolAid with cherry flavoring.")
(comment DorsalRamusT3 "The collection of all T3 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT3 and DorsalRamiT3 branch from SpinalRootT3.  DorsalRamiT3 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment Coffee-Instant "All the dry, instant coffee in the universe.")
(comment HumanAdult "A specialization of #$Person, and an instance of #$HumanTypeByLifeStageType. Each instance of this collection is a person old enough to participate as an independent, mature member of society. In most modern Western contexts it is assumed that anyone over 18 is an adult.  However, in many cultures, adulthood occurs when one reaches puberty.  Adulthood is #$contiguousAfter (q.v.) childhood. Notable specializations of this collection include #$AdultMaleHuman, #$AdultFemaleHuman, #$MiddleAgedHuman and #$OldHuman.")
(comment ComputerProcessRunning "The collection of events in which a process is executed on a #$Computer, and therefore using the #$Computer's resources. Examples: a #$ComputerProgram-CW running, an #$OperatingSystem in use, or a #$ComputerCrashing event.  Important specs are #$ComputerProcess-Generic for the complete operation of a computer program from start to finish and #$ProgramAction for the execution of code as designed (thus excluding the #$ComputerCrashing event.)")
(comment AntibacterialCleanser "A substance containing an antibiotic, which is intended to be used to clean wounds and inhibit them from becoming infected.")
(comment inhalingToxicityFor "(#$inhalingToxicityFor STUFF ORGTYPE TOXLEVEL) means that under ordinary circumstances, stuff has the #$Toxicity TOXLEVEL for instances of ORGTYPE that inhale it.")
(disjointWith FoodUtensil ControlDevice)
(comment Frangula "Rhamnus frangula, also known as glossy buckthorn.")
(comment SurinamePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Suriname, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment OrganizationTypeByGeographicReach "A collection of four disjoint collections, #$InternationalOrganization, #$NationalOrganization, #$StateOrProvinceWideOrganization, and #$LocalOrganization.  The #$Organizations that are instances of the collections which are instances of #$OrganizationTypeByGeographicReach are distinguished by their primary scope of activity, membership and ownership within a particular geographic region.  #$Organizations such as #$City, #$State-UnitedStates, and #$IndependentCountry are not specailizations of any of the instances of #$OrganizationTypeByGeographicReach.  Because instances of #$City or #$State-UnitedStates are not confined in terms of activity to a particular geographic region, those collections are not specializations of, respectively, #$LocalOrganization or #$StateOrProvinceWideOrganization. ")
(comment MedicalThermometer "Thermometers that are normally used for medical purposes.")
(disjointWith Hand Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(disjointWith VegetableMatter DairyProduct)
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization ConstructionCompany)
(comment VersionedProgram "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW which represent programs which are in the most literal sense bought, downloaded, and run on a machine.  Instances are typically NATs formed using #$SoftwareVersionFn where the first (and only) argument is an

instance of #$UnversionedProgram.  Positive examples: (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Linux-RedHat ''6.1'') (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$WU-FTPD-TheProgram ''2.5'').  Negative examples: #$Linux-RedHat, #$WU-FTPD-TheProgram.  The latter are instances of #$UnversionedProgram.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareOrganization DrugStoreChain)
(comment WeldingMask "The masks worn by people who are welding, to protect their faces from sparks and their eye from the intense glare.")
(disjointWith Constructing MakingWrittenMaterial)
(comment Menopause "The process in which a human woman stops going through a menstrual cycle.")
(comment DashboardPadding "The padding  which protects passengers and the dashboard from damage due to physical impact")
(comment lowercaseOfLetter "(#$lowercaseOfLetter LOWERCASE LETTER) means that LOWERCASE is the lower-case character corresponding to the character LETTER (which may be uppercase, lowercase, or case-less).  For example, the folowing holds: (#$uppercaseOfLetter #$LatinSmallLetterA #$A-TheLetter)")
(comment SunTanLotion "Applying this to skin prevents #$Sunburn for a few hours.")
(disjointWith Climbing Swimming-Generic)
(comment LawnMower-HandPushed "A collection of devices; a subset of #$LawnMower. Each instance of

#$LawnMower-HandPushed is a lawnmower which is pushed by its user, as

opposed to riding mowers (see #$LawnMower-Riding). This collection

includes both lawnmowers whose blades are powered by gas or electric (see

#$LawnMower-Power) and those whose blades are powered by hand (see

#$LawnMower-HandPowered).")
(comment Terrier-Yorkshire "A collection of very small dogs, ideally around 7 lbs., called, affectionately, Yorkies.  They generally have blue hair on their bodies with tan on their heads.  Their fur is long and silky.")
(disjointWith AttackByComputerOperation Attack-Verbal)
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByIndustry PersonTypeByPositionInOrg)
(comment Fishhook "The collection of all instances of #$Hook that are specifically designed to be attached to one end of a #$FishingLine and used to catch fish. Instances of #$Fishhook are #$PointyEnded and have a barb so that they go into the fish easily, but do not come out easily.")
(comment LatissimusDorsi "The #$Collection of all instances of #$LatissimusDorsi #$Muscle.  The #$LatissimusDorsi, located in the #$Back-AnimalBodyPart, is shaped like a triangle with its apex on the #$Humerus and its base on the lower #$SpinalColumn.  It moves the #$Humerus.")
(comment Sponge-CleaningImplement "A piece of very porous, absorbent material, which can hold quite a bit of liquid, used to clean surfaces.  True sponges are the 'skeletons' of colonial marine organisms; cleaning sponges are also made of synthetic material.")
(comment CervicalNerve "The first 8 pairs of #$SpinalNerves; arising roughly from the first 8 vertebra.")
(comment Morbier-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Morbier, a French cheese.

It has a distinctive line of edible wood ash through the middle.")
(comment Ribonucleotide-GIS "The collection of all abstract nucleotides [#$Nucleotide-GIS] which are instantiated by instances of #$Ribonucleotide.")
(comment WaterPropeller "The collection of propellers intended to be used in water, usually to propel ships or boats.")
(comment BacterialToxin "A collection of toxins produced by #$Bacterium.  This
collection includes #$Exotoxins and #$Endotoxins.  #$Exotoxins are
those toxins secreted by the #$Bacterium that affect particular sites
of the body.  #$Endotoxins are those toxins not secreted and are
instead released after death of the cell.")
(comment ColoringBook "a small book containing line drawings, intended for children to color.")
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument ContainerArtifact)
(comment KenyanPerson "The people who are #$citizens of #$Kenya, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment CentralDravidianLanguageFamily "Branch of major non-Indo-European languages of India")
(comment ElectricalHeatingElement "The collection of all heating elements that produce heat by having an electic current passed through them.")
(comment derivedConceptualWork "(#$derivedConceptualWork ORIGINAL_WORK DERIVED_WORK) means that DERIVED_WORK is a new #$DevisedPracticeOrWork that has been adapted or derived from ORIGINAL_WORK, but some of the ORIGINAL_WORK has been omitted.  This is the relationship of a #$2001-ASpaceOdyssey-TheBook to #$2001-ASpaceOdyssey-TheMovie, #$Golf to #$MiniatureGolf, Netscape 3.0 to Netscape 4.0, Francis Scott Key's version of the Star-Spangled Banner to Jimmy Hendrix's, or #$RomeoAndJuliet-ThePlay to #$WestSideStory-ThePlay (and transitively to the movie [#$Movie-CW]).")
(comment ManifestationOfFeelingFn "#$ManifestationOfFeelingFn takes an instance of

 #$FeelingAttribute and returns the collection of

 #$Actions that are physical manifestations of 

 that attribute.  For example, (#$ManifestationOfFeelingFn 

BlindRage) is the collection of activites that express

 blind rage.  An example instance of this collection

 might be Bob throwing his chair against the wall.")
(comment AdventureGameProgram "The collection of all  #$ComputerGamePrograms which are 'adventure' games.")
(comment HumanResourcesDepartment "Each instance of #$HumanResourcesDepartment consists of employees who are responsible for an organization's human resources (the hiring, firing, training, paying, and general looking after of personnel).")
(comment PerformaComputer "The Apple line of Performa computers.")
(comment tactuallyPerceives "(#$tactuallyPerceives AGENT OBJECT) means that AGENT perceives the (partially) tangible object or physical event OBJECT via the sense of touch.  This implies that AGENT is sensuously aware of one or more of OBJECT's tactile qualities.")
(comment AnteriorDirection "The general direction towards the front and away from the back, in or near an object that is #$AnimalBodyShaped and in an #$UprightPosture.  In the case of a #$Person this direction almost always corresponds to #$VentralDirection.")
(comment BritishCuisine "The collection of instances of what Americans think of as British food")
(comment MotorcycleAccessory "A collection of tangible objects.  Each element is something that may be useful for riding or traveling by motorcycle: special clothing, helmets, bags, etc.")
(comment Burner "A burner on a stove.")
(disjointWith (TransportViaFn LandTransportationDevice) (TransportViaFn Spacecraft))
(comment PublicTransportationScheduleDocument "The collection of documents that contain information about when various vehicles for public transportation are supposed to leave, where they're headed, etc.")
(comment Bone-BodyPart "The collection of hard largely calcareous body parts of which the adult skeleton of most vertebrates is chiefly composed.")
(disjointWith GardeningTool WritingImplement)
(comment CatTypeByBreed "A collection of collections. Each instance is a collection of cats all belonging to the same breed.")
(comment SaintHelenaIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$SaintHelena-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization RealEstateOrganization)
(comment TurbofanEngine "The collection of all #$TurbojetEngines in 

which a fan supplements the total thrust by forcing air

 diverted from the main engine directly into the

  hot turbine exhaust.")
(comment GSpot "A g-spot is a center of sexual maximum sensitivity in a woman's #$Vagina.  Whether or not the g-spot exists, or exists for all women has been debated.")
(comment ArtistsOilPaint "The oil paint used by artists.")
(comment SnowPea-Foodstuff "Snow peas in edible forms.")
(comment PoliceOrganization "The collection of law enforcement agencies that are legally empowered to enforce laws.  This collection includes police forces, national bureaux of investigation, some forest services, park police, hunting and game commission officers, border police, governmental executive protection services, military police, etc.  It does NOT include those instances of #$LawEnforcementOrganization that only track and disseminate information about criminal activity, but do not directly enforce laws (e.g., #$INTERPOL).")
(comment characterInCW "(#$characterInCW AGENT CW) means that AGENT is a character in the #$ConceptualWork CW.  AGENT may be a #$FictionalCharacter or not depending upon the CW.")
(comment InsecurePasswordFileFault "A program has

an #$InsecurePasswordFileFault if a specially-formed input

to that program will yield a copy of the #$PasswordFile to an

unauthorized user.")
(comment Heterotroph "A specialization of #$Organism-Whole.  Each instance of #$Heterotroph is an organism incapable of manufacturing organic nutrients from inorganic raw materials.  All instances of #$Animal are instances of #$Heterotroph, since animals must eat other living things, or parts of living things, in order to get the nutrients they need to live.  Other specializations of #$Heterotroph include #$ParasiticOrganism and #$Fungus. Cf. #$Autotroph.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterM "The lowercase letter 'm'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$M-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterM.")
(comment GasCookingRange "A #$CookingRange which usesEnergyType #$NaturalGas.")
(disjointWith CoveringOnesOwnFace SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment GunTypeByFeedSystem "Every instance of #$GunTypeByFeedSystem is a collection of guns  according to how ammunition is fed into the #$Gun.  For example, whether  a gun uses a clip or a belt of ammunition.")
(comment HardwareSerialBus "A type of bus found in computers that is only capable of transmitting a single bit of information at one moment in time. Typically accessed via the serial port. Because each byte has to be chopped up into bits, the transfer rate is low.")
(disjointWith SpeciallyCharteredInstitution Committee-Organization)
(comment TelephoneSystem "This collection includes systems involving two or more #$Telephones connected in a network. See also #$SystemOfDevices.")
(comment BicycleCrossbar "A #$BicycleCrossbar is an #$ExistingObjectType which can contain some containedSubstance.")
(comment MedialCord-BrachialPlexus "The collection of all medial cords of the brachial plexus.  The medial cord is formed by the anterior division of the #$InferiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus.  Nerves formed from the medial cord are the #$UlnarNerve and the #$MedianNerve.")
(comment BabyFood "This is the collection of all instances of baby food. Most baby food is

commerically produced and comes in jars, but instances of #$BabyFood can

also be home-made. What makes something baby food is that it is prepared

specially for consumption by a baby. This generally means that it requires

no chewing to eat.")
(comment presuppositionForUseOfTerm "(#$presuppositionForUseOfTerm TERM SENTENCE) says that SENTENCE makes explicit some of the information that is presupposed or glossed over in the use of the #$PresuppositionVocabTerm, TERM.")
(comment WindowManagerProgram "The collection of graphical, window-oriented command interpreters.")
(comment StorageRollCore "A cylindrical core on which sheetlike or cordlike stuff is wound for storage purposes.  Disposable cores are usually made of paper, cardboard, or plastic (for example, the paper core in a roll of toilet paper); reusable cores, such as bobbins, of plastic, wood, or metal.")
(comment TwoDimensionalArtObject "The collection of #$ArtObjects which are primarily two dimensional. Positive examples of subcollections include #$Painting-ArtForm, #$PenAndInkDrawing, and #$Engraving. Negative examples include #$Sculpture or #$LiteraryWork-CW.")
(comment ExteriorRegionFn "The function (ExteriorRegionFn REGOROBJ), applied to a region or object REGOROBJ, means the sub-region consisting of all the outer parts or sections of REGOROBJ, or the exterior main portion of REGOROBJ.  It applies when REGOROBJ itself has an intrinsic inside/outside orientation (unlike, say, a loop of thread), but if REGOROBJ is an enveloping part, surface membrane, ring or layer within or on a larger region or object that has its own inside/outside orientation, the function returns REGOROBJ's outside portion with respect to the inside and outside of the larger region or object.")
(comment publisherOfWork "(#$publisherOfWork WORK AGENT) means that the #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK was published by the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT.  Not all #$StructurallySpecificWorks have publishers.  To be published, copies of a work must have been distributed to the public or an identifiable subset of the public consisting of more than a few members.")
(comment SesameSeed "The seed of a sesame plant.")
(comment HermIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Herm-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OpticalShop PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization)
(comment VideoCassette-Blank "This is the collection of video cassettes

that have not yet been recorded on.")
(comment Andean-EquatorialLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages spoken mainly in South America")
(comment CasseroleDish "A dish that can be used either on the stove or in the oven, made of ceramic or glass, often with a lid.")
(comment WavingAFist "The set of actions in which a performer raises a clenched fist and moves it back and forth in a triumphant or defiant gesture.  This is not the personally threatening action of #$ShakingAFist at someone.")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent PreservingFood)
(comment TransportationCompany "A specialization of both #$TransportationOrganization and #$ServiceOrganization.  Each instance of #$TransportationCompany is an organization that provide transportation (of goods or persons) to customers for a fee.  Specializations of #$TransportationCompany include the collections #$ShippingOrganization and #$AirlineCompany.")
(disjointWith HarvesterAgriculturalImplement TrainEngine)
(comment EasterEggProgram "An Easter Egg is a hidden feature or novelty that the programmers            have put in their software. This can be anything from a hidden list            of the developers, to hidden commands, to jokes, to funny animations.")
(comment includesWithProductType "The predicate #$includesWithProductType is used to specify extra goods or services that a particular seller includes with a specific product.  (#$includesWithProductType SELLER MAINTYPE EXTRATYPE) means that the #$CommercialOrganization SELLER provides an item of the #$ProductType EXTRATYPE free of charge to its customers who purchase a product of #$ProductType MAINTYPE.  For example, to say that Ernie's Garage provides towing free with a car repair, we could say (#$includesWithProductType ErniesGarage (#$RepairingFn #$Automobile) #$TowingAnAutomobile).")
(comment NailScissors "Scissors designed for cutting fingernails or toenails.")
(disjointWith Respiration ImmuneResponse)
(comment Chalk-WritingImplement "The collection of pieces of calcite material used to write on blackboards.")
(comment Carnivore "An #$OrganismClassificationType that classifies organisms by their typical source of food.  Instances of #$Carnivore typically eat animals (or animal parts or animal-derived products) exclusively.  Note that #$Carnivore is _not_ an instance of #$BiologicalTaxon (q.v.); cf. #$CarnivoreOrder.  Also note that a #$Carnivore is not necessarily a #$Heterotroph; e.g. carnivorous plants both digest insects and produce food using #$Chlorophyll.")
(comment ProgramAction-HumanInitiated "A collection of events. Each #$ProgramAction-HumanInitiated is #$performedBy a #$Person, using a #$Computer as a device. See #$ProgramAction for actions performed by #$Computers. Each #$ProgramAction-HumanInitiated includes at least one #$ProgramAction as a subevent.")
(comment AnimalSoap "The kind of soap used to wash animals.")
(comment OilPainting "OilPaintings as representational art forms")
(comment Larynx "The collection of all Larynxes, which contains the #$VocalCords in #$Persons, most other #$Mammals, and some other air-breathing #$Vertebrates. A #$Larynx connects the windpipe (#$Trachea) to the #$Pharynx.")
(disjointWith Umbrella FurniturePiece)
(comment NorwegianElkhound "A collection of medium-sized dogs. The Norwegian Elkhound is the national dog of Norway.")
(comment MuslimPerson "The collection of all persons who believe in the basic fundamental tenets of Islam, or who practice Islamic religious rituals, or are recognized by other Muslims to be Muslims, or all of these.")
(disjointWith HealthcareOrganization StorageOrganization)
(comment GeographicInformationSystem "A #$GeographicInformationSystem is a computer system capable of            assembling, storing, manipulating, and displaying geographically           referenced information, i.e. data identified according to their            locations.")
(comment Insect "An instance of #$BiologicalClass, and a specialization of #$Arthropod.  Each instance of #$Insect is an arthropod whose body is segmented into thirds, with three pairs of legs, a pair of antennae, and sometimes two pairs of wings.  Specializations of #$Insect include #$Bee, #$Ant, and #$Butterfly.")
(comment ExtensorIndicis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExtensorIndicis #$Muscle.  The #$ExtensorIndicis extends the #$ProximalPhalanx of the #$IndexFinger.")
(comment BedSheet "The removable piece of cloth which covers a mattress.")
(disjointWith ProductDistributionEvent CreationEvent)
(comment MeatCutType "Instances of #$MeatCutType are the standard ways in which butchers divide animal carcasses into food portions and products.")
(disjointWith NonPublishedText Currency)
(comment GrayMatter "The collection of all instances of gray matter tissue, considered as an #$OrganicStuff.  #$GrayMatter is nervous tissue where the bodies of #$Neurons are concentrated, as opposed to #$WhiteMatter which is nervous tissue consisting of myelinated #$Axons with no cell bodies.")
(comment Dynamite "A specialization of #$HighExplosive.  Each instance of #$Dynamite is an explosive combination of nitroglycerin and diatomaceous earth.  Dynamite was invented by #$AlfredNobel.")
(comment FrameForPrepositions "Subcategorization frames which make sense for #$Prepositions.")
(comment CatholicPerson "The collection of people who adhere to a faith in #$Catholicism. Note that an instance of #$CatholicPerson may not necessarily  believe in (or adhere to) catholic edicts as laid down by the #$Pope and still consider themselves Catholics (e.g., they may use #$BirthControlPill or #$Condom and thus be technically outside #$Catholicism but still be a  #$CatholicPerson).")
(comment Gun-Repeating "The collection of #$Guns that have a number of cartridges stored in some form of magazine.  These are fed into the chamber by a hand-powered  mechanism.    It is necessary to work the mechanism before each shot.   #$Revolvers are an example.")
(comment Hacek-TheSymbol "A mark that looks like a small letter V. When placed above a letter, it often indicates that the letter should be pronounced as an affricate.")
(comment ToiletTank "The toilet tank where water for flushing is kept.")
(comment Decorating "The activity of making something nicer by adding ornaments.")
(comment PhysicalMemory "Physical or main memory")
(comment MaxiPad "A larger #$SanitaryNapkin - larger,

that is, than a #$MiniPad.")
(comment KoolAid "A beverage usually enjoyed by children, composed of sugar and fruit flavoring dissolved in water.")
(comment VentralRamusS2 "The collection of all S2 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusS2 and #$DorsalRamusS2 branch from SpinalRootS2.  #$VentralRamusS2 supplies the #$SacralPlexus.")
(comment Coffee-Hot "Coffee served hot, and thus always a liquid.  See also #$Coffee-Beverage if you strictly want the stuff in an unspecified state.")
(comment Mask "The collection of items worn on the face; used to protect the face, as part of a costume, or to obscure the identity.")
(comment Rifle "Single-user gun with a long rifled barrel - gets the bullet spinning and improves reliability of aim.")
(comment CoxiellaBurnetti "The pathogen (rickettsia) that causes Q Fever (#$QFever).")
(comment PayStub "The collection of all documents received by #$Employees from employers stating how much the employee was paid for the previous pay period, what monies were withheld from the wages due (e.g. taxes, insurance cotributions, union dues, ...), and to whom those funds were paid.  Other information that may appear on a pay stub relate to available leave.")
(comment SetOfTeeth "group of teeth used in chewing food")
(comment SubcollectionRelationFunction "A collection of ternary #$SubcollectionFunctions that take a predicate as their second argument and something that all instances of a collection denoted by them bear a relation to as their third argument.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice TransportationDevice-Vehicle)
(comment Hydrangea "The collection of Hydrangea woody shrubs and vines. Several species are cultivated in greenhouses and gardens for their showy flower clusters.")
(comment GambiaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Gambia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByGeographicReach PersonTypeByPositionInOrg)
(comment PruningSaw "A hand tool used for cutting, comprised of a handle and a blade that contains a row of sharp teeth along one edge.")
(disjointWith Foot-AnimalBodyPart Limb-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment RawEdibles "A collection of things that normal humans can eat or drink. Instances of #$RawEdibles have not been cooked. Of these, those that are normally eaten raw are instances of #$RawFood, while those that are not are typically converted into instances of #$FoodOrDrink in a #$CookingFood event.")
(comment IntransitiveFrameType "The collection of all frames for words that can be used intransitively, that is, without any complements at all.")
(comment POPClientProgram "#$POPClientProgram is the collection of #$EMailClientPrograms thatimplement the Post Office Protocol - Version 3 (POP3), which is intended to permit a workstation to access a maildrop on a server host

dynamically.  Usually, this means that the #$POPClientProgram is used

to allow a workstation to retrieve mail that the server is holding for

it.")
(disjointWith InformationProvidingOrganization MedicalCareOrganization)
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single Conveying-Generic)
(comment VaginalBirthEvent "Vaginal delivery of a baby.")
(comment PlaceMat "A sheet-like object, roughly twice the size of a plate, used to decorate and protect a table, one at each seating place.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType RoadVehicleType)
(comment compatibleWithStandard "(compatibleWithStandard PROD STAND SCRIPT ASLOT) states that instances of product type PROD are compatible in scripts of type SCRIPT with anything which meets standard STAND when it is the actor ASLOT in the script.")
(disjointWith DiggingAHole FluidFlowEvent)
(comment Gum-AnimalBodyPart "The tissue that surrounds the necks of teeth.")
(comment Terrier-Skye "A collection of small dogs with long, straight hair.")
(comment VersionsInclusiveFn "(#$VersionsInclusiveFn SOFTWARE-OBJ VER1 VER2) denotes the series of software versions from VER1 to VER2 inclusive that correspond to SOFTWARE-OBJ, an instance of #$UnversionedSoftwareObject.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType OrganizationTypeByIndustry)
(comment BowForStringInstrument "The collection of all bows designed to be used in events of type (#$InstrumentPlayingFn #$StringInstrument).")
(comment Subclavius "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Subclavius #$Muscle.  The #$Subclavius #$Muscle connects the #$FirstRib #$CostalCartilage junction with the #$Clavicle.")
(comment WashCloth "A small, approximately one-square-foot, piece of cloth used to clean surfaces.")
(comment CoccygealNerve "The pair of #$SpinalNerves located near the #$Coccyx, at the base of the spine.")
(comment MontereyJack-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Monterey Jack, an American cheese.

Most varieties are melting cheeses, although there are also aged Monterey Jacks.")
(comment BacterialNeurotoxin "A collection of a kind of #$Exotoxin that acts primarily on
the nerve-muscle junctions.  These toxins inhibit the release of
acetylcholine and consequently prevent the nerve stimulation of the
muscles.")
(comment EroticStory "The subset of #$Story whose elements contain the propositional content in which two or  more instances of #$Person engage in #$HumanSexualBehavior.")
(disjointWith ContainerArtifact CommunicationDevice)
(comment NepalesePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Nepal, or participates in its #$NationalCulture..")
(comment PortableAudioEquipment "The collection of #$AudioSystems which are also #$PortableObjects and#$SelfPoweredDevices. What makes an instance of #$AudioSystem portable or mobile is that it is both lightweight enough to be carried easily by a #$Person and  can be operated without requiring that it be plugged into a external power source. A device can be an instance of #$PortableAudioEquipment even if it can be operated by an external power source, as long as it is also an instance of #$SelfPoweredDevice. A positive example is a #$Walkman. A negative example is a #$CompactDiscPlayer that is part of a home entertainmnet audio system (#$HomeAudioSystem).")
(comment actorPartsAffected "(#$actorPartsAffected ACT PART) means that PART is an #$objectActedOn in ACT, and it is one of the #$anatomicalParts of the organism which is #$bodilyActedOn in ACT.  For example, during a man's morning shave, his #$Beard is an #$actorPartsAffected, but the hand with which he shaves is not, because his beard is changed, but his hand is not changed (`acted on') in any significant way.")
(comment SouthDravidianLanguageFamily "Branch of major non-Indo-European languages of India")
(comment Saucer "The small plate-like vessel which is often used beneath a teacup.")
(comment knownSentence "A #$KBDependentRelation (q.v.) and  specialization of #$trueSentence (q.v.) that is used to state  that a given sentence is \"known\" to be true to the Cyc system. More precisely, (#$knownSentence SENT) means that SENT is provable  by the Cyc inference engine from sentences currently in the Knowledge  Base.  #$knownSentence is a non-assertible predicate (see  #$notAssertible).  Note that this predicate is not to be confused  with #$assertedSentence, which is used to state that a given  sentence is explicitly asserted in the KB.")
(comment AnimalMigration "The collection of regular, species-linked movements of an animal or group of animals from one place to another, usually with a return to the starting point after a certain period of time.  In some species, the migration cycle occurs once in a lifetime, while others migrate annually on a seasonal basis.   Migration is typically linked with an animal's reproductive cycle (as in salmon), but may also involve seasonal relocation to a more hospitable climate and/or more plentiful food supply. For example, many birds exhibit seasonal migration; e.g., native Northeastern U.S. birds that spend their winters in the Southern U.S.")
(comment arg3NotIsa "(#$arg3NotIsa REL COL) means that nothing given as the third argument to the #$Relation REL may be known to be an element of the #$Collection COL.")
(comment ArcadeGameProgram "A specialization of #$ComputerGameProgram.  Each instance of #$ArcadeGameProgram is a program that was originally played in arcades, but is now playable on PCs and/or #$HomeVideoGameMachines. Instances are games such as 'Tetris' or 'Donkey Kong'.")
(comment InsuranceClaimsDepartment "A #$DepartmentTypeByFunction and a specialization of #$FinanceDepartment.  Each instance of #$InsuranceClaimsDepartment consists of employees who settle an organization's insurance claims.")
(comment EffexorProduct "An #$AntiDepressant drug product manufactuered by Wyeth.")
(comment AnimalTypeByBodyPosition "Describes the spatial relationship of the body to an object.")
(comment anteriorTo "(#$anteriorTo OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 lies in the #$AnteriorDirection of OBJ-2, when viewed in the frame of reference of the object with #$AnimalBodyShape (often, a #$Person) that they are located in.  In a #$Person, #$anteriorTo almost always corresponds to #$ventralTo, but in a #$Dog or other four-legged animal, #$anteriorTo usually corresponds to the inverse of #$caudalTo.  Note that if OBJ-1 is #$anteriorTo OBJ-2, OBJ-2 is posterior to OBJ-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `posterior to'.  OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.  #$anteriorTo is used in the #$Head-AnimalBodyPart and #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart instead of #$ventralTo.")
(comment NorthAmericanCuisine "All the kinds of foods `commonly eaten' in North America, most of which have been borrowed and adapted from elsewhere.  Not a very well-defined collection, but better than nothing at the moment")
(comment Mouthpiece-Instrument "This is the collection of the physical parts of instances of #$WindInstrument-Musical which are placed in the mouth when the instrument is played.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess LawEnforcementActivity)
(comment ElectricGrill "An electric grill used for #$GrillingFood.")
(comment RoadVehicle "A specialization of both #$LandTransportationDevice and #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle.  Each instance of #$RoadVehicle is a self-powered vehicle designed primarily for travel on roads (although some instances may also have limited off-road capabilities).  Notable specializations of #$RoadVehicle include #$Automobile, #$Truck, and #$Bus-RoadVehicle.  Since #$RoadVehicle is a specialization of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle, each instance of #$RoadVehicle is self-powered.  Consequently, road transportation devices which are not self-powered (for example, all the instances of #$Bicycle) are not included in this collection.")
(comment WorkScheduleDocument "The collection of documents that contain information about when each employee is supposed to work.")
(comment Hamstrings "Muscle which runs along the back of the thigh")
(disjointWith PryingImplement WritingImplement)
(comment CostaRicanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$CostaRica, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations engaged in the beauty or cosmetic industry or whose activities focus on that industry.  An example of a specialization of #$Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization is #$BodyPiercingStudio.")
(comment TurbojetPropelledAircraft "The collection of all aircraft propelled by #$TurbojetEngines.")
(comment AnsweringMachine "Telephone answering machine")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity ElevatorCarMoving)
(comment TurnipRoot-Foodstuff "Turnip root in any of its edible forms.")
(comment GovernmentIntelligenceOrganization "The collection of all intelligence organizations funded by governments, either military or non-military.  Examples include KGB, FBI, CIA, U.S. Navy Intelligence, etc.  Note that, currently (6/16/98), we assume that for each country, the group of all its intelligence organizations is also an intelligence organization.  For example, there is an element, (#$IntelligenceCommunityFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica), of this collection which includes FBI, CIA, as well as the U.S. Navy Intelligence, etc.")
(comment Pupa "A collection of stages in the lives of individual organisms; a subset of #$BiologicalStageOfDevelopment.  Each element of #$Pupa is a stage during which a metamorphic insect such as a butterfly changes its form from the larval to the adult stage.")
(comment EarthMovingVehicle "#$EarthMovingVehicle is a specialization of #$ConstructionVehicle.  Each instance of #$EarthMovingVehicle is a heavy construction vehicle that is used to alter the shape of a region's terrain by moving around large quantities of earth, rocks, and so forth.  Often, #$EarthMovingVehicles are used in road construction, but they can also be used to prepare construction sites, erect barricades, excavate in strip mines or demolition sites, etc. They are powered by internal combustion engines and either have wheels or treads like tanks.")
(comment TheNthFn "(#$TheNthFn COLL N) denotes an instance of the collection COLL, whose referent depends on how it is used.  For example, when used as a term in a #$Scenario-Generalized, (#$TheNthFn #$Person 2) means the second person introduced in that scenario.")
(comment WebAdministratorAccount "The collection of accounts with privileges allowing users to
alter the web pages for a web site.")
(comment Card "An instance of #$ExistingObjectType, and a specialization of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject.  Each instance of #$Card is a small, sturdy sheet of stuff -- usually cardstock paper, although it could be plastic or thin metal -- bearing some kind of information.  Specializations of #$Card include #$CreditCard, #$BusinessCard, and #$PostCard.  Note that electronic objects that perform the same functions as some instances of #$Card (for example, electronic greeting cards) are not instances of #$Card.")
(comment Nerve "The collection of all nerves.  Each instance of #$Nerve is a bundle of many nerve fibers (#$Axons) covered with a wrapping of #$ConnectiveTissue.  Sensory nerves (see #$SensoryNerve) carry nerve impulses to the central nervous system; motor nerves (see #$MotorNerve) carry impulses to the muscles.  Most nerves are mixed, containing axons of both motor and sensory neurons.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterN "The capital letter 'N'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$N-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterN.")
(comment ClothesWasherConnection "The electrical and water supplies and drain for a washer.  I can't figure out what the drain should be an instance of -- not #$DrainOfBasin I think.")
(disjointWith ArmMovement SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment GunTypeByFiringFrequency "Every instance of #$GunTypeByFiringFrequency is a collection of  guns according to the frequency with which they can be fired.  For example, a shotgun could be a spec of #$Gun-Multibarreled, or a machine gun is  typically a #$FullyAutomaticFirearm.  Mortars, on the other hand, are  #$Gun-SingleShot.")
(comment ComputerBoard "A specialization of #$IntegratedCircuit and #$ComputerHardwareComponent.  Each instance of #$ComputerBoard is an insulated board on which interconnected circuits are mounted or etched.  Major specializations are the disjoint collections #$ComputerMotherBoard and #$ExpansionCard.")
(disjointWith Committee-Organization Court-Judicial)
(comment SepticSystem "The collection of all SepticSystems, each consisting a septic tank and septic drainfield connected by sewage pipes.")
(comment SpaceShuttleLivingQuarters "The interior of a space shuttle, where people can actually live for an extended period of time")
(comment VentralRamusT5 "The collection of all T5 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT5 and #$DorsalRamusT5 branch from SpinalRootT5.  #$VentralRamusT5 supplies below the #$FifthRib.")
(comment FrenchRegion "Instances of #$FrenchRegion are the immediate administrative

subdivision of #$France. They've been created in 1986 by recent

reforms. #$AroundTheYear2000, #$France has 26 regions, 4 of these oversea.")
(comment PasswordInformationForFn "(#$PasswordInformationForFn ACCOUNT_SYSTEM) denotes the #$PropositionalInformationThing that contains all the valid username/password combinations on ACCOUNT_SYSTEM.  See also #$PasswordFileForFn.")
(comment Porifera "This is the collection of (individual) animals in

the phylum Porifera. Porifera is the phylum of animalia that contains animals such as sponges that have porous bodies and contain no true tissues.")
(comment NaturalLanguageProgram "#$NaturalLanguageProgram is the collection of all computer programs that process natural language.")
(comment DinnerFork "Standard table fork used as an eating implement.  Larger than a salad fork.")
(comment MultipleFission "A collection of events that involves a repeated #$BinaryFission within a common bag-like structure.  This process occurs in some cynobacteria.")
(comment InteriorRegionFn "The function (InteriorRegionFn REGOROBJ), applied to a region or object REGOROBJ, means the sub-region consisting of the core or inner parts or sections of REGOROBJ, or the interior main portion of REGOROBJ.  It applies when REGOROBJ itself has an intrinsic inside/outside orientation (unlike, say, a loop of thread), but if REGOROBJ is an enveloping part, surface membrane, ring or layer within or on a larger region or object that has its own inside/outside orientation, the function returns REGOROBJ's inside portion with respect to the inside and outside of the larger region or object.")
(disjointWith Water InformationRecordingDevice)
(comment Coconut-TheSeed "The seed of the coconut palm; one of the largest seeds any plant produces, it has a woody seed coat and a liquid endosperm, which is called coconut milk.")
(comment MaldivesPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Maldives, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OpticalRetailer PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganization)
(comment VideoCassette-PreRecorded "This is the collection of video cassettes

that have had something professionally recorded on them.")
(comment DravidianLanguageFamily "languages of the probably aboriginal dark peoples of southern #$India, unrelated to Hindi, etc.")
(comment FireplaceScreen "The screen some people put in their fireplace to protect from flying sparks.")
(comment Patting "The collection of events in which a person applies a brief, usually gentle, touch to someone or something, using the extended fingers and the palm of the hand; often part of a rapid series of such touches.")
(disjointWith HarvesterAgriculturalImplement RoadVehicle)
(comment ActivityTypeFocusGroup "#$ActivityTypeFocusGroup is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$ActivityTypeFocusGroup is an organization which focuses on some type of activity, such as stamp collecting or sailing.")
(comment PowderedLaundryDetergent "Powdered Laundry Detergent")
(comment FloweringPlant "An instance of #$BiologicalClass and a specialization of #$Plant. Each instance of #$FloweringPlant is a plant whose seeds are enclosed in ovaries; consequently, this is the collection of flowering plants in the botanical sense.  For flowering plants actually in bloom, see the collection #$FloweryPlant.")
(comment acceptableStorageForm "(#$acceptableStorageForm THINGTYPE PRODTYPE) means that other things being equal, instances of THINGTYPE can be converted into instances of PRODUCTTYPE and stored for several decades, in such a way as to retain their 'intended' capabilities throughout the period of storage.")
(comment SkeletalSystem "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$SkeletalSystem is a system of body parts used to support, separate, and protect the other parts of a body.  Instances of this collection are either external structures (see #$Exoskeleton and #$Shell-AnimalBodyPart) or internally interlinked bones (see #$Bone-BodyPart) and cartilage (see #$Cartilage).")
(comment ProkaryoticProteinSynthesis "The collection of protein synthesis events that are subevents of prokaryotic gene expression.")
(comment BiologicalIntakeEvent "A specialization of #$TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure.  In each instance of #$BiologicalIntakeEvent, some object(s) are taken into some living structure.")
(comment LoggingInOnAComputer "The process of logging in.")
(comment ElectricalSupplyMarketCategory "The things sold as electrical supplies, used by electricians to do wiring.")
(comment Painting-ArtForm "The collection of paintings as representational art forms.  Paintings are tangible #$InformationBearingObjects, consisting of pigment applied to some surface (usually flat, often rectangular and sheetlike)")
(comment Retina "The collection of all retinas, sensory membranes that line the eye of a #$Vertebrate or #$Cephalopod, receive the image formed by the lens, are the immediate instruments of vision, and are connected with the #$Brain by the #$OpticNerve.  Some #$Insects also have #$Retinas.")
(comment PersonalComputer "A specialization of #$SingleUserComputer. Each instance of this collection is a small, single-user #$Computer, such as a desktop computer, a laptop computer or a palm computer.")
(comment Newfoundland-TheDog "A collection of large, web-footed dogs with thick coats.")
(comment BuddhistPerson "The collection of all persons who believe in (at least some of) the tenets of some type of Buddhism, or who practice Buddhist religious rituals, or both.")
(disjointWith HealthcareOrganization WorkersOrganization)
(comment AmateurRadioEquipment "An instance of #$AmateurRadioEquipment is a radio (device) that           can both send and receive messages.")
(comment PeroneusMuscles "The #$Collection of all instances of #$PeroneusMuscles.  The set of #$PeroneusMuscles controls eversion of the foot and assists plantar flexion of the #$Ankle.  This set of muscles includes the peroneus longus and the peroneus brevis muscles.")
(comment BaseballBat "Bat used in hitting a baseball")
(comment MeatOrLegumeFood "The food group consisting of meats and legumes. It is characterized by being high in protein. Food that contains a significant amount of meat and legumes should be specs of this.")
(comment ServiceRepairStore "A store that repairs (installs) the products it sells, if it's reasonable to repair these types of products. For example, your local vacuum clearer sales store that also fixes vacuum cleaners.")
(comment Plant-NonWoody "The collection of non-woody, herbaceous #$Plants.  Those #$Plants such as grasses, herbs, wildflowers, etc. which are fairly low-growing, often annual, and don't grow woody stems.  Excludes large, hard bamboos, and Balsa.")
(comment CompositionC4 "A specialization of #$HighExplosive.  Each instance of #$CompositionC4 is a high quality, very high velocity military plastic explosive.")
(comment DeterminerModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which modify determiners.            Example: `exactly' as in `exactly five books'.")
(comment Gun-SingleShot "The collection of #$Guns that must be reloaded by hand before each shot.  Many older types of firearems were single-shot.  Also, most types of artillery, such as #$Mortars, are single-shot.")
(comment Circumflex-TheSymbol "A mark that looks like a rooftop or upside-down letter V. When placed above a vowel, it indicates that the pronunciation is different.")
(comment ToiletBowl "The toilet bowl: this includes the bowl, the base, the hinge, the seat, and the lid (if there is one).")
(comment PickingALeaf "The collection of events in which a single leaf is picked")
(comment DiskDrive "The collection of computer peripherals designed to manipulate disk-based memory media.")
(comment Lladro-Figurine "A collection of porcelain #$Figurines that are made by  #$Lladro-CommercialOrganization.  They are known for their high quality.")
(comment MedianNerve "The collection of all median #$Nerves.  A #$MedianNerve is formed by the #$LateralCord-BrachialPlexus and #$MedialCord-BrachialPlexus of its side of the body.  The #$MedianNerve runs from the #$BrachialPlexus (in the #$Shoulder) down through the #$Arm to the #$Wrist.  It does not directly innervate any part of the #$Arm.  It has many branches that innervate various regions of the #$Arm and #$Hand.")
(comment TableSalt "The collection of quantities of sodium chloride granules, commonly used as a condiment with food.")
(comment Mask-ForWater "The collection of masks of the sort one wears

when snorkelling or scuba diving.")
(comment MaleHuman "The collection of all male instances of #$HomoSapiens.")
(comment CottonSwab "Collection of thin sticks 3-6 inches long having cotton or other soft fibrous substance at one or both ends and typically used for cleaning the ears.")
(comment CheatingInstructionsForGameProgram "The collection of all #$Instructions on how to cheat at computer games.")
(comment Appendix-OrganPart "A vestigial organ which is part of the #$LargeIntestine.")
(comment SubcollectionRelationFunction-InstanceLevel "The collection of all #$SubcollectionRelationFunctions that denote collections instances of which bear the arg2 relation to the arg3 itself, and not to an instance of the arg3.")
(disjointWith ProtectiveAttire ControlDevice)
(comment Acacia "A member of the genus Acacia.  These are small trees or shrubs, often with thorns, occurring in arid climates.")
(comment SvalbardIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$SvalbardIslands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType OrganizationTypeByGeographicReach)
(comment ComputerStand "This is the collection of desk-like furniture designed to hold a desktop

computer.")
(comment AudioTapePlaying "Playing back sounds from an audio cassette")
(disjointWith Tail-BodyPart Limb-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment RawFood "The collection of all instances of #$Food that have not been cooked.")
(comment POP3ServerProgram "#$POP3ServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$POP3Protocol, which is intended to permit a workstation to access a maildrop on a server host

dynamically. Usually, the server host starts the POP3 service by

listening on TCP port 110. When a client host wishes to make use of

the service, it establishes a TCP connection with the server

host. When the connection is established, the POP3 server sends a

greeting. The client and POP3 server then exchange commands and

responses (respectively) until the connection is closed or aborted. POP3 daemons by default listen on TCP port 110, whereas #$POP2ServerProgram daemons run on port 109.")
(disjointWith SellingOrganization HumanitarianOrganization)
(comment Freezer "The household appliance used to freeze food for storage")
(comment Edentata "An order of mammals having only molars or no teeth at all.  Examples are armadillos, anteaters, and sloths.")
(disjointWith AudioCommunicating MakingSomething)
(comment NasalSinus "The collection of all paranasal sinuses. The paranasal sinuses are sets of paired single or multiple cavities located in four skull bones--the #$Maxilla, the #$FrontalBone, the #$Ethmoid, and the #$Sphenoid bones. Correspondingly, they are called the #$MaxillarySinus, which is the largest; the #$FrontalSinus; the #$EthmoidSinuses; and the #$SphenoidalSinus, which is located in the upper posterior wall of the nasal cavity. The sinuses have two principal functions: because they are filled with air, they help keep the weight of the skull within reasonable limits, and they serve as resonance chambers for the human voice.")
(comment TableCloth "A sheet-like object, used to decorate and protect a table, especially during a meal.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType SpatiallyDisjointRegionType)
(disjointWith MakingAnOralSound Writing)
(comment Tooth "Vertebrate teeth used in chewing food to aid digestion")
(comment LawnMower-HandPowered "The collection of old-fashioned hand-pushed and hand-powered lawnmowers, whose blades are powered by the user pushing the mower. A subset of #$LawnMower-HandPushed.")
(comment Terrier-Silky "A collection of small dogs with very shiny, relatively long,          silky fur.  Once referred to as the Australian silky          Terrier and the Sidney silky Terrier.  Today they are also called by the name           Silky.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByIndustry PhysiologicalConditionType)
(comment OffshoreGasPlatform "The collection of all off-shore platforms from which #$NaturalGas is collected. All instances of #$OffshoreGasPlatform are physical devices through which natural gas reservoirs are tapped. ")
(comment LevatorScapula "The #$Collection of all instances of #$LevatorScapula #$Muscle.  The #$LevatorScapula, located in the #$Back-AnimalBodyPart, connects the #$Scapula to the #$CervicalVertebrae so as to raise the #$Scapula.")
(comment LumbarNerve "The 5 pairs of #$SpinalNerves located between the #$ThoracicNerves and the #$SacralNerves.")
(comment Gruyere-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Gruyere.

Gruyere is a firm yellow cheese, less mild than Swiss, originally from

Switzerland.")
(comment amountProducedInEvent "This predicate relates a creation event to the number or level of production of a kind of thing in that event. (#$amountProducedInEvent EVENT OBJECT-TYPE NUM) means that the number of instances of  OBJECT-TYPE created in EVENT is NUM.")
(comment Courthouse "buildings which house a court.  In Texas at least, each county has one county court and this court, and possibly other offices of the county government, are housed in a courthouse.  Often these courthouses are at the center of the town in which they are found.")
(comment Enterotoxin "A collection of specific kinds of #$Exotoxins that affect
the cells of intestinal mucosa causing vomiting and diarrhea.")
(comment Novel-CW "The collection of all #$ConceptualWorks that are novels.")
(disjointWith HandTool Dishwasher)
(comment KavaPlant "The collection for kava plant (or Piper methysticum), a member           of the pepper family, with an aromatic odor, whose roots and           rhizomes have narcotic properties.")
(comment AlderneyIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Alderney-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HomeAudioSystemComponent "The collection of #$AudioSystemComponents designed and marketed for use in a home or office setting. Elements of #$HomeAudioSystemComponent are typically purchased separately and assembled to form a #$HomeAudioSystem. Once assembled, the system is left in a stationary position for long periods of time. Unlike elements of #$PortableAudioEquipment, elements of #$HomeAudioSystemComponent cannot be easily transported nor operated while in motion, although their positions in a room can be changed. Thus, with respect to their relatively fixed positions once configured into a #$HomeAudioSystem, elements of #$HomeAudioSystemComponent are more like furniture than hand-held devices.")
(comment ExcretionSubstance "Result of the excretion process.")
(comment NorthDravidianLanguageFamily "branch of the major non-Indo-European language family of India, with a single outlier, far from the others")
(comment SoupSpoon "A spoon with a larger-than-normal basin, used for eating soup.")
(comment securityCompromised "(#$securityCompromised BREACH OBJECT) means that in the instance of #$SecurityBreach, BREACH, an object whose security is breached is OBJECT, an instance of #$SomethingExisting.")
(comment CombingHair "The collection of hair combing events. Includes uses of brush, comb, afro pick, etc.")
(comment CardGameProgram "The set of all computer programs that (can be used by someone to) play some card game.")
(comment LuvoxProduct "An #$AntiDepressant drug product manufactuered by Solvay Pharmaceuticals.")
(comment UrgeToHaveSex "The type of internal feeling or urge to have sex.")
(comment Frying "Cooking food by partial or total immersion in hot oil until desired level of doneness.")
(comment MusicalPerformanceTicket "The collection of all paper tickets entitling a #$Person to attend a #$MusicalPerformance.")
(comment Lectern "a piece of furniture which is used in giving speeches -- the speaker stands behind it and puts their notes on it")
(comment UnwindingOfDNAHelix "Each instance is a process in which the two strands of a segment of the #$DNAMolecule double helix are uncoupled. The first stage of a process of #$Transcription-DNAToRNA is always an instance of this collection.")
(comment Log-Document "The collection of all logs, logbooks -- documents in which information is recorded on a regular basis.")
(comment Calf-AnimalBodyPart "The back of the leg from the knee to the ankle.")
(comment IndividualLevelPredicate "`Individual-level' predicates express properties that apply to

continuants more or less intrinsically, rather than only at a certain time

or stage in time (for which cf. #$StageLevelPredicate). Example: having

brown eyes is, under normal conditions, an individual-level property.")
(disjointWith WritingImplement WrinkleRemovingDevice)
(comment DevonRex "Each #$DevonRex is a medium-sized cat with a curly coat.  This variety of cat originated in Devonshire in England.")
(disjointWith Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization InsuranceOrganization)
(comment RamjetEngine "The collection of all #$JetEngines 

   that propell aircraft by igniting fuel with air

 taken and compressed by the engine in a 

fashion that produces greater exhaust than

 intake velocity.")
(comment PortableStereoSystem "Commonly called boom boxes, these are portable one-piece stereos that have built-in speakers, radio receivers and tape decks, and may have a compact disc mechanism as well")
(comment YoungHuman "A specialization of #$HomoSapiens. Each instance of this collection is a human less than 35 years of age. This collection is disjoint with #$OldHuman -- the collection of humans more than 60 years of age. Notable specializations of #$YoungHuman include #$HumanChild, #$HumanTeenager and #$HumanYoungAdult.")
(comment PulmonaryCapillary "The collection of all capillaries found in #$Lungs which absorb #$Oxygen.  A #$PulmonaryCapillary releases #$CarbonDioxide into a #$Lung, while taking up #$Oxygen from an #$Alveolus.  Note that #$Lung tissue is also served by normal arteries, and thus there are also some systemic capillaries in a lung.")
(comment Cassava-Foodstuff "Cassava in any of its edible forms.")
(comment centralBusinessObject "The type of object around which this Organization's business centers.  e.g., for a car dealership or auto rental office, this would be Automobile.")
(comment many-GenQuantRelnTo "(#$many-GenQuantRelnTo RELN COL THING) is true if for
many of the instances X of COL (RELN X THING) holds.")
(comment IBTGeneration "A specialization of #$InformationTransferEvent and of #$Action.  Each instance of #$IBTGeneration is an event which creates some #$InformationBearingThing.  The #$InformationBearingThing created may be either a transient wave phenomenon (e.g. sound, light, or radio waves), or it may be a relatively long-lasting instance of #$InformationBearingObject (cf. the important specialization of IBTGeneration -- #$IBOCreation).  Humans frequently generate such IBTs as spoken language, gestures, and handwritten notes.  It is irrelevant for instances of #$IBTGeneration whether there is another agent who accesses the resulting IBT.  Note that every communication act starts with an instance of #$IBTGeneration.  (Thus, see also #$Communicating and its specializations, especially #$CommunicationAct-Single.) For an analogous collection regarding instances of #$ConceptualWork, see #$CWCreation. Two important specializations of this collection are #$IBTGeneration-Original and #$IBTGeneration-Replication. See also the predicate #$ibtGenerated.")
(disjointWith ChangingDeviceState BodyMovementEvent)
(comment SpearGun "The collection of spear guns. A spear gun fires

a smallish spear rather than a bullet. They are sometimes used for

fishing. Spear guns for this purpose have a line attached to the

spear so that it can easily be retrieved.")
(comment DeciduousPlant "A specialization of #$Plant-Woody. Each instance of #$DeciduousPlant is a plant which sheds all of its leaves once a year, seasonally, and subsequently grows new ones. Cf. #$EvergreenPlant.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterN "The lowercase letter 'n'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$N-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterN.")
(comment ElectricClothesDryerConnection "One of those big ole 220V outlets and an exhaust vent.")
(disjointWith MakingAnOralSound SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment VehicleExhaustSystem "The collection of parts that make up a vehicle's #$VehicleExhaustSystem.  These parts work together to handle the #$Exhaust-InternalCombustionEngine #$chemicalProducts of a #$CombustionProcess of #$GasolineFuel, #$DieselFuel, or other fuel, in an #$InternalCombustionEngine.  The parts of an instance of #$VehicleExhaustSystem include (if present) the exhaust pipes, the exhaust manifold, the #$CatalyticConverter, the muffler [#$Muffler-VehiclePart], and the tail pipe.")
(comment Neanderthal "A sort of homo sapiens, the fossil bones

of which were first discovered in the Neander valley near Dusseldorf Germany. 

They were toolmakers and were not as unintelligent as was once thought, though

their appearance was more like that of earlier hominids than like that of Cromagnon man.  It is

still a mystery why they became extinct.")
(comment Microprocessor "A specialization of #$IntegratedCircuit.  Each instance of #$Microprocessor is an integrated circuit that functions as a #$CentralProcessingUnit.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam Committee-Organization)
(comment ProjectileCasing "Every element of #$ProjectileCasing contains a projectile (or a set of projectiles, e.g. shot fired from a shot gun) and explosive material.  When a gun is fired an explosive contained inside a #$ProjectileCasing is detonated.  This detonation forces the projectile out the open end of the #$ProjectileCasing at high velocity.")
(comment Tap-FlowControlDevice "A device through which fluid can flow and which can control the flow of liquid through itself.  Found on sinks, bathtubs, kegs of beer, etc.")
(comment CochlearNerve "The collection of all cochlear nerves.  The cochlear nerve is a branch of the #$AcousticNerve that provides afferent impulses for the sense of hearing.")
(comment Chili-Dish "This collection consists of all instances of

chili. Chili is a kind of dish which is flavored with chili peppers,

garlic, oregano, and usually other flavorings. It may or may not contain

meat. When it doesn't, it contains beans. It often contains tomatoes.")
(comment Rotifera "This is the collection of (individual) animals in the

phylum Rotifera. 

The rotifers derive their name from the characteristic

           ciliated crown or corona, found at the anterior end of

           the animal which, when beating, gives the impression

           of rotating wheels.")
(comment VideoGameProgram-Color "Video game programs that are in color.")
(comment Pitcher "Big containers from which one serves but does not drink beverages.")
(comment Budding-Cellular "A collection of events in which a daughter cell is formed from the parent cell as a localized outgrowth (the bud).")
(comment RespiratoryGasExchange "The collection of all events of respiratory gas exchange, in which oxygen and other gasses cross a membrane.  The purpose is intake of #$Oxygen and output of other gasses like #$CarbonDioxide.  In #$AirBreathingVertebrates, it occurs at the walls of the #$Alveolus within the #$Lung. ")
(comment DVDPlayer "A #$DVDPlayer is a type of home audio-visual equipment,  for playing #$DVD-Disks. See also #$DVDPlayer-Software.")
(comment CoconutEndosperm "The endosperm of a coconut-The Seed - has a liquid part, which is an instance of coconut milk, and a solid part, which is an instance of coconut meat.")
(comment UnitedArabEmiratesPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$UnitedArabEmirates, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PublicLodgingOrganization "The collection of all instances of #$LodgingOrganization that are open to the general public.  Instances of #$PublicLodgingOrganization may be either #$CommercialOrganizations (e.g., #$BedAndBreakfasts) or #$NonProfitOrganizations (e.g. homeless shelters).  Negative examples include battered women's shelters (only women and children can obtain lodging) and university clubs that provide accommodations to alumni).")
(comment spacecraftDestination "(#$spacecraftDestination CRAFT OBJ) means that the destination of #$Spacecraft is the instance of #$AstronomicalObject OBJ. Typically, a successful mission using CRAFT involves CRAFT either landing, orbiting, or flying by OBJ. For example, (#$spacecraftDestination #$Cassini-Probe #$PlanetSaturn) means that #$PlanetSaturn is the destination of #$Cassini-Probe. Use #$spacecraftDestinationType when the #$AstronomicalObject is specified at the type-level.")
(comment PhysiologicalProcess "The collection of events in which an organism does (typically unconsciously) some process which involves alteration of that agent's physiological state.  A #$PhysiologicalProcess is normally one that is done by organisms (or parts of organisms) in the course of living.  A large subcollection of #$PhysiologicalProcess is #$BodilyFunctionEvent, including its subcollections #$Respiration, #$DigestingInStomach, and #$Heartbeating.  (Compare this collection with #$PhysiologicalCondition, whose instances are more episodic than process-like.) ")
(comment UralicAndAltaicLanguageFamily "Languages scattered across Asia from eastern Europe to the Pacific")
(comment BreadPan "Pan used to bake breads in.")
(disjointWith DentalCareEvent GynecologicalCareEvent)
(comment ShakingAFist "The set of actions in which a performer presents a clenched fist and moves it back and forth within someone's sight, usually while standing close to him, as a personally threatening or defiant gesture.")
(disjointWith DecompositionProcess PreservingFood)
(comment ProductDistributionOrganization "Organizations that perform distribution acts involving products - often a suborganization of the company that manufactures or retails the products (e.g., includes an Anhueiser-Busch Distributor, but not Federal Express or the U.S. Postal Service). ")
(comment GunTypeByLoadingMechanism "A collection consisting of two important collections,  #$Gun-MuzzleLoading and #$Gun-BreechLoading.  Every #$Gun is a spec of one or  the other.")
(comment titleOfPersonInOrganization "The predicate #$titleOfPersonInOrganization relates a person to a title that s/he holds in an organization.  (#$titleOfPersonInOrganization PER TITLE ORG) means that the #$Person PER has the #$Title TITLE in the #$Organization ORG.")
(comment CirculatorySystem "A specialization of both #$AnimalBodyPart and #$ConnectedPathSystem.  Each instance of #$CirculatorySystem is a system of organs and body parts, found in #$Vertebrates and some other animals, which function together to circulate the animal's blood throughout its body, supplying needed substances to its cells and removing waste products from them.  An instance of #$CirculatorySystem is typically composed of blood vessels, heart, spleen, etc., considered as an interrelated functional system of each animal.")
(comment CellNucleusFn "(#$CellNucleusFn CELL) denotes the nucleus of  CELL, an instance of #$EukaryoticCell.")
(comment captor "ARG2 is the agent which is acting as the captor in the #$HeldCaptive configuration, ARG1.")
(comment Cigarette "A small, consumable smoking device.  The tobacco is rolled in paper and it usually has a filter on the end.")
(comment BodyMovementEvent "A specialization of #$AnimalActivity.  Each instance of #$BodyMovementEvent is an event in which an #$Animal moves a part of its own body, whether intentionally or reflexively.  Specializations of this collection include #$TakingAStep, #$BlockingAPunch, #$Hiccoughing, and #$Blinking.")
(comment PostscriptFormatFile "The subcollection of #$ComputerFile-AIS, instances of which are encoded in the Postscript (ps) file format.")
(comment OutletBox "The small box which houses electrical wall outlets.")
(comment StainedGlassWorkAsArtForm "StainedGlassWorks as representational art forms")
(comment Cornea "The collection of all corneas.  Each instance of #$Cornea is the transparent part of the coat of an #$Eye that covers the iris (#$Iris-EyePart) and pupil (#$Pupil-EyePart) and admits light to the #$Interior of the #$Eye.")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece FluidReservoir)
(comment Mastiff "A collection of very large dogs with coats of short hair.  Bred in England.")
(comment Aristocrat "The collection of all aristocrats, or persons who hold hereditary titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch.  This excludes British 'life-peers,' whose titles are not hereditary, and hereditary knights, who are not nobility.  It includes all hereditary aristocratic ranks from Baronet and Laird up to hereditary monarch.  It does not include moneyed or distinguished people who are only informally called 'aristocrats'.")
(disjointWith StockExchange HealthcareOrganization)
(comment MP3Player-Generic "The collection of all things --- hardware or software --- whose primary intended purpose is to play MP3 files.")
(comment Penguin "The collection of marine flightless birds native to the #$SouthernHemisphere-Region.")
(comment VastusMuscles "The #$Collection of all sets of #$VastusMuscles.  The #$VastusMuscles connect the superior #$Femur with the #$Kneecap, and via the patellar ligament to the #$Tuberosity of the #$Tibia.  They extend the #$Knee.  Together with the #$RectusFemoris, they form the #$Quadriceps.")
(comment LampShade "The part of a lamp which filters the light of the bulb.")
(comment Teat "The collection of all fleshy #$Organs found in (one or more) pairs on female #$Mammals, which produce milk when nursing. Although males also have vestigial #$Teats, we are excluding those from this collection. #$Teats are not necessary for and therefore are not part of the #$ReproductiveSystem.")
(comment Cheese "A product made from milk.  The cheese protein is coagulated, separated from the rest of the liquid, and hardened to some degree.")
(comment ShoeRepairShop "Local (one site) service organizations which have as one of their main functions to repair shoes for customers for a fee.")
(comment FreeSheet "A specialization of #$SheetOfSomeStuff.  Each  instance of #$FreeSheet is a sheet of tangible stuff that has two sides  open to the environment.  That is, over most of each of its surfaces, it is not related by #$sheetSurfaceConnected (q.v.) with something else. Specializations include #$SheetOfPaper, #$Towel, #$Fence, and  #$CreditCard.")
(comment ICQSnifferProgram "The collection of all sniffers used with the #$ICQ-TheProgram")
(comment Passport "A specialization of #$LegalDocument and #$IDDocument.  Each instance of #$Passport is a document issued to a person by the government of a country of which s/he is a citizen, in order to identify that person as a citizen of that country while s/he is travelling outside of its borders. It can also be used for ID purposes back home. #$Passports typically expire after a set period of time and require renewal. Countries generally allow only one valid passport per citizen.")
(comment NounPhraseModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which can modify a noun phrase.            Examples: `then' as in `the president then' and `even' as in            `even the president'.")
(comment weak-HL-TimePrecedence "A weak-HL-TimePrecedence relationship can be concluded from some other statement of temporal interval precedence. It facilitates temporal relations inference.")
(comment RecoillessGun "Unlike other guns, the #$RecoillessGun uses a different method of  harnessing explosive force to propel a projectile.  For most guns, a  projectile is put in front of a propellant in a tube closed at one end.  The #$RecoillessGun, on the other hand, has a barrel that is open in the rear.   On firing, the forward motion of the projectile is counteracted by the  rearward thrust of gases, and the barrel remains motionless.")
(comment Cedilla-TheSymbol "A curvy mark. When placed under the letter C, it indicates that the C should be pronounced as an S.")
(comment Sink "The container found in kitchens, bathrooms, utility rooms etc which holds water, dishes, etc.. The Sink is the whole of which the basin, faucets, etc, are a part.")
(comment ThrowingSomethingAway "The act of discarding something - chunking it in the trash can.")
(comment ComputerInternalClock "The chip which controls the rate at which the CPU operates")
(comment Microscope "Collection of scientific devices designed for viewing small biological objects or parts of objects.")
(comment PubescentHuman "The collection of people who are going through #$Puberty.")
(comment LongThoracicNerve "The collection of all long thoracic #$Nerves.  A #$LongThoracicNerve is formed by branches of its side's #$VentralRamusC5, #$VentralRamusC6, and #$VentralRamusC7 prior to their forming of the trunks of the #$BrachialPlexus.  This #$Nerve supplies the #$SerratusAnterior.")
(comment RiceCake "Pressed cakes of puffed rice.")
(comment DomesticatedAnimalFood "A specialization of #$Food.  Each instance of #$DomesticatedAnimalFood is a foodstuff produced by human beings and intended for consumption by domesticated animals.  This collection includes feed manufactured for horses, cattle, chickens, and other farm animals, as well as pet food.")
(comment FemaleHuman "A specialization of both #$HomoSapiens and #$FemaleAnimal. The collection of all female humans.")
(comment programCopyFoundOnComputer "This predicate relates computer program copies to computational systems.  (#$programCopyFoundOnComputer COPY COMPUTER) means that COPY is stored on COMPUTER (e.g., on disk or in memory). Compare this predicate to #$programFoundOnComputer.")
(comment XRayPhotographicDevice "The collection of machines intended for taking still X-ray photos of something, usually a BLO.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByStructure "A partition on the collection #$Bacterium, reflecting the classical morphological division of the Eubacteria into #$CoccusBacterium, #$BacillusBacterium, and #$SpirillaBacterium.")
(comment SkinPore "An opening in the skin for the secretion of fluids.")
(comment SubcollectionRelationFunction-TypeLevel "The collection of all #$SubcollectionRelationFunctions that denote collections instances of which bear the arg2 relation to an instance of the arg3, and not to the arg3 itself.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice LandTransportationDevice)
(comment PinaceaeFamily "The collection of all members of the pinaceae family.  The #$PinaceaeFamily is a #$BiologicalFamily of #$Conifers which includes #$PineTrees, ceders, #$SpruceTrees, and #$FirTrees.")
(comment GeorgianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Georgia-TheNation, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByGeographicReach PhysiologicalConditionType)
(comment BackupPowerSupply "This is the collection of systems designed to provide emergency

power when the usual power supply is interrupted.")
(comment Fertilizer "Solid or liquid compounds, natural or artificial, used to enrich soil and help plants to grow.")
(disjointWith Trunk-TheAppendage Limb-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment TypicalBehaviorOfTypeFn "#$TypicalBehaviorOfTypeFn takes any spec of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of action-types that are 'typical' for agents of that type.  This function is an instance of #$PresuppositionFunction, as the 'typical' behavior for an agent is dependent on certain kinds of situations.")
(comment CollaborativeWorkProgram "The collection of programs that function at least partly to foster collaborative work.  This function must be in the design of the program in question and not merely an artifact of the way it is used.")
(disjointWith SellingOrganization RevoltOrganization)
(comment FireHose "Large strong hoses used by firefighters to spray water on a burning HOC or other large structure.")
(disjointWith ProjectilePropelling ProgrammingAComputer)
(comment BloodTypeO "Blood type O")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent AnalyzingSomething)
(comment TableCovering "This collection is intended to include table cloths, placemats, and table runners.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType AccessingScriptType)
(comment subsumesStandard "(subsumesStandard ST1 ST2) states that standard ST1 is a subsuming extension of standard ST2.  Anything satisfying standard ST2 will also satisfy standard ST1.  For example, (subsumesStandard Intel80386Standard Intel80286Standard)")
(disjointWith FingerMovement SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment Defecating "Expelling solid waste from the body")
(comment Terrier-Sealyham "A collection of small dogs with wiry, almost completely           white fur.")
(comment numberOfErrorsOfType "(#$numberOfErrorsOfType SET ERR-TYPE NUM) means that the number of errors in SET that are members of #$Malfunction ERR-TYPE is NUM.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat OrganizationTypeByIndustry)
(comment SerratusAnterior "The #$Collection of all instances of #$SerratusAnterior #$Muscle.  The #$SerratusAnterior #$Muscle connects the superior eight ribs with the #$Scapula, holding the #$Scapula in place.  Weakness of the #$SerratusAnterior causes 'winged scapula'.")
(comment HairBrush "A brush used to groom the hair.")
(comment ThoracicNerve "The 12 pairs of #$SpinalNerves; located between the #$CervicalNerves and #$LumbarNerves.")
(comment OilPump "A collection of pumps which pump crude oil (petroleum) up from the ground.")
(comment Endotoxin "A collection of toxins associated with the outer membrane of
#$GramNegativeBacterium.  These toxins are not secreted by the
#$Bacterium, but are released only when the cells die.")
(disjointWith OfficialDocument PortalCovering)
(comment ExternalSexOrgan "Instances of #$ExternalSexOrgan are external animal body parts which have an important function in sexual copulation. Also called genitalia.")
(disjointWith HandTool ClothesWasher)
(comment Tulip-Plant "Tulip plants.")
(comment KiribatiPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Kiribati, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HomeAudioSystem "The collection of #$AudioSystems designed and marketed for use in a home or office setting. Elements are usually assembled and left in a stationary position. Unlike elements of #$PortableAudioEquipment, they cannot be easily transported nor operated while in motion, although their positions in a room can be changed. Each instance of #$HomeAudioSystem has several instances of #$HomeAudioSystemComponent as #$physicalParts. No instance of #$HomeAudioSystemComponent is itself an instance of #$HomeAudioSystem.")
(comment AustralianLanguageFamily "The collection of the numerous aboriginal languages of Australia, now believed to be genetically related.")
(comment CedarChest "Big boxes that sit on bedroom floor and have hinged lids and, oh yeah, are made of cedar.  Keeps clothes in, moths out.")
(comment TeethCleaning "A collection of events.  In each #$TeethCleaning event, an animal's teeth are cleaned.  In order to distinguish, e.g., professional teeth cleaning by a dental technician from daily personal care, different microtheories are used.  Consider just the frequencies of performing this action: in the #$HumanActivitiesMt, where a person brushes their own teeth as a subevent of #$DailyPersonalCleaning, this occurs once or twice per day.  In the #$ProviderOfServicePerspectiveMt, that is from the dental hygienist's point of view, it occurs about ten times per day.  In the #$RecipientOfServicePerspectiveMt, that is from the point of view of someone going to get their teeth cleaned at a dentist's office, it happens a couple times per year.")
(comment SolitaireProgram "The set of all computer programs that (can be used by someone to) play solitaire.")
(comment Executive "A collection of people.  An instance of #$Executive is a person who holds an executive managerial positions in some #$Organization.  Among the members of #$Executive are top managers of organizations, including corporate officers (#$ChiefExecutiveOfficer, etc.), Chiefs of Staff, Generals, Admirals and others like Chief Corporate Counsel, Managing Partner, Producer, Chief Scientist, Chief Engineer, as well as other upper and upper-middle managers.")
(comment Centerboard "A retractable board which protrudes from the bottom of some sailboats and is used to increase stability and prevent sideways motion.")
(comment UrgeToSneeze "This is a #$Collection of physical urges of a certain type, namely the urges that animals have to sneeze (and their accompanying internal sensations.)")
(comment AnteriorRegionFn "The function (AnteriorRegionFn REGOROBJ), applied to a region or object REGOROBJ, means the region consisting of the front half or section, or the anterior main portion, of REGOROBJ.  It applies only when REGOROBJ itself has an intrinsic front/back orientation, or is a (non-backward-facing) part of a larger region or object that has a front/back orientation.")
(comment FlourOrMeal "flour-finely ground cereal used in cooking")
(comment SeatBeltLock "The things that hols care seats in.")
(comment BuiltInDevice "A set of physical devices.  An instance of #$BuiltInDevice is an object that is a device in and of itself, is also a part of another object, and typically was added to the other object when that object was constructed.  
Note:  Its function may or may not be intrinsically dependent upon its being part of the object it was added to; e.g., the function of a built-in odometer is to measure miles driven on the car of which it is a part, but the intrinsic function of a built-in clock or CD player installed in that same automobile is not dependent on its being part of the automobile.")
(comment NationalizingAnIndustry "The collection of events in which the national government of a country takes over the facilities and other assets of an #$Industry-Localized operating within its national territory or jurisdiction.")
(comment Shin "The collection of all shins.  An individual #$Shin is a front region of a #$LowerLeg.")
(comment StageLevelPredicate "`Stage-level' predicates express properties that, at least in
principle, belong to individuals only at certain times or stages in time,
rather than intrinsically (cf #$IndividualLevelPredicate). Example: being
on one's way to London is typically a stage-level property.")
(disjointWith FuelPoweredDevice WritingImplement)
(comment Horse-WarmBlood "Members of horse breeds represented by specializations of the collection #$Horse-WarmBlood tend to be more slender than those that are members of breeds represented by specializations of #$Horse-ColdBlood.  In temperament, warm-blood horses are usually more high-strung than cold-blood horses.  They are generally used for sports such as racing, jumping, and dressage.  While the collections #$ThoroughbredHorse and #$ArabianHorse represent 'light breeds,' and have instances sharing many charactersitics with instances of #$Horse-WarmBlood, they are not specializations of #$Horse-WarmBlood because instances are considered pure-bred while warm-blood breeds are of mixed heritage.")
(comment CubanPerson "A #$citizens of #$Cuba, or someone who participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment CutFlower "Instances are pieces of vegetation, often consisting of a #$Flower-BotanicalPart and part of the stem, which are typically placed in water in combination with a variety of other #$CutFlowers and used as decoration in homes, offices and other places people hang out.  Not every instance of #$CutFlower includes a single flower -- some include multiple inflorescences, such as 'babies' breath'.  Some include no flowers at all, such as cuttings of willow or greenery.")
(comment PlasticBottle "Bottles made of plastic")
(comment HepaticCapillary "The collection of all hepatic capillaries (or 'sinusoids').  A #$HepaticCapillary releases nutrients and waste products into the #$Liver; it does not supply #$Oxygen.  That function is provided by systemic capillaries which are also in the #$Liver.  Kupffer #$Cells in hepatic capillaries destroy bacteria [see #$Bacterium] in the #$Blood, an important task since bacterial cells may have entered the bloodstream in the #$SmallIntestine.  A #$HepaticCapillary is a filtering pathway for #$Blood which has entered the #$Liver via the #$HepaticPortalVein.  Arterioles from the #$HepaticArtery provide #$OxygenatedBlood to the hepatic capillaries.")
(comment SausageCasing "The skin of sausages.")
(comment BorderCheckpointOrganization "A collection of local organizations, often but not necessarily located directly at a border between two countries.  An element of #$BorderCheckpointOrganization is any organization through whose installations and procedures people and goods must pass when entering a #$Country.  This collection includes all such checkpoint organizations, whether their facilities be on roads, at airports, or at seaports.")
(comment Rennet "Mucous membrane from a calf's stomach, used to promote the hardening of cheese")
(comment ItineraryDocument "A specialization of #$ScheduleDocument. Each instance of #$ItineraryDocument is a document that contains information about a trip, including the time/location of each leg of the trip, accomodations on the trip, and so forth. See also the related constants #$ConsultingASchedule, #$MakingTravelArrangements, and #$travelLegs.")
(disjointWith BiologicalProcess RecordedSoundPlaying)
(comment Sidearm "Single-user, hand-held personal weapons designed to be carried on the person; typically carried in a special holder that the person wears.")
(comment Bush "A specialization of #$Plant-Woody.  Each instance of #$Bush is a woody plant of branching growth habit that lacks a substantial trunk and is not usually taller than an adult person (and is typically re shorter than most specimens of #$Tree-ThePlant).   This is a commonsense collection without distinct boundaries.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterO "The capital letter 'O'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$O-TheLetter, and #$LatinSmallLetterO.")
(comment GasClothesDryerConnection "The electrical and gas supplies and exhaust for a dryer.")
(disjointWith Flatulence SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(disjointWith DirtBike StreetBike)
(comment BIOSChip "A specialization of #$IntegratedCircuit and #$ComputerHardwareComponent. Each instance of #$BIOSChip is meant to have a #$BasicInputOutputSystem instantiated in it in order to provide a low-level interface to the hardware for the #$OperatingSystem.")
(disjointWith LimitedPartnership GeneralPartnership)
(comment ShellForCasting "Instances of this collection are moulds used for casting objects from liquid metal or other material. The liquid is poured into the shell and allowed to solidify, and then the shell is removed. (See also #$Molding).")
(comment Cupboard "This is not the movable piece of furniture nor is it the closet or pantry.  This unit refers to kitchen cabinets, built into the kitchen.")
(comment LateralCord-BrachialPlexus "The collection of all lateral cords of the brachial plexus.  The lateral cord is formed by the anterior division of the #$SuperiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus and the anterior division of the #$MiddleTrunk-BrachialPlexus.  Nerves formed from the lateral cord are the #$SupraScapularNerve, then #$LateralPectoralNerve, and the #$MedianNerve.")
(comment Bisque-Soup "This collection consists of all instances of bisque. A bisque is a kind of

soup which is has a smooth, not brothy, base and may contain small amounts

of solid food. Bisques are usually intensely flavored. Bisques are not 

pureed soups but are thickened to a consistency similar to a pureed soup.

Bisques generally contain cream.")
(comment No-NLAttr "The attribute value carried by utterances of the form

 \"no XXX\".")
(comment Dodo-Bird "This is an extinct species, Raphus cucullatus, of large flightless birds

that formerly inhabited Mauritius.")
(comment WaxedPaper "Paper that has been coated or permeated with wax, so that it is resistant to water and oil.")
(comment CarbonMetabolicPathway "The collection of events in which a cell metabolizes #$Carbon.  The cell uses a series of chemical processes in order to take carbon from the environment and form complex organic compounds.")
(comment RespiratoryTract "The collection of all natural bodily airway systems used by animals for ventilation and respiration, including systems of nasal passages, mouth, blowholes, nasopharynx, throat, glottis, trachea and bronchi.  The tubes of a #$RespiratoryTract are connected at some point to a portal to the ambient air.  Excludes some parts of the respiratory system such as pulmonary blood vesels, pleurae and alveolar tissue that are not conduits for air.  Also excludes the whole #$Lungs as units.")
(disjointWith Ultralight Spacecraft)
(comment CocoaBean-TheSeed "The seed of a cacao tree.")
(comment HonduranPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Honduras, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment CommercialLodgingOrganization "The collection of all #$LodgingOrganizations that provide lodging services on a for profit basis.  Typical instances of #$CommercialLodgingOrganization include hotel/motel chains and single site bed and breakfasts.  Non-profit youth hostels, battered women's shelters, and homeless shelters are not included in this collection.")
(comment AudioVisualReceiver "This is the collection of single-unit

receivers for #$HomeTheaterSystems.")
(comment JuvenileFn "#$JuvenileFn is a Cyc function, and in particular a #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$JuvenileFn ORGCLASSTYPE) represents that subcollection of #$JuvenileAnimal whose instances are the juveniles of the group of animals denoted by ORGCLASSTYPE.  E.g., (#$JuvenileFn #$Deer) denotes the collection of all fawns.  Certain kinds of organisms have no juveniles (e.g., the members of #$Amoeba).")
(comment Eskimo-AleutLanguageFamily "Circumpolar languages ranging from Greenland westward to Siberia")
(comment BakingDish "The most general dish that can be put in the oven, in which food is baked or roasted.")
(comment ThrowingFlowers "The collection of events in which a person throws single cut flowers or bouquets as a expression of approval, admiration, or celebration of another person's achievement; usually at the conclusion of a performance or other public ceremony.")
(comment GunTypeByBarrelType "The two instances of #$GunTypeByBarrelType are #$RifledBoreWeapon and #$SmoothBoreWeapon.  Every #$Gun is a spec of one or the other.")
(comment ComputerWallpaperFile "A collection of #$ComputerImageFiles. Each instance of #$ComputerWallpaperFile represents an image that is intended to be displayed as the background of the GUI of an #$OperatingSystem like #$MSWindows, or the background of a web page.")
(comment SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients "#$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients is a specialization of both #$SingleSiteOrganization and #$LocalOrganization.  Each instance of #$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients is a single-site organization serving customers in a local area, working from a particular store, office, or other physical quarters where customers (or their agents) go in person to speak with company representatives about the services or products offered.  Instances of #$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients may be either stand-alone organizations or sub-organization of a larger company.  Notable specializations of #$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients include #$Pharmacy, #$AutoDealership, and #$Hospital.")
(comment Drawer "The collection of drawers")
(comment terminalPhaseAltitude-MissileType "(#$terminalPhaseAltitude-MissileType MISSILE ALT) means
  that when a #$CruiseMissile of type MISSILE is launched,
   its altitude while closing in on its target is ALT -- a
 #$Distance above sea level.  Every type of #$CruiseMissile
  also has a cruising altitude, which is its
  altitude following launch, prior to 
  the terminal phase.")
(comment BodyPartCollectionFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance ANIMAL of #$Animal, and a specialization PART-TYPE of #$AnimalBodyPart, #$BodyPartCollectionFn returns the collection of all instances  of PART-TYPE that are part (see #$anatomicalParts) of ANIMAL.  For example, (#$BodyPartCollectionFn #$BritneySpears #$Fingernail) is the collection whose instances are Britney Spears's fingernails.")
(comment CaptiveAnimal "The collection of all animals that are caged, tied, kept in an animal container, or otherwise held captive.  There is some intersection here with #$DomesticPet, but not complete.   Some elements of #$Person are members of #$CaptiveAnimal, e.g., political detainees, imprisoned criminals, kidnap victims.")
(comment ServiceEvent-ProviderIsPassive "A collection of #$ServiceEvents. In each instance of #$ServiceEvent-ProviderIsPassive, an agent passively provides a service to a recipient. Examples include providing of electrical service to a residence by an electrical utility. Such events happen when the consumer plugs in an electrical device and turns it on - the utility doesn't do anything actively to provide electricity for that event.")
(comment BloodType "The collection of blood types - A, B, O, AB, positive or negative Rh factor, and combinations thereof (e.g. AB-).")
(comment RichTextFormatFile "The collection of #$ComputerFile-AISs encoded in the Rich Text Format (RTF) file format.  The RTF format was developed by #$MicrosoftInc for the exchange of documents from Microsoft Word into some other word processing system.")
(comment BuildingWire "The wire used to do wiring in large structures.")
(comment PenAndInkDrawing "PenAndInkDrawings as representational art forms")
(comment Eardrum "The tight thin skin inside the ear, which makes one hear the sound waves that beat against it")
(comment InsecureScriptSourceCodeFault "A program has an #$InsecureScriptSourceCodeFault if a specially-formed input to that program will yield the source code of a script used by that program to an unauthorized user.  This is a common problem for web server programs.")
(disjointWith PathArtifact FurniturePiece)
(comment MiniaturePinscher "A collection of small dogs.  Very similar to the Doberman, but smaller.")
(comment ChristianPerson "The collection of all persons who believe in (at least some of) the basic fundamental tenets of Christianity, or who practice Christian religious rituals, or both.")
(disjointWith CriminalOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment AmateurVideoCamera "The class of #$VideoCameras used by amateurs.")
(comment ScalenusMedius "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ScalenusMedius #$Muscle.  The #$ScalenusMedius raises the #$FirstRib during forced inspiration when acting bilaterally.  It also is used bilaterally or unilaterally to assist flexion of the #$Neck-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment CardboardBox "Collection for boxes made out of cardboard used to package many different kinds of consumer products.")
(comment Ticket "The collection of (normally paper) document denoting that a person (either the bearer or a named person) has the right to obtain a specified type of service or object.  A card that permits multiple services or objects to be received is not an instance of #$Ticket.  An \"electronic ticket\" is a different type of record of such an authorization -- not a type of #$Ticket.  Common types of ticket entitle the bearer to admission to educational events or to transportation on a common carrier.")
(comment SubLingualGland "The collection of all submaxilary salivary #$Glands.  Instances of this collection are #$internalParts of the face below the tongue which secrete #$Saliva into the #$Mouth.")
(comment Cream-Dairy "Dairy cream (#$Cream-Dairy) is a dairy product which consists of milk fat that will settle out of non-homogenized milk to float on top.  #$WholeMilk consists of 3-4% cream by volume, while #$TwoPercentMilk is an artificial product consisting of 2% cream by volume, and #$SkimMilk being the

part of the milk that is left behind when the cream floating on top of non-homogenized milk has been skimmed off.")
(comment Spa "A collection of establishments.  Each instance of #$Spa is a place which draws visitors or clients, traditionally with the intention of improving their health or appearance .")
(comment IPSnifferProgram "The collection of sniffers used to collect IP addresses.")
(comment SqueezeTube "A flexible tube which dispenses a viscous substance when squeezed")
(comment FruitTree "The collection of trees which bear a fruit ordinarily eaten by human beings.  This would include many trees that bear nuts.")
(comment ContractDocument "A specialization of #$TextualMaterial. Each instance of this collection is a document which outlines the contents of a legally-binding agreement. See also #$LegalDocument.")
(comment Clock "A specialization of #$MechanicalDevice.  Each instance of #$Clock is a device designed to be used to keep track of time.")
(comment Pre-NounPhraseModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which can pre-modify a noun phrase.            Example: `even' as in `even the president'.")
(comment weakSuccessor-HL-TimePrecedence "A weakSuccessor-HL-TimePrecedence relationship can be concluded from some other statement of temporal interval precedence. It facilitates temporal relations inference.")
(comment ProjectileShell-FinStabilized "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is fin-stabilized. They obtain stability through the use of fins located at the aft end of the  projectile.  Normally four to six fins are employed.  Fin-stabilized  projectiles are advantageous because they follow the trajectory very well at  high-launch angles, and they can be designed with very low drag thereby  increasing range and or terminal velocity.  However, fin stabilized  projectiles are disadvantageous because the extra length of the projectile  must be accommodated and the payload volume is comparatively low in relation  to the projectile length.")
(comment Breve-TheSymbol "A u-shaped mark. When placed over a vowel, it usually indicates that the vowel should be shortened.")
(comment Chimney-HousePart "The structure through which smoke flows from the fireplace of a house to the outside.")
(comment PuttingOnAClothingItem "A specialization of #$HumanActivity.  Each instance of #$PuttingOnAClothingItem is an event in which some wearable item is donned.  Such an event may be performed either by the wearer or by someone else (e.g., putting on a horse's bridle or a child's mittens).  After an instance of #$PuttingOnAClothingItem occurs, there exists an instance of #$WearingSomething (q.v.); namely, the situation in which the item donned is #$wornOn the body of the wearer.")
(comment NumericCoprocessorChip "An optional chip which does numeric operations very quickly.")
(comment VentralRamusL2 "The collection of all L2 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusL2 and #$DorsalRamusL2 branch from SpinalRootL2.  #$VentralRamusL2 supplies the #$LumbarPlexus.")
(comment Butter "Butter made from milk")
(comment DrumInstrument "A specialization of #$PercussionInstrument.  Each instance of this collection is a percussion instument in which a hollow tube has a membrane stretched over one or both ends.")
(comment HumanChild "A specialization of #$YoungHuman, and an instance of #$HumanTypeByLifeStageType. Each instance of this collection is a human in the childhood stage of life.  Functionally, this life stage ends when the child begins to take responsibility for themselves, work, have children of their own (or, at latest, when the person's age greatly exceeds that at which most people reach those milestones).  Generally, this means that it spans the period from birth to teenage years. Notable specializations of this collection include #$MaleChild, #$FemaleChild, #$HumanToddler and #$HumanInfant.")
(comment Computer "A specialization of #$ComputationalSystem, #$ElectronicDevice, and #$ComputerHardwareItem.  Each instance of #$Computer is an electronic device that acts on input according to some set of instructions (often in the form of software -- see #$ComputerProgram-CW) producing some output.  Instances of #$Computer have specialized parts to handle input and output (sometimes peripherals like screens and keyboards, sometimes just input-output terminals on a chip), storage (internal memory and external storage such as disk drives), and reasoning (see #$CentralProcessingUnit).  The more specialized collection #$PersonalComputer is the collection of the popular archetypes of what a computer is (e.g., desktop, laptop, and palm computers); however, instances of #$Computer are incorporated into many devices (e.g., cars, cameras, and VCRs).  Hydraulic computers, analog computers, biological computers, etc. are not instances of this collection because #$Computer is a specialization of #$ElectronicDevice.")
(comment ExaminingTable "The sort of table that is found in a medical examining room, that the patient sits or lies on while being examined.")
(comment HistoryFn "#$HistoryFn takes as argument any #$Thing and returns the collection of all #$HistoricalNarratives about that thing.  For example, (#$HistoryFn #$DemocraticPartyIdeology) returns the collection of histories of Democratic #$PoliticalBeliefs, and (#$HistoryFn #$Automobile) returns the collection of histories of cars, Note that atemporal things may have this subtopic. For example, there are histories of collections whose instances are temporal, and there are histories of #$Intangible things, like #$BeliefSystems.")
(comment HairFollicle "An opening in the skin from which hair shafts grow.")
(comment SubcollectionRelationFunction-Canonical "Instances of this collection are such that for any nat (FN COL1 PRED COL2) formed with them, either (PRED COL1 COL2) or (relationAllExists PRED COL1 COL2) holds. In other words, COL1 and COL2 are in the same order in the expansion as in the NAT.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice WaterTransportationDevice)
(comment AlderTree "A ornamental shrub or tree. Their cones (strobilli) remain on the branches after the small, winged fruits (nutlets) are released.  Their oval leaves fall without changing color.")
(comment SwazilandPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Swaziland, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat OrganizationTypeByGeographicReach)
(comment ProgramConfigurationVulnerability "#$ProgramConfigurationVulnerability is a vulnerability had by instances of #$Computer.  A computer has a #$ProgramConfigurationVulnerability because it has a program running on it that is configured in an insecure manner.")
(comment CarWashing "This is the collection of events in which an automobile is cleaned.  Usually, washing a car involves at least washing the exterior of the automobile with water and detergent.  Sometimes, it may include vacuuming the interior, or other internal cleaning.  Also, it needn't always include washing the entire exterior of the car if only part is dirty, so long as the car as a whole is cleaner after the washing than it was before.  #$CarWashing may be done by a person, or by an automatic device.")
(disjointWith Undressing Conveying-Generic)
(disjointWith Tentacle Limb-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment DocumentViewerProgram "The collection of all computer programs that serve as document viewers.  These programs do not generally permit one to modify the viewed document.  This collection includes only those programs that do this exclusively.  For this reason it is disjoint with (e.g.) #$WordProcessingProgram.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareOrganization MailDepartment)
(comment Tub "The collection of all tubs - containers whose height and width are roughly equal, which have no top, and which frequently have a lipped edge.")
(comment HemiascomyceteClass "A class within the fungus kingdom whose members are simple, microspcopic, and are important to humans because they include  the yeasts we use in baking and brewing alcoholic beverages.")
(comment Poem-CW "A collection of #$PoeticWorks. Each instance of #$Poem-CW is a poetic literary work that is complete in itself - unlike a #$Lyric-WordsToSong it need not be an integral part of a piece of music, and unlike a #$PlayScript it is not associated with sets and #$Costumes and does not contain stage directions. #$Poem-CWs are sometimes recited publicly and in modern times are distributed in text form.")
(comment BloodTypeAB "Blood type AB")
(comment WallPaint "A spec of Paint; the type of paint used on walls")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType WavePropagationType)
(comment standardPartConstrains "(standardPartConstrains STAND THE SPART) states that anything which satisfies TheProduct in standard STAND must have all its parts which satisfy THE in STAND satisfy TheProduct in SPART.  SPART must be an intangibleParts of STAND. For example, (standardPartConstrains IBM-PC-AT-Standard TheProcessor Intel-80286-Standard)")
(disjointWith FingerMovement Biting)
(disjointWith SomethingToWear LawnMower)
(comment Terrier-Scottish "A collection of small dogs with wiry fur.  A working Terrier. ")
(comment TechnologyOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that are primarily or significantly engaged in the #$TechnologyIndustry or whose activities focus on that industry.  Examples of specializations of #$TechnologyOrganization include #$InternetServiceProvider, #$ComputerRepairShop, and #$AIResearchDepartment.  Both #$IBMInc and #$Cycorp are instances of #$TechnologyOrganizations.")
(comment ArmoredCar "The collection of #$ArmoredVehicles which have #$Automobile bodies (i.e. are 'cars'). These vehicles are often used to transport important or high-profile people through areas where they may be in danger of attack. They may also be used to transport valuables such as cash or jewels.")
(comment SeaMammal "Mammals which spend most of their lives in the ocean.")
(comment SupraSpinatus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$SupraSpinatus #$Muscle.  The #$SupraSpinatus #$Muscle lies on the dorsal side of the #$Scapula, connects the #$Scapula to the greater tubercleof the #$Humerus, and is used for abduction of the #$Humerus.")
(comment SacralNerve "The 5 pairs of #$SpinalNerves located between the #$LumbarNerves and the #$CoccygealNerve.")
(comment GoatCheese "This is the collection of all instances of goat cheese, cheese made from

goat's milk. There are dozens of #$SpecifiedCheeseTypes that are specs

of this collection.")
(comment Holster "Devices usually made of fabric or leather, used for carrying firearms")
(comment VideoClipOfWorkFn "(#$VideoClipOfWorkFn VIDEOWORK) denotes the collection of all #$VideoClips in which a segment of the #$VideoConceptualWork VIDEOWORK has been recorded. For example, (#$VideoClipOfWorkFn #$ApocalypseNow-TheMovie) denotes the collection of all #$VideoClips in which a segment of Apocalypse Now has been recorded.")
(comment BodilyOrifice "Instances of #$BodilyOrifice are animal body parts, such as #$Nostrils, consisting of surface openings that lead into bodily cavities.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice WritingImplement)
(comment NetherlandsAntillesPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$NetherlandsAntilles, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PersonalAudioPlayer "#$PersonalAudioPlayer is a collection of #$PortableAudioEquipment that is designed for use by a single person using #$Headphones. Elements of #$PortableAudioEquipment are designed to be both compact in size and light in weight. As a result, they can be used in activities in which they are strapped to the user's body, e.g., during jogging and exercise workouts.")
(disjointWith SolidAnimalMatter Agent-Generic)
(comment GeanOrPanoanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in the Caribbean region and/or South America ")
(comment TeaSpoon-MeasuringTool "The measuring tool which measures the exact quantity of one Teaspoon.")
(comment WebPage-AIS "The subset of #$ComputerFile-AIS whose instances are written in #$HypertextMarkupLanguage. Most instances of  #$WebPage-AIS are #$subInformation of the  #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource (see  #$WorldWideWebPage-AIS).")
(comment PersonalGrooming "Personal grooming includes any activity that can be performed on an individual (not necessarily a person) that could be construed as grooming.  These activities are quite often performed by oneself, i.e. brushing one's own teeth, applying one's own make-up, cutting one's own nails.  They also are frequently performed for someone else, that is, by one individual to another individual: teeth cleaning at the dentist's, photographers' applying make-up on models, a friend cutting another's hair.  In the #$BaseKB, this is not restricted to human beings.--Siegel, May 17, 1996")
(comment arg4NotGenl "(#$arg4NotGenl REL COL) means that nothing given as the fourth argument to the #$Relation REL may be a spec of the #$Collection COL.")
(comment OnlineGameProgram "The collection of computer games that  people can play online. Access to these games may or may not cost money.")
(comment Revolver "Handgun with a revolving piece containing multiple chambers that are lined up with the barrel for firing.")
(comment SerzoneProduct "An #$AntiDepressant drug product manufactuered by Bristol-Myers Squibb.")
(comment urgeTypeSatisfied "The urge of type arg2 is satisfied in the event of type arg1.")
(comment SkeletalMuscle "The collection of #$Muscles which are connected at at least one end to a bone. Skeletal muscles are involved in movements of the #$SkeletalSystem.")
(comment Beef "Meat from domestic cattle.")
(disjointWith MaintenanceEvent BiologicalEvent)
(comment Crib "The set of cribs -- beds for babies.")
(comment PolyATail "The collection of molecular structures appended to the 3' ends of #$EukaryoticMessengerRNAs during #$PolyadenylationProcess. Each instance of #$PolyATail consists of a few hundred #$AdenineRibonucleotides.")
(comment Shin "The collection of all rear regions of #$LowerLegs in humans and some other animals.")
(comment KindLevelPredicate "`Kind-level' predicates express properties that apply to kinds of individuals rather than to individual themselves. Example: being extinct, as in `the lynx is nearly extinct' -- this is not a property of any individual lynx, but rather of the species. NOTE: a kind-level predicate may admit type-level arguments in some arg positions, or may admit both type- and instance-level arguments (such is the case with underspecified predicates).")
(disjointWith WritingImplement Stapler)
(comment Balinese-Cat "Each #$Balinese-Cat is a slender cat with medium-length hair and markings like a #$SiameseCat. ")
(comment SaintLuciaPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$SaintLucia, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment GardeningSuppliesMarketCategory "This category includes plants, seeds, tools, fertilizer, pesticides, and other things used in gardens.")
(comment MusicalInstrument "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$MusicalInstrument is a device that  (in the standard case) is designed to be manipulated by a person to generate music -- that is, s/he successively plays the notes of the music  by manipulating the instrument during the playing.  Possibly the player also supplies by muscle power the force that produces the sound, but possibly it uses another power source (e.g., electricity, or steam).   The music may or may not be of his or her own composition, but the player's actions determine that the notes are produced by the instrument (in the standard sense).  

Note:  If the directive role of the human player is subsumed by the device -- as it is, e.g., by some electronic instruments which are programmable and/or pre-programmed to produce music or musical sounds -- the device loses some of its instrument-like quality, and some automated uses may be abnormal cases of `playing' an instrument.  An older but analogous example is: player pianos.  If the device is pre-programmed so that humans can't direct the music at all, then the device is not a musical instrument (but a musical device) -- for example, music boxes.  Also excluded from #$MusicalInstrument are devices which produce music `at random' (such as wind chimes).  Devices such as radios, tape decks, CD players, which are used to play wholly pre-recorded or otherwise other-controlled music, are also not included in this collection.")
(disjointWith SportsAction LawEnforcementActivity)
(comment IntestinalCapillary "The collection of all intestinal capillaries.  An #$IntestinalCapillary is a #$Capillary which accepts nutrients into the #$Blood while also exchanging #$Oxygen and #$CarbonDioxide with intestinal tissue.")
(comment Yam-Foodstuff "Foodstuff from the edible root of the sugar beet plant.")
(comment LocalReligiousCongregation "A collection of local organizations.  An element of #$LocalReligiousCongregation is a group of religious believers and worshippers associated with a single religious building or site which is used for their meetings.  This collection includes all religious denominations.  Commonly, local congregations are affiliated with some larger religious organization having the same belief system.  Examples: St. Martin's Lutheran Church of Austin, TX, or Shadyside Presbyterian Church in Pittsburgh, PA.  But a large national or interstate religious association, such as the Southern Baptist Church, would NOT be an instance of #$LocalReligiousCongregation.")
(comment CrawlingOnHandsAndKnees "Locomotion in which the body is close to the ground or floor, usually 'on all fours'.")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact TextualMaterial)
(disjointWith BodyMovementEvent RecordedSoundPlaying)
(comment isaBoth "(#$isaBoth TERM COL-1 COL-2) states that TERM is an element of both of the collections COL-1 and COL-2. This predicate is #$notAssertible, since it  must always be recomputed from the current state of the #$genls heirarchy.  For comparison, see also #$nearestCommonIsa and #$nearestCommonSpecs.")
(comment GarageDoor "The door that goes on garages for modern houses.  They open vertically and are big enough to cover the space cars go through.")
(comment Plant-Woody "A specialization of #$Plant and #$TerrestrialOrganism. Each instance of #$Plant-Woody is a plant whose trunk, stems, or branches (and usually roots) are woody.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterO "The lowercase letter 'o'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$O-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterO.")
(comment BuiltInCookingRange "An #$CookingRange which is fixed to the construction artifact it is in             (beyond just the gas lines or electrical wires being attached).            I don't know how to say `built-in' in Cyc--maybe make it a PartOfBuilding?")
(disjointWith Burping SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment ElectricTypewriter "Electric typewriter")
(comment Physeterid-Physical "Prototype of Physeterids")
(comment CentralProcessingUnit "A specialization of #$ComputerHardwareComponent.  All and only instances of #$CentralProcessingUnit are the parts of computers that perform the actual interpretation of instructions and processing of data.")
(comment GeneralPartnership "The collection of all #$Partnerships that have only #$GeneralPartners and no #$LimitedPartners.  Each #$PartnershipPartner in a #$GeneralPartnership is jointly and severally liable for the debts and other liabilities of the #$Partnership.  Instances of #$JointVentureOrganization are often also instances of #$GeneralPartnership.")
(comment PromotionalProduct "Instances are products given away as part of a promotion. Examples could include free drug samples, radio station bumper stickers, pens with corporate logos, and so on. Promotional products are used for marketing purposes.")
(comment filePermissions "(#$filePermissions IBT ACCT PERM) means that a user logged on to a #$Computer as ACCT has PERM access to the #$ComputerFileCopy IBT found on that #$Computer.")
(comment CleaningARoom "All room cleaning events")
(comment VentralRamusS1 "The collection of all S1 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusS1 and #$DorsalRamusS1 branch from SpinalRootS1.  #$VentralRamusS1 supplies the #$SacralPlexus.")
(comment Chowder "The collection of all instances of chowder. Chowders are thick soups

featuring shellfish or fish, containing potatoes, often containing

milk or cream. Chowder as a kind of soup originated in New England.")
(comment FrenchDepartment "Instances of #$FrenchDepartment are the second important administrative
subdivision of #$France, they usually are subsumed into a
#$FrenchRegion. Created by the French Revolution, departements became
autonoms in 1871. #$AroundTheYear2000, #$France as 100 departements, 4 of
these oversea.")
(comment registryKeySetToValueOnComputer "(#$registryKeySetToValueOnComputer KEY VALUE COMP) means that, on the #$Computer COMP, the #$RegistryKey KEY in the #$WindowsRegistry found on COMP is set to VALUE. See also #$registryKeyNotSetToValueOnComputer.")
(comment VideoGameProgram-BlackAndWhite "Video game programs that are in black and white.")
(comment NarrativeTypeByGenre "#$NarrativeTypeByGenre is a collection of collections. Each element of #$NarrativeTypeByGenre is a collection of instances of #$Narrative whose instances are all of a similar style.")
(comment BikeCarrier "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$BikeCarrier is a device used to transport a bicycle.  Common bike carriers attach to the rear or top of an automobile.")
(comment CocoaPod "The fruit of the cacao tree; contains cocoa beans, from which chocolate is derived.")
(comment MaliPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Mali, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AudioCassette-Blank "The collection of #$AudioCassettes

that have never been recorded on.")
(comment Hokan-SiouanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages spoken widely in North America")
(comment FireplaceTongs "Things by some fireplaces which allow one to pick up or push around burning logs in a fireplace.")
(comment BaseballContact "Hitting a baseball with a #$BaseballBat. Each #$BaseballContact is a #$subEvents of some #$BaseballSwing.")
(comment LookingSurprised "The subset of making facial expressions in which an agent reacts to something unexpected.  The expression, like the reaction, may range from mild to extreme.")
(disjointWith ProjectilePropelling PreparingFoodOrDrink)
(comment ProprietaryComputerImageFile "This is the spec of #$ComputerImageFile consisting of files of pictures which are owned

and were created for the purpose of making money. The pictures in question are 

copyrighted but often end up being used by persons who do not hold the copyright. Indeed, the owner of the computer image file

in question often got the file by scanning copyrighted hardcopy pictures or by copying a computer image file owned by someone else.

Most #$ProprietaryComputerImageFiles are of a pornographic nature.")
(comment IceCreamScoop "A heavy spoon-like device used to scoop out portions of ice cream.")
(comment Reptile "An instance of #$BiologicalClass, and a specialization of #$Vertebrate.  Each instance of #$Reptile is an air-breathing, cold-blooded vertebrate with a body covered by scales or bony plates.  Notable specializations of #$Reptile include #$Snake, #$Lizard, and #$Turtle.  Most species of #$Reptile are oviparous (see #$OviparousAnimal), but some are viviparous (see #$ViviparousAnimal).")
(comment cruisingAltitude-MissileType "(#$cruisingAltitude-MissileType MISSILE ALT) means
  that when a #$CruiseMissile of type MISSILE is launched,
   its initial cruising altitude is ALT -- a
 #$Distance above sea level.")
(comment FaceOfAnimal "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart and #$ExternalAnatomicalPart. Each instance of #$FaceOfAnimal is the bodily region of an animal where the eyes of that animal are located.  In most terrestrial animals, this is the front region of an animal's head, and it also turns out to be where the nose and mouth are located.")
(comment GeneticSubstrateFn "(GeneticSubstrateFn CELL) denotes the DNA of a CELL.")
(comment Charging-Rushing "The type of action in which an animal aroused by rage, fear, or mating instincts aggressively runs at another animal in a physical attack.")
(comment Cytoskeleton "This is the collection of those parts of cells called cytoskeletons. The cytoskeleton is both a muscle and a skeleton, and is responsible for cell movement, cytokinesis, and the organization of the organelles within the cell.")
(comment PortableDocumentFormatFile "Computer files encoded in the PDF file format. The PDF format was developed by #$AdobeInc.  This is a very versatile format, with the capability of including a wide range of fonts, graphics, colors, etc.")
(comment SiteDelivery "Delivery to a construction site or other job site.")
(comment OriginalWorkOfArt "Works of art that are originals, not copies.  This might have to be modified.  Oh well ....")
(comment Pupil-EyePart "The opening in the iris of an eye which lets in light")
(comment PrepaidTelephoneCard "An instance of #$MoneyTenderType and a specialization of both #$Card and #$PhysicalDevice. Each instance of this collection allows a user to make telephone calls by debiting the price of the call from the #$MonetaryValue (q.v.) remaining on the card. The value on the card may be encoded on a magnetic strip on the card, or kept track of by the company that issued the card.")
(comment LhasaApso "A collection of small dogs with coats of very long hair.")
(comment Puritan "The collection of members of a 16th and 17th century Protestant group in England and New England opposing as unscriptural the ceremonial worship and the prelacy of the Church of England.")
(disjointWith HealthcareOrganization IdeologicalOrganization)
(comment DigitalCamcorder "The class of digital cameras used to record moving images.")
(comment maleParentActor "(#$maleParentActor EVENT ORGANISM) means that ORGANISM is the male parent in the #$SexualReproductionEvent EVENT.")
(comment InternalOblique "The #$Collection of all instances of #$InternalOblique #$Muscle.  The #$InternalOblique #$Muscle flexes the #$SpinalColumn and compresses the abdominal contents.  If acting unilaterally,it rotates the #$Torso towards its side.  The fibers are aligned upward towards the midline of the #$Abdomen.The #$InternalOblique is sandwiched between the  #$ExternalOblique and the #$TransverseAbdominous.")
(comment ParotidGland "The collection of all parotid salivary #$Glands.  Instances of this collection are #$internalParts of the cheek which secrete #$Saliva into the #$Mouth.")
(comment Buttermilk "A cultured milk made by adding bacteria to sweet milk.  (Originally, the liquid left after butter was made from milk.)")
(comment Theater-Organization "An entertainment industry establishment that puts on plays and other forms of live entertainment.")
(comment PasswordSnifferProgram "The collection of sniffers used to collect passwords.")
(comment MedicalTestKit "A #$MedicalTestKit is the collection of medical tests which are used to help diagnosis the health and/or illness of patients.")
(comment OakTree "The collection of oak trees.  An oak has alternate, simple, deciduous or evergreen leaves.  The male flowers are borne in pendent yellow catkins, appearing with or after the leaves.  The female flowers each has a husk of overlapping scales that enlarges to hold the fruit, or acorn.")
(comment StockCertificate "A specialization of #$OfficialDocument and #$CertificateDocument.  Each instance of #$StockCertificate is a document issued by a corporation (see #$Business) to one of its shareholders, certifying the shareholder's ownership of some number of shares of #$Stock (q.v.) in that corporation. See also #$shareholders.")
(comment AtomicClock "A specialization of #$Clock.  Each instance of #$AtomicClock uses certain resonance frequencies of atoms to keep time with extreme accuracy.")
(comment PrepositionalPhraseModifyingFrame "This frame is used for adverbs which can modify a prepositional phrase,           such as `at least'.")
(comment strict-HL-TimePrecedence "A strict-HL-TimePrecedence relationship can be concluded from some other statement of temporal interval precedence. It facilitates temporal relations inference.")
(comment ProjectileShell-FixedLoading "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is loaded in a  fixed fashion is fixed to the #$ProjectileCasing.  Most small arm ammunition is fixed.")
(comment Apostrophe-TheSymbol "The symbol ' used as an apostrophe. It is used to indicate contraction or possessives.  This is the abstract characer (see #$Character-Abstract), not any physical instantiation.")
(comment FireEscape "A flight of stairs made of metal which are used in some old apartment buildings to escape in case of fire. They are attached to outside walls.")
(comment hasInterfaceDevices "This predicate identifies a particular interface device that is linked to a particular computer.  (#$hasInterfaceDevices COMPUTER INTERFACE) means that INTERFACE is a #$ComputerInterfaceDevice for the #$Computer COMPUTER.  E.g., this predicate holds between my desktop PC and the mouse that's connected to it, the monitor that's connected to it, the keyboard that's connected to it, etc.")
(comment TearGas "The collection of #$ToxicGases which are used in warfare, police raids, and riot control and which cause temporary blinding and excessive tearing.")
(comment PosteriorCord-BrachialPlexus "The collection of all posterior cords of the brachial plexus.  The posterior cord is formed by the posterior divisions of all three trunks, the #$SuperiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus, the #$MiddleTrunk-BrachialPlexus and the #$InferiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus.  Nerves formed from the posterior cord are the #$AxillaryNerve, the #$RadialNerve, the #$ThoracoDorsalNerve, the #$UpperSubScapularNerve and the #$LowerSubScapularNerve.")
(comment Chocolate "The tasty, chocolate-colored stuff most of us love to eat.")
(comment typesSimilarWRTTypeViaBinRel-Inverse "This is a 'type-level' version of
#$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel-Inverse.  That is,
(#$typesSimilarWRTTypeViaBinRel-Inverse COL1 COL2 COMCOL BINPRED)
implies that where INST1 is an instance of COL1 and INST2 is an
instance of COL2 such that (different INST1 INST2) and COM1 is an
instance of COMCOL such that (BINPRED COM1 INST1), either (BINPRED
COM1 INST2) or there exists an instance of COMCOL, COM2, such that
(#$similarTo COM1 COM2) and (BINPRED COM2 INST2).  Equivalently, where
INST1 and INST2 are respective instances of COL1 and COL2,
(#$typesSimilarWRTTypeViaBinRel-Inverse COL1 COL2 COMCOL BINPRED)
implies (#$similarWRTTypeViaBinRel-Inverse INST1 INST2 COMCOL
BINPRED).")
(comment Drumstick "The collection of sticks (i.e., #$Shaft's) used for playing #$DrumInstrument's.")
(comment DentalXRayMachine "The collection of machines intended for taking X-rays of someone's teeth.")
(comment Egg-Fish "This is the collection of all fully developed (but not necessarily fertilized)

fish eggs. Several important specs of this collection are food stuffs. ")
(comment TelephoneDirectory-Reverse "This collection includes TelephoneDirectories that have entries organized by phone number rather than by the last name of an individual.")
(comment Tonsil "The #$Collection of all #$Tonsils.  Individual #$Tonsils are small rounded masses appearing on each side of the rear of the #$Tongue at the top of the #$Throat.")
(comment SubcollectionRelationFunction-Inverse "Instances of this collection are such that for any NAT (FN COL1 PRED COL2) formed with them, either (PRED COL2 COL1) or (relationAllExists PRED COL2 COL1) holds. In other words, COL1 and COL2 are in the opposite order in the expansion from in the NAT.")
(disjointWith ShortPants FootballPants)
(comment FilbertTree "A deciduous shrub or tree producing brown, roundish or oblong nuts about 1-4 cms long, called filberts or hazelnuts.")
(comment SwedishPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Sweden, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment StateOrProvinceWideOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations whose scope of operations and ownership or membership is primarily confined to a particular #$Province or #$State-Geopolitical (but to no smaller subdivision within that geopolitical division - see #$LocalOrganization).  An example of a #$StateOrProvinceWideOrganization is #$StateBarOfTexas.")
(comment PowerCordAdapter "This is the collection of adapters designed to allow power cords

to be used in circumstances in which they otherwise could not be

used. Included are adapters to allow electrical devices to be used

on airplanes and in cars, and adapters that allow one to plug a

three-pronged cord into a two-holed socker.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfMacroCapableProgram "#$VulnerableBecauseOfMacroCapableProgram is a specialization of
 #$ProgramConfigurationVulnerability.  It is a vulnerability of a computer
 that arises as a consequence of installing macro-capable programs,
 such as #$MSWord or #$MSExcel. See #$MacroVirus and #$macroCapable.")
(comment Vase "A container or vessel capable of holding water, in which flowers are displayed or arranged.")
(disjointWith Conveying-Generic Rally)
(comment MicrosoftComputerProgram "Software products made by #$MicrosoftInc.")
(disjointWith UtilityCompany MedicalCareOrganization)
(comment WaterBottle "Bottles which are intended for storage/drinking of water.  This is mostly intended to mean those which are re-used, rather than those in which water is merely sold.")
(disjointWith ManipulatingFoodOrDrink ProgrammingAComputer)
(comment BloodTypeB "Blood type B")
(comment AbaCloth "The collection of #$Cloth woven from goat and camel hair, made in the #$ArabianPeninsula, #$Syria, or nearby places.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType MicrotheoryType)
(comment HorizontalStabilizer "The collection of aircraft horizontal stabilizers.  Typically, an aircraft horizontal stabilizer is part of the aircraft's tail assembly.")
(disjointWith FingerMovement TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment Ear "The organ of hearing, which occur in pairs on most animals")
(comment Leather "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleThing. Each instance of #$Leather is a piece of tanned animal hide. Instances of #$Leather are commonly used as material inputs to the manufacture of shoes, gloves, upholstery, satchels and purses, saddles, and other items.")
(comment Terrier-Norwich "A collection of very small dogs.")
(comment ChemOrBioWeaponPrecursorMaterialType "This collection includes all precursor chemicals, biological agents, and  equipment particular to the manufacture of #$ChemicalWeapons and   #$BiologicalWeapons.")
(comment Brachialis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Brachialis #$Muscle.  The #$Brachialis, located in the #$UpperArm is the strongest flexor of the #$ElbowJoint.")
(comment Closet "A walled, roomlike structure within a HOC, used for storage, and having a portal to another room or a passageway of the HOC.")
(comment SkeletalMuscleSet "The #$Collection of all sets of #$SkeletalMuscles. An individual #$SkeletalMuscleSet has as #$anatomicalParts several #$SkeletalMuscles.")
(comment Gasperone-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Gasperone, 

an Italian sheep's milk pecorino with black pepper.")
(comment GovernmentalBuilding "Buildings which are intended to house governments or parts of governments - state capitols, courthouses, etc.")
(comment StillLifeImage "The collection of visual images that depict only nonliving objects.  Typically, a still life depicts a group of objects having related  (including: contrasting) shapes, colors, or categories.")
(disjointWith Knife CleaningDevice)
(comment Endosperm "An endosperm is the storage tissue in the seeds of most angiosperms used to furnish the developing embryo with nutrients, (a sort of 'box lunch' to nurture the embryo during its entombment within the seed)); the endosperm results from the fertilization of the two polar nuclei cells by a male gamete during 'double fertilization' (and is therfore a genetic sibling of the embryo destined to consume it).")
(comment AncientRomanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of the #$RomanEmpire, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PortableAudioEquipmentTypeByUse "#$PortableAudioEquipmentTypeByUse is a collection of collections. Each element is a subcollection of #$PortableAudioEquipment, all of whose elements share the feature of being designed and marketed for use in a certain type of situation. For example, #$PortableStereoSystem is an element of #$PortableAudioEquipmentTypeByUse, all of whose elements are designed for use in situations that require that a #$StereoSystem be easily transportable but not be so lightweight as to be easily used while exercising.")
(comment BorotukeLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in the Caribbean region and/or South America ")
(comment TableSpoon-MeasuringTool "The measuring tool which measures the exact quantity of one Tablespoon.")
(comment InterrogativeUtterance "The collection of interrogative  utterances issued in any language.")
(comment PuzzleGameProgram "The collection of all  #$ComputerGamePrograms that are simulated versions of puzzles.")
(comment Halyard "A rope or tackle for hoisting and lowering something (as sails).")
(comment WellbutrinProduct "An #$AntiDepressant drug product manufactuered by Burroughs Wellcome.")
(comment UrgeToScratch "This is a #$Collection of physical urges of a certain type, namely the urges that animals have to scratch an itch (and their accompanying internal sensations.)")
(comment SuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of upper (superior or cephalic) major lobes of  #$Lungs in #$AirBreathingVertebrates.  Includes left and right upper  lobes (i.e., for both lungs).")
(comment ColdCereal "Cereal products that are sold in a form that doesn't require any (additional) cooking before consumption.  Usually such cereals are eaten cold with milk poured over them.")
(comment informationStore-FunctionalRole "(#$informationStore-FunctionalRole SYSTEM MEMORY) meansthat MEMORY functions as a component within SYSTEM whose purpose is to store information within SYSTEM for varying periods of time and for various purposes.")
(comment CueBall "The collection of #$PoolBalls that the player strikes with his cue.")
(disjointWith MaintenanceEvent PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment IBOCreation-NonVerbal "Actions where an agent expresses information non-verbally, generating non-verbal or non-textual IBOs (#$InformationBearingObject instances) such as gestures, facial expressions, diagrams, etc.")
(disjointWith Hammer WritingImplement)
(comment Abyssinian-Cat "Each #$Abyssinian-Cat is a slender shorthaired cat with a reddish coat, having tabby-like markings. ")
(comment CyprusPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Cyprus-TheCountry, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization)
(comment VirtualPet "Instances are electronic toys which simulate a real creature. Some are small, with a little LCD display and a few buttons for input. These devices are programmed to display a representation of a creature that is born/hatches, grows, and matures.  Other types of #$VirtualPet, such as the #$Furby-TheToy, are doll-like, having the shape and some of the behaviors of a mammal.")
(comment Calculator "Electronic calculator")
(comment SystemicCapillary "The collection of all systemic capillaries.  A #$SystemicCapillary is the normal type of #$Capillary in the body.  It releases #$Oxygen to body tissue while absorbing #$CarbonDioxide and waste products into the #$Blood.")
(comment Potato-Foodstuff "Potato in any of its edible forms.")
(comment InsuranceCompany "The collection of all #$InsuranceProviders that are CommercialServiceOrganizations and that offers financial protection (in the form of insurance policies) to its #$customers against loss occasioned by sickness, natural disaster, theft, accident and similar liabilities.  Instances of #$InsuranceCompany may specialize in one or more types of loss.")
(comment MaliciousComputerProgram-DenialOfService "The collection of 

#$MaliciousComputerPrograms that have as the objective of their use a

 successful #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService.")
(comment GraduatedCylinder "Device used in laboratories for measuring small  volumes of liquids; a glass cylinder standing on its flat base, and typically marked in ml gradations.")
(comment SolidAnimalMatter "All pieces of solid animal material.")
(comment Decrypting "A specialization of #$Decoding.  In each instance of #$Decrypting, a transformation is applied to the information in an encrypted information-bearing object (see the collections #$Encrypting and #$InformationBearingObject) so that the information is rendered into a readily accessible form.")
(comment complementaryNucleotideTypes "(#$complementaryNucleotideTypes N-TYPE1 N-TYPE2) means that instances of #$NucleotideType N-TYPE1 are complementary to instances of #$NucleotideType N-TYPE2 in virtue of their nitrogen bases being complementary. Type-level version of #$complementaryNucleotides.")
(comment CorkTheStopper "Like the one used in Wine Bottle.")
(comment Vine-Plant "A specialization of #$Plant and #$TerrestrialOrganism.  Each instance of #$Vine-Plant is a plant that grows in a form chacterized by long tendrils or long, narrow, flexible ropy strands.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterP "The capital letter 'P'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$P-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterP.")
(comment CentralAirConditioner "Central air conditioners")
(comment FishingLure "The collection of all fishing lures. These are the things at the user end of a #$FishingLine to lure fish to bite so that they will be caught on the #$Fishhook.")
(disjointWith Yawning SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment interArgNotIsa2-5 "(#$interArgNotIsa2-5 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the second argument to PRED, the fifth argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(disjointWith TransportFacility Platform)
(comment Stilt-Bird "A collection of long-legged birds.  Both Himantopus mexicanus (or H. himantopus) and Cladorhynacus leucocephala are considered ``stilts''.")
(comment PartnershipPartner "The collection of all partners in instances of #$Partnership.  #$PartnershipPartners may be either #$GeneralPartners or #$LimitedPartners, or both.")
(comment PinballMachine "The collection of machines used for #$PlayingPinball.")
(comment BathroomCloset "A closet for storing towels, toilet paper.  Not a WC or a stall.")
(comment SuralNerve "The collection of all sural nerves.  The sural nerve is a branch of the #$TibialNerve.  It supplies the skin on the distal third of the leg and the lateral side of the foot.")
(comment Dip-Food "This is the collection of all instances of dips. A dip is any food that is intended to be and is usually eaten by being scooped up onto some other

food such as a #$Chip-Snack or piece of raw vegetable. Fondue thus counts as a dip.

A borderline case is salsa, which is most often consumed as a dip in the

U.S.. It would probably not count as a dip in Mexico. Salsa is definitely

a condiment, so #$Dip-Food and #$Condiment are not necessarily disjoint.")
(disjointWith County FrenchDepartment)
(comment PassengerPigeon "A large migratory pigeon hunted to extinction by human beings.  The last surviving #$PassengerPigeon was #$MarthaThePassengerPigeon.")
(comment DeviceDriverProgram "The programs that act as interfaces between hardware and operating systems.  The device driver usually presents a standard interface to the operating system, allowing an idiosyncratic piece of hardware to be manipulated in a standard way.")
(comment Corral "A place where cows are kept - free to roam within the enclosure - but not free enough to excape it.")
(comment AudioClipOfSubjectFn "(#$AudioClipOfSubjectFn SUBJECT) denotes the collection of all #$AudioClips in which sounds produced by the #$SpatialThing-Localized, SUBJECT, occur. For example, (#$AudioClipOfSubjectFn #$BillClinton) denotes the collection of all #$AudioClips in which Bill Clinton can be heard; (#$AudioClipOfSubjectFn #$BombingOfSANGHeadquarters-1995) denotes the collection of all #$AudioClips in the #$BombingOfSANGHeadquarters-1995 can be heard.")
(comment FourCycleEngine "Any #$Engine in which the piston goes through two complete up-and-down cycles for every combustion event.  Some are #$DieselEngines and some are #$GasolineEngines.")
(comment HongKongPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$HongKong, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment networkMember "'(#$networkMember NETWORK MEMBER)' means that the #$Organization MEMBER is a member of the #$NetworkOrganization NETWORK.  For example, the #$networkMembers of a #$RetailPharmacyNetwork are the individual #$PharmaceuticalDispensingOrganizations that make up the #$RetailPharmacyNetwork.")
(comment Keepsake "The collection of keepsakes. A keepsake is a kind of gift which has

the additional purpose of memorializing a certain event, such as a

wedding.")
(comment placeOfDeath "(#$placeOfDeath ANIMAL PLACE) means that ANIMAL died in the location PLACE.  PLACE may be any instance of #$Place, such as a building or a geographical location.")
(comment Macro-OtomangueanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages spoken in #$Mexico and Central America")
(comment FireplacePoker "The collection of metal sticks that one uses to poke and stir up logs and coals in a fireplace in order to make them burn more thoroughly.")
(comment LookingPuzzled "The subset of making facial expressions in which an agent appears confused or hesitant about something; the signals may be subtle and vary, including eyebrows either raised or contracted in a slight frown.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink MovingEarth)
(comment useReformulationRuleForQuantifierMovement "(#$useReformulationRuleForQuantifierProcessing RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the QuantifierMovementRLModule, which serves to 

move ill-placed #$NLTagFn expressions into a position where they

can be used by the QuantifierProcessingRLModule.")
(comment ComputerDesktopTheme "The collection of all computer desktop themes and their subparts.  Themes are generally comprehensive sets of computer files that define how the desktop of a computer will look.  Elements of themes include background pictures, definitions of window borders, icons, sound effects,...")
(comment EyeglassFrames "The collection of eyeglass frames")
(disjointWith FaceOfAnimal ExtrudedBodyPart)
(comment Calcaneus "The #$Calcaneus is the 'heel bone'.")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece CordlikeObject)
(comment BiologicalSpecies "An instance of #$BiologicalTaxonType. Each instance of #$BiologicalSpecies is the most general taxon from which two breeding organisms of appropriate sexes can conceivably produce fertile offspring, or, in the case of asexual reproduction, is conventionally defined.  Members of different species of animals cannot produce fertile offspring by interbreeding.  If there are only two breeds of a given species and one breed becomes extinct, the second breed by virtue of that fact becomes an instance of #$BiologicalSpecies -- since the only organisms instances can breed with to produce fertile offspring are, at that point, members of that collection.  An instance of #$BiologicalSpecies has members who all have significant traits in common, and members of each biological species have other members as parents.  Exceptions occur when a species is conventionally defined to start since parenthood could conceivably be traced back billions of years, yet new species came into existence.  In biological taxonomy, related species are grouped into a particular instance of #$BiologicalGenus.  Some genera have only a single species, but they remain different taxons.")
(comment DocFile "The collection of #$ComputerFile-AISs encoded in the Doc File Format.  The Doc format is the native format used by #$MicrosoftInc, in Microsoft Word.")
(comment HomeDelivery "delivery of an object where it is brought to the recipients home.")
(disjointWith Locomotion-SolidSurface FloatingInASubstance)
(comment TravellersCheck "Checks issued by a financial institution to a purchaser, which can be used as cash by the purchaser (but not by others).  Travellers checks are protected in that, if they are lost or stolen, the issuing company wil replace them.  Travellers checks (in the US) are issued in values of 10, 20, 50, 100, and maybe 500 dollars")
(comment Glottis "The collection of all glottises (or 'glottides').

An individual #$Glottis is a unique part of a #$Person or other #$Vertebrate which consists of the #$VocalCords and the space between them.")
(comment learnedCapableOf "This generalization of #$skillCapableOf can be used to assert that a given individual agent has the ability to play a certain role in a certain type of #$LearnedActivity (q.v.).  (#$learnedCapableOf AGENT ACTTYPE ROLE) means that AGENT has acquired the necessary abilities to act in ROLE in normal instances of ACTTYPE.  For example, that #$Gumby has learned to walk is expressed by (#$learnedCapableOf #$Gumby #$WalkingOnTwoLegs #$performedBy).  #$learnedCapableOf entails that AGENT satisfies any physical or intellectual prerequisites for acquiring, possessing, and exercising the ability; but it is neutral as to whether AGENT has the necessary resources of time, money, opportunity, etc., to exercise the ability in any particular instance of ACTTYPE.  Note that ROLE should normally be a fairly \"central\" one to ACTTYPEs, i.e. a specialization of #$doneBy or #$deliberateActors.")
(comment CountingDevice "The collection of devices used to count occurrences of, for e.g., revolutions of a wheel, items produced, etc. For counting events, see #$Counting.")
(comment Kuvasz "A collection of large, white dogs, ancient in origin, going           back at least 7000 years.  A work dog.")
(comment MayanTribe "A tribe of Mayan indians (see #$EthnicGroupOfMayans).

The Mayan civilization of classical times (see #$ClassicalMayanCivilization) was

composed of a heterogeneous group of such tribes, each constantly forming

and breaking political and military allegiances.")
(disjointWith HealthcareOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment ChildrensBook "The collection of children's books.")
(comment Exotoxin "A collection of protein toxins released by some pathogenic #$Bacterium and affects particular sites in the body.  This collection includes #$BacterialNeurotoxin and #$Enterotoxin.  #$Exotoxins are produced by both #$GramPositiveBacterium and #$GramNegativeBacterium.  Toxicity

is normally destroyed at temperatures above 60 degrees Celsius.  These

toxins usually bind to specific receptors and do not usually produce

#$Fever in the host.")
(comment ScalenusAnterior "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ScalenusAnterior #$Muscle.  The #$ScalenusAnterior raises the #$FirstRib during forced inspiration when acting bilaterally.  It also is used bilaterally or unilaterally to assist flexion of the #$Neck-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment SupplyCabinet-PieceOfFurniture "the collection of all supply cabinets")
(disjointWith SportsCompetition AutoMaintenance)
(comment SubMaxillaryGland "The collection of all submaxilary salivary #$Glands.  Instances of this collection are #$internalParts of the cheek which secrete #$Saliva into the #$Mouth.")
(comment SnackFoodType "Instances are types of food which are typically eaten as snacks, and less commonly (though certainly plausibly) eaten as a meal or as part of a meal.")
(comment TowingShop "An organization which is a local customer point of contact, and will tow your car.")
(comment ApplicationProgrammingInterface "The collection of all application programming interfaces (APIs).
         An API is a specification for a set of computer functions 
         which describes only their input and output, while remaining
         neutral about how they operate, and (often) what operating
         system or what hardware the API is implemented on.  In theory,
         this allows software using the API to be unaffected by details
         in the way the API functions are actually written.")
(comment Milk "The collection of all volumes of mammalian milk.  Each instance of this collection is fluid secreted from the #$Teat of a female #$Mammal, or a mixture of such fluid from several teats.  Cow's milk which is pasturized is described by the more specific collection, #$CowsMilk-Product.")
(disjointWith PrepaidTelephoneCard PostageStamp)
(comment ComplementaryBasePairing "Collection of #$ChemicalBonding events in which instances of any
of the five specs of #$NitrogenBase become paired with their respective
complementary bases.")
(comment successorStrict-HL-TimePrecedence "A successorStrict-HL-TimePrecedence relationship can be concluded from some other statement of temporal interval precedence. It facilitates temporal relations inference.")
(comment ProjectileShell-Pierce "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is designed primarily to pierce its target.  The typical #$BulletAssembly is of this form.")
(disjointWith VegetableMatter AnimalBLO)
(comment AcuteAccent-TheSymbol "A slash pointing upwards and to the right. When placed over a letter, it may be used to indicate primary stress or accent.")
(comment StepOfStairs "A rest for the foot in ascending or descending.")
(comment AntiTankWeapon "The collection of #$Weapons intended for use against #$Tank-Vehicles and usually capable of piercing armor. In the modern military all #$AntiTankWeapons are #$Missiles, that is self-powered. This collection does not include #$IndirectFireWeapons such as #$Mortars, that although effective against #$Tank-Vehicles are not called anti-tank weapons.")
(comment Hearing "The collection of sensory #$Perceivings in which, by means of vibratory sensors, a #$PerceptualAgent #$hears something that is causing (or consisting of) sound waves, and thereby acquires information about it.  See also: #$ListeningDeliberately, the subcollection of #$Hearing events in which the aural stimulus is intentionally attended to.")
(comment VentralRamusT12 "The collection of all T12 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT12 and #$DorsalRamusT12 branch from SpinalRootT12.  #$VentralRamusT12 supplies below the #$TwelfthRib and the #$LumbarPlexus.")
(comment Pasteurization "The heating of a milk product in order to kill off microorganisms that might make it spoil.")
(comment RattleInstrument "A specialization of #$MusicalInstrument.  Each instance of this collection is a musical instrument in which a hollow section has pellets inside which cause a noise from hitting the walls when the instrument is shaken.--Foxvog, Aug. 2, 1999")
(comment DeadAnimal "A specialization of #$OrganicMaterial (and not, of course, of #$Animal, whose instances must be alive).  Each instance of #$DeadAnimal is a corpse or partial remains of an individual animal, somewhat intact, and prior to any butchering, burning, cooking, dissolving, or fully decomposing.")
(comment DentalChair "The kind of chair found in a dentist's office, that has a headrest, tilts waaay back, and is covered in a vinyl which won't soak up any body fluids.")
(comment Mold-Fungus "This is the collection of all instances of mold. Mold is a kind of fungus that

grows from airborne spores.")
(comment ArtGlass "Decorative glass objects, usually handblown by an artist.")
(comment Resting-Relaxing "The collection of events in which an animal abstains from strenuous physical activity.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice CommunicationDevice)
(comment DivisionGinkgophyta "This is the collection of ginkgoes.")
(comment SwissPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Switzerland, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization StateOrProvinceWideOrganization)
(comment ComputerMousePad "This is the collection of mouse pads.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfBrowserConfiguration "#$VulnerableBecauseOfBrowserConfiguration is a specialization of
 #$ProgramConfigurationVulnerability.  It is a vulnerability of a computer
 that arises as a consequence of the configuration of a browser
 installed on the computer.")
(comment Bucket "The collection of all tangible buckets")
(comment TerroristAgent "A specialization of #$SocialBeing and #$CovertAgent (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$TerroristAgent is a person (see #$Terrorist) or a group of people (see #$TerroristGroup) that commits terrorist activities (see #$TerroristAct and #$TerroristAttack).")
(disjointWith Antenna-AnimalBodyPart Limb-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment EdibleStuffComposite "#$EdibleStuffComposite is a specialization of #$EdibleStuff and #$Artifact-NonAgentive.  Each instance of #$EdibleStuffComposite is an edible substance that is made up of two or more foodstuffs as constituents.  Typically, some recipe is, explicitly or implicitly, associated with the production of such substances.  #$EdibleStuffComposite includes both some instances of #$FoodIngredientOnly (e.g., a dollop of ketchup) and some instances of #$FoodOrDrink (e.g., a slice of a cheese pizza).")
(comment TypicalBehaviorOfTypeInSitTypeFn "#$TypicalBehaviorOfTypeInSitTypeFn takes a spec of #$Agent-Generic and a spec of #$Situation and returns the collection of action-types that are 'typical' for that kind of agent when involved in that kind of situation. For example, (#$TypicalBehaviorOfTypeInSitTypeFn CowardlySoldier TrappedInFoxHoleEvent) is the collection of kinds of actions that an instance of CowardlySoldier is expected to engage in when s/he finds him/herself in any TrappedInFoxHoleEvent.")
(comment ProductSerialNumberMappingFn "Takes a #$FormalProductType and returns a mapping between IDStrings for instances of the #$FormalProductType and instances of the #$FormalProductType.")
(comment PersonalInformationManagementProgram "#$PersonalInformationManagementProgram is the collection of computer programs whose primary function is to store and enable access to an individual's 'personal' information such as personal contacts, calendar, etc.")
(disjointWith InsuranceProvider ProductDisplayOrganization)
(comment Cradle "The set of rocking beds for babies.")
(comment BiologicalSubclass "The collection of biological taxonomic subdivisions more specific than #$BiologicalClass but more general than #$BiologicalOrder.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent ProgrammingAComputer)
(comment BloodTypeA "Blood type A")
(comment ShowerCurtain "The collection of all curtains, usually made from (#$SolidFn #$Plastic), hung from a            #$ShowerCurtainRod with #$ShowerCurtainRings and used in instances of            #$TakingAShower to prevent water from leaving the #$ShowerStall.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType BeliefSystemType)
(comment AirplaneTailAssembly "The collection of airplane tail assemblies.  Typically, an airplane tail assembly is connected to an airplane's fuselage and has two horizontal stabilizers and one vertical stabilizer.")
(disjointWith MakingAnOralSound FingerMovement)
(comment VisualSystem "Visual systems considered as a whole part")
(disjointWith SomethingToWear InnerTube)
(comment Terrier-Norfolk "A collection very small dogs, with tough, wiry coats.  A work dog.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization TechnologyOrganization)
(comment Centerfold-PhotoOfPerson "The collection of all instances of #$Centerfold-Generic that depict #$StunninglyBeautiful (generally scantily clad or #$Nude) #$Persons. In many microtheories, many instances of #$Centerfold-PhotoOfPerson are #$PornographicMaterial.")
(comment KillerWhale "A species of large toothed whale, also known as Orcas")
(comment BrachioRadialis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$BrachioRadialis #$Muscle.  The #$BrachioRadialis flexes the #$ElbowJoint aginst resistance or rapidly.")
(comment Hallway "Hallways in instances of #$ShelterConstruction")
(comment HepaticPortalVein "The collection of all portal #$Veins of the #$Liver.  The #$HepaticPortalVein is the main #$Vein leading into the #$Liver.  The distal end of the #$HepaticPortalVein is formed by the conjunction of the #$SplenicVein and the #$SuperiorMesentericVein.  The proximal end of the #$HepaticPortalVein connects to the hepatic portal system.")
(comment FontinaGeneric-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Fontina, 

including #$FontinaDAosta-Cheese as well as the many poor imitations of it. Most

generic versions of Fontina are rubbery and have little flavor.")
(comment Robot "A device which operates autonomously, moving about or manipulating physical objects, .")
(comment toxinTypeProducedByOrganismType "(#$toxinTypeProducedByOrganismType TOXINTYPE ORGTYPE) means that ORGTYPE, an instance of #$OrganismClassificationType, produce toxins of the kind TOXINTYPE, a spec of #$BiologicalToxin.")
(disjointWith ArtObject Form-StandardizedIBO)
(comment SexOrgan "Instances of #$SexOrgan are body parts of animals which have an important function in sexual reproduction.")
(disjointWith FluidReservoir SheetOfSomeStuff)
(comment LaotianPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Laos, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PersonalAudioPlayerByComponentType "A collection of collections.  Each element of #$PersonalAudioPlayerByComponentType is a subcollection of #$PersonalAudioPlayer -- one which combines the basic elements of portable audio system (amplifier and headphone jack) with one of the different types of #$AudioSystemComponents. E.g., a #$PortableCDPlayer is a portable system version of a home #$CompactDiscPlayer.")
(comment MixtecanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of Mexico and/or Central America")
(comment WorkBench "A large, sturdy table upon which devices get fixed using tools")
(comment contentOfUtterance "The expression `(#$contentOfUtterance UTTERANCE FORMULA)' means that what

was asserted in the #$DeclarativeUtterance UTTERANCE was the proposition

expressed by the #$ELSentence-Assertible FORMULA.")
(comment admittedNAT "(#$admittedNAT NAT) states that NAT is a #$CycLNonAtomicTerm which is both syntactically and semantically well-formed wrt arg constraints.  For example, (#$admittedNAT (#$MotherFn #$Muffet)) is true precisely in those mts in which #$Muffet satisfies all the applicable arg1 constraints imposed by #$MotherFn.  See also #$admittedSentence.")
(comment SimulationGameProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerGameProgram that simulate a complex system of a certain type, such as a city, ecosystem, large building, art colony, or vehicle. Instances are game titles such as \"SimCity 2000\" or \"Microsoft Flight Simulator\".")
(disjointWith Organization InformationBearingThing)
(comment TruckCab-Compartment "The region of a Truck in which the driver rides (and perhaps a passenger).  Contains control devices for operating the vehicle.")
(comment AdalatProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by Bayer Corporation.")
(comment FlatulentUrge "The type of internal sensation or urge to pass gas.")
(comment Mediastinum "The collection of mediastina, the regions of the body that  are each between the #$Lungs, above the #$Diaphragm-BodyPart, and below the top of  the #$ChestCavity, all within the #$ChestCavity.  The #$Mediastinum  contains the #$Heart, the AscendingAorta, AorticArch, Thymus and other body parts.")
(comment BreakfastCereal "A food derived from grain; often, but not necessarily, eaten for breakfast.")
(comment PlumbingFixture "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$PlumbingFixture is a device whose primary function is to be a functional, significant part of some plumbing system (see the constant #$PlumbingSystem-Building).  Notable specializations of #$PlumbingFixture include #$Pipe-Plumbing, #$Toilet, and #$ShowerHead.")
(disjointWith OpeningAContainerArtifact PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment SemiTrailer-Truck "Truck tractor-trailer combinations used for hauling dry freight.")
(comment Waist "The middle of a torso")
(disjointWith BaseballBat WritingImplement)
(comment CornishRex "Each #$CornishRex is a very slender cat having a velvety soft, curly coat. ")
(comment SalvadoranPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$ElSalvador, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment BabyGate "The collection of all #$Gates which are used to keep babies from wandering to unsafe places such as #$Stairways.  #$BabyGates are placed in front of these places or between two #$RoomInAConstruction and cause a #$BarrierSituation for the baby.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single InformationGathering)
(comment SystemicVein "The collection of all #$Veins which drain #$DeoxygenatedBlood towards the #$Heart (the right #$VentricleOfHeart).  This includes all #$Veins except pulmonary veins (#$PulmonaryVein-Generic) which carry #$OxygenatedBlood and those in the #$HepaticPortalVein system which drain towards the #$Liver.")
(comment Onion-Foodstuff "Foodstuff from the edible bulb of the onion plant.")
(comment BonkProgram "The collection of #$MaliciousComputerPrograms called 'Bonk', that work by overwhelming a victim's machine with corrupt UDP (User Datagram Protocol) #$Packet-Internets.")
(comment developmentalSuccessor "Next subsequent developmental stages.")
(comment sellsProductType "This predicate relates a given legal agent (see #$LegalAgent) to a specific  type of product s/he/it sells.  (#$sellsProductType AGENT PRODTYPE) means that  AGENT sells PRODTYPE.  For example, McDonald's sells hamburgers.  The  implication is AGENT typically and often sells products of PRODTYPE.  See  also #$ProductProviderFn-Seller.")
(comment VerticalBlind "The collection of blinds which have vertical slats.")
(comment Fungus "A specialization of both #$EukaryoticOrganism and #$Heterotroph, and an instance of #$BiologicalKingdom.  Instances of #$Fungus are eukaryotic, heterotrophic organisms that are typically not capable of movement.  The cell walls of instances of #$Fungus are structurally similar to the cell walls of #$Plants, but the former are composed mostly of chitin, while the latter are composed mostly of cellulose (see the collections #$Chitin and #$Cellulose).  Instances of #$Fungus reproduce by means of spores, which are usually disseminated by the wind.  Some types of #$Fungus are parasites (see the collection #$ParasiticOrganism), some are saprophytic (see the collection #$Saprophyte), and some have symbiotic relationships with other organisms.  Notable specializations of #$Fungus include #$Mushroom, #$Yeast, and #$RingwormFungus.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterP "The lowercase letter 'p'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$P-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterP.")
(comment FreeStandingCookingRange "An #$CookingRange which is not fixed to the construction artifact it is in             (beyond just the gas lines or electrical wires being attached).")
(comment BicycleRack-BikePart "Not to be confused with #$BikeCarrier, this is the collection of devices that are usually over the rear wheel of a bike whose purpose is to allow the rider to carry things while riding. They are also sometimes (confusingly) called bike carriers.")
(disjointWith Blinking SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment NavalShipBase "#$NavalShipBase is a specialization of #$MilitaryBase-Grounds.  Each instance of #$NavalShipBase is a naval base with facilities for #$ModernNavalShips or operated by a #$Navy.")
(comment Echinodermata "This is the collection of (individual) animals in the phylum Echinodermata. It includes starfish, sea urchins, sea cucumbers and sand dollars. Echinoderms are #$Coelomates.")
(comment StraitJacket "The collection of jacket-like instances of #$SomethingToWear that are used to restrain people, for their own protection or the protection of others.  The arms of the wearer are covered completely (including the hands) and bound by the structure of the jacket.")
(comment MoleRat "A collection of all #$Rodents (resembling #$Rats) of several different genera in #$SouthEastAsia.  These are sometimes called 'bandicoot' or 'bandicoot rat', although actual bandicoots are Australian #$Marsupials.")
(comment NoAccessPermission "On #$Computers running #$MSWindowsNT, the #$filePermissions for a given #$UserAccount and a given #$ComputerFileCopy may be set to #$NoAccessPermission, meaning that someone logged in under that account may neither read, nor write to, nor execute that #$ComputerFileCopy.")
(comment StorageConstructInABuilding "The collection of built-in storage areas in a structure")
(comment SuperiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus "The collection of all superior trunks of brachial plexi.  The superior trunk of a #$BrachialPlexus is formed by the convergence of nerves from the #$VentralRamusC5 and #$VentralRamusC6 in its side of the body.  The superior trunk splits into its anterior and posterior divisions distally.")
(disjointWith Country FrenchDepartment)
(comment MSWindowsApplication "Programs that are made to run under #$MSWindows and #$MSWindowsNT")
(comment Backgammon-EquipmentSet "The collection of all Backgammon sets. A Backgammon set is the set of all the objects -- #$Backgammon-Board, #$Backgammon-Piece, #$Die-TheCube, #$DiceShakers and #$DoublingCube -- that are #$instrument-Generic in a  (#$PlayingFn #$Backgammon) event")
(comment MaltesePerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Malta-TheCountry, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Casino-Object "The collection of all spaces (be they stand-alone #$Buildings or rooms within a larger #$Building) where instances of #$Casino-Organization operate.  Instances of #$Casino-Object may contain spaces that are used for activities other than #$Gambling (e.g., the hotel rooms in The Mirage building in Las Vegas), so long as the primary function of the construct is to provide a venue for #$Gambling activities.")
(comment Favor-Gift "The collection of favors, such as party favors

and wedding favors. A favor is a small item intended as a gift for

the attendees of some event.")
(comment CaucasianLanguageFamily "Languages indigenous to southwest Asiatic #$Russia")
(comment SyntheticCloth "Any synthetic fabric - rayon, nylon, polyester, etc.")
(comment CoveringOnesOwnFace "The set of actions in which a person covers his (or her) face.  Often it is done to prevent others from seeing the person's expression of some emotional response; may be done with the hands, an article of clothing, a newspaper, etc.")
(disjointWith PreparingFoodOrDrink ConflictEvent)
(comment GunTypeByCoolingSystem "The two instances of #$GunTypeByCoolingSystem are primarily  collections of #$MachineGuns that use either air-cooling or water-cooling  systems.  This prevents the machine gun from overheating after shooting many  rounds in a short duration.")
(disjointWith LibraryFile ComputerProgram-CW)
(disjointWith DurableGood ConsumableProduct)
(comment RespiratorySystem "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$RespiratorySystem is a system of body parts which function together  to enable its owner (an instance of #$Animal) to breathe.  Note that it is generally required that the #$RespiratorySystem of a #$Vertebrate work together with the #$CirculatorySystem (q.v.), as the air is used to supply needed substances to the blood and to remove waste products from the blood.")
(comment ZygomaticArch "The #$ZygomaticArch is an arching #$BoneStructure out from the #$Skull underlying the #$Cheek-Facial which is composed of parts of both the #$Malar and

#$TemporalBone.")
(comment geneticSubstrateOf "(#$geneticSubstrateOf CELL DNA) relates a CELL to its DNA.")
(disjointWith HardwareTool CordlikeObject)
(comment MIMEFile "The collection of #$ComputerFile-AISs encoded according to the #$MIMEStandard.")
(comment SteeringWheel "The thing the driver uses to steer the car.")
(disjointWith FluidFlowEvent Patrolling)
(comment JigsawPuzzle "A large set of interlocking flat pieces which when assembled form a picture")
(comment Epiglottis "The collection of all epiglottises, unique parts of mammalian #$RespiratoryTracts.  Each instance of thiscollection is a thin plate of flexible cartilage, in front of the glottis, that folds back over and protects the glottis during swallowing, preventing matter being swallowed from entering the #$Larynx and #$Trachea (windpipe).")
(comment FishingReel "The collection of all fishing reels. These are the things at the user end of a #$FishingPole that let out #$FishingLine and reel it back in.")
(comment Keeshond "A collection of medium-sized dogs with very thick coats.  Their colors are             a combination of grey, black and cream.")
(disjointWith HealthcareOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment MuscleCar "The collection of #$Automobiles with a very high horsepower/weight ratio.")
(comment VegetativeCell "Bacteria which are not in the state of being

#$Spore-DormantBacteriums are #$VegetativeCells. This is the usual life of the cell when it is metabolizing.")
(comment Supinator "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Supinator #$Muscle.  The #$Supinator weakly supinates the #$ForeArm in which it is located.  The #$RadialNerve passes between layers of this muscl.")
(comment Mattress "The part of a bed that a person rests on.")
(disjointWith ProductionEvent SportsCompetition)
(comment OroPharynx "The collection of all oropharynges.  Each #$OroPharynx is the central section of a #$Pharynx, being located behind (dorsal to) the #$Mouth.")
(comment WebDevelopmentBusiness "A collection of businesses. Each #$WebDevelopmentBusiness is a firm that does #$WebDesign for clients.")
(comment SoftwareCrackProgram "Collection of computer programs that 'crack' software by making a trial version of a program a permanent version, by removing 'register now' reminders, and so on.  Note that not all software cracks are programs; some are simply text files that instruct humans on how to disable various protection devices.  The constant #$SoftwareCrack-Instructions covers these instances.")
(comment ElectroEncephalographMachine "An electroencephalograph is a device used to trace and record a patient''s brain waves.")
(disjointWith PrepaidTelephoneCard BankDebitCard)
(comment complementaryBases "Each nitrogen base in a nucleic-acid molecule is complementary to bases of a specific type (at most 2 types). Instance-level version of #$complementaryBaseTypes.")
(comment PasswordCrackingProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs designed to crack (that is, guess) passwords.")
(comment ProjectileShell-SemiFixedLoading "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is loaded in a semi-fixed  fashion propellant is divided into increments, or charges, and each increment is  contained in a cloth bag.  All of the cloth bags are held together by an  acrylic cord, and are stored in the cartridge case.")
(comment Hyphen-TheSymbol "The symbol '-'. May be used between morphemes in a compound word; may be used to divide a word at the end of a line; may be used to mark a pause.  Contrast this with #$MinusSign-TheSymbol.")
(comment PenComputer "Pen computers are small, portable  computers whose only input is through a stylus, or pen, which can be used to draw input on the screen.")
(comment FireFightingVehicle-Military "The collection of #$FireTrucks used in a military context.")
(comment thirstLevel "The level of thirst of an animal.")
(comment DorsalRamusT4 "The collection of all T4 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT4 and DorsalRamiT4 branch from SpinalRootT4.  DorsalRamiT4 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment Pastry-Stuff "Any number of foods or food parts made of baked flour in combination with sugar and butter.  Pastry is breadlike but differs from bread in its fat content and in that it usually doesn't contain yeast. ")
(comment SetUIDFault "A program has this fault if it runs SUID and can be exploited at some point during its operation to yield its elevated user privileges to a user that does not have these privileges.  An important specialization is #$SetUIDFault-Root.")
(comment CompactDisc-Audio "A specialization of #$CompactDisc-Generic.  Each instance of this collection is designed to be used for storing audio in the CD format, which is most commonly used for music.")
(comment fileCopyFoundOnComputer "This predicate relates computer file copies to computational systems.  (#$fileCopyFoundOnComputer COPY COMPUTER) means that COPY is found on COMPUTER, (e.g. in memory, on disk, etc.).  Cf. #$fileFoundOnComputer.")
(comment Suture-Thread "The thread used by doctors to sew up lacerations in a patient's skin.")
(comment Postage "A  collection of #$InformationBearingThings.  It has both hardcopy (i.e., #$PostageStamp) and electronic instances. An instance of #$Postage is a #$TenderObject designed to be exchanged for the sending of a #$MailableObject as an instance of #$SendingSomething.")
(comment Thyroid "A gland in the neck which helps control metabolism (I think)")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact CleaningDevice)
(comment Ginkgo "A tree belonging to the species, Ginkgo biloba, which is the only extant species in the class, Ginkgopsida.")
(comment SyrianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Syria, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment DollAccessory "A collection of tangible objects.  Each element is something

 that may be used for playing with dolls; e.g., doll wigs, toy eating

instruments, toy mirrors, and etc.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfMacroCapableBrowserHelper "#$VulnerableBecauseOfMacroCapableBrowserHelper is a specialization of

#$VulnerableBecauseOfBrowserConfiguration and #$VulnerableBecauseOfMacroCapableProgram.  It is a vulnerability of a computer that arises as a consequence of allowing a macro-capable program, such as #$MSWord or #$MSExcel, to be a browser helper. See #$MacroVirus and #$macroCapable.")
(disjointWith Menstruating QualitativeTimeOfDay)
(comment Vegetable-Food "A specialization of #$FoodOrDrink.  Each instance of #$Vegetable-Food is a foodstuff which is derived from a plant and is ordinarily considered a vegetable; e.g., a carrot (an instance of #$Carrot-Foodstuff), a potato (an instance of #$Potato-Foodstuff), a lima bean (an instance of #$Bean-Foodstuff), or a tomato (an instance of #$Tomato-Foodstuff).  Note that #$Vegetable-Food includes certain plant parts, such as tomatoes, that are technically classified as fruits by botanists, but which are treated as vegetables in food classification.")
(comment ComputerNetworkingServiceMC "Class of product types which are service events that deal with computer networks - training, installation, maintenance, etc.")
(disjointWith UtilityCompany InsuranceProvider)
(comment PigPen "A place when pigs are kept")
(comment Octopus "The collection of all members of the order Octopoda of the class Cephalopoda (#$Cephalopods).  Octopi have 8 mobile sucker bearing arms.")
(comment StabilizingFin "Fins used on missiles and other things for stabilizing them.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType TransportationEventByVehicleType)
(comment VerticalStabilizer "The collection of aircraft vertical stabilizers.  Typically, an aircraft vertical stabilizer is part of the aircraft's tail assembly.")
(disjointWith FingerMovement IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment Whisker "Long feline facial hairs -- curb feelers for cats")
(disjointWith Leather LandStuff)
(comment Terrier-Manchester "A collection small to medium-sized dogs with smooth, black fur.")
(comment PasswordInformation-PIT "A subcollection of #$PropositionalInformationThing (PIT).  Every instance of #$PasswordInformation-PIT is the information contained in some instance of #$PasswordFile.  The #$PasswordInformation-PIT contained in a password file on some computer will contain all GAFs of the form (#$passwordForAccount PWORD ACCT) for each account found on that machine.  In order to obtain access to an instance of #$PasswordInformation-PIT, an agent must first obtain access to a #$Plaintext copy of the password file containing the PIT.")
(comment PinewoodDerbyCar "The collection of model cars built (by cub scouts, et al.) to be raced in 'pinewood derbies'.")
(comment Eunuch "a male animal without testicles.")
(comment ExtensorDigitorum "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExtensorDigitorum #$Muscle. The #$ExtensorDigitorum extends the four fingers at the #$MetaCarpoPhalangealJoint.  It divides into four major #$Tendons on the dorsal side of the #$Hand.  If the muscle contracts beyond finger extension, it will (hyper)extend the #$Wrist.")
(comment ShavingCream "Generic shaving cream, including creams, foams, and gels")
(comment RenalVein "The collection of all renal #$Veins.  The left and right  #$RenalVeins drain the #$Kidneys and connect to the #$InferiorVenaCava at their proximal ends.")
(comment FetaCheese "This is the collection of all instances of Feta. 

The original Greek feta is a sheep's milk cheese that is kept in brine.

Other sorts of feta may be made of cow's milk or goat's milk. All varieties

are crumbly and salty.")
(comment ConveyorBelt "a device with one or more flat moving belts upon which items can be placed, to move them to a place along the belt.  Often the production area of a manufacturing company will have conveyor belts to move the product around as it is being assembled, packaged, etc. ")
(comment VideoClip "The collection of all #$VideoRecordedObjects the playings of which have a short duration, and which are typically recordings (or encodings) of portions of a longer sequence of moving images that are recorded or encoded in some other #$VideoRecordedObject. Examples include a #$VideoTape on which a short segment of #$Jaws-TheMovie is recorded, a #$VideoTape on which a robbery is recorded, and #$MPEGFile on which a portion of #$MusicVideo has been encoded. #$VideoClips which have acompanying audio portions are also #$AudioRecordedObjects (but not #$AudioClips). In some microtheories we may wish to make #$VideoClip a spec of #$AudioRecordedObject.")
(comment Snout-Animal "The part of the face of some animals that juts out; the nose and mouth are located there.")
(disjointWith Building GunTurret)
(comment PollenFn "#$PollenFn is a Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction, which is used to denote the various natural kinds of pollen.  #$PollenFn takes a single plant collection as its argument and returns the collection of pollen of that type of plant.  (#$PollenFn PLANTTYPE) denotes the collection of all portions of pollen from the elements of PLANTTYPE.  Examples: (#$PollenFn #$Ragweed) denotes the collection of portions of ragweed pollen, which afflicts sufferers of hay fever.")
(comment NewCaledoniaTerritoryPerson "A person who is a #$NewCaledonia-Territory #$citizens, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AutomobileAudioEquipment "The subcollection of #$AudioEquipment instances of  which are designed to be used in an #$Automobile.")
(comment OtomianLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of Mexico and/or Central America")
(comment BlowDryer "The collection of blow dryers -- hand-held devices which dry hair by directing a stream of warm air onto it.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent VisualArtActivity)
(comment ConceptualSynthesis "The collection of synthesis events where two or more ideas or concepts are brought together to form a new concept or idea.  Instances of #$ConceptualSynthesis are often subevents in the creation of instances of #$DevisedPracticeOrWork.")
(comment SportsGameProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerGameProgram that are simulated versions of sports games like baseball or basketball. Instances are game titles such as 'Triple Play' or 'Madden '99'.")
(comment OrganizationalTransfer "A specialization of #$PurposefulAction.  Each instance of #$OrganizationalTransfer is an event in which an #$IntelligentAgent changes membership with respect to an #$Organization.  So instances of #$OrganizationalTransfer include a particular person's becoming a
member of some organization, ceasing to be a member of some organization, or switching from one organization to another.  Instances of #$OrganizationalTransfer may be voluntarily undertaken by the transferee, but they may also be done by some other agent (perhaps against the transferee's will).  Notable specializations of #$OrganizationalTransfer include #$EmployeeHiring, #$EmploymentTermination, and #$GraduatingEvent.")
(comment Gaff-BoatPart "The spar on which the head (aka top) of a fore-and-aft sail is extended.")
(comment CalanProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by C.D. Searle.")
(comment SatisfyingAnUrge "The event in which a physical urge is satisfied.")
(comment Pleura "The collection of (left or right) pleurae, or enclosing sheath membranes, in  the #$ChestCavity of the #$Chest-BodyPart, including, but not limited  to, the #$VisceralPleura and #$ParietalPleura, which together form the #$PleuralCavity.  Each Pleura is a sac doubly wrapped around a #$Lung, the inner or visceral part being attached to the lung, and the outer or parietal part being attached to the walls of the #$ChestCavity.")
(comment OliveOil "Oil pressed from the dried fruit of the olive tree.")
(comment InterestPaymentFn "`(#$InterestPaymentFn AGENT LOAN PERIOD)' denotes the possibly iterative #$Paying performed by AGENT of interest on LOAN during the period PERIOD .")
(comment ComparisonPredicate "#$ComparisonPredicates are predicates used to represent comparisons between things. Although the distinction between relationships that compare and those that do not is not a sharp one, there are a large number of cases where people would agree that things are being compared when they stand in such-and-such relations, and there are a large number of cases where people would agree that things are not being compared when they stand in thus-and-so other relations. For example, GAFs using #$similarTo in arg0 represent a comparison between the things in arg1 and arg2, whereas GAFs using #$doneBy do not represent a comparison between the things in arg1 and arg2. One use for this distinction might be to narrow the range of appropriate predicates used to parse expressions such as '<type> is ____er than <type>'. An important subcollection is #$ComparisonWRTPredicate.")
(comment FireTruck "Truck which are used to extinguish fire in  fire outbreak cases.")
(comment Advertisement-PCW "The collection of #$ConceptualWorks of advertisements.  This includes advertisements for objects to sell, offers to buy, items to rent, give-away items, announcements of events, promotions for causes, personal ads, announcements of available jobs or availability for employment, etc.  For physical items instantiating such advertisements see #$Advertisement-IBT.")
(comment Heel "The back area on the bottom of a foot")
(disjointWith Corkscrew WritingImplement)
(comment MustangHorse "The collection #$MustangHorse represents the breed (really a mixture of a number of breeds) of feral horses living in the western UnitedStates.")
(comment CzechRepublicPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of the #$CzechRepublic, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization)
(comment BabyMonitor "A #$BabyMonitor is a device that a caretaker of a #$HumanInfant or #$HumanToddler might use.  Generally, one part (the transmitting end) goes in the baby's room, and the other part (the receiving end) goes in the caretaker's room.  If the baby begins #$Crying, #$Screaming, or otherwise audibly expressing distress, the caretaker can hear it on his or her end of the #$BabyMonitor will know to tend to the baby.")
(comment Crowbar "A hand tool used for prying large objects.")
(comment FictionalThing "The collection of all objects that are #$TemporalThings (beings, magical artifacts, spells, etc.) in fictional works but not extant in the world modeled by the KB in which something is asserted to be an instance of this.  This collection should have no instances in #$BaseKB or other general microtheories, but be restricted to microtheories dealing with the \"real world\" or some fictional world.  Note that instances of #$FictionalContext or stories about #$FictionalThings are not themselves #$FictionalThings, unless they are only defined as existing in some #$FictionalContext.")
(comment PulmonaryArtery-Main "The collection of all main pulmonary arteries.  A #$PulmonaryArtery-Main carries #$DeoxygenatedBlood from the #$PulmonaryTrunk to a #$Lung.")
(comment Lettuce-Foodstuff "Lettuce in edible forms. For example, a lettuce leaf on a sandwich, or torn lettuce in a salad.")
(comment HumanRightsOrganization "A collection of organizations; a subset of #$HumanitarianOrganization.  Instances of #$HumanRightsOrganization have as their main ends the dissemination of information about, and the protection of, human rights.  Human rights organizations are concerned with legal rights or what they consider should be legal rights of persons to freedom of speech and association, and to due process and equal treatment under law.  Such organizations may have international or local scope.  Examples include #$AmnestyInternational and the #$SouthernPovertyLawCenter.  Non-examples include #$Oxfam or #$DoctorsWithoutBorders that food or medical care are human `rights'. Cf. #$HumanitarianOrganization, broadly considered.")
(comment differsOnlyInArg "A ternary predicate that relates an instance of non-negative integer (representing an argument position) to two instances of CycL formula.  (#$differsOnlyInArg FORMULA-1 FORMULA-2 N) means that FORMULA-1 and  FORMULA-2 are the same length, that the arguments in every argument position (including 0, when N is not equal to 0) other than the Nth are the same in the two formulas, and that the two formulas differ in the Nth argument position. For example, the sentence `(#$differsOnlyInArg (#$genls #$Dog #$Mammal) (#$genls #$Cat #$Mammal) 1)' holds. Note that #$differsOnlyInArg's first and second argument-places are both \"quoted\" (see #$quotedArgument); thus in the context of the above #$differsOnlyInArg sentence the constituent sentence `(#$genls #$Dog #$Mammal)' denotes _itself_ and similarly for the constituent sentence `(#$genls #$Cat #$Mammal)'.")
(comment MetallurgicalGoods "The collection of pieces of metal sold for use in construction of other objects.  Included are sheet metal, metal rods and mesh, extruded wire, and metal pipes.  Insulated wire, nails, bolts, keys, paper clips, or other metal objects meant for end use are not instances of this collection.")
(comment VCDPlayer-Software "The collection of #$MultimediaPrograms designed to display movies on video CDs (VCDs) on the screen.")
(comment MagneticTape "Magnetic tape used to store information; used in #$AudioCassette and #$VideoCassette.  This is a collection of the stuff itself, not a packaging of it.")
(comment AnimalBodyGas "The collection of all pieces of #$GaseousTangibleThing that is generated inside the #$DigestiveSystems of #$Animals as a byproduct of some #$DigestionEvent (and eventually emitted from their bodies).")
(disjointWith ChangingDeviceState BiologicalEvent)
(comment VenetianBlind "The collection of blinds which have horizontal slats that can be set to different angles to allow light to come in.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterQ "The capital letter 'Q'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$Q-TheLetter, and #$LatinSmallLetterQ.")
(comment HotTub "Intermediate between #$BathTub's and #$SwimmingPool's.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess AthleticActivity)
(comment Sheepskin "The collection of instances of #$Leather made out of the tanned hides of #$Sheep.")
(comment OldWorldPolecat "A species in the Weasel Family (#$Mustelidae), native to northern Eurasia and northern Africa. #$OldWorldPolecats are nocturnal, and feed on small animals and eggs. Domesticated varieties used for hunting are called 'ferrets'.")
(comment loggedInAsOn "(#$loggedInAsOn AGENT ACCOUNT COMPUTER) means that AGENT is logged on to COMPUTER as ACCOUNT.  Note that AGENT might be logged into a computer under a certain account but not #$knowsLoginInformationForAccount.")
(comment WashBasin-PartOfSink "The bowl-shaped part of a sink")
(comment VentralRamusT11 "The collection of all T11 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT11 and #$DorsalRamusT11 branch from SpinalRootT11.  #$VentralRamusT11 supplies below the #$EleventhRib.")
(comment ElNino-WeatherEvent "Instances of this collection are global weather events lasting several            months to a year. It occurs every 3 to 7 years, and involves changes            in trade winds and warming of surface temperatures of the pacific off            the coast of Peru.")
(comment PowerUserAccount "A type of account on instances of #$NTWorkstation.  The #$PowerUserAccount combines the privileges of  #$AccountOperatorAccount, #$ServerOperatorAccount, and #$PrintOperatorAccount on the NT server.")
(comment Clostridiaceae-Family "A collection of #$Bacterium. A #$BiologicalFamily formed in the
#$MoneraKingdom.  This family contains #$Clostridium-Genus.")
(comment laterProgramVersions "(#$laterProgramVersions OLD NEW) means that NEW is a later version of OLD.  For example, MSWord3.1 is a followingVersion of          MSWord3.0 and MSWord2.0, but not #$MSWord.          The later version is assumed to be backwards compatible          with all previous versions.")
(comment Ramp "A sloping path along a solid.")
(comment carbonSourceOf "(#$carbonSourceOf BACTERIUM SOURCE) relates instances of #$Bacterium to their carbon sources SOURCE.  See also #$hasCarbonSourceType.")
(comment AudioClipOfWorkFn "(#$AudioClipOfWorkFn AUDIOWORK) denotes the collection of all #$AudioClips in which a segment of the #$AudioConceptualWork AUDIOWORK has been recorded. For example, (#$AudioClipOfWorkFn #$LittleGTO) denotes a collection including audio tapes and computer files in which a segment of the song Little GTO has been recorded.")
(comment directlyServesBodyParts "(#$directlyServesBodyParts PARTA PARTB) means that the #$Organ, system segment, or part PARTA directly provides a  biologically useful or necessary service to organ, system segment, or  part PARTB (both being #$anatomicalParts of the same #$Organism-Whole).  Examples: the  #$SplenicArtery serves the #$Spleen (as blood supply), the JugularVeins drain the #$Head-Vertebrate, the left  #$SuperiorLobarBronchus supplies air to the left #$SuperiorLobeOfLung,  the #$SciaticNerve innervates the leg, etc.  Part of PARTA joins and  is #$connectedTo part of PARTB.  This does not refer to general or  indirect serving: not, for example, the case of the #$Liver being  needed for all body parts, etc., nor the case that the #$SpinalCord  serves the left little toe, etc.  This predicate applies only to the final part of the supply system supplying just the target PARTB and no other target parts; it does not apply to all of the 'upstream' links of a supply system.")
(comment HepaticaeClass "A biological class within the plant kingdom which includes the liverworts.")
(comment UgandanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Uganda, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment GiftSet "The collection of gift sets. A gift set is a set of

instances of some product type, such as cheese or cosmetics, packaged 

together and intended to be given as a gift.")
(comment AustronesianLanguageFamily "indigenous languages of most islands of the Pacific.")
(comment PlaySuit "The typical jumper-style playsuit worn by infants.")
(disjointWith SportsAction WeddingEvent-Generic)
(comment PushingSomeone "The set of actions in which a person moves another person away from him/herself, by applying force generated by his/her own muscles or weight.")
(comment TelephoneCompany "The collection of companies that provide telephone service; they do not necessarily either manufacture or sell telephones.")
(comment AfterShaveLotion "Generic shaving lotion.")
(disjointWith RespiratorySystem ExtrudedBodyPart)
(comment ExternalAuditoryMeatus "The collection of all ear canals.  Each #$ExternalAuditoryMeatus (or 'ear canal' is a tube from outside the body to the #$Eardrum.  Medical names for ear canals include 'auditory canal' and 'auditory meatus'.  An #$ExternalAuditoryMeatus is considered to be part of the #$ExternalEar as it is external to the #$Eardrum.")
(comment Shotgun "The collection of all shotguns. Disjoint with #$Rifle. Unlike rifles,

shotguns have smooth bores and are designed to fire clusters of small

lead pellets, or shot. As a hunting weapon, they are primarily used for

small fast moving targets, such as birds and rabbits. They are also

useful in close-quarters combat situations.")
(disjointWith SymmetricAnatomicalPartType UniqueAnatomicalPartType)
(comment QuicktimeFile "The collection of #$ComputerFile-AISs encoded in the Quicktime format. #$QuicktimeFiles are either #$ComputerVideoFiles or #$ComputerSoundFiles.")
(comment AutomobileSeat "The things you sit on in your car, not a childscarseat.")
(disjointWith DescendingEvent AscendingEvent)
(comment EnteringInfoIntoComputer "Collection of events where information is being added into a computer system.")
(comment Gill "Organ used for breathing under water by fish and some amphibians. This unit refers to the entire assembly, not a single gill slit.")
(comment FireAlarm "A collection of objects; a subset of #$AlarmDevice.  Every instance of #$FireAlarm can emit an #$AlarmSignal signifying the presence of fire, i.e. #$CombustionProcess. It may do this automatically, e.g. by detecting smoke or rising temperature; or it may be manually activated.")
(comment ItalianGreyhound "A collection of small to medium-sized dogs.")
(comment Viscount "The collection of all viscounts, or male persons who hold hereditary viscount titles in the systems of nobility of Europe, or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf. See also #$Viscountess.")
(comment AutoCamper "The collection of all removable constructions with windows designed and used to put on the back of a truck to provide shelter for people.")
(comment Iliacus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Iliacus #$Muscle.  The #$Iliacus connects the #$Ilium to the #$Femur.  Together with the #$PsoasMajor it forms the IlioPsoas #$Muscle which is the strongest flexor of the #$Hip.  The IlioPsoas is, for example, the main #$Muscle involved in doing a sit up.")
(comment LampBase "The supporting part of a lamp.")
(disjointWith Teaching SportsCompetition)
(comment LemonJuice "The juice of (#$FruitFn #$LemonTree).")
(comment AudioVideoStore "Stores that sell audio and video electronic devices.  They also often sell supplies for these things, but seldom sell recorded sound or video products.")
(comment DemonstrationProgram "Software that is in the incomplete, demonstration stage.  #$DemonstrationPrograms usually do not have full functionality or stability and are designed to test certain aspects of the software.")
(comment Drum-Container " A drum is a container which can typically contain between 12 and 110 gallons of liquid stuff.")
(disjointWith CreditCard PrepaidTelephoneCard)
(comment InstructionsForGettingFn "#$InstructionsForGettingFn takes as argument any spec of #$SomethingExisting and returns the collection of all instructions for getting things of that type.  For example, (#$InstructionsForGettingFn #$Loan-WrittenLegalAgreement) returns the collection of all instructions for getting a loan.  For acquisitions that generally cost, use #$InstructionsForPurchasingFn.")
(comment HairMobFn "(#$HairMobFn MAMMALTYPE) returns the collection of instances of #$MobOfHair-Mammal belonging to instances of MAMMALTYPE.  E.g., (#$HairMobFn #$Raccoon) is the collection of #$Raccoon hair, or more properly, the collection of all #$Raccoon hair-mobs.")
(comment CharacterGeneratorProgram "#$CharacterGeneratorProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that typically listen on port 19.")
(comment ProjectileShell-SeparateLoading "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is loaded in a  separate fashion projectile, and fuze.  The four components are issued separately.  Upon  preparation for firing, the projectile and propellant are loaded into the #$Gun in two separate operations.")
(comment CloseAngleBracket-TheSymbol "The symbol '>' used as a text delimiter. Usually used with an #$OpenAngleBracket-TheSymbol.  This refers to the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract), not to any physical instantiation.")
(comment StairRail "A guard and support running along a flight of stairs.")
(comment InterringSomething "The event in which human (or animal) remains and possibly their accoutrements are buried in the earth or sealed in a tomb.")
(comment interArgNotGenl1-2 "(#$interArgNotGenl1-2 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when a spec of COL1 appears as the first argument to PRED, the second argument in that assertion is constrained to not be a spec of COL2 and vice versa.")
(comment ComputerGraphicsBoard "An expansion board that plugs into a desktop

             computer that converts the images created in the

             computer to the electronic signals required by the

             monitor. It determines the maximum resolution,

             maximum refresh rate and the number of colors

             that can be sent to the monitor. The monitor must

             be equally capable of handling its highest

             resolution and refresh.")
(comment FuelTankTruck "The collection of trucks intended for use to transport fuel.")
(comment sees "(#$sees AGENT OBJECT) means that the #$PerceptualAgent AGENT perceives the #$SpatialThing-Localized OBJECT via the sense of sight.  (#$sees AGENT OBJECT) implies that AGENT is sensuously aware of at least some of OBJECT's visible properties, such as its color, shape, or texture.")
(comment VentralRamusT10 "The collection of all T10 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT10 and #$DorsalRamusT10 branch from SpinalRootT10.  #$VentralRamusT10 supplies below the #$TenthRib.")
(comment DriedFish "The collection of all instances dried fish intentionally dried and           intended for consumption.")
(comment ProgramFault "#$ProgramFault denotes the most general fault of computer software that leads to vulnerabilities in computers running that software.  Only extremely rarely would one assert simply that a program has this attribute, because such an assertion would amount to saying merely that a program has some unspecified flaw that could cause computers to be vulnerable to some unspecified threat.  In general it is better to assert that a program has a much more specific fault.")
(comment soleFunction "A specialization of #$primaryFunction

(q.v.) that is used to specify the sole primary or most important 

function that a given object serves.  

(#$soleFunction OBJ SITTYPE ROLE) means that the single primary 

function of OBJ is to play ROLE in situations of the type SITTYPE.  

OBJ might be a natural object that has a sole primary function 

(e.g. pumping blood is arguably the sole primary function of a heart),

or OBJ might be an artifact that was intentionally designed to have 

the sole primary function that it does (e.g. the sole primary

function of a flyswatter is to swat flying insects).  For

cases of the latter sort, consider the more specialized predicate

#$intendedSoleFunction.  For things that have, or might have,

more than one primary function, consider the more general predicate

#$primaryFunction.")
(comment MiniDisc "A disc based digital medium for recording and distributing consumer audio that is ``near CD'' (cf. #$CompactDisc-Audio) in quality.")
(comment BiologicalAgentStuff "A specialization of #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance.  Instances are biologically harmful substances, including both microorganisms and toxins produced by organisms (See #$BiologicalToxins).  Every biological weapon has as its basis some type of #$BiologicalAgentStuff (See #$BiologicalWeapon, #$BiologicalAgentType, and #$weaponBasisObjectType).")
(comment ComputerServer "A specialization of #$Computer. Each instance of this collection provides some service for other computers connected to it via a #$ComputerNetwork, by running instances of #$ServerProgram.")
(comment CastForBrokenBone "Used to be made of plaster, now there are other lighter, more durable materials.")
(comment BlueBook-SocialRegistry "A collection of directories, generally of famous people.")
(comment BloodVessel "Tubular animal tissue which acts as a conduit for blood")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice FoodUtensil)
(comment HickoryTree "Hickory trees provide timber and produce nuts.  Their leaves turn yellow in the fall.")
(comment TaiwanesePerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment OrganizationTypeByClients "A collection of four collections, #$OrganizationWithClients, #$OrganizationWithoutClients, and two specializations of the former #$OrganizationWithBusinessClients, and #$OrganizationWithIndividualClients.  The #$Organizations that are instances of the collections which are elements of #$OrganizationTypeByClients are distinguished by the types of clients they serve or by their lack of clients (clients being used here in the sense of #$clients).  Clients are not necessarily members of an Organization (see #$groupMembers); although members of an #$Organization may also be clients of that #$Organization (an employee of a #$Hospital may also be a patient of the #$Hospital), a client of an #$Organization need not be a member.  University students are both #$clients and members of a university.")
(comment NaturalGasPoweredDevice "The collection of devices which are powered by #$NaturalGas.")
(comment accountLoggedInOn "(#$accountLoggedInOn ACCOUNT SYSTEM) means that the instance of #$UserAccount, ACCOUNT, is logged in to the instance of #$AccountSystem, SYSTEM.")
(comment RefrigeratedDisplayCase "The big open case in a grocery store that contains Meat, Egg, etc.")
(disjointWith ProgrammingAComputer MedicalCareEvent)
(disjointWith Pincer Limb-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment FrenchFry "The collection of french fries.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization ProfessionalOffice)
(comment SportsTeam "#$SportsTeam is specialization of #$Team and #$SportsOrganization.  Each instance of #$SportsTeam is a group of people who regularly play on one team during (more-or-less frequent) team sports games.  A sports team may be a commercial, professional team supported by a large full-time staff, or it may be semi-pro or amateur.  Only #$Athletes are members of the team itself; staff would belong to a related team organization.  Examples of #$SportsTeam include: #$PittsburghSteelers, #$PittsburghPirates, #$PittsburghPenguins.")
(comment Cannabis "A #$BiologicalGenus of #$Plants within the #$HempFamily, with #$taxonMembers including the #$BiologicalSpecies #$HempPlant.")
(disjointWith SheetOfPaper StationarySign)
(comment Sleeping "The collection of all #$Sleeping events, i.e., natural processes in which an #$Animal engages in some unconscious mental activity coupled with physical rest.  #$Sleeping is a subcollection of #$BodilyFunctionEvent-Involuntary; the process of #$Sleeping is essential for the health of sentient animals.")
(comment TowelRack "The sort of rack that is intended for towels to hang on.")
(disjointWith TimeOfDayType DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType)
(comment Vise "A device used to hold an object in a certain position such that it doesn't move while it is acted on.")
(disjointWith IntrinsicStateChangeEvent ArrangingObjects)
(comment AuditorySystem "The collection of all animals' auditory systems.  An #$AuditorySystem is a system of organs and appurtenant body parts (such as ears) which enable the animal to perform #$Hearing actions.  
Note: Necessary parts of the process other than body parts --- e.g., a medium through which the sound waves get to the animal --- are not considered part of the animal's #$AuditorySystem.")
(comment hasPartCount "(#$hasPartCount OBJ PART-TYPE INT) means that INT is the number of parts of type PART-TYPE that object OBJ has. For example (#$hasPartCount BookCW001 #$Chapter-PCW 15) says that BookCW001 has fifteen chapters.  To talk about physical parts, use the more specific #$hasPhysicalPartCount.")
(comment Terrier-Lakeland "A collection of small dogs with hard, dense fur.")
(comment encryptedIn "(#$encryptedIn PIT IND) means that the #$PropositionalInformationThing PIT is \"contained\" in the #$Individual IND, but in encrypted form.  That is, PIT is not necessarily accessible to someone who has access to IND.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment SatelliteTVAntenna "The collection of all dish-shaped antennas for receiving television broadcast signals relayed via satellite. Includes both small 18-inch antennas and larger 'C-Band' antennas.")
(comment PeanutPlant "The plant that gives us the Peanut.")
(comment InfraSpinatus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$InfraSpinatus #$Muscle.  The #$InfraSpinatus #$Muscle lies on the dorsal side of the #$Scapula (caudal to the #$SupraSpinatus), connecting to the #$Humerus and is used for extension and lateral rotation of the #$Humerus.")
(comment WallPaper "The generic material called wallPaper")
(comment BasilicVein "The collection of all basilic #$Veins.  The #$BasilicVein runs the length of the #$Arm, connecting to the #$BrachialVein at its proximal end just below the #$Shoulder.")
(comment Edam-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Edam,

a Dutch cheese similar to #$Gouda-Cheese.")
(comment NetworkComparisonPredicate "The collection of all #$Predicates that are used for comparing one #$PathSystem with another.")
(comment OxygenMask "a thing worn over the nose and mouth to deliver oxygen to the person.  Used in oxygen therapy, and also used by pilots or others working at very high altitude where the oxygen concentration is not high enough for human comfort.")
(comment MusicVideo "The collection of all #$VideoConceptualWorks that are music videos.")
(comment Navel "the depression in the center of the surface of the abdomen in #$Persons and other placental mammals (cf. #$Eutheria) indicating the point of attachment of the #$UmbilicalCord to the #$Embryo")
(comment ElectronicDevice "#$ElectronicDevice is a specialization of #$ElectricalDevice.  Each instance of #$ElectronicDevice is a device that uses electronic circuitry; more specifically, a device in which electricity passes through a vacuum or semiconductor.  Notable specializations of #$ElectronicDevice include #$Telephone, #$VideoCamera, and #$Computer.")
(comment Iris "The collection of plants of the iris family; perennial plants with long, sword-shaped leaves and thick stalks bearing three-petaled flowers.")
(comment BermudaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Bermuda, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HomeAudioEquipment "The subcollection of #$AudioEquipment instances of which are designed to be used in the home.")
(comment Cocoon "Containers secreted by some insects in which they pupate.  A Chrysalis is secreted as a unit, not spun out of fibers as a coccoon is.")
(comment CaribanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in the Caribbean region and/or South America ")
(comment PhysicalSynthesis "The collection of #$CreationEvents where two or more instances of #$PartiallyTangible come together to form an instance of #$PartiallyTangible, which is the #$outputsCreated.")
(comment BackgammonProgram "A specialization of #$ComputerGameProgram. Each instance of #$BackgammonProgram is a program that can be used by someone to play #$Backgammon.")
(comment HighwayBus "A large, heavy, comfortable bus typically used for long-distance transport of passengers between cities by commercial carriers and/or tour companies.  Capacity up to 60 people.")
(comment CardizemProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by Hoechst Marion Roussel.")
(comment UrgeToVomit "The type of internal sensation or feeling of nausea.")
(comment LobeOfLung "The collection of major lobes of #$Lungs in  #$AirBreathingVertebrates.  A LobeOfLung is divided into #$SegmentOfLungs.  Each LobeOfLung is supplied by a single large #$BronchialTube (a  #$LobarBronchus) that divides into many others within the lobe.")
(comment PeanutOil "Oil pressed from the dried seeds of peanuts.")
(comment filedJointReturnWith "`(#$filedJointReturnWith YEAR PERSON1 PERSON2)' means that
PERSON1 and PERSON2 filed joint returns together for YEAR.")
(comment AutomobileDriveTrain "the powertrain layout for an automobile")
(comment Embryo "A specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject. Each instance of this collection is a not yet fully-formed organism -- such as a mammal before birth, a bird before hatching, and a plant before sprouting from its seed. (Thus note that #$Embryo does not correspond exactly with the meaning of the English word 'embryo'.)  Note also that in mammals the #$Embryo is not the same as the #$Fetus, since it includes all tissue that has decended from the fertilized #$Ovum, including the fetal part of the Placenta (#$Placenta-FetalPortion), the #$AmnioticSac, and the #$UmbilicalCord, as well as the #$Fetus.")
(comment Speedometer "Device used to measure the speed at which one is travelling")
(comment EncryptedCommunication "Communication acts which involve the transfer of an encrypted #$communicationToken.  There are additional subevents, that of #$Encrypting and that of #$Decrypting, not present in most #$Communicating.")
(comment PectoralMuscle "Chest muscle")
(disjointWith SolderingIron WritingImplement)
(comment Horse-ColdBlood "Certain horse breeds are called 'cold blood' breeds (and are therefore represented in Cyc as specializations of #$Horse-ColdBlood) because of their temperaments, not because of their body temperatures.  These are also called 'heavy breeds' because they tend to be large and stocky.  In addition, they are sometimes called 'draft horses' because they were primarily used for work such as pulling heavy equipment.  They are still used in this way in many parts of the world.")
(comment SanMarinoPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$SanMarino, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization)
(comment Rattle-Toy "The collection of all rattles that are used to entertain #$HumanInfants and #$HumanToddlers.")
(disjointWith CandyMaking MedicalCareEvent)
(comment PulmonaryArtery-Peripheral "The collection of all pulmonary arteries within #$Lungs.  This collection includes every #$PulmonaryArtery-Generic except the #$PulmonaryTrunk and the right and left #$PulmonaryArtery-Main.")
(comment Tomato-Foodstuff "Foodstuff from the edible fruit of tomato plants.")
(comment HumanitarianOrganization "The collection of organizations that have humanitarian purposes as their main ends.  These include organizations that provide tangible aid in the form of goods and services provided directly to those in need, organizations that work on behalf of those in need (e.g., by working with government organizations to develop assistance programs), and organizations whose aid mission is primarily one of advocacy on behalf of some particular group.  Examples include #$AmnestyInternational, #$DoctorsWithoutBorders, and the #$InternationalCommitteeOfTheRedCross.")
(comment ModemDriver "A piece of software which acts as an interface between a modem and an operating system.")
(comment Shears-GardeningTool "Heavy scissors used for trimming grass or small plants.  Not #$PruningShears.  These are operated with one hand.")
(comment SpringLoadedWindowShade "The collection of opaque spring loaded devices that may be pulled down in front of a window in order to block out sunlight, or prevent others from seeing in from outside.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterQ "The lowercase letter 'q'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$Q-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterQ.")
(comment SepticTank "Tank for holding sewage whilst bacteria feast upon it and render it less septic.")
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure AthleticActivity)
(disjointWith FourWheelDrive FrontWheelDrive)
(disjointWith ToothedWhale BaleenWhale)
(comment FogMachine "#$FogMachine is the collection of devices which are used to produce fog. This is often done in order to create a dramatic effect, in connection with some sort of #$EntertainmentEvent, e.g., at a halloween party, or during a DramaticPerformance that calls for a foggy scene.")
(comment DrinkingGlass "The collection of drinking glasses, a particular kind of vessel for consuming liquids")
(comment SupraScapularNerve "The collection of all suprascapular nerves.  The suprascapular nerve branches off of the #$SuperiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus.")
(comment Garlic "This is the collection of all instances of garlic. By garlic we mean

the part of the garlic plant that is used in cooking. Both heads of

garlic and garlic cloves (including portions thereof) are instances of

#$Garlic.")
(comment LeonidMeteorShower "The collection of all annual occurrences of the Leonid #$MeteorShowers, which take place around November 15 and appear to originate from a point in the #$Leo-Constellation.")
(comment PrintOperatorAccount "Print Operators can perform tasks related to printer management.")
(comment PygmyHippopotamus "A collection of #$Pachyderms similar to but smaller than the #$Hippopotamus native to #$Guinea, the #$IvoryCoast, #$Liberia, and #$SierraLeone.")
(comment dbmsOfDB "(#$dbmsOfDB A B) means that B is the database management program responsible for handling queries and updates to the physical database A.")
(comment Basket "container products, often bowl-shaped, which are woven out of some material (usually out of some kind of plant material like straw or wicker, although metal baskets do exist.) ")
(disjointWith AncientNavalShip ModernNavalShip)
(comment HungarianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Hungary, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment LawnFurniture "This is the collection of pieces of furniture that are indended to be

outside on a lawn, patio, or deck, at least during warm weather.")
(comment Famine "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DisasterEvent.  Each instance of #$Famine is an event taking place in a contiguous geographical area in which a lot of people are undergoing #$Starvation.")
(comment SemiticLanguageFamily "Many languages, both ancient and modern, spoken in southwest Asia and northwest Africa")
(comment MuffinPan "A pan used for baking muffins, with 6 to 12 little basins in it which hold the muffins.")
(comment JumpingHurdles "An activity where one leaps (#$Jumping) many times while running.  Usually there is an obstacle over which the hurdler is jumping.")
(comment CerealFood "A specialization of #$EdibleStuff and an instance of #$FoodGroup.  Each instance of #$CerealFood is food that consists of a significant amount of grain products, such as breads and cereals.  Note that #$CerealFood is not a specialization of #$VegetableMatter because some breads contain non-plant constituents such as salt.")
(comment GunType "A collection of gun types.")
(comment AutoBodyPart "Includes all the parts of a car which form its `skin' and are normally painted--the hood, the trunk, the door panels, the roof panel, the querterpanels, etc.")
(disjointWith SkeletalSystem WoolStuff)
(comment Gomphosis "A #$Gomphosis is the insertion of a process into a socket.  Not found in bones, but applies to the connection between teeth and jaws.")
(comment FlyingDisc "A disk-like object which is used for recreational activities.  When in use, it is thrown so that it spins about its axis.")
(comment Living "This is the most general script for what living things do throughout their existence.  This includes cells within organisms, as well as the organism as a whole.")
(comment InterpretedComputerLanguage "#$InterpretedComputerLanguage is the

collection of all instances of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage that are used to write

#$ComputerProgram-CWISs which are typically run with the use of

an #$Interpreter-Computers, as opposed to programming languages used to write

#$ComputerProgram-CWISs which are typically compiled into different languages and run as

machine code.")
(comment AutomotiveMirror "A mirror either inside or outside of a car.")
(disjointWith FluidFlowEvent Condensation)
(comment PurchaseOrderDocument "PurchasingAgents send PurchaseOrderDocuments to vendors, to place an order for a particular amount of a stock item at a particular price.  Frequently, a #$PurchasingAgent sends a PO after receiving an #$FormalEstimateDocument from the vendor, who received a #$QuoteRequestDocument from the #$PurchasingAgent, who might have received a #$PurchaseRequisitionDocument from an employee, who lived in the house that Jack built - er, I mean, who wanted the item ordered in the first place.")
(comment Kneecap "The bone which protects the knee; aka patella.")
(comment ExtractedSampleFn "A #$UnaryFunction that takes some instance of    #$ExistingStuffType and returns the collection of #$ExtractedSamples of that stuff.  For example,   (#$ExtractedSampleFn #$Blood) is the collection of   #$Blood samples.")
(comment IrishWolfhound "A collection of dogs.")
(comment HinduPerson "The collection of all persons who believe in (at least some of) the tenets of a Hindu cult, or who practice Hindu religious rituals, or both.")
(disjointWith JudicialOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment Harp-TheStringInstrument "A subset of #$StringInstrument.  Instances of this collection are large triangular instruments whose strings are plucked with the fingers.")
(comment Lion "The collection of large carnivorous feline mammals found in Africa.")
(comment GluteusMedius "The #$Collection of all instances of #$GluteusMedius #$Muscle.  The #$GluteusMedius rotates and abducts the #$Femur.  It stabilizes the #$Pelvis when standing on one foot.  The two #$GluteusMedius #$Muscles alternately contract in walking.  Paralysis of the #$GluteusMedius results in a distinctive limp.")
(comment CounterTop "The shelf-like construct usually found in a Kitchen on which a variety of small Kitchen appliances (like a toaster or microwave) rest.")
(disjointWith SportsCompetition InformationRecordingProcess)
(comment HypoPharynx "The collection of all hypopharynges.  Each #$HypoPharynx (or 'laryngopharynx') is the inferior section of a #$Pharynx, being located caudal to the #$OroPharynx, and branching into the #$Larynx and the #$Esophagus.")
(comment CreamOfRice "Processed rice that is boiled with water to make a hot breakfast cereal.")
(comment AccountingFirm "Commercial organizations which perform financial accounting services for their clients/customers.")
(comment Can "Cylindrical storage device often used to store food")
(disjointWith OfficialDocument SignTheDisplay)
(comment mainProduct "The predicate #$mainProduct is used to identify the main item in a particular group of items that a customer gets when buying a packaged product.  (#$mainProduct PACKAGED-PROD PROD) means that the particular #$Product PROD is the main item of the #$PackagedProduct PACKAGED-PROD--as distinct from the accessories, agreements, packaging, literature, etc., that come along with it.")
(comment eventAnalog "(eventAnalog EVENT-PRED OBJECT-PRED) means that EVENT-PRED
relates events to events in a way analogous to the way in which
OBJECT-PRED relates events to objects. For example, #$eventOutcomes
relates an event with situations that are the result of that event
while #$outputsCreated related an event with the objects that are the
result of that event so we might say (#$eventAnalog #$eventOutcomes
#$outputsCreated).")
(comment ProjectileShell-SpinStabilized "The collection of #$ProjectileShellAssembly that is spin-stabilized. Spinning is obtained by firing the projectiles through a rifled tube.   They perform very well at relatively low trajectories.  In high trajectory  applications they tend to overstabilize, maintain the angle  at which they were fired, and, therefore, do not follow the trajectory satisfactorly.")
(comment AquaticOrganism "A specialization of #$Organism-Whole.  Each specialization of #$AquaticOrganism is a type of organism adapted to life underwater, whose instances spend all or most of their time immersed in water.  A notable specialization of #$AquaticOrganism is #$Fish.")
(comment CloseCurlyBracket-TheSymbol "The symbol '}'. Usually used with an #$OpenCurlyBracket-TheSymbol. this is the abstract symbol (see #$Character-Abstract), not any physical instantiation.")
(comment LightSwitchOnWall "Specifically the light switch found on the wall of a room. Not the one on lights and lamps themselves.")
(comment interArgNotIsa "(#$interArgNotIsa PRED FIRST-ARG FIRST-COL SECOND-ARG SECOND-COL) means that, when an instance of FIRST-COL appears as argument # FIRST-ARG to PRED, argument # SECOND-ARG in that assertion is constrained not to be an instance of SECOND-COL and vice versa.")
(comment DitransitiveNP-PassiveParticipleFrame "This frame is used for words which take exactly two complements, an NP and a passive participle verb. In HPSG terms: [COMPS  <NP> <V[passive]>] Example: 'We had the house painted.'")
(comment CoastalEscortBoat "The collection of boats intended for use in a military context as escorts for other watercraft involved in a military operation.")
(disjointWith VisualPerception EcholocationPerception)
(comment VentralRamusC5 "The collection of all C5 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC5 and #$DorsalRamusC5 branch from SpinalRootC5.  #$VentralRamusC5 supplies the #$BrachialPlexus.")
(comment EdibleFish "The collection of #$Fish species that are commonly consumed by people (this is of course variable across cultures and individuals).  See (#$MeatFn #$EdibleFish) for the stuff that's actually consumed.--Davis, April 28, 1998")
(comment InputValidationFault "#$InputValidationFault is an  attribute of computer programs.  A program  has an #$InputValidationFault if its corresponding process fails to recognize syntactically incorrect input, accepts extraneous input fields, or fails to handle missing input.  This fault is exploited by sending malformed commands to a machine running a program with this sort of fault.  An important spec attribute of this fault is #$CommandExecutionFault.")
(comment AmmunitionBelt "Instances of #$AmmunitionBelt are belts that hold groups of projectiles (bullets, usually).  The belt is attached to an #$AutomaticFirearm-BeltFed. When the firearm is discharged, projectiles

are dislodged from the belt and projected from the weapon.  A mechanism in the weapon advances the belt so as to put another projectile in place.")
(comment ComputerCode "A specialization of #$ComputerAIS.  Each instance of #$ComputerCode is an abstract list of instructions expressed in some computer language (see #$ComputerLanguage) including executable binary code.")
(comment Bandage "The soft things that are used to cover and protect wounds.")
(comment Certificate-IBT "The collection of actual hardcopy (#$CertificateDocument) or electronic  (#$DigitalCertificate) instances of a certificate. Examples  include instances of #$Passport and #$BirthCertificate.")
(comment Rectum "The end of the large intestine where feces collects before defecating")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice MeasuringDevice)
(comment PomegranateTree "The collection of trees which yield pomegranate fruit. Their flowers are orange-red.  The fruit is the size of a large orange; within, it is divided into several chambers containing many vesicles of reddish juicy pulp, each surrounding a seed.")
(comment AscensionIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are native to or reside on #$AscensionIsland.")
(comment OrganizationWithBusinessClients "#$OrganizationWithBusinessClients is the specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$OrganizationWithBusinessClients is an #$Organization whose #$clients are primarily businesses or other #$Organizations, rather than individuals.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfListeningInterpreter "#$VulnerableBecauseOfListeningInterpreter is a specialization of
 #$ProgramConfigurationVulnerability.  It is a vulnerability of a computer
 that arises as a consequence of permitting an instance of #$Interpreter-Computers installed on a computer to be listening on an instance of #$NetworkPortNumber.")
(comment ToiletBrush "A long-handled brush used to scrub toilet bowls.")
(disjointWith Hand Limb-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment Food-ReadyToEat "A specialization of (#$FoodOrDrinkForFn #$Person). Each instance of #$Food-ReadyToEat is food that is edible more or less in its current state, without further elaborate preparation. Instances of #$Food-ReadyToEat can require unwrapping, cutting, pouring, buttering, or cooling before being consumed, but not cooking or other complex or sophisticated preparation that is typically done in a kitchen or other food-preparation area rather than at the table or site of consumption. If a cook would inspect an item and pronounce it \"done,\" that item is probably an instance of #$Food-ReadyToEat.")
(comment EmergencyVehicle "#$EmergencyVehicle is a specialization of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle.  Each instance of #$EmergencyVehicle is a vehicle, which is used for emergency and rescue situations.  These include instances of FireTrucks, Ambulances, and, etc.")
(disjointWith RetailOrganization ProfessionalOffice)
(comment Marker-WritingImplement "The collection of all markers used for writing and drawing, e.g., felt tip markers, dry erase markers, etc.")
(disjointWith WritingAComposition CommunicationAct-Single)
(comment fitnessLevel "The fitness level of an animal.")
(comment DiArthrodialJoint "A #$DiArthrodialJoint is a #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart in which the bones are #$looselyConnectedTo each other, i.e. so that motion can occur between them.")
(comment GroupTransferIn "A subcollection of #$GroupTransfer.
Instances of this collection are those
in which there is necessarily something
that becomes a #$groupMembers of some instance
of #$Group.
This is a very diverse subcollection of #$TransferIn,
including transfers into organizations, families
(e.g. adoption), systems of physical devices, teams
or anything represented as a subcollection of
#$Group in the Cyc ontology.  For further clarification
see the #$NoteAboutGroupTransfers.  See also
#$GroupTransferOut, #$toGroup and #$fromGroup.
You may also want to look at #$OrganizationalTransfer
and constants closely related to it.")
(comment AutoLuggageRack "luggage racks that go on top of cars")
(comment InhalingFn "A collection-forming function - takes a type of thing and returns the class of events in which instances of that thing are inhaled.")
(disjointWith UpperCaseLetter UncasedLetter)
(comment DrillBit "A part that when attached to a drill is used to drill holes in materials.")
(comment TakingABreath "#$subEvents are #$Inhaling-BreathingIn and #$Exhaling-BreathingOut; #$TakingABreath is part of #$Breathing.")
(comment Nose "Facial organ used in smelling and breathing")
(disjointWith RoomInAConstruction Chamber-GunPart)
(comment Terrier-KerryBlue "A collection of medium-sized dogs with soft, blue-gray coats.  Their young            have black coats until about 18 months.")
(comment SolidFood "This is the subcollection of #$Food that is normally in a #$Solid-StateOfMatter when eaten.")
(disjointWith TechnologyOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment SatelliteTVReceiver "The collection of all satellite television receivers. Instances are generally black boxes with remote controls that take as input a signal from a #$SatelliteTVAntenna, tune in a channel, and pass video and audio signals out to a #$TelevisionSet, #$Receiver-AudioComponent, etc.")
(comment AngoraRabbit "A domestic breed of #$Rabbit with long, fine

 hair.")
(comment TeresMinor "The #$Collection of all instances of #$TeresMinor #$Muscle.  The #$TeresMinor #$Muscle, located in the #$Shoulder, connects the #$Scapula to the #$Humerus and is used for extension andlateral rotation of the #$Humerus in conjunction with the #$InfraSpinatus and #$SupraSpinatus.")
(comment Crossbow "The set of all crossbows")
(comment BrachialVein "The collection of all brachial #$Veins.  A #$BrachialVein's proximal end connects to the #$AxillaryVein in the #$Shoulder.  The distal end of the #$BrachialVein #$branchesInto the #$UlnarVein and #$RadialVein in the #$Elbow.")
(comment Stake "A short shaft made of rigid material such as wood or metal, intended to be driven into the ground to secure something (a tent, an animal's leash).")
(comment typeOfBacteriumInCultureType "(#$typeOfBacteriumInCultureType CULTURETYPE BACTYPE) relates kinds of bacterial cultures CULTURETYPE to the kind of bacterium BACTYPE grown in that culture.")
(comment GettingAnErection "The collection of events in which erotic stimulation, either sensory or from memory, causes the corpora cavernosa of the #$Penis of a #$MaleAnimal to fill with blood, with the result that the #$Penis becomes rigid, erect, and enlarged. This state is generally a prerequisite to #$SexualCopulation or #$Ejaculating. (Cf. #$CorpusCavernosum.)")
(comment NewZealandPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$NewZealand, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HomeAudioEquipmentTypeByLevel "A collection with two instances that are themselves collections: #$HomeAudioSystemComponent and #$HomeAudioSystem; each of which is a collection of instances of #$HomeAudioEquipment. Instances of #$HomeAudioSystem have instances of #$HomeAudioSystemComponent as #$physicalParts, hence the two collections are disjoint and are considered to be a different 'level'.")
(comment Cocoon "Containers secreted by some insects in which they pupate.  Cocoons are spun out of fibers, or ``silk''.")
(comment ZapotecanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of Mexico and/or Central America")
(comment MeowingSound "The collection of meowing sounds made by #$DomesticCats.")
(disjointWith ConceptualSynthesis PhysicalSynthesis)
(comment MacroVirus "#$MacroVirus is the collection of all elements of #$ComputerVirus that utilize the macro capability of some application (see #$macroCapable). Also called Document Viruses.")
(comment PlasticFilm "The collection of all instances of plastic film")
(comment UrgeToUrinate "The type of internal sensation or urge to urinate.")
(comment LobarBronchus "The collection of lobar bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) in the  #$Lung, each of which supplies air to one #$LobeOfLung.  They branch  off of the main bronchi.")
(comment Tequila "A hard liquor from #$Mexico")
(comment FabricSoftener "Liquids or Powders added while washing in order to make thm softer. Dryer Sheets are a different thing, though they have the same end effect.")
(disjointWith LegalProceeding BiologicalEvent)
(comment FuelGauge "Device used to measure the amount of fuel that is remaining in a fuel tank")
(comment controlsIBO "'(#$controlsIBO AGENT IBO)' means that access to this information bearing object is under the control of this agent.")
(comment Toenail "Protective covering at the end of a toe")
(disjointWith WritingImplement Speculum)
(comment MaineCoonCat "The #$MaineCoonCat is a breed originating in the northern US. Members are large, stocky and have long hair. ")
(comment CzechoslovakianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Czechoslovakia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization Beauty-CosmeticsOrganization)
(comment GliderChair "The collection of all #$GliderChairs.  A #$GliderChair is a type of #$Chair-PieceOfFurniture which is similar to a #$RockingChair.  The difference is that a #$GliderChair's base stays firmly on the ground while the seat 'glides' back and forth.  This collection is an element of #$ChildrensFurnitureMarketCategory because #$GliderChairs are often found in #$Nursery-BabysRooms where they are used by mothers to nurse their babies.")
(comment PryingImplement "A hand-held thing that can be used for prying.")
(disjointWith TransportInvolvingADriver MedicalCareEvent)
(comment InferiorMesentericArtery "The collection of all inferior mesenteric arteries.  The #$InferiorMesentericArtery supplies the #$DescendingColon and the #$Rectum.  It branches off of the #$AbdominalAorta.")
(comment Cabbage-Foodstuff "Cabbage in any of its edible forms, whether raw or cooked, shredded or grated.")
(comment PoliticalInterestGroup "A collection of groups. Each element is a group formed to achieve political goals.")
(comment DecryptionProgram "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used to decrypt files.  #$Decrypting typically involves applying a complex 'one-way' mathematical function to the data to obtain the original raw data.")
(comment ProkaryoticCell "A specialization of #$SingleCellOrganism.  Each instance of #$ProkaryoticCell is a single-celled organism that lacks both a  nucleus and mitochondria. Notable specializations of #$ProkaryoticCell include #$Bacterium, #$MoneraKingdom, and #$BlueGreenAlgae.")
(comment AutomobileTypeByModel "A collection of collections, each element of #$AutomobileTypeByModel is a collection of automobiles - i.e., cars, light trucks, vans (see #$Automobile) - categorized by model. For example, the collection of Subaru Imprezas would be an element of this collection.")
(comment WindowShade "The collection of window coverings which pull down from above and are typically a contiguous sheet (rather than composed of many slats).")
(disjointWith Virus ProkaryoticCell)
(comment LatinCapitalLetterR "The capital letter 'R'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$R-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterR.")
(comment WaterFrontProperty "Land adjacent to a lake, river, or ocean.")
(disjointWith RearWheelDrive FrontWheelDrive)
(disjointWith CommercialOrganization GovernmentalOrganization)
(comment Dildo "The collection of artificial erect penises used for sexual gratification.")
(comment DrinkingVessel "Containers used to hold beverages for consumption.")
(comment VentralRamusC2 "The collection of all C2 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC2 and #$DorsalRamusC2 branch from SpinalRootC2.  #$VentralRamusC2 supplies the #$CervicalPlexus.")
(comment Pudding "This is the collection of all instances of pudding. By pudding we mean

the common-sense American notion of pudding. Plum pudding and many

dishes that are called pudding in Britian are not pudding in the present 

sense. Instances of #$Pudding are made of dairy products (generally milk

and eggs) and are generally thickened by something other than the eggs, such as 

flour, cornstarch, or tapioca.  ")
(comment LaNina-WeatherEvent "This is the collection of hemispheric weather phenomena

which generally follow an #$ElNino-WeatherEvent. La Nina is characterized by unusually cold

ocean temperatures in the Equatorial Pacific. It's effects are essentially opposite

those of an El Nino.")
(comment Reins "Reins are ropes tied to a bridle on a horse.  One usually leads a horse with the reins, and one usually holds the reins while riding a horse.")
(disjointWith FluidReservoir TransportationDevice-Vehicle)
(comment MusciClass "A biological class within the plant kingdom which includes the mosses.")
(comment ManxPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$IsleOfMan-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Tag-IBO "The collection of all tags. A tag is a small

card-like thing, usually attached to some other item with a string.

The purpose of a tag is to give a small amount of information about

the thing it's attached to.")
(comment Tibeto-BurmanLanguageFamily "Languages of cenntral and southeast Asia")
(comment CakePan "Pans in which cakes are baked.")
(comment ClubbingSomeone "To hit a person with a club-like object, often repeatedly.")
(comment HamburgerSandwich "A type of #$Sandwich consisting of a fried or broiled ground beef patty on a bun or roll.  Named, for some reason, after the #$CityOfHamburgGermany, hamburgers were probably first eaten in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.")
(comment All-TerrainVehicle "land-transportation vehicles designed to be able

  to function effectively off-road, on a variety of

  terrain.  Some vehicles (e.g., tanks) are designed

  to be significantly more effective at this than

  others (e.g., 4x4 recreational vehicles).")
(comment PoundingDrivingImplement "A hand-held thing that can be used to pound or drive (force) an object.")
(comment storageLifeInContainerType "(#$storageLifeInContainerType TYPE DURATION CONTAINER-TYPE) means that, other things being equal, instances of TYPE can be expected to retain their 'intended' capabilities for a period of DURATION when stored in instances of CONTAINER-TYPE.")
(comment distalTo "(#$distalTo OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 lies in the #$DistalDirection of OBJ-2, with respect to a reference point (see #$centralReferencePoint) within an object having an #$AnimalBodyShapeType (often, a #$Person) that they are located in.  This reference point is determined by the location of OBJ-1 and OBJ-2.  For example, if OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are in the #$CirculatorySystem, the #$Heart is the point of reference, so (#$distalTo FredsFemoralArtery FredsAorta) means that Fred's aorta lies between Fred's femoral artery and his heart (see #$betweenOnPath for the relevant sense of between).  Note that (#$distalTo OBJ-1 OBJ-2) implies that OBJ-2 is proximal to OBJ-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent \"proximal to\".  OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.")
(comment FalseRib "A #$FalseRib is not connected to the #$Sternum directly by #$CostalCartilage, but -- if not a #$FloatingRib -- is connected by #$CostalCartilage to other #$CostalCartilage which is directly or indirectly connected to #$The #$Sternum.")
(comment Perfume "A substance with a pleasing odor, used by people to make themselves or their surroundings smell nice.  Perfumes are usually mixtures of substances derived from plants and sometimes from animal products, and are often solutions of these things in alcohol-ethanol.")
(disjointWith BiologicalProcess WavePropagation)
(comment HomepageFn-TypeLevel "#$HomepageFn-TypeLevel takes as argument any #$Collection COLL and returns all instances of #$WorldWideWebHomePage-CW created or authorized by instances of COLL or their owners or representatives. For example, (#$HomepageFn-TypeLevel #$City) returns the collection of all homepages created or authorized by the representatives of some city, and (#$HomepageFn-TypeLevel #$BasketballPlayer) returns the collection of all homepages created or authorized by some basketball player. (#$JulieF 11/23/99)")
(comment EngineStarter "The device attached to a battery that starts the car engine rotating.")
(comment Explosion "A collection of events, and a specialization of #$EnergyConversionProcess and #$DecompositionProcess.  Each instance of #$Explosion is an event that involves a chaotic release of energy.  It is not exactly controlled, even in the best circumstances, though it may be contained and channelled to do useful work (such as within the cylinders of a car engine, or  when a hole is blasted for a backyard swimming pool.). Specializations of this collection include #$Deflagration, #$Detonation, #$NuclearExplosion and #$Supernova.")
(comment CoverLetter "A formal, usually short, letter included with (and on top of) other material in the same envelope/container and briefly giving the reasons the material is being sent and/or instructions or requests of what to do with it.")
(comment Pharynx "The collection of all pharynges.  Each instance of this collection is a unique part of the body, being the throat cavity between the #$Mouth and nasal passages on one side and #$Esophagus and #$Larynx on the other.  The #$Pharynx is a part of both the #$RespiratorySystem and the #$DigestiveSystem.")
(comment ExtractedSample "The collection of all samples of some  #$PartiallyTangible stuff, to be used for study.  The  result of any successful #$TakingASample.")
(comment IbizanHound "A collection of medium-sized to large dogs, an ancient breed.  They have two            types of coats: the smooth coat and the wire coat.")
(comment MethodistPerson "The collection of people who

 consider themselves to be adherents of the #$MethodistReligion,

 regardless of whether they really live by (or understand) 

 most Methodist principles.  As such, this collection

is designed to capture the 'common sense' notion of 'being

a Methodist,' and not the prescriptive sense that a devout

Methodist or a Methodist church leader might attach to the phrase.")
(disjointWith ProductDisplayOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment LiquidFuel "The collection of combustible substances used as fuel which are typically in a liquid state.  These substaces can all be used in an #$InternalCombustionEngine.")
(comment ReturnToVegetativeState "A subset of #$BiologicalDevelopmentEvent. In each instance of #$ReturnToVegetativeState, an instance of #$Spore-DormantBacterium returns to its #$VegetativeCell state.")
(comment ExternalIntercostalSeries "The #$Collection of all sets of #$ExternalIntercostal #$Muscle.  An #$ExternalIntercostalSeries is the series of #$ExternalIntercostal #$Muscles on one side of the body.")
(comment FanMechanism-Electrical "Electrical Fan Mechanism -- Just the electrical motor and fan blade apparatus")
(comment Lawsuit "The collection of legal conflicts in which an agent or group of agents pursues a court case against another agent or group of agents.  A law suit may be settled, dropped, dismissed, or go to trial.")
(comment Jejunum "The collection of all #$Jejunums.  Each instance of this collection is the central section of a #$SmallIntestine, which runs from the #$Duodenum to the #$Ilium.")
(comment CreamOfWheat "Processed wheat that is boiled with water to make a hot breakfast cereal.")
(comment BodyPiercingStudio "The collection of organizations which specialize in performing #$BodyPartPiercing as a service.")
(comment Vial " A vial is a small bottle used to contain liquids.  It has a cap on it which may have an opening where a syringe could be inserted to extract the liquid inside.")
(comment InstructionsForPurchasingFn "#$InstructionsForPurchasingFn takes as argument any spec of #$SomethingExisting and returns the collection of information or instructions for purchasing things of that type. For example, (#$InstructionsForPurchasingFn #$House-Modern) returns the collection of all information on how to buy a house.")
(disjointWith Head-AnimalBodyPart Skin)
(comment Napalm "A specialization of #$Mixture.  Each instance of #$Napalm is a portion of a #$Mixture of gasoline thickened with the aluminum soap of naphthenic and palmitic acids.  Napalm burns longer and at a higher temperature than gasoline that hasn't been altered.  This #$Mixture is used in warfare as an incendiary device, usually delivered via missile warheads or other projectile launchers where a small explosive charge scatters the flaming liquid.  Napalm's high viscosity and stickiness enable it to travel further when projected and to adhere to what it hits until it burns out.")
(comment NNTPServerProgram "#$NNTPServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$NetworkNewsTransferProtocol (NNTP), which traditionally operates over TCP, port 119. A UNIX user can type 'telnet hostname 119' and connect with an instance of #$NNTPServerProgram on hostname, if one is present.")
(comment AirBreathingVertebrate "#$AirBreathingVertebrate is a specialization of #$Vertebrate and an instance of #$OrganismClassificationType.  Each instance of #$AirBreathingVertebrate is a vertebrate that usually respires by breathing #$Air during adult life.  Includes individual #$Mammals, #$Birds, #$Reptiles, and most #$Amphibians.  Most #$AirBreathingVertebrates are #$TerrestrialOrganisms, but some #$AquaticOrganisms breathe air (#$Whales, etc.).  All #$AirBreathingVertebrates have #$Lungs and #$RespiratoryTracts.")
(comment CloseSquareBracket-TheSymbol "The symbol ']'. Usually used with an #$OpenSquareBracket-TheSymbol. This refers to the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract), not any particular physical instantiation.")
(comment Doorbell "The device found by outside doors which ring inside the building to indicate that someone is at the door.")
(comment InsecureFilesystemFault "A program has
 an #$InsecureFilesystemFault if a specially-formed input
 to that program will yield a copy of the filesystem to an
 unauthorized user.")
(comment ChessComputer "Computers specialized (either via software or hardware) to play chess.")
(comment CommandShip "The collection of military command ships.")
(comment MaleInfant "The collection of male infants, male children who are babies.")
(comment tastes "(#$tastes AGENT THING) means that AGENT perceives the  (partially) tangible object or physical event THING via the sense of taste.
Perceptual agents can taste certain objects (such as lollipops) as well as, arguably, certain events (such as the \"finish\" of a wine).")
(comment DorsalScapularNerve "The collection of all dorsal scapular #$Nerves.  A #$DorsalScapularNerve branches off of its side's #$VentralRamusC5 prior to its convergence into the superior trunk in the #$BrachialPlexus (#$SuperiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus).  The #$DorsalScapularNerve #$innervates the #$RhomboidMuscles.")
(comment GroundBeef "Cattle meat, ground.")
(comment ArbitraryCommandExecutionFault "#$ArbitraryCommandExecutionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW, and an important specialization of #$CommandExecutionFault.  A program has an #$ArbitraryCommandExecutionFault if an attacker can manipulate the program into executing code chosen by the attacker.  An attacker may exploit an #$ArbitraryCommandExecutionFault in a number of ways: by sending commands directly to the program in the form of a malicious format string containing embedded metacharacters, or by installing an executable which the program (perhaps during some future login session) later executes (see #$TrojanAccommodatingFault), or by writing an executable which is received by the vulnerable machine and which the faulty program then executes without taking proper security measures (see #$FileCommandExecutionFault).  The commands that can be thus executed are \"arbitrary\" in the sense that the attacker can execute any command at the privilege level of the program.  The fact that many programs with the fault run with elevated privileges is what makes this fault particularly dangerous.")
(comment DiagnosingAndRepairingSomething "A specialization of both #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent and #$HumanActivity.  Each instance of #$DiagnosingAndRepairingSomething is an event in which something is diagnosed and repaired.  Such events can range from fixing an instance of #$PhysicalDevice (q.v.) to killing pests that infest a place.  All instances of #$DiagnosingAndRepairingSomething involve an intrinsic change in the thing which undergoes repairs.  Note that a diagnosis action alone, or a repair action alone, would not be instances of this collection, although they could be sub-events of an instance of this collection.")
(comment AdultFemaleHuman "The collection of all women; i.e., #$HomoSapiens who are adult and female.")
(comment FileOperation "The collection of all operations performed on instances of #$ComputerFileCopy.  These are typically events such as copying, moving or in some other manner altering the contents or storage location of a file.")
(comment IntravenousEquipment "The equipment used to introduce fluids directly into a patient's bloodstream, typically over an extended period of time (as distinct from a one-time injection).  Usually has one or more bags of fluid, and may use a pump or just gravity to control the flow.")
(comment BlueBook-GovernmentDocument "A collection of government issued documents.  This collection includes both         registries and directories as well as documents containing other sorts of            information.")
(comment MouthPortal "This is the opening or the #$containsPortals of the #$Mouth that allows passage into the #$Mouth.  The #$MouthPortal of primates has a border which are #$Lip-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment ControlDevice "#$ControlDevice is a specialization of #$ControlStructure-Physical and #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$ControlDevice is a device whose #$primaryFunction is to control the behavior/functioning/properties of another thing (usually another instance of #$PhysicalDevice).  Obvious instances of #$ControlDevice include: the remote control for one's TV (an instance of #$RemoteControlDevice), the brake pedal on one's car (an instance of #$Pedal-ControlDevice), the light switch on one's bedroom wall (an instance of #$ElectricalSwitch); a less obvious instance of #$ControlDevice is #$HooverDam (an instance of #$Dam).")
(comment CarobTree "Individual carob trees.")
(comment ZimbabwePerson "This is the collection of people who are either #$citizens of #$Zimbabwe, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AccessoryFn-Activity "The expression `(#$AccessoryFn-Activity ACTIVITY)' denotes the collection of

accessories for the #$ScriptType ACTIVITY.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfListeningBrowserInterpreter "#$VulnerableBecauseOfListeningBrowserInterpreter is a specialization of

#$VulnerableBecauseOfBrowserConfiguration.  It is a vulnerability of a computer

that arises as a consequence of permitting a web browser on the

computer to use an instance of #$Interpreter-Computers as a helper

application.")
(comment HypodermicSyringe "The collection of hypodermic syringes.")
(comment AsexualHuman "The collection of people who are not sexually attracted to other people.")
(comment Digit-AnatomicalPart "A specialization of #$Appendage-AnimalBodyPart. Each instance of a #$Bird, #$Bat-Mammal, or other #$Vertebrate.")
(comment Preservative-Food "A specialization of #$FoodIngredientOnly.  Each instance of #$Preservative-Food is a substance which can be added to food to prevent spoilage.")
(disjointWith PoliticalOrganization ChamberOfCommerce)
(comment VehicleFuelTank "The fuel tank of a motor vehicle.")
(disjointWith TextEditing BiologicalEvent)
(comment AnimalPartRegionFunction "A collection of functions that map from an #$AnimalBodyRegion to another #$AnimalBodyRegion that is a subregion of the first and whose location is indicated by the direction.  For example, (#$DorsalRegionFn LIVER) yields as a result the part of LIVER closest to the backside of the organism that LIVER is a part of.")
(comment SmoothMuscle "The collection of all pieces of muscle tissue of the kind that constitutes muscles which perform involuntary physiological functions such as digestion and breathing.  Muscles of the smooth kind differ in structure from striated muscles.  Unlike elements of #$StriatedMuscle, an element of #$SmoothMuscle has no light and dark bands.")
(comment RackOfDishwasher "The racks in dishwashers that hold the things to be washed.")
(disjointWith UncasedLetter LowerCaseLetter)
(comment Die-TheTool "A device used to help cut out or form material.")
(comment TouringARegion "The collection of all events in which an instance of #$Tourist or (#$GroupFn #$Tourist) travel about a site, sometimes but not always in the presence of a #$TourGuide, learning certain salient features concerning the place's history.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement BuildingCleaningChore)
(comment OlfactorySystem "The collection of all animals' olfactory systems.  An #$OlfactorySystem is composed of body parts (such as the nose) of the animal, which together function so as to enable it to perform smelling actions.")
(comment Terrier-Irish "A collection of medium-sized dogs, with wiry coats.")
(disjointWith JudicialOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment ConsumerAudioVideoComponent "The collection of all #$ElectronicHouseholdAppliances that are sold to be components in a home audio or audio-video system. Instances of #$ConsumerAudioVideoComponent are generally black in color and of a fairly uniform size, so they are visually inconspicuous and can be installed in standard cabinets. They are generally connected to one another using patch cords.")
(comment Microorganism "A specialization of both #$MicroscopicScaleObject and #$Organism-Whole.  Each instance of #$Microorganism is an organism too small to be seen by humans without the aid of a microscope.  Notable specializations of #$Microorganism include #$Protozoan, #$Virus, and #$ProkaryoticCell.")
(comment ExtensorCarpiRadialis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExtensorCarpiRadialis #$Muscle.  The #$ExtensorCarpiRadialis is a set of three #$Muscles which extends the #$Wrist.  The Longus portion also abducts, while the Ulnaris portion adducts.")
(comment ArrowHead "The set of arrowHeads")
(comment CephalicVein "The collection of all cephalic #$Veins.  The #$CephalicVein runs the length of the #$Arm, with its proximal end connecting to the #$AxillaryVein in the #$Shoulder.")
(comment Champignon-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Champignon,

which, generically, is any cheese containing mushrooms. A well-known version is a German double creme cheese containing Bavarian mushrooms.")
(comment Crayon "Type of drawing supplies, usually used by children.  Every Crayon has a color; crayons come in boxes where each is a different color.  Crayons are made of wax.")
(comment ScreenShot "#$ScreenShot is the collection of screen shots -- that is, the collection of pictures of computer screens. This includes shots from computer games, screen savers . . . even the chaotic screens of HumanCyclists.")
(comment AnimalBodyPart-Female "The collection of all #$AnimalBodyParts that are generally found only on female animals. Any collection representing a type of body part that is generally found only on female animals should have this collection as a #$genls. For example, all instances of #$Breast and #$Uterus are instances of #$AnimalBodyPart-Female, and the collections #$Breast and #$Uterus are subsets of it. See also #$AnimalBodyPart-Male.")
(comment VanillaOrchid "Individual vanilla orchid plants; their cured unripe fruit (vanilla bean) yields vanillin, the spice.")
(comment BolivianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Bolivia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PackagedAudioHomeTheater "A subcollection of #$HomeAudioSystem. Instances of #$PackagedAudioHomeTheatre are on the expensive and physically large end. They typically have surround sound speakers and a logic processor for DVD")
(comment PupalContainer "The class of secreted containers that insects pupate in.")
(comment ChadLanguageFamily "Languages spoken near Lake Chad, central Africa, and in West Africa")
(comment ElectricHairCurler "A device for curling hair by heating it.")
(comment HonkingSound "The collection of honking sounds made by geese.")
(disjointWith ExchangeOfUserRights PhysicalSynthesis)
(comment ActionGameProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerGamePrograms whose successful play involves simulated killing or destruction in realtime. Instances are game titles such as 'Doom' or 'Quake'.")
(comment DairyEstablishment "The collection of establishments at which cows are milked and butter and cheese are made.")
(comment ElectronicDisplayDevice "Electronic devices used to display images.  E.g. CRTs and LCDs.")
(comment PlendilProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by Merck.")
(comment LevelOfThirst "The type of internal sensation or feeling of experiencing thirst.")
(comment HorizontalFissureOfLung "The collection of horizontally situated main fissures  (cracks or crevices) that each separate a right #$SuperiorLobeOfLung  from a #$MiddleLobeOfLung (instances of #$LobeOfLung).  A  HorizontalFissureOfLung is deep from the surface to near the HylumOfLung,  and runs horizontally from the middle anterior border of the lung  around the side to join the right #$ObliqueFissureOfLung near the  latter's posterior medial part.  In normal human beings only the right  lung has a #$HorizontalFissureOfLung.")
(comment ShinerBock "Dark beer brewed in Shiner, TX which is beloved by University of Texas students")
(comment relativesForUSTaxPurposes "(#$relativesForUSTaxPurposes RELATIVE TAXPAYER) means that 
RELATIVE is related to TAXPAYER in such a way that RELATIVE is not requred 
to cohabitate with TAXPAYER in order to pass the household or residence 
condition of the dependency test with respect to TAXPAYER.  
#$relativesForUSTaxPurposes is a #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate, so that if 
RELATIVE satisifies the household or residence condition vis-a-vis TAXPAYER, 
then TAXPAYER satisfies that condition vis-a-vis RELATIVE. As a general rule, 
two persons are related in the #$relativesForUSTaxPurposes relationship if 
one is the ancestor (through biology or adoption), step-child, 
step-parent, aunt, uncle, niece or nephew of the other, or if they are 
siblings (including step-siblings) or in-laws.  A spouse does 
not qualify as a #$relativesForUSTaxPurposes.  In some cases, the determination 
of whether an individual stands in the #$relativesForUSTaxPurposes to a 
married taxpayer depends on whether the taxpayer files a joint or a separate return.  
For example, the child of a sibling of the spouse of a married taxpayer who 
files a joint return satisifies the #$relativesForUSTaxPurposes condition.  
Conversely, if that taxpayer files a separate return, the  
#$relativesForUSTaxPurposes condition is satisfied only vis-a-vis the 
spouse.")
(comment RoadVehicleBody "The outside metal skin of a road vehicle.")
(comment HarvestingAPlant "A specialization of #$RemovingSomething-Translational.  Each instance of #$HarvestingAPlant is an event in which a plant is harvested.  Harvesting may involve separating some part of the plant and leaving the rest in place (e.g., when one harvests fruit from fruit trees), or it may involve removing the entire plant from its growing location (e.g., when one harvests carrots).")
(comment WaterTank " Usually a closed large container used to store water.")
(comment Dictionary "The collection of all dictionaries: works that contain information about words and their definitions.")
(comment Claw "Sharp, pointed protrusions at the end of the extremities of many animals")
(disjointWith WritingImplement Otoscope)
(comment BurmeseCat "Each #$BurmeseCat cat is a small, chocolate brown cat with a sleek short coat. ")
(comment SaoTomeAndPrincipePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$SaoTomeAndPrincipe, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment ActiveSonar-Device "The collection of devices used to navigate and locate objects in water.  Instances consist of a tranmitter which emits high-frequency sound waves through water and a receiver which measures the returning sound waves reflected from objects in the path of the sound waves.

 This type of sonar is often employed by #$Torpedos and not by #$Submarine-Military

 because usage of #$ActiveSonar-Device gives away ones position.")
(comment HumanBody "#$HumanBody is the collection of instances of #$WholeBody which are the bodies of #$HomoSapiens.")
(comment Fan-ElectricalAppliance "Electric Fan appliance usually used for cooling people")
(disjointWith Teaching MedicalCareEvent)
(comment CeliacTrunk "The collection of all celiac trunks.  Each #$CeliacTrunk is a very short #$Artery branching off of the #$AbdominalAorta which has the #$CommonHepaticArtery, #$LeftGastricArtery, and #$SplenicArtery as branches.  This is a unique part of a body.")
(comment Beet-Foodstuff "Foodstuff from the edible root of the beet plant.")
(comment IdeologicalOrganization "A collection of #$Organizations, each of which is guided in its actions primarily by an ideology or cause -- i.e., by something other than in its own self-interest or the self-interest of its members.  Elements of #$IdeologicalOrganization include organizations which seek to promote some religious or political agenda and organizations which pursue humanitarian ends.")
(comment PhysiologicalConditionType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$PhysiologicalConditionType is a specialization of  #$PhysiologicalCondition (q.v.), and thus a type of physiological state into which some organisms can enter.  Instances of #$PhysiologicalConditionType include  #$Cancer, #$PsychologicalAilment, #$Infection, and #$Malnutrition.")
(comment accessoryFor-Strict "(#$accessoryFor-Strict COLL1 COLL2) means that every instance of COLL1 is, by design, usable as an accessory for every instance of COLL2.  Note that this is considerably stronger than its #$genlPreds, #$accessoryFor.")
(comment BlindForWindow "The collection of window coverings which have many slats, either vertical or horizontal, rather than a single continuous sheet of cloth.")
(disjointWith Virus EukaryoticOrganism)
(comment LatinSmallLetterR "The lowercase letter 'r'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$R-TheLetter, and #$LatinCapitalLetterR.")
(comment accessoryFor "(#$accessoryFor ACCESSORY_TYPE DEVICE_TYPE) means that instances of ACCESSORY_TYPE are designed to be used either as parts of instances of DEVICE_TYPE or as devices to be used with or to help care for instances of DEVICE_TYPE.")
(disjointWith ResearchOrganization ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable)
(disjointWith Holiday AthleticActivity)
(disjointWith SpeciallyCharteredInstitution GovernmentalOrganization)
(comment OfficeFurniture "This is the collection of instances of #$FurniturePiece which are manufactured specifically for use in the work place.")
(comment DorsalRamusL5 "The collection of all L5 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiL5 and DorsalRamiL5 branch from SpinalRootL5.  DorsalRamiL5 supplies the ????.")
(comment Brownie-Food "This is the collection of brownies. Brownies are denser, moister, and chewier

than cakes. They are made with ingredients similar to those of cakes but

with less flour and more eggs and sugar. Though prototypical brownies are

chocolate flavored and colored, other sorts, such as butterscotch brownies

also count as #$Brownie-Food.")
(comment Wicker "used to make baskets and furniture - a type of cane.")
(comment reproducesByMeansOf "(#$reproducesByMeansOf MEANS ORG) relates an organism to its means of reproduction.")
(comment InstantiationOfAISFn "A function which takes as its argument an #$AbstractInformationStructure, AIS, and returns the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings which are physical instantiations of that AIS.  I.e., it returns the collection of all #$InformationBearingThings, ?IBT, such that (#$instantiationOfAIS ?IBT AIS).")
(comment Bryophyte "Those plants lacking vascular tissue.")
(comment TuvaluPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Tuvalu, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment LoginAuthenticator "The collection of all #$ComputerServers which serve as login authenticators for some #$AccountSystem.  Each #$LoginAuthenticator serves as the location of a #$PasswordFile (#$fileFoundOnComputer) which machines on the network access when checking user login information (viz., the #$Username and #$Password-Computer entered at the machine).")
(comment DisabilityAidEquipment "The collection of #$PhysicalDevices that assist people with disabilities

in overcoming those disabilities.")
(comment MundaLanguageFamily "Language of southeast Asia")
(comment PiePan "A circular pan used to bake pies in.")
(comment QuickBurstOfEnergy "Releasing a quick burst of energy, as when sprinting.")
(comment ManipulatingFoodOrDrink "A specialization of #$MaterialHandling. Each instance of this collection is an event which involves moving #$FoodOrDrink around, and doing things to it physically.  One example is moving food from plate to mouth (note that once the food has been placed in the mouth this particular event is over). Animals generally use paws or hands to manipulate food.  If the 'performer' is a machine (a self-standing electric mixer, for example, or a blender) hands aren't needed, except to prepare the machine to do the activity.")
(disjointWith Book-CW ComputerGameProgram)
(comment HotBeveragePot "Serving containers for hot beverages, such as tea or coffee.  This is distinct from a kettle, because it is not necessarily used for heating on a stove.")
(comment Opossum "Specifically the species of oppossum found in America, not any
of the other marsupials which are called Opossums or possums.")
(comment DarkFn "This function returns a dark version of color ARG1.")
(comment DistalDirection "The general direction away from the center of the body and toward the extremities, or away from some other central reference point, such as the #$Heart (for objects in the #$CirculatorySystem) or the #$Brain (for objects in the #$NervousSystem), in or near an object with #$AnimalBodyShapeType.  This is a #$VectorInterval comprising a roughly cone-shaped set of vectors; note that its direction is dependent both on the location and on the types of objects involved.")
(comment KneeJoint "The #$KneeJoint is a complex joint involving the articulation of each #$Condyle of the #$Femur (thigh bone) with the #$Tibia.")
(comment LiftingALeg "Lifting a leg. Part of the #$TakingAStep process.")
(comment CohabitationUnit "A specialization of #$Group.  Each instance of #$CohabitationUnit is a group of humans or other animals all living together in the same place at the same time, where the place in question may be a house, nest, warren, or other dwelling.  A notable specialization of #$CohabitationUnit is #$FamilyCohabitationUnit.")
(comment FullyAutomaticFirearm "A specialization of #$AutomaticFirearm.  Each instance of #$FullyAutomaticFirearm is a firearm that fires continuously when its trigger is pulled.")
(comment Monotreme "A specialization of #$TerrestrialOrganism, #$Mammal and #$OviparousAnimal. There are only three living monotremes, the duck-billed #$Platypus and two species of #$Echidna (or \"spiny anteaters\").  Instances of the order #$Monotreme are mammals, yet lay eggs from which young are hatched, have a cloaca (hence the name monotreme, Greek for \"one hole\"), have poison glands, lack functional teeth, and secrete milk in a \"mammary patch\" rather than through teats. Their range is limited to #$Australia and New Guinea.")
(comment OnlineListingsFn-Event "Denotes the web pages devoted to certain online events, such      as online #$Auction-Events, #$Conferences, etc.")
(comment DistributorCap "The thing attached to your spark plug wires in a car engine.")
(comment PurchaseRequisitionDocument "A collection of documents.  Each element of #$PurchaseRequisitionDocument is a text document sent within an organization, to a purchasing agent, in order to request that the organization purchase some particular item(s).  Such a document may require authorization by the requestor's superior before it is recognized as a legitimate request.")
(comment OpticNerve "The collection of all optic #$Nerves.  Each #$OpticNerve (paired in #$Vertebrates) #$innervates the #$Retina of an #$Eye  conducting visual stimuli to the #$Brain.  The #$OpticNerve is the second #$CranialNerve of a #$Vertebrate.")
(comment GreatDane "A collection of very large dogs, originally bred in Germany.")
(comment JewishPerson "The collection of all persons who consider themselves to be Jewish.  This may simply entail some sort of loose ethnic tie or allegiance, and does not necessarily imply belief in any of the tenets of Judaism or practice of Jewish rituals.")
(disjointWith ChamberOfCommerce HealthcareOrganization)
(comment LowRiderMotorcycle "The collection of #$Motorcycles which have been lowered such that the #$RoadVehicleBody is close to the ground.")
(comment Lynx "The collection of all lynxes.  A #$Lynx is either a small European wildcat (Lynx lynx) or a similar one from northern North America (Lynx canadensis), with tufted ears, a short #$Tail-BodyPart, and thick #$Fur.")
(comment PronatorQuadratus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$PronatorQuadratus #$Muscle. The #$PronatorQuadratus pronates the #$ForeArm.")
(disjointWith TakingCareOfSomething Vandalism)
(comment Duodenum "The collection of all #$Duodenums.  Each instance of this collection is the proximal section of a #$SmallIntestine, extending from the #$PyloricValve to the #$Jejunum.")
(comment Rice-Foodstuff "Foods consisting of rice; may be in the form of grains, rice flour, or other forms, so long as it is wholly or mainly rice.")
(comment BuyingOrganization "An organization whose main function is to buy things, i.e. conduct buying activities (shop, negotiate prices, ...). ")
(comment eMailSourceAddress "(#$eMailSourceAddress MSG ADDRESS) means that the #$EMailAddress ADDRESS is  the source address for an #$EMailMessage MSG.  Note that a single message has  exactly one source address, and that address can never be changed.  A message  with the same content but a different address is still a different instance  of #$EMailMessage (although the same instance of #$EMailMessageText might be  a part of it).")
(comment FlexibleContainer " A flexible container is one which can be easily deformed without negatively affecting its contents.")
(disjointWith Skin RespiratorySystem)
(comment PetroleumProduct-Refined "A specialization of #$PetroleumProduct.  Each instance of #$PetroleumProduct-Refined is petroleum that has been derived from (see #$derivedFrom) crude petroleum (see #$Petroleum-CrudeOil) in an event that is an instance of #$Refining (q.v.).")
(comment EukaryoticOrganism "#$EukaryoticOrganism is a specialization of #$Organism-Whole.  Each instance of #$EukaryoticOrganism is an organism (individual organism, not type of organism) composed of #$EukaryoticCells (cells which have mitochondria, other organelles, and nuclei containing chromosomes).")
(comment DividedBySign-TheSymbol "A sign which looks like a dash with one dot above it and one dot beneath it.")
(comment Furnace "An enclosed structure in which heat is produced, e.g a furnace in a building.")
(comment Minicomputer "Smallish multiple-user machine, like VAXes.")
(comment CargoHelicopter "The collection of #$Helicopters used for cargo transport.")
(comment VentralRamusT3 "The collection of all T3 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT3 and #$DorsalRamusT3 branch from SpinalRootT3.  #$VentralRamusT3 supplies below the #$ThirdRib.")
(comment BlackForestCake "The collection of #$BlackForestCakes, which are chocolate cakes, usually containing cherry liqueur or #$Rum and cherries, and frosted with whipped icing.")
(comment ProgramCrashingFault "#$ProgramCrashingFault is a fault of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if the program can be crashed either remotely or at the console.")
(comment AdultMaleHuman "A specialization of #$HumanAdult and #$MaleHuman.  Each instance of #$AdultMaleHuman is a man, i.e., an instance of #$HomoSapiens who is adult and male.")
(disjointWith MusclePoweredDevice ComputationalSystem)
(comment TeethRetainer "The device held in a patient's mouth to hold teeth in place, typically after braces have been used to relocate them.")
(comment immuneWithRespectToPathogen "(#$immuneWithRespectToPathogen ORG PATHOGEN) means that ORG, an instance of #$Organism-Whole, is #$Immune to #$Infections caused by pathogenic organisms of the type PATHOGEN. More precisely, ORG is said to be resistant, or insusceptible, to toxic molecules, microorganisms and/or foreign cells of the specified type.")
(comment Calligraphy-ArtObject "The collection of art objects whose focus is the display of
ornamental handwriting.")
(comment LycheeTree "A tree bearing oval fruit with a hard scaly outer covering, small hard seed, and edible flesh that surrounds the seed.")
(comment GermanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Germany, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment OrganizationWithIndividualClients "#$OrganizationWithIndividualClients is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$OrganizationWithIndividualClients is an organization whose #$clients are primarily individuals, rather than businesses or other #$Organizations.")
(comment Ashtray "The collection of devices that people use to ash in when smoking a #$Cigarette or a #$Cigar.  This collection does NOT include things like beer bottles and soda cans which are often used as ashtrays.  This constant only represents those things which are designed to function as ashtrays.")
(comment RefrigeratedStorageDevice "The collection of electrical devices whose purpose is to maintain something at a lower temperature than the surroundings through refrigeration (usually through the compression/decompression of a gas).")
(comment CorpusCavernosum "The collection of all corpora cavernosa.  An individual #$CorpusCavernosum is a cylinder of erectile tissue inside the #$Penis lateral to the #$CorpusSpongiosum.  The left and right corpora cavernosa are attached to each other on the top side of the #$Penis.")
(disjointWith Condiment Preservative-Food)
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization FoodServiceOrganization)
(disjointWith Wheelbarrow BabyWalker)
(disjointWith PoliticalOrganization TradeAssociation)
(comment Wildcat "A collection of medium-sized cats, including the lynx (e.g. the bobcat and  Canada lynx of North America), the ocelot, serval, and caracal.")
(disjointWith Objecting-CommunicationAct Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment SkinOnFn "argument is a collection of external body parts, value is the skin on those body parts.")
(comment Rack-KitchenHanger "The thing that some kitchens have that you hang pots on.")
(comment PortingAComputerProgram "The collection of events in which an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW which was written to run on a particular kind of #$Computer is altered in order to be able to run on another kind of machine.")
(comment Punch-TheTool "A tool used in puncing or piercing a material.")
(disjointWith Kissing AquaticBodyMovement)
(comment Lung "The collection of all lungs, the primary respiratory organs of #$AirBreathingVertebrates.")
(disjointWith GrassTurf SomethingToWear)
(comment Terrier-Cairn "A collection of small dogs, the most famous being Toto.  Amanda has one,            called Zebediah.")
(comment ChristmasIslandPerson-Australian "A person who is an ChristmasIsland citizen.")
(disjointWith ProductDisplayOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment Harness "The collection of wearable lattice-shaped contraptions that are used to secure some object to the body of an #$Animal.")
(comment Mustelidae "A group of mammalian carnivores or insectivores which typically have sinuous body shapes")
(comment RhomboidMuscles "The collection of all sets of rhomboid #$Muscles.  The #$RhomboidMuscles (or 'rhomboids'), located in the #$Back-AnimalBodyPart, connect the #$Scapula to the #$SpinalColumn and retract and rotate the #$Scapula downward.  The minor rhomboid is cephalic to the major rhomboid, connecting to C7 and T1")
(comment CeramicTile "The collection of pieces of the material Tile that are sheet-like and made of ceramic.")
(comment CastelloToscana-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Castello Toscana.

This is a semi-hard sheep's milk cheese made in Tuscany.")
(comment Harness-Animal "gear worn by horses and other beasts of burden while pulling plows, wagons, sleds, etc.")
(comment EggHatching "This is the collection of events in which an egg hatches and
the animal within emerges.")
(comment AnimalBodyPart-Male "The collection of all #$AnimalBodyParts that are generally found only on male animals. Any collection representing a type of body part that is generally found only on male animals should have this collection as a #$genls. For example, all instances of #$Penis and #$Beard (in #$HumanPhysiologyMt at least) are instances of #$AnimalBodyPart-Male, and the collections #$Penis and #$Beard are subsets of it. See also #$AnimalBodyPart-Female.")
(disjointWith ContainerArtifact Engine)
(comment NicaraguanPerson "The people who are #$citizens of #$Nicaragua, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment CompactStereoSystem "A subcollection of #$HomeAudioSystem. Instances of #$CompactStereoSystem are on the physically small and inexpensive end.")
(comment Filly "The collection of juvenile female #$Horses.  A young female horse is referred to as a 'filly' at least until she is one year old.")
(comment AltaicLanguageFamily "Turkic, Mongolian, and Tungusic languages")
(comment IroningBoard "The collection of ironing boards -- usually lightly padded flat surfaces on legs, about waist-height, for ironing clothes.")
(comment BrayingSound "The collection of braying sounds made by #$Donkeys.")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething PhysicalSynthesis)
(comment DiversionaryComputerProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are entertaining, amusing,  distracting, or just a curiosity.  This includes #$ComputerGamePrograms as well as  screen savers, interactive desktop toys, animated cursors, etc.")
(comment institutionalFocus "(#$institutionalFocus ORG CONCEPT) means that CONCEPT is centrally related to the raison d'etre and institutional purpose of the #$Organization ORG in some way.  Specifics may vary with the organization type.")
(comment SandTrap "A kind of subregion of a golf course, where sand causes it to be difficult to hit the ball.")
(comment UrgeToDefecate "The type of internal sensation or urge to defecate.")
(comment SuperiorLobarBronchus "The collection of superior or upper lobar bronchi (#$BronchialTubes)  in the #$Lung, each of which supplies air to a #$SuperiorLobeOfLung.  It branches off of the left #$MainBronchus or the right #$MainBronchus.")
(comment Diary "The collection of diaries -- journals of personal happenings, usually kept private or shared only among intimate friends, until you're dead.  Then, if you're famous, it becomes public knowledge.")
(comment childrenForUSTaxPurposes "(childrenForUSTaxPurposes PARENT CHILD) means that CHILD is a 
child of PARENT for purposes of #$USIncomeTax.  #$childrenForUSTaxPurposes 
include a parent's natural-born children (if not subsequently adopted), and 
legally adopted children, but does not include foster children.")
(comment FacialMoisturizer "Liquid products, typically oil-based, applied to the skin of the face in order to moisturize it.")
(disjointWith BodyMovementEvent LawEnforcementActivity)
(comment CementTruck "Trucks which are used to carry concrete to construction sites.")
(comment TaxReturn "a report consisting of a form or set of forms, filled out, that an entity provides to the goverment to show how its taxes were calculated and what amount is due.  If there is money due, the return is accompanied by the payment.")
(comment Talon "The sharp claws possessed by birds of prey")
(disjointWith File-Tool WritingImplement)
(comment DomesticCat "Cats people commonly keep as pets")
(comment DaitoIslandsPerson "A person who is a #$DaitoIslands #$citizens, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment CribMattress "The collection of #$Mattresses that that are made to go in #$Cribs.")
(comment TypewriterRibbon "Typewriter ribbon")
(disjointWith SolidTangibleThing FluidTangibleThing)
(comment LeftColicVein "The collection of all left colic #$Veins.  The #$LeftColicVein drains the #$DescendingColon towards the #$HepaticPortalVein via the #$InferiorMesentericVein.")
(comment Soybean-Foodstuff "Foodstuff derived from the seed of a soybean plant.  May be in the form of whole beans, mashed beans, dried soybean flakes, etc.")
(comment BeliefSystemFocusGroup "The class of organizations which have as their focus some element of #$BeliefSystems.  A sample element of #$BeliefSystemFocusGroup is #$KuKluxKlan.")
(comment Compass "A device used to find directions, especially one which uses a magnet to point to magnetic north (a #$MagneticCompass), or a gyroscope to point to true north (a #$GyroCompass).")
(comment EscherichiaColi "A specialization of #$BacterialBioAgent. This type of bacteria is ubiquitously found

in lower digestive tracts and in feces. There are thousands of strains of E. coli.

Particular strains found in beef cattle have been responsible for several well-publicized

recent outbreaks of food poisoning.")
(comment Thread "A specialization of #$Cord-Textile.  Each instance of this collection is a single filament of some length created by
spinning and/or twisting textile fibers into a continous strand.")
(comment ShutterForWindow "The collection of window coverings which are not collapsible, but must be moved in order to allow light through.  Shutters are typically mounted outside a building, rather than inside.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterS "The capital letter 'S'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$S-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterS.")
(comment CatFood "The collection of all cat food")
(comment argIsaForType "A #$SetOrCollectionPredicate that is used to state that a particular #$argIsa (q.v.) constraint applies to all relations of a given type.  (#$argIsaForType RELNTYPE N COL) means that (#$argIsa RELN N COL) holds for any instance RELN of RELNTYPE.  Note that this does _not_ preclude (#$argIsa RELN N SUBCOL) holding for some specialization SUBCOL of COL; e.g. there might in some cases be an asserted constraint on that argument-place that is stricter than that given by COL.  For example, (#$argIsaForType #$ActorSlot 1 #$Event) holds even though some actor-slots' first argument-places are constrained to #$PhysicalEvents.")
(disjointWith ChangeInUserRights AthleticActivity)
(comment ComputerPrinter-Inkjet "The collection of computer printers which produce characters by impact of a molding of the character through an ink ribbon (normally) onto paper.")
(comment CrochetHook "Instances of #$CrochetHook are small shafts with a hook on one end, usually made of metal or plastic, 5 to 8 inches long, and 1/16 to 1/2 an inch in diameter.  They are used primarily for performing Crocheting.")
(comment TableKnife "A kind of knife used mainly as an eating implement")
(comment MedialPlantarNerve "The collection of all medial plantar nerves.  The medial plantar nerve is a branch of the #$TibialNerve and supplies the first 3 1/2 toes and the medial muscles of the foot.")
(comment NegativeIntegerRange "The collection of #$IntegerExtents which include only #$NegativeIntegers")
(comment SpeechToTextProgram "Software which transforms a speech signal into a textual representation.")
(comment Saddle "What one usually sits on when one rides a horse.")
(disjointWith HumanShelterConstruction FluidReservoir)
(comment IcelandicPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Iceland, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment NTDomainServer "The collection of all #$PrimaryDomainControllers and #$BackupDomainControllers.  These serve primarily as #$LoginAuthenticators for instances of #$NTDomain.")
(comment UralicLanguageFamily "Finno-Ugric and Samoyedic languages")
(comment RackForFirePlaceTools "The collection of support stands for fireplace tools.  We do not mean wall mounted hooks here - we mean stands that rest on the floor.")
(comment ShakingHead "The set of actions in which the performer shakes his head.")
(comment programAuthor "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW to instances of #$Agent-Generic.  (#$programAuthor CMPPROG AGENT) means that AGENT is an author of the #$ComputerProgram-CW CMPPROG. For example, (#$programAuthor #$LinuxKernel-TheProgram #$LinusTorvalds) means that Linus Torvalds wrote the Linux kernel.  Note that there can be more than one agent who is considered to be an author of a single computer program -- especially for most large computer programs.")
(comment DraperyHook "The sort of hook which is used to hang curtains/drapes by sticking into the fabric and hooking over a curtain rod.")
(comment DisplayingProduct "The collection of all instances of #$DisplayingSomething in which the items displayed are #$Products to be transferred to customers, or examples of #$ProductTypes which are available for customers  Examples, displaying an outfit worn by a manikin, putting a puppy in a store window [#$DisplayWindowSpace], and displaying videotapes at a tape renal store.")
(comment BoneSuture "A #$BoneSuture is a 'suture' of two #$FlatBone s.")
(comment LegMovement "Any movement of the leg. This unit was created to help talk about the #$subEvents of certain activities and what anatomical resource was required.")
(comment Globe-Map "The collection of all hardcopy #$Maps of planetary objects (normally the #$PlanetEarth) displayed upon a spherical object.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment AirPump "The collection of pumps used to move #$Air in or out of some object.")
(disjointWith FluidFlowEvent ConflictEvent)
(comment QuoteRequestDocument "A document typically sent by PurchasingAgents to vendors, requesting specific information about the terms of a proposed sale.  This is sometimes called a RequestForBids.  Vendors respond with a #$FormalEstimateDocument.")
(comment SpinalCord "Cord of nervous tissue that extends from the brain lengthwise along the back in the spinal canal")
(comment AutomaticFirearm "All fire arms that automatically load another round in the chamber after a round is fired (the first one must be manually loaded).")
(comment Dalmatian "A collection of medium-sized, white dogs with either black or liver spots.  Their fur is short and dense.  They have many other names: English Coach Dog, Carriage Dog, Plum Pudding Dog, Firehouse Dog and Spotted Dick.")
(comment PalestinianPerson "A person with Palestinian ancestry, whose family comes from the #$Palestine-Region.  Many #$PalestinianPersons now live in a diaspora.")
(comment LowRiderRoadVehicle "The collection of #$RoadVehicles where the #$RoadVehicleBody is lowered close to the ground, typically leaving only a few inches of clearance.")
(comment AbductorPollicisBrevis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$AbductorPollicisBrevis#$Muscle.  The #$AbductorPollicisBrevis brings the #$Thumb into opposition.")
(comment Shelf "This refers to any shelf that may be on the wall in a room, or part of a piece of furniture or appliance.")
(disjointWith CommercialActivity Vandalism)
(comment SigmoidFlexure "The collection of all sigmoid flexures.  A #$SigmoidFlexure (or 'Sigmoid colon') is the narrowest part of the Colon-BodyPart, and the part immediately proximal to the #$Rectum.")
(comment Coffee-Ground "Quantities of coffee grinds.")
(comment InsuranceClaimsAdministrationOrganization "The collection of all organizations whose main function is to administer (process) insurance claims.")
(comment AutoLoanCalculatorProgram "The collection of all #$CalculatorPrograms designed primarily to calculate the terms of a #$LoanAgreement made for the purpose of purchasing an automobile. Generally, given all but one of the following - loan amount, interest rate, length of loan, frequency (or number) of payments, and payment amount - a #$AutoLoanCalculatorProgram will calculate the missing value.")
(comment RollTheContainer " A roll is a type of package where the contents, in tablet form, are stacked together in such a way which produces a cylinder.  The tablets, drugs or candy, are wrapped in tinfoil or waxpaper and a paper label is wrapped around the package as a second layer.")
(comment ExplosiveDevice "A specialization of #$SelfPoweredDevice and #$Device-OneTimeUse.  Each instance of #$ExplosiveDevice is a device designed to detonate (see #$HighExplosive) or deflagrate (see #$LowExplosive).  Explosive devices may be used to make holes that help construct mines or swimming pools or flat areas for roads or house foundations; in the demolition/destruction/removal of buildings, tree stumps, and other sorts of property; in weapons of war or terrorism to harm or kill or deter people; or even as entertainment (e.g., fireworks -- see #$PyrotechnicDevice).")
(comment complementaryBaseTypes "Each nitrogen base in a nucleic-acid molecule is complementary to bases of a specific type (at most 2 types). Type-level version of #$complementaryBases.")
(comment MagneticSensor "A collection of sensor devices.  These use magnets to detect the presence of metal (or objects containing significant amounts of metal, such as road vehicles).")
(comment Sac-Organic "#$Sac-Organic is a specialization of #$OrganismPart  and #$Container.  Each instance of #$Sac-Organic is a plant or animal membranous sac or bladder, whether or not it is still part of a living #$Organism-Whole.  Instances of #$Sac-Organic have zero (some plant bladders), one (e.g. #$GallBladder), two (#$Stomach), or three  (#$Bladder-Urinary) tubes attached for the flow of material into or out of the bladder.  The bladder may used for storage of some material in the body, and possible processing thereof, or merely as a mechanism for separating structures (e.g. the #$Peritoneum).   Any tubes connected  to the bladder are of far smaller diameter than the bladder itself.")
(comment GraveAccent-TheSymbol "A slash pointing downwards and to the right. When placed over a letter, it may be used to indicate secondary stress or accent.")
(comment WindowPortalCovering-Glass "The physical object which 'covers' or fills in the #$WindowPortal. It is a physical barrier, but because it is made primarily of glass, it allows light to enter.")
(comment iQ "This predicate relates an animal to its IQ, or intelligence quotient, represented as a non-negative number.  (#$iQ ANIMAL NUMBER) means that the intelligence quotient of ANIMAL is NUMBER.  Among adult humans, 100 is (by definition) the average IQ number.")
(comment ComputerDisplayCable "The collection of all cables that connect instances of #$ComputerDisplay to some instances of #$Computer, e.g. instances of #$PersonalComputer.  Cables belonging to this collection will plug into a computer's video card.")
(comment MissileSilo "The collection of #$StorageConstructs that are meant for storing #$Missiles. By default any #$MissileSilo is a #$MilitaryFacility; although other organisations may own missiles, the common-sense assumption is that missile silos are military.")
(comment GenitofemoralNerve-GenitalBranch "The collection of all genital branches of the #$GenitofemoralNerves.  The #$GenitofemoralNerve branches into the #$GenitofemoralNerve-GenitalBranch and the #$GenitofemoralNerve-FemoralBranch.  The genital branch supplies the #$Cremaster and the #$Skin of the #$Scrotum in a male or the mons pubis and labium majus in a female.")
(comment GermanCuisine "The collection of instances of what many Americans tend           to think of as German food")
(comment SymlinkFault-Overwrite "#$SymlinkFault-Overwrite is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite if when running it creates files with predictable filenames and world write permissions in the /tmp directory.  This fault allows a user to create a file in the /tmp directory with the same name and then symlink that file to a file to which the user does not have write permissions.  When the malicious user or another user executes the program, it follows the symlink and overwrites the protected file.  As with other faults, the severity of #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite depends on the privilege level under which the exploited program is running.  If the program runs at root, for instance, when creating the /tmp files, then the malicious user can overwrite any known file on the computer.")
(comment TombOfFn "The function #$TombOfFn applied to an individual instance of #$Vertebrate animal (including a person), as in (#$TombOfFn CREATURE), denotes the #$Tomb or burial structure, if any, into which the remains of CREATURE are placed, after its death, or under which it is buried.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice ComputationalSystem)
(comment BracesForTeeth "The device attached to a patient's teeth by orthodontists to straighten teeth.")
(comment organismFoundInSubstance "(#$organismFoundInSubstance ORGTYPE STUFFTYPE) means that instances of ORGTYPE can often be found in instances of STUFFTYPE, such that instances of STUFFTYPE constitute good or probable places to look for instances of ORGTYPE.")
(comment TasteBud "The collection of all #$TasteBuds, which are #$ChemoReceptiveSensors located on the #$Tongue and the inner surface of the #$Mouth.")
(comment DirectoryTraversalFault "A program (usually a web server program) has a #$DirectoryTraversalFault if appending something (usually \"../\") to the end of a request allows an unauthorized user to access restricted files in a directory.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice SemiconductorDevice)
(comment MangroveTree "Common name for a certain shrub and tree that grows in dense thickets along tidal estuaries, in salt marshes, and on muddy coasts.")
(comment LebanesePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Lebanon, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganizationWithBusinessClients OrganizationWithIndividualClients)
(comment ScubaDivingTank "The collection of oxygen tanks designed

to be used for #$ScubaDiving.")
(comment PlungerPartOfSyringe "The part of a hypodermic syringe which is the plunger.")
(disjointWith PublishingWrittenMaterial MakingAnAudioRecording)
(comment Condiment "A specialization of #$FoodIngredientOnly.  Each instance of #$Condiment is a substance used to flavor or complement a foodstuff.  Some commonly used condiments are ketchup, mustard, relish, mayonaise, salt and pepper.  Instances of #$Condiment are not eaten by themselves, but they are often served in their own dishes, so that the consumer can season his/her own food directly.")
(disjointWith ManufacturingOrganization ProfessionalOffice)
(disjointWith MufflerAndBrakeShop Restaurant-Organization)
(comment Bird "An instance of #$BiologicalClass, and a specialization of #$Vertebrate.  Each instance of #$Bird is an air-breathing, warm-blooded, winged animal covered with feathers.  Members of most, but not all, species of bird can fly.")
(disjointWith TextEditing TransportationEvent)
(comment Rack-Holder "A framework on which articles or materials are arranged or deposited; e.g., a clothes rack.")
(comment DevelopingAProduct "Actions in which somebody or a group of agents thinks up a thing, and often prototypes it.  Sometimes this involves designing a specification for the thing as well as coming up with a specification for how to produce more of them.  It might involve several rounds of prototyping, trying out designs, etc.")
(comment Glanders-Infection "A collection of #$BacterialInfections.  It is a disease of horses transmittable to humans.  In horses, it has pulmonary
involvement.  Human infection may be fatal and begins as an ulcer of the skin or mucous membranes followed by lymphangitis and sepsis.  Although still present in Africa, Asia, and South America, it no longer occurs in North America or Western Europe.")
(disjointWith HandlingAnObject Kissing)
(comment Leg "The collection of all #$Animal appendages used for locomotion overland, supporting the animal and moving it along by walking, running, etc.  Thus wings, fins, etc., are not #$Legs.  The #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart is considered part of the #$Leg")
(disjointWith StepOfStairs ShelterConstruction)
(comment Terrier-Border "A collection of small, agile dogs.")
(disjointWith EventOrganizer-Organization TravelOrganization)
(comment Harness-Human "The collection of wearable lattice-shaped contraptions that are used to secure some object to the body of a #$Person.")
(comment CoracoBrachialis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$CoracoBrachialis #$Muscle.  The #$CoracoBrachialis #$Muscle lies ventral to the #$Humerus in the #$UpperArm, connects the #$Scapula to the #$Humerus, and is used for flexion and adduction of the arm.")
(comment MissileHead "The collection of heads of missiles.")
(comment FontinaDAosta-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Fontina d' Aosta, 

the original Fontina cheese made in the Valle d' Aosta in Italy. Unlike

the many generic version of Fontina, it is soft, ripened, very flavorful, and

smelly in somewhat they way Limburger is.")
(comment industryFacilities "(#$industryFacilities INDUSTRY THING) means that THING is an inanimate object involved in carrying out the activities performed by INDUSTRY.  Examples: a factory, a field, a broadcasting tower, an oil well.")
(comment Manger "food trough for animals.  In the story of Jesus' birth, a manger served as his bed after he was born.")
(comment LifeFn "'(#$LifeFn LIVING-THING)' refers to the life, that is, the
instance of #$Living of the #$BiologicalLivingObject LIVING-THING.")
(comment LabiaMajora "The collection of all labia majora. An instance of #$LabiaMajora is one of a pair of folds of fatty tissue which extend from the front of the #$Vulva almost to the #$Anus and protect the inner genitals.")
(disjointWith ProjectileWeapon ContainerArtifact)
(comment BarrelCactus "Barrel-shaped cacti, with strong stiff spines and prominent ribs.")
(comment BoninIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$BoninIslands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Radio "A subcollection of #$WirelessCommunicationDevice. Instances of #$Radio convert instances of #$RadioWave into instances of #$AudibleSound.")
(comment LanguageIsolate "'Singleton' languages seemingly unrelated to any others")
(comment ClothesIron "The collection of irons -- hand-held devices with heated, flat surfaces for removing the wrinkles from items of clothing.")
(comment arg4NotIsa "(#$arg4NotIsa REL COL) means that nothing given as the fourth argument to the #$Relation REL may be known to be an element of the #$Collection COL.")
(disjointWith LegalProceeding PhysicalSynthesis)
(comment UtilityProgram "Software which allows a user to manage a variety of aspects of their computer, such as decompressing files, memory management, hard drive scanning, anti-viral programs, etc. See also #$AdministrationProgram, #$BackEndUtilityProgram.")
(comment LocalOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$LocalOrganization is a non-geopolitical organization having local `scope' -- that is, its members are distributed in a local area (for example, in a #$Neighborhood, #$City, or rural region), or it has a local (as opposed to national or international) area of activity and concern.")
(comment BathSoapBar "Bar of body soap")
(comment CalanSRProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by C.D. Searle.")
(comment UrgeToYawn "The type of internal sensation or urge to yawn.")
(comment ChestCavity "The collection of #$Chest-BodyPart cavities, or cavities within the thorax, that each contains the #$Lungs, #$Pleura (pleurae), #$Mediastinum, #$Heart, etc.  A #$ChestCavity  includes its walls, such as the #$RibCage.")
(comment CannelloniNoodle "A short round fat noodle.")
(comment AirplaneTicket "The collection of all paper tickets entitling a #$Person to board an #$Airplane at a certain location and be taken on that airplane to a certain other location. An #$AirplaneTicket is often exchanged for a boarding pass, which is not itself an instance of #$AirplaneTicket. Electronic 'e-tickets' or other non-hardcopy authorizations to be a passenger on a flight are also not instances of #$AirplaneTicket.")
(comment Pedal-ControlDevice "A device used to control something by pressing your foot against it.")
(comment PhotocopyingAPage "Events in which a page of hardcopied printed or written matter is duplicated by a photocopy machine.")
(comment Fingernail "Protective covering at the end of a finger")
(disjointWith FireplaceTool WritingImplement)
(comment Spaniel "A collection of dogs, each instance of which belongs to one of the            Spaniel breeds.")
(comment SardinianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Sardinia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith InsuranceOrganization ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment InfantMobile "A subset of #$MobileSculpture.  #$InfantMobiles are the collection of mobiles that one might hang over a #$Crib or a #$Bassinet for a #$HumanInfant to look at and touch.")
(comment WindowAirConditioner "Window Unit air conditioners")
(disjointWith ProductDistributionEvent IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment LeftColicArtery "The collection of all left colic arteries.  The #$LeftColicArtery is an #$Artery which supplies the #$DescendingColon.  It branches off of the #$InferiorMesentericArtery.")
(comment Bean-Foodstuff "Food derived from the seed of a bean plant.")
(comment president "(#$president ORGANIZATION PERSON) means that PERSON serves in a leadership role in ORGANIZATION such that s/he holds the title of 'president'.  If ORGANIZATION isa #$Country the PERSON must be a #$President-HeadOfGovernmentOrHeadOfState.  National presidents may be elected by the people, appointed by the legislature or other ruling group, or be self-declared.")
(comment Sextant "A navigation tool to measure the angular distance between distant objects.")
(disjointWith TextualMaterial DrugSubstance)
(comment WindowCovering "The collection of curtains, blinds, and shades that block the light from coming in through the window of a building and prevent people from seeing in or out.  Also serve as indoor accessories to a window in a room.  This collection is not intended to include the window shades put in car windows in the summer when the car is unoccupied.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterS "The lowercase letter 's'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$S-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterS.")
(comment EuropeanCar "A car whose manufacturer is European.")
(comment relationCategoryType "This predicate relates instances of #$RelationshipType to instances of #$Collection that are required as #$argIsa constraints for predicates that are instances of the category. (#$relationCategoryType RELATION COLLECTION) means that any instance of RELATION must have at least one argument place such that the argIsa for that argument place is COLLECTION or one of its specs.  This is useful for defining relation types whose instances, by definition, must have some collection as one or more of its argument type restrictions, but where the definition of the predicate type places no restrictions on argument placement, i.e. is agnostic about N for (argIsa PRED N REQUIREDCOLLECTION).  For instance, (#$relationCategoryType #$MetaPredicate #$CycLExpression) means that for any instance of #$MetaPredicate, MPRED, (#$argIsa MPRED N CycLExpression) must be true for some positive integer although membership in the predicate category is not dependent on the value of N.")
(disjointWith MakingAGesture IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment interArgNotIsa3-4 "(#$interArgNotIsa3-4 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the third argument to PRED, the fourth argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(comment physicalMemorySize "A #$BinaryPredicate which relates instances of #$ElectronicDevice to instances of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity. (#$physicalMemorySize COMP SIZE) means that COMP has SIZE as the sum of its RAM and ROM. See also the more specific #$rAMSize and #$rOMSize. For virtual memory, see #$virtualMemorySize.")
(disjointWith GovernmentalOrganization CriminalOrganization)
(comment KnittingNeedle "Instances of #$KnittingNeedle are pointed, cylindrical shafts made of metal or plastic, from 6 to 16 inches long, from 1/16-inch to a half-inch in diameter, and primarily used in #$Knitting.")
(comment Mule "The collection of all mules; a subset of #$EquineAnimal.  Elements of #$Mule are the infertile hybrid offspring of a horse father and a donkey mother.  Mules are presumed to be elements of #$DomesticatedAnimal, used for draught or riding.  (An offspring of a donkey father and horse mother is called a jenny, and is recognizably distinct from the larger mule.)  See also #$Horse, #$Donkey.")
(comment Fork-SilverwarePiece "An eating implement having two or more parallel sharp tines, useful for stabbing and/or lifting solid foods.")
(comment DorsalRamusS2 "The collection of all S2 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiS2 and DorsalRamiS2 branch from SpinalRootS2.  DorsalRamiS2 supplies the posterior gluteal skin.")
(comment Jelly-Foodstuff "This is the collection of all instances of jelly. Jelly is generally made

from fruit, which is combined with sugar and cooked until a certain temperature

is reached. Sometimes pectin is added to aid in gelling. Jelly is then

strained so that it is clear.")
(comment NegativeScalarInterval "For a measurable negative quantity, the ordered sequence of possible values may be thought of as a line.  #$NegativeScalarIntervals are the line segments (or points) on such a line, representing a range of consecutive values, all less than 0.  An important subcollection is #$NegativeNumber the instances of which correspond to the non-positive part of the Real Number Line.  Instances of #$NegativeScalarInterval are either contiguous sets of points there (i.e., a range of numbers) or just single points there (i.e., a #$NegativeNumber).  Instances of #$NegativeScalarInterval for which there is some unit of measure (e.g. volts, degrees fahrenheit) are not instances of #$NegativeScalarInterval.")
(comment Sandbox "An outdoor play area which is a box a few feet wide filled with sand for children to play in.")
(comment completeAISOfIBT "(#$completeAISOfIBT IBT COMP-AIS) means that the #$AbstractInformationStructure COMP-AIS is the maximal #$AbstractInformationStructure instantiated by IBT.  More precisely, it means that for all ?AIS distinct from COMP-AIS, IBT instantiates ?AIS if and only if ?AIS is a #$subInfoStructures of COMP-AIS.")
(disjointWith RoomInAConstruction FluidReservoir)
(comment BryophytaDivision "A biologicalDivision including mosses, liverworts and hornworts - those plants lacking vascular tissue.")
(comment MarcusIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$MarcusIslands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment BackupDomainController "The collection of all instances of #$Computer which serve as backups to the #$PrimaryDomainController (PDC) in an #$NTDomain.  On some networks there may be more than one #$BackupDomainController (BDC).  The primary function of BDCs is to authenticate user login information, though all changes made to the domain's account database are made on the #$SAMFile found on the PDC.  The BDCs keep copies of the domain #$SAMFile to authenticate users, but they must communicate with the PDC every so often to ensure that those copies contain up-to-date login information.")
(comment Niger-KordofanianLanguageFamily "Languages spoken in the #$Sudan, south and central Africa, and west Africa below the Sahara")
(comment VelcroTheFastener "Pair of hook-and-loop cloth fasteners.")
(comment Hobbit "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent and #$Person in the fictional world of #$JRRTolkien's #$LordOfTheRings-Trilogy.")
(comment HangingOnesHead "The set of actions in which a performer lowers his (or her) head by bending the neck forward; usually understood to express shame or disappointment.")
(comment CriminalOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization and #$CovertAgent.  Each instance of #$CriminalOrganization is a group of agents, many of whom cooperate in the willful commission of criminal acts.  Not every member of the organization necessarily commits criminal acts (e.g. the group may have a lawyer, an accountant, or a receptionist who does not).  Examples instances of #$CriminalOrganization include the Sicilian Mafia, the Russian Mafiya, street gangs (e.g., Bloods and Crips), prison gangs. Criminal organizations may have local or international scope.  The latter will be instances of both #$CriminalOrganization and #$InternationalOrganization.")
(comment BedPillow "The collection of pillows that are intended to be used while sleeping on  a bed.")
(comment Marsupial "Mammals with pouches for their young")
(disjointWith Cell ExtrudedBodyPart)
(comment PulmonaryAcinus "The collection of all acini of the #$Lung, being the clusters of parenchymal respiratory parts that are involved directly in gas exchange, as opposed to #$RespiratoryTract parts that serve only to bring air to and from the PulmonaryAcinus.  The PulmonaryAcinus consists of the #$RespiratoryBronchioles, the #$AlveolarDucts, the #$AlveolarSacs, and each #$Alveolus in the #$Lung.")
(comment Chewing "A collection of events.  In each #$Chewing event, foodstuff is mashed in the mouth.  An element of #$Chewing consists of a large number of #$Biting sub-events.  Anatomical resources required for a #$Chewing are a tongue and whatever hard surfaces the species involved uses for #$Biting, e.g., teeth.  The teeth go up and down or grind, and the tongue maneuvers the food around.")
(comment Handgun "A specialization of #$Gun-Portable.  Each instance of #$Handgun is a firearm designed to be held and fired with one hand.")
(disjointWith Travel-TripEvent TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment ComputerProgramTypeByCreator "#$ComputerProgramTypeByCreator is a collection of types of computer programs.  Collections that are instances of #$ComputerProgramTypeByCreator are collections of programs whose instances all have a #$programAuthor in common.")
(comment RadiatorFlush "Stuff added to radiators that Cleans car.")
(disjointWith Communicating FluidFlowEvent)
(comment FormalEstimateDocument "A document sent by vendors in response to a #$PurchasingAgent's #$QuoteRequestDocument, containing specific information about the vendor's terms in a proposed sale.")
(comment Kidney "The collection of all kidneys.  Instances of this collection are paired #$InternalOrgans which remove nitrogen compounds (e.g. #$Urea) from the #$Blood, maintain electrolyte balance, pH, and osmotic pressure, and pass the waste products out of the body through a network of #$AnatomicalVessels and storage compartments.

In #$Mammals, #$Kidneys are structures which produce #$Urine, passing it through #$Ureters to a #$Bladder-Urinary which empties out of the body through a #$Urethra.")
(comment Dachshund "A collection of small dogs.  They come in three different           varieties, the Longhaired, Smooth and Wirehaired, as well as two           different sizes, Miniature and Standard.")
(comment areaThisLanguageNativeTo "The predicate #$areaThisLanguageNativeTo is used to indicate regions in which a language is spoken by natives.  (#$areaThisLanguageNativeTo LANG REG) means that the #$NaturalLanguage LANG is spoken in the #$GeographicalRegion REG.  REG may be a country, a subregion of a country, or a large or small area crossing national boundaries.  LANG may be native to more than one region (e.g., #$SpanishLanguage, which is now native to both Iberia and a large portion of the Americas.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment OffRoadAutomobile "The collection of #$Automobiles designed for traveling on not only paved roads, but also unpaved roads, trails, beaches, or other rough terrains.")
(comment TensorFasciaeLatae "The #$Collection of all instances of #$TensorFasciaeLatae #$Muscle.  The #$TensorFasciaeLatae (also known as the 'iliotibial band (ITB)' prevents collapse of the extended #$Knee when walking.  Assists extension of the #$Knee and abduction, flexion, and medial rotation of the #$Femur at the #$Hip.")
(disjointWith Evaluating Vandalism)
(comment DescendingColon "The collection of all descending colons.  Each element of this collection is the distal part of the #$LargeIntestine of an #$Animal, adjoining the #$Rectum.")
(comment CarrotPuree "What you get after carrots are through the blender")
(comment PestControlCompany "Companies that provide, as one of their main functions, pest control for a client/customer for a fee.")
(comment SalaryCalculator "The collection of all #$CalculatorPrograms designed primarily to calculate the salary required to maintain a standard of living when moving from one #$GeographicalRegion to another.  For example, given a standard of living determined by Salary 1 in City A, it will calculate the salary needed to maintain the same standard of living in City B.")
(comment DisposablePackage " A disposable package is a container which is only intended to last as long as its product is in it.  Once the product has been consumed, the disposable container may be thrown away.")
(comment brothers "(#$brothers ANIMAL BROTHER) means that BROTHER is one of ANIMAL's brothers -- a male sibling, related either by birth (sharing one or more of the same biological parents), by marriage (e.g. a step-brother), or by some other social arrangement.")
(comment DecontaminationProcedure-Personnel "The collection of all activities wherein one tries to decontaminate #$Persons who have been exposed to something toxic.")
(disjointWith Skin Joint-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment OpenAngleBracket-TheSymbol "The symbol '<'. Usually used with a #$CloseAngleBracket-TheSymbol.  this refers to the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract), not to any physical instantiation.")
(comment Tap-PlumbingFixture "The tap or faucet apparatus found on sinks, bathtubs, etc.")
(comment IndividualRitual " Things such as individual prayers, idiosyncracies such as looking east 3 times before writing an exam")
(comment ComputerTerminal "A collection of objects. Each instance of #$ComputerTerminal is an input/output device connected to an instance of #$Computer over an instance of #$ComputerNetwork. A computer terminal usually includes a monitor and a keyboard, and sometimes an instance of #$ComputerMouse or other input device.")
(comment Radiosonde "The collection of meteorological devices carried by weather balloons into the upper atmosphere to measure various weather phenomena, and transmit those readings to weather stations on land.")
(comment RingwormFungus "this is the fungus that causes ringworm, athlete's foot, jock itch, etc.  Probably not it's real name (The english 'ringworm' seems to denote the ailment, not the fungus).")
(disjointWith OpeningAContainerArtifact VisualPerception)
(comment GreatAuricularNerve "The collection of all greater auricular #$Nerves (also 'greater auricular nerve').  A #$GreatAuricularNerve is connected to #$VentralRamusC2 and #$VentralRamusC3 on its side of the body.  It #$innervates the #$Skin around the joint in the jaw (#$TemporoMandibularJoint) and immediately behind the #$Ear.")
(comment CremeBrulee "A kind of #$Custard that has sugar sprinkled on top and is usually broiled.")
(comment OSCrashingFault "#$OSCrashingFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has an #$OSCrashingFault when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to send commands
 to the copies of the program that cause it to crash, taking the operating
 system down along with it.  A reboot is usually required to regain
 service, so a computer running a program with an #$OSCrashingFault has the attribute #$VulnerableToDenialOfService.")
(comment inventedBy "(#$inventedBy INTANGIBLE PERSON) means that INTANGIBLE was invented by PERSON. Only intangibles can be invented. It is the design of the transistor that can be invented, for instance. Actual transistors are merely created.")
(disjointWith Water ComputationalSystem)
(comment DentalAppliance "Non-permanent devices used to protect/move teeth.")
(comment ResignationLetter "A letter which contains notice to terminate employment (and the terms) from an individual to an organization.")
(comment CommandExecutionOfDLLFault "A program has a #$CommandExecutionOfDLLFault if it calls
 procedures from dynamic link libraries without warning the user first.  This can be especially dangerous if it is possible to edit the the DLL first so that when executed it runs at the privilege level of the faulty program.")
(disjointWith ControlDevice Clothing-Generic)
(comment OliveTree "Individual olive trees.")
(comment ZambiaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Zambia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment OrganizationWithoutClients "The collection of all #$Organizations who do not have #$clients.  Positive examples include bridge clubs, photography clubs, #$HoldingCompanys, #$FanClubs, and #$Gangs.")
(comment CigarCutter "The collection of devices whose primary purpose is to cut #$Cigars.")
(comment Suitcase "Retangular piece of luggage with handle that is used when you are on a trip.")
(disjointWith BodyMovementEvent MediaTransferEvent)
(comment SeminalVesicle "The collection of all seminal vesicles.  Elements of this collection produce fluid which is the #$mainConstituent of #$Semen.  #$SeminalVesicles appear in all male #$Mammals and various other #$Vertebrates.")
(comment OrganizationalTransferIn "A subcollection of #$OrganizationalTransfer.  In each instance of #$OrganizationalTransferIn, an agent (an instance of #$IntelligentAgent) gains membership in some organization.  Note that the agent may also, but need not, lose membership in some other organization.  Instances of #$OrganizationalTransferIn would include hiring someone at a company or admitting a nation to NATO.  Note that any event in which an agent leaves one organization to join another would be an instance of both #$OrganizationalTransferIn and #$OrganizationalTransferOut (q.v.).")
(comment Balloon "#$Balloon is a specialization of #$Artifact-NonAgentive, #$BilateralObject, and #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$Balloon is a physical device made from an elastic and flexible material and filled with gas or air. The #$Balloon tends to be light (sometimes lighter than air).")
(disjointWith OilAndLubeShop Restaurant-Organization)
(comment Sheet-BoatLine "A rope or chain that regulates the angle at which a sail is set in relation to the wind.")
(disjointWith WritingAComposition MovementEvent)
(comment Topiary "The collection of all #$Bushes or trees [#$Tree-ThePlant] which have been trimmed into decorative representational shapes.  This collection does not include #$BonsaiTrees.")
(comment BiologicalTaxonType "An instance of #$CollectionTypeType and a specialization of #$DisjointCollectionType (q.v.).  Each instance of #$BiologicalTaxonType is a specialization of #$BiologicalTaxon (q.v.). Notable instances of #$BiologicalTaxonType include #$BiologicalSpecies, #$BiologicalClass, and #$BiologicalFamily.")
(comment DevelopingATangibleProduct "Product development for goods to be manufactured.  This often involves not only the design of the specification of the thing, but the design of a process for making it.")
(comment Dysentery-Infection "A collection of #$BacterialInfections caused by Shigella dysenteriae.  No no-human reservoirs exist, and the bacteria are highly communicable: less than 100 bacteria can cause infection in a healthy person.  Transmission occurs by contact with infected fingers, food, or water.  The resulting infection produces acute inflammation and shallow ulcers along the mucosal surface of the colon.")
(disjointWith HittingAnObject Kissing)
(comment Arm "The collection of all animal arms.  An #$Arm of an animal is one of its #$AnimalBodyParts, more particularly one of its appendages, a limb which it uses for manipulation moreso than for locomotion.  A #$Hand is considered part of an #$Arm.")
(disjointWith TextileArtifact Leather)
(comment Terrier-Bedlington "A collection of medium-sized dogs. Their coats will be either liver or blue            colored.")
(comment KuwaitiPerson "A person who is a citizen of #$Kuwait.")
(disjointWith TradeAssociation TravelOrganization)
(comment CableDescrambler "The collection of all boxes (legal or not) that descramble scrambled cable television signals and allow them to be viewed.")
(comment Donkey "The collection of all donkeys; a subset of #$EquineAnimal.  Also called burros, donkeys are slightly smaller than most horses.  Elements of #$Donkey may belong to either of the collections #$DomesticatedAnimal or #$WildAnimal.  Domesticated donkeys are used for draught and riding.  Donkeys can interbreed with horses to produce a nonfertile mule or a jenny (see #$Horse, #$Mule).")
(comment TeresMajor "The #$Collection of all instances of #$TeresMajor #$Muscle.  The #$TeresMajor, located in the #$Shoulder, pulls the #$Humerus towards the #$Scapula.")
(comment VideoScreen "A video display screen for a piece of electronic hardware")
(comment PeronealVein "The collection of all peroneal #$Veins.  The #$PeronealVein connects to the #$PosteriorTibialVein at its proximal end and to the dorsal venous arch at its distal end.  The #$PeronealVein runs alongside (#$alignedAlongLength) the #$PeronealArtery in the #$Leg.")
(comment Camembert-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Camembert, a French cheese with

a white mold crust. Camembert becomes more gooey and flavorful as it ages.

It is similar to #$Brie-Cheese, the main difference being that it comes

is smaller thicker wheels.")
(comment Firewood "pieces of wood used (by people) as fuel for fires")
(comment LabiaMinora "The collection of all labia minora. An instance of #$LabiaMinora is one of a pair of folds of fatty tissue located just inside the #$LabiaMajora that enclose the openings of the #$Urethra and #$Vagina.")
(disjointWith ContainerArtifact InformationRecordingDevice)
(comment NigerPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Niger, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PersonalDigitalAudioPlayer "A subcollection of #$PersonalAudioPlayer. Instances of #$PersonalDigitalAudioPlayer are designed to convert instances of #$ComputerSoundFile (not stored on instances of #$CompactDisc-Generic) into instances of #$AudibleSound.")
(comment EskimoLanguageFamily "A sub-family of #$Eskimo-AleutLanguageFamily, consisting of languages spoken in Greenland, #$Canada, Alaska, and Siberia, seemingly unrelated to any other than Aleut")
(comment Cabinet-PieceOfFurniture "the collection of all cabinets that are pieces of furniture -- that is, portable, not built into a structure")
(comment NeighingSound "The collection of neighing sounds made by #$Horses.")
(disjointWith Reading PhysicalSynthesis)
(comment InteractiveComputerProgram "Programs which interact intimately either with the user or with other programs.")
(disjointWith GeopoliticalEntity LocalOrganization)
(comment CardizemCDProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by Hoechst Marion Roussel.")
(comment UrgeToBurp "The type of internal sensation or urge to burp.")
(comment InferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of lower (inferior or caudal) major lobes of  #$Lungs in #$AirBreathingVertebrates.  Includes left and right lower  lobes (i.e., for both lungs).")
(comment SpaghettiNoodle "A long round skinny noodle.")
(comment AutomobileAlternator "The electrical device on your car's engine that controls the current to the engine.")
(comment AutoCarrierTruck " Trucks which are used for transporting cars.")
(comment Encyclopedia "The collection of all encyclopedia: generally, large reference works that aim to cover a broad swath (to varying degrees of depth) of human knowledge.")
(comment typeLevelCognates "(#$typeLevelCognates PRED TYPEPRED) means that TYPEPRED is a type-level variant of PRED with respect to some argument place. Example: (#$typeLevelCognates #$behaviorCapable #$typeBehaviorCapable). This meta-property is used to effect type-shifting via #$reformulatorRules for quantifier processing. It has no purpose in ordinary KE. Note that #$InstantiationInstanceFn is a way to get type-level cognate predicates `on the fly', but #$typeLevelCognates is simpler to use in #$reformulationPrecondition because it doesn't depend on the creation of a predicate-denoting NAT.")
(disjointWith ClimateControlDevice WritingImplement)
(comment Retriever-Dog " A collection of dogs.  Instances of #$Retriever-Dog are members of breeds used for retrieving game.")
(comment DanishPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Denmark, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith HealthcareOrganization ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment NurseryLamp "A subset of #$ElectricLamp.  The collection of all lamps that might be found in a #$Nursery-BabysRoom.  These lamps are decorated with pictures that #$HumanInfants and #$HumanToddlers might enjoy.")
(comment HeadLice-Condition "The collection of cases of head lice.  Individuals afflicted with 'head lice' have numerous elements of #$Louse which are #$in-Among the hairs on their head.")
(comment Keyboard-MusicalInstrument "Instances of this collection

are musical instruments which are played by means of a standard

musical keyboard.  In cases where

such instances are also instances of #$MusicalInstrument-Acoustic, the

instance will also be an instance of #$StringInstrument:

paradigm cases are the #$Harpsichord, where striking a key causes a

string to be plucked, and the #$Piano-Acoustic, where striking a key

causes a string to be hammered.  However, since the advent of the

electronic age, many kinds of electronic #$Keyboard-MusicalInstrument

have been produced which are not stringed instruments.  See #$ElectronicMusicalKeyboard.")
(disjointWith Collecting IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment CysticArtery "The collection of all cystic arteries.  The #$CysticArtery supplies the #$GallBladder.  It branches off of the right #$HepaticArtery.")
(comment Olive-Foodstuff "Foodstuff from the edible fruit of olive trees.  Usually pickled in a light brine.  May be served whole, chopped, or stuffed.")
(comment EducationalSystem "A system of educational organizations that are controlled by a central administrative system (e.g. AISD, UT-System).")
(comment TelnetServerProgram "#$TelnetServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$TelnetProtocol, which traditionally operates over TCP, port 23. A UNIX user can type 'telnet hostname 23' and connect with an instance of #$TelnetServerProgram on hostname, if one is present.")
(comment SingleCellOrganism "A specialization of both #$Microorganism and #$Cell.  Each instance of #$SingleCellOrganism is an organism composed of a single self-reproducing living cell.  Notable specializations of #$SingleCellOrganism include #$Protozoan, #$ProkaryoticCell, and #$Algae-LikeProtist.")
(disjointWith TranscriptCopy Form-StandardizedIBO)
(comment AccessoryFn-Artifact "The expression `(#$AccessoryFn-Artifact PRODTYPE)' denotes the collection of accessories for the product type PRODTYPE. To clarify, the resulting collection is such that every member of it is an accessory for some spec of PRODTYPE. For example, the collection of computer printers would be in the collection (#$AccessoryFn-Artifact #$PersonalComputer) because every computer printer is an accessory for some type of personal computer. However, no computer printer is an accessory for every personal computer.")
(comment RadioDish "A device used to receive radio signals sent from a satellite or originating in space.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterT "The capital letter 'T'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$T-TheLetter, and #$LatinSmallLetterT.")
(comment DishTowel "A small, approximately one-square-foot, towel-like cloth used in the kitchen, ususally for drying dishes or hands. Not a #$DishRag.")
(disjointWith MakingAGesture MakingWrittenMaterial)
(disjointWith SellingOrganization GovernmentalOrganization)
(comment Aquarium-Container "Instances of #$Aquarium-Container are containers with transparent walls (often made of glass) which are used to house aquatic animals (often fish).")
(comment likesRelationshipFromType "(#$likesRelationshipFromType AGENT REL COLLECTION) means that AGENT likes to be in the relationship REL with an instance of COLLECTION.  If the relationship is a #$Role and the #$Collection is a spec of #$Event, then (#$likesRoleInEventType AGENT REL COLLECTION).")
(comment AthenianTrireme "A very fast ancient vessel with three banks of oars. The keystone of Athenian naval power.")
(comment SaphenousNerve "The collection of all saphenous #$Nerves.  A #$SaphenousNerve is formed by #$VentralRamusL2, #$VentralRamusL3 and #$VentralRamusL4 and is the largest branch of the posterior branch of a #$FemoralNerve.  A #$SaphenousNerve #$innervates the #$Skin on the medial side of the foot and #$Leg.")
(comment CocktailSauce "This is the collection of all cocktail sauce. This sauce is basically

ketchup and horseradish with some other flavorings. It is usually purchased

pre-made. It is mostly used with shrimp.")
(comment FrenchCommune "Instances of #$FrenchCommune are the smallest administartive
subdivision of contemporary #$France, they usually are subsumed into a
#$FrenchDepartment. Created by the French Revolution, communes succeeded to
parishes and medieval cities. #$AroundTheYear2000, #$France as several
thousands of communes.")
(comment NonNegativeIntegerRange "The collection of #$IntegerExtents which include no #$NegativeIntegers")
(comment HelpProgram "Software which is designed to provide on-line help to users.")
(comment Crane-MotorizedDevice "A motorized device using pulleys and cables to move very large or heavy objects.  Some cranes can move along the ground, like those used in road construction; others may be fixed in place, like those used to load ships.")
(comment muscleInsertion "#$BinaryPredicate (#$muscleInsertion ?MUSCLE ?INSERTION) means that #$AnimalBodyPart ?INSERTION is an attachment structure for ?MUSCLE.  This is normally the more movable attachment point for the #$Muscle.")
(disjointWith MultiRoomUnit FluidReservoir)
(comment Wormwood "a bitter, aromatic plant, Artemisia absinthium, of the Old World, used as a vermifuge and a tonic, and as an ingredient in #$Absinthe.")
(comment TurkmenistanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Turkmenistan, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment NoveltyMagnet "The kind of magnets you find on kitchen refrigerators, stoves, file cabinets, etc.")
(comment Niger-CongoLanguageFamily "Languages spoken in south and central Africa, and west Africa below the Sahara")
(comment ManualCanOpener "The collection of hand-powered can openers. See also #$ElectricCanOpener.")
(comment Swimming-Underwater "Swimming underwater")
(comment SpecifiedCheeseType "This is a collection of types. Each type is a collection of instances of a particular variety (not brand) of cheese. A #$SpecifiedCheeseType must have a name, such as \"Brie\", and be such that all instances are made in more or less the same way.")
(comment fileFoundOnComputer "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$ComputerFile-Abstract to instances of #$ComputationalSystem. (#$fileFoundOnComputer FILE COMP) means that there is a copy of the #$ComputerFile-Abstract FILE on the #$ComputationalSystem COMP.  See also #$fileCopyFoundOnComputer and #$fileAccessibleToComputer.")
(comment ReligiousOrganization "A subcollection of #$BeliefSystemFocusGroup.  Each instance of #$ReligiousOrganization is an organization whose members share religious beliefs and participate in meetings, rituals, or practices related to those beliefs.  Religious organizations include #$LocalReligiousCongregations such as local churches, temples, mosques and shrines (qua organizations), as well as worldwide religious organizations such as the #$RomanCatholicChurch.")
(comment ChainLinkFence "A fence constructed from a very loose weave of metal wires.")
(comment BoneMarrow "Tissue that is found in the center of bones")
(comment Trapezium "The Trapezium is the first of the #$Carpalia in Humans.")
(comment RunningOnFourLegs "The process of running on four legs.")
(comment CommunionWafer "The wafer of unleavened bread eaten by #$ChristianPerson

as part of a ceremony to commemorate/honor the #$CrucifixionOfJesus and the

#$ResurrectionOfJesus. Instances of #$CatholicPerson take this ceremony very

seriously indeed, and actually believe an alchemical-like #$Transubstantiation

process to occur, while instances of #$ProtestantPerson view the consumption

of #$CommunionWafer as a symbolic event only.")
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure ChangeInUserRights)
(comment AutoFilterMarketCategory "Common things like #$OilFilter GasFilter #$AirFilter ...")
(comment HeatingProcess "A specialization of #$TemperatureChangingProcess.  During each #$HeatingProcess event, the temperature of the #$objectOfStateChange is increased by applying heat to the object.  Any instance of  #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent in which an object temperature is increased is also an instance of this collection.")
(comment Signature "A specialization of #$HandWriting.  The collection of tokens of a person's name, written by his or her own hand.")
(comment Spleen "Stores blood, involved in final destruction of blood cells, and produces lymphocytes.")
(comment instanceAccessoryFor "(#$instanceAccessoryFor ACCESSORY OBJECT) means that  ACCESSORY is designed to be used either as a part of OBJECT or  as a device to be used with or to help care for OBJECT.")
(comment ChowChow "A collection of medium-sized dogs.")
(comment HealthcareOrganization "Each instance of #$HealthcareOrganization is an #$Organization that is primarily or significantly engaged in the #$HealthcareIndustry or whose activities focus on that industry.  All of #$OccupationalSafetyAndHealthAdministration, #$AmericanMedicalAssociation and #$SetonNorthwestHospital are instances of #$HealthcareOrganization.")
(comment Ultralight "The collection of slow light single seat powered flying machines [#$AirTransportationDevice].  No pilot's license is required to fly one, but there are restrictions for use, such as not flying at night, not in clouds, not over town/settlements, not near airports,.  Unpowered ultralight vehicles as defined by the US government are not included.")
(comment PsoasMajor "The #$Collection of all instances of #$PsoasMajor #$Muscle.  The #$PsoasMajor connects the #$LumbarVertebrae to the #$Femur.  Together with the #$Iliacus it forms the IlioPsoas #$Muscle which is the strongest flexor of the #$Hip.  The IlioPsoas is, for example, the main #$Muscle involved in doing a sit up.")
(comment DryingDishes "The collection of dishes drying -- they can dry in the dish washer, by themselves in a dish rack, or they can be dried by hand with a #$DishTowel.")
(disjointWith Resting-Relaxing Vandalism)
(comment AscendingColon "The collection of all ascending colons.  Each element of this collection is the part of the #$LargeIntestine of an #$Animal which adjoins the #$SmallIntestine.")
(comment PlumbingServiceCompany "Companies that provide, as one of their main functions, plumbing services to customers/clients for a fee.")
(comment LoveCalculator "The collection of all programs designed to calculate the romantic compatibility of two #$Persons given as input various types of information about each person.")
(comment Packet "A packet is a small, thin container, usually made of paper.")
(comment sisters "(#$sisters ANIMAL SISTER) means that SISTER is one of ANIMAL's sisters -- a female sibling, related either by birth (sharing one or more of the same biological parents), by marriage (e.g. a step-sister), or by some other social arrangement.")
(comment DecontaminationProcedure "The collection of all activities wherein one tries to decontaminate a person, area, or object that has been exposed to something toxic.")
(disjointWith Skin Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment SatelliteReceiver "#$SatelliteReceiver is a specialization of #$WirelessCommunicationDevice.  It is the kind of device that is capable of receiving satellite transmissions.  Compare this constant to #$SatelliteTransmitter.")
(disjointWith Marsupial Eutheria)
(comment OpenCurlyBracket-TheSymbol "The symbol '{'. Usually used with a #$CloseCurlyBracket-TheSymbol.  This is the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract), not any physical instantiation.")
(comment WindowScreen "A #$WindowPortal may have one of two types of PortalCoverings: #$WindowThePortalCovering or #$WindowScreen.  Both are physical barriers, unlike a #$WindowCovering which blocks light.  A #$WindowScreen is a sheet of screen with a frame around it.  It is often a removable fixture.")
(comment ComputerPrinter-Laser "The collection of non-impact high-resolution printers which use a rotating disk to reflect laser beams onto the paper. When the beam touches the paper, it forms an electrostatic image area which attracts electrically-charged toner (magnetized dry ink powder). The toner is then fixed (heated) onto the paper, forming an image (i.e. text or graphics).")
(comment MedEvacHelicopter "The collection of #$Helicopters used in a military context to transport patients and medical personnel to and between medical facilities. These helicopters also often carry medical equipment.")
(comment TrueSeal "Those #$Seal-Animals that lack external ears.  #$TrueSeals constitute the            #$BiologicalFamily Phocidae.")
(comment ProfessionalServicing "Indicates the actions needed for the recipient to receive some service from a professional provider. Only one of these actions is the actual #$ProfessionalServicing process itself; the recipient must also make an appointment and (via inheritance from even more general scripts) show up for the appointment, pay for the service, etc.")
(comment VentralRamusT7 "The collection of all T7 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT7 and #$DorsalRamusT7 branch from SpinalRootT7.  #$VentralRamusT7 supplies below the #$SeventhRib.")
(comment CremeAnglais "A kind of #$Custard that has some flavoring added to it.")
(comment SeinesBookstall "The collection of parisian bookstalls that are located along the
Seine. They are typically large chest of a mesmerizing dark green color located on the
parapet overhanging both riverbanks of the Seine. Even though pricy, it is
possible to make an honest deal. Doubtlessly, a tourist attraction.")
(comment KillingFn "This function maps #$Collections of #$Organism-Wholes onto the #$KillingByOrganisms which result in instances of those collections dying. For example, (#$KillingFn #$Dog) maps to the set of #$KillingByOrganisms in which a dog is the #$organismKilled.")
(disjointWith LightingDevice ComputationalSystem)
(comment Otoscope "The device used by doctors to look inside a patient's ears and nose.")
(comment BacterialSporeFn "(#$BacterialSporeFn BACTERIUM-TYPE) returns the collection of

all bacteria of the type BACTERIUM-TYPE in their spore form.")
(comment DigitalArtObject "The collection of #$ArtObjects whose primary media (the media in which they were created) is digital.  That is, #$DigitalArtObjects are created 'on screen' using computer technology rather than in more traditional media such as paint, paper, stone, or plaster.")
(comment ElectricShock "When an electric current runs through the body.")
(comment UnauthorizedFileUploadFault "A server program has an #$UnauthorizedFileUploadFault if it

is possible for a remote user to load files onto the server without authentication.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice ControlDevice)
(comment BananaTree "Individual banana trees.")
(comment GhanaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Ghana, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByCustomers PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment GiftBasket "The collection of #$Baskets containing goodies that are usually given as #$Gifts.")
(comment maximalConstraint-Isa "(#$maximalConstraint-Isa PRED N COL) says that the known
maximal constraint for the Nth argument place of PRED is any instance
of COL.  Here, 'maximal constraint' means that typically, the best or
most sensible collection, any instance of which could fill the Nth
argument place, is COL.  The maximal #$isa constraint for a predicate
need not always be determined by its #$argIsa assertions, though
sometimes it will be (when it its not, the maximal #$isa constraint is
determined by the predicates #$typicalArgIsa assertions).  An example
of a predicate for which the #$argIsa assertions do not determine a
maximal #$isa constraint could be, #$primaryFunction, whose #$arg1Isa
is #$SomethingExisting.  This isn't maximal, since this allows one to
construct well-formed instances of #$ELSentence-Assertible by putting
an instance of #$HumanInfant in the arg1 position, and we generally do
not consider infants to be things with a 'primary function' (see the
#$comment on #$primaryFunction), though we *could*.")
(comment Stool-PieceOfFurniture "A seating device with no arms or back")
(disjointWith Undressing MediaTransferEvent)
(comment Prostate "The collection of all #$Prostate #$Glands.  Each instance of this collection is a gland situated adjacent to the urinary bladder (#$Bladder-Urinary) of a male #$Mammal within which the #$EjaculatoryDucts join the #$Urethra.")
(comment DairyProduct "A specialization of #$FoodOrDrink and an instance of #$FoodGroup.  Each instance of #$DairyProduct is a foodstuff that is milk or processed milk.  Important specializations of #$DairyProduct include #$CowsMilk-Product, #$Cheese, #$Butter, and #$IceCream.")
(disjointWith RetailStore ConstructionCompany)
(comment thingIncorporated "(#$thingIncorporated EVT OBJ) says that OBJ is the instance of #$PartiallyTangible that is added during EVT, an instance of #$Incorporation-Physical).")
(disjointWith BicycleLight ChristmasLightString)
(comment HTMLFile "The subcollection of #$ComputerFile-AIS written in the language #$HypertextMarkupLanguage.")
(disjointWith Restaurant-Organization Spa)
(comment FishingLine "A very thin piece of plastic (or thread or metal?) filament used to hold a hook when fishing.")
(comment BonsaiTree "The collection of all miniture #$Bushes or trees [#$Tree-ThePlant] which have been shaped and trimmed into the forms of full-sized trees.")
(comment Oar "The large paddle used to push a boat or raft through the water by hand.  An oar has a blade at exactly one end of the pole.")
(comment PelvicInflammatoryDisease "A collection of infections involving the endometrium and/or fallopian tubes.  These can be primary (spontaneously occurring, usually sexually transmitted) or secondary (occurring after invasive intrauterine surgical procedures).  Many types of #$Bacterium may be the cause of this type of infection, for example, #$EscherichiaColi or Mycoplasma hominis.")
(disjointWith ProjectilePropelling Kissing)
(comment Pincer "Hard grasping hand-like appendage of crustaceans")
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion Leather)
(comment Terrier-Australian "A collection of dogs.")
(disjointWith Secretariat TravelOrganization)
(comment Spandex-Fiber "The collection of all quantities of pure spandex, a synthetic fiber typically used in garments to increase their elasticity.")
(comment MarineOrganism "Organisms which spend most or all of their time immersed in salt water.")
(comment SubScapularis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$SubScapularis #$Muscle.  The #$SubScapularis #$Muscle lies on the ventral side of the #$Scapula, attaching it to the #$Humerus.  The #$SubScapularis #$Muscle is used for medial rotation of the #$Humerus.")
(comment CarvingKnife "A kind of knife used to cut food during its preparation - much sharper than one used during eating.")
(comment PoplitealVein "The collection of all popliteal #$Veins.  The #$PoplitealVein connects at its proximal end to the #$FemoralVein and branches into the #$AnteriorTibialVein  and #$PosteriorTibialVein at its distal end.")
(comment Brie-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Brie, a French cheese with

a white mold crust. Brie becomes more gooey and flavorful as it ages.

It is similar to #$Camembert-Cheese, the main difference being that it comes

is larger thinner wheels.")
(comment MotionDetector "A device that detects motion (within a certain range of energy) and can propagate a signal to indicate that.")
(comment Vulva "The collection of all sets of external female sex organs. The #$Vulva includes the #$Clitoris along with the #$LabiaMinora and the #$LabiaMajora.")
(comment CommercialFishingBoat "A specialization of #$Watercraft-Surface.  Each instance of #$CommercialFishingBoat is a watercraft designed to be used in catching fish or other water-dwelling life for some commercial purpose.  Some instances of #$CommercialFishingBoat are ocean-going craft, while others are used in rivers and lakes.")
(comment BotswanaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Botswana, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PersonalRadio "A subcollection of both #$Radio and #$PersonalAudioPlayer. Instances of #$PersonalRadio convert instances of #$RadioWave into instances of #$AudibleSound, and are small and portable enough to use while jogging.")
(comment Colt "The collection of juvenile #$Horses that are #$MaleAnimals.  A young male horse is a #$Colt at least until he is a year old.  If he is castrated, he becomes a #$Horse-Gelding, and if he is not, he becomes a #$Horse-Stallion.")
(comment typeOfWritingImplementsUsed "the implement this language is typically written with")
(comment IceCreamMaker "The collection of manual or electric icecream makers")
(disjointWith Communicating PhysicalSynthesis)
(comment UnixOS "A specialization of #$OperatingSystem. Each instance of #$UnixOS is an operating system derived from the original #$Unix operating system developed at Bell Labs in the 1960's.  An important specialization of this collection is #$LinuxOS.")
(comment Mantel "The collection of all fireplace mantels.  A mantel is a beam or shelf above the fireplace.  It is usually built in, part of the room, not a moveable piece of furniture.")
(comment WellbutrinSRProduct "An #$AntiDepressant drug product manufactuered by #$GlaxoInc.")
(comment InferiorLobarBronchus "The collection of inferior (lower) lobar bronchi (#$BronchialTubes)  in the #$Lung, each of which supplies air to an #$InferiorLobeOfLung.  It branches off of the left #$MainBronchus or the right #$MainBronchus  (including what, on the right side, is sometimes called the  intermediate bronchus).")
(comment Noodle "Little things made of flour.  We'll assume they are stored dried, and cooked by boiling.")
(comment AgeFn "`(#$AgeFn THING)' denotes the #$age of THING. This function
should generally only be used in temporally qualified contexts.")
(comment PartsFn-Device "#$PartsFn-Device takes as argument any spec of #$PhysicalDevice and returns the collection of parts for devices of that type.  For example, (#$PartsFn-Device #$SubaruCar) returns the collection of all parts for cars made by Subaru, and (#$PartsFn-Device #$VideoCassetteRecorder) returns the collection of all parts for VCRs.")
(disjointWith Travel-TripEvent PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment AntennaCord "The cord that connects the TV to the antenna")
(comment Thesaurus "The collection of all the thesauruses: books that contain information about the antonyms, homonyms, synonyms, of a (usually large) set of words.  Usually they describe other relationships between words as well.")
(comment Beard "Facial hair covering at least the chin.")
(disjointWith WritingImplement Breathalyzer)
(comment SaudiPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$SaudiArabia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment WrinkleRemovingDevice "The class of appliances, including #$ClothesIrons and #$ClothesSteamers, which are intended to be used to remove wrinkles from textiles.")
(comment ChronicFatigueSyndrome "#$ChronicFatigueSyndrome is an #$AilmentCondition characterized by fatigue, general pain, mental fogginess, and often gastro-intestinal problems.  The cause of the disease is unknown.  The clinical community is not fully convinced that it constitutes a genuine illness.")
(comment TrashCompactor-Household "The household appliance that stores and compacts trash")
(disjointWith SportsAction IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment MiddleCerebralArtery "The collection of all middle cerebral arteries.  An individual #$MiddleCerebralArtery is an #$Artery which extends to one side of the #$Brain from the #$CircleOfWillis.  Another name for this is 'Sylvian Artery'.")
(comment Carrot-Foodstuff "Foodstuff from the edible root of the carrot.")
(comment VideoGameSystemType "This is the collection of video game system types. Video game systems can

be typed by brand, model, bit number, etc.")
(comment RollerSkating "The act of moving along by rolling along on the wheels of roller-skates.")
(comment biologicallyMadeBy "The partially tangible ARG1 was produced biologically by the BLO ARG2.  All of a BLO's body parts are #$biologicallyMadeBy that BLO, as are secretions.  This relation is similar to the #$madeBy relation for commercial products.")
(comment BasePairing "#$BasePairing is the collection of #$HydrogenBonding events in which two instances of #$NitrogenBases become chemically bonded to each other via hydrogen bonds. Normally, the  #$NitrogenBases that are paired are complementary (see #$complementaryBases). However, although it occurs infrequently, it is chemically possible for two #$NitrogenBases that are not complementary to become paired. This collection includes all base pairing events, including base pairing error events. See #$ComplementaryBasePairing and #$ComplementaryBasePairingError.")
(comment RadarDetector-AutomobileAccessory "Automobile Radar Detectors")
(comment LatinSmallLetterT "The lowercase letter 't'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$T-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterT.")
(comment ClothesLine "The collection of clothes lines.  The simplest case is just a cord between two points of attachment.  More complicated ones use pulleys.  Clothes may be hung on and supported by the #$ClothesLine to dry by means of a #$ClothesPin.")
(comment DryCough "A subcollection of #$Cough-AilmentCondition, the
#$PhysiologicalConditionType corresponding to dry cough.")
(disjointWith MarkingOnASurface MakingAGesture)
(comment RecordedSoundProduct "#$RecordedSoundProduct is a specialization of  #$AudioRecordedObject, #$PartiallyTangibleProduct and #$PublishedMaterial.  Each instance of #$RecordedSoundProduct is (a particular copy of) a sound recording which is mass-produced -- i.e. it is one of a class of similar recordings with the same information content.")
(comment ComputerProcessor "A specialization of #$ComputerHardwareComponent. Each instance of this collection is a computer processor which is in the shell (part of the #$ComputerMainBox) and contains the #$CentralProcessingUnit.")
(comment GovernmentalOrganization "#$GovernmentalOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$GovernmentalOrganization is an organization that is governmental, either departments of one particular government (e.g., the #$FederalCommunicationsCommission) or confederations or cooperative groups consisting of different governments or  representatives from a number of different governments (e.g., #$OPEC).  Because instances of #$GovernmentalOrganization cannot properly be said to have owners (rather, they have members), they are not instances of #$CommercialOrganization, and, hence, the two collections, #$GovernmentalOrganization and #$CommercialOrganization, are disjoint.")
(comment FountainPen "A pen which uses a specialized nib to transmit the ink to a writing surface. Some fountain pens contain the ink within their body; others contain ink only at the nib when it is dipped into an ink well.")
(comment likesRelationshipToType "(#$likesRelationshipToType AGENT REL COLLECTION) means that AGENT likes to be in the relationship REL to an instance of COLLECTION.")
(comment CookingVessel "Containers used to cook food.")
(comment DorsalRamusT9 "The collection of all T9 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT9 and DorsalRamiT9 branch from SpinalRootT9.  DorsalRamiT9 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment ChilePepper-FreshIngredient "This is the collection of fresh chiles, also called chili peppers. Many, though

not all, chili peppers are #$Hot-Spicy.")
(comment NonPositiveIntegerRange "The collection of #$IntegerExtents which include no #$PositiveIntegers")
(comment TextToSpeechProgram "Software which 'reads' text and produces a speech signal.")
(comment Deck-Ship "The upper surface of a boat upon which people can walk around.")
(disjointWith LevelOfAConstruction FluidReservoir)
(comment Aster "A plant order in the dicot subclass.  includes sunflowers, daisies, etc.")
(comment IndianCitizenOrSubject "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$India, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Cavalier-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of 'Cavalier.'")
(comment AlgonquianLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally northeast and north central")
(comment Hook "A curved or angular piece of metal or other hard substance for catching, pulling, holding or suspending something.")
(comment Blackmail "A specialization of #$Extortion. Each instance of this collection is an event in which one agent extorts another by threatening to reveal information that would harm them.")
(comment Swimming-Surface "Swimming on the surface of the water.")
(comment Pizza "The collection of flat baked pie crusts topped with tomato sauce, cheese, spices, and various other ingredients, including anchovies.")
(comment Applet-ComputerProgram "Applets are small computer programs written in #$JavaProgrammingLanguage. See also #$Servlet-ComputerProgram.")
(comment ResearchOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$ResearchOrganization is an organization that carries out basic or applied research as its main function (or one of its main functions).  A given instance of #$ResearchOrganization may or may not be a commercial, or a governmental, organization.  Examples of #$ResearchOrganizations include  #$UnitedStatesSpaceProgram, Thomas J. Watson Research Laboratory at #$IBMInc, and the Hoover Institute.")
(comment PowerSander "The collection of all power sanders -- devices used for smoothing (usually wood or metal) surfaces")
(comment RunningOnTwoLegs "The process of running on two legs.")
(comment Gun-Portable "A specialization of both #$SmallArm-Weapon and #$PortableObject. Each instance of #$Gun-Portable is a gun light enough for its average user to move easily.")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment CarburetorCleaner "Spray stuff to clean your carburetor.")
(comment BouncingProcess "A process in which an object bounces off of something else.")
(comment Resume "The collection of short (1-4 pages) written #$ConceptualWorks detailing someone's experience, education, and expertise in certain relevant areas.  Usually prepared for use in a job interview.")
(comment SalivaryGland "The collection of all salivary #$Glands.  Instances of this collection are #$internalParts of the head which secrete #$Saliva into the #$Mouth.")
(comment BullMastiff "A collection of large dogs, originally resulting          from a cross between the Mastiff and the Bulldog.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam HealthcareOrganization)
(comment Ultralight-Airplane "The collection of #$Ultralight vehicles in the shape of an airplane.")
(comment Pectineus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Pectineus #$Muscle.  The #$Pectineus flexes and assists adduction of the #$Femur at the #$Hip.")
(comment Wastebasket "The collection of all wastebaskets")
(disjointWith MakingAnOralSound Vandalism)
(comment TransverseColon "The collection of all transverse colons.  Each element of this collection is the central section of the #$LargeIntestine of an #$Animal.")
(comment Pie "A baked pastry shell containing a filling of fruit, meat, or pudding.")
(comment AdvertisingAgency "An organization which designs and organizes advertising and promotional activities for other agents.")
(comment DecoderProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs whose purpose         is to perform an #$IBTRecoding with a #$ComputerFileCopy as its         #$informationOrigin and an #$InformationBearingThing containing         the same information as its #$ibtGenerated. See #$EncoderProgram         for programs going the other direction.")
(comment StripTheContainer "A strip is a disposable foil, plastic and paper container which contains one dose of pills.  Usually the pills are sealed into the package until they are ready to be used.  The container is broken by pressing on the pills hard enough to break the foil.")
(comment SwellingInRegionTypeFn "#$SwellingInRegionTypeFn is a Cyc function that is used to describe swelling in a particular region of the animal's body in which it is found.  (#$SwellingInRegionTypeFn REGION) denotes the collection of the conditions of swollen regions of the body REGION.  Hence, (#$SwellingInRegionTypeFn #$Ankle) would return the collection of all swollen ankle conditions.")
(disjointWith Chest-BodyPart Skin)
(comment nitrogenBaseOf "(#$nitrogenBaseOf NUCL BASE) means that #$NitrogenBase BASE is the nitrogen base of #$Nucleotide NUCL.")
(comment SatelliteCommunicationsEquipment "#$SatelliteCommunicationsEquipment is a specialization of #$WirelessCommunicationDevice.  It is equipment that has components that are capable of transmitting and receiving satellite communications.  Compare this constant to #$SatelliteTransmitter and #$SatelliteReceiver.")
(comment OpenSquareBracket-TheSymbol "The symbol '['. Usually used with an #$CloseSquareBracket-TheSymbol. This refers to the abstract character (see #$Character-Abstract), not any particular physical instantiation.")
(comment HotWaterHeater "The device which heats up water for use in showers, etc.")
(comment CD-RDrive "The collection of CDR-Drives, or CD-recordable drives which can write to recordable CompactDiscs as well as read them")
(comment CommunicationDevice "The subcollection of #$PhysicalDevice that contains all instances that are intended to be the #$deviceUsed in a #$Communicating (one way or bidirectional). Examples include #$RadioReceiver, #$Telephone, etc.")
(comment GrassTurf "Sheetlike clumps of dirt held together by the roots of mobs of turf grass blades.  These grass blades stick out from the dirt like human hair does cut in the crew cut style. Grown not as a crop but to serve as ground cover, as for a golf course or football field.")
(comment GenitofemoralNerve-FemoralBranch "The collection of all femoral branches of #$GenitofemoralNerves.  The #$GenitofemoralNerve branches into the #$GenitofemoralNerve-GenitalBranch and the #$GenitofemoralNerve-FemoralBranch.  The femoral branch supplies the #$Skin anterior to the upper part of the femoral triangle.")
(comment CremeCaramel "A kind of #$Custard that is baked and topped with caramel.")
(comment CycLReformulatorRule "The subcollection of #$CycLAssertions which express reformulation rules to be used by

the #$CycLReformulator.  Even though the reformulator may treat these as

rules, they are GAFs in the KB.  Each #$CycLReformulatorRule must

have a #$CycLReformulationRulePredicate as its predicate.

They are relevant in the microtheory in which they are

asserted, and in specMts of that microtheory unless overridden.

For meta-directives, the convention is that the #$CycLReformulatorRule

argument comes last.")
(comment eventTypeCausedDeathOf "(#$eventTypeCausedDeathOf EV-TYPE ORG) means that ORG's death, where ORG is an instance of #$Organism-Whole, occured as a consequence of an event that is an instance of EV-TYPE.")
(disjointWith ConsumableProduct ComputationalSystem)
(comment TongueDepressor "The stick that a doctor uses to push down a patient's tongue while looking down their throat.")
(comment CookBook "This is the collection of instances of #$Book-CW which contain recipes. (See #$Recipe-CW.)")
(comment Sighing "Exhaling longer, with more air than normal, often with a soft noise; usually connotes emotion, such as relief or melancholy.")
(comment PlaintextApplicationPasswordFileFault "A program has a #$PlaintextApplicationPasswordFileFault if
it stores passwords for #$ApplicationAccounts specific for that
program in a plaintext file.")
(disjointWith Weapon ControlDevice)
(comment ChestnutTree "The collection of chestnut trees.  Deciduous, ornamental and timber trees, native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere. Their burlike fruits contain two or three edible nuts.")
(comment LesothoPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Lesotho, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment FlannelCloth "A soft, lightweight cloth made of cotton or wool.")
(comment KeyLock "Locks that must be opened by keys.")
(disjointWith Collecting MediaTransferEvent)
(comment VasDeferens "The collection of all vas deferns vessels.  An individual member of this collection is one of two #$AnatomicalVessels that transmit #$SpermCells from the #$Testicle to the #$EjaculatoryDuct (and #$SeminalVesicle) on the same side of the body in a male #$Vertebrate.")
(comment EdiblePartFn "The Cyc function #$EdiblePartFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to a set of tangible objects OBJ-TYPE, (#$EdiblePartFn OBJ-TYPE) represents the collection of all the edible parts of objects of OBJ-TYPE.  This collection includes any #$EdibleStuff (i.e., edible by humans or koalas or whatever the current microtheory is talking about) that is part of instances of OBJ-TYPE.  To represent only parts that humans eat, we may restrict the #$resultGenl to a specialized subcollection of #$FoodOrDrink defined in #$HumanActivitiesMt or other appropriate microtheory.  Examples: the collection (#$EdiblePartFn (#$FruitFn #$AppleTree)) includes the skin and flesh of all apples, but not --- in the #$HumanActivitiesMt --- the instances of #$Stem or #$Seed found in them; the collection (#$EdiblePartFn #$Egg-Chickens) includes the yolks and whites of chicken eggs, but does not  --- in the #$HumanActivitiesMt ---  include any instances of #$Eggshell.  Because of cultural or philosophical preferences and prohibitions about food, exactly what parts are edible may differ in different human cultural microtheories; e.g., in a FundamentalistJewish or FundamentalistIslamic cultural #$Microtheory, the function call (#$EdiblePartFn #$Pig) would return NIL; in a vegan #$Microtheory, even (#$EdiblePartFn #$Animal) would return NIL.")
(comment subOrgs-OnlyDuringOperation "(#$subOrgs-OnlyDuringOperation SUPER SUB) means that SUB is

an organization subordinate to the organization SUPER for a very short

term -- during a particular task, trial or battle, for example, or in a specific field operation.  This kind of relationship is often established between units in the course of military field operations.  This relationship is deemed very temporary, more so than for #$subOrgs-Temporary.  (See also #$subOrgs-Permanent.)")
(comment ProjectileSlug-Ball "The collection of #$ProjectileSlug-Bullets that contain a slug of antimony-hardened lead.  This is the typical bullet.")
(comment MSWindowsOperatingSystem "#$MSWindowsOperatingSystem is a specialization of #$OperatingSystem.  It is the collection of all operating systems developed by Microsoft with windows technology.")
(disjointWith RentalShop Restaurant-Organization)
(comment PocketOfGarment "The collection of garment pockets")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess IBTGeneration)
(comment LateralDirection "The general direction of sideways (toward the sides of the body, away from the midline) in or near an object with #$AnimalBodyShape.")
(comment ShapedPlant "The collection of all #$Bushes or trees [#$Tree-ThePlant] that have been intentionally shaped by people.  This collection includes instances of #$Topiary, #$BonsaiTrees, and trimmed #$Hedges.")
(comment LongBow "The kind of bow used in archery.")
(comment acceptableTreatmentForMaleficiaryType "This predicate is used to represent
 the relationship between kinds of #$MedicalTreatmentEvents and
 the kinds of #$Organism-Wholes that, because of some
 affliction or other, need to undergo them.  For example,
 (#$acceptableTreatmentForMaleficiaryType #$Chemotherapy
   #$Cancer #$Person) says that chemotherapy is a
 common treatment for people with cancer.")
(disjointWith LegMovement Kissing)
(comment Tongue "The movable fleshy organ in the mouth, used for tasting, moving food around, and, in human beings, for producing speech")
(comment LawnMower-Riding "The collection of rider mowers; i.e., those which the user rides on top of while operating. These mowers are powered by fossil fuel.")
(comment Terrier-AmericanStaffordshire "A collection of medium-sized dogs, also called the AmStaff.")
(comment PuertoRicanPerson "A person who is a citizen of PuertoRican")
(disjointWith ChamberOfCommerce TravelOrganization)
(comment SpandexCloth "The collection of all pieces of cloth containing #$Spandex-Fiber.")
(comment AdductorLongus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$AdductorLongus #$Muscle.  The #$AdductorLongus adducts and assists flexion and medial rotation of the #$Femur at the #$Hip.")
(comment Pliers "Hand tool made of two piecesw of (usually) metal, connected with a rotating joint so that closing one side with the hand closes the grasping jaws at the other end.")
(comment GreatSaphenousVein "The collection of all great saphenous veins.  The great saphenous vein is the longest vein in the body.  The proximal end connects to the femoral vein just below the pelvis and the distal end connects to the dorsal venous arch.")
(comment Appenzeller-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Appenzeller, 

a gruyere-like cheese from Switzerland.")
(comment ExerciseBike "This is a type of exercise equipment designed to give the user a simulated bicycle-riding experience.  This collection is not a spec of #$Bicycle, because exercise bikes are not bicycles: they often have only one wheel, and they are not intended for transportation purposes.")
(comment BiologicalProductionOfFn "(#$BiologicalProductionOfFn TYPE) returns the collection of all

 instances of #$BiologicalProductionEvent whose #$outputsCreateds are instances of TYPE.")
(comment Areola "The collection of all dark rings of #$Skin surrounding a nipple (#$Nipple-AnimalBodyPart) on a #$Teat of a #$Mammal.")
(disjointWith Rowboat CommercialFishingBoat)
(comment Seed "A specialization of #$PlantBLO.  Each instance of #$Seed is a small nodule or granule consisting of a young angiosperm and its protective container during the early (zygotic and embryonic stages) of development.  If conditions are right, instances of #$Seed will grow to become adult plants.")
(comment NigerianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Nigeria, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PersonalMP3Player "A subcollection of #$PersonalDigitalAudioPlayer. Instances of #$PersonalMP3Player are designed to convert instances of #$MP3File (not stored on instances of #$CompactDisc-Generic) into instances of #$AudibleSound.")
(comment Muskmelon "The collection of melons belonging to

the gourd family, including, e.g. cantaloupe and honeydew")
(comment ConsonantalAlphabeticWriting "writing with, primarily, a one-to-one correspondence between each significantly different CONSONANT of a language and a specific letter -- or, letters, where form variations such as upper and lower case or internal vs. final letters are involved.")
(comment ElectricSkillet "The collection of electric skillets -- different enough from Skillet to warrant being a separate collection.")
(comment CluckingSound "The collection of clucking sounds made by #$Poultry animals.")
(comment arg5NotGenl "(#$arg5NotGenl REL COL) means that nothing given as the fifth argument to the #$Relation REL may be a spec of the #$Collection COL.")
(comment BusinessComputerProgram "This is the collection of programs that were designed for use in business, though they may also be used in other ways. A notable specialization is #$ECommerceProgram.")
(comment Threshold "The part of a doorway that is on the ground, often a distinct board or strip of metal.")
(comment AdalatCCProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by Bayer Corporation.")
(comment DetectableOdorStrength "Odor strengths which are strong enough to be detected.")
(comment VisceralPleura "The collection of visceral pleurae, the inner enclosing  sheath membranes directly surrounding and attached to the #$Lungs, in the #$ChestCavity, within the #$ParietalPleura  in the #$PleuralCavity.  In human being there are separate right and  left VisceralPleurae.")
(comment FettuciniNoodle "A long flat narrow noodle.")
(comment ActionFigure-Toy "The collection of action figure toys.")
(disjointWith AsexualReproductionEvent SexualReproductionEvent)
(comment SewingScissors "Scissors used for cutting textile fabric and thread.")
(comment BalanceSheet "A document detailing an agent's assets and liabilities.")
(comment Moustache "Hair just above a man's upper lip")
(disjointWith CircuitTester WritingImplement)
(comment Setter-TheDog "A collection of large bird dogs.")
(comment DjiboutiPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Djibouti, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment AutomaticCamera "The collection of cameras which could be said

to be 'automatic' in terms of focus, exposure duration, flash, etc.. 

They are also commonly referred to as 'point and shoot' cameras.")
(comment SleepApnea "#$SleepApnea is an #$AilmentCondition characterized by cessation of breathing during sleep.  Subtypes of #$SleepApnea include obstructive sleep apnea and central sleep apnea.")
(comment TypewriterKey "The button having a certain function on a typewriter keyboard")
(disjointWith Undressing IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment AorticValve "The collection of all aortic semilunar #$Valves.  Each instance of this collection is #$Valve at the #$Portal from the left #$VentricleOfHeart into the #$Aorta which prevents #$Blood from passing back from the aorta into the #$Heart.")
(comment Spinach-Foodstuff "The green leafy vegetable.")
(comment seniorExecutives "The predicate #$seniorExecutives is used to identify the upper-level managers in a particular organization.  (#$seniorExecutives ORG PERSON) means PERSON is an employee with a high executive position in the #$Organization ORG.  #$seniorExecutives relates an organization to the people who hold its principal corporate offices (CEO, President, etc.) and also positions like Chief of Staff, General, Admiral, Chief Corporate Counsel, Managing Partner, Chief Scientist, Chief Engineer, etc.")
(comment AudioDriver "A piece of software which acts as an interface between a audio card and an operating system. The audio device driver usually presents a standard interface to the operating system, allowing the audio hardware to be manipulated in a standard way.")
(comment InLineSkating "The act of moving along by #$RollingOnASurface on the #$Wheels of in-line #$RollerSkates.")
(comment BiologicalToxin "A #$ToxicSubstance produced by some #$Organism-Whole. An example is the toxin produced by the bacterium Clostridium botulinum; the toxin is responsible for the cluster of effects seen in #$Botulism.")
(comment Credential "A specialization of #$PropositionalInformationThing.  Each instance of #$Credential is specific information about one #$SocialBeing (q.v.), provided by another #$SocialBeing.  The information content of a credential consists of favorable, enabling, or empowering propositional declarations.  Although each instance of #$Credential is wholly intangible, instances of #$Credential usually have some associated #$TextualMaterial (e.g. a diploma associated with a college degree, a driver's license).  A credential may certify that the holder (i.e. the subject of the credential) has a particular skill (e.g. legal bar certification or the ability to drive); has completed certain training (e.g. GED schooling or satisfying PhD requirements); is allowed to do a certain thing (e.g. a travel visa or permission slip); and so on.  See also the predicate #$issuesCredential.")
(comment FormalProductType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$FormalProductType is a collection of products (i.e. a subcollection of #$Product (q.v.)),  all of which conform to the same standardized product specification  (or \"form\").  In Western-style capitalistic markets, instances of  #$FormalProductType are often associated with a particular brand name  (and perhaps model), since competing providers of products design them  to be distinctive.  For example, the collection  #$InternalCombustionEngine is not an instance of #$FormalProductType,  but a specific collection of engines manufactured by (e.g.) Mazda might  be.  On the service side, the collection #$HairCuttingEvent is not a  formal product-type, but a subcollection of hair stylings for men (e.g.  at a particular salon) might be.")
(comment StereoSystem "A collection of audio systems. Each instance of StereoSystem is capable of reproducting 2-channel sound.")
(comment AnimalBLO "A specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject that includes all living animals, body parts of living animals, and body regions of living animals.  #$AnimalBLO is thus the \"union\" (see #$collectionUnion) of #$Animal, #$AnimalBodyPart, and #$AnimalBodyRegion (qq.v.).")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterU "The capital letter 'U'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$U-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterU.")
(comment WashingDishesByMachine "Turning dirty dishes into clean dishes, by using a dishwasher to wash, rinse, and sometimes dry them.")
(comment FatigueCondition "The #$PhysiologicalCondition in which an #$Organism-Whole is suffering from pathologic fatigue.  This is to be characterized by a continuous, sustended #$LevelOfExhaustion caused by some other
#$AilmentCondition.  Do not confuse with either the collection of #$Events
during which somebody is tired following an effort or at the other extreme
the #$ChronicFatigueSyndrome.  #$FatigueCondition is intended to describe
the #$LevelOfExhaustion of an #$Organism-Whole suffering from a
underlying, longlasting #$AilmentCondition such as certain #$Infections.")
(disjointWith Paying CapturingAnAnimal)
(disjointWith RearWheelDrive FourWheelDrive)
(comment ComputerDisplay "A specialization of #$ComputerOutputDevice. Each instance of this collection is a device with which computer output is displayed visually. An important specialization is #$ComputerMonitor-VideoKind, but see also #$DataProjector.")
(comment QuasiGovernmentalOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations which are neither strictly governmental nor strictly private in nature and character.  For example, #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation is an instance of #$Organization that was created by a specific Congressional charter and, as such, is exempt from some governmental regulations that apply to private sector, publicly held companies (e.g., filings under the Securities and Exchange Act).  #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation is, however, subject to other regulations that do not apply to strictly private sector organizations (e.g., the Federal Housing Enterprises Financial Safety and Soundness Act of 1992).  #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganizations may or may not engage in profit-making activities.  Not all instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitution are #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganization; in fact, most are not.  #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganizations, like #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation, were specifically contemplated by the chartering organization (in the case of #$FederalHomeLoanMortgageCorporation, the #$USCongress).  Many instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitutions (e.g., instances of #$NationalBank) were not specifically contemplated by the chartering organization; rather, the generic idea of such institutions was contemplated and provided for by statute.")
(comment PlacingSensoryOrganToSenseThrough "The collection of all #$Actions in which the #$Animal performing the action places a sensory organ against or near something in order to sense some other thing through the item it is being placed up against.  Examples include listening or peeking through a keyhole, looking through a microscope, placing ones face against a window to see through [#$PressingFaceAgainstToSee], listening for a train by putting ones ear against the rail, sniffing at a jar to determine its contents, and feeling a bag to determine what is inside.  This collection does not include actions taken to sense the object being moved up against.")
(comment StoveTopCookingPot "A container that maximizes volume rather than heated surface, used to hold food for cooking over a fire or stove.")
(comment SubClavianNerve "The collection of all subclavian #$Nerves.  A #$SubClavianNerve branches off of the superior trunk of the #$BrachialPlexus on its side of the body.  This nerve #$innervates the #$Subclavius.")
(comment ChilePepper-DriedIngredient "This is the collection

 of whole dried chile peppers.")
(comment available-Generic "(#$available-Generic AGENT OBJECT) means that OBJECT

is available (possibly in a metaphorical sense) for AGENT. Example:

(#$available-Generic #$Fred Sally'sCopyOfGormenhast) or

(#$available-Generic #$Sally #$Fred).  The former means that

the book denoted by Sally'sCopyOfGormenhast is available to Fred

(presumably for reading) and the latter means that #$Fred is available

to #$Sally (presumably for sex). The \"presumably\"s above indicate

presuppositions.")
(comment PositiveIntegerExtent "The collection of #$IntegerExtents which include only #$PositiveIntegers")
(comment SpokenLanguageCommunicationProgram "Software which forms part of a natural language system where speech is either understood or generated.")
(comment Boom-Arm "A boom is a long arm which is used to reach hard to reach places with equipment or people.  The long, extensible part of a crane is called a boom.  Film and video production often uses microphones on a boom, to get them out over the action without having them show up on the film.")
(comment MaintenanceOfDataBase "#$MaintenanceOfDataBase is the collection whose members are all and only those instances of #$MaintainingSomething in which the entity maintained is a data base.")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedRegionOfTransportationDevice FluidReservoir)
(comment Ragweed "A plant order in the dicot subclass.")
(comment MarshallIslandsPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$MarshallIslands-TheNation, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Club-TheSuit "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which are clubs.")
(comment Protozoan "The collection of protozoa; a subcollection of #$SingleCellOrganism.  Instances of #$Protozoan are also instances of #$EukaryoticCell.  Subcollections include #$Amoeba and many others.  Protozoa lack cell walls made of cellulose.  Many protozoa are motile, using pseudopoda, cilia, or flagella to move.  Some cause diseases in larger organisms.  The class #$Protozoan is an instance of #$BiologicalSubkingdom in many classification systems, sometimes placed under the #$ProtistaKingdom.")
(comment HamiticLanguageFamily "Currently, languages spoken throughout northern and mostly eastern Africa")
(comment SnapTheFastener "Any kind of fastening that closes or locks with a click; consists of two parts of which one snaps into the other.")
(comment SuckingOnSomethingInMouth "A collection of events.  Each element of #$SuckingOnSomethingInMouth is an act in which an animal sucks something in its mouth.  The object sucked may or may not be ingested.  This might involve using suction created by the mouth to move something, including drinking with a straw, an infant's sucking milk from breast or bottle, a motorist (unwisely) siphoning gasoline.  In other cases, such as an infant sucking on a pacifier, there is no (significant) translocation.")
(comment localEMailAddressText "The local email address of an entity, whose email server host is implied by the context.  This address consists only of the name portion and does not include the @ symbol nor host name.")
(comment JavaVirtualMachine "#$JavaVirtualMachine is a specialization of #$Interpreter-Computers. Instances of this collection interpret programs

(instances of #$Applet-ComputerProgram and #$Servlet-ComputerProgram) that are written in #$JavaProgrammingLanguage.")
(disjointWith Organization NaturalTangibleStuff)
(comment NaturalSponge "Collection of cleaning tools that are derived from the skeletons of marine organisms of phylum Porifera.")
(comment EvergreenPlant "A specialization of #$Plant-Woody.  Each instance of #$EvergreenPlant is a plant that retains its leaves or needles throughout all the seasons of the year.  See also the collection #$DeciduousPlant.")
(comment PieFn "This function takes a set of ingredient-types and produces
the collection of pies with that filling.")
(comment BodilyFunctionEvent "A specialization of both #$AnimalActivity and #$PhysiologicalProcess.  Each specialization of #$BodilyFunctionEvent is a type of action done by an animal that can be (and often is) done without the doer's conscious volition.  Specializations of #$BodilyFunctionEvent include #$Breathing, #$Swallowing, and #$DigestionEvent.  If an instance of #$BodilyFunctionEvent involves the doer moving all or part of its body, either volitionally or as a reflex, it is also an instance of #$BodyMovementEvent.")
(comment GinglymusJoint "An #$GinglymusJoint is a #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart in
which the bones are #$hingedTo each other.")
(comment ProjectileWeapon "A specialization of #$Weapon.  Each instance of #$ProjectileWeapon is a weapon that is thrown, hurled, or launched at its target.  Notable specializations of #$ProjectileWeapon include #$Arrow, #$ProjectileSlug-Bullet, and #$Missile. See also the related collection #$ProjectileLauncher.")
(comment GasCap "A specialization of #$PortalCovering. Each instance of #$GasCap is a device designed to cover the portal leading to an automobile's gas tank.")
(comment frequencyOfWave "(#$frequencyOfWave WAVE FREQ) means that the #$WavePropagation event WAVE consists of waves that occur at intervals of FREQ.  FREQ is a measure of #$Frequency generally expressed as cycles per unit of time; frequency of electromagnetic radiation is standardly measured in #$Hertz.")
(comment Pamphlet "A collection of #$InformationBearingThings.  They are generally small unbound books, usually < 48 pages, their physical size smaller than normal hardback books.")
(comment LargeIntestine "Large intestine")
(comment GardeningTool "A collection of tools.  An instance of #$GardeningTool is a tool (not limited to hand tools) which is used in gardening.  This includes elements of the collections #$Hoe, #$Rake, #$PruningShears, #$PruningSaw, and more.   Note that types of tools which are used in much more general contexts are not specifically included here as subsets -- e.g., #$Shovel.  They are likely to have subsets worth distinguishing which ARE also subsets of #$GardeningTool.   Note that a particular physical object might be a #$GardeningTool even if other members of the same class generally aren't; e.g., a soup spoon that you use for digging holes for plants in your garden one day is a #$GardeningTool that day.")
(comment Briard "A collection of large sheepdogs.")
(comment nationalLanguage "(#$nationalLanguage NAT LANG) means that LANG is officially recognized by the political region NAT as a national language. A country may have more than one #$nationalLanguage.")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization InsuranceOrganization)
(comment Ultralight-Helicopter "The collection of #$Ultralight vehicles in the shape of a helicopter.")
(comment GluteusMinimus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$GluteusMinimus #$Muscle.  The #$GluteusMinimus rotates and abducts the #$Femur.  It works in concert with the #$GluteusMedius.")
(comment Dresser-PieceOfFurniture "Pieces of furniture found in bedrooms, used for storing clothes, having drawers.")
(disjointWith RudeAction SociabilityBasedAction)
(comment Cecum "The collection of all ceca.  The #$Cecum (also 'caecum')is located at the proximal end of the #$LargeIntestine, situated below the #$IleoCecalValve.  The #$Appendix-OrganPart arises from the #$Cecum.")
(comment BoiledEgg "An egg which has been boiled.")
(comment Bookstore "A local (one site) organization that sells books.")
(comment EncoderProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs whose purpose         is to perform an #$IBTRecoding with an #$InformationBearingThing         as its #$informationOrigin and a #$ComputerFileCopy containing the         same information as its #$fileCopyCreated. See #$DecoderProgram         for programs going the other direction.")
(comment Diaphragm-Contraceptive "The collection of all contraceptive diaphragms.  The #$primaryFunction of an instance of this collection is to serve as a barrier to #$SpermCells in the #$Vagina entering the #$Cervix on the way to the #$Uterus.  Such a use is a #$BirthControlEvent.")
(comment iboCreated "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$IBOCreation to instances of #$InformationBearingObject. (#$iboCreated CREATION IBO) means that the tangible information-bearing object IBO is created in the event CREATION.  For example, my copy of today's morning newspaper was created during the previous night's paper-publishing event. If the \"information-bearing object\" generated by CREATION is not a physical object (i.e. an instance of #$PartiallyTangible), use the less specific predicate #$ibtGenerated.")
(disjointWith Mouth Skin)
(comment DiacriticSymbol "The collection of all abstract diacritic symbols, such as the umlaut and the hacek. Instances are abstract, mental, linguistic objects, not marks on paper or the like. Cf. #$DiacriticMark for the collection of concrete manifestations of these symbols.")
(comment MechanicalButton "A button which will make something happen when pressed.  This can include manual typewriter keys, buttons on the armrests in airplanes, buttons on some doorbells, etc. Not electrical (see #$ElectricalButton).")
(comment SpaceStation "The collection of spacecraft intended to remain in orbit for a relatively long period of time, with personnel being transported between #$PlanetEarth and the space station via a #$SpaceShuttle or similar vehicle.")
(comment Brush "The collection of all brushes")
(comment VentralRamusC8 "The collection of all C8 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC8 and #$DorsalRamusC8 branch from SpinalRootC8.  #$VentralRamusC8 supplies the #$BrachialPlexus.")
(comment Custard "A sweet dessert made with milk and eggs. Custard usually has a thick, smooth consistency.")
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice ComputationalSystem)
(comment ElectricWheelchair "The type of wheelchair that has an electric motor which powers its movement.")
(comment BacterialSporeGermination "A collection of events. During each #$BacterialSporeGermination, a bacterial spore [see #$Spore-DormantBacterium] germinates to a single #$VegetativeCell. These complex events may occur once spores have found suitable environment for germination.")
(comment AirRespiration "A collection of activities constituting a natural #$PhysiologicalFunction; #$AirRespiration is the collection of all #$Respiration events in which an organism trades some of the carbon dioxide in its tissues for oxygen from the atmosphere.")
(comment SoftwareSuite "The collection of computer programs that consist of several large programs bundled together.  Examples of the collection include #$MSOffice and #$MSBackOffice.")
(disjointWith HumanOccupationConstruct ControlDevice)
(comment CinnamonTree "tree whose bark is the spice cinnamon.  Laurel family")
(comment MagnifyingGlass "The collection of magnifying glasses. This collection includes hand-held

magnifying devices with a glass or glass-like lens which magnify the

images of objects about 2x. It excludes every sort of microscope.")
(comment Padlock "Locks that have a loop.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent MediaTransferEvent)
(comment CoronaryValve "The collection of all coronary #$Valves.  Each instance of this collection is #$Valve at the #$Portal from the #$CoronarySinus into the right #$AuricleOfHeart which prevents #$Blood from passing out of the auricle into the #$Vein.")
(comment FoodComposite "This is the collection of food items that have been prepared and which contain two or more ingredients. It includes almost anything that is served as a dish at a meal. #$FoodComposite needn't be cooked, nor do the ingredients have to form a #$Mixture.  The collection excludes beverages, and is thus a proper spec of #$EdibleStuffComposite.")
(comment subOrgs-Permanent "(#$subOrgs-Permanent SUPER SUB) means that SUB is an organization subordinate to SUPER in an organizational hierarchy, that this relation has

obtained for some time, and that it is likely to obtain for the

foreseeable future.  For example, the US Air Force is a

#$subOrgs-Permanent of the United States Armed Forces.")
(disjointWith Wheelbarrow BabyCarriage)
(comment PrivilegeEscalationProgram "The collection of all instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW which, when executed on some instance of #$Computer, creates a #$UserAccount (typically a #$RootAccount or #$AdministratorAccount) with a #$Username and #$Password-Computer already belonging to some instance of #$UserAccount on that machine.  That is, executing an instance of #$PrivilegeEscalationProgram on a machine will create a #$UserAccount giving the user superuser privileges on that macine.  Note that these programs are often very simple batch files and may be written by any competent programmer.")
(disjointWith MetalWorkingShop Restaurant-Organization)
(comment Daggerboard "A fin-like boat part which helps provide resistance to sideways motion.  When in use, the daggerboard is `sheathed'--i.e. inserted through a hole in the bottom of the boat so that it extends down into the water.  It should be `unsheathed' or raised in shallow water.  It is not necessary when sailing downwind, but it is necessary when sailing close-hauled or reaching (i.e. upwind or sideways to the wind).  The hole through which the daggerboard is sheathed is above the water-line, so that removing the daggerboard does not cause the boat to sink.")
(comment BiologicalSuperfamily "The collection of biological taxonomic subdivisions below #$BiologicalOrder (or #$BiologicalSuborder)           and above #$BiologicalFamily.")
(disjointWith ProgrammingAComputer Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment lateralTo "(#$lateralTo OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 lies in the #$LateralDirection of OBJ-2, when viewed in the frame of reference of the object with #$AnimalBodyShape (often, a #$Person) that they are located in.  Note that OBJ-2 is therefore medial to OBJ-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `medial to'.  OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.")
(comment hasUserAccount "(#$hasUserAccount AGENT ACCOUNT) means that AGENT has been assigned a valid username and password for ACCOUNT.")
(comment Hay "Cut and dried herbage (e.g., grass, clover, alfalfa) used as animal feed.")
(comment ChampagneBottle "The collection of bottles in which champagne is packaged and stored.")
(comment LookingForSomething-AcquaintedWith "This is the subcollection of #$LookingForSomething-Definite consisting of cases in which the reason the searcher believes there is exactly one thing satisfying the #$searchCriterion-Definite is that s/he believes s/he has been acquainted with the thing sought. Being acquainted in this sense means having been in (direct) perceptual contact with the thing and being familiar enough with it to allow future identification in similar and normal circumstances.")
(disjointWith TakingAStep AquaticBodyMovement)
(comment Heart "The collection of all hearts.  A #$Heart is an #$Organ that pumps blood throughout the body of an #$Animal.")
(comment ArbitraryDestinationPortFault "#$ArbitraryDestinationPortFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if, when opening a communication link with a server running it, an attacker can open a connection to a port of the attacker's choosing on a machine that may not be the originating client.  See also #$VulnerableToBounceAttack.")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact Leather)
(comment Basenji "A collection of short-haired, medium-sized dogs.  Each member of this breed is also  a sighthound.")
(comment BritishAntarcticTerritoryPerson "A person who is an BritishAntarcticTerritory resident")
(disjointWith Trust-LegalEntity TravelOrganization)
(comment Spear "The collection of all spears. Instances of #$Spear consist of a long, slender shaft with a sharp point, designed to be thrown or otherwise launched at an adversary or target.")
(comment AdductorMagnus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$AdductorMagnus #$Muscle.  The #$AdductorMagnus adducts and assists flexion and medial rotation of the #$Femur at the #$Hip.  Posterior fibers(from the ischial tuberosity assist extension of the femur.  A gap in the #$AdductorMagnus allows passage of the #$FemoralArtery and #$FemoralVein.")
(comment Forceps "A hand tool made of two much-longer-than-wide, almost-flat pieces of springy metal attached at one end with flat sides together so that, while not in use, there's a space between the two pieces at the grasping end.  It's used to grasp objects by squeezing the two pieces together.")
(comment FemoralVein "The collection of all femoral #$Veins.  The #$FemoralVein passes from the #$Pelvis down to the #$Knee.  The proximal end of the #$FemoralVein connects to the #$ExternalIliacVein.  The distal end of the #$FemoralVein connects to the #$PoplitealVein.  The #$FemoralVein drains the deep structures of the #$Thigh.")
(comment BlueCheese "This is the collection of all instances of blue cheese. A blue cheese is

a soft cheese shot through with streaks of bluish or greenish-blue mold.

Blue cheeses are generally very flavorful, and usually made with cow's

milk, although the most famous blue cheese, #$Roquefort-Cheese, is made

with sheep's milk.")
(comment MIDIFile "The collection of computer files containing digitally encoded musical sounds.")
(comment Telescope "Device using lenses and/or mirrors to collect, amplify, focus, and magnify light waves from distant sources.")
(comment authorOfPublication-IBT "(#$authorOfPublication-IBT AUTHOR BOOK_COPY) means that AUTHOR wrote the #$ConceptualWork which is instantiated in the #$InformationBearingThing, BOOK_COPY.")
(disjointWith CommercialFishingBoat Raft)
(comment PerennialPlant "The collection of all #$Plants that live for more than one growing season.")
(comment BrazilianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Brazil, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PersonalMiniDiscPlayer "A subcollection of both #$PersonalAudioPlayer and #$MiniDiscPlayer. #$PersonalMiniDiscPlayers are devices which read and play music from #$MiniDiscs, and are small and compact enought that they can be used while jogging.")
(comment IdeographicWriting "pictorial characters used in writing primarily represent concepts/things")
(comment ElectricCanOpener "The collection of electric can openers -- different enough from manual can openers to warrant a separate collection.")
(comment BleatingSound "The collection of bleating or baah-ing sounds made by #$Sheep or #$Goats.")
(disjointWith VoluntaryBodyMovement Synthesis-Generic)
(comment DoorStep "A step found right before a doorway.")
(comment CardizemSRProduct "A #$CalciumChannelBlocker drug product manufactuered by Hoechst Marion Roussel.")
(comment MiddleLobeOfLung "The collection of middle major lobes of #$Lungs in  #$AirBreathingVertebrates.  In human beings, it includes only the  right middle lobes (i.e., for the right lung), since the normal human  left lung has no middle lobe.")
(comment LasagnaNoodle "A long flat wide noodle.")
(comment AgeAtTimeFn "`(#$AgeAtTimeFn THING DATE)' denotes the #$age that THING
has/had at TIME.")
(comment LawnSprinkler "This collection includes all instances of individual sprinklers used to water lawns and gardens. See also #$SprinklerSystem.")
(comment TVAntenna " The antenna that allows TVs to recieve TV signals")
(comment GeneralLedger-Document "A document with comprehensive records of an agent's financial status, containing a summarized entry for each subsidiary account's status (e.g. Accounts Payable).")
(comment Fur "Hair on non-human mammals")
(comment WritingImplement "#$WritingImplement is a specialization of #$StationeryProduct and #$HandTool.  Each instance of #$WritingImplement is a hand-held tool which is intended to be primarily used, by a person, for writing.  Specializations include the collections #$Chalk-WritingImplement and #$WritingPen (but not #$Typewriter).")
(comment LabradorRetriever "A collection of medium-sized dogs with short, thick fur.")
(comment ScottishPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Scotland, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment BabyFeedingDevice "The collection of all #$PhysicalDevices that are used to aid in the feeding of #$HumanInfants and #$HumanToddlers.")
(comment Apnea "#$Apnea is a specialization of the #$AilmentCondition
collection for cases characterized by cessation of breathing. Subtypes
of #$Apnea include #$SleepApnea and apnea during feeding. Since sleep
apnea is the most common case, usage of #$Apnea should be restricted
to the generic interpretation, such as in medical texts.")
(comment Rake "A hand tool used for moving materials such as plant parts and soil.  Comprised of a long handle and a head with a row of tines or prongs.")
(comment Cucumber-Foodstuff "Foodstuff derived from the fruit of the cucumber plant; for example, sliced cucumber in a salad.")
(comment ReferenceComputerProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are

intended for reference purposes (e.g. encyclopedia, thesaurus etc.).")
(disjointWith ApplianceStore AutoDealership)
(comment PolishingShoes "Making the uppers of shoes shiny by rubbing them with polish and a shoe brush.")
(comment Amoeba "A collection of #$Protozoan distinguyished by having no       definite form and consisting of a mass of protoplasm containing one or more nuclei surrounded by a flexible       outer membrane. It moves by means of pseudopods. Some instances are instances of #$ParasiticOrganism.")
(comment CorrectionFluid "The collection of fluids which are intended to be used to cover over misprints so that they can be retyped or rewritten. Instances dry quickly and are intended to match the color (normally white) of the surface (normally paper) upon which the correction is being made.")
(comment AudioSystem "The collection of all audio systems, characterized by having an audio amplifier, some kind of speaker (which may be headphones), and some sound producing component such as a radio receiver or tape deck mechanism.")
(comment PlantBLO "A specialization of #$BiologicalLivingObject that includes all plants and parts of plants.  #$PlantBLO is thus the \"union\" (see #$collectionUnion) of #$Plant and #$PlantPart (qq.v.).")
(comment LatinSmallLetterU "The lowercase letter 'u'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$U-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterU.")
(comment Sidewalk "The collection of all sidewalks. This does not include walkways that are part of a building. They are outside, and often made of concrete or of a series of flat stones placed on the ground. If the ground is covered in some way, and the path created is intended for walking, then it is a sidewalk.")
(comment productTypeLicensedForTreatmentOf "(#$productTypeLicensedForTreatmentOf ?PRODUCTTYPE ?ORGTYPE) means that there exists a #$License-LegalAgreement that specifies that if PRODUCT is an instance of PRODUCTTYPE, it is OK for PRODUCT play the role of #$instrument-Generic in a #$MedicalCareEvent in which an instance of ORGTYPE is the #$objectTakenCareOf.")
(disjointWith Dancing CapturingAnAnimal)
(comment MilitaryFacility "#$MilitaryFacility is a specialization of #$ConstructionArtifact and #$Facility-Construct. Each instance of #$MilitaryFacility is a building or other type of construction that is used by a #$MilitaryOrganization.  This is taken to also include a military training field, where there may not be a lot of construction (maybe only a fence surrounding it). More concrete examples include instances of #$MilitaryAirfield and #$MissileSilo. ")
(comment FlatPanelDisplay "A specialization of #$ComputerMonitor-VideoKind. This is the collection of computer monitors that are a few inches deep, rather than the usual depth of more than a foot.")
(disjointWith QuasiGovernmentalOrganization GovernmentalOrganization)
(comment BassGuitar-Electric "An electric guitar having 4 heavy strings, which play low notes.  The typical tuning for these four strings is the E below the bass staff, the A at the bottom space of the bass staff, the D in the middle of the bass staff, and the G in the top space of the bass staff.")
(comment EquineAnimal "A collection of animals including horses and species closely related to horses.  Subsets of #$EquineAnimal include #$Horse, #$Donkey, #$Zebra, #$Mule, among others.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single PlacingSensoryOrganToSenseThrough)
(comment Skillet "A container for cooking food that is relatively wide rather than tall, maximizing the area exposed to heat during cooking.")
(comment LesserOccipitalNerve "The collection of all lesser occipital #$Nerves.  Each #$LesserOccipitalNerve is connected to its side's #$VentralRamusC2 and #$innervates the scalp behind the #$Ear.")
(comment PickledFood "This is the collection of pickles in the broad sense, that is, any food

that has been pickled. ")
(comment valueInRange "(#$valueInRange VALUE RANGE) means that VALUE is an individual value in the specified range.  The range is not restricted to a range of numbers, but may include ranges such as (#$Meter 1 3).")
(comment FileSynchronizationProgram "Software which allows files to be synchronized when the file is changed on one computer which is networked to to other computers.")
(comment Bridle "A bridle is device which fits on a horse's head.  The reins and a bit are usually connect to the bridle.")
(comment muscleOrigin "#$BinaryPredicate (#$muscleOrigin ?MUSCLE ?ORIGIN) means that #$AnimalBodyPart ?ORIGIN is an attachment structure for ?MUSCLE.  This is normally the attachment point for the more fixed or central part of the #$Muscle.")
(disjointWith HumanHighOccupancyConstruct FluidReservoir)
(comment TurkishPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Turkey, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SymbolicsMachine "The set of Symbolics LispMachines, ie., 3640, 3650...")
(comment Diamond-TheSuit "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which are diamonds.")
(comment KordofanianLanguageFamily "Languages spoken in the Sudan")
(comment BakingSheet "Flat sheet of metal used for cooking cookies, pizzas, etc in the oven.")
(comment SuckingOnAFoodMorsel "The action of consuming something through abrasion with the tongue while creating a suction with the parts of the mouth, like when someone consumes a piece of candy by sucking on it.")
(comment TransitiveNPFrameType "The collection of transitive frames that take an NP as their complement.")
(comment SpreadsheetProgram "A specialization of #$InteractiveComputerProgram and #$MathematicalComputingProgram. Each instance of this collection is a #$ComputerProgram-CW

in which data can be entered and manipulated in a tabular format and calculations performed on the data.")
(disjointWith NaturalTangibleStuff (GroupFn Organization))
(comment UprightVacuumCleaner "The set of all upright type vacuum cleaners.")
(comment Kangaroo "Large marsupials found in #$Australia. Some smaller species found
on nearby islands.")
(comment MuscularSystem "A specialization of both #$InternalAnatomicalPart and #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$MuscularSystem is composed of all the muscles in the body of an individual animal, where those muscles are considered as a functional whole.  As a system, the muscles of an individual animal work together to enable foot motions in locomotion, pumping in circulation, breathing in respiration, biting and chewing and swallowing in eating, and so on.")
(comment XiphoidProcess "The collection of all xiphoid processes.  A #$XiphoidProcess is the most caudal #$BoneSubPart of the #$Sternum.  It is #$LongAndThin, ossifying from a #$Cartilage form in an adult.")
(comment cohabitingFamilyMembers "A #$FamilyRelationSlot that is a specialization of both #$cohabitants and 
#$relatives.  (#$cohabitingFamilyMembers MEMBER1 MEMBER2) means that MEMBER1
and MEMBER2 are members the same family (see #$Family-SocialEntity) -- such 
as relatives, spouses, or in-laws -- that live with one another.  See also
#$FamilyCohabitationUnit.  Note that MEMBER1 and MEMBER2 might be #$Animals 
of any type whatsoever; although in certain contexts (e.g. #$HumanSocialLifeMt)
they are presupposed to be #$Persons.")
(comment ProvidingTechnologicalAssistance "A specialization of both #$HelpingAnAgent and #$ServiceEvent.  Each instance of #$ProvidingTechnologicalAssistance is an event in which one agent provides technological assistance to another.  The assistance may consist exclusively of the transmission of information or exclusively of the provision of physical devices, or it may be some mix of both.  The agents might be, for example, individuals, businesses, or countries (in any combination).")
(disjointWith Place OrganismPart)
(comment FuelPump-VehiclePart "Device that causes the transfer of fuel from a tank to an engine.")
(comment amplitudeOfWave "(#$amplitudeOfWave WAVE AMP) means the distance from the average to the extremes of the signal WAVE is AMP.")
(comment Recipe-CW "A collection of #$ConceptualWorks.  Each instance of #$Recipe-CW is a set of instructions including a list of ingredients or components needed and instructions on how to combine them to produce an edible product.")
(comment GallBladder "Storage sack for bile.")
(disjointWith TactileSensor SONAR-Device)
(comment Boxer-TheDog "A collection of medium-sized, short-haired dogs.")
(comment Countess "The collection of all countesses, or female persons who hold hereditary count titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch (whether in their own right, by marriage or by courtesy) in the systems of nobility of European countries like #$France, #$Italy, #$Spain, or the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland, or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf.  See also #$Earl and #$Count-Nobleman.")
(disjointWith ManufacturingOrganization InsuranceOrganization)
(comment Still-Device "Collection of devices used to distill alcohol.")
(comment InnermostIntercostalSeries "The #$Collection of all sets of #$InnermostIntercostal #$Muscle.  An #$InnermostIntercostalSeries is the series of #$InnermostIntercostal #$Muscles on one side of the body.")
(comment BottleBrush "A brush used to clean bottles, typically long and flexible with the bristles radiating symmetrically from the shaft.")
(disjointWith SolarPoweredDevice FuelPoweredDevice)
(comment CommonBileDuct "The collection of all common bile ducts. Each instance of this collection is an #$AnatomicalVessel emptying #$BileTheSecretion and pancreatic fluid into the #$Duodenum.")
(comment Dough "Gooey precursor to baked goods")
(comment ButcherShop "A local (at one site) organization that performs as its main function selling and cutting up meat for customers in exchange for money.")
(comment MP3Player-Software "The collection of computer programs whose primary intended            purpose is to play MP3 files.")
(comment IBOCreation "A specialization of both #$PhysicalCreationEvent and #$IBTGeneration.  Each instance of #$IBOCreation is an event in which an instance of #$InformationBearingObject (hereafter IBO) is created.  Examples of #$IBOCreation include publishing a book, making a film, printing a photograph, molding a plastic credit card, painting a billboard, and minting a coin.  When an IBO is created, its content may be either original, be copied from a prior #$InformationBearingThing, or be instantiated from an existing #$ConceptualWork. See also the predicate #$iboCreated.")
(disjointWith Nose Skin)
(comment DoubleReedWoodwindInstrument "The collection of all double-reed #$WoodwindInstruments")
(comment PunctuationSymbol "The collection of all abstract punctuation symbols, such as the comma, the period, etc. Instances are abstract, mental, linguistic objects, not marks on paper or the like. Cf. #$PunctuationMark for the collection of concrete manifestations of these symbols.")
(comment Frame "A physical border or frame that encloses or 'contains' or otherwise marks a boundary, e.g. a picture frame, a window frame (one around the portal, and one around the panes of glass), a television screen frame, etc.  This is NOT the AI use of the word 'frame'.")
(comment CareAndFeedingFn "#$CareAndFeedingFn takes as argument any spec of #$Organism-Whole and returns the collection of activities involved in the care and feeding of organisms of that type.  For example, (#$CareAndFeedingFn #$Bullfrog) returns the collection of all activities, such as terrarium maintenance and attending to nutritional needs, involved in the care and feeding of bullfrogs.")
(comment RAMDisk "RAM memory that is configured to behave like a disk drive.")
(comment DorsalRamusC2 "The collection of all C2 dorsal rami.  VentralRamusC2 and #$DorsalRamusC2 branch from SpinalRootC2.  #$DorsalRamusC2 supplies the #$GreaterOccipitalNerve.")
(comment BuffaloWing "Crispy, spicy fried chicken wings, supposedly invented in 

Buffalo, New York.")
(comment longTermInformationStore-FunctionalRole "(#$longTermInformationStore-FunctionalRole SYSTEM STORE)
means that if it holds in any time frame TEMP such that
(#$temporallySubsumes SYSTEM TEMP) that (#$containsInformation STORE
INFO), it holds from the beginning of TEMP through the end of the
lifetime of SYSTEM that (#$containsInformation STORE INFO).  It is
also assumed that it is not true that (#$containsInformation STORE
INFO) for any INFO and for any time frame TEMP that is not temporally
subsumed by SYSTEM, and that there is some time frame subsumed by the lifetime of SYSTEM during which STORE does contain some piece of information.  In the vernacular: if
(#$longTermInformationStore-FunctionalRole SYSTEM STORE) then STORE
contains whatever information is stored in it during the lifetime of
SYSTEM for the lifetime of SYSTEM, and only stores information during
the lifetime of SYSTEM.")
(comment Euthanasia "A specialization of #$KillingByOrganism and #$ShowingSupportForSomeone. Each instance of #$Euthanasia is an #$Event in which   a #$Person willfully ends or permits the end of the life of another #$Animal in a way in which the latter suffers very little or no physical pain. When the animal is a #$Person this is done after and only after he or she has requested that this be done.")
(disjointWith ContainerArtifact ComputationalSystem)
(comment Splint "A stiff object which is used to give support to an injured joint or fractured bone.")
(comment Backdoor-SecurityBypassInstructions "The collection of all #$Instructions for bypassing computer security.")
(comment WaterRespiration "Respiration which trades carbon dioxide in the organism's tissues with #$Oxygen from the water surrounding the organism.--Siegel, May 17, 1996")
(comment RouterProgram "The collection of computer programs that are used to route computer network traffic.")
(comment Engine "#$Engine is a specialization of #$PoweredDevice and #$MechanicalDevice.  Each instance of #$Engine is a device that changes some form of energy into motion (usually rotation).  An engine may operate by burning some type of fuel (as do jet engines and internal combustion engines), or it may be powered by electricity, fluid flow, etc.  Some notable specializations of #$Engine are #$ElectricalMotor, #$ExternalCombustionEngine, and #$RocketEngine.")
(comment BreadfruitTree "tree which bears breadfruit")
(comment GibraltarPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Gibraltar, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByCustomers PersonTypeByPositionInOrg)
(comment PaperWeight "The collection of paper weights.")
(comment typicalArgGenl "(#$typicalArgGenl PRED NUM COL) says that typically, the NUMth argument-place of PRED is filled by a spec of COL.  Note that COL must be a spec of COLGENL, where (#$argGenl PRED NUM COLGENL).")
(disjointWith Braking CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment RhPositive "#$Blood either has or does not have the Rh factor.  Adding foreign blood which is #$RhPositive to the #$CirculatorySystem of a body whose blood which is #$RhNegative will cause the recipient's body to develop anitbodies against the Rh factor.  If the recipient of #$RhPositive blood is a woman who later has an #$RhNegative fetus, then her immune system will attack the fetus's blood.  Rh factor is controlled by a recessive gene.")
(comment CookingFood "A specialization of #$PreparingFoodItem and #$HeatingProcess.  Each instance of #$CookingFood is an event in which some item of #$Food (q.v.) is prepared by heating it.  Typically, the foodstuff is heated until it reaches a certain temperature over some period of time; during the heating, chemical and/or physical changes occur which are supposed to make the foodstuff healthier or tastier (or, in some cases, ethically acceptable).  A #$CookingFood event may last from a few minutes (e.g., #$SteamingFood (vegetables), #$MakingToast) to several hours (e.g., #$RoastingFood).")
(comment InformationRecordingDevice "#$InformationRecordingDevice is a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$InformationRecordingDevice is a device used for the recording of sensory information (i.e., audio and visual, but not encoded as character strings.)  So an instance would be your answering machine at home (an #$AnsweringMachine), your cam-corder (a #$VideoCamera), but NOT your address book or your copy of the Yellow Pages.   Note: A borderline case is a #$PersonalDigitalAssistant (such as an Apple Newton) used to record handwritten script.  If it then processes that information and converts it to ASCII characters, it has stopped being an #$InformationRecordingDevice as this constant is defined.")
(comment FTPClientProgram "#$FTPClientProgram is the collection of FTP software that can be used to move files to and from machines running instances of #$FTPServerProgram.")
(disjointWith Restaurant-Organization FinancialOrganization)
(comment Loofah "Collection of cleaning tools that are derived from the fibrous skeletons of gourds of genus Luffa.")
(disjointWith ProgrammingAComputer (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(comment MedialDirection "The general direction towards the midline of the body, away from the sides, in or near an object with #$AnimalBodyShape.")
(comment Oilseed "A collection of #$Seeds harvested primarily             for their oil.  A prominent example is flaxseed.")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject EdibleStuff)
(comment Cigar " A small roll of tobacco leaf for smoking .")
(comment BinaryPredicateTypeByLogicalFeature "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$PredicateType. Each instance of #$BinaryPredicateTypeByLogicalFeature is a collection of #$BinaryPredicates whose instances all share some significant logical feature, such as reflexivity or asymmetry.  Examples include  #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate, #$AntiSymmetricBinaryPredicate, and  #$EquivalenceRelation.")
(disjointWith HandlingAnObject TakingAStep)
(comment Excreting "The process in which a living structure excretes useless substances.")
(comment VulnerableToBounceAttack "A vulnerability had by instances of
 #$Computer. A computer is #$VulnerableToBounceAttack if an attacker can
 establish a connection between it and an arbitrary port on another
 system. This connection may be used to bypass access controls that
 would otherwise apply. This vulnerability typically arises as a
 consequence of running a server program with an
 #$ArbitraryDestinationPortFault.")
(comment AlaskanMalamute "A collection of relatively large, sled dogs.")
(comment FalklandIslandsDependenciesPerson "A person who is a FalklandIslandsDependencies native/resident")
(disjointWith FoundationOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment Sartorius "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Sartorius #$Muscle.  The #$Sartorius is the longest muscle in the body.  It assists in flexion of the #$Hip and #$Knee, abduction and lateral rotation of the #$Femur and medial rotation of the #$Knee.")
(comment Scissors "hand tool made of two longish thinish pieces of usually metal connected with flat sides together by a rotating joint near the center of their longest dimension;  they are opened to let material to be cut in, and as they are closed shear force is applied to the material causing it to be cut.")
(comment ExternalIliacVein "The collection of all external iliac veins.  The external iliac vein's proximal end is connected to the common iliac vein and its distal end is connected to the femoral vein.")
(comment WhiteCastello-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of White Castello.

This is a  white-mold-crusted Danish cheese shaped like a clover leaf with a hole in

the middle.")
(comment toOrganization "A specialization of #$to-Generic, #$toOrganization can

be used to indicate, in a more specific way,

the instance of #$Organization in which the

instance of #$IntelligentAgent

ends up in some instance of #$OrganizationalTransfer.

(#$toOrganization TRANS ORG) means that in the 

instance TRANS of #$OrganizationalTransfer, the

#$transferredThing ends up in the instance

ORG of #$Organization.  See also #$OrganizationalTransferIn and

#$fromOrganization.")
(comment JavaScriptFile "#$JavaScriptFile is the collection of #$ComputerFile-AIS whose instances are written in  #$JavaScriptProgrammingLanguage.")
(comment ScientificInstrument "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$ScientificInstrument is a device designed for use in scientific research.  In most instances, that implies that the device has been made with a high quality and (for measuring devices) high precision.  Many #$ScientificInstruments have either a primary or auxiliary function as measuring devices; and many of those also are, or incorporate, an instance of #$InformationRecordingDevice.")
(comment HumanChromosome "A collection of #$Chromosomes that are found in humans.

These hold the #$Gene-HereditaryUnits of humans and direct the synthesis

of #$ProteinStuff.")
(disjointWith CommercialFishingBoat OceanLiner)
(comment Pansy "Pansy flower.")
(comment NiueanPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Niue, or participates in its #$NationalCulture")
(comment PersonalCassettePlayer "A subcollection of both #$PersonalAudioPlayer and #$AudioTapePlayer. Instances of #$PersonalCassettePlayer are used to listen to instances of the intersection of #$AudioCassette and #$AudioRecordedObject, and are small and portable enough to use while jogging")
(comment DevanagariCharacter "characters composed of major sections for consonants and added squiggles for vowels other than A")
(comment ServingTray "The collection of trays designed mainly to support other food vessels in a serving event.  Significantly different from a platter; food is not usually placed directly on a serving tray.")
(comment Birdsong "The collection of sounds made by #$Birds.")
(disjointWith AcademicTesting Synthesis-Generic)
(comment Aisle-PathArtifact "The collection of all aisles, each being a #$Path-Generic separating sections of seats, as in a church or movie theater.")
(comment MiddleLobarBronchus "The collection of middle lobar bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) in  the #$Lung, each of which supplies air to a #$MiddleLobeOfLung.  In  human beings, it occurs only on the right side, where it branches off  of the right #$MainBronchus.")
(comment VermicelliNoodle "A long round really skinny noodle.")
(comment coinhabitDuringYear "`(#$coinhabitDuringYear YEAR PERSON1 PERSON2)' means that PERSON1
and PERSON2 are considered members of the same household for the year YEAR A.D.
according to IRS standards. The main purpose of this predicate is to
enable the writing of rules that don't involve #$holdsIn.")
(comment amountActionPerformed "(#$amountActionPerformed EVENT-TYPE NUM) means that

EVENT-TYPE is performed NUM times. In essence, this

predicate allows one to state in a gaf how many instances of

EVENT-TYPE exist. In uses of this predicate, one would expect the

EVENT-TYPE itself to be fairly specific. For example, one might use

it for something like:

(#$amountActionPerformed FredReadingTheGormenghastTrilogy 5).")
(comment CuticleCream "Creamy products applied to the cuticles surrounding the fingernails (and maybe also toenails), in order to soften them.")
(disjointWith Ablation PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment Coffin "A container for storing a human body in a grave.")
(comment Ledger "The book associated with an account in which the transactions that affect that account are recorded.")
(comment PubicHair "Hair covering the groin area")
(disjointWith WritingImplement PlumbingTool)
(comment HimalayanCat "A collection of cats bred (in part) by crossing instances of #$PersianCat with           instances of #$SiameseCat.")
(comment DominicaPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Dominica, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment HighChair "The collection of all high chairs.  A #$HighChair is a subset of #$Chair-PieceOfFurniture, as well a #$deviceUsed in a #$FeedingEvent where the #$recipientOfService is either a #$HumanInfant or a #$HumanToddler.  #$HighChairs are usually about the height of an average #$EatingTable and have a #$Tray attached to a seat.")
(comment AlzheimersDisease "A degenerative disease of nerve cells in the cerebral cortex that leads to atrophy of the brain and senile dementia. Symptoms include loss of memory, confusion, irritability, and restlessness, as well as disorientation and impaired judgment and concentration. Cause is unknown, and only treatment is alleviation of symptoms and counseling for loved ones.")
(comment Shovel "A hand tool used for cutting or moving soft or granulated materials like soil and sand.  Comprised of a long handle and a concave head with a sharp edge.")
(comment TurnipGreen-Foodstuff "Foodstuff from the leaves and stems of the turnip plant. Typically cooked before serving.")
(comment overlappingOrgs "The organization denoted by ARG1 shares some possibly significant attribute with the organization denoted by ARG2. In the extreme case, ARG1 might denote the same entity as ARG2.")
(comment EncyclopediaProgram "This is the collection of programs that

effectively put an encyclopedia on one's computer.")
(disjointWith ClothingStore AutoDealership)
(comment Bassoon "large double-reed instrument ")
(comment RedDeer "A specification of #$Deer. Instances of #$RedDeer live in  the #$ContinentOfEurope.  Their scientific name is Cervus elaphus.")
(comment InventoryDocument "A specialization of #$TextualMaterial. Each instance of this collection is a document that contains information about some organization's collection of some kind of item, such as office furniture, or (for a #$SellingOrganization) unsold or unused items in stock.")
(comment productTypeLicensedForUse "(#$productTypeLicensedForUse PRODUCTTYPE ROLE EVTTYPE) means that there exists a #$License-LegalAgreement that specifies that if PRODUCT is an instance of PRODUCTTYPE, it is OK for PRODUCT to play the role ROLE in instances of EVTTYPE.")
(comment StereoSpeaker "The speaker which produces the sound from a stereo system.  It usually includes some sort of cubical housing")
(comment BiologicalEvent "A specialization of #$BiologicalProcess (q.v.) instances of 
which are non-deliberately \"done by\" biological organisms.  
Each instance of #$BiologicalEvent is a biological process that 
has an instance of #$Organism-Whole as a \"bodily doer\" (see
#$bodilyDoer).  Note that not all physical events that have 
bodily doers are #$BiologicalEvents; they might (e.g.) be #$PhysiologicalConditions that are not biological events.
Thus, having a bodily doer is a necessary but not a sufficient
condition for being an instance of #$BiologicalEvent.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterV "The capital letter 'V'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$V-TheLetter, and #$LatinSmallLetterV.")
(comment BeautyDevice "Devices such as hair curlers or hair dryers used in improving one's appearance.")
(comment AirplaneRunway "#$AirplaneRunway is a specialization of #$PathForWheeledVehicles.  Each instance of #$AirplaneRunway is an airstrip at an airport, on an aircraft carrier, or in some field where airplanes taxi, take off, and land.")
(comment ComputerBus "A specialization of #$ComputerHardwareComponent. Each instance of this collection is a computer bus, a device which transmits data from one part of a #$Computer to another. Generally the computer bus will connect all devices to the computer #$CentralProcessingUnit and main memory.

The computer bus consists of two parts -- the address bus and a data bus. The data bus transfers actual data, whereas the address bus transfers information about where the data should go. See also the specializations #$HardwareBusInternal and #$HardwareBusPeripheral.")
(comment PrivateSectorOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that operate in what is thought of as the private sector and that have no governmental component.  Instances of #$PrivateSectorOrganizations may be either #$CommercialOrganizations or #$NonProfitOrganizations.  Examples of #$PrivateSectorOrganizations include #$IBMInc, #$Cycorp, #$FloridaNationalBank, and #$SierraClub.")
(comment DiscographyFn "#$DiscographyFn takes as argument
any instance of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of catalogues
(discographies) of that agent's audio recordings. Note that this is a
collection of lists and/or narratives, not of actual audio
recordings. For example,(#$DiscographyFn #$RollingStones) returns the
collection of all catalogues of recordings by the Rolling Stones.")
(disjointWith Conveying-Generic PlacingSensoryOrganToSenseThrough)
(comment AncientNavalShip "Oar and wind powered sailing vessels.")
(comment VentralRamusC3 "The collection of all C3 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC3 and #$DorsalRamusC3 branch from SpinalRootC3.  #$VentralRamusC3 supplies the #$CervicalPlexus.")
(comment TartarSauce "This is the collection of all instances of tarter sauce. Tarter sauce is

essentially mayonnaise with pickle relish in it. It is sometimes more

elaborate, containing capers and other ingredients. It is primarily used

with fish, especially fried fish.")
(comment PhysicalDestructionOfIndividualFn "#$PhysicalDestructionOfIndividualFn is a function that takes as an argument an instance of #$PartiallyTangible and returns the instance of #$PhysicalDestructionEvent in which the #$PartiallyTangible thing is destroyed.  That is, (#$PhysicalDestructionOfIndividualFn TANG) denotes the event in which TANG is destroyed in an instance of #$PhysicalDestructionEvent.  See also #$PhysicalDestructionFn.")
(comment FileDecompressionProgram "Software which decompresses a compressed file. Instances would be specific decompression tools like 'Pkunzip'.")
(comment SafetyGlasses "Eyewear designed to protect the eyes from flying debris or chemicals.")
(comment isolableFrom "(#$isolableFrom MICROORGTYPE STUFFTYPE) means that specimens
of MICROORGTYPE can be isolated from STUFFTYPE using conventional
laboratory methods.")
(disjointWith Watercraft FluidReservoir)
(comment CompositeOrder "A plant order in the dicot subclass.")
(comment IndonesianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Indonesia-TheNation, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment IBMPC "A small personal computer manufactured by a non-member company, with a lot of games software available for it.")
(comment Eight-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '8.'")
(comment SaharanLanguageFamily "Languages spoken near Lake Chad and in the central Sahara")
(comment Mirror "a reflecting surface, usually made of glass with a metal backing.")
(comment FeedingAnAnimal "A collection of events.  Each element of #$FeedingAnAnimal is a #$FeedingEvent in which a #$Person feeds a #$NonPersonAnimal.")
(disjointWith Freeware MarketedComputerProgram)
(disjointWith ConductingMedium (GroupFn Organization))
(comment ToothpasteTube "The collection of container products in which tooth paste is packaged and sold.")
(comment Koala "Australian marsupials which eat only eucalyptus leaves.")
(comment innervates "A #$Nerve #$innervates an #$AnimalBodyPart by being attached to it.  #$The #$Nerve can send signals to or from #$The #$AnimalBodyPart and a more central area of #$The #$CentralNervousSystem.  The nerve controls the action of #$MuscleTissue or sends sensory signals towards #$The #$Brain.")
(comment Lunate "The #$Lunate is also designated 'semi lunar' or (in non-humans) 'intermedium'.")
(disjointWith BiologicalIntakeEvent MarkingOnASurface)
(comment AutomotiveAntenna "The electrical component used to receive radio signals located on you car.")
(comment WillAndTestament "A document containing a person's directions on actions they wish taken after their death.")
(disjointWith TactileSensor RadarDevice)
(comment BouvierDesFlandres "A collection of large dogs.")
(comment Earl "The collection of all earls, or male persons who hold hereditary count title in the systems of nobility of the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf.  This is distinct from a European count, though of equal rank.  See also #$Count-Nobleman and #$Countess.")
(disjointWith InsuranceOrganization JudicialOrganization)
(comment Cam-ForceConverter "Oval-shaped device used for mechanical linkage (typically for transforming linear movement into rotational movement, or vice versa).")
(comment FlexorDigitorumProfundus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$FlexorDigitorumProfundus #$Muscle.  The #$FlexorDigitorumProfundus connects to each #$DistalPhalanx by digitorum tendons.  The profundus tendons pass through the tendons of the #$FlexorDigitorumSuperficialis.")
(comment GlassBottle "Bottles made of glass")
(disjointWith SocialGathering SingleDoerAction)
(comment IleoCecalValve "The collection of all ileocecal (or 'ileocaecal') #$Valves.  Each instance of this collection is a one-way #$Portal (#$Valve-Unidirectional) from a #$SmallIntestine to the #$LargeIntestine of the same #$Animal.")
(comment Cocoa-ThePowder "The powder obtained from grinding cocoa beans, used to make hot chocolate.")
(comment ClothingStore "The collection of establishments that sell exclusively clothing")
(comment plaintextVersionOfFile "(#$plaintextVersionOfFile PLAINTEXT ENCRYPTED) means that PLAINTEXT is _the_ plaintext version of ENCRYPTED.")
(comment GunBarrel "The part of a gun which is a hollow cylinder, one or more orders of magnitude longer than its diameter, through which the mass being fired (a bullet, buckshot, etc.) travels when the gun is discharged.")
(comment RequestForComments-Internet "Requests For Comments, or RFCs, form the basis of the #$Internet's technical documentation. The Internet is best thought of as a layered series of protocols, each of which is documented by one or more RFCs. Once issued, RFCs do not change. Protocol revisions are documented by issuing new RFCs. The older RFCs are

still available, but are said to be obsoleted by the newer RFCs. Not all RFCs document protocols; some are simply for discussion or informational purposes, and a traditional series of April Fools' RFCs can be distinguished by

their date. For more information and the protocols themselves, see http://freesoft.org/CIE/RFC/index.htm .")
(disjointWith Ear Skin)
(disjointWith Wheelbarrow MountableTransporter)
(comment basesBasePaired "(#$basesBasePaired BASE1 BASE2) means that there is a hydrogen bond between #$NitrogenBases BASE1 and BASE2. Normally, only complementary nitrogen bases are base paired (see #$complementaryBaseTypes), but it is possible for two #$NitrogenBases to be base-paired incorrectly, e.g., a hydrogen bond can be formed between two #$NitrogenBases that are not complementary. See #$basesComplementaryBasePaired for the relation when the bases are paired correctly.")
(comment closeToWRTScale "(#$closeToWRTScale INT1 INT2 SCALE) says 

that the #$ScalarIntervals INT1 and INT2 bear the #$approximately relationship

to each other, in so far as the standard by 

which we make the comparison is SCALE.  For example, (#$closeToWRTScale

 (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 300) (#$Foot-UnitOfMeasure 301) HeightOfBuilding) says that 300 feet and 301 feet are very close values where heights of buildings are concerned.")
(comment Contrabassoon "large double-reed instrument ")
(comment UncasedLetter "The collection of uncased instances of #$Letter-Alphabetic, which are not designated as being either #$UpperCaseLetters or #$LowerCaseLetters.  For example, this collection includes #$A-TheLetter, but not #$LatinCapitalLetterA or #$LatinSmallLetterA.  Reference to this collection and its members is appropriate when the issue of case is irrelevant, as in: ''There are twenty-six letters in the modern Roman alphabet''.  See also #$uppercaseOfLetter and #$lowercaseOfLetter.")
(comment AirVentSystem "The system by which air is circulated in a building, consisting of pipe-like passageways from the furnace or central air conditioner, portals in the walls, and vent covers which control the flow of air into the room.")
(comment SmallComputerSystemInterfaceProtocol "The collection of SCSI protocols for interfaces between computers and peripherals. There are currently three instances, referred to as SCSI-1, SCSI-2, and SCSI-3.")
(comment Device-SelfControlled "The collection of #$PhysicalDevices that are at some point controlled by internal mechanisms.  Inclusion in this collection does not imply exclusion from the collections #$Device-UserControlled and #$Device-RemoteControlled.  A device may be included in all three collections if this accurately reflects the locus of control at different times.")
(comment Stylus-WritingImplement "basically, a stick with a point at the end")
(comment PerinealNerve "The collection of all perineal #$Nerves.  A #$PerinealNerve is the inferior and larger branch of a #$PudendalNerve.  It #$innervates the sphincter ani and levator ani.  In males it #$innervates #$CorpusCavernosum and #$Scrotum, while in the female it #$innervates the labia.")
(comment Sushi "In Japanese cooking, cold boiled rice moistened with rice  vinegar, usually shaped into bite-size pieces and topped with raw  seafood (nigiri-zushi) or formed into a long seaweed-wrapped roll,  often around strips of vegetable or raw fish, and sliced into  bite-size pieces (maki-zushi).")
(comment HomoGenus "A specialization of #$HominidaeFamily and an instance of #$BiologicalGenus. The Homo genus is separated from other, earlier hominids because of the emergence of tool use, language, and culture. The genus begins about 2.3 million years ago. The characteristics of these species are bigger brain (above 1000ml), the forehead rises straight up, the skull becomes rounder, the teeth are reduced, arms are shorter and legs are longer, and the skeleton becomes more delicate. A notable specialization of this collection is #$HomoSapiens.")
(disjointWith Organization ComputerMarketCategory)
(comment CATScanner "CAT (computerized axial tomography) scanners use X-rays and computerization to produce a 3D image of (part of) a patient's body.")
(comment Macrophage "A subclass of #$WhiteBloodCell that ingest microbes, #$Antigens
and other substances. Not found in #$Blood, they resides where body organs
interface with bloodstream or the outside world.")
(disjointWith Engine Weapon)
(comment CacaoTree "Member of species Theobroma cacao; this is the plant that gives us cocoa butter, cocoa powder, and chocolate.")
(comment LiberianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Liberia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByCustomers PhysiologicalConditionType)
(comment InkWell "The collection of paper weights.")
(comment HouseholdFurnishingsMC "This category includes rugs, curtains, towels, etc, some of which may be found in places other than a household, i.e. in an office.")
(comment compatibleBloodTypes "(#$compatibleBloodTypes BLOODTYPE1 BLOODTYPE2) means that an organism with #$Blood of type BLOODTYPE1 will not adversely react when blood of type BLOODTYPE2 is added. (Blood of type O can be given to anyone, and AB can receive from anyone; blood of type AB can only be given to those with AB and O can only receive O blood.)")
(disjointWith Meat VegetarianCuisine)
(comment DirectFireWeapon "#$DirectFireWeapon is a specialization of #$ProjectileLauncher and #$Weapon.  Each instance of #$DirectFireWeapon is a weapon that shoots a projectile such as a bullet in a flat trajectory as opposed to the arching trajectory of an #$IndirectFireWeapon.")
(comment JavaClass "#$JavaClass is a specialization of #$ProgramSpecification.  Instances
of #$JavaClass determine what sorts of operations programs written in
#$JavaProgrammingLanguage are able to perform when they include the
class and are interpreted by an instance of #$JavaVirtualMachine.")
(disjointWith Restaurant-Organization Laundromat)
(comment Jar "The collection of jar-like containers: generally glass or ceramic and cylindrical in shape with an opening at the top")
(comment SeaMonkey "The collection of all #$SeaMonkeys, a kind of #$Crustacean that is usually sold in powder form as 'instant life' in little paper bags to be mixed with water, often used in fish tanks.")
(disjointWith MetalPlating MakingWrittenMaterial)
(comment toGroup "A specialization of #$to-Generic, #$toGroup can
be used to indicate, in a more specific way,
the instance of #$Group in which the #$transferredThing
ends up in some instance of #$GroupTransfer.
(#$toGroup TRANS GROUP) means that in the 
instance TRANS of #$GroupTransfer, the
#$transferredThing ends up in the instance
GROUP of #$Group.  See also #$GroupTransferIn and
#$fromGroup.")
(comment daughters "(#$daughters ?PAR ?FEM) means that ?FEM is one of the daughters (female children) of ?PAR.  ?FEM could be a child of ?PAR by birth, by adoption, by marriage (e.g., if ?PAR had married a biological parent of ?FEM), or by some other social arrangement.")
(comment byProducts "This predicate relates a given purposeful action of physically creating or destroying something to an unintended tangible \"output\" (see #$outputs) of that action. (#$byProducts EVENT OBJECT) means that OBJECT is one of the outputs of EVENT, but not one of its intended outputs.  For intended outputs, see #$products.  Note that no output can be _both_ a product and a by-product of the same event, i.e. (#$negationPreds #$products #$byProducts)

holds.")
(disjointWith HarvestingAPlant TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment CommunicatingBetweenComputers "Computers transferring information.  This is not a communicating event, since it doesn't necessarily involve transfer of information into or out of agents' heads.")
(comment BasketballShoe "The collection of shoes one often wears while playing #$Basketball-TheGame.")
(comment attempts "#$attempts AGENT ACT means that AGENT attempts to perform action ACT. Attempts are generally regarded as initial segments of actions: think of Joe's attempt to buy flowers as the early portion of what would be, if completed, a flowers-buying action. Also, attempts are intrinsically intentional: the initial portion of an action constitutes an attempt only if it occurs because of the agent's intention to perform the action.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement Hugging)
(comment Mouth "The collection of all animal mouths.  A mouth is a container #$AnimalBodyPart of an #$Animal.  It has an opening (a #$Portal) to the region outside the organism.  Through that opening, the animal ingests tangible substances from the environment, such as food, water, air, etc.  Additional activities, such as #$Chewing, may occur in the #$Mouth, and it may participate in other activities such as talking, kissing, etc.")
(comment AfghanHound "A collection of large dogs with long-haired coats.")
(comment ScandinavianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Norway.")
(disjointWith RevoltOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment SternoCleidoMastoid "The #$Collection of all instances of #$SternoCleidoMastoid #$Muscle.  The #$SternoCleidoMastoid flexes the #$Neck-AnimalBodyPart and also rotates the #$Head-AnimalBodyPart if the other #$SternoCleidoMastoid is not simultaneously active.")
(comment AircraftCabin "The region of a plane where passengers ride.")
(comment CommonIliacVein "The collection of all common iliac veins.  The right and left common iliac veins connect at their proximal ends to become the inferior vena cava.  The common iliac vein then passes through the pelvis and becomes the external and internal iliac veins.")
(comment BlueCastello-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Blue Castello.

This is a Danish triple creme blue cheese.")
(comment ScreenMateProgram "This is the collection of computer software products that display animated images which interact with the computer's desktop display.")
(comment ReviewingStand "A raised platform from which dignitaries can watch an event, such as a parade.")
(comment AdultFn "(#$AdultFn ANIMALKIND) is the collection of instances of ANIMALKIND
that are adult.")
(comment Inhaling-BreathingIn "The typically involuntary portion of the breathing process in which air enters the lungs.")
(comment Seedling "A subset of #$Plant.  #$Seedling is the collection of all growing plants in the stage after germination but before primary development.  The seedling stage begins with the rupture of the seed coat and ends at the vague time that the growing plant is 'well established'.")
(comment BrechouIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Brechou-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HomeCDPlayer "A subcollection of both #$CDPlayer-AudioComponent and #$HomeAudioSystemComponent. Instances of #$HomeCDPlayer are designed to be used in the home to play instances of #$CompactDisc-Generic.")
(comment SaradaCharacter "if like Devanagari, characters composed of major sections for consonants and added squiggles for vowels other than A")
(comment TorqueWrench "A wrench used to tighten bolts to a specific torque")
(comment VulnerableToProgramCrashing "#$VulnerableToProgramCrashing is a vulnerability had by instances of                                                                                                               #$Computer.  A computer has this attribute if it is running a program                                                                                                               that crashes in response to certain invalid input.")
(comment ServiceOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$ServiceOrganization is an organization whose main function is to provide some service or services (as opposed, e.g., to mainly selling goods or manufacturing products).  A service organization might or might not be a subsidiary or department in some larger organization; it might or might not be  a for-profit organization (for-profit service organizations are instances of the subcollection #$CommercialServiceOrganization). Notable specializations of #$ServiceOrganization include #$MedicalCareOrganization, #$ShippingOrganization, and #$Restaurant-Organization.")
(comment SeatingDeviceBack "The collection of the backs of seating devices.")
(comment ApolloSpacecraft "The collection of all Apollo manned #$Spacecraft.  Each #$ApolloSpacecraft could transport three #$Astronauts to Earth orbit.  Several #$ApolloSpacecraft went to the moon (#$MoonOfEarth).")
(comment ObliqueFissureOfLung "The collection of diagonally situated main fissures (cracks  or crevices) that separate lung lobes (instances of #$LobeOfLung).  An  ObliqueFissureOfLung extends deep from the surface to near the hylum of the Lung,  and runs diagonally from the lower anterior border of the lung around  the side up to the upper posterior medial part.  In normal human  beings each #$Lung has an ObliqueFissureOfLung (the right lung also  has a #$HorizontalFissureOfLung).")
(comment MacaroniNoodle "A short tubular noodle.")
(comment CommercialPassengerAirplaneCabin "The cabin (passenger carrying area) of a commercial passenger airliner")
(disjointWith AccessingAnIBT PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment Lamppost "An outdoor lamppost or streetlight.")
(comment stateOfAddress "(#$stateOfAddress LOC STATE) means that the  #$ContactLocation LOC is found in the STATE, where STATE is either a  #$State-UnitedStates or another #$CountrySubsidiary. For example, as  #$CycorpHeadquarters is a #$ContactLocation for #$Cycorp, then  (#$stateOfAddress #$CycorpHeadquarters #$Texas-State) means that the Cycorp Headquarters building is located in Texas.  Note that the arg-constraint on the first argument should be an instance of #$ContactLocation which serves as a #$pointsOfContact for an agent and not the agent itself.")
(comment Antler "Long, branching horns on deer and other animals")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice WritingImplement)
(comment Saluki "One of the oldest breeds of dog. Of Arab origin.")
(comment SenegalPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Senegal, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization "#$ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization is an #$Organization that is primarily engaged in the construction industry or the business of repairing and maintaining physical structures or whose activities focus on that industry.  Examples of specializations of #$ConstructionRepairOrMaintenanceOrganization include #$PestControlCompany and #$BuildingContractor-Organization.")
(comment BabyBottle "A subset of #$DrinkingBottle.  The collection of all bottles out of which an infant or a young toddler drink.  A #$BabyBottle is a bottle made of either #$Plastic or #$Glass which has a screw cap and a plastic nipple from which the baby drinks.")
(comment EndStageRenalDisease "A collection of #$AilmentConditions in which the #$Kidneys completely stop working and dialysis, hemodialysis or a transplant is required.")
(comment Hoe "A hand tool used for cutting (chopping) or movement of materials like soil and sand.  Comprised of a long handle and a flat rectangular head with one sharp edge.")
(comment SuperficialTemporalVein "The collection of all superficial temporal #$Veins.  An individual #$SuperficialTemporalVein is one of a paired set of #$SystemicVeins which drains the #$Scalp on its side of the head.  It runs alongside the #$SystemicArtery and drains into #$RetroMandibularVein in the #$ParotidGland upon joining up with the #$MaxillaryVein.")
(comment Radish-Foodstuff "Radish in any of its edible forms, whole or grated.  Horseradish is a type of radish.")
(comment formationAuthorizedBy "(#$formationAuthorizedBy ORG COVENANT) means that the #$Organization ORG was established in accordance with the #$Agreement COVENANT, which authorized its formation and indicated its purpose and basic structure and powers.")
(comment DictionaryProgram "This is the collection of programs that

effectively put a dictionary on one's computer.")
(disjointWith InternationalOrganization SingleSiteOrganization)
(comment Cello "medium-sized stringed instrument in the violin family ")
(comment Leopard "The collection of all leopards.  Each #$Leopard is a large feline #$Mammal with either a tawny hide with dark spotted markings or a completely dark hide.  #$Leopards are native to the #$ContinentOfAfrica and the #$ContinentOfAsia.")
(comment EnteringInfoIntoDevice "The act of conveying information to some kind of device.  You can't convey information to a hammer, so #$informationDestination is minimized to be #$Computer #$CashRegister #$Clock or whatever else you care to add.")
(comment GoCart "A #$GoCart is a small vehicle with an engine, made of an open frame on four wheels and used in races.")
(comment AutomobileSubwoofer "Automobile subwoofer")
(disjointWith MuscleTissue Cell)
(comment LatinSmallLetterV "The lowercase letter 'v'.    This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).See also #$V-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterV.")
(comment NailClippers "Cutting tool used in clipping one's nails.")
(disjointWith HittingAnObject StoringSomething)
(comment ComputerInputDevice "A specialization of #$ComputerInterfaceDevice. Each instance of this collection is an #$ElectronicDevice which delivers information from a user to a computer.")
(comment DiscographyFn "#$DiscographyFn takes as argument any instance of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of catalogues (discographies) of that agent's audio recordings. Note that this is a collection of lists and/or narratives, not of actual audio recordings.  For example,(#$DiscographyFn #$RollingStones) returns the collection of all catalogues of recordings by the Rolling Stones.")
(comment Whale "The collection of all whales, including most types of cetacean.  #$Whale is a subset of #$Mammal, including the largest mammals on Earth.")
(disjointWith Cleaning PlacingSensoryOrganToSenseThrough)
(comment LateralPlantarNerve "The collection of all lateral plantar nerves.  The lateral plantar nerve is a branch of the #$TibialNerve and supplies the last 1 1/2 toes and the lateral muscles of the foot.")
(comment Marinade "This is the collection of all instances of marinades. A marinade is a

mixture in which food soaks for a period of time prior to cooking. Marinades

are mostly applied to meat or fish. The purpose of a marinade is to impart

flavor to the items marinated and sometimes to change their texture.

Brining can be considered marination, so the solution of salt, water, 

and sugar is a particularly simple marinade. Most marinades containing more

flavoring ingredients. ")
(comment ScriptingProgram "Software which allows a user to create macros or scripts in order to automate certain tasks.")
(comment Platform "a large, flat, construction artifact which is usually elevated")
(comment maximumTakeOffWeight "(#$maximumTakeOffWeight PLANE MASS) means that

   PLANE cannot take off unless the Mass of

   PLANE plus the combined Mass of all objects

    in PLANE does not exceed MASS.")
(disjointWith AirTransportationDevice FluidReservoir)
(comment PollenGrain "The angiosperm male gametophyte.  It is released by the anthers when mature, is transported to a stigma by wind, animal vectors or to the stigma of its own flower by gravity, where it may germinate, send a tube down through the female tissues and discharge sperm cells in the vicinity of the female gamete where fertilization may take place.")
(comment MartiniquePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Martinique, or participates in its #$NationalCulture")
(comment TIPersonalComputer "Personal computer made by Texas Instruments")
(comment Eighteen-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '18.'")
(comment SonghaiLanguageFamily "Languages spoken in Mali")
(comment Mirror-Wall "The kind of mirror you hang on a wall in a living room or bedroom")
(comment Whinnying "neighing quietly")
(comment TransitiveThatClauseFrameType "The collection of all transitive frames that take either a finite that-clause complement or a simple (that-less and wh-less) finite clause complement.")
(comment OperatingSystem "A specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  Each instance of #$OperatingSystem is a program that provides an environment in which a user can execute instances of #$ApplicationProgram (q.v.) on the hardware of a computer. That is, running copies of instances of #$OperatingSystem serve as systems that look for and understand user commands, regulate how system resources are used by application programs, handle the internal operations of computers, and so on.  Note that #$OperatingSystem is disjoint with #$ApplicationProgram and #$OperatingSystemKernel (q.v.), and that together these three collections partition #$ComputerProgram-CW.")
(comment SingleSiteOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$SingleSiteOrganization is an organization that has a single location (see #$physicalQuarters).  For example, the #$KMartStore at Parmer Lane and the Great Hills FireStation Number 2 in Austin are instances.  But #$KMart-TheCompany and the Austin City Fire Department are not instances, since those \"parent\" organizations have several sites as their physical quarters. To be contrasted with #$ChainOrganization, among other things.")
(comment ElectricBlanket "A blanket which has wires threaded through it which heat up when connected to an electrical outlet and switched on.")
(comment Appendage-AnimalBodyPart "An #$AnimalBodyPartType and a specialization of both #$ExternalAnatomicalPart
and #$AnimalBodyPart.  #$Appendage-AnimalBodyPart is the collection of all 
appendages of #$Animals.  An appendage is a body part that is connected to, 
and extends from, an animal's #$Torso (or from another of the animal's appendages, 
such as a hand extending from an arm).  Each appendage is used by the #$Animal 
for one or more functions.  Altogether, appendages serve a wide variety of 
functions, including locomotion, manipulation, sensing, fighting, scratching, 
heat dissipation, and balance.  Note that appendages are not crucial for the 
life of the animal; thus a #$Neck-AnimalBodyPart or #$Head-AnimalBodyPart is 
not considered to be an appendage.")
(comment CondyloidJoint "An #$ArthrodialJoint is a #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart in which the bones are #$rotationallyConnectedTo each other so that the second bone can move with two degrees of freedom, but without axial rotation.  A #$Condyle of the first bone articulates with the second bone.")
(comment Running "The collection of instances of #$LocomotionProcess-Animal in which an #$Animal agent travels on foot using rapid voluntary movements of its legs; similar to walking, only faster.")
(disjointWith Scroll Card)
(disjointWith DeviceRunning TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment OilTreatment "Stuff (like STP) added to motor oil that enhances the performance of your car.")
(comment Pile "A pile is a group or mob of things stacked or piled on top of each other in either an organized or disorganized  fashion. If it's neat, it could be called a stack.")
(comment WarrantyDocument "A written guarantee of the quality of a product, and detailing the manufacturer's responsibilities in case of product failure.")
(comment SmallIntestine "The collection of all small intestines.  A member of this collection is an #$AnatomicalVessel which isthe part of the #$DigestiveSystem which is the chief site of the absorption of digested nutrients.  A #$SmallIntestine is the section of the #$AlimentaryCanal between the #$Stomach and the #$Colon-BodyPart.")
(comment Arrow "The collection of arrows.")
(comment Borzoi "A collection of large dogs.  Before 1936 in North America he was known as the Russian Wolfhound.")
(disjointWith LanguageGroupingType LifeStageType)
(disjointWith InsuranceOrganization ChamberOfCommerce)
(comment CamShaft "The shaft of a #$FourCycleEngine that ensures that the valves open and close at the proper time relative the position of the pistons.")
(comment SerratusPosteriorInferior "The #$Collection of all instances of #$SerratusPosteriorInferior #$Muscle.  The #$SerratusPosteriorInferior #$Muscle connects the lower #$Vertebrae with the ninth through twelfth ribs, serving to lower the ribs and compress the chest during #$Exhaling.")
(comment FloorLamp "The collection for lamps that sit on the floor")
(comment PersonEnrolledInFn "#$PersonEnrolledInFn is a  #$CollectionDenotingFunction used to represent people who are enrolled in a specific kind of #$EducationalOrganization.  For example, (#$PersonEnrolledInFn #$HighSchool) returns a collection identical with the collection #$HighSchoolStudent.  In general, (#$PersonEnrolledInFn ORGTYPE) returns a collection of people who are enrolled at an educational institution of ORGTYPE.  Note that this function does not return a particular individual enrolled, but rather a collection of people whose common characteristic (``type'') is the kind of educational program they are pursuing.  See also #$PersonTypeByActivity.")
(comment Peritoneum "The collection of all peritonea.  An instance of this collection is a membranous sac in the #$AbdominalCavity which wraps the abdominal #$Organs.")
(comment ComputerStore "Local (at one site) retail organization that sells computers, peripherals, and ancillary products to customers in exchange for money.")
(comment MP3ToWavCompiler "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs whose purpose         is to convert an #$MP3File to a #$WAVFile with the same         information content.")
(comment AssaultRifle "The collection of firearms that fire multiple bullets with each trigger pull.")
(disjointWith Appendage-AnimalBodyPart Skin)
(comment StemCell "A specialization of #$Cell. Each instance of #$StemCell is a cell that is as-yet undifferentiated and thus is capable of becoming different sorts of tissue.  Most stem cells are found in embryonic and fetal tissue.")
(comment ArabicNumeral "The collection of all Arabic #$Numerals, '0' through '9'.  Note that these numerals, despite their name, are not part of the numeric system currently used in the Arabic countries; rather, they appear

in the ordinary Western European numeric system.")
(comment AltarTable "A table-like piece of furniture at which some religious ceremonies occur.")
(comment Flying-FlappingWings "Locomotion of an animal through the air by means of flapping its wings.")
(disjointWith CoastGuardOrganization AirForce)
(comment SewerLine "The collection of all sewer lines, conduits of sewer pipes used to drain sewage or rainwater.  Each #$SewerLine has two ends, and a natural direction of flow; most work because of gravity rather than active pumping.  See also #$SewerSystem.")
(comment DorsalRamusC5 "The collection of all C5 dorsal rami.  #$VentralRamusC5 and #$DorsalRamusC5 branch from SpinalRootC5.  #$DorsalRamusC5 supplies the #$Skin on the back (#$Back-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment Salsa-TheCondiment "A spice sauce used in mexican food.  It consists of (#$FruitFn #$TomatoPlant), #$Onion-Foodstuff, and #$Pepper-Foodstuff.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice ComputationalSystem)
(comment ArmSling "A piece of fabric which is wrapped around the neck and used to support an injured arm.")
(comment Neutrophil "A subclass of #$WhiteBloodCell, quite similar to #$Macrophage in size, structure and function, which, unlike macrophages, circualte in the #$Blood. Given chemical stimulus they exit the bloodstream and enter tissues.")
(comment Cartoon-Animated "The collection of all #$Cartoons that are animated.")
(comment KnuckleWalking "The process of walking on one's legs and knuckles.")
(disjointWith Engine TransportationDevice)
(comment CashewTree "Individual cashew trees; yield delicious nuts.")
(comment YugoslavianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Yugoslavia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat OrganizationTypeByCustomers)
(comment RubberBand "The collection of rubber bands.")
(comment Spatula "an implement with a broad flat usually flexible blade, used for blending foods or removing them from cooking utensils, e.g. flipping hamburgers.")
(comment Bomb-RoadVehicleDelivered "A specialization of #$Bomb.  Each instance of #$Bomb-RoadVehicleDelivered is a device typically employed by a terrorist organization.  Each instance is an explosive device that is brought into proximity to its target by covert means involving a road vehicle (see #$RoadVehicle).  The vehicle may be parked in the vicinity of the target and evacuated by its driver prior to detonation, or it may be driven into the target by a suicide bomber or bombers who are killed when the device explodes.  Do not confuse this collection with #$CarBomb-BoobyTrap, which refers to bombs wired into the ignition systems of vehicles unbeknownst to their occupants.")
(comment PregnancyEndingEvent "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent and #$AnimalActivity. Each instance of this collection is an event which terminates a #$Pregnancy. Notable specializations of this collection include birth (cf. #$BirthEvent), abortion (cf. #$Abortion-Intentional), and #$Miscarriage.")
(disjointWith ElementStuffType SpecifiedCheeseType)
(comment SecurityManager-Java "#$SecurityManager-Java is a specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.
Instances of #$SecurityManager-Java determine whether an instance of
#$Applet-ComputerProgram interpreted by an instance of
#$JavaVirtualMachine can read or write from the client's hard disk or
manipulate the client's input/output devices.")
(comment SportsOrganization "#$SportsOrganization is a specialization of #$EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization and #$ActivityTypeFocusGroup.  Each instance of #$SportsOrganization is an organization whose main function is involved with #$SportsEvents.")
(comment ProgramSpecification "A specialization of #$Specification. Each instance of this collection is not a computer program itself (i.e. lines of code), but an abstract characterization of how a program should behave.  For instance, a sorting program can be specified by requiring that the program's output be a list of the same elements as the input such that no element follows an element that is greater than it. A notable example of a #$ProgramSpecification is UNIX - which is not (contrary to popular belief) an operating system per se, but a specification to which many different operating systems (instances of #$UnixOS) conform. Note that instances of #$ProgramSpecification do not necessarily specify single, discrete programs -- thus many of the internet's \"RFC\" protocol-establishing documents (see #$RequestForComments-Internet) fall into this collection.")
(comment Ischium "The #$Ischium forms the the rear and lower part of the #$PelvicBone.")
(disjointWith HarvestingAPlant Boating)
(comment CourtShoe "The collection of shoes which are designed for court play.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement EmittingAnObject)
(comment Finger "The collection of all digits of all #$Hands (q.v.).  Fingers are (typically) flexibly jointed and are necessary to enabling the hand (and its owner) to perform grasping and manipulation actions.")
(disjointWith Leather Sandpaper)
(comment Terrier-Boston "A collection of smooth-coated, small dogs with short tails.  There are three             different sizes of instances of #$Terrier-Boston: less than 15 lbs.,              between 15 and 20 lbs. and between 20 and 25 lbs.")
(comment BiffechePerson "The collection of all people who are of the culture of the kingdom of Biffeche in northern Senegal (#$Biffeche-KingdomOf), and who identify themselves as 'Biffeche'.")
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment Jukebox "The collection of all jukeboxes. A #$Jukebox is a coin-operated CD- or record-playing machine, usually found in restaurants or bars.")
(comment TransverseAbdominous "The #$Collection of all instances of #$TransverseAbdominous #$Muscle.  The #$TransverseAbdominous #$Muscle compresses the abdominal contents.  The fibers are aligned perpendicular to the axis of the #$Torso.  The #$TransverseAbdominous lies internal to the #$InternalOblique.")
(comment PassengerCompartment "The region of transportation devices such as planes, cars etc. which are meant for occupation by people")
(comment RadialVein "The collection of all radial #$Veins.  The proximal end of the #$RadialVein connects to the #$BrachialVein, passes through the #$ForeArm and then ends in the palmar venous arches of the #$Hand.")
(comment TripleCremeCheese "This is the collection of instances of triple creme cheese. Triple creme

refers to the proportion of butterfat in the cheese, this being the

category which is highest in that respect, around 75%. A famous example of a triple creme

cheese is #$StAndre-Cheese.")
(comment ZipFile "This is the collection of computer files which have been compressed using the PKZIP utility.")
(comment GolfBag "Cylindrical bag about one meter long, open on one end; for carrying golf clubs.  Has shoulder strap.")
(disjointWith FoodUtensil NaturalTangibleStuff)
(comment AnemiaGenus "A genus of ferns having pinnatifid fronds. Found mainly in tropical parts of the Americas.")
(comment NorfolkIslandPerson "A person who is a #$NorfolkIsland #$citizens, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HomeAudioReceiver "A subcollection of both  #$Receiver-AudioComponent  and #$HomeAudioSystemComponent. Instances of #$HomeAudioReceiver are meant to be components of instances of #$HomeAudioSystem.")
(comment CreoleLanguage "languages based on a \"combination\" of 2 or more others; pidgins are 2nd languages for their speakers, creoles are mother tongues")
(comment Wrench "A tool used for rotating things like bolts")
(comment QuackingSound "The collection of quacking sounds made by ducks.")
(comment exportsDirectoryToComputer "A predicate used to relate instances of #$Computer with instances of #$FileDirectory.  (#$exportsDirectoryToComputer SERVER DIRECTORY CLIENT) means that SERVER allows CLIENT to mount DIRECTORY, which is located on SERVER.  Thus the user of CLIENT can access to files and subdirectories of DIRECTORY.  That is, SERVER and CLIENT participate in a file sharing system, which could be implemented by NFS, AFS,

NTFS, etc.")
(comment SeatingDeviceArm "The collection of the arms of seating devices.")
(comment Salyut "The collection of all Salyut #$SpaceStations.  The first #$Salyut, Salyut I, was the first #$SpaceStation constructed by humanity.  The #$UnionOfSovietSocialistRepublics launched seven of such craft, the first on 19 April 1971, and the last in 1982.")
(comment ParietalPleura "The collection of parietal pleurae, the outer enclosing sheath membranes surrounding the #$VisceralPleura which in turn  contains the #$Lung.  The ParietalPleura is in the #$ChestCavity, forming the outer wall of the #$PleuralCavity.  In human beings there are separate right and left ParietalPleurae.")
(comment Cake "Spongy dessert food item")
(comment AgreementForOngoingService "A collection of agreements. In this sort of agreement, there are two types of parties: the #$agreeingServiceProvider and the #$agreeingServiceRecipient.  During the term of this agreement, the recipient has the right to be the #$beneficiary in some #$ServiceEvent, with the provider as the #$providerOfService. Specializations include PhoneServiceAgreement, CableServiceAgreement, InternetServiceAgreeement, #$InsurancePlan. These kinds of agreements have a 'base rate' (which might be zero) and a 'per use fee' (which might be zero, or might be a function of time or of quantity used, etc.).")
(disjointWith BiologicalEvent VehicleAccident)
(comment Lamppost "An outdoor lamppost attached to a streetlight.")
(comment TouristAttraction "A site or object that draws tourists. E.g., a historic landmark, a site of remarkable scenic beauty; famous architecture; a museum containing famous art; a zoo; a home of, or monument to, a famous person; ... ")
(comment Tentacle "A flexible, boneless arm-like appendage which sometimes has suction cups, and sometimes occurs on invertebrates")
(comment TrainEngine "#$TrainEngine is a specialization of #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle, #$FuelPoweredDevice, and #$WheeledTransportationDevice.  Each instance of #$TrainEngine is a fuel-powered, non-steerable, wheeled vehicle that runs on #$Railway tracks, and has enough power to pull or push a group of #$TrainCars with it.")
(comment Affenpinscher "A specialization of #$ToyDog.   Affenpinschers are sometimes called \"monkey dogs\" because they have very monkey-like faces.")
(comment DominicanRepublicPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of the #$DominicanRepublic, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AnimalOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations whose activities focus on the care, breeding, other welfare, or study of animals. Examples of specializations of #$AnimalOrganization include #$AnimalBreeder-Business and #$Kennel-Organization.  Some organizations may be instances of both #$AnimalOrganization and #$AgricultureOrganization.")
(comment LaundryHamper "The collection of all laundry hampers.  A #$LaundryHamper is a container in which one puts dirty clothes until one gets around to washing them.")
(comment Ectropion "A collection of #$AilmentConditions in which the lower eyelid sags away from the eyeball.  It can result in #$Conjunctivitis.")
(comment Axe "A hand tool used for cutting, comprised of a long handle and a heavy wedge-shaped head with one sharp edge.")
(comment Pepper-Foodstuff "Foodstuff from the edible fruit of pepper plants.")
(comment hasDepartments "The predicate #$hasDepartments relates a particular organization to some particular department(s) within that organization.  (#$hasDepartments ORG DEPT) means that ORG, an instance of #$Organization, has DEPT among its #$Departments.  DEPT is a sub-organization of ORG that performs some of the activity of ORG.  In Cyc, the collection #$Department (q.v.) covers generically what may be called a division, department, office, bureau, ministry, etc., within an actual organization.  Commercial organizations, for example, commonly have instances of #$AccountingDepartment, #$HumanResourcesDepartment, and perhaps #$LegalDepartment, among others.  For example, (#$hasDepartmentTypes KMartStoreAtParmerLane #$CustomerServiceDepartment).  Government organizations have different specialized departments to carry out the functions of that government; e.g., (#$hasDepartments CityOfAustinTXCityGovernment AustinFireDepartment).  Cf. #$hasDepartmentTypes.")
(comment EducationalComputerProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are

intended for educational purposes.")
(disjointWith AutoDealership ConvenienceStore)
(comment BassViolin "large stringed instrument of the violin family ")
(comment FelisGenus "The genus which contains the species to which domestic cats belong.")
(comment TextEditing "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent. Each instance of this collection is an act of editing some sort of #$TextualMaterial -- which could be a text on a computer, or a tangible piece of writing.")
(comment TakingOffAClothingItem "A specialization of #$RemovingSomething-Translational.  Each instance of #$TakingOffAClothingItem is an event in which something being worn is removed, either by the wearer or by someone else (e.g., removing a child's boots or a horse's saddle).  After an instance of #$TakingOffAClothingItem occurs, the situation (an instance of #$WearingSomething) in which the item was being #$wornOn the body is over.")
(comment Subwoofer "A specialized #$StereoSpeaker responsible for producing deep bass.")
(disjointWith Organism-Whole Gamete-Mature)
(comment LatinCapitalLetterW "The capital letter 'W'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$W-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterW.")
(comment NailFile "File used on one's finger- or toenails.")
(disjointWith HittingAnObject Project)
(comment interArgNotIsa3-5 "(#$interArgNotIsa3-5 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the third argument to PRED, the fifth argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(comment ComputerOutputDevice "A specialization of #$ComputerInterfaceDevice. Each instance of this collection is an #$ElectronicDevice which delivers information from a computer to its user.")
(disjointWith GovernmentalOrganization PrivateSectorOrganization)
(comment AudioRecordingFn "#$AudioRecordingFn takes as argument any

instance of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of all

AudioRecordings of that agent. For example, (#$AudioRecordingFn

#$RollingStones) returns the collection of all audio recordings by the

Rolling Stones.")
(disjointWith CreatingAnArtifact PlacingSensoryOrganToSenseThrough)
(comment Toothbrush "The set of toothbrush-like objects")
(comment DorsalRamusC8 "The collection of all C8 dorsal rami.  #$VentralRamusC8 and #$DorsalRamusC8 branch from SpinalRootC8.  #$DorsalRamusC8 supplies the #$Skin on the back (#$Back-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment BarbecueSauce "This is the collection of all instances of barbeque sauce. Barbeque sauces

vary considerably in composition. The most common ones are tomato-based,

but some varieties are not. Barbeque sauces are generally somewhat spicy.

What they all have in common is that they are intended to be eaten as

a condiment with grilled or barbequed meats.")
(comment typicalBehaviorInSitType "(#$typicalBehaviorInSitType AGT SITTYPE ACTTYPE) says that if AGT is in an instance of SITTYPE it is #$expected-ToBe that AGT will play the #$doneBy role in some instance of ACTTYPE that is temporally subsumed by the instance of SITTYPE in question.  Note that it is possible for there to be many different ACTTYPEs that are typical for an agent in a particular SITTYPE.")
(comment FileCompressionProgram "Software which compresses files.  This could be done to save space on a hard drive or to speed transfer of the file over the internet.")
(comment Splicing "The collection of events in which two long, thin objects, such as pieces of rope, wood, or tape, are connected at their ends.")
(comment orgTypesSimilarWithRespectToGenotype "(#$orgTypesSimilarWithRespectToGenotype ORGTYPE1 ORGTYPE2)
means that instances of ORGTYPE1 have #$Genomes that are similar,
possibly suggesting a common evolutionary origin.  Sometimes, but not always, it is the case that (#$orgTypesSimilarWithRespectToPhenotype ORGTYPE1 ORGTYPE2) as well, although it can certainly come about that species with very similar genotypes have markedly different phenotypic forms, e.g., humans and chimpanzees.")
(comment AppointmentCard "The sort of card a dentist gives you to confirm and remind you of an appointment.")
(disjointWith Luggage FluidReservoir)
(comment DicotSubclass "One of the two subclasses in the angiosperm class.  Includes taxa whose members usually have two cotyledons in the embryo phase, may have a cambium, and usually have broad leaves with branching veins.")
(comment TunisianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Tunisia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment CrayMachine "Multi-user supercomputer.")
(comment Eleven-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '11.'")
(comment FurianLanguageFamily "Languages spoken in the Sudan")
(comment Kettle "A kettle with a spout, handle, and lid, for boiling water on the stove top.")
(comment CrossingLegs "The movement of crossing one's legs, while sitting, standing, or reclining.")
(comment RibosomeAttachesToRNA "The collection of events in which a ribosome attaches to the 5' end of an RNA molecule.")
(comment DitransitiveInfinitivePhraseFrameType "The collection of all frames that take two complements, one of which is an NP and the other an infinitive phrase.")
(comment ServerProgram "A specialization of #$NetworkingProgram. Each instance of this collection is a #$ComputerProgram-CW used to process requests that come in across a #$ComputerNetwork. It is thus to be contrasted with #$LocalProgram. More technically, the defining characteristic of a #$ServerProgram is that it listens on a port.")
(comment SellingOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization and #$Vendor.  Each instance of #$SellingOrganization is an organization whose main function is to sell things by conducting sales activities.  Specializations include #$SalesDepartment, #$AdvertisingAgency, and #$RetailOrganization.")
(comment SurgicalNeedle "Needles used for stitching flesh during surgery or to aid healing of a wound.")
(comment PizzaFn "This function takes a set of ingredient-types and produces
the collection of pizzas with those toppings.")
(disjointWith Appendage-AnimalBodyPart Head-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment FloatingRib "A #$FloatingRib connects to #$CostalCartilage which is not connected to any other #$CostalCartilage.")
(comment WalkingOnFourLegs "The process of walking on four legs.")
(comment SubmachineGun "A specialization of both #$AutomaticFirearm and #$Gun-Portable.  Each instance of #$SubmachineGun is a portable, personal automatic firearm, designed for firing from the hip or shoulder.")
(comment FuelDeicer "Like the stuff to make airplanes fly, but for your car..")
(comment Titanium "All pieces (i.e., specific collections of nearby molecules) of titanium; typically, these will be tightly bound into solid form, although the collection includes liquid, gasseous, and chmically bound forms as well.")
(comment SpecificationDocument "The document on which a specification is written.")
(comment Trachea "The collection of all tracheas (Windpipes): air tubes, each of which runs from the #$Larynx to the #$TracheobronchialJunction where it is connected to the two main #$BronchialTubes or bronchi, which lead to the #$Lungs.")
(comment ArbitraryFileDeletionFault "A program has an #$ArbitraryFileDeletionFault if allows arbitrary files to be deleted by an unauthorized user.  Because deletion is a kind of overwriting, #$ArbitraryFileDeletionFault is a specialization of #$ArbitraryFileOverwriteFault.")
(comment PocketKnife "The collection of pocket knives. A pocket knife is a folding knife in which the blade is safely sheathed inside a casing while the knife is being carried around. Many pocket knives contain a number of tools in addition to the main blade.")
(comment BerneseMountainDog "A collection of relatively large dogs.")
(disjointWith DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType LanguageGroupingType)
(disjointWith RevoltOrganization InsuranceOrganization)
(comment CrankShaft "The part of an internal combustion engine that turns linear movement of the pistons into rotational movement, which can then be used by the device the engine is powering.")
(comment QuadratusLumborum "The #$Collection of all instances of #$QuadratusLumborum #$Muscle. The #$QuadratusLumborum #$Muscle connects the lower #$Vertebrae with the #$Ilium and #$TwelfthRib.  It flexesthe #$Torso laterally or raises the #$Hip.")
(comment ElectricLamp "The collection for all kinds of freestanding (easily moveable) electrical lamps.")
(comment LeftLobeOfLiver "The collection of all left lobes of #$Livers.  Each element of this collection is a part of a #$Liver located in the caudal region of an #$Abdomen near the midline of the body.")
(comment Sweetener "Substances used to sweeten other ConsumableStuffs")
(comment SmallGasConvenienceStore "This is a gas station, without repair service, that happens to also be a convenience store (i.e., it has a smaller selection of goods then normal convenience stores that sell gas.")
(comment CD-ROMDriver "An instance is a piece of software that is used to control           a #$CD-ROMDrive.")
(comment MagazineForBullets "The magazine for an automatic firearm. It holds bullets for the gun to fire.")
(disjointWith Eye Skin)
(comment Towel "The collection of sheets of cloth or paper manufactured and used primarily to dry objects.")
(comment ReedWoodwindInstrument "The collection of all single or double reed #$WoodwindInstruments")
(comment Invertebrate "A specialization of #$Poikilotherm.  Each instance of #$Invertebrate is an animal that lacks a backbone. #$Invertebrate includes insects, molluscs, sea squirts, worms (in a large variety of worm phyla), and many others. Note: Although #$Invertebrate is a scientific category, it is not a standard taxon in the biological taxonomy, hence it is not an instance of #$BiologicalTaxon.")
(comment uppercaseOfLetter "(uppercaseOfLetter UPPERCASE LETTER) means that UPPERCASE is the upper-case character corresponding to the character LETTER (which may be uppercase, lowercase, or case-less).  For example, both of the following hold: (#$uppercaseOfLetter #$LatinCapitalLetterA #$A-TheLetter) and (#$uppercaseOfLetter #$LatinCapitalLetterA #$LatinSmallLetterA).  See also #$uppercaseOfLowercase.  #$uppercaseOfLetter connot be applied directly to instances of #$SubLString; but see #$stringVersionOfCharacter.")
(comment BenchWithBack "Long pew-like seats with backs.")
(comment DeclarativeUtterance "The collection of declarative utterances issued in any language.")
(comment TransistorNetwork "An electrical device, consisting of pass transistors, whose inputs and outputs are digital signals and that implements a boolean function.")
(comment DorsalRamusC1 "The collection of all C1 dorsal rami.  #$VentralRamusC1 and #$DorsalRamusC1 branch from SpinalRootC1.  #$DorsalRamusC1 supplies the #$SubOccipitalNerve.")
(comment CocktailDrink "The collection of cocktail drinks, mixture of #$AlcoholicBeverages, #$FlavoringCompounds and often #$Juice, typically served as refreshments preceding or accompanying a meal.")
(comment ConsumableProduct "A specialization of #$PartiallyTangibleProduct.  Each instance of #$ConsumableProduct is a product of which any portion can be used only once.  A portion of a #$ConsumableProduct is `used up', i.e., destroyed or transformed into an unusable or waste form, during normal use.  Note: `consumable' here does not necessarily mean consumed by mouth; the consumption may be any use of the product.")
(disjointWith PlumbingFixture ComputationalSystem)
(comment NeckBrace "A device used to support and immobilize an injured neck.")
(comment Antigen "The collection of substances that can stimulate immune

response. For example, bacteria [#$Bacterium], #$Viruses, proteins [#$ProteinMolecule] can serve as #$Antigens.")
(comment Cartoon-Animated-Silent "The collection of all instances of #$Cartoon-Animated that consist entirely of #$MovingImages and have no subevents of #$SoundInformationBearingThing.")
(comment Ovulating "The process in which an ovum is discharged by an ovary.")
(disjointWith Language VisualWork)
(disjointWith PoundingDrivingImplement GraspingImplement)
(comment GrapefruitTree "A tree that grows grapefruits")
(comment GreatSarkIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$GreatSark-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType OrganizationTypeByCustomers)
(comment Tack "The collection of tacks. Tacks are basically

short nails with broad heads.")
(comment SafeTheLocker "A locking metal container for valuables.")
(comment IndustrialGoods "The collection of goods or components produced primarily as tools for the production of other goods.")
(comment PosteriorRegionFn "An instance of #$PartialFunction and #$ReifiableFunction.  When applied to an instance REGION of #$AnimalBodyRegion, #$PosteriorRegionFn returns the region consisting of the rear half or section, or posterior main portion, of REGION.  Note that #$PosteriorRegionFn applies only when REGION itself has an intrinsic front/back orientation, or is a (non-backward-facing) part of a larger region or object that has a front/back orientation.")
(disjointWith GrillingFood SteamingFood)
(comment StockExchange "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$StockExchange is an organization that provides or maintains a marketplace (or marketplaces) where securities, options, futures, or commodities can be traded.  Examples of such organizations in the UnitedStates include the New York Stock Exchange, the American Stock Exchange, and NASDAQ.")
(disjointWith BicycleLight AutomotiveLight)
(comment ClassLoader-Java "#$ClassLoader-Java is a specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.

Instances of #$ClassLoader-Java examine instances of #$JavaClass to

ensure they do not violate the Java run-time system. One way to

violate the run-time system would be to have a malicious program

disable the standard SecurityManager class (see

#$SecurityManager-Java), or replace it with a more permissive

version. ")
(disjointWith CommercialServiceOrganization SportsOrganization)
(comment Pillowcase "The collection of pillowcases - removable fabric envelopes designed to go around a pillow, which are easier to clean than the entire pillow.")
(comment BiologicalSubfamily "The collection of biological taxonomic subdivisions below #$BiologicalFamily and above #$BiologicalGenus.")
(disjointWith Communicating EnteringInfoIntoDevice)
(comment Ilium "The #$Ilium is the part of the of the #$PelvicBone underlying the #$Hip.")
(disjointWith SportsCar Truck)
(comment EMailMessageText "#$EMailMessageText is the subcollection of #$ComputerAIS consisting of all of the information structures of the authored textual part of #$EMailMessages.")
(comment BoxingShoe "The collection of shoes one normally wears while boxing.")
(comment EncephalitisInfection "The collection of all #$Infections whose principle characteristic (and threat to the host organism) is a swelling of the brain tissue (as opposed to swelling, say, of the meninges or other tissues surrounding the brain).  This is a very broad category, in that various forms of #$EncephalitisInfection are caused by different types of organism: some types are bacterial, others are viral, with a wide variety of bacteria and viruses being implicated.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement WavePropagation)
(comment Forearm "The segment of an arm farthest away from the torso; between the elbow and the wrist")
(disjointWith Film-SheetOrCoating Leather)
(comment Terrier-Airedale "A collection of dogs, the largest of any breed of Terriers, also called simply              the Airedale.")
(comment PolynesianPerson "A person who is a citizen of Polynesia-AtPresent.")
(disjointWith ManufacturingOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment PlasticFoodContainer "The collection of all reusable #$PlasticContainers designed primarily for storing food in. Many instances are made by Tupperware and Rubbermaid.")
(comment HumanImmunodeficiencyVirus "The virus that causes AIDS.")
(comment AdductorBrevis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$AdductorBrevis #$Muscle.  The #$AdductorBrevis adducts and assists flexion and medial rotation of the #$Femur at the #$Hip.")
(comment Elevator "The #$Collection of all #$Elevators.  An #$Elevator is a device with a normally closed compartment which moves vertically, lifting or lowering people and goods located in that compartment, normally between floors of a building.")
(comment ownerOfProprietaryThing "(#$ownerOfProprietaryThing THING AGENT) means that AGENT is the proprietary 'owner' of THING. THING may be tangible or
intangible; it may be a piece of information, for example.")
(comment UlnarVein "The collection of all ulnar veins.  The proximal end of the ulnar vein connects to the brachial vein, passes through the forearm and then ends in the palmar venous arches of the hand.")
(comment StAndre-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of St. Andre, a French cheese.

It is a #$TripleCremeCheese with a rich mellow flavor that deepens as it ages.

Given that it is 75% butterfat, it is soft and buttery.")
(comment fromOrganization "A specialization of #$from-Generic, #$fromOrganization can

be used to indicate, in a more specific way,

the instance of #$Organization from which the instance

of #$IntelligentAgent is transferred in some

instance of #$OrganizationalTransfer.

(#$fromOrganization TRANS ORG) means that in the 

instance TRANS of #$OrganizationalTransfer, the

#$transferredThing is transferred from the instance

ORG of #$Organization.  See also #$OrganizationalTransferIn and

#$toOrganization.")
(comment amountOfMainOutputProducedInEvent "(#$amountOfMainOutputProducedInEvent CRE NUM) means that in #$CreationEvent CRE the number of outputs produced is NUM, where CRE is an event of type TYPE which is a kind of creation event which results in a single kind of output. For instance, in a car manufacturing event, automobiles and only automobiles are the outputs created, so we might forego use of the more complicated ternary predicate #$amountProducedInEvent.")
(comment Poker-ComputerCardGame "The collection of all computer programs designed to play the game of poker (#$Poker-CardGame).")
(comment SalsaMusic "Latin music that has roots in rhythm & blues, jazz and rock")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice InformationRecordingDevice)
(comment BritishPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of the
#$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HomeStereoSpeaker "A subcollection of both #$HomeAudioSystemComponent and #$StereoSpeaker. Instances of #$HomeStereoSpeaker are designed to output sound as components of instances of  #$HomeAudioSystem.")
(disjointWith Water (DeadPhysicalRemainsFn MuscleTissue))
(comment BerberLanguageFamily "An Afro-Asiatic language family of languages spoken primarily in North Africa.")
(comment Voltmeter "Device for measuring electrical voltage which is commonly used in repairing electrical devices")
(comment RoaringSound "The collection of roaring sounds made by lions.")
(comment directoryForFile "A predicate relating instances of #$FileDirectory with instances of #$ComputerFile-Abstract.  (#$directoryForFile DIRECTORY FILE) means that DIRECTORY \"contains\" FILE in either the subdirectory itself or in

one of its subdirectories.  Note that FILE can also be a directory, in

which case FILE is a subdirectory of DIRECTORY.")
(comment PowerGenerationComplex "The collection of all power-generation complexes/facilities.  Typically, these may cover several acres and consist of more than one building + transformers, generators, etc.")
(comment GeminiSpacecraft "The collection of all Gemini manned #$Spacecraft.  Each #$GeminiSpacecraft could transport two #$Astronauts to Earth orbit.")
(comment HypoglossalNerve "The collection of all hypoglossal #$Nerves.  A #$HypoglossalNerve is a twelfth #$CranialNerve.  The #$HypoglossalNerve #$innervates the #$Tongue #$Muscles.")
(comment Butchering "The collection of butchering events -- events in which an animal or animal part (by default, dead and uncooked or uncured or unsmoked or unsalted, etc.) is cut up into pieces.")
(comment TaxResidentsFn "`(#$TaxResidentsFn STATE)' denotes the collection of persons
who, for tax purposes, are considered to be residents of STATE.")
(comment Toilet "The collection of modern 20th century western-style toilets")
(comment HorseCarriage "Horse-drawn carriages.")
(comment Trunk-TheAppendage "Elephant's long nose")
(disjointWith TrainEngine LawnMower)
(comment DomesticatedAnimal "A specialization of #$TameAnimal.  Each instance of #$DomesticatedAnimal is an animal that has been bred and trained in such a way that it cannot readily survive in the wild.  Domesticated animals are kept by humans for labor, transportation, food, or as pets, and their relations with humans are more or less cooperative.  #$DomesticatedAnimal does _not_ include most wild animals kept in zoos (see #$CaptiveAnimal).  Cf. #$WildAnimal.")
(comment SeychellesPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Seychelles, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith AnimalOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment DiaperBag "The collection of all diaper bags.  A #$DiaperBag is a bag which the caretaker of a baby may put #$Diapers, wipes, and other baby-related products into to bring with him or her when traveling with a #$HumanInfant or #$HumanToddler.")
(comment Amblyopia "A collection of #$AilmentConditions. Each instance is an eye disorder that causes dimness of vision.   It may be gradual or sudden in onset and can be permanent or transient.  The condition commonly known as 'lazy eye' is a form of #$Amblyopia.")
(comment Hatchet "A hand tool used for cutting, comprised of a short handle and a wedge-shaped head with one sharp edge.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single AccessingAnIBT)
(comment InterventricularSeptum "The collection of all interventricular (or 'ventricular') septa.  An individual #$InterventricularSeptum is the partition separating the left and right #$VentricleOfHeart.")
(comment BeanPod-Foodstuff "Foodstuff made from bean pods, whole or sliced or, for that matter, pulverized.")
(comment ComputerOfficeSuiteProgram "This is the collection of computer office suites, such as #$MSOffice and #$StarOffice. These are bundles of

programs designed primarily for business use. They programs

they contain are integrated with one another, so that the

suite as a whole can be considered a single program. They generally include

a spreadsheet program, a word processor, an email program, and a

presentation program.")
(disjointWith InternationalOrganization NationalOrganization)
(comment Viola "stringed instrument slightly larger than a violin")
(comment BusinessCard "A specialization of #$Card. Each instance of this collection is a small piece of cardstock paper (typically 2 x 3.5 inches) containing basic contact information for an individual in a business context; at least their #$Name, company, mailing address, #$PhoneNumber.")
(comment CleaningDevice "#$CleaningDevice is a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$CleaningDevice is a device, manually powered or otherwise, whose #$primaryFunction is to be used in cleaning things.  Specializations of #$CleaningDevice include #$Mop, #$Dishwasher, #$ShoeBrush, and #$ClothesWasher.")
(comment AudioSpeaker "The electrical component used to convey sound")
(comment LatinSmallLetterW "The lowercase letter 'w'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$W-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterW.")
(comment HairDryer "The collection of hair dryers -- not necessarily hand-held devices which dry hair by directing a stream of warm air onto it.")
(disjointWith HittingAnObject Washing)
(comment Concrete "#$Concrete is a specialization of #$ArtificialMaterial and #$BuildingMaterial.  Each instance of #$Concrete is a piece of an artificial mixture of cement, gravel, sand, and (during mixture, pouring, and forming) water.  Used widely in construction, pieces of concrete are formed into the desired shape while fluid and afterward hardened into a sturdy, durable material.  Instances of #$Concrete include bridge pilings, foundations of houses, and sidewalks.")
(comment ComputerInterfaceDevice "A specialization of #$ElectronicDevice. Each instance of this collection is a device that allows a user to communicate with a #$Computer.  One sigificant specialization of #$ComputerInterfaceDevices is #$ComputerInputDevice -- with its subsets #$ComputerKeyboard, #$Scanner-Optical, #$ComputerMouse, etc.  Another is #$ComputerOutputDevice -- with its subsets #$MonitorPort, #$ComputerMonitor-Color, etc.")
(disjointWith QuasiGovernmentalOrganization PrivateSectorOrganization)
(comment LASER-Device "A collection of devices used to create, amplify, and transmit narrow, intense beams of coherent light. The word 'LASER' is an acronym for 'light amplification by stimulated emission of radiation'.")
(comment TerrestrialOrganism "A specialization of #$Organism-Whole.  Each instance of #$TerrestrialOrganism is an organism adapted to life on land, out of water.  Instances of #$TerrestrialOrganism spend all or most of their time out of the water, either on the land surface or under it.  Specializations of #$TerrestrialOrganism include #$Dog, #$Bird, and #$Person.")
(comment PressingFaceAgainstToSee "The collection of all #$Actions in which the #$Animal performing the action places its face against or near something in order to see through that thing better.  Examples include peeking through a keyhole and placing ones face against a window to see through.")
(comment BathTowel "A standard size towel, intended for drying the body after bathing.")
(comment DorsalRamusT7 "The collection of all T7 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT7 and DorsalRamiT7 branch from SpinalRootT7.  DorsalRamiT7 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment Liquor-Drink "This is the collection of all instances of liquor. Alcoholic beverages are

usually divided into beer, wine, and liquor. Liquors are made by a

distilling process, although ingredients are generally added

after distillation. #$Liquor-Drink does not include fortified

wines, but does include liqueurs. With the possible exception of a few fortified

wines and liqueurs, instances of #$Liquor-Drink have a higher ethyl alcohol content

than wines or beers. ")
(comment FileAccessSecurityProgram "Software which controls access to files stored on a computer.")
(comment PaddleWheel "The large wheel on the back of a paddle boat which provides the forward propulsion")
(comment PostCard "Written correspondence on (typically) a 3 x 5 inch card.  Postcards often don't contain much content and are usually just a short note to say 'hi' to friends and family during vacations")
(comment SweetPotatoPlant "Individual sweet potato plants.")
(comment IranianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Iran, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HPWorkstation "The Unix-based workstations manufactured by HP")
(comment Face-PlayingCardType "A collection of subcollections of #$PlayingCard in which each instance is a collection containing all #$PlayingCards of a particular face, i.e. #$One-TheCard, #$Two-TheCard, #$Jack-TheCard, etc.")
(comment Chari-NileLanguageFamily "Languages spoken in the Sudan and Ethiopia and many other countries")
(comment RoastingPan "Those big pans in which a turkey is roasted or in which gravy is made on the stovetop.")
(comment Reaching "The collection of actions where an agent extends their arm(s) to reach something.")
(comment RNAThroughNuclearEnvelope "The subevent in a #$EukaryoticGeneExpression in which #$MessengerRNA passes from the nucleus of a #$Cell (#$CellNucleusFn) to #$Ribosomes in the #$Cytoplasm.")
(comment GarbageCan "The metal or plastic garbage cans that are kept outside the house and which get banged up by the sanitation workers when they empty them.")
(disjointWith Appendage-AnimalBodyPart Neck-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment SaddleJoint "A #$SaddleJoint allows movements similar to #$CondyloidJoint, but freer.")
(comment WalkingOnTwoLegs "The collection of events in which an animal or similarly-shaped agent walks on two legs.")
(disjointWith BiologicalEvent ChangeInUserRights)
(comment programCopyUsed "(#$programCopyUsed EV COPY) means that COPY is a #$ComputerProgramCopy used in the action EV.")
(comment AutoFuse "See Fuse, but one that is in your car.")
(comment Autograph " The collection of autographs, i.e famous person's handwritten signature .")
(comment Vein "Tubular, branching vessel which carries blood to the heart from the body")
(comment WINSFileDeletionFault "A program has a #$WINSFileDeletionFault if it allows the
 contents of the Windows Internet Name Service directory to be deleted
 by an unauthorized user.")
(comment GolfCart "#$GolfCart is a specialization of both #$WheeledTransportationDevice and #$TransportationDevice-Vehicle.  Each instance of #$GolfCart is a motorized vehicle that is designed for golfers to use to drive around on #$GolfCourses while they are playing #$Golf.  #$GolfCarts drive very slowly compared with #$Automobiles.")
(comment BorderCollie "A collection of medium-sized, sheep-herding dogs.  Also called the            Shepherd's Dog, the English Collie and the Working Collie.")
(disjointWith LanguageGroupingType PersonTypeByCulture)
(disjointWith CommunicationsOrganization InsuranceOrganization)
(comment TwoCycleEngine "The collection of #$Engines in which combustion takes place in each cylinder with every rotation of the crankshaft.")
(comment SpleniusCervicis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$SpleniusCervicis #$Muscle.  The #$SpleniusCervicis #$Muscle extends the neck if acting bilaterally, or flexes the neck and rotates it in the direction of the muscle if acting unilaterally.")
(comment VideoCassette "Video cassette tapes, blank or not.")
(disjointWith SportsAction Murder)
(comment RightLobeOfLiver "The collection of all right lobes of #$Livers.  Each element of this collection is located in the caudal region of an #$Abdomen on the right side of the body.")
(comment Vanillin "A piece of vanillin - a piece of substance made of vanillin molecules - the compound responsible for vanilla flavoring.")
(comment ConvenienceStore "The collection of establishments that sell a tiny subset of the things found in a good supermarket for twice the price.  Sometimes they also sell gasoline.  A favorite target for robbers and people addicted to automatic teller machines.")
(comment ibtTypeAmenableToCarryInfoType "(#$ibtTypeAmenableToCarryInfoType IBT-SPEC AIT-SPEC) means that instances of AIT-SPEC are often instantiated in instances of IBT-SPEC or that instances of IBT-SPEC, for whatever reasons, naturally lend themselves to instantiation of AITs of type AIT-SPEC.  For instance, we might note that (#$ibtTypeAmenableToCarryInfoType #$BookCopy #$Novel-CW).")
(comment AudioClipFn-Downloadable "#$AudioClipFn-Downloadable takes as argument any instance of #$SpecifiedMovieType or #$BroadcastSeriesType and returns the collection of all #$ComputerSoundFiles encoding partial or complete audio recordings of that instance of #$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType. These files are linked to the Internet so that they can be downloaded (see #$DownloadingAFile). For example, (#$AudioClipFn-Downloadable #$Seinfeld-TheTVShow) denotes the collection of #$ComputerSoundFiles which when played by appropriate software produce an instance of #$AudioClip from #$Terminator-TheMovie.")
(comment TargetRifle "small caliber rifle used for sport-target shooting.")
(comment CellularImmuneResponse "A subcollection of #$ImmuneResponse. Instances of  #$CellularImmuneResponse are those #$ImmuneResponses that are mediated by cells. See #$Lymphocyte and #$Antigen.")
(comment SingleReedWoodwindInstrument "The collection of all single-reed #$WoodwindInstruments")
(comment ExternalAnatomicalPart "#$ExternalAnatomicalPart is a specialization of #$OrganismPart.  Each instance of #$ExternalAnatomicalPart is a part of the external anatomy of an organism. Example subcollections include #$Earlobe and #$Leaf.")
(comment uppercaseOfLowercase "(uppercaseOfLowercase UPPERCASE LOWERCASE) means that UPPERCASE is the uppercase character corresponding to the lowercase character LOWERCASE.  The characters are instances of #$Character-Abstract rather than physical written, printed or displayed characters.  For example, the folowing holds: (#$uppercaseOfLetter #$LatinCapitalLetterA #$LatinSmallLetterA).  See also #$uppercaseOfLetter and #$lowercaseOfLetter.  This does not work directly  on instances of #$SubLString; see #$stringVersionOfCharacter.")
(comment AltarStage "A stage found in religious buildings used exclusively for religious ceremonies.")
(comment ImperativeUtterance "The collection of declarative utterances issued in any language.")
(comment Armory "A human-constructed storage facility used by a military organization

for storing weapons.")
(comment FemaleChild "The collection of female children, female kids about 12 years of age or less.")
(comment Soil-Product "The collection that includes all instances of #$Soil-Generic that can be bought in a store.")
(comment PudendalNerve "The collection of all pudendal (or 'pudic') #$Nerves.  An individual #$PudendalNerve is formed by #$VentralRamusS2, #$VentralRamusS3 and #$VentralRamusS4 and #$innervates areas of the genitals and #$Rectum.")
(comment TiramisuCake "The collection of all Tiramisu, an Italian dessert made with #$MascarponeCheese, #$EggYolk-Food, #$Coffee-Beverage and Lady Fingers cookies.")
(comment Cycad "A plant that is a member of the cycadopsida class.  They resemble palms; cycad species are dioecious (have male and female sex functions on separate plants.)")
(disjointWith ConsumableProduct (GroupFn Computer))
(comment DrivingDirections "A collection of #$PropositionalInformationThings.  Each instance of #$DrivingDirections is a set of instructions for how to travel from one place to another by car.")
(comment Puberty "The stage of physical development in which humans become sexually mature.")
(disjointWith Engine RecordingOfWaveIBT)
(comment LemonTree "A tree that grows lemons")
(comment LibyanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Libya, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment OrganizationWithoutCustomers "The collection of all #$Organizations that do not have #$customers.  Positive examples include #$LocalReligiousCongregation and #$NationalTaxAgency.")
(comment WindowCurtain "The collection of hanging, cloth window coverings - curtains, drapes, etc.")
(comment Flooding "A specialization of #$NaturalHazard.  Each instance of #$Flooding is an event in which water levels reach dangerous heights.")
(comment PulmonaryVein-Generic "The collection of all #$Veins which supply #$OxygenatedBlood to the left side of the #$Heart (the left #$AuricleOfHeart) from a #$Lung.")
(disjointWith BakingFood GrillingFood)
(comment Club-Organization "The collection of all Clubs. Each element of #$Club-Organization involves a group of people (i.e. typically more than one) who share some common characteristic (e.g. profession, interest, experience) and participate through membership in the organization, usually meeting periodically.")
(comment JavaScriptImplementation "#$JavaScriptImplementation is a collection of helper applications for instances of #$WorldWideWebClientProgram.  Its instances enable browsers to display features of web pages written in #$JavaScriptProgrammingLanguage.")
(disjointWith Camp-Recreational SportsOrganization)
(comment Tail-BodyPart "The appendage attached to the rear end of an animal.")
(disjointWith EnteringInfoIntoDevice TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment LateralRegionFn "The function (LateralRegionFn REGOROBJ), applied to a region or object REGOROBJ, means the sub-region consisting of the flanks or side parts or lateral main sections (away from the mid-line) of REGOROBJ, or the lateral main areas of REGOROBJ as opposed to the medial or middle area; the right and left regions then both include parts of the lateral regions.  #$LateralRegionFn applies when REGOROBJ itself has an intrinsic right/left orientation (unlike, say, a sphere), but if REGOROBJ is a part within a larger region or object that has its own right/left orientation, the function returns REGOROBJ's portions farthest from the mid-line (with respect to left and right) of the larger region or object.")
(comment sons "(#$sons PAR MALE) means that MALE is one of the sons (male children) of PAR.  MALE could be a child of PAR by birth, by adoption, by marriage (e.g., if PAR had married a biological parent of MALE), or by some other social arrangement.")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType AnimalTypeBySex)
(comment InternetNewsgroup "The collection of all internet newsgroups, such as rec.music.makers or alt.food.preserving.  Each instance of #$InternetNewsgroup has as #$episodes instances of #$InternetNewsgroupMessage, each of which is more or less on the group's central topic of focus.")
(comment BikeShoe "The collection of shoes one sometimes wears while riding a bicycle.")
(comment HodgkinsDisease "A type of malignant lymphoma, in which the #$Spleen, lymph nodes, and other lymphatic tissues progressively enlarge.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment Ankle "The flexible joint between the lower leg and the foot")
(comment Refinishing "A collection of events.  In each #$Refinishing event, some type of coating or finish is removed from the surface of an object in order to replace it with a new coating (of possibly a different type).  Thus, a #$Refinishing will have some sub-events in which the old finish is removed and some later sub-events in which the new finish is added.  The #$objectOfStateChange in a #$Refinishing may be a car, a doorframe, one of your fingernails, etc., but in general must be in a #$Solid-StateOfMatter.  Note that an event such as stripping the wood away from a doorframe, though prepatory to refinishing that doorframe, is not in and of itself an element of #$Refinishing; it is just one of the #$subEvents of a #$Refinishing event.")
(comment Terrier-WhiteBull "A collection of medium-sized, white dogs.")
(disjointWith StorageOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment JobRecruitmentServiceEvent "The collection of service events in which the #$providerOfService           finds new people to work in a company, join an organization, do a job etc.")
(comment DeepTibialMuscleSet "The #$Collection of all #$DeepTibialMuscleSets.  The #$DeepTibialMuscleSet invert the foot and flex the #$Toes.  The muscles lie deep in the #$Calf-AnimalBodyPart and attach to tendons whichloop around the inside of the #$Ankle and attach to bones on the plantar (under) side of the Foot.  The #$DeepTibialMuscleSet include the TibialisPosterior, FlexorDigitorumLongus, and FlexorHallucisLongus.")
(comment Escalator "A moving stairway which people stand on to go between floors of buildings.")
(comment HepaticVein "The collection of all hepatic veins.  The left and right hepatic veins exit the liver and connect proximally to the InferiorVenaCava.  Distally they connect to the hepatic portal system.  The hepatic veins carry all the blood returning from the digestive organs.")
(comment CheeseFondue "#$CheeseFondues are usually made of melted #$Cheese mixed with a little #$Wine which is then eaten by dipping cube-shaped pieces of #$Bread in the #$Mixture.")
(comment Shareware "An instance of #$ProductType. Instances of #$Shareware are #$ComputerProgram-CWs provided free of charge, but for which the author requests some voluntary payment (usually in the accompanying documentation files or in an announcement made by the software itself). Such payment may or may not buy additional support or functionality.")
(comment Fan-Handheld "The collection of hand-held fans, a typical example being oriental hand-fans.")
(comment MicroorganismMob "The collection of mobs (see #$Mob) of #$Microorganisms.  Often, elements of this collection will be mobs of microorganisms of the same type, in which case one should also assert #$groupMemberType regarding the type of microorganisms that make up the mob.")
(comment RapMusic "This is the collection of contemporary popular music known as 'rap', in which the lyrics are chanted more than sung.")
(comment Crocus "Low-growing bulblike species of the Iris order.  Saffron is the dried orange tip of the pistil of certain crocuses.  Some crocuses are reknowned for blooming in early spring when there is still snow on the ground (e.g. in the Alps).")
(comment NorthKoreanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$NorthKorea, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AnimalSound "A specialization of #$InformationBearingWavePropagation.  Each instance of #$AnimalSound is a sound of a type which originally was, and typically is, made by an animal using just its body parts (though such a sound may subsequently have been reproduced by imitation or recording).  Examples of #$AnimalSounds include instances of #$Birdsong, #$NeighingSound, #$PurringSound, #$BarkingSound, and #$BrayingSound.  Note that the restriction to sounds produced by body parts alone excludes noises produced by moving external objects; consequently, #$AnimalSound does _not_ include rustling the leaves underfoot, splashing water, or playing a musical instrument. Note that this collection is not a specialization of #$Action, or #$BodyMovementEvent, since it refers to animal sounds themselves, not to the activity of making animal sounds (though events of both types usually accompany one another. See #$EmittingSound for the latter.)")
(comment PicnicTable "A table designed for picnicing.")
(comment ClientProgram "A specialization of #$LocalProgram and an instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction.  Copies of #$ClientProgram are run by computers on a network with connections to computers running copies of #$ServerProgram.  Copies of #$ClientProgram request information or processing services from the copies of #$ServerProgram, which the server then provides to the client. See, for instance, #$DatabaseClientProgram. For relating client to their server programs, see the predicate #$client-Software.")
(comment AdmitToMembership "The collection of all events in which one or more people or organizations are granted permission [#$GrantingPermission] to become members of some #$Organization.  A person may be admitted to membership in some organization but not join (e.g. a #$HighSchoolStudent may be admitted to several colleges but will generally become a student of at most one of them).")
(comment MercurySpacecraft "The collection of all Mercury manned #$Spacecraft.  Each #$MercurySpacecraft could transport one #$Astronauts out of Earth's atmosphere.  The first two flights were suborbital, the last five were orbital.")
(comment FemoralNerve "The collection of all femoral #$Nerves.  A #$FemoralNerve is formed by #$VentralRamusL2, #$VentralRamusL3 and #$VentralRamusL4.  The #$FemoralNerve has an anterior and a posterior branch, each of which branches again.")
(comment SesameOil "Oil pressed from dried sesame seeds.")
(comment NailPolishRemover "Substances used for removing nail polish from fingernails or toenails; usually acetone-based.")
(comment Word-UnitOfComputerMemory "A function and an instance of #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity. (#$Word-UnitOfComputerMemory 1) represents a unit of memory equivalent to two #$Bytes or 16 #$Bits.")
(comment PharmacyFormalProductType "These are pharmaceutical products specified at #$NationalDrugCode (NDC) level. Instances are drug packages identified by the labeler/vendor, product, and trade package size. ")
(comment FinancialDocument "The collection of documents that describe or are directly concerned with the finances of a person or organization")
(comment Flipper "Broad, flat limb adapted for swimming")
(disjointWith Motorcycle RecreationalVehicle)
(comment DutchPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of the #$Netherlands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith AnimalOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment ToiletTrainingProduct "The collection of products used to aid in toilet training a #$HumanToddler.")
(comment Dystonia "A collection of #$AilmentConditions in which sustained muscle contractions cause twisting and repetitive movements or abnormal postures.  There are different types of dystonia -- a single muscle may be affected or groups of muscles may be affected.")
(comment MaterialMovementHandTool "A hand-held thing that can be used to move material in a small area.")
(disjointWith AccessingAnIBT IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment HerbPlant "This is the collection of herb plants (not types). Note

that #$Herb-HumanUse is not an #$OrganismClassificationType, though it contains

some whole herb plants, since it mostly contains those plant parts which are

in fact used by humans.")
(comment NumericalQuant-NLAttrFn "(#$NumericalQuant-NLAttrFn NUM) is that #$NLQuantAttribute that represents the numeric quantifier 'NUM.' 

#$NumericalQuant-NLAttrFn NAUTs are used with #$NLQuantFn to say that some term TERM occurred with the quantifier 'NUM.'  For example, (#$NLQuantFn (#$NumericalQuant-NLAttrFn 10) #$Dog) means that some word meaning #$Dog occurred with the quantifier '10.'")
(comment HTTPCookie-AIS "The collection of information structures

  that are instantiated in #$HTTPCookies.")
(comment Banjo "stringed instrument of the guitar family")
(comment RepairableProduct "Some products are repairable, like cars and vcrs.  Some are not, like distilled water.  Distilled water might be contaminated and could be purified, but that's not a repair script. It would be weird to call it repairing the water. But this collection also is intended to exclude products which are not intended to be serviced - for example, a pocket calculator would not be an instance of #$RepairableProduct, even though one can, in principle, repair them.")
(comment Mixer-AudioComponent "A collection of audio equipment. Each instance of   Mixer-AudioComponent accepts two or more inputs from audio devices,   microphones, etc. and has one or more output signal combining multiple   inputs.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterX "The capital letter 'X'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$X-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterX.")
(comment NailPolish "A usually colored liquid used in painting nails.")
(disjointWith HittingAnObject PhysiologicalProcess)
(disjointWith Plastic Concrete)
(comment rAMSize "This predicate relates electronic devices to computer memory capacities.  (#$rAMSize DEV MEM-CAP) means that DEV has MEM-CAP amount of random-access memory (see #$RAM).")
(comment PrivateSectorOrganization "#$PrivateSectorOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$PrivateSectorOrganization is an organization that operates in the private sector and has no governmental component.  Instances of #$PrivateSectorOrganizations may be either #$CommercialOrganizations or #$NonProfitOrganizations.  Examples of #$PrivateSectorOrganizations include #$IBMInc, #$Cycorp, #$FloridaNationalBank, and #$SierraClub.")
(comment AdobeBrick "The collection of #$Bricks made from #$AdobeClay. Buildings made with #$AdobeBricks are popular in the Southwestern United States. ")
(comment Bowl-Eating "A bowl that holds about the right amount of food for one person.")
(comment DorsalRamusC4 "The collection of all C4 dorsal rami.  #$VentralRamusC4 and #$DorsalRamusC4 branch from SpinalRootC4.  #$DorsalRamusC4 supplies the #$Skin on the back (#$Back-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment TypicalBehaviorOfFn "#$TypicalBehaviorOfFn takes any instance of #$Agent-Generic and returns the collection of action-types that are 'typical' for that agent.  This function is an instance of #$PresuppositionFunction, as the 'typical' behavior for an agent is dependent on certain kinds of situations.")
(comment TelecommunicationsProgram "Software which allows a user to connect to the Internet, send faxes, record phone messages, or do similar tasks, usually via a modem.")
(comment FishingNet "a net whose primary function is to catch fish")
(comment orgTypesSimilarWithRespectToPhenotype "(#$orgTypesSimilarWithRespectToPhenotype ORGTYPE1 ORGTYPE2)
means that instances of ORGTYPE1 share similar phenotypes with
instances of ORGTYPE2. It may or may not be the case that
(#$orgTypesSimilarWithRespectToGenotype ORGTYPE1 ORGTYPE2);
alternatively, it could be the case that both ORGTYPE1 and ORGTYPE2
have been subject to similar selection pressures, resulting in
superficially similar phenotypic forms.")
(comment Acrostic-IBO "The collection of acrostic puzzles of the kind found in newspapers.")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece ConsumableProduct)
(comment MauritanianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Mauritania, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment MacMainBox "The main box of a mac, which contains the processor, and possibly other stuff")
(comment Fifteen-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '15.'")
(comment KomanLanguageFamily "Languages spoken in the Sudan and Ethiopia")
(comment Spout "The part of a kettle or teapot from which the water is poured.")
(comment BalancingSomething "Physically balancing two things (or two halves of the same thing), by adjusting their mass and distance in relation to a pivot point so that gravity doesn't affect one side more than the other; that is, keeping the two sides in equilibrium.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam SmallBusiness)
(comment Head-AnimalBodyPart "A specialization of #$ExternalAnatomicalPart, and #$AnimalBodyPart, and an instance of #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType: the collection of all heads of #$Animals. See also the more specialized #$Head-Vertebrate.")
(comment CostalCartilage "#$CostalCartilage connects a #$Rib-AnimalBodyPart to the #$Sternum.")
(comment VoluntaryBodyMovement "A specialization of both #$PurposefulPhysicalAction and #$BodyMovementEvent.  Each instance of #$VoluntaryBodyMovement is an event in which an animal intentionally moves one part of its body relative to another part of its body.  Specializations of #$VoluntaryBodyMovement include #$Biting, #$PunchingSomeone, and #$MakingAGesture.")
(comment CarAlarm "Automobile alarm.")
(comment WebDirectoryPage "A collection of WWW pages. Each #$WebDirectoryPage consists primarily of an ordered list of links into other web pages. The links will typically belong to a common subject area or set of subject areas.  Some instances of #$WebDirectoryPage are pages within a portal site such as yahoo.com.  Others belong to (and are maintained by) other organizations or individuals.")
(comment RadiatorTreatment "Stuff added to radiators that enhances the performance of your car.")
(comment CrushedFragmentedFn "`(#$CrushedFragmentedFn TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances (groups of pieces) that are the result of taking 1 or more instances of TYPE and crushing them (in a #$PulverizationEvent) so that they are broken into pieces. For example, (#$CrushedFragmentedFn #$ChilePepper-DriedIngredient) is the collection of crushed dried chile pepper. Note that, when what is crushed are instances of an #$ExistingObjectType, instances of (CrushedFragmentedFn TYPE) are no longer instances of TYPE, they are merely composed of the same stuff as are instances of TYPE.")
(comment Graffiti "An inscription or drawing made on some public surface (e.g., a wall).")
(comment Artery "Tubular, branching vessel which carries blood from the heart to the body")
(comment VulnerableToFileDeletion "#$VulnerableToFileDeletion is a specialization of
#$VulnerableToFileOverwrite.  A computer has this vulnerability if
it allows unauthorized users to delete certain files.")
(comment LandTransportationWheel "the collection of #$Wheels that are #$physicalParts of #$WheeledTransportationDevices, in many cases fitted inside the #$Tires of vehicles, so that the vehicles can move.")
(comment Bloodhound "A collection of large dogs; considered among the most gentle and easy-going of dogs.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat LanguageGroupingType)
(disjointWith InsuranceOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment MusicTrack "The collection of all subdivisions of audio recordings. On musical recordings these generally correspond to songs. Example: the recording of #$Roxanne-TheSong on a specific instantiation of #$EveryBreathYouTakeTheSingles-TheAlbum.  Each instance of #$MusicTrack is an instantiation of an instance of #$AudioConceptualWork.")
(comment SpleniusCapitis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$SpleniusCapitis #$Muscle.  The #$SpleniusCapitis #$Muscle extends the neck if acting bilaterally, or flexes the neck and rotates it in the direction of the muscle if acting unilaterally.")
(comment ChinaCabinet-PieceOfFurniture "A type of furniture used for storing and/or displaying chinaware and crystalware")
(disjointWith ProductDistributionEvent MedicalTesting)
(comment LemonLimeFlavoring "instances are pieces of a compound with a flavor like some combination of lemons and limes (really a sort of `generic' citrus fruit, used mostly in soft drinks.")
(comment DepartmentStore "The collection of establishments that sell a variety of household and other items.  This can include clothing.  Think of JCPenney or Target or Foleys or Sacks.")
(comment ScreenShotFn "#$ScreenShotFn takes as an argument an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW and returns a collection of all 'stills,' or #$ScreenShots from that ComputerProgram.  For example, (#$ScreenShotFn #$Doom-TheGame) is the collection of all still, complete frames one would/could get on one's screen while running a copy of the Doom program.  The word 'complete' here is used to distinguish a screen shot from any sub-image in the screen shot.  So, for example, one pixel from a screen shot is not a screen shot.  An image of a person, considered by itself outside of the screen shot in which it appears, is not a screen shot.  For more info on this function, see the comment under its close relative, #$PicturesFromFn.")
(comment SheetSet "A group of linens for a bed, consisting of a flat sheet and a fitted sheet of the same size and the appropriate number of pillowcases.")
(comment Eye "A specialization of both #$ExternalOrgan and #$ElectroMagneticRadiationSensor.  Each instance of #$Eye is an organ of sight.")
(comment Device-OneTimeUse "The collection #$Device-OneTimeUse is a subset of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each element of #$Device-OneTimeUse is a device which is intended to be used only once in its primary or intended function.  In many cases, it will be impossible to use the device again because of some effect of its use which destroys its ability to perform its function.  In some cases, it may be physically possible to use the device again, but normally it wouldn't be re-used. Examples include instances of #$HandGrenade and #$Condom. For stuff-like products that are 'used up', see #$ConsumableProduct.")
(comment MultiReedWoodwindInstrument "The collection of all multi-reed #$WoodwindInstruments")
(comment CanineAnimal "A specialization of #$CarnivoreOrder.  Each instance of #$CanineAnimal is a member of a dog-like species belonging to the #$CarnivoreOrder.  The collection #$CanineAnimal includes the specializations #$Dog, #$Wolf, and #$Fox (qq.v.).  Canine animals constitute an instance of #$BiologicalFamily, the Canidae.")
(disjointWith WearingSomething Gesture)
(comment LitterFn "A collection denoting function which results in a group which is a litter (bunch of offspring from the same birth event) of animals.")
(comment VentralRamusC1 "The collection of all C1 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC1 and #$DorsalRamusC1 branch from SpinalRootC1.  #$VentralRamusC1 supplies the #$CervicalPlexus.")
(comment PinaColada "The collection of #$PinaColada drinks, a mixture of #$CoconutMeat cream, pineapple juice and #$Rum

served over ice and usually garnished with a pineapple chunk.")
(disjointWith RoomInAConstruction FurniturePiece)
(comment GinkgopsidaClass "A biological class within the gymnosperm group in the plant kingdom which contains Ginkgo biloba as its only living species.")
(comment ComputerNetwork "A specialization of #$ConnectedPathSystem and #$ComputationalSystem. Each instance of this collection is a network used to link computational systems together to allow them to transfer information between each other. This is typically done using \"packets\" of information (see #$Packet-Network) exchanged according to certain well-defined protocols (see #$NetworkProtocol). A particularly large and notable instance of this collection is #$Internet. Networks may be structured according to certain specific topologies, the most notable of which are #$BusNetwork, #$StarNetwork and #$RingNetwork.")
(comment MedicalScale "Devices used to measure a person's weight - typically while as a patient of a medical care provider.")
(comment IncisorTooth "The teeth in the front of an animal's mouth, which are sharp and are used for cutting.")
(disjointWith GraspingImplement Paddle-Water)
(comment LimeTree "A tree that grows limes")
(comment YemenPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Yemen, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment CorrectionTape "The collection correction tape.

This is tape which is intended to be used to cover over misprints

so that they can be retyped or rewritten. It comes in plastic

dispensers which allow one to simply rub it across the mistake

and tape will be dispensed to cover that mistake.")
(comment PillowStuffing "NOTE!! The notion of a pillow or cushion being filled with something needs to be reworked.  We probably want to kill this unit.")
(comment Biting "Biting is the coming-together of upper and lower teeth into the thing bitten: usually the thing bitten is some kind of food, but it can also be the mailman's ankle, bitten by the dog.")
(disjointWith GrillingFood Microwaving)
(comment performedByPart "(#$performedByPart ACT ORG) means that the #$Organization ORG is considered to be the performer of the #$Action ACT, though in fact only some subordinate part of ORG (i.e., a member or a sub-organization), rather than all of the organization, is directly involved in ACT.  For example, (#$performedByPart OperationDesertStorm USArmy) since only certain divisions of the US Army participated in Operation Desert Storm.")
(disjointWith SomethingToWear GardenHose)
(disjointWith InsuranceProvider MailDepartment)
(comment SoapDish "The collection of bowl-shaped containers intended to hold soap.")
(comment Pachyderm "Large mammals having a thick hide, specifically elephants, rhinos, and hippos")
(disjointWith EnteringInfoIntoDevice FluidFlowEvent)
(comment MedialRegionFn "The function (MedialRegionFn REGOROBJ), applied to a region or object REGOROBJ, means the sub-region consisting of the center parts or middle section (near the mid-line) of REGOROBJ, or the medial main portion of REGOROBJ as opposed to the right and left portions.  It applies when REGOROBJ itself has an intrinsic right/left orientation (unlike, say, a sphere), but if REGOROBJ is a part within a larger region or object that has its own right/left orientation, the function returns REGOROBJ's portion nearest the mid-line (with respect to left and right) of the larger region or object.")
(comment OralSex "The collection of events involving oral stimulation of the genitals.")
(comment TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure "A specialization of #$Translation-Complete.  Each instance of #$TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure is a movement event in which the trajectory of the object moving (see #$trajectory-Complete and #$primaryObjectMoving) follows a living structure (an instance of #$BiologicalLivingObject) internal to some organism (see #$Organism-Whole) for a significant portion of the movement (so that the living structure is a #$motionPathway-Partial (q.v.) for the movement).  Notable specializations of #$TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure include #$EatingEvent, #$DigestionEvent, and #$Inhaling.")
(comment UploadingAFile "A collection of actions done by computers on files. In each instance of #$UploadingAFile, a computer copies a file from a local #$ComputerDisk or other long-term storage device, i.e. one that it #$physicallyContains or that is located within a few yards of it, to a file system that it is #$remotelyConnectedTo over a #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment TennisShoe "The collection of shoes designed to be used for playing Tennis")
(comment PanicAttack "A psychological ailment during which the patient feels an intense or incapacitating fear or nervousness.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment Wrist "Flexible joint between the hand and the forearm")
(comment WorkStation " A permanent or semi-permanent arrangement with a device and  facilities for working on that device. Includes cash register stations, check out counters, milling machine stations, kitchen top region (with all the gadgets), ")
(comment Terrier-StaffordshireBull "A collection of medium-sized, smooth-coated dogs.  Sometimes called the            Staffie.")
(comment Texan "People living in the state of Texas")
(disjointWith WorkersOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment FlexorDigitorumSuperficialis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$FlexorDigitorumSuperficialis #$Muscle.  The #$FlexorDigitorumSuperficialis connects to the side of each #$MedialPhalanx by digitorum tendons. Each tendon divides to allow the #$FlexorDigitorumProfundus to pass medially to a #$DistalPhalanx.")
(comment LemonOil "Oil pressed from the peels of lemons.")
(comment AxillaryVein "The collection of all axillary veins.  The axillary vein is a major vein passing through the shoulder.  Its proximal end connects to the subclavian vein and the distal end connects to the cephalic and basilic veins.")
(comment Pecorino-Cheese "The collection of all Pecorino, a kind 

  of #$Cheese made from sheep milk.")
(comment GreekOrthodoxChurchBuilding "The collection of all Greek Orthodox church buildings")
(comment ProducingHardcopy "The collection of events in which hardcopy of any form is produced: specs include things such as PrintingABook, #$PhotocopyingAPage, #$PhotocopyingADocument, #$ComputerPrintingHardcopy, #$FaxingADocument, etc.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice Wire)
(comment Peyote "Cactus well-known for its hallucinogenic effects. #$Mescaline is a derivative of Peyote.")
(comment BritishVirginIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$BritishVirginIslands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Batrachotoxin "Batrachotoxin is a toxin produced by certain   species of #$Frogs.")
(disjointWith DeadAnimal Water)
(comment InuitLanguageFamily "A sub-family of the #$EskimoLanguageFamily, consisting of languages primarily spoken in Alaska, Canada, and Greenland.")
(comment SideTable "A table designed to be placed at the end of a couch.")
(comment containsModules "(#$containsModules PROG MODULE) means that 
 MODULE is a subprogram of PROG, is routinely shipped with PROG and not 
 executable on its own (for subprograms which are separately executable, see
 #$containsPrograms).")
(comment BroomHandle "The collection of all handles like broom handles.  This would also include mop handles, etc.")
(comment Spam-MeatProduct "The collection for Spam, a type of inexpensive canned meat made mainly of #$Pork shoulder and ham.")
(comment UlnarNerve "The collection of all ulnar #$Nerves.  An #$UlnarNerve is formed by the #$MedialCord-BrachialPlexus.  The #$UlnarNerve runs from the #$BrachialPlexus in the #$Shoulder (of its side of the body) down through the #$Arm to the #$Wrist.  It does not directly innervate any part of the #$Arm.  It has many branches that innervate various regions of the #$Arm and #$Hand.")
(comment BoilingFood "Cooking food by immersing it in boiling water.")
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure GroupActivity)
(comment ModelFn "The Cyc function #$ModelFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction which is used to represent models of a certain type of thing.  (#$ModelFn OBJ-TYPE) denotes the collection of all models of objects that belong to the type OBJ-TYPE.  For example, all sculptures of horses are elements of the collection (#$ModelFn #$Horse-Domesticated).")
(disjointWith KnowledgeEditingActivity MaterialHandling)
(comment ProgressReport "The Collection of all documents which report of the activities of some agent regarding the achievement of some goal set")
(comment Fin "Appendage that fish and sea mammals use to locomote")
(comment predicateIntersection "(#$predicateIntersection PRED GENLPRED1 GENLPRED2) means that (PRED ARG1 ...) holds iff (#$and (GENLPRED1 ARG1 ...) (GENLPRED2 ARG1 ...)).  That is, if both GENLPRED1 and GENLPRED2 hold for a given sequence of arguments, then PRED holds for those arguments; and vice versa.  If either GENLPRED1 or GENLPRED2 has fixed arity, then PRED has (the same) fixed arity; but if both have variable arity, so does PRED.")
(disjointWith Train-TransportationDevice All-TerrainVehicle)
(comment SicilianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Sicily, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization AnimalOrganization)
(comment PottyChair "The collection of all potty chairs.  A #$PottyChair is a device which looks like a very small #$Toilet.  The most significant way in which a #$PottyChair differs from a #$Toilet is that a #$PottyChair is not connected to any #$PlumbingSystem-Building.  Rather, it is just a seat and a chamber into which the #$HumanToddler (hopefully) goes to the bathroom.")
(comment Alkaptonuria "A collection of rare inherited #$GeneticDisorders. Each instance is a disorder of protein metabolism characterized by an inability of the body to metabolize certain amino acids.")
(comment AdjustableWrench "Hand tool used for grasping objects. A threaded joint between two sides of the grasping apparatus allows the wrench to be fit snugly around objects of various sizes.")
(disjointWith AccessingAnIBT MedicalCareEvent)
(comment CoccygealPlexus "The collection of all coccygeal plexi. A #$CoccygealPlexus is usually supplied by #$VentralRamusS4 and #$VentralRamusS5 via the fifth #$SacralNerve, and #$VentralRamusC0 via the #$CoccygealNerve. The anococcygeal #$Nerves arise from the #$CoccygealPlexus.")
(comment hasDepartmentTypes "The predicate #$hasDepartmentTypes indicates what kinds of departments a particular organization has among its sub-organizations.  (#$hasDepartmentTypes ORG DEPTYP) means that a particular instance of #$Organization, ORG, has some #$Department(s) of the type DEPTYP among its sub-organizations.  Note that DEPTYP in (#$hasDepartmentTypes ORG DEPTYP) does not represent a particular #$Department within ORG, but instead refers to a type of #$Department that ORG has.  For example, universities have many #$AcademicDepartments, and (#$hasDepartmentTypes #$UniversityOfPittsburgh #$AcademicDepartment) is true.  So is the more specialized assertion (#$hasDepartmentTypes #$UniversityOfPittsburgh #$PhilosophyDepartment).  But neither assertion names a particular department.")
(comment StringInAStringedInstrument "A string made of nylon, metal or gut which is used to produce particular sounds on a stringed instrument - depending on its length and width and material.")
(comment Oomycota "This class contains water molds. The term \"mold\" is

a misnomer, however, as these organisms are not considered not to be in the

fungus kingdom.")
(comment SpokenCommunicating "A specialization of #$AudioCommunicating.  Each instance of #$SpokenCommunicating is a transmission of sound-borne verbal information by spoken words between two or more agents (in this way #$SpokenCommunicating differs from #$Speaking, which is a #$SingleDoerAction).  The communication may be one-way or two-way (or multi-way).  Examples of #$SpokenCommunicating include a telephone conversation, a classroom discussion, and the #$GettysburgAddress-Speech.")
(comment WindupDevice "A collection of physical devices;  a subset of #$MechanicalDevice.  An instance of #$WindupDevice  is powered by coiled springs through a #$WindingProcess.  The coiled  springs are tightened manually by winding a wheel or a tab,  #$CoilTightening; the coiled spring slowly releases itself while it  is powering the #$WindupDevice, otherwise known as #$CoilLoosening.   Examples of windup devices are watches, clocks, music boxes, and  toys.")
(comment AutomobileEqualizer "Automobile equalizer")
(comment IvoryBilledWoodpecker "The largest North American woodpecker,  similar to the pileated woodpecker but with a white bill, it is now probably extinct.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterX "The lowercase letter 'x'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$X-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterX.")
(comment Rouge "A cosmetic for coloring the cheeks red.")
(disjointWith Research AthleticActivity)
(disjointWith Ceramic Concrete)
(comment rOMSize "This predicate relates electronic devices to memory capacities.  (#$rOMSize DEV MEM-CAP) means that DEV has MEM-CAP amount of read-only memory (see #$ROM).")
(comment AirBrush "The collection of all reusable #$Atomizers for spraying #$Paint.

    Does not include cans containing #$SprayPaint.")
(comment Bowl-Generic "Containers usually used to contain food, although could contain anything.  ")
(comment VentralRamusC4 "The collection of all C4 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC4 and #$DorsalRamusC4 branch from SpinalRootC4.  #$VentralRamusC4 supplies the #$CervicalPlexus and sometimes contributes to the #$BrachialPlexus.")
(comment FileTranslationProgram "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs whose instantiations alter the #$ComputerFileTypeByFormat of instances of #$ComputerFileCopy in some way. Typically instances of this collection will be programs which translate a file from one file format to another (#$JPEGFile to #$GIFFile for example).  The basic data is preserved in the translation, only the format in which the data is saved is changed.")
(comment LifePreserver "This collection is equivalent personal floatation devices. Includes life jackets (aka life vests) as well as life rings.")
(comment Crossword-IBO "The collection of crossword puzzles of the kind found in
Sunday newspapers.")
(comment Pubis "The collection of #$AnimalBodyParts consisting of all pubic areas of mammalian bodies. This is a unique part of a mammal which in #$Persons is covered-Hairlike by #$PubicHair.")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact ConsumableProduct)
(comment (FruitFn DatePalm) "The collection of individual dates.")
(comment TristanDaCunhaTerritoryPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$TristanDaCunha-Territory, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment ApplePowerCD "A #$CD-ROM drive made by Apple.")
(comment Five-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '5.'")
(comment SouthAfricanKhoisanLanguageFamily "Languages spoken in south Africa")
(comment FrameForPictureOrMirror "An open border or case for enclosing  a picture, mirror, etc..")
(disjointWith SportsTeam HonorSociety)
(comment HarvesterAgriculturalImplement "The collection of large wheeled agricultural vehicles whose primary function is to harvest a field")
(comment Anchovy "Any of several species of small, silvery fish eaten by
people or used as bait to catch larger fish.")
(comment Foot-AnimalBodyPart "A specialization of #$Appendage-AnimalBodyPart, and an instance of #$SymmetricAnatomicalPartType: the collection of all feet (a foot is a terminal part of a #$Vertebrate's #$Leg, used in locomotion, support, balance, #$Kicking, etc.). Notable specializations of this collection include #$WebbedFoot and #$Paw.")
(comment PhosphoesterGroup "The collection of all #$PhosphateRadicals of which at least one of the oxygen atoms is connected to a carbon atom of another #$MolecularRadical.")
(comment ArthrodialJoint "An #$ArthrodialJoint is a #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart in which the bones can glide slightly over each other.")
(comment AnimalWalkingProcess "A specialization of #$SimpleWholeBodyMovement, #$Walking-Generic, and #$LocomotionProcess-Animal. Each instance of this collection is a walking event in which the locomotor is an #$Animal. A notable specialization of this collection is #$HumanWalkingProcess.")
(disjointWith DeviceRunning BiologicalEvent)
(comment HomepageFn-Individual "#$HomepageFn-Individual takes as argument any instance of #$Individual and returns the subcollection of #$WorldWideWebHomePage-CW whose instances are created or authorized by that #$Individual or its owners or representatives. For example (#$HomepageFn-Individual DennisRodman) would return the collection of all homepages created or authorized by #$ChicagoBulls forward DennisRodman, and (#$HomepageFn-Individual #$CityOfAustinTX) returns the collection of all homepages created or authorized by representatives of the City of Austin. (#$Vizedom 1/14/99)")
(comment HouseFuse "See Fuse, but one that is in your house's electrical system, not in your stereo.")
(comment AudioClip "The collection of all #$AudioRecordedObjects the playings of which have a short duration, and which are typically recordings (or encodings) of portions of a longer sequence of sounds recorded or encoded in some other #$AudioRecordedObject. Examples include an #$MP3File in which a portion of a song has been encoded, and a cassette tape on which segment of a speech has been recorded. Note that no #$VideoRecordedObject (such as a #$VideoClip) is an #$AudioClip. A #$VideoRecordedObject with an audio portion is instead an instance of #$AudioRecordedObject.")
(comment Aorta "The collection of all aortas.  An #$Aorta is the main #$Artery in a body, containing oxygenated #$Blood, leaving the #$Heart and relaying #$Blood to the arterial network.")
(comment canopyClosureOfRegion "(#$canopyClosureOfRegion ?REGION ?PERCENT) means that #$GeographicalRegion ?REG has a canopy closure of ?PERCENT.")
(disjointWith SnowSki WheeledTransportationDevice)
(comment Maltese-TheDog "A collection of very small dogs, ancient in origin.  Their coats consist of long, silky, white hair.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup InsuranceOrganization)
(comment CreatineProduct "This is the collection of all #$DietarySupplements for which the chemical compound #$Creatine is the major ingredient.  #$CreatineProduct is a type of product used by athletes (notably #$TroyAikman) to build muscle mass.  At the time of creation for this constant, #$Creatine supplements are mildly controversial, though generally legal to use in most professional sports.")
(comment ErectorSpinae "The #$Collection of all sets of #$ErectorSpinae #$Muscles.  The #$ErectorSpinae is the set of muscles (on each side of the body) which extend or laterally flex the spine (depending on whether acting bilaterally or laterally).  The lateral layer is the Iliocostalis (I. Thoracis & I. Cervicis); the middle layer is the Longissimus (L. Cervicis, L. Throacis, & L. Spinali); and the medial layer is the Spinalis (S. Cervicis & S. Spinalis).")
(comment LawnChair-PieceOfFurniture "A type of chair thet normally can be found in the garden or in the poolside")
(comment CysticDuct "The collection of all cystic ducts. Each instance of this collection is an #$AnatomicalVessel allowing #$BileTheSecretion to flow between the #$GallBladder and the #$CommonBileDuct.")
(comment CherryFlavoring "instances are pieces of a compound with a flavor like cherries, used in foods and drinks.")
(comment FurnitureStore "The collection of establishments that sell furniture as their main product.")
(comment TimerTriggeringMechanism "A timer as a triggering mechanism.  This mechanism can be set for some amount of time, after which the mechanism will automatically activate.")
(comment twins-Identical "(#$twins-Identical DUM DEE) means that DUM and DEE are identical

twins, meaning the are twins that arose from the same zygote.")
(disjointWith Database-Physical HumanAccessibleIBO)
(comment ImmuneResponse "A collection of events. An instance of #$ImmuneResponse is the response of organism's #$ImmuneSystem to an encounter with microbial or viral agents. See #$HumoralImmuneResponse, #$CellularImmuneResponse, and #$ImmuneSystem.")
(comment PaperTowel "The subcollection of #$Towels made out of #$Paper.")
(comment hasAccessToAccount "A predicate relating instances of #$ComputerUser with instances of #$ComputerAccount.  (#$hasAccessToAccount AGENT ACCOUNT) means that AGENT has access to ACCOUNT.")
(comment ReedWoodwindInstrumentTypeByNumberOfReeds "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$ReedWoodwindInstrument whose instances are all of the same number of reeds.")
(comment OviparousAnimal "#$OviparousAnimal is a specialization of #$NonPersonAnimal.  Each instance of #$OviparousAnimal is an animal that hatches from eggs expelled from its mother's body.  Cf. #$ViviparousAnimal.")
(comment Piano-Acoustic "Instances of this collection are instances of #$MusicalInstrument-Acoustic and #$Keyboard-MusicalInstrument.  All have the feature that depressing one of the keys entrains a mechanical process whereby a string of taut piano wire is hammered, producing a vibration that is audible as a musical tone.  For this reason instances are also properly considered instances of #$PercussionInstrument.  A similar process occurs in instances of #$Harpsichord, with the signal difference being that in a #$Harpsichord, the strings are plucked, not hit.")
(disjointWith WearingSomething MentalSituation)
(comment BootSectorFn "#$BootSectorFn takes as its argument any element of #$ComputerDisk and returns
    an instance of #$DiskSector which is the boot sector for that disk.")
(comment SmokeAlarm "A collection of objects; a subset of #$AlarmDevice.  Every instance of #$SmokeAlarm automatically emits an #$AlarmSignal when it detects instances of #$Smoke.")
(comment WaterwayLock "artificial structure for restraining flow of a stream; can be opened to release water")
(comment SuperiorGlutealNerve "The collection of all superior gluteal nerves.  The superior gluteal nerve is formed by the #$VentralRamusL4, #$VentralRamusL5 and #$VentralRamusS1 and supplies the gluteus medius and gluteus minimus.")
(comment MapleSyrup "#$MapleSyrup is a sweet sticky liquid, obtained from some kinds           of maple tree (see #$MapleTree).")
(comment FuelPoweredDevice "A collection of physical devices; a subcollection of 
#$PoweredDevice.  An instance of #$FuelPoweredDevice is directly
powered by combustible fuels such as gasoline, coal, and natural gas.  Common examples of #$FuelPoweredDevice include automobiles with gasoline-powered engines, kerosene heaters, propane torches, and jet airplanes.")
(comment CycadopsidaClass "A biological class within the gymnosperm group in the plant kingdom which contain nine extant genera of cycads and several that are now extinct.  Members of this class were most widespread in Mesozoic times.")
(comment MaintainingAWebsite "A specialization of #$MaintainingSomething and #$ComputerActivity. In each instance of this collection, some instance of #$WorldWideWebSite is maintained (maintenance is performed on a website).")
(comment UltrasoundScanner "Devices which are used to image internal body structures.  They emit ultrasound which is reflected from the object being scanned.  The scanner receives the reflected ultrasound and forms an image.")
(comment carriesOrganismType "(#$carriesOrganismType OBJ ORGTYPE) means 

that OBJ carries organisms of the type ORGTYPE within or upon itself.  OBJ can 

be an inanimate thing, such as a hypoderimic needle or a solution contaminated 

with bacteria, or it can be an infected organism.  This predicate is not used 

for a #$FemaleAnimal carrying a #$Fetus.")
(comment HaikuPoem "The collection of all haikus. A Haiku is a short poem, generally with three lines - five syllables in the first and third lines, and seven in the second line. The literary quality of haikus is typically judged by their ability to create a mood or image within the tight constraints of the form. They often describe #$Nature.")
(comment CanineTooth "The pointy teeth between the incisors and the bicuspids, which are used for puncturing and shredding.")
(disjointWith Needle GraspingImplement)
(comment OrangeTree "A tree that grows oranges")
(comment GreekPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Greece, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment BulletinBoard-Physical "The collection of bulletin boards.")
(comment Wood "A specialization of #$PlantProduct.  Each instance of #$Wood is a piece of solid, rigid, fibrous organic substance in or #$derivedFrom (q.v.) the inside of the trunks and limbs of trees.  Specializations of #$Wood include #$Firewood, (#$WoodFn #$OakTree) and (#$WoodFn #$CherryTree).")
(comment Cushion-PartOfFurniture "The pillow-like part of sofas and chairs. Can be attached or removable.")
(comment TakingAStep "The act of raising a foot, moving it forwards (backwards in ab cases) and placing it down again.")
(disjointWith SmokingFood SaltingFood)
(comment WorkersOrganization "A collection of organizations.  Each instance of #$WorkersOrganization is a group consisting of workers as members and having some aspect of the workers's welfare as a #$positiveVestedInterest, e.g., wages and benefits, professional development, impact of legislation on those workers, etc.  Important subsets of #$WorkersOrganization are #$TradeUnion and #$ProfessionalOrganization.")
(disjointWith Unicycle BabyWalker)
(comment CDRipper "The collection of computer programs that convert digital audio from a #$CompactDisc-Audio into computer files.")
(disjointWith SportsOrganization EntertainmentPerformer)
(comment SchoolBus "A large, lightweight, utilitarian bus used typically by schools for conveying children to and from school and school-related activities.  Capacity up to 60 people.")
(disjointWith EnteringInfoIntoDevice Conveying-Generic)
(comment LeftRegionFn "The function (LeftRegionFn REGOROBJ), applied to a region or object REGOROBJ, means the region consisting of the left half or flank or left main portion of REGOROBJ.  It applies only when REGOROBJ itself has an intrinsic left/right orientation, or is part of a larger region or object that has a left/right orientation.")
(comment fromGroup "A specialization of #$from-Generic, #$fromGroup can
be used to indicate, in a more specific way,
the instance of #$Group from which the #$transferredThing
is transferred in some instance of #$GroupTransfer.
(#$fromGroup TRANS GROUP) means that in the 
instance TRANS of #$GroupTransfer, the
#$transferredThing is transferred from the instance
GROUP of #$Group.  See also #$GroupTransferOut and
#$toGroup.")
(comment aggressor "The predicate #$aggressor relates a conflict event to the agent who initiates the conflict.  (#$aggressor CONFLICT AGENT) means that the agent AGENT deliberately initiates the conflict event CONFLICT.  For example, (#$aggressor #$WorldWarII #$Germany). If a conflict event has multiple agents initiating the conflict, each will be an aggressor in the conflict.")
(comment MotorcycleTypeByModel "A collection of collections, each element of MotorcycleTypeByModel is a collection of motorcycles categorized by model. For example, the collection of Harley Davidson Sportsters would be an element of this collection.")
(comment ComputerFileTypeByFormat "A collection of collections of computer files [#$ComputerFile-AIS]. Each instance of #$ComputerFileTypeByFormat (e.g. #$JPEGFile) is a collection of all #$ComputerFile-AISs that conform to a single preestablished layout for electronic data. Programs accept data as input in a certain format, process it, and provide it as output in the same or another format. This constant refers to the format of the data. For every instance of #$ComputerFileCopy, one can assert a #$fileFormat for it.")
(comment SnowGoggles "The set of #$Goggles used while #$SnowSkiing")
(comment Scoliosis "A relatively common disease of the #$SpinalColumn. It involves moderate to severe lateral curvature of the spine, and, if not treated, may lead to serious deformities later in life.")
(disjointWith ThrowingAnObject FloatingInASubstance)
(comment UpperArm "The collection of all upper arms.  A member of this collection is the segment of an #$Arm closest to the #$Torso, between the #$Shoulder and #$Elbow.")
(comment AirplaneControlWorkStation "The area in which a person who is flying an airplane sits - especially includes the control panel.")
(comment Terrier-FoxSmooth "A collection of small to medium-sized dogs with smooth but thick coats.            Their coats are mostly white.")
(comment ArchaicAgeGreekPerson "A person who lived in, Ionia, #$Attica, or one of the many other territories or city-states of `Greece' in the Archaic Age, c.750 to c.500 BCE")
(disjointWith CriminalOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment MagneticCompass "A #$Compass that uses a magnet to indicate the direction of magnetic north.")
(comment Gopher-Rodent "The collection of all pocket gophers, i.e., members of any of the 40 or so species in the biological family 'Geomyidae', stocky rodents native to North and Central America.")
(comment OpponensDigitiMinimi "The #$Collection of all instances of #$OpponensDigitiMinimi #$Muscle.  The #$OpponensDigitiMinimi brings the #$LittleFinger into opposition so that it can meet the #$Thumb.")
(comment InternalCombustionEngine "Device that, when it runs, turns a crankshaft by controlled combustion of a hydrocarbon fuel, often gasoline.")
(comment InternalJugularVein "The collection of all internal jugular veins.  The paired right and left internal jugular veins are large veins that pass through the neck.  The proximal end of the internal jugular vein connects to the brachiocephalic vein and the distal end connects to the dural sinuses.  The internal jugular veins drain blood from the brain.")
(comment EmulatorProgram "A collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs.  Every instance of #$EmulatorProgram is a program written to perform instances of #$Emulation.  See also #$EmulatorHardware, #$emulatesType.")
(comment RobotHand "The collection of mechanical devices that can manipulate objects and/or materials automatically.")
(comment Nameplate "a small sign bearing a person's name, near their office or workplace.")
(disjointWith StorageConstruct TransportationDevice)
(comment NorthernIrishPerson "A #$citizens of the country of #$NorthernIreland, or someone who participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment FlatRoof "The collection of flat, level roofs.  Instances
of #$FlatRoof are found atop some human shelter 
constructions.")
(comment systemOfWriting "The predicate #$systemOfWriting relates a particular writing system to the type of linguistic element typically represented in it, e.g., words, syllables, phonemes.  (#$systemOfWriting WRIT CHACTYPE) means that the #$WritingSystem WRIT is a script whose elements primarily (if not exclusively) represent linguistic units of the type CHACTYPE.  Some possible values of CHACTYPE include: #$LogographicWriting, #$IdeographicWriting, #$SyllabicWriting, #$Quasi-AlphabeticWriting.  To relate a particular language to the writing system(s) usually used to record it, see #$orthography.")
(comment Armoire "For hanging clothes in.  Sort of a portable closet.")
(comment ScratchingOneself "Animal scratching to relieve an itch.")
(comment arg5NotIsa "(#$arg5NotIsa REL COL) means that nothing given as the fifth argument to the #$Relation REL may be known to be an element of the #$Collection COL.")
(comment DeletePermission "An instance of #$FilePermission associated with
computational systems using the #$MSWindowsNT operating system.  If an
account has #$DeletePermission to a file or folder, then the user of the
account can delete that file or folder.")
(comment FTPServerProgram "#$FTPServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$FileTransferProtocol (FTP), which traditionally operates over TCP, port 21. A UNIX user can type 'ftp hostname 21' and connect with an instance of #$FTPServerProgram on hostname, if one is present.")
(comment PezCandy "The collection of fruit flavored candies produced by the
company #$Pez-TheCompany.")
(comment SciaticNerve "The collection of all sciatic nerves.  The sciatic nerve is actually two nerves, #$CommonPeronealNerve and #$TibialNerve, wrapped in a single sheath until just above the knee where they split.")
(comment Leavening "The rising of dough.  Can be accomplished with yeast, baking soda, or mechanical aeration.")
(comment PersonalHygieneProduct "Products used in cleaning the body or in promoting its cleanliness.")
(disjointWith ReproductiveFertilizationEvent DegenerationEvent)
(comment DataRecovery "The collection of actions performed with the intent of recovering electronic data presumed to be lost.")
(comment FishingNet-Sport "A net used by sportsmen to scoop up a fish after it has been caught with a fishing pole.")
(comment NewsArticle "The collection of all articles [#$Article-PCW] which present #$News.")
(comment TechnicalReport "The set of all documents that have as their main function the description of technical/scientific research (and/or the results of such research).")
(comment TailFin "Tail used by fish and sea mammals for propelling and steering")
(comment HardwareTool "#$HardwareTool is a specialization of #$Tool.  Each instance of #$HardwareTool is an object used to perform a task, usually by applying a particular kind of force to another object.  The tool is used to produce a physical effect in the position, structure, or arrangement of the other object.  Specializations of #$HardwareTool include #$Hammer, #$Screwdriver, and #$HandSaw.  Borderline nonexamples include eating utensils, robot servants, screws, nails, and levers.")
(comment EastGermanPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$EastGermany, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith Restaurant-Organization AnimalOrganization)
(comment BabyToiletrySubstance "The collection of toiletry products for #$HumanInfants and #$HumanToddlers.")
(comment CyclicVomitingSyndrome "A collection of #$AilmentConditions, a childhood disorder characterized by bouts of vomiting that last from a few hours to

 several days. The vomiting episodes occur regularly: Some children have them every few days, others every few months.")
(comment Tongs "Hand tool used for grasping objects. Two long sides are joined at one end or in the middle, and a squeezing motion of the hand at the grip ends brings the grasping ends together.")
(disjointWith TakingOffAClothingItem IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment MaxillarySinus "The collection of all maxillary sinuses, which are located inside maxillae. Cf. #$Maxilla.")
(comment holding "This constant relates an organization to the collection (not #$Collection) of its holdings.  Note that this may  differ from ownership.  For instance, an art gallery may have a painting that it controls or is allowed to display although it does not necessarily  own it.   Or, a university may have the correspondence of a famous author in its holdings although ownership is maintained by the author's estate.  Hence, it is not clear that we'd want to say that such organizations own their holdings.")
(disjointWith DepartmentStore AutoDealership)
(comment Tympani "large orchestral drum; also kettle drum")
(comment AudioCommunicating "A specialization of #$Communicating.  Each instance of #$AudioCommunicating is a transmission of sound-borne information between two (or more) agents.  Specializations of #$AudioCommunicating include #$SpokenCommunicating and #$MusicalCommunicating.")
(comment DriedFn "(#$DriedFn COL) returns the collection of instances of COL that have been subjected to a production process which includes significant drying or dessication.")
(comment AudioSystemComponent "The collection of audio components intended for use in an #$AudioSystem.  Each instance of #$AudioSystem has several instances of #$AudioSystemComponent as #$physicalParts.  No instance of #$AudioSystemComponent is itself an instance of #$AudioSystem.")
(comment MotherFn "This function maps animals to their biological mothers.
(#$MotherFn ANIMAL) is the biological mother of ANIMAL.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterY "The capital letter 'Y'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$Y-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterY.")
(comment EyeShadow "A colored cosmetic cream or powder applied to the eyelids to accent the eyes.")
(disjointWith Cleaning AthleticActivity)
(disjointWith Metal Concrete)
(comment MACAddress "A specialization of #$IDString.  Each instance of #$MACAddress identifies a network card within a particular #$LocalAreaNetwork. #$IPAddresses, in contrast, identify machines on the #$Internet. A #$MACAddress is contained in the source and destination fields of a #$Frame-Network's header.")
(comment RentalCar "The collection for rental cars.")
(comment presentParticiple "(#$presentParticiple WORD STRING) means that STRING is the present participle, or progressive form of WORD. The regular present participle is formed from the infinitive verb form with an `-ing' suffix. Verbs in the Cyc lexicon will have a #$presentParticiple entry only if they are irregular. Regular forms are generated by the morphology component.")
(comment DinnerPlate "Not just for dinner - A plate that holds about the right amount of food for one person.")
(comment VentralRamusC7 "The collection of all C7 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC7 and #$DorsalRamusC7 branch from SpinalRootC7.  #$VentralRamusC7 supplies the #$BrachialPlexus.")
(comment TypicalBehaviorOfInSitTypeFn "#$TypicalBehaviorOfInSitTypeFn takes an instance of #$Agent-Underspecified and a spec of #$Situation and returns the collection of action-types that are 'typical' for that agent when involved in that type of situation. For example, (#$TypicalBehaviorOfInSitTypeFn BobTheSoldier TrappedInFoxHoleEvent) is the collection of kinds of actions BobTheSoldier is apt to engage in when he finds himself in any TrappedInFoxHoleEvent.")
(comment GraphicDesignProgram "#$GraphicDesignProgram is a subset of #$ComputerProgram-CW and an instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction.  It includes all and only those instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW that have been designed to manipulate instances of #$ComputerImageFile.")
(comment Palette "A portable flat surface used to hold oil or acrylic paints while painting a picture.  Traditionally made of thin wood, having rounded edges and a thumb hole.  A convenient innovation is a pad of oil-resistant paper palettes with a stiff cardboard back.")
(comment PencilDrawing "Elements of #$PencilDrawing are elements of

#$Drawing-Depictions made using a pencil.")
(comment VestigialBiologicalPart "The collection of all vestigia.  An individual vestigium is the remnant of a structure which functioned in a previous stage of development, either in heredity or in individual development, including the remains of any structure which served a function solely in a Fetus.")
(disjointWith HouseholdAppliance ConsumableProduct)
(comment IraqiPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Iraq, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HPDeskWriter "A computer printer made by Hewlett-Packard Inc. Often used with Macintosh computers.")
(comment Four-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '4.'")
(comment MabanLanguageFamily "Languages spoken east of Lake Chad")
(comment WineBottle "Bottle in which wine is packaged and stored")
(comment GrabbingOntoWithHand "What one must do before one holds something with a hand. Since a holding implies a grabbing, it is not necessary to state for example, that both grabbing and holding are #$subEvents of a turning a door handle event.  One need only state that e.g. a holding is happening and this will imply that a grabbing preceeded the holding.")
(comment arg1NotGenl "(#$arg1NotGenl REL COL) means that nothing given as the first argument to the #$Relation REL may be a spec of the #$Collection COL.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam TelevisionCrew)
(comment FuelTank "Any tank used to contain a FuelSubstance.")
(comment Hoof "A specialization of #$Nail-AnimalBodyPart. Each instance of this collection is a hard covering over the foot of an #$EquineAnimal, #$Ruminant, etc.  Though the hoof is commonly thought of as the foot itself, this is not the case.")
(disjointWith LegMovement PhysiologicalProcess)
(disjointWith CuttingDevice Balloon)
(disjointWith BiologicalIntakeEvent Emission)
(comment GasTreatment "Stuff (like STP) added to gas that enhances the performance of your car.")
(comment Earthquake "A specialization of #$NaturalHazard.  Each instance of #$Earthquake is an event in which the earth's surface shakes as a consequence of violent seismic activity.")
(comment CarAirFreshener "The scented thing that people hang in their car to make it smell better.")
(comment Pelvis "The lower torso region around the pelvic bone")
(comment roofCoverageOfRegion "(#$roofCoverageOfRegion ?REGION ?PERCENT) means that #$GeographicalRegion ?REG has roof coverage of ?PERCENT.")
(disjointWith WheeledTransportationDevice Snowboard)
(comment BelgianSheepdog "A collection of medium-sized dogs.  In Canada, this breed name includes four varieties: Groenendael, Tervuren, Malinois and Laeken or Laekenois.  In the US, these are considered four separate breeds (with the Groenendae being the same as the #$BelgianSheepdog) , though the Laeken is not yet recognized.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization InsuranceOrganization)
(comment Album-IBO "The collection of #$RecordedSoundProducts that instantiate instances of #$Album-CW.")
(comment Transversospinalis "The #$Collection of all sets of #$Transversospinalis #$Muscle.  The #$Transversospinalis is the set of muscles (on each side of the body) which extend or rotate the spine (depending on whether acting bilaterally or laterally).  From superficial to deep, they are semispinalis, multifidus, interspinales, rotatores, and intertranversarii.  They connect #$Vertebrae to other #$Vertebrae from one to six cephalic from the origin.")
(comment Paint "Paint of all kinds, both in its liquid state and (later) in its dried state on a surface.")
(comment Scrotum "The collection of all scrotums (or 'scrota').  An individual #$Scrotum is an external sac (#$Sac-Organic) of Skin, attached near the base of the #$Penis, which encloses the #$Testicles.")
(comment MintFlavoring "Instances are pieces of a compound with a flavor like mint, used in foods and drinks.")
(comment GroceryStore "The collection of establishments that sell groceries and the other goods commonly found in a supermarket")
(comment isTheUnique "(#$isTheUnique OBJ COLL) is true iff (#$elementOf OBJ COLL) and OBJ is
the only element or instance of COLL. This predicate is primarily intended 
for use in representing definite noun phrase like 'The steering wheel in a 
car'. Note that the COLL argument has to be constrained carefully, for 
uniqueness is usually only up to some context or background.")
(comment GameForSystemFn "The Cyc function #$GameForSystemFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction. It takes as an argument a spec of #$Computer and returns an instance of #$GameProgramTypeByHardware. For example, (#$GameForSystemFn #$SonyPlayStation-TheProduct) denotes the collection of all game programs played on a Sony PlayStation system.")
(comment Stomach "A specialization of #$InternalOrgan.  Each instance of #$Stomach is an organ which is part of the digestive system (see the collection #$DigestiveSystem) of some animal.")
(comment ExecutableFTPExploit "The collection of #$ExecutableRootExploits whose instances
are designed to exploit FTP programs.")
(comment PPCompFrameFn "(#$PPCompFrameFn FRAME WORD) returns a spec of #$PPCompFrame FRAME that takes the specified #$LexicalWord WORD.")
(comment EarthRemoteSensingSatellite "The collection of all artificial satellites (#$Satellite-Device) which 
use powerful cameras to collect information about the Earth's surface.
They orbit the #$PlanetEarth in a LowEarthOrbit of about 300 miles from
the Earth's surface.")
(disjointWith InternalAnatomicalPart ExternalAnatomicalPart)
(comment UnicodeCompatibleCharacter "The collection of all Unicode-compatible characters: characters that have a binary encoding in the #$UnicodeStandard. Each instance of #$UnicodeCompatibleCharacter is a #$Character-Abstract, rather than a specific physical character as written, printed, or displayed. All #$ASCIICompatibleCharacters are also #$UnicodeCompatibleCharacters.")
(comment FixedTheaterSeat "Seats in theatres, some auditoriums; similar to seats on airplanes, trains.")
(comment DiskSector "This is the collection of all sectors on elements of #$ComputerDisk.")
(comment GasPipeline "The collection of #$Pipelines whose primary function is the transportation of #$NaturalGas.  See also #$OilPipeline.")
(comment Herbivore "A specialization of #$Animal.  An animal is an instance of #$Herbivore just in case it is an animal whose natural diet consists exclusively of plants or plant parts.  (Thus a horse that was forced or conditioned by humans to eat meat would still be a herbivore, since meat is not part of its natural diet.)  Notable specializations of #$Herbivore include the collections #$Ruminant and #$EquineAnimal.")
(comment commerciallyUsefulPartTypes "The #$commerciallyUsefulParts of a plant, etc.")
(comment DorsalRamusT6 "The collection of all T6 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT6 and DorsalRamiT6 branch from SpinalRootT6.  DorsalRamiT6 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment Caramel "A chewy candy made from caramelized sugar.")
(comment packaging "The various items constituting disposable packaging for a product.  Includes labels, wrappers, or boxes that are discarded before using the product.  Also includes the disposable storage containers, such as cardboard boxes and plastic bottles, that the product comes in and which are used to store a consumable product until it's all consumed.")
(comment FilicopsidaClass "A biological class within the plant kingdom which includes the TrueFerns")
(comment InternetCommunication "A specialization of #$Communicating and #$ComputerActivity. Each instance of this rather general collection is some kind of message-exchange that occurs over the #$Internet. Specializations of this collection include #$PostingToNewsgroup and #$OnlineChat.")
(comment MRIMachine "MRI (magnetic resonance imaging) machines use magnetic fieldsand computerization to produce a 3D image of (part of) a patient's body.")
(comment DirectionsToGetSomewhere "A collection of #$PropositionalInformationThings.  Each instance of #$DirectionsToGetSomewhere is a set of instructions for how to travel from one place to another.")
(comment BicuspidTooth "The teeth in front of an animal's molars, which have two cusps.")
(disjointWith HandTool Engine)
(comment CloveTree "Inidividual cloves trees, members of the species Syzygium aromaticum; their flower bud are harvested and dried to be used a s a spice.")
(comment LiechtensteinPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Liechtenstein, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment StapleRemover "The collection of staple removers.")
(comment Mammal "An instance of #$BiologicalClass, and a sub-taxon of #$Vertebrate.  Each instance of #$Mammal is an air-breathing, warm-blooded animal which, if female, nurses its young with milk secreted by mammary glands. The skin of instances of #$Mammal is typically covered with hair (or sometimes hair modified into scales or plates, as in pangolins), but some types are almost hairless.  All mammals other than the Monotremes of Australia bear live young rather than laying eggs, and have teats, which on females are used for nursing the young.  Monotremes do not have teats, but both male and female produce milk from mammary glands.")
(comment TerryCloth "The cloth that towels, washcloths, and some bathrobes are made of.")
(comment InvoluntaryBodyMovement "The collection of involuntary bodily movements, those movements in which an #$Animal's body does the action automatically -- the agent's consent doesn't enter into it.  Subsets of #$InvoluntaryBodyMovement include #$Heartbeating, #$Sneezing, #$Snoring, etc.")
(disjointWith SmokingFood Pasteurization)
(comment makesProductType "The predicate #$makesProductType is used to indicate that a particular company makes a specific (i.e., type of) product.  (#$makesProductType ORG PRODTYP) means that the #$CommercialOrganization ORG manufactures the #$ProductType PRODTYP.  Cf. #$madeBy, #$mainProductType and #$soleProductType.")
(disjointWith TrafficLight ChristmasLightString)
(comment SMTPServerProgram "#$SMTPServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP), the #$Internet's standard host-to-host mail transport protocol that traditionally

operates over TCP, port 25. A UNIX user can type 'telnet hostname 25'

and connect with an #$SMTPServerProgram on hostname, if one is present.")
(disjointWith InsuranceProvider TransportationCompany)
(comment Bolt "A strong solid fastening rod with a shaft threaded in order to receive of nut.")
(comment Cow "Female cattle.")
(disjointWith OutOfControlCrowdEvent IBTGeneration)
(comment RightRegionFn "The function (RightRegionFn REGOROBJ), applied to a region or object REGOROBJ, means the region consisting of the right half or flank or right main portion of REGOROBJ.  It applies only when REGOROBJ itself has an intrinsic left/right orientation, or is part of a larger region or object that has a left/right orientation.")
(comment Anilingus "The collection of #$SexualBehavior events in which somebody's #$Anus is orally stimulated in order to bring about #$SexualArousal.")
(comment MessageThread "A collection of collections of #$InformationBearingThings. Each instance of #$MessageThread is a series of electronic messages in which each message except the first is a response to the message that precedes it.")
(comment SkiCap "The collection of all skicaps")
(comment Sinusitis "This is the collection of all instances of sinusitis. Sinusitis is caused by an allergic response with accumulation of fluid or mucosal thickening in the sinus cavities.")
(disjointWith TakingAStep ThrowingAnObject)
(comment Head-Vertebrate "The collection of all heads of #$Vertebrates (animals with backbones).  Vertebrate heads all have faces (see #$FaceOfAnimal) and connect to the animal's torso via a neck; these things are not generally true for most non-vertebrates.")
(comment CarAudioEquipmentTypeByLevel "A collection with two instances that are themselves collections: #$AutomobileAudioEquipment and #$AutoAudioSystem. Instances of #$AutoAudioSystem have instances of #$AutomobileAudioEquipment as #$physicalParts, hence the two collections are disjoint and are considered to be a different 'level'.")
(comment Terrier-FoxWire "A collection of small to medium-sized dogs with wiry, thick coats.            The coat is mostly white.")
(comment VirginIslandsOfTheUSPerson "A person who is a citizen of the US by virtue of being born in the VirginIslands.")
(disjointWith ResearchOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment Paint-DryLayer "This is the collection of layers of dry paint on the surface of an 
object.  The paint need not cover the entire object.")
(comment ExternalOblique "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExternalOblique #$Muscle.  The #$ExternalOblique flexes the #$Torso and compresses the abdominal contents.  If acting unilaterally, it rotates the #$Torso to the opposite side.  The fibers are aligned with the fingers of a hand going into a pants pocket.")
(comment ElectricalMotor "An engine or motor that runs on electricity.")
(comment ExternalJugularVein "The collection of all external jugular veins.  The paired right and left external jugular veins are large veins that pass through the neck.  The proximal end of the external jugular vein connects to the subclavian vein and the distal end of the external jugular vein connects to the auricular vein.  The external jugular veins drain blood from the face and scalp.")
(comment Sandpaper "Paper with an abrasive coating on (at least) one side.")
(comment Announcement "The #$PropositionalConceptualWork bearing a message to some agent(s) that a particular event has occurred or is scheduled to occur.")
(comment normalGestationPeriod "This collection relates types of mammals to the typical  length of such a mammal's gestation periods, i.e., the time between  conception and birth, during which the embryo or fetus is developing  in the uterus.")
(comment objectsInVisualField "The objects in the line of sight of this sentient object.")
(disjointWith ComputerHardwareItem TransportationDevice)
(comment Gladiola "Flowering plants of the Iris family native in Europe, Africa, and the Medit. area. Widely cultivated for cut flowers.")
(comment BruneiPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Brunei, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SlopedRoof "The collection of sloping roofs.  An instance of 

#$SlopedRoof might consist of a single plane-like covering, 

but is more likely to consist in two or more such planes 

which meet at \"peaks\" and \"valleys\".")
(comment Cabinet-StorageConstruction "Storage compartments that are part of buildings.  They can be affixed to the wall at eye-level, or resting on the floor. They have doors and shelves.  Little closets.")
(comment Crying "The process of excreting tears from the eyes.")
(comment TakeOwnershipPermission "An instance of #$FilePermission associated with
computational systems using the #$MSWindowsNT operating system. If an
account has #$TakeOwnershipPermission to a file or folder, then the
user of the account can take ownership of that file or folder, which
means that he could also change the permissions on that file or folder.")
(comment ComputerSportsGame "This the collection of #$ComputerGamePrograms that simulate some sport.")
(comment EyebrowPencil "A pencil used to apply a dark coloring to accent the eyebrows.")
(comment PezDispenser "The collection of #$PezCandy dispensers")
(comment AccessoryNerve "The collection of all accessory #$Nerves.  The #$AccessoryNerve is the eleventh #$CranialNerve.  The #$AccessoryNerve #$innervates the #$Larynx, #$Pharynx and the large neck #$Muscles (#$Trapezius and #$SternoCleidoMastoid).")
(comment YeastLeavening "Aerating dough via the production of ethanol and CO2 from sugar by yeast.")
(comment Eraser-Board "erasers for whiteboards and blackboards.")
(disjointWith LicenseRequiringActivity TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment Font-ComputerTypeface "The collection of #$ComputerFile-AIS that contain information that allows a computer or printer to display or print text in a particular typeface. See also #$FontType.")
(comment CarouselHorse "An ornate model horse which is part of a carousel.")
(comment DorsalFin "Fin located on the back of fish and sea mammals, used for stabilizing")
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument MeasuringDevice)
(comment SierraLeonePerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$SierraLeone, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization AnimalOrganization)
(comment VHSCamcorder "Camcorders which record directly to #$VHSCassettes.")
(comment CreutzfeldtJakobDisease "A collection of #$AilmentConditions -- a rare fatal degenerative disease.")
(comment ElectricShaver "The collection of all electric shavers")
(comment EthmoidSinus "The collection of all ethmoid sinuses. The ethmoidal sinuses, from 3 to 18 thin-walled cavities between the nasal cavities and the eye sockets, make up the ethmoidal labyrinths. Their walls form most of the inner walls of the eye sockets and are joined together by a thin perforated plate of bone at the roof of the nose.")
(comment methodOfPreparation "The predicate #$methodOfPreparation is used to indicate how a particular item of food or drink was prepared.  (#$methodOfPreparation EDIBLE PREP) means that the particular instance of #$Food or #$Drink EDIBLE was prepared using the preparation method PREP.  For example, every portion of #$Beer had the #$methodOfPreparation #$Fermenting.")
(comment PolicyFn "#$PolicyFn takes as argument any instance of #$Organization and returns the collection of that organization's policies.  For example, (#$PolicyFn #$AustinISD) returns the collection of all policies of the Austin Independent School District.")
(disjointWith LocalOrganization NationalOrganization)
(comment BassDrum "low pitched drum ")
(comment VisualCommunicating "A specialization of #$Communicating.  Each instance of #$VisualCommunicating is an action in which information is transmitted by visual media.  Every instance of #$VisualCommunicating has at least one #$communicationToken (q.v.) which is an instance of #$VisualInformationBearingThing.  Examples of #$VisualCommunicating include: a performance by mime Marcel Marceau; Seiji Ozawa conducting the Boston Symphony Orchestra; a policeman directing traffic; shaking a fist at someone in anger; sending a message with flags, light pulses, or smoke signals.")
(disjointWith (RepairingFn Automobile) (RepairingFn ElectricalHouseholdAppliance))
(comment AudioEquipment "A collection of electronic devices.  An instance of #$AudioEquipment is a device that may be used in audio recording, playback, amplification, and/or reception.  This collection doesn't include musical instruments.  It does include both self-contained systems, e.g. boom boxes, and individual stereo components, such as microphones, amplifiers, etc.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterY "The lowercase letter 'y'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$Y-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterY.")
(comment Lipstick "A waxy, solid, usually colored cosmetic in stick form for the lips.")
(disjointWith RemovingSomething MakingAnOralSound)
(disjointWith TireRepairSubstance BuildingMaterial)
(comment ComputerPeripheralDevice "A specialization of #$ComputerHardwareItem. Each instance of this collection is an electronic device intended to be used with (but not in) some computer. Examples include #$ComputerKeyboard and #$ComputerPrinter. An external floppy drive is a positive exemplar, but an internal floppy drive is a negative exemplar.  Notable specializations of this collection include #$ComputerInputDevice and #$ComputerOutputDevice.")
(comment MuzzleForAnimal "The collection of removeable coverings placed over an animal's mouth, usually to stop it from biting or barking.")
(comment DeVerbalNoun "The collection of all nouns derived from verbs, including (but not limited to) those ending in '-ing', '-er/or', and 'tion'.")
(comment Bowl-Serving "Bowls used for serving food. These bowls are large, and they hold several individual servings.")
(comment DorsalRamusL1 "The collection of all L1 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiL1 and DorsalRamiL1 branch from SpinalRootL1.  DorsalRamiL1 supplies the ????.")
(comment WorldWideWebServerProgram "#$WorldWideWebServerProgram is a specialization of #$ServerProgram, instances of which were written to enable instances of #$Computer to respond to requests for information or processing from instances of #$WorldWideWebClientProgram.  Every instance of #$WorldWideWebServerProgram typically runs on an instance of #$WebServer-Network that is a node in an instance of #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment CardboardSheet "Pieces of cardboard used as a stiffening board, e.g., at the back of tablets or in packing frangibles.")
(comment Bacterium-MotileBySwarming "A collection of #$Bacterium which form concentric rings of growth in suitable mediums.  For example, #$Proteus-Genus begin a colony, then after a few hours, cells at the edge of the colony develope additional flagella and swim out a few millimeters from the original colony.  These cells then divide and form a concentric ring around the first colony.  Later other groups of swarm cells will create additional rings of growth.")
(comment PenOrPencilDrawing "Elements are elements of

#$Drawing-Depiction, usually on paper, made with ink or pencil.  Some

but not all #$PenOrPencilDrawings are elements of #$ArtObject.")
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice ConsumableProduct)
(comment MintFamily "An instance of #$BiologicalFamily, and a sub-taxon of #$DicotSubclass.  #$MintFamily is a collection of mostly annual or perennial herbs or shrubs, commonly found in temperate regions.  The leaves of many instances of #$MintFamily emit a pleasant odor when those leaves are crushed.")
(comment MauritiusPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Mauritius, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment NintendoEntertainmentSystem-TheProduct "The original 8-bit video game system manufactured by Nintendo.")
(comment Fourteen-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '14.'")
(comment WakashanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally northwestern U.S.")
(comment WineGlass "Distinctively-shaped glass used for drinking wine")
(comment SittingDown "The action of sitting down.")
(comment AutoDealership "#$AutoDealership is a specialization of #$RetailStore, #$Business, and #$TransportationOrganization.   Each instance of #$AutoDealership is an establishment (an organization located at one site) that sells automobiles and other types of road vehicles to consumers.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam SupportGroup)
(comment DeskScissors "Scissors designed for cutting paper.")
(comment Paw "A specialization of #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart. Each instance of this collection is a padded, furry foot found on some non-human mammals (e.g. #$Cats, #$Dogs).")
(comment TrochoidJoint "An #$TrochoidJoint is ich one #$Bone-BodyPart pivots relative to the other.")
(disjointWith LegMovement TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(disjointWith CuttingDevice StorageConstruct)
(disjointWith HeatingProcess TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment ChromeCleaner "Spray stuff to clean Chrome.")
(comment LiquidTangibleThing "An instance of #$TangibleStuffStateType and a specialization of #$FluidTangibleThing; the collection of all portions of liquid.  Each instance of #$LiquidTangibleThing is a tangible thing that has similar properties to those exhibited by things in the #$Liquid-StateOfMatter.  Specifically, its volume is relatively constant at varying pressures, and it freely changes shape (e.g. to conform to the shape of its container).  Liquids can never be said to break.  Note that not all #$LiquidTangibleThings are in #$Liquid-StateOfMatter : state-of-matter attributes (see #$MatterTypeByPhysicalState) apply only to quantities consisting of a single type of substance, whereas liquids can be mixtures of different substances.  Examples of #$LiquidTangibleThings include all substances in the #$Liquid-StateOfMatter, such as the water in a room-temperature glass of beer; liquid/liquid mixtures like the beer itself; solutions of solids in liquids, such as sea water; emulsions, such as milk; and suspensions of solids in liquids, like blood.  Compare #$FluidTangibleThing and #$GaseousTangibleThing.")
(comment CertificateDocument "The actual piece of paper on which a certificate is printed.")
(comment Lens-EyePart "The collection of all lenses in #$Eyes.  Each #$Lens-EyePart is a transparent lens of an #$Eye which focuses images onto the #$Retina of that #$Eye.")
(comment PerlCommandExecutionFault "#$PerlCommandExecutionFault is an attribute of some instances of
 #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$PerlCommandExecutionFault if
 an unauthorized person can pass Perl code to a program and have it execute
 arbitrary commands.")
(disjointWith TrainCar Wheelchair)
(comment BelgianSheepdog "A collection of medium-sized dogs.  In Canada, this breed includes              four varieties: Groenendael, Tervuren, Malinois and Laeken or Laekenois.              In the US, these are considered four separate breeds (with the               Groenendae being the same as the #$BelgianSheepdog),  though the Laeken              is not yet recognized.")
(comment AfghanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Afghanistan, or who participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment InsuranceOrganization "Each instance of #$InsuranceOrganization is an #$Organization that is primarily or significantly engaged in the insurance industry or whose activities focus on that industry.  Both #$AetnaLifeAndCasualty-Corporation and The Texas State Board of Insurance would be instances of #$InsuranceOrganization.")
(comment AnteriorBasalSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all anterior basal segments of #$InferiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by an #$AnteriorBasalSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung.")
(comment VideoCassetteRecorder "The device used to record television programs or play programs stored on a video cassette. Usually called a VCR")
(comment MedicalSpecialistType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection, and a specialization of #$PersonTypeByOccupation. Each instance of #$MedicalSpecialistType is a type of profession in the field of health care. Instances include #$Doctor-Medical, #$Dentist, and #$Nurse.")
(comment EjaculatoryDuct "The collection of all ejaculatory ducts.  An individual member of this collection is one of two #$AnatomicalVessels that transmit #$Semen to the #$Prostate from the #$SeminalVesicle and #$VasDeferens on the same side of the body.")
(comment StrawberryFlavoring "Instances are pieces of a compound with a flavor like strawberries, used in foods and drinks.")
(comment HardwareStore "The collection of establishments that sell building and gardening supplies")
(comment ScientificTheory "The collection of scientific theories. Minimal criteria that
apply to the notion of scientific theory are such that an instance of
#$ScientificTheory has to be logically or internally and empirically
consistent.")
(comment RemoteControlDevice "A control device that affects a device which is some distance away from the control device and its user.")
(comment PersonalCheck "A specialization of #$Check-TenderObject. Each instance of #$PersonalCheck is a check issued to a person who has a #$CheckingAccount (q.v.) with a bank.  Each instance of #$PersonalCheck is inscribed with a unique checking account number, as well as information about the person to whom it is issued (usually, this information will include the person's name and mailing address).")
(comment usesObject "If (#$usesObject A B) is true, then it follows that there exists some instance of performing an action with A as the performer and B as the tool or object.")
(comment Decoration "Instances of this collection are (typically non-essential) accessories or components that are added to a thing; they are used to visually enhance (e.g., beautify or possibly to connote something) the thing they are added to.")
(comment FTPAccount "The collection of #$ApplicationAccounts that give users access to files in the FTP directory of a computational system.")
(comment Altimeter "Device used to measure one's altitude.  Useful especially in aviation or in mountaineering.  Some altimeters measure distance to the ground below.  Other altimeters measure height above sea level via barometric pressure.")
(comment InternalAnatomicalPart "#$InternalAnatomicalPart is a specialization of #$OrganismPart.  Each instance of #$InternalAnatomicalPart is a part of the internal anatomy of an organism.  Example subcollections include #$CirculatorySystem and #$MiddleEar.")
(comment stringVersionOfCharacter "(stringVersionOfCharacter CHARACTER STRING) means that STRING is the #$SubLString representation of the abstract #$ASCIICompatibleCharacter CHARACTER.  For example, the following holds: (stringVersionOfCharacter #$LatinCapitalLetterA \"A\").")
(comment AcrylicSheet "Clear plastic sheets used like glass.")
(comment WearingSomething "A specialization of #$Configuration.  Each instance of #$WearingSomething is an arrangement of tangible objects, one of which is wearing the other(s).  Typically the wearer is a living person or animal, although surrogates are possible (e.g., mannequins, dolls, or corpses).  Objects worn are instances of #$SomethingToWear (q.v.).  See also #$wearer, #$wearsClothing, #$itemWorn.")
(comment interArgNotIsa1-3 "(#$interArgNotIsa1-3 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the first argument to PRED, the third argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(comment OilPipeline "The collection of #$Pipelines whose primary function is the transportation of petroleum products such as crude or refined oil (see #$PetroleumProduct).  See also #$GasPipeline.")
(comment BiologicalSubkingdom "A specialization of #$BiologicalTaxon.  Each instance of #$BiologicalSubkingdom is an immediate taxonomic subdivision of some instance of #$BiologicalKingdom (q.v.).  Instances of #$BiologicalSubkingdom include #$Protozoan, #$EmbryophyteSubkingdom, and #$AlgaeSubkingdom.")
(comment TelevisionSet "A television set")
(comment AxillaryNerve "The collection of all axillary #$Nerves.  Each #$AxillaryNerve branches off of a #$PosteriorCord-BrachialPlexus. The #$AxillaryNerve splits into anterior and posterior branches.  The anterior branch #$innervates the anterior part of the #$Deltoid.  The posterior branch #$innervates the posterior part of the #$Deltoid and the #$TeresMinor.")
(comment Pizza-ChicagoStyle "The collection of #$Pizzas cooked the #$CityOfChicagoIL way, with a deep-pan doughy base.")
(comment powerRating "The power rating of this device")
(comment GnetopsidaClass "A biological class within the gymnosperm group in the plant kingdom which contains the orders Gnetales, Welwitschiales and Ephedrales.")
(comment EnteringInfoIntoSpreadSheet "A specialization of #$ComputerActivity. Each instance of this collection is an event in which someone enters information  into some #$Spreadsheet by means of some #$SpreadsheetProgram.")
(comment DiagnosticScanningMachine "Diagnostic scanning machines are used to take 3D images of the inside of (part of) a patient's body.")
(comment SporeGermination "The collection of events in which spores, instances of #$Spore-PlantLifeStage, 

germinate.")
(comment TVShowTypeByGenre "#$TVShowTypeByGenre is a collection of collections.  Each element of #$TVShowTypeByGenre is a collection of specs of #$TVShow-CW whose instances all have a similar type of content, style or format, e.g. #$EducationalTVShowForChildren, #$AnimatedTVShow, or #$TVMiniseries.  Though this collection consists of various subsets of the collection #$TVShow-CW, it is not a partition of #$TVShow-CW since many instances of #$TVShow-CW will belong to more than one #$TVShowTypeByGenre,  #$TheSimpsons-TVShow is an instance of #$AnimatedTVShow as well as of #$SituationalComedy.")
(comment MolarTooth "The teeth in the back of an animal's mouth, which have four cusps and are used for grinding.")
(disjointWith File-Tool GraspingImplement)
(comment HorseChestnutTree "A large tree that has palmate leaves and conical clusters of showy flowers.  Widely cultivated as an ornamental and shade tree, its fruit, a prickly green bur, eventually splits open, revealing one or two shiny brown seeds.")
(comment WesternSamoanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$WesternSamoa, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment InkPad "The collection of ink pads. 

These are pads which store ink used for #$RubberStampDevices.")
(comment femaleParentActor "(#$femaleParentActor EVENT ORGANISM) means that ORGANISM is the female parent in the #$SexualReproductionEvent EVENT.")
(comment typicalArgIsa "(#$typicalArgIsa PRED NUM COL) says that typically, the NUMth argument-place of PRED is filled by an instance of COL.  Note that COL must be a spec of COLGENL, where (#$argIsa PRED NUM COLGENL).")
(comment ArmChair "A comfortable chair with cushions")
(comment MusicalCommunicating "The communication of a musical idea.")
(comment SteamingFood "A specialization of #$CookingFood.  In each instance of #$SteamingFood, some food is cooked by exposing it to steam.")
(comment ManagementOfTypeFn "#$ManagementOfTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$Organization, and returns the collection of activities involved in the management of organizations of that type.  For example, (#$ManagementOfTypeFn #$NonProfitOrganization) returns the collection of activities involved in the management of non-profits, and (#$ManagementOfTypeFn #$Pharmacy) returns the collection of activities involved in the management of pharmacies.")
(comment NLPhraseType "The collection of all subcollections, or types, of #$NLPhrase. Any instance of this collection is itself a collection of #$NLPhrases.")
(disjointWith ResearchOrganization EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization)
(comment BabyCarriage "The collection of baby strollers/carriages")
(comment EuropeanWildcat "european wildcat resembling domestic tabby; bushy tailed; regarded as ancestor of domestic cat.  Its scientific name is Felis

sylvestris.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single ProgrammingAComputer)
(comment SexualPositionType "The collection of all sexual position types, such as the missionary position.  Each element           of #$SexualPositionType is           a specialization of #$ArrangementOfLikeObjects that corresponds to some sexual position.")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType AnimalTypeBySex)
(comment EarProtectionGear "The collection of equipment used to protect the eardrum  against the loud sounds that occur during shooting a gun")
(comment EndogenousInfection "A specialization of #$Infection. Each instance 
of #$EndogenousInfection is an infection caused by pathogens normally present in 
the victim's body. These infections occur typically in case of reduced immunity 
or when the pathogens change their location, leaving a 'dormant focus' for a 
part of the host more propitious to their multiplication. See also #$ExogenousInfection. ")
(disjointWith TakingAStep IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment Chin "The protrusion of the face below the mouth")
(comment RoadVehicleControlWorkstation "The area in which a person who is driving a car or (semi-) truck sits. Especially includes the steering wheel.")
(comment Terrier-FoxWire "A collection of small to medium-sized dogs with wiry, thick coats.            Their coats are mostly white.")
(comment EnglishCanadianPerson "These are the prototypical default values for allInstances of #$EnglishCanadianPerson")
(disjointWith BeliefSystemFocusGroup TravelOrganization)
(comment Paint-WholeDryCoat "This is the collection of all coats of paint, that is, a layer of dry
paint that completely encases an object.")
(comment GuineaPig "A collection of domesticatable mammals originally from South America. Most are kept as pets, although wild ones are probably present in South America.  Their scientific name is Cavia porcellus.  According to most of the sources I could find, instances of #$GuineaPig are #$Rodents.  According to one source, they  are members of the order Rodentia and the family Caviidae.")
(comment RectusFemoris "The #$Collection of all instances of #$RectusFemoris #$Muscle.  The #$RectusFemoris connects the anterior iliac spine and #$Acetabulum with the Patella (#$Kneecap), and via the patellar ligament to the #$Tuberosity of the #$Tibia.  It extends the knee and assists flexion of the #$Hip.")
(comment Spoon "An implement one can use for scooping or stirring")
(comment SplenicVein "The collection of all splenic #$Veins.  The #$SplenicVein drains #$Blood from the #$Spleen and empties into the #$HepaticPortalVein.")
(comment BaseballBat-Wooden "Regulation bats; the kind used in professional baseball games.")
(comment SoftwareCrack "Collection of instructions that when implemented, either by humans or computers, result in the \"crack\"ing of some piece of software by making a trial version of a program a permanent version, by removing \"register now\" reminders, and so on.  Two of the most common forms of software cracks are computer programs that disable protection devices on execution and text files that instruct humans on how to disable various protection devices.  Use the more specific #$SoftwareCrackProgram and #$SoftwareCrack-Instructions for instances of these.")
(comment fieldsOfCompetence "(#$fieldsOfCompetence PERSON FIELD) means that the #$Person PERSON has actual competence and knowledgability in the #$FieldOfStudy FIELD, or at least is recognized by peers and colleagues in FIELD as being competent in FIELD. See also the related predicates #$expertRegarding and #$domainsOfSpecialization.")
(comment NorwegianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Norway, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment productTypeLicensedBy "(#$productTypeLicensedBy PRODUCTTYPE AGENT) means that AGENT
is legally empowered to grant licenses pertaining to PRODUCTTYPE and
that there do exist in the reasoning domain licenses pertaining to
PRODUCTTYPE of which AGENT is the issuer.")
(disjointWith AnimalSound SirenSound)
(comment Blinking "The reflex movement of closing one's eyelids.")
(comment AddPermission "An instance of #$FilePermission associated with
computational systems using the #$MSWindowsNT operating system. If an
account has #$AddPermission to folder, the user of the account can add
files to that folder.  This level of permission applies to folders
only (i.e., not files).")
(comment InternetNewsgroupMessage "A specialization of #$Letter-CW. Each instance of this collection is an individual posting to some #$InternetNewsgroup.")
(comment Mascara "A thick, dark-colored colored coating applied to the eyelashes to accent the eyes.")
(comment KryptoniteLock "A brand of #$Lock that suggests superior strength and durability via its association with #$Kryptonite, and thus #$Superman.")
(comment VagusNerve "The collection of all vagus #$Nerves.  The #$VagusNerve is the tenth #$CranialNerve.  The #$VagusNerve provides parasympathetic fibers to many #$Organs of the body.  The #$Heart, #$Lungs, #$Spleen, #$Liver, #$Stomach, each #$Kidney, #$SmallIntestine, and #$LargeIntestine are all innervated by the #$VagusNerve.  The vagus also #$innervates the #$Pharynx, #$Larynx, #$Esophagus, and #$Tongue.")
(comment VegetarianCuisine "a type of cuisine which includes plant products, and usually dairy products and eggs, but no animal flesh.")
(comment filedJointReturn "`(#$filedJointReturn YEAR PERSON)' means that PERSON filed a joint
tax return for YEAR.")
(disjointWith Atom MolecularRadical)
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject PlumbingFixture)
(disjointWith Perceiving BiologicalProductionEvent)
(comment Megaword "A function and an instance of  #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity. It equals approximately four million (8-#$Bit) #$Bytes. Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two, and its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a precise quantity of megabytes (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). Thus, the value of (#$Megaword 1) is one megaword. The value of (#$Megaword 1 2) is \"between one and two megawords. See also #$Word-UnitOfComputerMemory.")
(comment Paddle-Water "Paddle used in paddling a watercraft by hand.")
(comment substanceTypeProducedByCellType "(#$substanceTypeProducedByCellType SUBSTANCE-TYPE CELL-TYPE) relates a type of cell CELL-TYPE to the kind of #$OrganicStuff SUBSTANCE-TYPE it produces.  This predicate allows for type-level assertions about the substances produced at the cellular level.  It is confined only to substances produced within the cell and makes no conjecture on whether or not those substances are released from the cell.")
(comment PhotocopyingADocument "The collection of all events in which a hardcopy document is reproduced by means of a photocopy machine.")
(comment WebbedFoot "Foot used by aquatic creatures for swimming")
(disjointWith PlumbingFixture MeasuringDevice)
(comment EcuadoranPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Ecuador, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment EmploymentOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that are engaged in the employment or labor industry or whose activities focus on employment or labor matters.  Among the specializations of #$EmploymentOrganization are #$CareerCenter and #$TradeUnion")
(comment 8MMCamcorder "Camcorders which record on #$8MMCassettes.  These

types of #$AmateurVideoCameras usually need to be hooked up to the TV

directly to view the tapes.")
(comment CysticHygroma "A collection of #$AilmentConditions in which there are one or more non-malignant malformations of lymphatic vessels (cystic hygromas).")
(comment PaintBrush "A stick with a set of fibers at the end used to paint.")
(disjointWith PhysicalTransformationEvent ChangeInUserRights)
(comment FrontalSinus "The collection of all frontal sinuses, which are located inside #$FrontalBones. There are two #$FrontalSinuses inside each #$FrontalBone, one over each eye.")
(comment CriminalOrganization "A collection of organizations.  Each instance of #$CriminalOrganization is a group of agents, many of whom cooperate in the willful commission of criminal acts.  Not every member of the organization necessarily commits criminal acts (e.g. their lawyer, accountant, or receptionist may not).  Examples include the Sicilian Mafia, the Russian Mafiya, street gangs (e.g., Bloods and Crips), prison gangs. Criminal organizations may have local or international scope.  The latter will be instances of both #$CriminalOrganization and #$InternationalOrganization.")
(disjointWith FloristShop AutoDealership)
(comment Chime "tubes of varying lengths that are struck with a hammer ")
(disjointWith NonVerbalCommunicating SpokenCommunicating)
(comment RadioScanner "The collection of all radio scanners, used to listen in on radio transmissions of police, fire departments, etc.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterZ "The capital letter 'Z'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$Z-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterZ.")
(comment Razor "Collection of all razors, used in shaving or cutting hair, electric or manual.")
(disjointWith MakingAnOralSound IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(disjointWith ConsumableProduct BuildingMaterial)
(disjointWith ComputerMainBox ComputerPeripheralDevice)
(comment PottersWheel "A rotating horizontal disc used in making clay bowls, pots, etc.")
(comment Lemonade "Lemonade, the drink.  The real thing, not the flavored water you buy at the supermarket.  C.f. #$KoolAid.")
(comment MaxillaryNerve "The collection of all maxillary nerves.  The maxillary nerve is a branch of the #$TrigeminalNerve.  It serves the nasal cavity, the upper teeth, cheek, upper lip and lower eyelid.")
(comment InternetSoftwareMarketCategory "#$InternetSoftwareMarketCategory is the collection of software which is known and marketed as the particular 'internet software' market category within the software industry.  It consists of programs that implement, extend or exploit (in significant ways) use of the #$Internet.  Such programs, as available products, will usually be grouped together, in stores, in catalogues, etc.  This market category includes some electronic mail products, programs of #$Internet service providers, and #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource software, such as #$WorldWideWebServerPrograms and #$WorldWideWebClientPrograms.")
(comment Trombone "long medium-sized brass instrument ")
(comment UmbilicalCord "The collection of all umbilical cords.  An instance of this collection is an #$AnatomicalVessel containing two arteries and a vein that attaches a #$Fetus to its #$Placenta.  The #$UmbilicalCord is immersed in amniotic fluid, since the #$AmnioticSac surrounds it completely (#$surroundsCompletely).")
(disjointWith ConsumableProduct Clothing-Bottom)
(comment PowderyMildew "A fungus belonging to the fungus order Erysiphales which causes a plant disease.")
(comment TrinidadAndTobagoPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$TrinidadAndTobago, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SuperNintendo-TheProduct "The 16-bit video game system manufactured by Nintendo as an
          improvement to the original NES
          (#$NintendoEntertainmentSystem-TheProduct).  The two systems
          are not backward-compatible, however.")
(comment Heart-TheSuit "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which are hearts.")
(comment Uto-AztecanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages composing the Nahuatlan, Pima-Sonorran, Shoshonean sub-groups")
(comment MeasuringCup "a cup which measures volume")
(comment Shingles-Ailment "A very painful adult disease caused by the same #$Virus (varicella zoster virus) that causes #$ChickenPox usually in children.")
(comment BalancingSomethingOnHead "Holding something by balancing it on  one's head - the object remains stationary with respect to the head.")
(comment NationalOrganization "#$NationalOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization whose scope of operations and ownership or membership is primarily confined to a particular #$Country (but to no smaller subdivision within that country - see #$StateOrProvinceWideOrganization and #$LocalOrganization).  Examples of  #$NationalOrganization are the Daughters of the American Revolution and the National Association for the Advancement of Colored People in the United States, and the Red Guards and the Young Pioneers in China (PROC).")
(disjointWith SportsTeam FanClub)
(comment DresserDrawer "the collection of dresser drawers")
(comment PrePubescentHuman "The collection of people who have not yet gone through #$Puberty.")
(comment SaladFn "This function takes a set of ingredient-types and produces
the collection of salads containing those ingredients.")
(comment Scaphoid "The #$Scaphoid is designated 'radiale' in non-humans.")
(disjointWith LegMovement WavePropagation)
(disjointWith CuttingDevice HumanOccupationConstruct)
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(comment AutoWaterPump "Circulates coolant throught a car's engine.")
(comment PhotonicCrystal "Photonic crystals are artificial lattices which guide electromagnetic radiation by a method fundamentally different               from traditional index-of-refraction techniques. Waves are trapped in column-like arrays that -- when fabricated to               appropriate dimensions -- reflect desirable wavelengths as mirrors do light. Transmission is achieved through use of               deliberately added defects, which act as wave guides.")
(comment BankAccountStatement "The sort of document periodically sent from a bank to each of its account holders, listing the transactions that have affected their account and the balance of the account.")
(comment Neuron "The collection of nerve cells. The #$Neuron is the basic structural unit of the #$NervousSystem. A bundle of #$Neurons together makes up a #$Nerve. #$Neurons can have axons which are quite long.")
(comment ReadableKernelMemoryFault "#$ReadableKernelMemoryFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  Programs with this fault allow unprivileged users to read kernel memory that may contain sensitive information, such as unencrypted passwords.")
(disjointWith TrainCar BabyWalker)
(comment BichonFrise "A collection of small, white dogs.  This breed was formally called the Teneriffe. The plural of Bichon Frise is Bichons Frises.")
(comment AlbanianPerson "A person who is a citizen of #$Albania, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AgricultureOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that are primarily or significantly engaged in the agriculture industry or whose activities focus on that industry.")
(comment AutomobileTire "The collection of all #$Tires which belong on #$Automobiles.")
(comment ApicalSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all apical segments of right #$SuperiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by an #$ApicalSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.  (On the left side the apical and posterior segments of the #$SuperiorLobeOfLung are usually combined in the #$ApicoposteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.)")
(disjointWith AutoMaintenance SocialGathering)
(comment CorpusSpongiosum "The collection of all corpera spongiosum.  An individual #$CorpusSpongiosum is a cylinder of erectile tissue inside the #$Penis through the length of which the #$Urethra passes.  Its distal expansion is the #$GlansPenis.")
(comment FlavoringCompound "instances are pieces of a chemical compound that is used to flavor foods or drinks; may be synthetic or derived from natural sources. ")
(comment LightingStore "The collection of stores that sell all kinds of lamps and lighting fixtures")
(comment WebPageHitCounterProgram "Software to count hits on a #$WebPage-AIS.")
(comment TrapDeviceTriggeringMechanism "triggering mechs for trapping devices.")
(comment ancestors "(#$ancestors YOUNGER OLDER) means OLDER is one of the biological ancestors of YOUNGER.  OLDER could be one of YOUNGER's biological parents, biological grandparents, biological great-grandparents, etc.")
(comment Database-AbstractContent "The collection of all databases considered as abstract repositories of information rather than as physical storage devices.   A database generally has some means of accessing the data from structured records, frames or relational structures, using some query language.  A particular #$Database-AbstractContent may exist in multiple copies, and may be distributed over several different physical data storage sites: see also #$Database-Physical.")
(comment ftpAccountForSystem "(#$ftpAccountForSystem ACCOUNT SYSTEM) means that users of

ACCOUNT have access to certain files on SYSTEM that they may download

using #$FileTransferProtocol.")
(comment KneeChair "A collection of chairs [#$Chair-PieceOfFurniture] with knee pads, forward-sloping seat,  and often no back.  When one sits on a #$KneeChair, a significant portion of the body weight is supported by the legs.  These are ergonomically designed chairs.  Some #$KneeChairs can rock a little, while others are #$FoldingChairs.")
(comment CassavaPlant "Individual cassava plants.")
(comment EatingTable "Tables found in kitchens, restaurants, bars,  etc, at which people eat or drink.")
(comment MakingFacialExpression "A specialization of #$BodyMovementEvent.  Each instance of #$MakingFacialExpression is an event during which the configuration of a particular animal's face changes.  Such a change is usually (but not always) associated with the expression of some emotion by the animal in question.")
(comment CD-RWDrive "A collection of computer devices that can read and write data  onto both #$CD-R or #$CD-RW discs. Note, a #$CD-RDrive (as of July 99) can  only read and write onto #$CD-R discs while a #$CD-RWDrive can read and write onto both #$CD-R and #$CD-RW discs.")
(comment Barge "A #$Barge is a flat, usually rectangular #$WaterTransportationDevice.  It usually is not self-powered but is towed or pushed by a #$Watercraft.  Barges often tranport cargo, but it is not unlikely that some barges transport passengers.")
(comment DorsalRamusL3 "The collection of all L3 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiL3 and DorsalRamiL3 branch from SpinalRootL3.  DorsalRamiL3 supplies the ????.")
(comment Absinthe "a green, aromatic liqueur that is 68 percent alcohol, is made with wormwood and other herbs, and has a bitter, licorice flavor: now banned in most Western countries.")
(comment shortTermInformationStore-FunctionalRole "(#$shortTermInformationStore-FunctionalRole SYSTEM STORE)
means that STORE stores some piece of information (see
#$containsInformation) during some phase of the lifetime of SYSTEM,
and that STORE does not store any information during any time frame
not subsumed by the lifetime of the system, and that it is not true
that STORE contains any piece of information throughout the whole
lifetime of SYSTEM. ")
(comment Shingle-BuildingMaterial "An instance of #$ExistingObjectType and a subset of #$BuildingMaterial. Each instance of #$Shingle-BuildingMaterial is a thin piece of some material (e.g., wood or metal); many such instances are mounted in rows to cover the roof of some building.")
(comment SphenophytinaSubdivision "A subdivision in the plant kingdom which contains the horsetails.  Most are now extinct,")
(comment ComputerMarketCategory "A specialization of #$Product. Each instance of this collection is a product somehow associated with computers.  The collection includes computer hardware and software as well as supplies that are used with computers such as magnetic media, printer paper, cables, etc. Important specializations of this collection are #$ComputerHardwareItem and #$ComputerSoftwareMarketCategory.")
(comment XRayImage "An image produced by an X-Ray machine")
(comment Yaoi "Instances of the collection #$Yaoi are highly romanticized, but sexually explicit, Japanese-style #$Hentai cartoons about #$GayMales.  Members of this collection may also be instances of #$Cartoon-Still, or #$Animation-MovingImage.  #$Yaoi as a cartoon form originated in Japan in the 1990's primarily for a female audience.")
(comment WisdomTooth "The fourth(?) molars that a person usually gets during their adulthood, which nowadays frequently cause problems and are removed before they completely grow in.")
(disjointWith HouseholdAppliance Engine)
(comment ManchineelTree "The collection of manchineel trees.  A manchineel is a poisonous tree which grows in the #$Everglades.  Sap from this tree, or even rainwater dripping off its leaves damage bare human #$Skin.")
(comment ShippingLabel "The collection of shipping labels.")
(disjointWith TypicalArgPredicate CanonicalizerDirectivePredicate)
(comment interArgFormat2-2 "An instance of #$InterArgFormatPredicate (q.v.). (#$interArgFormat2-2 PRED COL FORMAT) means that FORMAT is a #$Format (q.v.) requirement for the second argument-place of PRED when PRED's second argument is restricted to being an instance of COL.  That is, with respect to a sentence of the form  (PRED ARG1 ARG2 ... ARGN) in which ARG2 is an instance of COL, PRED's arg2 position (i.e. the position occupied by the metavariable `ARG2' in the preceding sentence-form) is subject to FORMAT.  See #$Format and its instances for further explanation.  Note that #$interArgFormat2-2 is one of several  \"degenerate-case\" inter-argument format predicates, in which the specified  condition and the corresponding format constraint both have to do with the  _same_ argument-place of a given predicate.")
(comment Jogging "Less strenuous form of running")
(disjointWith SteamingFood RoastingFood)
(comment titleOfPosition "(#$titleOfPosition POSITION ORG STRING) means that people that have the position POSITION in ORG have the title STRING. For example, (#$titleOfPosition #$HeadOfState (#$GovernmentFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) 'president'). ")
(disjointWith Flashlight TrafficLight)
(comment Tiller "A lever used to turn the #$Rudder-ShipPart of a #$Watercraft-Surface from side to side.")
(comment Echidna "The collection of all echidnas; a subset of #$Mammal.  Elements of #$Echidna are Australian or New Guinea #$Monotremes, the females of which lay eggs which they keep in a pouch.  When the eggs are hatched, the young live in the pouch between 1 and 2 months.  Echidnas are covered with spines/quills and curl up in a ball for protection.  Their normal diet is #$Invertebrates.  Echidna milk (#$MilkFn #$Echidna) is #$PinkColor.")
(comment Swallowing "A specialization of both #$BodilyFunctionEvent and #$BodyMovementEvent.  Each instance of #$Swallowing is an event in which an #$Animal moves a solid or a liquid from its #$Mouth to its #$Stomach.")
(comment BoneSubPart "A #$BoneSubPart is a distinuishable part (or all) of a #$Bone-BodyPart.")
(comment NLTagFn "(#$NLTagFn TAG TERM) means that TERM appeared in a natural language utterance with the linguistic feature denoted by TAG.  For example, (#$NLTagFn #$Indefinite-NLAttr #$Dog) would mean that some word meaning #$Dog occurred with an indefinite determiner (\"a\" or \"an\").  This function serves as a hint to the NL subsystems that this term was used with a particular feature, and is only intended to serve as a stand-in until the NL subsystems can determine the correct form of TERM to use in the semantic translation of the utterance.  Note that uses of this can (and frequently should) be nested.  For instance, \"some cats\" would return from the parser as (#$NLTagFn #$Some-NLAttr (#$NLTagFn #$Plural-NLAttr #$Cat)).")
(comment Endoscope "An endoscope is a device used to view the insides of hollow organs or body cavities.")
(comment ComputerCode-Mobile "This collection includes all instances of #$ComputerCode which can be

    implemented on 'any' platform.  Typically instances of #$ComputerCode-Mobile

    will also be instances of #$ComputerCode-Interpreted.  This includes code written in #$JavaScriptProgrammingLanguage, ActiveX, etc.")
(comment WrestlingShoe "The collection of all wrestling shoes")
(comment Frostbite "A specialization of #$AilmentCondition. Each
instance of #$Frostbite is an individual case in which some
#$ExternalAnatomicalPart of an organism has been frozen. As a
specialization of #$AilmentCondition, this collection precludes
cryogenic freezing.")
(disjointWith TakingAStep FingerMovement)
(comment Cheek-Facial "Area on face between nose, mouth and ears")
(disjointWith CombustibleFuelSubstance FoodOrDrink)
(comment Terrier-SoftCoatedWheaten "A collection of medium-sized dogs with a soft, silky fur coat.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup TravelOrganization)
(comment OpponensPollicis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$OpponensPollicis #$Muscle.  The #$OpponensPollicis rotates the #$FirstMetaCarpal to put the #$Thumb into opposition.")
(comment DrinkingMug "A drinkingVessel usually made of ceramic material, with a handle.")
(comment ChilePepper "This is the collection chile peppers, 

including both fresh and dried forms. Chile peppers contain

various amounts of capsicum, which makes them hot to various degrees.")
(comment Lotion "#$Lotion is a collection of lotions.  Lotions are opaque, fluid, tangible stuff applied externally on the skin.  Lotions are less viscous than creams.")
(disjointWith VideoConceptualWork BookGeneric-CW)
(comment PublicTelephoneSystem "The collection of instances of #$TelephoneSystem that are designed for use by members of the general public in some region.  Communications among the telephones in the network may be transmitted along wires or light fibers, or via electromagnetic radiation.")
(comment Bulb-ThePlantPart "A collection of parts found in some monocotyledonous plants.  Typical elements of #$Bulb-ThePlantPart are found just below the surface of the soil.  A plant bulb is NOT a root; rather, it is a very short stem with associated leaf bases that are thick and broad, forming a roundish bulb with many layers of leaf bases.")
(comment BulgarianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Bulgaria, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment BotanicalOrgan "A specialization of #$PlantPart.  Each instance of #$BotanicalOrgan is a major morphological and functional feature of an individual plant.  Notable specializations of #$BotanicalOrgan include #$Flower-BotanicalPart, #$Leaf, and #$Stem.")
(comment LivingLanguage "A specialization of #$NaturalLanguage.  An instance of #$NaturalLanguage is an instance of #$LivingLanguage just in case it has at least one extant native speaker.")
(comment TireIron "X-shaped wrench used to remove lug nuts from automobile wheels")
(comment PunchingSomeone "The action of hitting someone with a fist--serious punches only, not playful ones.")
(comment argNotGenl "(#$argNotGenl REL N COL) means that nothing given as the Nth argument to the #$Relation REL may be an spec of the #$Collection COL.")
(comment ChangePermissionPermission "An instance of #$FilePermission associated with
computational systems using the #$MSWindowsNT operating system. If an
account has #$ChangePermissionPermission, then the user of the account
can change the permissions on the file or folder, which means that he
could also take ownership of that file or folder.")
(comment EliminatingAComputerVirus "A collection of events and a specialization of #$ComputerActivity and #$InformationRemoving. In each instance of this collection, computer virus(es) are removed from some information storage device (most likely a #$ComputerStorageDevice) via the use of an #$AntiVirusProgram. For the human activity of running an anti-virus program, see (#$HumanInitiatedFn #$EliminatingAComputerVirus).")
(comment LaundryDetergent "Detergent used in washing clothing")
(comment CoronaBeer "Light lager #$Beer brewed in #$Mexico, and often served cold with a slice of (#$FruitFn #$LimeTree) jammed into the bottle top. See also #$SolBeer.")
(comment ImpulsiveUrge "The type of internal sensation or feeling which propels one toward action that one might not do, had s/he thought about it.")
(comment FacialNerve "The collection of all facial #$Nerves.  The facial nerve is the seventh cranial nerve.  Each member of a pair of #$FacialNerves branches into a cervical branch, mandibular branch, buccal branch, zygomatic branch, and temporal branch.")
(comment Baking-Rising "Baking food to get it to rise, like bread or cake-- NOT just to cook it, like lasagna or a potato.")
(comment verbStrings "(#$verbStrings WORD STRING) states that STRING is one of the verb strings for the word unit WORD in some microtheory.  In other words, some verbal #$SpeechPartPredicate is used on WORD to relate it to STRING.  This predicate is

#$notAssertible since it is concluded from the current state of the knowledge base.")
(disjointWith BodyMovementEvent ChangeInUserRights)
(comment virtualMemorySize "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$Computer to instances of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity.. (#$virtualMemorySize COMP SIZE) means that COMP has SIZE as the size of its virtual memory. See also #$physicalMemorySize.")
(comment InnerTube "A ring-shaped inflatable tube usually made of rubber.")
(comment BiochemicalSynthesis "A collection of events. During instances of #$BiochemicalSynthesis, some chemical object is produced by synthesis (usually from more elementary objects) by some living organism or its parts. See #$BiochemicalSynthesisFn to denote the collection of biochemical synthesis of a given type of molecules; and #$biochemicalSynthesisOfMolecularType, the corresponding predicate for this function.")
(comment FormalLetter "formal letters --- in contrast with informal (often personal) letters. typically, either the recipient or sender is a business.")
(comment Cartilage "Translucent elastic tissue")
(disjointWith EmploymentOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment VHSCassette "VHS video cassettes.  The standard around the year

2000 for #$VideoTapePlaying.")
(comment Cataract-Ailment "A collection of #$AilmentConditions in which one or both of one's eye lenses loses transparency.  This results in dim, distorted or blurred images on the retina and decreased vision.")
(comment GameBoard "The collection of flat portable surfaces (usually rectangular) designed for board games")
(disjointWith ChangeInUserRights MedicalCareEvent)
(comment SphenoidalSinus "The collection of all sphenoidal sinuses, which are located inside #$Sphenoid bones. There are two #$SphenoidalSinuses inside each #$Sphenoid bone.")
(comment EdibleCalcium "The kind of calcium that people consume -- e.g. the calcium in yogurt or broccoli.")
(comment primaryTheoreticalField "(#$primaryTheoreticalField THEORY FIELD) means that the

#$ScientificTheory THEORY essentially belongs to the

#$ScientificFieldOfStudy FIELD. This predicate is a specialization of

#$theoreticalField. It can be use meaningfully in two cases: i) when a theory

belongs to a field that has relatively many superfields, possibly one

subfield of the other, and plays a significant role from the perspective of

many of these fields but there is one of those fields that is more directly

correlated to the theory, or ii) when a theory is considered to belong to

relatively many overlapping domain but is conventionnally designated as

pertaining mostly to that of a particular field.")
(comment ComputerVirusCopy "A specialization of #$ComputerProgramCopy, the instances of #$ComputerVirusCopy are copies of some computer virus.  That is, for all instances VIR of #$ComputerVirusCopy, there is some #$ComputerVirus, VIRUS, such that (#$programCopies VIRUS VIR).")
(disjointWith ServiceOrganization ManufacturingOrganization)
(comment Xylophone "A type of percussion instrument made of wooden bars and played with

small mallets.")
(comment SnowLeopard "A collection of large spotted cats with gray to white fur native to central   Asia.  Their scientific name is Panthera uncia.")
(comment languageOfCommunication "The predicate #$languageOfCommunication is used to indicate a language used by agents in a particular communication event.  (#$languageOfCommunication COM LANG) means that in the #$Communicating COM,  at least some of the information transferred is expressed in the language LANG.  LANG may be a natural language, a computer language, a musical system, or other symbolic system such as #$AmericanSignLanguage.")
(comment ElectricCookingRange "A #$CookingRange which uses #$Electricity instead of #$NaturalGas (or other fuel) to heat pans.")
(comment CycLNonAtomicTerm-Askable "The collection of #$CycLNonAtomicTerms

that can appear within sentences that are askable as queries to the Cyc system

(see #$CycLSentence-Askable).  More precisely, each instance of 

#$CycLNonAtomicTerm-Askable is a CycL non-atomic term that is constructible via 

the syntax of CycL without violating any applicable arity constraints (see 

#$arity).  Note that askable CycL non-atomic terms do not necesarily obey other 

semantic constraints beyond arity, such as argument-type constraints (see 

#$ArgTypePredicate); thus they are not always semantically well-formed in 

the fullest sense (cf. #$CycLNonAtomicTerm-Assertible).")
(comment RadioReceiver "The device used to receive transmissions broadcast in radio frequencies (does not include radio transmitters).")
(comment LatinSmallLetterZ "The lowercase letter 'z'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$Z-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterZ.")
(comment Eyeliner "Makeup used to emphasize the contour of the eyes.")
(disjointWith DisplayingSomething TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment interArgNotIsa4-5 "(#$interArgNotIsa4-5 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the fourth argument to PRED, the fifth argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(disjointWith Styrofoam BuildingMaterial)
(comment ComputerMainBox "The main box of a computer, which contains the processor, and possibly other devices such as a fan, internal CD or floppy drives, or sound and video cards.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByActivityType PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment SpiralStaircase "A flight of stairs which is coiled around a vertical axis.")
(comment VestibularNerve "The collection of all vestibular nerves.  The vestibular nerve is a branch of the #$AcousticNerve that provides afferent impulses for the sense of equilibrium.")
(comment WorldWideWebClientProgram "#$WorldWideWebClientProgram is the collection of programs whose instantiations run on on client computers with #$Internet access to the World Wide Web. #$WorldWideWebClientPrograms make information and service requests to#$WorldWideWebServerPrograms, which respond and may return the requested information or perform the requested services.  #$WorldWideWebClientPrograms include browsing software for accessing the information contained in instances of #$WebPage-AIS.")
(comment StageForPerformances "A stage-- usually a raised platform on which people can perform for an audience.  This can be an indoor or outdoor stage.")
(comment objectIsExposedToSubstanceType "#$objectIsExposedToSubstanceType allows one to say

 that some object OBJ is/has been exposed to some

 type of substance SUBS, without having to specify

 the #$PhysicalEvent in which this exposure takes place.

  To relate OBJ and SUBS to the event, use

  #$exposureOfObjectToSubstanceType.")
(disjointWith NaturalTangibleStuff TextualMaterial)
(comment Ureter "The collection of all ureters, #$AnatomicalVessels for the passage of #$Urine from the #$Kidneys to the #$Bladder-Urinary.")
(disjointWith ConsumableProduct Clothing-Top)
(comment Nintendo64-TheProduct "The 64-bit video game system manufactured by Nintendo beginning
          around 1996.")
(comment Jack-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of 'Jack.'")
(comment CaddoanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages mostly of the West")
(comment Ladle "A large spoon with a deep basin used to ladle out soup, punch, etc.")
(comment CommunityOrganization "#$CommunityOrganization is a specialization of both #$LocalOrganization and #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly.  Each instance of #$CommunityOrganization is a group that consists of residents of a #$Neighborhood (q.v.) or apartment building or condominium complex, and which is concerned with issues affecting the #$Neighborhood or complex.")
(comment containsPrograms "This predicate relates computer programs to their subprograms.  (#$containsPrograms BIG LITTLE) means that BIG has LITTLE as one of its subprograms. For example, (#$containsPrograms #$MSOffice #$MSPowerPoint) means that Microsoft Office contains Microsoft PowerPoint.  Use the more specific #$containsModules if LITTLE is not executable on its own.")
(comment SquareSail "A 4-sided #$Sail-Device extended on a #$Yard-BoatPart suspended at the middle from a #$Mast-Device.")
(comment DownyMildew "A fungus belonging to the fungus family Peronosporaceae which causes a plant disease.")
(comment Eyelid "The collection of all eyelids.  An eyelid is a flap of #$Skin in front of and above or below the eyeball which half covers the #$Eye when the #$Eyelids are closed.  The #$Eyelids on one side of the face are closed when #$WinkingAnEye.  Those on both sides are closed when #$Blinking or when #$Sleeping")
(comment Triquetrum "The #$Triquetrum is also designated 'cuneiform ', 'triquetral bone', 'triangular bone', or (in non-humans) 'ulnare'.")
(disjointWith LegMovement EmittingAnObject)
(disjointWith CuttingDevice BuildingMaterial)
(comment Pump-Mechanical "Used to move fluid from one spatial region to another.")
(comment Blueprint "Diagrams and plans for the construction of a building")
(comment Wing-AnimalBodyPart "Appendage used in flying through the air")
(comment FirewallBypassFault "A #$ProgramFault of some instances of #$OperatingSystem.  A firewall running an operating system with this fault will, under certain conditions, allow data to be sent to a blocked port on a machine on the network.")
(disjointWith AirplaneRunway Railway)
(comment Brittany-TheDog "A collection medium-sized dogs.  He is called the Brittany Spaniel in Canada and            was also so called in the United States before 1982.")
(comment AlgerianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Algeria, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith AgricultureOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment SawHorse "This is the collection of all #$SawHorses -- #$Tools used primarily in pairs by #$Carpenters to prop up pieces of wood to be cut, stained, painted, etc.  #$SawHorses are usually constructed out of five wooden boards (four of which are the same length) and two connecting clamps, giving them a 'stick-figure' #$Horse appearance.")
(comment PosteriorSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all posterior segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of right (and sometimes left) #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a right #$SuperiorLobeOfLung, that supplies air to a #$PosteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung in the #$SuperiorLobeOfLung (or the posterior part of the #$ApicoposteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung on the left side). It branches from the #$SuperiorLobarBronchus.")
(comment JuiceConcentrate "Juice from which much of the water has been extracted (how?). Frozen juice concentrate is a common consumer product.  Juice concentrates are also used in manufacturing juice drinks and blends.")
(comment LiquorStore "The collection of local establishments that sell alcoholic beverages .")
(comment TrapTrippingEvent "The action in which a trap is activated.  It may be activated by a human operator, by the actions of an animal, or accidentally by other natural forces.  Often a trap tripping results in the capture of an animal, but not necessarily.")
(comment usesCommunicationConvention "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$InformationStore to instances of #$CommunicationConvention. (#$usesCommunicationConvention INFO_STRUCT CC) means that INFO_STRUCT uses CC to represent its information.  For example, the original [#$originalInfoStructureOfCW] Iliad uses the #$AncientGreekLanguage as a #$CommunicationConvention, while a modern translation into Tagalog uses the #$TagalogLanguage and, when written, uses the #$WesternEuropeanWriting #$orthography as another #$CommunicationConvention. See also the more specific #$languageWrittenIn.")
(comment InstructionsForUsingOrDoingFn "#$InstructionsForUsingOrDoingFn takes as argument any spec of #$Thing and returns the collection of all instructions for things of that type. For example, (#$InstructionsForUsingOrDoingFn #$ComputerGameProgram) returns the collection all instructions for computer games, (#$InstructionsForUsingOrDoingFn #$VideoCassetteRecorder) returns the collection of all instructions for VCRs, and (#$InstructionsForUsingOrDoingFn (#$MakingFn #$Beer)) returns the collection of all instructions for making beer.")
(comment Shampoo "A specialization of #$ToiletrySubstance, #$LiquidTangibleThing, and #$Surfactant. Each instance of this collection is a portion of liquid typically used as a cleanser for hair on the head. (Note that this is shampoo qua #$ExistingStuffType i.e. the liquid only and not shampoo plus its packaging in bottles, etc.).")
(comment PowderDispenser "A container for storing and dispensing powder such as baby powder.  It has holes in the top through which the powder is shaken.")
(disjointWith WearingSomething MolecularConfiguration)
(comment GraphicsAcceleratorCard "A type of #$ComputerGraphicsBoard that contains a specialized microprocessor           for doing the calculations necessary for redering 3D graphics on a video           display.")
(comment CerealPlant "A specialization of both #$CropPlant and #$GrassFamily.  Each sub-collection of #$CerealPlant is a type of grain-bearing plant.")
(comment HouseholdAppliance "A specialization of #$MechanicalDevice.  Each instance of #$HouseholdAppliance is a device used in one of the tasks typically carried on in a home, such as food preparation, food storage, laundry, household cleaning, personal cleaning, and cooling or heating the house for comfort.  Specializations of #$HouseholdAppliance include the collections #$Oven, #$Refrigerator, #$ClothesDryer,  #$VacuumCleaner, #$HotWaterHeater, and #$Furnace.")
(comment GreaterOccipitalNerve "The collection of all greater occipital #$Nerves.  A #$GreaterOccipitalNerve is the medial branch of #$DorsalRamusC2 on its side of the body.  The #$GreaterOccipitalNerve innervates the scalp on the back of the head (#$Head-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment Seafood "The collection of portions of meat of edible fish and shellfish.")
(comment SpermWhaleFamily "The biological family Physeteridae of the suborder Odontoceti            (#$ToothedWhales).  Distinguishing features of the members            of this family include a squared snout and a relatively large head.")
(comment PostingToNewsgroup "A collection of actions and a specialization of #$InternetCommunication and #$OneToManyCommunication. In each instance of #$PostingToNewsgroup, an agent causes the generation of a new #$InternetNewsgroupMessage - by causing a message to be sent out as one of the #$episodes of a newsgroup.")
(comment SurgicalMask "The masks worn by medical professionals over their noses and mouths to reduce the likelihood of spreading infections.")
(comment SporeFormingBacterium "The collection of bacteria [#$Bacterium] that are capable of forming spores. When a group of these bacteria is placed in an hostile environment, some of them may form a single internal spore, an endospore [#$Spore-DormantBacterium], which is liberated when the mother cell undergoes autolysis.")
(comment SalesCatalog "The collection of all sales catalogues -- documents that list and describe types of items which can be bought, along with the prices per some unit(s) of the items.")
(comment Lap-BodyRegion "a region of the body that only people have, and only when they are seated.")
(disjointWith Brush ControlDevice)
(comment CoconutPalm "Individual Coconut palm trees.")
(comment LithouIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Lithou-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PackingTape "The collection packing tape.

This is strong wide tape used for packaging.")
(comment ConsumingFoodOrDrink "A specialization of both #$Ingesting and #$AnimalActivity.  Each instance of #$ConsumingFoodOrDrink is an event in which an animal ingests some portion of food or drink through its mouth.  Notable specializations of #$ConsumingFoodOrDrink are #$EatingEvent and #$DrinkingEvent.")
(comment TypicalArgPredicate "The collection of all instances of #$MetaPredicate that specify the typical, or expected identity of #$isa or #$genls of arguments of predicates.  These predicates are not used in wfchecking, and so should never be used in place of #$ArgConstraintPredicates.")
(comment Canvas "A coarse cloth of hemp, cotton, etc. used for tents, sails, paints, etc.")
(comment DrinkingASip "The liquid analogue of #$EatingAMorsel.   Consists of manually grasping a drinking vessel, moving it to the mouth and pouring fluid into the mouth.  The last thing to happen is swallowing.")
(comment GrillingFood "A specialization of #$CookingFood.  In each instance of #$GrillingFood, food is placed on a cooking utensil consisting of several parallel metal bars, where the food is exposed to direct radiant heat from below.")
(disjointWith BabyWalker BabyCarriage)
(comment Nuke-ComputerVirusCreator "#$Nuke-ComputerVirusCreator is the collection of related

#$MaliciousComputerPrograms which are used to produce instances of #$ComputerVirus.")
(comment BiologicalFamily "The collection of biological taxonomic subdivisions below #$BiologicalOrder (or #$BiologicalSuborder) and above #$BiologicalGenus.  Especially important in Botanical classification.")
(disjointWith InformationRecordingProcess Conveying-Generic)
(comment Synarthrosis "A #$Synarthrosis is an immovable #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment NLQuantFn "(#$NLQuantFn TAG TERM) means that TERM appeared in a natural language utterance with the quantification denoted by TAG.  For example, (#$NLQuantFn #$Some-NLAttr #$Dog) would mean that some word meaning #$Dog occurred with the quantifier \"some\".  This function serves as a hint to the NL subsystems that this term was used with a particular feature, and is only intended to serve as a stand-in until the NL subsystems can determine the correct form of TERM to use in the semantic translation of the utterance.  Note that uses of this can (and frequently should) have as its arg2 another #$NLTagFn expression.  For instance, \"some cats\" would return from the parser as (#$NLQuantFn #$Some-NLAttr (#$NLNumberFn #$Plural-NLAttr #$Cat)).")
(comment ElectroMyograph "An electromyograph is an instrument used which translates the electrical activity used in muscles to a visual or sound record.  It is used in diagnosing neuroskelatal disorders and in biofeedback.")
(comment WildAnimal "A specialization of #$NonPersonAnimal. Each instance of this collection is a non-human animal that is not domesticated or tame.  Note that a captive animal may still be a wild animal, e.g. zoo animals that are not tame or domesticated.  Specializations of #$WildAnimal are returned by #$WildAnimalFn. See also #$CaptiveAnimal, #$DomesticatedAnimal.")
(comment ComputerTextFile "This is the collection of all files of #$ComputerDocumentFiles that contain text without any graphics.")
(comment FigureSkate "The collection of all skates used for figure skating")
(disjointWith HittingAnObject TakingAStep)
(comment Nail-AnimalBodyPart "Hard covering over fingers and toes")
(comment Terrier-WestHighlandWhite "A collection of small dogs with white fur, also called the          Westie.")
(comment EastIndianPerson "collective term applied loosely and vaguely to people native to #$India, Indochina, & the Malay Archipelago; excludes Melanesia, #$HongKong")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment FigureSkating "The collection of all #$IceSkating events in which the performer intensionally performs specific patterns of movement, as opposed to mere transportation or racing via #$IceSkates.")
(comment FlexorPollicisBrevis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$FlexorPollicisBrevis #$Muscle.  The #$FlexorPollicisBrevis flexes the #$Thumb at the #$MetaCarpoPhalangealJoint.")
(comment PickupTruck "A fuel-burning mechanical device which is a conveyance, a kind of truck, usually with an open back for light hauling, etc.")
(comment SuperiorVenaCava "The collection of all superior vena cava veins.  The superior vena cava is the main vein of the upper chest that empties into the right atrium.  Its distal end is formed by the junction of the proximal ends of the right and left brachiocephalic veins.  The superior vena cava returns all blood from the upper body to the heart")
(comment siblingOrganizations "The predicate #$siblingOrganizations relates two organizations which are immediate #$subOrganizations of a common (unspecified) parent organization.  (#$siblingOrganizations ORG1 ORG2) means that the #$Organizations ORG1 and ORG2 are sister organizations within some hierarchically structured organization; ORG1 and ORG2 are at the same `level' from the top.")
(comment NewsGroupMessageFn "#$NewsGroupMessageFn takes as argument any instances of #$Thing and returns the collection of all #$InternetNewsgroupMessages that make reference to that thing.  For example, (#$NewsGroupMessageFn #$PreservingFood) returns the collection of all news group messages mentioning food preservation.")
(comment Tape "#$Tape is the #$Collection of all tape.  An instance of #$Tape is a thin, flat strip.  It can be made from plastic, cloth, or similar material.  Tape is very flexible.  Its strength depends on the material from which it is made.")
(comment Obituary "The collection of #$InformationBearingObjects whose contents include public notices of the deaths of their subjects.  An #$Obituary typically is accompanied by a biographical sketch of the person who has died.")
(comment anatomicalPartTypeAffected "(#$anatomicalPartTypeAffected ACT BODYPARTTYPE) means that body parts of the #$AnimalBodyPartType BODYPARTTYPE are affected by the action ACT.  For example, if BRUSHING is a #$TeethCleaning event, then (#$anatomicalPartTypeAffected BRUSHING #$SetOfTeeth).")
(comment Inspecting "The act of inspecting something : looking over, viewing closely, eyeing critically.  In the manufacturing domain, the result of an inspection is a judgement as to whether the thing inspected meets its specification.  We leave the representation of this last fact for later.")
(disjointWith ElectronicDevice PlumbingFixture)
(comment CantaloupePlant "The collection of individual cantaloupe plants.")
(comment OkinawaIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Okinawa-Islands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment productTypeLicensedForUseInRegion "(#$productTypeLicensedForUseInRegion PRODUCTTYPE ROLE
EVTTYPE REGION) means that there exists a #$License-LegalAgreement
which stipulates that if PRODUCT is an instance of PRODUCTTYPE it is
permissable for PRODUCT to play ROLE in an event of type EVTTYPE that
occurs within the #$GeographicalRegion REGION.")
(comment PlantPartType "A collection of collections.  Each element of #$PlantPartType is a collection of parts of plants, characterized by their structure and function, rather than along taxonomic lines.  Since #$PlantPartType is a #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType, any two instances of it (such as #$NutShell and #$Leaf) can be assumed disjoint, unless we know that one is a subset of the other.  (For more information, see comment on #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.)")
(comment Belt-Mechanical "Closed loop of material used to transfer rotational energy; like belts in a car or chains on bicycles or motorcycles.")
(comment Vomiting "The action where the stomach convulses to expel the contents inside.")
(comment ownerPermissions "(#$ownerPermissions COPY PERM) means that someone logged
into a machine under the #$ComputerAccount which the machine
recognizes as the #$ownerAccountForFile of COPY has all the rights and
privileges associated with PERM.")
(comment (HumanInitiatedFn EliminatingAComputerVirus) "A collection of events and a specialization of #$ComputerActivity and #$InformationRemoving. Each instance of this collection involves deliberately removing a computer virus from some information storage device via the use of an #$AntiVirusProgram.")
(comment Microfilm "The collection of all pieces of microfilm, whether exposed or not.  Microfilm generally consists of a sequence of images (frames) in a roll.  See also Microfiche.")
(comment SolBeer "Light lager #$Beer brewed in #$Mexico, and often served cold with a slice of (#$FruitFn #$LimeTree) jammed into the bottle top. See also #$CoronaBeer.")
(comment AbducensNerve "The collection of all abducens #$Nerves.  An #$AbducensNerve (or 'abducent nerve') is the sixth #$CranialNerve.  Each #$AbducensNerve #$innervates the lateral rectus #$Muscle (one of the #$ExtraocularMuscleSet) to move the #$Eye on its side of the body.")
(comment FoodServingFn "This function returns a collection whose members are individual-sized servings of edibles and potables.")
(comment CorrugatedCardboardBox "The 2-ply, ridged type of a cardboard box.")
(disjointWith MovingEarth BiologicalEvent)
(comment ComputerCode-Interpreted "The subcollection of #$ComputerCode-Source which is directly interpretable

by some #$ProgrammingLanguageImplementation, without necessarily being compiled into #$ComputerCode-Binary first.")
(comment KayakPaddle "Paddle with a blade on both ends that is used in Kayaking.")
(comment InstructionalWork "The set of all documents that contain as their information content instructions for how to do something.")
(comment Iris-EyePart "The part of the eye which has color")
(comment Tripod "A three legged device used to support or steady something,  particularly #$StillCameras.")
(comment stuffTypeUsed "(#$stuffTypeUsed EVT STUFFTYPE) says that some instance(s) of STUFFTYPE were used during EVT.  In other words, (#$relationInstanceExists   #$stuffUsed EVT STUFFTYPE).")
(comment EgyptianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Egypt, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EmploymentOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment 8MMCassette "8mm video cassettes.  Typically used only for

#$AmateurVideoCameras but usually of higher quality than other video medias

available to the amateur.  Must be played back from #$8MMCamcorder or copied to

a #$VHSCassette for playback on a #$VideoCassetteRecorder.")
(comment CushingsSyndrome "A collection of #$AilmentConditions, a metabolic disorder caused by overactivity of the adrenal cortex, usually secondary to other disease processes. If caused by a tumour of the pituitary gland, it is called Cushing's disease.")
(comment Needle "A sharp, pointy object.")
(disjointWith PlayingAGame ChangeInUserRights)
(comment RhNegative "#$Blood either has or does not have the Rh factor.  Adding foreign blood which is #$RhPositive to the #$CirculatorySystem of a body whose blood which is #$RhNegative will cause the recipient's body to develop anitbodies against the Rh factor.  If the recipient of #$RhPositive blood is a woman who later has an #$RhNegative child, then her immune system will attack the child's blood.  Rh factor is controlled by a recessive gene.")
(comment LegalCorporation "The collection of all #$Organizations which have been incorporated in accordance with the laws of a jurisdiction.  Each instance of #$LegalCorporation is a legal entity distinct from its owners and employees, and is afforded certain powers both by law and by its incorporating documents.  Instances of #$LegalCorporation may be either #$CommercialOrganizations or #$NonProfitOrganizations.  Each instance of #$LegalCorporation organized in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica is incorporated under the laws of a particular state, although it may be empowered to carry on activities in any state.  Most American jurisdictions require that one of the words or abbreviations `corporation', `company', `incorporated', `corp', `co', or `inc' be included in the registered name of a corporation.  Instances of #$LegalCorporation include #$IBMInc and #$Cycorp.")
(comment Glockenspiel "percussion instrument made of metal bars that are struck with
a hammer ")
(comment CookingRange "An appliance which has (at least) one #$Burner.  Also often called \"stove.\"")
(comment PhotocopyMachine "Machines used for the photo-duplication of hardcopied printed matter.")
(comment PaliCharacter "characters used for the Pali Prakrit")
(comment Makeup "Consumable products used in improving one's appearance.")
(disjointWith Cleaning CommunicatingUsingADevice)
(disjointWith Glass Concrete)
(comment Harmonica "The collection of all harmonicas, a small wind instrument. In a harmonica, tones are produced by inhaling and exhaling through a series of free reeds that sit behind a row of air holes.")
(comment Aspartame "Aspartame, a sweetening agent used in soft drinks and other prepared foods.")
(comment IlioinguinalNerve "The collection of all ilioinguinal #$Nerves.  An #$IlioinguinalNerve comes from a #$VentralRamusL1 and #$innervates the #$InternalOblique, the #$Skin of the proximomedial #$Thigh and the #$Skin of either the penile root and #$Scrotum (male) or the mons pubis and labium majus (female).")
(comment MuscatCanelli-Wine "The collection of all instances of

Muscat Canelli wine.")
(comment AccountingProgram "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used for financial accounting.")
(comment SnareDrum "two-headed drum with a snare attached to one side")
(comment BlueBook-Examination "The collection of thin booklets normally used in many North American universities for writing examinations.")
(comment Omentum-Greater "The collection of all greater omenta.  An individual of this collection is a large fold of the #$Peritoneum which is suspended from the #$Stomach and passes between the intestines (#$SmallIntestine and #$TransverseColon) and the #$TransverseAbdominous #$Muscles. An #$Omentum-Greater is also connected to the #$TransverseColon.")
(disjointWith ConsumableProduct ProjectileLauncher)
(comment ErysiphalesOrder "A fungus family which includes downy mildews.")
(comment MayottePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Mayotte, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment NintendoSystem "The collection of all #$VideoGameSystems manufactured by Nintendo.")
(comment Joker-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which are jokers.")
(comment TanoanLanguageFamily "Western Amerindian languages")
(comment SaltShaker "A container for storing and dispensing salt")
(disjointWith MedicalCareEvent EnteringAComputerPassword)
(comment NonProfitOrganization "#$NonProfitOrganization is a specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$NonProfitOrganization is an organization that is not operated with the purpose of making a profit.  Instances of #$NonProfitOrganization have members, rather than owners.  Charities, clubs, schools, political action groups, political parties and churches are usually instances of #$NonProfitOrganization.  Instances of #$NonProfitOrganizations are often exempt from certain taxes in particular jurisdictions.  Specific examples of elements of #$NonProfitOrganization are #$RedCrossSociety-National and #$RomanCatholicChurch.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam CriminalOrganization)
(comment CityBus "A large bus used typically by municipalities for conveying passengers between public bus stops within the municipal limits, for a small fee.  Capacity up to 60 people.")
(comment SoupFn "This function takes a set of ingredient-types and produces
the collection of soups made from those ingredients.")
(disjointWith ChemicalReaction Resting-Relaxing)
(comment WormianBone "A #$WormianBone is an extra #$IrregularBone that may form in a #$BoneSuture of the #$Skull.")
(disjointWith LegMovement DecompositionProcess)
(disjointWith CuttingDevice Clock)
(comment DeathFn "A #$PartialFunction (q.v.)that maps a given #$BiologicalLivingObject that has died to the event of its death.  If BLO has died, then (#$DeathFn BLO) is the event that is the death of BLO (see #$DyingOfBLO); otherwise #$DeathFn is undefined for BLO.  See also the corresponding predicate #$deathOf.")
(comment FanSitePage "A collection of WWW pages. Each #$FanSitePage is an instance of #$WorldWideWebPage-CW that is designed by and for fans of something which is the #$topicOf that page.")
(comment AutoSoundMarketCategory "Different types of stereo and radio equipment.")
(comment Tattoo "A collection of visual marks.  Each element of #$Tattoo is a mark made on the skin of a person or other animal, having a pattern formed by scar tissue or by pigment applied in or under the skin.  In medical terms, `tattoo' includes marks resulting from accidental tattooing.  But typically tattoos are deliberately applied for purposes of identification or decoration.")
(comment Elbow "The joint where the arm bends")
(comment VulnerableToFirewallBypass "A spec-attribute of #$ComputerVulnerability.  If a computer is #$VulnerableToFirewallBypass, it is possible to send data to some machine on the network over some port which is supposedly blocked by the network's firewall.")
(comment ChineseCrested "A collection of small dogs.  There are both hairless and coated varieties.")
(comment AngolaPerson "This is the collection of citizens, or participants in the #$NationalCulture, of #$Angola")
(disjointWith AgricultureOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment Suiseki "The collection of all found rocks [#$StoneObject-Natural] which have been cleaned mounted on wooden stands as \"found art\" objects.  This is a Japanese form of art.")
(comment AnteriorSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all anterior segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a (left or right) #$SuperiorLobeOfLung that supplies the #$AnteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.  It branches from the #$SuperiorDivisionBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.")
(comment AudioCassette "Audio cassette tapes")
(disjointWith AutoMaintenance BiologicalEvent)
(comment AmnioticSac "The collection of all amniotic sacs (or 'amnions').  An individual member of this collection is a sac (#$Sac-Organic) filled with amniotic fluid surrounding a mammalian #$Fetus.  Amniotic sacs are considered to be part of the #$Embryo along with the #$Fetus and #$Placenta-FetalPortion.  A human #$AmnioticSac is formed two months after fertilization of a human egg (#$Ovum) and exists inside the maternal #$Uterus.  The remains of the #$Placenta and #$AmnioticSac are expelled from the #$Uterus after the fetus(es) are born.")
(comment Ketchup "Ketchup")
(comment OfficeSupplyStore "The collection of office supply stores, such as individual BizMarts and OfficeDepots.")
(comment DownloadOfTypeFn "A function that takes a specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW and returns the collection of all #$DownloadingAFile events in which that type of program is downloaded.")
(comment MedicalDevice "A collection of tools.  Instances of #$MedicalDevice are physical implements or tools which are normally used in the practice of medicine.  These include hand-held tools used by medical professionals, including scalpels, dental tools, stethoscopes.  Other examples of this collection include devices such as a hospital beds, casts, slings, x-ray devices, etc.")
(comment HairTrigger "The collection of all triggers (often on firearms) that are set off with relatively small amount of force, relative to the amount of force the agent that sets it off normally expends.")
(comment accountSystemOnNetwork "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$AccountSystem to instances of #$ComputerNetwork.  (#$accountSystemOnNetwork SYSTEM NETWORK) means that SYSTEM is an instance of #$AccountSystem such that either (#$nodeInSystem SYSTEM NETWORK) holds or (#$subNetwork NETWORK SYSTEM) holds.")
(comment ViviparousAnimal "A specialization of #$Animal.  Each instance of #$ViviparousAnimal is an animal which is born from its mother's body.  Cf. #$OviparousAnimal.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterA "The capital letter 'A'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$A-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterA.")
(comment CardboardCanister "A cardboard canister used to package consumer products.  It's what Quaker Oats is packaged in.")
(disjointWith Fight-Physical Torture)
(comment NetworkHub "A kind of #$ComputerHardwareItem.  Instances are portable router devices with multiple network connections supporting high volume network traffic.")
(comment RecoillessLauncher "A collection of #$MissileLaunchers.  Each instance of #$RecoillessLauncher 
is intended to launch #$Missiles without recoil.")
(comment Inhaling "A specialization of both #$PassingThroughPortal and #$BiologicalIntakeEvent.  Each instance of #$Inhaling is a bodily event in which an animal takes air in through an appropriate portal (e.g., its mouth or nose) and passes it into its lungs.  Each instance of #$Breathing (q.v.) has an instance of #$Inhaling as a sub-event.")
(comment TableLamp "The collection for lamps that sit on top of a desk or table or counter-top")
(comment CommonPeronealNerve "The collection of all common peroneal nerves.  The common peroneal nerve is formed by #$VentralRamusL4, #$VentralRamusL5, #$VentralRamusS1 and #$VentralRamusS2.  It descends until just above the knee as part of the #$SciaticNerve.  The two major branches of the common peroneal nerve are the #$DeepPeronealNerve and the #$SuperficialPeronealNerve.")
(comment GyroSandwich "The collection of all gyro sandwiches, the default variety of which includes spit-roasted lamb meat, onions, and cucumber sauce on a #$PitaBread.")
(comment Stegosaurus "a type of dinosaur with a spiked tail and a series of plates running down its spine.")
(comment Megabyte "An instance of #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity.  When applied to a number or pair of numbers, #$Megabyte returns an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity as its value.  For example, (#$Megabyte 2) is a memory capacity of two megabytes.")
(comment Directory-ReferenceWork "The collection of all directory #$ReferenceWorks.")
(comment Metamorphosis-Insect "The extended event during which a larval insect changes to the adult form of its species.")
(disjointWith GraspingImplement Spoon)
(comment DatePalm "Individual date palm trees.")
(comment WestGermanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$WestGermany, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment MailingTube "The collection of mailing tubes.

These are cardboard tubes used for mailing things.")
(comment Spore-DormantBacterium "The collection of bacterial spores. An

instance of #$Spore-DormantBacterium is the product of sporulation - when

in a hostile environment, some bacteria, see #$SporeFormingBacterium,

become dormant in order to survive. #$Spore-DormantBacteriums are well

resistant to heat, chemicals and radiation. In certain conditions, they may

last for years. Spores can germinate into a single new vegetative cell, see

#$BacterialSporeGermination, when environment is favorable. Do not confuse

bacterial spores with spores of certain plants or fungi, for these later

see #$Spore-PlantLifeStage.")
(comment Tent "A portable shelter made of canvas, cloth, etc. stretched over poles.")
(comment resultGenlArg "A #$MetaFunction predicate that holds of certain #$CollectionRelatingFunctions with respect to certain argument-places.  (#$resultGenlArg FUNC N) means that FUNC always returns a subcollection of its own corresponding Nth-place argument, and that FUNC is \"#$genls preserving\" in that argument-place.  More precisely: (i) the value of FUNC for any sequence of arguments for which it is defined is a subcollection of the Nth item in that sequence (i.e. (#$genls (FUNC ARG1..ARGN..) ARGN)) and (ii) (#$preservesGenlsInArg FUNC N) holds.  For example, (#$resultGenlArg #$JuvenileFn 1) entails (#$genls (#$JuvenileFn #$Dog) #$Dog) and -- given that (#$genls #$Dog #$Mammal) --   (#$genls (#$JuvenileFn #$Dog) (#$JuvenileFn #$Mammal)).  See also #$resultIsaArg and #$resultGenl.")
(comment PerformingADanceMotion "Performing a dance motion, any of many different bodily movements that, taken together, make up a dance.")
(disjointWith GrillingFood BoilingFood)
(comment controllingSuborganizations "(#$controllingSuborganizations ORG SUBORG) means that SUBORG is a #$subOrganizations of ORG which has controlling power over ORG.  For example, (#$controllingSuborganizations #$RomanCatholicChurch #$HolySee).  This is not a #$FunctionalPredicate since an organization may have a hierarchy of controlling suborganizations, e.g. a #$CommunistParty may have a CentralCommittee as a #$controllingSuborganizations, and both the central committee and the party  may have a Politburo as a #$controllingSuborganizations.  Other examples would be a corporate #$BoardOfDirectors or the cabinet in a #$ParliamentaryGovernment.")
(disjointWith BicycleLight TrafficLight)
(comment IRCServerProgram "#$IRCServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the IRC protocol. IRC allows internet users to have a \"conversation\" by typing messages back and forth. This conversation may involve any number of users.  The server forms the backbone of IRC, providing a point to which clients may connect to to talk to each other, and a point for other servers to connect to, forming an IRC network.  The only network

configuration allowed for IRC servers is that of a spanning tree.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup EventOrganizer-Organization)
(comment Flagpole "A device which is used to fly a flag from, often with a loop at the top which is used to help pull the flag to the top.")
(disjointWith IBTGeneration Mounting-Installing)
(comment ExternalOrgan "#$ExternalOrgan is a specialization of #$Organ and #$ExternalAnatomicalPart.  Each instance of #$ExternalOrgan is an organ that is an external anatomical part; e.g., a nose or eye.")
(comment FifthMetaCarpal "The #$FifthMetaCarpal is a bone of the #$Hand which is connected to the #$LittleFinger.")
(comment sexualPosition "This predicate is used to represent what sexual positions are used in instances of #$SexualCopulation.  (#$sexualPosition SEX

 POSITION) means that some instance of the collection #$SexualPositionType POSITION is used sometime during the instance of #$SexualCopulation SEX.")
(comment NuclearPoweredDevice "A specialization of #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$NuclearPoweredDevice is a device which uses nuclear fission or fusion reactions as a source of its power.  Specializations of #$NuclearPoweredDevice include #$NuclearSubmarine and #$NuclearAircraftCarrier.")
(comment PlantPart "A specialization of #$PlantBLO and #$OrganismPart.  Each instance of this collection is a physical part of some #$Plant.  An important specialization of this collection is #$BotanicalOrgan; but #$PlantPart also includes many smaller plant parts which display a similar level of organization -- they have vascular tissue, ground tissue, and an epidermis -- but are not included in the traditional understanding of a #$BotanicalOrgan (i.e. leaves, stems, roots and flowers). See also #$PlantPartType.")
(comment EMailMessage "A subcollection of #$ComputerAIS, #$EMailMessage is the collection of all email message information structures.  They are generally composed of  several parts: an instance of #$EMailMessageText, a header containing instances of #$EMailAddress that correspond to the sender and recipient of the message, and  sometimes instances of #$ComputerFile-AIS which are attached (see #$attachedToEMail).")
(comment IceSkating "The act of moving along by sliding on the blades of ice-skates.")
(comment AilmentCondition "The most general collection of ailment events; a subcollection of both #$PhysiologicalCondition and #$DysfunctionalCondition.  An instance of #$AilmentCondition is a dynamic state of sickness, injury, or physiological impairment.  The rationale for construing ailments in this way is the obvious fact that to have an ailment is to undergo an event: an individual ailment has temporal features, it progresses dynamically, and so on.  It is not just a matter of being in some static state of \"unwellness\".  Subcollections of #$AilmentCondition include #$RespiratoryAilment, #$HeartCondition, #$Cancer, #$MotionSickness, #$Poisoning, #$Infection, and #$InjuryCondition.  If a particular person has an infection, that event is an instance of #$AilmentCondition.  An #$AilmentCondition does not begin before there is an actual, developed sickness or impairment, and thus does not include the event of getting sick or becoming impaired.  Also note that each type of ailment, such as #$Infection, is the collection of all \"cases\" or \"instances\" of individuals suffering from that condition.  See also #$DiseaseType.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment Toe "Digits of the foot")
(comment AustralianCattleDog "A collection of medium-sized dogs.  They make good working dogs.")
(comment KoreanPerson "These are the people who live in or are from Korea (either north or south).")
(comment TravelOrganization "Each instance of #$TravelOrganization is an #$Organization that is primarily or significantly engaged in the travel industry (a broader concept than #$TouristIndustry) or whose activities focus on that industry.  Many instances of #$Organization are instances of both #$TravelOrganization and #$TransportationOrganization (e.g., #$UnitedAirlines).")
(comment PrisonCell "The collection of all containers designed to hold imprisoned human felons (#$Prisoner-Felons).")
(comment Gracilis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Gracilis #$Muscle.  The #$Gracilis adducts the #$Femur at the #$Hip.  It also assists flexion and medial rotation of the #$Knee.")
(comment LightFixture "Light fixtures are lights that are permanently attached as parts of rooms or buildings. e.g. Flourescent light fixtures in office building ceilings.")
(comment VertebralVein "The collection of all verebral #$Veins.  The paired right and left #$VertebralVeins drain the #$CervicalVertebrae and the #$SpinalCord.  The proximal end of the vertebral vein connects to the #$BrachioCephalicVein.")
(comment ChocolateCandy "An instance of #$Collection and a subset of #$Candy. Each instance of #$ChocolateCandy is a piece of candy containing chocolate as its main ingredient.")
(comment Bakery "Organizations which manufacture baked goods.  Not the organization that sells baked goods retail.  (See #$BakeryStore)")
(comment SourceCodeFn "#$SourceCodeFn is a collection denoting function.   (#$SourceCodeFn PROGRAM) denotes the collection of source codes that could be source code for PROGRAM (i.e. #$programCode).")
(comment ChewingGum "A gummy substance intended to be chewed but not swallowed.  Has sweetener and flavorings, which are released as the chewer chews.")
(comment Goring "The action in which a horned animal thrusts its horn(s) into another animal, thereby injuring it.")
(comment ProtectingSomething "A subset of #$TakingCareOfSomething. Each element of #$ProtectingSomething is a purposeful action in which an agent either acts to protect some other agent from threats to its well-being, or acts to protect some object from threats to its good condition. Examples include a military unit protecting some other unit from enemy attacks, or a person protecting a precious object from destruction.")
(disjointWith SportsEquipment PlumbingFixture)
(comment BurkinaFasoPerson "A person who is a citizen of #$BurkinaFaso, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Jack-LiftingDevice "a device used to lift and support heavy objects, like a car")
(comment Kicking "Powerful swinging of a leg, usually to hit something with the leg or foot.")
(comment groupPermissions "(#$groupPermissions COPY PERM) means that someone logged into a machine under a #$ComputerAccount which the machine recognizes as a member of the #$groupAccountForFile of COPY has all the rights and privileges associated with PERM.")
(comment MP3File "MP3 stands for MPEG 1 layer 3, a way to store music files using a relatively small amount of storage space (about 1MB per minute) with an almost CD quality. Thousands of recordings are downloadable from the internet in this format. See also #$MP3FileCopy.")
(comment Microfiche "The collection of all pieces of microfiche.  A Microfiche is a rectangular piece of film media with frames arranged in columns and rows.  See also Microfilm.")
(comment BassBeer "A brand of #$AleBeer popular in Britain (i.e., #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland).")
(comment ExperiencingPerception "A collection of events that are related to perception.  We can think of instances of this collection as the mental component of perceptual events, (see #$Perceiving).  For instance, if one sees an apple, then there is a physical component to this event, i.e. the apple being in place, the light reflecting from it and into the eyes, etc.  However, the aspect of perceiving an apple that is an instance of #$ExperiencingPerception is the apple-like images that appear, so to speak, in one's mind as a result of the perception event.  We might note that while apples are necessary components in perceiving apples, they are not necessary components in having apple-like mental experiences.  This points out a possible gulf that is the source of much discussion in philosophy and cognitive science, i.e. the possible gulf between the real world and the world as it is experienced.")
(comment TrigeminalNerve "The collection of all trigeminal #$Nerves.  The #$TrigeminalNerve is the fifth #$CranialNerve.  Each member of the pair branches into an #$OphthalmicNerve, a #$MaxillaryNerve and a #$MandibularNerve.")
(comment LunchMeat "Meat that is typically sold at deli counters and/or eaten on sandwiches.")
(comment hasTaxLiabilityForYear "`(#$hasTaxLiabilityForYear PERSON YEAR)' means that PERSON incurred
liability for federal income tax during YEAR. This means only
that PERSON had enough taxable income for some of it to be owed, it doesn't
mean that PERSON currently owes any money in taxes. For example, it tax
was withheld, PERSON may in fact be owed money in refund for YEAR even though
(hasTaxLiabilityForYear PERSON YEAR) is true.")
(comment MobileSculpture "The collection of sculptures suspended in midair whose delicately balanced parts can be set in motion by air currents.")
(disjointWith BiologicalEvent Baking-Hardening)
(disjointWith HardcopyInformationBearingObject ComputationalSystem)
(comment HuntingKnife "A large pointed knife typically used in hunting or fishing.")
(comment FlightlessBird "#$FlightlessBird is the collection of #$Birds that can't fly.  Notable specializations include #$Penguin and #$Emu.")
(comment ShippingAndReceivingForm "The collection of forms used to notify the agents involved about the state/progress of a shipping/receiving event.")
(comment Nipple-AnimalBodyPart "The protuberance of a mammary gland upon which the ducts open and from which milk is drawn")
(disjointWith MeasuringDevice Implant-Medical)
(comment SingaporePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Singapore, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith Restaurant-Organization EmploymentOrganization)
(comment BabyWalker "The collection of all baby walkers.  A #$BabyWalker is a device with wheels in which a #$HumanToddler sits/stands and uses his or her legs to move around.")
(comment AnkylosingSpondylitis "A collection of instances of a degenerative disease of the spine seen chiefly in adolescent boys and young men.  It is characterized by stiffness, limitation of movement, swollen joints, joint fusion and anemia. Treatment, and some symptoms, are similar to that of #$RheumatoidArthritis.")
(comment MowingGrass "The collection of grass cutting events involving a lawn mower.  Because #$MowingGrass has genls #$CuttingSomething, the #$objectActedOn is not the Lawn, but the #$GrassTurf which is one of the #$physicalParts of a #$Lawn.")
(disjointWith AccessingAnIBT ChangeInUserRights)
(comment Perineum "This is the collection of perineums, that area of body extending from the

in front of the anus to the fourchette in the female and to the scrotum in

the male. This collection includes the perineums of any animal that has 

such.")
(comment EdibleIron "The kind of iron that everyone should consume a small amount of as part of their diet.")
(comment extensionOfTheory "(#$extensionOfTheory THEORY EXT) means that EXT is a #$ScientificTheory which extends THEORY in the sense that the deductive

closure of EXT contains that of THEORY.")
(comment Tambourine "small hand held drum with metal disks in the sides")
(comment Supplies "The collection of food, clothes, and other materials that are stored for later use.")
(comment deviceTypeUsesWaveType "(#$deviceTypeUsesWaveType DEV WAV) means that DEV is a specialization of #$ElectronicDevice whose members use a #$WavePropagationType WAV in order to perform their function.  For example, #$RadioTelescopes use #$RadioWaves to transmit or receive signals from great distances.  #$CitizenBandRadios use more specific radio wave frequencies, e.g CitizenBandRadioWave.")
(comment OghamicLetter "characters used by ancient Celts in the British Isles")
(comment MakeupBase "A flesh-colored cosmetic used as the base makeup.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent SimpleWholeBodyMovement)
(comment PetroleumBasedProduct "The collection of #$PartiallyTangibleProducts that are derived wholly or principally from #$Petroleum-CrudeOil.  This includes crude oil itself, #$PetroleumProducts derived from components of crude oil through #$Refining, and #$Petrochemicals manufactured from refined petroleum products through some chemical alterations.")
(comment Treadmill "A collection of equipment. Each #$Treadmill is a device with a wide belt mounted on rollers. The user walks or runs on the belt, which moves under the user's feet while the user stays in more or less the same place. A #$Treadmill is used for exercise or medical evaluation.")
(comment Saccharin "Saccharin, a sweetening agent used in soft drinks and other prepared foods.")
(comment MandibularNerve "The collection of all mandibular nerves.  The mandibular nerve is a branch of the #$TrigeminalNerve.  It serves the lower teeth, the temporal scalp, the skin of the chin and the anterior tongue muscles.")
(comment Cymbal "metal disk that is struck with a stick or with another
cymbal ")
(comment GingerOrder "An order of plants within the monocot subclass.")
(comment TonganPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Tonga, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Voodoo-GraphicsAccelerator "A popular brand of graphics accelerator boards, manufactured by 3Dfx Corporation.")
(comment King-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of 'King.'")
(comment AndeanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages composing the Araucanian, Aymara, and Quechua sub-groups")
(comment PepperShaker "A container for storing and dispensing pepper")
(disjointWith RemovingSomething EnteringAComputerPassword)
(comment WebPortal "Usually used as a marketing term to describe a web site that is or is intended to be the first place people see when using the #$Internet. Typically a #$WebPortal has a catalog of #$WorldWideWebSites, a #$SearchEngine, or both. A #$WebPortal may also be a #$EMailServiceProvider-WebBased and offer other services to entice people to use that site as their main 'point of entry' (hence 'portal') to the #$Internet.  Some major general portals include Yahoo, Excite, Netscape, Lycos, CNET, Microsoft Network, and America Online's AOL.com.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam Carpool)
(comment BathroomRug "The collection of throw rugs intended to be used in bathrooms.  They are typically backed with rubber to be skid-resistant.")
(comment Fetus "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart and #$SolidTangibleThing, and an instance of #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType. Each instance of this collection is a #$BiologicalLivingObject resident in a pregnant #$Mammal which, after the separation of the #$AmnioticSac, will develop into a mammalian baby.  By contrast, the term #$Embryo means all tissue that has decended from the fertilized #$Ovum, including the fetal part of the #$Placenta (#$Placenta-FetalPortion), the #$AmnioticSac, and the #$UmbilicalCord, as well as the #$Fetus. (Thus note that a #$Fetus is an #$AnimalBodyPart not because it is a body-part of its mother, but because it is a body-part of its #$Embryo.)")
(comment EnarthrodialJoint "An #$EnarthrodialJoint is a #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart in which the bones are #$rotationallyConnectedTo each other to form a #$BallAndSocketJoint.")
(disjointWith LegMovement HandAndWristMovement)
(comment mother "An instance of #$FamilyRelationSlot and a specialization of #$coreRelatives.  (#$mother CHILD MOTHER) means that MOTHER is a female  animal (there might be more than one) that fills the role of mother for CHILD. In the case of humans, MOTHER might be CHILD's biological mother, adoptive  mother, stepmother, or foster mother.  But note that being a person's  #$biologicalMother (q.v.) is neither necessary nor sufficient for being  his/her mother in the present sense.  In the case of nonhuman animals (see #$NonPersonAnimal), however, #$mother holds between two given creatures  if and only if #$biologicalMother does.")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice Ball)
(disjointWith Ingesting SpreadingOntoSurface)
(comment Vagina "The passage which leads from the outer sex organs of female animals to the uterus")
(comment InsecureDataStorageFault "A program has an #$InsecureDataStorageFault if it stores (saves to memory, caches, allows querying of) information in an insecure way. For insecure data that is in a SQL database, see the more specific #$InsecureSQLDataStorageFault.")
(comment ArgentinePerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens, or participants in the #$NationalCulture, of #$Argentina.")
(disjointWith AgricultureOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment SuperiorLingularSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all superior lingular segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of left #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a left #$SuperiorLobeOfLung, that supplies air to a #$SuperiorLingularSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung in the #$SuperiorLobeOfLung. It branches from the #$LingularBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.  (These segments and bronchi do not exist in right #$Lungs.)")
(comment SprayPaint "Paint propelled out from aerosol cans; used in Graffiti ")
(disjointWith AutoMaintenance TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment Placenta-FetalPortion "The collection of the fetal portion of all #$Placentas.  Members of this collection are #$ExternalOrgans which form where an #$Embryo becomes attached to a maternal #$Uterus.  Each member of this collection is attached to the fetus of which it is an #$ExternalOrgan by an #$UmbilicalCord.")
(comment TomatoBasedSauce "Generic tomato-based sauces.")
(comment PhotoEquipmentStore "stores which sell photography equipment (cameras, lenses, tripods, etc.) and sometimes supplies such as film, photographic paper, etc.")
(comment cardinalityAtMost "(#$cardinalityAtMost SET N) means that SET contains at most N
elements. Example (#$cardinalityAtMost (#$SubcollectionWithAttributeFn
#$Cat #$BlackColor) 3) iff there are at most 3 black cats.")
(comment FreeThing "The collection of all #$TemporalThings that are available at no cost.")
(comment IntravenousDripBag "Plastic bags containing fluids which are to be transfused into an organism.")
(disjointWith ChangingDeviceState StrictlyMentalEvent)
(comment LatinSmallLetterA "The lowercase letter 'a'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$A-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterA.")
(comment VehicleTransmission "The automobile part that transmits the power from the engine to the axle.")
(disjointWith Execution-Judicial Fight-Physical)
(comment TransportHelicopter "The collection of #$Helicopters used for transporting people,
rather than cargo.")
(disjointWith DeciduousPlant EvergreenPlant)
(comment ElectronicHouseholdAppliance "A collection of electronic devices which are also household appliances.  An instance of #$ElectronicHouseholdAppliance is a #$HouseholdAppliance which is electrically powered and controlled.  Common instances of #$ElectronicHouseholdAppliance belong to the subsets #$HomeVideoGameMachine, #$TelevisionSet, #$AnsweringMachine, #$Telephone, #$LaserDiscPlayer, etc.")
(comment OphthalmicNerve "The collection of all opthalmic #$Nerves.  An #$OphthalmicNerve is a branch of a #$TrigeminalNerve.  It #$innervates the anterior #$Scalp, the #$UpperEyelid and the #$Nose.")
(comment Pasta "The #$ItalianCuisine foodstuff made from #$FlourOrMeal that is boiled (as in #$SpaghettiNoodle) or baked (as in #$LasagnaNoodle). Pasta is the generic term for #$ItalianCuisine food of this nature, and is thus the collection of all forms and instances of #$SpaghettiNoodle, #$LasagnaNoodle, etc.")
(disjointWith PhysicalTransformationEvent ComputerProcessRunning)
(comment Travelogue "A non-fictional narrative describing travel to one or more locations.  This may be in lecture, movie, or written format.")
(comment Capillary "The collection of all capillaries.  An individual #$Capillary is a small, thin-walled #$BloodVessel in which gases, nutrients, and/or waste products are exchanged between the #$Blood and surrounding body tissues.  There are four types of #$Capillary:  a #$SystemicCapillary releases #$Oxygen to body tissue while absorbing #$CarbonDioxide and waste products into the #$Blood; a #$PulmonaryCapillary releases #$CarbonDioxide into a #$Lung, while taking up #$Oxygen; an #$IntestinalCapillary accepts nutrients into the #$Blood while also exchanging #$Oxygen and #$CarbonDioxide with intestinal tissue; and a #$HepaticCapillary releases waste products into the #$Liver.")
(disjointWith Knife GraspingImplement)
(comment PalmTree "Individual Palm trees.")
(comment GrenadaPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Grenada, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment ShippingEnvelope "The collection of shipping envelopes.

These are large envelopes, generally a little larger than an 8 1/2 by

11 sheet of paper, though some are even larger. They are used for

flatish rectangular objects such as booklets, stacks of paper, etc.")
(comment EmbryoFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance LIFETYPE of #$OrganismClassificationType (q.v.), #$EmbryoFn returns the collection of organisms which are embryonic instances of LIFETYPE.  For instance, (#$EmbryoFn #$Dog) is the collection of all embryonic instances of #$Dog.")
(comment TypicalArgTypePredicate "Instances of this collection are #$MetaPredicates that
specify the expected identity of the #$isa or #$genls of one argument
(the dependent argument) of a predicate. These predicates do not
contribute to wff-checking, and so should never be used in place of
#$ArgTypePredicates.")
(comment Pedaling "Pedaling once on each pedal. A physical activity in which legs are pumped in a circular motion as if driving a crankshaft.  Pedaling consists of #$LiftingALeg and #$PushingAnObject, one time with each leg.  Normal pedaling events consist of lots of #$Pedaling sub-events. This unit was broken down to this degree of granularity so that we could more easily talk about the #$anatomicalResourceRequired, namely, 2 legs and 2 feet.")
(disjointWith GrillingFood Frying)
(comment Leader "A collection of persons.  Each instance of #$Leader is a person who heads an instance of #$Organization.  Typically, a leader of an organization makes major decisions on behalf of the whole organization, has the authority to direct the organization's personnel to carry out those decisions, and is empowered to engage or negotiate with external agents to achieve the organization's goals.  This collection includes leaders of sub-organizations of larger organizations, such as department heads within larger organizations.  Note that a single person may be a leader in more than one organization.  See also the predicates #$hasLeaders and #$seniorExecutives, and the collection #$Manager.")
(disjointWith Trailer HorseCarriage)
(comment AppleControlPanel "The program that starts the Apple control panel which itself is an interface to utilities that are used to customize features (like color and sound) on a Macintosh computer.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup TradeAssociation)
(comment SlideTheRecreationalDevice "The collection of all sliding boards, sliding tubes, and similar recreational devices.  We may want to add some specializations of this later.  The prototypical example is the standard playground sliding board.")
(comment Zebra "The collection of all zebras; a subset of #$EquineAnimal.  These black-and-white striped relatives of horses are native to the #$ContinentOfAfrica.  Zebras are almost impossible to tame, therefore by default they are elements of #$WildAnimal, although a few have been successfully domesticated and harnessed.")
(comment TextualMaterial "A specialization of #$InformationBearingThing (IBT).  Each instance of  #$TextualMaterial is an IBT a significant part of whose informational  content is both (i) encoded in some #$CommunicationConvention (q.v.),  usually a #$Language, and (ii) represented or displayed in a spatial  format.  Examples include a copy of a newspaper printed in English using  the Roman alphabet, a copy of a book printed in English using Braille,  and a poster written in Chinese characters.  Condition (i) excludes things like hardcopies of drawings, while condition (ii) excludes things like  magnetic tapes containing recorded speech.  A piece of textual material  always involves one or more spatially-localized representations -- usually  physical inscriptions (see #$CharacterStringToken-Inscribed) -- of  #$CharacterStrings (q.v.).  Textual materials are usually tangible objects  (such as the examples given above), but are sometimes intangibles like  patterns of light projecting words onto walls or screens.  Specializations  of #$TextualMaterial include #$OfficialDocument and #$NonPublishedText.  Note that, while there is considerable overlap between #$TextualMaterial  and #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject, these collections differ in that  the latter both includes IBTs that involve no character-string representations and excludes intangibles of any sort.")
(disjointWith Lip-AnimalBodyPart Skin)
(comment HeadOfBone "A #$HeadOfBone is a #$BoneSubPart at one end of a #$LongBone or #$Rib-AnimalBodyPart made of denser #$BoneTheStuff and labled by the 'head' of the bone.")
(comment Knife "A long thin piece of metal, plastic, bone, or stone, useful for cutting.")
(comment environmentHostileToOrganism "(#$environmentHostileToOrganism
BLO ENVIRON) means that the #$Place ENVIRON is such that the
#$BiologicalLivingObject BLO may need to undergo some
#$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent, or else it may result in debilitating the
#$BiologicalLivingObject or causing a #$PhysicalTransformationEvent.")
(comment ComputerDocumentFile "This is the collection of all files of #$TextualMaterial.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement MakingFacialExpression)
(comment Thumb "A specialized finger opposed to the other fingers of the hand which allows the hand to grasp objects")
(comment AustralianShepherd "A collection of medium-sized dogs with thick coats.  Also called the Aussie.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment ItalianCar "The collection of cars that are made in #$Italy.")
(comment ScalenusPosterior "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ScalenusPosterior #$Muscle. The #$ScalenusPosterior raises the #$FirstRib and #$SecondRib during forced inspiration when acting bilaterally.  It also is used bilaterally or unilaterally to assist flexion of the #$Neck-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment CorkBoard "A rectangular sheet of pressed cork wood, usually framed and supported by a stand or hung on a wall, for holding messages.  Popular in business/corporate offices and school rooms.")
(comment DuralSinus "The collection of all dural sinuses.  The dural sinuses are large venous #$BloodVessels within the #$Skull which drain the cerebral #$Veins.  A #$DuralSinus is not a normal #$Vein in that it has a different structure, is not necessarily of circular cross-section, may have a greater cross-section than a normal #$Vein, and does not have any #$Valve.   The set of the dural sinuses drain to the #$InternalJugularVeins.")
(comment HighTechManufacturingEnterprise "The colleciton of organizations (businesses) that manufacture high tech items.")
(comment TestStrip "Test strips are used in conjunction with diagnostic tests.  They can be made of plastic or paper and usually have some sort of chemical on them which reacts with some bodily fluid. For example, diabetics use test strips to test their blood-sugar levels.")
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice PlumbingFixture)
(comment HoneydewMelonPlant "The collection of individual honeydew melon plants.")
(comment OmanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Oman, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Hose "Flexible tubing usually used to transport liquids.")
(comment SpiderWeb "The collection of webs woven by #$Spiders.")
(comment worldPermissions "(#$worldPermissions COPY PERM) means that someone logged
into a machine under a #$ComputerAccount which the machine recognizes
as a member of the #$worldAccountForFile of COPY has all the rights and
privileges associated with PERM.")
(comment ProjectionDisplayDevice "Devices which display images via projection onto a screen.")
(comment PersonTypeByCulture "A collection of collections.  Each instance of  #$PersonTypeByCulture is the collection of all and only those persons who participate (see #$cultureParticipants) in some particular human culture.  Examples include #$FrenchPerson and #$EthnicGroupOfAustralianAborigines.")
(comment ColorPerception "This is the collection of events in which the color of objects is seen.")
(comment TrochlearNerve "The collection of all trochlear #$Nerves, paired in a #$Vertebrate body.  A #$TrochlearNerve is a fourth #$CranialNerve.  Each member of the pair #$innervates the superior oblique #$Muscle (one of the #$ExtraocularMuscleSet).")
(comment CannedFood "The collection for canned food, processed foodstuff which when bought is typically packaged in a can; e.g., canned fruit, vegetables, soup.")
(comment FullTimeStudent "This is the collection of full-time students.")
(comment adjStrings "(#$adjStrings WORD STRING) states that STRING is one of the adjective strings for the word unit WORD in some microtheory.  In other words, some adjectival #$SpeechPartPredicate is used on WORD to relate it to STRING.  This predicate is

#$notAssertible since it is concluded from the current state of the knowledge base.")
(comment PackageFn "(#$PackageFn PROD-TYPE) denotes a collection of packaged objects of type PROD-TYPE that are sold as products.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess Baking-Hardening)
(disjointWith HardcopyInformationBearingObject CharacterStringToken)
(comment RaceCar "Cars which were specifically designed to be raced in competitions.  This includes dragsters, formula-1 cars, stock cars, sprint cars etc.")
(comment Canary "The collection of small yellow finches native to the Canary Islands.")
(comment GrantProposal "The collection of all documents in which the author requests another agent (typically an organization) to enter into a grant agreement with the author.  The document typically includes a description of the actions which will be financed by the grant, if it is given.  It also includes descriptions of the agents involved in the plan, supporting the proposition that they are caplable of executing the plan.")
(comment Groin "Area of body containing external genitalia")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece MeasuringDevice)
(comment OldWorldPitcherPlant "Common name for any insect-catching plant with pitcher-shaped leaves.")
(comment SlovakiaPerson "The people who are #$citizens of #$Slovakia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup EmploymentOrganization)
(comment Trimmers-NoseHair "Cutting tool used in clipping one's nose hair.")
(comment CankerSore "A collection of #$AilmentConditions in which a small and painful whitish ulcer forms, usually in the mouth or on the lips.  It is possibly caused by a virus that normally lives in the body cells without causing symptoms.  It may be more prevalent in the presence of a disorder, like the common cold, or during menstruation.")
(comment PruningShears "Shears used to prune trees or shrubs")
(disjointWith AutoMaintenance IBTGeneration)
(comment ImmuneSystem "The collection of all animal immune systems considered as instances of #$AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment OrganizationalTransferOut "A specialization of #$OrganizationalTransfer.  Each instance of #$OrganizationalTransferOut is an event in which some agent (an instance of #$IntelligentAgent) loses membership in some organization.  Instances of #$OrganizationalTransferOut would thus include lay-offs, expulsions, and excommunications.  Note that any event in which an agent leaves one organization to join another would be an instance of both #$OrganizationalTransferIn (q.v.) and #$OrganizationalTransferOut.")
(comment historicallyDerivedTheory "(#$historicallyDerivedTheory DER-THORY THEORY) means that DER-THORY is a #$ScientificTheory that is derived from a previous theory, THEORY. This relation is used to keep track of conceptual and historical inheritance, so #$historicallyDerivedTheory is a specialization of #$startsAfterStartingOf. For a relation that records a relation of logical subsumpsion, see #$extensionOfTheory.")
(disjointWith FurnitureStore AutoDealership)
(comment Clarinet "small single-reed instrument ")
(comment InformationRecordingProcess "A specialization of #$IBOCreation. Each instance of this collection is an event in which information is recorded, using an #$InformationRecordingDevice.  Every #$InformationRecordingProcess produces an #$InformationBearingObject. Specializations include #$SavingAFile and #$AudioTapeRecording.")
(comment ChineseCharacter "characters composed of multiple strokes and originally used in writing Chinese languages; called 'kanji' when used in Japanese writing")
(comment Pin "A sharp pointy thing that is not hollow, nor has any holes in it. Smaller than most nails.  May be part of some larger device like Safety Pin or Brooch.")
(disjointWith MakingFacialExpression IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(disjointWith Concrete PetroleumBasedProduct)
(comment HardDisk "This is the collection of all Hard Disks.  These are usually fixed magnetic
    disks which are used for memory storage by a #$HardDiskDrive.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType OrganizationTypeByActivityType)
(comment Forklift "The collection of all vehicles (a.k.a. 'forklift trucks') with prongs in front that can be inserted under a load and raised to lift and transport the load.")
(comment SQLServerProgram "#$SQLServerProgram is a type of #$RelationalDatabaseServerProgram

 which supports queries written in the popular SQL (see #$SQL-Language).")
(comment Umbrella "A mechanical device used for protection against certain elements of nature")
(comment ObturatorNerve "The collection of all obturator #$Nerves.  The #$ObturatorNerve is formed by #$VentralRamusL2, #$VentralRamusL3, and #$VentralRamusL4.  An #$ObturatorNerve separates into anterior and posterior branches.  These branches supply the #$Skin on the medial side of the #$Thigh, the #$HipJoint, the obturator externus muscle (one of the #$RotatorsOfHip), and parts of the #$Knee.")
(comment ThesaurusProgram "This is the set of computer programs that

effectively put a thesaurus on one's computer.")
(comment Scrapbook "The collection for scrapbooks; books with empty pages where           you can stick pictures, newspaper articles, or other things           you want to keep.")
(comment Bill-Birds "The collection of all bills (or 'beaks') belonging to #$Birds.  An individual #$Bill-Birds is a hard structure, which contains the #$Mouth and the #$Nostrils.  For the similar structure of a #$Turtle see #$Beak.")
(comment AngiospermSpecies "Not itself a species, but a set of species encompassing those that are angiosperms.")
(comment IsraeliPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Israel, or participate in its #$NationalCulture..")
(comment Commodore64 "A brand of personal computer popular in the 1980s.")
(comment Nine-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '9.'")
(comment SalishanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally northwestern U.S.")
(comment ShakerDispenser "A container for storing and dispensing powdery stuff")
(disjointWith MakingSomething EnteringAComputerPassword)
(comment SpreadingArmsApart "The collection of all events in which a person spreads apart his or her arms.  This usually signifies magnanimousness, feelings of inclusion, welcoming, etc.")
(comment LegalGovernmentOrganization "#$LegalGovernmentOrganization is a specialization of #$GovernmentalOrganization and #$LegalAgent.  Each instance of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization is an organization which is a part of, and funded by, the government of a geopolitical entity.  Examples include the #$InternalRevenueService, #$UnitedStatesNavy, and #$CityCouncilOfAustin (TX).  Some instances of #$LegalGovernmentOrganizations have legal standing in courts.")
(comment programUsed-Generic "This predicate is an #$ActorSlot (q.v.) that relates computer programs to events in which their copies are used. (#$programUsed-Generic EVENT PROG) means that a copy of PROG is used in EVENT. Compare this predicate to the more specialized #$programUsed (q.v.) -- when EVENT is an instance of #$ComputerActivity (q.v.), use #$programUsed, otherwise use #$programUsed-Generic.")
(disjointWith AlumniOrganization SportsTeam)
(comment DrinkingCan "Cans, often made of aluminum, in which soda, beer, and other potable liquids are contained and sometimes drunk from.")
(comment Wolverine "A collection of mammals, solitary by nature.  Its    scientific name is Gulo gulo.")
(disjointWith Resting-Relaxing BiologicalProductionEvent)
(comment Condyle "A #$Condyle is a rounded attachment on a bone at point of
contact with another bone.  It is used to control articulation of the joint.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice CuttingDevice)
(disjointWith Project TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment AutoMechanicShopMarketCategory "Products that are typically sold at an #$AutoMechanicShop, whether or not you want another service performmed that is associated with the product. i.e., I can buy a fan belt at the local service station garage.")
(comment AwardCertificate "An award certificate-- a paper symbol of an award.")
(comment Anus "Posterior opening of the digestive tract.")
(disjointWith PartOfAnHSC Spacecraft)
(comment Pointer-GermanShorthaired "A collection of medium-sized dogs.")
(comment ArmenianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens, or participants in the #$NationalCulture, of #$Armenia.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup AgricultureOrganization)
(comment MedialBasalSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all medial basal segments of #$InferiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by a #$MedialBasalSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung.  (There is no #$MedialBasalSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung in the left #$Lung.)")
(comment Headphones "The audio devices put very close to the ears to permit personal listening")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity AthleticActivity)
(comment Placenta-MaternalPortion "The collection of the maternal portion of all #$Placentas.  Members of this collection are #$InternalOrgans which form in and attached to the #$Uterus of a pregnant #$Mammal.")
(comment Sauce "The collection of sauces: liquids that aren't eaten by themselves, but only if applied to other foods, as a coating or dip for them.")
(comment PrintShop "A print shop, like Ginny's or Kinko's or QuikCopy - They duplicate documents and provide a bunch of related services (binding, etc.). ")
(comment DiagnosticComputerProgram "#$DiagnosticComputerProgram is a subset of  #$ComputerProgram-CW.  Each individual in the collection #$DiagnosticComputerProgram is a program that is used to monitor computer hardware or software to determine whether it is operating correctly.")
(comment IntravenousEquipmentSet "The set of equipment used to transfuse liquids intravenously. Usually consists of a bag, a tube, and a needle.")
(comment Crucifix-ChristianSymbol "A specialization of #$ArtObject and #$ReligiousSymbol.  Each instance of #$Crucifix-ChristianSymbol is a representational (usually 3-d, carving or sculpture) work of art that depict #$JesusOfNazareth on the #$CrossOfJesus.")
(disjointWith ChangingDeviceState PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment interArgNotReln "(#$interArgNotReln PRED M N RELN) means that a GAF with PRED as its arg0 can only be asserted if the #$BinaryPredicate RELN is known _not_ to hold between the Mth and Nth arguments to PRED in the GAF, with the Mth argument appearing as the first argument of RELN and the Nth argument appearing as the second argument of RELN.")
(comment highwayFuelConsumption "This relation corresponds to the concept of 'highway mileage' which is often specified for road vehicles with internal combustion engines (see #$RoadVehicle-InternalCombustionEngine).  (#$highwayFuelConsumption ROAD-VEHICLE CONSUMPTION-RATE) means that the average rate of fuel consumption by ROAD-VEHICLE while it is being driven on the open highway is CONSUMPTION-RATE.")
(comment SpermCell "A specialization of #$Gamete.  Each instance of #$SpermCell is a specialized gamete cell which is produced by meiosis in the reproductive tract of a male animal.  Each sperm cell usually has half the number of chromosomes that regular body cells do, and when it fertilizes an ovum (see #$Ovum), the ovum becomes a zygote and continues to develop into a mature individual animal.  See also #$MaleAnimal, #$SexualReproductionEvent.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterB "The capital letter 'B'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$B-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterB.")
(comment wearer "This predicate indicates the individual (typically a person, but perhaps an animal or a mannequin) that wears some item of clothing (or some other wearable item) in a particular situation.  (#$wearer WEARING OBJ) means that OBJ is the wearer during WEARING.  To specify the item worn in a situation, use the predicate #$itemWorn.")
(comment ComputerPrinter-ThermalTransfer "The collection of printers that use heating elements (a moving or fixed head) to transfer ink to paper. They are most commonly used to print bar-codes, receipts, etc.")
(comment Cattle-Domestic "This is the collection of all cattle that have been domesticated for meat, milk or labor.  Every instance of this collection is a descendant of some instance of the collection #$Aurochs.  There are many different breeds of domesticated cattle -- see #$Cattle-DomesticatedTypeByBreed.")
(comment ElectricalHouseholdAppliance "Electric-powered Household Appliances")
(comment VentralRamusT6 "The collection of all T6 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT6 and #$DorsalRamusT6 branch from SpinalRootT6.  #$VentralRamusT6 supplies below the #$SixthRib.")
(comment AleBeer "A dark form of #$Beer (contrast with #$LagerBeer) that originated in the British Isles. Real #$AleBeer contains a bitterness derived from malted hops, and is most often served at room-temperature. #$AleBeers are typically red colored, with little or no gas content (e.g., from #$CarbonDioxide).")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity LocomotionEvent-Animal)
(comment Baton-Musical "Long, skinny wand used in musical conducting.")
(comment NonSporeFormingBacterium "A collection, a specialization of #$Bacterium. The collection of bacteria that are not capable of forming spores.")
(comment WhosWho "The collection of all directories [#$Directory-ReferenceWork] giving short biographies [#$Biography] of the significant people in a given field (which can be very narrow or very broad).")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece ControlDevice)
(comment PecanTree "Tree native to temperate North America, yielding tasty nuts.  These nuts have the highest fat content of any vegetable product, and a caloric value close to butter!")
(comment LithuanianPerson "The people who are #$citizens of #$Lithuania, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment importantCompany "'(#$importantCompany ORGANIZATION REGION) means that ORGANIZATION is a major or important company in the territory or area REGION.  This predicate represents an intuitive, fuzzy notion, that of companies with high visibility and importance (in terms of value, assets, market share, etc.).  What is a major or important company today might not be tomorrow and vice versa, so claims involving this predicate should be time indexed (e.g., (#$holdsIn #$AroundTheYear2000 (importantCompany MicrosoftInc (#$TerritoryFn #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica))).")
(comment LetterOpener "The collection of letter openers.

These are knife-life devices, except they are not nearly as

sharp as knives.")
(comment EndosporingEvent "An #$EndosporingEvent is the #$Event in which a #$VegetativeCell becomes a #$Spore-DormantBacterium. Not all bacteria are capable of undegoing this change. An #$EndosporingEvent occurs when bacteria that are capable of this change are in a hostile environment.")
(comment SwivelChair "A chair that swivels, often an office chair")
(disjointWith CerealFood Nutrient)
(comment SocialOrganization "An organization formed by its members around an activity.  The main purpose of the group is to have fun and socialize.")
(disjointWith AutomotiveLight TrafficLight)
(comment AppleComputerProgram "Software products made by Apple Inc.")
(comment FittedBedSheet "The sort of sheet which has sewn-together corners designed to wrap around a mattress.")
(disjointWith Lip-AnimalBodyPart Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment Acromion "The #$Acromion is a #$BoneSubPart of the #$Scapula which articulates with the #$AcromialExtremityOfClavicle.")
(comment NLDefinitenessFn "(#$NLDefinitenessFn TAG TERM) means that TERM appeared in a natural language utterance with the definiteness feature denoted by TAG.  For example, (#$NLDefinitenessFn #$Indefinite-NLAttr #$Dog) would mean that some word meaning #$Dog occurred with an indefinite determiner (\"a\" or \"an\").  This function serves as a hint to the NL subsystems that this term was used with this definiteness, and is only intended to serve as a stand-in until the NL subsystems can determine the correct form of TERM to use in the semantic translation of the utterance.  Note that uses of this can (and frequently should) have as its arg2 another instance of #$NLTaggedTerm.  For instance, \"the cats\" would return from the parser as (#$NLDefinitenessFn #$Definite-NLAttr (#$NLNumberFn #$Plural-NLAttr #$Cat)).")
(comment Turf-Artificial "fake grass.")
(comment InstallingAProgramCopy "#$InstallingAProgramCopy is the collection of all events in which software is installed on an instance of #$ComputationalSystem.")
(disjointWith FingerMovement Hugging)
(comment Thigh "The upper leg between the knee and hip")
(comment AnatolianShepherd "A collection of dogs.")
(comment OceanianPerson "The set of people who live on Islands in the Pacific Ocean; excludes ethnically Asiatic populations such as Japanese, Taiwanesei, but includes Melanesia")
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment Herbalife "an herbal medical product.")
(comment BiologicalSuborder "A specialization of #$BiologicalTaxon.  Each instance of #$BiologicalSuborder is an immediate taxonomic subdivision of some instance of #$BiologicalOrder.  Instances of #$BiologicalSuborder include #$Crocodile and #$Lizard.")
(comment AbductorPollicisLongus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$AbductorPollicisLongus #$Muscle.  The #$AbductorPollicisLongus abducts the #$Thumb in a radial direction.")
(comment Bookcase "A type of furniture used for storing and/or displaying books")
(disjointWith Teaching WeddingEvent-Entire)
(comment PosteriorTibialVein "The collection of all posterior tibial #$Veins.  The #$PosteriorTibialVein connects to the #$PoplitealVein at its proximal end and to the plantar #$Veins at its distal end.")
(comment WhiteRice-Foodstuff "The collection of white rice.")
(comment ManufacturingCompany "A collection of organizations; a subset of #$ManufacturingOrganization.  An element of #$ManufacturingCompany is a manufacturer that is also a company in its own right.  (See #$Business.)  This collection excludes manufacturers which are #$subOrganizations of some larger #$ManufacturingOrganization.")
(comment Elixir "#$Elixir is the collection of all elixirs. An elixer is a sweetened liquid - usually containing alcohol - into which medicine is mixed.")
(comment MaintenanceEvent "An action done in the course of maintaining something.  Typically instances will also be instances of either Cleaning, #$ReplacingAnObject (especially a part), adjusting, or topping off a substance (usually a liquid).")
(disjointWith PartOfBuilding AutoPart)
(comment WatermelonPlant "Individual watermelon plants.")
(comment BurmesePerson "A citizen of #$Burma, or someone who participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PapuanLanguageGrouping "a necessary tho unsystematic indication of some/ sort or sorts of Papuan language")
(comment TransmissionFluid "Lubricant for automobile transmissions")
(comment Artifact-AnimalCreated "A collection of #$Artifacts. Each instance of #$Artifact-AnimalCreated is a tangible thing made by a #$NonPersonAnimal. Examples include #$Dams built by #$Beavers, spiderwebs, birds' nests, #$Termite mounds, and coral reefs.")
(comment argNotIsa "(#$argNotIsa REL N COL) means that nothing given as the Nth argument to the #$Relation REL may be known to be an element of the #$Collection COL.  It is not necessary to prove that it is not an element of that collection.")
(comment readableBy "(#$readableBy FILE ACCT) means that someone logged in under #$ComputerAccount ACCT can read some copy of the #$ComputerFile-Abstract FILE.")
(comment ComputerProgramTypeByFunction "A collection of types of computer programs.  Each instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction is a collection of programs (see #$ComputerProgram-CW) whose instances all serve a similar function and can be used for a similar purpose.  This purpose might be very specific (see e.g. #$AutoLoanCalculatorProgram) or more general (see e.g. #$FinancialProgram).")
(disjointWith MedicalCareOrganization MarketingDepartment)
(comment SolidDeodorant "Solid stick deodorant: the stuff, not a package of the product.")
(comment OculomotorNerve "The collection of all oculomotor #$Nerves.  An #$OculomotorNerve is the third #$CranialNerve.  Each member of the pair serves four of the six #$Muscles in the #$ExtraocularMuscleSet.")
(comment taxableIncomeDuringYear "`(#$taxableIncomeDuringYear PERSON INCOME YEAR)' means that
PERSON's federally taxable income for the year YEAR A.D. was INCOME.")
(comment EntertainmentPerformanceTicket "The collection of all paper tickets entitling a #$Person to attend an #$EntertainmentPerformance.")
(disjointWith LicenseRequiringActivity BiologicalEvent)
(disjointWith CharacterStringToken ComputationalSystem)
(comment RaceCar "The collection of cars made specifically for the purpose of racing, and generally owned and driven only by professional race-car drivers.")
(comment LiposuctionSurgery "#$LiposuctionSurgery is a technique to remove fat cells           from the (human) body using suction.")
(comment Earlobe "Fleshy bottom of the outer ear; people often pierce them")
(comment Bookend "The collection of bookends. A bookend is a device placed at the end of a row of books to keep them from falling over onto their sides. Bookends come in many shapes but the most common is an L shape, where the bottom of the L is placed under the books.")
(comment Saxifrage "The collection of plants belonging to the saxifrage family, mostly perennial herbs, native primarily to northern cold and temperate regions.  Leaves usually alternate along the stem and sometimes form rosettes. Often planted in rock gardens or as border ornamentals.")
(comment EquatorialGuineaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$EquatorialGuinea, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization EmploymentOrganization)
(comment CoaxialCable "#$CoaxialCables have the main conductor inside an

 insulating, grounded outer sheath.  They are very often used for video 

transmission (as for TVs).")
(comment Blepharospasm "A collection of #$AilmentConditions in which one suffers from spasmodic winking from involuntary contraction of the orbicular muscle of the eyelids.")
(comment DentalPick "The collection of all dental picks, the instruments dentists and dental hygienists use to scrape tartar off teeth and to probe loose fillings.  Sigh.")
(disjointWith PunchingSomething IBTGeneration)
(comment LymphaticSystem "The collection of all animal lymphatic systems, considered as anatomical parts of the #$ImmuneSystem.")
(comment OrganizationOfPeopleOnly "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly is an organization each of whose members (see the predicate #$hasMembers) is an instance of #$Person.  Examples of #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly include a human nuclear family, a carpool, or a sports team. Negative examples include #$UnitedNationsOrganization or #$OrganizationOfAmericanStates.")
(comment numRange-GenQuant "This is a macro-predicate which can be used to represent the

meaning of English sentences such as `two or three cats live in

my house' in NL parsing. (#$numRange-GenQuant COL1 COL2 N M) means

that there are between N and M elements of COL1 which are also

elements of COL2. N and M must be different integers, and M is

greater than N. This constant doesn't replace num-GenQuant or

any other more specific GeneralizedQuantifier. Its primary use

is as an intermediate target for parsing: not for general

KE/OE.")
(comment fileCopyContainsVirusCopy "(fileCopyContainsVirusCopy FILECOPY VIRUSCOPY) means that an instance of #$ComputerVirusCopy, VIRUSCOPY, is contained in the #$ComputerFileCopy FILECOPY.  More precisely, it means that the #$ComputerCode of VIRUSCOPY is one of the #$subInfoStructures of the #$ComputerFile-AIS of FILECOPY.")
(disjointWith ServiceOrganization StockExchange)
(comment Harpsichord "Instances are instances of #$MusicalInstrument-Acoustic and #$Keyboard-MusicalInstrument.  All instances share the characteristic feature that depressing a key will entrain a mechanical process that results in the plucking of a taut string, causing a vibration which is audible as a musical tone.  Thus, instances are also considered instances of #$StringInstrument.  The process is similar to that used in instances of #$Piano-Acoustic, with the signal difference that in instances of #$Piano-Acoustic the string is hammered, not plucked.")
(comment infectionTypeHasVectorType "(#$infectionTypeHasVectorType ORG-TYPE INFECTION-TYPE) relates an #$InfectionType INFECTION-TYPE to the type of #$Organism-Whole that can serve as its vector.  The vector is usually (but not always) an #$Arthropod that transfers an #$Infection from one host to another.  For example, fleas are the #$infectionTypeHasVectorType of the #$BubonicPlague.  Human infection occurs when an infected flea bites a human and regurgitates #$Plague-Bacterium into the bite wound. See #$InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmission and related predicates.")
(disjointWith Communicating Holiday)
(comment HouseholdAttachment "More or less built-in stuff like washbasins,  closets, on the wall coat hangers etc. that one finds in houses or other buildings.")
(comment CarryStrap "A strap of some material attached to an object, and used for grasping and carrying the object.")
(comment MkhedruliLetter "the script commonly used at present in printing; a slightly modified cursive form for hand-writing also exists")
(comment SafetySeatBelt "Seat belts used in airplanes, cars and other transportation vehicles, to secure one in their seat, as a safety measure. The seat belts on infant seats, baby strollers, etc., are included in this unit. ")
(disjointWith MakingFacialExpression Conveying-Generic)
(comment objectTypeUsed "(#$objectTypeUsed EVT OBJTYPE) says that some instance(s) of OBJTYPE were used during EVT, where OBJTYPE is an instance of  #$ExistingObjectType.  This is a \"sibling\" predicate of  #$stuffTypeUsed.")
(disjointWith PhotographicFilm BuildingMaterial)
(comment HardwareBusInternal "The collection of all computer hardware buses that connect components that are internal to the computer in such a way that the function of the computer depends on it. This includes the memory subsystem or I/O ports, but not necessarily the disk drives.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByActivityType PhysiologicalConditionType)
(comment Pager "The collection of small sized telecommunications devices that operate over the telephone line but only receive text messages. Such messages are displayed on a small screen on the device itself.")
(comment posOfPhrase "(#$posOfPhrase PHRASE POS) indicates that the syntactic category of PHRASE is POS. For example, for any #$NounPhrase NP, it is true that (#$posOfPhrase NP #$Noun).")
(comment UmbrellaUsedAsCovering "A subAbstractionType of umbrella, being used as a covering to protect the user against elements of nature")
(comment DorsalRamusT2 "The collection of all T2 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT2 and DorsalRamiT2 branch from SpinalRootT2.  DorsalRamiT2 sometimes supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment FumeBlanc-Wine "The collection of all instances of

Fume Blanc wine.")
(comment Freeware "This collection includes all instances of Freeware, software which is available free of charge.")
(comment BayWindow "Bay windows are large windows projecting outward from a     building, creating an alcove within. They are a common feature of     Victorian houses.")
(comment Photocopy "The collection of copies of documents produced by a photographic process, such as xerography.")
(comment MotorNerve "The collection of all solely motor #$Nerves.  Each #$MotorNerve is a #$Nerve that #$innervates a #$Muscle by signalling for it to contract or relax.  A #$Nerve containing both motor and sensory #$Neurons is a #$SensoryMotorNerve.")
(comment MonoeciousPlantSpecies "The collection of #$BiologicalSpecies of monoecious #$Plants (plant species in which one plant has both male and female reproductive organs, e.g., stamen and pistil, but in widely separated structures on the plant).  Compare #$HermaphroditicPlantSpecies and #$DioeciousPlantSpecies.")
(comment Melilla-EnclavePerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Melilla-Enclave, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Dreamcast-GameSystem "A video game system manufactured by Sega.")
(comment Nineteen-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '19.'")
(comment HokanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages mostly of the West")
(comment Buckle-Fastener "A buckle is attached to one end and holds the other end by a catch.")
(disjointWith EnteringAComputerPassword PuttingSomethingSomewhere)
(comment subOrgs-Temporary "(#$subOrgs-Temporary SUPER SUB) means that SUB is a subordinate organization to SUPER in an organizational hierarchy only for the time being, and the relationship is supposed to end prior to the dissolution of either organization.  This relation could be established in the course of a particular major undertaking, enterprise or campaign, but it is not likely to persist beyond the end of it.  For example, in the military a particular battalion might be attached to a particular brigade to provide logistical support during a military campaign: this relationship would be a subOrgs-Temporary relation if it is expected to end in the reasonably near future or at the end of the campaign.  (See also #$subOrgs-Permanent and

#$subOrgs-OnlyDuringOperation.)")
(disjointWith SportsTeam PersonFocusGroup)
(comment SolarReflector "The collection of all solar reflectors: mirrored devices for reflecting and focusing sunlight")
(comment Organ "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$Organ is a part of an animal that has a specialized physiological function  and is more or less localized within the animal.  Examples include hearts, kidneys, and tongues.  Specializations include #$InternalOrgan and #$ExternalOrgan.  Note that, in most contexts, a distributed system like a #$NervousSystem or a (#$SkinOnFn #$WholeBody) is not an #$Organ.")
(comment inferiorTo-Spatial "(#$inferiorTo-Spatial OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 lies in the #$InferiorDirection of OBJ-2, when viewed in the frame of reference of the object with #$AnimalBodyShape (often, a #$Person) that they are located in.  In a #$Person, #$inferiorTo-Spatial almost always corresponds to #$caudalTo, but in a #$Dog or other four-legged animal, #$inferiorTo-Spatial usually corresponds to #$ventralTo.  Note that if OBJ-1 is #$inferiorTo-Spatial OBJ-2, OBJ-2 is superior to OBJ-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `superior to'.  OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.")
(comment CuttingDevice "A specialization of #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$CuttingDevice is a device whose #$primaryFunction is to (enable its user to) cut another object.  Specializations of #$CuttingDevice include the collections #$Razor, #$Scissors, and #$LawnMower.")
(disjointWith BiologicalIntakeEvent ElectricalEvent)
(comment AutoTireMarketCategory "Different Types of Tires, and tire-related things.")
(comment issuesDocument "Arg1 issues the document ARG2. ")
(comment TearGland "The collection of all tear #$Glands, each of which secretes #$LacrimalFluid which moistens an #$Eye.  Terrestrial #$Vertebrates possess #$TearGlands, while aquatic ones do not.")
(comment VBCommandExecutionFault "A program has a #$VBCommandExecutionFault if an
unauthorized person can pass Visual Basic code to a program and have it execute arbitrary
commands.")
(comment AlarmDevice "A collection of objects; a specialization of #$PoweredDevice.  Every instance of #$AlarmDevice triggers an #$AlarmSignal.  It may do this automatically when it detects certain physical phenomena, or it may be manually activated.")
(comment GermanPointer-Wirehaired "A collection of medium-sized dogs.")
(comment AustrianPerson "The collection of people who are either #$citizens of #$Austria, or participants in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization AgricultureOrganization)
(comment StillCamera-Digital "The collection of cameras that record still images (as opposed to strictly moving images) digitally, rather than on film. Some digital cameras may be both DigitalStillCameras and DigitalCamcorders, if they can be used both for taking still pictures and for video.")
(comment PosteriorBasalSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all Posterior basal segments of #$InferiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by a #$PosteriorBasalSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung.")
(disjointWith EnteringInfoIntoDevice AthleticActivity)
(comment Margarine "margarine")
(comment RecordedMusicStore "An establishment that sells records, cassettes, and CDs --some with music or speech on them, and some blank (probably only blank CASSETTES).")
(comment communicationToken "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$Communicating to instances of #$InformationBearingThing.  (#$communicationToken COM IBT) means that IBT carries the information transferred in COM and was used to convey that information in COM.  IBT may be a tangible object (e.g., a newspaper), a sound (e.g., a voice), an image (e.g., from a television broadcast), or even a touch (e.g., a staying hand).")
(disjointWith DiagnosingAndRepairingSomething InformationBearingThing)
(comment nodeOfTypeInNetwork "(#$nodeOfTypeInNetwork HARDWARE HARDWARE-TYPE NETWORK) means that HARDWARE is one of the #$Computers that constitutes the #$ComputerNetwork NETWORK, and HARDWARE plays the role of HARDWARE-TYPE in NETWORK. This predicate is useful for stating that computers are nodes (with particular roles) in networks larger than a local area network. For instance, (#$nodeOfTypeInNetwork Router001 #$Router-Network #$Internet)  means that Router001 is a network router on the #$Internet. See also the more specialized predicates #$nodeOfTypeInLAN, #$nodeOfTypeInAccountSystem.")
(comment SmokingDevice "a device which is used to allow some kind of plant leaf, usually tobacco, to be burnt for smoking")
(comment BiologicalReproductionEvent "A specialization of #$BiologicalProductionEvent.  Each instance of #$BiologicalReproductionEvent is an event in which one or more instances of #$BiologicalLivingObject (q.v.) (related to the event by #$parentActors) produce at least one new instance of #$BiologicalLivingObject (related to the event by #$offspringActors), generally of the same kind as the parents.  Notable specializations of #$BiologicalReproductionEvent include #$AsexualReproductionEvent and #$SexualReproductionEvent.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterB "The lowercase letter 'b'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$B-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterB.")
(comment StationWagon "Four doors, a BIG non-trunk luggage space, and back seats which usually can be folded forward, eliminating some passenger space but creating an even LARGER luggage space.")
(comment interArgNotIsa1-4 "(#$interArgNotIsa1-4 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the first argument to PRED, the fourth argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(comment CSTearGas "A subset of tear gas with the chemical formula C10H5ClN2.")
(comment ReformulatorHighlyRelevantFORT "The collection of Cyc FORTs that are highly relevant to the reformulator.           An example of such a FORT would be one that is referenced in a large           number of reformulator rules in the KB (see intances of            #$CycLReformulationRulePredicate).")
(comment Telephone "Electrical Telephones of all sorts.  A Device used to transmit sound information long distances by converting them into electrical signals")
(comment DorsalRamusT10 "The collection of all T10 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT10 and DorsalRamiT10 branch from SpinalRootT10.  DorsalRamiT10 supplies the skin on the back.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity ChemicalReaction)
(comment DevelopingAFn "returns the class of product development events for products of type ARG1.")
(comment SoftwareCrack-Instructions "Collection of instructions for 'cracking' software by making a trial version of a program a permanent version, by removing 'register now' reminders, and so on.  Note that some software cracks are programs; the constant #$SoftwareCrackProgram covers these instances.")
(comment Armpit "The area under where the arm meets the torso; opposite of shoulder on the arm")
