(comment Smiling "Only primates smile.  Requires lips.  Also may involve the whole face and perhaps mouth.   Should that be inferable from the fact use of lips involves face and mouth? ")
(disjointWith CerealFood Candy)
(comment Subsidiary "An organization that is fully controlled by another.")
(disjointWith TrainCar HorseCarriage)
(comment WorldWideWebRobot "#$WorldWideWebRobot is a collection of programs that automatically traverse the Web's hypertext structure by retrieving a document, and recursively retrieving all documents that are referenced. Note that \"recursive\" here doesn't limit the definition to any specific traversal algorithm -- if it applies some heuristic to the selection and order of documents to visit and spaces out requests over a long space of time, it is still a #$WorldWideWebRobot. Normal Web browsers are not #$WorldWideWebRobot, because they are operated by humans, and don't automatically retrieve referenced documents (other than inline images). Instances of #$WorldWideWebRobot are sometimes referred to as \"Web Crawlers\", \"Worms\", or \"Spiders\".")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup Secretariat)
(comment SewerSystem "The collection of all sewer sytems, systems of one or more #$SewerLines interconnected together to allow the flow of sewage or rainwater.  #$SewerSystems may be municipal, and may include wastewater-treatment plants.")
(comment weldedTo "(#$weldedTo ?obj1 ?obj2) means that ?obj1 and ?obj2 are rigidly connected by a piece of metal solidified during #$Welding.  This piece may be a part of ?obj1 or ?obj2 as it is in welding, or may be a part of a third piece of metal as it is in sodering or brazing.")
(disjointWith FaceOfAnimal Trunk-BodyCore)
