(comment WireGrill "A standard grill, more or less 2-D, made of metal bars arranged in a lattice or as slats.")
(comment partOfIBT "(#$partOfIBT WHOLE PART) means that the #$InformationBearingThing PART is an information-containing part of the #$InformationBearingThing WHOLE.  If WHOLE is an instance of  #$PartiallyTangible, PART will be one of the #$physicalParts of WHOLE.  If WHOLE is an #$Event (e.g. an instance of #$InformationBearingWavePropagation), PART will be one of the #$subEvents of WHOLE.  In any case, the information contained in PART will be #$subInformation of the information contained in WHOLE.")
(disjointWith AutomaticCarWindow Windshield)
(comment PolypeptideMolecule "The collection of all #$PeptideMolecules comprised of between 10 and 100 #$AminoAcids.")
(comment RotaryDial-Telephone "A collection of devices for inputing telephone numbers. Each instance of #$RotaryDial-Telephone consists of a disk with ten holes arranged around the periphery connected via a rotary shaft through its center to an instance of TelephoneBody. The ten holes correspond to the ten single-digits numerals 0-9, and the typical mode of operation is for the caller to insert a fingertip into a hole, rotate the dial clockwise until the fingertip hits a stop device attached to the telephone body, and then release the dial by removing the fingertip from the hole and let the dial return to its initial position. The dial generates clicks while rotating back to its initial position, and the clicks encode one digit of a telephone number.")
(comment HerdAnimal "A subcollection of #$Animal; the collection of all large plant-eating animals that travel and graze in social groups.  Instances of #$HerdAnimal also belong to #$Herbivore; most instances of #$Ruminant are also instances of #$HerdAnimal.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterC "The capital letter 'C'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$C-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterC.")
(comment TrunkOfCar "The enclosed trunk of a car found in notchback cars, for instance.")
(comment ArmMovement "A specialization of #$BodyMovementEvent.  Each instance of #$ArmMovement is a movement of an animal's arm, where the movement in question is generated by the animal, and involves movement of the upper arm or elbow in relation to the animal's body.  Specializations of #$ArmMovement include #$RaisingAnArm and #$Reaching.")
(comment ComputerPrinter-LED "The collection of LED computer printers.")
(comment Petrochemical "A subcollection of #$PetroleumBasedProduct, such as benzene, ethylene, and styrene, obtained from petrochemical feedstocks such as ethane, propane, and naphtha.  Many #$Plastics are manufactured from #$Petrochemicals.")
(comment ReformulatorHighlyRelevantFORT "The collection of Cyc FORTs that are highly relevant to the reformulator.")
(comment LegalCounsellingService "legal counselling as a service")
(comment MedialPectoralNerve "The collection of all medial pectoral #$Nerves.  Each #$MedialPectoralNerve branches off a #$MedialCord-BrachialPlexus and #$innervates the #$PectoralisMajor and #$PectoralisMinor of the #$Shoulder in which it is located.")
(comment TranslationOfPolymerase-Transcription "An instance of this collection is an event in which an instance
of #$RNAPolymerase or #$DNAPolymerase acting as a catalyst in a
#$Transcription-DNAToRNA moves along a #$DNAMolecule, combining each
nucleotide base with a complementary one.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity BodyMovementEvent)
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument ControlDevice)
(comment GuadeloupePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Guadeloupe-TheDependency, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment NewspaperOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations which are responsible for the publication of #$NewspaperIssues.")
(comment PaperClip "The collection of paper clips. This includes

only the familiar wire objects, not the larger spring clips.")
(comment SupportColumn-FurniturePart "The central support column of an object, e.g. #$SwivelChair, certain tables, etc.")
