(disjointWith Sauce CerealFood)
(disjointWith Trailer BabyCarriage)
(comment NeuralNetwork "A computer simulation of the way that biological nervous systems (such as the brain) process information.  A #$NeuralNetwork is composed of a large number of highly interconnected, simple processing elements working in parallel to solve specific problems.  Learning involves adjustments to the connections between these  elements.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup ChamberOfCommerce)
(comment gluedTo "(#$gluedTo ?x ?y) means ?x is rigidly #$bondedTo ?y by means of #$Glue.")
(disjointWith Neck-AnimalBodyPart Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment FourthMetaCarpal "The #$FourthMetaCarpal is a bone of the #$Hand which is connected to the #$MiddleFinger.")
(comment obligatedMeansOfLocomotion "(#$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion AGENT MOVETYPE) means that MOVETYPE is a form of #$LocomotionProcess-Animal that the particular individual AGENT is physically obliged to use in the course of 'daily' existence.  A requirement is that the obligation be fairly persistent over some significant portion of obligated agent's #$Entity, or over the temporal extent of the context of the assertion. I.e., it cannot be something imposed for a short span of time by a comparatively fleeting circumstance.  I.e., someone who was forced to use a wheelchair to leave the hospital after an examination requiring a powerful local anaesthetic would not have #$Wheelchair-LocomotionEvent as an #$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion, unless this assertion were being made in a context whose temporal window was restricted to just that time span.  Note also that (#$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion AGENT MOVETYPE) does not mean that AGENT is incapable of being the #$performedBy of locomotion processes of types not known to be specializations of MOVETYPE: figuring out what an organism with a particular #$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion can and cannot do is a potentially complex story.  See #$restrictsAsObligatedMeansOfLocomotion")
(comment BoardGame-EquipmentSet "The collection of all board games equipment sets, eg. board + pieces + dice for backgammon, board + pieces for chess, etc ...")
(comment VideoTape "Magnetic tape suitable for video recording or having been recorded with video information.  Each video cassette has some length of such tape as a physical part.")
(disjointWith ManipulatingWithFingers PhysicalTransformationEvent)
(comment HairOnHead "A mob of hairs found on the top of a head")
(comment Rowboat "#$Rowboat is a specialization of #$Watercraft-Surface and #$Device-UserPowered.  Each instance of #$Rowboat is a boat which is usually powered by one or more persons' rowing (generally using #$Oars).")
(comment GordonSetter "A collection of large dogs, originally bred in Scotland.")
(comment Viking-CultureType "An instance of #$PersonTypeByCulture, #$Viking-CultureType is the collection of people who originated from Scandinavia and became famous for their sea-faring and war-making abilities.  Compare this constant to #$Viking, which is the group of professional sea-faring warriors employed by #$Viking-CultureType.")
(disjointWith LimitedLiabilityCompany TransportationOrganization)
(comment DoorKnocker "The collection of #$PhysicalDevices found outside doors (#$DoorInABuilding) which make a sound inside the building to indicate that someone is at the door as a result of the user manipulating them to strike one part against another part or the door itself.  The sound comes from the energy imparted to the knocker by the user.")
(comment FootMuscleSet "The #$Collection of all instances of #$FootMuscleSet.  The #$FootMuscleSet controls most #$Toe movevement.  These include the Abductor hallucis, Adductor hallucis, Flexor hallucis brevis, Plantar interosseous, Quadratus plantae, and the foot's Dorsal interosseous, Flexor digitorum brevis, Flexor hallucis brevis, Flexor digiti minimi brevis, Abductor digiti minimi, &  Lumbricals.")
(comment FileCabinet-PieceOfFurniture "A type of furniture/office storage device used for storing paper files")
(comment OldHuman "A specialization of #$HomoSapiens. Each instance of this collection is a person more than 60 years of age. This collection is disjoint with #$YoungHuman -- the collection of persons less than 35 years of age.")
(comment MedianCubitalVein "The collection of all median cubital #$Veins.  The #$MedianCubitalVein connects at its proximal end to the #$BasilicVein and at its distal end to the #$CephalicVein.")
(comment Broccoli-Foodstuff "Broccoli in any of its edible forms, whether raw or cooked.")
(comment FrontOffice " Front office department deals directly with clients")
(comment administratorAccountForSystem "(#$administratorAccountForSystem ACCT SYS) means that someone who #$hasAccessToAccount on the #$ComputerAccount ACCT on the #$AccountSystem SYS has #$AdministratorAccount privileges on SYS. These privileges are the Windows equivalent of \"root\" privileges on a UNIX account system (cf. #$rootAccountForSystem). If SYS is comprised of a single machine, ACCT will be a \"local administrator account\". If it is comprised of a number of machines, ACCT will be a \"domain administrator account\". See also #$systemAccountForSystem.")
(comment CurrencyConverterProgram "The collection of all #$CalculatorPrograms designed primarily to, when given a figure expressing an amount of money in one type of currency, calculate the equivalent amount of money in another currency.")
(comment Kit "A #$Kit is some device which has many parts which are used together in some specified way.")
(comment worksCreated "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$IntelligentAgent to instances of #$Artifact-Generic.  (#$worksCreated AGT ARTIFACT) means that AGT created ARTIFACT.")
(comment commitsForFutureUses "(#$commitsForFutureUses EVENT OBJECT) means that as a result of EVENT, OBJECT is subsequently put into a configuration and/or a form where it is serving some ongoing #$Role.  Things which are re-usable in their typical uses: a videocassette, a battery, a brick, an artist's canvas, a canvas tent.  Non-reusable things: paint, glue, mortar.  See also #$inputsCommitted, #$recyclableActors.   Consider a brick in a wall in a building.  It is `committed for future use' in the role of part-of-a-wall in the event of that building existing.  While the building is standing, it can't be part-of-a-wall in another building, though it could serve other roles such as an artistic accent, or to anchor a coat-hook.  After the building is torn down, that brick might still be intact, and could be used as part-of-a-wall in a future building.  Notice that the brick isn't necessarily transformed by being part of a wall.  However, so long as OBJECT serves the use to which it is `assigned' by EVENT, OBJECT is unavailable to be assigned the same #$Role by another event of the same type, at least an event that would temporally intersect with this committed use of OBJECT.  That is what is meant by it being `committed' for a particular future use.  An object may be re-used in a similar event, ONLY IF the #$Role to which it was assigned in EVENT either comes to its natural end or is given up (or thwarted), or in cases where EVENT is composed of discontinous pieces of time --- to illustrate that latter case, consider a tent that's used to shelter a certain group of workers on weekdays, but is used to shelter a different group in a different location on weekends.")
(disjointWith PlumbingFixture Weapon)
(comment StoneFruit "The collection of fruit with a hard inedible interior enclosing the seed of the fruit. This collection includes plums, peaches, and cherries.")
(comment BurundiPerson "A person who is a citizen of #$Burundi, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType (q.v.), and thus a collection of collections.  Each instance of #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType is a collection of beverages or foodstuffs (a specialization of #$EdibleStuff) that is by default disjoint with every other instance of #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType.  Instances of #$DefaultDisjointEdibleStuffType include #$SubmarineSandwich, #$Rice-Foodstuff, and #$Sauerkraut.")
(comment SignLanguage "A collection of languages. Each

element of #$SignLanguage is a language in which hand gestures

are the primary means of communication, instead of spoken

utterances, e.g., #$AmericanSignLanguage. Note that 

#$SignLanguage is not itself a language, but a collection.")
(comment SofaBed "A sofa that can be made to serve as a bed by lowering a hinged upholstered back,             or pulling out a concealed mattress.")
(comment ContractAnchorExtendLocomotion "What an inchworm does -- locomoting by getting small, planting one end of the body, then extending the body.")
(comment executableBy "(#$executableBy FILE ACCT) means that someone logged in under ACCT may execute FILE.")
(disjointWith ComputerUserInteraction (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(comment ChildrensProductMarketCategory "Includes products which are intended to be used by, for, or with children who are younger than teens.")
(comment SerotrilProduct "A drug taken by people to lose weight.")
(comment GlossopharyngealNerve "The collection of all glossopharyngeal #$Nerves.  The #$GlossopharyngealNerve is the ninth #$CranialNerve.  It #$innervates parts of the #$Tongue and #$Pharynx providing the sense of taste.")
(comment claimsAsDependent "`(#$claimsAsDependent YEAR SUPPORTER SUPPORTEE)' means that SUPPORTER
claims SUPPORTEE as a dependent for the year YEAR A.D. for federal income tax purposes.")
(comment OilFieldEquipment "Miscellaneous equipment used during the development of an #$OilField.  Includes the construction equipment, the specialized drilling apparatus, and everything else used during the construction.")
(disjointWith Landing PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment ComputationalSystem "A specialization of #$InformationBearingObject and #$PoweredDevice. Each instance of this collection is a system used for computing purposes.  It includes as specializations both #$Computer and #$ComputerNetwork.  Anything that can be said about both collections can more efficiently be stated about this collection.  For example, instead of saying that system administrators maintain instances of #$Computer and #$ComputerNetwork, one can simply say that system administrators maintain instances of #$ComputationalSystem.")
(comment Doll-Toy "A toy person which children usually play with or collect")
(comment BlackWidowSpider "A collection of spiders found in North America. 

They are venomous, and their bites can cause muscle spasms, breathing difficulties, and even death. The female black widow has a characteristic red

hourglass-shaped marking on its underside.")
(comment ConfidentialityAgreementDocument "An agreement, often made as part of the conditions for hire, in which one agent promises not to reveal certain information to a third party.")
(disjointWith ElectronicDevice MusclePoweredDevice)
(comment Style-FlowerPart "A style is an extension from the ovary supporting the stigma, through which the pollen tube grows.")
(comment EritreanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Eritrea, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment RelationshipType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$RelationshipType is a collection of #$Relations.  The relations in a given relationship-type represented in the Knowledge Base are typically those sharing some common feature(s) -- often having to do with what kinds of things the relations relate (see e.g. #$argIsa and #$argGenls) -- considered significant enough that the collection of all such relations is useful to reify.  Although what constitutes a \"significant common feature\" is difficult to specify precisely, there are many clear-cut cases.  Examples include #$UnaryFunction, #$LogicalConnective, #$IndividualDenotingFunction, #$GenericTimePredicate, and #$LanguageDescribingPredicate.  Two important specializations of #$RelationshipType are #$PredicateType and #$FunctionType.")
(comment CardiacArrhythmia "The collection of instances of the #$PhysiologicalCondition in which one has odd alterations from one's regular heartbeat.   The condition may be medically innocuous.")
(comment Bathtub "The collection of all #$Tubs primarily used for #$TakingABath.")
(disjointWith Undressing BuildingCleaningChore)
(comment EdiblesRichInFn "The Cyc function #$EdiblesRichInFn is a #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  It is used to represent foodstuffs which have a high concentration of a certain nutrient.  (#$EdiblesRichInFn NUTRIENT) denotes the collection of edible things that are rich in the type of #$Nutrient NUTRIENT.  For example, (#$EdiblesRichInFn #$EdibleCalcium) denotes the collection of all #$EdibleStuff rich in calcium; that collection will have the collection #$DairyProduct as a subset.")
(comment subOrgs-MaterialSupport "(#$subOrgs-MaterialSupport SUPER SUB) means that SUB is in an organizational relationship with SUPER in which SUPER is ordinarily responsible for providing most of the materials, supplies, and logistic support or 'infrastructure support' for SUB's activities, and SUB depends on SUPER for this support.  Such support may include equipment, facilities, fuel, and supply and/or resupply of goods and materiel.  (Different organizations may supply services or money, or may have command over SUB.  These are not indicated by this predicate.)  For example, if a military field reconnaissance unit ordinarily calls upon a logistics unit for most of its materiel support--e.g., for mess equipment or for ammunition, then the logistics unit has the reconnaissance unit as one of its #$subOrgs-MaterialSupport dependents.  Similarly, if a company COMP offers its labs, facilities and lab supplies to a research team TEAM from a university, then (#$subOrgs-MaterialSupport COMP TEAM) is true, even if money for the team's salaries comes from the university.  SUB need not be directly supported by SUPER, -- it could also be several steps down in the metrials distribution chain.  (See also #$subOrgs-Financial, #$subOrgs-AdministrativeServiceSupport, and #$subOrgs-Command.)")
(comment productTypeName "The name the product type is marketed under.")
(comment containsMaliciousCode "(#$containsMaliciousCode FILE MALPROG) means that the #$ComputerFile-Abstract, FILE, instantiates a bit of #$ComputerCode which is source or executable code for MALPROG.")
(disjointWith HardwareStore AutoDealership)
(comment Bugle "a trumpet without valves")
(comment Platypus "The collection of all duck-billed platypi; a subset of #$Mammal.  Elements of #$Platypus are Australian monotreme mammals, the females of which order lay eggs and lactate over a broad chest area rather than through teats.  They have broad leathery bills and webbed feet.  They swim in streams and rivers and live in burrows.  #$Platypus constitutes an instance of #$BiologicalSpecies (also called Ornithorhynchus anatinus).")
(disjointWith HandlingAnObject Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment SealedCan "The collection of non-resealable tin, steel or aluminum cans which are used for storage of items such as pet food, canned vegetables, juices, etc.")
(comment CycLNonAtomicTerm-Assertible "A #$CycLExpressionType and a specialization of both #$CycLExpression-Assertible and #$CycLNonAtomicTerm (qq.v.).  The collection of all CycL non-atomic terms that could appear within a sentence that could be asserted to the Cyc Knowledge Base.  More precisely, each instance of #$CycLNonAtomicTerm-Assertible is a non-atomic term that is both syntactically and semantically well-formed.  By definition, any CycL non-atomic term is syntactically well-formed.  To be semantically well-formed, a non-atomic term sentence must be constructible via the syntax of CycL without violating any applicable arity or argument-type constraints (see #$arity and #$ArgTypePredicate).  A CycL term must be semantically well-formed in order to be interpretable as having a \"semantic value\", which for terms means having a denotation.  Note that being \"assertible\" in the present sense does not require a sentence's actually being asserted in the KB.")
(comment Handle-Curved "A curved handle like on a suitcase, bucket, or *some* fireplace screens.")
(comment MuscleTissue "A specialization of #$OrganismPart. Each instance of #$MuscleTissue is a quantity of muscle tissue; that is, tissue composing biological organs that converts chemical energy into mechanical energy. Note that as this collection is a specialization (via #$OrganismPart) of #$BiologicalLivingObject, it only covers \"undetached\" muscle parts. An important specialization of this collection is #$Muscle, the collection of masses of #$MuscleTissue attached at both ends that are controlled by nerves, and move one or more body parts.")
(comment ChamealiCharacter "characters used for the Chameali dialect of Punjabi")
(comment VendingMachine "Any machine into which you can put coins or bills , and out comes food! soda! pamphlets! and perhaps some change. This does not include ATM machines or change-making machines; they will have a common genls with #$VendingMachine.")
(disjointWith Swimming-Generic Locomotion-SolidSurface)
(comment SNRNPsFuseEndsOfIntron "The second scene or stage in the RNA splicing-script.  At this stage, the group of snRNPs that has bonded to the #$Intron-Molecule in the ")
(comment Ambulance "#$Ambulance is a specialization of #$RescueVehicle, #$EmergencyVehicle, and #$SpecialPurposeVehicle.  Each instance of #$Ambulance is a road vehicle equipped primarily for transporting wounded, injured, or sick persons.")
(comment HardwareBusGraphicsSubSystem "This collection specifies all of the bus imlementations that have been    built with the specific intent of high throughput on the graphics output.   This includes memory access optimizations #$and block transfer abilities.")
(comment LendingLibrary-Organization "The collection of all instances of #$Library-Organization that lend materials to their users and permit them to remove those materials from the premises of the #$LendingLibrary-Organization.")
(comment EasterEgg "An Easter egg is an egg that has been colored and decorated,           usually at Easter (see #$EasterHoliday).")
(comment barLevelOfPhrase "(#$barLevelOfPhrase PHRASE N) indicates that the degree of syntactic saturation, or bar level, of PHRASE is N. For example, in most linguistic theories incorporating this concept, for any #$NounPhrase NP, it is true that (#$barLevelOfPhrase NP 2).")
(comment Soap-Personal "Soap-Like substances which can be used on human skin (not the strict chemical definition, #$Sodium Salts of Fatty Acids)")
(comment DorsalRamusC6 "The collection of all C6 dorsal rami.  #$VentralRamusC6 and #$DorsalRamusC6 branch from SpinalRootC6.  #$DorsalRamusC6 supplies the #$Skin on the back #$Back-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment CheninBlanc-Wine "The collection of all instances of

Chenin Blanc wine.")
(comment ThumbnailImage "The collection of all thumbnail images.  A thumbnail image is a computer image file which has been reduced to small size.  Often, thumbnail images are used on the World Wide Web to reduce download time and may link to a larger version of the same image.")
(comment Axle "A bar that a wheel or wheels are mounted on and that supports the wheel(s) as they turn.")
(comment Sticker-Adhesive "The collection of all adhesive labels, decals, etc. with text and/or an image on the non-adhesive side.")
(comment ExternalNose "The collection of all external (or 'outer') noses.  Each member of this collection is the part of a #$Nose sticking out from the face.  The part of the #$Nose inside the head is called the #$InternalNose.")
(comment HermaphroditicPlantSpecies "The collection of #$BiologicalSpecies of normally hermaphroditic #$Plants, plants with male and female organs occurring together in the same structure (e.g., pistils and stamens in the same flower).  Compare #$DioeciousPlantSpecies and #$MonoeciousPlantSpecies.")
(comment ItalianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Italy, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment NintendoGameBoyROM "This is the collection of all #$ROM-ConsoleGames intended for use in

#$Gameboy-TheProduct.")
(comment Queen-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of 'Queen.'")
(comment CoahuiltecanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages mostly of the West")
(comment HeatingOil "The collection of all instances of heating oil")
(disjointWith Teaching EnteringAUsername)
(comment HandAndWristMovement "Any movement of the hand; requires wrist movement as well.  Thus any kind of holding is not a proper spec since holding implies a stationary process.")
(comment ProfessionalOffice "#$ProfessionalOffice is a specialization of #$SingleSiteLocalOrganizationWithClients.  Each instance of #$ProfessionalOffice is an organization located at a single site and comprising one or more professionals (physicians, dentists, lawyers, accountants, etc.), their support staff, and clients.")
(comment HumanToddler "The toddler stage begins at about 1 year of age, when a child begins to walk and talk, and ends at about 3-1/2 when the child is probably toilet trained and has a number of advanced physical skills, like running and climbing with coordination.")
(disjointWith MicroPhysicalEvent BodilyFunctionEvent)
(comment hostCellInGeneExpression "(#$hostCellInGeneExpression GENE CELL) means that in the gene expression event GENE, it is (#$GeneticSubstrateFn CELL) that is being expressed.")
(comment erects "(erects AGENT STRUCTURE MATERIAL-TYPE LOCATION) means that

AGENT erects STRUCTURE using material of the type MATERIAL-TYPE in or

at LOCATION.")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice RecordingOfWaveIBT)
(disjointWith BiologicalDestructionEvent TakingCareOfPeople)
(comment webPageInfoAbout "The #$WorldWideWebPage-CW in ARG1 has information (text, pictorial, sound) about the object ARG2.")
(comment UsedAutomobile "A fuel-burning mechanical device which is a conveyance, for ground transportation - in short `a used car'")
(comment Diaphragm-BodyPart "The part of the body responsible for the inhaling and exhaling actions of the lung.")
(comment issueDividesGroup "(#$issueDividesGroup ISSUE GROUP) means GROUP is divided by its members' disagreement over ISSUE.")
(comment Consulate-TheBuilding "The collection of all consulates, the buildings in which official diplomatic representations are hosted. For the office itself see #$Consulate-TheMission.")
(comment Harrier-TheDog "A collection of dogs.")
(comment BahamasPerson "A person who is a citizen of the #$Bahamas, or a participant in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EnergyOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment ApicalSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all apical segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a (left or right) #$SuperiorLobeOfLung that supplies the #$ApicalSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung (or the apical part of the #$ApicoposteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung on the left side).  It branches from the #$SuperiorLobarBronchus.")
(comment VideoTapePlaying "The displaying of images that were stored on a video cassette")
(disjointWith Hunting HikingEvent)
(comment LacrimalCanal "The collection of all lacrimal canals.  A pair of #$LacrimalCanals drains the #$LacrimalFluid from the #$Eye to the #$NasolacrimalDuct.")
(comment NouvelleCuisine "The collection of instances of food that tends to be lighter and more daring (more experimental and cosmopolitan) than `traditional' American cuisine.  Might also be known as Yuppie cuisine, except that lots of non-yups like it too.")
(comment ShoeStore "An establishment that sells shoes")
(comment MagneticTapeCassette "The collection of all types of cassettes, including #$AudioCassette and #$VideoCassette.")
(comment memberOfSpecies "(#$memberOfSpecies ORG SPECIES) means that the organism ORG is a member of the #$BiologicalSpecies SPECIES.")
(comment OrganizationalChart "A collection of #$InformationStores and a subcollection of #$StructuredInformationSource.  Each instance of #$OrganizationalChart graphically or in outline fashion depicts information about the control structure or resource use structure of an organization.  E.g., a diagram of Exxon Corporation's top managers showing their reporting structure.")
(comment WeaponsGradeSpraytank "The subcollection of #$SprayingDevices designed to hold #$Weapons grade #$FluidTangibleThings, such as #$ChemicalWeapons. #$MagazineForBullets is to #$Gun as #$WeaponsGradeSpraytank is to #$WeaponsGradeSprayer (ignoring the stuff/object distinction).")
(comment Packet-ICMP-ECHO-Spoofed "#$Packet-ICMP-ECHO-Spoofed is the collection of packets used in instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation-Smurfing.")
(comment TelephoneKeypad "A collection of devices for inputing telephone   numbers. Each instance of TelephoneKeypad contains at least 12   buttons, one for each digit 0-9, plus one marked * and one marked   #. Unlike the NumericKeypad used as a computer input device, a   TelephoneKeypad generally has the small numbers at the top. The   buttons are typically arranged in four rows of three buttons apiece,   from top to bottom as follows: 123 456 789 *0#. When one of these   buttons is pressed, the keypad generates a tone consisting of two   pitches sounding simultaneously. Each tone corresponds in the   Dual-Tone MultiFrequency (DTMF) standard to a digit 0-9, the symbol   * or #, or (on some keypads) a letter A-D.")
(comment Ovum "A specialization of #$Gamete.  Each instance of #$Ovum is a specialized gamete cell produced by meiosis (see #$Meiosis) in the reproductive tract of a female animal.  Each ovum usually has half the number of chromosomes that a regular body cell does, and when fertilized by a sperm cell (see #$SpermCell), it becomes a zygote and continues to develop into a mature individual animal.  See also #$FemaleAnimal, #$SexualReproductionEvent.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterC "The lowercase letter 'c'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$C-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterC.")
(comment SportUtilityVehicle "street-legal vehicles which are capable of driving off the road as well.")
(comment ComputerPrinter-Inkjet "The collection

of inkjet computer printers.")
(comment CNTearGas "A subset of tear gas; also known as Chlororacetophenone.")
(comment DownFeatherStuff "soft fluffy feathers sometimes used to stuff pillows, bedding, etc.")
(comment NTDomain "An #$NTDomain is a #$AccountSystem consisting of a group of #$NTWorkstations and one #$PrimaryDomainController (PDC), and one or more #$BackupDomainControllers (BDCs).")
(comment TelephoneReceiver "A collection of electronic   components. Each instance of TelephoneReceiver includes at least a   small speaker and a small microphone installed in an object that can   be held in the user's hand or worn on the user's head so that the   microphone is in position to pick up the user's voice and the   speaker is near the user's ear. A telephone receiver can be   connected to an instance of TelephoneBody via a telephone cord or a   wireless connection. It may or may not include a telephone keypad   for dialing and other functions.")
(comment DorsalRamusL4 "The collection of all L4 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiL4 and DorsalRamiL4 branch from SpinalRootL4.  DorsalRamiL4 supplies the ????.")
(comment WeddingCake "The collection of #$WeddingCakes, 

which are usually elaborate, multi-tiered cakes covered with frosting and decorations

like frosting flowers. Wedding cakes are served at wedding receptions. At some

weddings, two wedding cakes are served: a #$BridesCake, and a #$GroomsCake.")
(comment aheadWRTTrajectory "(#$aheadWRTTrajectory EVT OBJ1 OBJ2) is true iff OBJ1 lies ahead of
OBJ2 along the trajectory of EVT, where EVT is an instance of
#$Movement-TranslationEvent. The trajectory of EVT may be cyclical, or
anyway non-linear. Note that neither OBJ1 nor OBJ2 need be objects moving in
EVT: for instance, in a trip from Austin to New Orleans this predicate would
hold true of, respectively, the trip itself, New Orleans and Austin -- as
well as of the trip, New Orleans and Houston.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity PreparingFoodOrDrink)
(comment Breathalyzer "The collection of all hand-held devices that determine the blood alcohol percentage from a subject's breath.  Also see (#$UsingAFn Breathalizer).")
(disjointWith GraspingImplement Brush)
(comment SpruceTree "The collection of spruce trees.")
(comment LittleSarkIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$LittleSark-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment MoneyBag "The collection of money bags.

These are largish bags generally made of canvas.")
(comment typicalInterArgGenl "(#$typicalInterArgGenl PRED M COL1 N COL2) says that when a spec of COL1 fills the Mth argument-place of PRED, then, typically, the Nth place of PRED will be filled by a spec of COL2.")
(comment ClothesPin "The collection of all clothes pins, devices used for suspending pieces of clothing from a stretched cord, so they can dry")
(disjointWith Conveying-Generic BuildingMaintenance)
(comment Coughing "coughing events -- spasmodic exhalation of the lungs sometimes due to a lung or throat  irritant")
(disjointWith CerealFood Condiment)
(comment BranchOrganization "A branch organization is a subOrganization with its own PhysicalQuarters.")
(disjointWith Trailer Wagon)
(comment ExpertSystem "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs based on logical rules and a set of narrow domain-specific knowledge to provide expertise for some task.  Instances of #$ExpertSystem may or may not have been written using an instance of #$ExpertSystemShell.")
(disjointWith ProfessionalAssociation ActivityTypeFocusGroup)
(comment Harrow "A  horse-drawn tool for cultivating and smoothing the soil.")
(comment Centrifuging "A collection of events.  In each instance of this collection, a fluid is centrifuged (ie., spun rapidly around, simulating a very strong gravitational force) in order to separate suspended particles of varying density.")
(disjointWith Trunk-BodyCore BodilyOrifice)
(comment SecondMetaCarpal "The #$SecondMetaCarpal is a bone of the #$Hand which is connected to the #$IndexFinger.")
(comment NLQuantAttribute "Instances of #$NLQuantAttribute are attribute values that specify the type of quantifier that occurred in an utterance.  See #$NLTagFn for more info.")
(comment Game-EquipmentSet "Instances of #$Game-EquipmentSet are groups of objects which, taken together, form the set of things needed to play some game.  Examples include: A chess set.  A badminton net, birdie and two racquets.  A 'Trivial Pursuit' board, timer, game pieces and cards.  A set of playing cards.  When someone buys a game, what they are really buying is the set of gear to play that game.")
(comment ComputerProgramCopy "A collection of #$InformationBearingThings which are #$programCopies of a #$ComputerProgram-CW. Examples: A bank of memory registers, a set of hard disk sectors, a stack of punch cards, a printout of #$ComputerCode, a satellite transmission. A #$ComputerProgramCopy might not have the exact same #$ComputerCode as  other #$programCopies of the same #$ComputerProgram-CW, and it might not even have the exact same algorithms, but the functionality must be about the same.")
(comment RunningShoe "The collection of shoes made for running.  See #$RunningSpike also.")
(disjointWith DeviceRunning BodyMovementEvent)
(comment Breathing "A collection of activities constituting a natural #$PhysiologicalFunction; #$Breathing is the collection of #$AirRespiration events in which the respiring organism takes air into its internal #$Lungs, where the gas exchange occurs.  See also #$Respiration.")
(comment HouseBoat "A specialization of #$Watercraft-Surface and #$HumanResidence. Each instance of this collection is a boat constructed with rooms so that it resembles a floating house. Note that boats large enough to resemble floating hotels rather than houses fall into other collections such as #$OceanLiner.")
(comment EnglishSetter "A collection of large dogs.")
(comment IndianOceanPerson "collective term applied to inhabitants of a few islands scattered thruout the Indian Ocean")
(disjointWith EducationalOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment HotRod-ModifiedCar "The collection of #$Automobiles whose engines have been modified such that they enable the #$Automobile to accelerate and travel faster.")
(comment Soleus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$Soleus #$Muscle.  The #$Soleus provides plantar (downward) flexion of the #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart.  The #$CalfMuscle and #$Soleus taken together are called the 'triceps sural'.")
(comment VerticalFileCabinet-PieceOfFurniture "A type of furniture/office storage device used for storing paper files.  A vertical file cabinet is the most common kind, with a short x-axis and a longer y-axis.  When you open the drawers, you are looking at the flat sides of the files, not at their edges (as you would be with a lateral file cabinet).")
(comment InferiorMesentericVein "The collection of all inferior mesenteric #$Veins.  The #$InferiorMesentericVein drains portions of the #$LargeIntestine and the #$Rectum into the #$HepaticPortalVein via the #$SplenicVein.")
(comment Espresso "A strong coffee drink made by forcing steam through ground coffee beans. Espresso usually is served in smaller amounts than regular coffee.")
(comment FieldMarketingOrganization "A marketing organization that is assigned to a geographic region.  They deal with any potential customers in that region.")
(comment HKLM-SOFTWARE-Microsoft-Windows-CurrentVersion-Run-Directory "An #$NTStandardFileType.  The #$Collection of all
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run directories
(instances of #$ExecutableRegistryKey) found on #$NTMachines.")
(comment FaxProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs designed primarily to handle fax (see #$FaxMachine) transmissions (see #$FaxingADocument).")
(comment Ampule "The Collection of all ampules.  An ampule is a small, completely-sealed glass tube that is broken to release the contents.  (e.g., smelling salts, or measured saline solution for asthma spiration machines.)")
(comment dislikesSensorially "(#$dislikesSensorially AGT SENSUM) means that the #$PerceptualAgent AGT derives some displeasure from the sensory experience of SENSUM (a taste, odor, or other #$SensoryAttribute).")
(disjointWith TrainCar SelfPoweredDevice)
(comment PanamanianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Panama, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Psilocybin "The collection of hallucinogenic compounds obtained from the fungus genus Psilocybe.")
(comment ChaiseLounge "A long reclining chair.")
(comment PettingAnAnimal "Stroking or rubbing an animal by a person, usually as a sign of affection for the animal.")
(comment deletableBy "(#$deletableBy COPY ACCT) means that someone logged in under
ACCT may delete COPY.")
(disjointWith Meeting-SocialGathering ComputerUserInteraction)
(comment ToiletrySubstance "Grooming and hygiene substances used by people.  Includes only products that are partly or wholly consumed in personal care events, such as shampoo and deodorant.  For durable items such as tooth brushes and shavers, see other subsets of #$PersonalHygieneProduct.")
(comment Shellfish "The collection of all #$Mollusks and #$Crustaceans that people commonly eat and that have shells. They are aquatic invertebrates, and are not actually #$Fish.")
(comment RioMP3Player "The collection of all Rio #$MP3Players, made by Diamond Multimedia.")
(comment physiologicalConditionOnsetRate "This predicate relates physiological conditions to their
onset rate as determined by their intensification rate compared to
other physiological conditions of the same type or physiological
conditions in general.")
(comment CervicalPlexus "The collection of all cervical plexi.  A #$CervicalPlexus is served by #$VentralRamusC1, #$VentralRamusC2, #$VentralRamusC3 and #$VentralRamusC4 on its side of the neck (#$Neck-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment Interaction-GuidingPredicate "This is the collection of CycL #$Predicates whose main intended
purpose is to register information about the state of Cyc in the course of
an interaction. This information can then be used by Cyc to guide its own
behavior. Assertions involving these predicates will depend upon the current
state of the KB and hence these predicates should be #$notAssertible, but
they are not, since currently this makes it impossible to conclude clauses
employing such predicates via forward rules and hence makes it impossible
for Cyc to reason about it's current state.")
(comment StationeryProduct "The collection of items used for producing written communication")
(disjointWith Landing BiologicalEvent)
(comment EtherTalkNetwork "A kind of network via which Macintosh computers may interconnect.")
(comment Deck-BuildingPart "A large balcony, usually wooden and connected to the back of a house.")
(comment Tarantula "A collection of large, hairy, tropical spiders. They are venomous, but their venom is weak and rarely harmful to humans. #$Tarantulas are sometimes kept as pets.")
(comment Tendon "Connecting tissue between muscle and bone")
(disjointWith MusclePoweredDevice ElectricalLightingDevice)
(comment Stigma-PlantPart "A stigma is the receptive tip of the carpel, upon which pollen is deposited and germinates.")
(comment SomalianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Somalia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic is a collection whose instances are distinguished by structural characteristics.  For example, the collections #$ChainOrganization, #$BranchOrganization and #$Department are all instances of #$OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic.  An instance of #$ChainOrganization is distinguished by the structure which exists among the parent company and the #$subOrganizations through which it operates.  Similarly, instances of #$BranchOrganization are distinguished by the fact that they are part of a larger structure.  Instances of #$Department are distinguished by the fact that they are formal groups within a larger organizational structure.")
(comment BabyCarrier "The collection of baby carriers.  A #$BabyCarrier is a device which is used to transport a #$HumanInfant or a #$HumanToddler.  Every #$BabyCarrier has at least one #$Handle or #$CarryStrap.")
(comment AcuteMyelogenousLeukemia "The collection of instances of acute myelogenous leukemia.")
(comment Urinal "Toilets for male urination while standing")
(disjointWith BuildingCleaningChore MedicalCareEvent)
(comment subOrgs-Command "(#$subOrgs-Command SUPERUNIT SUBUNIT) means that SUBUNIT is formally subject to command and direction by SUPERUNIT.  In the military services this means that SUBUNIT is assigned, or has at least been 'attached', to SUPERUNIT in such a way that at least one of the #$controllingSuborganizations of SUPERUNIT, or its commanding officer, are authorized to issue orders to SUBUNIT.  SUBUNIT need not be an immediate subordinate of SUPERUNIT, -- it could also be several steps down in the chain of command.  Even if SUBUNIT is not getting any financial or logistic support from SUPERUNIT, it is still in a #$subOrgs-Command relation if it is ordinarily supposed to obey the directives of SUPERUNIT.")
(comment fileContainsVirus "(#$fileContainsVirus FILE VIRUS) means the abstract sequence of bits FILE (an instance of #$ComputerFile-AIS) contains some bit of code which is source or executable code for the #$ComputerVirus VIRUS.")
(disjointWith AutoDealership KnickKnackStore)
(comment FrenchHorn "medium-sized brass instrument ")
(comment BiologicalPhylum "The collection of main taxonomic subdivisions of #$BiologicalKingdom (or #$BiologicalSubkingdom if present) for the #$Animal kingdom and for the animal-like organisms within the #$ProtistaKingdom.  The other elements of #$BiologicalKingdom have divisions belonging to #$BiologicalDivision instead of Phyla (Phyla is the plural of Phylum).")
(disjointWith Requesting-CommunicationAct Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment AudioEquipmentTypeByUse "#$AudioEquipmentTypeByUse is a collection of collections. Each element is a subcollection of #$AudioEquipment, all of whose elements share the feature of being designed and marketed for use in a certain situation. For example, one element is #$AutomobileAudioEquipment, the collection of #$AudioEquipment designed and marketed for use in an #$Automobile. #$PortableAudioEquipment is an element of #$AudioEquipmentTypeByUse because all of its elements are designed and marketed for use in situations where it's best if the equipment is portable.")
(comment Pillar "a tall strong support column used in buildings")
(disjointWith BoneTheStuff MuscleTissue)
(comment GothicLetter "characters adapted from Greek, for writing the Gothic language")
(comment Pencil "The collection of pencils with which one can write, use as cosmetics, etc.  A pencil is made of wood with a hollow in the middle with lead or color in it.")
(disjointWith ArmMovement MakingFacialExpression)
(comment IntronExcisedFromPrimaryTranscript "The third scene or stage in the RNA-Splicing script.  At

this stage the intron-lariat (see #$Intron-MolecularLariat) is excised

from the RNA transcript.")
(disjointWith Ambulance Motorcycle)
(disjointWith ComputerStorageDevice CleaningDevice)
(comment JudicialOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that adjudicate or are otherwise engaged in finding facts or law that are the subject of dispute or in deciding among competing interests in some kind of organized forum.  The #$UnitedStatesSupremeCourt is an instance of #$JudicialOrganization, as is a tribal council and the disciplinary arm of a local bar association.")
(comment BatikCloth "The set of instances of Batik, brightly coloured cloth originally from
Indonesia-Java. Batik cloth is produced by using a wax resist process - wax is
applied to areas to preserve the color while dye of a different color
is applied.  This can be done in several steps.")
(comment Plunger-HandTool "The collection of plunger that are devices consisting of a handle with a rubber suction cup at one end. A #$Plunger-HandTool is primarily used as a force pump to free clogged drains and toilet traps.")
(comment Surfactant "Stuff used as cleanser. Solubilizes oil and grease.")
(comment DorsalRamusT11 "The collection of all T11 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT11 and DorsalRamiT11 branch from SpinalRootT11.  DorsalRamiT11 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment most-GenQuantRelnFrom "(#$most-GenQuantRelnFrom RELN THING COL) is true if, for most of the instances X of COL (RELN THING X) holds.")
(comment Warez-ComputerProgram "Software that has been made available on the Internet for downloading. Some of this software are instances of Freeware, but some of it is pirated.")
(comment Satellite-Device "A man-made device intended to orbit a celestial body (for most of them, Earth).")
(comment TombStone "A stone grave marker which stands upright and has the grave marker information engraved in it.")
(comment InternalNose "The collection of all internal (or 'inner') noses (also called 'nasal fossoe').  Each member of this collection is the part of a #$Nose behind the face.  The part of the #$Nose sticking out from the head is called the #$ExternalNose.")
(comment GentianOrder "Those structures which are capable of biological reproduction. This includes self-reproducing organelles  like mitochondria and chloroplasts.")
(comment MexicanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Mexico, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SegaGenesisROM "This is the collection of all #$ROM-ConsoleGames intended for use on a

#$SegaGenesis-TheProduct.")
(comment Seven-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '7.'")
(comment SiouanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of the central and northern plains of North America")
(comment RollingPin "A rolling pin used for flattening dough, clay etc")
(comment ReleasingGraspOfSomething "No one holds on to something forever, therefore this always follows holding on to something.  Since a holding implies a releasing, it is not necessary to state for example, that both a grabbing and a releasing are #$subEvents of a turning a door handle event.")
(comment PoliticalOrganization "A specialization of #$AdvocacyOrganization and #$IdeologicalOrganization.  Each instance of #$PoliticalOrganization is an organization whose members share some common political, social, or economic values and goals, and whose main function  is to achieve those goals by influencing governmental powers, or by helping persons who favor the views and interests of its members to win elections or otherwise obtain governmental power.  The collection #$PoliticalOrganization includes instances of #$PoliticalParty and also instances of #$PoliticalInterestGroup.  Note that governmental bodies (such as a #$CityCouncil) are not considered instances of #$PoliticalOrganization.  Although such governmental bodies often act in political arenas, that is not their primary function.")
(comment FacilitiesDepartment "Each instance of #$FacilitiesDepartment consists of employees who are responsible for an organization's facilities (such as buildings, grounds).")
(comment PizzaCutter "A rotating blade with a handle attached at the axis, used to cut pizza into individual portions.")
(comment FemaleInfant "The collection of female infants, female children who are babies.")
(disjointWith ArmMovement BodilyFunctionEvent)
(comment SuperiorRegionFn "(#$SuperiorRegionFn BODYPART) refers to the region of BODYPART which higher than the other parts when the animal is in \"standard position\".  Thus the superior region of a human lung would be the caudal region (closest to the head) while the superior region of a hippo lung would be the dorsal region (closest to the back).")
(comment CowsMilk-Product "The collection of all volumes of processed cow's #$Milk.  This is the drinkable #$Product that can be bought in #$GroceryStores.")
(comment blocks "(#$blocks AGENT THING PLACE) means that agent prevents THING from moving into PLACE.")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice FuelCell)
(disjointWith SelectingSomething BiologicalDestructionEvent)
(comment WebCamPage "#$WebCamPage, a subset of #$WorldWideWebPage-CW, is a subset of the collection of all WWW pages that are connected to digital cameras that periodically or aperiodically update a photographic image which appears on the page.")
(comment MultiPurposeDevice "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$MultiPurposeDevice is a device which is designed to have more than one #$primaryFunction.  See also #$SinglePurposeDevice.  Of course even a #$SinglePurposeDevice might be employed for some unintended purpose, especially in an emergency.")
(comment TornadoAsEvent "A specialization of #$NaturalHazard and #$ImmediateWeatherProcess.  Each instance of #$TornadoAsEvent is the event in which a tornado moves through space.  See also #$TornadoAsObject for the collection of tornado objects.")
(comment Beak "The collection of all beaks belonging to #$Turtles and similar animals.  An individual #$Beak is a hard structure, located above the #$Mouth, which contains the #$Nostrils.  For the similar structure of a #$Bird see #$Bill-Birds.")
(comment opinionOnIssue "(#$opinionOnIssue AGENT ISSUE OPINION) means that AGENT has the opinion PROP, where PROP is an opinion regarding ISSUE. A sentence stating an opinion about an issue typically mentions that issue, but not always. 'People have the right to bear arms' is an opinion about the issue of gun control. Containing a mention of an issue is not sufficient for a sentence to be an opinion about that issue, as in 'The issue of abortion is widely discussed.'")
(comment PharaohHound "A collection of dogs.")
(comment BahrainPerson "The collection of people who are either #$citizens of #$Bahrain, or participants in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EnergyOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment FlywheelBattery "A kind of electromechanical battery employing a flywheel.")
(comment LateralSegmentOfMiddleLobeOfLung "The collection of all lateral segments of #$MiddleLobeOfLungs on the right side.  Each is served by a #$LateralSegmentalBronchusOfMiddleLobeOfLung.  (There is no lateral segment  in the left #$Lung, since there is no middle lobe in the left lung.)")
(comment VideoGameCartridge "A video game cartridge used in a home video game unit like Nintendo")
(disjointWith Communicating Hunting)
(comment NasolacrimalDuct "The collection of all nasolacrimal ducts, which occur in pairs in land #$Vertebrates.  Each #$NasolacrimalDuct drains #$LacrimalFluid from the #$EyeSocket to the #$NasalSinus.")
(comment HotBeverage "A beverage which is served warm or hot.")
(comment SportingGoodsStore "The collection of stores that sell primarily sporting goods, such as Rooster Andrews or Oshman's")
(comment Pulpit "A raised platform from which a speaker may address her audience.")
(disjointWith Agent-Generic OrganismPart)
(disjointWith Dictionary OrganizationalChart)
(comment SprayingDevice "A collection of tangible objects, containers which are designed to spray out their contents, and which are more or less self-contained systems for doing so.  An instance of #$SprayingDevice is a container for liquids which has a part that causes the contents to spread out into a mist when they are emitted.  Aerosol cans, plant sprayers, and inhalant devices (e.g., for asthma medication) are all instances of #$SprayingDevice.  Non-examples include lawn sprinklers, the spray nozzles that fit on the end of hoses, a rain cloud, a runny nose, etc.  A borderline example includes the case where a powder is being sprayed, rather than a liquid.")
(comment Cooler-Container "This is the collection of coolers. A cooler is an insulated container in which either ice or reusable ice substitute is placed along with food or drink that one wishes to keep cool.")
(comment nucleotidesComplementaryBasePaired "(#$nucleotidesComplementaryBasePaired NUCL1 NUCL2) means that there is a hydrogen bond between the nitrogen bases that are the respective components of #$Nucleotides NUCL1 and NUCL2 and that the nitrogen bases are complementary (see #$complementaryBaseTypes).")
(comment TelephoneNumberSignalGenerator "A collection of electronic components. Each instance of   TelephoneNumberSignalGenerator is used for generating the clicks or   tones that are standardly used to encode telephone numbers. Examples   include telphone dials and touch tone keypads, as well as tone   generators inside computer modems, fax machines, etc.")
(disjointWith Ovum SpermCell)
(comment LatinCapitalLetterD "The capital letter 'D'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$D-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterD.")
(comment SedanCar "Sedans. The collection of cars that have container-like trunks, as opposed to hatchbacks.")
(comment Heartbeating "Repeated pulsing of the heart muscle, which pumps blood to the cells of the heartbeater's body, blood being a supplier of oxygenated hemoglobin, sugars, and other necessary substances, and also being a receiver for poisonous waste byproducts of these processes.")
(comment ComputerPrinter-DotMatrix "The collection of

dot matrix computer printers.")
(comment OrganizationByEntityType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$OrganizationByEntityType is a subcollection of #$Organization whose instances are all the same type of legal entity.  For example, the collections #$LegalCorporation, #$Partnership, and #$Association are all instances of #$OrganizationByEntityType.")
(comment Petroleum-Condensate "The glossary in the EIA's 'International Energy Annual 1996' has the entries:  Lease Condensate: A liquid recovered from natural gas at the well or at small gas/oil  separators in the field. Consists primarily of pentanes and heavier hydrocarbons. Also called field condensate. Does not include plant condensate. Crude Oil (including Lease Condensate): A mixture of hydrocarbons that exists in liquid phase in underground reservoirs and remains liquid at atmospheric pressure after passing through surface separating facilities. Included are lease condensate and liquid hydrocarbons produced from tar sands, Gilsonite, and oil shale. Drip gases are also included, but topped crude oil (residual) and other unfinished oils are excluded. Liquids produced at natural gas processing plants and mixed with crude oil are likewise excluded where identifiable.")
(comment BlackBear "The American black bear")
(comment NTWorkstation "An #$NTDomain is a #$AccountSystem consisting of a group of #$NTWorkstations, one #$PrimaryDomainController (PDC), and one or more #$BackupDomainControllers (BDCs).  #$NTWorkstations are also stand-alone #$AccountSystems.  When someone logs on to an #$NTWorkstation locally, authentication is handled by the machine logged into and not by the BDCs.")
(comment GasolineFuel "Derived from petroleum, #$GasolineFuel provides the power to run engines, in particular those which are #$TransportationDevices")
(comment VentralRamusL1 "The collection of all L1 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusL1 and #$DorsalRamusL1 branch from SpinalRootL1.  #$VentralRamusL1 supplies the #$LumbarPlexus.")
(comment WeddingCake "The collection of #$WeddingCakes, 

which are usually elaborate, multi-tiered cakes covered with frosting and decorations

like frosting flowers. Wedding cakes are served at wedding receptions.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-Fraggle "#$AttackByComputerOperation-Fraggle is a specialization of #$AttackByComputerOperation-UDPPacketStorm.  Instances of this collection are similar to instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation-Smurfing, except they involve flooding a computer with UPD packets instead of ICMP packets.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity Travel-TripEvent)
(comment LiabilityInsurance "This type of insurance pays for events which the #$insuredAgent is responsible for, especially those which (intentionally or accidentally) harm other agents.")
(comment stuffInhaled "(#$stuffInhaled INHALING STUFF) means that during
INHALING, an instance of #$Inhaling, STUFF, an instance of
#$PartiallyTangible, is what is inhaled.")
(comment RubiksCube "The collection of all Rubik's Cubes.  Each face of a Rubik's Cube has 9 subsections, each of which may be a different color.  The object of the puzzle is to rotate sections of the cube so that each face has a homogeneous color.")
(disjointWith InformationRecordingDevice ControlDevice)
(comment TeaPlant "Individual tea plants; the plant which yields black tea, green tea and oolong tea, from which tea-the beverage is brewed.")
(comment WallisAndFutunaIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$WallisAndFutunaIslands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment MoneySorter "The collection of money sorters.

These are devices which sort currency. There are types that

sort and count coins and types that sort and count paper

currency.")
(comment Mop "The collection of all mops")
(comment Yawning "Yawning event -- caused by tiredness or boredom.")
(comment MakingCheese "A specialization of #$PreparingFoodItem.  Each instance of #$MakingCheese is an event in which cheese is made from milk.")
(comment stockListedWith "(#$stockListedWith COMPANY EXCHANGE) means that COMPANY's stock is traded on the #$StockExchange EXCHANGE.")
(disjointWith TrainCar BabyCarriage)
(comment ExpertSystemShell "#$ExpertSystemShell denotes the collection of programs that are designed to be used to generate expert systems (see #$ExpertSystem).")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup Trust-LegalEntity)
(comment PennyFarthingBicycle "The collection of the sort of old-fashioned bicycle which has one wheel much larger than the other.")
(disjointWith Pinna Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment ThirdMetaCarpal "The #$SecondMetaCarpal is a bone of the #$Hand which is connected to the #$MiddleFinger.")
(comment Some-NLAttr "The attribute value carried by utterances of the form \"some XXX\".")
(comment Doghouse "Each #$Doghouse is a small structure, usually found in backyards, intended to provide a pet dog shelter from the weather.")
(comment AutomobileHeadLight "Located at the front of the car and used for night driving.")
(disjointWith Ripping PushingAnObject)
(comment HoldingBreath "When you hold your breath, you keep air in your lungs and refrain from either inhaling or exhaling.")
(comment MakingFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to a specialization TYPE of #$PartiallyTangible (q.v.), #$MakingFn returns the collection of events in which one or more instances of TYPE are made (the collection in question will be a specialization of #$MakingSomething).  For example, (#$MakingFn #$Automobile) is the collection of events in which at least one car is manufactured.")
(comment EnglishToySpaniel "A collection of dogs.")
(disjointWith ManufacturingOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment GameToken "An instance is a small round object used in some board games.")
(comment PronatorTeres "The #$Collection of all instances of #$PronatorTeres #$Muscle.  The #$PronatorTeres pronates the #$ForeArm and assists #$Elbow flexion.")
(comment LateralFileCabinet-PieceOfFurniture "A type of furniture/office storage device used for storing paper files.  A lateral file cabinet is less common than the vertical kind, with a short y-axis and a longer x-axis (when viewed from the front).  When you open the drawers, you are looking at the edges of the files, not at their faces.")
(comment SuperiorMesentericVein "The collection of all superior mesenteric #$Veins.  The proximal end of the #$SuperiorMesentericVein connects to the #$HepaticPortalVein.  The #$SuperiorMesentericVein drains the #$SmallIntestine and part of the #$LargeIntestine and #$Stomach.")
(comment Coffee-Beverage "Coffee, the stuff type.  See also #$Coffee-Hot for a more specific version of this.")
(comment HospitalCustomers-MarketingOrganization "A marketing organization that is assigned to some number of hospitals. ")
(comment HKLM-SOFTWARE-Microsoft-Windows-CurrentVersion-RunOnce-Directory "An #$NTStandardFileType.  The #$Collection of all
HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnce
directories (instances of #$ExecutableRegistryKey) found on
#$NTMachines.")
(comment InternetProgram "The collection of all programs designed to use the Internet for some important part of their functionality.")
(comment InhalerCanister "The collection of all InhalerCanisters.  An #$InhalerCanister is a small aerosol can used in orally administering medicine to an individual.  The #$InhalerCanister fits inside an #$InhalerCanisterHolder, and together they comprise an #$InhalerDevice, which can be operated by an individual for use on her/himself.")
(comment Bill-PaymentRequest "A specialization of #$TextualMaterial.  Each instance of #$Bill-PaymentRequest is a written notification of a demand or request made by a creditor (or its agent) to a debtor, for payment of a debt (see #$PaymentObligation) previously incurred for some loan, goods, or services.  Instances of #$Bill-PaymentRequest include telephone bills, tax bills, department store bills, cleaning bills, and fuel bills. Note that this collection includes only actual physical copies of bills -- for the information contained in a given bill (which might be reproduced in more than one physical copy of it), see #$Bill-PaymentRequest-PIT. Nor is this mere piece of paper to be construed as the actual request (or demand) for money (for which see  collections such as #$Requesting-CommunicationAct). See also the predicate #$owesDebts.")
(comment considersAsEnemy "(#$considersAsEnemy U V) means that U has deep enmity towards V and is likely to take actions against V.  The feeling may be mutual, or V may be striving for reconciliation, or V may not even be aware of the relationship.  See also #$opponents.")
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument PlumbingFixture)
(comment FruitFn "#$FruitFn is a Cyc function, specifically a #$CollectionDenotingFunction, which is used to denote the various natural kinds of fruit.  #$FruitFn takes a single plant collection as its argument and returns the collection of fruits of that type of plant.  (#$FruitFn PLANTTYPE) denotes the collection of all fruits from the elements of PLANTTYPE.  Examples: (#$FruitFn #$AppleTree) denotes the collection of apples; (#$FruitFn #$CashewTree) denotes the fruit of the cashew tree (note this does NOT correspond with #$Cashew-TheSeed; the red pulpy fruit is used to make cashew wine).")
(comment CabindaEnclavePerson "A person who is a resident of #$Cabinda-Enclave, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment FoodOrDrink "A specialization of #$EdibleStuff (q.v.). Each instance of #$FoodOrDrink is a substance which instances of some type of organism (that is, some sub-collection of #$Organism-Whole) normally consume a significant part of. Important specializations of #$FoodOrDrink include #$Food (instances of which require chewing in order to be consumed) and #$Drink (instances of which are liquids that can be consumed without chewing).")
(comment typeOfWritingSurface "What a typical user of the writing system of the language --often a scribe-- writes on")
(comment FootStool "A type of low stool used to support feet.")
(comment HandingSomethingToSomeone "The collection of events involving the physical passing of an object from one person to another. The object's change in location does not entail a change in user rights, although some instances of #$HandingSomethingToSomeone do involve a temporary or permanent change in user rights. Those instances involving such a change are also instances of #$GivingSomething and/or #$TransferringPossession.--#$Causley, 2/22/99")
(comment permissionChangeableBy "(#$permissionChangeableBy COPY ACCT) means that someone logged in
under ACCT may execute COPY.")
(comment ComputerGameAdd-On "This is the collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs whose function is to provide further features to an existing #$ComputerGameProgram. Game add-ons allow the player to create more levels or environment, employ more weapons, interact with more characters, and so on.")
(comment MaleChild "The collection of male children, male kids about 12 years of age or less.")
(comment RioPMP300 "The collection of all Rio PMP300 #$MP3Players.  This is a specific version of #$RioMP3Player.")
(comment symptomOnsetRateInConditionType "(#$symptomOnsetRateInConditionType SYM AIL RATE) means that when an instance of

SYM is a subevent or true symptom of an instance of AIL, it often  has an onset rate of RATE.")
(comment LumbarPlexus "The collection of all lumbar plexi.  A #$LumbarPlexus is part of the #$LumboSacralPlexus and usually supplied by the ventral rami #$VentralRamusT12, #$VentralRamusL1, #$VentralRamusL2, #$VentralRamusL3, and #$VentralRamusL4.")
(comment deservesFurtherInquiry "`(#$deservesFurtherInquiry SENTENCE)' means that SENTENCE
expresses a proposition about which not enough is currently
known by Cyc to determine its truth value but which is such that Cyc knows
enough information suggesting truth 
to warrant pursuing further information. The
main intended purpose for such an assertion is to guide Cyc's behavior
in interactive contexts.")
(comment adverbStrings "(#$adverbStrings WORD STRING) states that STRING is one of the adverb strings for the word unit WORD in some microtheory.  In other words, some adverbial #$SpeechPartPredicate is used on WORD to relate it to STRING.  This predicate is

#$notAssertible since it is concluded from the current state of the knowledge base.")
(comment GiftCertificateFn "#$GiftCertificateFn takes as an argument any instance of #$ProductType and returns the collection of all #$GiftCertificates for that product.  For example, (#$GiftCertificateFn #$Clothing-Generic) denotes the collection of all clothing gift certificates.")
(disjointWith ProtectingSomething BiologicalEvent)
(disjointWith SheetOfSomeStuff ComputationalSystem)
(comment PicketFence "A fence constructed from a series of vertical wooden slats with gaps between them.")
(comment Genome "The collection of genomes. A genome is the complete genetic information about

an individual organism. The term is often used in the context of organism types, which is somewhat confusing.")
(comment CameraShutter "Elements of #$CameraShutter are parts of elements of #$StillCamera.  Elements are apertures which open and close to allow light to expose film.")
(comment AchillesTendon "The tendon which connects calf muscle to heel")
(disjointWith MusclePoweredDevice RefrigeratedStorageDevice)
(comment Ovule "The protective and nutritive tissue and the female gamete within, which develops into the seed after fertilization.")
(disjointWith OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic PersonTypeByPositionInOrg)
(comment BabySoftCarrier "The collection of all soft carriers for infants, a subset of #$BabyCarrier.  A #$BabySoftCarrier is a device that is used to carry a #$HumanInfant on one's #$Back-AnimalBodyPart or #$Chest-BodyPart.  They are made of soft, flexible material and have at least two #$CarryStraps which go over the adult's shoulders.")
(comment CombForHair "The collection of all combs for combing hair")
(comment Plumage "The elements of this collection consist of the entire
covering of feathers on a bird.")
(comment subOrgs-Financial "(#$subOrgs-Financial SUPER SUB) means that

SUB is below SUPER in an organizational hierarchy of financial

dependencies.  Specifically, SUB is ordinarily financially dependent

upon SUPER.  For example, the FBI ultimately depends upon the US

Government to provide for its expenses; a military battalion depends

on its superior military division for funding.  SUB need not be an

immediate financial dependent of SUPER, -- it could also be several

steps down in the money distribution chain.  Even if SUB is not

otherwise controlled by SUPER, it is still in a #$subOrgs-Financial

relation if it regularly gets the bulk of its income from the budget

of SUPER.")
(comment standardDefinedBy "see english on inverse")
(comment VirusScan "A collection of events in which an anti-virus program is
used to detect the presence of viruses in the files
scanned.")
(disjointWith AutoDealership LawnAndGardenStore)
(comment Valve-Mechanical "The collection of all manufactured #$Valves.  Each instance of this collection consists of a section of #$FluidConduit with at least one moving part which can limit the volume or direction of flow within a system.  Every #$Valve-Mechanical is a #$FlowControlDevice.  A #$PhysicalDevice which inserts and removes a #$Stopper would be a #$FlowControlDevice and, also, a #$Valve if the surrounding #$FluidConduit was included.")
(disjointWith ApplyingAForce Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment AbstractStructure "This collection was reified prior to completing its basic representation in order to facilitate the loading of files on which it depends.")
(comment Screen-Mesh "A piece of woven mesh used in windows, fireplace screens.")
(disjointWith MuscleTissue Nerve)
(comment SequoyahCharacter "characters, many distantly based on Roman, for writing Cherokee")
(comment TemperaPaint "Paint composed of pigment and egg (the egg yolk, actually).")
(disjointWith MakingFacialExpression TakingCareOfSomething)
(comment SNRNP "A special kind of enzyme that plays a key role in the
#$RNASplicingProcess.  The name is an acronym for 'small nuclear
ribonucleoprotein particles'.")
(comment Collie "A collection of large dogs. There are two varieties: rough-coated and             smooth-coated.")
(disjointWith CleaningDevice ComputerInterfaceDevice)
(disjointWith FinancialOrganization JudicialOrganization)
(comment VocabularyDefiningPredicate "The collection of all #$Predicates that are considered sufficiently ``definitional'' for a term for assertions using such #$VocabularyDefiningPredicates to be stated in a #$definingMt #$VocabularyMicrotheory.")
(comment Toothpaste "The semi-liquid stuff used for cleaning teeth")
(comment VentralRamusL5 "The collection of all L5 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusL5 and #$DorsalRamusL5 branch from SpinalRootL5.  #$VentralRamusL5 supplies the #$SacralPlexus.")
(comment PortWine "The collection of all instances of

Port wine. Port does not fit into the red/white/rose scheme.")
(comment Staple "usually metal connector for attaching a sheetlike object to something else")
(comment genotypeOfIndividual-Enumeration "(#$genotypeOfIndividual-Enumeration ORG GENE) means that ORG, an

instance of #$Organism-Whole, has among its genes GENE, an

instance of #$Gene-GenInfo. In practice, the genotype of an individual is a

recording of the allelic repartition of genes as they differ from the type

of reference. There will often be a genotype of reference for a type of organism, and genotypes of individuals will consist in the listing of variations with respect to that genotype of reference.")
(comment GraveMarker "The marker at a grave usually detailing the name, date of birth  and date of death of the person buried there.")
(comment LacrimalPunctum "The collection of all lateral puncta.  An individual #$LacrimalPunctum is a portal of a #$LacrimalCanal in an #$Eyelid.")
(comment PalmOrder "The biological order Arecales (within the monocot class or subclass) containing            only one family: Palmae or Arecaceae.")
(comment TogoPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Togo, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment MameROM "A piece of hardware that allows to emulate arcade games on a PC.")
(comment Seventeen-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '17.'")
(comment Dolphin-Fish "The collection of all (game) fish called \"dolphins\".  This contrasts with the type of mammal, #$DolphinOrPorpoise.")
(comment MuskogeanLanguageFamily "Amerindian language group of southeastern North America")
(comment PancakeSpatula "Spatula with a broad, flat, and stiff head.")
(disjointWith Traditional Alternative)
(comment Trumpeting-ElephantNoise "Action which produces the utterance made by elephants.")
(comment arg2NotGenl "(#$arg2NotGenl REL COL) means that nothing given as the second argument to the #$Relation REL may be a spec of the #$Collection COL.")
(comment InvestmentDepartment "Each instance of #$InvestmentDepartment consists of employees who are responsible for an organization's investments.")
(comment MattressPad "The removable piece of padding which goes between a mattress and the fitted sheet.")
(comment Predator "An organism which preys on living animals")
(disjointWith BodilyFunctionEvent IncurringBodilyHarm)
(comment KneeCapJoint "The #$Kneecap articulates with both #$Condyles of the #$Femur (thigh bone).")
(comment ScriptPredicate "#$ScriptPredicate is the collection of predicates which are used to make assertions about #$ScriptedEventTypes. Like other instances of #$EventPredicate, #$ScriptPredicates are associated with expansions. However, unlike other #$EventPredicates, the expansion for a #$ScriptPredicate consists in an ordered list of assertions that decompose the original assertion. Please see the documentation on Plans and Scripts for details.")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice PlumbingFixture)
(comment WorldWideWebHomePage-CW "#$WorldWideWebHomePage-CW is a subset of #$WorldWideWebPage-CW. Every instance of #$WorldWideWebHomePage-CW is the 'entrance' into a #$WorldWideWebSite. Visitors typically go to this page first, and navigate via hyperlinks from there to other pages in the site. The homepage usually has a simple URL of the form http://www.NAME.SUFFIX, where NAME is the one-word name of the site and SUFFIX is a suffix indicating the nature or geographical location of the site. Common suffixes include 'com' (commercial), 'edu' (educational), 'gov' (government), and 'org' (non-profit organization). original comment by Kathy Burns")
(comment CycloneAsObject "A collection of swirling high-speed wind storm, usually accompanied by heavy rains.  Subsets of this concept include #$HurricaneAsObject, #$TornadoAsObject, and tropical storm.  The word \"cyclone\" also has the narrower meaning of a #$HurricaneAsObject situated in the #$IndianOcean or #$CoralSea.")
(comment Urethra "Urethras -- canal that carries urine from the bladder out the body")
(comment Pointer-TheDog "A collection of medium-sized to large dogs with short, thick fur.")
(comment BangladeshPerson "The collection of people who are either #$citizens of #$Bangladesh, or participants in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup EnergyOrganization)
(comment SpaceProbe "These are unmanned vehicles which are sent to other bodies in the Solar System

for the purpose gathering data. Sometimes a separate vehicle is launched from the main vehicle,

the smaller vehicle usually being referred to as a probe. In these cases, both vehicle

would be #$SpaceProbes in the present sense.")
(comment InferiorLingularSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all inferior lingular segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of left #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a left #$SuperiorLobeOfLung, that supplies air to a #$InferiorLingularSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung in the #$SuperiorLobeOfLung. It branches from the #$LingularBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.  (These segments and bronchi do not exist in right #$Lungs.)")
(comment SmallApplianceBattery "Small batteries uses for appliances.  AAA, AA, A, B, C, D, 9V ")
(comment Cochlea "The collection of all cochlea.  Each #$Cochlea is a tube (#$AnatomicalVessel)that is part of an #$InnerEar which spirals through a #$TemporalBone.  Hairs in a #$Cochlea detect sound.")
(comment Arrowroot-Starch "Quantities of starch extracted from the rhizomes of #$ArrowrootPlant.")
(comment RetailStore-ParentCompany "A collection of businesses; a subset of #$ChainOrganization.  An element of #$RetailStore-ParentCompany is a multi-location business with branches or franchises which are (all or mostly) retail stores; e.g., KMart or Penneys.  This is distinct from chain service businesses, such as H&R Block and JiffyLube, as well as from single-site retail businesses.")
(comment ComputerProgramTypeByDistribution "A collection of collections.  Instances are subcollections of #$ComputerProgram-CW,

faceted by their method(s) of distribution.")
(comment Buffet-PieceOfFurniture "A piece of furniture which typically stores table settings - such as plates, silverware and tablecloths.")
(comment Ingesting "A specialization of #$BiologicalIntakeEvent.  Each instance of #$Ingesting is a complex process in which a thing is brought into some organism's mouth from the outside, is swallowed, and is moved to the organism's stomach.  Every instance of #$Ingesting has among its #$subEvents an instance of #$Swallowing which occurs after the intake (thus, although a particular chewing of gum is a #$BiologicalIntakeEvent, it is not an #$Ingesting unless the gum is swallowed.)  An ingesting event ends when the ingested stuff reaches the ingester's stomach (where an instance of #$DigestionEvent begins, provided that what was ingested is an instance of #$EdibleStuff).")
(disjointWith DishRag DishTowel)
(comment unauthorizedUserOfAccount "A predicate relating instances of #$IntelligentAgent with
instances of #$UserAccount.
(#$unauthorizedUserOfAccount AGENT ACCOUNT) means that AGENT is an
not an authorized user for ACCOUNT, or (#$not (#$groupMembers
(#$AccessorFn ACCOUNT) AGENT)).")
(comment IntraBuildingTransportationDevice "Devices used to move people or goods within a building")
(comment HaploidCell "A specialization of #$EukaryoticCell.  Each instance of #$HaploidCell is a cell which has a single chromosome set.  For example, gametes such as sperm and ova are haploid cells (see #$Gamete).  There also haploid forms of some mature multicellular organisms.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterD "The lowercase letter 'd'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$D-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterD.")
(comment LuggageSpaceInAVehicle "This could be, for instance, the trunk of a car, the luggage compartment of a bus, the little area behind the back seats in hatchbacks, etc.")
(comment DailyPersonalCleaning "A collection of events.  Each #$DailyPersonalCleaning encompasses the standard cleaning and grooming activities that an animal engages in over the course of a day.  Such a `daily routine' is almost sure to include many brief grooming and cleaning actions, such as licking one's paws, combing one's hair, washing one's hands, shaving, bathing, etc., and those are sub-events of that #$DailyPersonalCleaning event.  For example, a human's #$DailyPersonalCleaning might have a #$TeethCleaning as one of its sub-events, along with a #$TakingABath, two instances of #$CombingHair, etc.  
Note:  Those specialized kinds of events, like #$CombingHair, are NOT subsets of #$DailyPersonalCleaning, since it would be abnormal for someone to JUST comb their hair each day (and do absolutely no other daily cleaning activity whatsoever).
Note:  In the context #$HumanActivitiesMt --- where all the performers of actions are, by default, human beings --- #$DailyPersonalCleaning designates human grooming activities only.  In that microtheory, dog-grooming performed by human beings does not constitute #$DailyPersonalCleaning, even if it happens on a daily basis for some pampered poodle, as it is not PERSONAL (i.e, self-) cleaning.")
(disjointWith OrganizationByEntityType PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment BlackFootedFerret "A wild species in the Weasel Family (#$Mustelidae), native to #$ContinentOfNorthAmerica.  The #$BlackFootedFerret inhabits the Great Plains and is now extremely rare. Its range nearly coincides with that of prairie dogs, which constitute most of its diet. It is often found in prairie dog burrows.")
(disjointWith PrimaryDomainController NTWorkstation)
(comment CommodityProduct "Commodities are those products for which the only relevant data are the quantity and the price (and possibly the location).  That is, their quality is completely specified or describable in standardized terminology.  Thus, fashion clothing is not a commodity, since opinions on it vary, whereas grade A extra large eggs are.  The collection of all eggs is covered by various collections that are commodities, but is not itself an instance of commodity.")
(comment DorsalRamusS4 "The collection of all S4 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiS4 and DorsalRamiS4 branch from SpinalRootS4.  DorsalRamiS4 supplies the skin over the coccyx.")
(comment BirthdayCake "The collection of #$BirthdayCakes. These are cakes served in honor of soomeone's birthday. They are often elaborately decorated, and may have a birthday message written on them in frosting.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity Washing)
(comment Suppository "An object composed of a substance which is hard at room temperature, but soft at body temperature, and which is inserted into either the anus or the vagina where its contents are absorbed.")
(comment BiologicalSubphylum "A collection of #$BiologicalTaxons that is more restrictive than #$BiologicalPhylum.  All instances of a particular #$BiologicalSubspecies have significant traits or collections of traits in common which are not shared by all other members of the same #$BiologicalPhylum.")
(comment BodyArt "A collection of items that decorate the #$Skin or other surface of the body (e.g. #$Tongue).  Types of #$BodyArt include #$Tattoos, #$PiercedBodyParts, #$Bodypaint applied to #$Skin, and scarring (a type of #$Tattoo).")
(disjointWith SilverwarePiece GraspingImplement)
(comment CitrusFruit "The collection of individual citrus fruits.")
(comment GuatemalanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Guatemala, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SubscriptionToFn "This function takes as its argument any
 instance of #$PeriodicalSeries and returns
 the collection of #$PeriodicalSubscriptions to that
 #$PeriodicalSeries.  For example,
 (#$SubscriptionToFn #$SportsIllustrated-TheMagazine)
 is the collection of subscriptions to 
 Sports Illustrated.")
(comment ToyBalloon "A inflatable rubber bag used as toys.")
(comment Flatulence "Slang: passing gas")
(comment BakingFood "A specialization of #$CookingFood.  Each instance of #$BakingFood is an event during which which food is baked in an instance of #$RegularOven.  After an event of #$BakingFood occurs, the food involved has been baked (see #$Baked).")
(disjointWith BabyWalker Wagon)
(comment IntelligentComputerProgram "The collection of programs whose running copies can act as agents in a limited capacity.  They can be atomic or a collection of cooperating sub-programs, which may be loosely or tightly coupled.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup GovernmentOwnedCompany)
(comment SolarPanel "Device consisting of an array of photovoltaic cells, designed to produce electrical current when illuminated by sunlight.  Since sigle solar cells often do not produce enough current to power devices, they are arrnaged in panels.  The current produced by an array is a linear function of the number of cells.")
(disjointWith Trunk-BodyCore ExternalEar)
(comment CarinaTracheae "The collection of all Carinae (keel-shaped ridges of cartilage) that are each naturally located at the #$TracheobronchialJunction of an #$AirBreathingVertebrate, splitting the left #$MainBronchus from the right #$MainBronchus.  Lung cancer often originates there.")
(comment Each-NLAttr "The attribute value carried by utterances of the form \"each XXX\".")
(comment TeddyBear "A stuffed bear.")
(comment LifeStageType "A collection of collections and a specialization of  #$ExistingObjectType. Each instance of #$LifeStageType is a collection all of whose instances are organisms that share a specific variety and level of biological and/or social development.  For example, one instance of #$LifeStageType is the collection #$HumanChild, which has as its instances all human children.  Other instances of #$LifeStageType include #$Larva, #$FloweryPlant, and (#$BacterialSporeFn #$Anthrax-Bacterium).")
(comment CreatingAFile "#$CreatingAFile is the collection of actions done by            computers to generate instances of #$ComputerFileCopy. In            each instance of #$CreatingAFile, a computer stores           information on an instance of #$InformationStorageMedia.")
(comment JumperCables "Wires used to connect the batteries of two cars. ")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity FaceToFacePresenceCommunicating)
(disjointWith HittingAnObject PullingAnObject)
(comment Spouting "Exhaling through a blowhole done by cetaceans")
(comment deviceControlledBy "This predicate relates physical devices to the devices that control them.  (#$deviceControlledBy DEV CONTROL) means that CONTROL controls DEV.  Most of the time, the controls will be #$physicalParts of the device.  However there are some notable exceptions --  TV remote controls, for example -- which control a device but are not #$physicalParts of that device.")
(comment EnglishSpringerSpaniel "A collection of medium-sized dogs with long ears and a long coat.  His            colors are usually either liver and white or black and white.")
(comment Duke "The collection of all dukes, or male persons who hold hereditary ducal titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch.  This excludes a #$GrandDuke-HeadOfState.  See also #$Duchess.")
(disjointWith StorageOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment PhonographRecord-LP "The collection of long-playing #$PhonographRecords.  They are designed to be played at 33 1/3 rpm.")
(comment ExtensorPollicisBrevis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExtensorPollicisBrevis #$Muscle.  The #$ExtensorPollicisBrevis extends the #$ProximalPhalanx of the #$Thumb.")
(comment ComputerTable-PieceOfFurniture "The collection of tables or desks specifically designed to hold a computer.")
(comment IntercostalMuscle "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExternalIntercostal, #$InternalIntercostal  #$InnermostIntercostal #$Muscle.  An #$IntercostalMuscle is one of three muscles which connect two adjacent ribs.  It elevates the ribs during inspiration and helps maintain the intercostal space.")
(comment ColaFlavoring "instances are pieces of a compound with a flavor like cola nuts, used mostly in soft drinks.")
(comment ManagedCareCustomers-MarketingOrganization "A marketing organization that is assigned to some number of managed care organizations.")
(comment HKLM-SOFTWARE-Microsoft-Windows-CurrentVersion-RunOnceEx-Directory "An #$NTStandardFileType.  The #$Collection of all
HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnceEx directories
(instances of #$ExecutableRegistryKey) found on #$NTMachines.")
(comment GraphicalUserInterfaceProgram "Software that provides a graphical interface to a program.")
(comment MedicalPad "The collection of medical pads.  A medical pad is a thin layer of gauze used to cover and protect an injury to the skin.")
(comment NonPublishedText "A specialization of #$TextualMaterial, and thus of #$InformationBearingObject (IBO). Each instance of this collection is (a physical copy of) a text that has not yet been published. It may have been rejected for publication (e.g. a rejected book manuscript) or it may not be intended for publication (e.g. a memo or personal letter). It is, of course, disjoint with #$PublishedMaterial.")
(comment BileTheSecretion "A viscid alkaline fluid secreted by the liver and passed into the duodendum where it aids esp. in the absorption of fat. Not sure if ChemicalMixtureType is the correct place to put this.")
(comment awardWinners "(#$awardWinners COMPETITION AGENT) means that AGENT wins an award for performance in COMPETITION.  Typically awards are given to competitors in first, second and third place.  However, sometimes awards are given only to the first place contestant or in recognition of a unique and particular strength of a given contestant's performance (e.g. sometimes awards are given for `most original').  See also #$winner-First, #$competingAgents.")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject ProjectileLauncher)
(comment PapuaNewGuineaPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$PapuaNewGuinea, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment LanguageGroupingType "An instance of #$SecondOrderCollection, and a specialization of #$ObjectType.  Each instance of #$LanguageGroupingType is a subcollection of #$HumanLanguage (q.v.).")
(comment Hammock "A swinging couch or bed usually made of netting or canvas and slung by cords from supports at each end.")
(comment Swimming-Generic "Elements are instances of #$LocomotionProcess-Animal in which an #$Animal agent moves through water, typically by moving (some of) its appendages.")
(comment BrachialPlexus "The collection of all brachial nerve plexi located in #$Shoulders below/behind the #$Clavicle.  A #$BrachialPlexus is supplied by #$VentralRamusC5 - #$VentralRamusC8 and #$VentralRamusT1.  #$VentralRamusC4 and #$VentralRamusT2 are often included as suppliers to the #$BrachialPlexus but not always.  The ventral rami connect to create the #$SuperiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus, #$MiddleTrunk-BrachialPlexus, and #$InferiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus (also known as upper, middle, and lower branches).  Each of the 3 trunks then splits into anterior and posterior divisions.  The 6 trunk divisions then converge to form the #$PosteriorCord-BrachialPlexus, #$MedialCord-BrachialPlexus, and #$LateralCord-BrachialPlexus.  Most of the #$Nerves in the #$Arm are then formed from these cords.")
(comment Stew-Foodstuff "A thick soup filled with hunks of meat.")
(comment infoNeededForDeterminationOf "`(#$infoNeededForDeterminationOf INFO SENTENCE)' means that Cyc
does not currently know the truth value of INFO or of SENTENCE but does
know that knowing the truth value of INFO (or, if INFO is an open formula,
knowing what bindings there are for INFO) is part of what would establish
the truth and hence the assertibility of
SENTENCE. (infoNeededForDeterminationOf INFO SENTENCE) should imply that
(deservesFurtherInquiry SENTENCE). (See the comment on that constant). Note
that INFO might contain a free variable, since it might represent a
quantity whose value should be known. 
The main intended purpose for an assertion using
infoNeededForAssertionOf is to guide Cyc's behavior in interactive
contexts.")
(disjointWith PartOfRoomInAConstruction GutterSystem)
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure LocatingInIntendedPosition)
(comment StockCar "A racing car which is meant to appear like an American domestic sedan.  The NASCAR racing circuit races stock cars.")
(comment Extinction "This is the collection of events in which a species becomes extinct. Such events

would presumably include both the final cause of the extinction and the dying off of

the last members of the the species.")
(comment Biography "A collection of instances of #$PropositionalInformationThing.  Each instance of #$Biography is a narrative containing information about the life of some #$Person.")
(comment Eyelash "The little hairs that protrude from eyelids")
(disjointWith MedicalDevice FoodUtensil)
(comment Stamen "A stamen is the part of a flower which produces pollen.")
(comment EthiopianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Ethiopia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HearingAid "The collection of all #$PhysicalDevices that are used to aid in hearing.")
(comment ElectricHairShaver "The collection of electric devices intended for cutting hair.")
(comment PoliteSpeech-Activity "A specialization of #$Speaking. Each instance of this collection is speech of a form generally considered polite.")
(comment diastolicBloodPressure "ARG2 is the pressure exerted by ARG1's heart while resting between beats; this is the lower of the two values in a blood pressure.")
(disjointWith LightingStore AutoDealership)
(comment DrumHead "the membrane covering the cylinder portal of a drum.")
(disjointWith Cleaning Meeting-SocialGathering)
(comment CoffeeFilter "The filter which holds coffee grounds used to brew coffee.")
(comment Drink "A specialization of both #$FoodOrDrink and #$LiquidTangibleThing.  Each instance of #$Drink is a portion of a liquid of a type that is ingestible and commonly consumed by humans or animals.  Instances of #$Drink, unlike instances of #$Food (q.v.), are ingested by drinking without chewing.  Since soup and applesauce are normally ``eaten'' by being placed in the mouth with a spoon, they are not considered to be drunk (although one can certainly drink either), and so are not specializations of this collection.  Specializations of #$Drink include #$Water-Ingestible, #$Tea-Hot, #$HotChocolate, #$Lemonade, and #$Beer.")
(comment HangulCharacter "the squarish symbols of the Korean syllabary")
(comment MakingAnAudioRecording "A collection of processes in which sound-borne information is recorded--e.g., music, voice, utterances, whale songs.  The #$outputsCreated can be tapes, records, compact discs, etc.; the #$inputsCommitted include the blank media on which the recording was done.  The outputs are elements of #$AudioRecordedObject; mass-produced recordings belong to the more specialized collection #$RecordedSoundProduct.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent MakingFacialExpression)
(comment Intron-MolecularLariat "The output of the RNA splicing process
(#$RNASplicingProcess) by which snRNP enzymes act to excise introns
from a capped and polyadenylated RNA transcript.")
(comment AutomobileBattery "A specialization of #$AutoPart.  Each instance of #$AutomobileBattery is a battery intended to be used to provide electrical power to an instance of #$Automobile.")
(comment CockerSpaniel "A collection of relatively small dogs, also called the American Cocker Spaniel or simply the Cocker.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup JudicialOrganization)
(comment Solitaire-TheGem "The set of all pieces of jewelry consisting of a single
precious stone in some setting.")
(comment ThrowingADiscWithOnesToes "The collection of events in which a #$Person throws a #$FlyingDisc with his/her toes.  Such a throw is executed with a single foot and at least two toes.")
(comment TurningOnWater "The collection of events in which a tap is opened and water is permitted to flow through it.")
(comment DorsalRamusC7 "The collection of all C7 dorsal rami.  #$VentralRamusC7 and #$DorsalRamusC7 branch from SpinalRootC7.  #$DorsalRamusC7 supplies the #$Skin on the back (#$Back-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment SportsDrink "This is the collection of instances of sports drinks. These are drinks

which are generally fruit-flavored, contain nutritional sweeteners, and

chemical which provide the body with electrolytes.")
(comment NTMachine "The collection of all #$Computers that run (#$runsOS) some version of #$MSWindowsNT. Important specializations are #$Win2000Machine and #$XPMachine.")
(comment KnowledgeManagementProgram "The collection of all instances of Knowledge Management Software: software that gets the right knowledge sources (including documents and references to web pages and human experts) to the right person at the right time.  The definition of this is nebulous and controversial, but it includes at least all pieces of software which are (a.) marketed as 'Knowledge Management Software', and (b.) used to steer relevant documents to the people that need them.  Includes information retrieval software based on subject relevance metadata.")
(comment HDTVSet "High Definition Television sets")
(comment DepositSlip "A collection of #$InformationBearingObjects. The type of hardcopy or electronic document given to someone when they make a deposit at a bank, as a receipt that they did so.")
(comment Pinna "The collection of all pinnas.  Each member of this collection is the fleshy portion of an ear sticking out from a head.  In common parlance the term 'ear' normally refers merely to this portion of the ear.  Other medical terms for #$Pinna are 'auricle', 'auricula', and 'flap of the ear'.")
(disjointWith TextileArtifact ConsumableProduct)
(comment RadishPlant "A plant whose red root is eaten as a vegetable, usually raw, e.g. in salads, or as a garnish.")
(comment IvoryCoastPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$IvoryCoast, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SegaSaturn-TheProduct "This is the collection of Sega Saturn game platforms.")
(comment Six-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '5.'")
(comment IroquoianLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages of the eastern Great Lakes and southern Appalachian area")
(comment ScrubbingPad "Collection of rough sponges that are made to be used in scrubbing.")
(disjointWith Experimental Traditional)
(comment cruisingAltitude-Aircraft "(#$cruisingAltitude-Aircraft AIR ALT) means

  that when the #$AirTransportationDevice AIR is in flight,

   the range of cruising altitude is ALT -- a

 #$Distance above sea level.")
(comment SecurityProgram "An instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction.  Each instance of #$SecurityProgram is a computer program used to maintain, diagnose or otherwise safeguard the security of instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  Note that many instances of #$SecurityProgram can also be used to undermine the security of instances of #$ComputationalSystem.")
(comment PublicRelationsDepartment "Each instance of #$PublicRelationsDepartment consists of employees of an organization who are responsible for its public relations (cf. #$PublicRelationsActivity).")
(disjointWith Resting-Relaxing ProtectingSomething)
(comment SeltzerWater "Carbonated DrinkingWater")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice NavigationDevice)
(disjointWith SociabilityBasedAction PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment WebPage-CW "#$WebPage-CW is a specialization of #$ConceptualWork.  It is the collection of works designed to be accessed via an implementation of the #$HypertextTransferProtocol.  See also #$WorldWideWebPage-CW, the specialization of #$WebPage-CW that comprises the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource.")
(comment TapeFastForwardingProcess "The #$Collection of all #$TapeFastForwardingProcess events.  In each event an #$AudioTapePlayer-Recorder, #$VideoCassetteRecorder, #$AnsweringMachine, etc. fast-forwards a #$Tape (usually a #$MagneticTape).")
(comment WindstormAsObject "The collection of all storms with strong winds or violent gusts but without much rain.  Every instance of #$TornadoAsObject is considered a #$WindstormAsObject, while #$HurricaneAsObjects are not.")
(comment MarriageLicenseDocument "A marriage license - the document, not the agreement.")
(comment Eyebrow "Protective strips of hair over the eyes.")
(comment PortugueseWaterDog "A collection of medium-sized dogs.  Able to swim and dive well.")
(comment BarbadosPerson "This is the collection of people who are either #$citizens of #$Barbados, or participants in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization EnergyOrganization)
(comment LateralSegmentalBronchusOfMiddleLobeOfLung "The collection of all lateral segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of right #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a (right) #$MiddleLobeOfLung that supplies the #$LateralSegmentOfMiddleLobeOfLung.  It branches from the (right-side only) #$MiddleLobarBronchus.  (There is no #$LateralSegmentalBronchusOfMiddleLobeOfLung in the left #$Lung.)")
(comment HouseholdPaint "Paint used for painting walls, furniture, house exteriors, etc.  It can be either oil-based or water-based.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity CandyMaking)
(comment SemiCircularCanal "The collection of all semicircular canals of #$Ears.  Each member of this collection is a tube in an #$InnerEar that arches through a space in a #$TemporalBone.  Sensations ofhead rotation are detected by the movement of hairs in the #$SemiCircularCanals.")
(comment Fudge "A very sweet soft chocolate candy.")
(comment RetailOrganization "A collection of organizations.  Each instance of #$RetailOrganization is an organization that engages primarily in selling goods or services to end-users or consumers, rather than to wholesale customers. Specializations of #$RetailOrganization include the collections #$RetailStore and #$AutoDealership.")
(comment MarketedComputerProgram "A subset of #$ComputerProgram-CW whose instances have physical instantiations

that are sold as products.  It's not the instances themselves that are sold

as products, because the instances are intangible.")
(comment StageForIndoorPerformances "Part of a public building where performances (e.g some entertainment performances, religious ceremonies, etc) take place. A stage is the entire space between its floor and its ceiling, and should include the lighting, stage supports (if any), etc. Some stages are simply a 

raised portion of the #$FloorInAConstruction.")
(comment Gargoyle-Spout "The collection of ornamental spouts (typically grotesque representations of humans or animals or demons) commonly known as gargoyles")
(comment SystemAccountForNT "An instance of #$SystemAccountForNT is an account

normally used by programs under #$MSWindowsNT.  It is not typically

the kind of account to which a user could log in.  Programs that use

the System account operate usually a higher level of privilege than

the users who run the programs.")
(comment hasAccessToInformation "(#$hasAccessToInformation AGENT INFO) means that PERSON \"has access\" to INFO in the epistemic sense.  This is the relation that holds between someone who is reading a copy of #$MobyDickNovel and the #$AbstractInformationStructure instantiated by that copy, as well as the relation that holds between the reader and the propositional content (i.e., an instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing) of the book, given that the reader understands what she is reading.  In some cases (notably those in which INFO is an instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing) (#$hasAccessToInformation AGENT INFO) will imply that AGENT thereby #$knows some bit of information.")
(comment FerrisWheel "Ferris wheels that you'd find at a carnival or amusement park.")
(disjointWith Primate HerdAnimal)
(comment LatinCapitalLetterE "The capital letter 'E'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$E-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterE.")
(comment Tachometer "A device for measuring rotational frequency (usually in rpm).")
(comment ComputerGameController "This is the collection of input devices designed to allow video game players

to have greater control over their games.  Most game controllers have a

main four-way lever to control direction as well as assorted buttons and

such which can control other functions such as weapon choice. Controllers

designed for use with driving games have steering wheels rather than levers

for direction control.")
(disjointWith OrganizationByEntityType PersonTypeByPositionInOrg)
(comment NuclearReactorHardware "An #$ExistingObjectType, and a subset of #$NuclearProduct.  The collection of all specialized hardware items required for the operation of #$NuclearReactors.")
(comment PrimaryDomainController "An #$NTDomain is a #$AccountSystem consisting of a group of #$NTWorkstations, one #$PrimaryDomainController (PDC), and one or more #$BackupDomainControllers (BDCs).  The PDC houses the #$PasswordFile containing all usernames and passwords for #$UserAccounts on the domain.  #$BackupDomainControllers handle the actual authentication when someone logs on to the domain, and for that purpose they also keep copies of the #$PasswordFile (see #$SAMFile).  However, since all changes to account information on the domain need to be made to the password file on the PDC, the BDCs need to communicate with the PDC periodically to update their copies of the #$PasswordFile.")
(comment Electricity "The sort of energy that flows through electrical conductors, is produced by electrical generators, etc.")
(comment VentralRamusS3 "The collection of all S3 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusS3 and #$DorsalRamusS3 branch from SpinalRootS3.  #$VentralRamusS3 supplies the #$SacralPlexus.")
(comment BridesCake "The collection of #$BridesCakes. These are cakes served at a wedding reception. #$BridesCakes are usually white and more elaborate than the corresponding #$GroomsCake, if both happen to be served at a reception.")
(comment interArgDisjoint "(#$interArgDisjoint RELN ARG-1 ARG-2) states that well-formed uses of the relationship RELN have disjoint terms in  argument positions number ARG-1 and ARG-2. For example, (#$interArgDisjoint #$complementOfIn 1 2) enforces the constraint that two complementary collections are disjoint.  (#$interArgDisjoint RELN ARG-1 ARG-2) is short-hand for (#$interArgReln-Inferred RELN ARG-1 ARG-2 #$disjointWith).")
(disjointWith ProgramAction-HumanInitiated (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(comment MedicalDrugImplant "A device which is surgically placed inside the body, and which releases a substance directly into the bloodstream in a controlled fashion.")
(comment Prion "The collection of #$Prions (proteinaceous infective
particles). Suggested as the causative agents of several infectious
diseases such as scrapie (in sheep), kuru and Creutzfeld Jakob disease in
man. Apparently contain no nucleic acid. The 27 kD protein of scrapie is
related to a normal cell protein and may possibly cause its over
production.")
(comment PiercedBodyPart "A collection of holes in visible body parts (see #$OrganismPart, #$ExternalAnatomicalPart, and #$visibleParts) produced by #$BodyPartPiercing events.  Each element of #$PiercedBodyPart is designed for the insertion of an instance of #$Jewelry.")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice ControlDevice)
(comment BlackPepperVine "Individual black pepper vines; fruits, when harvested and dried, are peppercorns.")
(comment LuxembourgPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Luxembourg, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SpeakerStand "The collection of speaker stands. These are stands which hold speakers

at a desired height and angle off the floor.")
(comment MoppingAFloor "The collection of all floor mopping events")
(comment HeatingFood "A specialization of #$HeatingProcess and #$PreparingFoodItem.  Each instance of #$HeatingFood is an event in which the temperature of an instance of #$Food is intentionally increased.")
(comment OrgRelatedFn "#$OrgRelatedFn takes as argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the collection of all organizations directly related to that thing.  Relevant forms of relation include being formed around a (positive or negative) interest in that thing.  For example, (#$OrgRelatedFn #$Marxism-Leninism) returns the collection of all organizations related directly to Marxist-Leninist beliefs (pro- or con-), and (#$OrgRelatedFn #$UniversityOfTexasAtAustin) returns the collection of organizations related directly to the main branch of the University of Texas (including alumni organizations and the University itself).")
(disjointWith Bicycle BabyWalker)
(comment TypesettingProgram "Document preparation systems for high-quality typesetting.  These programs interpret or compile files written in a typesetting language to produce professional-looking documents.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup RevoltOrganization)
(comment GyroCompass "A compass that uses a gyroscope instead of a magnet to indicate the direction of true north rather than magnetic north.")
(disjointWith ExternalNose Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment AlveolarDuct "The collection of all alveolar ducts of the #$Lung, each being the small, final passage for inhaled air between a #$RespiratoryBronchiole and an #$Alveolus.  The walls of an AlveolarDuct consist mainly of alveoli used directly for #$RespiratoryGasExchange in #$Respiration.")
(comment Every-NLAttr "The attribute value carried by utterances of the form \"every XXX\" or \"all XXX\".")
(comment MustardGas "A collection.  This gas is produced by an oily, volatile liquid, (CH2ClCH2)2S.  The gas causes blistering chemical burns on human skin and is used in warfare to disable troops.")
(comment ComputerProgram-CWIS "The collection of all #$ComputerCode that corresponds to a complete #$ComputerProgram-CW.")
(comment SilverMedal-Physical "Physical silver medals of the type awarded in competitions.")
(comment Feather "Light horny epidermal outgrowth that forms the external covering of birds.")
(disjointWith NavalShipBase AirForceBase-Grounds)
(comment ClumberSpaniel "A collection of medium-sized dogs with thick, white coats.")
(comment Duchess "The collection of all duchesses, or female persons who hold hereditary ducal titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch (whether in their own right, by marriage or by courtesy).  This excludes a Grand Duchess.  See also #$Duke.")
(disjointWith SocialOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment PhonographRecord-45 "The collection of #$PhonographRecords containing (normally) a single song on each side.  They are designed to be played at 45 #$RevolutionsPerMinute.")
(comment AbductorDigitiMinimi "The #$Collection of all instances of #$AbductorDigitiMinimi #$Muscle.  The #$AbductorDigitiMinimi abducts the #$LittleFinger away from the other #$Fingers parallel to the #$PalmOfHand.")
(comment passengerCompartments "Relates a transportation device to that part of it in which people can be carried.  The passenger compartment often includes solid objects such as seats, floors, window shades as well as non-solid objects such as a cavity.  One open question is whether such a compartment includes windows or just the inside surface of windows.")
(comment MainLungSurface "The collection of (named) surface areas of #$Lungs: curved concave or convex areas between the angular edges (margins 'corners' or 'crests') of #$Lungs which divide the overall lung surface into different major areas.")
(comment HotChocolate "Quantities of the beverage made by mixing cocoa powder with hot milk.")
(comment NewAutoDealerPartsDepartment "The parts department of a new car dealership.")
(comment DevelopmentProgram "Software which is used to create other software.  Instances would be programs like 'Microsoft Visual C++', 'PowerBuilder', 'Oracle Forms', 'GNU C'.")
(comment Teardrop "The fluid excreted from the eyes")
(comment contenders "(#$contenders COMP AGENT) indicates that AGENT, a competing agent in the #$Competition COMP, is considered by anyone who is knowledgeable about the competition to have a good possibility of winning.")
(comment CambodianPerson "A person who is a citizen of #$Cambodia, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment FoodOrDrinkForFn "A unary function that takes as an argument a specialization of #$Organism-Whole, ORG, and returns returns the collection of all substances that can be and normally are consumed and successfully metabolized by typical instances of ORG.  Thus (#$FoodOrDrinkForFn #$Horse) returns the collection of all substances that can be and normally are consumed and metabolized by \"normal\" horses, etc., including instances of #$Hay and #$Water. A given specialization of #$FoodOrDrink may be normal food for more than one specialization of #$Organism-Whole. For instance, #$Water is a normal drink for virtually every kind of organism on Earth.")
(comment Chain "A type of cord consisting of metal links.")
(comment Mounting-Sitting "Getting up onto something--often, but not always, for riding.")
(comment ownershipTakeableBy "(#$ownershipTakeableBy COPY ACCT) means that someone logged in under
ACCT may take ownership of COPY.")
(disjointWith CommercialOrganization NonProfitOrganization)
(comment Methane "CH4. A combustible gas produced either synthetically or by decomposing plant and animal matter. The main component of #$NaturalGas.")
(comment HarpBeer "A popular type of lager.")
(comment SacralPlexus "The collection of all sacral plexi. A #$SacralPlexus is part of a #$LumboSacralPlexus and is usually supplied by #$VentralRamusL4, #$VentralRamusL5, #$VentralRamusS1, #$VentralRamusS2, #$VentralRamusS3, and #$VentralRamusS4.")
(comment Soup "The food soup.")
(comment RiverBoat "A large boat usually used on rivers which has a large paddle wheel at the back to push it forward.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess Mounting-Installing)
(comment ComputerMemoryCapacity "A specialization of #$PhysicalQuantity. Each instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity is a measure (for the range of possible units of this measure, see the collection #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity) of the amount of information that can be stored on some computer. It includes measures of #$RAM, #$ROM and #$VirtualMemory. For making assertions of a particular #$Computer that it has a particular #$ComputerMemoryCapacity, see the predicates #$physicalMemorySize and #$virtualMemorySize.")
(comment Dragster "Race cars specifically designed to be drag-raced; very fast for a short distance in an exact straight line.")
(comment Apoptosis "This is the collection of events in which cells, in a sense,

commit suicide. It is often called programmed cell death.")
(comment RecipeCopy "A collection of textual #$InformationBearingThings.  Each instance of #$RecipeCopy contains as information some instance of #$Recipe-CW (a list of ingredients or components needed and instructions on how to combine them to produce an edible product).  Instances of #$Recipe-CW have in common a distinct literary form, recognizable by most people as that of a recipe.")
(comment MammaryGland "The collection of all #$Glands which produce #$Milk in female #$Mammals.  An individual #$MammaryGland is an internal part (#$internalParts) of a #$Teat.")
(disjointWith FoodUtensil Paddle-Water)
(comment Ovary-PlantPart "Do not confuse with #$Ovary-AnimalBodyPart. An ovary is the basal part of a plant's carpel which contains ovules; in angiosperms it developes into fruit.")
(comment SouthGeorgiaIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$SouthGeorgia-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic)
(comment HearingAid-NonPrescription "#$HearingAid-NonPrescription is a collection of #$HearingAid devices that are not for the severely impaired. Things to improve hearing while bird watching would fall in this collection,")
(comment HairCuttingRazor "Collection of thick razors used for human head hair cutting at certain HairSalons.")
(comment systolicBloodPressure "ARG2 is the pressure exerted by ARG1's heart while pumping the blood; this is the higher of the two values in a blood pressure.")
(comment subOrgs-AdministrativeServiceSupport "(#$subOrgs-AdministrativeServiceSupport SUPER SUB) means that SUB is in an organizational relationship with SUPER in which SUPER is ordinarily responsible for providing most of the administrative services or 'service support' for SUB's activities, and SUB depends on SUPER for this support.  Such support may include engineering, programming, legal, personnel, or religious services, or SUB's primary planning, analysis, or advice.  (Different organizations may supply material goods or money, or may have command over SUB. These are not necessarily indicated by this predicate.)  For example, if a military field reconnaissance unit ordinarily calls upon another unit for most administrative support services --e.g., for maintenance, programming computers, legal issues, personnel management, etc.-- then the engineering unit has the reconnaissance unit as one of its #$subOrgs-AdministrativeServiceSupport dependents.  Similarly, if a company COMP offers its legal department's advice and health coverage to a research team TEAM from a university, then (#$subOrgs-AdministrativeServiceSupport COMP TEAM) is true, even if money for the team's salaries comes from the university.  (See also #$subOrgs-Financial, #$subOrgs-MaterialSupport, and #$subOrgs-Command.)")
(comment satisfiesStandard "The predicate #$satisfiesStandard is used to identify a product standard that applies to a certain type of products.  (#$satisfiesStandard PRODTYPE STAND) means that every instance of the #$FormalProductType PRODTYPE satisfies the #$ProductStandard STAND.  STAND will contain a description of the desired physical form and/or function for the type of product (or service) denoted by PRODTYPE, and the instances of PRODTYPE fulfill those specifications.  See also #$ProductStandard.")
(comment ComputerFileCopy-VirusInfected "The collection of all #$ComputerFileCopys that are infected by a computer virus.")
(disjointWith LiquorStore AutoDealership)
(disjointWith PhysicalCollectionEvent IBTGeneration)
(comment roleTypeDependsOnRoleType "(#$roleTypeDependsOnRoleType COLTYPE1 ROLE1 COLTYPE2 ROLE2 EVENTTYPE) means that an instance of an instance, INS1, of COLTYPE1 plays ROLE1 and that an instance of an instance, INS2, of COLTYPE2 plays ROLE2 in instances of EVENTTYPE.  However, and more importantly, the instance of COLTYPE1 of which  INS1 is a member plays a role in determining of which instance of COLTYPE2 INS2 will be an instance.  For instance,  (#$roleTypeDependsOnRoleType PersonByReligiousDenomination #$socialParticipants       ChurchBuildingByDenominationType       #$eventOccursAt #$Worshipping) means that the religious denomination of a person explains or determines the kind of church building, faceted by denomination type, in which the person will worship.")
(comment ZipperTheFastener "Any kind of zipper.")
(comment PandaBear "A specialization of #$Eutheria.  Commonly known as the Giant Panda. Pandas are not bears, despite superficial appearances.")
(comment FrakturLetter "The old-time fancy style of German print, sometimes called 'gothic'")
(comment WoodenPencil "The pencil that we use to write on paper.")
(comment CumulativeEventType "A collection of collections. Each instance of an instance of #$CumulativeEventType is an event. Moreover, each instance of #$CumulativeEventType is a collection with the following property of 'cumulativity': if PROCESS-COL is an instance of #$CumulativeEventType, and PROCESS-1 and PROCESS-2 are instances of PROCESS-COL, then the minimal event containing PROCESS-1 and PROCESS-2 (that is, (#$EventSumFn PROCESS-1 PROCESS-2)) is also an instance of PROCESS-COL.")
(disjointWith MakingFacialExpression MakingSomething)
(comment Poodle "A collection of small to medium-sized dogs.  Poodles come in three different sizes:           the toy poodle is less than ten inches tall (at the withers), the miniature poodle          (also called the mini poodle) is between ten and fifteen inches, and the standard           poodle is taller than fifteen inches.")
(comment Firewall-Network "A specialization of #$Computer and of #$SinglePurposeDevice. Each instance of this collection is a dedicated hardware machine designed to run #$FirewallPrograms in order to increase the security of a #$ComputerNetwork by filtering out incoming packets (see #$Packet-Network) according to specific rules.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization JudicialOrganization)
(comment Stencil-TheImplement "A #$Stencil-TheImplement is a template made of a flat sheet of stiff
material, with holes in particular shapes.  When the stencil is
placed against a surface, and paint, pencil, or other pigment is
applied through one of more of the holes, markings in the shape of
each of the holes is left behind on the surface.")
(comment SouthernItalianCuisine "A style of #$ItalianCuisine associated with southern Italy.")
(comment TurningOffWater "The collection of events in which a tap is closed and water can no longer flow through it.")
(comment RadialNerve "The collection of all radial nerves.  The radial nerve is formed by the #$PosteriorCord-BrachialPlexus.  The radial nerve runs from the brachial plexus down through the arm to the wrist.  It does not directly supply any part of the arm.  It has many branches that supply various regions of the arm and hand.")
(comment Scone "This is the collection of scones. Scones are rich biscuit-like baked goods,

originally British, which may include currents, raisins, or other fruit.

In Britian they are served with tea, here they are more likely to be eaten

at breakfast.")
(comment CycLSentence-ClosedPredicate "The subcollection of #$CycLSentences whose arg0 does not contain a free variable although free variables may occupy other argument positions.")
(comment OpticalCharacterRecognition "A collection of all events in which a hardcopy text is automatically            converted to digital form.")
(comment WithdrawalSlip "A collection of #$InformationBearingObjects. A instance of #$WithdrawalSlip is a form [#$Form-StandardizedIBO] filled out by a person making a withdrawal from a bank, requesting the specifics of that withdrawal.")
(comment OvalWindowInEar "The collection of all vestibular windows which separate #$MiddleEars from #$InnerEars.  Each instance of this collection is an oval #$Portal from a #$MiddleEar into an #$InnerEar which is closed by the base of the #$Stapes.  Medical terms for the #$OvalWindowInEar include 'oval window', 'vestibular window', 'fenestra ovalis', and 'fenestra vestibuli'.")
(comment ConiferopsidaClass "A #$BiologicalClass within the #$GymnospermGroup in the plant kingdom which contains the #$Conifer taxa, such as species of #$PineTree, #$SpruceTree, sequoia, etc.")
(comment MonacanPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Monaco, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment WatchguardFirebox2-Network "Watchguard's popular firewall for networks.")
(comment Sixteen-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '16.'")
(comment JicaqueLanguageFamily "Amerindian language group of North America")
(comment RubberSpatula "A spatula whose head is made of rubber, used to scrape the inside of bowls.")
(comment (VersusFn ObjectType StuffType) "Note that specializations of instances of #$ObjectType need not themselves be instances of #$ObjectType, and some specializations of instances of #$StuffType need not themselves be instances of #$StuffType. For example, #$Event is an instance of #$TemporalStuffType, but some specializations of #$Event, such as #$LunarRoundTrip, are instances of #$TemporalObjectType.  #$Events qua #$Events are temporally stuff-like, but #$Events qua $LunarRoundTrips are temporally object-like. To put it another way, if one cuts an #$Event in half into two time slices, one is left with two things which are themselves #$Events. On the other hand, if one cuts a #$LunarRoundTrip in half, one is left with two objects that are *not* #$LunarRoundTrips. Those two time slice objects are, however, #$Events.")
(comment RaisingAnArm "Actions of lifting one's own arm.")
(comment PopularMusicBand "The collection of all instances of #$Band-MusicGroup that have had a \"hit\" on the pop charts at some time or other.  By definition, such bands are professional bands and are not merely

 bands that play a particular genre of music.")
(comment Primer-Molecule "The collection of #$Molecules used as primers in a chemical reaction. It may be that the only application for this concept is to #$RNAMolecules. During #$Replication-DNA, primase synthesizes a short length of an #$RNAMolecule, which is base-paired to the DNA template strand. The RNA strand serves as a primer by providing a 3' end as a starting point for #$DNAPolymerase to synthesize the new #$DNAStrand complementary to the template strand.")
(comment ProgrammingLanguageImplementation "A specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  Each instance of #$ProgrammingLanguageImplementation is a program which takes source code written in an #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage as input and generates either the behavior specified by the sdource code (if the #$ProgrammingLanguageImplementation is an instance of the more specialized collection #$Interpreter-Computers) or another program with the same semantics as the source code (if the #$ProgrammingLanguageImplementation is an instance of the more specialized collection #$Compiler).")
(comment ProductionDepartment "The collection of departments whose direct (main) function is the production/manufacture of some kind of item.  Any given instance of #$ProductionDepartment will be a suborganization of some larger organization.")
(comment Walker-SupportDevice "A device used to help old or disabled people to walk, by giving them something to lean on while they step and/or rest between steps.")
(comment Brain "A specialization of #$InternalOrgan and instance of #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType.  Each instance of #$Brain is an organ that controls most bodily movement, receives sensory input from the body and objects outside the body, and also thinks (insofar as the organism that has the brain can be said to do so).")
(comment CuttingAPieceOfFood "This is the collection of actions in which the agent cuts food into pieces using an implement, that is, a knife or fork.  So, biting off a piece of food is not an instance; see #$Biting.")
(disjointWith CuttingDevice HeatingDevice)
(disjointWith PhysicalCollectionEvent PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment ComputerGameSeries "Elements of #$ComputerGameSeries are particular named series of computer games such as #$Quake-TheGameSeries. Each such element will have #$episodes that are #$ComputerProgram-CWs, such as #$QuakeII-TheGame.")
(comment TriggeringMechanism "A part of physical system that releases the potential energy stored in the system's configuration.  The triggering mechanism does not provide significant energy to the system.  Examples: a trigger on a gun, the triggering mechanism on a mouse trap, the shutter release on a camera.")
(disjointWith PipeFlow TransportationEvent)
(comment DiplomaDocument "A diploma - the document, not the achievement.")
(comment Bladder-Urinary "The collection of all urinary bladders.  An individual #$Bladder-Urinary is a part of a #$UrinarySystem which stores #$Urine prior to #$Urinating.")
(comment Puli "A collection of dogs.")
(comment BelgianPerson "The collection of people who are either #$citizens of #$Belgium, or participants in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ProfessionalAssociation FoodAndBeverageOrganization)
(comment Energy-Renewable "This is an #$EnergyType and a spec of #$EnergyStuff. It is the collection of instances of #$EnergyStuff which are derived from sources which are not depletable in the sense that they will likely be around about as long as we will be and our use

of these sources does not deplete them. Examples include solar-, wind-, and geothermal-derived energy. Non-instances most notably include energy derived from fossil fuels.

Energy derived from by-products of industrial or agricultural production should also

count as #$Energy-Renewable, because the use of these sources, unlike the burning of coal, does

not deplete a fixed finite store.")
(comment ApicoposteriorSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all apicoposterior segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of left #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a left #$SuperiorLobeOfLung that supplies the #$ApicoposteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung (the combined apical and posterior parts of the #$ApicoposteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung on the left side).  It branches from the #$SuperiorDivisionBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.")
(comment VideoAmplifierComponent "Electronic Device which amplifies electrical video signals.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single CandyMaking)
(comment DorsalRamus "The collection of all dorsal rami.  Each #$SpinalNerve branches into one #$DorsalRamus and one #$VentralRamus.  Each #$DorsalRamus #$innervates #$Muscles in the back (#$Back-AnimalBodyPart) as well as contains #$SensoryNerves for the #$Skin of the back.")
(comment PitaBread "The collection of all portions of pita bread, an unleavened Middle Eastern bread that is flat and round and has a 'pocket' inside it into which various things can be stuffed.")
(comment Wholesaler "A commercial organization that sells merchandise to other commercial organizations.  Typically, a wholesale store gets merchandise directly from the manufacturer, to be distributed in relatively very large quantities, for a relatively low unit price.  The buyer typically either resells the merchandise (e.g., to a retailer) or uses it as input to to a commercial manufacturing activity or some other commercial activity.")
(comment Skating "The collection of body movement events in which some sort of skate is used on the feet.")
(comment actorPartsInvolved "(#$actorPartsInvolved ACT PART) means that PART is one of the parts (see the predicate #$anatomicalParts) of an organism that is playing an active role (see the predicate #$doneBy and its specializations) in the event ACT, and, moreover, that PART is somehow involved in the event ACT.  Some examples of #$actorPartsInvolved include: the eyes of someone who is sneezing (or crying); the left foot of someone playing in a football game; the right hand of someone who is shaking hands; the claws of a cat who is scratching someone.  As a negative example, consider a person's hair when that person is getting a haircut.  The hair is not an #$actorPartsInvolved, because the person is passive in that event; it is, however, an #$actorPartsAffected (q.v.) in that event.")
(disjointWith Paper-IBO PrepaidTelephoneCard)
(comment Paint-Dry "The collection of all instances of all dried #$Paint.  Prototypical exemplars include dried paint on a surface.  Less common exemplars include a thick chunk of solid paint.  This does not include solid compounds designed to be mixed with a liquid (e.g. water) in order to make a paint.")
(comment SSHServerProgram "#$SSHServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the Secure Shell Protocol (SSH), which traditionally operates over TCP, port 22. A user can type 'ssh hostname 22' and

connect with an #$SSHServerProgram on hostname, if one is present.")
(comment EncryptedAIS "The collection of all #$AbstractInformationStructures which are, in the salient context, #$Encrypted.  Any assertion of the form (#$isa AIS #$EncryptedAIS) will be highly context-dependent, and no #$AbstractInformationStructure should be thought of as intrinsically #$Encrypted or #$Plaintext.  The character string 'The eagle has landed' might, in the context of two spies communicating, encrypt some information, but in another context it is simply a report that some eagle has landed.  It is inherently neither.  Whether, in a given context, it is one or the other will depend upon a great many facts (none of which are facts about the state of one's brain, nor of the state of some vaguely-conceived mental substance).")
(comment RollerCoaster "A train of cars that race at high speeds up and down hills on tracks.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterE "The lowercase letter 'e'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$E-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterE.")
(comment interArgNotIsa1-5 "(#$interArgNotIsa1-5 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the first argument to PRED, the fifth argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(comment AnophelesMosquito "The collection of anopheles mosquitos. Instances are mosquitoes belonging to the genus Anopheles. Many species in this genus are vector of malaria.")
(comment OpticalDrive "This is the collection of optical drives for computers.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType OrganizationByEntityType)
(comment NuclearServiceEvent "A subset of both #$ServiceEvent and #$NuclearProduct.  This collection comprises events involving technical assistance in the field of nuclear engineering.  Examples: operating a nuclear power plant, designing a nuclear warhead, or repairing a #$NuclearPoweredDevice.")
(comment Capybara "an aquatic rodent")
(comment DishDryingRack "A simple rack device on which to lean dishes while they dry in the air.")
(comment VentralRamusL3 "The collection of all L3 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusL3 and #$DorsalRamusL3 branch from SpinalRootL3.  #$VentralRamusL3 supplies the #$LumbarPlexus.")
(comment Cheesecake "The collection of #$Cheesecakes. These are rich, dense cakes atop a crumb crust, made with cream cheese and sometimes flavored with chocolate or fruit.")
(comment inTheSuburbOf "(#$inTheSuburbOf SUB CITY) means that SUB is in the suburban area of CITY. This #$BinaryPredicate relates an #$UrbanArea to the main city of which it is a suburb, see below. The notion of suburb can be difficult to delineate and would necessitate more work, see the #$cyclistNotes. The notion of suburb that this term assumes corresponds to the traditional definition of an area lying immediately outside a city of significant importance for the region it's located in. Because #$inTheSuburbOf relates a city and a part only of its suburb there is no clause of contiguity when applying this relation. The importance of the city can be evaluated in different ways corresponding for instance to the physical, historical, political, military properties of an area. Note additionally that while 'being in the suburb of' can be to some extend considered as an inheritable property, we chose to define #$inTheSuburbOf as functional in its second argument and an area can be in the suburb of only one city. Note also that this relation wouldn't be transitive if the first argument ranged on #$City and for instance, while (#$inTheSuburbOf #$JimsCity #$CityOfPasadenaCA) and (#$inTheSuburbOf #$CityOfPasadenaCA #$CityOfLosAngelesCA) we do not want to conclude (#$inTheSuburbOf #$JimsCity #$CityOfLosAngelesCA), we would use instead a more general relation and assert (#$inTheVicinityOf-Geographical #$JimsCity #$CityOfLosAngelesCA) in #$UnitedStatesGeographyDualistMt. Positive examples, both #$CityOfIvry-sur-SeineFrance and #$CityOfVillejuifFrance are in the suburb of #$CityOfParisFrance, the first one is spatially contiguous to Paris while the second isn't. Let's emphasize on the fact that while a city like Paris has many areas in its suburban area, each of these is in the suburb of one only, namely Paris.")
(comment ApplicationAccount "A person with an instance of #$ApplicationAccount is able to access a set of files associated with a computer application program.  The most notable subcollection of #$ApplicationAccount is #$FTPAccount, but there are many others.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity BiologicalProcess)
(comment InhalerDevice "The sort of container which is used to spray inhalants through the mouth to the bronchia.")
(comment Lesson-CW "The collection of all #$InstructionalWorks that present the material of a single #$Lesson to the #$recipientOfInfo.")
(comment Spitting "This is the collection of acts of forcibly expelling saliva or other liquid from the mouth; expectorating.")
(disjointWith DomesticatedAnimalFood Food-ReadyToEat)
(comment CucumberPlant "Individual cucumber plants")
(comment VolcanoIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$VolcanoIslands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AudioCrossover "This is the collection of crossovers. A crossover is a piece of #$AudioEquipment

designed to process audio signals in the frequency ranges where different

drivers have frequency overlaps.")
(comment CuttingBoard "The collection of all cutting boards -- movable flat surfaces, usually of wood or plastic, on which quantities of food can be cut up.")
(disjointWith CommunicationAct-Single GameEvent)
(comment Hiccoughing "The spasmodic inhaling of air. Note that inhaling is a subProcess and thereby cotemporal with this. This is just one hiccoughing event.  That they often occur in a series (as do #$Coughing, #$Sneezing, etc) is not yet expressed here.")
(disjointWith CerealFood Drink)
(comment powerInOrganization "#$powerInOrganization specifies the amount of influence or sway that AGENT has in ORG.  (#$powerInOrganization AGENT ORG GENERIC-VALUE) means that AGENT's level of influence in ORG is GENERIC-VALUE.")
(comment ArtificialIntelligenceProgram "Artificial intelligence programs are computer programs designed to perform extremely complex tasks such as common-sense reasoning, pattern recognition, natural language understanding, sophisticated game-playing, and medical diagnosis.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup ReviewCommittee)
(comment OperatingTable "The collection of tables used in Hospital Operating Rooms.")
(disjointWith Trunk-BodyCore Pubis)
(comment Bronchiole "The collection of all very small #$BronchialTubes found in the #$Lung, that are over (about) ten generations of division away from the primary bronchi, and which lack #$Cartilage in their walls.")
(comment BareForm-NLAttr "The attribute value carried by utterances without a determiner or quantifier, e.g. \"dogs\".")
(comment restrictsAsObligatedMeansOfLocomotion "(#$restrictsAsObligatedMeansOfLocomotion ORGTYPE CONTSTRAINTTYPE EVTTYPE ROLE) means that an organism pf type ORGTYPE who has CONSTRAINTTYPE as its #$obligatedMeansOfLocomotion is not capable, under ordinary circumstances, of playing ROLE in events of type EVTTYPE.")
(comment Lewisite "A chemical compound created for military use around the 

end of WWI. #$Lewisite acts as a vesicant, and is thus suited to chemical warfare. Industrially-produced lewisite has a strong

penetrating geranium odor; the pure compound is odorless.")
(comment AccessingAFile "The collection of actions done by computers in which a computer reads information from a file.")
(comment GoldMedal-Physical "Physical gold medals of the type awarded in competitions.")
(disjointWith TakingAStep ArmMovement)
(comment WakingUpFromSleep "The collection of events in which an #$Animal goes from the state of being asleep to being in a waking state.")
(comment imagePerspective "The visual image ARG1 depicts the object ARG2 in the perspective attribute ARG3.")
(disjointWith MarineBase-Grounds AirForceBase-Grounds)
(comment Whippet "A collection of fast, medium-sized dogs, capable of   reaching speeds up to 35 mph.  Sometimes called 'the poor man's race horse.'")
(comment Princess "The collection of all princesses, or female persons, whether sovereign or not, who hold hereditary princely titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch (whether in their own right, by marriage or by courtesy).  This excludes female Co-princes of #$Andorra.  See also #$Prince.")
(disjointWith WorkersOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment Armadillo "A collection of shy, armored mammals; their habitat ranges from the southern United States through South America.  There are twenty different species existing today.  The scientific name for this family is Dasypodidae.")
(comment InternalIntercostal "The #$Collection of all instances of #$InternalIntercostal #$Muscle.  An #$InternalIntercostal is the middle of three muscles which connect two adjacent ribs.  It elevates theribs during inspiration and helps maintain the intercostal space.")
(comment WasteConversionDevice "Devices used for the disposal of wastes or to convert them from one form to another")
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent BaseballInning)
(comment CostalSurfaceOfLung "The collection of costal (outer, ribcage) surface areas of #$Lungs.  Each CostalSurfaceOfLung faces the ribs, and is a convex, rounded, roughly triangular area between the #$PosteriorMarginOfLung, the #$AnteriorMarginOfLung, and the #$InferiorMarginOfLung.")
(comment Tea-Hot "Tea served hot.")
(comment NewAutoDealership "Organizations whose primary business is to sell new cars of a certain company. ")
(comment MultimediaProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs designed to manipulate audio-visual computer files.  Instances would be 'PowerPoint', 'Macromedia Shockwave'.")
(disjointWith TextualMaterial ArtGlass)
(comment LacrimalFluid "The collection of all lacrimal fluid.  Instances of this collection are secreted by #$TearGlands, lubricate an #$Eye, and when produced in too great a quantity may flow onto the face (#$FaceOfAnimal) as #$Teardrops.  #$LacrimalFluid contains salt water, Water-Saline, and antibiotic agents.")
(comment expectedWinner "(#$expectedWinner ?COMP ?AGENT) indicates that ?AGENT, a competing agent of ?COMP, is expected to win by anyone who has an interest in the competition")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject Tool)
(comment ParaguayanPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Paraguay, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment BateauMouche-Boat "The collection of boats that are used to tour the Seine, see #$BateauMouche-Cruise.")
(disjointWith LanguageGroupingType ExistingStuffType)
(comment RockingChair "A type of a chair which is mounted on rockers.")
(comment Rickettsialpox "A disease characterized by fever, chills, headache,
backache, and spotty rash and caused by a 
#$Rickettsia.")
(comment hasOpinionAsToTruthOf "(#$hasOpinionAsToTruthOf AGT PROP) means that the Agent AGT has an opinion as to the truth of the proposition PROP.  This may be knowledge, doubt, or a mere feeling.  See the specPreds, #$beliefs, #$knows, #$opinions, #$biases, #$notices, and #$doubts.")
(comment fileAccessibleToComputer "A #$BinaryPredicate that relates instances of #$ComputerFile-Abstract to instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  A more specific predicate tha #$containsInformation and a more general predicate than #$fileFoundOnComputer, (#$fileAccessibleToComputer FILE COMP) means that although there may not be a copy (#$ComputerFileCopy) of FILE which is a part of COMP, there is a copy of FILE found on some machine to which COMP is appropriately linked.  If a file is accessible from COMP then, for all COMP cares, there is a copy of FILE on COMP.  That is, a user on COMP will not have to log in to a different machine (viz., the machine that FILE is found on) in order to read from, write to, or execute FILE.")
(comment ArtesianWell "A #$WaterWell in which the water flows upward under pressure.")
(comment AtlasRocket "A family of rockets used primarily by the military and built by #$LockheedMartin-CommercialOrganization.  Typically used for satellite launching.")
(comment feelsSensationInBodyRegion "`(#$feelsSensationInBodyRegion ORG SENSATIONTYPE REGION)' means that

the organism ORG is experiencing a sensation of type SENSATIONTYPE

as being located in the region of their body REGION.")
(comment TibialNerve "The collection of all tibial nerve.  The tibial nerve is formed by #$VentralRamusL4, #$VentralRamusL5, #$VentralRamusS1, #$VentralRamusS2 and #$VentralRamusS3.  The tibial nerve descends through the leg as part of the #$SciaticNerve until just above the knee.  The tibial nerve then descends to through the lower leg and foot.  It has many branches, including the #$SuralNerve, the #$MedialPlantarNerve and the #$LateralPlantarNerve.")
(comment Salami "a salty sausage - often used as luncheon meat")
(comment StickDispenser "Solid substance container which dispenses the product by slowly pushing the product out of the dispenser (such as lipstick or solid deodorant).")
(disjointWith SimpleRepairing PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment Bit "A function and an instance of #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity, generally used to denote the #$sizeOfObject for some sort of #$ComputerFileCopy or #$ElectroMagneticIBT.  Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two, and its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a precise quantity of bits (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). Thus, (#$Bit NUM) denotes a

particular quantity of binary bits. (#$Bit NUM1 NUM2) returns a

range of binary bits. See also #$Byte, #$Megabyte.")
(comment Trophy "A collection of objects.  Each element of #$Trophy is a solid tangible object with a symbolic meaning, awarded to some agent(s) in recognition for winning some competition or achieving some goal.  Trophies typically contain (e.g., in engraved writing) the name of the award, date, and name(s) of the recipient(s).  Examples: the Heisman trophy, the Americas Cup, an Oscar.")
(comment Animation-MovingImage "Members of this collection are #$MovingImages made from a series of drawings simulating motion by means of slight progressive changes in the drawings. Unlike #$Cartoon-Animated, instances of #$Animation-MovingImage need not be humorous or satirical; membership in #$Animation-MovingImage is based solely on the method by which the image was created. See also #$AnimatedMovie.")
(comment Abdomen "Part of body between the chest and the pelvis")
(disjointWith BaseballBat FoodUtensil)
(comment PhloemNetwork "Network of phloem conduits, enabling food and water flow within an angiosperm .")
(comment FaeroeIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$FaroeIslands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ClimateCycleType OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic)
(comment BabyPlayYard "The collection of all play yards for babies.  A #$BabyPlayYard is a construction in which a #$HumanToddler can freely and safely play without causing his or her parent or guardian too much concern about wandering away.")
(comment ShoeBrush "The set of brushes one may use to polish one's shoes.")
(disjointWith SimpleRepairing PlantingAField)
(comment CentralSulcus "The collection of all central sulci of mamalian #$Brains.  An individual #$CentralSulcus is a brain sulcus (#$SulcusOfBrain) between the #$FrontalLobe and #$ParietalLobe on one side of the brain.  The #$MotorCortex forms the anterior wall of the #$CentralSulcus and the #$SomaticSensoryCortex forms its posterior wall.")
(comment ComputerSoftwareServiceMC "Class of product types which are service events that deal with computer software - training, installation, maintenance, etc.")
(comment programDetectsVirus "Ideally, (#$programDetectsVirus AVP VIR) would hold just in case the
#$AntiVirusProgram, AVP, is able to identify the presence of the the #$ComputerVirus
VIR when it is used to scan files/programs/drives infected by VIR.")
(disjointWith MusicalEquipmentStore AutoDealership)
(comment Mouthwash "The liquid stuff used for cleaning and disinfecting the mouth")
(disjointWith Meeting-SocialGathering MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment EukaryoticRNAProcessing "The collection of subevents in #$GeneExpression in which a #$PrimaryTranscript-RNAMolecule is processed before leaving the cell nucleus.")
(comment WeightLiftingBench "This is the collection of weightlifting

benches. These are benches, sometimes with a part that can be adjusted

for angle, which are used to lie down or sit when lifting weights.")
(comment GreekLetter "the first alphabet, originally devised for writing ancient Hellenic languages")
(comment Button-ControlDevice "Telephone buttons, keyboard keys, doorbell buttons -- not buttons for clothes, but buttons that are depressed with the finger.")
(disjointWith MakingFacialExpression TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(disjointWith Metal PetroleumBasedProduct)
(comment Bulldog "A collection of medium-sized, stocky dogs (the male weighs around 50 lbs).              Also called the English Bulldog.")
(comment ComputerWorkstation "A specialization of #$SingleUserComputer. Each instance of this collection is a computer usually found in some kind of work setting, which one person uses at any given time for the bulk of their computing tasks.")
(disjointWith SellingOrganization JudicialOrganization)
(comment String-Textile "The set of cordlike textiles larger than thread but smaller
than yarn in diameter often used in packaging.")
(comment ShavingRazor-Manual "The collection of razors used for shaving.  Manual, non-electric devices used primarily for cutting beards.  See #$ElectricShaver for the powered kind.")
(comment VentralRamusC0 "The collection of all C0 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusC0 and #$DorsalRamusC0 branch from SpinalRootC0.  #$VentralRamusC0 supplies the #$CoccygealPlexus.")
(comment MixForBakedGoods "This is the collection of commercially produced mixes for baked goods.

This includes cake mixes, mixes for pancakes, biscuits, muffins etc.

Cake mixes are the most prominent type of mix for baked goods.")
(disjointWith CycLSentence-ClosedPredicate CycLNonAtomicTerm-ClosedFunctor)
(comment ComputerImageFile "A specialization of #$ComputerFile-AIS. Each #$ComputerImageFile contains a digital representation of some #$VisualImage, and is linked to an instance of #$ComputerImageFileTypeByFormat via the predicate #$fileFormat. A #$ComputerImageFile has a bit-depth and resolution that specify the number of hues it distinguishes and the number of pixels per linear inch it represents.")
(comment ClimbingShoe "shoes especially for rock climbing; having a soft rubber sole.")
(comment SpecifiedAcademicTest "This is the spec of #$SpecifiedTest-CW consisting of academic tests, for example, the 1998 GRE test.")
(comment RoundWindowInEar "The collection of all 'round windows' which separate #$MiddleEars from #$InnerEars.  Each instance of this collection is a round #$Portal from a #$MiddleEar into an #$InnerEar which is closed by a #$SecondaryTympanicMembrane.  Medical terms for the #$RoundWindowInEar include 'round window', 'cochlear window', 'fenestra rotunda', and 'fenestra cochlea'.")
(comment OrchidOrder "An order of plants within the monocot subclass which contains one family, the Orchidaceae. The family is very diverse and one of the largest plant families.  Members have complex floral anatomy, and very tiny seeds which lack endosperm, have rudimentary, undifferentiated embryos, and require association with species-specific fungal partners to develop.")
(comment ThaiPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Thailand, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment IBM360Mainframe "A kind of #$MainframeComputer.  It was the first computer to use a byte-addressable word length. The 360 system popularized remote computing, with terminals communicating to the host via phone lines.")
(comment Spade-TheSuit "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which are spades.")
(comment YumanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of the southwest of North America")
(disjointWith LegalAction IllegalAction)
(disjointWith JudicialSystem DiplomaticMission-ThePost)
(comment loadCapacity-TakeOff "(#$loadCapacity-TakeOff CONVEYANCE MASS) 

 says that MASS is the greatest mass that CONVEYANCE can carry at #$AirplaneTakeOff before damage results to CONVEYANCE.  For example, (#$loadCapacity-TakeOff FighterPlane-A10-0003 (#$Kilogram 22950)) says that this particular fighter plane can safely carry up to 22950 #$Kilograms at takeoff.  It is possible for CONVEYANCE to be heavier while in flight, which is when you would use #$loadCapacity-Conveyance.")
(comment OperatingSystemKernel "A specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW and an instance of #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction.  Each instance of #$OperatingSystemKernel is a computer program that functions as the kernel of an instance of #$OperatingSystem (q.v.).  Some functions of kernels include controlling the interface between user programs and hardware devices, and scheduling processes.  Not every operating system has a kernel, but all Linux operating systems come with a Linux kernel (see #$LinuxKernel-TheProgram).  Important specializations or #$OperatingSystemKernel are #$Microkernel and #$MonolithicKernel (qq.v.).")
(comment AccountingDepartment "A specialization of #$FinanceDepartment. Each instance of this collection is a department whose members are typically responsible for monitoring and recording the financial transactions of a given organization.")
(comment StraightBodyTruck "Type of truck that has the truck cab and cargo-carrying part incorporated onto the same rigid frame.  Not a tractor-trailer combination.")
(comment superAbstracType "(#$superAbstracType SUBTYPE SUPERTYPE) means that the #$LifeStageType SUBTYPE is a type of temporal stage in the life of some organisms, and SUPERTYPE is a more inclusive #$LifeStageType under which SUBTYPE is classified.  Also, SUPERTYPE is a #$genls of SUBTYPE.  Examples: if SUBTYPE were #$HumanToddler, SUPERTYPE could be #$HumanChild.")
(comment DisplayWindowSpace "Part of a #$Building in which items are displayed so that they can be viewed from outside of the building (or from outside of a store if that store opens onto a hallway or other open space within a building) through a #$WindowPane, which is not part of the #$DisplayWindowSpace, but is part of a #$DisplayWindow-Complete.  Items displayed may be for sale or rent, or may be prototypical of items for sale or rent [see #$DisplayingProduct], or may be displayed for artistic, religious, or advertising reasons.")
(comment Liver "A specialization of #$InternalOrgan and instance of #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType: the collection of all living #$Animal livers.  Each instance of #$Liver is a large compound #$InternalOrgan.  A #$Liver breaks down dead #$RedBloodCells, removes certain poisons and waste material from the blood stream, creates glycogen from sugars and proteins, stores glycogen, removes certain chemicals from the blood, secretes bile (#$BileTheSecretion) which is used for digestion,and regulates metabolism of carbohydrates, #$ProteinStuff, #$Vitamins, #$Minerals, and fats.")
(comment MedialCarpusBone "There is one or two #$MedialCarpusBone (one for humans) in the #$Carpus.  This is the middle 'row' of such bones.")
(comment WheatFlour "Finely ground wheat grain used in cooking.")
(disjointWith PoundingDrivingSomething PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment PuttingUpAWebsite "A subcollection of #$TransferIn in which an instance of #$WorldWideWebSite is information added to the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource.")
(comment TapeRewindingProcess "The #$Collection of #$TapeRewindingProcesses.  In an individual instance an #$AudioTapePlayer, #$VideoCassetteRecorder, #$AnsweringMachine, etc. rewinds #$Tapes (usually #$MagneticTapes).")
(disjointWith ChemicalReaction PumpingFluid)
(comment Timecard "A document on which an employee reports the times (or at least number of hours) during a given time period in which s/he worked.")
(comment UrinarySystem "The collection of all urinary systems.  An instance of this collection is the unique complete urinary system in a single #$Animal.")
(comment GiantSchnauzer "A collection of large, robust dogs with wiry coats.")
(comment BelizeanPerson "This is the collection of people who are either #$citizens of #$Belize, or participants in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization HumanServicesOrganization)
(comment FuelOxygenate "This is the collection of instances of fuel additives which work by making the

fuel burn more completely, thereby creating less pollution.")
(comment SuperiorSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all superior segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a (left or right) #$InferiorLobeOfLung that supplies the #$SuperiorSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung.  It branches from the #$InferiorLobarBronchus.  (Distinct from the SuperiorLingularBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung which is in the left #$SuperiorLobeOfLung.)")
(comment VideoReceiverComponent "Electronic Device which receives video signals and decodes them into signals of visual images which can be amplified for display.  See also Television and #$VideoCassetteRecorder")
(comment CarBomb-VehicleDelivered "A specialization of #$Bomb-RoadVehicleDelivered.  Each instance is a bomb contained in a car.  Typically a car containing a #$CarBomb-VehicleDelivered is left near the intended target and detonated remotely or by a timer device, though sometimes they are driven by suicide bombers.  Car bombs are weapons with only terrorist applications. Cf. #$CarBomb-BoobyTrap.")
(comment VentralRamus "The collection of all ventral rami.  Each #$SpinalNerve branches into one #$DorsalRamus and one #$VentralRamus.  Each #$VentralRamus #$innervates #$Muscles in the side and front of the trunk (#$Trunk-BodyCore) as well as contains #$SensoryNerves for the #$Skin of this region.")
(comment Toast "toast")
(comment GasCompany "The utility company which delivers natural gas to its customers")
(comment programCode "(#$programCode PROGRAM CODE) means that the #$ComputerCode CODE is source or executable code for the #$ComputerProgram-CW PROGRAM.")
(comment CanopyTheShelter "A shelter made of canvas, cloth, etc. stretched over a frame.  Unlike a tent, it lacks sides")
(disjointWith DeliveringSomeoneSomething BodilyFunctionEvent)
(comment Soil-Generic "An instance of #$ExistingStuffType, and a specialization of #$LandStuff.  Each instance of #$Soil-Generic is a portion of earth in which one can (usually) grow plants.  Instances of #$Soil-Generic include soils that are part of the top layer of the ground, as well as soils that are processed and sold at lawn and gardening stores.")
(comment ExecutableSystemPrivilegeExploit "The collection of #$ExecutableExploits that are designed to give a regular user of a computational system using #$MSWindowsNT access to the #$LoginAccount for that system.")
(comment PlaintextFn "(PlaintextFn FILE) denotes _the_ plaintext version of the encrypted #$ComputerFile-Abstract FILE.")
(comment Carousel "Merry-go-rounds.  A relatively slow-moving, circular,  amusement park ride in which people sit on carousel horses or benches.")
(comment Amphibian "A specialization of #$Poikilotherm and #$Vertebrate.  Each instance of #$Amphibian isa a cold-blodded and smooth-skinned vertebrate that hatches from an egg to form an aquatic larva (see #$Larva), which then metamorphoses into an air-breathing adult (see #$AirBreathingVertebrate).  Important subcollections include #$Frog and #$Salamander.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterF "The capital letter 'F'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$F-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterF.")
(comment GlazeForCeramics "A liquid applied to bisqued ceramic, to add durability and color to the piece.")
(comment ComputerTVCard "This is the collection of #$ComputerBoards that allow computers to

interface with ordinary television sets.")
(disjointWith OrganizationByEntityType PhysiologicalConditionType)
(comment NuclearGeneratedElectricity "The collection of instances of electricity generated by nuclear reactors.")
(comment GuineaPig "A collection of domesticated mammals originally from South America. Their scientific name is Cavia porcellus.  According to most of the sources I could find, instances of #$GuineaPig are #$Rodents.  According to one source, they  are members of the order Rodentia and the family Caviidae.")
(comment AdministratorAccessFn "(#$hasMembers (#$AdministratorAccessFn ACCT_SYS) ComputerSecurityPerson001) means that ComputerSecurityPerson001 has access to an administrator account the #$AccountSystem ACCT_SYS.  People with administrator access to a system have near-unlimited access to the files on the system, including the #$WindowsRegistry.  Note that ACCT_SYS may be either an #$NTDomain or an #$NTWorkstation.")
(comment GumArabic "A gummy substance derived from crops of acacia plants, and the main ingredient of chewing gum.")
(comment MusculocutaneousNerve "The collection of all musculocutaneous #$Nerves.  A #$MusculocutaneousNerve is formed by a branch of the #$LateralCord-BrachialPlexus (#$VentralRamusC5, #$VentralRamusC6, #$VentralRamusC7) of its side of the body.  The #$MusculocutaneousNerve runs from the #$Shoulder to the #$Elbow where it becomes the lateral cutaneous #$Nerve of the #$ForeArm.  It supplies the heads of the bicep, the coroacobrachialis, most of the brachialis, and a small part of the humerus.")
(comment Cupcake "The collection of #$Cupcakes. These are small, muffin-shaped cakes baked in a special muffin pan. Usually, only the tops are frosted.")
(comment NTAccountSystem "The union of #$NTDomain and #$NTMachine, #$NTAccountSystem is the collection of all #$AccountSystems which are built around the #$MSWindowsNT #$OperatingSystem.")
(comment LoginAccount "A login account is a computer account to which a user could log in.  A person with an instance of #$LoginAccount is able to access storage space and CPU time on an instance of #$AccountSystem with a certain kind of operating system. Important subcollections of #$LoginAccount are #$UserAccount, #$RootAccount, #$AdministratorAccount. Important non-specs include #$SystemAccountForNT.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity RestrainingSomeone)
(comment Antacid "Drugs which relieve the discomfort of an overly acidic stomach.")
(comment BacteriumTypeByMetabolism "A collection of collections and a partioning of #$Bacterium
according to differences in energy used for
#$BiologicalMetabolismEvents.  This collection divides #$Bacterium
into two disjoint collections: the #$Chemotrophs and the
#$Phototrophs.  They use different types of environmental energy in their #$MetabolicPathways.")
(comment PornographicMovie "#$PornographicMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which depicts #$SexualBehavior in a graphic manner that is judged by some sectors of a particular community to be obscene.")
(comment Exhaling-BreathingOut "The portion of the breathing process in which air exits the lungs - typically involuntary.")
(disjointWith StorageConstruct ControlDevice)
(comment SquashPlant "This is the commonsense notion of squash, i.e. not including pumpkins, cucumbers, etc.")
(comment GuernseyIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Guernsey-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment EmergencyRoomOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that are #$subOrganizations of #$MedicalCareOrganizations and that provide emergency services (and sometimes simply after-hours services) to patients.  #$EmergencyRoomOrganizations operate out of #$EmergencyRooms.")
(comment DigitalAudioRecorder "The collection of electronic devices that digitally record sound.")
(comment Vertebrate "An instance of #$BiologicalTaxon within the #$BiologicalPhylum #$ChordataPhylum.  Each instance of #$Vertebrate is an animal that has a backbone or spine made of bony or cartilaginous vertebrae, which may be separate or fused.  Notable specializations of #$Vertebrate include #$Mammal, #$Reptile, #$Bird, and #$Fish.")
(comment typicalInterArgIsa "(#$typicalInterArgIsa PRED M COL1 N COL2) says that when an instance of COL1 fills the Mth argument-place of PRED, then, typically, the Nth place of PRED will be filled by an instance of COL2.")
(comment EarthMovingScoop "The collection of bucket or scoop-like attachments that fit onto some kinds of bulldozers, backhoes, tractors, etc, and are used to scoop out large pieces of earth.")
(comment TranssexualPerson "A collection of #$Persons. A #$TranssexualPerson is a #$Person who has undergone hormonal and surgical treatment in order to attain the physical characteristics of the opposite sex. Every member of this collection has gone from being a #$FemaleAnimal to being a #$MaleAnimal or vice versa.")
(comment Frowning "Only primates frown.  Requires lips.  Also may involve eyebrows.  Finally the whole face.   Should the latter be inferable from the fact use of lips involves face?  See also #$Smiling for related problem. ")
(disjointWith Water FoodComposite)
(comment totalProjectedAmountForOrgDuring "The organization ARG2 reported a projected total of ARG4  units/doses dispensed/sold for the product type ARG1 during the time interval ARG3.")
(comment MP3Compressor "The collection of all computer programs whose function is to compress an #$MP3File.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup HumanServicesOrganization)
(comment OomycotaDivision "A Biological Division within the fungus kingdom which includes the water molds.")
(disjointWith Appendage-AnimalBodyPart Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment TerminalBronchiole "The collection of all terminal bronchioles, those #$Bronchioles (small #$BronchialTubes) that each adjoin the #$RespiratoryBronchioles, two steps before the #$Alveolus.  A #$TerminalBronchiole does not have any Alveoli along its sides, unlike the #$RespiratoryBronchioles.")
(comment DNAMoleculeType "The collection of collections of DNAMolecule.  Each instance will be a kind of DNA molecule.  Each specified subcollection of this collection will be a means of faceting DNAMolecules.")
(comment CyanogenChloride "A colorless, poisonous, flammable gas.")
(disjointWith Fox Dog)
(comment ModifyingAFileInPlace "A collection of actions done by computers on files.

In each instance of this collection, a #$ComputerFileCopy

is modified in place.  If a file is modified in this way, its low-level

attributes like its size, the disk sectors (or memory region, etc.) it occupies,

etc. must all remain the same.")
(comment AutomotiveLightBulb "Any of the lights attached to car except an enclosed headlight.")
(disjointWith ArmMovement CrossingLegs)
(comment ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Root "#$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Root is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Root when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to create arbitrary files with root privilege. See also #$SetUIDFault-Root.")
(disjointWith ArmyBase-Grounds AirForceBase-Grounds)
(comment WelshCorgi-Pembroke "A collection of dogs.  A distinction feature of this breed is that they have no tails.")
(comment Prince "The collection of all princes, or male persons who hold hereditary princely titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch.  This includes sovereign, hereditary, courtesy and other princes.  It excludes the co-princes of the #$CoPrincipality of #$Andorra.  See also #$Princess.")
(disjointWith IdeologicalOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment LowRiderCar "The collection of large non-sportive luxury cars that ride low.")
(comment LineaAlba "The #$Collection of all #$LineaAlba (Abdominis) Tissues.  The #$LineaAlba is located along the medial line of the #$Abdomen, connecting the #$PubicSymphysis to the #$XiphoidProcess and the #$RectusAbdominis #$Muscles to each other.  Note that there is also a linea alba cervicalis in the #$Neck-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment Coin-Currency "A small disk-shaped currency item, made of metal.  In recent times, the face value of the coin may be more than the value of the material in it; in the past, coins were pieces of precious metal, whose value would be similar whether they were fashioned into a coin or not.")
(comment HilumOfLung "The collection of all hila of #$Lungs; each #$HilumOfLung is the indented place on a #$MedialSurfaceOfLung where the #$RootOfLung containing the major tubes and vessels enter the lung.  Also called the Hilus.")
(comment Tea-Iced "Tea served iced.")
(comment ApplianceRepairShop "An organization which is a local customer point of contact, and which repairs appliances.")
(comment AudioProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs designed to manipulate audio computer files.  Instances would be 'KSCD', 'Microsoft's CD Player'.")
(comment ScheduleDocument "A specialization of #$TextualMaterial (and thus of #$InformationBearingThing). Each instance of this collection is a document that contains information about the #$Schedule of something. Instances might be  printed on paper (and thus be instances of #$Paper-IBO) or they might be represented in some other medium. Notable specializations include #$WorkScheduleDocument and #$PublicTransportationScheduleDocument. For making assertions regarding the usage of such documents, see #$ConsultingASchedule.")
(comment Mucus "The collection of oozy, slimy secretion found in many different places in and on one's body, including in your nose.")
(comment longshots "(#$longshots COMP AGENT) indicates that AGENT, a competing agent in the #$Competition COMP, is expected NOT to win by anyone who is knowledgeable about the competition.")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece NaturalTangibleStuff)
(comment CameroonPerson "A person who is a citizen of #$Cameroon, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PassengerTrainCar "The collection of all #$TrainCars that are meant to carry passengers, as opposed to cargo.")
(disjointWith MatterTypeByPhysicalState LanguageGroupingType)
(comment SeatingDeviceFootRest "The collection of the footrests of seating devices.")
(comment CountriesWithTechnologyFn "A #$SubTopicFunction created for  #$ProjectBroadsword.   This function takes as its argument any    instance of #$ProductType and returns    the collection of instances of #$Country     that 'have' that #$ProductType.  For     example, (#$CountriesWithTechnologyFn     #$ChemicalWeapon) is the collection of      countries that have chemical weapons.")
(comment DismountingFromSitting "Getting down off something on which one has (or is) mounted.")
(comment ComputerHardwarePackage "We are baffled as to what this is, so we don't know if this should be in the #$ComputerHardwareMarketCategory. the types of computer hardware packages")
(comment percentNaturalPopulationIncrease "The predicate #$percentNaturalPopulationIncrease is used to indicate the annual percent increase in the population of a particular culture.  Used with #$holdsIn, (#$percentNaturalPopulationIncrease CULTURE AMOUNT) means that, for the specified year, AMOUNT is the percentage of increase in the population belonging to the #$HumanCultureType CULTURE.  Elements of #$HumanCultureType (q.v.) are typically ethnic groups or national populations.")
(comment DeltaRocket "A family of satellite-launching rockets built by McDonnell Douglas (now Boeing).")
(comment ThirdOccipitalNerve "The collection of all third occipital #$Nerves.  The third occipital nerve is connected to #$DorsalRamusC3 and #$innervates the #$Skin of the upper part of the back of the neck (#$Neck-AnimalBodyPart) and head (#$Head-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment Bacon "Smoked pork - in America, typically served as a breakfast food")
(comment nounStrings "(#$nounStrings WORD STRING) states that STRING is one of the noun strings for the word unit WORD in some microtheory.  In other words, some nominal #$SpeechPartPredicate is used on WORD to relate it to STRING.  This predicate is

#$notAssertible since it is concluded from the current state of the knowledge base.")
(disjointWith Practicing-Preparing BiologicalDevelopmentEvent)
(comment Byte "A function and an instance of #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity, representing a common unit of computer memory and disk capacity, consisting typically of 8 #$Bits. Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two, and its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a precise quantity of bytes (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). Thus, (#$Byte NUM) denotes a particular quantity of bytes. (#$Byte NUM1 NUM2) returns a range of bytes. See also #$Megabyte, #$Megaword.")
(comment PersonalWatercraft "A single-person water transportation device in which the rider kneels or stands on the device.  It is powered by jetting water out the back and hydroplanes on top of the water as it goes along.  The driver is exposed to the elements and gets very wet.  Great fun to use.")
(comment PoeticWork "A collection of intangible artifacts (cf. #$Artifact-Intangible). Each instance of #$PoeticWork consists of words carefully chosen and arranged both for the meaning and images they express and for the sounds that are produced when they are spoken. The subject of a 

#$PoeticWork is often, but need not be, timeless and abstract.")
(comment Blowhole "Hole on back of a Cetacean's head, used for breathing")
(disjointWith FoodUtensil PlumbingTool)
(comment XylemNetwork "Network of xylem conduits, enabling water and dissolved minerals to move within an angiosperm .")
(comment SouthKoreanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$SouthKorea, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment NetworkOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations, each of which is a network of organizations that work together as a single unit to accomplish specific, defined goals.  For example, in order to cut costs, many health insurers establish networks of independently owned healthcare providers that agree to provide services to insureds at agreed upon prices.  That network (i.e., the combination of all participating #$Organizations) is an instance of #$NetworkOrganization.")
(comment BoosterSeat "The collection of all booster seats for children.  A #$BoosterSeat is a device which is used to 'boost' small children, generally #$HumanToddlers, up high enough to reach the #$Table-PieceOfFurniture at which they are eating.")
(comment ShoePolish-Paste "The collection of pastey stuff used for polishing shoes.")
(disjointWith PlantingAField ChangingDeviceState)
(comment TransverseFissure "The collection of all transverse fissures of mamalian #$Brains.  An individual #$TransverseFissure is a brain sulcus (#$SulcusOfBrain) between the #$Cerebrum and the #$Diencephalon.")
(comment VideoClipOfSubjectFn "(#$VideoClipOfSubjectFn SUBJECT) denotes the collection of all #$VideoClips in which images of the #$SpatialThing-Localized, SUBJECT, appear. For example, (#$VideoClipOfSubjectFn #$BillClinton) denotes a collection including all #$VideoClips in which images of Bill Clinton appear. Likewise (#$VideoClipOfSubjectFn #$FirstLunarLanding) denotes the collection of all #$VideoClips in which images of the first lunar landing appear. To denote the collection of all #$VideoClips in which part of a #$VideoConceptualWork (such as a #$MusicVideo) is recorded, use #$VideoClipOfWorkFn.")
(comment AutomatedTextToSpeechConversion "A collection whose instances are events in which a #$TextToSpeechProgram is used to produce, from a piece of text, a series of audible signals having the same propositional content as the text.  The input to a #$AutomatedTextToSpeechConversion need not be typed, though it probably typically is.")
(disjointWith OfficeSupplyStore AutoDealership)
(comment WoolCloth "Cloth made out of wool fibers.")
(disjointWith PoundingDrivingSomething AudioCommunicating)
(comment CycLExpression-Askable "The collection of #$CycLExpressions

that are either themselves askable as queries to the Cyc system (see 

#$CycLSentence-Askable) or could appear as non-atomic terms within 

sentences that could be so asked (see #$CycLNonAtomicTerm-Askable). 

More precisely, each instance of #$CycLExpression-Askable is a CycL 

expression that is constructible via the syntax of CycL without 

violating any applicable arity constraints (see #$arity).  Note that 

askable CycL expressions do not necesarily obey other semantic 

constraints beyond arity, such as argument-type constraints (see 

#$ArgTypePredicate); thus they are not always semantically 

well-formed in the fullest sense (cf. #$CycLExpression-Assertible).")
(comment TorpedoTube "A collection.  Each instance is a specialized #$ProjectileLauncher that is built into the exterior wall of a #$ModernNavalShip.  If the #$TorpedoTube is on a #$WaterPlatform-Surface, it is located on the portion of the ship that is submerged in water.")
(comment DogriCharacter "characters used for the Dogri dialect of Punjabi")
(comment Orlon "The collection of acrylic fibers known by the trademark name            Orlon.  Used in making yarns and fabrics.")
(comment PunctualEventType "A collection of collections of events. If PUNCT is an instance of #$PunctualEventType, then each instance of PUNCT is temporally `unextended', i.e., its occurrence bisects an imaginary timeline in a `before' and an `after' segment without residue. More precisely, we'll say that EVT is an instance of an instance of #$PunctualEventType iff its starting point and its ending point coincide, i.e., if its temporal extent is `point-like' up to a reasonable time granularity scale.")
(disjointWith RecreationalActivity LegalProceeding)
(disjointWith HumanOccupationConstruct Lamppost)
(comment GoldenRetriever "An instance of #$DogTypeByBreed, and a specialization of #$Retriever-Dog. Instances of #$GoldenRetriever are distinguished from other instances of #$Retriever-Dog by their characteristic color.")
(comment Woodwork "The collection of #$Wood #$Artifacts")
(comment ComputerNetworkTypeByTopology "#$ComputerNetworkTypeByTopology is a collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$ComputerNetwork whose instances are all of the same general topology.")
(comment IndustrialCleaningStuff "Just what is says")
(comment VentralRamusT4 "The collection of all T4 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT4 and #$DorsalRamusT4 branch from SpinalRootT4.  #$VentralRamusT4 supplies below the #$FourthRib.")
(comment CakeMix "This is the collection of commercially produced cake mixes.")
(comment CycLNonAtomicTerm-ClosedFunctor "The subcollection of denotational #$CycLNonAtomicTerms which have no free variable in the arg0 position.

Examples: (#$JuvenileFn #$Platypus), (#$JuvenileFn #$isa #$genls), (#$TheSetOf ?X (#$colorOfType ?X #$GreenColor)), (#$JuvenileFn ?X).  Counterexample: (?SOMEFN #$Gold) ((#$USDollarFn ?YEAR) 5).")
(comment JPEGFile "A collection of #$ComputerImageFiles. Each #$JPEGFile is a #$ComputerImageFile whose #$fileFormat conforms to the standard image compression algorithm designed by the Joint Photographic Experts Group for compressing either full-colour or grey-scale digital images of 'natural', real-world scenes. Instances of #$JPEGFile often have filenames that end in '.jpg' or '.jpeg'.")
(comment Meiosis "The class of events in which a cell divides twice (actually, the cell divides once and then the two offspring cells each divide once) to produce up to four offspring cells which have half the amount of genetic material than the parent cell had.  Meiosis occurs in the reproductive tissues of eukaryotic organisms that reproduce sexually, and is a precondition of forming #$Gametes.")
(comment SpecifiedTest-CW "This is the collection of tests (not testing events) which are named and are developed for repeated administration. Examples would include the 1998 ACT test in English and the Myers-Briggs Type Indicator test for personality type. ")
(comment SecondaryTympanicMembrane "The collection of all membranes between #$MiddleEars and #$InnerEars.  In medicine this concept is also called 'membrana tympani secundaria', 'Scarpa's membrane', and 'membrane of the round window'.")
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument ConsumableProduct)
(comment DioeciousPlantSpecies "The collection of #$BiologicalSpecies of dioecious #$Plants, or plant species in which each individual plant has only the reproductive organs of one sex, not both (e.g., either female pistil or male stamen).  Compare #$HermaphroditicPlantSpecies and #$MonoeciousPlantSpecies.")
(comment JamaicaPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Jamaica, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PowerMacintoshComputer "The Apple line of Power Macintosh computers.")
(comment Suit-PlayingCardType "A collection of subcollections of #$PlayingCard in which each instance is a collection containing all #$PlayingCards of a particular suit, i.e. #$Club-TheSuit, #$Diamond-TheSuit, #$Heart-TheSuit, #$Spade-TheSuit, and #$Tarot-TheSuit.")
(comment ChibchanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages of Central and/or South America")
(comment CombustionHeatingElement "The collection of all heating elements that produce heat through the combustion of some fuel substance")
(comment LearningASkill "This is the subcollection of #$Learning containing those events in which the performer learns some new skill.")
(disjointWith Department Hospital)
(comment loadCapacity-TakeOff "(#$loadCapacity-TakeOff CONVEYANCE MASS) 

 says that MASS is the greatest mass that

   CONVEYANCE can carry at #$AirplaneTakeOff before damage

    results to CONVEYANCE.  For example,

  (#$loadCapacity-TakeOff FighterPlane-A10-0003

  (#$Kilogram 22950)) says that this particular

   fighter plane can safely carry up to 22950 #$Kilograms at takeoff.  It is possible for CONVEYANCE to be heavier while in flight, which is when you would use #$loadCapacity-Conveyance.")
(comment Interpreter-Computers "A specialization of #$ProgrammingLanguageImplementation.   Each instance of #$Interpreter-Computers is a program that simultaneously runs and translates other programs.  Note that instances of #$Interpreter-Computers are distinct from instances of #$Compiler (q.v.) in that an instance of #$Compiler will not execute its input program -- the \"source code\" -- but will simply translate it into executable \"machine code\" -- also called \"object code\" -- which is output to a file for later execution.")
(comment PayrollDepartment "A specialization of #$Department. Each instance of this collection is a group of employees who administer an organization's payroll -- delivering employees their wages.")
(comment RecreationalVehicle "Large, van-shaped vehicles intended for camping or overnight travelling, and equipped with built-in furniture (seating, table, bunks), kitchen, and sanitary facilities.")
(comment NewbornBaby "The stage of life from birth to a few weeks old, normally before a child interacts much with its environment.")
(comment DisplayWindow-Complete "Part of a #$Building in which items are displayed in one part (the #$DisplayWindowSpace) so that they can be viewed from outside of the building (or from outside of a store if that store opens onto a hallway or other open space within a building) through a #$WindowPane which is another part of the #$DisplayWindow-Complete.  Items displayed may be for sale or rent, or may be prototypical of items for sale or rent [see #$DisplayingProduct], or may be displayed for artistic, religious, or advertising reasons.")
(comment Skin "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$Skin is an outer protective and tactile sensory covering (or part of such a covering) for (part of) an animal's body.  This collection includes both the entire skins of animals, as well as proper parts of such skins (such as Yul Brynner's scalp).")
(comment ProximalCarpusBone "The bones in the first row of the #$Carpus are
#$ProximalCarpusBone s.")
(disjointWith BiologicalProcess InformationBearingThing)
(comment PublicWaterSystem "A system of pipes for carrying fresh water from municipal water supply to Buildings.")
(disjointWith MakingAnAgreement Conveying-Generic)
(comment PurchaseReceipt "The page included with a purchase which certifies that the seller has received payment for the purchased items.")
(comment Lip-AnimalBodyPart "The tissue surrounding the mouth of an animal.  Mammals have two of these, an #$UpperLip and a #$LowerLip.")
(comment StandardSchnauzer "A collection of medium-sized dogs.  Their coats are usually   pepper and salt or pure black.")
(comment BeninPerson "This is the collection of people who are either #$citizens of #$Benin, or participants in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization HealthcareOrganization)
(comment GunByCaliberFn "This collection allows one to reify gun types on the

 fly, by identifying gun types by caliber.  For example,

  (#$GunByCaliberFn #$MachineGun ((#$Milli #$Meter) 12.7)) 

 is the collection of all 12.7 mm machine guns.")
(comment ApicoposteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all apicoposterior segments of left #$SuperiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by an #$ApicoposteriorSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.  (On the left side the apical and posterior segments of the #$SuperiorLobeOfLung are usually combined in the #$ApicoposteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.)")
(comment CompactDiscPlayerMechanism "Compact Disc mechanism; can play compact dics.  See also StereoSystemCompactDiscPlayer")
(disjointWith InformationRecordingProcess TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment MedialSuralCutaneousNerve "The collection of all medial sural cutaneous #$Nerves.  A #$MedialSuralCutaneousNerve is a branch of a #$TibialNerve.  It #$innervates the skin on the proximal #$LowerLeg and communicates with the #$SuralNerve.")
(comment UnleavenedBread "Bread which is made without a leavening agent; that is, no yeast, no baking soda, no sourdough.  Sometimes called flat bread.  Includes pita bread and tortillas.")
(comment CommercialServiceOrganization "A specialization of #$CommercialOrganization.  Each instance of #$CommercialServiceOrganization is a commercial organization which sells some service(s), rather than tangible goods, as its main product.  Some tangible goods may accompany or supplement the main service sold, but only as side products; for example, some instances of #$HairSalon sell hair care products.")
(comment num-GenQuant "(#$num-GenQuant COL1 COL2 N) means that there are exactly N elements of COL1 which are also elements of COL2.  This predicate is a sort of macro-predicate which can be used to represent the meaning of arbitrarily many English numeric determiners like \"two\", \"three\", etc.  More specialiuzed predicates for specific numbers can be defined in terms of #$num-GenQuant.  Thus, for instance, #$two-GenQuant can be defined as (#$num-GenQuant COL1 COL2 2).")
(comment EdibleByFn "A function to be used in referring to 'All the things that can be ingested by a typical instance of --'.  More specifically, where ORG is some collection of whole organisms, (#$EdibleByFn ORG) returns the collection of all substances that can be consumed and successfully metabolized by typical instances of ORG.  Thus (#$EdibleByFn #$Horse) returns the collection of all substances that can be consumed and metabolized by 'normal' horses, etc. Such a collection will ordinarily be larger than the collection of substances 'normally' consumed by typical instances of the argument collection.  To refer to such collections, use #$FoodOrDrinkForFn.")
(comment CottonCloth "A specialization of #$Cloth and #$OrganicStuff.  Each instance of #$CottonCloth is a piece of cloth made completely of #$CottonStuff.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseRespondsToICMPECHORequests "#$VulnerableBecauseRespondsToICMPECHORequests is a specialization of
 #$NetworkVulnerability.  It is a vulnerability of a computer
 that arises as a consequence of the configuration of the OS
 installed on the computer.  Computers with this vulnerability have not disabled responses to broadcast addresses.  See also #$VulnerableToSmurfAttack.")
(comment AmusementParkRide "Devices which move people around a fixed  area for amusement.  Usually found at carnivals and amusement parks.")
(comment Primate "An instance of #$BiologicalOrder, and a sub-taxon of #$Eutheria.  Each instance of #$Primate has a relatively large brain case, an unfused radius and ulna in the forelimbs, an unfused tibia and fibula in the hind limbs, and opposable thumbs.  Notable specializations of #$Primate include #$Person, #$Orangutan, #$Gorilla, and #$Baboon.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterF "The lowercase letter 'f'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$F-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterF.")
(comment FrenchCar "Cars made in #$France")
(comment ComputerChassis "This is the collection of #$ComputerChassis. The chassis houses the main electronic components, including the #$ComputerMotherBoard (with places to insert or replace microchip for the main and possibly specialized #$ComputerProcessor and #$RAM (random access memory) and places for adding optional adapters (for example, for audio or video capabilities). Typically, room is provided for a #$HardDiskDrive and a #$CD-ROM drive.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat OrganizationByEntityType)
(comment SatelliteTransmitter "#$SatelliteTransmitter is a type of device used to broadcast radio or tv signals to or from satellites.  Compare this constant to #$SatelliteReceiver.")
(comment AdministratorAccount "The collection of #$WindowsNTAccounts (including all #$NTDomains and #$NTWorkstations) which grant the holder of the account access to all (or nearly all) the files on that account system.")
(comment VentralRamusL4 "The collection of all L4 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusL4 and #$DorsalRamusL4 branch from SpinalRootL4.  #$VentralRamusL4 supplies the #$LumbarPlexus and the #$SacralPlexus.")
(comment Fruitcake "The collection of #$Fruitcakes. These are cakes with various dried fruits and nuts baked in.")
(comment subcatFrameOfConstituent "(#$subcatFrameOfConstituent CONST FRAME) relates the #$SententialConstituent CONST to its unique #$SubcategorizationFrame FRAME.")
(comment PrivilegedAccount "A person or process with access to an instance of #$PrivilegedAccount is able to perform a greater range of actions on an instance of #$ComputationalSystem than those with access only to #$UserAccounts do.  Important subcollections of #$PrivilegedAccount are #$RootAccount and #$AdministratorAccount.")
(comment HomoErectus "The collection of members of #$HomoGenus of the species that is the immediate ancestor to modern man, Homo Sapiens.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment Bodypainting "The collection of all body paintings [#$Painting-ArtForm] as representational art forms")
(comment Jawbone "the mandible; the inferior maxillary bone.")
(disjointWith DomesticatedAnimalFood ChildrensFood)
(comment MacaoEnclavePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Macao-Enclave, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment AmusementParkOperator "The collection of all #$EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganizations that operate, manage or otherwise run instances of #$AmusementPark.")
(comment SingleLensReflexCamera "This is the collection of single lens reflex cameras. What makes a camera

a single lens reflex camera is that the viewfinder looks out through the

lens via a mirror which flips out of the way when the shutter opens. This

allows the photographer to see exactly what will be in the frame.")
(comment SentientAnimal "A subset of #$Animal, the collection of all animals which have a mind and are capable of conscious thought, or at least are best treated as such if you have to deal with them.")
(comment Thermometer "Thermometers that are normally used for measuring purposes.")
(comment HumanLifecycleMilestone "Elements of #$HumanLifecycleMilestone are major positive developmentally related events in the life of some #$Person. Examples include, saying the first word, taking the first step, graduating from high school, marriage, giving birth etc..  They are, by default, the sort of event such that the doer would be expected to feel proud.  The parents of the doer would feel proud, happy for them, etc..  Of course, such inferences are somewhat culturally and situationally dependent.  For example, an unwed mother giving birth in the early 20th century anglo society would feel less pride than a married one in the same.")
(disjointWith Water AlcoholicBeverage)
(disjointWith Wheelbarrow Wagon)
(comment MP3Decoder "The collection of all computer programs whose function is to decode an audio recording in the mp3 format.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup FinancialOrganization)
(comment Rudder-ShipPart "A flat piece or structure of wood or metal attached upright to a ship's stern so that it can be turned causing the ship's head to turn in the same direction.")
(comment ChordataPhylum "An instance of #$BiologicalPhylum within the #$BiologicalKingdom #$Animal, the #$ChordataPhylum contains the many chordate taxa.  All chordate taxa have members who have a notochord (a flexible rod running the length of the body) at some stage of development and pharyngeal gills at some stage of development.  The #$ChordataPhylum has as #$taxonMembers all the specializations of #$Vertebrate (including #$Person), as well as some non-vertebrate chordates like Amphioxus.")
(disjointWith ExternalOrgan Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment Alveolus "The collection of all alveoli in mammalian #$Lungs, being tiny air chambers used as the sites of gas-exchange of gasses in the inhaled air with the pulmonary capillaries.  Alvioli are connected #$distalTo the #$AlveolarDucts, which are connected to the #$RespiratoryBronchioles.  The #$RespiratoryBronchioles also have alvioli directly connected along their sides.  Many also are connected directly to neighboring alveoli by small holes.")
(comment ConcentrateProduct "A mixture whose ingredients (#$solute) have been concentrated into a  more potent form, e.g. orange juice concentrate.")
(comment Arthropod "A #$BiologicalPhylum and a specialization of #$Invertebrate.  Each instance of 
#$Arthropod is a member of a species whose members are typically chitin-armored 
invertebrates with jointed bodies and limbs.  Specializations include #$Insect, 
#$Crustacean, and #$Arachnid.")
(comment AccessingAFile-ReadOnly "The collection of actions done by computers in which a computer reads information from a file without modifying the file.")
(comment BronzeMedal-Physical "Physical bronze medals of the type awarded in competitions.")
(comment GoingToSleep "The collection of events in which an #$Animal goes from the state of being awake to being in a state of sleep.")
(comment ElevatedPrivilegeFault-User "#$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-User is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-User when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to create arbitrary files with the privileges of the user executing the program.")
(comment Weimaraner "A collection of medium-sized dogs with very short fur,   usually some shade of gray.  Originally bred as hunting dogs.")
(comment Baroness "The collection of all baronesses, or female persons who hold baronial titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch (whether in their own right, by marriage or by courtesy) in the systems of nobility of European countries like #$France, #$Italy, #$Spain, or the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland, or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf.  See also #$Baron.")
(disjointWith TechnologyOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment AdductorPollicis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$AdductorPollicis #$Muscle.  The #$AdductorPollicis adducts the #$Thumb at the #$CarpoMetaCarpalJointOfThumb, significantly increasing the power of the grasp of the #$Thumb.")
(comment PaperBag "The collection of bags made of paper")
(comment primaryActivityTypeOfLocation "(#$primaryActivityTypeOfLocation LOC ACT-TYPE) means that ACT-TYPE is a main type of activity to occur at the #$HumanOccupationConstruct, LOC.  A place might have more than one main activity.")
(comment MedialSurfaceOfLung "The collection of medial surface areas of #$Lungs, each a concave area extending from the root of the lung to the angular edge at the bottom, the #$InferiorMarginOfLung, the edge at the front, the #$AnteriorMarginOfLung, and the rear edge, the #$PosteriorMarginOfLung, facing the #$Mediastinum.")
(comment Tea-Beverage "Beverage made by steeping tea leaves, or by mixing with water a powder ultimately (we hope) derived from tea leaves")
(comment AutoBodyShop "An organization which is a local customer point of contact, and which performs body repairs on automobiles and other road vehicles.")
(comment MP4File "The set of #$ComputerSoundFiles and #$ComputerImageFiles that have been encoded  using the format MP4.")
(comment PhotographAsArtForm "A specialization of #$ArtObject. Photographs as representational art forms.")
(comment Pus "the thick opaque white fluid containing white blood cells (leucocytes) that is secreted from bacterial infections on the skin.")
(comment hasInsignia "(#$hasInsignia AGENT INSIGNIATYPE) means that AGENT is symbolized or represented by instances of INSIGNIATYPE (which may be a crest, badge, flag, coat of arms, etc.)")
(disjointWith VehiclePart NaturalTangibleStuff)
(comment fruitOfType "A binary predicate that relates specializations of #$Plant to specializations of #$Fruit.  (#$fruitOfType PLANT-TYPE FRUIT-TYPE) means that FRUIT-TYPE is the type of fruit that PLANT-TYPE bears.")
(comment PenghuIslandsPerson "A person who is a #$PenghuIslands #$citizens, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SeineNet "The collection of all #$FishingNets designed to hang suspended in a #$BodyOfWater with floats at the top and weights at the bottom.")
(comment HumanLanguage "A specialization of #$Language. Each instance of this collection is a language that is used by human communities for communication.  This collection differs from #$NaturalLanguage in that a #$HumanLanguage may be purposefully created, while #$NaturalLanguages evolve without a purposeful creation process.  Instances of #$HumanLanguage thus include not only many #$NaturalLanguages, but also made-up languages like Esperanto and many (non-natural) #$SignLanguages.")
(comment RecliningChair "A type of an armchair with an adjustable back and footrest.")
(comment GuidingAnAnimal "action where one animal (could be a person) directs the movement (could be any kind of physical transfer) of another animal (could also be a person).")
(comment TitanRocket "A family of large rockets built by LockheedMartin.")
(comment EcholocationPerception "#$EcholocationPerception is the collection of spatial #$Perceivings in which a #$PerceptualAgent (such as a bat or a submarine) generates sounds (potentially ultra- or sub- sonic in frequency), hears the sounds reflected from surfaces, and thereby acquires information about the position of other objects in its environment.")
(comment DorsalRamusT1 "The collection of all T1 dorsal rami.  #$VentralRamusT1 and #$DorsalRamusT1 branch from SpinalRootT1.  #$DorsalRamusT1 supplies the #$Skin on the back (#$Back-AnimalBodyPart).")
(comment PoultryPiece "The collection of pieces of poultry that you would see in the supermarket, like wing, thigh, etc.  #$PoultryWing, #$PoultryBreast, are specs of this.")
(comment qualifyingResidenceForTaxDeduction "`(#$qualifyingResidenceForTaxDeduction OWNER HOME YEAR)' means
that OWNER #$owns HOME and that HOME passes IRS criteria for OWNER to be
able to claim its mortgage interest as a deduction as long as OWNER does
not claim this deduction on two other homes. A taxpayer might have more
than one #$secondaryResidence that is a
$qualifyingResidenceForTaxDeduction.  In such a case, OWNER can designate
any of these to be OWNER's #$designatedSecondaryResidence. Don't confuse
this predicate with the similarly named
#$qualifiedResidenceForTaxDeduction. The latter means that HOME is either
OWNER's #$primaryResidence or OWNER's #$designatedSecondaryResidence for
YEAR.")
(comment Clutch "Device attached to the transmission of your car may be controled by the driver in order to shift gears properly.")
(disjointWith PhysicalDevice ComputerFileCopy)
(comment Lei-Necklace "Necklace made of flowers which is commonly seen in south pacific cultures.")
(comment Cartoon "The collection of drawings of characters. The following 4 facts are often but not always true about them: 1: Their characters are doing some action. 2: They involve social or political commentary. 3: They involve humorous or satirical content. 4: They are often part of cartoons strips. Some are animated moving pictures (see #$Cartoon-Animated) others are still, see #$Cartoon-Still.")
(comment Ligament "Connecting tissue between bones")
(disjointWith File-Tool FoodUtensil)
(comment VascularNetworkOfPlant "Networks of conduits, both xylem and phloem, enabling food and water flow within an angiosperm .")
(comment FalklandIslandsPerson "A person who is a #$FalklandIslands #$citizens, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization NetworkOrganization)
(comment Stock-GunPart "The collection of nondischarging ends of #$Guns that are used for bracing or gripping.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForSubcollectionProcessing "(#$useReformulationRuleForSubcollectionProcessing RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$SubcollectionProcessorRLModule.  This predicate is a spec pred of #$useReformulationRuleForCanonicalization because we 

 prefer, e.g., expressions of the form (and ... (isa ?X COL) (PRED ?X THING)) to expressions of the form (and ... (isa ?X (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToFn COL PRED THING)).")
(comment VacuumingACarpet "The clean-a-carpet-with-an-electric-vacuum-cleaner process. By default, the #$objectActedOn is a carpet, although the carpet is not always on a #$FloorInAConstruction.  Carpeted areas of transportation vehicles are also frequently vacuumed.  Other surfaces can be vacuumed, so #$Carpet is only a default.  You gotta pull and push the vacuum back and forth a mob of times.")
(comment ParietoOccipitalSulcus "The collection of all parital-occipital sulci of mamalian #$Brains.  An individual #$ParietoOccipitalSulcus is a brain sulcus (#$SulcusOfBrain) between the #$OccipitalLobe and #$ParietalLobe on one side of the brain.  Unlike the other sulci, it arises from the mesial side of the cortex.")
(disjointWith AutoDealership OutletStore)
(comment Felt "Cloth made out of a combination of compressed wool and cotton fibers.")
(comment FelidaeFamily "The family of which cats - housecats, lions, tigers, etc. - are members.")
(disjointWith AudioCommunicating Cleaning)
(comment RNAProcessingType "The collection of the kinds of RNA processing events that can occur prior to #$Translation-RNAToProtein in #$GeneExpression.")
(disjointWith Mammal SheetOfSomeStuff)
(comment EtruscanLetter "characters used by the Etruscans")
(comment Rayon "A collection of textile fibers made from cellulose and having a variety of            uses ranging from clothing to automobile tires.")
(comment DurativeEventType "A collection of collections. If TYPE is an instance of #$DurativeEventType, each instance of TYPE is a \"durative event\" extended through time, i.e., it endures continuously between its starting and ending points, and such points are not simultaneous. As an example, writing a letter is a durative event type, since an event of this type will (except in \"degenerate\" cases) have a distinct starting point, a period of time in the middle during which writing occurs, and an end point at which the letter is written. By contrast, winning a prize is an instantaneous change: up to the moment the event takes place, you don't have the prize, after that you do. Granted, the awarding of the prize might in fact have a physical duration, but from a conceptual or logical point of view it might as well have none. If one thinks of events as the occurrence of \"changes\", one may regard durative events as changes that intrinsically occupy a continuous, non-zero chunk of time, and non-durative events (for which see #$PunctualEventType) as instantaneous changes. #$CumulativeEventType is a proper specialization of this collection, because the cumulativity property (see the salient assertion for #$CumulativeEventType) implies that all process types can have temporal extension. Naturally, many #$DurativeEventTypes are not cumulative, but rather #$AccomplishmentTypes.")
(disjointWith LegalProceeding AthleticActivity)
(disjointWith Currency PrepaidTelephoneCard)
(comment Chihuahua-Dog "A collection of very small dogs, usually 2 to 4 pounds in weight.")
(comment knowsLoginInformationForAccount "#$knowsLoginInformationForAccount is a predicate that relates an

instance of #$IntelligentAgent to an instance of #$ComputerAccount.

(#$knowsLoginInformationForAccount AGENT ACCOUNT) means that

AGENT knows a #$passwordForAccount and a #$usernameForAccount for some

#$UserAccount ACCOUNT on a computational system.")
(disjointWith AdvocacyOrganization StockExchange)
(comment Yo-Yo "The collection of inexpensive toys made of a spool and a
string that winds and unwinds around and from around it as it is
dropped from the hand of a player and rebounds.")
(comment ComputerServerTypeByFunction "#$ComputerServerTypeByFunction is a collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$ComputerServer whose instances all serve the same function.  Note that instances of this collection need not be disjoint with one another.  A single machine may simultaneously play the role of #$NameServer-Network and the role of #$WebServer-Network for a particular network.")
(comment DomesticCleaningTool "objects used in domestic cleaning actions - that is, cleaning of the rooms of a house (not laundry or cleaning associated with cooking)")
(comment VentralRamusS5 "The collection of all S5 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusS5 and #$DorsalRamusS5 branch from SpinalRootS5.  #$VentralRamusS5 supplies the #$CoccygealPlexus.")
(comment RemoteAdministrationProgram "#$RemoteAdministrationProgram is a specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  It is the collection of programs used to administer computers remotely.")
(comment ComputerSoundFile "A specialization of #$ComputerFile-AIS. Each

#$ComputerSoundFile contains a digital representation of some #$AudibleSound, and is linked to an instance of #$ComputerSoundFileTypeByFormat via the

predicate #$fileFormat.")
(comment PhotographicFilm-Unexposed "A piece of photographic film, not yet exposed to light.")
(comment Sporophyte "Sporophytes are the diploid, spore-producing life stage in the plant reproductive life cycle.  #$Meiosis occurs in the reproductive tissues of the sporophyte generation, producing spores [#$Spore-PlantLifeStage], which develop into #$Gametophytes.  Gametophytes produce #$Gametes, which fuse to form a #$Zygote, which develops into a #$Sporophyte, etc.  In the seed plants (which include flowering plants and conifers) and ferns, what we recognize as the plant is the sporophyte generation.  The gametophyte generation is quite small and parasitic on the sporophyte.")
(comment WaxedBoard "Soft surface on board (wood or ivory) for ease of correction and re-use.")
(comment VestibuleOfInnerEar "The collection of all vestibules of #$InnerEars.  Each member of this collection is an ovoid #$Cavity in an #$InnerEar which is connected to the #$SemiCircularCanals on one side and the #$Cochlea on the other.  Sensor spots at the entrance to the other two parts of the #$InnerEar detect head orientation.  The #$OvalWindowInEar is a #$Portal between the #$VestibuleOfInnerEar and the #$MiddleEar which is filled by the base of the #$Stapes.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice ConsumableProduct)
(comment MongolianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Mongolia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Tarot-TheSuit "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which are tarots.")
(comment AthabascanLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of western North America")
(comment FoodProcessor "The collection of electrical food processors.")
(comment Ejaculating "The collection of ejaculation events.  In an individual event in this collection #$Semen passes through the #$Urethra from the #$Prostate out of the body transiting the #$CorpusSpongiosum (which would normally be engorged with blood for this process), the #$GlansPenis, and therefore the length of the #$Penis.  This is a normal subevent (see #$subEvents) of #$SexualCopulation.")
(disjointWith CommunityOrganization MedicalClinic)
(comment Compiler "A specialization of #$ProgrammingLanguageImplementation.  Each instance of #$Compiler is a program that converts another program from some source language (or programming language) to machine language (object code). Some compilers output assembly language which is then converted to machine language by a separate assembler. Cf. #$Interpreter-Computers.")
(comment MailDepartment "A specialization of #$ShippingAndReceivingDepartment. Each instance of this collection is a group of employees who handle an organization's incoming and outgoing mail.")
(comment ControlPanel "A collection of tangible things.  An instance of #$ControlPanel is the physical part of a device where all (or most) of the controls for the device are located.  E.g., the instrument panel of a car or plane.  
Note: A device's control panel may be unattached from (and used to control) the rest of the device --- e.g., a TV remote control.  So in some contexts, the TV is a compound object consisting of two physically separated parts; in other contexts, the remote control is a separate device (a #$ControlDevice) from the TV.  See also #$ControlDevice.")
(comment SweetNLow "#$SweetNLow, a sweetening agent used for coffee, tea, and other potable liquids traditionally requiring table sugar")
(comment AmphiArthrodialJoint "An #$AmphiArthrodialJoint is a #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart in which the bones are connected with slight mobility in all directions.")
(comment CoconutOil "Oil pressed from the dried white flesh of coconuts; also called palm oil.")
(comment cleans "A cleans B.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess ChangeInUserRights)
(comment ComputerCode-Compiled "The subcollection of #$ComputerCode-Binary

which was generated from #$ComputerCode-Source by a #$Compiler.")
(disjointWith MakingSomething Conveying-Generic)
(comment Newsletter "The sort of document published by an organization to keep its members/clients updated on recent events that relate to the organization's business.")
(comment Ovary-AnimalBodyPart "The organ of a female animal that produces eggs")
(comment MiniatureSchnauzer "A collection of small dogs.")
(comment QuemoyAndMatsuIslandsPerson "A person who is a #$QuemoyAndMatsuIslands #$citizens, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment SuperiorDivisionBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all Superior division bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) in left #$Lungs.  This is a short #$BronchialTubeSegment intermediate between a #$LobarBronchus and a #$SegmentalBronchus.  It occurs only in the left #$SuperiorLobeOfLung and it #$branchesInto the left #$AnteriorSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung and the #$ApicoposteriorSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.")
(comment VideoTapeDeckMechanism "#$VideoTape deck mechanism;  can record and play video cassette tapes.  See also #$VideoCassetteRecorder")
(disjointWith InformationRecordingProcess BodyMovementEvent)
(comment LateralSuralCutaneousNerve "The collection of all lateral sural cutaneous #$Nerves.  A #$LateralSuralCutaneousNerve is a branch of a #$CommonPeronealNerve.  It #$innervates the skin of the lateral side of the proximal #$LowerLeg and communicates with the #$PeronealCommunicatingBranch.")
(comment Saffron "Spice derived from the pistil of crocuses, used in cooking, i.e. to spice up rice dishes.")
(comment MailOrderPharmacy "The collection of all pharmacies that sell drugs by mail (i.e., USMail, UPS, or some other surface delivery organization is the mode of transporting the items to be delivered to the customer).")
(comment programCopyCode "(#$programCopyCode COPY CODE) means that the #$ComputerCode CODE is source or executable code for the #$ComputerProgramCopy COPY.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseRespondsToUDPBroadcastRequests "#$VulnerableBecauseRespondsToUDPBroadcastRequests is a specialization of
 #$NetworkVulnerability.  It is a vulnerability of a computer
 that arises as a consequence of the configuration of the OS
 installed on the computer.  Computers with this vulnerability have not disabled responses to UDP broadcast addresses.  See also #$VulnerableToFraggleAttack.")
(disjointWith Autotroph Heterotroph)
(comment LatinCapitalLetterG "The capital letter 'G'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$G-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterG.")
