(comment ExtensionTelephone "A collection of telephones. Each telephone extension can   be reached by dialing a normal telephone number and then either   entering an instance of PhoneNumberExtension (usually 4 digits) via   a touch tone keypad or having the call routed manually by the person   who answers the main number.")
(comment Tree-ThePlant "A specialization of #$Plant-Woody.  Each instance of #$Tree-ThePlant is a tall woody plant (typical mature specimens are usually taller than a person or a bush), generally having a branching form overall, and with roots in the ground, a trunk, and the branches having numerous leaves exposed to the sky.  Notable specializations of #$Tree-ThePlant include #$OakTree, #$MapleTree, #$GiantSequoia, and #$BananaTree.")
(comment AccountOperatorAccount "Account Operators can create new user accounts, but they do not have the authority
to assign user rights.")
(comment ElectricalSwitch "A device that is placed in the path of electrical current (on a wire) to control its passage. In one position, the switch allows current to pass, and when moved to the 'off' position, the connection is broken and current can no longer pass.")
(comment GenitofemoralNerve "The collection of all genitofemoral #$Nerves.  #$GenitofemoralNerves are paired structures in the #$Pelvis.  Each #$GenitofemoralNerve is formed by branches from #$VentralRamusL1 and  #$VentralRamusL2 on its side of the body.  The #$GenitofemoralNerve branches into the #$GenitofemoralNerve-GenitalBranch and the #$GenitofemoralNerve-FemoralBranch.")
(comment GroomsCake "The collection of #$GroomsCakes. These are cakes served at a wedding reception. In contrast to #$BridesCakes, they are often some really rich flavor, like chocolate, although they are usually not as architecturally fancy as the #$BridesCake.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfJavaScriptEnabledBrowser "#$VulnerableBecauseOfJavaScriptEnabledBrowser is a specialization of
 #$VulnerableBecauseOfBrowserConfiguration.  It is a vulnerability of a
 computer that arises as a consequence of configuring a browser on a
 computer to enable JavaScript.")
(comment WindowsNTAccount "A person with an instance of #$WindowsNTAccount is able to

access storage space and CPU time on an instance of

#$NTAccountSystem. The level of access of the account depends on

whether it is an instance of #$UserAccount, #$AdministratorAccount, etc.")
(comment WorldWideWebSite "#$WorldWideWebSite is the subset of #$WebSites accessible from the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource.  Each instance of #$WorldWideWebSite is composed of a homepage and zero or more additional instances of #$WebPage-CW connected by hyperlinks to the site's homepage. A #$WorldWideWebSite is maintained by a single webmaster or group of webmasters, and is thematically unified in some way, often as an individual's or corporation's 'presence' on the #$WorldWideWeb-DynamicIndexedInfoSource. A #$WorldWideWebSite is designed with the intention that a visitor will enter the site via its homepage, and navigate to other pages in the site via hyperlinks.")
(comment SpraySubstance "Substances which are intended to be applied by spraying.")
(comment Chemoorganotroph "The collection of all #$Chemotrophs that process organic chemical
compounds for energy.  These #$Bacterium have two main types of
metabolism: #$Fermentation-Bacterium and #$Respiration-Bacterium.
This group includes all human pathogens.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice ControlDevice)
(comment Radicle "The embryonic root, which in the seed is directed towards the micropile.")
(comment VietnamesePerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Vietnam, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith AmusementParkOperator SportsOrganization)
(comment Monocular "Like #$Binoculars except with a single lens system

and for use with a single eye.")
(comment EducationalMovie "#$EducationalMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW, each of which has educational content.")
(comment Kissing "The physical act of kissing. There is not necessarily a receiver, so this is not necessarily a #$Communicating (e.g., a little kid kissing a favorite doll, a sailor kissing land after surviving a shipwreck).")
(comment MakingBread "A specialization of #$PreparingFoodItem .  Each instance of #$MakingBread is an event in which bread is made.  Making bread typically involves includes kneading the dough, letting the dough rise, and baking the bread (see #$BakingBread).")
(comment positionToFill "#$PositionSelection involves looking for a person to fill a position.  This predicate gives the organization and position to be filled in a such a selecting.")
(disjointWith HarvesterAgriculturalImplement Tractor)
(disjointWith OperatingSystem ApplicationProgram)
(disjointWith CommunicationsOrganization ActivityTypeFocusGroup)
(comment KeyRing "A key ring is a device that holds keys.")
(comment EuascomycetesClass "A Class of fungi. Includes the fungi that cause Dutch Elm disease and oak wilt.")
(disjointWith Head-AnimalBodyPart Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment RespiratoryBronchiole "The collection of all respiratory bronchioles (small #$BronchialTubes in the #$Lungs): those #$Bronchioles that each adjoin the #$TerminalBronchioles at one end, and the #$AlveolarDuct at the other, one step before the #$AlveolarSacs.  A #$RespiratoryBronchiole has active alveoli along its sides, unlike the #$TerminalBronchioles, and is part of the respiring part of the lung, the #$PulmonaryAcinus.")
(comment DNATypeByOrganismType "A collection of collections, each instance will be a collection of DNAMolecules categorized according to the type of organism in which they are found.")
(comment NebulizationSolution "The collection of all nebulization solutions.  A Nebulization solution is one which will be atomized for use as a fine spray.  For example, young asthmatics use a machine which takes a nebulization solution and turns it into an aerosol spray.")
(comment ToxicGas "Gases which are usually considered harmful to breathe.")
(comment ComputerInformationStorageMedia "#$ComputerInformationStorageMedia is the subset of #$InformationStorageMedia whose instances are all and only those entities on which instances of #$ComputerFileCopy are stored.")
(comment WindshieldWiperFluid "The fluid that squirts from your car to clean the windshield (and is sold).")
(comment Almanac "Systematized listing of information on either specifc or general topics.  Often in book form.")
(comment Urinating "The collection of urination events")
(comment SetGIDFault-bin "#$SetGIDFault-bin is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if it runs SGID bin (i.e., with an effective GID of bin) and can be exploited to yield bin group privileges to an authorized or unauthorized user.")
(comment ShihTzu "A collection of small dogs with very long fur.")
(comment Baron "The collection of all barons, or male persons who hold hereditary baronial titles in the systems of nobility of Europe, or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf. See also #$Baroness.")
(disjointWith JudicialOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment CD-R "#$CD-R is the collection of `Write Once' CompactDiscs. With the use of a #$CD-RDrive or #$CD-RWDrive, a user can record data onto a #$CD-R disc. This process can only be performed once per #$CD-R disc. This collection contains both blank and already `burned' or recorded #$CD-Rs. Note, the collection #$CD-RW contains compact discs that are `Rewriteable'.")
(comment FlexorCarpiUlnaris "The #$Collection of all instances of #$FlexorCarpiUlnaris #$Muscle.  The #$FlexorCarpiUlnaris flexes the #$Wrist in the ulnar direction or combines in adducting the #$Wrist.")
(comment Bag "The collection of bags used as containers")
(comment OrganicMaterial "A collection of tangible things.  Each instance of #$OrganicMaterial is a tangible thing composed of one or more types of organic #$Molecule.  Instances of #$OrganicMaterial usually have their origin in the bodies (or other products) of living things.  Since some organic substances can be synthesized, #$OrganicMaterial is not a subcollection of #$NaturalTangibleStuff.  Chemically, instances of #$OrganicMaterial have fairly (or very) complex carbon-based structures.  Examples include all instances of the collections #$Oil, #$DNAStuff, #$Alcohol-Compound, #$Ivory, and #$AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment BaseSurfaceOfLung "The collection of base (basal or bottom) surface areas of #$Lungs, each being above the #$Diaphragm-BodyPart: a concave area between the medial surface and the angular edge at the bottom, the #$InferiorMarginOfLung.  It is also called the diaphragmatic surface.")
(comment VanillaExtract "A alcolhol extract of vanillin, derived from vanilla beans, which is used as a flavoring agent.")
(comment AutoMechanicShop "An organization which is a local customer point of contact, and which performs repairs on automobiles and other road vehicles, but not body work.")
(comment MassNoun-Generic "The collection of all mass nouns.  Mass nouns are syntactically singular, and often they denote stufflike things. Example: 'water'. This collection also includes proper mass nouns like 'Pepsi', agentive mass nouns like 'moisturizer', etc.")
(comment AudioWareComputerProgram "A subclass of #$Warez-ComputerProgram. Freely downloadable #$ComputerProgram-CWs that can be used to process or listen to #$ComputerSoundFiles. ")
(disjointWith PhotographAsArtForm TextualMaterial)
(comment Saliva "The fluid secreted from the salivary glands of the mouth")
(comment dependents "'(#$dependents PERSON DEPENDENT)' means that DEPENDENT is one of PERSON's dependents, that is, DEPENDENT depends upon PERSON for some type of support, especially financial.")
(comment MonocotSubclass "#$MonocotSubclass is a specialization of #$FloweringPlant and instance of #$BiologicalSubclass.  It is an angiosperm subclass containing taxa whose members have only one cotyledon in the embryo phase and lack normal secondary growth.")
(comment CanadianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Canada, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment ArtObjectTypeDisplayedInFn "(#$ArtObjectTypeDisplayedInFn ART PLACE) denotes the group of
object that belong to a certain kind of #$ArtObjects that are displayed in PLACE.")
(comment birthParent "A predicate relating a birth event to the parent giving birth.  (#$birthParent BIRTH PARENT) means that the #$Animal PARENT is the parent giving birth in the #$BirthEvent BIRTH.  Note that PARENT is typically also the #$femaleParentActor of some preceding #$BiologicalReproductionEvent.")
(comment DeadLanguage "A specialization of #$NaturalLanguage.  Each instance of #$DeadLanguage is a natural language that is no longer spoken as a native language (though written texts may survive and continue to be interpretable -- as is the case with #$LatinLanguage).")
(comment PorchSwing "A seat (usually for several people) suspended by chains from a porch's ceiling for swinging to and fro on for pleasure.")
(comment ComputerStorageDevice "The collection of devices used by computers to store information, e.g., floppy disks, direct access storage devices (DASD), optical disk devices, microfilm libraries, and 5.25 inch hard drives.")
(comment AudioRecordedObject "A collection of information bearing objects (IBOs).  Each element of #$AudioRecordedObject is a tangible object (such as an audiocassette tape) that contains audio information.  For mass-produced audio, see #$RecordedSoundProduct.")
(comment Mildew "Mildew is a fungal growth that can occur on the shower curtain or as a disease of plants.  Mildews may belong to the fungus family Peronosporaceae(downy mildew) or to the fungus order Erysiphales (powdery mildew).")
(comment DidrexProduct "A CNS stimulant commonly used for the short-term treatment of obesity.")
(comment SmellPerception "The collection of sensory #$Perceivings in which a #$PerceptualAgent #$smells something and thereby acquires information about it.")
(comment DorsalRamusL2 "The collection of all L2 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiL2 and DorsalRamiL2 branch from SpinalRootL2.  DorsalRamiL2 supplies the ????.")
(comment CuticleRemover "Substances used for removing overgrowth of cuticles from surface of fingernails.")
(disjointWith BiologicalDevelopmentEvent BodyMovementEvent)
(comment regexFileMatch "A text-processing predicate used to indicate a match between a 'regular expression template' and a string of characters the occcurs within a computer file. (#$regexFileMatch REGEX COMPFILE) means that the #$RegularExpression template (or 'regex') REGEX matches some substring within the computer file COMPFILE.  It allows for 'wildcard characters' and other regular expression features in the template. The rules for what characters to use in the regex, and what constitutes a valid match, depend on the particular regular expression matcher being used. (Regular expressions are used for matching in the GREP, EGREP, AWK, VI, TCL, Emacs, PERL and PYTHON programs.) Some regex features are common to all such programs, including these: . [...] [^...] char ? * + ^ $ \\< \\> | (...) \\1,\\2,\\3,... Some other features vary. This predicate assumes that the PERL specification is used for regular expression matching. Briefly: The period matches 'any character'. Square brackets match a class of characters, those listed, possibly with ranges like A-Z or a-z or 1-8. Square brackets with a caret-character as the first included character match the class of characters other than those listed between the brackets. Backslash-character means the following special character is directly matched and is not treated as a special character. Caret matches the position of the start-of-line. Dollar-sign matches the position at the end-of-line. \\< matches any start of word. \\> matches any end-of-word. Parentheses group whatever they enclose. A character or group followed by a question-mark is optional; it matches zero or one occurence of that group or charater. A character or group followed by an asterisk matches any number of repetitions that group or character, including zero. A character or group followed by a plus-sign matches one or more repetitions of that group or character. A vertical bar | separates alternative matches -- either may succeed. \\1,\\2,\\3, etc. are backreference variables to which each matched group is assigned in order, and they will match later occurrences of the assigned group. For further details, see standard documentation for regular expressions or for PERL.  See also #$regexStringMatch.")
(comment Sail-Device "The sail of a sailboat, sailboard, or other wind-powered transportation vehicle.")
(comment Bacteriophage "Also called \"phages\", this is a type of virus

which specifically attacks bacteria.")
(comment ResearchPaper "A collection consisting of all instances of #$TextualPCW which are research papers. The absract works -- not their physical embodiments.")
(comment Hip "The area on the side of the thighs, just below the waist")
(disjointWith HardwareTool FoodUtensil)
(comment Stomate "Specialized structures in the epidermis of plants, consisting of a minute pore and two surrounding guard cells, which allow for exchange of gasses between the external atmosphere and the substomatal space with its associated intercellular spaces.  The guard cells regulate the size of the pore by changes in their turgor pressure.")
(comment SovietUnionPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$UnionOfSovietSocialistRepublics, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment CellPhoneDataCable "#$CellPhoneDataCable are used for uploading and

downloading information to instances of #$CellularTelephone.  They can be used to

 connect #$CellularTelephones to #$Modems or to #$Headphones.")
