(comment SylvianFissure "The collection of all Sylvian fissures of mamalian #$Brains.  An individual #$SylvianFissure (or 'lateral fissure/sulcus') is a brain sulcus (#$SulcusOfBrain) between the #$TemporalLobe and #$ParietalLobe on one side of the brain.  The #$TemporalLobe lies below the #$SylvianFissure and the #$ParietalLobe lies above it.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization RetailStore)
(comment HuntingRifle "Rifle used for hunting.")
(disjointWith PhotoEquipmentStore AutoDealership)
(comment Crystalware "A drinking vessel used at formal meals made of fine glass usually with a trace amount of lead.")
(comment BiologicalKingdom "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$BiologicalKingdom is a sub-collection of #$Organism-Whole whose instances all belong to one of the highest, most general taxonomic divisions of organisms.  Notable instances of #$BiologicalKingdom include #$Animal, #$Plant, #$ProtistaKingdom, and #$MoneraKingdom.")
(disjointWith Collision IBTGeneration)
(comment BreastImplant-Saline "The collection of #$BreastImplants consisting of a silicone shell filled with a saline solution.")
(comment GaelicLetter "An abbreviated set of letters usually but not always similar to Roman")
(comment Polyester "A collection of synthetic resins and fibers used in making clothes, ropes,           and many other items.")
(disjointWith BodyMovementEvent (TransportViaFn TransportationDevice))
(disjointWith HouseholdAttachment RoofOfAConstruction)
(comment BassetHound "A collection of short-legged, sturdy hunting dogs.")
(comment DomesticCleaningStuff " Domestic")
(comment DorsalRamusC0 "The collection of all C0 dorsal rami.  #$VentralRamusC0 and #$DorsalRamusC0 branch from SpinalRootC0.  #$DorsalRamusC0 supplies the #$Skin over the #$Coccyx.")
(comment VascoIdiazabal-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Vasco Idiazabal, a Basque 

sheep's milk cheese.")
(comment ScreenSaver "This collection includes all instances of #$ScreenSaver software. A #$ScreenSaver is a program that displays an animated image that is activated on a personal computer display when no user activity has been sensed for a certain time. The original purpose of a screen saver was to prevent burn-in (the burning of an image into the phosphor inside the cathode ray tube after hours of the same image being rescanned).")
(comment AnimalLine "leashes, reins, etc - the various tools used to lead animals.")
(comment FillingOutAForm "Filling in the blanks on a standard form, with information that pertains to the current situation.")
(comment PineappleOrder "A biological order within the monocot sublass in the plant kingdom.  Members are often epiphytic, meaning they use other plants as a substrate (grow on them), but don't get any water or nutrients fromthem.")
(comment TanzanianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Tanzania, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment CeleronProcessor "A specialization of #$Microprocessor, #$CeleronProcessor is the collection of all Celeron processors developed by #$IntelCorporation.")
(comment Ten-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '10.'")
(comment YokutLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment Blanket "A large typically rectangular piece of soft fabric, used as a bedcovering for warmth.")
(disjointWith CommunityOrganization BodyPiercingStudio)
(comment versionOfSoftware "A predicate relating two #$SoftwareObjects. (#$versionOfSoftware UNVERSIONED VERSIONED) means that VERSIONED is a version of UNVERSIONED. In most cases VERSIONED will be a NART expressed using #$SoftwareVersionFn.  Note that #$versionOfSoftware is more specific than #$genlPrograms.  Although it is true that (#$genlPrograms #$GnuEmacs #$Emacs-TheProgram), #$GnuEmacs is not a version of #$Emacs-TheProgram in the manner expressed by #$versionOfSoftware.")
(comment SecurityDepartment "A specialization of #$Department. Each instance of this collection is a department which performs some kind of security-related function for an organization. Notable specializations include #$CampusPolice and #$SystemsAdministrationDepartment.")
(comment PhotographicFlashDevice "Devices used to produce a bright flash to illuminate the subject of a photograph.")
(comment EqualTheSweetener "Equal, a sweetening agent used for coffee, tea, and other potable liquids traditionally requiring table sugar")
(comment uniqueAnatomicalPartOfType "(#$uniqueAnatomicalPartOfType ANIMAL TYPE PART) means that the #$AnimalBodyPart PART is an anatomical part (see the predicate #$anatomicalParts) of the #$Animal ANIMAL, and is an instance of the #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType TYPE.")
(comment MainBronchus "The collection of all primary or main bronchi, the big #$BronchialTubes each leading from the #$TracheobronchialJunction into the #$Lung of an #$AirBreathingVertebrate.  The PrimaryBronchus branches out into smaller, lobar bronchi within the #$Lung.  Note that the primary bronchi in Human beings are somewhat asymmetric -- the left differs in size and angle from the right.")
(comment Sugar-Table "Common table sugar, or sucrose. A white crystalline substance used to sweeten foods and beverages. Molecules have the empirical formula C12H22O11.  ")
(disjointWith Cleaning PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment HypodermicNeedle "the needle part of a hypodermic syringe")
(disjointWith Boating LongDistanceAutomobileTransportation)
(comment BondCertificate "The collection of certificates issued by a company to represent a bond debt.")
(comment Cervix "The collection of all cervixes.  An individual #$Cervix is a narrow opening from the #$Vagina into the #$Uterus of a female #$Mammal.")
(comment SharPei "A collection of medium-sized dogs with blue-black tongues.  Also called           the Chinese Shar-Pei.  Note that the natural language name for this dog is Shar-Pei, not Shar Pei.")
(comment CocosIslandsPerson "A person who is a #$CocosIslands #$citizens, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization ChamberOfCommerce)
(comment TruckTire "The collection of all #$Tires that belong on #$Trucks.")
(comment LateralBasalSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all lateral basal segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a (left or right) #$InferiorLobeOfLung that supplies the #$LateralBasalSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung.  It branches from the #$InferiorLobarBronchus.")
(comment AudioAmplifierComponent "Electronic Device which amplifies electrical audio signals.")
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure MakingSomething)
(comment PeronealCommunicatingBranch "The collection of all peroneal communicating branch #$Nerves.  A #$PeronealCommunicatingBranch is in the #$LowerLeg and connects that leg's #$SuralNerve with its #$LateralSuralCutaneousNerve.")
(comment EdibleFat "Fats used in cooking - #$CookingOil, Butter, Shortening, Lard...This should be connected to #$EdibleOil and Fat somehow.")
(comment MailOrderCompany "The collection of all companies that sell products by mail. (i.e., USMail, UPS, or some other surface delivery organization is the mode of transporting the items to be delivered to the customer)")
(comment DesignProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used for designing something.")
(comment BlisterAgentStuff "The collection of #$ToxicSubstances designed to destroy skin and tissue. They may also cause blindness and respiratory damage.")
(comment Packet-UDP-Spoofed "#$Packet-UDP-Spoofed is the collection of packets used in instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation-Fraggle.")
(disjointWith Primate Pachyderm)
(comment LatinSmallLetterG "The lowercase letter 'g'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$G-TheLetter, and #$LatinCapitalLetterG.")
(comment SouthKoreanCar "Cars made in South Korea")
(comment Applauding-Clapping "To clap the hands to express approval.")
(comment Pombe-FissionYeast "Species of fission yeast commonly used for studies on cell cycle
control.")
(comment ParallelComputerCable "The collection of computer cable

to connect parallel devices.")
(comment SpeciallyCharteredInstitution "The collection of all instances of #$Organization organized in accordance with a particular jurisdiction's law governing the organization of institutions permitted to participate in particular activities or businesses.  For example, within the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, #$Organizations are allowed to participate in banking or savings or savings and loan activities only to the extent that they are chartered by specific state or federal laws.  Instances of #$LegalCorporation or #$Partnership are not permitted to engage in those types of activities.  The collection #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitution is disjoint with other instances of #$OrganizationByEntityType; those collections have instances of #$Organization that can ordinarily engage in a wide variety of activities and businesses.  By contrast, instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitutions are created pursuant to specific statutory authority and can only engage in particular types of activities and businesses as authorized by that statute.  Within the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, some #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitutions are organized pursuant to federal law, while other instances are organized pursuant to state law.  Instances of #$SpeciallyCharteredInstitution are either #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganizations or #$PrivateSectorOrganizations; they are not #$GovernmentalOrganizations.")
(comment PayPhone "A collection of telephones. Each pay phone is operated by   determining at the beginning of each call how the call will be paid   for. The caller either deposits enough coins to cover the cost of   the call, inserts a pre-paid calling card into a card-reader on the   telephone, or arranges to have the call paid for by dialing a   special number or talking to an operator. Emergency and toll-free   calls can be made without doing any of that.")
(comment Cameloid "Camels and Llamas")
(comment BackupOperatorAccount "The Backup Operators group is a built-in group for Windows NT Servers (i.e., instances of #$NTDomainServer).  Members of this group have the right to log on to a Windows NT Server locally, shut down the server, back up files and directories on the server and restore files and directories to the server. Backup Operators group members do not have the right to manage servers remotely.")
(comment PowerCord "The cord that provides electricity to devices that need it.")
(comment VentralRamusT9 "The collection of all T9 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT9 and #$DorsalRamusT9 branch from SpinalRootT9.  #$VentralRamusT9 supplies below the #$NinthRib.")
(comment Ham "The collection of hams. Ham is a meat cut from the thigh of a #$Pig. Hams are often cooked by smoking.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfJavaEnabledBrowser "#$VulnerableBecauseOfJavaEnabledBrowser is a specialization of

#$VulnerableBecauseOfListeningBrowserInterpreter.  It is a vulnerability of a

computer that arises as a consequence of configuring a browser on a

computer to enable Java programs to run.")
(comment UnixAccount "A person with an instance of #$UnixAccount is able to

access storage space and CPU time on an instance of

#$UnixAccountSystem. The level of access of the account depends on

whether it is an instance of #$UserAccount, #$RootAccount, etc.")
(disjointWith ComputerProcessRunning FluidFlowEvent)
(comment StainedGlassWindow "The collection of all windows made of stained glass")
(comment eventAffectsPlantPart "(#$eventAffectsPlantPart EVT PART) says that EVT affects #$PlantPart PART.  For example, (#$eventAffectsOrganismPart WeedingEvent562 RootSystem075) says that WeedingEvent562 affects RootSystem075.")
(comment musicTracks "The tracks of an #$Album-CW or #$SingleRecording-CW")
(comment ReproductiveSystem "The collection of all animals' reproductive systems.  A #$ReproductiveSystem is a system of organs used by the #$Animal for reproduction; i.e., for creating an offspring, a new member of that species.  
Note:  Strictly speaking, it might be more accurate to describe a #$ReproductiveSystem as containing the above sorts of systems for a mated male and female of a sexual species, as only that combined system is capable of actually producing an offspring.  But most of the things one wants to say about a #$ReproductiveSystem really do only make sense for one single animal at a time.  So think of reproduction as a cooperative activity, such as having a conversation, where we still refer to each animal's incomplete reproductive system as a #$ReproductiveSystem.")
(disjointWith DomesticatedAnimalFood Pasta)
(comment Root "The subterranean parts of plants.  Roots provide support and obtain water and mineral nutrients from the surrounding soil.")
(comment Guinea-BissauPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Guinea-Bissau, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment operatesFacilities "'(#$operatesFacilities AGENT FACILITY)' means that AGENT is responsible for the operation and running of the FACILITY.  The FACILITY may be either all or part of a #$ConstructionArtifact and its furnishings or movable equipment that can be operated at any number of different locations (e.g., a crane and its operator, an amusement park and the agents that manage and operate it) or it may be some natural or physical phenomenon (e.g. #$ZionNationalPark).")
(comment GiftWrap "The collection of all gift wrap. Gift wrap is usually

paper with some sort of design on it, but it need not be paper. Gift wrap is

any sheet-like product intended for wrapping gifts.")
(disjointWith TypicalArgTypePredicate TypicalInterArgTypePredicate)
(comment Wick "The string-like thing that delivers fuel to a lantern or candle flame.")
(comment DramaticMovie "#$DramaticMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which relates a story involving human conflict.")
(comment WashingHands "What one does with soap and water to clean one's hands.")
(comment MacaroniAndCheese "This is a dish of macaroni noodles served in a cheese sauce.")
(comment CooperativeOrganization "A cooperative is an organization in which each of its members contribute to the organization's capital.  In return the members get dividends and the right to vote in the organization's elections (for board of directors).")
(disjointWith HarvesterAgriculturalImplement GoCart)
(comment Shareware-ProgramDistributionType "The collection of all computer program types that are distributed
as shareware. When a computer program type such as the game
#$Maelstrom-TheGame is distributed as shareware, users are allowed to
make copies of the program and use it freely for a trial period,
usually lasting thirty days. At the end of the trial period the user
is requested to decide whether to discard the copy freely obtained or
send to the distributor a modest fee.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup ManufacturingOrganization)
(comment EmeryBoard "Short, flat, abrasive-coated stick used for smoothing or shaping one's fingernails or toenails.")
(disjointWith Cheek-Facial Trunk-BodyCore)
(comment Tole "The collection for tole, a type of lacquered or enameled           metalware used for trays, lamps, etc. It's commonly dark-green,            ivory, or black.")
(comment AfricanGreyParrot "A specialization of #$Parrot.  African Grey Parrots are indigenous to Africa, and have mostly grey feathers with red feathers on the tail.  African Greys are widely believed to make good pets, and can learn to reproduce the sounds of human speech (and indeed many other sounds) very accurately.")
(comment PCComputer "This is the collection of all PC computers. `PC' here does not stand for 

`personal computer' but rather indicates the kind of architecture (X86)

the computer uses. #$PCComputers typically run Windows operating systems but

this is not their defining feature (a PC running Linux is still a PC).")
(comment AutomotiveFluid "Fluids used in cars, e.g., #$AntiFreeze, #$BrakeFluid, ..., but not water")
(comment MagazineCopy "The collection of instances of #$PeriodicalCopy appearing in magazine format.  As of 1998, instances of #$MagazineCopy are often elements of #$HardcopyInformationBearingObject")
(comment Knee "Joint between the thigh and lower leg")
(comment AttributiveOnlyAdjFrame "Frames for adjectives that can be used attributively but not 

predicatively, e.g., \"former\" in \"the former President.\"")
(comment ShetlandSheepdog "A collection of small to medium-sized dogs, also known as   Shelties.  Related to the Collie.")
(comment Viscountess "The collection of all viscountesses, or female persons who hold hereditary viscount-level titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch (whether in their own right, by marriage or by courtesy) in the systems of nobility of European countries like #$France, #$Italy, #$Spain, or the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland, or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf.  See also #$Viscount.")
(disjointWith ProductDisplayOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment CD-RW "#$CD-RW or CD-ReWritable is a standardised CompactDisc on which you  can write and rewrite data. You re-use the disc space of deleted files  (like you do with a floppy or harddisk) or erase the complete disc. Note, the  collection #$CD-R contains CompactDiscs that are only `Writeable Once'.")
(comment InternalIntercostalSeries "The #$Collection of all sets of #$InternalIntercostal #$Muscles.  Instances are series of #$InternalIntercostal #$Muscles on one side of the body of an #$Organism-Whole.")
(comment PlasticBag "The collection of bags made of plastic")
(comment SegmentalBronchus "The collection of all segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) in #$Lungs.  Each SegmentalBronchus branches off of a larger #$LobarBronchus and supplies air to one #$SegmentOfLung.")
(comment Breakfast "The morning meal.")
(comment AutoRepairShop "An organization which is a local customer point of contact, and which repairs automobiles/road vehicles.")
(comment FreeThingOfTypeFn "The function #$FreeThingOfTypeFn, applied to some collection of objects, substances or services, yields the collection of all instances of that type which are available basically for #$Free-MonetaryCost, that is, that can be obtained at zero #$cost, available for nothing  - without payment of money or other 'consideration'.  Thus (#$FreeThingOfTypeFn #$Automobile) denotes the collection of all cars that are available for free.")
(comment ChatRoomBackdoorComputerProgram "The class of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used by #$AmericaOnlineInc subscribers in order to gain unregistered entry into a #$ChatRoom.")
(comment BacteriumTypeBySporulationAbility "A partition on the collection #$Bacterium, reflecting class
ability or inability to form endospores.")
(comment Check-TenderObject "A specialization of #$TenderObject.  Each instance of #$Check-TenderObject is a financial instrument, drawn on a particular #$CheckingAccount at some instance of #$FinancialOrganization (q.v.), which is redeemable for a monetary value by the agent who is the payee.  The financial organization pays the payee funds from the account, upon proper presentation of the check. See also #$SaleByCheck.")
(comment SkinOil "Oil secreted by glands, e.g.  hair follicles to keep your skin or hair from drying out.")
(comment competitors "(#$competitors AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT1 and AGENT2 are competitors.")
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject)
(disjointWith MonocotSubclass DicotSubclass)
(comment PeruvianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Peru, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith LanguageGroupingType SpatialThingTypeByShape)
(comment Netting "A fabric of cords or wires that cross at regular intervals and are knotted at the crossings.")
(comment Fight-Physical "The collection of all #$ConflictEvents in which two or more #$competingAgents try to subdue each other by inflicting physical injury. A #$Fight-Physical may be between individuals or between groups, and may involve weapons or not. The #$competingAgents may be #$Persons or #$NonPersonAnimals. The fighting must be mutual; if one side refuses to attack the other or tries to flee instead of attacking, it is not a #$Fight-Physical.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedAccess "A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible for unauthorized users to gain some kind of user rights on it (where this has been deliberately left vague and includes such things as reading files, using devices connected to the computer). Sometimes this occurs because a piece of software on the machine has an #$AccessValidationFault, sometimes because it is on a network which has been wrongly configured.")
(comment ComputerCluster "A computer cluster consists of one or more computer hardware components and is seperate from the rest of a system because of physical or logical requirements.")
(comment VideoRecordedObject "A collection of information bearing objects (IBOs).  Each element of #$VideoRecordedObject is a tangible object (such as a videotape) that contains visual information.  For mass-produced videos, see #$RecordedVideoProduct.")
(comment Advil "The collection of drugs for relieving pain that are produced 
under the brandname Advil.")
(comment Fume "a vapor of some volatile substance that smells bad")
(comment LumboSacralPlexus "The collection of all lumbosacral plexi.  The #$LumboSacralPlexus on one side of a body is the combination of the #$LumbarPlexus and the #$SacralPlexus.  The #$LumbarPlexus is usually supplied by #$VentralRamusT12, #$VentralRamusL1, #$VentralRamusL2, #$VentralRamusL3 and #$VentralRamusL4.  The #$SacralPlexus is usually supplied by #$VentralRamusL4, #$VentralRamusL5, #$VentralRamusS1, #$VentralRamusS2, #$VentralRamusS3, and #$VentralRamusS4.  #$VentralRamusL3 sometimes supplies the #$SacralPlexus and #$VentralRamusL5 sometimes supplies the #$LumbarPlexus but not both in the same body.")
(comment Doughnut "A fried cake.")
(comment designatedSecondaryResidence "`(#$designatedSecondaryResidence OWNER HOME YEAR)' means that HOME meets certain
qualifications set by the IRS, that HOME is not OWNER's #$primaryResidence, and that
OWNER has designated HOME as his/her other home the interest on which can be claimed
as a tax deduction for YEAR. A taxpayer may own several #$secondaryResidences which meet the
IRS's qualifications, so being a #$designatedSecondaryResidence can in part be a matter of
choice on the part of the taxpayer.")
(comment BathBrush "Collection of brushes that are made for scrubbing the body while bathing.")
(comment HominidaeFamily "A specialization of #$Primate.  The collection #$HominidaeFamily is the family to which humans, human primate ancestors, and chimps, gorillas, and orangutans belong. Hominids range in weight from 48 kg to 270 kg. Males are larger than females. Hominids are the largest primates, with robust bodies and well-developed forearms. A notable specialization of this collection is #$HomoGenus.")
(disjointWith ArtObject ComputationalSystem)
(comment Banister "A stairway railing and the upright posts that support it.  This is the railing on the outer side of an open stairwell. Also called a balustrade.")
(comment Acoelomate "This is the collection of (individual) organisms that

are have three well-defined germ layers,  an ectoderm, endoderm, and mesoderm, but

lack a coelem. A coelem is a fluid-filled body cavity between the outer body wall and

the gut. Members of the phylum Platyhelminthes (flat worms), as well as some

Nemertea (ribbon worms) are #$Acoelomates.")
(comment Chest-BodyPart "The collection of the chests of #$Animals.  The animal's chest is its #$AnimalBodyPart region located between its neck and its abdomen.  For people and many other types of animals, the chest is bounded by (defined by, given shape by) the animal's ribcage.")
(disjointWith TransportationDevice Clothing-Generic)
(comment Hypocotyl "The region in the angiosperm body between the root system and the shoot system; in the embryo, the region between the cotyledons and the radicle; also called the vascular transition zone, because it is here that the transition between the root vascular arrangement and the shoot vascular arrangement occurs.")
(comment FijianPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Fiji, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment UnderwaterCamera "The collection of cameras which can be used

underwater.")
(comment SpoofedUsernameAndPasswordPopUpWindow "#$SpoofedUsernameAndPasswordPopUpWindow is a collection of programs
written in #$JavaScriptProgrammingLanguage and
#$JavaProgrammingLanguage.  Instances of this collection are designed
to run inside browser windows, and to request username/password
combinations.")
(comment DishRag "A small, approximately one-square-foot, piece of rag  used to clean things in the kitchen sink.")
(disjointWith SportsCompetition Mounting-Installing)
(comment TricuspidValve "The collection of all tricuspid #$HeartValves.  Each instance of this collection is #$Valve at the #$Portal from the right auricle [#$AuricleOfHeart] into the right #$VentricleOfHeart which prevents #$Blood from passing back into the auricle during systole.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization FoodServiceOrganization)
(comment ComputerHardwareServiceMC "Class of product types which are service events that deal with computer hardware - training, installation, maintenance, etc.")
(comment ExecutableExploit "#$MaliciousComputerPrograms that are

distinct, executable programs.")
(disjointWith AutoDealership PrintShop)
(comment PrimaryTranscript-FivePrimeEnd "The collection of 5' ends of any primary transcript of an RNA molecule.")
(comment BreastImplant-Silicone "The collection of #$BreastImplants consisting of a silicone shell filled with a silicone #$Gel.")
(comment RunicLetter "characters with straight or angular lines suitable for cutting into wood")
(comment AirCoolingDevice "The collection of devices used to cool the air in humanly-occupied constructs. Different from freezers or refrigerators, whose primary functions are NOT to cool the air, but to cool something else.")
(comment ClothingTypeByFormality "This type-level collection represents one way of dividing #$ClothingOutfit into subcollections.  Instances are specializations of #$ClothingOutfit suitable to certain activities or occasions, such as #$FormalWear or #$SportsAttire.")
(disjointWith MaintenanceEvent RecreationalActivity)
(disjointWith Fireplace RoofOfAConstruction)
(comment ArabianHorse "A breed of horse originating in what was Arabia.")
(disjointWith SellingOrganization AdvocacyOrganization)
(comment Die-TheCube "The collection of all small, regular objects with clearly defined and labeled sides, used to generate random numbers. The most common variety are cubes, with dots representing the numbers 1 to 6.")
(comment SilverwarePiece "Not necessarily silver - eating implements like knife, fork, spoon.  These are not #$GraspingImplements.")
(comment PleuralCavity "The collection of pleural cavities, each being a normally  collapsed chamber of a #$Pleura in the #$Chest-BodyPart.  It is made of an internal #$VisceralPleura and a  more superficial #$ParietalPleura, which together form the walls of  the #$PleuralCavity.  There are separate Pleural Cavities on the left  and right.  The #$PleuralCavity is slippery inside and normally empty except for a small amount of mucous.  The inner #$VisceralPleura membranes directly surround, and are  attached to, the #$Lungs.  Each #$PleuralCavity is in one side of the  the #$ChestCavity.  ")
(comment Treccione-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Treccione, a braided Mozzarella-like Italian cheese.")
(comment MusicalInstrument-Acoustic "The collection of #$MusicalInstruments that is not powered by electronic or some other `artificial' means.  Some specializations e.g. #$PercussionInstrument, #$WoodwindInstrument, etc  are default rather than monotonic, because there are rare exceptions such as electronic clarinet, electronic drums and such.")
(comment Engraving "The collection of all engraved regions (the physical space where the engraving is located) of tangible objects")
(disjointWith ConsumableProduct PathArtifactSystem)
(comment EchinaceaPlant "#$EchinaceaPlant is a collection which correponds to the genus Echinacea.  Plants of this genus are native to North America.  #$EchinaceaDerivedDrugs are derived from instances of #$EchinaceaPlant.")
(comment JapanesePerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Japan, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment OSCrashingSYNFloodFault "#$OSCrashingSYNFloodFault is an attribute of some versions of operating systems.  Running an operating system with this fault makes a computer vulnerable to #$VulnerableToSYNFlood.")
(comment Thirteen-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '13.'")
(comment Sahaptin-ChinookLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment KitchenTimer "The collection of kitchen/egg timers.")
(comment TimeIndependentCollection "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$TimeIndependentCollection is a collection whose membership cannot change over time.  Examples of time-independent collections are #$Number-General and #$MathematicalObject.  By contrast, #$Supermodel is clearly a #$TimeDependentCollection (q.v.).")
(comment Spanking "The collection of #$Spankings, which involve the hitting of a person's #$Buttocks, usually with an open hand or a paddle.")
(comment SoftwareVersionFn "An instance of #$ReifiableFunction.  When given an instance of #$UnversionedSoftwareObject, UNV, and a string, STR, #$SoftwareVersionFn returns the instance of #$VersionedSoftwareObject that is the version of UNV refered to as the \"STR version\" of UNV.   (#$SoftwareVersionFn UNV STR) denotes the STR version of UNV; thus, (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Emacs-TheProgram \"20.4\") denotes Emacs version 20.4. ")
(comment TrashCompactor "A mechanical device that reduces the volume of waste material by subjecting it to pressure.  Has a container part and a moving compression surface.")
(comment CocaCola "The collection of instances of different varieties of The Real Thing")
(comment UniqueBodyPartFn "An instance of both #$IndividualDenotingFunction and #$ReifiableFunction.  This function takes as its arguments an animal (see #$Animal) and a type of body part that occurs uniquely in the animals that have it (see #$AnimalBodyPartType and #$UniqueAnatomicalPartType).  (#$UniqueBodyPartFn ANIMAL UNIQUE-PART-TYPE) is the instance (if there is one) of UNIQUE-PART-TYPE that is part of ANIMAL.  For example, (#$UniqueBodyPartFn #$GeorgeWashington #$Heart) is George Washington's heart.")
(comment BronchialTubeSegment "The collection of all simple segments of #$BronchialTubes (natural airways in the #$Lungs) however large or small, that have no branchings (except possibly at the ends of a segment).")
(comment MakingToast "Subjecting a slice of bread to heat for about 5 minutes, allowing its surface to brown.")
(comment finds "A finds some thing B. This entails that A is perceptually aware
of B, even though A need not believe that s/he has found B. Note that the
interpretation of #$finds is 
`specific': if A finds B, then there exists an ?X such that (#$finds A
?X). This sets #$finds apart from predicates like #$looksFor, #$wants,
etc.")
(disjointWith Communicating TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity "A specialization of #$UnitOfComputerResourceCapacity. Each instance of this collection is a function representing a unit of computer information storage capacity (of memory, cache, disk etc.). Instances include #$Bit, #$Byte and #$Megaword.")
(comment PlowBlade "NOT a spec of #$BladeOfADevice, because the blades do not cut something; rather they turn over soil when attached to the frame of a plow.  The collection of all plow blades.")
(comment Vizsla "A collection of medium-sized dogs with smooth fur coats, used (at least in North      America) primarily as bird dogs.  At one time (in Hungary) they were known as      the Yellow Pointer.  His color is usually some shade of golden rust.")
(comment ReunionPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$ReunionIsland, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization TravelOrganization)
(comment TruckWheel "the collection of #$Wheels that

  go on #$Trucks.")
(comment MedialSegmentOfMiddleLobeOfLung "The collection of all medial segments of #$MiddleLobeOfLungs on the right side.  Each is served by a #$MedialSegmentalBronchusOfMiddleLobeOfLung.  (There is no #$MedialSegmentOfMiddleLobeOfLung in the left #$Lung.)")
(comment Microphone "The electrical component used to transform sound into electrical signals")
(disjointWith Perceiving Murder)
(comment HotCereal-Cooked "Cereals such as oatmeal or cream of wheat, in their cooked state.  Often served with milk on the side or poured over them, but need not be.")
(comment CommercialOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$CommercialOrganization is an organization whose primary goal is to generate a profit for its owners, usually through the buying and selling of goods or services.  A given instance of #$CommercialOrganization may also be an instance of #$Business, or it may merely be a sub-organization of some instance of #$Business.")
(comment NetworkProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs which can communicate over a network.")
(comment Feces "Solid waste created by the digestion process and excreted ")
(comment nodeInAccountSystem "A predicate relating instances of #$Computer with instances of #$AccountSystem.  (#$nodeInAccountSystem COMPUTER ACCOUNTSYSTEM) means that users of COMPUTER are able to log in to an instance of #$UserAccount in ACCOUNTSYTEM via COMPUTER.")
(comment LikesPredicate "The collection of predicates that relate agents to things they like (or things they dislike).")
(comment OuijaSet "a device consisting of a small board, or planchette, on legs that rest on a larger board marked (typically) with the letters of the alphabet arranged in two curved rows, the numerals 1-0 in a row under the letters, the words 'yes' and 'no' in the upper corners, and the phrase 'good bye' at the bottom. Typically, two people sit facing each other and place their fingers on the planchette, which eventually begins to move and point to letters, numbers, etc. on the larger board, spelling out a (possibly cryptic) message or answer to a question. Ouija sets were invented and patented in the U.S. around 1890. Parker Bros. currently owns the rights and manufactures ouija sets.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterH "The capital letter 'H'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$H-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterH.")
(comment PeronosporaceaeFamily "A fungus family which includes downy mildews.")
(comment USBComputerCable "The collection of computer cable

used to connect USB (Universal Serial Bus) devices.")
(disjointWith SpeciallyCharteredInstitution Association)
(comment DialTelephone "A collection of telephones. Each dial telephone has a   rotary dial instead of a touch tone keypad for entering the number   the user wishes to call.")
(comment ServerOperatorAccount "#$ServerOperatorAccount is a specialization of #$WindowsNTAccount and #$PrivilegedAccount.  Instances of ths collection give users the permission to edit some keys in the #$WindowsRegistry file but do not give the user the ability to create new user accounts.")
(comment RecordedSoundPlaying "Prerecorded sound output.")
(comment DorsalRamusS5 "The collection of all S5 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiS5 and DorsalRamiS5 branch from SpinalRootS5.  DorsalRamiS5 supplies the skin over the coccyx.")
(comment PorkBelly "The collection of pork bellies. Pork bellies are a meat cut from the belly of a #$Pig.")
(comment UnixAccountSystem "The collection of instances of #$AccountSystem that are
built around the #$UnixOS.")
(comment FalconiformOrder "The order Falconiformes, comprising the vultures, hawks, eagles, ospreys, falcons, caracaras, etc. They are swift and graceful, and known for their raptorial, or predatory, skills. The have hooked beaks, and highly developed senses of sight and hearing.")
(disjointWith ComputerActivity PullingAnObject)
(comment SingleRecording-CW "Each instance of #$SingleRecording-CW denotes a named #$AudioConceptualWork, which has been recorded. Singles are typically a single song [#$Song-CW], but when instantiations are marketed as 45s [#$PhonographRecord-45] a second song is commonly put on the back of the disc.")
(comment Scapula "The collection of all shoulder blades.  Each individual #$Scapula is a #$Bone-BodyPart that lies within the #$Shoulder, connecting the #$Humerus to the bones of the #$Torso.")
(comment JuiceFn "This function denotes a collection of juices from some fruit or vegetable.")
(comment MadagascarPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Madagascar, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment DayCareOrganization "The collection of all #$Organizations that provide child care services in their own facilities (i.e., not in the home of the child).  Instances of #$DayCareOrganization may be either #$CommercialOrganizations or #$NonProfitOrganizations and may be either #$GovernmentalOrganizations, #$QuasiGovernmentalOrganizations, or #$PrivateSectorOrganizations.  Some #$DayCareOrganizations are #$ChainOrganizations (e.g., La Petite Academies), while others are instances of #$SingleSiteOrganization.")
(comment GiftTag "The collection of all gift tags. These are small

cards which are intended to be put on gifts to identify the

giver and receiver and perhaps also contain a short message.")
(comment TypicalInterArgTypePredicate "Instances of this collection are #$MetaPredicates that
specify the expected identity of the #$isa or #$genls of one argument
(the dependent argument) of a predicate given the #$isa or #$genls of
another argument (the independent argument). These predicates do not
contribute to wff-checking, and so should never be used in place of
#$InterArgConstraintPredicates.")
(comment MedicineBottle "A small bottle for storing medicine. It has special cap so it is hard to open by children.")
(comment ScienceFictionMovie "#$ScienceFictionMovie is a collection of instances of #$Movie-CW each of which relates a science fiction story.")
(comment DiggingAHole "A collection of events.  In each #$DiggingAHole, one or more agents (usually #$Animals) removes material from some substrate (such as the soil), so that a hole is formed.  If the digger is a person, tools or heavy equipment may be used; other organisms just use their claws, snouts, etc.  A borderline case of this concept occurs when a plant's roots grow.  Another borderline case occurs when an animal finds an existing hole and enlarges it.")
(comment Microwaving "A specialization of #$CookingFood: a collection of events in which a #$MicrowaveOven is used to heat food (or drink).")
(disjointWith TrainCar Train-TransportationDevice)
(comment ComputerProgramDistributionType "The collection of types of computer program distributions.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization Secretariat)
(comment DigestiveSystem "A specialization of #$AnimalBodyPart and #$ConnectedPathSystem. Each instance of #$DigestiveSystem is a system of organs and other body parts which work together to accomplish the digestion function (see #$DigestionEvent).")
(comment AlveolarSac "The collection of all alveolar sacs of the #$Lung, each being the small, final dead-end sac for inhaled air from an #$AlveolarDuct. The walls of an AlveolarSac consist of alveoli used directly for #$RespiratoryGasExchange in #$Respiration.  Each AlveolarSac is served by a PulmonaryArteriole and a PulmonaryVenule.")
(disjointWith VehiclePart HouseholdAppliance)
(comment Monkey "A specialization of #$Primate and #$NonPersonAnimal.  Each instance of #$Monkey is an arboreal (i.e., tree-dwelling) primate.  Contrast this collection with #$Person and #$Ape.")
(comment Medal-Physical "A small object, usually made of metal, generally with a pattern stamped in it, that symbolizes or commemorates something.")
(comment Memorandum "A note from an agent or group of agents in an organization to another agent or group of agents in the same organization, pertaining to the goals, practices, or conditions of the organization.")
(comment Shoulder "The region of the body where the arm joins the torso")
(comment SetUIDFault-Root "A program has #$SetUIDFault-Root if it runs SUID root (i.e., with an effective UID of root) and can be exploited to yield root user privileges to a user that does not have these privileges.")
(disjointWith TextileArtifact AluminumFoil)
(comment ScottishDeerhound "A collection of dogs.")
(comment Count-Nobleman "The collection of all counts, or male persons who hold hereditary count titles in the systems of nobility of European countries other than the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland.   This is distinct from a British #$Earl, though of equal rank.  See also #$Countess.")
(disjointWith EventOrganizer-Organization TransportationOrganization)
(comment DemonstrationCar "The collection of cars that are usually still in development and are not yet available to consumers.  A #$DemonstrationCar is often designed to showcase an automobile company's new line or model.  An example of an  instance of #$DemonstrationCar could be a solar or battery powered car.")
(comment VitaminC "Ascorbic acid.  Take a lot of this vitamin and it may keep you healthy.  Tastes yummy too.  Citrus fruit is a good source of this nutrient.")
(comment FlexorDigitiMinimi "The #$Collection of all instances of #$FlexorDigitiMinimi #$Muscle.  The #$FlexorDigitiMinimi flexes the #$ProximalPhalanx of the #$LittleFinger.  Together with the AbductorDitiMinimi and the #$OpponensDigitiMinimi it forms the HypothenarEminence.")
(comment SingleUserComputer "Workstations and small desktop computers.")
(comment RootOfLung "The collection of the 'roots' where #$Lungs are attached to their supply vessels and to other organs; each #$RootOfLung enters the #$Lung at the #$HilumOfLung, which is an indented place on a #$MedialSurfaceOfLung.  The #$RootOfLung contains the major tubes and vessels entering the lung.  Also called the Radix Pulmonis or Pedicle of Lung.")
(comment Snack "Random meal where small amounts of food, usually junk food, is eaten")
(comment CareerCenter "A career (development) center is a #$ServiceEstablishment           that help people find employment.")
(comment EMailClientProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are used in #$EMailSending events and #$EMailReceiving events.")
(comment Bacterium-Immotile "The collection of bacteria which are incapable of locomotion.")
(comment SkunkSpray "Extremely bad smelling stuff emitted only by skunks for defense.  Hard to wash off.")
(comment NuclearReactor "A specialization of both of #$MechanicalDevice and #$NuclearProduct (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$NuclearReactor is a device that uses instances of #$NuclearFuel (q.v.) to produce energy, which in turn is typically used to produce electricity via an #$ElectricalGenerator-Nuclear (q.v.).  Note that some instance of #$NuclearReactor is a physical part of each instance of #$ElectricalGenerator-Nuclear.")
(comment CanaryIslandsPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of the #$CanaryIslands, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith LanguageGroupingType PersonTypeByActivity)
(comment SupportRocker "A curving piece of wood or metal on which an object rocks.")
(disjointWith CourseOfStudy MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment HoldingHands "The human action of holding one person's hand in another's, as a sign of intimacy, sharing, comfort, etc.  Because this involves more than one person, it can not be a spec of #$SingleDoerAction.")
(comment argsNotIsa "(#$argsNotIsa REL COL) means that anything given as an argument to the Relation REL must not be an element of the Collection COL.")
(comment ImageInputDevice "Computer hardware components whose function is image input.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization CriminalOrganization)
(comment AdhesiveTape "#$AdhesiveTape is the #$Collection of all adhesive #$Tape.  An instance of #$AdhesiveTape is a thin, flat adhesive.  It consists of a normal #$Tape with at least one side having #$surfaceAttributeOfObj #$Sticky.  If this is true of both sides of the #$Tape, it is a #$DualSidedAdhesiveTape.")
(comment BayerAspirinProduct "The specialization of #$AspirinProduct for those produced by Bayer.")
(comment LateralPectoralNerve "The collection of all lateral pectoral #$Nerves.  A #$LateralPectoralNerve branches off from either the anterior divisions of the #$SuperiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus and #$MiddleTrunk-BrachialPlexus or from the #$LateralCord-BrachialPlexus.  Either way the #$LateralPectoralNerve is traced back to the same spinal roots.  It #$innervates the #$PectoralisMajor and #$PectoralisMinor of the #$Shoulder in which it is located.")
(comment Chicken-Meat "Meat from chickens")
(comment ChangingOfDesignatedSecondaryResidence "A collection of #$Actions.  Each instance of is an #$Action that is carried out by a taxpayer with the result that the taxpayer changes the designation of one of his qualified residences (pursuant to #$USIncomeTax).  In a #$ChangingOfDesignatedSecondaryResidence, one of the taxpayer's secondary residences stops being a qualified residence and another residence of the taxpayer starts being a qualified residence upon the occurrence of the #$Action.  Both of the taxpayer's residences whose designations as (or as not) qualified residences are the #$objectActedOns.  Technically, a #$ChangingOfDesignatedSecondaryResidence consists of two sub-events, a removal of the designation as a qualified residence with respect to one residence and the naming of another residence as that taxpayer's qualified secondary residence. ")
(comment passiveParticiple "(#$passiveParticiple WORD STRING) means that STRING is the passive participle form of WORD. The regular passive participle in English is generally identical to the #$perfect form. Verbs in the Cyc lexicon will have a #$passiveParticiple entry only if they are irregular. Regular forms are generated by the morphology component.")
(disjointWith PortalCovering Card)
(disjointWith TextualMaterial ComputationalSystem)
(comment BeachUmbrella "Large umbrellas used for shade at the beach.")
(comment Gastropod "This is the collection of (individual) animals

belonging to the class Gastropoda. The derivation of the term is from

Greek roots meaning \"stomach foot\". Members include snails, slugs, abalone,

and conchs.")
(comment authorOfLiteraryWork-CW "(#$authorOfLiteraryWork-CW PERSON LITERARYWORK) means that PERSON is one of the authors of LITERARYWORK.")
(comment Tusk "Hard protrusions from the sides of the mouths of Elephants and Walruses, made of Ivory")
(disjointWith MusicalInstrument Weapon)
(comment TracheophytaDivision "The division in the plant kingdom that contains the vascular plants.")
(comment SpanishPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Spain, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment OrganizationTypeByOwnership "A collection of two disjoint collections, #$PrivatelyHeldOrganization and #$PubliclyHeldOrganization.  Each instance of #$OrganizationTypeByOwnership is a set whose elements are distinguished by, in the case of #$PubliclyHeldOrganizations, the fact that the securities or other ownership interests in the #$Organization are traded among members of the general public (usually using an instance of #$FinancialExchange).  The specialization #$PrivatelyHeldOrganization includes those Organizations which are owned by a (usually small) group of entities and whose securities or other ownership interests cannot, pursuant to law, be traded among members of the general public.  Because ownership is a concept that properly applies only to #$CommercialOrganizations, #$OrganizationTypeByOwnership facets only #$CommercialOrganization.")
(comment CellPhoneCase "The collection of cases meant to protect cell

 phones from scratches, moisture, dings, etc.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForNegationProcessing "(#$useReformulationRuleForNegationProcessing RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the NegationProcessingRLModule.")
(comment HatRack "The collection of all hat racks")
(disjointWith (TransportViaFn Bicycle) (TransportViaFn WaterTransportationDevice))
(comment caudalTo "(#$caudalTo OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 lies in the #$CaudalDirection of OBJ-2 (i.e. away from the head and towards the tail), when viewed in the frame of reference of the object with #$AnimalBodyShapeType (often, a #$Person) that they are located in.  #$caudalTo is not used on limbs.  Note that OBJ-2 is therefore cephalic to OBJ-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `cephalic to'.  OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.")
(comment EdibleSodium "The kind of sodium that people consume -- e.g. the sodium in salt.")
(disjointWith LawEnforcementOrganization ManufacturingOrganization)
(comment ExecutableRootExploit "The collection of #$ExecutableExploits that are designed to
give a regular user of a computer access to the root account on that
computer.")
(disjointWith AutoDealership RecordedMusicStore)
(comment AlgaeSubkingdom "A major group within the Plant Kingdom which includes the green alga, brown algae, and red algae.")
(disjointWith Communicating SeparationEvent)
(comment BreastImplant "The collection of all breast implants.  Includes the #$Water-Saline and #$Silicon filled           varieties.")
(comment BiologicalGenus "The collection of biological taxonomic subdivisions (see #$BiologicalTaxon) created below #$BiologicalFamily and above #$BiologicalSpecies.  Sometimes, hybrids are possible between different instances of #$BiologicalSpecies that belong to the same #$BiologicalGenus.")
(comment GurmukhiCharacter "characters used for the Sikh scriptures")
(comment Tool-PowerTool "A collection of tools.  An instance of #$Tool-PowerTool is a tool which utilizes a non-kinetic power source, such as #$Electricity.  The power tool uses that power source --- converts it somehow into kinetic energy, causing mechanical motion (of part of the tool).  Often a #$Tool-PowerTool enables a person to things which would be very arduous (if not impossible) for that same human user to do with a purely manual tool.  Most power tools are designed to be operated by an adult human being; rarely for a particular person, rarely requiring multiple people at the same time to operate.  A #$Tool-PowerTool may be hand-held, or may be large and stationary.")
(comment BuildingInCityNamedFn "(#$BuildingInCityNamedFn CITY NAMESTRING) returns the #$Building in the #$City CITY with the name NAMESTRING.")
(disjointWith RecreationalActivity LawEnforcementActivity)
(comment AssateaguePony "The collection #$AssateaguePony includes all instances of #$Pony descended from the original Spanish ponies that inhabited #$AssateagueIsland following the legendary shipwreck of a Spanish ship on its shore in the sixteenth or seventeenth century. American children are fascinated by the story of these ponies, in part because they constitute one of the very few wild horse breeds living in North America.")
(comment Propane "C3H8. A combustible gas which is commonly compressed into

a liquid and used as a fuel.")
(comment Platter "A large plate used to serve food -- specifically meat such as ham, whole turkeys, etc. Significantly different from a serving tray! A platter will never have glasses and dishes placed directly upon it (although serving utensils such as carving knives, etc., may be).")
(comment LingulaOfLeftLung "The collection of all lingulae of #$Lungs (lingula pulmonis  sinistri), each being the protuberance of the lower anterior corner of the left  #$SuperiorLobeOfLung, which curves around the front of the #$Heart to its left.")
(comment Taleggio-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Taleggio, a creamy Italian cheese

with a mold crust.")
(comment MPEGFile "The collection consisting of all instances of #$ComputerFileCopy which are encoded in one of the MPEG family of encoding algorithms. #$MPEGFiles are either #$ComputerVideoFiles or #$ComputerSoundFiles. One popular subcollection of #$MPEGFile is #$MP3File, which is audio-only.")
(comment SporophyteFn "(#$SporophyteFn PLANT-TYPE) denotes the class of organisms which are the #$Sporophyte life stage of PLANT-TYPE.")
(comment SpeakingToCamera "The action of conveying information by speaking to a video or movie camera.")
(comment Scalp "The collection of all living scalps.  A #$Scalp is the part of the #$Skin covering someone's head (other than the face) from which a significant amount of hair normally grows.--Foxvog, Dec 8, 1997")
(comment FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice is a device designed to be used in the preparation of food or drink.  Specializations of #$FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice include #$CoffeeMaker, #$SpiceMill, and #$ElectricalToaster.")
(comment gametophyteOfPlantType "(#$gametophyteOfPlantType GAM-TYPE PLANT-TYPE) means that GAM-TYPE is the type of gametophyte produced by the plant taxon PLANT-TYPE.")
(comment MoroccanPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Morocco, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Packet-SYN-Spoofed "#$Packet-SYN-Spoofed is a #$Packet-Internet.  Under normal circumstances, following the #$InternetProtocol, a #$Packet-SYN is sent from a specific port on a computer to a specific port that is in a
\"listen\" state on another computer.  The listening computer sends a
SYN/ACK packet back to the first computer, which completes the
handshake by sending an Packet-ACK. When an
#$AttackByComputerOperation-SYNFlooding is initiated, attackers
initiate this handshaking sequence with a #$Packet-SYN with a spoofed
source address, forcing the listening computer to send SYN/ACK
packets and wait for #$Packet-ACKs that will never arrive.")
(comment Three-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '3.'")
(comment MaiduLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment MixingDevice "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$MixingDevice is a device whose #$primaryFunction is to mix up substances --- usually substances of some particular sorts (salads, paint, etc.)  Typically, an instance of #$MixingDevice is used with some kind of container in which the stuff to be mixed is contained during the mixing.  In some types of #$MixingDevice, the mixer is a #$BuiltInDevice with the container (e.g., a cement truck, a blender) and in some cases it isn't (e.g., a hand-held electric mixer that is designed to be held above any large bowl.)")
(comment Masturbating "This collection involves events of non-copulatory genital stimulation; many instances of this collection are reflexive events, where the #$performedBy and the #$objectActedOn roles are filled by the same participant.")
(comment arg2NotIsa "(#$arg2NotIsa REL COL) means that nothing given as the second argument to the #$Relation REL may be known to be an element of the #$Collection COL.")
(comment FirewallProgram "A specialization of #$SecurityProgram and #$ServerProgram. Each instance of this collection is a program designed to filter  packets (see #$Packet-Network) that enter the network or computer that it is protecting. Firewall filtering rules -- usually stored in a coinfiguration file accessed by th program -- describe what the program should do with various kinds of packets -- accepting them and routing them toward their destination, discarding them as though they were never received, or dropping them with a notification sent to the sending machine. Which occurs is determined by whether information in the packet headers satisfies criteria stated in the firewall rules. Any machine that runs a firewall program is a #$Firewall-Network.")
(comment PurchasingDepartment "A specialization of #$Department and #$BuyingOrganization. Each instance of this collection is a group of employees who make decisions about purchases for a given organization. Also sometimes referred to as \"Supply Department\".")
(comment PlasticBox "Boxes made of plastic.")
(comment DietCoke "The collection of instances of the sugarless version of The Real Thing")
(comment ListeningToMusic "Generally listening to music for entertainment or for extracting some sort of information from the music")
(comment BronchialJunction "The collection of all bronchial junctions in #$Animal #$Lungs; the junctions at which the #$BronchialTubes branch into smaller #$BronchialTubes, including #$Bronchioles.  At each BronchialJunction, a larger-diameter #$BronchialTube branches into two or more smaller-diameter #$BronchialTubes.  This excludes the #$TracheobronchialJunction,  in which one tube at the junction is a #$Trachea.")
(comment PreparingAMeal "An event in which a meal is made.  Since meals (which include snacks, cf #$Meal) can be made of merely a beverage, or merely a food, or several of both, #$PreparingAMeal has #$subEvents which can be either PreparingFood or #$PreparingABeverage.")
(comment Gigabyte "A function (an instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction and

of #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity) used to represent a common unit of computer memory and disk capacity. Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two. Its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a precise quantity of gigabytes (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is an instance of

#$ComputerMemoryCapacity). Thus, the value of (#$Gigabyte 1) is

one gigabyte (approximately one thousand million #$Bytes, each with a length of 8 #$Bits). The value of (#$Gigabyte 1 2) is \"between one and two gigabytes\". See also #$Megaword, #$Word-UnitOfComputerMemory.")
(comment AgriculturalImplement "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$AgriculturalImplement is a device which is intended for use in some agricultural activity.  These include rotary tillers, plows, hoes, pitchforks, mechanical planters, threshing machines, hay balers, and so on.")
(comment ExpenseReport "The document submitted by an employee when requesting reimbursement for travel expenses.")
(comment Uterus "The female sex organ of a mammal where her young can develop. The lining of the uterus is shed during #$Menstruating.")
(comment JavascriptCommandExecutionFault "A program has a #$JavascriptCommandExecutionFault if an unauthorized person can pass Javascript code to a program and have it execute arbitrary commands.")
(comment Akita-TheDog "A collection of large dogs.  Primarily used as working dogs.")
(comment ColombianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Colombia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization EnergyOrganization)
(comment Flywheel "the collection of #$Wheels used inside of 

   engines to store energy.")
(comment AnteriorSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all anterior segments of #$SuperiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by an #$AnteriorSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.")
(comment TurntableMechanism "Record Turntable mechanism.  See also StereoSystemRecordPlayer")
(disjointWith MakingAnOralSound Murder)
(comment Cremaster "The collection of all cremaster #$Muscles.  A #$Cremaster muscle exists in a male body, serving to raise the #$Testicle on its side of the body.  It extends from the #$InternalOblique #$Muscle to the #$Scrotum, encasing both the #$VasDeferens and the #$Testicle.")
(comment Frosting "Sweet, gooey paste which often covers a cake")
(comment UserInterfaceProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that provide the user with an interface to another #$ComputerProgram-CW.")
(comment Brick "A rectangular block of #$Clay-Wet hardened by drying in the sun or burning in a kiln and used for building, paving, etc..")
(disjointWith Cell CellPart)
(disjointWith Algorithm Language)
(comment systemAccountForSystem "#$systemAccountForSystem is a predicate relating instances of #$SystemAccountForNT with instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  (#$systemAccountForSystem ACCOUNT SYSTEM) means that ACCOUNT is the account with #$SystemPrivilege on SYSTEM.")
(comment LawnMower-Power "A collection of devices; a subset of #$LawnMower. It includes all lawnmowers which have a power source other than the user, whether gas or electric. Currently, the majority of lawnmowers belong to this class. See also #$LawnMower-HandPowered.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterH "The lowercase letter 'h'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$H-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterH.")
(comment Snoring "The action of making a snoring noise while sleeping.")
(comment Basidiomycota "This is the division of the fungus kingdom containing

what we ordinarily call mushrooms.")
(comment SerialComputerCable "The collection of computer cable

used to connect serial devices.")
(disjointWith GeopoliticalEntity SpeciallyCharteredInstitution)
(comment TouchToneTelephone "A collection of telephones. Each touchtone telephone has a   touch tone keypad instead of a rotary dial for entering the number   the user wishes to call.")
(comment NTStandardFileType "A collection of collections.  Instances of #$NTStandardFileType are collections of #$ComputerFile-AISes, instances of which are typically found on #$NTWorkstations and #$NTDomainServers.")
(comment ElectricalLightingDevice "Devices that provide light by transforming electrical current into light energy.")
(comment DeepPeronealNerve "The collection of all deep peroneal #$Nerves.  A #$DeepPeronealNerve is a branch of a #$CommonPeronealNerve.  Branches of the #$DeepPeronealNerve innervate #$Muscles in the #$LowerLeg and foot.")
(comment PorkChop "The collection of pork chops. Pork chops are a chop cut from a #$Pig. In the Southern United States, they are often breaded and broiled.")
(disjointWith NTAccountSystem UnixAccountSystem)
(comment KnowledgeEditorProgram "The class of programs intend to edit knowledge base structures")
(comment AutomaticTellerMachine "The bank machines which can take a bank card to handle deposits and withdrawals for most clients and are open at all times (except when they're broken).")
(comment PornographicCartoon "The collection of all pornographic cartoons. Members of this collection may be specs of #$Cartoon-Still or #$Cartoon-Animated.")
(comment ShoulderJoint "Joint between the trunk and the arm.")
(disjointWith DomesticatedAnimalFood SnackFood)
(comment CoconutMeat "A portion of the white flesh inside coconuts; good to eat; the flesh in a single coconut forms part of its endosperm.")
(comment VenezuelanPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Venezuela, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareOrganization DayCareOrganization)
(comment DecorativeBalloon "A kind of balloon used as decoration.

These balloons are often made of shiny materials rather than the

usual rubber.")
(comment Futon-PieceOfFurniture "The whole futon, i.e the frame and the mattress.")
(comment BitingByFn "Collection-Forming function.  Takes a class of animal, and returns the subclass of #$Biting events in which an instance of the animal type does the biting.")
(comment InternationalOrganization "A collection of organizations.  Each instance of #$InternationalOrganization is an organization with international `scope' -- that is, one which has substantial operations, physical facilities, or substantial membership in multiple countries.  International organizations may have persons, other organizations, or countries as members.  They may be political or commercial in nature.  International organizations with countries as members belong to the specialization #$InternationalOrganizationOfCountries.  Instances of #$InternationalOrganization include #$UnitedNationsOrganization, #$OPEC, and #$IBMInc.  See also #$internationalOrganizationMemberCountries.")
(disjointWith TrainCar Wagon)
(comment CGIScript "Collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs (often written in #$Perl-ProgrammingLanguage, C/C++, TCL, and many others) run under the #$CommonGatewayInterface (CGI). These external programs are known as `Scripts' or `Gateways', and are usually run under an information server.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization GovernmentOwnedCompany)
(comment AnimalDrawnPlow "The collection of plows pulled by draft animals - usually horses or oxen.  These are structurally different from modern, industrial plows.")
(comment Crustacean "Typically aquatic arthropods that have an exoskeleton and appendages on each segment and two pairs of antenna.")
(comment Shell-AnimalBodyPart "A specialization of #$SkeletalSystem and #$ExternalAnatomicalPart. Each instance of #$Shell-AnimalBodyPart is an external part of an animal's body which functions as a hard protective outer covering for it.")
(comment Carpalia "The bones in the distal row of the #$Carpus are called #$Carpalia.")
(disjointWith HouseholdAppliance Weapon)
(comment BoaConstrictor "A specialization of #$Constrictor.  Each instance of #$BoaConstrictor is a member of the species Constrictor constrictor.  Boa consytrictors are non-poisonous tropical snakes. They are found in Central and South America and often reach lengths of up to 1.5m.")
(comment fileCopied "(#$fileCopied COPYING FILE) means that the instance of #$ComputerFileCopy that is the input to the #$CopyingAComputerFile process COPYING is FILE.")
(comment AnimalCage "A container used to keep a mobile animal within a certain area.  Usually has a fair amount of open space along the perimeters, often to permit viewing of the caged animal.")
(disjointWith Water PolymerMolecule)
(comment VocalCord "Mucus membranes which produce sound from inside the larynx.")
(disjointWith TextileArtifact BuildingMaterial)
(comment Schipperke "A collection of small, black, stocky dogs.")
(comment Marchioness "The collection of all marchionesses, or female persons who hold hereditary marquessal titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch (whether in their own right, by marriage or by courtesy) in the systems of nobility of the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf.  See also #$Marquess.")
(disjointWith NaturalGasCompany TransportationOrganization)
(comment PhonographRecord-78 "The collection of #$PhonographRecords containing (normally) a single song on each side.  They are designed to be played at 45 #$RevolutionsPerMinute.")
(comment RectusAbdominis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$RectusAbdominis #$Muscle.  The #$RectusAbdominis flexes the #$Torso and supports compression of the abdominal contents.  It contracts strongly when doing situps or raising the legs when in #$LyingOnBackPosture.")
(comment OpticalDisk "The set of optical storage disks.")
(comment IntersegmentalMembraneOfLung "The collection of fibrous sheets of tissue that divide the different #$SegmentOfLungs from one another within a particular #$LobeOfLung.  Each IntersegmentalMembraneOfLung is attached to the #$VisceralPleura membrane surrounding and attached to that #$Lung.")
(comment Lunch "The midday meal.")
(comment Cinema-Organization "The collection of entertainment industry establishments that show movies.  Aka as movie theatres.")
(comment MassMailerComputerProgram "#$MassMailerComputerProgram is the subset of #$NetworkingProgram, copies of which are used in instances of #$MassEMailSending.")
(comment Sweat "By definition this is a liquid.  If sweat freezes or evaporates then it becomes (#$GaseousFn #$Water-Saline) or (#$SolidFn #$Water-Saline).  In case you haven't caught on by by now,  #$Sweat is the fluid excreted from the sweat glands of the skin")
(comment assistingAgent "(#$assistingAgent ACT AGENT) means that AGENT is one of the agents assisting in the performance of ACT; AGENT itself may or may not also be performing ACT.  AGENT is doing some tasks related to ACT but which are not directly #$subEvents of performing the main or focus action.  Thus, `assisting' here means doing such supporting activities as fetching supplies or tools needed in ACT; helping to manipulate objects involved in ACT; gathering an audience, or booking the performer, if ACT is a public performance, and so forth.")
(disjointWith Cord-Textile DrugSubstance)
(comment FloweryPlant "A specialization of #$FloweringPlant and an instance 
of #$LifeStageType (q.v.).  Each instance of #$FloweryPlant is a flowering plant that is actually and visibly in bloom (i.e. has flowers showing).  This collection includes both bushes and trees with visible flowers.")
(comment PhilippinesPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of the #$Philippines, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment HighSpeedTrain "The collection of all high-speed trains")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType LanguageGroupingType)
(comment LoveSeat "A small sofa, usually for two people.")
(disjointWith BaseballInning MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment Neighing "Action which produces the common horse utterance.")
(comment MouseButton "The prototype mouse button.")
(comment DualSidedAdhesiveTape "#$DualSidedAdhesiveTape is the #$Collection of all dual sided #$AdhesiveTape.  An instance of #$DualSidedAdhesiveTape is af a normal #$Tape with both sides of the #$Tape having the #$surfaceAttributeOfObj #$Sticky.")
(comment StirlingAircraftEngine "Stirling engines are a kind of #$AircraftEngine.")
(comment SubOccipitalNerve "The collection of all suboccipital nerves.  The suboccipital nerve is connected to the #$DorsalRamusC1.  The suboccipital nerve supplies the ?????.")
(comment changeOfDesignatedSecondaryResidenceForYear "`(#$changeOfDesignatedSecondaryResidenceForYear CHANGE RES1 RES2 YEAR)' means that
CHANGE is a #$ChangingOfDesignatedSecondaryResidence from RES1 to RES2 for YEAR. Specifically,
before the change, RES1 was the #$designatedSecondaryResidence of the #$performedBy
of CHANGE for YEAR while RES2 was not, and after the change the situation is reversed.")
(comment NonMessengerRNA "The collection of #$RNAMolecules that are not 

#$MessengerRNA molecules.  Important specs include

 #$TransferRNA and #$RibosomalRNA.")
(comment RollOnDeodorant "Roll-on deodorant: the stuff itself, not a package of it.")
(comment networkName "the network name for a computer (a string)")
(comment Mast-Device "The rigid support column on wind-powered transportation devices which support the sails.")
(comment Radiata "This is the collection of (individual) animals which

are members of the invertebrate phyla Cnidaria and Ctenophora. The former

contains hyrda, corals, and jellyfish. The bodies of these animals have radial

symmetry.")
(comment Hentai "Members of Hentai are pornographic cartoons. Members of this collection may be specializations of #$Cartoon-Still, or #$Animation-MovingImage. Hentai as a cartoon form originated in Japan. ")
(comment Nostril "The collection of all nostrils.  An individual #$Nostril is any opening (#$Portal) in the head (#$Head-AnimalBodyPart) through which #$Breathing occurs other than a #$Mouth or part of one.  #$Nostrils may be symmetric parts of #$Noses or #$Beaks, or single holes on the top of a head (a #$Blowhole).")
(disjointWith FoodUtensil Weapon)
(comment FinnishPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Finland, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment PubliclyHeldOrganization "The collection of all #$CommercialOrganizations whose securities or other ownership interests are freely tradable among members of the general public, usually on an instance of #$FinancialExchange.  In the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica, instances of #$PubliclyHeldOrganizations are usually either #$LegalCorporations or #$LimitedPartnerships.  Each instance of #$PubliclyHeldOrganization in the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica must be registered with the #$SecuritiesAndExchangeCommission under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 and is regulated by the #$SecuritiesAndExchangeCommission.")
(comment BoxedSet-TheProduct "A boxed set is a commercial product that usually contains books, CDs, or videotapes.  For example, a group of Kung Fu vidoetapes

could be sold together as a boxed set.   The complete works of an author or a musician are also often sold in collector's editions of

 boxed sets.")
(comment PlasticJar "Jars made of plastic")
(disjointWith SnowSkiing (TransportViaFn Bicycle))
(disjointWith Penis Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(comment LawEnforcementOrganization "A specialization of both #$Organization and #$LegalAgent.  Each instance of #$LawEnforcementOrganization is an official organization whose purpose is to support or perform law enforcement.  Instances of #$LawEnforcementOrganization include organizations which are legally empowered to enforce laws (see the specialization #$PoliceOrganization), as well as information agencies (such as #$INTERPOL) whose purpose is to assist and coordinate police activities.")
(comment NameServerProgram "#$NameServerProgram is the collection of programs written to enable #$Internet hosts to process DNS requests.")
(disjointWith RetailChainStore AutoDealership)
(comment Teaspoon "The small spoon used to stir beverages with")
(disjointWith StateOfMatterChangeEvent IBTGeneration)
(comment Implant-Dental "A collection of #$PhysicalDevices used in replacing lost teeth.")
(comment HebrewLetter "characters devised for writing the ancient Hebrew language")
(comment MetalworkingTool "Tools used to shape, join, and cut metal manually:  hammers, anvils, pliers, welding torches, soldering irons...  These tools/devices are capable of being used and are designed to be used on metal, but this doesn't preclude their use on other types of materials (having similar textures, properties, etc.) for which they might be suited.")
(disjointWith TransportationAccommodation ConflictEvent)
(disjointWith LawEnforcementActivity AthleticActivity)
(disjointWith PlumbingSystem-Building RoofOfAConstruction)
(comment ShetlandPony "#$ShetlandPony is a collection whose instances are extremely popular riding animals amoung children in Western cultures.  For the most part, this is because of the their appearance rather than because of their temperament.")
(comment eventErrorRateForType "(#$eventErrorRateForType ERR-TYPE EVT-TYPE AGT-TYPE RATE) means that in normal circumstances in which EVT-TYPE is done by AGT-TYPE, the ratio of the number of errors of type ERR-TYPE to the number of events of type EVT-TYPE is RATE. For example, (eventErrorRateForType EngineMisFiring EngineFiring FordV-6Engine .0001) means that the ratio of engine misfirings to the total number of engine firings is 1 in a thousand, when the engine firing is done by a Ford V-6 engine.")
(comment ShotGlass "A small cylindrical glass used for drinking shots of alcoholic

beverages, or for measuring out amounts of alcohol when making mixed drinks.

Some people collect souvenir shot glasses.")
(comment RibSeries "The collection of all #$SeriesWithoutRepetition of ribs (#$Rib-AnimalBodyPart) in vertebrates.  #$Vertebrates other than #$Fish have one #$RibSeries on each lateral side of the body.  #$Fish have two #$RibSeries on each side of the body.  #$Snakes have ribs connected to each #$Vertebra, while most #$Vertebrates have them connected to fewer.  The length of a mammalian #$RibSeries varies from 9 in #$Whales to 24 in Sloths.")
(comment Swiss-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Swiss cheese.

This is a particular type of cheese, a mild cow's milk cheese best known

for the largish holes throughout it. This collection is not the collection

of all cheeses made in or originating in Switzerland.")
(comment currentNetworkConfiguration "(#$currentNetworkConfiguration GROUP CONFIG) means that some subset of the elements composing GROUP figure as nodes in an instance of #$PathSystem CONFIG, and that the link structure of CONFIG represents one possible way of organizing the constituent elements of GROUP.")
(comment WAVFile "The collection of all #$ComputerSoundFiles that use the WAV format, developed by #$MicrosoftInc and used extensively in #$MSWindows.")
(disjointWith ReferenceWork PoeticWork)
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice SomethingToWear)
(comment AzoresIslandsPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Azores-Islands, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Twelve-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '12.'")
(comment TlingitLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of western North America")
(comment BBQGrill "A usually stand-alone device for broiling food.")
(comment Agent-Intangible "The collection of #$Agent-Generics that have no tangible component.  Possible examples include souls (say in a Cartesian or a religious belief context), ghosts, demons, and some gods and angels.")
(comment LickingEvent "The collection of events in which an agent licks something.")
(comment StockInFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction. When applied to an instance of #$LegalCorporation, #$StockInFn returns the subcollection of #$Stock consisting of all shares of stock in that instance of

#$LegalCorporation.")
(comment PacketSnifferProgram "#$PacketSnifferProgram is a specialization of #$DiagnosticComputerProgram and #$PacketSniffer.  Copies of #$PacketSnifferProgram are used to examine packets sent over the #$Internet and extract information from them. Copies of #$PacketSnifferProgram are used as tools by network administrators, and can also be used as spying devices on networks.")
(comment CustomerServiceDepartment "A specialization of #$Department. Each instance of this collection is a department in an organization whose purpose is to help its customers and keep them happy.")
(comment MountainDew "The collection of instances of #$MountainDew")
(comment ExperiencingHunger "Being hungry")
(comment TracheobronchialJunction "The collection of all junctions of animal airway conduits in which a #$Trachea (windpipe) joins (and in human beings splits into two) #$BronchialTubes.  In human beings the TracheobronchialJunction is outside the lungs, in the #$Mediastinum, at the lower end of the #$Trachea.  The #$CarinaTracheae is a cartilage structure at the #$TracheobronchialJunction.  Each #$AirBreathingVertebrate with two #$Lungs has one TracheobronchialJunction.")
(comment SoftDrink "Soda pop, also called pop in some places, or in a generic sense, coke")
(comment SimpleActionPredicate "A specialization of #$ActionPredicate (q.v.).  Each instance of #$SimpleActionPredicate is such that a task specification formed with it does not decompose into further actions, in contrast to specifications formed with instances of #$ComplexActionPredicate (q.v.).  By convention, expressions that denote relations that are typically instances of #$ComplexActionPredicate are characterized by having the prefix \"do\", whereas expressions that denote relations that are typically instances of #$SimpleActionPredicate lack this prefix.  Note, however, that whether a predicate is an instance of #$SimpleActionPredicate or #$ComplexActionPredicate depends on context.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing)
(comment FanSiteFn "#$FanSiteFn takes as argument any instance of #$Thing and returns the collection of all #$FanSitePages designed by and for fans of that thing.  For example, (#$FanSiteFn DougFlutie) would return the collection of all #$WorldWideWebPage-CWs by and for fans of #$FootballQuarterback Doug Flutie,and (#$FanSiteFn #$BalletDancePerformance) returns the collection of all #$WorldWideWebPage-CWs by and for ballet fans. (#$Vizedom 1/14/99)")
(comment PlowAgriculturalImplement "The collection of agricultural implements whose primary function is to plow a field")
(comment RotaryWingAircraft "A specialization of #$AirTransportationVehicle.  Each instance of #$RotaryWingAircraft is a heavier-than-air vehicle which is supported in the air by blades rotating about an axis. A notable specialization of #$RotaryWingAircraft is #$Helicopter.")
(comment ATMTransactionReceipt "The type of document given to someone when they make a transaction at an automatic teller machine, as a receipt that they did so.")
(comment ReproductiveSystem-Female "The collection of all the #$ReproductiveSystems of #$FemaleAnimals.")
(comment BeardedCollie "A collection of dogs.")
(comment RioMuniEnclavePerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$RioMuni-Enclave, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization RepairAndMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment JetEngine "the collection of all #$Engines designed

   for use in #$JetPropelledAircraft")
(comment InferiorLingularSegmentOfSuperiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all inferior lingular segments of left #$SuperiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by a #$InferiorLingularSegmentalBronchusOfSuperiorLobeOfLung.  (These segments and bronchi do not exist in right #$Lungs.)")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess Murder)
(comment FemoralArtery "The collection of all femoral arteries.  The #$FemoralArtery passes from the #$Pelvis down to the #$Knee.  The proximal end of the #$FemoralArtery connects to the #$ExternalIliacArtery.  The distal end of the #$FemoralArtery connects to the #$PoplitealArtery.  The #$FemoralArtery supplies the deep structures of the #$Thigh.")
(comment ScrambledEgg "An egg which has been scrambled.")
(comment SeatingDeviceSeat "The collection for the regions where persons/agents sit.")
(comment decreasesLevelInBody "The expression `(#$decreasesLevelInBody CHEMTYPE1 CHEMTYPE2)'

means that, at least in normal cases, an increase in the amount of CHEMTYPE1 results

in a decrease in the level of CHEMTYPE2 in the body. See also #$increasesLevelInBody.")
(comment MovieReel "The collection of all reels of movie film (exposed #$PhotographicFilm) containing an instantiation of a movie [#$Movie-CW] or part of a movie.  This collection does not include metal reels without attached film.")
(comment likes-Generic "(#$likes-Generic SUBJ OBJ) means that SUBJ likes OBJ. This is a very general liking relation which is most useful for organising

liking relations and for use during inference; for representation

purposes, use a spec-Pred.")
(comment BladeOfADevice "The collection of blades for cutting tools, cutting devices, cutting instruments, etc.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterI "The capital letter 'I'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$I-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterI.")
(comment Burping "The action of expelling gas from the stomach.")
(comment interArgNotIsa2-3 "(#$interArgNotIsa2-3 PRED COL1 COL2) means that, when an instance of COL1 appears as the second argument to PRED, the third argument in that assertion is constrained to not be an instance of COL2 and vice versa.")
(comment DivisionGnetophyta "This is the collection of vessel-bearing

gymnosperms.")
(comment ComputerMonitorCable "The collection of cables

used to connect computers to monitors.")
(disjointWith Trust-LegalEntity SpeciallyCharteredInstitution)
(comment ClockRadio "A collection of electronic devices. Each clock radio   includes the functions of both an alarm clock and a radio. It is   generally a small device suitable for placing on top of a bedside   table. It can generally be configured so that at a preset time   either an electronic beeping alarm sounds or the radio turns on   automatically.   Note: As defined, this collection does not include devices that have   radio and clock functions, but no alarm function.")
(comment WindowsRegistry "Each computer running some (post-3.1) version of #$MSWindows (e.g., an instance of #$NTWorkstation) has on it an instance of #$WindowsRegistry.  An instance of #$WindowsRegistry on a machine contains all information about the operating system configuration, information for Windows-based applications, hardware configuration settings, networking setup data, user preferences, and much else.  See also #$RegistryKey.")
(comment DorsalRamusT12 "The collection of all T12 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiT12 and DorsalRamiT12 branch from SpinalRootT12.  DorsalRamiT12 supplies the skin on the back.")
(comment PorkLoin-MeatCut "The collection of pork loins. Pork loin is a meat cut from the loin of a #$Pig.")
(comment Scroll "This collection includes documents printed or written on rolled paper.")
(comment InterfaceProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used to interface with other #$ComputerProgram-CWs.")
(comment Rug "From plush room-sized Oriental rugs to rubber-backed bathroom rugs, this collection represents textile floor coverings that are not attached.")
(comment HipJoint "Joint between the trunk and leg")
(disjointWith NavigationDevice Tool)
(comment Juice "Instances of #$Juice are quantities of liquid derived from fruits or other plant parts by either squeezing them or pulverizing them.  Instances of #$Juice consist mostly of water, with bits of plant tissue and dissolved compounds (e.g., sugars). Many kinds of #$Juice are considered to be #$Drink; i.e., they are typically drunk as is, possibly chilled.  Other kinds of #$Juice are considered only food ingredients, such as lime or lemon juice.  Still other kinds of #$Juice might not be considered food at all, such as the #$Juice one might obtain by squeezing a bunch of grass clippings.")
(comment GuineaPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Guinea, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith InsuranceProvider DayCareOrganization)
(comment PhoneJackAdapter "This is the collection of adapters designed to allow 

phone jacks to be plugged in to sockets they otherwise would not fit.")
(comment AnatolianLanguageFamily "Ancient dead languages of Anatolia and vicinity")
(comment Wire "A collection of physical devices, namely all the slender stringlike pieces of metal, with or without insulative casing.  Various instances of #$Wire are designed for and serve many different functions: connecting, carrying electrical power and/or electrically coded information, heat or light radiation, etc.  Pieces of wire may be coated with insulation (instances of #$InsulatingCover).  Wires not intended to carry electricity are still instances of this collection; e.g., wires that are used in a piano, in a person's dental braces, etc.")
(comment MakingAnOralSound "The collection of actions in which the lips and other mouth parts are

used to make sound. #$MakingAnOralSound means the event in which sound

is produced more-or-less voluntarily, using the mouth, mouth portal,

lips, and tongue.--Kean, July 11, 1997")
(comment EducationalOrganization "A specialization of #$Organization.  Each instance of #$EducationalOrganization is an organization whose primary function is to provide teaching and/or training as a service for students.  Instances of #$EducationalOrganization may be either public or private institutions.  Instances of this collection include #$AustinISD (the #$CityOfAustinTX Independent School District), #$StanfordUniversity, #$BrynMawrCollege, #$UniversityOfPennsylvaniaSchoolOfMedicine, and many other institutions.")
(disjointWith HarvesterAgriculturalImplement GolfCart)
(comment PlugInProgram "The collection of all computer programs that are not used by themselves but in combination with another program to which they add some additional functionality. Adding this functionality is easy enough that it can be carried out by an average software user without any programming knowledge, which distinguishes them from standard instances of #$ComputerProgramModule-CW. For example, a variety of #$PlugInPrograms exist for web browsers, to which they add functionalities like viewing image types that the browser itself does not support, to navigational aids, to remembering passwords, etc.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization ReviewCommittee)
(comment HandTowel "A smaller-than-standard towel, intended for drying the hands or face after washing.")
(disjointWith Skin Shell-AnimalBodyPart)
(comment TrapezoidBone "The Trapezoid is the second of the #$Carpalia in Humans.")
(comment coreRelatives "(#$coreRelatives ANIMAL1 ANIMAL2) means that ANIMAL1  is a close or \"core\" relative of ANIMAL2.  Note that the exact nature of this relationship will vary widely from culture to culture.")
(comment Pickaxe "The collection of hafted #$HandTools called \"picks\" or \"pickaxes\" used for breaking hard materials like rock or hard-packed soil.  A pick is comprised of a long (often wooden) handle and a pair of heavy blades that come to a somewhat blunt point or short line segment.")
(comment FuseBox "The box in which fuses are housed.")
(comment ChemicalSynthesis "The collection of  processes by which chemical compounds are created  (usually out of simpler chemical compounds).")
(comment HistoricalNarrative "A narrative intended to convey facts about events.")
(comment Mouth-Mammal "Mammalian mouths")
(disjointWith TextileArtifact Turf-Artificial)
(comment Samoyed-TheDog "A collection of medium-sized, usually white, biscuit, or cream colored dogs            with dark eyes.")
(comment Marquis "The collection of all marquis, or male persons who hold hereditary marquessal titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch, in the systems of nobility of #$France, #$Luxembourg or #$Belgium.  This distinct from the British #$Marquess.")
(disjointWith ChamberOfCommerce TransportationOrganization)
(comment Kaleidoscope "Each #$Kaleidoscope is a toy which one looks into to see symmetrical patterns of moving colors.  Kaleidoscopes are generally cylindrical, with an eye-hole at one end, and with a compartment at the far end which contains colored objects that can move freely within the compartment.  The far end is either translucent or transparent, so that light can enter.  The inside walls of a kaleidoscope have mirrors, usually two set at an angle, so that when the compartmentalized objects move around, they appear to be multiplied N-fold (depending on the angle of the mirrors) and moving in symmetry with their reflections.")
(comment ExternalIntercostal "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExternalIntercostal #$Muscle.  An #$ExternalIntercostal #$Muscle is the outermost of three muscles which connect two adjacent ribs.  It elevates the ribs during inspiration and helps maintain the intercostal space.")
(comment FoodStorageContainer "The collection of objects produced to be primarily food storage containers")
(comment MarginOfLung "The collection of margins of #$Lungs, the angular flaplike edges ('corners' or 'crests') of #$Lungs, which divide the major lung surfaces from each other.  Note that the so-called  #$PosteriorMarginOfLung, the ridge where the #$Lung  meets the #$SpinalColumn, is included, even though it is  not as flat a margin as the others")
(comment Supper "The food served at the evening meal.")
(comment ComputerRepairShop "An organization which is a local customer point of contact, and which repairs computers.")
(comment PhysiologicalFunction "The collection of those #$PhysiologicalProcesses that serve some end for their doers, which may be cells, tissues, or whole organisms; for example, #$Photosynthesis-Plant.")
(comment BankDebitCard "A specialization of #$Card and #$TenderObject. Each instance of #$BankDebitCard is a plastic card that enables the holder to access the #$BankAccount with which the card is associated. It is typically used to withdraw funds from the account. See also #$CreditCard.")
(comment VenomOfFn "(#$VenomOfFn ANIMALTYPE) denotes the collection of all portions of #$Venom secreted by animals of type ANIMALTYPE.")
(comment governedByAgreement "The predicate #$governedByAgreement relates an event to an agreement that stipulates something with respect to it, such as certain conditions that are to hold during the event, or whether the event should or should not occur.  (#$governedByAgreement EVT AGR) means that some aspects of the instance of #$HumanActivity EVT are controlled by, or 'under the jurisdiction of', the instance of #$Agreement AGR.  For example, a #$BuyingGroup may have #$SalesContracts with its #$suppliers that specify what prices may be charged for goods bought by members of the group during the agreement period.  But note that an event's being governed by an agreement does not entail that the event conforms to what the agreement stipulates: an act that violates the agreement is still governed by it.")
(comment RootFn "#$RootFn takes a single plant collection as its argument and returns the collection of roots of that type of plant.  (#$RootFn PLANTTTYPE) denotes the collection of all roots from the elements of PLANTTYPE.  For example, (#$RootFn #$GingerPlant) denotes the collection of ginger roots.")
(comment CapeVerdePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$CapeVerde, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment MP3Player-GenericTypeByPhysicality "A collection of collections. Each instance is a spec of #$MP3Player-Generic whose instances are all of the same physicality.")
(comment PlasterTheConstructionMaterial "A pasty substance (composed of lime, water, and sand) that hardens on drying and is used for coating walls, ceilings, etc.")
(disjointWith PlantingAField MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment Tackling "The process of catching, immobilizing, and slamming to the ground some moving object (like Herschel Walker).")
(comment ComputerMouse "A computer device which when moved across a surface, transmits relative position data to its host.  Usually has one or more buttons the user can push.")
(comment PepperGrinder "A device which may be used to store peppercorns, with a grinding apparatus at the bottom so that it can dispense freshly ground pepper.")
(comment BrandNameGame "The collection of all games [#$Game], equipment for which is sold as a #$ProductTypeByBrand.  For example, #$Scrabble")
(comment OpticalIllusion "A collection of #$VisualImages. Each #$OpticalIllusion is a #$VisualImage that can lead a viewer to believe something to be true that is not true.")
(comment PhrenicNerve "The collection of all phrenic #$Nerves.  A #$PhrenicNerve is connected to #$VentralRamusC3, #$VentralRamusC4 and #$VentralRamusC5 on its side of the body.  The #$PhrenicNerve #$innervates the #$Diaphragm-BodyPart.")
(comment Poultry-Meat "Raw meat of various poultry birds like chicken, turkey, goose etc.")
(comment TaxDocumentMicrotheory "This is the collection of microtheories which store information given in
various IRS documents. The microtheory names encode the location of the information
within those documents.")
(comment GargleSolution "A substance which is swirled around in the mouth and upper throat and then spit out.  Gargles are usually used to produce effects on the throat, teeth, or breath.")
(comment Eggshell-Stuff "The stuff of which the hard shell surrounding a bird's egg consists.")
(comment Styrofoam "styrofoam")
(comment Pollination "This is the process in which pollen from flowering plants and

trees is redistributed in such a way that reproduction is possible. This may be

done intentionally by humans or unintentionally. It most notably occurs as a

side-effect of the actions of insects, especially bees.")
(comment PelvicBone "Bone connecting torso to legs")
(disjointWith StorageConstruct Weapon)
(comment EmbryophyteSubkingdom "A major group within the plant kingdom which includes those taxa whose members have an embryonic stage which is dependent on the parent plant for some period.  Includes vascular plants (tracheophyta division) and mosses/liverworts/etc. (bryophyte division).")
(comment SriLankanPerson "The people who are #$citizens of #$SriLanka, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment EyeSkinCareProduct "Creams and lotions used around the eye area.")
(comment GlassJar "Jars made of glass")
(disjointWith Limb-AnimalBodyPart Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(comment UnversionedProgram "A specialization of #$UnversionedSoftwareObject and #$ComputerProgram-CW.  The collection of all instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW which are \"unversioned\" in the sense that, strictly speaking, not they, but versions of them, are downloaded, run on a machine, etc. Instances of #$UnversionedProgram are thus highly abstract entities. Positive examples:  #$LinuxKernel-TheProgram, #$Linux-RedHat, #$WU-FTPD-TheProgram.")
(disjointWith ServiceStation AutoDealership)
(comment Chopstick "The collection of thin sticks used in pairs for eating, especially by Asians, or at least Asian food.")
(disjointWith Cleaning LawEnforcementActivity)
(comment BronchialTube "The collection of all bronchial tubes in the lungs, along with the two main bronchi embedded in the lungs, as well as all the little #$Bronchioles.  The two main bronchi are attached to the #$Trachea.")
(comment CochlearImplant "The collection of all cochlear implants.  A cochlear implant is a device which is surgically implanted into the inner ear or a person who suffers profound or total hearing loss to aid in hearing and communication.")
(disjointWith LifeStageType RoadVehicleType)
(comment BrahmiCharacter "the original Indic syllabary")
(comment StoneworkingTool "Tools used to shape, and cut stone.  Includes sculpturing tools used to work directly on the stone.  These tools/devices are capable of being used and are designed to be used on stone, but this doesn't preclude their use on other types of materials (having similar textures, properties, etc.) for which they might be suited.")
(disjointWith IntrinsicStateChangeEvent TransportationAccommodation)
(disjointWith PushingAnObject PhysiologicalProcess)
(disjointWith GutterOnARoof RoofOfAConstruction)
(comment WelshPony "The #$WelshPony is a collection whose instances tend to have #$ArabianHorses as well as Celtic ponies as ancestors.  Instances can grow up to 158 cm. tall (measured from fore-hoof to #$Withers) or can be as small as 100 cm.")
(comment ProfessionalServiceOrganization "The collection of all #$ServiceOrganizations that provide professional services.  Examples of specializations of #$ProfessionalServiceOrganization include #$LawFirm and #$AccountingFirm.")
(comment Backgammon-Board "The collection of all Backgammon boards")
(comment EatingVessel "Containers to hold an individual's portion of food while it is being eaten.")
(comment BaseOfBone "A #$BaseOfBone is a #$BoneSubPart at one end of a #$LongBone made of denser #$BoneTheStuff and labled by the 'base' of the bone.")
(comment Roquefort-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Roquefort, a French sheep's milk cheese.

It is one of the three great blue cheeses.")
(comment CalculatorProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs designed primarily to perform calculations on numbers. Results of calculations may be output as numbers or graphed.")
(comment PhotoFlashBulb "Bulbs that produce short intense flashes of light to illuminate subjects being photographed.  Not reusable.")
(disjointWith Novel-CW ReferenceWork)
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice Weapon)
(comment GametophyteFn "(#$GametophyteFn PLANT-TYPE) denotes the class of organisms which are the #$Gametophyte life stage of PLANT-TYPE.")
(comment JerseyIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Jersey-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Twenty-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '20.'")
(comment EyakLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, generally of western North America")
(comment ElectricMixer "An electrical device to mix the ingredients into a single mass.")
(comment SkippingAStone "The collection of acts of throwing a #$Pebble at a #$BodyOfWater with the intent that it should skip across the surface of the water")
(comment NetworkingProgram "#$NetworkingProgram is a specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  Each instance of #$NetworkingProgram is designed to enable a computer to communicate with another device on a computer network. Examples of tasks that networking software facilitates include emailing, filesharing, and connecting to printers.")
(comment StoreDepartment "A specalization of #$Department and #$RetailOrganization. Store departments have some characteristics of specialty stores, but are part of some larger retail store (and usually located in the same building).")
(comment WireWhisk "A wire utensil usually used to beat eggs or mix batter.")
(comment CokeClassic "The collection of instances of The Real Thing")
(comment ExperiencingThirst "Being thirsty")
(comment CostalCartilageSeries "A #$CostalCartilageSeries is the #$Series of #$CostalCartilage of a #$Vertebrate.")
(comment SouthEastAsianCuisine "The collection of instances of what many Americans tend to think of as SouthEastAsian (Thai, Vietnamese, etc.) food.  Add specs as appropriate")
(comment ActionPredicate "A specialization of #$EventPredicate (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ActionPredicate is a predicate used to make an assertion about an action performed intentionally by an agent.  The first argument to each instance of #$ActionPredicate will be the \"agentive force\" of the action, and the remaining arguments will be \"objects\" that the agentive force interacts with in some way.   The representation of actions in terms of #$ActionPredicates is an alternative to the Davidsonian-style representation of actions in which the \"participants\" in actions  are related to the reified individual actions in which they participate (for that alternative, see #$Role and #$ActorSlot).   Important specializations of #$ActionPredicate include #$SimpleActionPredicate and #$ComplexActionPredicate (qq.v.).")
(comment MotorcycleTypeByBrand "A collection of collections, each element of #$MotorcycleTypeByBrand is a collection of motorcycles produced by a particular manufacturer, e.g., Harley Davidson.")
(disjointWith Communicating PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment Kilobyte "A function (an instance of #$IndividualDenotingFunction and of #$UnitOfComputerStorageCapacity) used to represent a common unit of computer memory and disk capacity.  Like all instances of #$UnitOfMeasure, its #$arity is variable between one and two. Its arguments must be instances of #$SubLRealNumber. If a single instance of #$SubLRealNumber is put in the argument position to this function, it returns a precise quantity of megabytes (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). If two #$SubLRealNumbers are put in the argument position, it returns an interval (which is an instance of #$ComputerMemoryCapacity). Thus, the value of (#$Kilobyte 1) is one kilobyte (approximately one thousand #$Bytes, each with a length of 8 #$Bits). The value of (#$Kilobyte 1 2) is \"between one and two kilobytes\". It is often referred to as \"K\". See also #$Megaword.")
(comment RotaryTiller "The collection of all rotary tillers, used for turning over soil in preparation for planting a <relatively small> area of land.")
(comment RoadVehicleTypeByUse "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$RoadVehicleTypeByUse is a collection of instances of #$RoadVehicle which share a particular use/function.  Instances of #$RoadVehicleTypeByUse include #$DumpTruck (used for carrying/dumping stuff), #$TaxiCab (used for carrying #$Persons to destinations for money), and #$OffRoadAutomobile (used for traveling off of paved roads).")
(comment AppointmentLetter "A letter which contains an offer of employment (and the terms) from an organization to an individual.")
(comment ReproductiveSystem-Male "The collection of all the #$ReproductiveSystems of #$MaleAnimals.")
(comment ChesapeakeBayRetriever "A relatively large dog with a thick coat.  Also referred to as the Chessy.")
(comment RomanianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Romania, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup FoodAndBeverageOrganization)
(comment WirelessCommunicationDevice "The collection of 

#$CommunicationDevices in which the communication signals are either not transmitted or not received entirely over a wire.")
(comment SuperiorSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all superior segments of #$InferiorLobeOfLungs.  Each is served by an #$SuperiorSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung.")
(comment HandSaw "A hand tool used for cutting, comprised of a handle and a blade that contains a row of sharp teeth along one edge.")
(comment BrachialArtery "The collection of all brachial arteries.  A #$BrachialArtery's proximal end connects to the #$AxillaryArtery in the #$Shoulder.  The distal end of the #$BrachialArtery #$branchesInto the #$UlnarArtery and #$RadialArtery in the #$Elbow.")
(comment MilkPowder "A dried, powdery extract of milk that does not require refrigeration and has a longer shelf life than fresh milk.  It may be reconstituted (with water) into a drinkable milk, or the powder may be used as an additive in recipes to enrich the protein or calcium content of foods.")
(comment RetailStore "A specialization of #$RetailOrganization.  Each instance of #$RetailStore is a local single-site organization (but not necessarily a stand-alone business, since it might be part of a chain of retail stores) which sells goods directly to consumers at the organization's #$physicalQuarters.  Note that the parent company in a chain of retail stores (such as #$KMart-TheCompany) is _not_, in general, an instance of #$RetailStore, but a local store in a chain generally is (for example, all instances of #$KMartStore are instances of #$RetailStore).")
(comment EncryptionProgram "The subcollection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used to encrypt files.  #$Encrypting typically involves applying a 'one-way' mathematical function to the data to render it unreadable by anyone who does not have the proper decryption function/password.  There are a large number of encryption-decryption routines.")
(comment FileFolder "The collection of all file folders")
(comment increasesLevelInBody "The expression `(#$increasesLevelInBody CHEMTYPE1 CHEMTYPE2)' means that, in normal cases, an increase in the amount of CHEMTYPE1 in a human body results

in an increased level of CHEMTYPE2 in that body. Many drugs work in this indirect way. For example, Selective Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitors such as Prozac work by decreasing the brain's ability to \"reuptake\" serotonin, thereby resulting in an increase in its level in the brain.

Note that this predicate is irreflexive.")
(disjointWith FieldOfStudy CommunicationConvention)
(comment PhosgeneOxime "A chemical warfare agent (See #$ChemicalAgentType). When used in gaseous form to it can cause pulmonary edema and skin and tissue lesions in humans.")
(comment complementaryNucleotides "(#$complementaryNucleotides NUCL1 NUCL2) means that the #$Nucleotides  NUCL1 and NUCL2 are complementary in virtue of their nitrogen bases being complementary (see #$complementaryBases). Instance-level version of #$complementaryNucleotideTypes.")
(comment HTMLCommandExecutionFault "#$HTMLCommandExecutionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$HTMLCommandExecutionFault if an unauthorized person can pass HTML code to it and have it execute commands.")
(comment ProjectileSlug-Bullet "Every #$ProjectileSlug-Bullet is contained (#$in-Snugly) within some #$ProjectileCasing until fired inside of a gun.  Once fired, a detonated explosive within the #$ProjectileCasing causes the #$ProjectileSlug-Bullet to be ejected from the #$ProjectileCasing at high velocity. The word 'bullet' is ambiguous.  It sometimes refers to the entire bullet and shell-casing assembly and other times refers to #$ProjectileSlug-Bullet.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterI "The lowercase letter 'i'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$I-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterI.")
(comment AutomobileWindow "Windows of cars")
(comment Scrubbing "Cleaning by vigorously rubbing, usually with a sponge or a brush.")
(comment DivisionChytridiomycota "These fungi are characterised by their asexual state, a zoospore (motile) with a single whiplash flagellum oriented and located posteriorly. The

   zoospore is formed in a sporangium. Zoospores are released through an opening in the wall, and their release usually indicates the death of the

   thallus. 

Zoospores of opposite mating type may meet, fuse (plasmogamy immediately followed by karyogamy) and go on to form a single resting

   sporangium. After meiosis, the sporangium germinates to release further zoospores, which may be asexual, in which case, the single zoospore

   attaches (encysts) to and colonises a substrate. The cyst may be a resting structure or it may grow to form a sporangium. It may be located on

   or in the substrate. 

In some species, resting sporangia may take the form of a multicelled, thick walled sorus. The sorus is commonly found within parasitised

   tissue such as a root, where it remains until the surrounding tissue has rotted away.")
(comment AntiGlareComputerScreen "This is the collection of anti-glare screens that fit over the

#$VideoScreens on computer monitors.")
(disjointWith JointVentureOrganization SpeciallyCharteredInstitution)
(comment RadioTransmitter "Device used for transmitting radio signals.")
(comment ExecutableRegistryKey "The collection of all instances of #$RegistryKey which may take filenames as their value (they are much like Unix environment variables in this regard).  The files named in #$ExecutableRegistryKeys are typically executed upon startup, making #$ExecutableRegistryKeys a great place for a malicious user to place trojan programs.")
(comment Rubber-TheNaturalStuff "Not synthetic rubber - The sap of the rubber tree; milky when harvested, it congeals into natural rubber.")
(comment DorsalRamusS3 "The collection of all S3 dorsal rami.  VentralRamiS3 and DorsalRamiS3 branch from SpinalRootS3.  DorsalRamiS3 supplies the posterior gluteal skin.")
(comment PorkPicnicShoulder "The collection of pork picnic shoulders. Picnic shoulders or picnic hams are meat cuts from the shoulder of a #$Pig. They are often served smoked.")
(comment AluminumFoil "Very thin sheets of aluminum used primarily for food storage or cooking.")
(comment AccipitrineFamily "The family Accipitridae, comprising the hawks, Old World vultures, kites, harriers, and eagles.")
(comment CADToolProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs used for computer-aided drafting and design.")
(comment WallClock "A type of clock which hangs on the wall.")
(comment LetterCopy "The collection of copies of letters (#$Letter-Missive).  These may be #$InformationBearingObjects on instances of #$SheetOfPaper or photon patterns being emitted from a #$CathodeRayTube, for example.")
(comment ventralTo "(#$ventralTo OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 lies in the #$VentralDirection of OBJ-2, when viewed in the frame of reference of the object with #$AnimalBodyShape (often, a #$Person) that they are located in.  Note that OBJ-2 is therefore dorsal to OBJ-1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `dorsal to'.  OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are often, but not always, #$AnimalBodyRegions.  #$anteriorTo is used instead of #$ventralTo in the #$Head-AnimalBodyPart and #$Foot-AnimalBodyPart.")
(disjointWith Water Card)
(comment MadeiraIslandsPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Madeira-Islands, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment LuggageOrganizer "This is the collection of products which fit into luggage whose purpose

is to structure the space inside in such as way that the items stored

therein are more organized and perhaps better protected.")
(comment SouthernCaucasianLanguageFamily "Languages of the South Caucases unrelated to Slavic, including Georgian, Laz, Svan, and others.  Also called Kartvelian.")
(comment Fireplace "The brick construction attached to a chimney which 

opens into a room and in which fuel is burned. A negative example would be

#$ElectricFireplace, because it is not a permatnent structure, nor does it 

burn fuel.  A positive example would be a #$GasFireplace.")
(disjointWith SportsCompetition MakingWrittenMaterial)
(comment FingerMovement "Using one finger to perform an activity. Not necessarily movement per se.")
(comment InformationProvidingOrganization "A collection of organizations; a subset of #$ServiceOrganization.  An element of #$InformationProvidingOrganization is an organization that gathers and provides information.  This includes: news services, credit-checking companies, stock wire services, data sources, publishing companies, etc.")
(comment SQLClientProgram "A collection of computer programs which (can or do) receive information from

a database queried using SQL (#$SQL-Language). This often occurs via an #$SQLServerProgram.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization HumanServicesOrganization)
(comment LiquidLaundryDetergent "Liquid Laundry Detergent")
(comment taxonMembers "The predicate #$taxonMembers is used to relate taxonomic groups to the types of organism that belong to those groups.  (#$taxonMembers TAXON ORGTYPE) means that the #$BiologicalTaxon TAXON includes the #$OrganismClassificationType ORGTYPE.  ORGTYPE may or may not be a scientific category; nonetheless, all members are classified under the scientific taxon TAXON.  If ORGTYPE is also an instance of #$BiologicalTaxon, use the more specific (#$superTaxons ORGTYPE TAXON).  Example: (#$taxonMembers #$Mammal #$FemalePerson).  Organism types may be related to more than one taxon, so long as they are at diffent levels (e.g. #$BiologicalClass and #$BiologicalOrder).")
(comment Joint-AnimalBodyPart "A specialization of #$Joint-Physical and #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$Joint-AnimalBodyPart is a juncture between the ends or edges of abutting bones of an animal's skeleton.  Joints are of several types mechanically (e.g., ball-and-socket, hinged).  Many major joints function as hinges, in which the ends of the abutting bones are joined with ligaments and cushioned by cartilege.")
(comment TemporoMandibularJoint "The #$TemporoMandibularJoint (TemperoMandibularJoint) connects the #$Jawbone with the #$TemporalBone.  It is located on the side of the

face immediately in front of the ear canal (#$ExternalAuditoryMeatus).  The #$TemporoMandibularJoint enables complex motion of the #$Jawbone (up-down, forward-back, rotational, & combined).")
(comment PassiveSonar-Device "The collection of devices used for passively listening to noises in the water.  This type of sonar is often employed by  #$Submarine-Military to avoid detection inherent in using #$ActiveSonar-Device.")
(comment BiologicalClass "A #$BiologicalTaxonType that is 
the collection of taxonomic subdivisions directly under 
#$BiologicalPhylum (for animals and for animal-like organisms 
in the #$ProtistaKingdom) and directly under #$BiologicalDivision 
(for plants and for plant-like organisms in the #$ProtistaKingdom).")
(comment ElectricalConduit "The housing through which wires are run when buildings are wired.")
(comment Lake "A specialization of #$BodyOfWater.  Each instance of #$Lake is a land-locked body of water, typically but not necessarily of fresh water.  Two important specializations are #$FreshWaterLake (instances of which are fresh-water lakes) and #$InlandSea (instances of which are salt-water lakes).  Instances include #$LakeMaracaibo, #$LakeWinnipeg, #$LakeTanganyika, #$LochNess-Lake, #$LakeErie, #$LakeTahoe, #$CaspianSea, and #$DeadSea.")
(comment CommercialDocument "The collection of all written reports")
(comment Femur "The collection of all thighBones.  The #$Femur (or 'thighbone') is located in the #$Thigh.")
(disjointWith TextileArtifact Sandpaper)
(comment Rottweiler "A collection of medium-sized to large dogs that are robust and black.")
(comment Marquess "The collection of all marquesses, or male persons who hold hereditary marquessal titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch, in the systems of nobility of the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland or #$Biffeche-KingdomOf.  This distinct from the French #$Marquis.  See also #$Marchioness.")
(disjointWith FoundationOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment EnigmaCryptographicMachine "The collection of all Enigma cipher machines used by the Germans in #$WorldWarII.")
(comment ExtensorPollicisLongus "The #$Collection of all instances of #$ExtensorPollicisLongus#$Muscle.  The #$ExtensorPollicisLongus extends the #$DistalPhalanx of the #$Thumb.")
(comment UnwrappingSomething "The collection of events in which a wrapper is removed from an object")
(comment PartPredicate "A collection of binary #$ObjectPredicates that are used to relate individuals to their (tangible or intangible) parts or components of various sorts.  Each instance PRED of #$PartPredicate (i) has both of its argument-places constrained (see #$argIsa) to instances of #$Individual or some subcollection thereof and (ii) is a specialization (via either #$genlPreds or #$genlInverse) of the predicate #$parts (q.v.).  Examples include #$physicalDecompositions, #$subEvents, and #$subOrganizations.")
(comment ApexOfLung "The collection of the general uppermost (superior) portions of #$Lungs.")
(comment MealType "Types of meals , characterized by the time of day they usually occur.")
(comment FurnitureRepairShop "A commercial organization with a specific location (site) which performs furniture repair, refinishing, etc.")
(disjointWith ViviparousAnimal OviparousAnimal)
(comment MoneyOrder "Checks issued by a financial institution to a purchaser.  Money orders are safer for the recipient than regular checks, because the issuing organization verifies that the money is allocated for this purpose.  Money orders are issued in whatever value the purchaser specifies (possibly up to some limit). See also #$BuyingAMoneyOrder.")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece DrugSubstance)
(comment SeedFn "#$SeedFn takes a single plant collection as its argument and returns the collection of seeds of that type of plant.  (#$SeedFn PLANTTTYPE) denotes the collection of all seeds from the elements of PLANTTYPE.  For example, (#$SeedFn #$VanillaOrchid) denotes the collection of vanilla \"beans\".")
(comment PitcairnIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$PitcairnIsland, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith ContactLocationType LanguageGroupingType)
(comment DoorKnob "A mechanical device found at hip-level on #$DoorInABuilding, which is turned in order to open the door. We don't think it should be a spec of #$ControlKnob, despite its name.")
(comment argsNotGenl "(#$argsNotGenl REL COL) means that anything given as an argument to the #$Relation REL must not be a spec of the #$Collection COL.")
(comment GenericSynthesisFn "(#$GenericSynthesisFn OUTPUT) is the collection of all synthesis events, where the #$outputsOfSynthesis is OUTPUT.")
(comment ComputerBitmapDisplay "A type of computer peripheral used for displaying bitmap information to a computer user.")
(comment SpiceMill "A device which is used to grind various types of spices.")
(comment Scavenger "The collection of animals that feed wholly or partly on dead animals that they find rather than kill.")
(comment InferiorTrunk-BrachialPlexus "The collection of all inferior trunks of all brachial plexi.  The inferior trunk of a #$BrachialPlexus is formed by the convergence of nerves from #$VentralRamusC8 and #$VentralRamusT1.  The inferior trunk splits into its anterior and posterior divisions on its distal end.")
(comment Turfgrass "This is the collection of turfgrass plants. Turfgrasses are any kind of grass

that can be used for lawns, athletic fields, and the like.")
(comment Plywood "plywood")
(comment Bioenergy "This is the collection of instances of #$Energy-Renewable which are produced

from crops. Ethanol is probably the best-known sort.")
(comment Joke-CW "The collection of all #$PropositionalConceptualWorks consisting of a small number of sentences intended primarily to amuse an addressee. Instances of #$Joke-CW often involve wordplay that depends on the identity of the words used in addition to the propositions expressed. Instances of #$Joke-CW can be either monologues, in which the speaker relates an instance of #$Narrative with a humorous ending, or (usually formulaic) dialogues, in which the addressee reponds to the speaker's utterances in a predictable way. Use #$JokeAboutFn to create specializations of #$Joke-CW. (See #$Joke-IBT for actual written or spoken jokes and #$JokeTelling for acts of telling jokes.)")
(comment Quadriceps "The muscle which runs along the top of the thigh")
(disjointWith HairAccessory Hat)
(comment Meristem "A region in a plant containing actively or potentially actively dividing cells.  Includes apical merstems of the shoot and root, marginal meristems of leaves, lateral meristems, cambia, etc.")
(comment FrenchGuiananPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$FrenchGuiana, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment VideoProjector "Stand alone devices which take inputs from 

various electronic video sources (S-Video, computer video cards, etc.) 

and not #$MovieReels.  Therefore, a negative example would of course be 

#$MovieProjector.")
(comment VacuumDustBag "The collection of bags made for collecting dust in a vacuum cleaner.")
(comment containedObject "(#$containedObject CONT OBJ) means that OBJ is the physical object which is being contained in the instance of #$ContainingSomething, CONT.")
(disjointWith Foot-AnimalBodyPart Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(comment PreparingFoodItem "A specialization of #$PreparingFoodOrDrink.  Each instance of #$PreparingFoodItem is an event in which a single item of #$Food is prepared to make it ready to eat.  For example, instances of #$MakingToast, roasting a turkey, or #$BakingBread.")
(disjointWith ShoeStore AutoDealership)
(comment DeliveryTruck "Typically boxy, panel-sided vehicles used for delivery of goods on local [vs. long-distance] routes.")
(comment Reindeer "A specification of #$Deer, also known as Caribou.  Both the male and the female of this species grow antlers.  Their scientific name is Rangifer tarandus.")
(comment WritingAComposition "Composing that musical composers, novelists, book authors, students, etc. do.  Developing ideas into a substantive conceptual work.  The process normally involves putting ideas down in written form, reviewing them, making changes and repeating the process.  Takes a couple of hours to years.  This is usually a noncontinuous event.  This process is not a spec of #$Writing just as performing long division \"by hand\" is not.  Writing is used to assist the process to alleviate having to store the whole conceptual work in mind at one time.")
(comment Esophagus "The collection of esophagi, each being a tube (#$AnatomicalVessel) that joins the #$Pharynx to the #$Stomach.  #$The #$Esophagus is a unique part of the #$AlimentaryCanal.")
(comment structureOfCW "'(#$structureOfCW WORK STRUCTURE)' means that STRUCTURE is the #$CWStructure corresponding to the whole of #$StructurallySpecificWork WORK.  For example, an instance of #$MusicalText corresponds to the whole of a particular recorded performance of an instance of #$Symphony.")
(comment Implant-Medical "A collection of #$PhysicalDevices surgically placed or intended to be placed inside living             tissue to serve some medical purpose.  This collection includes instances of #$Implant-Dental.")
(comment GlagoliticLetter "characters adapted from Greek, for writing Slavic languages; now used only liturgically near the Adriatic")
(comment wasteProducts "(#$wasteProducts EV OBJ) means that OBJ is one of the by-products of EV which is disposed of, rather than used or sold.  See also #$unwantedMatter.")
(comment TouringABuilding "The specialization of #$SightSeeing which consists of comprehensive tours of buildings, usually, but not always, conducted in the presence of a guide.  Instances are to be distinguished by the fact that they are systematic, endeavoring to cover all of the historically salient features of the construction toured.  Instances may be performed by individual tourists or by groups of the same.  See #$BuildingTourFn")
(disjointWith IntrinsicStateChangeEvent Playing-Primate)
(comment instrumentType-Generic "(#$instrumentType-Generic EVT TYPE) says that some instance(s) of TYPE were used during EVT.  In other words,  (#$relationInstanceExists #$instrument-Generic EVT TYPE).  This is an extremely general predicate. Whenever possible, one of  the spec preds, #$objectTypeUsed or #$stuffTypeUsed should be used.")
(disjointWith GutterSystem RoofOfAConstruction)
(comment ClydesdaleHorse "Instances of the collection #$ClydesdaleHorse tend to grow impressively long hair, or 'feathers,' covering their hooves.")
(comment Sentence "The collection of all sentences of any (natural or artificial) language.  This excludes \"open\" formulae of formal languages: expressions that are like sentences except for containing one or more unbound (or \"free\") variables.")
(comment RepairAndMaintenanceOrganization "The collection of all #$ServiceOrganizations that provide repair and/or maintenance services to its clients or consumers.  Examples of specializations of #$RepairAndMaintenanceOrganization include #$PestControlCompany and #$ComputerRepairShop.")
(comment Backgammon-Piece "The collection of all Backgammon pieces")
(comment ServingVessel "Containers that hold food for serving - typically used in Western family-style meals, they hold several servings of a food and are usually placed on the table during the meal.")
(comment ThoracoDorsalNerve "The collection of all thoracodorsal nerves.  The thoracodorsal nerve branches from the #$PosteriorCord-BrachialPlexus and supplies the #$LatissimusDorsi.")
(comment PecorinoRomano-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Romano, an Italian cheese.

It is a sharp, aged, ewe's milk cheese made for grating.")
(comment FinancialProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs designed primarily to manipulate, analyze, or represent financial data. General-purpose programs that can be used for financial data, including spreadsheets and word processors, are not instances.")
(comment PhotographicEnlarger "Devices used in a darkroom to enlarge photographs.")
(comment sporophyteOfPlantType "(#$sporophyteOfPlantType SPOR-TYPE PLANT-TYPE) means that SPOR-TYPE is the type of sporophyte produced by the plant taxon PLANT-TYPE.")
(disjointWith ReferenceWork Play-CW)
(comment AbdominalAorta "The collection of all abdominal aortas.  Aa #$AbdominalAorta is the section of an #$Aorta below the diaphragm [#$Diaphragm-BodyPart].  The #$AbdominalAorta splits into the left and right common illiac arteries.")
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice TransportationDevice)
(comment MozambiquePerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Mozambique, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment TwentyOne-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '21.'")
(comment AnimalTypeBySex "The collection consisting of the collections #$FemaleAnimal and #$MaleAnimal. One of the #$facets-Strict of #$Animal.")
(comment WintunLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment ElectricMixerBeater "The collection of electric mixer beaters")
(comment Juggling "The collection of all events of keeping three or more objects in the air by repeatedly catching and throwing them.")
(comment arg3NotGenl "(#$arg3NotGenl REL COL) means that nothing given as the third argument to the #$Relation REL may be a spec of the #$Collection COL.")
(disjointWith AutoDealership BicycleShop)
(comment LegalDepartment "A specialization of #$Department. Each instance of this collection is a group of employees who perform legal work for a given organization (such as evaluating and/or drafting legal documents).")
(comment DoorMat "A small rug placed near a doorway, usually to prevent tracking of dirt and mud into the room.")
(comment CherryCoke "The collection of instances Cherry Coke")
(comment Dreaming "Having a dream while sleeping")
(comment ThoracicVertebrae "#$The #$ThoracicVertebrae is the #$Series of individual #$ThoracicVertebra in #$The #$SpinalColumn.  There are twelve in the human body (T1-T12).  There is one for each #$Rib-AnimalBodyPart.")
(comment ContinentalCuisine "The collection of instances of what many Americans tend to think of as Continental food, i.e., food that is vaguely, perhaps undefinably `European'")
(comment ComplexActionPredicate "A specialization of #$ActionPredicate (q.v.).  Each instance of #$ComplexActionPredicate is such that a task specification formed with it may decompose into further actions, in contrast to specifications formed with instances of #$SimpleActionPredicate (q.v.).  By convention, expressions that denote relations that are typically instances of #$ComplexActionPredicate  are characterized by having the prefix \"do\", whereas expressions that denote relations that are typically instances of #$SimpleActionPredicate lack this prefix.  Note, however, that whether a predicate is an instance of #$SimpleActionPredicate or #$ComplexActionPredicate depends on context.")
(comment ToyTypeByBrand "Instances are types of toy products, specific as to brand.  These are not usually #$FormalProductTypes, since they usually include a whole line of different #$FormalProductTypes.  Instances include 'BarbieDoll', 'HotWheels', 'Legos'.  Instances would NOT include #$Doll-Toy or #$StuffedAnimal, because these aren't specific as to brand.")
(disjointWith Thinking BiologicalEvent)
(comment PlanterAgriculturalImplement "The collection of farm implements used for holding crop seeds and sowing them in a field")
(disjointWith ElevatorCarMoving WaterSurfaceTransportation)
(comment ServiceContractDocument "The collection of documents which describe and represent a maintenance agreement.")
(comment Stinger "A sharp organ, as of a bee, scorpion or stingray, of offense and defense usually connected with a poisonous gland or otherwise adapted to wound by piercing and innoculating a poisonous secretion")
(comment ChesapeakeBayRetriever "A collection of relatively large dogs with thick coats.  This breed is also referred to as the Chessy.")
(comment ComorosPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Comoros-TheNation, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment FoodAndBeverageOrganization "Each instance of #$FoodAndBeverageOrganization is an #$Organization that is primarily or significantly engaged in the #$FoodAndBeverageIndustry or whose activities focus on that industry.  Specializations of #$FoodAndBeverageOrganization include #$Restaurant-Organization and #$GroceryStore.")
(comment VehicleTrack-Device "The collection of all instances of 

#$Belt-Mechanical that are the defining

feature of #$TrackedVehicles.  On such

vehicles, each (there are usually two) 

#$VehicleTrack-Device

 is strapped around a series of 

#$LandTransportationWheels.  The #$Wheels 

turn, and the vehicle rolls

 along the tracks (instead of #$Tires).")
(comment PosteriorBasalSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all Posterior basal segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a (left or right) #$InferiorLobeOfLung that supplies the #$PosteriorBasalSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung.  It branches from the #$InferiorLobarBronchus.")
(comment CassetteDeck "A collection of audio components. Each cassette deck is a non-portable device used for playing and recording audio cassettes. It is generally used in an audio rack or audio cabinet in conjuntion with a receiver or amplifier and stereo speakers or headphones. It is generally connected to an electric wall outlet for power and to an audio amplifier for sound input and output.")
(comment SplenicArtery "The collection of all splenic #$Veins.  The #$SplenicArtery supplies #$Blood to the #$Spleen, #$Pancreas, #$Stomach, and greater omentum (#$Omentum-Greater). ['arteria splenica' or 'arteria lienalis']")
(comment Spice "Seasonings used to add flavor to food")
(comment GraphicsEditingProgram "This is a #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction where the function in question is

the creation and manipulation of computer images.")
(comment BodyLotion "Liquid products, typically oil-based, applied to the skin in order to moisturize it.")
(comment Caffeine "A popular alkaloid stimulant, found in tea, coffee, soft drinks, matte, and various other consumables.")
(comment Screenplay "The outline of a #$Movie-CW or #$TVShow-CW, giving the action in the order in which it takes place, the description of scenes and characters, etc.")
(comment SpecifiedCurrencyType "A collection of collections;  each instance of #$SpecifiedCurrencyType is a subcollection of #$Currency, distinguished by denomination, issuing #$GeopoliticalEntity, and often date range.")
(comment EnumeratedIndexicalConcept "Instances are denoted by terms formed with a function like #$TheNthFn, and represent such indexical (context-dependent) concepts as ''the first car'' and ''the second car''.")
(comment CustomWheel "The collection of custom wheels.")
(comment Eutheria "#$Eutheria is a specialization of #$Mammal.  Each instance of #$Eutheria is a placental mammal; most mammals are members of this collection.  #$Eutheria are born live, nurse from their mothers' #$MammaryGlands and live outside their mothers' bodies.")
(comment LatinCapitalLetterJ "The capital letter 'J'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$J-TheLetter and #$LatinSmallLetterJ.")
(comment WoodwindInstrument "Musical instruments using reeds or flute/whistle-type mechanisms to produce sound.")
(comment eatsWillingly "The predicate #$eatsWillingly is used to relate an #$Animal to the type of food it will willingly eat.  In a normal #$EatingEvent, the food consumed is of a type that the eater #$eatsWillingly.  As negative examples, no vegetarian or herbivore #$eatsWillingly meat.")
(comment DivisionPolypodiophyta "Also called Pteridophyta, this is the collection

of ferns.")
(comment TVTransmitter "Device used for transmitting tv signals.")
(comment HKLM-Software-Microsoft-WindowsNT-CurrentVersion-AeDebug-Directory "The #$Collection of all HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\WindowsNT\\CurrentVersion\\Aedebug\\ directories (instances of #$ExecutableRegistryKey) found on NT machines.")
(comment Table-PieceOfFurniture "A piece of furniture usually made entirely of rigid material, used to support objects.")
(comment MiddleTrunk-BrachialPlexus "The collection of all middle trunks of all brachial plexi.  The middle trunk of a #$BrachialPlexus is formed by the convergence of nerves from #$VentralRamusC7.  The middle trunk then splits into its anterior and posterior divisions.")
(comment PorkRoast "The collection of pork roasts. Pork roasts are roasts from a #$Pig.")
(comment Nematode "Nematodes are microscopic worms that cause eighty billion dollars of crop loss in the world each year. Nematodes constitute one of the most important and abundant groups within the animal kingdom and are highly capable of surviving in any

environment. In general, nematodes have slender, cylindrical, non-segmented bodies tapering towards the head and tail, but females of some of the

plant-parasitic species assume varying forms, such as pear, lemon or kidney shapes. They are called plant-parasitic because of the nutrients they get

from plants and have a needle-like structure called stylet, which is used to pierce plant cells to get food.")
(comment packageProgrammingLanguages "(#$packageProgrammingLanguages PACK LANG) means that some #$ProgrammingLanguageImplementation of the #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage LANG is included in the #$SoftwarePackage PACK.")
(comment GrandfatherClock "A type of clock which usually stands on the ground and has a pendulum.")
(comment MusicalTextCopy "The collection of all (partially tangible) sheet(s) of music that can be put on a music stand, plus the musical text on a computer screen, which has lots of characters indicating notes, timing, volume, etc. The musician 'reads' this the way others might read a book, a newspaper, or a text of words on a computer screen.")
(disjointWith Water MusicalInstrument)
(comment VaticanCityPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$VaticanCity, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment SingleSiteFn "#$SingleSiteFn maps instances of #$SingleSiteOrganization to the #$SpatialThing that they occupy.  '(#$SingleSiteFn THEATERORG)' means the #$SpatialThing that THEATERORG occupies.  For example, the Paramount Theater organization operates out of the Paramount Theater building on Congress Avenue.  An instance of #$Restaurant-Organization may operate out of some natural structure, out of a #$SpaceInAFixedHOC, or out of a #$ConstructionArtifact.")
(comment StorageOrganizer "This is the collection of products which fit into 

either a #$StorageConstruct and whose purpose is to organize

the items stored therein.")
(comment NorthernCaucasianLanguageFamily "Languages of southeastern Russia, including that of the fabled Circassian maidens")
(comment Oven "A receptacle or compartment for baking, drying or heating something.")
(comment TurningSomethingWithHand "Turning some object (e.g. a #$ControlKnob, a #$DoorKnob...) with the hand.")
(comment Hot-Spicy "The collection of all food that is hot in the spicy as opposed to temperature sense. Hot food is generally hot in virtue of containing
chilies, which contain capsaicin. Other ingredients, however, such as ginger, can make food hot.")
(comment MusicPerformanceOrganization "A collection of organizations.  An element of #$MusicPerformanceOrganization is a group whose main function is the members playing music together.  The collection #$MusicPerformanceOrganization includes popular music bands, orchestras, choirs, and marching bands; it does not include record companies, music publishers, etc.")
(disjointWith HarvesterAgriculturalImplement Train-TransportationDevice)
(comment ApplicationProgram "A specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  Each instance of #$ApplicationProgram is a program whose running copies perform specific functions either directly for users or as background processes.  #$ApplicationProgram is disjoint with #$OperatingSystem and #$OperatingSystemKernel.  Together, these three collections partition #$ComputerProgram-CW.")
(disjointWith EntertainmentOrRecreationOrganization BuyingGroup)
(comment HairCuttingScissors "Scissors designed for cutting hair.")
(comment Crab-Hermit "A collection of false crabs; they have only three walking legs (while  true crabs have four) but they resemble crabs in many other respects.")
(comment pluggedInto "(#$pluggedInto MALE FEMALE) means that MALE has a convex part which is #$in-Snugly a #$Cavity in FEMALE.  A specific alignment between MALE and FEMALE which is necessary for this to be the case maintains.  For example, the plug of a #$ElectricalToaster #$PowerCord is #$pluggedInto an #$ElectricalOutlet when it is operating.")
(comment StriatedMuscle "A specialization of #$MuscleTissue.  Each instance of #$StriatedMuscle is a piece of muscle tissue of that constitutes a muscle which normally performs functions that are under an organism's voluntary control.  Muscles of this kind differ in structure from smooth muscles, which are involved in involuntary physiological functions such as digestion and breathing.  Elements of #$StriatedMuscle are composed of multinuclear cells and distinguished by light and dark bands (viz., striations).  Cf. #$SmoothMuscle.")
(comment ProkaryoticDNAMolecule "the collection of DNA molecules found in the cells of prokaryotic organisms.")
(comment Carpet "The generic material called carpet.")
(comment JuvenileAnimal "An instance of #$AnimalTypeByMaturity (q.v.) and a specialization
of #$Animal.  #$JuvenileAnimal is the collection of all animals 
that are not fully grown or fully mature.  Cf. #$AdultAnimal.")
(comment ComputerType "This is the collection of types of computer. Computers can be typed by

maker, architecture, function, size, etc.")
(comment CircuitTester "A device used to test how much electrical current is flowing through a connection.")
(comment SignedPurchaseContract "Agreement to purchase something specific, like a service or a computer")
(comment Skull "The protective skeletal encasing of the the brain")
(disjointWith TextileArtifact AcrylicSheet)
(comment RhodesianRidgeback "A collection of large dogs with short, thick fur.")
(disjointWith HumanServicesOrganization TransportationOrganization)
(comment MP3Player "The collection of hardware devices whose primary intended purpose is to play MP3 files.  A computer is not an #$MP3Player (even if that's all it's used for) because that was not its primary intended purpose.")
(comment FlexorCarpiRadialis "The #$Collection of all instances of #$FlexorCarpiRadialis #$Muscle.  The #$FlexorCarpiRadialis flexes and abducts the #$Wrist.")
(comment Wrapper "The collection of pieces of sheet-like material that become containers when they are wrapped around objects.  Examples include shrink-wrap packages and candy bar wrappers.")
(comment BaseOfLung "The collection of the general lowermost (inferior) portions of #$Lungs.")
(comment Meal "The foods and drinks that make up the group of things consumed when a person or group of people eat a meal.")
(comment HairSalon "A localized (one site) commercial organization that performs hair-cutting/styling.")
(comment MaliciousComputerProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are designed to have malicious uses, whether designed by the military or by adolescent hackers. This class of program includes #$ComputerViruses, Trojan Horses, Internet worms and punters.")
(disjointWith Homeotherm Poikilotherm)
(comment HardDiskDrive "#$HardDiskDrive is the collection of #$DiskDrives which are used by instances of #$Computer as storage devices. A #$HardDiskDrive is generally a semi-permanent peripheral for a computer. #$ComputerProgram-CWs and #$ComputerFile-CWs which are used often and which a user needs easy access to are generally stored on an instance of #$HardDiskDrive.")
(comment (FruitFn VanillaOrchid) "Known as vanilla beans\"; the fruit of the vanilla orchid, rich in vanillin which is extracted to be used as a flavoring.")
(comment CeutaEnclavePerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$Ceuta-Enclave, or participates in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment ProductionOfArtifactFn "(#$ProductionOfArtifactFn PRODUCTTYPE) returns the collection of all

#$ProductionEvents whose #$outputsCreateds are instances of

PRODUCTTYPE.")
(disjointWith Wolf Dog)
(comment AlphabeticWriting "writing with, ideally, a one-to-one correspondence between each significantly different speech-sound (phoneme) of a language and a specific letter -- or, letters, where form variations such as upper and lower case are involved--, an ideal but rarely achieved")
(comment DoorLock "A device on a door that permits a person to lock the door using a key. There are other kinds of door locks, but for now this is only the kind that has a doorknob and is locked by key.")
(comment ComputerKeyboard "A device used for accepting typed input from a computer user.")
(comment Lens-Artificial "The collection of all manufactured lenses, as in #$Telescopes, #$Microscopes, #$Binoculars, and #$EyeGlasses.")
(comment NeoGeoPocket-TheProduct "This is a compact portable video game platform.")
(comment VentralRamusT1 "The collection of all T1 ventral rami.  #$VentralRamusT1 and #$DorsalRamusT1 branch from SpinalRootT1.  #$VentralRamusT1 supplies the #$BrachialPlexus and also below the #$FirstRib.")
(comment Goose-Meat "Raw goose meat.")
(comment ArtificialLighting "The collection of all instances of #$VisibleLight that are deliberately created by intelligent agents. Includes light from a spotlight on a stage, light from a neon sign, light from interior lighting fixtures in a home, etc.")
(disjointWith GoingSomewhere BiologicalEvent)
(comment DownloadingAFile "A specialization of #$CopyingAComputerFile. In each instance of this collection, a computer copies a file from a file system that it is #$remotelyConnectedTo over a #$ComputerNetwork to a local #$ComputerDisk or other long-term storage device.")
(comment Distiller-Device "an apparatus used for distillation.")
(comment YellowPages "A sub-collection of #$TelephoneDirectory. Each instance of #$YellowPages lists #$PhoneNumbers for #$Businesses. The listings may be sorted alphabetically by the name of the #$Business, or by names of business categories, and by name of #$Business within each category.")
(comment MobOfHair-Mammal "A mob of hairs found on mammals")
(disjointWith PersonalHygieneProduct NavigationDevice)
(comment Pericarp "Wall of a fruit; may be fleshy or dry at maturity.")
(comment StKittsAndNevisPerson "A person who is a #$citizens of #$SaintKitts-Nevis, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment TelevisionSetTypeByColor "A collection of collections. Each instance is a specialization of #$TelevisionSet whose instances are all of the same color.")
(comment EncryptionAlgorithm "The collection of all #$Algorithms which are used in the encrypting and decrypting of information.  See #$encryptionAlgorithms.")
(comment GasolinePump "Device which pumps Gasoline through a nozzle, usually into a #$VehicleFuelTank")
(disjointWith Braking MedicalCareEvent)
(disjointWith Fin Digit-AnatomicalPart)
(disjointWith SportingGoodsStore AutoDealership)
(comment RadioTelescope "A device designed to pick up radio signals from outer space; used by astronomers to study objects and phenomena in outer space.")
(comment Horse "The collection of all horses, of all breeds; a subset of #$EquineAnimal.  Horses may be domesticated  (for riding, draught, racing or breeding) or wild; see #$DomesticatedAnimal, #$WildAnimal.  #$Horse constitutes an instance of #$BiologicalSpecies (called Equus caballus).  Horses can interbreed with donkeys to produce a nonfertile mule or a jenny (see #$Donkey, #$Mule).")
(disjointWith Conveying-Generic Talking)
(comment VentricleOfHeart "Pumping chamber of the heart")
(comment ElectricalPlug "The thing at the end of a power cord which has prongs that plug into an electrical outlet.")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType LifeStageType)
(comment ArabicLetter "very flowing character set originally devised for writing Arabic")
(comment FreeTourTime "The collection of #$Shopping events and #$SightSeeing events that are not on the travel itinerary per se.")
(disjointWith Swimming-Generic Locomotion-Air)
(comment userAccountForSystem "A predicate expressing the relationship between instances of #$UserAccount and instances of #$AccountSystem.  (#$userAccountForSystem ACCOUNT SYSTEM) means that SYSTEM hosts ACCOUNT, through which a user can log in to perform operations on (and use the resources of) SYSTEM. SYSTEM may be an individual computer, or it may be some larger account system, such as that on an #$Intranet.")
(disjointWith PlasterTheConstructionMaterial Metal)
(comment PercheronHorse "Instances of the collection #$PercheronHorse are usually grey.  They are descended from instances of #$ArabianHorse.")
(disjointWith MedicalCareOrganization RepairAndMaintenanceOrganization)
(comment DiceShaker "The collection of all dice shakers, small cup shaped containers that are used as an aid for dice rolling in games of chance")
(comment mereologicalSumOf2 "(#$mereologicalSumOf2 SUM PART1 PART2) means that SUM is the mereological sum of PART1 and PART2, i.e., SUM, PART1 and PART2 are #$Individual such that PART1 is a part of SUM, PART2 is a part of SUM and any #$Individual which is a part of SUM at least have a part with PART1 or PART2 or both.")
(comment TurningOnEngine "The turning on/starting of an engine.")
(comment LowerSubScapularNerve "The collection of all lower subscapular nerves.  The lower subscapular nerve branches from the #$PosteriorCord-BrachialPlexus and supplies the subscapularis and the teres major.")
(comment Raclette-Cheese "This the collection of all instances of Raclette, a Swiss melting cheese.

This cheese is often called Bagnes. It is melted for a dish called Raclette.")
(comment MortgageCalculatorProgram "The collection of all #$CalculatorPrograms designed primarily to calculate the terms of a #$MortgageAgreement. Generally, given all but one of the following - loan amount, interest rate, length of loan, frequency (or number) of payments, and payment amount - a #$MortgageCalculatorProgram will calculate the missing value.")
(comment DarkroomEquipment "Miscellaneous equipment used in darkrooms for developing and printing exposed photographic film.")
(disjointWith PlayScript ReferenceWork)
(comment AscendingAorta "The collection of all ascending aortas.  An #$AscendingAorta is the proximal part of an #$Aorta as it rises from the left ventricle (#$VentricleOfHeart)  Each #$CoronaryArtery branches off of an #$AscendingAorta.  It continues as the #$AorticArch.")
(disjointWith FoodOrDrinkPreparationDevice HumanOccupationConstruct)
(comment JethouIslandPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Jethou-Island, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment Two-TheCard "This is the subcollection of #$PlayingCard that contains all of the cards which have the face value of '2.'")
(comment Mixe-ZoqueLanguageFamily "Amerindian languages, spoken in Central America and western North America")
(comment MeasuringSpoon "Little spoons of varying sizes used to measure cooking ingredients, medicine, etc.")
(comment Relationship-GenericFn "\"(#$Relationship-GenericFn ?THING1 ?THING2)\" denotes the relationship between ?THING1 and ?THING2. It is impossible to neatly delimit a class of cases which are appropriate arguments for this function except to say that  it would be coextensive with the set of cases for which the common English expression `the relationship between ... and ...' is apt. Instances would include the relationship between smoking and health, the relationship between science and religion,  the relationship between Pat and Chris. Though relationships are typically grounded in garden-variety physical facts, they are themselves intangible.")
(comment ShapingByBlowing "This collection includes instances of distending a material and shaping it by the action of blowing or injecting air. Examples include blowing bubbles or creating blown glass.")
(disjointWith AutoTireStore AutoDealership)
(comment RegistryKey "Registry keys are hierarchically organized subfiles of the #$WindowsRegistry.  These files are organized according to a system which was introduced with Windows 3.x to replace the old system of storing configuration information in .INI files. Registry keys take values, which may be simple integers or executable code.  What value a given registry key is set to will determine a machine's configuration in a host of ways, many of which will affect the level of security of information stored on the machine.  See also #$ExecutableRegistryKey, #$MSRegistryEditor.")
(comment AutoBodyRepairDepartment "#$Departments in an auto dealership or other retail store that perform repairs of auto bodies.")
(comment BathtubSkidlessMat "Please find a better name for me.  This is the collection of mats used to prevent or at least reduce slipping in a tub/shower.  Usually they are made of rubber and have suction cups on the bottom.")
(comment DietCherryCoke "The collection of instances of Diet Cherry Coke")
(comment SacralVertebrae "#$The #$SacralVertebrae is the #$Series of individual #$SacralVertebra in #$The #$SpinalColumn.  The five in the human body (S1-S5) are united in a single bone, the #$Sacrum.")
(comment MexicanCuisine "The collection of instances of what many Americans tend to think of as Mexican food")
(disjointWith Thinking BodyMovementEvent)
(comment ChainSaw "Gasoline- or electrically- powered device for cutting trees")
(comment Calendar-Document "The collection of all documents that provide information about correspondences between, e.g., the days of the week and the days of the month, the days of the month and the phases of the moon, etc.")
(comment Antenna-AnimalBodyPart "A movable segmented organ of sensation located on the head of insects, crustaceans and arachnids")
(comment CurlyCoatedRetriever "A collection of dogs.")
(comment RussianPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Russia, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith FoodAndBeverageOrganization JudicialOrganization)
(comment ISOStandard "The international standards developed by the #$InternationalOrganizationForStandardization.")
(comment AnteriorBasalSegmentalBronchusOfInferiorLobeOfLung "The collection of all anterior basal segmental bronchi (#$BronchialTubes) of #$Lungs, each being a #$SegmentalBronchus in a (left or right) #$InferiorLobeOfLung that supplies the #$AnteriorBasalSegmentOfInferiorLobeOfLung.  It branches from the #$InferiorLobarBronchus.")
(comment CDPlayer-AudioComponent "The device used to play compact discs")
(comment SoupStock "The collection of all broth used to make soup.  Members of this collection are liquids in which meat, fish, or vegetables have been simmered.  Soup stock is used as a basis for soup, gravy, or sauce.  It is usually a food ingredient only, but may occasionally be consumed as is.")
(comment governingBody "The predicate #$governingBody identifies the suborganization which has governing authority over a particular organization.  (#$governingBody ORG GOVORG) means that GOVORG sets the policies and rules for ORG.  GOVORG is recognized, at least informally, and effectively functions by administering the internal and external affairs of ORG, whether or not the relationship is rigidly defined.  An important specialization of this predicate is #$government, which relates a #$GeopoliticalEntity to its #$RegionalGovernment.")
(comment cardinalityGreaterThan "The class COL1 has more elements than the class COL2. This predicate does *not* compare the number of reified instances (for which cf. #$extentCardinality).")
(comment Chitosan "Chitosan is a polymer which is derived from the polysaccharide #$Chitin.")
(comment VisualizationComputerProgram "This is a #$ComputerProgramTypeByFunction where the function in question is

the presentation of information in visual form, typically in a way other than the way information is presented by a photograph. A common sort of instance

creates 3D images of proposed buildings from blueprints, thus allowing architects and

their clients to see what they might be getting before committing to it.")
(comment Yarn "A type of cordlike textile larger in diameter than thread.  Used for knitting and weaving.")
(comment Flax-TheFiber "Quantities of fiber derived from the flax plant.")
(comment Encrypting "A specialization of #$Encoding.  In each instance of #$Encrypting, a transformation is applied to the information in some instance of #$InformationBearingThing, with the intention of making that information inaccessible to all but the intended audience for that #$InformationBearingThing (the intended audience, in almost all cases, will have a decryption method which will allow it to transform the information back into an accessible form).")
(comment Pipe-SmokingDevice "A smoking pipe: a rigid, reusable device for containing the substance burned during smoking.")
(comment CD-ROM "A stable optical data storage medium that uses the same physical format as #$CompactDisc-Audio, readable by a computer with a

#$CD-ROMDrive.")
(comment Fruit "A specialization of #$PlantPart.  Each instance of #$Fruit is a plant structure containing the seeds of an angiosperm.  Many instances of #$Fruit have fleshy walls with high concentrations of sugars or fats, and these are often eaten by humans and other animals.  Fruits usually develop from the ovary wall, although some fruits include other tissues; e.g., the flesh of apples and of strawberries develops from the receptacle, and the fruits of pineapple and fig develop from a whole inflorescence (group of flowers).  See also #$EdibleFruit.")
(comment LatinSmallLetterJ "The lowercase letter 'j'.  This is a #$Character-Abstract rather than any physical written, printed, displayed or sounded instantiation (see #$CharacterToken).  See also #$J-TheLetter and #$LatinCapitalLetterJ.")
(comment WindInstrument-Musical "Musical instruments into which one blows air to produce a sound.")
(comment PersonalWashing "This is the collection of events in which a person washes parts of him or her self.")
(comment BromeliaceaeFamily "A botanical family which includes the genus Tillandsia, so-called

Air Plants, a group of plants that grow without soil.")
(disjointWith ActivityTypeFocusGroup SpeciallyCharteredInstitution)
(comment RailControlTower "A specialization of #$ControlTower. Instances of
#$RailControlTower are located within railroad station traffic areas and house
persons and equipment used to control the flow of rail traffic.")
(comment LocalProgram "A specialization of #$ApplicationProgram. Each instance of #$LocalProgram is a program that cannot be accessed remotely (i.e. across a #$ComputerNetwork). #$LocalProgram is dijoint with #$ServerProgram, and the two form a partition of #$ComputerProgram-CW.")
(comment TollBooth "The collection of toll booths")
(comment NLGenerationProgram "The collection of instances of 

#$ComputerProgram-CW that are designed to generate natural language from

 some non-natural language input.")
(disjointWith UserAccount SuperuserAccount)
(comment ScenarioIndexicalFn "(#$ScenarioIndexicalFn ?N) denotes a term whose referent  depends on how it is used.  For example, when (#$ScenarioIndexicalFn 1) is used as a term in one #$Scenario-Generalized, it could have a  completely different meaning than if used in a different scenario.  Terms formed with #$ScenarioIndexicalFn are like variables in that  their meaning is determined by the constraints on them, which can  vary from use to use.")
(comment patchAppliedToComputer "(#$patchAppliedToComputer PATCH COMPUTER) means that the #$ComputerPatchProgram PATCH has been installed/run on COMPUTER and has thereby (presumably) removed some computer vulnerability from COMPUTER.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureDataStorage "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program on it with a #$InsecureDataStorageFault.")
(comment HammeringANail "The collection of events in which someone uses a #$Hammer to drive a #$Nail into another object.  Frequently this is a subevent of #$Nailing one object to another.")
(comment DroppingAnObject "The collection of physical actions in which an agent -- purposefully or not -- releases an object so that it falls and collides with something below (like the floor or the ground).  Before the release, the object might be supported by part of the agent's body or by some device the agent controls.  Since the action might be unintentional, this collection includes accidental droppings.  For intentional droppings specifically, see

#$DroppingAnObject-Purposeful.")
(disjointWith DefenseSystem Excavation-Hole)
(comment linkClosedSubSystems "(#$linkClosedSubSystems SYS SUBSYS) means that the path system SUBSYS is a subsystem of the path system SYS (i.e., (#$subPathSystems SYS SUBSYS) holds) and SUBSYS 'preserves' all links in SYS between nodes in SUBSYS, i.e., if (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) holds and X and Y are in SUBSYS, LINK is a link in SUBSYS.")
(disjointWith HumanOccupationConstruct Shaft)
(comment Flat-TheShoe "Flats are slip-on womens shoes with (almost) no heels.")
(comment CertificateSourceValidationFault "A web browser program has this fault if it fails to validate  certificates issued in an SSL connection.  Attackers can exploit this fault to trick users into disclosing information (such as credit card numbers, personal data, or other sensitive information) intended for a legitimate web site.")
(comment getUserToRunProgramOnComputer "(#$getUserToRunProgramOnComputer AGENT TARGET PROGRAM) means that AGENT gets a user who is logged in on TARGET to start a process associated with PROGRAM on TARGET.")
(comment AnalogyAgentInContextCaseFn "(#$AnalogyAgentInContextCaseFn AGENT EVENT) denotes the #$AnalogyCase which is based on the given AGENT as referred to in EVENT.  This function is primarily used with #$matchBetween to state that an #$AnalogyMatch exists between two cases which are based on two agents.")
(comment LockerRoom "A room for containing lockers as is often connected to a gymnasium room for the temporary storage of belongings.  Is connected to a bathroom which has a shower stalls.")
(comment NLTaggedTerm "The collection of terms that contain NL tags.")
(comment altitudeAboveSeaLevel "(#$altitudeAboveSeaLevel OBJECT ALTITUDE) means that ALTITUDE is the vertical distance between the bottom of an arbitrary object and sea level.  #$Altimeters measure ALTITUDE.  See also #$altitudeAboveGround and #$distanceAboveSeaLevel (the latter applies only to #$GeographicalRegions.")
(disjointWith DisconnectedSpaceRegion ConnectedSpaceRegion)
(comment ComputerWorm "#$ComputerWorm is the collection of all #$MaliciousComputerPrograms that break into systems and replicate themselves in a fully automated manner.  Note that this is distinct from the collection of #$ComputerViruses which attach themselves to other computer instructions.")
(comment BodilyRecoiling "The collection of all bodily recoiling events, or involuntary reactions of the body to being startled or suddenly repelled.  Usually accompanied by blinking and mild tachycardia.  The body pulls back or 'starts' at some shock or stimulus.")
(comment Marburg "A specialization of #$ViralInfection.  Instances of #$Marburg are characterized by sudden onset of fever, malaise, headache and rash, progressing to vomiting, diarhhea, and hemorrhage. Recognised in 1967, when an outbreak affected workers who were experimenting on imported African green monkeys in Marburg and Frankfurt in Germany, and Belgrade in Yugoslavia. Similar to #$EbolaHemorrhagicFeverInfection.")
(comment organismTypeHasHabitat "(#$organismTypeHasHabitat ORGTYPE HABITAT) means that HABITAT is one of the #$EcologicalRegions in which members ORGTYPE naturally occur.")
(comment NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded "The collection of all network flow systems with single source and sink nodes: #$PathSystems of interlinked nodes in which each link, considered alone, has a single direction and has a certain local capacity for the flow of some quantity of something in that direction along that link.  For example, a road network in which the road capacity for each individual stretch of road (the maximum number of vehicles per hour), or the conductance of a pipe or wire, is known and recorded for each link.  Given such a network, all connected up, the capacity for flow along a particular link situated in the network may be less than it would be for the local link unconnected to the rest of the network.  For example, in a simple chain of links, a road-link with a high local flow capacity of 200 cars-per-hour while disconnected from the rest of the chain, might have an effective 'situated' flow capacity of only 60 cars-per-hour within the chain, because of bottlenecks (like another link in the chain with capacity of only 60), i.e. links with lower capacities upstream or downstream. Given the values of #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn for all links in a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded, the net value of #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn can be calculated for every link (e.g. using the Ford-Fulkerson Algorithm).  Each #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded as defined here has only one source node and one sink node.")
(disjointWith SomethingToWear GarmentBag)
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfWeakPasswordTransmissionEncryption "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$WeakPasswordTransmissionEncryptionFault on it.")
(comment signifiesTo-Index "This is a specialized representation (semiotic) predicate meaning representation due to causation, such as when a deer track 'represents' the deer to a tracker because the deer caused the deer track to be the way it is.  Similarly, a weathervane 'represents' the wind direction because of the way the wind direction has caused the vane to move. (#$signifiesTo-Index THING1 THING2 AGENT) means that, to AGENT, THING1 represents THING2 because AGENT regognizes that THING2 has caused  THING1 to be the way it is.  This is called 'indexical' representation. Compare this with the predicates #$signifiesTo-Icon and #$signifiesTo-Symbol.  It's possible for all three to apply to the same representation.  If the basis for the representation is unknown, use the more general predicate #$signifiesTo.")
(comment chatServerProgram "A predicate used to relate an instance of #$OnlineChat to an instance of #$IRCServerProgram.  (#$chatServerProgram CHAT SERVER) means that SERVER is run as the central server for chat clients to connect to in order to talk to each other.")
(comment FileRecoveryFault "A program has this fault if files deleted using that program can be recovered by existing disk utilities.")
(comment Intimidation-CommunicationAct "A specialization of #$CommunicationAct-Single.  Each instance of #$Intimidation-CommunicationAct is a communication act in which the sender (see the predicate #$senderOfInfo) intentionally attempts to intimidate one or more other agents (who serve as the #$communicationTargets of the intimidation act).")
(comment NonintrusiveJunction "The collection of junctions or crossings of #$Path-Generics in each of which: one path crosses, or its end joins the side of, another path of the same, or possibly a somewhat different, #$PathType, without so intruding upon or affecting the path as to cause it to be different in nature or name on either side of that junction. (Examples: A small side street joins a major boulevard and the boulevard does not change size or name at the junction.  A hallway ends at another hall, but only allows looking through a window into it.  A railroad crossing.  A small vein is one of the #$sideBranches of a large vein and the name of the large vein doesn't change at that point.)")
(comment ShaleOil "A collection of all portions of the crude #$Oil that are extracted via           a #$HeatingProcess from oil shale.")
(comment BasketballShorts "The collection of pants one often wears while playing organized basketball games.")
(comment Fly-InsectBiting "The collection of events in which the female #$Fly-Insect
takes a blood meal from a warm-blooded animal. She uses the blood from
the blood meal as nourishment for her eggs. It is in these events in
which disease from flies may be transmitted.")
(comment pathsJoinAt "(#$pathsJoinAt JUNCTION PATH1 PATH2) means that PATH1 and PATH2 (and possibly other paths as well) meet at JUNCTION.  That is, PATH1 and PATH2 contain respective segments such that 

both segments are related to JUNCTION by #$groupMembers.  See also #$PathJunctionFn")
(comment WindowPortal "#$WindowPortal is a specialization of #$Portal and #$PhysicalPartOfObject.  Each instance of #$WindowPortal is a portal found in a human occupation construct, typically covered by some instance of #$WindowThePortalCovering (q.v.).")
(comment RenterOccupiedHousehold "Those households where the resident is renting the dwelling.")
(comment Staining "Applying a colored stain to a piece of #$StructuralSupportStuff.")
(comment DefaultDomainSocketConnectionFault "An operating system has this fault if any socket created by any application is set in a highly permissive mode. The applications are vulnerable to being connected to and written to by anyone.")
(comment WaitingForABus "The collection of all events in which a person waits for a bus (public transportation road vehicle)")
(comment BPVI-SouthBluegrassHourMtFn "(#$BPVI-SouthBluegrassHourMtFn HOUR-NUM) is the
#$BPVI-Microtheory which captures the state of the South Bluegrass
forces at hour HOUR-NUM (12, 24, 36, ...) of the Block Party VI Scenario.")
(comment ActiveBuyingActivity "Activities which are intended to lead to a Buying, and in which the performer interacts with specific providers of desired goods or services.  Perhaps `FocussedBuyingActivity' would be a better name.  Visiting a store would be an #$ActiveBuyingActivity, but announcing that proposals are being accepted, which does not target a particular vendor, would not.  Contrast with #$PassiveBuyingActivity.")
(comment MagneticDevice "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$MagneticDevice is a device whose functioning depends on magnetism and which incorporates magnetized parts as a fundamental (functional) component in its design.  Typical instances include a compass, a VHS videotape, the VCR machine that tapes on it, an MRI machine in a hospital, etc.")
(disjointWith SomethingToWear PathArtifactSystem)
(comment VulnerableToFileRecovery "#$VulnerableToFileRecovery is a specialization of
 #$VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureDataStorage.  A computer has this vulnerability if
 it allows unauthorized users to recover files from it.")
(comment literacyRateForGroupInRegion "(#$literacyRateForGroupInRegion REGION GROUP RATE) means that the #$literacyRate of GROUP in REGION is RATE.")
(comment Projectile-Device "The collection of all projectiles.  Some instances of this collection, such as cannon balls, arrows, missiles are (intended to be) thrown, hurled, fired, or launched at their targets.  The other instances, such as pistol cartridges, shot gun cartridges, or #$ArtilleryShells have parts which are intended to be fired at their targets.   Many are #$ProjectileWeapons, e.g. instances of  #$Arrow, #$ProjectileSlug-Bullet, or #$Torpedo, while others are not, e.g. #$FootballBall-American. The motive force in a propelling of a #$Projectile-Device may come from a distinct #$ProjectileLauncher or #$Person, but many are self-propelled after leaving the launcher.")
(comment QuantumMechanicsTheorist "The collection of all #$QuantumMechanicsTheorists.  These #$Physicists are concerned with the physical theory that describes the motion of objects by the principles of the quantum theory.")
(comment MarineControlTower "A specialization of #$ControlTower. Instances of
#$MarineControlTower are located within port traffic areas and house
persons and equipment used to control the flow of marine traffic.")
(comment ArtifactType "The collection of all specs of #$Artifact.")
(comment StorageShed "The collection of relatively small sheds, shacks, used primarily for storing lawn and garden tools, carpentry equipment, etc.")
(comment FileSystemManagementProgram "The collection of programs that are used to manage file systems, through mounting, moving, copying or deleting files, directories, or other objects in the filesystem.")
(comment warningOf "'(#$warningOf WARNING EVENT-TYPE ROLE)' means that the
#$Warning WARNING warns the #$warnee of danger from playing ROLE in an
event of type EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment averageIncubationPeriod "(#$averageIncubationPeriod INFECTION-TYPE ORG-TYPE TIME-QUANTITY)

means that, on average, the duration of the time period between the

initial onset of an infection of type INFECTION-TYPE and the point at

which the infection becomes clinically symptomatic for an instance of ORG-TYPE is TIME-QUANTITY.")
(comment NamedPipeGenerationFault "A spec-attribute of #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault.  A telnet server creates things called \"named pipes\" when someone connects to it.  A server has this fault if the algorithm it uses to generate names for named-pipes is easily guessable.  A malicious user can exploit this fault by guessing the name of a named pipe and then \"attaching\" arbitrary code to it which will be executed when the server tries to create the named pipe.  This fault is similar in some ways to a #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite.")
(comment EpochOfCalendarSystemFn "The starting date of the specified #$CalendarSystem in the (extended) Gregorian calendar. The (#$EpochOfCalendarSystemFn #$GregorianCalendar) is (#$YearFn 1) while the (#$EpochOfCalendarSystemFn #$JewishCalendar) is (#$YearBCE-JulianFn 3761).  This should not be confused with the date on which the calendar was first used. ")
(disjointWith Doorway Excavation-Hole)
(disjointWith MechanicalDevice SheetOfSomeStuff)
(comment Buck-TheShoe "Bucks are casual lace-up shoes.  Bucks are usually white, tan, or brown.")
(comment getLoginInformationForAccount "(#$getLoginInformationForAccount AGENT ACCT) means that AGENT groks the login information for ACCT.")
(comment cultureProscribes-Hypothetical "(#$cultureProscribes-Hypothetical CULTURE COND ACTTYPE ROLE) 
  means that within CULTURE, when COND is true, it is considered improper 
  or immoral or wrong for one to play ROLE in any instance of ACTTYPE.
  For example, some cultures expect one not to belch in public.  This 
  predicate applies equally to moral rules, rules of conduct or etiquette, 
  and customs.  See also #$cultureProscribes-Categorical,
  #$culturePrescribes-Categorical, and
  #$culturePrescribes-Hypothetical.")
(comment DelegatingAuthority "This is the collection of actions in which an agent delegates some power, function, or authority to a subordinate agent.  The temporal extent of an instance of this collection extends throughout the period of time that the delegation of authority holds.")
(comment CyclicCommutativeRelation "The collection #$CyclicCommutativeRelation is a

#$RelationshipType and a spec of #$Relation.  An instance of

#$CyclicCommutativeRelation is a relation which is commutative with

respect to even permutations of its arguments and is anti-commutative

with respect to odd permutations of its arguments.  (See the

accompanying #$cyclistNotes on this constant for the definitions of

even and odd permutations.)  If REL is both a

#$CyclicCommutativeRelation and a #$Predicate and if the term

(REL . ARGS) is true, then (REL . ARGS-PRIME) is true whenever

ARGS-PRIME is an even permutation of ARGS and (#$not (REL .

ARGS-PRIME)) is true whenever ARGS-PRIME is an odd permutation of

ARGS.  If REL is a #$CyclicCommutativeRelation and a

#$Function-Denotational, then the term (REL .  ARGS) #$equals the term

(REL . ARGS-PRIME) whenever ARGS-PRIME is an even permutation of ARGS

and the two are different whenever ARGS-PRIME is an odd permutation of

ARGS.  For example, the predicate `#$counterClockwise' #$isa

#$CyclicCommutativeRelation.  If POINT-1, POINT-2, and POINT-3 are

three points such that (#$counterClockwise POINT-1 POINT-2 POINT-3)

holds, then it is necessary and sufficient that (#$counterClockwise

POINT-3 POINT-1 POINT-2) holds as well.  Furthermore the above hold if

and only if (#$not (#$counterClockwise POINT-2 POINT-1 POINT-3))

holds.")
(comment IndependentIonFn "Where CHEMOBJTYPE is a spec of #$ChemicalObject that admits #$Molecules, #$Ions, and #$MolecularComponents as instances, (#$IndependentIonFn CHEMOBJTYPE) returns the collection of all instances of CHEMOBJTYPE that are independent #$Ions, i.e., radicals with net negative or positive charge, due to having either more or fewer electrons than there are protons in its atomic components. ")
(comment maximalConnectedSubSystems "(#$maximalConnectedSubSystems SYS SUB) means that SUB is a maximal connected subsystem of SYS, i.e., that SUB is an entire connected piece of SYS without other disconnected pieces of SYS.  That is to say, (i) SUB is a connected path system (see the collection #$ConnectedPathSystem), and consequently must have at least one node, say NODE, in it, (ii) SUB is a subsystem of SYS, and (iii) for every connected subsystem SUB1 of SYS containing NODE, SUB1 is a subsystem of SUB.  Thus a maximal connected subsystem SUB of a path system SYS must satisfy the conditions that (a) for each point X in SUB and each point Y in SYS that is not in SUB, X and Y are not connected in SYS, (b) for any nodes X and Y in SUB, for any link LINK in SYS between X and Y, LINK must also be in SUB, and (c) for each point X in SYS, if X is on a link in SYS which is also a link in SUB, then X must also be in SUB.  It follows that if SUB is a maximal connected subsystem of SYS, SUB must be a link-closed subsystem as well as a point-closed subsystem of SYS.  Another consequence is that if SUB is a maximal connected subsystem of SYS, and if X is a point in SUB and is on a loop in SYS, then the loop must also be in SUB.")
(disjointWith PartOfAnHSC Artifact-AnimalCreated)
(comment NaturalLanguageServiceProgram "The collection of NLS programs. The Natural Language Service
is the component of UNIX 
systems that provides facilities for customizing the natural language
formatting for the system. Examples of the types of characteristics
that can be set are language, monetary symbols and delimiters, numeric
delimiters, and time formats.")
(comment Machupo-Virus "A specialization of #$Virus.  #$Machupo-Virus is the type of virus that causes instances of #$Machupo (Bolivian Hemorrhagic Fever).")
(comment flowTypeOfSystem "(flowTypeOfSystem NETFLOWSYS FLOWTYPE) means that, in the #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded NETFLOWSYS, the given recorded numerical value of #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn on each link refers to the maximum feasible rate or maximum capacity (or #$FlowRate) of the #$UnitOfFlowRate FLOWTYPE.  FLOWTYPE could be cars-per-hour or some rate of fluid flow through a pipe, or any other real-world derived number to associate with a link of a NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded.")
(comment Classroom "Class rooms are rooms filled with desks or tables where teaching and learning takes place.")
(disjointWith SomethingToWear DuffelBag)
(comment VulnerableToNetBIOSCachePoisoning "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a
 #$NetBIOSCachePoisoningFault on it.")
(comment ActivityLogBypassFault "A program has this fault if it should log a certain type of activity (for example, failed attempts at the UNIX su command, which allows a user to assume a different identity), and does not -- because a user can exploit some feature of the program to bypass logging, because logging is unwisely turned off by default when the program is installed, or for some other reason.")
(disjointWith FluidTangibleThing CordlikeObject)
(comment LifeJacket "The collection of lifejackets used by people involved in water             sports like yachting, and white water rafting")
(comment LosingControlOfAControlledActor "A specialization of #$Action and #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent. Each instance of this collection is an event in which some #$IntelligentAgent loses control of something it had been previously controlling (this may be its own body). A notable specialization of this collection is #$TransferOfControl.")
(comment MiteBiting "The collection of events in which a #$Mite is the doer of
#$InsectBiting.")
(disjointWith TollBooth SubwayStation)
(comment fiveToThreePrimeDirectionPred "The corresponding predicate of #$FiveToThreePrimeDirectionFn.")
(comment Packet-TCP "The collection of all #$Packet-Internets in which the #$TransmissionControlProtocol is specified as the packet's #$TransportLayerProtocol in the packet's IP header.")
(comment OwnerOccupiedHousehold "Those households where the owner is also the resident.")
(comment NISCachePoisoningFault "An NIS server has this fault if it allows an attacker to add bogus directory objects to the global shared cache, thus allowing the attacker user to specify rogue NIS servers that are under the attacker's control.")
(comment LegalBloodAlcoholLimit "This unit should probably only have a value in a legal-system mt.  It is typically expressed as a percentage.")
(disjointWith MolecularComponentType PersonTypeByCulture)
(disjointWith DeviceRunning SocialGathering)
(comment Dressing "The process of putting clothes on, putting on body or face paint, fixing hair, etc..  See also subevent #$PuttingOnAClothingItem.")
(comment VulnerableToArbitraryFileOverwrite "#$VulnerableToArbitraryFileOverwrite is a specialization of
#$VulnerableToFileOverwrite.  A computer has this vulnerability if
it allows unauthorized users to overwrite any file.")
(comment FeverInfection "An instance of #$InfectionTypeBySymptomology, and a specialization of #$Infection.  Each instance of #$FeverInfection is an infection whose symptoms include prolonged episodes of fever (see the constant #$Fever).")
(comment keRequirementTernaryPreds "(#$keRequirementTernaryPreds COL TER-PRED) means that for every instance INS of COL, there is an expectation that there exist some VALUE-1 and some VALUE-2 such that (TER-PRED INS VALUE-1 VALUE-2) is known in the KB.  Any violation of this kind of expectation essentially represents a violation of KB construction integrity rather than a logical contradiction.")
(comment smellsThat "(#$smellsThat AGENT PROP) means that AGENT perceives, by sense of smell, that PROP is true.")
(comment Gear "A wheel with teeth.")
(comment longitudeMax "(#$longitudeMax OBJ LAT) means that the 

#$SpatialThing-Localized OBJ has its most eastern part(s) geographically 

located at LAT, where LAT denote a longitude line

[#$LongitudeLine] in the \"geographical universe\".")
(comment ClassicalMechanicsTheorist "The collection of all #$ClassicalMechanicsTheorists.")
(comment enzymeComplementOfCell "(#$enzymeComplementOfCell CELL ENZYME-GROUP) matches a cell
to the group (#$Group) of all instances of #$Enzyme that are
physically part (#$internalParts) of CELL in the time frame of the
context of the assertion.  The relationship is functional: the
#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical of #$EnzymeComplementFn.")
(comment StockExchangePhysicalQuarters "A place where stocks and bonds are bought and sold.")
(comment FileDeletingProgram "The collection of programs that are used to delete files from a filesystem.")
(comment keSalientQueryPredForCol "(#$keSalientPredicate COL PRED) means that in any
#$RKF-InteractionContext that sees the #$Microtheory where it is asserted,
PRED is salient when querying about any instance of COL.")
(comment averageDischarge "the amount of water a body of water discharges per unit time.")
(comment exampleSentences-Extended "(#$exampleSentences-Extended PRED SENTENCE) says that SENTENCE is an example usage of PRED as an argument for some instance of #$RuleMacroPredicate that is the arg0 of SENTENCE.")
(comment softwareDownloadLink "(#$softwareDownloadLink PROGRAM URL) means that  PROGRAM (which will often be a computer patch or hotfix of some kind, but may also be a full application program) can be downloaded from the website that URL points to.")
(comment hasInstallationPrivilegesOn "(#$hasInstallationPrivilegesOn ACCOUNT COMPUTER) means that ACCOUNT's privileges on COMPUTER are such that anyone logged in on COMPUTER as ACCOUNT may install files.")
(comment ScubaDiving "#$ScubaDiving is a type of underwater swimming during which the performer uses #$ScubaGear (which includes tanks of compressed air with a regulator to enable underwater breathing).  Because the diver takes an air supply along, he or she can remain underwater for much longer than would otherwise be possible.")
(comment Moai "Giant stone monoliths that dot the coastline of #$EasterIsland.")
(comment pointClosedSubSystems "(#$pointClosedSubSystems SYS SUBSYS) means that the path system SUBSYS is a subsystem of the path system SYS (i.e., (#$subPathSystems SYS SUBSYS) holds) and SUBSYS 'preserves' all points in SYS that are on links in SUBSYS, i.e., if LINK is a link in SUBSYS (and hence is a link in SYS) and X is a point in SYS and is on LINK, then X must be a point in SUBSYS.")
(disjointWith Metal Plastic)
(comment AmishClothing "A set of clothes characteristic of the Amish people - deliberately conservative and drab.")
(comment dividedAmongGroup "This predicate relates a group of intelligent agents to some thing that has been divided up among the group's members. (#$dividedAmongGroup THING GROUP) means THING has been divided or split into two or more shares, portions, or amounts among the group-members of GROUP.  The default assumption is that each portion is at least roughly equal to the others, and that each member of group gets a portion.  THING might be an individual physical object that has been cut or otherwise separated into physical portions (e.g. \"They split the last piece of cake.\"), a group of objects that has been distributed in (roughly) equal numbers among the group members, something of value that has been divided into shares of (roughly) equal value (e.g. \"The crooks divided up the spoils.\"), and so on.")
(comment doRemoteBufferOverflowAttack "(#$doRemoteBufferOverflowAttack AGENT COMPUTER TARGET) means that AGENT performs a buffer overflow attack on TARGET using COMPUTER.  It is \"remote\" in the sense that it exploits a program listening on a port on TARGET.  Cf. #$doLocalBufferOverflowAttack.")
(comment delegate "'(#$delegate DELEGATING AGENT)' means that AGENT is the receiver of the delegated power or function in the #$DelegatingAuthority DELEGATING.")
(comment isolatedNodeInSystem "(#$isolatedNodeInSystem NODE SYSTEM) means that the node NODE in the #$PathSystem SYSTEM is an isolated point in SYSTEM, i.e., NODE is not on any link or loop in SYSTEM.  Note that an isolated point in SYSTEM must be a node in SYSTEM.")
(disjointWith Building PartOfAnHSC)
(comment physicalQuarters "A #$PartPredicate (q.v.) that relates an organization to the building(s) or other #$ConstructionArtifact(s) it occupies. (#$physicalQuarters ORG QUARTERS) means that the ORG is (wholly or partly)  located in QUARTERS, which may consist of one or more buildings, rooms,  offices, etc.  A given organization will have more than one physical quarters  if it has multiple divisions, branches, plants, local offices, or the like in various locations.")
(comment vulnerableToAgent "(#$vulnerableToAgent OBJECT AGENT) means that OBJECT is vulnerable to harm by AGENT. For example, (#$vulnerableToAgent #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland #$IrishRepublicanArmy) states that Britain is vulnerable to the IRA. Note that the type of harm can be made explicit via #$vulnerableTo.")
(comment Machupo "A specialization of #$HemorrhagicFeverInfection.  Instances of #$Machupo are characterized by the gradual onset of malaise, headache, sustained fever progressing to hemorrhagic symptoms, including nose bleed, bloody vomit, and blood in stool or urine.  First noted in Bolivia in 1962, in the village of Magdalena.")
(comment UniqueLinkIDFn "The function #$UniqueLinkIDFn, when applied to a #$Path-Generic LINK and a #$PathSystem SYS in which LINK is a link, as in (#$UniqueLinkIDFn LINK SYS), results in the unique #$IDString by which that link is designated within the #$PathSystem SYS.  Example: if (#$UniqueLinkIDFn Link-9865656 CommNet) = 'Arc2', then this means that the link object Link-9865656 is labeled as 'Arc2' in the #$PathSystem CommNet.  It may often be the case that the internal machine name for the link is the same as that used in the #$PathSystem, but if they are not the same, this function allows reference to the name used in the #$PathSystem for that link.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfReadableKernelMemory "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a
#$ReadableKernelMemoryFault on it.")
(comment BulletinBoardPostOverwriteFault "A bulletin board program has this fault if valid posts to the board can be overwritten and

erased by a malcious user.")
(comment CrossStitchArtifact "The collection of cross stitch artifacts.")
(comment SwimmingTrunks "The collection of swimming trunks. These are usuallly worn by men while swimming")
(comment ailmentContagiousWithContactFromTo "This relation is used to state a measure of the likelihood
of an ailment's being transmitted from one type of organism to
another.  Specifically, (#$ailmentContagiousWithContactFromTo
INFECTION-TYPE TRANSMITTER-TYPE TRANSMITTEE-TYPE LEVEL) means that in
a case where there is a #$PhysicalContactSituation between an instance
of TRANSMITTER-TYPE and an instance of TRANSMITTEE-TYPE at a time
while the instance of TRANSMITTER-TYPE has an infection of type
INFECTION-TYPE, the #$likelihood that the instance of TRANSMITTEE-TYPE
will contract the infection is LEVEL.")
(comment FleaBiting "The collection of events in which a #$Flea is the doer of
#$InsectBiting.")
(disjointWith SubwayStation StorageShed)
(comment Packet-TCP "Packets in which #$TransmissionControlProtocol is specified as the packet's #$TransportLayerProtocol in the packet's header.")
(comment BuildingCluster "An instance of #$BuildingCluster is a group of two or  more buildings whose members are situated #$near each other, and are particularly close to each other relative to any other  buildings in the same general vicinity.  Many building complexes and compounds count as building clusters.  When located in a  city, the buildings in a given cluster are usually all situated  within the same #$CityBlock.  In densely-populated areas  building clusters often occupy one side of an entire  #$BlockOfStreet, and in downtown areas of large cities it is  not uncommon for a cluster of buildings to take up an entire  city block.  For building clusters that are in the form of  rows, see #$BuildingRow.")
(disjointWith ApplyingSomethingToSurface ProjectilePropelling)
(comment BPVI-NorthBluegrassHourMtFn "(#$BPVI-NorthBluegrassHourMtFn HOUR-NUM) is the
#$BPVI-Microtheory which captures the state of the North Bluegrass
forces at hour HOUR-NUM (12, 24, 36, ...) of the Block Party VI
Scenario.")
(disjointWith EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus MolecularComponentType)
(comment PlantProduct "The collection of #$Products that are plants or plant parts (individually or in bulk), or substances derived from plants, which are produced by people or countries and made available for use, sale or exchange.  If an item is a plant or plant part, it is also an instance of #$VegetableMatter.")
(comment BallGown "The collection of #$Gowns worn by women on the most formal occasions.  #$BallGowns typically are floor length.")
(comment VulnerableToArbitraryContentArbitraryFileOverwrite "#$VulnerableToArbitraryContentArbitraryFileOverwrite is a specialization of #$VulnerableToArbitraryFileOverwrite.  A computer has this vulnerability if it allows unauthorized users to overwrite any file with any content.")
(comment HemorrhagicFeverInfection "A specialization of #$FeverInfection.  Instances of #$HemorrhagicFeverInfection are infections characterized by high fever, progressing to internal hemorrhaging and external bleeding from the bodily orifices.")
(disjointWith BarAreaInPrivateResidence (CollectionDifferenceFn Bar-Place BarAreaInPrivateResidence))
(comment ARPTablePoisoningFault "A name server has this fault if it allows its #$AddressResolutionProtocol table to be tampered with, for e.g. by updating it with static entries provided by other hosts (which may send spoofed ARP packets). In this way, an attacker could reroute traffic intended for specific hosts to any other machine on the same subnet as the target. See also #$Arp-TheProgram.")
(comment dataTypeGeneratedByProgram "(#$dataTypeGeneratedByProgram INFO PROGRAM) means that information of the kind INFO is generated by PROGRAM running on computers. ")
(comment Wheel "The collection of all instances of the most general kind of wheel.  Each instance is a disk-shaped thing which can be rotated on an #$Axle which typically goes through the center of its circular cross-section. #$Wheels are found on #$LandTransportationDevices, serving the function of allowing #$RollingOnASurface for such  devices.  Wheels may take the form of #$Gears, parts of a #$Pulley, or may be present instead of ball bearings in places where a device needs to roll against a surface - like on the edges of some #$GarageDoors, which roll in a track when they are raised (#$LiftingAnObject).")
(comment BedfordshireCountyResident "The collection of residents of #$BedfordshireCounty-England.    ")
(comment ControllingAPhysicalDevice "This is the subcollection of actions of #$ControllingSomething in which the #$objectControlled is a #$PhysicalDevice.")
(comment Barn "A large, rural building usually found on farms which is used to house livestock or for storage of farm implements.")
(comment InterArgConstraintPredicate "The collection of  #$ArgConstraintPredicates used to put conditional constraints on polyadic relations in regard to two of their argument-places (or, in a few cases, to put a conditional constraint on relations in regard to two different features of one argument-place).  Each instance of #$InterArgConstraintPredicate specifies, with respect to a given #$Relation, that one of its argument-places (the \"dependent\" one) has a certain feature, contingent upon one (usually a different one) of its argument-place's (the \"independent\" one's) having a certain (possibly different) feature.  The \"features\" in question might be either argument-type specifications (see #$InterArgTypePredicate) or format specifications (see #$InterArgFormatPredicate).  An inter-argument constraint predicate PRED has argument-places for designating the relation and the two features; the identities of the relation's corresponding dependent and independent argument-places might be fixed (as in #$interArgIsa1-2) or might be variable and specified (by number) via two additional argument-places of PRED's (as in #$interArgIsa).")
(comment NationalMonument "A place or construct thought to be significant in the history or cultural life of a particular national entity.  This includes Monuments of national import, but also objects of rare national beauty such as Old Faithful or the Matterhorn etc.")
(comment InstanceTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate "A specialization of #$RuleMacroPredicate and #$TernaryPredicate.  Each instance of #$InstanceTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate relates a collection in its third argument place to an instance of #$Thing in its second argument place via an instance of #$BinaryPredicate in its first argument place.  Examples of instances of this collection include #$relationInstanceExists and #$relationInstanceAll.")
(comment objectRemoved "(#$objectRemoved REMOVING OBJ) means OBJ is removed from its previous
location in the removing event REMOVING.  OBJ may be destroyed during
REMOVING.  REMOVING is #$performedBy some entity other than OBJ.")
(comment CastingAFishingLine "The collection of events in which someone throws a #$Fishhook attached to the end of a #$FishingLine into a #$BodyOfWater. The other end of the #$FishingLine is ordinarily attached to a #$Reel on a #$FishingPole. Instances include only the event where the #$Fishhook is cast out, not those where it is reeled in. Cf. #$Fishing.")
(comment CorrespondingGenQuantAttr-NLAttrFn "(#$CorrespondingGenQuantAttr-NLAttrFn INT) denotes the instance INS of #$NLGenQuantAttribute such that (#$correspondingIntegerExtent INS INT).")
(disjointWith HumanOccupationConstruct Well)
(comment Vest-Bulletproof "The collection of #$Vests that are reinforced so as to afford protection for the wearer against being shot by a gun.")
(comment doLocalBufferOverflowAttack "(#$doLocalBufferOverflowAttack AGENT COMPUTER TARGET) means that AGENT performs a local buffer overflow attack on TARGET using COMPUTER.  It is \"local\" in the sense that it does not exploit a program listening on a port on TARGET, but the program exploited must be running on TARGET. Cf. #$doRemoteBufferOverflowAttack.")
(comment delegatedAuthority "'(#$delegatedAuthority DELEGATING SIT-TYPE ROLE)' means that the authority, power, or function to play ROLE in situations of type SIT-TYPE is delegated to the #$delegate by the #$DelegatingAuthority DELEGATING.")
(comment ConnectedPathSystem "A subcollection of #$PathSystem 

instances of which are \"connected\", as opposed to being in 

separate pieces.  For any distinct points A and B in a connected

path system SYS, there is a path PATH in SYS that both A and B are 

on.  That is, a path system SYS is an instance of 

#$ConnectedPathSystem if and only if, for any distinct points A and 

B in SYS, there is a path PATH in SYS such that 

(#$pathBetweenInSystem PATH A B SYS) holds.  Note that according to 

this definition, a connected path system does not necessarily

contain a link -- a path system containing a single node and no 

links will be a connected path system.  Note also that because of 

the CycL treatment of paths (see #$pathInSystem) and nodes (see 

#$nodeInSystem), there is a path between every two points in 

SYS just in case there is a path between every two nodes in SYS.")
(comment favors-SitType "(#$favors-SitType AGENT SITTYPE) means that AGENT favors or approves of a situation of type SITTYPE.  That is, AGENT wants either (i) a pre-existing situation of type SITTYPE to continue or (ii) a situation of type SITTYPE to come about.  We assume that if an agent favors a particular kind of temporal situation, s/he favors any more general kind of temporal situation.")
(comment SpaceInAHOC "A specialization of both #$Cavity and #$HumanOccupationConstruct.  Each instance of #$SpaceInAHOC is a space found inside some instance of #$HumanOccupationConstruct (HOC).  Instances include all major spaces inside any #$HumanOccupationConstruct, including not only rooms (instances of #$RoomInAConstruction), but also halls, elevator shafts, attics, stairwells, and the spaces inside trains, cars, and airplanes that are designed for human occupation.  Other building parts which are not open spatial regions (e.g., walls, plumbing, etc.) are _not_ included in this collection; cf. #$PartOfBuilding.")
(comment HearingAid-Prescription "The collection of all prescription #$PhysicalDevices that are used to aid in hearing. These require proper testing by a qualified administrator, unlike #$HearingAid-NonPrescription which can be bought over the counter to aid in hearing for things like hunting and bird watching.")
(comment EndoplasmicReticulum "A collection.  Instances are systems of membranes that assist in the transport of materials within a cell.")
(comment initiator "The predicate #$initiator relates a social occurrence to the agent who initiates the occurrence.  (#$initiator EVENT AGENT) means that the agent AGENT deliberately initiates the social occurrence EVENT.  For example, (#$initiator #$BombingOfHiroshima #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica).  If an event has multiple agents initiating it, each will be an initiator of the occurrence.")
(comment RabiesVirus "The virus that that causes the disease #$Rabies (sometimes known as 'Lyssa'), distinctively bulletshaped and belonging to the order Mononegavirales.")
(comment UniqueNodeIDFn "The function #$UniqueNodeIDFn, when applied to a thing NODE and a #$PathSystem SYS in which NODE is a node, as in (#$UniqueNodeIDFn NODE SYS), results in the unique #$IDString by which that node is designated within SYS.  Example: if (#$UniqueNodeIDFn Point-454545 CommNet) = 'B2', then this means that the node object Point-454545 is labeled as 'B2' in the #$PathSystem CommNet.  It may often be the case that the internal machine name for the node is the same as that used in the #$PathSystem, but if they are not the same, this function allows reference to the name used in the #$PathSystem for that node.")
(comment SchoolBuilding-KThrough12 "There are lots of properties that are shared by high school buildings, grammar school buildings, and middle school buildings:  e.g. they have cafeterias, gyms, principals, lockers, etc (KThrough12 means kindergarten through 12th grade).")
(comment wornOn "This predicate is used to describe on what part of an individual's body a particular device or garment is worn.  (#$wornOn ITEM BODYPART) means that ITEM is being worn on the body part BODYPART.  #$wornOn can apply to human or animal wearers, and the items worn can include clothing, jewelry, medical devices, harnesses, carrying devices, wigs--basically, anything which can be attached to or borne upon a body part without intentionally holding or carrying it.  Note that more than one item can be worn on a single body part at a single time -- one can simultaneously wear eyeglasses and a hat on one's head.  Also, a single item can be worn on multiple body parts at once -- overalls, e.g., are worn simultaneously on the shoulders, the torso and the legs.  See #$SomethingToWear for its specializations of things that can be worn.  See #$wearsClothing, which relates entire wearers, rather than body parts, to items worn. See #$wornOn-TypeType for a predicate used to relate types of items worn to the body parts types they are by default worn on.")
(comment degreeOfDifficulty "'(#$degreeOfDifficulty ACTION DEGREE)' means that the doer
of the #$SingleDoerAction ACTION had the degree of difficulty DEGREE
in doing ACTION.  Degree of difficulty is not a subjective evaluation
by the doer, but an objective measure based on the amount of time
spent on ACTION, energy expended, number of mistakes and corrections,
and so on.")
(comment VulnerableToPhysicalPathDisclosure "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$PhysicalPathDisclosureFault on it.")
(comment signifiesTo-Symbol "This is a specialized representation (semiotic) predicate meaning representation due to some arbitrary symbolic convention, such as when the English word 'Parthenon' represents the actual Parthenon, when a roaring lion represents MGM Studios, or when the abstract tetrahedron represent 'Fire' in alchemy. (#$signifiesTo-Symbol THING1 THING2 AGENT) means that, to AGENT, THING1 represents THING2 because of some arbitrary convention or association of the two (that is known to AGENT).  THING1 need not resemble THING2 in any way, nor need it be causally related to THING2.  THING1 acts as an 'arbitrary sign' of THING2.  This is called 'symbolic' representation.  Compare this with the predicates #$signifiesTo-Icon and #$signifiesTo-Index.  It's possible for all three to apply to the same representation.  The spoken word 'Bow-Wow' is not only a conventional 'symbol' of barking but also an 'icon' because it resembles what it represents.  If the basis for the representation is unknown, use the more general predicate #$signifiesTo.")
(comment DestinationIPFn "(#$DestinationIPFn IP_ADDRESS) denotes the collection of #$Packet-Internets whose destination is the machine indicated by IP_ADDRESS.  For example, (#$DestinationIPFn \"234.234.34.2\") denotes the collection of all packets whose destination IP address is 234.234.34.2.")
(comment originInDecompositions "This predicate is used to express the relation between a #$PartiallyTangible and the #$PartiallyTangible it was once a part of.  (#$originInDecompositions ?PART ?WHOLE) means that the thing ?PART comes from ?WHOLE, in the sense that ?PART was once part of ?WHOLE, but is no longer.")
(comment DigitalSignatureBypassFault "A program has a #$DigitalSignatureBypassFault if it is possible for an attacker to make modifications to a digitally signed message file (or multiple message file) that will go unnoticed by the program.")
(comment CarvedArtwork "The collection of all #$ArtObjects carved out of stone, wood, metal, etc.  #$Statues which are assembled from pieces or molded

(e.g. the #$StatueOfLiberty) are not instances of this collection.")
(comment WeightLiftingSuit "The very very low cut leotard-like body suit worn by weight-lifters.")
(comment InstitutionalAccount "An instance of #$AccountType and a specialization of #$Account.  Each instance of #$InstitutionalAccount is an account in which the agent or agents holding the account (see the predicate #$accountHolder) are organizations, rather than persons.")
(comment subPathSystemsProper-WRTNodes "(subPathSystemsProper-WRTNodes SYS SUB_SYS) means that SUB_SYS is a
subsystem of the #$PathSystem SYS and is a proper subsystem with
respect to its nodes. Specifically, (#$subPathSystems SYS SUB_SYS)
holds, and moreover, there is at least one node in SYS which is not
shared by SUB_SYS.")
(disjointWith SubwayStation Tower)
(disjointWith SingleResidenceUnit MultiFamilyHousing)
(disjointWith Cleaning ChangeInUserRights)
(comment GraspingSomethingWithATool "A specialization of #$HandlingADevice and #$HoldingAnObject: a collection of events in which a tool (cf. #$GraspingImplement) is used to grasp some object.")
(comment majorUndertakingsOf "A specialization of #$performedBy. (#$majorUndertakingsOf ACTION AGENT) means that AGENT consciously performed ACTION, and the success and consequence(s) of ACTION are important to AGENT.  As a result, for a sentient AGENT, the failure of ACTION usually results in AGENT feeling negative emotions, and success positive emotions.")
(comment SoftwareObject-Individual "A specialization of #$SoftwareObject.  Each instance of #$SoftwareObject-Individual is either a versioned or unversioned non-series software object, such as a program, a version of a program, a software package, or a library.  Positive examples include Netscape Navigator, Netscape Navigator version 4.76, glibc, and SUNWzip.  Negative examples include Netscape Navigator versions 3 through 4 inclusive, which is an instance of #$SoftwareVersionSeries (q.v.).  #$SoftwareObject-Individual and #$SoftwareVersionSeries are disjoint and they partition #$SoftwareObject.")
(comment PasswordlessLoginFault "#$PasswordlessLoginFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has this fault when it allows unauthorized users to log on to an account on the system without a password.")
(comment MedicalFacilityType "Instances are kinds of medical care facilities.  Some may be organizations, some may be places and some are equipment.")
(disjointWith ClothingOutfit ClothingItem)
(comment SabiaHemorrhagicFeverInfection "A specialization of #$HemorrhagicFeverInfection. Instances of #$SabiaHemorrhagicFeverInfection are characterized by gradual onset of malaise, headache, sustained fever progressing to hemorrhagic symptoms, including nosebleed, bloody vomit, and blood in stool or urine.")
(comment Marxist "The collection of all instances of #$Person who subscribe to the doctrines of #$Marxism.")
(comment EscalationOfHostilities "The increasing of hostilities between two countries.  Usually, this leads to war.")
(disjointWith WallOfAConstruction Fence)
(comment hearsThat "(#$hearsThat AGENT PROP) means that AGENT perceives, by sense of hearing, that PROP is true. #$hearsThat is distinct from the relation that holds between an agent and a proposition that is verbally conveyed to that agent. Consequently, #$hearsThat is not appropriate for representing the sentence 'Jack heard that quarks are not really parts of protons.")
(comment vulnerableToAttackWithType "(#$vulnerableToAttackWithType SOMETHING-EXISTING THING-TYPE) means that in the context of the assertion SOMETHING-EXISTING is vulnerable to an attack in which an instance of THING-TYPE plays an instrumental role. SOMETHING-EXISTING's vulnerablity persists, even if it is never in fact subjected to such an attack.")
(comment likesEvent "(#$likesEvent AGT EVENT) means that the sentient agent AGT likes EVENT in some way --- that is, (#$feelsEmotion AGT (#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn #$Enjoyment)).  The kinds of interactions that produce pleasure depend largely on what kind of thing EVENT is.")
(comment longitudeMin "(#$longitudeMin OBJ LAT) means that the 

#$SpatialThing-Localized OBJ has its most western part(s) geographically 

located at LAT, where LAT denote a longitude line

[#$LongitudeLine] in the \"geographical universe\".")
(comment BodyPainter "The collection of all #$BodyPainters.")
(disjointWith PantsWithBeltLoops PantsWithoutBeltLoops)
(comment PerlFile "#$PerlFile is the collection of #$ComputerFile-AIS whose instances are written in  #$Perl-ProgrammingLanguage.")
(comment VulnerableToSymlinkAttack "A vulnerability of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer
 is #$VulnerableToFileOverwriteSymlinkAttack if it is running a program that allows 
 a user to create symlinks to and either execute commands or overwrite arbitrary files on the computer, including
 commands and files for which the user does not have authorized access.")
(comment keSalientPredicate "(#$keSalientPredicate PRED) says that PRED is salient in any #$RKFInteractionContextMicrotheory that sees  the #$Microtheory where

 (#$keSalientPredicate PRED) is asserted. If a predicate PRED is salient in some RKF context R, then an example assertion involving PRED as the arg 0 will be made available for the SME to clone.")
(comment CardingWool "The collection of all events in which wool is brushed between two 'cards' in preparation for spinning. Also includes events in which wool is similarly prepared using other kinds of devices, such as carding machines.")
(comment AuthenticationProgram-Remote "The collection of 

authentication applications for users and services on a network.")
(comment MetalAlloy "A collection of tangible stuffs; a subcollection of #$Metal.  Each instance of #$MetalAlloy is a metallic stuff which is a homogeneous blend of at least one part of #$UnalloyedMetal with at least one other substance.  #$MetalAlloy is not a subcollection of #$Mixture, because each instance of #$MetalAlloy is defined not only by the amounts and kinds of its #$constituents, but also (unlike a mixture) by the internal structures formed during its creation.  Furthermore, the creation process is typically more complex than #$Mixing.  Common metal alloys include the instances of #$Bronze-Stuff, #$Brass, and #$Steel.  Note that #$GalvanizedMetal is _not_ a subcollection of #$MetalAlloy, because every instance of #$GalvanizedMetal has a coating of some #$Zinc on its surface, and thus (unlike an alloy) the components of galvanized metals are not homogenously distributed throughout.")
(comment Sarong-Skirt "This is the collection of loose #$Skirts, traditionally worn by both men and women in the South Pacific.")
(comment insertShellCommandIntoDataStringForProgram "(#$insertShellCommandIntoDataStringForProgram AGENT PROGRAM) means that AGENT constructs a data string intended for a copy of PROGRAM, and that data string contains a command to spawn a user or root shell on the computer on which the copy of PROGRAM is running.")
(comment awareOfProp "(#$awareOfProp AGENT PROP) means that AGENT is aware of the proposition, PROP, in some way.  Maybe AGENT believes or disbelieves the proposition, is trying to decide on the truth of PROP, is aware that the truth of PROP is at issue, has a positive or negative interest in the proposition being or becoming true, or in some other way has considered PROP.  Normally, a more specific predicate can be used.  See #$hasOpinionAsToTruthOf (and its specializations) and #$interests-Prop (and its specializations).")
(comment PathChain "A specialization of #$List.  Each path chain is a #$List LIST = (X(1) Y(1) X(2) Y(2) ... X(n) Y(n) X(n+1)) satisfying the following conditions: (i) each X(k) is a #$Thing (q.v.) and each Y(k) is a #$Path-Generic (q.v.), i.e., the length of LIST is an odd number greater than 2, every even-numbered position in LIST is a #$Path-Generic, and every odd-numbered item is a #$Thing.  (ii) Each #$Path-Generic in LIST joins the points just before and after it in LIST.  That is to say, (iia) if the kth item PATH in LIST is a #$Path-Simple (q.v.), and if A is the (k-1)th item and B is the (k+1)th item in LIST, then (#$pathBetween PATH A B) holds, and (iib) if the kth item CYCLE is a #$Path-Cyclic (q.v.), and if A is the (k-1)th item and B is the (k+1)th item in LIST, then (#$pointOnCycle A CYCLE) holds and A = B.  Note that the concatenation of all the paths (simple or cyclic) in such a list results in a #$Traversal (q.v.).  For example, letting PATH1 and PATH2 be instances of #$Path-Simple and CYCLE a #$Path-Cyclic, if (#$pathBetween PATH1 A B), (#$pathBetween PATH2 B C) and (#$pointOnCycle C CYCLE), then (#$TheList A PATH1 B PATH2 C CYCLE C) is a #$PathChain.  Note that although each instance of #$PathChain determines a unique instance of #$Traversal that is from X(1) to X(n+1), many different #$PathChains may determine the same #$Traversal.")
(disjointWith SpaceInAHOC Tent)
(comment linuxRedHatManPageString "#$linuxRedHatManPageString relates instances of #$CycSecureFORT to snippets of text from RedHat Linux man pages that document computer programs.  These snippets of text should provide some information about these programs as development of #$CycSecure-TheProgram procedes, and they can be used as inspirations for #$cycSecureDocStrings, but they should not be included in commercial releases of #$CycSecure-TheProgram.")
(comment FollowingAStandardProcedure "The collection of all events in which the performer of the event follows a standarized procedure which the agent knows prior to performing the event.  The performer of some specialization of #$FollowingAStandardProcedure is apt to perform multiple instances of that event type.")
(disjointWith OutOfControlCrowdEvent Teaching)
(comment FTPCommandExecutionFault "An FTP program has this fault if it allows an FTP user to execute certain ftp commands they

are not authorized to perform.")
(comment num-GenQuantRelnToType "(#$num-GenQuantRelnToType RELN SETORCOL1 SETORCOL2 NUM) means that for NUM elements X of SETORCOL1 there is an INST, where (elementOf INST SETORCOL2),  such that (RELN X INST)

holds.")
(comment LymphocyticChoriomeningitisVirus "The virus that causes #$LymphocyticChoriomeningitis.")
(comment LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn "The function #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn, applied to a link within a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded as in (LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn LINK SYSTEM), denotes the given, local 'flow capacity' for LINK alone, regardless of its connections to the rest of SYSTEM.  A 'flow capacity' is a number that is the measure of the maximum capacity of LINK, in isolation from other links, for the flow of something along the link, such as vehicles-per-hour, gallons-per-minute, or some other flow or quantity that conforms to the #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded rules.  (To find out what kind of flow is assumed by a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded, see the predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem.)  Because it is a local measure on LINK, #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn need not take into account flow bottlenecks upstream or downstream from it (for that, see #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn).  Technical note: Every link in a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded has a direction.  If the value of #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn is negative, it refers to minimum flow in the backward direction.  This is unusual.")
(comment Campus "The area consisting of the grounds of an organization such as a university (but not restricted to universities).")
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic CornerOnObject)
(comment VulnerableToElevatedPrivilegePrinting "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$PrintingElevatedPrivilegeFault on it. See also #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedPrinterAccountAccess.")
(comment PersonWithPsychologicalAilment "The collection of #$Persons with a #$PsychologicalAilment. This would include such #$AilmentCondition as #$Depression-PsychologicalCondition and #$Phobias.")
(comment ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-WebServer "A program has this fault if an unauthorized remote user can access an httpd account.")
(comment Religion "The collection of all religions or equivalent sets of beliefs that answer the `big questions' about creation, existence, etc.  Some elements of this are: #$AnimistReligion, #$Catholicism, #$Buddhism, etc.")
(disjointWith HandTool CordlikeObject)
(comment BodySuit "The collection of body suits worn by skiiers, divers etc")
(comment queryForOutcomeExplanation "A #$QueryDedicatedPredicate that is used to query for explanations for causal relations' obtaining between event types.")
(disjointWith PersonalAccount InstitutionalAccount)
(comment TakingCareOfPeople "Includes babysitting, care of the elderly, and nursing a sick friend.")
(comment Restroom "Any room that contains a toilet.  Specs are the various kinds.")
(comment DenyLegitimateUserLoginFault "#$DenyLegitimateUserLoginFault is a fault of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  This sort of fault     can be exploited to prevent legitimate users with accounts from logging in to the system.")
(comment VulnerableToDNSCachePoisoning "A computer has this vulnerability if it running a server
 program that has a #$DNSCachePoisoningFault.")
(comment DestinationPortFn "(#$DestinationPortFn PROTOCOL PORT) denotes the collection of all #$Packet-Internets that list PROTOCOL as their #$TransportLayerProtocol (i.e., TCP or UDP) in the IP header and list PORT as their destination port in the PROTOCOL-specific header.")
(comment OneBathDwelling "The collection of #$SingleResidenceUnits which have exactly one #$FullBath.")
(disjointWith Landing Communicating)
(comment MakingAnAgreement "A specialization of #$CreationEvent, #$CooperationEvent and #$Communicating.  Each instance of #$MakingAnAgreement is an event in which two or more agents specify the terms of an agreement (see the collection #$Agreement) to which they will be agreeing parties (see the predicate #$agreeingAgents), and subsequently enter into that agreement.  Specializations of #$MakingAnAgreement include  #$EngagementEventPart-BecomingEngaged, #$EmployeeHiring, #$DeclaringCeaseFire, and #$MakingAReservation. See also #$BreakingAnAgreement.")
(disjointWith DeviceRunning ChangeInUserRights)
(comment ClothingOutfit "A specialization of both #$Clothing-Generic and #$Group.  Each instance of #$ClothingOutfit is a group of clothing items (see the collection #$ClothingItem) that are intended to be worn together.  An instance of #$ClothingOutfit may include some accessories, as well as garments. The different parts of an instance of #$ClothingOutfit are often sold together, rather than separately.  Specializations of #$ClothingOutfit include #$MensSuit, #$Uniform, and #$Bikini.")
(comment ComputerFile-CW "#$ComputerFile-CW is a collection of conceptual works. Each instance of #$ComputerFile-CW is abstract information that was created at a particular time to be stored on a computer or on media that is readable by a computer.  Commonly, files are either programs or data or both.  Instances of this collection have associated #$ComputerFile-AISes and #$fileCopies.  A physical instantiation of a #$ComputerFile-CW is a #$ComputerFileCopy which is an #$InformationBearingThing.  Notable specializations include #$ComputerProgram-CW and #$FileDirectory.")
(comment Abbr-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify an abbreviation.")
(comment SabiaVirus "A specialization of #$Virus.  #$SabiaVirus is a type of virus responsible for causing cases of #$SabiaHemorrhagicFeverInfection.")
(comment UnfairlyPrejudicedPerson "The collection of instances of 

#$Person who have one or more #$Prejudices.")
(comment DisputeEvent "A collection of events with multiple participants.  In each #$DisputeEvent,  some participants seek to achieve states of affairs that other participants seek to prevent.  Disputes may or may not get settled.  Settlement of a dispute may be by fighting, by competition, by using a mediator or court, by chance, by mutual reasoning, etc.")
(disjointWith WallOfAConstruction Breakwater)
(comment findsInPlace "A finds some thing B in location C. Cf. #$finds.")
(disjointWith Shaft CordlikeObject)
(comment HumanConsumer "The collection of all human consumers.  A consumer is a #$Person that buys goods and services for personal use, and not for resale or to use in the production of other goods.  See also #$AdultConsumer.")
(comment ThreeToFivePrimeDirectionFn "Where STRAND is a 'straightened' #$PolynucleotideStrand, (#$ThreeToFivePrimeDirectionFn STRAND) returns the #$UnitVector-Precise that points from the (#$ThreePrimeEndFn STRAND) to the (#$FivePrimeEndFn STRAND).  See also #$NucleotideChain-FivePrimeEnd, #$NucleotideChain-ThreePrimeEnd, FiveToThreePrimeDirection.")
(comment ParkingGarage "Large buildings in which many automobiles can be parked, usually for a fee.  May be public or restricted use.  May stand alone or be incorporated into a larger building.  Usually do not have closed-in sides, A/C or heat.  For Garages in Modern Houses, see #$Garage-Household.")
(disjointWith ShortSleeveShirt LongSleeveShirt)
(comment AwkFile "#$AwkFile is the collection of #$ComputerFile-AIS whose instances are written in  #$Awk-ProgrammingLanguage.")
(comment FileCopyingProgram "The collection of programs that copy a file in one location to a file in another location.")
(comment MountingOntoSurface "A collection of events. In each #$MountingOntoSurface event, a physical object is attached to a surface using physical connector(s).  The connector(s) may be an adhesive substance or a fastener.  Important subcollections of this are #$MountingOntoSurface, #$ApplyingAdhesiveBackedMaterialToSurface, and #$SpreadingSheetOntoSurface.")
(comment SmokingACigarette "The collection of all actions of #$Smoking a #$Cigarette.")
(comment ContentFilteringProgram "The collection of programs designed to prevent internet browser users from visiting sites with certain types of content.")
(comment PresidentOfRussia "The collection of persons who hold, or have held,

the office of President in Russia.")
(disjointWith SignTheDisplay Token-Physical)
(comment LongUnderwear "The collection of #$Underwear that typically cover all of the body except the head and neck, hands, and feet.  They are worn under the clothes for warmth.")
(comment repeatPrecedingActionNTimes "(#$repeatPrecedingActionNTimes AGENT TIMES) means that AGENT repeats the immediately preceeding action in a plan TIMES many times.  See also #$repeatPrecedingActionAtIntervalNTimes")
(comment PathToFn "An instance of #$BinaryFunction.  For each instance SYS of #$DirectedPathSystem, and for each path PATH in SYS, (#$PathToFn PATH SYS) is 'the ending point' of PATH, i.e., the unique point END-POINT in SYS such that (#$pathFromToInSystem PATH START-POINT END-POINT SYS) holds for some point START-POINT in SYS (where START-POINT is the unique point in SYS such that (#$PathFromFn PATH SYS) = START-POINT).")
(comment containsCavityInteriorRegion "(#$containsCavityInteriorRegion OBJECT CAVITY) means that #$PartiallyTangible OBJECT has #$CavityInteriorRegion CAVITY as a hole or cavity.")
(comment AssertionGeneratingRKFTool "The collection of instances of #$RKFTool that can be used to enter assertions into a #$CycKB.")
(comment vulnerableToAgentType "(#$vulnerableToAgentType OBJECT AGENT-TYPE) means that OBJECT is vulnerable to a threat of the type typically done by AGENT-TYPE. For example, (#$vulnerableToAgentType #$Israel #$TerroristAgent) states that Israel is vulnerable to the attacks done by terrorists. Note that the type of harm can be made explicit via #$vulnerableToType.")
(comment AutomobileTailLight "The red or yellow  lights located at the rear of a car and used for visibility at night.")
(comment Gift "The collection of all #$SomethingExistings that are #$objectGiven in a #$GiftGiving event.")
(comment DefaultConfigurationFault "A very general #$ProgramFaultAttribute used, in general, to collect more
 specific instances of #$ProgramFaultAttribute that, because of their
 default configurations, allow for some sort of exploitation.")
(comment num-GenQuantRelnFromType "(#$num-GenQuantRelnFromType RELN SETORCOL1 SETORCOL2 NUM) means that for NUM elements X of SETORCOL2 there is an INST, where (elementOf INST SETORCOL1),  such that (RELN INST X)

holds.")
(comment LymphocyticChoriomeningitis "A viral infection presenting marked diversity of manifestations, from flu-like to meningitis. Recovery may be prolonged.")
(comment SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn "The function #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn, applied to a link and the #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded of which it is a part, as in (SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn LINK SYSTEM), denotes the net (usally calculated) 'flow capacity' for LINK taking into account the effects of its connections to the rest of SYSTEM.  Here the 'flow capacity' is a number that is the measure of the maximum capacity of LINK, as restricted by any connections to other links, for the flow of something along the link, such as vehicles-per-hour, gallons-per-minute, or some other flow or quantity that conforms to the #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded rules.  (To find out what kind of flow is assumed by a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded, see the predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem.)  Because it is a 'situated' or 'context-dependent' measure on LINK, it must take into account any flow bottlenecks upstream or downstream from it (for the local total capacity of the link in isolation, see #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn). Technical notes: The value of #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn is often calculated from the #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn values of all the links in the #$PathSystem using an algorithm like the Ford-Fulkerson algorithm. Every link in a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded has a direction.  If the value of #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn is negative, it refers to minimum flow in the backward direction.  This is unusual.")
(comment DiningRoom-Home "dining rooms found in homes, with dining room tables, sometimes china cabinets, etc.")
(comment Clothing-Generic "A specialization of #$SomethingToWear.  Each instance of #$Clothing-Generic is something that a person wears as a protective and/or decorative covering or ornament.  Instances of #$Clothing-Generic are usually made of flexible materials, such as cloth, leather, or yarn.  Important specializations of #$Clothing-Generic include #$ClothingOutfit and #$ClothingItem.")
(comment VulnerableToTCPChorusing "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$TCPChorusingFault on it.")
(comment IPDisclosureFault "A program has this fault if a user can obtain the IP addresses of machines despite the fact that the program is supposed to prevent users from getting that information.")
(comment claims "This predicate relates an agent to a proposition that s/he has asserted or otherwise publicly endorsed.  (#$claims AGENT SENT) means that AGENT claims that the proposition PROP expressed by SENT is true.  Typically, AGENT wants others to believe PROP and will take action to convince others that it is true.  Note that AGENT need not believe PROP or know it to be true.  For example, an advertiser might knowingly make false or exaggerated claims about his product in order to get people to buy it.")
(comment Bead "The collection of beads. Typically, a bead is small and has a hole through which a string may be passed. Beads are often used as parts of jewelry, and are sometimes sewn onto clothing or accessories like purses. Beads are usually ball-shaped or tube-shaped.")
(comment TennisShorts "The collection of Tennis shorts")
(comment subPathSystemsProper-WRTLinks "(subPathSystemsProper-WRTLinks SYS SUB_SYS) means that SUB_SYS is a subsystem of the #$PathSystem SYS and is a proper subsystem with respect to its links. Specifically, (#$subPathSystems SYS SUB_SYS) holds, and moreover, there is at least one link in SYS which is not shared by SUB_SYS.")
(disjointWith PlumbingFixture RoofOfAConstruction)
(comment JavascriptSurveillanceFault "A web server program has this fault if it permits JavaScript programs to monitor a user's browser activities beyond the security context of the page with which the program was downloaded, possibly transmitting information back to its web server.")
(comment IntrusionDetectionProgram "The collection of programs designed to monitor networks and scan for signs of break-ins.")
(disjointWith ProjectilePropelling Mounting-Installing)
(comment needs-Generic "This is a generic \"needs\" predicate that generalizes

over a fairly diverse range of predicates having to do with an

agent's needing something in order to attain some goal or other.

In most cases, one of these more specialized predicates should be 

used instead of #$needs-Generic itself.  The sense of \"needs\" 

intended here includes everything from moderate practical convenience 

to matters of life and death, so as to cover all sorts of situations 

in which one might say that \"So-and-so _needs_ such-and-such\", 

where this need is currently unfulfilled (e.g. the agent So-and-so 

does not, at least yet, have the thing such-and-such).

(#$needs-Generic AGENT THING) means that AGENT has a need with 

respect to THING, where AGENT's satisfying that need is -- 

given AGENT's current circumstances -- practically necessary for 

AGENT's achieving or furthering some goal (see #$goals) that s/he 

has.  By \"practically necessary\" we mean that, if this need of 

AGENT's goes unsatisfied, then AGENT is unlikely to achieve or 

further that goal, at least not without being significantly delayed 

or otherwise inconvenienced.  For example, suppose I am in the habit 

of driving several miles to work each morning in my (only) car.  

Given those circumstances, I might well say that I need my car to 

get to work tomorrow.  Now, if I were unexpectedly to be denied 

access to my car tomorrow (e.g. if it were stolen overnight), I 

could probably still make it to work (by taking a bus, walking, 

or whatever), but getting there would involve extra hassling and 

take longer than usual.  Of course, it's _conceivable_ that a Good 

Samaritan might happen by and kindly offer to drive me directly to 

work; but the likelihood of something like that occurring is poor.  

Thus, all things considered, the claim that -- in a practical, 

everyday sense of \"need\" -- I need my car to get to work tomorrow seems 

legitimate.  Second example: Suppose I've just ingested a fatal 

dose of poison X, whose only (known or unknown) antedote is substance 

Y.  I need a dose of antedote Y (to further my goal of continuing to 

live); if I don't get it I'll die -- period.  It is this broad sense of 

the word \"need\" -- ranging from moderate practical convenience to 

requirements for something's continued existence-- that the various specializations of #$needs-Generic 

(each with respect to its own particular domain of application) are 

intended to represent.  See also #$needsFor and #$satisfiesNeed.")
(comment valueOfOwnersEquity "The difference between assets and liabilities.  May be negative.")
(comment BreakingAnAgreement "A specialization of #$SocialOccurrence and #$DestructionEvent: the collection of events in which one of the #$agreeingAgents to an #$Agreement does something which goes against the terms of that agreement. Examples would include a country defying the provisions of some treaty it has signed; a tenant breaking a lease agreement by moving out before the lease term has expired; a hotel refusing to honor a reservation a customer had made; and so on. See also #$MakingAnAgreement.")
(comment BoundedDirectedAcyclicGraph "The collection of all those #$DirectedAcyclicGraphs in each of which there is only a single source node and a single sink node. This is the intersection of #$DirectedAcyclicGraph and #$BoundedDirectedPathSystem.  See #$sourceNodeInSystem and #$sinkNodeInSystem.")
(comment StationarySign "The collection of all signs [#$SignTheDisplay] without moving parts. Each instance of #$SignTheDisplay is an object typically posted where people can see it so that they can obtain information from it. Instances of #$StationarySign do not have flashing lights, moving images, or physically moving parts.")
(disjointWith BraLikeGarment OverGarment)
(comment NetBIOSCachePoisoningFault "Similar to a #$DNSCachePoisoningFault.  An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if it mishandles incoming datagrams in such a way that it is possible to plant false NetBIOS name/IP address information in the NetBIOS cache of the server TARGET_SERVER running the faulty program.  A malicious remote attacker who controlled an SMB/NetBIOS server MAL_SERVER with IP address XXXX could exploit the #$NetBIOSCachePoisoningFault of the OS on TARGET_SERVER by sending a specially-formed NetBIOS datagram to TARGET_SERVER.  The NetBIOS datagram header contains a  source and destination NetBIOS name, as well as a source IP  address, in addition to the IP headers.  Upon receiving a NetBIOS packet, an #$OperatingSystem with this fault will blindly (i.e., without verifying the authenticity of the source) extract the source NetBIOS name/IP address information from the packet and store it in the NetBIOS cache. If an attakcer could discover a NetBIOS name NAME used by some machine COMP on TARGET_SERVER's network, a remote attacker could redirect all NetBIOS datagrams intended for COMP to MAL_SERVER.")
(comment PETComputer "The Commodore #$PETComputer was the first computer introduced by #$CommodoreBusinessMachines.  The #$PETComputer was introduced in 1977. It was one of the most 'complete' portable all-in one systems for its time.")
(comment Address-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify an address.")
(comment CattleRanch "A #$LivestockFarm whose main activity is raising cattle.")
(comment RevengeAction "The collection of revengeful actions.")
(disjointWith WallOfAConstruction Gate)
(comment containsInstructionsForMakingType "(#$containsInstructionsForMakingType IBT TYPE) means that IBT contains instructions for making an instance of TYPE. For example, (#$containsInstructionsForMakingType Recipe539 #$BlackForestCake) means that Recipe539 contains instructions for making black forrest cake. (But use #$recipeCopyFor to relate a #$RecipeCopy to the relevant type.)")
(comment relyOnAgent "(#$relyOnAgent AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT1 relies on activities performed by AGENT2 for a significant part of AGENT1's normal activities.  See #$relyOnType and #$relyOnObject.")
(comment HandGrip "The part of a handlebar which one actually grasps.  This part is often made of some soft rubber or plastic.")
(comment LaundryRoom "A room where clothing is cleaned.  Usually contains a washing machine and a dryer.")
(disjointWith SleevelessShirt LongSleeveShirt)
(comment PrintingProgram "The collection of programs that send data to be printed to a printer.")
(comment Loading "Placing objects or materials into or onto a container.")
(comment SmokingAPipe "The collection of all actions of #$Smoking a #$Pipe-SmokingDevice.")
(comment RemoteApplicationAdministrationProgram "The collection of programs that are used for remote maintenance of larger programs.  They do not allow the user to change major settings of the computer itself, however.")
(comment DeviceTypeByInternalPowerSource "This covering collection on #$SelfPoweredDevice facets the collection by 'power source', where this is considered to be, loosely speaking, a type of #$PhysicalDevice such that instances are considered to be sources of the motive power of instances of the collection. ")
(comment Professional-Adult "A specialization of both #$HumanAdult and #$PersonWithOccupation.  A person is an instance of #$Professional-Adult just in case he or she is an adult and a professional.")
(comment underlyingGraph "(#$underlyingGraph RED SYS) means that (i) every node in SYS is a node in RED, (ii) every point in RED is a node in RED (and hence a node in SYS), and (iii) (#$linkClosedSubSystems SYS RED) holds. It is easy to see that when (#$underlyingGraph RED SYS) holds, RED must be an instance of #$Multigraph.  But RED is not only a multi-graph, it is THE multi-graph that underlies the path system SYS, i.e., the only difference between SYS and RED is that SYS is obtainable by adding to RED some points that are on a link in RED between the end-nodes.")
(comment DeviceRunning "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent.  Each instance of #$DeviceRunning is an event in which some device is running.  This collection includes events which are complete cycles of a device's normal function (see the specialization #$SingleCompleteRunOfADevice), as well as random time slices (see the predicate #$timeSlices) of such events.  Examples of #$DeviceRunning include instances of the collections #$AirplaneTakeOff, #$SkateBoarding, and #$OffRoadMotorcycleRiding.  Note that an instance of #$DeviceRunning does not need to be a continuous event.  Examples of discontinuous instances of #$DeviceRunning include the following: the event of all the ignition phases of the firing of a particular automobile's engine during November of 1996; the event in which a  particular TV was on and showing a commercial in the year 2001.")
(comment MensUnderpants "This is the collection of #$Underpants worn by men.")
(comment exploitFaultOfProgramOnSystem "(#$exploitFaultOfProgramOnSystem AGENT FAULT PROGRAM SYSTEM) means that AGENT exploits the FAULT of PROGRAM when PROGRAM is running on SYSTEM.")
(comment SetOfLinksAtNodeFn "A function from path-systems and nodes in those path-systems to set-or-collections of links in those systems. (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn NODE SYS) is the #$SetOrCollection (q.v.) of all links in the #$PathSystem SYS that NODE is on, i.e., the set-or-collection of all links LINK in SYS such that (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK NODE OTHER-NODE SYS) holds for some OTHER-NODE.  Note that if SYS is a #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem (q.v.) and NODE is a node in SYS, then (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn NODE SYS) equals the union of (#$InwardLinkSetFn NODE SYS) and (#$OutwardLinkSetFn NODE SYS) (these two set-or-collections will overlap if there are any 'bidirected' links at that node).  Note also that (#$SetOfLinksAtNodeFn NODE SYS) = #$TheEmptySet if there is no link in SYS that is between NODE and another node in SYS.  Loops, if any, are not included as links.")
(comment objectFoundByInspection "(#$objectFoundByInspection INSPECTING OBJ) means that OBJ is a #$SomethingExisting whose existence is only discovered by the #$performedBy of INSPECTING during the course of INSPECTING and because of it.  Discovery of something like OBJ may or may not have been the purpose for which INSPECTING was being carried out.")
(disjointWith SpaceInAHOC Stadium)
(comment SupernaturalBeing "The collection of all supernatural beings, including gods, angels, devils, demons, ghosts, spirits, banshees, fairies, elves, and woodland sprites (e.g. the mischievous Puck).  Instances of #$SupernaturalBeing might be immortal or mortal, good or evil, intangible or partially tangible.")
(disjointWith PhysicalTransformationEvent Communicating)
(comment DefaultAllowsAnonymousFTPFault "Normally, anonymous ftp is used to allow people on a network who do not have an account on your machine to deposit or retrieve files from a directory reserved for that purpose. Certain security risks are inherent in it since it potentially gives system access to everyone on the network. An ftp program which by default allows for anonymous ftp has a #$DefaultAllowsAnonymousFTPFault.")
(comment Crown "The collection of ornamental headgear made of gold or other precious metal, typically worn by royalty.")
(comment LoupingIllVirus "The virus that causes the disease #$Louping-Ill.")
(comment FlowRateOnLinkFn "The function #$FlowRateOnLinkFn applied to a thing and to the #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded of which it is a link, as in (#$FlowRateOnLinkFn LINK SYSTEM), denotes the actual flow rate occuring across that link (often varying with time), such as the actual vehicles-per-hour, gallons-per-minute, or any other flow or quantity that conforms to the rules for #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded.  This function results in the actual value of the flow along the link, not to the flow capacity of the link within the system nor to the flow capacity the link would have if isolated from the rest of the system -- for these see #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn and #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn, respectively.  The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded.")
(comment DressingRoom "rooms found in theatres or homes where one gets dressed; usually contains mirrors, make-up lights, costumes or clothing, etc.  This also can mean the dressing rooms found in clothing stores.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice Clothing-Generic)
(comment typeDegreeOfDifficulty "'(#$typeDegreeOfDifficulty AGT-TYPE ACT-TYPE DEGREE)' means
that the type of agent AGT-TYPE typically has the degree of difficulty
DEGREE doing actions of type ACT-TYPE.")
(comment VulnerableToKerberosIDSpoofing "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$KerberosIDSpoofingFault on it.")
(comment ContainerArtifact "#$ContainerArtifact is a specialization of #$Container, #$PhysicalDevice, and #$Artifact-NonAgentive. Each instance of #$ContainerArtifact is an object whose primary function (or one of whose main functions) is to be a container.  Instances of #$ContainerArtifact include storage containers for books, office records, food, clothing, tools, and materials; containers for transporting the same; passenger compartments of various kinds of vehicles; and artificial constructs for housing humans and animals.  Specializations include #$Crib, #$Sandbox, #$OfficeSpace, and #$Coffin.")
(comment Sequin "The collection of small, shiny, usually round objects used as decoration on clothing and other items.")
(comment BaseballJersey "The collection of shirts normally worn by players in organized baseball games.")
(comment Gene-GIS "A specialization of
#$GeneticInformationStructure. Each instance of #$Gene-GIS is a
#$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS that is the abstract structure of a gene. Each
instance GENE-GIS of #$Gene-GIS is in the relation
#$structureEncodesGenInfo with an instance of #$GeneticInformation
GENE-INFO, i.e. (structureEncodesGenInfo GENE-GIS GENE-INFO) and
GENE-GIS is instantiated in a #$Gene-HereditaryUnit.")
(disjointWith TwoDimensionalShapeType ThreeDimensionalShapeType)
(comment keCommonQueryExampleReln "This relation is a 'query' analog of

#$examplePredSentences.  It is used to specify, for a given #$Predicate, examples that typify frequently asked questions (FAQs) that

users may reasonably be expected to have with regard to that predicate.")
(disjointWith RoofOfAConstruction FlowControlStructure)
(comment ServeWarrant "The collection of actions in which an agent of the court serves any kind of warrant [#$Warrant-Writ] upon a legal person [#$LegalAgent].")
(comment VulnerabilityScannerProgram "The collection of programs designed to scan networks for instances of #$ComputerVulnerability that could be exploited.")
(comment packetsOfTypeFromReachTarget "(#$packetsOfTypeFromReachTarget PACKET_TYPE FROM_COMP TO_COMP) means that #$Packet-Networks of the type PACKET_TYPE, sent from FROM_COMP, will (barring some sort of snafu) reach TO_COMP.  More precisely, it means that either (a) there is no #$Firewall-Network mediating remote connections between FROM_COMP and TO_COMP, or (b) there is a #$Firewall-Network between the two computers, but it does not filter packets of PACKET_TYPE from FROM_COMP to TO_COMP.")
(disjointWith CuttingSomething ProjectilePropelling)
(comment valueOfAccountsReceivable "The summation of the balance of all receivable accounts held by the agent.  The balance of a recievable account is the sum of all active recievables (unpaid obligations that you still think will be paid) due the agent by the account debtor less any outstanding overpayment")
(comment SetOfLoopsAtNodeFn "A function that, when applied to a #$PathSystem SYS and a node X in SYS as in (#$SetOfLoopsAtNodeFn X SYS), returns the set of all loops in SYS that X is on, i.e., the set of all loops LOOP in SYS such that (#$pointOnCycle X LOOP).  (A loop in SYS is a #$Path-Cyclic that goes from a node immediately back to the same node, see #$loopInSystem.)  Note that (#$SetOfLoopsAtNodeFn X SYS) = #$TheEmptySet if there is no loop in SYS that X is on.")
(disjointWith DeviceRunning OutOfControlCrowdEvent)
(disjointWith Underwear OverGarment)
(comment MechanicalFatigue "How fatigued an object is.")
(comment NISDomainRestrictionBypassFault "An NIS client has this fault if it 
 will accept ypset requests from hosts outside its NIS domain.")
(comment Commodore128 "A brand of personal computer popular in the 1980s.")
(disjointWith WallOfAConstruction LawnEdging)
(comment Handle "A collection of devices.  Each instance of #$Handle is a part (it might be a detachable part, it might be a specially shaped region of a thing) of another object, of which it is the handle.  Each instance of #$Handle is a physical device which is designed to be grasped with the human hand in such a way that the grasper can more easily control his or her orientation to the object that the handle is attached to.  In most cases, handles are intended to help in manipulating the object, by allowing the user to move the object in a more controlled way than s/he could without the handle.  Handles are found on cookware, suitcases, crutches, doors, hand-held and hand-powered tools -- in fact, on most artifacts that humans need to manipulate frequently and which are bigger and heavier than a dinner plate or a book.  In other, less common cases, handles are provided on objects (a) to facilitate moving oneself around the object (rather than vice versa), e.g., handles on a pommel horse or other exercise equipment, or on a ladder, in a spacecraft, or pounded into a rock face; or (b) for holding oneself stationary with respect to some moving object, e.g., handles inside a subway car.  Note that handles are sometimes used to perform other functions, such as hanging one's dry cleaning from the little handle above the rear door of a passenger car.")
(comment FiveToThreePrimeDirectionFn "Where STRAND is a 'straightened' #$PolynucleotideStrand, (#$FiveToThreePrimeDirectionFn STRAND) returns the #$UnitVector-Precise that points from the (#$FivePrimeEndFn STRAND) to the (#$ThreePrimeEndFn STRAND).  See also #$NucleotideChain-FivePrimeEnd, #$NucleotideChain-ThreePrimeEnd, FiveToThreePrimeDirection.")
(comment genericPathway-Complete "For those transfers in which the item transferred follows some spatial path, this predicate allows representation of the relation between the transfer and the single path followed by the item in that transfer.  More formally, (#$genericPathway-Complete TRANS PATH) means that the route of the instance TRANS of #$GeneralizedTransfer is spatial and the #$transferredThing follows some (perhaps improper) part of the instance PATH of #$Path-Spatial throughout all of TRANS.  Thus, any #$genericPathway-Complete of an instance TRANS of #$GeneralizedTransfer connects the \"starting\" and \"stopping\" points, the #$from-Generic and the #$to-Generic, of TRANS; if this is the complete extent of the path, use the more specific #$genericPathway-Exact.  Note that the instance PATH of #$Path-Spatial may, and often will, extend beyond these \"starting\" and \"stopping\" points.  See also #$infoPathway-Complete and #$motionPathway-Complete;  it is usually better to use one of these more specific predicates.  Another related predicate is #$genericPathway-Partial.")
(disjointWith SleevelessShirt ShortSleeveShirt)
(comment TelnetClientProgram "#$TelnetClientProgram is the collection of telnet software that can be used to establish network connections with machines running #$TelnetServerPrograms.")
(disjointWith TypeInstanceTernaryRuleMacroPredicate InstanceTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate)
(comment InstallingFn "A function, which, when applied to a type of tangible object, denotes the set of actions in which objects of that type are installed (placed somewhat permanently into the place where they will be used.)")
(comment MakingALocalCall "A collection of events. In each instance of MakingALocalCall, the caller uses a Telephone to call a number for which no long-distance charges apply.")
(comment RegistryRestrictionBypassFault "A registry protection program has this fault if it allows users to circumvent restrictions on registry access.")
(comment serialNumber "A binary predicate that relates instances of physical devices to serial numbers.  (#$serialNumber DEVICE STRING) means that the manufacturer of DEVICE has assigned the serial number STRING to DEVICE.")
(comment Underpants "The collection of #$Underwear, for either men or women, that is worn on the lower part of the body, with separate openings for each #$Leg.")
(comment VulnerableToCrossSiteScriptingAttack "A computer is #$VulnerableToCrossSiteScriptingAttack if it
is running a program that has a #$CrossSiteScriptingFault.  Users of
this computer may unintentionally execute scripts written by an
attacker when they follow hyperlinks in web pages, mail messages,
or newsgroup postings.")
(comment decryptFile "(#$decryptFile AGENT FILE) means that AGENT succesfully decrypts FILE.  This action may involve AGENT deploying an instance of #$DecryptionProgram or #$PasswordCrackingProgram.")
(comment SpaceOccupiedByFn "This function can be used to denote the exact spatial region occupied

by some object.

(#$SpaceOccupiedByFn OBJECT) denotes all and only the piece

of the embedding space in which OBJECT is located that

OBJECT occupies.  Moreover, this function denotes a piece

of intangible space (see its #$resultIsa, #$SpaceRegion.)

Note that this function does not require or make reference to any

temporal parameter; thus it can be used in contexts concerning

purely spatial situations, abstract as well as empirical.

Also see the corresponding predicate, #$exactlyLocatedAt-Spatial.")
(comment motionPathway-Exact "(#$motionPathway-Exact MOVE PATH) indicates that the trajectory or trajectories travelled by one or more objects during a movement event is the spatial path PATH.  More formally, if MOVE is an instance of #$Translation-SingleTrajectory, (motionPathway-Complete MOVE PATH) means that the instance PATH of #$Path-Spatial is the entire instance of #$Trajectory along which the objects moving (see #$objectMoving) travel in MOVE.  Note that there can be at most one #$motionPathway-Complete if MOVE is an instance of #$Translation-SingleTrajectory.  If MOVE is an instance of #$Translation-MultiTrajectory, (#$motionPathway-Exact MOVE PATH) means that the instance PATH of #$Path-Spatial is the entire instance of #$Trajectory along which at least one of the objects moving in MOVE travels.  In this case, more than one #$motionPathway-Complete may exist.  (Note that the instance of #$Traversal determined by the trajectory-Complete need not occupy the whole length of PATH.) To explain this predicate somewhat differently, any #$motionPathway-Complete of an instance of #$Movement-TranslationEvent connects the starting and stopping points (the fromLocation and toLocation) of the whole trajectory of at least one object in the movement event (See also #$pathConnects).  Note that PATH may be a marked or unmarked instance of #$Path-Spatial.  See also #$trajectoryPassesThrough and #$motionPathway-Complete.")
(disjointWith SingleResidenceUnit ApartmentBuilding)
(comment CreatingANewConceptInUIA "The collection of events in which a UIA user is able to

create new terms and add them to the interaction context in which they

are working. This process can occur singly, as when a user accesses

the #$CycConceptCreator from the left pane of the UIA interface. In

addition to direct access, the #$CycConceptCreator is called whenever a

user uses an unfamiliar term and indicates they would like to describe

it at that time. For example, if a user has typed in a sentence in the

text window containing a term unfamiliar to Cyc, the Sentence Reader

will highlight the term and let the user know it is not recognized. If

the user clicks [Describe Now], the Sentence Reader calls up the

Concept Creator to create the term.")
(comment UnauthorizedFileDownloadFault "A client program has an #$UnauthorizedFileDownloadFault if it

is possible for a remote user to cause files to be downloaded on the client's computer without the consent of the user.")
(comment AFew-NLAttr "The attribute value carried by utterances of the form 'a few XXX.'")
(comment Louping-Ill "A paralytic disease of sheep. It can also affect humans, in which case it causes symptoms ranging from mild fever and headache to high fever, stupor, tremors and coma. 4 to 10 days after apparent recovery, there is a return of fever with encephalitis.")
(comment SituatedFlowCapacityInToNodeFn "The function #$SituatedFlowCapacityInToNodeFn, applied to some thing and to a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded in which it is a node, as in (#$SituatedFlowCapacityInToNodeFn NODE FLOWSYS), denotes the net maximum inward flow to NODE that can possibly flow into NODE, given the complete FLOWSYS in which every link has a value of #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn.  The result is the total of the #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn values on all the links going into that node from other nodes (it excludes all of the node's outward links). Note: The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used to find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded. See also #$SituatedFlowCapacityOutFromNodeFn.")
(comment MovieProjectionRoom "The room from which the movie is projected in a movie theatre.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice ProtectiveAttire)
(comment DisappearingFromSight "This is the collection of events in which an object becomes hidden from an animal's sight, either by becoming too distant to be seen, or by the animal's line of sight becoming blocked by another object.  An animal may not actually see the object before it disappears, but it was visible in the context.")
(comment VulnerableToPortDenialOfService "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$PortDenialOfServiceFault on it.")
(comment TimeZone "A region extending from the north pole(?) to the south pole(?) within which standard time is uniform.  The eastern adjacent time zone is one hour ahead. The western adjacent time zone is one hour behind.")
(comment SimpleSegmentOfPath "The collection of all segments of #$Path-Generics each of which has no path junctions between its ends.  The two ends of such a segment may or may not coincide at the same location (i.e. a #$SimpleSegmentOfPath may form a loop -- see also #$SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPath and #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPath).  The only access to something located along a #$SimpleSegmentOfPath is via the #$endsOfPathSegment locations for that #$SimpleSegmentOfPath.  When the segment is part of a specified #$PathSystem (as opposed to a mere #$CustomarySystemOfLinks), the predicate #$linkInSystem (or else #$loopInSystem) may apply to it and the system.")
(comment Costume "A special set of clothes worn in a play, a masquerade, or some other occasion.")
(comment infectionRoute "(#$infectionRoute INFECTION-TYPE ORGANISM-TYPE PART-TYPE) means, colloquially, that organisms of type ORGANISM-TYPE are ordinarily vulnerable to infections of type INFECTION-TYPE through physical parts or features of type PART-TYPE, when some instance of an appropriate infection-causing pathogen penetrates the organism through such a part.  More formally, it means that  if an organism of the type ORGANISM-TYPE is penetrated by at least one instance of a pathogen such that this pathogen causes infections of type INFECTION-TYPE, and the penetration occurs through a physical part of the organism of type PART-TYPE, then the organism is #$vulnerableTo an infection of type INFECTION-TYPE caused by the pathogen, unless of course the organism is for some reason immune to infections of that kind.  It also entails that a pathogen of a type capable of causing infections of type INFECTION-TYPE is capable of entering an organism of type ORGANISM-TYPE through a physical part of type PART-TYPE.")
(disjointWith Cleaning LegalProceeding)
(comment Genome-GenInfo "A specialization of #$GeneticInformation. Each instance of
#$Genome-GenInfo is a totality of genetic information which is definitive
of a biological system or of a type of biological system. It can be either 1)
the totality of genetic information carried in the genes of a particular
biological living object (as in 'the genome of Muffet'), or 2) the totality
of genetic information that is definitive of a type of organism (as in 'the
human genome') and can be seen as the genome of a typical member of the
class.")
(comment keCommonQueryExampleCol "This relation is a 'query' analog of #$examplePredSentences.
It is used to specify, for a given #$Collections, examples that typify
frequently asked questions (FAQs) applying either to the collection as
a whole or to its instances.")
(comment keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestion-Generalize "(#$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestion-Generalize TERM) says that TERM is never to be

 offered as by the precision suggestor as a possible generalization.")
(comment nodesCut-SubSystem "(#$nodesCut-SubSystem SYS SET SUB_SYS) means that SUB_SYS is the path system obtained by subtracting SET from SYS. This is the predicate corresponding to the function #$NodesCut-SubSystemFn; i.e., (#$nodesCut-SubSystem SYS SET (#$NodesCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET)) is true just in case (#$NodesCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET) a well-formed term.")
(disjointWith ElectricalComponent RoofOfAConstruction)
(comment LocomotionEvent "This is the collection of movement events in which the #$primaryObjectMoving is moving under its own control, and usually under its own power.  This entails that the moving object is an agent.  Most animals, many bacteria, and some robots are capable of #$LocomotionEvents; inanimate objects and plants are not.")
(comment NTShellPathUnderspecificationFault "A fault common to all versions of #$MSWindowsNT (4.0 to 2000 inclusive).  Upon startup, #$MSWindowsNT checks the value of the \"Shell\" registry key, HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WindowsNT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\Shell, to determine the name of the executable that should be loaded as the Shell.  By default, this value specifies Explorer.exe.  The fault is the result of a combination of factors: (1) the fact that the file Explorer.exe is there specified by a relative rather than absolute pathname, and (2) the algorithm according to which #$MSWindowsNT searches the filesystem when a file is specified with a relative pathname.  (Hence the #$genlAttributes to #$UnderspecifiedPathFault).  A malicious user could exploit this fault by placing a malicious file called \"Explorer.exe\" somewhere in the filesystem which lies shallower in the filesystem searchspace than the \"real\" Explorer.exe.  Depending upon the privileges of the user logging in, the trojan Explorer.exe could extend #$AdministratorAccount privileges to the hacker.  Microsoft has published patches for this fault which insert a special-case subroutine into the startup code.  In effect, the patch prepends '%systemroot%' to the value of the salient #$RegistryKey.")
(comment faultOfProgramOnSystemExploitedBy "The effect of #$exploitFaultOfProgramOnSystem.")
(disjointWith ProjectilePropelling AccessingAnIBT)
(comment n-WayJunctionInSystem "(#$n-WayJunctionInSystem X N SYS) means that X is an N-way junction in the #$PathSystem SYS, where N is a natural number greater than 2.  This means that exactly N ends of links (or of loops) join at X, in the system SYS.")
(disjointWith SwimWear OverGarment)
(comment HostFilteringBypassFault "A specialization of #$CommandFilteringBypassFault.  If a program is intended to filter access by specifying hosts (such as \"localhost\") that should be denied access, and yet there is a way to bypass that filtering method (e.g., by sending requests to IP addresses), the program in question has a #$HostFilteringBypassFault.")
(comment AmigaComputer "#$AmigaComputer is type of personal computer first released by #$CommodoreBusinessMachines in 1985.")
(comment Acronym-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify an acronym.")
(comment recipeCopyFor "(#$recipeCopyFor RECIPE TYPE) means that RECIPE is recipe for preparing food of type TYPE.")
(comment PostStuckInGround "A roughly cyclindrical object, long and thin, that is spiked into the ground.  Examples;  telephone poles, a fence post, sign posts, or a pylon.")
(disjointWith StateOfMatterChangeEvent ControllingAPhysicalDevice)
(comment ClockTower "A #$Tower with #$Clock(s) enabling people to tell the time from significant distances.  A modern #$ClockTower may have faces on four sides which can be read from far away, or may sound the time with bell(s), drums(s), gong(s), etc.  It is possible for there to be rooms or offices within a #$ClockTower. ")
(comment programRecodesFromTo "#$programRecodesFromTo is a ternary predicate that relates an
instance of #$FileTranslationProgram to two instances of
#$ComputerFileTypeByFormat.  (#$programRecodesFromTo PROG FORMAT-1
FORMAT-2) means that PROG translates file from FORMAT-1 to FORMAT-2.")
(comment SSHClientProgram "#$SSHClientProgram is the collection of programs used to establish connections with #$SSHServerPrograms.")
(comment TypeInstanceTernaryRuleMacroPredicate "A specialization of #$RuleMacroPredicate and #$TernaryPredicate.  Each instance of #$TypeInstanceTernaryRuleMacroPredicate relates a collection in its second argument place to an instance of #$Thing in its third argument place via an instance of #$BinaryPredicate in its first argument place.  Examples of instances of this collection include #$relationAllInstance and #$relationExistsInstance.")
(comment InstallingAnObject "The action of installing some object somewhat permanently in the place where it is to be used.  For example, placing a door in a doorway or placing a car stereo system in a car.  This concept probably also includes actions in which substances are put in a place where they are to be used, as in placing oil in car or freon in an air conditioning system, even though we do not commonly use the word 'install' in those cases.")
(comment TakeOff-Flight "Instances of #$TakeOff-Flight are events in which an object
leaves the ground or other supporting surface and becomes airborne.")
(comment UnauthorizedDataUploadFault "A server program has an #$UnauthorizedDataUploadFault if it is possible for a remote user to load some kind of data onto the server without authentication. The data may be in the form of a file (in which case the more specific #$UnauthorizedFileUploadFault should be used) but it may not be - for instance, the server program might be a chat server and the fault may involve the ability to upload arbitrary user IDs onto the contact list of an unfortunate user.")
(disjointWith ContraceptiveDevice BuildingMaterial)
(comment PantsSuit "Every instance of the collection #$PantsSuit is an instance of #$ClothingOutfit and is thus a group of coordinated items intended to be worn together.")
(comment DestinationComputerFn "(#$DestinationComputerFn COMPUTER) denotes the collection of #$Packet-Internets whose destination is COMPUTER.  For example, (#$DestinationComputerFn #$Crystal-Cyc-Com) denotes the collection of all packets whose destination is crystal.cyc.com.  The packets themselves will encode this information by referencing their destination in their \"Destination IP Address\" field.")
(comment CrossSiteScriptingFault "A program has a #$CrossSiteScriptingFault if it allows an
 attacker to execute code from a malicious web site within the security
 context of a trusted web site.  This fault makes it possible for a
 user visiting a malicious web site to follow a hyperlink to a
 legitimate web site and, in doing so, run \"injected\" code from yet
 another web site, because of the way the hyperlink is constructed.")
(comment disableDeviceWithRespectToFunction "(#$disableDeviceWithRespectToFunction AGENT DEVICE SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that AGENT prevents DEVICE from playing the role ROLE in situations of type SIT-TYPE.")
(comment independentMoleculeSpec "The predicate corresponding to #$IndependentMoleculeFn (see
#$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical).  Where CHEMOBJTYPE is a
class of #$ChemicalObject which is 'agnostic' as to whether its
instances are #$Molecules or #$MolecularComponents,
(#$molecularComponentSpec CHEMOBJTYPE MOLECULETYPE) means that
MOLECULETYPE is the class of all instances of CHEMOBJTYPE which are
#$Molecules.")
(comment traversalOf "(#$traversalOf TRAV CHAIN) means that TRAV is the #$Traversal of the #$PathChain CHAIN.  See also #$TraversalFn.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction MeasuringDevice)
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfPredictableEncryptionKey "A computer his this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$PredictableEncryptionKeyFault on it.")
(comment IcyVolatileStuff "A collection of tangible things.  Each element in #$IcyVolatileStuff is a composed of frozen volatiles (liquids that evaporate and solids that sublimate at or near Earth temperatures).")
(comment ActiveXCommandExecutionFault "A program has a #$ActiveXCommandExecutionFault if ActiveX objects (instances of #$ActiveXControl) may be executed without warning via a web page or HTML message. An example of an ActiveX object is 'SaveAs,' which would allow an attacker to save files on a victim computer.")
(comment LegionellaPneumophila "The bacterium that causes Legionnaire's Disease (#$LegionnairesDisease) also known as legionellosis.")
(comment Biodiversity "This is the collection of degrees of biodiversity. These degrees are measures

of the number, variety, and density (number per unit area) of #$BiologicalSpecies in a particular geographical region.")
(comment SituatedFlowCapacityOutFromNodeFn "The function #$SituatedFlowCapacityOutFromNodeFn, applied to some thing and to a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded in which it is a node, as in (#$SituatedFlowCapacityOutFromNodeFn NODE FLOWSYS), denotes the net maximum outward flow from NODE that can possibly flow from NODE, given the complete FLOWSYS in which every link has a value of #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn.  The result is the total of the #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn values on all the links going out of that node into other nodes (it excludes all of the node's inward links). Note: The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used to find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded. See also #$SituatedFlowCapacityInToNodeFn.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice Jewelry)
(comment hiddenObject "'(#$hiddenObject DISAPPEAR OBJECT)' means that in the
#$DisappearingFromSight DISAPPEAR, OBJECT is the thing which is no
longer visible.")
(comment VulnerableToRpcRequestForwarding "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$RpcRequestForwardingFault on it.")
(disjointWith HumanScaleObject TimeZone)
(comment OrganismTypeByComplexity "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$OrganismTypeByComplexity is a collection of #$Organism-Whole.  This collection has exactly two disjoint instances.")
(comment SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPath "The collection of all segments of #$Path-Generics that do not have any branching points along them and such that each has both of its endpoints at the same location, that is, it is a loop from one place back to the same place.  (For contrast, see also #$SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPath.)  When the segment is part of a specified #$PathSystem (as opposed to an unspecified surrounding #$CustomarySystemOfLinks), the predicate #$cycleInSystem may apply to it and the system.")
(comment MechanicalDevice "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$MechanicalDevice is a physical device which has at least one part that moves with respect to another one of its parts.  Thus a spoon is not an instance of #$MechanicalDevice, but a pair of scissors is, as are more complex devices such as vacuum cleaners and the #$SpaceShuttleChallenger.")
(comment Muleta "A short red cape used by a matador in the final stages of a bullfight.")
(disjointWith MakingSomething Talking)
(disjointWith Gene-GenInfo Genome-GenInfo)
(comment linksCut-SubSystem "(#$linksCut-SubSystem SYS SET SUB_SYS) means that SUB_SYS is the path system obtained by subtracting SET from SYS. This is the predicate corresponding to the function #$LinksCut-SubSystemFn; i.e., (#$linksCut-SubSystem SYS SET (#$LinksCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET)) is true just in case (#$LinksCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET) a well-formed term.")
(disjointWith Stairway RoofOfAConstruction)
(disjointWith TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure LocomotionEvent)
(comment Bathroom-Home "A room in a home with a toilet.  If an instance of #$Bathroom-Home it also has a #$BathTub or #$ShowerStall, it is an instance of #$FullBath; if not, it is an instance of #$HalfBath.")
(disjointWith Ripping Washing)
(comment VenezuelanEquineEncephalitisVirus "The virus that causes #$VenezuelanEquineEncephalitis.")
(comment InwardLinkSetFn "A function, when applied to a #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS and a node X in SYS as in (#$InwardLinkSetFn X SYS), returns the set of all links directed toward X, i.e., the set of links in SYS each of which is directed in SYS from some other node to X.  Note that if SYS is a #$DirectedPathSystem, (#$InwardLinkSetFn X SYS) is disjoint with (#$OutwardLinkSetFn X SYS).  If SYS is not a #$DirectedPathSystem, however, (#$InwardLinkSetFn X SYS) is not in general disjoint with (#$OutwardLinkSetFn X SYS) because a 'bidirected' link, if any, belongs to both sets.  So for an inexperienced user, it is recommended to use a #$DirectedPathSystem as the second argument of this function. Note also that loops, if any, are not included as links.")
(disjointWith Sock OverGarment)
(comment CommandFilteringBypassFault "#$CommandFilteringBypassFault is a specialization of both #$SecuritySoftwareBypassFault and #$CommandExecutionFault.  A program has this fault if it is intended to reject certain requests, and yet accepts them.")
(comment Body-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify the body of a document (which, in #$HypertextMarkupLanguage, consists of everything other than the head).")
(comment PersonTypeByPrejudice "A collection of collections.  Each instance  of #$PersonTypeByPrejudice is a collection of instances of #$Person who share  a #$Prejudice.")
(disjointWith Ray-Geometrical LineSegment)
(comment SupportColumn "a column of some material used to support something")
(comment Traveller "The collection of all instances of a person going somewhere on a #$Travel-TripEvent: on a vacation, on a business trip, etc.  This collection does not include trips such as going to the grocery store or coming home from work.")
(comment ConnectingTypeFn "A function that yields the collection of all #$ConnectingTogether events that join things in a particular structural connection.  (#$ConnectingTypeFn CONNECTION) denotes the collection of all joining-together events in which the joined pieces end up in the CONNECTION relation as an immediate result.   For example, (#$ConnectingTypeFn #$endToEndConnected) refers to acts of connecting things end-to-end.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess ControllingAPhysicalDevice)
(comment FortnightsDuration "A #$UnitOfTime function that takes one or two real numbers as arguments and returns, as its value, a comparable #$Time-Quantity attribute measured in fortnights. More precisely, an expression of the form (#$FortnightsDuration NUM) denotes the (\"point-value\") #$Time-Quantity of being exactly NUM fortnights in duration, and an expression of the form (#$FortnightsDuration MIN MAX) denotes the (properly interval-like) #$Time-Quantity of being at least MIN fortnights and at most MAX fortnights in duration.")
(comment faultVulnerability-Running "(#$faultVulnerability-Running FAULT VULN) means that a #$LocalProgram with #$ProgramFaultAttribute FAULT will lead to the existence of #$ComputerVulnerability VULN on a #$Computer on which that #$LocalProgram is running.")
(comment SymlinkFault-MailSpool "A program has this fault if a remote user can create symlinks to obtain a copy of any other user's mail.")
(comment InitializationOfProgramFn "(#$InitializationOfProgramFn CW) denotes the collection of instances of #$InitializationOfProgram which result in the running of an instantiation of CW.")
(comment VulnerableToCABFileExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$CABFileExecutionFault on it.")
(disjointWith TypeTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate InstanceTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate)
(comment CoveringSomething "The set of actions in which an agent places and/or holds a covering over a thing; the purpose may be to obscure the thing from view (''hiding it'') or to protect it from weather conditions.")
(comment InterpretingSignificance "The collection of all #$Evaluating events in which some object or event is evaluated in order to gain information about something else.  This includes reading animal tracks to determine what animals passed by, reading the sky for knowledge of future weather, and reading tea leaves.")
(comment FilingNails "The event in which fingernails or toenails are filed in order to smooth or shape them. A nail file or emery board is held throughout.")
(comment CorruptibleKernelMemoryFault "A program has this attribute if it can be exploited to corrupt kernel memory.")
(comment StoneFence "The collection of #$Fences constructed of stones.")
(comment relatedToVia "(#$relatedToVia OBJ1 OBJ2 SET NUM) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are related via some sequence of NUM or fewer steps via the binary relations in the set SET.  More precisely, (#$relatedToVia OBJ1 OBJ2 SET NUM) means that there is a sequence of objects of the length equal to or less than NUM and such that OBJ1 is the first element of the sequence, OBJ2 is the last element of the sequence, and each element of the sequence is related to its successor (if any) by some predicate in SET, or by the inverse of some predicate in SET. For instance, if (#$likesAsFriend #$BillClinton #$TonyBlair) and (#$knows #$TonyBlair #$GeorgeWBush) are true, then (#$relatedToVia #$BillClinton #$GeorgeWBush (#$TheSet #$likesAsFriend #$acquaintedWith) 2) is true (given that (#$genlPreds #$knows #$acquaintedWith) is true). Note that a predicate in SET may be used to relate more than one pair: if (#$likesAsFriend #$BillClinton #$TonyBlair) and (#$likesAsFriend #$TonyBlair #$GeorgeWBush) are true, then (#$relatedToVia #$BillClinton #$GeorgeWBush (#$TheSet #$likesAsFriend #$acquaintedWith) 2) is true.")
(comment PresidentOfChina "The collection of persons who hold, or have held,

the office of President in China.")
(comment pointOnPath-Generic "(#$pointOnPath-Generic POINT PATH-GENERIC) holds just in case either (#$pointOnPath POINT PATH-GENERIC) or (#$pointOnCycle POINT PATH-GENERIC) holds.  Note that (#$pointOnPath POINT PATH-GENERIC) and (#$pointOnCycle POINT PATH-GENERIC) cannot both hold, and hence (#$pointOnPath-Generic POINT PATH-GENERIC) amounts to (#$xor (#$pointOnPath POINT PATH-GENERIC) (#$pointOnCycle POINT PATH-GENERIC)).")
(comment Hoopskirt "The collection of instances of #$Skirt stiffened with hoops.  These were worn primarily in western cultures beginning around 1714 (although a similarly stiff skirt was worn even earlier).  In the 18th century the hoops were often made of whalebone.  Hoop skirts went out of fashion in the late 18th century, but returned to fashion in the mid 19th century (Victorian era), finally losing favor again around 1870.")
(comment V-EDay "The holiday commemorating end of World War II [#$WorldWarII] in Europe, 8 May 1945.")
(comment repeatPrecedingActionAtIntervalNTimes "(#$repeatPrecedingActionAtIntervalNTimes AGENT INTERVAL TIMES) means that AGENT repeats the immediately preceeding action in a plan INTERVAL often and TIMES many times.  See also #$repeatPrecedingActionNTimes.")
(comment holidayCelebratedByCulture "(#$holidayCelebratedByCulture HOLIDAY CULTURE) means that HOLIDAY is celebrated within CULTURE.")
(comment ownershipDocumentFor "(#$ownershipDocumentFor DOCUMENT OBJ) means that the #$OwnershipDocument DOCUMENT records an agent's ownership in the #$PartiallyTangible OBJ.")
(comment loopInSystem "(#$loopInSystem LOOP SYS) means that LOOP is a 'loop' in SYS, which is like a link in SYS except that it has exactly one node on it as if it is a link whose two end nodes are the same.  Each loop in SYS is also a cycle in SYS, see #$cycleInSystem.  The differences between a loop and a (non-loop) cycle in SYS include that (i) there is exactly one point in SYS on a loop (which must be a node in SYS), but there may in general be any finite number of nodes (and even as many points as there are real numbers) on some (non-loop) cycle in SYS, and that (ii) The unique node in SYS on a loop may or may not be an end point of a link in SYS, but each node on a (non-loop) cycle in SYS must be an end point of at least two links in SYS.  These imply that there can be at most one 'intersection point' on a loop in SYS but there can be any finite number of 'intersection points' on a (non-loop) cycle in SYS.  See #$pointOnCycle and #$junctionInSystem. Note that under current treatment of loops in a path system, if one would like to talk about a 'loop' in a path system a 'part' of which is a path in the system, then he/she should make it a cycle rather than a loop in the system because according to what we said above, no 'part' of a loop in the system can be presented as a path in the system.  Note also that in some cases (such as talking about relations between different #$PathSystems), using (#$LoopsInSystemFn SYS) to denote the set of all loops in SYS is more convenient than using the predicate #$loopInSystem.")
(disjointWith SpaceInAHOC MeasuringDevice)
(comment VulnerableToEncryptionKeyRecovery "A computer his this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$RecoverableEncryptionKeyFault on it.")
(comment vulnerableToSituationType "(#$vulnerableToSituationType OBJECT SITUATION-TYPE) means that OBJECT is vulnerable to a threat specified by SITUATION-TYPE. For example, (#$vulnerableToSituationType #$Israel #$TerroristAttack) states that Israel is vulnerable to terrorist attacks. This leaves open the type of agents that are the source of the vulnerability, which can specified via #$vulnerableToType.")
(comment waterAreaOfRegion "(#$waterAreaOfRegion ?REG ?AR) means that ?AR is the total #$Area of all the significant bodies of water in the region ?REG. See also #$areaOfRegion, #$landAreaOfRegion, and #$BodyOfWater-Large.")
(comment LegionnairesDisease "A disease causing anorexia, malaise and headache progressing to fever, chills, abdominal pain, diarrhea and pneumonia. The disease acquired its name in 1976 when an outbreak of pneumonia occurred among persons attending a convention of the American
Legion in Philadelphia. It has a milder form (without pneumonia) called Pontiac fever")
(comment EcologicalRegion "A collection of geographical regions.  Each instance of #$EcologicalRegion is a region having one or more characteristic ecosystems.  From knowledge of those ecosystems, we can posit whether certain organisms can forage, reproduce, and live successfully there.  Information about ecological regions typically also includes what kinds of organisms are in fact found there.  In theory, any arbitrary continuous region could be analyzed as an ecological region, but most regions identified in practice have some kind of sameness or systematic interconnection in their topology, climate, and biology.  Examples: the #$WesternDesertOfEgypt, the #$GreatBarrierReef, the #$Amazon-Region.")
(comment LocalLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn "The function #$LocalLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn, applied to a set of some things and to a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded in which they are links forming a 'cutset', as in (#$LocalLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn LINKCUTSET FLOWSYS), denotes the sum of all the #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn values of the links in LINKCUTSET, in FLOWSYS.  This is without regard to the links' connections to other links in FLOWSYS (for the context-sensitive version, see #$SituatedLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn).  The result is the total of the #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn values on all the links going in or out of that node.  Note: The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used to find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded.  See also #$SituatedLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn.")
(comment HotelRoomUnit "A 'room' in a hotel -- usually includes at least one bedroom and a bathroom.")
(disjointWith Shirt BraLikeGarment)
(comment VulnerableToIPDisclosure "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$IPDisclosureFault on it.")
(comment Zoophile "The collection of all #$Persons who engage in
#$Bestiality.")
(comment lexicalRootMtForLanguage "(#$lexicalRootMtForLanguage MT LANG) means that MT is the most general #$LexicalMicrotheory which is specific to the #$NaturalLanguage, LANG.")
(comment DatabaseServerProgram "A specialization of #$DatabaseProgram. Each instance of this collection is some instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW which stores and manages databases, often presenting that information to #$DatabaseClientPrograms. See also #$RelationalDatabaseServerProgram.")
(comment SelfPoweredDevice "A specialization of both #$MechanicalDevice and #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$SelfPoweredDevice has, as one of its internal parts, a device which converts some kind of potential energy into force.  For example, a cordless electric drill would be an instance of #$SelfPoweredDevice, since it contains a battery and motor that convert electricity stored in the battery into kinetic energy.  Other examples of #$SelfPoweredDevices are the instances of #$Automobile, which (typically) convert gasoline and battery power to get the energy to move.  Of course, some muscle power is involved in operating both a cordless drill and an automobile, but in neither case is it the main part of the power.  Negative exemplars of a #$SelfPoweredDevice include all instances of #$Bicycle (powered by the people who ride them), cable cars (since they are pulled along by cables embedded in the street) and subway trains (often powered by an electrified `third rail').")
(comment HockeyHelmet "A helmet worn while playing hockey.")
(comment Gene-GenInfo "A specialization of #$GeneticInformation. Instances of
#$Gene-GenInfo represent the genetic information contained in a gene, see
#$Gene-HereditaryUnit. The abstract genetic structure of a #$Gene-GenInfo
is recorded in a corresponding #$Gene-GIS.")
(comment SurgicalTreatment "This is the collection of surgeries which are #$MedicalTreatmentEvents, that is, it includes surgery designed to treat a medical condition, but excludes both diagnostic and cosmetic surgery.")
(comment pathInPathArtifact "This predicate can be used to relate two instances of #$PathArtifact such
that one is a part of the other. (#$pathInPathArtifact PATH PART-PATH) means
that PART-PATH is a part of PATH.  Note that the sense of \"part\" is that
used in the predicates #$physicalParts and #$spatiallySubsumes. An example:
the portion of #$RouteOne-Vietnam that is on the
#$RouteOneBridge-HueVietnam is a #$pathInPathArtifact of the bridge.")
(disjointWith Portal RoofOfAConstruction)
(disjointWith WeatherEvent LocomotionEvent)
(comment LoggingInToAccountOnFn "(#$LoggingInToAccountOnFn ACCOUNT COMPUTER) denotes the collection of events in which someone enters the login information for ACCOUNT at COMPUTER.")
(comment RecoverableEncryptionKeyFault "#$RecoverableEncryptionKeyFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program (usually an encryption program) has this fault if it is possible for an attacker to recover a key the program has used to encrypt data.")
(comment needsFor "This predicate relates an agent, a goal the agent has, and

something the agent needs (in a very broad sense of `needs') in order

to achieve or further that goal.  The goal is represented by a 

sentence (i.e. an #$ELSentence-Assertible; see #$goals).  The 

\"something\" needed might be either a thing the agent needs directly 

(such as a physical object or person) or a thing the agent has a need 

in (close) connection with (such as an object-type or a proposition); 

see the specializations of #$needs-Generic for a fuller account.  

(#$needsFor AGENT THING GOAL) means that AGENT needs THING (or has a 

need in connection with THING that s/he must fulfill) in order to 

achieve her/his GOAL.  The sense of `need' relevant here ranges from 

matters of practical convenience to matters of life and death; see the 

comment on #$needs-Generic.  See also #$satisfiesNeed.")
(comment valueOfAccountsPayable "The summation of the balance of all payable accounts held by the agent.  The balance of a payable account is the sum of all active payables owed by the agent to the account creditor less any previous overpayment")
(comment PurposefulMentalActivity "The intersection of #$StrictlyMentalEvent and #$PurposefulAction, and also a specialization of #$IntentionalMentalEvent. Each instance of this collection is an event involving intentional mental activity on the part of at least one performer (see #$performedBy).  
Solving a math problem (cf. #$DoingMath), planning an attack and performing a thought experiment (cf. #$ThoughtExperimenting) are all examples of #$PurposefulMentalActivity.  However, daydreaming or having undesired obsessive thoughts are not examples.  A borderline example might be arriving at the solution to a math problem in one's sleep after intentionally working on the problem during the previous day.")
(comment VenezuelanEquineEncephalitis "A viral infection whose intial symptoms are flu-like with abrupt onset of severe headache, chills, fever, pain behind the eyes, nausea and vomiting. Central nervous system symptoms range from drowsiness to disorientation, convulsions, paralysis, coma and death.")
(comment OutwardLinkSetFn "A function, when applied to a #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS and a node X in SYS as in (#$OutwardLinkSetFn X SYS), returns the set of all links directed outward from X, i.e., the set of links in SYS each of which is directed in SYS from X to some other node in SYS. Note that if SYS is a #$DirectedPathSystem, (#$OutwardLinkSetFn X SYS) is disjoint with (#$InwardLinkSetFn X SYS).  If SYS is not a #$DirectedPathSystem, however, (#$OutwardLinkSetFn X SYS) is not in general disjoint with (#$InwardLinkSetFn X SYS) because a 'bidirected' link, if any, belongs to both sets.  So for an inexperienced user, it is recommended to use a #$DirectedPathSystem as the second argument of this function.  Note also that loops, if any, are not included as links.")
(comment BuildingMaterial "#$BuildingMaterial is a specialization of #$Artifact-NonAgentive and #$PartiallyTangibleProduct.  Each instance of #$BuildingMaterial is an artifact of a type typically incorporated in the construction of new structures.  Specializations of #$BuildingMaterial include lumber (but not wood), bricks (but not clay), quaried blocks of marble (but not rock in general), slabs of concrete, batches of wet concrete, roof shingles, copper nails, double-paned windows, etc.")
(disjointWith ThongWear OverGarment)
(comment InterfaceStatisticsResetFault "A program has this fault if it allows non-root users to reset interface stattistics.  (Only root should be able to reset interface statistics.)  Exploitation of this fault could potentially interfere with programs that track statistical information.")
(comment Caption-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a caption.")
(comment productsCreated "'(#$productsCreated MAKING PRODUCT)' means that PRODUCT is both a #$products and an #$outputsCreated of the #$MakingSomething MAKING; in other words, PRODUCT was intentionally created in the #$CreationEvent MAKING.")
(comment SoftwareObject "A specialization of #$ConceptualWork.  #$SoftwareObject is the most general collection of software.  Each instance of #$SoftwareObject is either an individual computer program, a computer program module, a software package, a software library file (see #$ComputerSoftwareLibrary-CW), or a version or series thereof.  Each instance of #$SoftwareObject is such that either it (or a member of the version series that constitutes it) could conceivably be instantiated in code that could run on some computer system, even if the code has not been written yet, and even if it could not run independently of other code (see the specialization #$ComputerProgramModule-CW).  #$SoftwareObject does not include purely data objects that software could operate on.  Pine, Pine version 4.20, and Pine versions 4.20 through 4.33 inclusive are each instances of #$SoftwareObject. #$SoftwareObject is partitioned into #$SoftwareObject-Individual and #$SoftwareVersionSeries.")
(comment originallyFromRegion "Where a tangible object has come from, where it was made.  A Russian automobile is #$originallyFromRegion #$Russia.  An African person is #$originallyFromRegion Africa.  Etc, etc. How do we axiomatize the sufficient conditions for this predicate?  This is not always clear.  Often, wherever an artifact has been fabricated is the value on #$originallyFromRegion.  (But there are some exceptions. E.g.  some Japanese Autos are fabricated in USA.)  Often, a person is #$originallyFromRegion where they were from.  (But I doubt a 25 year resident of the USA who was born 26 years ago to Anglo parents would be considered `African'.)")
(comment Ferrule "A small metal ring or cap used to strengthen a shaft, prevent splitting, or to make a tight joint.")
(comment BusinessTraveller "The collection of #$Persons travelling for business purposes.")
(comment NationalIDDocument "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$IDDocument.  Each instance of #$NationalIDDocument is a document issued by the government of some country to one of its citizens or resident aliens.  In the countries in which such documents are issued, possession of such a document is usually required in order to establish work eligibility, or to obtain certain kinds of government benefits.")
(comment WindowManagerAuthorityBypassFault "A window manager program has this fault if it allows users' clients to connect to the window manager server from the local machine. This can be dangerous on multi-user systems since the other users can perform window manager-related attacks (e.g., keyword logging, window watching).")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedProcessKilling "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$ProcessKillFault on it.")
(disjointWith TypeTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate TypeInstanceTernaryRuleMacroPredicate)
(comment BuryingSomething "Covering something, typically by digging a hole in the ground, putting the object in the hole, and covering it with the dirt that was dug out.  Above-ground burials involve piling something on top of the object to be buried, until it is covered.")
(comment ElectricalIntaking "When an electrical device is plugged into an electrical socket.")
(comment Unloading "A collection of events.  An #$Unloading event is one in

which an agent purposefully takes something (the #$objectRemoved) out

of a container (the #$objectRemaining).")
(comment ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-Printer "A program has this fault if an unauthorized remote user can access the printer account without authentication.  The printer account typically has a low level of privilege, but access to the printer account can nevertheless lead to some serious consequences, if some other vulnerabilities are present on the computer.")
(comment UnderspecifiedPathFault "An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if, in those situations where it is called upon to retrieve or execute some file without being given the file's full location (path), it looks for the file in a manner that makes insertion and execution of trojan programs a fairly trivial matter.  Note that both #$UnixOSes and #$MSWindowsOperatingSystems may have this fault.  In #$UnixOSes the fault is usually due to the OS's including the user's current directory in the $PATH environment variable; this makes it easy for a malicious user to insert malicious programs called 'ls', 'more', 'grep', etc.  In the case of #$MSWindowsOperatingSystems, the fault is usually due to the order in which the OS searches the filesystem in looking for the relevant file (this search may or may not include checking the user's HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Environment\\Path registry setting).  One common and very dangerous fault of this kind is the #$NTShellPathUnderspecificationFault.  Commands executed via exploitation of an #$UnderspecifiedPathFault are executed with the privileges of the user running the command.")
(comment ChildSexualAbuser "The collection of all #$Persons that engage in #$ChildSexualAbuse.  This differs from #$ChildMolester in that the #$ChildSexualAbuser does not necessarily engage in the physical sexual abuse of a child.  A positive example of this collection would include the person that shows a child a pornographic movie.  See also #$ChildSexualAbuse.")
(disjointWith PoweredDevice CornerOnObject)
(comment SheepskinCoat "The collection of #$Coats made out of sheepskin.")
(comment TFTPServerProgram "#$TFTPServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$TrivialFileTransferProtocol (TFTP).")
(comment enterLoginInformationForAccountAtComputer "(#$enterLoginInformationForAccountAtComputer AGENT ACCT COMP) means that AGENT enters the #$usernameForAccount and #$passwordForAccount for ACCT at COMP.  Note that COMP must be a #$nodeInAccountSystem for the #$AccountSystem of which ACCT is a #$UserAccount, and that AGENT must have physical access (#$hasPhysicalAccess) to COMP.")
(comment AssessingWhatAnAgentWillDo "A collection of processess.  Each instance of #$Evaluating is a process
in which an agent makes some assessment as to what some agent is likely to do. 
Examples include assessing whether or not a certain politician will run for the
presidency or assessing whether or not an enemy military unit is likely to attack.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction Weapon)
(comment landAreaOfRegion "(#$landAreaOfRegion REG AR) means that the physical region REG has the area AR, excluding any large bodies of water which might be found in that region. See also #$areaOfRegion, #$waterAreaOfRegion, and #$BodyOfWater-Large.")
(comment LassaFever-Virus "The virus that causes #$LassaFever.")
(comment SituatedLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn "The function #$SituatedLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn, applied to a set of some things and to a #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded in which they are links forming a 'cutset', as in (#$SituatedLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn LINKCUTSET FLOWSYS), denotes the sum of all the #$LocalLinkFlowCapacityFn values of the links in LINKCUTSET, in FLOWSYS.  This is without regard to the links' connections to other links in FLOWSYS (for the version is limited by connections, see #$LocalLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn).  The result is the total of the #$SituatedLinkFlowCapacityFn values on all the links going in or out of that node.  Note: The predicate #$flowTypeOfSystem is used to find what kind of 'flow' is represented in a particular #$NetworkFlowSystem-Bounded.  See also #$LocalLinkCutSetFlowCapacityFn.")
(comment RetailStoreSpace "Spaces which are the physical quarters for store enterprises.")
(disjointWith Shirt Vest)
(comment VulnerableToTCPPortDenialOfService "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a
#$TCPPortDenialOfServiceFault on it.")
(comment setUIDOfProgramOn "(#$setUIDOfProgramOn PROGRAM COMPUTER ACCOUNT) means that the default owner of a process started on COMPUTER by PROGRAM is ACCOUNT.")
(disjointWith Cell MulticellularOrganism)
(comment linksOfCustomarySystem "(#$linksOfCustomarySystem ASSUMEDSYSTEM LINK) means that the #$CustomarySystemOfLinks ASSUMEDSYSTEM has the individual #$SimpleSegmentOfPath LINK as one of its links (where 'link' means a path with no junctions along it).  Each such link is of the path type that ASSUMEDSYSTEM is made of: a highway system is assumed to be comprised of roadways linking junctions or towns (and some dead-ends); each roadway without junctions is one of the links.  The parts of a road (pavement, streetlight, stripe in middle, culverts, etc.) are not #$linksOfCustomarySystem.  Similarly the #$linksOfCustomarySystem of a plumbing system are the pipes, but not the straps holding the pipes.  Thus a #$CustomarySystemOfLinks may have various kinds of #$parts that are not #$linksOfCustomarySystem.  Contrast this with the formal case where a specified #$PathSystem is given; in this case the predicates #$linkInSystem and #$pathInSystem are used.")
(comment RidingHelmet "A helmet worn while riding horses.")
(comment keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestion-Precisify "(#$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestion-Precisify TERM) says that TERM is never to be

 offered as by the precision suggestor as a possible specification.")
(comment ProtectingFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which something is protected.")
(comment PlaintextSystemPasswordFileFault "#$PlaintextSystemPasswordFileFault is an attribute of some instances of #$OperatingSystem. An operating system has a #$PlaintextSystemPasswordFileFault if it stores any passwords for its #$LoginAccounts in a plaintext file.")
(comment Walking-Generic "A specialization of #$Ambulation: the collection of all instances of #$LocomotionProcess in which the locomotor (usually but not necessarily an animal) always has at least one foot in contact with the surface. #$Walking-Generic is therefore disjoint with #$Running. Notable specializations of this collection include #$AnimalWalkingProcess, #$WalkingOnTwoLegs and #$WalkingOnFourLegs.")
(comment ScrubTyphus "A bacterial infection characterised by sudden onset of headache, chills, prostration, fever and general pains with a dull red to dark purple rash.  Rash appears first on the trunk and then sreads to the arms and legs.  Pulmonary, encephalitic and/or cardiac complications can occur.  Recovery is prolonged.")
(comment SingleSinkFn "A function, when applied to a #$BoundedDirectedPathSystem SYS as in (#$SingleSinkFn SYS), returns the unique sink node X in SYS, i.e., the node in SYS that has only inward links.  Note that since SYS is a #$BoundedDirectedPathSystem, there can be no sink node in SYS other than (#$SingleSinkFn SYS).  See also #$sinkNodeInSystem.")
(comment RunningSpike "The collection of shoes made for running races on tracks.")
(comment PacketFilteringBypassFault "A #$ProgramFault of some instances of #$OperatingSystem.  A program has this fault if it is intended to block packets from reaching an address, but actually lets them reach that address.")
(comment Cite-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a citation to another work.")
(comment subSoftwareObjects "(#$subSoftwareObjects SO-IND IND-OR-SERIES) means that one of the three following conditions holds: (i) SO-IND and IND-OR-SERIES represent the same object (i.e., (#$equals SO-IND IND-OR-SERIES holds), or (ii) SO-IND is a version of IND-OR-SERIES (i.e., (#$versionOfSoftware IND-OR-SERIES SO-IND) hold, or (iii) SO-IND is one of the programs in the series IND-OR-SERIES (i.e., (#$softwareInVersionSeries SO-IND IND-OR-SERIES) holds).")
(comment spatialSettingOfPIT "The location(s) where a PIT takes place.")
(comment relyOnObject "(#$relyOnObject AGENT OBJ) means that AGENT relies on OBJ for a significant part of AGENT's normal activities.  See #$relyOnType and #$relyOnAgent.")
(comment Filter "A generic type of filter.")
(comment ComputerUser "A specialization of #$Agent-Generic. Each instance of this collection is an agent that uses a #$Computer. This collection includes #$Persons, and also copies of certain computer programs that access other programs  (such as web spiders). #$ComputerUsers may be using their computers for personal, scientific, and/or institutional purposes.")
(comment ApparentFn "The function (#$ApparentFn THING), as applied to an individual thing, donates the collection of all things which appear to be that thing.  The apparent thing need not be an imitation; it could just be based on coincidental resemblance.   The 'audience' to whom the appearance is evident is unspecified.  As a default, the resulting thing should seem like the original THING to the typical observer in the relevant context.")
(comment EMailReplyCommandExecutionFault "A program has this fault if an attacker can place a carefully-formed string containing shell meta-characters in the Reply-To: field of an email message.  If the attacker then sends the email to a victim/recipient, and the message elicits a response, the contents of the Reply-To: field will be interpreted as a reference to a pre-existing file in /tmp (or some other directory), placed earlier by the attacker, which can contain arbitrary commands. Of course, exploitation of this fault requires the attacker to be able to trick the user into replying to the message.")
(comment SepticDrainfield "The instances of SepticDrainfield are the areas of land through which a network of sewage pipes travel.")
(comment InitializationOfProgram "A specialization of #$CreationEvent and #$ComputerActivity. Each instance of this collection is an event in which a #$ComputerProgramCopy of a #$ComputerProgram-CW is initialized (set up and run for the first time). See also #$InitializationOfProgramFn.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfPlaintextPasswordFile "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$PlaintextPasswordFileFault on it.")
(comment TypeTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate "A specialization of #$RuleMacroPredicate and #$TernaryPredicate.  Each instance of #$TypeTypeTernaryRuleMacroPredicate relates collections in its second and third argument places via an instance of #$BinaryPredicate in its first argument place.  Notable instances include #$relationAllExists and #$relationExistsAll.")
(comment LoadingADishwasher "Putting dirty dishes into a dishwasher to be cleaned.")
(disjointWith MentalSituation-SingleSubject InterAgentSituation)
(comment PackageManagerProgram "The collection of package manager programs, which build, install, query, verify, update, and uninstall individual software  packages.")
(comment PredictableSessionIDFault "A server program has this fault if it generates session IDs in a predictable manner, allowing an unauthorized user to spoof that session ID and hijack the session.")
(comment VulnerableToArbitraryFileDeletion "This vulnerability is a specialization of #$VulnerableToFileDeletion.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible for an unauthorized person to delete arbitrary files from the computer.")
(comment SimilarityWRTPredicate "A collection of #$ComparisonWRTPredicates used to represent the respect in which two things are similar. Predicates that represent that two things are similar but do not represent the manner or respect in which they are similar are excluded from #SimilarityWRTPredicate. For example, #$similarTo is not an instance of #$SimilarityWRTPredicate.  This collection can be used to constrain Asks designed to return assertions that represent known similarities between two specified things. Cf. #$DifferenceWRTPredicate.")
(disjointWith Token-Physical CornerOnObject)
(comment MinkCoat "The collection of fur coats made out of the fur of instances of #$Mink.")
(comment ApolloComputer "The collection of Apollo machines.")
(comment doGetAccessToAccount "(#$doGetAccessToAccount AGENT ACCOUNT) means that AGENT gets access to ACCOUNT on an instance of #$AccountSystem.")
(comment dislikes-Generic "(#$dislikes-Generic SUBJ OBJ) means that SUBJ dislikes OBJ. This is a very general dislike relation which is most useful for organising dislike relations and for use during inference; for representation purposes, use a specialization.")
(comment ShelterConstruction "A specialization of #$ConstructionArtifact.  Each instance of #$ShelterConstruction is an artifact built by some agent, including but not limited to humans, and intended for use as a shelter.  Instances of #$ShelterConstruction include bird nests, termite mounds, beaver dams, the #$SydneyOperaHouse, the #$PalaceOfFineArts-SanFrancisco, and the #$NewYorkHiltonAtBroadway.")
(comment InformationTransferPhysicalEvent "A specialization of #$InformationTransferEvent (q.v.) and #$PhysicalEvent each instance of which involves at least one #$PartiallyTangible, either as its source (see #$informationOrigin), as (at least one of) its destination(s) (see #$informationDestination), or both.  (A partially tangible source or destination, note, must pre-exist the transfer event.)  Indeed, most if not all actual information transfer events are physical events; but #$InformationTransferPhysicalEvent does in principle exclude those such as telepathic communications between disembodied spirits or other #$Agent-Intangibles.")
(comment LassaFever "A viral infection characterised by gradual onset of malaise, fever, headache, sore throat, cough, nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea with chest and abdominal pain progressing to hemorrhage and seizure. Deafness may occur.")
(comment FieldFn "(#$FieldFn ?PLANT) denotes the collection of fields of plants of type ?PLANT.")
(comment JoinPathsFn "A function that, when applied to a CHAIN as in (#$JoinPathsFn CHAIN) where CHAIN is a #$PathChain whose 'path-concatenation' results in a #$Path-Simple, returns the #$Path-Simple obtained by the concatenation.  More strictly, let CHAIN be a #$PathChain (#$TheList POINT(1) PATH(1) ... POINT(n) PATH(n) POINT(n+1)) such that the concatenation of all the PATH(k)s is a #$Path-Simple.  Then (#$JoinPathsFn CHAIN) is the result of concatenating PATH(1), ..., PATH(n), which is a single as-long or longer path.  Note that this function is a partial function.  Note also that for (#$JoinPathsFn (#$TheList POINT(1) PATH(1) ... POINT(n) PATH(n) POINT(n+1))) to be defined, all PATH(k)s must be instances of #$Path-Simple, and no PATH(j) and PATH(k) can be the same if j and k are different.  Note, finally, that if all PATH(k)s are links, and all POINT(k)s are nodes, in a #$PathSystem, (#$JoinPathsFn (#$TheList POINT(1) PATH(1) ... POINT(n) PATH(n) POINT(n+1))) is defined if and only if all POINT(k)s are different.")
(comment OfficeSpace "A room or set of rooms which comprises an office. Many people work in one #$OfficeSpace, whereas usually only one or two work in an office room.  There is often a small reception area in the #$OfficeSpace where the secretary  or assistant works.")
(disjointWith SomethingToWear MeasuringDevice)
(comment hiddenFrom "'(#$hiddenFrom DISAPPEAR AGENT)' means that in the

#$DisappearingFromSight DISAPPEAR, the #$hiddenObject can no longer be

seen by AGENT.  For example, if you close your fist around a watch, it becomes #$hiddenFrom you.  This type of hiding involves only the loss of visibility of an object; for instance, you may still be able to hear the watch ticking.")
(comment VulnerableToSchemeCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a
#$SchemeCommandExecutionFault on it.")
(comment BondageAndDisciplinePractioner "The collection of #$Persons that engage in
#$BondageAndDiscipline activities.")
(comment processRunningAs "(#$processRunningAs PROCESS ACCOUNT) means that PROCESS executes with all the privileges of ACCOUNT.")
(comment OutgoingWRTLANFn "(#$OutgoingWRTLANFn LAN) denotes the collection of all #$Packet-Internets that are outgoing with respect to the

#$LocalAreaNetwork, LAN.  That is, it denotes the collection of

packets whose source #$IPAddresses belong to machines on LAN, and whose destination #$IPAddresses do not belong to machines on LAN.")
(comment OpeningAContainerArtifact "The collection of events in which an #$isa #$ContainerArtifact is opened by an Agent.  NOTE that the #$ContainerArtifact is the #$objectOfStateChange, and that each such object has at least one portal, presumably with a portal covering.  So #$OpeningAContainerArtifact means removing the portal covering from the portal (one of the portals) of a container product.  The portal of a container product can be either explicitly marked (as with an `open this end' notice on a box), or implicit but conventionally understood (as with the top or lid of a tin can).")
(comment MulticellularOrganism "#$MulticellularOrganism is a specialization of #$Organism-Whole.  Each instance of #$MulticellularOrganism is an organism that is composed of more than one cell.  In other words, this is the collection of all instances of #$Organism-Whole that are not instances of #$SingleCellOrganism.")
(comment FiniteLogFile "The collection of finite log files; i.e. files that may run out of room to store data.  Compare to #$FiniteLogFile.  Whether a file is finite is controlled by the program that writes to it.")
(comment ImitationOfCollection "#$ImitationOfCollection is the collection of all collections           whose instances have been created in order to seem to be instances of distinct           collections.  Notable instances of #$ImitationOfCollection           include (#$ImitationOfCollectionFn #$EdibleFruit) and (#$ImitationOfCollectionFn           #$Currency).  Compare the collection type #$ImitationOfCollection to the collection           #$ImitationOfIndividual.")
(comment outfitParts "The clothing outfit ARG1 has separate component parts ARG2.")
(disjointWith SurgicalTreatment CosmeticSurgery)
(comment onlineChatAlias "A ternary predicate relating a person to the character string used to identify that person in a particular online chat session. (#$onlineChatAlias CHAT PERSON STRING) means that the #$CharacterString STRING is used to identify PERSON during CHAT. Typically STRING would be an alias for PERSON, but not always.")
(disjointWith Conveyance RoofOfAConstruction)
(disjointWith PhysicalDestructionEvent LocomotionEvent)
(comment PlaintextPasswordFileFault "#$PlaintextPasswordFileFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has a #$PlaintextPasswordFileFault if it stores passwords for accounts (system accounts or #$ApplicationAccounts) in a plaintext file. Important                                                                                  
specializations of #$PlaintextPasswordFileFault are #$PlaintextSystemPasswordFileFault and #$PlaintextApplicationPasswordFileFault.")
(comment valueOfNotesPayable "The sum of the balances remaining on loans and promissory notes incurred by the agent.")
(comment Visa-Document "A specialization of #$LegalDocument. Each instance of #$Visa-Document is a document issued by the government of some country to one (or more) person(s), authorizing that person (or those persons) to enter that country and remain for a certain period of time while engaging in certain specified activities (e.g., study, travel, work).")
(comment SingleSourceFn "A function, when applied to a #$BoundedDirectedPathSystem SYS as in (#$SingleSourceFn SYS), returns the unique source node X in SYS, i.e., the node in SYS that has only outward links.  Note that since SYS is a #$BoundedDirectedPathSystem, there can be no source node in SYS other than (#$SingleSourceFn SYS).  See also #$sourceNodeInSystem.")
(comment LiquidTangibleArtifact "The collection of all liquid artificial substances: teas, liquid petroleum derivatives, wood stain, liquid pait, etc.  If such a substance is frozen it is no longer a member of this collection.")
(comment Knickers "Loose fitting #$Pants that come down to the knees, gathered there with a button or elastic, etc.")
(comment madeBy "The predicate #$madeBy is used to indicate that a particular product was made by a particular company (or companies).  (#$madeBy PROD COMORG) means that PROD, an instance of #$Product, was made by the #$CommercialOrganization COMORG.  See also the predicate #$makesProductType.")
(comment UserRestrictionBypassFault "#$UserRestrictionBypassFault is a specialization of #$SecuritySoftwareBypassFault.  A program has this fault if it is possible to circumvent restrictions the software purports to make on the range of actions users are permitted to perform.")
(disjointWith CohabitationUnit GeopoliticalEntity)
(comment Col-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a column within a table.")
(comment softwareOnComputerHasFault "(#$softwareOnComputerHasFault SOFTWARE COMP FAULT) means that SOFTWARE, as it is installed and configured on COMP, manifests FAULT.")
(comment tastesThat "(#$tastesThat AGENT PROP) means that AGENT perceives, by sense of taste, that PROP is true.")
(comment NonPoweredDevice "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$NonPoweredDevice is a device which does not need to have any kind of energy supplied to it in order for it to perform its intended function. Examples of #$NonPoweredDevices include tables, floor mats, bookshelves, shirts, and coat hangars.  A hammer would not be an instance of #$NonPoweredDevice, since it requires kinetic energy to perform its intended function.")
(comment SMBServerProgram "#$SMBServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$ServerMessageBlockProtocol.")
(comment PlaintextTransmissionFault "The software fault of transmitting data in plaintext.")
(comment graphRepresentsType "This predicate specifies a relation between path systems and the kind of thing that the path system is intended to model.  It is possible that a path system be used or even intended to model more than one kind of thing, so the second argument is not #$SingleEntry. Similarly, types of things can be modelled by more than one path system so the first argument is not #$SingleEntry.  However, we should also be careful not to assume that paths represent genls of collection types that it represents.  For instance, if a graph represent a kind of communication event, it does not necessarily represent all more general kinds of communicating.")
(comment FileCreationFault "A program has this fault if a malicious user could exploit the program to create a file (most likely an executable).")
(comment EmbassyBuilding "The collection of all embassies, the buildings in which
official diplomatic representations are hosted. For the office itself
see #$Embassy-TheMission.")
(disjointWith HatBrim MainHatPart)
(comment DebuggerProgram "Programs used to aid in debugging applications, usually by providing useful information about errors.")
(comment VulnerableToTCP-IPParameterModification "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$TCP-IPParameterModificationFault on it.")
(comment MentalSituation-SingleSubject "A specialization of #$MentalSituation (q.v.) each
instance of which has a single agent (normally an 
#$IndividualAgent) as its \"subject\".  A subject in this sense
is an agent who has, undergoes, experiences, entertains, or 
performs the mental situation, as the case may be.  Instances 
of #$MentalSituation-SingleSubject can be mental _events_ (see 
#$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent) such as acts of perception or 
mental _states_ (see #$MentalState) such as Alice's loving Bob.  
This collection excludes any mental situations that have more 
than one subject, such as (perhaps) an event of mutual recognition 
between two people, as well as any mental situations that have 
no proper subject at all, such as (perhaps) an event of mass 
hysteria or a state involving the Jungian \"collective unconscious\".
It of course does not exclude a given mental situation merely 
because it happens to _involve_ more than one agent; Alice's 
loving Bob involves two people, but Alice is nevertheless its 
only subject. The two notable specializations of this collection are  #$IntentionalMentalSituation and #$StateOfUnconsciousness.")
(comment ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-RemoteAdministrator "#$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-Root is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A web server program has this fault when it allows unauthorized remote users access to the remote administrator account for the program.  This account may or may not have the full privileges of the administrator or root account the the system the program is running on.")
(comment DifferenceWRTPredicate "A collection of #$ComparisonWRTPredicates used to represent the respect in which two things are different. Predicates that represent that two things are different but do not represent the manner or respect in which they are different are excluded from #$DifferenceWRTPredicate. For example, #$different is not an instance of #$DifferenceWRTPredicate.  This collection can be used to constrain Asks designed to return assertions that represent known differences between two specified things. Cf. #$SimilarityWRTPredicate.")
(comment TajikistaniPerson "The collection of people who are #$citizens of  #$Tajikistan, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(comment accessibleFromInSystem "(#$accessibleFromInSystem X Y SYS) means that X is accessible from Y in the #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, which in turn means that either X = Y or there is a path PATH from Y to X in SYS, i.e., (#$pathFromToInSystem PATH Y X SYS) holds.  Note that if we fix a #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, the relation #$accessibleFromInSystem is reflexive and transitive (i.e., a quasi-order).  If we fix a #$BidirectedPathSystem SYS, this relation is an equivalence relation, the same as #$connectedInSystem.")
(comment PoweredDevice "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$PoweredDevice is a device that requires some power input in order to perform its intended function(s).  The power supplied might be muscle power, kinetic energy, electricity, fuel-generated, and so on.  Note that #$PoweredDevice and #$NonPoweredDevice partition the collection #$PhysicalDevice.")
(comment Kilt "The collection of pleated, wraparound #$Skirts traditionally worn by Scottish men.  #$Kilts are usually made of tartan cloth.")
(comment Need-Immediate "A collection of microtheories containing statements that describe a thing's immediate needs.")
(comment doRedirectDNS "(#$doRedirectDNS HACKER MANNER NS)  means that, in manner MANNER, HACKER exploits the functionality of a name server program in such a way that the program looking at the DNS table on NS directs traffic in a way other than intended by the designer of the network NS is on.  See also #$doRedirectDNSFrom.")
(disjointWith TwoDimensionalGeometricThing ThreeDimensionalGeometricThing)
(comment negativeInterest-Prop "(negativeInterest-Prop AGT PROP) means that AGT has a con-attitude towards PROP -- i.e., AGT has a negative interest in PROP being or becoming true. #$negativeInterest-Prop is a generalization of more specific con-attitude predicates such as #$embarrassed, #$fears, #$regrets. In contrast with #$desires and #$goals, #$negativeInterest-Prop is not strictly future-directed. An agent may have a negative interest in a proposition which already holds. Indeed, this is always the case with such backward-looking emotional attitudes such as #$embarrassed and #$regrets. It captures the sense in which these emotions involve a wishing that something that is the case not be so.")
(disjointWith ModernShelterConstruction Water)
(comment ActiveSubjectForRelnInArgFn "An instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  For any instance of #$Relation RELN of #$arity 0 through N+M, (#$ActiveSubjectForRelnInArgFn RELN N) will evaluate to COL, where 

(#$assertedSentence (#$argGenl RELN N COL)).  Otherwise, it will return COL, where 

(#$assertedSentence (#$argIsa RELN N COL)).")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfShellPathUnderspecification "A computer has this vulnerability if it runs an #$OperatingSystem with an #$NTShellPathUnderspecificationFault.")
(comment Chassis-VehiclePart "The collection of supporting frames for vehicles.")
(comment DivineBeing "The collection of all divinities, or supernatural beings that are gods, demi-gods, or otherwise god-like.  Instances of #$DivineBeing are believed to be immortal in some cultures.  Note that this collection is _not_ a specialization of #$Agent-Intangible, since some god-like beings are believed to have physical bodies.")
(comment SlabFoundation "Poured concrete slab on which the rest of the building rests.")
(comment Dress "#$Dress is a specialization of #$Clothing-WholeBody, #$WomensClothing, and #$EnvelopingCovering.  Each instance of #$Dress is an article of women's clothing that covers the upper and lower body, but which usually does not drape down to the feet.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfGlobalRootPrivileges "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a
#$GlobalRootPrivilegesFault on it.")
(comment programRunByOn "(#$programRunByOn PROG AGENT COMP) means that AGENT runs PROG on COMP.")
(comment InsecureTemporaryFilesFault "A program has this fault if it creates
  temporary files with sensitive information, which can then be accessed by an 
 unauthorized user, or if it somehow enables the creation of symlinks to other,
 sensitive files (see the more specific #$SymlinkFault).")
(comment RollingLogFile "The collection of rolling log files; i.e. files that discard old data to make room for new data.  Compare to #$FiniteLogFile.  Whether a file is rolling or not is typically controlled by the program that writes to it.")
(comment HeatingDevice "A specialization of #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$HeatingDevice is a device whose primary function (see the predicate #$primaryFunction) is to generate heat to raise the temperature of something else.  The thing being heated might be in gaseous form (for example, the air in a room), in liquid form (for example, the water in a pool), or in solid form (for example, food in an oven).  A given instance of #$HeatingDevice typically has some energy input, some way of converting that energy to heat, and some way of delivering the heat to the object(s) to be heated.")
(comment ExerciseClothing "Articles typically worn during some form of exercise.  Exercise clothing has some of its features designed to meet the needs of the exerciser (e.g., running shorts side-slashed for freedom of leg movements, absorbency of sweats, padded biking shorts, etc.).")
(comment CircumferenceFn "A unary function that returns an instance of #$Distance when given an instance of #$RoundShape as an argument.  (#$CircumferenceFn CIRCLE) denotes the distance that is the circumference of CIRCLE.")
(comment typicalInfectionRoute "(#$typicalInfectionRoute INFECTION-TYPE ORGANISM-TYPE
PART-TYPE) means that if an organism of type ORGANISM-TYPE is
penetrated by a pathogen capable of causing infections of type
INFECTION-TYPE via a physical part of the organism of the type
PART-TYPE, it is highly likely that the organism would contract an
infection of type INFECTION-TYPE caused by the invading pathogen,
unless the organism were already immune to infections of that type.")
(comment subGeneticInformation "(#$subGeneticInformation GI SUBGI) means that GI contains SUBGI,
where both GI and SUBGI are instances of #$GeneticInformation. For
instance, this relation holds between an instance of #$Genome-GenInfo
GENOME and an instance of #$Gene-GenInfo GENE (\"the information encoded by a
gene\"). The fact that GENOME contains GENE is expressed by
(#$subGeneticInformation GENOME GENE).")
(comment termStrings-Guessed "(#$termStrings-Guessed TERM PHRASE) indicates that Cyc TERM can be referred to by PHRASE. This is a specialization of #$termStrings, for use when the phrase has been guessed based on properties of the term, such as it's name. Note that this is not intended for general KE.")
(comment PropertyDeed "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$LegalDocument.  Each instance of #$PropertyDeed is a legal document that records an agent's ownership in some real property (that is, some instance of #$RealEstate).")
(disjointWith DoorwayCovering RoofOfAConstruction)
(disjointWith SeparationEvent LocomotionEvent)
(comment CycLNLAssertion "The collection of #$CycLAssertions whose main (i.e. arg0) operators denote #$NLPredicates.")
(comment WeaklyEncryptedApplicationPasswordFileFault "#$WeaklyEncryptedApplicationPasswordFileFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has a #$WeaklyEncryptedApplicationPasswordFileFault if it stores any passwords for its #$ApplicationAccounts in a weakly encrypted file.")
(comment CycProprietaryImageCollection "The collection of all visual image types which belong to the Cyc group, or to which the Cyc group has unlimited use rights.")
(comment PasswordProtectedMacroExecutionFault "A program has this fault if it (a) normally alerts users when they are about to open a file containing macros and (b) fails to do so when the file being opened is password protected.  This fault may be exploited by a macro virus to spread in password protected
 documents.")
(comment Div-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a division within a document.")
(comment eatsWillingly-Instance "This is intended as an instance-level counterpart of #$eatsWillingly, meaning that its second argument is an instance of a collection, rather than being a collection.")
(comment eMailMessageSent "(#$eMailMessageSent SENDING MESSAGE) says that MESSAGE is the instance of #$EMailMessage that is \"sent\" during SENDING, an instance of #$EMailSending.  When an instance of #$EMailMessage MESSAGE is \"sent,\" an instantiation of that message -- i.e., an instance COPY of #$ComputerFileCopy such that (#$fileCopies MESSAGE COPY) -- is filed into the recipients mailbox, or \"returned\" to the user, etc.")
(comment Pipe-ConduitArtifact "The collection of all manufactured enclosed tubular fluid conduits with openings at both ends.  The more general #$Pipe-GenericConduit encompasses both such manufactured pipes and natural pipes which are not instances of #$Pipe-ConduitArtifact, i.e. those found naturally occurring in the environment or in an organism's body, such as #$BloodVessels.")
(comment BauxiteOre "Bauxite ore - macroscopic quantities of the same.")
(comment SandyBeach "Beaches are sandy regions along the edge of a large body of water such as a river, a lake, or a sea.")
(comment PathSystemType-Model "This collection classifies path systems according to the kind of event or structured system that they are used to model as opposed to the structural features of the path system (see #$PathSystemType-Structural).  An example of an instance of this collection is #$ScriptGraph which is the collection of path systems used to model apects of  scripts and script types.")
(comment GeopoliticalRegion "The collection of geographical regions that are conventionally

defined by geopolitical treaties and in relation to geopolitical agents 

[#$GeopoliticalEntity] or as results of agreements among a certain number 

of such agents. Any region circumscribed by an instance of #$GeopoliticalBorder.

 This collection comprise the territory of a country, a notable specialization 

is #$TimeZone. See the sibling #$LocalGeopoliticalRegion for regions related to 

less than national and international entities.")
(comment Cabin "A collection of construction artifacts.  Each element of #$Cabin is a #$HumanResidence of a rustic nature, usually made primarily of wood.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedSystemLogAccess "A specialization of #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedAccess. A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible for users to gain access to files which audit/log the use of the system the computer is a part of (cf. #$ComputerAuditLogFile), when not authorised to do so. This could be because the computer has a program with a #$SystemLogAccessFault on it, or due to a faulty configuration. This vulnerability is to be distinguished from #$VulnerableToActivityLogBypass -- the ability to bring it about that activities are not logged when they should be. See also #$VulnerableToLogFileOverwrite.")
(comment GoingSomewhere "A very general set of events in which an animal goes somewhere.")
(comment AutomobileRunning "An automobile running.")
(disjointWith GroupActivity MentalSituation-SingleSubject)
(comment VirusScanBypassFault "A virus scanning program has this fault if there is a file on the scanned computer's directory where viruses will remain undetected.")
(comment SomeExampleFn "(#$SomeExampleFn COL) denotes a term which represents an indeterminate instance of COL for use in generating an example.  See also #$SomeExampleNumberFn.")
(comment AmateurPornStar "The collection of #$Persons that are amateur #$PornStars.")
(comment linkFromToInSystem "(#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SYS) means that SYS is a directed path system, (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) holds, and LINK is directed from X to Y in SYS (i.e., Y is accessible from X via LINK in SYS).  Note that each link in a semi-directed path system (see #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem) must be directed one way or the other or both, and each link in a directed path system (see #$DirectedPathSystem) must be directed one way or the other but not both, and each link in a bidirected path system (see #$BidirectedPathSystem) must be directed in both ways.")
(comment MeasuringDevice "#$MeasuringDevice is a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$MeasuringDevice is a device used for measuring some quantity such as #$Distance, #$Volume, #$Temperature, etc.  Specializations of #$MeasuringDevice include #$Thermometer, #$Scale-MeasuringDevice, and #$Odometer.)")
(comment SableCoat "The collection of fur coats made out of sable, the fur of the martes zibellina, a marten of north Asian forests having luxuriant dark brown fur.")
(comment subCultures-Friendly "This predicate is a specialization of #$subCultures that relates a culture to those of its subcultures with which it maintains a non-antagonistic, or even friendly, relationship. (#$subCultures-Friendly SUPERCULT SUBCULT) means that SUBCULT 

  is a specific form of SUPERCULT that is not antagonistic to SUPERCULT.")
(comment connectedByPathType "(#$connectedByPathType PATHTYPE THING1 THING2) means that there is some instance of PATHTYPE (where PATHTYPE is a specialization of both #$Path-Simple and #$PartiallyTangible) connecting (see #$pathConnects) THING1 and THING2.")
(comment SugarPhosphateBackbone "Instances of this collection form the backbones of the individual strands of polynucleotide molecules.")
(comment CGIFileAccessFault "A CGI script has this fault if it can be exploited to obtain remote access to files to which the web server running the CGI script has access.")
(comment JuninHemorrhagicFever "A specialization of #$HemorrhagicFeverInfection. Instances of #$JuninHemorrhagicFever are characterised by the gradual onset of malaise, headache, sustained fever progressing to hemorrhagic symptoms, including nose bleed, bloody vomit, and blood in stool or urine (as in its close cousin, #$Machupo, or Bolivian Hemorrhagic Fever). Also known as Argentinian Hemorrhagic Fever. ")
(comment LinksFn "For each #$PathSystem SYS, (#$LinksFn SYS) denotes the set of all links in SYS (see #$PathSystem).  Note that the function #$LinksFn and the predicate #$linkInSystem are interdefinable.  We normally use #$LinksFn, for convenience, when we consider some relations between different path systems even though for a single path system SYS, we can also replace each (#$linkInSystem X SYS) by (#$elementOf X (#$LinksFn SYS)).")
(comment PierAndBeamFoundation "Network of post and lintels on which the rest of the building rests.")
(disjointWith Dress ExerciseClothing)
(comment VulnerableToCoreDump "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$CoreDumpFault on it.")
(comment IncomingWRTLANFn "(#$IncomingWRTLANFn LAN) denotes the collection of all #$Packet-Internets that are incoming with respect to the

#$LocalAreaNetwork, LAN.  That is, it denotes the collection of

packets whose destination #$IPAddresses belong to machines on LAN, and whose source #$IPAddresses do not belong to machines on LAN.")
(comment SpoofableProxyFault "A program has a #$SpoofableProxyFault if it can be fooled into using or attempting to use a non-authorized server as a proxy server.  Attackers can exploit this fault to set up hostile machines as proxies.")
(comment ImperativeTemplate "This template category covers English imperative phrases.")
(comment Spool "The set of cylinder shaped objects whose primary purpose is
to have a #$CordlikeObject wound around them.")
(comment Tutu "The collection of short skirts worn by ballerinas.")
(comment structureEncodesGenInfo "(#$structureEncodesGenInfo GIS GI) means that the instance of
#$GeneticInformation GI is encoded in GIS, an instance of
#$GeneticInformationStructure. In other words, GI is the content of GIS.")
(comment surrounds-2D "This predicate describes situations in which one object surrounds
another in (at least) two dimensions.  More formally, if
(#$surrounds-2D SURROUNDER SURROUNDED), then there is an abstract
plane that cross-sections SURROUNDER and SURROUNDED.  In this plane,
the cross-section of SURROUNDER encircles the cross-section of
SURROUNDED.  Thus, any ray drawn from SURROUNDED in that plane
#$spatiallyIntersects SURROUNDER.  This is a generalization of
#$surroundsHorizontally (q.v.), the special case in which the planar
cross-section is defined by gravity.  Another specialization is
#$surrounds-3D, where SURROUNDER 'covers' SURROUNDED as well (e.g. a
baseball cap on someone's head).  See also #$surroundsCompletely.")
(comment OwnershipDocument "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType.  Each instance of #$OwnershipDocument is an official document that records an agent's ownership of some item. Examples of #$OfficialDocument include property deeds and certificates of ownership of automobiles.")
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess LocomotionEvent)
(comment WeaklyEncryptedSystemPasswordFileFault "#$WeaklyEncryptedSystemPasswordFileFault is an attribute of some instances of #$OperatingSystem. An operating system has a #$WeaklyEncryptedSystemPasswordFileFault if
 it stores any passwords for its #$LoginAccounts in a weakly encrypted file.")
(comment Negotiating "A specialization of #$SocialOccurrence and #$MultiDirectionalCommunication.  In each instance of this collection an #$IntelligentAgent communicates with another #$IntelligentAgent with the (ostensible) purpose of their reaching an #$Agreement. Two notable specializations of this collection are #$Bargaining and #$ContractNegotiation.")
(comment Tularemia-Bacterium "The subcollection of #$Bacterium instances of which causes #$Tularemia (q.v.).")
(comment RunningShorts "Shorts for running or jogging.")
(comment AutomaticHTMLAttachmentDownloadFault "A program has this fault if it automatically downloads HTML documents attached to email messages.")
(comment Dl-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a list of definitions.")
(comment DeterminingInterrelationship "The collection of events in which an intelligent animal (or machine) determines what the interrelationship between two or more things is.")
(comment tactuallyPerceivesThat "(#$tactuallyPerceivesThat AGENT PROP) means that AGENT perceives, by sense of touch, that PROP is true.")
(comment relyOnType "(#$relyOnType AGENT COL) means that AGENT relies on instances of the #$Collection COL for a significant part of AGENT's normal activities.  See #$relyOnObject and #$relyOnAgent.")
(comment GemStone "The collection of all #$Minerals which are traditionally cut and polished by skilled gem-cutters. #$GemStones have traditionally been used for ornamentation.")
(comment ScriptGraph "Instances of this collection are path systems designed to model complex scripts.  Usually the nodes of the graph will be event types and the directed links between the nodes model the temporal ordering or some other relevant ordering (e.g. causal dependence) of subevent within scripts of the type represented by the graph.")
(comment LandedSingleResidenceUnit "A collection of human residences.  Each element of #$SingleResidenceUnit is either a modern-style detached house, an apartment, or another instance of #$ModernHumanResidence designed to accomodate either a single person or a single family (i.e., instance of #$FamilyCohabitationUnit).  Usually, each element of #$SingleResidenceUnit has a unique mailing address.")
(comment Nest "The collection of all nests built by animals. #$NestForBirds and #$NestForBees are two major specializations of #$Nest")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfWeakAdministratorPasswordReset "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$WeakPasswordResetFault-Administrator on it.")
(comment DeviceRunningPartFn "#$DeviceRunningPartFn is a Cyc function and, more specifically, an #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  It is used to represent the particular instance of #$DeviceRunning which is associated with a particular transportation event.  (#$DeviceRunningPartFn TRANS) takes as its argument the #$TransportViaFn TRANS and returns an event (a #$subEvents of TRANS) which represents the functioning of the #$transporter in that #$Event.")
(disjointWith NuclearEvent MentalSituation-SingleSubject)
(disjointWith Ripping ShapeChangeWithoutLosingMaterial)
(comment providesServiceType "The agent ARG1 provides the type of service ARG2.")
(comment internalPowerSourceTypes "The type-level version of #$internalPowerSource.  (#$internalPowerSourceTypes DEVICETYPE SOURCETYPE) means that every instances of DEVICETYPE has an instance of SOURCETYPE as an #$internalPowerSource.")
(disjointWith SelfPoweredDevice RecordingOfWaveIBT)
(comment GrassSkirt "A subset of #$Skirt whose instances are made out of long blades of grass.  These are worn as part of traditional native Hawaiian dress.")
(comment PredictableInitialTCPSequenceNumbersFault "A program has a #$PredictableInitialTCPSequenceNumbersFault
if there is insufficient variance in the range of likely ISN values
allowing an attacker to disrupt or hijack existing TCP connections or
spoof future connections against vulnerable TCP/IP stack
implementations.")
(comment dislikesType "(#$dislikesType AGENT COL) means that when the sentient agent AGT is interacting in some way with an instance of COL, that agent feels some measure of #$Dislike --- that is, (#$feelsEmotion AGT #$Dislike). The kinds of interactions that produce #$Dislike depend largely on what kind of thing OBJ is.  See #$dislikesObject, #$dislikesType.")
(comment functionAs "(#$functionAs OBJ TYPE) means that although OBJ is not an instance of TYPE, it is #$behaviorCapable of playing a role in a situation that TYPE is #$typeIntendedBehaviorCapable of playing.")
(comment traversalFrom "(#$traversalFrom TRAV POINT) means that POINT is a starting point of the #$Traversal TRAV along some paths.")
(disjointWith PathArtifactSystem Tower)
(comment linkBetween-IntermedPredicate "Intermediate predicate: (#$linkBetween-IntermedPredicate X Y Z) iff
X is something that establishes a link -- of underspecified nature --
between Y and Z.")
(comment InstitutionalTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections, a specialization of
#$CulturalTerrainFeatureType. Instances of
#$InstitutionalTerrainFeatureType are collections of objects, structures or
complex objects composed of several structures that are operated by some
institutional agent or under the control of some government. One way of
partitioning further this collection type could be to consider the type of
institution on which features depend. In the military context, the relevant
instances of this collection-type are for instance the collections of
artillery batteries, forts and other features under the control of some
military organization.")
(comment territoryOf "This predicate corresponds to the function #$TerritoryFn.  (#$territoryOf GEO-AGT TERRITORY) means that the complete planetary region [see #$GeographicalRegion] occupied by and considered part of the instance GEO-AGT of #$GeographicalAgent is the instance TERRITORY of #$GeographicalRegion.  This applies solely to the region that is considered ``part of'' GEO-AGENT, excluding colonies, trust territories, or territories occupied by GEO-AGENT's military, but which are the territory of some other country.  #$territoryOf will specify different regions in different microtheories for countries which have territorial disputes with their neighbors.  For more information see #$TerritoryFn.")
(comment JapaneseEncephalitisVirus "The virus that causes #$JapaneseEncephalitis.")
(comment Tree-PathSystem "The collection of all those #$ConnectedPathSystems that look like trees, i.e., those #$ConnectedPathSystems that have no #$Path-Cyclics at all.  Note that since each instance of #$Tree-PathSystem has no cycles in it, it has no loops, nor multiple links between two nodes.")
(comment BasementStyleFoundation "Poured concrete sides of a basement upon which the rest of the building rests.")
(disjointWith Dress BodySuit)
(comment ConcealingFromSight "This is the collection of events in which an animal conceals an object from the line of sight of another animal.  For instance, a squirrel staying on the opposite side of a tree trunk, a robber

donning a mask, and a pirate burying a treasure.  Note that no animal needs to be looking at the hidden object at the moment that it is hidden for an instance of this collection to occur.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedDLLUpload "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$UnauthorizedDLLUploadFault on it.")
(comment PersonWithLatentPedophilia "The collection of all #$Persons that see children as sexual
objects without acting upon those desires. See also
#$ChildMolester to describe the person that does act on those fantasies.")
(comment softwareObjectUsesLibrary "(#$softwareObjectUsesLibrary SOBJ LIB) means that to function properly, instances of SOBJ installed and running on a computer must call at least one subroutine in LIB.")
(disjointWith Device-UserPowered AnimalPoweredDevice)
(comment SurgicalGlove "The rubber gloves worn by medical professionals to reduce the likelihood of spreading infections.")
(comment SmartCard "A specialization of #$IDDocument.  Each instance of #$SmartCard is a credit-card sized plastic card containing one or more semiconductor chips.  Instances of #$SmartCard include some credit cards, as well as some health insurance cards.")
(disjointWith LevelOfAConstruction Stairwell)
(comment GlobalRootPrivilegesFault "An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if there is some danger of its being unwittingly configured so as to give all users root privileges.")
(comment ContractNegotiation "A specialization of #$Negotiating, Each instance of this collection is a negotiation which leads to the formation of a #$Contract -- either between the participants or between the parties they represent in the negotiations. See also the more specialized #$SalesContractNegotiation.")
(comment UnversionedSoftwareObject "The collection of all #$SoftwareObjects which are unversioned and are therfore highly abstract entities.  Positive examples: #$NetscapeNavigator, #$Libc-TheLibrary.  Negative examples: (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Libc-TheLibrary \"2.0\"), (#$VersionsInclusiveFn #$NetscapeNavigator \"3\" \"6\").")
(comment Tularemia "A bacterial disease associated with both animals and man. The rabbit is most often involved in disease outbreaks. If caused by insect bites, early symptoms include ulceration at the bite location with swelling of the regional lymph node. If caused by ingestion of the bacterium, produces throat and abdominal pain with diarrhea and vomiting. If caused by inhalation of the bacterium, produces pneumonia.")
(comment linkCutSetInSystem "(#$linkCutSetInSystem SET SYS) means that the set SET of links in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS is a link-cut set in SYS, i.e., SET is a subset of (#$LinksFn SYS) such that cutting of all links in SET from SYS results in a disconnected path system.  More strictly, to say that SET is a link-cut set in SYS, we mean that (#$LinksCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET) is not a #$ConnectedPathSystem.  Note that when (#$linkCutSetInSystem SET SYS) holds, there could be some proper subset SUBSET of SET such that (#$linkCutSetInSystem SUBSET SYS) also holds.  If you want a minimal link-cut set, without redundant links, use #$linkCutMinimalSetInSystem instead of #$linkCutSetInSystem.")
(comment PalaceBuilding "palace-HistoricConstruction, castles, chateaux!")
(comment programInSeriesUsesLibrary "(#$programInSeriesUsesLibrary PROG-SERIES LIB) means that programs in the series PROG-SERIES call at least one subroutine in LIB.")
(comment Dt-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a term that is defined within a list of definitions (see #$Dl-HTMLTag).")
(comment DistilledWater "#$Water purified by distillation.  Despite the distillation, there may still be some impurities remaining.  Thus, #$DistilledWater is largely but not 100% (#$PureFn #$Water). ")
(comment pathInsideRegion "This predicate relates spatial paths to spatial regions that completely contain them.  (#$pathInsideRegion PATH REGION) means that the whole of PATH is in REGION.  As a limiting case, one or both of PATH's #$endsOfPathSegments might be at the border of REGION, but neither may be outside it.")
(comment FullBath "A room with both a toilet and a bathtub or shower.")
(comment VulnerableToProgramSlowing "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$ProgramSlowingFault on it.")
(comment CleaningFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an agent cleans some object.")
(comment Companionship-Feeling "The collection of feelings of comradery, companionship")
(comment CompleteRunOfAnEngine "The engine starting up, running awhile and then stopping. Very eventType like. Does not include a random time slice of a device running (like a small perriod of it running")
(disjointWith SocialGathering MentalSituation-SingleSubject)
(comment SymlinkFault-Execute "A program has a #$SymlinkFault-Execute if when running it creates files with predictable filenames and permissive execute permissions in the /tmp directory.  This fault allows a user to create a file in the /tmp directory with the same name and then symlink it to another file to which the user does not have execute permission.")
(comment Teaching "One agent imparting learned knowledge to another.  This may have #$subEvents of the student asking or responding to questions, but the teacher is the primary performer.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice OpticalDevice)
(comment Coat-Chesterfield "#$Coat-Chesterfield is a collection of Chesterfield coats--fitted overcoats with collars made of #$VelvetCloth.")
(comment Need-LongTerm "A collection of microtheories containing statements that describe a thing's long-term needs.")
(comment eMailDataOfTypeToAccountsOfUsersOfSystem "(#$eMailDataOfTypeToAccountsOfUsersOfSystem AGENT DATA-TYPE SYSTEM) means that AGENT emails data of DATA-TYPE to the accounts of users on SYSTEM.")
(comment subCultures-Unfriendly "This predicate is a specialization of #$subCultures that relates a culture to those of its subcultures with which it maintains an unfriendly or antagonistic relationship. (#$subCultures-Friendly SUPERCULT SUBCULT) means that SUBCULT is a specific form of SUPERCULT that is  antagonistic to SUPERCULT.  For example, the 1960s counterculture in the US was an unfriendly subculture of the mainstream ''establishment''.")
(comment ApplyingForSomething "This is the collection of actions in which an agent applies for something--for example, a job, a loan.  Applying is a fairly formal request, usually involving paperwork such as filling out an application form. For specializations of this collection, see the function #$ApplyingForFn.")
(comment EMailReceiving "The collection of #$Events in which an e-mail message is pulled down from a #$MailServer-Network by the recipient's #$EMailClientProgram.")
(comment PortDenialOfServiceFault "A program/OS has this fault if it can be forced into a state in which certain ports are rendered useless.")
(comment JapaneseEncephalitis "A form of #$EncephalitisInfection. Symptoms range from mild fever and headache to high fever, headache, stupor, tremors, coma and spastic paralysis.")
(disjointWith Weapon SomethingToWear)
(comment VulnerableToActivityMonitoring "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$ActivityMonitoringFault on it.")
(comment SourceIPFn "(#$SourceIPFn IP_ADDRESS) denotes the collection of #$Packet-Internets whose source is the machine indicated by IP_ADDRESS.  For example, (#$SourceIPFn \"234.234.34.2\") denotes the collection of all packets whose source IP address is 234.234.34.2.")
(comment LevantCountry "The collection of nation-states of the Middle East that border the Eastern end of the Mediterranean Sea.")
(comment ContentFilteringBypassFault "A content filtering program has this fault if it is possible for users to circumvent the filtering and visit restricted web sites.")
(comment Skullcap "a small tight-fitting cap.  Aka yarmulke")
(comment structureEncodesGenInfo-Exactly "(#$structureEncodesGenInfo-Exactly GIS G-INFO) means that GIS
is an abstract structure encoding exactly G-INFO. It may be the case that
GIS encodes many pieces of genetic information; this predicate gives a
measure of how optimal this encoding can be. For instance, any instance of
#$Gene-GIS encodes exactly one instance of #$Gene-GenInfo. On the other
hand, the same #$Gene-GIS is composed of a certain number of subsequences
that are instances of #$Codon-GIS, and thus it will encode all of the
genetic information encoded by these subsequences. An instance of
#$Genome-GIS may contains sub-parts that encode a plurality of instances of
#$Gene-GenInfo; however, there is a functional relation with the instance
of #$Genome-GenInfo that contains all and only those abstract genes as
#$subGeneticInformation.")
(comment IMAPServerProgram "#$IMAPServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$InternetMessageAccessProtocol (IMAP).")
(comment genericPathway-Exact "For those transfers in which the item transferred follows some spatial path, this predicate allows representation of the relation between the transfer and the single path followed by the item in that transfer.  More formally, (#$genericPathway-Exact TRANS PATH)

means that the route of the instance TRANS of #$GeneralizedTransfer

is spatial and the #$transferredThing follows the complete instance PATH of #$Path-Spatial throughout all of TRANS.  Thus, any #$genericPathway-Exact of an instance TRANS of #$GeneralizedTransfer has the \"starting\" and \"stopping\" points, the #$from-Generic and the #$to-Generic, of TRANS as its endpoints.  The instance PATH of #$Path-Spatial may not extend beyond these \"starting\" and \"stopping\" points (use #$genericPathway-Complete for that meaning).  See also #$infoPathway-Exact and #$motionPathway-Exact; it is usually better to use one of these more specific predicates.  Another related predicate is #$genericPathway-Partial.")
(disjointWith Closet LevelOfAConstruction)
(disjointWith ChangeInUserRights LocomotionEvent)
(comment negationInverseWRTTypes "(#$negationInverseWRTTypes BINPRED1 BINPRED2 COL1 COL2) means that if (BINPRED1 INS1 INS2) where INS1 is an instance of COL1 and INS2 is an instance of COL2, then (#$not (BINPRED2 INS2 INS1)).  This allows us to specify a pseudo-negationPreds relationship between two #$BinaryPredicates when their arguments are of the appropriate types.  At a more specific level, #$negationInverseWRTTypes can serve as a useful rule macro predicate.  See also #$genlPredsWRTTypes, #$genlInverseWRTTypes, and #$negationPredsWRTTypes.")
(comment KFDInternalKRTerm "The collection of Cyc terms used internally by Cyc to reason about the UIA knowledge entry process. Only UIA-specific terms should be made instances of this collection -- terms relevant to KR and KE processes in general do not belong in this collection.")
(comment DirectoryAccessFault "#$DirectoryAccessFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program (usually a web server program) has a #$DirectoryAccessFault if it allows an attacker to determine whether files exist in a directory, either by traversing the directory (as when the program has a #$DirectoryTraversalFault), or by searching for a particular file by name (as when the program has a #$DirectoryProbingFault).")
(comment FederalTaxExpenseAccount "An account for the money which goes for paying federal taxes.")
(comment Diagnosing "A collection of processes; a subset of #$Evaluating.  Each element of #$Diagnosing is an activity in which an agent figures out what is wrong with something.  After a successful diagnosing, the performer has specific information about a discrepancy between the current state of the thing being diagnosed and the description it is supposed to match.  ")
(disjointWith UnversionedSoftwareObject VersionedSoftwareObject)
(comment TrenchFever-Bacterium "The bacterium (rickettsia, to be more precise) that causes #$TrenchFever.")
(comment OfficeBuilding "The collection of `modern' office buildings")
(comment WomensClothing "A specialization of #$Clothing-Generic.  Each specialization of #$WomensClothing is a type of clothing item worn usually by women.  Specializations of #$WomensClothing include #$Bra, #$Dress, and #$Skirt.")
(comment AttachmentFilteringBypassFault "A program has this fault if its attachment-filtering security mechanisms do not function properly.")
(comment Dd-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify the definition of a term defined in a list of definitions.")
(comment PolynucleotideStrandTrimming "Cutting of a polynucleotide strand at some point in the its nucleotide sequence.")
(comment mindsEvent "(#$mindsEvent ANIMAL EVENT) means that when the sentient animal ANIMAL finds EVENT to be a minor irritant.")
(comment GalvanizedMetal "#$Iron or steel which has been plated with #$Zinc.  You can only plate something if it is solid, thus liquid or gaseous galvanized steel can not exist, it can only be in the solid state.")
(comment DenyConnectionFault "#$DenyConnectionFault is a fault of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A server program has this fault if a malicious user can connect to the program and make the case that other users cannot also connect to it, creating a denial of service condition.")
(comment Diamond-Gem "A #$PreciousStone made by cutting and polishing a chunk of #$Diamond. #$Diamond-Gems vary in color, but are always translucent. Colorless #$Diamond-Gems are considered to be the best.")
(comment counterClockwise "(#$counterClockwise POINT-1 POINT-2 POINT-3) means that the
straight line traversal originating at POINT-1, passing through
POINT-2, and terminating at POINT-3 is in the counterclockwise
direction.")
(comment pathIntersectsRegion "This predicate relates spatial paths to the spatial regions they intersect. (#$pathIntersectsRegion PATH REGION) means that some segment of PATH is in REGION.  More precisely, there is some #$subPaths SUBPATH of PATH such that SUBPATH is #$pathInsideRegion REGION.  PATH might be wholly contained in REGION or might continue beyond REGION in one or both directions.(Note that it is possible in principle for a path to #$spatiallyIntersects a region and yet not be related to it by #$pathIntersectsRegion, say if only part of the edge of the path overlaps the region.)  For more specific predicates, see #$pathIntoRegion, #$pathInsideRegion, #$pathThroughRegion, #$pathPassesThroughRegion, #$pathEndsInRegion, and #$pathDividesRegion.")
(comment Penthouse "An #$ApartmentUnit or #$HotelRoomUnit on the top floor of a building. Such room-units usually rent/sell for a premium, since they can possess extraordinary views of the surrounding cityscape. Note that it makes little or no sense to call a room a  #$Penthouse if it is on the top floor of a single-storey, or low-storeyed, building.")
(comment InstantMessengerProgram "The collection of programs that enable users to take advantage of instant messenger sevices.")
(comment programInitialized "(#$programInitialized INIT PROG) says that PROG is the program initialized during INIT.  (#$programInitialized INIT PROG) entails the existence of a #$ComputerProgramCopy COPY such that (#$programCopies PROG COPY) and (#$programCopyInitialized INIT COPY).")
(comment displaysValue "(#$displaysValue DEVICE VALUE) means that #$PhysicalDevice DEVICE displays a reading of VALUE.")
(comment VulnerableToMountRequestForwarding "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$MountRequestForwardingFault on it.")
(comment physiologicalConditionAffects "(#$physiologicalConditionAffects CONDITION ORGANISM) means that ORGANISM has the physiological condition CONDITION.  See also #$hasPhysiologicalConditionType.")
(comment RoadwayJunction "The collection of junctions of instances of 

#$Roadway. Two important (non disjoint) specs are #$Intersection-Street (the collection of 

intersections of roadways in named urban areas) and #$RoadwayJunction-Primary 

(the collection of intersections of primary roads, see #$Primary-RoadClassification).")
(comment ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Administrator "#$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Administrator is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Administrator when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to create arbitrary files with adminstrator privilege.")
(comment ComputerKeyboardTyping "Typing using a computer or word processor keyboard.")
(disjointWith PlantingAField MentalSituation-SingleSubject)
(comment PacketMishandlingFault "An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if a remote attacker can cause the OS to crash by sending it (malformed) packets from a remote client.")
(comment WorldWideWebSearcher "The collection of #$ComputerUsers that search the web, whether human or programs themselves.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice Weapon)
(comment Corset "A type of #$WomensClothing worn before the advent of the #$Bra as an undergarment.  #$Corsets are worn some today, but not as part of normal clothing.  #$Corsets fit very tightly around the torso.")
(disjointWith CalendarCoveringType SpatialThingTypeByShape)
(comment infoPathway-Exact "(#$infoPathway-Exact TRANS PATH) indicates that the instance of #$InformationBearingThing transferred in some instance of #$InformationTransferEvent follows, throughout the entire transfer, the whole of PATH, an instance of #$Path-Spatial.  (#$infoPathway-Complete TRANS PATH) means that PATH is the entire ``route'' of TRANS and is spatial.  By definition, any #$infoPathway-Exact of an instance ITE of #$InformationTransferEvent connects the ``starting'' and ``stopping'' points (the #$informationOrigin and #$informationDestination) of all of ITE (See #$pathConnects). See also #$infoPathway-Complete and #$infoPathway-Partial.")
(comment ProxyServerProgram "#$ProxyServerProgram is the collection of programs written to store data on a system closer to the requesting site than to the source.")
(comment translationAlong "(#$translationAlong MOVE TRAV) means that the object OBJ in the Translation-SingleTrajectory MOVE moves along the #$Traversal TRAV.  This predicate is exactly like #$translationAlongWithinDistance, but with \"distance\" unspecified.  It is used when the distance between OBJ and TRAV is unknown or ignored. Note that whenever (#$translationAlongWithinDistance MOVE TRAV DIST) holds, so does (#$translationAlong MOVE TRAV).")
(disjointWith SheetOfSomeStuff Tower)
(comment resultIsaArgIsaType "(#$resultIsaArgIsaType FUNC N COL-TYPE) means that the NAT resulting from a use of FUNC is a member of the same collections that the term in arg N is a member of, where these collections are constrained to be members of the collection type COL-TYPE. For example: (#$resultIsaArgIsaType #$MotherFn 1 #$BiologicalTaxon) means that if CHILD is  an instances of TAXON which is an instance of #$BiologicalTaxon, then (#$MotherFn CHILD) is also an instance of TAXON.  But #$resultIsaArgIsa won't do because the mother won't be a member of *all* of the collections that her child will be a member of, e.g. #$MaleAnimal or #$Mule. In this case we need to make a #$resultIsaArgIsaType assertion to constrain the resulting NAT to be a member of a specific subset of the collections the child is a member of, in this case, those that are instances of #$BiologicalTaxon. Then, if (#$isa CHILD #$EquineAnimal), (#$isa (MotherFn CHILD) #$EquineAnimal) as well.")
(comment RepairingFn "This function can be used to denote the set of events in which an agent diagnoses and repairs some object.")
(comment HistoplasmaCapsulatum "The fungus that causes #$Histoplasmosis.")
(comment Darkroom "A room which can easily be shut off from outside light, usually lit with red light, containing special equipment with which to develop photographs.")
(disjointWith ProtectiveAttire NavigationDevice)
(comment VulnerableToDataCorruption "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$DataCorruptionFault on it.")
(comment ChildMolestation "The collection of all #$ChildSexualAbuse that involves
direct and invasive contact.")
(comment Staff "A collection of instances of #$Person, a spec of #$Group.  To be a staff is to be an organization of employees of an organization.")
(comment VikingHat "The collection of stereotypical Viking helms with two horns stiking out of it.  Invented in the 19th century for use as an operatic costume.")
(comment cultureArtifacts "This predicate relates cultures to types of artifacts

  that are characteristic of them and important to their participants.

  (#$cultureArtifacts CULTURE ARTIFACT) means that instances of 

  ARTIFACT are commonly found among, used by, and quite possibly created by

  (see #$cultureArtifacts-Domestic) participants in CULTURE.  ARTIFACT might

  be something created for

  either practical, recreational, religious, or aesthetic purposes.  See also

  #$cultureArtifacts-Significant.")
(comment providesResourceTo "(#$providesResourceTo GIVER RESOURCE RECEIVER) means that RESOURCE is useful to RECEIVER in some action, and GIVER provides that RESOURCE to that  RECEIVER. Positive examples include: rain providing mosquitoes with puddles, a parent providing a child with an allowance, a massage therapist providing a client with a masssage, and a scientist providing people with an explanation of phenomena.")
(comment IMAPServer-Network "A subcollection of #$ComputerServer, whose instances function as IMAP servers for instances of #$ComputerNetwork.")
(disjointWith RoomInAConstruction Portal)
(disjointWith IntrinsicStateChangeEvent LocomotionEvent)
(comment SecuritySoftwareBypassFault "#$SecuritySoftwareBypassFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if there are documented ways to circumvent the security features of the program (such as its filtering, hardening, or authentication methods), allowing an attacker to perform malicious actions despite the use of the program.")
(comment DirectoryProbingFault "#$DirectoryProbingFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program (usually a web server program) has a #$DirectoryProbingFault if it allows an attacker to determine whether specific files exist in a directory.  This is less threatening than a #$DirectoryTraversalFault, which allows attackers to see entire directories.")
(comment Contract "A collection of agreements.  Each instance of #$Contract is a legal agreement in which two or more #$agreeingAgents promise to do (or not do) something.  There are legal consequences to breaking the promises made in a contract.")
(comment TrenchFever "Symptoms of this illness include fever with pain and soreness in muscles, bones and joints. May produce a transient macular rash. Symptoms may continue to reappear years after the primary infection. First discovered in 1915, it reached epidemic proportions on the Western Front, but then suddenly disappeared when World War 1 ended. It was again reported during World War 2, when it affected thousands of German soldiers on the Russian Front, but it is now exceedingly rare.")
(comment ClothingItem "A specialization of #$Clothing-Generic.  Each instance of #$ClothingItem is something that a person wears as a protective and/or decorative covering or ornament.  Items of clothing are usually made of flexible materials, such as cloth, leather, or yarn.  The collection #$ClothingItem contains primarily individual garments (e.g., instances of the collections #$Pants, #$Shirt, #$Coat, #$Shoe), together with pairs of shoes, socks, and gloves (since each wearer needs a pair).  Jewelry, suspenders, belts, etc., are in the specialization #$ClothingAccessory.

Note: outfits (esp. specialized outfits) made up of several individual items worn together belong to the collection #$ClothingOutfit, which is _not_ a specialization of #$ClothingItem but _is_ a specialization of the broader collection, #$SomethingToWear.")
(comment VulnerableToAuthenticationSoftwareBypass "#$VulnerableToAuthenticationSoftwareBypass is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible to bypass an authentication procedure that software running on the computer is supposed to implement.")
(comment PuttingBallInPlay "The collection of events in which a continuous action portion [#$subEvents] of a #$GameEvent is started by a ball (or similar object) being put in motion.  This collection includes pitches in baseball, serves in squash, kickoffs and hikes in American football, balls being tossed in from out of bounds in basketball or ultimate, face-offs in ice hockey, etc.")
(comment SomeExampleSpecFn "(#$SomeExampleSpecFn COL) denotes a term which represents an indeterminate spec of COL for use in generating an example.  See also #$SomeExampleFn.")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByEthnicity HumanTypeByLifeStageType)
(comment Dfn-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify text that defines a term (not contained within a definition list).  For definitions contained within definition lists, see #$Dd-HTMLTag.")
(comment typicalGenderOfOccupationType "(#$typicalGenderOfOccupationType OCCTYPE GENDER) says that typically, instances INS of OCCTYPE are such that (#$hasGender INS GENDER).")
(comment resultantThought "(#$resultantThought MENTAL_EVENT SENTENCE) means that as a result of MENTAL_EVENT, an instance of #$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent, the thinker is thinking about [#$awareOf] the formula, SENTENCE, and was not thinking about SENTENCE before.  However the thinker does not necessarily believe [#$beliefs] that it is true.")
(comment Bronze-Stuff "The stuff bronze -- the alloy of copper and tin.")
(comment vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString "#$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString is used to specify the general format of the URL string for reports of faults and vulnerabilities in on-line databases.  To generate an actual URL, it should be the case that all that need be added to the string are characters that map to the ID string for the fault or vulnerability.  For example, \"http://www.cert.org/advisories/~A.html \" is an appropriate #$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString for #$CERTAdvisoryDatabase because, to generate the URL for a CERT entry, it is necessary only to substitute the ID of the fault (say, \"CA-2000-13\") for the occurrence of \"~A\" in the #$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString to generate the appropriate URL (\"http://www.cert.org/advisories/CA-2000-13.html \").  Similarly, \"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/~A \" is an appropriate #$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString for #$BugtraqFaultDatabase because it is necessary only to substitute the ID of the fault (say \"219\") for the occurrence of \"~A\" in the #$vulnerabilityDatabaseURLFormatString to generate the appropriate URL (\"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/219 \").")
(comment Ruby-Gem "#$PreciousStones which are red in color and translucent.")
(comment clockwise "(#$clockwise POINT-1 POINT-2 POINT-3) means that the

straight line traversal originating at POINT-1, passing through

POINT-2, and terminating at POINT-3 is in the clockwise direction.

Equivalently, the straight line traversal originating at POINT-2,

passing through POINT-1, and terminating at POINT-3 is in the

counterclockwise direction.  Consequently, this predicate is an

#$ELRelation with #$expansion (#$counterClockwise POINT-2 POINT-1

POINT-3).")
(comment Ziggurat "The collection of all monumental pyramids that are created as a stepped and tiered structure, one that gradually recedes toward an alter or some dwelling structure at its apex. #$Ziggurats are found in Mesopotamia and the Americas, and contrast primarily with the #$EgyptianPyramids because the most famous examples of the latter were constructed with stone 'skins' to give them a smooth, non-tiered appearance. In many cases this skin has now deteriorated, causing many #$EgyptianPyramids to resemble #$Ziggurats.")
(comment VulnerableToDeviceDriverCrashing "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$DeviceDriverCrashingFault on it.")
(disjointWith Dock RoadwayJunction)
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedAdministratorAccess "A computer has this vulnerability if it allows an unauthorized user to access an administrator account.  When remotely exploitable, it is a consequence of an #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-RemoteAdministrator  When locally exploitable, it is typically a consequence of an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Administrator.")
(comment Typing "The act of pressing a bunch of buttons in a sequence like typing on a keyboard or a typewriter or cash register etc. Requires at least one hand.")
(comment LoginMishandlingFault "An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if it fails to handle malformed logins (e.g., extremely long username entries) appropriately and can be caused to crash.")
(comment mountDirectoryContainingFileLocally "(#$mountDirectoryContainingFileLocally AGENT FILE) means that AGENT locally mounts the directory containing FILE.")
(comment Semi-DirectedPathSystem "An instance of #$PathSystemType-Structural and a subcollection of #$PathSystem.  Each instance of #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem is a path system SYS in which every link LINK is given at least one direction (specified by (#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SYS)), and in which every loop is given two directions (so in a sense we can ignore the directions of loops).  The directions of paths and non-loop-cycles (if there are any) in SYS are determined by the directions of links in SYS.  When designing a particular semi-directed path system, it is convenient to create a constant for the system (say SYS1) and to assert that it is an instance of #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem (#$isa SYS1 #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem)). One can then create a constant for each node (such as Node1) in the system, and a constant for each link (such as LinkA) in the system (using (#$isa LinkA #$Path-Simple)), and then assert the directions of links using #$linkFromToInSystem (e.g., (#$linkFromToInSystem LinkA Node1 Node2 SYS1)).  The axioms for #$linkFromToInSystem will allow one to infer other assertions, such as those involving #$pointOnPath, #$linkBetweenInSystem, #$nodeInSystem, and #$linkInSystem.  One can then proceed creating loops, isolated points, and extra points on links, if they are desired.")
(comment MusclePoweredDevice "#$MusclePoweredDevice is a specialization of #$KineticEnergyPoweredDevice. Each instance of #$MusclePoweredDevice is a device which is powered by animal muscle power (including human labor).  Specializations of #$MusclePoweredDevice include #$Wagon, #$Bicycle, and #$Canoe.")
(comment Poncho "#$Poncho is a collection, instances of which typically are squares of heavy #$Cloth with a central opening for the head of the wearer.  The edges drape over the arms and often to midthigh.")
(comment TradingDepartment "Each instance of #$TradingDepartment consists of employees who are responsible for an organization's trading - buying, selling financial instruments.")
(comment dataMtTheory "(#$dataMtTheory DATAMT THEORYMT) means that DATAMT is a #$DataMicrotheory which contains assertions about instances of #$SomethingExisting for which THEORYMT is the #$TheoryMicrotheory.  This is the relationship between #$UniverseDataMt and #$UniverseGeneralMt.")
(disjointWith IDStringType SpatialThingTypeByShape)
(comment blockedPath "(#$blockedPath SITUATION PATH) means that PATH is blocked in SITUATION:  Some instance of #$PartiallyTangible obstructs PATH, so that (the usual or expected type of) movement along PATH cannot occur. SITUATION must be a #$BarrierSituation, and PATH must be a #$Path-Customary.  See also:  #$barrier, #$motionPathway-Partial, #$pathState.")
(comment Workplace "#$Workplace is a specialization of #$PhysicalContactLocation.  Each instance of #$Workplace is a place where people customarily work.  #$Workplace includes as instances offices, restaurant buildings, construction sites, agricultural sites, the #$SpaceNeedle, and so on.  Some places may be #$Workplaces only during a small part of their existence (a piece of residential property while the house is being built, for example); some may almost always be #$Workplaces (grocery store buildings, office buildings, smithies, hospitals, and so on.).")
(comment ChatClientProgram "The collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are used in #$OnlineChat #$Events.")
(comment transportsFromTo "Agent A transports thing B from some location C to some location

D.")
(comment PollutionProcess "The process by which something is polluted-- made impure or contaminated.  This includes air pollution, water pollution, noise pollution, etc.")
(comment Histoplasmosis "Cases of this fungal infection may be asymptomatic, mild (general malaise, fever, chills, headache, muscle and/or chest pain), or disseminated (debilitating fever, gastric symptoms, infection of the lymph system - often fatal without treatment).")
(comment SolidSurfaceTrajectoryThroughAir "The collection of all trajectories of motions that pass through air along a solid surface.  Any #$objectMoving following such a #$Trajectory (see #$trajectory-Partial) is immersed in the air but supported by the solid surface.  Examples: a person walking on a sidewalk, or a bug crawling up a wall.")
(comment PhotographyStudio "The collection of rooms in an HOC where subjects are photographed.")
(disjointWith Hat Tie-Clothing)
(comment FileArchivingProgram "The collection of programs that store  and

extract  files  from an archive.")
(comment SourcePortFn "(#$SourcePortFn PROTOCOL PORT) denotes the collection of all #$Packet-Internets that list PROTOCOL as their #$NetworkProtocol (i.e., TCP or UDP) in the IP header and list PORT as their source port in the PROTOCOL-specific header.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam Staff)
(comment MedicalUniform "The sort of outfit worn by doctors and nurses when on duty - a.k.a. scrub uniforms")
(comment touchesWith "(#$touchesWith AGENT OBJECT2 OBJECT3) means that AGENT touches OBJECT2 with OBJECT3. This implies (#$touches AGENT OBJECT3) and (#$touches OBJECT2 OBJECT3), but not (#$touches AGENT OBJECT2): AGENT may or not be touching OBJECT2 in the sense of #$touches. For example, if #$Zaiss touches POSSUM45 with the end of long STICK87, opposite to the end he is holding, then although (#$touchesWith #$Zaiss POSSUM45 STICK87), it is not the case the (#$touches #$Zaiss POSSUM45). Whereas if #$Zaiss touches POSSUM45 with his hand, or with a gloved hand, then it is true that (#$touches #$Zaiss POSSUM45) (see the comment of #$touches).")
(comment POP3Server-Network "A subcollection of #$ComputerServer, whose instances function as POP3 servers for instances of #$ComputerNetwork.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction Quarry)
(disjointWith Communicating LocomotionEvent)
(comment CycLNLPragmaticAssertion "The collection of #$CycLAssertions whose main (i.e. arg0) operators denote #$NLPragmaticPredicates.")
(comment keIrrelevantArgIsaConstraint "(#$keIrrelevantArgIsaConstraint REL COLL) says that COLL is to be ignored as an argument constraint for REL during UIA interactions in which the argument constraints for REL are used to guess or suggest an #$isa for a term to be related by REL.")
(comment SystemLogAccessFault "#$SystemLogAccessFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  Programs with this fault readily yield the system logs to unauthorized users.  Often system logs contain sensitive information (such as login information) that could facilitate further compromises of security.")
(comment VulnerableToDirectoryProbing "A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a server program with a #$DirectoryProbingFault.")
(comment ContinuousPhysicalContactEvent "A collection of physical contact events in which two or more objects are in physical contact (see #$touches) throughout the event's entire duration.")
(comment StLouisEncephalitis-Virus "The virus that causes #$StLouisEncephalitis (a flavivirus antigenically related to #$JapaneseEncephalitis-Virus).")
(comment linkCutMinimalSetInSystem "(#$linkCutMinimalSetInSystem SET SYS) means that the set SET of links in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS is a minimal link-cut set in SYS, i.e., SET is a subset of (#$LinksFn SYS) such that (#$linkCutSetInSystem SET SYS) holds, and such that no proper subset SUBSET of SET satisfies (#$linkCutSetInSystem SUBSET SYS).")
(comment Kitchen "The collection of kitchens as they tend to be in the late 20th century in more developed countries or in more developed places in the Third World.  Small kitchens like in staff rooms of small organizations which don't have stoves or refrigerators are considered ab.  So are kitchens where you would tend a bar.")
(comment ClothingAccessory "A specialization of #$ClothingItem.  Each instance of #$ClothingAccessory is something that is worn as an accessory with other clothing items.  Notable specializations of #$ClothingAccessory include #$Hat, #$Cufflinks, #$Purse, #$Scarf, and #$Wallet.")
(disjointWith PuttingBallInPlay CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment positionSanctionedByOrganization "(#$positionSanctionedByOrganization AGT POS ORG) says that the fact

that (#$occupation AGT POS) is officially sanctioned by ORG.  Typically,

 this will hold where AGT holds POS as an employee of ORG, but this need

 not be the case.  For example (#$positionSanctionedByOrganization #$JohnPaulII #$Pope #$CollegeOfCardinals) holds by virtue of the process by which

 popes are selected, and not by virtue of the pope being an employee of

 the college (he's not).")
(comment BinaryConstraintMetaPredicate "This collection of predicates contains predicates which relate

binary relations to sets or collection and specify whether or not a

particular relation is reflexive, symmetric or transitive, or holds some relevant combination of these, with respect to the given instance

of #$SetOrCollection.   These predicates allow us to specify the way in

which a predicate \"behaves\" with respect to a certain set or collection,

one that may be a proper subset of the relation's domain.")
(comment transferredAIS "#$transferredAIS is used to identify an instance of #$AbstractInformationStructure for which an instantiation plays the role of #$transferredThing in a given #$InformationTransferEvent.  For example, (#$transferredAIS BobSendsAnEmailToTedAt12:15PM EMailMessageToTedFromBob001) says that a certain instance of #$EMailMessage was \"sent\" by Bob to Ted at 12:15 PM.  To be precise, there is an instantiation (see #$instantiationOfAIS) of that instance of #$EMailMessage that was transferred.  If Ted forwards the message to Sally, it will be the same #$EMailMessage, but a new instantiation will be transferred.")
(comment EnclosingSomething "This is the collection of all events in which something becomes enclosed.  This can happen either as the result of an object moving into an enclosure, such as a person entering a room, or the enclosure surrounding the object, such as a hand grasping a pencil. 'Enclosure' means that the enclosed object is at least surrounded in a plane by the enclosure.  The enclosing event is considered to last as long as the enclosed object is inside the enclosure.  An enclosing may come about either by movement, growth or shape change.")
(comment Steel "The collection of all contiguous portions of steel, an alloy of iron containing a small amount of carbon.")
(comment Sapphire-Gem "#$PreciousStones which are blue in color and translucent.")
(comment pathIntoRegion "This predicate relates spatial paths to spatial regions they pass into.  (#$pathIntoRegion PATH REGION) means that PATH crosses the border of REGION in at least one place, and exists partly outside of and partly inside of REGION.  PATH might either end inside of REGION or pass through it (see #$pathEndsInRegion and #$pathPassesThroughRegion).")
(comment FalloutShelter "Collection of shelters constructed to protect humans from nuclear radiation.")
(comment VulnerableToProcessExploitingSymlinkAttack "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$SymlinkFault-ProcessExploiting on it.")
(comment UnlimitedLoginAttemptFault "A program has this fault if it does not limit the number of login attempts, allowing for the possibility of a brute-force password attack.")
(comment Stapling "Stapling two objects together with a stapler.")
(comment IntentionalMentalEvent "A specialization of both #$AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent and #$IntentionalMentalSituation (qq.v.).  This is the collection of (at least partially) mental events whose instances are characterized by intentionality: they are \"of\" or \"about\" some thing external to themselves.  Thoughts and acts of perception are two common types of intentional mental events.  Thus, a particular act of thinking about the Eiffel Tower and a particular act of seeing the Eiffel Tower are both intentional mental events, each having (at least) the Eiffel Tower as their object.  Any thing whatsoever can in principle be the object of an intentional mental event: I can think about a certain physical object, an #$Event, a #$Relation, an attribute, a #$Proposition, a mental state (my own or another's), a set, a #$Collection, or anything else.  Mental events that are _not_ intentional, and thus not in this collection, include non-localized pain experiences, and at least some instances of #$ExperiencingEmotion (q.v.).   Note that, although they are indirectly related (see e.g. #$PurposefulMentalActivity), the sense of \"intentional\" described above is not to be confused with its other sense as an antonym of \"accidental\".  Nor is it to be confused with the logico-semantic concept of _intensional_ meaning.  See also  #$IntentionalMentalState, #$objectOfMentalSituation, and #$thinksAbout.")
(comment OfficialRecord "A collection of #$InformationBearingObjects.  Each element of OfficialRecord is a record of some agent and exists for a particular purpose.  For example, #$PersonnelRecord may contain employee information and other facts that are pertinent to the functioning of a business.  #$OfficialRecords are typically issued and generated by institutions and they are held to a higher degree of veracity and authenticity than a mere collection of data.  For example, official financial records are 'official' enough to be used to file taxes, request a loan, or appear as evidence in a court of law.  There is an important distinction between #$OfficialDocument and #$OfficialRecord.  An #$OfficialRecord may record the the number of passports issued to whom and on which date, but the #$OfficialDocument is the passport itself.  In the same sense, a list of transactions for a business on a particular day is an #$OfficialRecord, the credit card receipts and tickets of sale are #$OfficialDocuments.  One should read the comment for #$OfficialReport as a third distinction.")
(comment FuelCellPoweredDevice "The collection of all #$SelfPoweredDevices that are powered by internal #$FuelCells.  This is considered to be a spec of #$ElectricalDevice by definition.")
(comment PathFromFn "For each instance SYS of #$DirectedPathSystem, and for each path PATH in SYS, (#$PathFromFn PATH SYS) denotes 'the starting point' of PATH, i.e., the unique point X in SYS such that (#$pathFromToInSystem PATH X Y SYS) for some point Y in SYS (where Y is actually the unique point in SYS such that (#$PathToFn PATH SYS) = Y).")
(disjointWith Weapon MeasuringDevice)
(comment AthleticSupporter-Clothing "Instances of #$AthleticSupporter-Clothing are a type of undergarment worn by men to protect their genitalia from mechanical shock (but not impact) that might be caused by vigorous athletic activity.")
(comment FoodServicesDepartment "Each instance of #$FoodServicesDepartment consists of employees who are responsible for feeding an organization.")
(comment ActiveXControl "The collection of programs that perform a single task
or a collection of related tasks. An instance of #$ActiveXControl can
be called by programs or web sites that need the functionality it
provides.")
(comment cultureArtifacts-Domestic "This predicate relates cultures to characteristic types of artifacts

  that are produced within those cultures and important to their participants.

  (#$cultureArtifacts-Domestic CULTURE ARTIFACT) means that instances of 

  ARTIFACT are commonly created by, found among, and used by 

  participants in CULTURE.  ARTIFACT might be something created for

  either practical, recreational, religious, or aesthetic purposes.")
(comment popServer "The predicate #$popServer is used to indicate the source of information for a particular #$EMailReceiving. (#$popServer RECEIVING SERVER) means that in the #$EMailReceiving RECEIVING, the email transferred is pulled down from the #$POPServer-Network SERVER, usually to the intended recipient's client machine.")
(comment asIfBy "(#$asIfBy EVENT AGENT) means that AGENT is the actor in the #$TreatingAsIfEvent EVENT. For example, in the event #$FredAsksSallyToHelpMove, #$Fred is treating #$Sally as if the proposition (#$friends #$Fred #$Sally) were true, so we could say (#$asIfBy #$FredAsksSallyToHelpMove #$Fred).  See also #$asIfTo and #$asIfDuringByTo.")
(comment initialismString "(#$initialismString THING STRING) means that THING may be referred to by the initialism STRING. This is a special case of #$acronymString where the string is formed by the first letters of each word; also, the string generally isn't pronounced as a word.")
(comment AirPollutionProcess "The process by which air is contaminated.")
(comment HemorrhagicColitis "A specialization of #$BacterialInfection.  Instances of #$HemorrhagicColitis are caused by the somewhat well-known bacterium E.Coli, and are characterized by diarrhea and/or bloody stools, but generally no fever. The infective dose is extremely low.")
(disjointWith Hat Glove)
(comment keComparisonSentences "(keComparisonSentences TERM1 TERM2 SENTENCE1) means that SENTENCE1 has
the following properties:
it mentions TERM1,
it remains true if TERM2 is substituted for TERM1,
it contains no #$keIrrelevantTerms,
and it is useful for comparing TERM1 and TERM2.")
(comment Cuisine "The collection of types of #$EdibleStuff that are commonly associated with a region, ethnic group, culture, etc. ")
(comment FolkCostume "A set of clothes characteristic of the culture of a particular ethnic group or geographical region and not of modern western attire.  Examples: national or tribal costumes,...")
(comment structureOfGene-GenInfo "(#$structureOfGene-GenInfo GIS GENE-GENINFO) means that
GENE-GIS encodes GENE-GENINFO. Note that this predicate is functional
in its second argument place, as a given instance of
#$GeneticInformationStructure will encodes a unique instance of
#$Gene-GenInfo. Note also that the converse isn't true. An instance of
#$Gene-GenInfo may be instantiated by a certain number of instances of
#$GeneticInformationStructure; it may in particular be encoded by two
distinct instances of #$Gene-GIS, one being a mutated form of the other.")
(comment SMTPServer-Network "A subcollection of #$ComputerServer, whose instances function as SMTP servers.")
(comment cycleInSystem "(#$cycleInSystem CYCLE SYS) means that CYCLE is a cycle in the path system SYS.  A cycle in SYS is either a loop in SYS or the concatenation of two different paths PATH1 and PATH2 in SYS satisfying the following conditions: (i) there are two points X and Y in SYS such that (#$pathBetweenInSystem PATH1 X Y SYS) and (#$pathBetweenInSystem PATH2 X Y SYS), and (ii) no point in SYS other than X and Y is on both PATH1 and PATH2.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction Dock)
(disjointWith MakingSomething LocomotionEvent)
(comment WeakPasswordEncryptionFault "#$WeakPasswordEncryptionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$WeakPasswordEncryptionFault if it uses a weak encryption algorithm to encrypt passwords.  Important specializations of this fault are #$WeakPasswordStorageEncryptionFault and #$WeakPasswordTransmissionEncryptionFault.")
(disjointWith Writing Talking)
(comment InsecureMailListAdministrationPagesFault "A program has
 this fault if a specially-formed input
 to that program will allow access to the list administration pages to an
 unauthorized user.")
(comment StLouisEncephalitis "A viral infection whose symptoms range from mild fever and headache to high fever, headache, stupor tremors, coma, and spastic paralysis. Named for the city where the first cases were recognized in 1933, is the most common variety of viral encephalitis in the USA")
(comment DoorInABuilding "Any door which is part of a building such as the front door of a house or the door to a closet in the house.  Note that this is the portal covering NOT the portal.  The portal is the doorway.  #$Doorway and #$DoorInABuilding are meant to go together, although #$Doorway can have other kinds of #$DoorwayCovering (e.g. sliding doors in elevators, supermarkets, Star Trek, etc).")
(comment KneePad "Heavy pads used to protect the knees from falls and other impacts.")
(disjointWith BaseballFielding PuttingBallInPlay)
(comment H1-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a level one heading (the highest level of heading).")
(comment ClearPlastic "plastic that is transparent")
(comment Emerald-Gem "#$PreciousStones which are green in color and translucent.")
(comment AstronomicalObservatoryBuilding "The collection of all instances of  #$AstronomicalObservatory which are also #$ConstructionArtifacts.  Astronomical instruments are housed in each #$AstronomicalObservatoryBuilding (and may even be a part of the building).")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedDecryption "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$EncryptionFault on it.")
(comment Nailing "Connecting solid objects together with a #$Nail.  Usually involves connecting wooden objects.")
(comment BulletinBoardServerProgram "The collection of programs that host online bulletin boards.")
(comment OfficialRecordType "A collection of all the subcollections of OfficialDocument whose instances are a particular and distinct type of official

document.")
(comment BatteryPoweredDevice "The collection of all #$SelfPoweredDevices in which a #$Battery serves as a noteworthy #$internalPowerSource.")
(comment SomeExampleNumberFn "(#$SomeExampleNumberFn NUM COL) denotes a term which represents an indeterminate instance number NUM of COL for use in generating an example.  See also #$SomeExampleFn.")
(disjointWith Connector Weapon)
(comment Girdle-Undergarment "The collection of lightweight undergarments, worn esp. by women, often partly or entirely of elastic or boned, for supporting and giving a slimmer appearance to the abdomen, hips, and buttocks.")
(comment BudgetDepartment "A specialization of #$FinanceDepartment. Each instance of this collection is a group of employees responsible for planning and drawing up an organization's budget(s).")
(disjointWith ProductType SpatialThingTypeByShape)
(comment Path-Simple "An instance of #$Collection, and a specialization of #$Path-Generic. Each instance of #$Path-Simple is a path with two distinct ends that do not \"overlap\" each other (in the case of spatial paths, the two ends are spatially disjoint). Since no instance of #$Path-Simple has ends that join at one point, #$Path-Simple is disjoint with #$Path-Cyclic.  Although instances of #$Path-Simple have distinct ends, some instances may have more than two things that are its \"end-points\".  For example, a path between Austin and Pittsburgh can also be a path between Texas and Pennsylvania.  Notable specializations of #$Path-Simple include #$Pipe-GenericConduit, #$Nerve, and #$Stream.")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact Tool)
(comment EMailServerProgram "#$EMailServerProgram is a subset of #$NetworkingProgram.  Copies of #$EMailServerProgram implement #$PostOfficeProtocol, #$InternetMessageAccessProtocol or #$SimpleMailTransferProtocol.")
(comment Hantaan-Virus "A specialization of #$Virus.  #$Hantaan-Virus is the type of virus that causes instances of #$Hantaan.")
(comment Fence "Fences -- fixed structures intended to prevent animals and people from crossing a boundary.")
(disjointWith Hat Scarf)
(comment UnifiedMessagingProgram "The collection of programs that enable users to incorporate various forms of communication (e-mail, fax and voice messages) into a single system.")
(comment keContrastingSentences "(keContrastingSentences TERM1 TERM2 SENTENCE1) means that SENTENCE1 has
the following properties:
it mentions TERM1,
it is not true if TERM2 is substituted for TERM1,
it contains no #$keIrrelevantTerms,
and it is useful for contrasting TERM1 and TERM2.")
(comment setGIDOfProgramOn "(#$setGIDOfProgramOn PROGRAM COMPUTER GROUP) means that any process inititaed by PROGRAM on COMPUTER will run with the privileges of an arbirary account in the GROUP group.")
(comment HotfixDeletionFault "A program has a #$HotfixDeletionFault if allows  software patches to be deleted by an unauthorized user, leaving the platform on which the patches were installed vulnerable to whatever security issues the patches were fixing.")
(comment Path-Cyclic "The collection of all cyclic paths, i.e. paths that form cycles, circles, loops or circuits.  An instance of #$Path-Cyclic is a #$Path-Generic that can be described as a cycle, i.e., a thing like a #$Path-Simple except that the ends of the path join at one point.   A #$Path-Cyclic cannot cross itself (as in a figure-eight) nor double back along itself.  More formally, let PATH1 and PATH2 be two #$Path-Simples.  Suppose that each end-point of PATH1 is an end point of PATH2 and vice versa, and for each X, X is a point on both PATH1 and PATH2 only if X is an end point of both paths.  Then PATH1 and PATH2 together form a #$Path-Cyclic.  We allow 'loops'; a loop is a cycle with only one point on it, looping from the point right back to itself.   Each loop of a path system is a special instance of #$Path-Cyclic.  For differences between a cycle and a loop in the same #$PathSystem, see #$loopInSystem and #$cycleInSystem.")
(comment TraditionalClothing "A thing to wear which is characteristic of the culture of a particular ethnic group and not of modern western attire.  Examples: Viking hats, lederhosen, kimonos, ...")
(comment cultureInfluences "This predicate relates cultures to other cultures that
  have influenced them, and to the areas in which this influence 
  has occurred.  (#$cultureInfluences CULTURE1 CULTURE2 THING)
  means that the character of CULTURE1 has been significantly 
  influenced by that of CULTURE2 with respect to THING.  THING
  might concern language, law, religion, agriculture, politics, 
  arts and crafts, or anything else having to do with culture.  
  The influence might have occurred strictly in the past, or might 
  be ongoing.")
(comment PasswordFileForFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  (#$PasswordFileForFn ACCOUNT_SYSTEM) denotes the collection of all #$ComputerFile-Abstracts that contain all the valid username/password combinations for ACCOUNT_SYSTEM, either in #$Encrypted or #$Plaintext form.")
(comment PathSystem "The collection of all specified systems of paths and links, including both tangible path systems (such as the system of streets in a city) and abstract path systems (such as a multigraph).  Each instance of #$PathSystem consists of a nonempty set of points (where each point is an instance of #$Thing, and is related to the instance of #$PathSystem via the predicate #$pointInSystem), a set of nodes (a subset of the set of points -- each node is related to the instance of #$PathSystem via the predicate #$nodeInSystem) a set of links (where each link is an instance of #$Path-Simple, and is related to the instance of #$PathSystem via the predicate #$linkInSystem), and optionally a set of loops (where each loop is an instance of #$Path-Cyclic, and is related to the instance of #$PathSystem via the predicate #$loopInSystem).  In order to specify which link is between which two nodes in the system, which point is on which link in the system, which node is on which loop in the system, and so on, see the following predicates: #$pathBetween, #$pointOnPath, #$pointOnCycle, #$betweenOnPath, #$linkBetweenInSystem, #$junctionInSystem, #$deadEndInSystem, #$isolatedNodeInSystem, and #$connectedInSystem.  Notable specializations of #$PathSystem include #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem, #$Multigraph, and #$SimplePathSystem.  In order to specify the subsystem relation between path systems, see the predicate #$subPathSystems.")
(comment allies "(#$allies AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT1 has a strong #$positiveVestedInterest in the welfare of AGENT2 and is likely to take actions in support of AGENT2 when needed.  This relationship is mutual, so this is a symmetric predicate.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction TopographicalFeature)
(disjointWith MakingFacialExpression LocomotionEvent)
(comment keIrrelevantArgGenlsConstraint "(#$keIrrelevantArgGenlsConstraint REL COLL) says that COLL is to be ignored as an argument constraint for REL during UIA interactions in which the argument constraints for REL are used to guess or suggest a #$genls for a term to be related by REL.")
(comment WeakPasswordTransmissionEncryptionFault "#$WeakPasswordTransmissionEncryptionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$WeakPasswordTransmissionEncryptionFault if it uses a weak encryption algorithm for transmitted passwords.")
(comment DisplayLockBypassFault "A program has this fault if it is possible for an attacker to unlock a locked workstation without supplying the proper password.")
(comment CityStateMethod "The last three characters are a comma and two letter state code; the name of the city begins the field; blanks fill any space between the city name and the comma.  Example: 'Austin      ,TX', in the case of a 15-character field.")
(comment HarmingAnAgent "A specialization of #$ActionOnObject. Each instance of #$HarmingAnAgent is an event in which some agent is harmed, either physically or psychologically.  Note that #$HarmingAnAgent is not a specialization of #$PurposefulAction, since it includes as instances some events in which an agent is harmed, but not intentionally harmed.  Neither is it a specialization of #$IncurringDamage, because that does not cover psychological injury.  Although #$HarmingAnAgent is not a specialization of #$PurposefulAction, important specializations of #$HarmingAnAgent (such as #$Murder and #$Torture) are also specializations of #$PurposefulAction.")
(comment softwareInVersionSeries "A predicate relating instances of #$VersionedSoftwareObject with instances of #$SoftwareVersionSeries. (#$softwareInVersionSeries SOFTWARE SERIES) means that SOFTWARE is included in the collection denoted by SERIES. For example (#$softwareInVersionSeries (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Pine-TheProgram \"4.10\") (#$VersionsInclusiveFn #$Pine-TheProgram \"4.0\" \"4.5\")) means that version 4.10 of Pine is a version of Pine between versions 4.1 and 4.5.")
(comment SinNombre-Virus "The virus that causes Sin Nombre disease (#$SinNombre), a Hantavirus from the family Bunyaviridae.")
(comment OfficeRoom "Single-room offices where one or two people typically work.  Several of these can comprise an #$OfficeSpace.")
(comment FootwearPart "The collection of the parts of items of footwear")
(disjointWith ShootingAProjectileWeapon PuttingBallInPlay)
(disjointWith PersonTypeByEthnicity PersonTypeByGender)
(comment H2-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a level two heading (the second highest level of heading).")
(comment asymmetricOn "(#$asymmetricOn PRED COL) means that if MEM1 and MEM2 are elements of COL  and (PRED MEM1 MEM2), it follows that (not (PRED MEM2 MEM1)).")
(comment mindsEventType "(#$mindsEventType ANIMAL EVENTTYPE) means that the sentient animal ANIMAL finds events of type EVENTTYPE to be somewhat irritating.")
(comment Polypropylene "Polypropylene is a carbon-chain polymer created from propylene.           It is used to make fibers that go into common items such as           #$Upholstery, #$Carpets, #$Rope and #$Diapers and that are also used in           medical aplications.  It is also blow-molded into #$PlasticBottles for many            household liquids, e.g. #$Shampoo, contact lens solutions, etc.")
(comment Aquamarine-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which is light blue in color and translucent.")
(comment TattooStudio "The collection of professional #$Studios in which #$Tattooing events take place.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedEncryptionKeyAlteration "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$AlterableEncryptionKeyFault on it.")
(comment LaCrosseEncephalitisInfection "The collection of all #$EncephalitisInfections which are caused by the La Crosse encephalitis virus.")
(comment GearShifting "What happens when a driver shifts the gears.  This is a subEvent of a DrivingEvent in the #$DriverPerspectiveMt:  Since #$performedBy transfersThro #$subEvents we only want #$GearShifting to be #$performedBy the Driver.  Thus a suEvent assertion should not be placed in a perspective neutral mt.")
(disjointWith Configuration MentalState)
(comment unmountDirectoryContainingFile "(#$unmountDirectoryContainingFile AGENT FILE) means that AGENT unmounts the directory containing FILE.")
(comment ThongUnderwear "The collection of #$Briefs for men or women that have just a thin vertical strip in the back, exposing most of the wearer's #$Buttocks.")
(comment FinanceDepartment "A specialization of #$Department. Each instance of this collection is a sub-organization of a business, government, or academic organization which deals somehow with the organization's finances or cash-flow. Notable specializations of this collection include #$BudgetDepartment,  #$PayrollDepartment and #$AccountingDepartment.")
(comment cultureOfMt "(#$cultureOfMt MICROTHEORY CULTURE) defines the culture dimension of MICROTHEORY. It relates a #$Microtheory to the culture(s) it is relevant for or pertains to.  (#$mtOfCulture MICROTHEORY CULTURE) means that the assertions in MICROTHEORY are maden the context of CULTURE.  Beyond this, the precise type of relevance or pertinence will depend on other dimension attributes for MICROTHEORY, including modality.  See #$mtOfCulture for describing microtheories that are believed true in a given culture.  The predicate #$mtDefinesCulture relates a culture to the microtheory that precisely specifies its associated beliefs, practices, and artifacts.  See also #$mtCultureBeliefs.")
(comment LineBetweenFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for denoting a line which intersects ARG1 and ARG2.")
(comment imapServer "The predicate #$imapServer is used to indicate the source of information for a particular #$EMailReceiving. (#$imapServer RECEIVING SERVER) means that in the #$EMailReceiving RECEIVING, the email transferred is pulled down from the #$IMAPServer-Network SERVER, usually to the intended recipient's client machine.")
(comment independentIonSpec "The predicate corresponding to #$IndependentIonFn (see #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical).  Where CHEMOBJTYPE is a class of #$ChemicalObject which is 'agnostic' as to whether its instances are #$Molecules, #$Ions, or #$MolecularComponents, (#$independentIonSpec CHEMOBJTYPE IONTYPE) means that IONTYPE is the class of all instances of CHEMOBJTYPE which are #$Ions.")
(comment traversalInSystem "(#$traversalInSystem TRAV SYS) means that TRAV is a #$Traversal of some paths in the #$PathSystem SYS.  Let TRAV be represented by (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X(1) PATH(1) ... X(n) PATH(n) X(n+1))).  To say that TRAV is a #$Traversal in SYS we mean that (i) TRAV is a #$Traversal (and thus (#$TheList X(1) PATH(1) ... X(n) PATH(n) X(n+1)) is a #$PathChain), and (ii) each X(k) is a point in SYS and each PATH(k) is either a link or a loop in SYS, or a subpath of a loop in SYS.  Our favorite description of a traversal in SYS is such a list that all X(k) are nodes in SYS except X(1) and X(n+1), and all PATH(k)s are links or loops in SYS except PATH(1) and PATH(n).")
(comment transports "Agent A transports thing B.")
(comment RecreationalTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections, a specialization of
#$CulturalTerrainFeatureType. Instances of #$RecreationalTerrainFeatureType
are collections of constructed sites where take place recreational
activities. Also included are structures of significant importance that are
found in such sites. The collections of amusement park, of golf courses or
of zoo are in this category.")
(comment Diluting "The collection of all mixing events of two or more stuff types in which the concentration of the focal ingredient on one of the inputs commmitted (considered the #$objectActedOn) is reduced without the resulting stuff becoming a significantly different type of stuff.")
(comment Hantaan "A specialization of #$ViralInfection.  Instances of #$Hantaan are characterised by sudden onset of high fever, headache, malaise and anorexia, progressing lower back pain, often with nausea and vomiting. A sudden drop in blood pressure and hemorrhagic symptoms follows. Normal blood pressure returns and there is a dramatic drop in urine production. Recovery may be prolonged.")
(comment indigenousTo "Organisms of type ARG1 are #$indigenousTo the geographical area ARG2.  This means that the species ARG1 developed in ARG2 and/or that in a `natural state', members of ARG1 are found in ARG2.  This allows us to state things such as `Giraffes are African animals,' meaning that giraffes in their present form arose in Africa and are found there `in the wild'.")
(comment Archway-PartOfBuilding "Arches which are part of buildings.")
(disjointWith Hat Belt-Clothing)
(comment IndeterminateTermDenotingFunction "#$IndeterminateTermDenotingFunction is the collection of all functions that denote indeterminate terms.  See also #$IndeterminateTerm, #$SkolemTerm, and #$SkolemFunction.")
(comment ArbitraryMemberFn "(#$ArbitraryMemberFn GROUP) denotes an arbitrary member of GROUP.  CYC should infer no more about (#$ArbitraryMemberFn GROUP) than it could infer about any member of GROUP.")
(disjointWith AmorphousThing ShapedObject)
(comment useReformulationRuleForNLQuantifierPlaceholderProcessing "(#$useReformulationRuleForNLQuantifierPlaceholderProcessing RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$NLQuantifierPlaceholderProcessingRLModule.")
(comment UnknownProgramFn "A function that takes as an argument a string that is determined to refer to a #$ComputerProgram-CW, and denotes the program to which the string refers.  For instance, (#$UnknownProgramFn \"obscure-program\") denotes the #$ComputerProgram-CW referred to by the string \"obscure-program\".")
(comment Mortarboard "The cap used in graduation ceremonies (usually square with a tassle).")
(comment cultureLanguages "This predicate relates cultures to languages that are

  prevalent within them.  (#$cultureLanguages CULTURE LANGUAGE)

  means that LANGUAGE is commonly spoken or written by participants

  in CULTURE.")
(disjointWith EmployeeTypeByWorkStatus MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType)
(comment linkBetweenInSystem "(#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) means that in the #$PathSystem SYS, the #$Path-Simple LINK (a link in SYS, so that (#$linkInSystem LINK SYS) holds) has as its two end points X and Y (nodes in SYS, so that both (#$nodeInSystem X SYS) and (#$nodeInSystem Y SYS) hold). Since LINK connects the two end points X and Y when (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) holds, (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) implies (#$pathBetween LINK X Y).   A link in a path system is a path whose end points are nodes in the system, and which has no other nodes along it (although it may have any number of non-node points along it).  For each link LINK in SYS, there is a unique pair {X, Y} of different nodes in SYS such that (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) and (#$linkBetweenInSystem LINK Y X SYS) hold, and for any two nodes in SYS, there could be several different ('parallel') links between them.  No point in SYS that is not a node can be an end point of a link.  Only a node in SYS can be an 'intersection' point in SYS (see #$junctionInSystem), which implies that there is, in the system SYS, no point on a link LINK between X and Y that is an 'intersection' point of LINK and another link or a loop.")
(comment sponsorsAgentInAction "(#$sponsorsAgentInAction SPONSOR DOER ACTION) means that the agent SPONSOR provides a key incentive and/or backing to the agent DOER so that DOER will perform ACTION.  SPONSOR has some reason related to its own goals for sponsoring DOER to perform ACTION.  The incentive may be a plan, payment, equipment, information, training, etc. represented using instances of #$HelpingAnAgent or other relevant collections.  See also #$givesSupportToAgent.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction Terrace-Topographical)
(comment NLTaggedTermType "A collection of collections, a spec of

#$IntermediateVocabTermTypeByModule.  Each instance of #$NLTaggedTermType is

 a collection of terms used by the #$CycPhraseStructureParser to capture syntactic information about number, gender, determiners, etc.")
(disjointWith Surgery LocomotionEvent)
(comment FilteringSoftwareBypassFault "#$FilteringSoftwareBypassFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if it is possible to circumvent a data filtering method the program is designed to implement.")
(comment DataCorruptionFault "A program has a #$DataCorruptionFault if it tends to corrupt or otherwise mis-store the data it is supposed to store.  This might happen, for example, when the program takes up a lot of memory.")
(comment DefaultAccountFault "A program has this fault if it is shipped with a canonical (or easily guessable) username and password combination by which unauthorized users could log on to the system.")
(comment SinNombre "A viral lung disease whose initial symptoms include fever, muscular pain and nausea followed by an abrupt onset of respiratory distress with low blood pressure. This progresses rapidly to severe respiratory failure and shock.")
(comment cutLinkInSystem "(#$cutLinkInSystem LINK SYS) means that LINK is a single link in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS whose removal would cause the system to be disconnected.  Thus {LINK}, i.e., (#$TheSet LINK), is a link-cut-set in SYS.  That is to say, (#$cutLinkInSystem LINK SYS) holds if and only if (#$linkCutSetInSystem (#$TheSet LINK) SYS) holds. Note that since SYS is a #$ConnectedPathSystem whenever (#$cutLinkInSystem LINK SYS) holds, it is easy to see that (#$cutLinkInSystem LINK SYS) holds if and only if (#$linkCutMinimalSetInSystem (#$TheSet LINK) SYS) holds.")
(comment CafeteriaSpace "A relatively large set of rooms in a construction for communal eating.  Different from a restaurant in that admittance is often restricted to those meeting some criterion such as membership or employment.  Also, in a cafeteria diners generally get their food by walking through a line and serving themselves.  A cafeteria includes the kitchen, the dining area, and other areas.")
(comment MainHatPart "The main part of a hat -- does not include brims, bills, bands, etc.")
(comment InsecureEncryptionKeyFault "#$InsecureEncryptionKeyFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if under some circumstances an intruder can predict, recover or alter a key the program has used to encrypt data.  More specific attributes should be used whenever possible: see #$PredictableEncryptionKeyFault, #$AlterableEncryptionKeyFault, and #$RecoverableEncryptionKeyFault.")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByEthnicity HumanTypeBySexualOrientation)
(comment H3-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a level three heading (the third highest level of heading).")
(comment SubcollectionByRegionFn "(#$SubcollectionByRegionFn COLLECTION REGION) is the collection of all instances of COLLECTION located at least partially in REGION.  Thus (#$isa #$MississippiRiver (#$CollectionIntersectionFn (#$TheSet (#$SubcollectionByRegionFn #$River (#$TerritoryFn #$Louisiana-State)) (#$SubcollectionByRegionFn #$River (#$TerritoryFn #$Minnesota-State))))).")
(comment Growth-Physical "The class of events which are focally about some #$PartiallyTangible increasing in physical size.  The object affected will increase in volume and also in mass. ")
(comment Rubber-Synthetic "Synthetic Rubber - the manufactured substance.")
(comment Garnet-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which is red in color and translucent.")
(comment pathPassesThroughRegion "This predicate relates spatial paths to spatial regions they pass through.  (#$pathPassesThroughRegion PATH REGION)   means that PATH runs all the way through REGION and beyond (in    both directions).  PATH must run through a ''significant portion''    of REGION, as judged with respect to the dimension of REGION that    corresponds most closely to the location and orientation of PATH   (see #$pathThroughRegion).  It is not enough, for example, for PATH    merely to pass through a remote corner of REGION.")
(comment numberOfStories "This predicate relates a building to the number of 
stories it has.  (#$numberOfStories BLDG N) means that BLDG
has a total of N stories at or above ground level.  See also 
#$numberOfLevels and #$nthLevelOfBuilding.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureUsernames "A computer has this vulnerability if it can be used to discern usernames for the network of which it is a part in an unauthorized fashion. This might be because it has a program with an #$InsecureUsernameFault on it, or for other reasons.")
(comment OperatingAHouseholdAppliance "The collection of situations corresponding to the operation of household appliances. This should be the genls for all the situation types dealing with the operating of the different household appliances.")
(comment IntentionalMentalState "A collection of mental states whose instances are 

characterized by intentionality: they are \"of\" or \"about\" 

some thing external to themselves.  Propositional attitudes 

(as held by particular agents) are a common type of intentional 

mental state.  Thus, believing that the Eiffel Tower is located

in Paris is an intentional mental state that has the Eiffel Tower 

and the city of Paris (and arguably the located-in relation as 

well) as its objects.  Any thing whatsoever can in principle

be the object of an intentional mental state: I can have a

belief (or doubt, wish, etc.) about a certain physical object, 

an event, a relation, an attribute, a proposition, a mental 

state (my own or another's), a set, a collection, or anything 

else.  (Note that the above mentioned belief about the Eiffel 

Tower and Paris is arguably not itself about the _proposition_ 

that the Eiffel Tower is in Paris.  But now note that my belief 

in the content of the sentence preceding this one clearly _is_, 

in part, about that proposition.)  Mental states that are _not_ 

intentional, and thus not in this collection, include moods,

such as being in a general state of happiness or depression.  (These 

states are to be distinguished from an experience of feeling 

happy or depressed, which are mental _events_ rather than states.

One can be in an uninterrupted state of depression for weeks, 

even though one doesn't feel depressed continuously throughout 

that time; e.g. one would not feel depressed while asleep.)

Note that, although they are indirectly related, the sense of 

\"intentional\" described above is not to be confused with 

its other sense as an antonym of \"accidental\".  See also

#$IntentionalMentalEvent and #$objectOfMentalSituation.")
(comment RoadVehicleTypeByPowerSource "A covering collection on #$RoadVehicle.  More specifically, this collection facets #$RoadVehicle by the principle type of power source employed (see #$internalPowerSource.")
(comment sinkNodeInSystem "(#$sinkNodeInSystem X SYS) means that X is a sink node in the #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, i.e., a node to which all links attached to it come 'in', and from which no such links go 'out'.  A sink node X in SYS is a node in SYS such that X is on some links but no loops in SYS, and such that each link in SYS that X is on is a link directed to X from another node.  Another way to put this is that X is a node in SYS that is neither on any loop in SYS, nor an isolated node in SYS, nor a node from which a link in SYS is directed.  See #$loopInSystem, #$isolatedNodeInSystem and #$linkFromToInSystem.")
(comment Connector "A specialization of #$NonPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$Connector is a device which connects two objects.  An instance of #$Connector may be a part incorporated into one or both of the objects connected, or it may be a totally separate device.  Notable specializations of #$Connector include #$Staple, #$Pin, and #$Nail.")
(comment ThongBikini "The collection of bikinis each of which is composed of a #$GString-BikiniBottom and a regular #$BikiniTop.")
(comment fartherNorthThan "(#$fartherNorthThan THING-1 THING-2) means that THING-1 is farther to the north than THING-2 is, although it need not be #$northOf THING-2; they must be on the same planet surface, and the northernmost point(s) of THING-1 is, strictly speaking, closer to the North Pole than the northernmost point(s) of THING-2.   Example: (#$fartherNorthThan #$CityOfRomeItaly #$CityOfBostonMA). An example shows a technical difference between #$northOf and #$fartherNorthThan:  the #$CityOfRioDeJaneiroBrazil is #$fartherNorthThan the #$CityOfMelbourneAustralia, even though the shortest air route from Melbourne to Rio is to fly directly south (almost over the #$SouthPole).")
(comment Asterism "A collection of instances of #$CelestialRegion which are distinguished by a set of visible stars in some pattern. Examples include #$BigDipper-Asterism and #$OrionsBelt.  See also #$Constellation, which is the more formal notion of 'constellation' used by astronomers.")
(comment cultureArtifacts-Significant "This predicate relates cultures 

to individual artifacts that are particularly significant to them.

(#$cultureArtifacts-Significant CULTURE OBJECT) means that OBJECT was 

probably produced within CULTURE, and is highly valued by and meaningful to 

the participants of CULTURE.  Generally speaking, most of the artifacts

associated with a given culture (see #$cultureArtifacts) will not be 

#$cultureArtifacts-Significant.  For example, while the #$StatueOfLiberty 

is certainly one of #$UnitedStatesCulture's #$cultureArtifacts-Significant, 

a souvenir reproduction of the statue is not.  Note that, unlike

#$cultureArtifacts, which takes a _type_ of artifact as its second 

argument, this predicate takes an individual instance of #$Artifact-Generic

in that argument position.")
(comment smtpServer "The predicate #$smtpServer is used to indicate the SMTP server used in a particular #$EMailSending. (#$smtpServer SEND SERVER) means that in the #$EMailSending SEND, the email sent is sent via the  #$SMTPServer-Network SERVER.")
(comment FlowPath "A #$CustomaryPathCycLConstant and a specialization of both #$Path-Customary and #$Path-Simple.  Each instance of #$FlowPath is a path whose extent is delineated by the movement of a fluid over an area; for example, the path of a lava flow or the #$AlaskanPipeline.  Instances of #$FlowPath may (but need not) be constrained by objects or forces that channel the flow of fluid; see also the subcollection #$FluidConduit.")
(comment asIfTo "(#$asIfTo EVENT THING) means that THING is the object of the #$TreatingAsIfEvent EVENT. For example, in the event #$FredAsksSallyToHelpMove, #$Fred is treating #$Sally as if the proposition (#$friends #$Fred #$Sally) were true, so we could say (#$asIfTo #$FredAsksSallyToHelpMove #$Sally).  See also #$asIfBy and #$asIfDuringByTo.")
(comment NuclearPowerPlantBuilding "The collection of buildings that serve primarily to house components of nuclear powered electrical generators (see #$ElectricalGenerator-Nuclear).  Important specializations of #$NuclearPowerPlantBuilding include #$NuclearReactorCoolingTower and #$NuclearReactorContainmentBuilding.  Instances of #$NuclearPowerPlantBuilding are typically found at instances of #$PowerGenerationComplex-Nuclear.")
(comment initialsString "(#$initialsString AGENT STRING) means that AGENT may be referred to by the initials STRING. This is a special case of #$initialismString where the agent is a human (or is anthropomorphized as in fiction).")
(comment TranscriptionEvent "The collection of all acts of transcription.  If PERFORMER is the performer of a #$TranscriptionEvent, TRANSCRIBE, then PERFORMER brings it about that the information (to some degree of specificity) contained in the  #$informationOrigin, ORIGIN, of TRANSCRIBE comes to be contained in the #$informationDestination, DESTINATION, of TRANSCRIBE. ORIGIN and DESTINATION must both instantiate instances of #$AbstractInformationStructure (at times during TRANSCRIBE), and some of the #$AbstractInformationStructures instantiated by ORIGIN must come to be instantiated by DESTINATION, during TRANSCRIBE. #$TranscriptionEvents are distinguished from other sorts #$IBTGeneration-Replication (such as #$PhotocopyingADocument) in that, generally, the performer of a #$TranscriptionEvent is aware (sometime during that event) of the #$AbstractInformationStructures instantiated by ORIGIN, and is also aware (sometime during TRANSCRIBE) of the #$AbstractInformationStructures that come to be instantiated by DESTINATION. #$TranscriptionEvents are typically composed of many subevents that are also #$TranscriptionEvents. For example, if TRANSCRIBE is the transcription of an audio tape, ORIGIN, to the tablet DESTINATION, then TRANSCRIBE will typically be composed of other #$TranscriptionEvents in which small segments of the whole tape are #$informationOrigins in transcription events that have small portions of the tablet as #$informationDestinations.")
(comment UserAccountDataFile "Contains the #$PasswordForCycorpProtectedFile.")
(comment Joint-Physical "A specialization of #$Connection-Physical.  Each instance of #$Joint-Physical is a group consisting of parts of at least two instances of #$PartiallyTangible that are mechanically connected in the manner of a joint. Examples include an elbow, and a hinge joining a door to a frame. While each #$Joint-Physical is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible, and therefore has a determinate spatial boundary, there are many cases in which there are no easily describable boundaries between the parts of joint-connected objects that are parts of the joint, and those which are not. For example, consider a ball and socket joint connecting some hip bone to a femur. The boundaries of this joint are obscure due to the fact that exact boundaries of the socket portion of the hip and the ball of the femur are obscure. In contrast, the spatial boundaries of a joint comprising a detachable hinge, such as those that typically connect a door to frame, are clear.")
(comment WaitingRoom "Rooms in a building which are used for clients to sit/relax while they wait to be seen.")
(disjointWith Connector Eyewear)
(comment Title-Aristocratic "The collection of all collections, instances of which are persons who hold hereditary titles of nobility granted or recognized by some government or monarch.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfPlaintextSystemPasswordFile "A computer has this vulnerability if it has an operating system with a #$PlaintextSystemPasswordFileFault on it.")
(comment InjuredPerson "The collection of #$Persons with an #$InjuryCondition.")
(comment Summons-Legal "The collection of all #$OfficialDocuments which order a person to appear in a specific court at a specific time (as a defendent, juror, or witness).")
(comment pickupCourier "A predicate for relating an occasion of sending an object to a courier who picks up that object from the person who sends it.")
(comment UnauthorizedADKFault "A program has an #$UnauthorizedADKFault if it allows an attacker to add an unauthorized Additional Decryption Key (ADK) to a user's public key.  Attackers who are able to thus modify a victim's public key will be able to decrypt any data encrypted with the key.")
(comment CachePoisoningFault "A program has this fault if it is possible for an attacker to insert malicious data into the cache for the program, causing it to behave in a way inconsistent with its proper function.")
(comment nameableCollection "This predicate is used to identify collections whose specs are reasonable to treat as \"nameable\" -- i.e., one might reasonaby use a name when making generic claims about the collection qua class of its instances.  For example, one might use the word \"cancer\" as a name for the class of instances of #$Cancer conditions, say in \"Cancer is a terrible disease.\"")
(comment Gown "A piece of clothing, generally full-length")
(comment EmployeeBadge "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$IDDocument.  Each instance of #$EmployeeBadge is a badge issued by an employer to an employee, for purposes of identification and security.  People with such badges will be allowed to enter the employer's workplace(s), while those without will not.")
(disjointWith PersonTypeByActivity MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType)
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedRegionOfTransportationDevice LevelOfAConstruction)
(disjointWith NuclearEvent LocomotionEvent)
(comment ClothingMarketCategory "The kinds of clothing you would expect to buy in a clothing store <like Last Call or By George> or in the clothing department of a department store")
(comment DefaultPermissionsFault "A very general #$ProgramFaultAttribute. A program has a #$DefaultPermissionsFault if it creates files whose default permissions do not accord with good security practices.")
(comment InfectiousDiseaseType "The intersection of #$InfectionType and #$DiseaseType.  Each instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseType is a type of infection that is also a type of disease.  For example, #$TrenchFever belongs in this collection, but #$ViralInfection, which is an instance of #$InfectionType but is not a type of disease, does not belong.")
(comment SoftwareVersionSeries "A specialization of #$SoftwareObject. Each instance of #$SoftwareVersionSeries is a series consisting of versions of software.  A positive example is the Pine versions 4.0 through 4.5 inclusive.  Negative examples include Pine and Pine version 4.0, which are both instances of #$SoftwareObject-Individual.  #$SoftwareObject-Individual and #$SoftwareVersionSeries are disjoint and they partition the collection #$SoftwareObject.")
(comment FrontDoorwayOfHouse "The formal doorway to the house.")
(comment Pom-Pom "The collection of decorative bunches of thread or yarn used to decorate clothing.")
(comment H4-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a level four heading (the fourth highest level of heading).")
(comment irreflexiveOn "(#$irreflexiveOn PRED COL) means that if MEM is an element of COL, then (#$not (PRED MEM MEM)).")
(comment PolynucleotideStrandSegment "The collection of all #$PolynucleotideStrands which are
components (see #$molecularSubComponents) of larger
#$PolynucleotideMolecules.  Important specs include
#$Intron-MolecularSegment, #$Exon-MolecularSegment, and
#$Codon-MolecularSegment.")
(comment Fascist "The collection of all instances of #$Person who subscribe to the doctrines of fascism.")
(comment enclosedObject "'(#$enclosedObject ENCLOSING OBJECT)' means that OBJECT becomes
enclosed in the #$EnclosingSomething ENCLOSING.")
(comment Jade-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which is green in color and translucent.")
(comment pathThroughRegion "This predicate relates spatial paths to spatial regions they run through.  (#$pathThroughRegion PATH REGION)   means that PATH runs through REGION for a significant distance relative to the size of REGION (especially the dimension of REGION that corresponds most closely to the location and orientation of PATH).  PATH might go outside of REGION or might be wholly contained in REGION, but it should at least run nearly \"from one end to the other\" of REGION, as judged with respect to the relevant dimension.")
(comment numberOfLevels "This predicate relates a building to the number of 
levels it has.  (#$numberOfLevels BLDG N) means that BLDG
has a total of N levels above, at, or below ground level.
For a count of a building's levels that are at or above 
ground level, see #$numberOfStories.  See also 
#$nthLevelOfBuilding.")
(comment programCopyInitialized "(#$programCopyInitialized INIT PROGCOPY) says that PROGCOPY is initialized during INIT. To identify the actual #$ComputerProgram-CW that is initialized, use #$programInitialized.")
(comment VulnerableToKerberosKDCSpoofing "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$KerberosKDCSpoofingFault on it.")
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-ProgramCrashing "#$AttackByComputerOperation-ProgramCrashing is the subset of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService whose instances are intended to crash running programs.")
(comment RadiusFn "This function denotes the Radius of an object.  (RadiusFn OBJ) denotes the Radius of OBJ.")
(comment DirectedAcyclicPathSystem "The collection of all #$DirectedPathSystems each of which has no directed cycle in it (see #$directedCycleInSystem).  Note that each instance of #$DirectedAcyclicPathSystem has no loops in it, although it may have an undirected graph cycle in it.")
(comment GraspingImplement "#$GraspingImplement is a specialization of #$HandTool.  Each instance of #$GraspingImplement is a tool which is intended to be used to grasp (and often to subsequently immobilize or control the location/movement of) some other solid object.  Specializations of #$GraspingImplement include #$Vise, #$Forceps, and #$Tweezers.")
(comment ThongSwimsuit "The collection of #$SwimSuits that leave the #$Buttocks of those who wear them completely exposed.")
(comment GroundsMaintenanceDepartment "A specialization of #$FacilitiesDepartment. Each instance of #$GroundsMaintenanceDepartment consists of employees who maintain an organization's outdoor spaces.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForNPPOutputTersification "(#$useReformulationRuleForNPPOutputTersification RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$NPPOutputTersificationRLModule.")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact DrugSubstance)
(disjointWith SummerOlympicsCompetition WinterOlympicsCompetition)
(comment EmergencyRoom "The collection of sections of a hospital intended to handle emergencies and after-hours patients.")
(disjointWith ProtectiveAttire Connector)
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedDomainSocketConnection "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$DefaultDomainSocketConnectionFault on it.")
(comment failedGoal "(#$failedGoal GOAL-SENTENCE) means that, in the current planner-state, the planner has tried to find plans for GOAL-SENTENCE and failed.  For example: (#$failedGoal (#$doGetLoginInformationForAccount AGENT ACCOUNT)) means that, in the current state of the planning domain, the planner has already tried and failed to solve (#$doGetLoginInformationForAccount AGENT ACCOUNT).")
(comment arrestee "The predicate #$arrestee relates the person arrested to the #$ArrestingSomeone event in which he or she was arrested.  (#$arrestee EVENT PERSON) means that PERSON was the person arrested during EVENT.")
(comment ReadableMailFault "A program has this fault if it allows any user logged onto the email #$AccountSystem administered by the program to read any other user's mail. See also #$InsecureMailStorageFault-System and #$InsecureMailStorageFault-Local.")
(comment LipidBilayer "The collection of all membranes consisting of a double layer of amphipathic lipid molecules in aqueous solution, oriented so that their hydrophobic ends are in contact.  Such bilayers form more-or-less spontaneously when phospholipids are introduced into aqueous solution, since lipid molecules in water tend to aggregate in structures such that their hydrophobic ends are oriented to the interior of the bilayer and their hydrophilic ends are oriented to the exterior.")
(comment XWindowManagerProgram "X Windows System window managers, such as #$FVWM-WindowManager and #$Dtwm-WindowManager.")
(comment EncryptionFault "#$EncryptionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this fault if it is feasible for a person to decrypt the information it encrypts (by using a third party utility, by compromising the encryption key, etc.).  Important specializations of #$EncryptionFault are #$WeakPasswordStorageEncryptionFault and #$InsecureEncryptionKeyFault.")
(comment intends-SitType "This predicate relates an agent to a kind of situation it intends, or has in mind as a purpose, to help bring about or maintain. (#$intends-SitType AGENT SITTYPE) means that AGENT intends either

that (i) a situation of type SITTYPE come about or (ii) some particular pre-existing situation of type SITTYPE continue.  This implies that AGENT believes it has at least some degree of influence or control over (i) or (ii) occurring.  Although clearly similar to a goal (see e.g. #$goalSitRole), AGENT's intending SITTYPE is likely to be more short-term (\"I did it because I intended that...\") and more mechanically satisfied (\"I intend that the lamp be turned off.\") than any of AGENT's goals.  You may intend that the lamp be turned off, but it would be odd to call that one of your goals.  We assume that if AGENT intends a particular kind of temporal situation, it intends any more general kind of temporal situation as well.  For a similar predicate that represents intending as a propositional attitude, see #$intends.")
(comment CapAndGown "The outfit worn by participants in formal academic ceremonies (e.g, graduation).")
(disjointWith LifeStageType MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType)
(disjointWith NaturalTangibleStuff PathArtifactSystem)
(disjointWith Propelling LocomotionEvent)
(comment CycLNLSyntacticAssertion "The collection of #$CycLAssertions whose main (i.e. arg0) operators denote #$NLSyntacticPredicates.")
(comment PolynucleotideComponentType "A type level collection.  Each instance is a salient collection of #$Polynucleotides that are components (see #$MolecularComponent) within larger #$PolynucleotideMolecules.  It should be emphasized that instances of instances of this collection must themselves be #$Polynucleotides.  Hence, negative examples of instances would be collections such as #$Monomer, #$AdenineRibonucleotide, and #$Adenine-Base.  Positive examples would be #$PolyATail and #$Intron-MolecularSegment.")
(disjointWith TakingCareOfSomething Collision)
(comment HTMLSourceEditingFault "#$HTMLSourceEditingFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  Programs with this fault enable users to edit the source HTML of a web site they are browsing.  This is most notoriously a problem with certain shopping cart programs.")
(comment pluralVerb-Present "The relationship between an #$EnglishWord and its present-tense plural verb form.")
(comment cutNodeInSystem "(#$cutNodeInSystem X SYS) means that X is a single node in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS whose removal would cause the system to be disconnected.  Thus {X}, i.e., (#$TheSet X), is a node-cut-set in SYS.  That is to say, (#$cutNodeInSystem X SYS) holds if and only if (#$nodeCutSetInSystem (#$TheSet X) SYS) holds.  Note that since SYS is a #$ConnectedPathSystem whenever (#$cutNodeInSystem X SYS) holds, it is easy to see that (#$cutNodeInSystem X SYS) holds if and only if (#$nodeCutMinimalSetInSystem (#$TheSet X) SYS) holds.")
(comment Amenity "Features conducive to material comfort or convenience, or that enhance the value of a #$HumanOccupationConstruct.")
(comment Skirt-GarmentPart "A subset of #$SomethingToWearPart.  Each instance is such that, when the garment it is part of is being worn, it extends from the #$Waist (instance) of the person wearing it to some distance below his waist.  #$Skirt-GarmentPart instances do not include separate spaces for each leg.")
(comment H5-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a level five heading (the second lowest level of heading).")
(comment symmetricOn "(#$symmetricOn PRED COL) means that if MEM1 and MEM2 are elements of COL  and (PRED MEM1 MEM2), it follows that (PRED MEM2 MEM1).")
(disjointWith Marxist Fascist)
(comment biologicalSons "A specialization of #$biologicalOffspring (q.v.)  that relates a given person or other animal to each of its male biological offspring.  (#$biologicalSons PARENT SON) means that PARENT is a biological 
parent of the male SON.")
(comment VirusType "The collection of all specs of #$Virus that are used to to classify viral strains.")
(disjointWith GeographicalHemisphere HumanScaleObject)
(comment DecorativeCovering "The set of coverings that decorate an object.")
(comment Moonstone-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which is blue in color and translucent.")
(comment nthLevelOfBuilding "This predicate relates buildings to their levels by

number.  (#$nthLevelOfBuilding BLDG N LEVEL) means that LEVEL

is the Nth level of BLDG.  More precisely: if N > 0, LEVEL

is the Nth floor of BLDG that is at or above ground level

(starting from the 1st floor at ground level); if N < 0,

LEVEL is the Nth floor of BLDG that is below ground level

(starting from the (-1)th floor immediately  below ground 

level); if N = 0, (#$nthLevelOfBuilding BLDG N LEVEL) is

undefined.  Note that N denotes the _actual_ number of LEVEL

relative to the ground (when calculated as just described),

regardless of what numeral (or letter, etc.) might be used 

by the designers or occupants of the building to denote

LEVEL.  For example, some buildings with 13 or more stories,

for superstitious reasons, have no floor designated as '13';

nevertheless, such buildings have a floor (probably called 

'14') whose #$nthLevelOfBuilding is 13.  See also 

#$numberOfLevels and #$numberOfStories.")
(comment northOf "(#$northOf NORTH SOUTH) means that the #$SpatialThing-Localized NORTH is situated to the north of the #$SpatialThing-Localized SOUTH, when viewed in a planetary frame of reference, typically the terrestrial frame of reference.  To relate the positions of fixed instances of #$GeographicalThing, use the more specific, #$permanentlyNorthOf.")
(comment VulnerableToHyperlinkCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$HyperlinkCommandExecutionFault on it.")
(comment RussianSpring-SummerEncephalitis "A type of viral encephalitis.  Symptoms range from mild fever and headache to high fever, headace, stupor, tremors, coma, focal epilepsy, and flaccid paralysis.")
(comment Bite-Wound "The collection of all #$Wounds which are caused by #$Biting.")
(comment ThongWear "The collection of #$Garments designed to be worn around the #$LowerTorso, much like #$Briefs are, that leave the #$Buttocks of those who wear them completely exposed. The two main subclasses of this collection are #$ThongUnderwear and #$ThongSwimsuit")
(comment FundraisingDepartment "Each instance of #$FundraisingDepartment consists of employees who are responsible for an organization's fundraising activities.")
(comment ExportOfFn "(#$ExportOfFn PRODTYPE) denotes the class of events in which instances of PRODTYPE are commercially transferred between countries.")
(comment hasEmotionAboutExistingThing "(#$hasEmotionAboutExistingThing AGENT OBJ) means that when the sentient agent AGENT is interacting in some way with OBJ, that agent feels some emotion --- that is, (#$feelsEmotion AGENT <something>). The kinds of interactions that produce such emotion depend largely on what kind of thing OBJ is.  Thus, `Joe likes the Mona Lisa' implies that Joe feels Enjoyment when viewing the Mona Lisa.  But `Joe dislikes pizza' implies that Joe feels displeasure [(#$LowAmountFn #$Pleasure-Feeling)] when eating that kind of food.  Use specializations of #$hasEmotionAboutExistingThing (including #$likesObject and #$dislikesObject) whenever possible.")
(comment POPServerProgram "#$POPServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$PostOfficeProtocol. #$POP3ServerProgram daemons by default listen on TCP port 110, whereas #$POP2ServerProgram daemons run on port 109.")
(comment pathConnects "A #$CustomaryPathCycLConstant used for stating that a given path connects 
two things.  (#$pathConnects PATH HERE THERE) means that PATH connects HERE 
and THERE.  Often PATH is a physical path or connection along which objects 
or information may travel between HERE and THERE.  Note that PATH might 
extend beyond HERE or THERE (cf. #$pathBetween).  If PATH is bidirectional, 
then (#$pathConnects PATH THERE HERE) holds as well; but if PATH is 
unidirectional (see #$DirectedCustomaryPath), this does not hold; cf. the 
more general #$pathConnects-Commutative.")
(comment goalSitRole "This predicate relates agents to types of situations that the agent has plans to actualize. (#$goalSitRole AGENT SITUATION ROLE) means that AGENT will take steps towards actualizing some instance of SITUATION and play the role ROLE in the situation.  See also #$goals and #$goalCategoryForAgent.")
(disjointWith PhysicalDevice EcologicalRegion)
(disjointWith PredicateType FunctionType)
(comment PryingSomething "the event in which a tool is used to pry some object.")
(comment PseudomonasMallei "An instance of #$BiologicalSpecies, and a specialization of #$Bacterium.  #$PseudomonasMallei is a type of bacterium that causes Glanders (see the collection #$Glanders-Infection).")
(comment Splitting "A collection of separation events in which something splits apart, often at a seam (e.g. in an item of clothing), perforation, or grain-line (e.g. in a piece of wood).  That is, two areas of the thing are separated from one another (though perhaps not separated completely into discrete pieces or parts).  Usually, a splitting occurs along a single \"line\" or \"plane\" that runs parallel to, and for a significant distance relative to, the length of the thing split. In order to undergo a #$Splitting, the #$objectOfStateChange must be in a #$Solid-StateOfMatter.  See also #$Cracking.")
(comment RecordsRoom "Rooms in a building which are used for storage (and access) of the organization's records.")
(disjointWith Connector Garment)
(comment VulnerableBecauseAllowsUnlimitedLoginAttempts "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$UnlimitedLoginAttemptFault on it.")
(comment IPPacketMishandlingFault "An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if a remote attacker can cause the OS to crash by sending it (malformed) #$InternetProtocol packets from a remote client.")
(comment dropOffCourier "A predicate for relating an act of sending an object to a courier who delivers that object to its final destination, in that act of sending.")
(comment DoubleHelix "A #$ThreeDimensionalShapeType and a specialization of #$Helix (q.v.).  This is the collection of all double helices, whether spatially-localized or abstract.  Each #$DoubleHelix consists of two \"single\" helices that turn about a common axis.  An important specialization of this collection is #$DNAMolecule.")
(comment ServerConnectionRequestInformation "The collection of abstract information about server connection requests.")
(comment PartiallyTangibleProduct "A specialization of both #$PartiallyTangible and #$Product.  Each instance of #$PartiallyTangibleProduct is a product that has some tangible component and may, but need not, also have an intangible component.  Instances of #$PartiallyTangibleProduct include copies of a newspaper, photographs, videotapes of `Star Wars', sacks of flour, lumber, and mobile homes.")
(comment ConsumerActivist "The collection of all activists working to protect themselves and the public against dangerous or misrepresented consumer products.")
(comment cultureParticipants "This predicate relates persons (and, potentially, other
  animals) to the cultures that they participate in, are members of,
  or identify with.  (#$cultureParticipants CULTURE PARTICIPANT) 
  means that PARTICIPANT is one of the #$socialParticipants in 
  the complex instance of #$SocialOccurrence that is CULTURE.  
  Participation in a given culture implies tendencies toward certain 
  characteristic beliefs and practices (see #$cultureBeliefs and 
  #$culturePractices).")
(comment resourceCapableOf "(#$resourceCapableOf AGENT SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that AGENT has the necessary resources available to it to play ROLE in elements of SIT-TYPE.  Note that the notion of resource is different than skill (see #$skillCapableOf), technology (see #$technologicallyCapableOf), authority (see #$authorityCapableOf).  Resources are external to the agent, so that anatomy is not a resource (see #$anatomicallyCapableOf).  Money is one kind of resource and thus #$fiscallyCapableOf is implied by #$resourceCapableOf.  Having the resources to play ROLE in SIT-TYPE entails that the appropriate (necessary or sufficient) things are present or are present in sufficient amounts.--BillJ, edited by Curtis")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction LuggageSet)
(disjointWith RemovingSomething LocomotionEvent)
(comment PortScanningProgram "#$PortScanningProgram is a specialization of #$PacketSnifferProgram.  Copies of #$PortScanningProgram are used to determine what processes are running on machines in a network.")
(comment keIrrelevantArgConstraint-Inferrable "(#$keIrrelevantArgConstraint-Inferrable REL COLL) says that COLL is to be ignored as an argument constraint for REL during UIA interactions in which the argument constraints for REL are used to guess or suggest an #$isa or #$genls for a term to be related by REL.")
(comment LightingMarketCategory "The market category for all kinds of lighting supplies, including but not restricted to lamps and lightbulbs.")
(comment HyalommaTick "A kind of #$IxodidTick.")
(comment HumanHighOccupancyConstruct "A #$HumanOccupationConstruct which you might expect to find occupied by a large group or groups of people.  Examples would include theatres, dance clubs, airplane cabins, etc.")
(comment SleeveOfGarment "The collection of garment sleeves")
(comment useReformulationRuleForNBarProcessing "(#$useReformulationRuleForVPPProcessing-NonStateVerbs RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$NBarProcessingRLModule.")
(comment cultureCoreParticipants "This predicate is a specialization of #$cultureParticipants that relates persons (and, potentially, other   animals) to the cultures that they participate in in a central way.  (#$cultureCoreParticipants CULTURE PARTICIPANT)    means that PARTICIPANT is one of the primary #$socialParticipants in    the complex instance of #$SocialOccurrence that is CULTURE.     Core participation in a given culture implies possession of the qualities that the culture is defined in terms of, and implies strong tendencies toward certain    characteristic beliefs and practices of that culture (see #$cultureBeliefs and    #$culturePractices).  For example, although it is not necessarily the case that all #$cultureParticipants in teenage culture are actually in their teens, this is the case for all of that culture's #$cultureCoreParticipants.")
(comment H6-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a level six heading (the lowest level of heading).")
(comment transitiveOn "(#$transitiveOn PRED COL) means that if MEM1 and MEM2 are elements of COL  and (PRED MEM1 MEM2) and there is some thing, THING3, such that (PRED MEM2 THING3), then it follows that (PRED MEM1 THING3).")
(comment BandAidBandageProduct "Band Aids are a kind of #$Bandage made by #$JohnsonAndJohnson-Corporation.")
(comment Remembering "The class of events in which an intelligent agent recalls something from memory.  Before the remembering, the doer did not have the recalled fact in mind.  Afterwards, they do.")
(comment FloorCovering "The collection of all objects designed to be used as coverings for floors. The intended purpose could be to shelter or protect the floor, or even just to serve a decorative function. Examples include #$FloorTiles, #$Rugs, #$Carpets and wooden flooring.")
(comment executablePathname "A binary predicate that relates an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW to an instance of #$Pathname.  (#$executablePathname PROGRAM PATHNAME) means that PATHNAME is a string that indicates a typical path for the standard installation of PROGRAM.  For example, (#$executablePathname #$MSWord \"\\Program Files\\Microsoft Office\\Office\\winword.exe\") means that \"\\Program Files\\Microsoft Office\\Office\\winword.exe\" is a typical pathname for Microsoft Word.")
(comment Topaz-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which is yellow in color and translucent.")
(comment CorrespondingIntegerExtentFn "(#$CorrespondingIntegerExtentFn ATTR) denotes the instance of #$PositiveIntegerExtent QUANT such that (#$correspondingIntegerExtent ATTR QUANT).  For example, (#$CorrespondingIntegerExtentFn #$Several-NLAttr) is #$Several-Quant.")
(comment TriumphalArch "The collection of all #$TriumphalArches, free standing arches constructed as #$Monuments to commemorate great things.  The first instances were constructed by the Romans.  They are usually decorated and descriptions of great deeds are inscribed.")
(comment VulnerableToSymlinkCommandExecutionAttack "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$SymlinkFault-Execute on it.")
(comment RussianSpring-SummerEncephalitisVirus "The virus that is responsible for causing cases of #$RussianSpring-SummerEncephalitis.")
(comment markCreated "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$MarkingOnASurface (a specialization of #$Event) to instances of #$VisualMark (a specialization of #$InformationBearingThing). (#$markCreated MARKING MARK) means that MARK is the visual mark left by the event MARKING. See also the predicates #$marks (which relates the agent doing the marking to the object marked), and #$objectHasVisualMarks (which relates the mark itself to the object marked).")
(comment InsectBiting "The collection of all instances which are commonly referred
to as #$Insects biting. This collection includes #$HavingABloodMeal
which is the action done by mosquitoes that results in what is
commonly referred to as a mosquito bite, as well as instances of ant
bites, flea bites, etc.")
(comment correspondingGenQuant "Use this predicate to relate instances of #$NLGenQuantAttribute to the appropriate instance of #$GeneralizedQuantifier.")
(comment ShortShort-WomansClothing "The collection of all short shorts (with the accent on the first 'short') - i.e., #$ShortPants for women that are tight and very short.")
(comment Boeing707 "Class of jet-propelled, single-aisle passenger aircraft.")
(comment ComparisonOfInstancesFn "(#$ComparisonOfInstancesFn TYPE1 TYPE2) denotes the collection

of all #$Comparings in which exactly one instance of TYPE1 is compared

with exactly one instance of TYPE2 by some entity capable of performing comparisons.")
(comment POPServer-Network "A subcollection of #$ComputerServer, whose instances function as POP servers for instances of #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment pathTerminus "A predicate that relates a given simple customary path (see #$Path-Simple and #$Path-Customary) to its terminating ends. (#$pathTerminus PATH END) means that END is a terminating end of PATH, and that there are no further paths of the same type issuing from END that are spatially disjoint from PATH itself. A terminal end of any simple customary path may be a \"dead-end\" (i.e. a closed-off path end) or it may be open; it cannot be a #$JunctionOfPaths with more paths of the same basic type issuing beyond it. Contrast this with the predicate #$deadEndInSystem, which indicates a terminus with respect to a specified #$PathSystem only.")
(disjointWith Portal WallOfAConstruction)
(comment AbilityOfTypeToTypeFn "(#$AbilityOfTypeToTypeFn AGTTYPE TYPE) refers to the ability to engage in the spec of #$Event TYPE, that instances of AGTTYPE typically share.  For example, (#$AbilityOfTypeToTypeFn #$BasketballPlayer (#$PlayingFn #$Basketball-TheGame)) is the ability of basketball players have to play basketball.")
(comment FunctionType "A collection of collections that is a specialization of #$RelationshipType.  Each instance of #$FunctionType is a collection of #$Function-Denotationals.  The functions in a given function-category represented in the Knowledge Base are typically those sharing some common feature(s) -- often having to do with what kind of thing the functions return (see #$resultIsa and #$resultGenls) -- considered significant enough that the collection of all such functions is useful to reify.  Although what constitutes a \"significant common feature\" is difficult to specify precisely, there are many clear-cut cases.  Examples include #$IndividualDenotingFunction, #$CollectionDenotingFunction, and #$FunctionDenotingFunction.  See also #$PredicateType.")
(comment GasGangrene "A form of gangrene caused by the bacterium #$ClostridiumPerfringens. It has two main forms: cutaneous, where anaerobic infection of skin lesions results in the production of gas within affected tissue (which can then spread to the muscles), and ingested, in which infection produces gangrene of the small intestine. ")
(comment ExaminingRoom "Rooms in a medical facility which are used when the doctor (nurse, etc.) is performing the exam, or doing simple procedures.")
(disjointWith Connector ClothingOutfit)
(comment departmentHead "(#$departmentHead DEPT HEAD) says that HEAD is the head of the #$Department DEPT.")
(comment VulnerableToCGICommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a web server program with a #$CGICommandExecutionFault or a #$WebServerCGICommandExecutionFault on it.")
(comment ICMPPacketMishandlingFault "An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if a remote attacker can cause the OS to crash by sending it (malformed) #$InternetControlMessageProtocol packets from a remote client.")
(comment PresidentOfOrganization "A collection of people.  An instance of #$PresidentOfOrganization is a person who is among the highest leaders of some organization. Presidents often represent their organizations to outside entities, and may or may not have day-to-day authority within their organizations.")
(comment InformationTransferEvent-Electronic "The collection of all events in which information is transferred electronically. Examples include all instances of #$TelephoneConversation, #$EMailSending, and #$PuttingUpAWebsite.")
(comment hasAgents "(#$hasAgents AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT2 acts on behalf of AGENT1.  This does not mean that AGENT2's actions are entirely controlled by AGENT1, but that AGENT1's desires and goals can influence (prohibit, enable or constrain) the behavior of AGENT2 in some domain.  Examples include several kinds of situations: #$subOrganizations (the U.S. government has the U.S. Army as an agent), servants and slaves, and agents engaged for shorter periods of time or more restricted purposes, such as #$buyingAgents and #$sellingAgents.  In these latter cases, where control is not absolute, the predicate #$hasAgents applies only in a narrow context.  Often, but not always, AGENT1 and AGENT2 temporally intersect.")
(comment KuKluxKlanUniform "White robe and white peaked cap worn by KKK members to conceal their identity and terrify their victims.")
(comment portForProgram "A predicate relating instances of #$ServerProgram to the port numbers (and transport layer protocols) on which they customarily listen. (#$portForProgram PROGRAM PROTOCOL PORT) means that running copies of versions of PROGRAM customarily listen on PORT for packets that conform to PROTOCOL. See also #$portForProgramType.")
(disjointWith MicrotheoryType MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType)
(comment CustomarySystemOfLinks "A specialization of #$SpatialThing-Localized.  Each instance of #$CustomarySystemOfLinks is a customary or conventional network system consisting of interconnected links (instances of #$Path-Customary) and nodes of obvious types, where the elements of the system (i.e., the points, nodes, and links of the system) can be assumed without specifying them as sets (note that this is in contrast to instances of #$PathSystem, in which the sets of point, nodes, links, and loops (if any) have to be specified for the system).  Instances of #$CustomarySystemOfLinks include pipe systems, road systems, vascular systems, wiring systems, and mechanical linkages.  The links of any #$CustomarySystemOfLinks are assumed to share certain characteristics.  For example, in a road system, pipes are not links, nor are streetlights, road paint, or other non-roadways; only the roadways forming the road system are links in that system.  Moreover, what constitutes a #$JunctionOfPaths (q.v.) or #$pathTerminus (q.v.) in the system should be obvious from the system type.   The links are related to the assumed system by #$linksOfCustomarySystem (q.v.).")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction FlowerBed)
(comment VaccineForFn "(#$VaccineForFn x) denotes the collection of vaccine's for prevention of contracting infection x.")
(disjointWith ApplyingSomethingToSurface LocomotionEvent)
(comment PacketSnifferDetectionProgram "#$PacketSnifferDetectionProgram is a subset of #$DiagnosticComputerProgram .  Copies of #$PacketSnifferDetectionProgram are used to determine whether a #$PacketSnifferProgram has been installed on a network.")
(comment linkCutSetBetweenInSystem "(#$linkCutSetBetweenInSystem SET X Y SYS) means that SET is a link-cut-set in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS, and that the points X and Y in SYS are disconnected in the subsystem of SYS obtained by cutting all links in SET from SYS.  More strictly, (#$linkCutSetBetweenInSystem SET X Y SYS) is true if and only if (#$linkCutSetInSystem SET SYS) is true and (#$connectedInSystem X Y (#$LinksCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET)) is false.")
(comment ElevatorDoorway "The opening to an elevator, covered by an ElevatorDoor.")
(comment ShoeHeel "The collection of footwear heels")
(comment PersonTypeByPoliticalCulture "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$PersonTypeByCulture (since political beliefs and activities are assumed to influence a person's general beliefs, attitudes, and (at least to some extent) behavior).  Each instance of #$PersonTypeByPoliticalCulture is a collection of #$Persons who share a political culture.")
(comment Li-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify an item in a list.")
(comment TransparentProxyServerProgram "#$TransparentProxyServerProgram is the specialization of #$ProxyServerProgram whose instances are designed to run in such a way that their clients don't need to know there is a proxy involved.")
(comment DNAIntron-MolecularSegment "The collection of all instances of #$Intron-MolecularSegment
that are components of #$DNAMolecules.")
(comment UserProgram "#$UserProgram is a specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  It is the collection of programs whose running processes computer users typically interact with.  Computer users are usually able to configure these programs to suit their individual needs.  For example, #$NetscapeNavigator is a #$UserProgram because users interact with it when they browse web pages, and they can configure it to implement various security features, to store passwords, to cache a history, etc. Note that #$UserProgram and #$ServiceProgram partition #$ComputerProgram-CW.")
(comment RegionDifferenceFn "(#$RegionDifferenceFn REGION EXCLUDED) denotes the largest subregion (see #$geographicalSubRegions) of REGION that is spatially disjoint with EXCLUDED.  The returned region might not be #$spatiallyContinuous, even if REGION is.  #$RegionDifferenceFn is undefined where REGION is a subregion of EXCLUDED.  See also #$subRegionExcluding.")
(comment rememberedProp "(#$rememberedProp REM FORM) means that in the #$Remembering event, REM, the doer remembers the fact represented by the formula FORM.")
(comment Tile "The collection of pieces of the material  Tile, in sheets.")
(comment Constructing "A specialization of #$MakingSomething. In each instance of this collection, one or more #$ConstructionArtifacts, such as a house or a road, are made (or incrementally enlarged or remodeled).")
(comment Tourmaline-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which exists in a wide range of colors, and is translucent.")
(comment GreenCard-Document "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$Visa-Document.  Each instance of #$GreenCard-Document is a document issued by the #$USImmigrationAndNaturalizationService to someone who is not a citizen of the United States; the document identifies its bearer as a permanent resident of the United States, able to reside and work in any part of the United States.")
(comment Obelisk "The collection of all #$Obelisks, each being a tall and thin, pointed, fixed free-standing monumental structure, square or triangular in cross section, and tapering with height, surmounted by a more-tapering point.  Originally an Egyptian monumental design.  Many Egyptian #$Obelisks are made of single pieces of stone and are carved with hieroglyphics.  A different kind occurs in Axum in Ethiopia.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfWeaklyEncryptedSystemPasswordFile "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$WeaklyEncryptedSystemPasswordFileFault on it.")
(comment crashProgramOn "(#$crashProgramOn AGENT PROGRAM COMPUTER) means that the instance of #$IntelligentAgent, AGENT, crashes the instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW, PROGRAM, on the instance of #$Computer, COMPUTER.")
(comment LookingForSomething "A specialization of #$Perceiving-Voluntary.  Each instance of #$LookingForSomething is an event in which an agent searches for some object.  Note that #$LookingForSomething includes cases in which the search is successful, and the object is found, as well as cases in which the search is unsuccessful, and the object is not found.")
(comment OfficeOfTheRegistrar "A specialization of #$UniversityDepartment.  Each instance of this collection is an office that maintains student academic records and coordinates registration.")
(comment InsectBite "The collection of all #$Bite-Wounds that are the physical
result of #$InsectBiting.")
(comment finitaryJunctionInSystem "(#$finitaryJunctionInSystem X SYS) means that X is a finitary junction in the #$PathSystem SYS, i.e., X is an intersection joining only finitely many links and loops in SYS.  More strictly, a junction X in a #$PathSystem SYS is finitary if there are only finitely many links and loops in SYS that X is on.  As examples, all 3-way or 4-way junctions in SYS are finitary junctions.  See #$threeWayJunctionInSystem, #$fourWayJunctionInSystem, #$junctionInSystem and #$FinitaryJunctionPathSystem")
(disjointWith NavigationDevice Weapon)
(comment Miniskirt "An instance is a very short skirt.")
(comment Boeing727 "Class of jet-propelled, single-aisle passenger aircraft.")
(comment CaseProduct "Instances are products which consist of several to many instances of some type of product, packaged together in a box.  For example, a case of beer or a case of staplers.")
(comment linkedViaAffiliation "This predicate is a transitive form of the CycL relation #$affiliatedWith.  #$affiliatedWith is not itself transitive, for the good reason that the fact that, where AGENT1, AGENT2, and AGENT3 are all different, (#$affiliatedWith AGENT1 AGENT2) and (#$affiliatedWith AGENT2 AGENT3) cannot ordinarily be taken to entail (#$affiliatedWith AGENT1 AGENT3).  However, for 'link discovery' purposes, it can be very useful to know that a pair of agents can be tied together via a series of #$affiliatedWith links; moreover, because #$affiliatedWith is a #$genlPreds of a great many more specialized binary relations, #$linkedViaAffiliation affords the user of ferreting out 'chains of affiliation' between agents from masses of data that it might otherwise take a considerable amount of time to sift through.")
(comment deadEndInSystem "A #$PathSystemCycLConstant that is a specialization of #$nodeInSystem.
(#$deadEndInSystem END SYS) means that END is a dead-end node in the 
#$PathSystem SYS.  A node END in SYS is a dead-end node in SYS if there 
is exactly one link LINK in SYS that END is on and END is not on any loop 
in SYS.  One easy way to illustrate a deadend END in SYS is to picture 
it as a node with only one path (possibly very \"short\") in the system 
through which one can approach or leave END.  Note that no totally 
isolated node in SYS can be a deadend in SYS, nor can any point in SYS 
that is on a loop in SYS.  If there is no specified path-system in which 
the path ends, but the ending is a dead end of a #$Path-Customary like 
a road or wire, then use #$pathTerminus instead.")
(comment Building "A specialization of both #$FixedStructure and #$HumanShelterConstruction.  Each instance of #$Building is a (usually large) fixed structure with walls and a roof, and with some inside area or areas designed to be occupied by humans (but not necessarily as a residence).  Examples include the #$EmpireStateBuilding, Hearst Castle, an #$AircraftHangar at O'Hare, a #$Lighthouse in the Mediterranean sea, the #$SydneyOperaHouse, and the #$WashingtonMonumentInWashingtonDC.")
(comment AbilitiesOfTypeFn "A type-level version of #$AbilitiesOfFn. (#$AbilitiesOfFn AGTTYPE) 

denotes the collection of instances of #$AgentCapacity typically shared by instances of AGTTYPE.")
(comment Collector "The collection of instances of #$Person who collect things as a hobby.")
(comment HandlingADevice "A specialization of #$HandlingAnObject.  Each instance of #$HandlingADevice is an event in which a device is manipulated (with the operator holding and touching the device) so that it can be used for its #$primaryFunction.  Specializations of #$HandlingADevice include #$Pruning, #$PlayingAMusicalInstrument, #$OperatingAHouseholdAppliance, #$PumpingGasEvent, and #$WritingByHand.")
(comment MediaPlayerProgram "#$MediaPlayerProgram is the collection of #$ComputerProgram-CWs that are used to play music or video.  They interact with #$DeviceDriverPrograms, but are typically distinct from them.")
(comment EasternEquineEncephalitis-Virus "The virus that causes #$EasternEquineEncephalitis.")
(comment vulnerabilityBulletin-DOD "#$vulnerabilityBulletin-DOD is a unary predicate used to assert that a #$CycLAssertion expresses information contained in a vulnerability bulletin (IAVB) on the DOD CERT webpage at http://www.cert.mil/iava/index.htm.")
(comment PrivateRoom "A patient room which is not shared - the user has exclusive user rights to it.")
(disjointWith Shoe Connector)
(comment promisesToDoActType "'(#$promisesToDoActType PROMISING ACT-TYPE)' means that the
#$senderOfInfo in the #$MakingAPromise PROMISING promises to do an act
of type ACT-TYPE.")
(comment VulnerableToWindowManagerAuthorityBypass "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$WindowManagerAuthorityBypassFault on it.")
(comment IGMPPacketMishandlingFault "An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if a remote attacker can cause the OS to crash by sending it (malformed) #$InternetGroupManagementProtocol packets from a remote client.")
(comment VBAScriptCommandExecutionFault "A program has a #$VBAScriptCommandExecutionFault
 if it can open Visual Basic for Applications files and execute their code without giving a user prior warning.")
(comment treatProperSpecsAsNameableCollections "This predicate is used to identify collections whose proper specs are prima facie reasonable to treat as \"nameable\" -- i.e., one might reasonaby use a name when making generic claims about these specs qua classes of their instances.  For example, one might use the word \"cancer\" as a name for the class of instances of #$Cancer conditions, say in \"Cancer is a terrible disease.\" Thus (#$treatProperSpecsAsNameableCollections #$AilmentCondition) means that if a UIA user defines a new constant TERM as a spec of #$AilmentCondition, it is reasonable for Cyc to believe that (#$nameableCollection TERM).")
(comment BaseballUniform "Uniforms worn by baseball players-- includes the jersey, pants, shoes, etc.")
(comment privilegedAccountForSystem "#$privilegedAccountForSystem is a predicate relating instances of #$PrivilegedAccount (e.g., #$RootAccount, #$SystemAccountForNT) with instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  (#$privilegedAccountForSystem ACCOUNT SYSTEM) means that ACCOUNT is the account with elevated privileges on SYSTEM.")
(comment cultureReligions "This predicate relates cultures to religions that are
  prevalent within them.  (#$cultureReligions CULTURE RELIGION)
  means that RELIGION is, or has been historically, commonly 
  practiced by participants in CULTURE.")
(comment FileOnFn "(#$FileOnFn COMP PATHNAME) denotes the #$ComputerFile-Abstract on (#$fileFoundOnComputer, q.v.) COMP stored in the location specified by PATHNAME.")
(disjointWith OrganismTypeByHabitat MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType)
(comment DissuadingFromAction "A #$CommunicationAct-Single in which the #$senderOfInfo successfully induces the #$recipientOfInfo not to perform an action.  This does not cover cases where situations, rather than agents, dissuade: e.g., polling results dissuaded the politician from running.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction InnerTube)
(disjointWith Talking LocomotionEvent)
(comment TerrainFeatureTaxonType "A collection of collections of collections of terrain

features. By \"terrain feature\" is meant any natural geographical object

or feature or artificial object or purposely man-altered area that can

sensibly be indicated on a map as characteristic of a region. This notion

is very important in terrain analysis -- this activity being primarily

conceived as a military task, but applicable in any context where the

location of objects or events in a geographical environment is

relevant to the reasoning. See the very broad concept of

#$GeographicalThing and its various specializations.")
(comment keIrrelevantArgConstraint "(#$keIrrelevantArgConstraint COLL) says that COLL is to be ignored as an argument constraint for every instance of #$Relation in the KB during UIA interactions in which the argument constraints for REL would otherwise be used to guess or suggest an #$isa or #$genls for a term to be related by REL.")
(comment FrozenFoodMarketCategory "Generic market category for the many types of foods that are sold in a frozen state, a technique for extending shelf life of the product.")
(disjointWith Designing MovementOrShapeChangeEvent)
(comment typeOfSupportProvided "(#$typeOfSupportProvided HELP SUPPORT-TYPE) means that SUPPORT-TYPE is the kind of support (see #$InterAgentSupportAttribute) given to the #$beneficiary of HELP by the #$performedBy of HELP.")
(comment nodeCutSetBetweenInSystem "(#$nodeCutSetBetweenInSystem SET X Y SYS) means that SET is a node-cut-set in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS, and that the points X and Y in SYS are disconnected in the subsystem of SYS obtained by cutting all nodes in SET from SYS.  More strictly, (#$nodeCutSetBetweenInSystem SET X Y SYS) is true if and only if (#$nodeCutSetInSystem SET SYS) is true and (#$connectedInSystem X Y (#$LinksCut-SubSystemFn SYS SET)) is false.")
(comment StudyRoom "A room (usually of a house or apartment) used for reading, studying, etc.  Studies usually have lots of books in them, a desk, etc.  Usually, at least in modern human residences, studies begin by default as bedrooms.  It is the differences in funishings and activities that distinguishes a study from a bedroom")
(comment ShoeHighHeel "Heels characteristic of some of women's shoes which make the woman look taller.")
(disjointWith Organization EdibleStuff)
(comment doDefaceWebSiteHostedOn "(#$doDefaceWebSiteHostedOn AGENT MANNER SYSTEM) means that, in manner MANNER, AGENT defaces the web site hosted by SYSTEM.")
(comment cultureRegions "This predicate relates cultures to the  geographical regions in which they are found.  (#$cultureRegions CULTURE REGION) means that a significant part of the complex social occurrence that is CULTURE takes place in REGION.")
(comment equivalenceRelationOn "This predicate relates binary predicates to the collections of things to which they are equivalence relations.  Note that bearing all three relations, #$transitiveOn, #$reflexiveOn, #$symmetricOn is necessary and sufficient for bearing the relation #$equivalenceRelationOn.  Other predicates relevant to discussing equivalence relations are #$equivalenceClassWRT, #$equivalenceCollectionWRT.  See also #$EquivalenceRelation, #$EquivalenceClassFn and #$EquivalenceCollectionFn.")
(comment Nazi "The collection of all believers in the #$GermanNaziIdeology.")
(disjointWith UserProgram ServiceProgram)
(comment subRegionExcluding "(#$subRegionExcluding REGION EXCLUDED SUBREGION) means that SUBREGION is the largest subregion (see #$geographicalSubRegions) of REGION disjoint with EXCLUDED.  SUBREGION might  not be #$spatiallyContinuous, even if REGION is.")
(comment Turquoise-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which is blue in color and opaque.")
(comment requestForCommentsDocument "A series of numbered informational documents and standards widely followed by commercial software and freeware in the Internet and Unix communities. Few RFCs are standards but all Internet standards are recorded in RFCs.")
(comment MonumentalColumn "The collection of all #$MonumentalColumns, each being a tall and thin, fixed, free-standing monumental column, often round in cross-section. Examples are #$TrajansColumn in Rome, and #$NelsonsColumn in London.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfPredictableSessionID "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$PredictableSessionIDFault on it.")
(comment instrumentalRole-Type "This predicate is a type-level version of  #$instrumentalRole (q.v.) that relates an event (or other temporal  situation) to a type of individual an instance of which plays an instrumental role in it (or in bringing it about).   (#$instrumentalRole-Type SIT INSTRTYPE) means that an instance  of INSTRTYPE is used (in a broad sense of `used') by the \"doer\"  DOER of SIT in order to \"do\" (or bring about) SIT.")
(comment ComputerVulnerabilityDatabase "The #$Collection of all #$IndexedInformationSources which are databases containing information pertaining to attributes of specific pieces/brands/models/versions of hardware/software which make them vulnerable to electronic attack in some way.  See, for example, #$BugtraqFaultDatabase.")
(disjointWith TakingCareOfSomething AttackOnObject)
(comment RoadVehicle-InternalCombustionEngine "#$RoadVehicle-InternalCombustionEngine is a specialization of #$BatteryPoweredDevice, #$InternalCombustionPoweredDevice, and #$RoadVehicle.  Each instance of #$RoadVehicle-InternalCombustionEngine is a #$RoadVehicle whose principle motive power is supplied by a #$InternalCombustionEngine.  This collection is disjoint with RoadVehicle-Electric.")
(comment BursarsOffice "A specialization of both #$UniversityDepartment and #$AccountingDepartment.  Each instance of this collection is an office that supports an official in charge of funds (a treasurer), usually at a college or university.")
(comment MosquitoBite "The collection of all #$InsectBites caused by #$Mosquitos.
This collection denotes the physical object that is a result of a
#$HavingABloodMeal.")
(comment influencesAgent "(#$influencesAgent AGENT AFFECTED) means that AGENT influences the actions of AFFECTED. It does not imply that there is a present action of AFFECTED that can be explained by the influence of AGENT.  For example, (#$influencesAgent TEACHER STUDENT) can true over the period of a semester when only of some the student's actions can be explained by the influence of the teacher. In the defining context for this predicate, we do not give any examples intended to distinguish the minimum amount and frequency of influence that is sufficient for this predicate to apply at a given interval of time.")
(disjointWith Water MechanicalDevice)
(comment WomensShoe "The collection of shoes designed to be worn by women and not by men.")
(comment Boeing737 "Class of jet-propelled, single-aisle passenger aircraft.")
(comment CaseFn "(#$CaseFn PRODTYPE) denotes the class of formal products often intended for #$WholesaleBuying, and consisting of many instances of PRODTYPE packaged in some sort of box, usually cardboard.")
(comment hasEmotionAboutType "(#$hasEmotionAboutType AGENT COL) means that when the sentient agent AGENT is interacting in some way with an instance of the #$Collection COL, that agent generally feels some emotion about that instance --- that is, (#$relationInstanceExists #$feelsEmotion AGENT #$FeelingAttributeType).")
(comment linkedViaPositiveInterest "This predicate is a transitive form of the CycL relation #$positiveVestedInterest.  #$positiveVestedInterest is not itself transitive, for the good reason that the fact that, where AGENT1, AGENT2, and AGENT3 are all different, (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT1 AGENT2) and (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT2 AGENT3) cannot ordinarily be taken to entail (#$positiveVestedInterest AGENT1 AGENT3).  However, for 'link discovery' purposes, it can be very useful to know that a pair of agents can be tied together via a series of #$positiveVestedInterest links; moreover, because #$positiveVestedInterest is a #$genlPreds of a great many more specialized binary relations, #$linkedViaPositiveInterest affords the user of ferreting out 'chains of affiliation' between agents from masses of data that it might otherwise take a considerable amount of time to sift through.")
(comment pathEndsInRegion "This predicate relates a spatial path to a spatial region inside of which the path ends.  (#$pathEndsInRegion PATH REGION) means that there is a #$subPaths of PATH that contains one of  PATH's #$endsOfPathSegment and is #$pathInsideRegion REGION  (as a limiting case, the path end might be #$onLine REGION's  border).  PATH might or might not be a #$subPaths of some  SUPERPATH that does not end inside REGION; so it does _not_  follow from the above formula that REGION contains a  #$pathTerminus (q.v.) of PATH.")
(comment ActivityLoggingProgram "The collection of programs whose primary function is to record network data automatically, or to administer the files so created.")
(comment ableToAffect "'(#$ableToAffect AGENT THING)' means that AGENT is capable of causing some change in THING.  This does not imply that AGENT ever actually does cause any change in THING, but that THING is within AGENT's 'zone of influence'.  For instance, I am able to affect the ceiling panel above my head, even though I've never done anything to it.  In contrast, I cannot affect the moon.  This is an inherently vague notion, since one's ability to influence objects tends to diminish as they grow larger--or smaller--and farther away.  However, it's an important common sense concept, since we must learn what we can and cannot affect in order to understand our capabilities and limitations and plan actions accordingly.")
(comment scalarResult "ARG2 is the scalar value returned by the ParameterMeasurement test ARG1.  Although it does not necessarily reflect reality, in general we will assume that test results are accurate.")
(comment FileExecutionFault-Local "A type of #$ProgramFault. A program has this fault if a malicious user can exploit the program to run any executable already existing on the machine running the program.")
(comment EasternEquineEncephalitis "A form of encephalitis which ranges from mild fever and headache to high fever, headache, stupor, tremors, coma and spastic paralysis.")
(comment vulnerabilityAlert-DOD "#$vulnerabilityAlert-DOD is a unary predicate used to assert that a #$CycLAssertion expresses information contained in a vulnerability alert (IAVA) on the DOD CERT webpage http://www.cert.mil/iava/index.htm.")
(comment PatientRoom "Rooms in a medical facility where patients sleep and generally move into during their stay at the facility.  This can probably be generalized but for now we only mean rooms in medical facilities like hospitals, convalescant homes, and nursing homes - not prisons, summer camps, dormitories, or hotels.")
(disjointWith Hat Connector)
(comment Fleeing "This is the collection of actions in which an animal leaves
an area because of some perceived or suspected danger there.")
(comment VulnerableToDomainSocketDenialOfService "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a
#$DomainSocketDenialOfServiceFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableToLoginDenial "A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a login program that can be corrupted by an unauthorized user, making it
 impossible for legitimate users to log in.  This vulnerability is locally exploitable when it is a vulnerability that is the consequence of running a faulty local application. This vulnerability is remotely exploitable when it is the consequence of running a faulty operating system or server program.")
(comment JavaFileAccessFault "A program has a #$JavaFileAccessFault if it permits a Java applet to read files from the local file system.  This fault makes it possible for a malicious web site to download arbitrary files (if the name of the file is known) from an unsuspecting user visiting the site.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForQuantifierUnification "(#$useReformulationRuleForQuantifierUnification RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$QuantifierUnifierRLModule, which serves to 

remove un-needed #$NLTagFn expressions.")
(comment IceHockeyUniform "Uniforms worn by ice hockey players-- includes the jersey, pants, pads, etc.")
(comment VoterRegistrationCard "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$IDDocument.  Each instance of #$VoterRegistrationCard is a document certifying that its holder can vote in certain elections. Instances of #$VoterRegistrationCard will typically include the following information: the name of the voter, his or her address, his or her party affiliation, and the polling place for his or her voting precinct.  In some jurisdictions, a voter may be required to display an appropriate instance of #$VoterRegistrationCard in order to vote in certain elections.")
(comment Path-Customary "A specialization of #$Path-Spatial.  Each instance of #$Path-Customary is a spatial path which was either designed as a path by some intelligent agent, or which has a significant known function as a path for movement.  Examples include roads, railroads, sea-lanes, cowpaths, boardwalks, tubes, channels, blood vessels, fibers, wires, and communication links. An instance of #$Path-Customary may be either an instance of #$Path-Simple (in which case it would be a path with two distinct ends, not forming a cycle) or an instance of #$Path-Cyclic.")
(comment drugAdministered "This predicate relates a drug administration event to the drug administered in the event.")
(disjointWith PlayingABoardGame LocomotionEvent)
(comment equippedToDo "'(#$equippedToDo AGENT ACT-TYPE)' means that AGENT has
immediate access to whatever equipment is needed to perform instances
of ACT-TYPE.  For example, to be equipped to go skiing is to have
access to skis, poles, etc.; to be equipped to go fishing is to be
able to lay hands on a fishing pole, lure, etc.  This is a restricted
version of #$equipmentCapableOf.")
(comment CannedGoodsMarketCategory "Market category for a broad range of foodstuffs, but especially fruits and vegetables, that have been canned in order to give them an extremely long shelf life.")
(disjointWith Designing IntrinsicStateChangeEvent)
(comment TickBite-Wound "The collection of all #$InsectBites caused by #$Ticks.")
(comment cutLinkBetweenInSystem "(#$cutLinkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) means that LINK is a link somewhere between the points X and Y in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS, the removal of which would leave X and Y in disconnected components.  That is to say, (#$cutLinkBetweenInSystem LINK X Y SYS) holds if and only if (#$linkCutSetBetweenInSystem (#$TheSet LINK) X Y SYS) holds.")
(comment HoodOfGarment "Headgear usually attached to another garment like anoraks or cloaks.")
(disjointWith EdibleStuff (GroupFn Organization))
(comment ethnicity "(#$ethnicity PERSON GROUPTYPE) means that the instance of #$Person PERSON belongs to the instance of #$PersonTypeByEthnicity GROUPTYPE.   For example, (#$ethnicity #$JohnWilkesBooth #$CensusGroupOfCaucasians).  Note that an instance of #$Person may belong to more than one instance of #$PersonTypeByEthnicity.")
(comment P-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a paragraph.")
(comment RightWingExtremist "The collection of all instances of #$Person who tout #$RightistIdeology to an extreme.  Such persons are willing to fight for a return to a past socio-economic state that, by their perception, was more

reflective of their current value system.")
(comment NobelPrizeWinner "The collection of all recipients of a #$NobelPrize.")
(comment InertArtifact "The collection of artifacts (including devices) with no moving parts, no parts that move (relative to the rest of the object, excluding compression) while they perform their primary functions, and do not operate by transforming energy from one form to another or by change in state of the artifact.  Borderline examples: common elecric wire, rocking chair, pillow.  Borderline negative examples: heating element in toaster, solar oven, liquid crystal thermometer strip, and photoelectric cell.")
(comment Wig "Fake hair worn on the head.  Made of lots of chord shaped things (hairs) which are sometimes made of real hair.  Also has a bottom piece which the hair attaches to.  This a sheet of some stuff made of who knows what.")
(comment Amethyst-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which is purple in color and translucent.")
(comment maximalPathSystemOfType "(#$maximalPathSystemOfType SYSTEM TYPE) means that

SYSTEM is a \"maximal\" path system of TYPE.  That is, 

SYSTEM is of TYPE and is not a proper #$subPathSystems

of any other path system of TYPE.  SYSTEM might, however,

be a proper #$subPathSystems of some path system not

of TYPE.  Thus a given path system might be maximal with

respect to one type to which it belongs, yet not maximal 

with respect to another (perhaps broader) path system 

type to which it also belongs.  For example, a maximal 

#$GridStreetSystem that is part of a larger road system

is not a maximal #$RoadSystem.")
(comment gaugeFor "(#$gaugeFor GAUGE THING) means that GAUGE produces readings for THING.")
(comment VulnerableToNISDomainRestrictionBypass "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$NISDomainRestrictionBypassFault on it.")
(comment CommandInterpreter "#$CommandInterpreter is a specialization of #$Interpreter-Computers.  It is the collection of shells and graphical mouse and window interpreters that allow users to interact with an operating system.")
(comment SmokingCigars " The act of smoking (a) cigar(s).")
(comment Dyeing "The collection events in which some tangible thing is dyed or stained by an agent or device.")
(comment OfficeOfStudentAffairs "A specialization of both #$UniversityDepartment and #$HumanResourcesDepartment.  Each instance of this collection is an office that provides services to the students of its institution such as enrollment, housing, health, financial assistance and multicultural support.")
(comment HavingABloodMeal "The collection of events in which an #$Insect takes a blood meal from a warm-blooded animal. Several kinds of insects engage in this activity, including ticks and mosquitos. Some insects use the blood as a nutrition source; however, a female #$Mosquito takes the warm blood to develop her fertile eggs.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForVPPProcessing-NonStateVerbs "(#$useReformulationRuleForVPPProcessing-NonStateVerbs RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$VPPProcessingNonStateRLModule.")
(disjointWith Water Weapon)
(comment BikiniBottom "Bottom part of a #$Bikini.  Two main types are #$BikiniBottom-PantyLike and #$GString-BikiniBottom.")
(comment Boeing747 "Class of jet-propelled, double-aisle, double-floor passenger aircraft.")
(comment PacketMishandlingFaultFn "(#$faultOfSoftwareObject (#$PacketMishandlingFaultFn PROTOCOL PORT) PROGRAM) means that copies of PROGRAM can be caused to crash by a remote attacker who sends them #$Packet-Networks to the port specified by PORT, because PROGRAM will interpret them as conforming to PROTOCOL although they are actually malformed in some way.")
(comment ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Group "#$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Group is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Group when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to create arbitrary files with the privileges of the group executing the program.")
(comment linkedViaInterest "This predicate is a transitive version of the CycL relation #$vestedInterest.  Ordinarily, where AGENT1, AGENT2, and AGENT3 are all #$different, it would not be legitimate to infer that because (#$vestedInterest AGENT1 AGENT2) and (#$vestedInterest AGENT2 AGENT3), (#$vestedInterest AGENT1 AGENT3).  However, there are circumstances in which it can be very useful to know that two agents are linked via a transitive chain of 'interests', especially when the underpinning relationships involved may be more specialized forms of #$vestedInterest:  in a 'raw' database, it could take a human a considerable amount of time poring over the data to discover such linkages.")
(comment pathDividesRegion "This predicate relates a spatial region to a spatial path that runs through and divides it into two parts. (#$pathDividesRegion PATH REGION) means that PATH is a #$pathThroughRegion of REGION and #$pathConnects two points #$onLine the border of REGION.  That is, PATH cuts completely  through REGION and might or might not go outside of REGION  (in either or both directions).  For a specialization of this  predicate that entails that PATH goes outside of REGION in both  directions, see #$pathPassesThroughRegion.")
(comment SAMFile "Instances of #$PasswordFile found on #$NTWorkstations and #$NTDomainServers.  #$SAMFiles are instances of #$ComputerFile-AIS containing usernames and (feebly) encrypted passwords of all users on the local system.  A #$SAMFile on a given machine is located in that machine's #$WindowsRegistry.  'SAM' stands for 'Security Accounts Manager'.")
(comment ProductFn "'(#$ProductFn COLL)' picks out the subcollection of instances of the #$Collection COLL which are also instances of #$Product.  For example, (#$ProductFn #$Cookie) is the collection of cookies made to be sold.")
(comment ComputationalSystemInformation "The collection of abstract information about computers, files and processes on computers, and computer networks.")
(comment SwivelDevice "The mechanism that makes something, e.g a chair, swivel.")
(comment ParameterTest "The collection of tests which return a scalar interval as a value.")
(comment CorynebacteriumDiphtheriae "The Bacterium that causes Diphtheria.")
(comment vulnerabilityTechAdvisory-DOD "#$vulnerabilityTechAdvisory-DOD is a unary predicate used to assert that a #$CycLAssertion expressies information contained in a vulnerability technical advisory on the DOD CERT webpage http://www.cert.mil/iava/index.htm.")
(comment PathThroughSolid "The collection of all existing or designated #$Path-Spatials through solid material.  Designated paths for drilling and machining are examples, as are the paths of tunnel digging and animal burrowings.  Boring into wood and burrowing through the earth are locomotions which may follow paths of this type.  For the pure #$Trajectory of a motion through a solid (not a designated or pre-existing path), use #$TrajectoryThroughSolid.")
(comment SemiPrivateRoom "A patient room which is shared by two patients.")
(disjointWith NavigationDevice Clothing-Generic)
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureMailListAdministrationPages "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$InsecureMailListAdministrationPagesFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfPlaintextApplicationPasswordFile "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program installed on it that stores the passwords for accessing that program in a plaintext file.  This would allow a local user who does not have authorized access to that program to hijack a legitimate user's account.")
(comment GeographicalPoint-Intangible "The collection of zero dimensional intangible geographical

objects [#$GeographicalThing-Intangible.] Instances of this collection are typically points on a map.")
(comment CacheBypassFault "A program has a #$CacheBypassFault if it allows attackers to
use an HTML-formatted message to store files outside the cache. Inside
the cache, the files are usually governed by a more restrictive
security policy than outside the cache.  When exploited, this
vulnerability allows an attacker to store an HTML file in an area that
is not protected by the policies in cache.   This file may
then be used to open arbitrary files on the victim's machine and send
their contents back to the attacker.")
(comment ProfessionalTennisPlayer "The collection of instances  of #$TennisPlayer who are paid to play.")
(comment linkInSystem "(#$linkInSystem LINK SYS) means that LINK is an instance of #$Path-Simple taken as a primitive path (called a link) in the #$PathSystem SYS.  For each link LINK in a path system SYS, there is a unique pair {X, Y} of different nodes in SYS (see #$nodeInSystem) such that X and Y are the two end-points of LINK in SYS.  Other points can also be on LINK, but they cannot be nodes in SYS.  There can be no point on a link that is different from its end points but nevertheless on another link; in other words, no matter how many points there are on a particular link in a path system, none of them can be an 'intersection' (see #$junctionInSystem) except the end points of the link, which are nodes in the system.  Each link in SYS is also a path in SYS; that is, (#$linkInSystem LINK SYS) implies (#$pathInSystem LINK SYS).  Note that there is no general collection of all links.  Any path can be a link if you can somehow ignore the intersection points on it -- it all depends on the #$PathSystem.  Note also that in some cases (such as talking about relations between different #$PathSystems), using (#$LinksFn SYS) to denote the set of all links in SYS is more convenient than using the predicate #$linkInSystem.")
(comment BasketballUniform "Uniforms worn by basketball players-- includes the jersey, shorts, etc.")
(comment SystemV "#$SystemV is the collection of the other major versions of the Unix operating system apart from #$BSDUnix. Developed by AT&T. Later instances of #$UnixOS such as #$SunOS-OperatingSystem combined the best features of #$SystemV and #$BSDUnix.  For the versions of this operating system released by AT&T see #$SystemV-OperatingSystem.")
(comment cultureSpecialPractices "This predicate relates a human culture to types of 
  practices that are distinctive of it though normally only
  participated in by a relatively small number of its participants.  
  (#$cultureSpecialPractices CULTURE ACTTYPE ROLE) means that 
  a specialized subcollection of the participants in CULTURE play 
  ROLE in instances of ACTTYPE from time to time, and that most 
  participants in CULTURE would consider such activities important 
  to or distinctive of CULTURE itself.  Examples include 
  religious ceremonies and artistic endeavors that, while 
  distinctive of a given culture, are only directly participated
  in by a fraction of its members.  For a similar predicate that 
  applies to characteristic practices that are participated in by
  most or many of a culture's participants, see #$culturePractices.")
(comment CoalField "The collection of regions which are naturally rich in deposits of
coal. #$CoalField includes both developed and undeveloped coal fields. See
also #$CoalField-Developed, which is specialized for fields where coal
deposits are being mined.")
(comment SubstituteFormulaArgFn "(#$SubstituteFormulaArgFn N SUBST-ARG FORMULA) denotes the #$CycLFormula formed by replacing the Nth argument of FORMULA with SUBST-ARG.")
(disjointWith Atom PolyatomicIon)
(comment Path-Generic "A collection of things that are paths or can be considered paths.  Each #$Path-Generic is either a a non-self-crossing path (see #$Path-Simple) or a cycle (see #$Path-Cyclic).  A #$Path-Generic may be spatio-temporally abstract (e.g. links in Graph Theory; see #$Multigraph), spatially-located but intangible (e.g. a #$LatitudeLine might be used as a path in some system; see #$Path-Spatial and its specializations), or fully concrete (such as a road, railroad, sea-lane, cowpath, pipe, blood vessel, fiber, or wire; see #$Path-Customary and #$PathArtifact).  #$Path-Generic includes anything that is used as a path in some #$PathSystem (q.v.).  If a #$Path-Generic is a #$Path-Customary, then it might or might not have a specified #$PathSystem in which it is a path; if the #$Path-Generic is not a #$Path-Customary, then it can only be a path in some given #$PathSystem.  For example, an orange is not a customary path, but it can be a path for ants in a specified ant path system.  For any #$Path-Generic, there can be a #$Traversal (q.v.) of something moving along the entirety of that path (and a single #$Traversal can cross itself, double back along itself, or go back and forth along some part of a #$Path-Generic any number of times.)  Note that #$Path-Generic is _not_ a subcollection of #$Individual, because there is nothing in principle to prevent a mathematical set or a collection from being \"used as a path\" in some path system. For similar reasons, few if any (non-empty) collections or sets can definitively be considered disjoint with

#$Path-Generic.")
(comment PerformingFn "#$PerformingFn is a collection denoting function which takes as its argument a subcollection of #$Event and returns a collection of events, which collection is itself a collection of subevents of the instances of the subcollection entered in the arg1 position. For example, (#$PerformingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) returns the collection of events which consist of activities on the production end of some entertainment event or other. In other words, this is the part of an entertainment event which is work, not recreation. Moreover, producing or performing in an entertainment event would constitute a subevent of the entertainment event in question, which is itself an instance of #$EntertainmentEvent, so (#$PerformingFn #$EntertainmentEvent) is a collection of subevents of instances of #$EntertainmentEvent.  Another more specific example would be (#$PerformingFn #$BalletDancePerformance), which would be the collection of all instances of attending an instance of #$BalletDancePerformance. Since producing or performing in a ballet is a subevent of an instance of ballet, (#$PerformingFn #$BalletDancePerformance) is a collection of subevents of instances of #$BalletDancePerformance. Instances of this collection might include instances of dancing the role of Aurora in a particular performance of The Sleeping Beauty, or the activities performed by the lighting tech during that performance. Yet a third example is as follows: (#$PerformingFn #$SocialGathering) returns the collection of events in which some agent attends some instance of SocialGathering. In each case, '#$PerformingFn' is meant to distinguish the spectators from the performers, or the guests from the hosts.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction Shipyard)
(comment DrugTest "The collection of all tests for illegal drugs.  A result of True means that the substance in question was detected.")
(disjointWith CoveringSomething LocomotionEvent)
(comment exampleRelnRules "(#$exampleRelnRules RELN RULE) means that RULE is a good example of how RELN might be used in writing a #$CycLRuleAssertion.")
(comment mtImageFeature "The visual image associated with the image microtheory ARG1 has the image attribute ARG2.")
(comment PhysicalContactMakingEvent "A collection of physical contact events in which two or more objects come into physical contact with one another (see #$touches).  At the start of a #$PhysicalContactMakingEvent the objects in

question (see #$objectsInContact) are spatially separated; they make contact sometime during the event, and might or might not be touching at the end of the event.  Specializations of #$PhysicalContactMakingEvent include #$HittingAnObject and #$Landing.")
(disjointWith NuclearEvent InformationTransferEvent)
(comment NairobiSheepVirus "The virus that causes #$NairobiSheepFever.")
(comment cutNodeBetweenInSystem "(#$cutNodeBetweenInSystem NODE X Y SYS) means that NODE is a node somewhere between the points X and Y in the #$ConnectedPathSystem SYS, the removal of which would leave X and Y in disconnected components.  That is to say, (#$cutNodeBetweenInSystem NODE X Y SYS) holds if and only if (#$nodeCutSetBetweenInSystem (#$TheSet NODE) X Y SYS) holds.")
(comment Warehouse "Buildings where people (or businesses and corporations) store things ususally in bulk.  Generally this refers to commodities of some sort")
(comment SomethingToWearPart "A collection of tangible objects.  Each element of #$SomethingToWearPart is a sheetlike object that is part of a garment.  Typically they are made of some type of cloth, leather, or another thin, flexible material.  Examples of #$SomethingToWearPart include any elements of the collections #$PocketOfGarment, #$SleeveOfGarment, and #$HatBand.  #$SomethingToWearPart does NOT include belt buckles and buttons.")
(comment needs "This predicate relates agents to individual things they need to obtain or possess in order to achieve or futher some (unspecified) goal.  (#$needs AGENT OBJECT) means that AGENT needs OBJECT.  The intended sense of `needs' includes everything from matters of practical convenience to matters of life and death; see the comment on #$needs-Generic for a fuller account.  The most common cases are ones where OBJECT is some (partially) tangible object, such as a person or a tool; but OBJECT might arguably be intangible (i.e. non-spatial), such as when a chef needs a certain #$Recipe-CW. What AGENT needs OBJECT for (i.e. what goal of hers will it further) and what will happen to AGENT if she fails to obtain OBJECT (e.g. whether she will die, suffer an important loss, or just be noticeably inconvenienced or disappointed) are left unspecified in the above formula, though in practice they might be inferable from other assertions in the context (see e.g. #$needsFor).  Note that #$needs has to do with a relatively \"objective\" requirement of AGENT's for OBJECT, and does not entail a corresponding \"felt need\" on the part of AGENT.  A felt need is perhaps best represented as an assertion that a given agent both #$knows that s/he objectively #$needs a certain thing and #$desires that s/he obtain or possess that thing.  #$needs does imply, however, that AGENT is at least #$awareOf OBJECT.  See also #$needs-Type, #$needs-Prop, #$needsToDo, and #$satisfiesNeed.")
(comment requiredActorSlots "A typed-specialization (see #$typedGenlPreds) of #$rolesForEventType (q.v.), whose second argument-place is constrained to instances (see #$argIsa) of #$ActorSlot.  (#$requiredActorSlots EVENTTYPE ACTORSLOT) means that for any instance EVENT of EVENTTYPE, there is some participant ACTOR that fills ACTORSLOT in EVENT (i.e. (ACTORSLOT EVENT ACTOR) holds).  For example, (#$requiredActorSlots #$CreationEvent #$outputsCreated) means that in any creation event some output is created.")
(comment RNAIntron-MolecularSegment "The collection of all instances of #$Intron-MolecularSegment that are
components of #$RNAMolecules.")
(comment NobelPrizeForChemistryWinner "The collection of all recipients of a #$NobelPrizeForChemistry.")
(comment Candle "The collection of pieces of wax, tallow, etc. with embedded wicks designed to be burned to give light.  Modern candles are often long and slender.  The whole of a candle burns up, unlike a torch, which remains after its fuel has been consumed by the fire.")
(comment Undershirt "The collection of undershirts -- both tank tops [#$Undershirt-Sleeveless] and T-shirts designed as underwear.")
(comment QueryDedicatedPredicate "This is a collection of CycL #$Predicates that are used exclusively in querying: more specifically, to tersely implement (via backchaining) queries that would otherwise be complex disjunctions.")
(comment BarAreaInPrivateResidence "The collection of bar areas in people's homes. Typically, these are not separate, enclosed rooms, but instead are small spaces within a living room or other room. 'Wet bars' have a sink; 'dry bars' do not.")
(comment eastOf "(#$eastOf EAST WEST) means that the #$SpatialThing-Localized EAST is situated to the east of the #$SpatialThing-Localized WEST, when viewed in a planetary frame of reference (typically the terrestrial frame of reference).  To relate the positions of fixed (as opposed to moveable) instances of #$GeographicalThing, use the more specific predicate #$permanentlyEastOf.")
(comment VulnerableToFileCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$FileCommandExecutionFault on it.")
(comment LaCrosseEncephalitisVirus "The virus responsible for causing cases of #$LaCrosseEncephalitisInfection.")
(comment marks "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$Agent-Generic to instances of #$PartiallyTangible. (#$marks AGENT OBJECT) means that AGENT makes or places a #$VisualMark MARK on OBJECT, after which (#$objectHasVisualMarks OBJECT MARK) holds.")
(comment Smoking " To inhale and exhale the fumes of burning plant material, especially tobacco .")
(comment RoadVehicle-GasolineEngine "#$RoadVehicle-GasolineEngine is a specialization of #$RoadVehicle-InternalCombustionEngine.  Each instance of #$RoadVehicle-GasolineEngine is a road vehicle whose principle motive power is provided by a #$GasolineEngine.  This collection is disjoint with #$RoadVehicle-DieselEngine.")
(comment sourcePatternFor "(sourcePatternFor THING1 THING2) means that THING1 is the source pattern for the structure, arrangement or shape of THING2.  This applies to physical pattern sources (like rubber-stamps, stencils, DNA strands, record-masters and photocopied documents) as well as abstract patterns that are copied or transformed or that affect the configuration of something else (like a source text or abstract encoding).  THING2 need not be a direct copy; it can be an indirect copy (a copy of a derivative of the original), a complementary 'reverse' copy or a 'negative', or an approximate or partial derivative of the original pattern.  But it needs more than just causal influence: some basic structure of the original pattern should be preserved.  A procedural computer program that generates a wall-paper design would not be a #$sourcePatternFor it, not would a DNA strand encoding an organ structure.")
(comment BloodFeedingArthropod "The collection of #$Arthropods that take a blood meal. These
arthropods are frequently infection vectors for a number of
viruses and bacteria-causing diseases. Infected arthropods carry the
pathogens, and when they take a blood meal from another animal, those
pathogens are passed to the animal.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForVPPProcessing-StateVerbs "(#$useReformulationRuleForVPPProcessing-NonStateVerbs RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$VPPProcessingStateRLModule.")
(comment LinkFinitePathSystem "The collection of all #$PathSystems each of which has finitely many links, i.e., the collection of every #$PathSystem SYS such that the set (#$LinksFn SYS) is finite.  See also #$linkInSystem.")
(comment WindPoweredDevice "#$WindPoweredDevice is a specialization of #$KineticEnergyPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$WindPoweredDevice is powered by the wind.  Specializations of #$WindPoweredDevice include #$Windmill and #$Sailboat.")
(comment BikiniBottom-PantyLike "Bottom part of a normal #$Bikini (distinct from a #$GString-BikiniBottom).  Not the same as #$Briefs, as #$BikiniBottom is meant to be outerwear, not a spec of #$Underwear.")
(comment PostScriptCommandExecutionFault "A program has a #$VBCommandExecutionFault if an
 unauthorized person can pass PostScript code to a program and have it execute arbitrary
 commands.")
(comment DirectedPathSystem "An instance of #$PathSystemType-Structural 
and a specialization of #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem.  Each instance of 
#$DirectedPathSystem is a path system SYS in which every link LINK is 
given exactly one direction (specified by (#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SYS), 
(#$PathFromFn LINK SYS), or (#$PathToFn LINK SYS)).  Note that #$PathFromFn 
and #$PathToFn are only defined for directed path systems.")
(comment NetworkTrafficInformation "The collection of abstract information about computer network traffic.")
(comment GrindingDevice "A device that grinds objects into fine particles.")
(comment DengueFeverVirus "The collection of all of thie instances of #$Virus that cause #$DengueFever.")
(comment BiopolymerMolecule "The collection of macromolecules which are produced by and can be found within living things, such as proteins (essentially polymers of amino acids), nucleic acids (such as DNA or RNA), and polysaccharides (polymers of simple sugars).")
(comment PathThroughAirHangingFromSolid "A #$Path-Spatial through air, while hanging from a solid, such as brachiating from one tree branch to another.  An object following this #$Path-Spatial is immersed in the air but supported by the solid.")
(comment WardRoom "A patient room which is shared by many patients.")
(disjointWith ClothingAccessory ThongWear)
(comment VulnerableToStartupFileOverwrite "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$StartupFileOverwriteFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableToJavaAccessingUnauthorizedFiles "A computer has this vulnerability if is has a program 
with a #$JavaFileAccessFault.")
(comment messageAddressedTo "A predicate for relating a message to an individual to whom that message is adressed. (#$messageAddressedTo MESSAGE OBJECT) means that MESSAGE, and instance of #$Message, is addressed to OBJECT, an instance of #$SpatialThing-Localized.")
(comment keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestion "(#$keIrrelevantPrecisionSuggestion TERM) says that TERM is never to be

 offered as a precision/generalization suggestion during a UIA interaction.")
(comment KerberosAuthenticationServerProgram "The collection of Kerberos programs.  Kerberos is a
third-party authentication server for users 
and services on a network.  All principals share a secret password (or
key) with the kerberos server and this enables principals to verify
that the messages from the kerberos server are authentic. Thus
trusting the kerberos server, users and services can authenticate each
other.")
(comment instantiationOfGenInfo "(#$instantiationOfGenInfo CGIBT GI) means that CGIBT a
#$ChemicalGeneticIBT instantiates the #$GeneticInformation GI. CGIBT
carries or contains some #$GeneticInformation, consequently there's at
least one instance of #$GeneticInformationStructure that is instantiated
[#$instantiationOfGIS] in CGIBT; namely that which encodes
[#$structureEncodesGenInfo] GI.")
(comment CoalField-Developed "The collection of regions which are naturally rich in deposits of
coal [#$Coal] and have been developed to the point of commercial
production. A developed coal field has production facilities located on the
field.")
(comment Undershirt-Sleeveless "The collection of sleeveless undershirts. This is the kind of undershirt that is also called a tank top in some parts of the country, or a Guinea T in New Jersey.")
(comment PolyatomicIon "The collection of all #$Ions whose physical structure encompasses more than a single atom.  Like all #$Ions, #$PolyatomicIons possess a net electric charge that is greater than or less than 0, owing to an imbalance of #$Protons and #$Electrons.")
(comment DrugTestWithUrine "DrugTests which involve testing a sample of the subject's urine.")
(disjointWith Gardening LocomotionEvent)
(comment languagePostedOnUIA "(#$languagePostedOnUIA LANGUAGE) means that LANGUAGE is merely listed as a language option on the UIA login screen, regardless of whether it is supported.")
(comment EnvironmentVariableFault "A program has an #$EnvironmentVariableFault if it (or one of its subprograms) runs with a significant level of privilege and takes the value of some #$EnvironmentVariable as one of its inputs when executing.  Since the values of environment variables may be set by the user, a program that runs with a high degree of privilege that has this fault could be exploited by a user to execute arbitrary commands at a higher-than-user level of privilege.")
(comment DuplicateHostnameHandlingFault "On practically all networks, if two hosts come to have the same hostname, the result will be that one of the hosts will lose its connection to network services.")
(disjointWith ComputerProcessRunning PhysicalContactMakingEvent)
(disjointWith Designing Perceiving)
(comment PublicRestroom "A restroom in which you would not be surprised to see a stranger.  Usually restricted for use by only one sex. Can have several stalls.")
(comment needs-Type "This predicate relates an agent to a type of object an instance of which s/he needs to obtain or possess in order to achieve or further some (unspecified) goal (as in \"Pam needs a computer\").  The intended sense of 

\"needs\" here is broad, ranging from matters of practical convenience to matters of life and death; see the comment on #$needs-Generic for a fuller account.  (#$needs-Type AGENT OBJTYPE) means that AGENT needs an instance of OBJTYPE.  The default assumption is that there is no one particular instance needed: any instance of OBJTYPE will do.  (If there were a _particular_ computer that Pam needed, we could represent this using #$needs (q.v.) to relate her to that computer directly.)  The above formula does not imply that AGENT needs OBJTYPE itself in the sense of needing a certain abstract collection qua collection, which is a dubious notion anyway.  What AGENT needs an OBJTYPE for (i.e. what goal of hers it would further) and what will happen to AGENT if she fails to obtain one (e.g. whether she will die, suffer an important loss, or just be noticeably inconvenienced) are left unspecified in the above formula, though in practice they might be inferable from other assertions in the context (see e.g. #$needsFor).  Note that #$needs-Type has to do with an \"objective\" requirement of AGENT's for an OBJTYPE, and does not entail a corresponding \"felt need\" on the part of AGENT.  A felt need of this sort is perhaps best represented as an assertion that a given agent both #$knows that s/he objectively #$needs-Type a certain type of thing and #$desires that s/he obtain or possess such a thing. #$needs-Type does imply, though, that AGENT is at least #$awareOf OBJTYPEs in general.  See also #$needs-Prop, #$needsToDo, #$needsToHaveAttribute, and #$satisfiesNeed.")
(comment Connection-Physical "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleThing. Each instance of #$Connection-Physical is a group consisting of parts of at least two instances of #$PartiallyTangible that are in physical contact and which are connected in way such that they resist spatial separation. Examples include the connection between a table leg and a tabletop, two pieces of metal welded together, and a hinge joining a CD case cover to its backing (the last would be an instance of the more specialized collection #$Joint-Physical). While each #$Connection-Physical is an instance of #$SolidTangibleThing, and therefore has a determinate spatial boundary, there are many cases in which there are no easily describable boundaries between the parts of connected objects that are parts of the connection, and those which are not. For example, consider a connection between a table and one of its legs. If the leg is merely glued to the bottom surface of the table top, the exact spatial boundaries of the connection bewteen the parts is not clear. In contrast, the connection between a sewing needle and a thread attached by a knot to its eye is more clearly defined, because the boundaries of their connected parts are more easily determined. The group consisting of the knot and the eye of the needle determine the spatial extent of the connection.")
(comment ProfessionalCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance   of which is a culture whose core participants work in the    same profession, and which has developed around the experiences    of those core participants.  For example, there are instances    of #$ProfessionalCulture associated with #$Teacher and #$Engineer.")
(comment identityConditionsFor "This predicate relates instances of #$Collection to the relations which constitute identity conditions for members of that collection. (#$identityConditionsFor PRED COL) means that if A and B are members of COL and (PRED A B), we may infer that A and B are the same instance of COL.   #$equals is the relationship against which all identity conditions are defined and is, trivially, an identity condition for any collection.")
(comment Engraving-Print "The class of prints, usually on paper, made from an engraved plate")
(comment GeographicalThing-Intangible "A specialization of both #$GeographicalThing and #$IntangibleExistingThing (qq.v.).  The collection of all things that occupy definite locations in geographic space (in the sense of being representable on a map) but that are nevertheless best considered #$Intangible or \"imaginary\".  Examples include #$LatitudeLines and #$LongitudeLines, the courses of airplanes and ships, ballistic trajectories, territorial boundaries and borders, air traffic control zones, etc.  Contrast with #$GeographicalRegion.")
(comment CollarOfGarment "The collection of the part of the garment that goes around the neck")
(comment PreciousStone "#$PreciousStones are #$GemStones which are traditionally thought to have great value in terms of beauty, rarity, and durability. #$PreciousStones are typically used for adornment, often being incorporated into #$Jewelry.")
(comment keCommonQueryExample "This relation is the 'query' analog of
#$examplePredSentences.  It is used to specify, for a given knowledge
domain, examples that typify frequently asked questions (FAQs) that
users may reasonably be expected to have with regard to that domain.")
(comment Fountain-ArtObject "The collection of fountains that are also #$Sculptures designed by #$Sculptors or #$Architects. Instances are #$ArtObjects, in contrast with instances of #$Fountain-Artificial that are commercially produced products.")
(comment MarkingForIdentification "A collection of events.  #$MarkingForIdentification is a specialization of #$MarkingOnASurface

instances of which involve an agent making or placing a mark (or marks)

on a surface of some partially tangible object in order to make it easier 

to recognize or identify the object in the future.  Such markings might 

enable one to identify the object as a particular individual (as in the case

of stamping an automobile engine block with a VIN) or might only enable it to 

be recognized as belonging to a certain group or class (as in branding cattle).")
(comment VulnerableToProxySpoofing "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$SpoofableProxyFault on it.")
(comment RocioVirus "The virus that causes RocioEncephalitis.")
(comment objectMarked "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$MarkingOnASurface (a specialization of #$Event) to instances of #$PartiallyTangible. (#$objectMarked MARKING OBJECT) means that OBJECT is the thing whose surface is marked in the event MARKING. See also the predicates

#$marks (which relates the agent doing the marking to the object marked), #$objectHasVisualMarks (which relates the mark itself to the object marked), and #$markCreated.")
(comment Riveting "Connecting solid objects together with a rivet fastener.  The connection is not easily undone, as it involves a deformation of the rivet itself.")
(comment Automobile-GasolineEngine "The collection of all #$Automobiles that feature a #$GasolineEngine as the main #$internalPowerSource.")
(comment InsectProboscis "The collection of all body parts that are the long tubular
mouth parts to some #$Insects. Most use this to suck nectar from
flowers, like the #$Butterfly, but the female mosquito uses it to take
blood from vertebrates.")
(comment FinitaryJunctionPathSystem "The collection of all #$PathSystems in which all junctions are finitary, i.e., all junctions are intersections joining only finitely many links and loops.  A junction X in a #$PathSystem SYS is finitary if there are only finitely many links and loops in SYS that X is on.  See #$junctionInSystem and #$finitaryJunctionInSystem.")
(disjointWith Water Pipe-ConduitArtifact)
(comment BikiniTop "Top part of a #$Bikini.  Unlike a #$Bra, a
#$BikiniTop is meant to be outerwear.")
(comment VulnerableToPacketAttackFn "(#$hasVulnerability COMP (#$VulnerableToPacketAttackFn PROTOCOL)) means that COMP can be caused to crash by a remote attacker who sends a #$Packet-Network to COMP which nominally conforms to PROTOCOL but which is malformed in some way.")
(comment nationalAnthemOfCountry "The national song of a country.")
(comment hasEmotionAboutProposition "(#$hasEmotionAboutProposition AGENT PROP) means that AGENT has some emotion of some kind about the proposition, PROP.  Normally a more specialized predicate is used.")
(comment CircleAtCenterWithRadiusFn "(#$CircleAtCenterWithRadiusFn POINT DISTANCE) denotes the circle

centered at POINT and of radius DISTANCE.")
(comment BodyArmor "The collection of clothing designed to serve as a defensive covering to protect the wearer against weapons.  Early body armor was typically made of metal, wood, or leather.  Later body armor includes the \"flak jacket,\" which is constructed of ballistic nylon, and anti-bullet body armor made of Kevlar.")
(disjointWith HardcopyInformationBearingObject PathArtifactSystem)
(comment FileModificationInformation "The collection of abstract information about modifications made to files.")
(comment DrainOfBasin "The portal of a basin or container through which the liquids contained are emptied by means of gravity (as opposed to being emptied by pouring).")
(comment UsingADevice "This is the specialization of #$UsingAnObject (q.v.) instances of which involve the use of some #$PhysicalDevice.  See also  #$deviceUsed.")
(comment DengueFever "A viral infection which produces a sudden onset of fever with intense headache, pain behind the eyes, nausea and vomiting. Recovery may be prolonged and accompanied with fatigue and depression. Has a more severe form - #$DengueHemorrhagicFever ")
(comment OrganicChemicalObject "The collection of molecules or other #$ChemicalObjects which are produced by and can be found within living things, such as #$Biopolymers or #$AminoAcids.")
(disjointWith ClothingAccessory Garment)
(comment VulnerableToBinGroupSymlinkAttack "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$SymlinkFault-BinGroupOnly on it.")
(comment TCPPacketMishandlingFault "An #$OperatingSystem has this fault if a remote attacker can cause the OS to crash by sending it (malformed) #$TransmissionControlProtocol packets from a remote client.  Use this fault if the entire range of TCP ports are faulty -- if less than all are faulty, use (#$PacketMishandlingFaultFn #$TransmissionControlProtocol PORT).")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedADKInsertion "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$UnauthorizedADKFault.")
(comment InformationGatheringProgram "The collection of programs whose primary function is to record information automatically.  Important specializations include #$Spyware, instances of which are designed to gather personal information surreptitiously, and #$ActivityLoggingProgram, which includes as further specializations #$PacketSnifferProgram and #$PortScanningProgram.")
(comment IndirectFireWeapon "The collection of #$Weapons which launch  #$ProjectileWeapons in a high-angle trajectory as opposed to the flat trajectory of a #$DirectFireWeapon.")
(comment BSDUnix "#$BSDUnix is the collection of Unix versions developed by Bill Joy and others at the University of California at Berkeley.

#$BSDUnix held the technical lead in the #$Unix world until AT&T's successful standardization efforts after about 1986 (see #$SystemV), and are still widely popular.")
(comment Line-Straight "A specialization of both #$Line and #$LinearObject-Straight (qq.v.). Each instance of #$Line-Straight is an endless straight line. Examples include spatially localized objects as well as abstract lines.")
(comment RemoteLoginProgram "A specialization of #$LoginProgram.  Copies of #$RemoteLoginProgram allow remote users to log in to accounts on the computer and execute commands on the computers running those programs.  Specs of this collection include #$SSHServerProgram and #$TelnetServerProgram.")
(comment mtDefinesCulture "This predicate relates culture-defining microtheories 
  to the cultures they define.  (#$mtDefinesCulture MT CULTURE) 
  means that MT contains assertions that describe the beliefs, 
  practices, and types of artifacts that characterize CULTURE.
  See also #$cultureBeliefs, #$culturePractices, 
  #$cultureSpecialPractices, and #$cultureArtifacts.")
(comment MineralField "A collection of #$GeographicalRegions.  Each #$MineralField is a
region on the surface of the planet underground of which is rich in a
specific type of #$Mineral.")
(comment TransitiveViaArgPredicate "A collection of #$MetaPredicates used for stating that one predicate is \"transitive\" with respect to another.  See the instances #$transitiveViaArg and #$transitiveViaArgInverse for more details.")
(comment endsOfPathSegment "(#$endsOfPathSegment PATH END) means that END is at one end of the #$Path-Generic PATH; END may be either a junction or a genuine terminal-end of the path segment (note that if PATH is an instance of #$Path-Simple, then it would be related to one of its genuine terminal-ends via the more specialized predicate #$pathTerminus).  #$endsOfPathSegment is also used to relate an instance of #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPath (q.v.) to its single end-point.  Note that if PATH is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible, #$SpatialThing, or #$TemporalThing, then END is also; however, neither of them need to be an instance of any of these collections.")
(comment DrugTestWithBlood "DrugTests which involve testing a sample of the subject's blood.")
(disjointWith Biting LocomotionEvent)
(comment propEnablesAgentTo "(#$propEnablesAgentTo PROP AGT COL) says that

 the scenario described in PROP enables AGT to play the #$performedBy role in instances of COL.")
(comment EnvironmentVariable "The collection of all environment variables used (most frequently in Unix systems - see #$UnixOS) to assign default system configurations to a user.  For example, the $SHELL environment varible (represented in CYC as #$SHELL-TheEnvironmentVariable) takes as its value a filename, which is the location of the program that will be executed (by default) when a program is run for the purposes of providing the user with command-line interface with the kernel (see #$OperatingSystemKernel).")
(comment HosieryMarketCategory "The market category for miscellaneous hosiery, including socks, pantyhose, stockings, tights, and leggings.  The category is often subdivided into men's hosiery and women's hosiery.")
(disjointWith MaintenanceEvent StrictlyMentalEvent)
(comment Shigella-Dysenteriae "The bacterium that causes #$Shigellosis.")
(comment HalfBath "A room with a single toilet and sink.  One person at a time uses it.  No shower or bath.")
(comment LiningOfGarment "The collection of pieces of cloth that covers the inside surface of the garment")
(comment needs-Prop "This predicate relates an agent to a proposition

(represented by a sentence that expresses it) that s/he stands in need of being true in order to achieve or further some (unspecified) goal. The intended sense of \"needs\" includes, but is weaker than, strict physical necessity; see the comment on #$needs-Generic for a fuller account.  (#$needs-Prop AGENT SENT) means that AGENT needs or requires the proposition expressed by SENT to be true.  This implies that SENT is not currently true, but is indeterminate as to whether AGENT #$knows this (though in many cases s/he will). For example, the statement \"I need you to come here\" can be represented as my needing it to be the case that you are here; \"Joe needs a haircut\" can be represented as Joe needing it to be the case that his hair is cut (whether Joe himself realizes this or not).  What AGENT needs SENT to be true for (i.e. what goal of hers it would further) and what will happen to AGENT if SENT fails to become true (e.g. whether she will die, suffer an important loss, or just be noticeably inconvenienced) are left unspecified in the above formula, though in practice they might be inferable from other assertions in the context (see e.g. #$needsFor).  Note that #$needs-Prop is _not_ a #$PropositionalAttitudeSlot.  This is because, as the above examples show, #$needs-Prop represents a more-or-less \"objective\" requirement of AGENT's for SENT to be true, and does not entail (or preclude) a corresponding \"felt need\" on AGENT's part.  A felt need of this sort is perhaps best represented as an assertion that a given agent both #$knows that s/he objectively needs some proposition to be true and #$desires that it be true.  See also #$needs, #$needs-Type, #$needsToDo, and #$satisfiesNeed.")
(comment HurricaneHunter "Instances are people who have an unusual interest in hurricanes, to the point of \"hunting\" them.")
(comment MilitaryServiceCulture "A specialization of #$ProfessionalCulture, each instance   of which is a culture whose core participants belong to the    same branch of military service, and which has developed    around the experiences of those core participants.  For    example, there are instances of #$MilitaryServiceCulture    associated with the #$UnitedStatesArmy and the    #$UnitedStatesAirForce.")
(comment Table-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a table.")
(comment CardinalPriest "One of the three orders of #$Cardinal-CatholicBishop.")
(comment Rightist "The collection of instances of #$Person

 who accept #$RightistIdeology.")
(comment DomainExamplePredicate "The collection of instances of #$Predicate used by the #$CycDomainExamplesTool in generating example sentences in the #$UIA-CycProgram.")
(comment ServiceProgram "#$ServiceProgram is a specialization of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  It is the collection of programs whose associated running processes computer users typically do not interact with.  The configuration of these programs occurs at the system level and is typically not alterable at the user level.  For example, #$OpenSSH-TheProgram (sshd) has options that are configurable at the system level in a central location by someone with appropriate privileges, and whenever a user runs a process associated with that centrally configured program, the program's system configuration applies.  Note that #$UserProgram and #$ServiceProgram partition #$ComputerProgram-CW.")
(comment Roadway "A specialization of #$PathForWheeledVehicles.  Each instance of #$Roadway is a path artifact designed to accomodate road vehicles (see the collection #$RoadVehicle) such as cars, trucks, and motorcycles.  Specializations of #$Roadway include #$Street-Generic and #$Highway.")
(disjointWith StrictlyMentalEvent ContaminationEvent)
(comment MetamorphicRock "Instances of #$MetamorphicRock are pieces of rock that have
been altered from their original form by heat, pressure, or chemical
activity while maintaining a solid state.")
(comment FileReadAccessFault-Global "A program has this fault if a user could exploit the program to gain read access to all files on the filesystem.")
(comment similarWRTTypeSpecsViaBinRel "(#$similarWRTTypeSpecsViaBinRel THING1 THING2 COL BINPRED) means that if SPEC1 is a spec of COL such that (BINPRED THING1 SPEC1), then either (BINPRED THING2 SPEC1) or there exists a different SPEC2 such that SPEC2 is also a spec of COL, (#$similarTo SPEC1 SPEC2), and (BINPRED THING2 SPEC2).")
(comment Frieze "a decorative carving on the wall of a building")
(comment readsLanguage "(#$readsLanguage PERSON LANGUAGE) means that IntelligentAgent AGENT can read the language LANGUAGE at least somewhat fluently.")
(comment VulnerableToCommandFilteringBypass "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$CommandFilteringBypassFault on it.")
(comment RocioEncephalitis "A form of viral #$EncephalitisInfection.  Symptoms range from mild fever and headache to high fever, headache, stupor, tremors, coma, and spastic paralysis.")
(comment Talking "A collection of actions. Each instance of #$Talking is an action in which somebody (often by #$Speaking) creates a meaningful phrase.  #$Talking is often a subevent in various #$Communicating events. Note that not all instances of #$Talking involve #$Speaking, since sometimes people can talk using some non-oral language, e.g., #$AmericanSignLanguage.  #$Talking, however, is disjoint with #$Writing.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForQueryProcessing "(#$useReformulationRuleForQueryProcessing RULE) indicates that RULE will be used by the #$QueryProcessingRLModule.")
(comment IntermediateVocabTermTypeByModule "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$IntermediateVocabTermTypeByModule is a spec of #$IntermediateVocabTerm for which at least one #$CycRelatedProgram has been defined.  In CycL, this means that for any instance INS, there is some program PROG such that (#$typeUsedWithCycModule INS PROG).")
(comment CoolingAirWithADevice "Cooling the ambient air using a device, as opposed to just opening a window, etc.")
(comment RoadVehicle-DieselEngine "#$RoadVehicle-DieselEngine is a specialization of #$RoadVehicle-InternalCombustionEngine.  Each instance of #$RoadVehicle-DieselEngine is a road vehicle whose principle motive power is provided by a #$DieselEngine.  This collection is disjoint with #$RoadVehicle-GasolineEngine.")
(comment FiniteMultigraph "The collection of all #$Multigraphs (interconnected systems of nodes and links) that have only finitely many nodes, links and loops.  This is the intersection of #$Multigraph, #$NodeFinitePathSystem and #$LinkFinitePathSystem.")
(disjointWith LightingDevice Weapon)
(comment BraLikeGarment "The collection of #$Bra -like items.  This is a broader concept than #$Bra, in that #$BraLikeGarment need not be #$Underwear.")
(comment InternetServicesDaemon "The collection of programs that listen for connections on certain internet sockets. When a connection is found on one of its sockets, they           decide what service the socket corresponds to, and invoke a program to service the request.")
(comment ChainMail "#$BodyArmor that is constructed of multiple interlinking chains.")
(disjointWith OlympicSummerGames OlympicWinterGames)
(comment afford-Financial "(#$afford-Financial AGENT THING) means that AGENT can financially afford to obtain THING by paying for it, where THING may be a collection of events, objects, or service occupations or an individual event, object, or service provider and the type of transaction may be purchase, rental, or hiring.  This predicate is too general for almost any purpose, and one of its specializations should be used.")
(comment DengueHemorrhagicFever "A specialization of #$DengueFever.  Instances of #$DengueHemorrhagicFever are characterized by sudden worsening of symptoms, and a marked weakness occurs with severe restlessness, facial pallor, blotchy skin and cool extremities. May progress to bleeding nose and gums. Death usually occurs from shock.")
(disjointWith Water OrganicChemicalObject)
(disjointWith BikiniBottom Pants)
(comment VulnerableToNISCachePoisoning "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$NISCachePoisoningFault on it.")
(comment doGetCodeToExecuteAsOn "(#$doGetCodeToExecuteAsOn AGENT CODE ACCOUNT MACHINE) means that AGENT takes steps toward the goal of having CODE executed on MACHINE with the privilege-level of ACCOUNT.")
(comment VulnerableToCachePoisoning "A computer has this vulnerability if it running a server program that has a #$CachePoisoningFault.")
(comment Spyware "The collection of programs whose primary function is to gather information secretly about the user and relay it to advertisers or other interested parties. Spyware can get in a computer as a software virus or as the result of installing a new program. Data collecting programs that are installed with the user's knowledge are not, properly speaking, spyware, if the user fully understands what data is being collected and with whom it is being shared.")
(comment CellMembrane "The collection of all #$LipidBilayers that enclose eukaryotic or prokaryotic #$Cells.")
(comment CommandExecutionFault "#$CommandExecutionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW, and an important specialization of #$InputValidationFault.  A program has a #$CommandExecutionFault if an unauthorized person can execute code by sending commands directly to the program, sometimes in the form of a malicious format string (typically with metacharacters), sometimes in the form of a file sent to the program.  When this fault is present in a CGI script, for instance, it allows a remote attacker to run commands on a web server.  This fault is also found on some local programs, which often allows a local user to run commands at an elevated privilege level.  The privilege level of the commands resulting from the exploitation depends on the privilege level of the program being exploited.  For instance, exploiting an #$CommandExecutionFault on a program that runs with root privileges allows a unprivilged user to run commands as root.")
(comment Yersinia-Pseudotuberculosis "The bacterium that causes #$Yersiniosis.")
(comment EMailCommandExecutionFault "An #$EMailClientProgram program has this fault it is possible for an attacker to send specially-formed email to the program that will execute unauthorized code.  The code can be in the message itself or in an attachment to the email.")
(comment ExpellingFromMembership "The collection of all #$Actions in which a member of an #$Organization is expelled from membership in that organization.  This collection does not include voluntarily quitting membership.")
(comment argAdmittanceTestedDuringTransitiveViaInference "This QuaternaryPredicate is used to state that, when 
certain sorts of inferences take place, argument admittance 
verification is required for a specified argument-place of 
a certain predicate, where this predicate and argument-place number
are related to some transitive binary predicate via either 
#$transitiveViaArg or #$transitiveViaArgInverse.  More precisely, 
(#$argAdmittanceTestedDuringTransitiveViaInference TVA-PRED INDEX-PRED TRANS-PRED N) 
means that when the assertion corresponding to (TVA-PRED INDEX-PRED TRANS-PRED N)
is used for unification of some atomic sentence SENTENCE 
during #$transitiveViaArg or #$transitiveViaArgInverse reasoning, 
argument admittance is verified for the term in SENTENCE that has the 
position specified by N.  The INDEX-PRED predicate (i.e. the 
0th-place argument in SENTENCE), its relevant argument-place N, and
the transitive predicate, TRANS-PRED,  with respect to which the argument 
admittance verification is to be carried out are all specified 
by the argAdmittanceTestedDuringTransitiveViaInference assertion. The utility of 
#$argAdmittanceTestedDuringTransitiveViaInference is as follows.
Suppose (e.g.) that (#$transitiveViaArg INDEX-PRED TRANS-PRED N) 
and (INDEX-PRED ... ARGN ...) both hold.  In some such cases, any term in 
the \"transitive closure\" of ARGN via TRANS-PRED is itself an admissible 
argument for INDEX-PRED's Nth argument-place.  But in certain other cases 
this is not so, and thus argument admittance testing is needed to determine 
whether a given member of this transitive closure is admissible in 
INDEX-PRED's Nth argument-place.
#$argAdmittanceTestedDuringTransitiveViaInference is used to specify 
cases of the latter sort, where argument admittance testing is required,
and thereby enables us to avoid the unnecessary expense of testing all
cases.")
(comment fourWayJunctionInSystem "(#$fourWayJunctionInSystem JUNCT SYS) means that JUNCT is a 4-way junction in the #$PathSystem SYS.  Formally, a 4-way junction in SYS is any node X in SYS such that either there are exactly 4 links and no loops in SYS that X is on, there are exactly 2 loops and no links in SYS that X is on, or there are exactly 2 links and 1 loop in SYS that X is on.")
(comment domainsOfSpecialization "(#$domainsOfSpecialization PRO X) means that PRO is not only an #$expertRegarding X, but PRO has formal training about X and deals professionally with X on a regular basis. For example, (#$relationAllInstance #$domainsOfSpecialization #$Linguist #$NaturalLanguage) means that the domains of specialization of all linguists include natural language. For a similar predicate relating #$Persons to instances of #$FieldOfStudy, see #$fieldsOfCompetence and its specializations.")
(comment BasementLevelInAConstruction "#$BasementLevelInAConstruction is a specialization of #$LevelOfAConstruction.  Each instance of #$BasementLevelInAConstruction is a level in a construction that is below ground level.  See also #$AboveGroundLevelInAConstruction and #$BalconyLevelInAConstruction.")
(disjointWith KnowledgeEditingActivity LocomotionEvent)
(comment VulnerableToComputerWormInfiltration "An attribute of some instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  A computational system has the attribute #$VulnerableToComputerWormInfiltration if it is configured in such a way as to allow an instance of #$ComputerWorm to infiltrate the system.")
(comment LengthAxisFn "(#$LengthAxisFn OBJ) is a function that, applied to an individual object OBJ, returns the longest (straight) axis through the object (an #$IntrinsicAxisOfObject).  Thus #$LengthAxisFn is an #$IndividualDenotingFunction that returns a particular axis of an individual object.")
(comment Shigellosis "A bacterial infection whose symptoms begin with fever and abdominal pains followed by diarrhea, vomiting and dehydration. May progress to toxemia. Infection requires very few organisms.")
(comment WomensRoom "A restRoom for women only.  In a public place.")
(comment BodiceOfGarment "A subset of #$SomethingToWearPart.  Each instance of #$BodiceOfGarment is the part of a garment that typically covers the upper part of the torso of the person wearing that garment.")
(comment ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-User "#$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-User is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has this fault when it allows unauthorized remote users access to user accounts on the system.")
(comment ProjectileWeapon-Biological "The class of projectile weapons that are based on known
biological agents.  This is considered to be the most significant
specialization of the intersection of #$ProjectileWeapon and
#$BiologicalWeapon.")
(comment CardinalDeacon "One of the three orders of #$Cardinal-CatholicBishop.")
(comment packetTypeFirewallTarget "(#$packetTypeFirewallTarget PACKET-TYPE-BY-DIRECTION PACKET-TYPE-BY-PORT FW TARGET) means that packets of type PACKET-TYPE-BY-PORT and PACKET-TYPE-BY-DIRECTION are assigned the attribute TARGET by a firewall program running on FW.  For example, (#$packetTypeFirewallTarget (#$OutgoingWRTLANFn #$CycorpLAN) #$Packet-Internet #$Helmet-Cyc-Com #$Deny-FirewallTarget) means that helmet drops all IP packets that are outgoing with respect to the Cycorp LAN.  Again, for example, (#$packetTypeFirewallTarget (#$DestinationIPFn \"208.209.34.175\") (#$DestinationPortFn #$TransmissionControlProtocol 80) #$Helmet-Cyc-Com #$Accept-FirewallTarget) means that helmet does not filter TCP packets bound for port 80 on 208.209.34.175.")
(comment DNAExon-MolecularSegment "The collection of all instances of #$Exon-MolecularSegment that are
components of #$DNAMolecules.")
(comment programConfigurationForAccount "(#$programConfigurationForAccount U-PROGRAM ACCOUNT CONFIG) means that for the #$UserAccount ACCOUNT, the #$UserProgram U-PROGRAM has the #$ProgramConfigurationAttribute CONFIG. If it is true that ACCOUNT is logged in on a computer (see #$accountLoggedInOn) a computer and a process associated with U-PROGRAM is running on the same computer, then the process is most likely running within parameters delineated by CONFIG.")
(comment Ejecta "A possibly discontinuous mass of planetary stuff ejected violently from another topographical feature.  Typically, ejecta are those pieces of planetary stuff ejected by an impact event or the explosion of a volcano.")
(disjointWith Airport-Physical Roadway)
(comment SingleCompleteRunOfADevice "A collection of events.  An instance of #$SingleCompleteRunOfADevice is an event in which some device goes through exactly one complete cycle of the processes it normally executes.  In essence, the device starts up, runs for awhile (maybe executing a more complex series of steps), then stops.  The collection #$SingleCompleteRunOfADevice does not include random #$timeSlices of a device running, but only events which represent a whole cycle.  For example, an instance of #$CompleteRunOfAnEngine in which my Honda Civic runs through the action of all four pistons of its mighty engine, is a #$SingleCompleteRunOfADevice.  So is an instance of (#$TransportViaFn #$Airplane)  Of course the engine will carry out many full cycles in the course of its lifetime, in fact even in the course of a single second; and the airplane will carry out many flights in the course of its lifetime, in fact even in the course of a single day perhaps.")
(comment Uniform "The collection of all standardized clothing items that actors wear for some kind of Scripts that they perform be it for their job or for playing on a sports team, etc..")
(comment DiseaseType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$DiseaseType is a subcollection of #$AilmentCondition that is normally classified as a type of disease.")
(disjointWith MakingSomething MoneyTransfer)
(comment Basalt "Volcanic rock which makes up a large portion of the Earth's crust.")
(comment endSubPaths "This predicate relates a spatial path to a subpath 

that contains (at least) one of the path's ends.  

(#$endSubPaths PATH SUBPATH) means that SUBPATH is a #$subPaths 

of PATH and that PATH and SUBPATH have a #$endsOfPathSegment in 

common.  If one were to divide a simple (i.e. non-cyclic) spatial

path at any point along its length, the resulting subpaths would 

both be #$endSubPaths of the original path.")
(comment RouterBypassFault "A #$ProgramFault of some instances of #$OperatingSystem.  A router running an operating system with this fault will, under certain conditions, allow data to be sent to a blocked port on a machine on the network.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedMacroExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$UnauthorizedMacroExecutionFault on it.")
(comment RoadwayJunction-Primary "The collection of junctions of roadways that join at least two

different roads of primary importance [#$Primary-RoadClassification].")
(comment CoreDumpFault "A program has this fault if it dumps core in response to nonstandard input.  If the program is running at a privileged level on a computer, this could be a way for an attacker to get sensitive information on the computer.")
(comment Bagging "Putting objects into a bag.")
(comment HKLM-SOFTWARE-Microsoft-TransactionServer-Packages-Directory "The collection of all HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\TransactionServer\\Packages registry keys, a spec of #$ExecutableRegistryKey.  Not an #$NTStandardFileType, but fairly common.  A directory of this kind is created on an #$NTMachine when #$MSTransactionServer has been installed on it.")
(comment RoadVehicle-Electric "The collection of all #$RoadVehicles which are powered by #$ElectricalMotors, and not by #$InternalCombustionEngines.")
(disjointWith SportsTeam Cell-Organization)
(comment DirectedGraph "The collection of all directed simple graphs, i.e., node-and-link structure in which every link has one direction and no multiple links (between a pair of nodes) or loops are allowed, as studied in graph theory.  This is the intersection of #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic and #$DirectedMultigraph, which is the same as the intersection of #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic and #$DirectedPathSystem.")
(disjointWith Water RecordingOfWaveIBT)
(comment GString "Collection of all g-strings.  Includes #$GString-BikiniBottom, men's #$ThongSwimsuits, #$ThongUnderwear, and #$GString-Costumes.  By virtue of being #$ThongWear, all elements of this collection leave the #$Buttocks exposed.")
(comment PropositionPredicate "A collection of predicates that are used to make statements that are in part about the proposition expressed by a given sentence. As such, each instance of #$PropositionPredicate has at least one argument place constrained (see #$argIsa) to instances of #$ELSentence-Assertible, and is such that the meaning of the predicate depends on the proposition (see #$Proposition) expressed by the sentence (as opposed to the sentence's syntactic form or truth-value).  Instances of this collection include #$causes-SitProp and #$alleged.  An important specialization is #$PropositionalAttitudeSlot (q.v.).")
(comment VulnerableToDirectoryAccess "A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a server program with a #$DirectoryAccessFault.")
(comment NationalAnthem "The offical song of a country.")
(comment ScaleMail "#$BodyArmor constructed by attaching individual plates, or scales, to the outside of a cloth or leather garment by sewing or riveting.")
(disjointWith HomoPolymer HeteroPolymer)
(comment OlympicCompetition "The collection of Olympic competition events.  Each #$OlympicGames has many #$OlympicCompetition as #$subEvents.  The #$InternationalOlympicCommittee awards medals in each type of #$OlympicCompetition at either #$OlympicSummerGames or #$OlympicWinterGames.")
(comment ProgramBehaviorInformationFn "(#$ProgramBehaviorInformationFn PROG) denotes information about the
behavior of processes of the program PROG.")
(comment Net-Filter "Nets ; used to filter out relatively large objects from a fluid  such as air or water, or contain objects which are too large to fit  through the holes in the netting.")
(comment Coccidioidomycosis-Fungus "The Fungus that causes #$Coccidioidomycosis.")
(comment mtRefinementDomainBasis "(#$mtRefinementDomainBasis MT1 MT2) states that MT1 contains domain-specific information that is relevant to the domain represented by MT2.  MT1 does not necessarily need to be a spec-mt of MT2, because it may contain assertions of a particular nature which are not domain knowledge, but are nonetheless domain-specific.  For example, in (#$mtRefinementDomainBasis #$EBertTemplateMt #$MassMediaMt), #$EBertTemplateMt is a microtheory containing parsing templates that are particular to the domain of movies and (potentially) other media-related things.")
(comment GrainSilo "a place to store grain.")
(comment Skirt "A specialization of #$Clothing-Bottom.  Each instance of #$Skirt is an item of clothing intended to cover the lower part of the body.  Skirts are typically women's clothing, but a #$Kilt is a skirt traditionally worn by men in Scotland.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedHTMLSourceEditing "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$HTMLSourceEditingFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedBinGroupAccess "A computer has this vulnerability if it is has a program that has a #$SetGIDFault-bin.")
(comment AntiSpywareProgram "Software to detect and/or eliminate #$Spyware.")
(comment NuclearEnvelope "Each instance of this collection is a structure surrounding the nucleus of a #$EukaryoticCell.  Each #$NuclearEnvelope consists of a double membrane consisting of two #$LipidBilayers, the #$OuterNuclearMembrane and the #$InnerNuclearMembrane, and is perforated by numerous #$NuclearPores which allow for outflow of #$MessengerRNA and ingress of raw #$NitrogenBases and genetic material.")
(comment SymlinkFault "#$SymlinkFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$SymlinkFault if it, when running with root privileges, creates files in the /temp directory.  This fault allows a user to create a file in the /temp directory with the same name and then symlink that file to a file to which the user does not have authorized access.  The user then executes the program, which follows the symlink and accesses the protected file.")
(comment Yersiniosis "A bacterial infection whose symptoms include pain in the lower right abdominal area resembling appendicitis, as well as fever, vomiting and possibly diarrhea. May also produce arthritis. Carriers may be asymptomatic.")
(comment mtOfCulture "This predicate relates microtheories to the cultures 
  they are relevant for or pertain to.  (#$mtOfCulture MT CULTURE) 
  means that the assertions in MT are made, and considered true, 
  from the perspective of CULTURE.  Beyond this, the precise type of 
  relevance or pertinence will depend on other dimension attributes 
  for MT, including modality.  For a more specialized predicate 
  that relates a culture to the microtheory that precisely 
  specifies its associated beliefs, practices, and artifacts, see 
  #$mtDefinesCulture.  See also #$mtCultureBeliefs.")
(disjointWith ResigningFromEmployment ExpellingFromMembership)
(comment optionAvailableToAgent-SitType "This instance of #$TernaryPredicate is used to specify the salient characteristics of a particular kind of option available to an agent in a specific context. Specifically, (#$optionAvailableToAgent-SitType AGENT SIT_TYPE ROLE) means that playing the role ROLE in a #$Situation of type SIT_TYPE is an option available to AGENT in the context in which the assertion is made. Ordinarily GAFs which use this predicate will be asserted in fairly constrained contexts in which a limited number of contingent options exist. Also, because of #$CollectionSubsetFn, it is possible to state the conditions that SIT_TYPE must satisfy to an arbitrary degree of precision.")
(disjointWith BalconyLevelInAConstruction BasementLevelInAConstruction)
(comment PrescriptionDrugTherapy "#$DrugTherapy involving a #$PrescriptionDrug.")
(disjointWith PlacingSensoryOrganToSenseThrough LocomotionEvent)
(disjointWith Writing PhysicalSynthesis)
(comment objectPlaced "'(#$objectPlaced PUTTING OBJECT)' means that OBJECT is the something which is put somewhere in the #$PuttingSomethingSomewhere PUTTING.")
(comment MaliciousCodeAccommodatingFaultFn "(#$faultOfSoftwareObject (#$MaliciousCodeAccommodatingFaultFn MALWARE) PROGRAM) means that running copies of PROGRAM makes computers susceptible to having the worm or virus MALWARE installed on them.")
(disjointWith MaterialHandling AnalyzingSomething)
(comment RockyMountainSpottedFever "A febrile disease caused by #$RickettsiaRicketsii. Results in sudden onset of moderate to high fever, malaise, deep muscular pain, severe headache, chills and bloodshot eyes. May progress to hemorrhage.")
(comment ArtStudio "An artist's studio where the art gets made.")
(comment ShoeUppers "The collection of footwear upper parts")
(comment InsecureFilesFault "A program (in most cases a web server) has
 an #$InsecureFilesFault if it is possible for an unauthorized user to obtain files from that program, when the files' permissions are supposed to prevent this.  Typically they are the files to which the program has access.")
(comment Th-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a cell header for a row of a table.")
(comment programConfigurationForSystem "(#$programConfigurationForSystem S-PROGRAM MACHINE CONFIG) means that
on the #$Computer MACHINE, the #$ServiceProgram S-PROGRAM has the
#$ProgramConfigurationAttribute CONFIG.  Any process associated with S-PROGRAM that is running on the network of MACHINE is running within parameters delineated by CONFIG.")
(disjointWith Railway Roadway)
(comment Satanist "The collection of instances of #$Person who worship #$Satan.")
(comment SolarPoweredDevice "A specialization of #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$SolarPoweredDevice is a device which is powered by energy from sunlight.  Instances of #$SolarPoweredDevice include solar-powered calculators and solar heating systems.")
(comment Coat "Outerwear intended to cover at least the torso and arms, and possibly the legs as well.  Coats have sleeves, but not legs.")
(comment formOfDisease "(#$formOfDisease SPEC-DISEASE GENL-DISEASE) says that the instance of #$DiseaseType SPEC-DISEASE is a form of the instance of #$DiseaseType GEN-DISEASE.  For example, (#$formOfDisease (#$CancerFn #$Lung) #$Cancer) says that lung cancer is a form of cancer.")
(disjointWith SelectingSomething MakingSomething)
(comment SedimentaryRock "Instances of #$SedimentaryRock are pieces of rock that have been
formed through a process of compaction and cementation of instances of
#$Sediment.")
(comment Cottage "A small house, not necessarily modern, that is most likely in a rural area.")
(comment DNSCachePoisoningFault "A name server has this fault if it blindly receives records from other DNS servers and caches them without
 verification. Therefore, intruders who control a nameserver on the internet can force a nameserver with this fault to look up data from them and then feed it back additional and corrupt records.")
(comment VulnerableToMailAccessSymlinkAttack "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$SymlinkFault-MailSpool on it.")
(comment Cleaning "A collection of events and a specialization of #$RemovingSomething and #$TakingCareOfSomething.  In each #$Cleaning event, dirt (or some other unwanted substance) is removed from the #$objectOfStateChange of that event.  If a #$Cleaning event is successful, then the #$Dirtiness level of the object will have been lowered. A notable specialization of this collection is #$Scrubbing.")
(comment ProcessKillFault "An operating system has this fault if it allows processes to receive signals (e.g., SIGIO, SIGURG) from other unrelated processes. The processes receiving the signals may exit unexpectedly. This could allow malicious users to kill processes which were not their own. Surgical exploitation application of this fault can be used to compromise the system - for example, a process holding a bound address (NFS port 2049, for instance) can be killed off and its port stolen; this can be used to steal NFS file
 handles.")
(comment NLTaggedTermDenotingFunction "The collection of instances of #$IntermediateVocabFunction that denote intances of #$NLTaggedTerm.")
(comment Varnishing "Applying varnish to a piece of wood.")
(comment LocalGeopoliticalRegion "The collection of geographical regions 

that are conventionally defined by and in relation to geopolitical agents of 

\"local\" significance. Any region circumscribed by an instance of 

#$HumanRegionalBorder and is not an instance of its sibling #$GeopoliticalRegion 

due to its size or its relative importance in the structue of the geopoltical 

space. A good default assumtion is therefore, any regions related to less than 

national and international entities. For instance, administrative districts 

like states, regions, department, counties and cities, but also any area defined 

by a local activity such as a battle field, a playground maybe, the area where is

conducted an easter eggs hunt are positive examples.")
(comment RoadVehicle-ElectricWithBattery "The collection of all instances of #$RoadVehicle-Electric in which the #$ElectricalMotor in the vehicle is run by an on-board #$Battery.")
(comment costars "(#$costars ACTOR1 ACTOR2) means that actors ACTOR1 and ACTOR2 appear as actors in 
the same film.  For example, because Woody Allen and Diane Keaton appear
together in several movies (such as Annie Hall), (#$costars #$WoodyAllen
#$DianeKeaton) is true. Note that this predicate does not, as the name might
suggest, imply that the two actors have roles with equal status in the movie,
only that they appear in the same movie.  See also #$costarsIn")
(comment cellInOrganization "(#$cellInOrganization CELL ORG) means that the instance of #$Cell-Organization CELL is a cell within the instance of #$Organization ORG.")
(disjointWith LightingDevice Water)
(comment GString-BikiniBottom "Bottom part of a #$ThongBikini; leaves the buttocks completely exposed.")
(comment VulnerableToSecuritySoftwareBypass "#$VulnerableToSecuritySoftwareBypass is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible to bypass an security procedure that software running on the computer is supposed to implement.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with an #$SecuritySoftwareBypassFault.")
(comment NonTheisticReligion "The collection of all instances of #$Religion in which the divine (ultimate reality) is conceived in impersonal, non-agentive terms")
(comment PlateMail "#$BodyArmor constructed of a sheet of metal formed into a breast plate and backplate, a flexible metal \"skirt\", articulated metal coverings for the arms and legs, and a metal helmet.")
(comment pointOnPath "A specialization of the predicate #$onPath 
that relates a simple path (see #$Path-Simple) to any point on that 
path.  (#$pointOnPath POINT PATH) means that POINT is a point along 
PATH.  That is, POINT is on PATH but cannot move along PATH (even if 
it could move in some other sense).  It might or might not be the case 
that POINT, or some part of it, is a part of PATH.  POINT is not a 
subpath (see #$subPaths) of PATH; it is not something that is on PATH 
only occasionally (such as something moving along or stopped on PATH);
and it is does not have PATH as a part (e.g. Washington DC is not a 
point on its own Pennsylvania Avenue).  Note that the relative positions 
of points on a path do not in general form a linear order (see 
#$TotalOrdering) unless the points and the path are part of a 
particular #$PathSystem.  For example, if no path system is specified, 
both Austin and Texas can be veiwed as points on Interstate 35.")
(comment SummerOlympicsCompetition "A sporting competition which is part of the Summer Olympics.")
(comment programLogsDataType "(#$programLogsDataType PROG DATA) means that the instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW, PROG, logs the sort of #$ComputationalSystemInformation, DATA.")
(comment affordToBuy "(#$affordToBuy AGENT OBJECT) means that AGENT can financially afford to buy OBJECT.")
(comment Scale-MeasuringDevice "The collection of devices which measure mass, typically using springs or balancing weights.")
(comment constituent-MostActive "The principle or most distinctive or patentable or  what-have-you constituents of this product.  The motivation for  this was in describing drugs:  Certain drugs have several active  ingredients (see #$constituents-Active) but only one of them is so important that the drug should be named after this constituent.")
(comment InhalationalCoccidioidomycosis "The milder form of #$Coccidioidomycosis, fatal only in around 1% of cases.")
(comment Language-SpecificMicrotheory "Instances are collections of microtheories, each of which contains information pertinent to a single #$NaturalLanguage.  Examples include #$EnglishTemplateMt, #$EnglishParaphraseMt, and #$EnglishMt. ")
(comment PlayhouseClubhouse "The collection of all #$Buildings built by or for children.  Includes #$TreeHouse, secret meeting houses for children's clubs,

and purchased buildings assembled from kits. Instances of #$PlayhouseClubhouse are normally far smaller than residences, often do not have roofs, and are not climate controlled.")
(disjointWith Skirt Overalls)
(comment VulnerableToEmailReplyCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$EMailReplyCommandExecutionFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedPhysicalRootAccess "A computer has this vulnerability if its operating system permits someone with physical access to it to interfere with the boot script and thereby gain access to an account with root privilege. See also #$BootFault-RootAccess.")
(comment careerPathInOrg-OrganizationalPosition "Where LIST is a list of #$OrganizationalPositions, (#$careerPathInOrg-OrganizationalPosition ORG LIST) means that the sequence of positions represented by LIST represents one expected 'path' that an individual's career may takethrough ORG.  That is, it is expected that an individual who is 'rising through the ranks' through ORG would hold the positions listed in LIST in the temporal order in which they are listed.")
(comment InnerNuclearMembrane "Each instance is a #$LipidBilayer constituting the inner membrane of a #$NuclearEnvelope.")
(comment FileOverwriteFault "A program has this fault if it allows an unauthorized user to overwrite files to which the program has access.")
(comment YellowFeverVirus "The virus that causes #$YellowFever.")
(comment junctionInSystem "(#$junctionInSystem JUNCTION SYS) means that JUNCTION is a junction in the #$PathSystem SYS, i.e., a node in SYS that is an 'intersection' or 'branching point' of links or loops in SYS.  (For the case when no SYS is specified, see #$JunctionOfPaths.)  Formally, a node X in SYS is a junction in SYS iff either there are three (different) links in SYS such that X is on all of them, or there are two (different) loops in SYS such that X is on both of them, or there is a link in SYS and there is a loop in SYS such that X is on both of them.  For different kinds of junctions in a path system, see #$threeWayJunctionInSystem, #$fourWayJunctionInSystem.")
(comment Device-UserControlled "#$Device-UserControlled is a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each 

instance of #$Device-UserControlled is an artifact which is normally controlled by its user while serving its intended function(s).  The artifact may be guided 

during part or all of its operation, and the user may guide it by hand or 

some other means of interaction.  #$Tool is an important specialization of this collection, and further examples of #$Device-UserControlled include instances of the collections #$PomPom, #$Van, #$Spoon, and #$ToiletPaper.  This collection does not include those devices which merely require some user intervention to get started or to be set up, e.g., instances of #$SofaBed, #$Holster, or #$LightBulbIncandescent.  #$ManualCarWindow and #$AutomaticCarWindow are also not included, since they do not require user guidance while performing their main task (keeping out the wind), although they can be adjusted by the user.")
(comment Loafer "Loafers are (usually) leather shoes that slip on.")
(comment waitForOccurrenceOfEventOfType "#$waitForOccurrenceOfEventOfType is an instance of #$ActionPredicate

that relates an instance of #$IntelligentAgent to an instance of

#$TemporalObjectType.  (#$waitForOccurrenceOfEventOfType AGENT TYPE)

means that AGENT waits for an event of type TYPE.")
(disjointWith RetirementEvent ExpellingFromMembership)
(comment LocalAdministratorAccountFn "(#$LocalAdministratorAccountFn COMPUTER) denotes the #$AdministratorAccount on the particular computer COMPUTER.  That is, (#$administratorAccountForSystem (#$LocalAdministratorAccountFn COMPUTER) COMPUTER) holds. This type of account is different than a \"Domain Administrator Account\" (cf. #$DomainAdministratorAccountFn) which typically governs a number of machines.")
(comment DirectedMultigraph "A specialization of both #$DirectedPathSystem and #$Multigraph.  Each instance of #$DirectedMultigraph is a multigraph in which every link has one direction.  Note that there can be loops and multiple links between a pair of nodes in a given instance of #$DirectedMultigraph.")
(disjointWith LevelOfAConstruction ElevatorShaft)
(comment OutpatientDrugTherapy "#$DrugTherapy that occurs while one is an outpatient.")
(disjointWith Kissing LocomotionEvent)
(comment languageAvailableForUIAInteractions "(#$languageAvailableForUIAInteractions LANGUAGE) means that LANGUAGE is supported by the UIA -- i.e., the user can select LANGUAGE from the menu of languages in the user modeller, and conduct a KE session.")
(comment DesktopSecuritySoftwareBypassFault "#$DesktopSecuritySoftwareBypassFault is a specialization of #$UserRestrictionBypassFault.  A #$DesktopSecurityProgram has this fault if it is possible to circumvent the access restrictions it purports to place on files.")
(disjointWith ConnectingTogether Writing)
(disjointWith Communicating MaintenanceEvent)
(comment AuditoriumRoom "A large room with many chairs suitable for lectures or performances.  This includes lecture halls and theatre auditoria.  The ones in theatres have stages, others probably don't.")
(disjointWith ShortPants LongPants)
(comment UnaryIndividualDenotingFunctionForFn "#$UnaryIndividualDenotingFunctionForFn is an instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  For any collection COL, if there is a single #$IndividualDenotingFunction FN such that (#$assertedSentence (#$resultIsa FN COL)), the expression (#$UnaryIndividualDenotingFunctionForFn COL) evaluates to FN.  Otherwise, it is unevaluatable.")
(comment Tr-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to identify a row within a table.")
(disjointWith EMailSending SendingTangibleMail)
(comment ShoppingCartProgram "#$ShoppingCartProgram is the collection of computer programs whose primary function is to store information about products to be purchased while consumers browse e-commerce web sites.")
(disjointWith Roadway Heliport-Physical)
(comment Beret "Soft, crushable hats usually made of felt.")
(comment hasDisease "(#$hasDisease ORGANISM DISEASE) says that the instance of #$Organism-Whole ORGANISM has the instance of #$DiseaseType DISEASE.  This is a rule macro predicate, shorthand for (#$relationExistsInstance 

#$ailmentConditionAffects DISEASE ORGANISM).")
(disjointWith MakingSomething Collision)
(comment Granite "All pieces of granite, which is a solid substance composed of several kinds of rock mixed together")
(comment Gazebo "The class of usually vaguely circular (could be hexagonal, octagonal) structures found in yards and gardens, having a roof but usually open on the sides. These are mostly decorative, but can be used as a pleasant shady place to sit outside.")
(comment MyLittlePony "The largest unit of the MyLittlePony unit i.e.

the class of all the MyLittlePonies in the known universe -- or in fact the unknown universe as well in case there is or might be such a universe -- ie unknown.")
(comment VulnerableToFileDeletionSymlinkAttack "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$SymlinkFault-Deletion on it.")
(comment PursuingSomething "The collection of all instances of #$LocomotionProcess in which the locomotor is moving around in pursuit of another locomoting object.")
(comment axiomForOpenCycAssertedBy "(#$axiomForOpenCycAssertedBy ASSERTION CYCLIST) means that ASSERTION is being considered for inclusion in the first release of OpenCyc, and that ASSERTION was asserted by CYCLIST.")
(comment Galvanizing "A collection of events.  In each #$Galvanizing event, iron or steel is coated with zinc.  This coating is usually accomplished by hot-dipping, but can be done with the aid of an electric current.")
(comment thinksAbout "This rather generic cognitive awareness predicate relates an agent to a thing that s/he/it is currently thinking about, in a 

quite broad sense that includes any sort of conscious awareness

of the thing.  (#$thinksAbout AGENT THING) means that AGENT

thinks about, perceives, recalls, or is otherwise consciously 

aware of or attending to THING.  Even #$Dreaming about a given thing counts as being consciously aware of it, in the sense of \"conscious\" relevant here.  Note that the above formula means that AGENT is thinking about THING _now_; it does not mean merely that AGENT has thought about THING at some time or other, nor does it imply that AGENT thinks about THING from time to time.

Note also that any #$Thing whatsoever can in principle be the object of somebody's thinking.  See also #$subjectOfMentalSituation,  #$objectOfMentalSituation, and #$IntentionalMentalEvent.")
(comment RoadVehicle-ElectricWithFuelCell "The collection of all instances of #$RoadVehicle-Electric in which the #$ElectricalMotor in the vehicle is run by an on-board #$FuelCell.")
(comment directedCycleInSystem "(#$directedCycleInSystem CYCLE SYS) means that CYCLE is a cycle in the #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS that observes the directions of paths in SYS, i.e., all parts of CYCLE that are paths in SYS must observe the orders or directions of the paths in SYS.  For example, if PATH is a path in SYS directed from X to Y in SYS, and if LINK is a link in SYS directed from Y to X, and in addition if LINK is different from PATH, then (#$JoinPathsIntoCycleFn (#$TheList X PATH Y LINK X)) is a cycle in SYS that observes the directions of paths in SYS. Note that in a #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, every loop in SYS is a directed cycle in SYS.  Otherwise a directed cycle is a 'proper' cycle, i.e., it is the concatenation of some directed paths in SYS.")
(disjointWith HeatingDevice Water)
(comment GString-Costume "The collection of #$GStrings used as part of costumes, typically by #$Strippers.")
(comment VulnerableToActivityLogBypass "#$VulnerableToActivityLogBypass is a specialization of #$VulnerableToSecuritySoftwareBypass.  A computer has this vulnerability if a program running on the computer should log a certain type of activity  and yet a user can exploit some feature of the program to ensure that such activity is not logged.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with an #$ActivityLogBypassFault.")
(comment PolytheisticReligion "A collection of #$Religions.

In a polytheistic religion, there are believed to be multiple

#$Gods.")
(comment onlineChatParticipants "A predicate relating an online chat event to a participant in that event. (#$onlineChatParticipants CHAT AGENT) means that AGENT, an instance of #$IntelligentAgent is a participant in CHAT, an instance of #$OnlineChat.")
(comment traversalInSystem-OrderObserved "(#$traversalInSystem-OrderObserved TRAV SYS) means that TRAV is a #$Traversal of some paths in the #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, and that TRAV observes the orders or directions of links (and paths) in SYS. To say that TRAV observes the orders or directions of links in SYS, we mean that for each link LINK in SYS between X and Y, (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X LINK Y)) is a subtraversal of TRAV only if (#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SYS) holds, and for each subpath SUB between A and B of a link LINK in SYS between X and Y, (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList A SUB B)) is a subtraversal of TRAV only if (#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SYS) holds.")
(comment ApartmentUnit "An apartment where people live.")
(comment WinterOlympicsCompetition "A sporting competition which is part of the Winter Olympics.")
(comment inertIngredients "The constituents of this product which do not actually produce the effects intended by the product.  For example, ingredients which are included to affect color or flavor are #$inertIngredients if coloring or flavoring is not the intended purpose of the product.")
(comment InputtingData "The collection of all #$InformationTransferEvents in which a computational device inputs data from an #$InformationBearingThing.  Use the specialization, #$ReadingData, for cases in which the information comes from a static #$InformationBearingObject.")
(comment objectImproved "'(#$objectImproved IMPROVEMENT OBJECT)' means that in the #$ImprovementEvent IMPROVEMENT, OBJECT is the thing changed in a way viewed by the performer as an improvement.")
(comment DisseminatedCoccidioidomycosis "The more severe form of #$Coccidioidomycosis, fatal in around 50% of cases.")
(comment DirectedCustomaryPath "The collection of all instances of #$Path-Customary with a customary direction.  They can be followed (in the customary system) in one direction, but not the other.  See #$BidirectionalCustomaryPath for customary paths that can be followed in either direction in the customary system.")
(comment DomedRoof "A domed roof.")
(disjointWith Skirt BikiniBottom)
(comment ScatteringStuff "This is the collection of events in which some #$Mob of stuff is separated and dispersed.  This can be an intentional

action, as in #$SowingSeed, or unintentional, as in wind blowing

sand.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedFilePermissionChange "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$ChangeFilePermissionsFault on it.")
(comment doInstallProgram "(#$doInstallProgram AGENT PROGRAM COMPUTER) means that AGENT takes steps toward the goal of having PROGRAM installed on COMPUTER's hard drive.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureEncryptionKey "A computer has this vulnerability if is running a server
 program with a #$InsecureEncryptionKeyFault.")
(comment successiveOrgPositions "(#$successiveOrgPositions ORG POS1 POS2) means that in the #$Organization ORG, an individual who holds POS1 in ORG is expected to hold POS2 at a later date.  To put it another way, the expectation is that POS1 and POS2 will be held in temporal succession, though not necessarily in immediate temporal succession.")
(comment OuterNuclearMembrane "Each instance is a #$LipidBilayer constituting the outer shell or skin of a #$NuclearEnvelope.")
(comment FileDeletionFault "A program has an #$FileDeletionFault if allows files to be deleted by an unauthorized user.")
(comment eventPosesThreat "(#$eventPosesThreat EVT AGT) means that EVT significantly increases the chances that a vital interest of AGT will be harmed. The class of 'vital' interests in this sense includes (for instances of #$Person) physical and financial well-being, (for instances of #$Country) goals which fall under #$VitalNationalInterest, (for other instances of #$Organization) the ability to fulfill AGT's main function.")
(comment YellowFever "A viral infection whose symptoms are of short duration and varying severity, including fever, chills, headache, backache, muscle pain, nausea and vomiting. May progress to hemorrhage of the nose and gums.")
(disjointWith MusclePoweredDevice WindPoweredDevice)
(disjointWith Rhomboid EquilateralPolygon)
(comment BootFault-RootAccess "#$BootFault-RootAccess is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$BootFault-RootAccess when someone with physical access to a machine can interfere with the boot script and gain access to an account with root privilege.")
(comment hasRooms "(#$hasRooms BUILD ROOM) means that the #$SpaceInAHOC ROOM is a room or demarcated space which is physically contained within the #$ConstructionArtifact BUILD, and that ROOM is not removable from BUILD.  Spaces that can be identified in this way include lobbies, hallways, kitchens, closets, dining rooms, gymnasia, studios, stairwells, and bedrooms.")
(comment OTCDrugTherapy "#$DrugTherapy involving an #$OverTheCounterDrug")
(disjointWith TakingAStep LocomotionEvent)
(comment DiskUsageManagementProgram "#$DiskUsageManagementProgram is the collection of computer programs whose primary function is to set

and enforces hard disk quotas.")
(comment ElevatedPrivilegeFault-System "A program with this fault will, under certain conditions, allow users to elevate their account to a #$SystemAccountForNT.")
(comment RiftValleyFever "A specialization of #$HemorrhagicFeverInfection.  Instances of #$RiftValleyFever are characterized by fever, headache, malaise, joint and/or muscle pain, and inflammation of the eyes with an intolerance to light. There may also be occasional nausea and vomiting. May progress to hemorrhagic complications or encephalitis.")
(comment MovieTheaterSpace "The space known as a movie theatre or a cinema.  Not the organization.")
(comment Shirt "#$Shirt is a specialization of #$Clothing-Top.  Each instance of #$Shirt is a clothing item that is worn to cover the upper part of the human torso, with openings for the neck and lower body, and either openings for, or sleeves encircling, the arms.  Specializations of #$Shirt include #$LongSleeveShirt, #$Blouse, and #$TankTop.")
(comment Rightward "From the perspective of a specified observer, A is #$Rightward of B if from the observer's perspective A is located further toward the positive end of the Cartesian x axis than is B.")
(comment SendingTangibleMail "The collection of all events of sending a physical piece of mail via a mail delivery system, such as a government or private postal service.")
(comment RNAExon-MolecularSegment "The collection of all instances of #$Exon-MolecularSegment that are
components of #$RNAMolecules.")
(comment ChangeFilePermissionsFault "A program has this fault if an unauthorized user can change the permissions on arbitrary files on a computational system using that program.")
(comment several-GenQuantRelnFrom "(#$several-GenQuantRelnFrom RELN COL THING) is true if

several of the instances INST of COL are such that (RELN THING INST) holds.")
(comment HelperProgramTypeForFn "#$HelperProgramTypeForFn is a binary function that denotes the configuration attribute a program has by virtue of having a certain type of program designated as its helper application.")
(comment creationDateOfArtObject "(#$creationDateOfArtObject ART-OBJECT DATE) means that the date of creation

of ART-OBJECT, an instance of #$ArtObject, is DATE, an instance of

#$TimeInterval. Datation is ofently an expert matter, and even based on scientific

methods open to inherent errors and approximations. Therefore, date of creation of

object is oftenly estimated only or conventional. Although, some could

argue on the mere notion of creation of art objects, this predicate ignores

such ratiocinations and attributes to objects typically belonging to museum's

holdings a date, or a time interval, accepted by historians of art. This predicate will be

mostly usefull to enable assignation of a time period to certain objects

such as archeological pieces.")
(comment Sweatshirt "A warm heavy shirt without buttons, might have hoods, zippers.")
(disjointWith MakingSomething LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing)
(comment Phosphorite "The collection of all pieces of sedimentary rocks containing enough            #$Phosphate minerals to be a good source of #$Phosphorus.")
(comment similarWRTTypeSpecsViaBinRel-Inverse "(#$similarWRTTypeSpecsViaBinRel-Inverse THING1 THING2 COL BINPRED) means that if SPEC1 is a spec of COL such that (BINPRED SPEC1 THING1), then either (BINPRED SPEC1 THING2) or there exists a different SPEC2 such that SPEC2 is also a spec of COL, (#$similarTo SPEC1 SPEC2), and (BINPRED SPEC2 THING2).")
(comment directionsOfPath-EndToEnd "This predicate relates a spatial path to the directions between one of            its ends and the other.  (#$directionsOfPath-EndToEnd PATH DIR OPPDIR)            means that the direction from one of PATH's #$endsOfPathSegment to the            other -- call them END1 and END2 -- is DIR and the direction from            END2 to END1 is OPPDIR.  DIR and OPPDIR must of course be opposite            directions, and #$directionsOfPath-EndToEnd is symmetric with respect            to its second and third argument-positions.  This predicate is more            general than #$directionsOfPath in that it does not require that PATH            be relatively straight.  #$directionsOfPath-EndToEnd depends only on            the relative positions of END1 and END2.")
(disjointWith CordlikeObject PartOfAnHSC)
(comment northeastOf "(#$northeastOf OBJ1 OBJ2) means that the #$SpatialThing-Localized OBJ1 is to the north-east of the #$SpatialThing-Localized OBJ2, when viewed in the terrestrial frame of reference.  Note that OBJ2 is therefore southwest of OBJ1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `southwest of'.  Example: (#$northeastOf AirForceOne #$SanFranciscoBay).  If both objects are fixed instances of #$GeographicalThing, use the more specific predicate, #$permanentlyNortheastOf.")
(comment ProduceOrganizedEventType "The collection of all events in which an #$IntelligentAgent organizes an intricately planned #$Event (or series of events).  The event may be an instantiation of some #$ConceptualWork such as a play [#$Play-CW] or movie [#$Movie-CW], or it may be a political demonstration [#$PublicProtesting] or a #$Conference.")
(comment VulnerableToKernelMemoryCorruption "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$CorruptibleKernelMemoryFault on it.")
(comment HydrographicalTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections. Instances of
#$HydrographicalTerrainFeatureType are collections of natural or human made
terrain features that relate to water surface and, for some of them,
navigational use.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForComparisonRepresentation "(#$useReformulationRuleForComparisonRepresentation RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$ComparisonRepresentationRLModule.")
(comment DirectedAcyclicGraph "The collection of all those #$DirectedGraphs (node-and-link structures in which each link has one direction) each of which has no directed cycle in it.  This is the intersection of #$DirectedGraph and #$DirectedAcyclicPathSystem (which is the same as the intersection of #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic and #$DirectedAcyclicPathSystem).  A #$DirectedAcyclicGraph is often used as a representation of a #$PartialOrdering.")
(comment SportsBra "#$Bra used for sports.  Provides extra support and comfort during vigorous exercise.")
(comment VulnerableToNetworkIntrusionDetectionBypass "#$VulnerableToNetworkIntrusionDetectionBypass is a specialization of #$VulnerableToActivityLogBypass.  A computer has this vulnerability if an intrusion detection program running on the computer allows remote attackers to attack the network without detecting the attack.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with a #$NetworkIntrusionDetectionBypassFault.")
(comment Shamanism "The collection of #$AnimistReligions of northern Asia and elsewhere that embrace a belief in powerful spirits that can be influenced only by #$Shamans.")
(comment likesType "(#$likesType AGENT COL) means that when the sentient agent AGT is interacting in some way with an instance of COL, that agent feels some measure of #$Enjoyment --- that is, (#$feelsEmotion AGT #$Enjoyment). The kinds of interactions that produce #$Enjoyment depend largely on what kind of thing OBJ is.  See #$likesObject, #$dislikesType.")
(comment pathInSystem "A #$PathSystemCycLConstant predicate that 
relates a given path system to each of the simple paths in it.  
(#$pathInSystem PATH SYS) means that PATH is a path in the system SYS.
What constitutes a path in SYS is defined as follows.  (i) Every link 
in SYS (see #$linkInSystem) is a path in SYS.  (ii) Every subpath 
between points (see #$SubPathBetweenFn and #$pointInSystem) on a 
link in SYS is a path in SYS.  (iii) The concatenation of paths PATH1 
and PATH2 in SYS (see #$JoinPathsFn) is a path in SYS, provided there 
is only one point shared by both paths.  Every path in the system is 
constructible by applying (i), (ii), and/or (iii) finitely many times.  
So for example a path in SYS might \"start\" somewhere along a link, 
\"go through\" several other links and nodes (see #$nodeInSystem),  
and \"end\" somewhere along a link.  Or the path might simply go from 
one node to another.  See also #$pathBetweenInSystem and 
#$linkBetweenInSystem.")
(comment GroundsOfOrganization "A specialization of #$RealEstate and #$OutdoorLocation.  Each instance of #$GroundsOfOrganization is an area which contains buildings inhabited by some organization.  Notable specializations of #$GroundsOfOrganization include #$Campus and #$MilitaryBase-Grounds.")
(comment OlympicMedalAwardCeremonyFn "The ceremony in which the medals are awarded for this competition.")
(comment Tablet "A small, hard, object made of some compressed substance.")
(comment HomeSecuritySystem "This is the collection of instances of #$BuildingSecuritySystem which are used in #$HumanResidence(s).")
(comment ReadingData "The collection of all #$InformationTransferEvents in which a computational device inputs data from an #$InformationBearingObject.  See #$InputtingData for cases in which the data comes from a process.")
(comment ChikungunyaVirus "The virus that causes #$Chikungunya.")
(comment mtLanguage "(#$mtLanguage MT LANG) states that the #$Language-SpecificMicrotheory, MT, contains information pertinent to the language LANG.")
(comment PathOpen "#$PathOpen is the attribute of instances of #$Path-Customary that are open for transit.")
(comment Poolside "The area around a swimming pool.  Typically paved or tiled, and used for relaxing and/or sunbathing.  Patio furniture is found here.")
(comment Skirt "A specialization of #$Clothing-Bottom.  Each instance of #$Skirt is an item of clothing intended to cover the lower part of the body.  Skirts are typically women's clothing, but instances of the specialization #$Kilt (q.v.) are skirts traditionally worn by men in Scotland.")
(comment VulnerableToJavaCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$JavaCommandExecutionFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableToMaliciousHelpFileCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a program with a #$HelpFileCommandExecutionFault.")
(comment keCommonQueryPredForInstances "A macro predicate for #$keCommonQueryForTerm.  (#$keCommonQueryPredForInstances COL PRED) means that for any instance INST of COL, (#$keCommonQueryForTerm INST (PRED INST :WHAT).")
(comment NuclearPore "Each instance is a protein-scaffolded pore in the #$NuclearEnvelope surrounding some #$CellNucleus, through which #$MessengerRNA and other genetic material is capable of traveling")
(comment NetworkIntrusionDetectionBypassFault "An intrusion detection program has this fault if it allows remote attackers to attack the network without detecting the attack.")
(comment VesicularStomatitisFeverVirus "The virus that causes VesicularStomatitisFever.")
(comment SeatingDevice "#$SeatingDevice is a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$SeatingDevice is a device whose #$primaryFunction is to serve as a sitting place for people.  Types of seating devices include sofas, chairs, benches, camp and stadium stools, theatre seats, swings, bicycle seats, saddles, and more.")
(comment CombatBoot "Army soldiers wear combat boots.  Misguided youth do too.")
(comment doRemoveAuthenticationForAccount "A predicate relating instances of #$IntelligentAgent with instances of #$ComputerAccount.

(#$doRemoveAuthenticationForAccount AGENT ACCOUNT) means that AGENT removes the authentication procedure by which users log into ACCOUNT.")
(comment AgeCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture whose focal participants are of a 
  particular age group, and which has developed around the 
  experiences of that group.  Examples include teenage culture, 
  adult culture, and middle-age culture.")
(comment pseudo-antisymmetricVia "(#$pseudo-antisymmetricVia PRED EQ) means that if (PRED INS1
INS2) and (PRED INS2 INS1) both hold, then (EQ INS1 INS2) holds.")
(comment pathBetween "(#$pathBetween PATH X Y) means that the #$Path-Simple PATH goes between points (or places) X and Y, where X and Y do not 'overlap', and no further.  Both X and Y have to be on PATH (see #$pointOnPath).  Note that (#$pathBetween PATH X Y) is more specific than (#$pathConnects PATH X Y) because here the PATH cannot extend beyond X and Y.  Within a particular #$PathSystem, a path's end points in the system are unique, and #$pathBetweenInSystem (q.v.) is restricted to paths and points in the system.  When considered without a context of a path system, a path may have several different places at one end, such as Austin and Texas both being at the same end of some path along Highway I-35.")
(comment objectSought "#$objectSought is a predicate that relates an instance of #$PurposefulAction in which something is being looked for to the thing sought. (#$objectSought ACTION OBJECT) means that one of the purposes of ACTION is to locate OBJECT.")
(comment MemorialMarker "A specialization of #$SymbolicObject and #$ConstructionArtifact. Each instance of this collection is an artifact built to commemorate an individual, group of individuals or event. The collection includes gravestones, statues, and pyramids.  See #$honorsThing and its specializations. Large and imposing instances of #$MemorialMarker fall under the more specialized collection #$Monument.")
(comment Chemotherapy "Chemical treatment of cancer.")
(disjointWith MakingAGesture LocomotionEvent)
(comment DiskUsageManagementSoftwareBypassFault "#$DiskUsageManagementSoftwareBypassFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A #$DiskUsageManagementProgram has this fault if it is possible to circumvent the disk quota policies it purports to have established.")
(comment UnauthorizedMacroExecutionFault "A program has this fault if it is possible for a file, when opened, to execute macros without first alerting the user.")
(comment containsInstructionsForActionType "(#$containsInstructionsForActionType IBT TYPE) means that IBT contains instructions for performing an activity of type, TYPE. For example, (#$containsInstructionsForActionType InstructionSheet392 (#$MakingFn (#$ModelFn #$Airplane))) means that InstructionSheet392 contains instructions for performing the activity of making a model airplane.")
(comment RelapsingFever "A recurring febrile disease transmitted to humans by ticks (endemic form) and by body lice (epidemic form), and is caused by several forms of Borrelia recurrentis (#$BorreliaRecurrentis-Species). Produces periods of fever (lasting 2 to 9 days) followed by periods without fever (lasting 2 to 4 days). The number of cycles varies from 1 to 10.")
(comment Clothing-Bottom "#$Clothing-Bottom is a specialization of #$Garment.  Each instance of #$Clothing-Bottom is a clothing item that covers at least the #$LowerTorso, but does not significantly cover the #$Chest-BodyPart.  Instances of #$Clothing-Bottom are outerwear, in the sense that in modern western cultures someone wearing a #$Clothing-Bottom only needs a #$Clothing-Top and shoes to be considered #$FullyClothed.  #$Overalls are a marginal case, in that they do cover some of the chest, but are normally worn with a #$Clothing-Top.")
(comment ChallengingSomeone "This is the collection of actions in which one agent (the
#$challenger) issues a challenge to another agent (the #$challengee)
to do something (the #$challengesToDo).")
(comment loggedInOnComputer "(#$loggedInOnComputer AGENT COMPUTER) means that AGENT has
access to an account on COMPUTER, which allows AGENT to execute
commands on that computer.")
(comment prepositionStrings "(#$prepositionStrings WORD STRING) states that STRING is the preposition form for the word unit WORD in some microtheory.")
(comment HelperProgramForFn "#$HelperProgramForFn is a binary function that denotes the configuration attribute a program has by virtue of having a certain  program designated as its helper application.  Compare this function with #$HelperProgramTypeForFn.")
(disjointWith Roadway LaunchPad)
(comment pathGrade "The steepness of the slope of this #$Path-Generic  expressed as a ratio (rise/run).  For example, a highway with a grade of 0.07 is fairly steep.  Stairs have a grade of about 1, and ladders have an extremely high grade, infinite if they go straight up.")
(comment StoneSculpture "Stone sculptures as art forms.")
(comment ButtonTheFastener "Buttons on cloth or leather which have corresponding holes.")
(comment dislikesObject "(#$dislikesObject AGT OBJ) means that when the sentient agent AGT is interacting in some way with OBJ, that agent feels some measure of displeasure --- that is, (#$feelsEmotion AGT (#$LowAmountFn #$Enjoyment)).  The kinds of interactions that produce displeasure depend largely on what kind of thing OBJ is. Thus, `Joe dislikes the Mona Lisa' implies that Joe feels displeasure when viewing the Mona Lisa. But `Joe dislikes pizza' implies that Joe feels displeasure when eating that kind of food, and would prefer not to eat it.  There are some specialized predicates of #$dislikesObject that give more information such as #$hates.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureDTMLFiles "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$InsecureDTMLFilesFault on it.")
(comment HypsographicalTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections. Instances of
#$HypsographicalTerrainFeatureType are collections of natural terrain
features that pertain to the measurement and description of topographical
relief. On Earth, the focus of interest is on features above sea level.")
(comment ApplyingAdhesiveBackedMaterialToSurface "A collection of events. In each #$ApplyingAdhesiveBackedMaterialToSurface event, a physical object is attached to a surface by and along its adhesive surface.  Examples of #$ApplyingAdhesiveBackedMaterialToSurface include attachment of stickers, stamps, stamp hinges,  some linoleum, and some wallpaper to appropriate surfaces.")
(disjointWith UnintendedLossOfUserRights AbandoningSomething)
(comment sourcePatternFor-Direct "(sourcePatternFor THING1 THING2) means that THING1 is the direct source pattern for the structure, arrangement or shape of THING2 in a single stage without intermediate patterns.  This applies to physical pattern sources (like rubber-stamps, stencils, immediate mRNA copies of DNA strands, and documents directly copied from the original) as well as abstract patterns that immediately  determine  the configuration of something else (like a source text or abstract encoding).  THING2 must be a direct copy or derivative; it cannot be an indirect copy (a derivative of a derivative of the original).  It can be a complementary 'reverse' copy or a 'negative', or an approximate or partial derivative of the original pattern.  But it needs more than just causal influence: some basic structure of the original pattern should be preserved. See also #$sourcePatternFor-Indirect.")
(comment VectorBornePathogenType "The class of all types of pathogens (#$Microorganisms that are capable of causing some pathology in another kind of organism) such that they cause illnesses that are spread by vectors.  More specifically, every instance of #$VectorBornePathogenType is a spec of #$Microorganism whose instances are typically capable of causing an #$Infection that is of a type normally propagated by some vector, i.e, such that there exists an #$infectionTypeHasVectorType for the type.  See also #$VectorBorneInfectionType.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForTypeShifting "(#$useReformulationRuleForTypeShifting RULE) indicates

that RULE will be used by the #$TypeShiftingRLModule.")
(comment SwimWear "The collection of all #$Garments that are worn for swimming.  Includes as members #$SwimSuits and the various subpieces of any #$SwimSuits.")
(comment exportTypeOf "(#$exportTypeOf IMP-EXP-TYPE PT) means that the event type IMP-EXP-TYPE, a spec of #$ImportExportEvent, is the collection of events in which instances of PT are commercially transferred between countries.")
(comment VulnerableToPortscanProtectionBypass "#$VulnerableToPortscanProtectionBypass is a specialization of #$VulnerableToActivityLogBypass.  A computer has this vulnerability if a #$FirewallProgram running on it allows remote attackers to conduct a port scan on its network without logging the attack.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running a program with a #$PortscanProtectionBypassFault.")
(comment MonotheisticReligion "The collection of all monotheistic religions, or religions whose believers are taught to acknowledge and worship only one God.")
(comment BidirectedPathSystem "An instance of #$PathSystemType-Structural 
and a specialization of #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem.  Each instance of #$BidirectedPathSystem is such that every link in it has two directions 
(see #$linkFromToInSystem).")
(comment ComputerFileFormatFn "(ComputerFileFormatFn CONV) denotes the collection of all computer files that are encoded according to convention CONV.  For example, (#$ComputerFileFormatFn #$Perl-ProgrammingLanguage) denotes the collection of all computer files that are written in Perl, and (#$ComputerFileFormatFn #$LanManHash) denoted the collection of files encrypted according to the #$LanManHash.")
(comment OlympicSummerGames "The set of #$OlympicGames which occur in the summer.")
(comment affordToBuyType "(#$affordToBuyType AGENT OBJECTTYPE) means that AGENT can financially afford to buy an instance of OBJECTTYPE.")
(comment Syrup "Syrup is a sweet sticky substance with the same viscousity as honey.")
(comment BuildingSecuritySystem "Intrusion detectors, alarms, or whatever.")
(comment seemsLikeTo "(#$seemsLikeTo THING1 THING2 AGENT) means that, to the person or other agent AGENT, THING1 seems like THING2.  For example, a fake #$MonaLisa-Painting might seem like the real one to a non-expert.  Or #$Canada might seem like the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica to an Asian visitor.")
(comment Chikungunya "A form of viral infection. Causes arthritis in wrist, knee, ankle and small joints of extremities, and possibly a rash. Infected persons may present hemorrhagic symptoms. Recovery may be prolonged.")
(comment pathState "(#$pathState PATH STATE) means that PATH has the attribute STATE.  For example, (#$pathState #$StraitOfHormuz-InternationalWaterwayPart #$PathBlocked).  See also #$BlockingTraffic, #$UnblockingTraffic.")
(comment PersonAssemblyRoom "The collection of all rooms designed primary to hold a group of people who are participating in some event.")
(comment VulnerableToMailCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an
 #$EMailCommandExecutionFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableToPostScriptCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if is has a program on it that has a #$PostScriptCommandExecutionFault that can be exploited locally.")
(comment nonConcurrentPositions-OrganizationalPosition "In many organizations, it is important to be able to record
the fact that a pair of positions (see #$OrganizationalPosition), are
not expected to be held concurrently by the same
individual. #$nonConcurrentPositions-OrganizationalPosition allows us
to do this with respect to a specified temporal 'granularity'.
Specifically, (#$nonConcurrentPositions-OrganizationalPosition ORG
POS1 POS2 DURATION) means that we would not expect to find the same
individual holding POS1 and POS2 in ORG within the space of a
time-frame demarcated by DURATION.  More specifically,
(#$nonConcurrentPositions-OrganizationalPosition ORG POS1 POS2
DURATION) means that if it is the case that (#$holdsIn TEMP1 (POS1 ORG
AGENT)) and (#$holdsIn TEMP2 (POS2 ORG AGENT)), the expectation is
that the #$duration of (#$TimeIntervalBetweenFn TEMP1 TEMP2) is
#$greaterThan DURATION.")
(comment ProgramSlowingFault "A program suffers from a #$ProgramSlowingFault if it can be compelled by a
malicious user to enter a long period of unresponsiveness, before
again offering its usual services.")
(comment VesicularStomatitisFever "A viral infection which produces flu-like symptoms as well as pain in the limbs and back. Blisters and lesions may appear in the mouth, throat and occasionally on the hands. Illness may produce a prolonged mental depression. ")
(comment threeWayJunctionInSystem "(#$threeWayJunctionInSystem JUNCT SYS) means that JUNCT is a 3-way junction in the specified #$PathSystem SYS.  Formally, a 3-way junction in SYS is any point (actually, any node) X in SYS such that either there are exactly 3 links and no loops in SYS that X is on, or there are exactly 1 link and 1 loop in SYS that X is on.  See #$junctionInSystem.  When the junction is is simply a customary junction not based on a specified #$PathSystem, use #$ThreeWayJunctionOfPaths.")
(comment LightingDevice "#$LightingDevice is a specialization of #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$LightingDevice has the #$primaryFunction of providing light.  The light provided may be provided in different ways and for different specialized purposes.  For example, it may be for general illumination of a fixed area (as by instances of #$Candle, #$Lantern, #$ElectricLamp, and #$Streetlight); or it may be for specially directed illumination (as by instances of #$AutomotiveLight and #$Flashlight); or it may be for use in a signal or sign (as by instances of #$TrafficLight and #$IndicatorLight); or it may be for some other special purposes (as by instances of #$StrobeLight).")
(comment Pump-TheShoe "Pumps are slip-on womens shoes with low heels.")
(comment makeTCPConnectionToComputer "(#$makeTCPConnectionToComputer AGENT COMPUTER TARGET) means that AGENT uses COMPUTER to make a TCP connection to TARGET.")
(comment AncestralCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture whose core participants identify 
  themselves as descendants of some common ancestors.  An 
  ancestral culture is characterized by its development as 
  part of, and in response to, the experiences of such an 
  ancestral group.  For example, there are instances of 
  #$AncestralCulture associated with #$AfricanAmericanPerson 
  and the #$EthnicGroupOfSerbians.")
(comment instantiationOfGene-GIS "(#$instantiationOfGene-GIS GENE-HU GENE-GIS) means that GENE-HU instantiates GENE-GIS, where GENE-HU is an instance of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit (a physical gene) and GENE-GIS is an instance of  #$Gene-GIS.")
(comment pseudo-antisymmetricViaOn "This relation is used to indicate that an instance of

#$BinaryPredicate is pseudo-antisymmetic via a particular equivalence

relation on a given collection. (#$pseudo-antisymmetricViaOn PRED EQ COL)

means that if INS1 and INS2 are instances of COL and (PRED INS1 INS2) and

(PRED INS2 INS1), then (EQ INS1 INS2).")
(comment NodesInSystemFn "A function from path-systems to the set-or-collections of nodes in those systems.  (#$NodesInSystemFn SYSTEM) is the #$SetOrCollection (q.v.) of all nodes (see #$nodeInSystem) in the #$PathSystem (q.v.) SYSTEM.  See also #$PointsInSystemFn.")
(comment doorwayHasCovering "A predicate that relates a doorway to a physical covering used to seal it.  (#$doorwayHasCovering DOORWAY COVER) means that the instance DOORWAY of #$Doorway has as a physical covering the instance COVER of #$DoorwayCovering.")
(comment LocalAnesthesia "The collection of events in which drugs are used to make some body part numb, so that it will not feel the pain/discomfort associated with a medical procedure.")
(disjointWith HandAndWristMovement LocomotionEvent)
(comment languageUnsupported "(#$languageUnsupported LANGUAGE) means that LANGUAGE is not supported by the UIA -- i.e., the user cannot successively conduct a KE session through the UIA by entering LANGUAGE input.")
(comment ArbitraryFileOverwriteFault "#$ArbitraryFileOverwriteFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has an #$ArbitraryFileOverwriteFault if it allows arbitrary files to be overwritten by an unauthorized user.  Note that \"arbitrary\" here modifies \"file\" -- it's arbitrary files that are overwritable, not files that are overwritable with arbitrary new content.  If arbitrary content can be written, the more  specialized fault, #$ArbitraryContentArbitraryFileOverwriteFault is applicable.  Because deletion is a kind of overwriting, #$ArbitraryFileDeletionFault is a specialization of #$ArbitraryFileOverwriteFault.")
(comment JavaCommandExecutionFault "A program has a #$JavaCommandExecutionFault if an unauthorized person can pass Java code to it and have it execute arbitrary commands.")
(comment softwareFoundOnComputer "(#$softwareFoundOnComputer SOFT COMP) means that SOFT is an instance of #$SoftwareObject, some copy of which is stored on the instance of #$ComputationalSystem, COMP.")
(comment QFever "A zoonotic (transmitted to humans from animals) disease caused by #$CoxiellaBurnetti.  Symptoms range from inapparent or non-specific to severe, e.g., sudden onset of fever, chills, severe sweating, headache, weakness and malaise.  Because the disease is underreported, scientists cannot reliably assess how many cases have actually occurred worldwide.")
(comment MusicStudio "Recording studios, usually not in a building of their own.")
(disjointWith Skirt Pants)
(comment PotatoSalad "The collection of all instances of #$Salad

 whose main ingredient is potatoes.")
(comment Img-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to indicate that a particular image is part of the document that is generated by the #$HTMLSource.(although that image may have as its source another, different document).  The #$Img-HTMLTag is typiclly attached to a #$UniformResourceLocator that acts as the link to the image (an #$AbstractVisualStructure) and that causes the image to be displayed in the document generated by the #$HTMLSource.")
(comment SmallpoxInfection "A specialization of #$ViralInfection.  Each instance of #$SmallpoxInfection is a potentially life-threatening infection, characterized by initial flu-like symptoms, including headache, chills, a fever of 106-107 degrees, aching joints, and an initial macular rash, progressing to papules and finally blisters.")
(comment determinerStrings "(#$determinerStrings WORD STRING) states that STRING is the determiner form for the word unit WORD in some microtheory.")
(comment transportsFrom "Agent A transports thing B from some location or place C.")
(disjointWith Roadway SeaportFacility)
(comment SolidSurfacePathThroughAir "The collection of all existing or designated #$Path-Spatials that pass through air along a solid surface.  An object following such a path is immersed in the air but supported by the solid surface of the path.  To refer to a pure trajectory of the motion, regardless of whether there is any pre-existing or pre-designated #$Path-Spatial, see #$SolidSurfaceTrajectoryThroughAir.")
(comment WoodSculpture "WoodSculptures as art forms")
(comment Boot-Footwear "Footwear that covers the foot and ankle, and often the lower leg.")
(disjointWith OpeningSomething MakingSomething)
(disjointWith GainingUserRights AbandoningSomething)
(comment Opal-Gem "A #$SemipreciousStone which varies in color and is iridescent, much mined in #$Australia.")
(comment PathJunctionFn "(#$PathJunctionFn PATH1 PATH2) denotes the unique

#$JunctionOfPaths (if any) where PATH1 and PATH2 meet or intersect.  See also

#$pathsJoinAt.")
(comment PartOfRoomInAConstruction "A specialization of #$PartOfBuilding.  Each instance of #$PartOfRoomInAConstruction is a part of some room in a construction artifact (see the collection #$RoomInAConstruction).  The collection #$PartOfRoomInAConstruction includes as instances both solid parts, such as instances of #$Mantel, as well as enclosed regions, such as those contained by cabinets and cupboards.  Note that instances of #$PartOfRoomInAConstruction are required to be features which are 'built-in'; that is, built with the intention of remaining as part of the room.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedPasswordProtectedMacroExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$PasswordProtectedMacroExecutionFault on it.")
(comment Washing "A specialization of #$Cleaning.  In each #$Washing event, some #$Water is being employed in the cleaning. Typically there will be some surfactant such as soap (cf. #$Soap-Personal) dissolved in the water.  If only water (i.e., no soap) is used in a #$Washing, then the event also belongs to the more specialized #$Rinsing. Other notable specializations include #$Bathing and #$PersonalWashing. #$Scrubbing is not a specialization of this collection, since such events may occur without any water being involved.")
(comment NLParser-CW "The collection of instances of 

#$ComputerProgram-CW that are designed to parse natural language input.")
(comment PlantingATrap "Those #$Trappings in which the trap was not dropped, but planted (hidden).")
(comment sourcePatternFor-Indirect "(sourcePatternFor-Indirect THING1 THING2) means that THING1 is indirectly the source pattern for the structure, arrangement or shape of THING2, only through some intermediate patterned things.  This applies to physical pattern sources (like rubber-stamps as sources of photocopied designs, stencils derived from copies, viral DNA strands indirectly copied, CDs derived indirectly from record-masters via vinyl records, and photocopies of photocopies) as well as abstract patterns that are transformed in multiple stages or that only indirectly affect the configuration of something else.  THING2 is thus a derivative of a derivative of the original, including complementary 'reverse' copies or indirect 'negatives', or an approximate or partial derivative of another derived pattern.  But it needs more than just causal influence: some basic structure of the original pattern should be preserved, despite the multiple stages. See also #$sourcePatternFor-Direct.")
(comment sourceNodeInSystem "(#$sourceNodeInSystem X SYS) means that X is a source node in the #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem SYS, i.e., a node that all links attached to it go 'out' from it and no such links come 'in' to it.  A source node X in SYS is a node in SYS such that X is on some links but no loops in SYS, and such that each link in SYS that X is on is a link directed from X to another node (but not from another to X).  Another way to put this is that X is a node in SYS that is neither on a loop in SYS, nor an isolated node in SYS, nor a node to which a link in SYS is directed.  Note that if a node X in SYS is on a 'bidirected' link, i.e., a link directed both from X to Y and from Y to X for some node Y, then X cannot be a source node in SYS.  See #$loopInSystem, #$isolatedNodeInSystem and #$linkFromToInSystem.")
(comment PromDress "The collection of #$BallGowns designed to be worn at #$Proms.")
(comment VulnerableToFilteringSoftwareBypass "#$VulnerableToFilteringSoftwareBypass is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible to bypass a filtering procedure that software running on the computer is supposed to implement.")
(comment AnimistReligion "The collection of #$LocalTraditionalReligions that hold that #$NonPersonAnimals, trees, rocks, and/or other #$NaturalTangibleStuff have spirits.")
(comment PeptideChain "The collection of all molecular chains consisting of two or more #$AminoAcids.  Instances include both independent molecules (see #$PeptideMolecule) and segments of lengthier #$PeptideMolecules.")
(comment subTraversals "(#$subTraversals TRAV SUBTRAV) means that every point on the #$Traversal SUBTRAV (see the predicate #$pointOnTraversal) is also on the #$Traversal TRAV.")
(comment Dike "structure restraining the spread of water, usually river or seawater")
(comment OlympicWinterGames "The set of #$OlympicGames which occur in the winter.")
(comment Timer "A type of time measurment device that can be set for a particular amount of time.  When activated, it will begin counting the time, and will finish when that amount of time has passed.  Sometimes a timer will activate a bell or something to let the user know the time is up, but timers can also be used to activate other devices.")
(disjointWith OverGarment Loincloth)
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfWeakPasswordReset "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a
#$WeakPasswordResetFault on it.")
(comment WesternHemispherePerson "The collection of instances of #$Person who identify themselves (or who are identified by others as) 'westerners.' This is a very broadly defined collection, subsuming both nationalities and ethnic group types.")
(comment VulnerableToExecutionOfDLL "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program on it  that has a #$CommandExecutionOfDLLFault.")
(comment keCommonQueryPredForInstances-Inverse "A macro predicate for #$keCommonQueryForTerm.  (#$keCommonQueryPredForInstances-Inverse COL PRED) means that for any instance INST of COL, (#$keCommonQueryForTerm INST (PRED :WHAT INST).")
(comment SymlinkFault-Deletion "#$SymlinkFault-Deletion is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  It is a specialization of #$FileDeletionFault and #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite.  A program has a #$SymlinkFault-Deletion if when running it writes null to a standard file.  If the file is not the expected file but rather a a symbolic link,
 the null will be written to the file pointed to.  When the malicious user or another user executes the program, it follows the symlink and deletes the specified file.  As with other faults, the severity of #$SymlinkFault-Overwrite depends on the privilege level under which the exploited program is running.  If the program runs at root, for instance, when writing null to the standard files, then the malicious user can delete any known file on the computer.")
(comment surmises "(#$surmises AGENT PROP) means that AGENT thinks that it is likely that PROP is true but is unsure.  See #$thinksProbable and #$beliefs.")
(comment KerberosKDCSpoofingFault "Kerberos is a cryptographic authentication protocol that allows users
 of a network to access services without transmitting cleartext
 passwords. A common implementation of the protocol includes a login
 service which is vulnerable to an attack which involves spoofing
 responses from the Key Distribution Center (KDC). The login service
 authenticates a user by first requesting a ticket granting ticket
 (TGT) from the authentication server. If the TGT can be decrypted
 using the password supplied by the user, the login service attempts to
 verify the identity of the KDC by making a request with the received
 TGT for a service ticket for itself. The service ticket returned by
 the KDC is encrypted with a secret shared between the KDC and the
 service host. If the service ticket cannot be verified with the
 service's secret key it is assumed that the KDC is not authentic. If
 the login service has not been registered as a principal with the KDC
 or the service's secret key has not been installed on the host the
 login service will proceed without verification that the TGT was
 returned by the authentic KDC. In these circumstances it is possible   
 to log into the server illicitly if an attacker can spoof responses
 from the Key Distribution Center. If these circumstances occur then a
 program has this fault.")
(comment copyProduced "A binary predicate which relates instances of #$IBTCopying (a specialization of #$InformationTransferEvent) to instances of

#$InformationBearingThing. (#$copyProduced COPYING COPY) means that COPY is the copy produced in the #$IBTCopying COPYING. This predicate is a specialization of #$IBTGeneration. See also #$itemCopied, which relates copying events to items copied.")
(comment PhysicalFilter "#$PhysicalFilter is a specialization of #$NonPoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$PhysicalFilter is a simple physical filter device, which allows some materials/objects to pass through, while preventing others from doing so.  Some notable specializations are #$CoffeeFilter and #$WindowScreen.  Natural filters do not fall within this collection.")
(comment Kimono "Type of traditional Japanese clothing, usually full-length or nearly full-length.")
(comment RectangularParallelepiped "A #$ThreeDimensionalShapeType and a specialization of #$Parallelepiped (q.v.).  Each instance of #$RectangularParallelepiped is a three-dimensional object each of whose six faces is a #$Rectangle.  Examples include certain spatially-localized objects (e.g a matchbox) as well as abstract rectangular parallelipipeds.  Specializations of this collection include #$Cube, #$Block, and #$Beam.")
(comment GenderCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture whose core participants display the 
  same or similar gender characteristics, and which has developed 
  around the experiences of those core participants.  The most 
  inclusive examples are feminine culture and masculine culture.  
  Note that participation in a gender culture is not strictly 
  determined by one's biological sex: a transvestite who ''passes'' 
  as a female, for example, is a core participant in feminine culture.")
(comment PassingBySomething "In every #$PassingBySomething, the #$objectPassing passes near the 
#$objectPassed while moving in this #$Translocation event.  Examples
include passing by a landmark while driving and passing go in Monopoly. In the event that the two objects are going opposite directions, both objects will be #$objectPassing.")
(comment PointsInSystemFn "A function from path-systems to the set-or-collections of points in those systems.  (#$PointsInSystemFn SYSTEM) is the #$SetOrCollection (q.v.) of all points (see #$pointInSystem) in the #$PathSystem (q.v.) SYSTEM.  See also #$NodesInSystemFn.")
(comment mainProductType "A binary predicate linking a particular
#$Agent-Generic to the main kind of product or service it
produces. (#$mainProductType AGENT PRODUCTTYPE) means that AGENT is a
person or organization that sells or performs instances of product
type PRODUCTTYPE, and most of the sales, by far, that AGENT makes are
of instances of this type. See also #$soleProductType and
#$makesProductType.")
(comment hasLevels "This predicate relates buildings (or other instances of #$ConstructionArtifact) to their levels.  (#$hasLevels ARTIFACT LEVEL)  means that LEVEL is a level (e.g., a floor) of ARTIFACT.")
(comment GeneralAnesthesia "The collection of events in which drugs are used to make someone unconscious, so that they will not feel the pain/discomfort associated with a medical procedure.")
(disjointWith FluidFlowEvent LocomotionEvent)
(comment SubProgramOfSeriesFn "(#$SubProgramOfSeriesFn SUB_PROG PROG-SERIES) denotes the series of programs which are #$genlPrograms to SUB_PROG and each of which is contained by some member of PROG-SERIES (see #$containsPrograms).  So, for example, (#$SubProgramOfSeriesFn Inews-TheProgram (#$VersionsInclusiveFn #$INN-TheProgram \"1.5.1\" \"2.2\")) denotes the following series of programs: the version of the inews executable packaged with version 1.5.1 of Internet News, the version of the inews executable packaged with version ... of Intenet News, the version of the inews executable packaged with version 2.2 of Internet News.")
(comment InformationGathering "A specialization of both #$Action and #$InformationTransferEvent.  In each instance of #$InformationGathering, some instance of #$IntelligentAgent gathers information about something.")
(comment evaluatedInMathEvent "(#$evaluatedInMathEvent MATH-EVENT LIST) means that, in the instance of 
#$DoingMath MATH-EVENT, each element of the list LIST is being evaluated.  All
individuals in the list LIST are evaluted in the particular instance of a 
specification of DoingMath in the order in which they appear in the list.")
(comment ChlamydiaPsittaci "The bacterium that causes #$Psittacosis.")
(comment Theater-PhysicalStructure "Where plays and such happen.")
(comment Clothing-WholeBody "#$Clothing-WholeBody is a specialization of #$Garment.  Each instance of #$Clothing-WholeBody is a #$Garment that covers the whole body. Someone wearing one would only require #$Shoes to be considered #$FullyClothed in modern western culture.")
(comment Anarchist "The collection of instances of #$Person who believe in #$Anarchism.")
(comment PhysicalCreationEvent "The collection of all #$CreationEvents in which something #$PartiallyTangible is created.")
(comment organismTypeFoundInClimateOfType "(#$organismTypeFoundInClimateOfType ORG-TYPE CLIMATE) means that at least some of the regions in which instances of ORG-TYPE ordinarily live (see #$indigenousTo, #$organismTypeHasHabitat) have the #$ClimateCycleType CLIMATE.")
(disjointWith Dock Roadway)
(comment PathType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$PathType is a collection that is a subcollection of #$Path-Generic.  There are several types of path, according to the medium or surface the path goes through or over.  In addition, the collection #$PathArtifact can be broken down into more specific #$PathTypes.  At a #$JunctionOfPaths, the joined paths all have at least one #$PathType in common.")
(comment Vane "The flat, blade-like components of a windmill that catch the wind and turn the turbine")
(comment Galosh "Boots made of rubber, worn on other shoes; protect from snow and slush.")
(comment NetworkVulnerabilityAssessment "This is the collection of #$Evaluatings in which what is assessed is the vulnerability to attack of a #$ComputerNetwork.")
(disjointWith MakingSomething AnalyzingSomething)
(comment DHCPClientProgram "#$DHCPClientProgram is the collection of DHCP client software that implements the Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol.")
(comment smallestSubSystemUnderTraversal "(#$smallestSubSystemUnderTraversal SUB SYS TRAV) means that
SUB is the smallest subsystem of SYS such that TRAV is a traversal in
SUB. (See #$SubSystemUnderTraversalFn, #$traversalInSystem and
#$pointClosedSubSystems)  Note that 'smallest' here means that no link
LINK between X and Y in SYS is a link in SUB if neither (#$TraversalFn 
(#$TheList X LINK Y)) nor (TraversalFn (#$TheList Y LINK X)) is a 
#$subTraversals of TRAV. Note also that since SUB is a point-closed
subsystem of SYS, every point in SYS that is on TRAV (see
#$pointOnTraversal) is a point in SUB. Note finally that since SUB is the
'smallest' subsystem of SYS in which TRAV is a traversal, SUB must be
a #$ConnectedPathSystem.")
(comment MensRoom "A restroom for men only.  In a public place.")
(comment VulnerableToFTPCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$FTPCommandExecutionFault on it.")
(comment CycNLParser "The collection of all instances of #$NLParser-CW created at Cycorp.")
(comment MayDay "The first day of May is considered an holiday in many countries around the world. Since the 1890's it has been a celebration of the ideal of international peace and solidarity among workers in commemoration of the Haymarket \"riots\" in Chicago. It has been a spring holiday for centuries. The lily, symbolizing the overcoming of winter by spring, became the flower of the first of May.")
(comment ArtObject "A specialization of both #$HumanAccessibleIBO and #$Artifact.  Each instance of #$ArtObject is a physical object that is a work, or a reproduction of a work, in one of the representational or plastic arts, such as a painting, sculpture, quilt, or stained glass composition.  #$ArtObject does not include as instances plays, movies, music, performance art, or other activities.  #$ArtObject is a specialization of #$InformationBearingObject, but its instances need not have any propositional content.  Examples of #$ArtObject include the #$StatueOfLiberty, the Mona Lisa, a poster reproduction of Van Gogh's `Starry Night', Rodin's `Burghers of Calais', a piece of Ju ware from the Sung Dynasty, the windows of Chartres Cathedral. See also #$Artist, #$artisticWorksCreated.")
(comment VulnerableToAttachmentFilteringBypass "#$VulnerableToAttachmentFilteringBypass is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible to bypass an attachment filtering procedure that software running on the computer is supposed to implement.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with an #$AttachmentFilteringBypassFault.")
(comment TheisticReligion "The collection of all instances of #$Religion in which the divine (ultimate reality) is conceived as one or more intelligent agents")
(comment Prison "The collection of facilities designed for incarcerating prisoners [#$Prisoner-Legal] and thereby removing them from general circulation among #$ThePublic. A building, set of buildings, or part of a building comprised of #$PrisonCells.")
(comment OlympicGames "The international athletic competition held every four years.")
(comment VolumeMeasuringDevice "Devices used to measure volume, such as cup measure, graduated cylinders, and cooking teaspoons.")
(comment extendedRuleMacroExample "This predicate is used to organize example sentences in the UIA.  Specificallly, (#$extendedRuleMacroExample PRED SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE will be accessible from the \"variations\" link accessible from the example sentence generated for PRED.")
(comment onTraversal "(#$onTraversal ARG1 TRAV) means that ARG1 is located along the #$Traversal TRAV.  ARG1 could be a moving object or a stationary point (see the more specific predicate #$pointOnTraversal).  For example, if I drive from Austin to Dallas to LA and back to Dallas, and if the #$Traversal TRAV here is characterized by the #$PathChain 'Austin--Dallas--LA--Dallas, then all Austin, Dallas and LA are qualified to be the ARG1 in (#$onTraversal ARG1 TRAV), and so are my car and me.  Let TRAV be (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X(1) PATH(1) ... X(n) PATH(n) X(n+1))).  Then (#$onTraversal A TRAV) holds if and only if there is a k = 1, ..., n such that (#$onPath A PATH(k)) holds.")
(comment MeetingSpace "The collection of all (usually fairly large) rooms designed to be used as meeting places (business meetings, club meetings, etc.")
(comment Shoe "A specialization of #$ClothingItem.  Each instance of #$Shoe is a shoe (or shoelike thing) worn on the feet.  Important specializations of #$Shoe include #$Boot-Footwear, #$Sandal, #$Slipper, and #$CasualShoe.  Note that instances of the collection #$Shoe are single shoes; pairs of shoes are instances of the collection (#$PairFn #$Shoe).")
(comment VulnerableToInterfaceStatisticsReset "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$InterfaceStatisticsResetFault on it.")
(comment EasternHemispherePerson "The collection of instances of #$Person who identify themselves (or who are identified by others as) 'easterners.' This is a very broadly defined collection, subsuming both nationalities and ethnic group types.")
(comment VulnerableToPerlCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if is has a program that has a #$PerlCommandExecutionFault.")
(comment PrintingElevatedPrivilegeFault "A program suffers from a  #$PrintingElevatedPrivilegeFault if it can be compelled by an unauthorized user to print files to which the user does not have read access. See also #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedPrinterAccountAccess.")
(comment Comparing "This is the collection of actions in which an agent compares two or more items.")
(comment Cube "A #$ThreeDimensionalShapeType and a specialization of #$RectangularParallelepiped (q.v.).  This is the collection of all three-dimensional cubes, whether spatially-localized (e.g. dice) or abstract.")
(comment lureToMaliciousWebSite "(#$lureToMaliciousWebSite AGENT COMPUTER) means that AGENT persuades the user of COMPUTER to visit #$HackersMaliciousWebPage.  It is accomplished by sending the user the enticing #$HackersMaliciousEMailMessage.")
(comment GenerationCulture "A specialization of #$AgeCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture defined at least in part by the fact 
  that its core participants were born or came of age during a 
  certain (roughly ten- to twenty-year) period.  Interesting 
  instances of #$GenerationCulture are often defined in relation 
  to some significant social or historical event; for example, 
  the Baby Boomers are defined as having been born in the US in 
  the years immediately following the end of WWII.")
(comment PathSystemCycLConstant "The collection of CycL constants specifically created to state things about #$PathSystems (q.v.) and their components.")
(comment OrderingFn "This is a function that, applied to a collection (type)  of object or services, denotes the collection of all events in which one or more objects or services of the specified type are ordered by someone for subsequent delivery.  (#$OrderingFn FOO) denotes the collection of events in which instances of the collection FOO are ordered.")
(disjointWith Doorway WindowPortal)
(disjointWith ManipulatingWithFingers LocomotionEvent)
(comment Psittacosis "A bird disease transmissable to humans. It has various symptoms including fever, headache, rash, chills and/or upper or lower respiratory infection. Disease is usually mild or moderate but can be severe, especially in the untreated elderly. Also known as 'parrot fever', ornithosis or chlamydiosis.")
(comment Greenhouse "The collection of greenhouses")
(comment Clothing-Top "#$Clothing-Top is a specialization of #$Garment.  Each instance of #$Clothing-Top is a #$Garment that extends from the shoulders to the #$Waist or #$Hips.  #$Clothing-Tops are outerwear, in the sense that in modern western culture someone wearing a #$Clothing-Top with trousers, shorts, or a skirt and shoes is considered #$FullyClothed.")
(comment challenger "'(#$challenger CHALLENGE AGENT)' means that AGENT issues the
challenge in the #$Challenging CHALLENGE.")
(comment Ol-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to indicate an ordered (i.e. numbered) list.")
(comment sequenceCodesForType-Continuous "(#$sequenceCodesForType-Continuous SEQUENCE PEPTIDETYPE)
means that SEQUENCE is a #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS that specifies the
sequence of amino acids (see #$AminoAcid) in PEPTIDETYPE and that
SEQUENCE does not contain any noncoding subsequences, such as introns
(see #$Intron-GIS).")
(comment LeftWingExtremist "The collection of all instances of #$Person who tout #$LeftistIdeology to an extreme.  Such persons are willing to fight for a return to a past socio-economic state that, by their perception, was more

reflective of their current value system.")
(comment serverInitiatesProgramOn "A predicate relating instances of #$ServerProgram with
instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW and instances of #$Computer.
(#$serverInitiatesProgramOn SERVER PROGRAM COMPUTER) means that SERVER
can start a process of PROGRAM usable by remote users of SERVER.
Important spec preds of #$serverInitiatesProgramOn are
#$serverInitiatesServerProgramOn and #$webServerInitiatesProgramOn.")
(comment PathThroughAir "A designated or pre-defined #$Path-Spatial all of which passes through air (mid-air).  This includes air lanes, designated air navigation routes, etc.  An object following this #$Path-Generic is immersed in, and supported by, if anything, the air.  Thus it excludes a #$SolidSurfacePathThroughAir, a #$PathThroughAirHangingFromSolid, and a #$WaterSurfacePath.  For general trajectories of moving objects through air, use #$TrajectoryThroughAir.")
(comment StationaryArtifact "The collection of artifacts (including devices) which do not move by translational motion while performing their primary functions.")
(comment Clog-TheShoe "Shoes made of wood; worn as protection from water, mud or dirt or as home footwear in lieu of slippers.")
(disjointWith Propelling MakingSomething)
(comment DHCPServerProgram "#$DHCPServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol.")
(comment OneStoryBuilding "#$OneStoryBuilding is a specialization of #$Building.  Each instance is a building with exactly one story.")
(comment northwestOf "(#$northwestOf OBJ1 OBJ2) means that the #$SpatialThing-Localized OBJ1 is to the northwest of the #$SpatialThing-Localized OBJ2, when viewed in the terrestrial frame of reference.  Note that  OBJ2 is therefore southeast of  OBJ1; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `southeast of'.  Example: (#$northwestOf #$BillClinton #$LongIsland).  If both objects are fixed instances or #$GeographicalThing, use the more specific predicate, #$permanentlyNorthwestOf.")
(comment VulnerableToIPPacketForwarding "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$IPPacketForwardingFault on it.")
(comment TemplateParser "The collection of instances of #$NLParser-CW that are template-driven.")
(comment ApplyingToSurfaceWithTool "A collection of events. In each #$ApplyingToSurfaceWithTool event, a physical object is attached to a surface by use of a tool.")
(comment CanonicalizerDirectiveArgConstraintCollection "Instances of this collection are argument constraints which,
when they or their specs are used as the #$argIsa for a relation, express
certain directives to the #$CycCanonicalizer when canonicalizing that
argument of that relation.  For example, if it is asserted that
(#$arg1Isa PRED #$KeywordVariableTemplate), then the canonicalizer
will permit keywords as variables within the first argument of PRED.")
(disjointWith SeatingDevice PathArtifactSystem)
(comment ClothingIBO "The collection of #$Clothing-Generic that 

functions also as an #$InformationBearingObject.  For example, t-shirts

that have on it a logo, a writing, a picture, or any combination of

these.")
(comment libraryProgramForType "(#$libraryProgramForType LIBRARY PROG-TYPE) means that LIBRARY is a shared library file designed to be used by an instance of the program type PROG-TYPE in its execution.")
(comment VulnerableToContentFilteringBypass "#$VulnerableToContentFilteringBypass is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible to bypass a content filtering procedure that software running on the computer is supposed to implement.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with a #$ContentFilteringBypassFault.")
(comment MultiRoomUnit "A suite, bunch of rooms, (or even just one single room) which are thought of as one unit. #$MultiRoomUnits can have rooms.")
(comment interArgGenl2-4 "(#$interArgGenl2-4 REL INDEPENDENT-COL DEPENDENT-COL) means that, when a spec of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the second argument to REL, the fourth argument is constrained to be a spec of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.")
(disjointWith OlympicGames QualitativeTimeOfDay)
(comment doEliminateEvidenceOfIntrusionOnSystem "(#$doEliminateEvidenceOfIntrusionOnSystem AGENT SYSTEM) means that AGENT removes all evidence of infiltrating SYSTEM.")
(comment affordToHire "(#$affordToHire AGENT PERSON) means that AGENT can financially afford to hire PERSON.")
(comment Boeing757 "Class of jet-propelled, single-aisle passenger aircraft.")
(comment BellTower "Cathedrals definitely have one, as do many other church buildings.  A tower that houses a bell.")
(disjointWith Cardigan Sweater-Pullover)
(comment covers-Dustlike "'(#$covers-Dustlike STUFF OBJECT)' means that the #$Mob STUFF covers OBJECT in the way in which dust covers a tabletop, or a layer of snow covers the ground.  That is, the covering is a mob of separate,

loose particles, which are not attached to the surface they cover, but

are randomly strewn over it.  The layer of STUFF may be thin enough to

see OBJECT through, or it may conceal it; and the individual particles may be touching their neighbors, or they may be separated by space.")
(comment VulnerableToBulletinBoardPostOverwrite "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$BulletinBoardPostOverwriteFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableToVBCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if is has a program
on it that has a #$VBCommandExecutionFault.")
(comment keCommonQueryPredForSpecs "A macro predicate for #$keCommonQueryForTerm.  (#$keCommonQueryPredForSpecs COL PRED) means that for any specialiazation SPEC of COL, (#$keCommonQueryForTerm SPEC (PRED SPEC :WHAT).")
(comment logInToAccountOn "(#$logInToAccountOn AGENT ACCOUNT COMPUTER) means that AGENT logs into ACCOUNT on COMPUTER locally, i.e., either physically at COMPUTER or while already logged in to another account on COMPUTER.")
(comment FileModificationFault "A program has this fault if it allows an unauthorized user either to overwrite, delete, or recover files to which the program has access.")
(comment WesternEquineEncephalitisVirus "The virus that causes #$WesternEquineEncephalitis.")
(comment Multigraph "An instance of #$PathSystemType-Structural and a subcollection of #$PathSystem.  Each instance of #$Multigraph is an instance of #$PathSystem in which the only points are nodes in the system and all paths are made of links (i.e., no intermediate points along links). Sometime such a system is called a graph or multi-graph in graph theory.  A #$Multigraph consists of nodes interconnected by links, with loops on single nodes allowed, and with multiple links between the same two nodes also allowed.  (For a graph with no parallel links and no loops, see #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic.")
(comment SerialNumber-String "A specialization of #$UniqueID and #$IDString.  Each instance of #$SerialNumber-String is a number that is assigned by the manufacturer of a device to that device and which uniquely identifies that device among all the other devices of that type the manufacturer has made.  Manufacturers usually assign these strings serially, so among two devices of the same type from the same manufacturer the one having the largest serial number is typically the one most recently made.  The instances of this collection are typically called \"serial numbers\" although they often are comprised of characters other than numbers.")
(comment StockingCap "The collection of all stocking caps: warm, snug-fitting caps, usually made of wool and or a synthetic, with elastic to make them fit more tightly.")
(comment GeopoliticalCulture "A specialization of both #$PoliticalCulture and
  #$RegionalCulture, each instance of which is a culture 
  whose participants, in addition to sharing political views or 
  activities, live in the same geographic region.  For example,
  there are instances of #$GeopoliticalCulture associated with
  Texas Democrats and the German branch of the 
  #$GreenParty-Ecological.")
(comment geneInGenome "(#$geneInGenome GNM GENE) means that the instance of

#$Gene-GenInfo GENE is contained in the #$Genome-GenInfo GNM and is an

encoding of an instance of #$Gene-GIS.")
(comment objectPassing "(#$objectPassing EVENT OBJ) means that, in the #$PassingBySomething event EVENT, the 
#$objectMoving is OBJ.  In the case that the #$objectPassed is also moving the same direction,
the #$objectPassing approaches the #$objectPassed and eventually overtakes it. In the case that the objects pass each other going opposite directions, both will take the #$objectPassing predicate.")
(comment PointFinitePathSystem "The collection of all #$PathSystems each of which has at most finitely many 'points' on each link, i.e., the collection of every #$PathSystem SYS such that for each link LINK in SYS, (#$TheSetOf X (#$and (#$elementOf X (#$PointsInSystemFn SYS)) (#$pointOnPath X LINK))) is finite.  (See also #$pointInSystem.)  Note that in #$PathSystems, 'points' may occur along links between nodes (see #$nodeInSystem), while nodes themselves are always 'points' of the system.")
(disjointWith Doorway Ditch)
(comment DrugTherapyUseFn "The collection of events in which instances of ARG1 are used to achieve a medical purpose.  These events do not include the administration of the drug - they are the scripts which result from that administration.")
(disjointWith AccessingAnIBT LocomotionEvent)
(comment equivPredsWRTTypes "(#$equivPredsWRTTypes BINPRED1 BINPRED2 COL1 COL2) means that if either BINPRED1 or BINPRED2 apply to (INS1 INS2) where INS1 is an instance of COL1 and INS2 is an instance of COL2, then the other one does also.  This is a combination of (#$genlPredsWRTTypes BINPRED1 BINPRED2 COL1 COL2) and (#$genlPredsWRTTypes BINPRED2 BINPRED1 COL1 COL2).")
(comment Specifying "The collection of #$StrictlyMentalEvents in which some mental object is intentionally created, with the intent that that mental object be communicated to others so as to influence their actions.  The types of things that can be specified include rules, definitions, and agreements.  The communication of the created mental object is not part of the #$Specifying act.")
(comment Powassan-Virus "Powassan or 'POW' virus is a North American tickborne flavivirus related to the Eastern Hemisphere's tickborne encephalitis viruses. Causes #$PowassanEncephalitis")
(comment Workshop "A room in a house where things normally get repaired. Probably contains a workbench.")
(comment ShortPants "A specialization of #$Pants. Each instance of #$ShortPants is a pair of pants with pantlegs that cover only the upper part of the wearer's legs, being typically knee-length or shorter.")
(comment doGetAccessToAccountOfTypeOn "(#$doGetAccessToAccountOfTypeOn AGENT ACCT_TYPE NETWORK) means that AGENT takes steps toward the goal of controlling an account of type ACCT_TYPE on some machine on NETWORK.")
(comment objectSent "(#$objectSent SEND OBJECT) means that OBJECT, in an instance of #$PartiallyTangible was one of things sent in the action SEND, an instance of #$SendingSomething. For example, if SEND45 is an event in which a package of fruit is sent in the mail, this predicate would relate SEND45 to the whole parcel, to each piece of fruit in the parcel, and to the package in which the fruit is wrapped.")
(comment formerOccupation "(#$formerOccupation ?PERSON ?OCCUPATION-TYPE) indicates that ?PERSON previously was employed in ?OCCUPATION-TYPE. More precisely, #$formerOccupation is a binary predicate linking instances of #$Person to the types representing their former occupations.")
(disjointWith PoweredDevice NonPoweredDevice)
(comment SolidSurfacePathThroughWater "The collection of all existing or designated #$Path-Spatials through #$Water that are situated along solid surfaces.  An object following such a  path is immersed in the water but supported by the solid surface.  For the pure #$Trajectory of any #$objectMoving through water along a solid surface, use #$SolidSurfaceTrajectoryThroughWater.")
(comment Moccasin "Boots made mainly of leather, without a heel.")
(comment ContaminationEvent "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  In each instance of #$ContaminationEvent, some instance of #$PartiallyTangible comes to contain a #$contaminant, and this state of affairs is considered undesirable from the point of view of some agent (see the related predicate #$unwantedMatter).  Specializations of #$ContaminationEvent include #$InfectionTransmissionEvent and #$PollutionProcess.")
(comment DeoxyribonucleotideSequence-GIS "An instance of #$StuffType and a subset of #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS.  Each instance of #$DeoxyribonucleotideSequence-GIS is an abstract chemical structure consisting of a sequence of deoxyribonucleotides; each such sequence is represented as an instance of #$List, each of whose members is an instance of #$Deoxyribonucleotide-GIS.")
(comment LevelOfAConstruction "#$LevelOfAConstruction is a specialization of #$SpaceInAFixedHOC.  Each instance of a #$LevelOfAConstruction is a level, also called floor or story, of a #$ConstructionArtifact.  Levels are regions in space; they are not two-dimensional planes.")
(comment ConfiguringProgram "The collection of programs that are used to configure other programs, computers or computer networks.")
(comment GroundToOrbitVehicle "The collection of vehicles whose purpose is to carry loads from a planetary surface to orbit around that planet.  So far, these are rocket powered.")
(comment DisplayStatus "The collection of all #$DisplayingSomething events in which some instance of #$PhysicalDevice displays an indication of the status of itself or another device (of which it may be a part or temporarily connected) as the result of physical or electrical processes.  Displays in which the observer directly views the status unmediatated by action of any device, which are set through human intervention, or which depend merely on \"clockwork\" are not included.  Positive examples include displays indicated by the position on a vertical scale of a weight connected by a rope over a pulley to a float in a water tank, as well as those indicated by instances or #$FuelGauge, TirePressureGauge, #$Voltmeter, and #$Thermometer.  Counter-examples include direct viewing of the level of the water against a vertical scale painted inside the tank as well as instances of #$DisplayingSomething by instances of #$Clock or billboards which state today's fire danger or the current value of a lottery.")
(comment occupiedWith "This predicate relates an agent to a thing that s/he/it 

is currently occupied with, in the sense of closely attending 

to or thinking about the thing in a focused way.  

(#$occupiedWith AGENT THING) means that AGENT is occupied with 

THING.  For a predicate that relates agents to events that

they are occupied with participating in, see #$occupiedActors.")
(disjointWith Weapon PathArtifactSystem)
(comment VulnerableToPacketFilteringBypass "#$VulnerableToPacketFilteringBypass is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible to bypass a packet filtering procedure that software running on the computer is supposed to implement.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with a #$PacketFilteringBypassFault.")
(comment OpenTagFn "For a particular instance of #$MarkupLanguageTag, (#$OpenTagFn TAG) returns the opening tag form of the #$MarkupLanguageTag TAG.  For example, the result of (#$OpenTagFn #$Caption-HTMLTag) is <caption>. ")
(comment CoveredBridge "Kind of bridge in which the pathway has walls on the sides and a roof.")
(comment cleansWith "A cleans B using C.")
(comment Boeing767 "Class of jet-propelled, twin-aisle passenger aircraft.  The most widely used plane for transatlantic crossings.  Shares a common type rating with the #$Boeing757.")
(comment TemplateParsingMicrotheory "Instances are microtheories which contain templates intended to parse strings in some natural language into objects of some syntactic category.")
(comment translationAlongWithinDistance "(#$translationAlongWithinDistance MOVE TRAV DIST) means that the moving object OBJ (see #$objectMoving) in #$Translation-SingleTrajectory MOVE moves along the #$Traversal TRAV with the #$Distance specified by DIST.  For example, an airplane may fly along the Great Wall, and a person may walk on the top of an oil pipe, or on the side of a river.  But in any case, the 'distance' between OBJ and TRAV should be at most the distance specified by DIST (e.g. (#$Kilometer 100)).  DIST here is an instance of #$Distance which is greater than or equal to the distance between OBJ and TRAV at each moment during the event MOVE.  Note that when DIST equals 'zero-unit' (whatever the #$UnitOfDistance is), we mean that at every moment during MOVE, OBJ is on TRAV (see onTraversal), and hence we would have (#$traverses-Complete MOVE TRAV).")
(comment Pagoda "Far Easterm towers serving a shrines, usually part of a temple or monastery.")
(disjointWith HighHeelShoe Flat-TheShoe)
(comment SowingSeed "This is the collection of actions of scattering seeds onto
the earth in order to grow plants.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfWeaklyEncryptedApplicationPasswordFile "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$WeaklyEncryptedApplicationPasswordFileFault on it.")
(comment VulnerableToVBAScriptCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if is has a program on it that has a #$VBAScriptCommandExecutionFault.")
(comment thinksProbable "(#$thinksProbable AGENT PROP) means that AGENT thinks that it is likely that PROP is true.  This is a very general predicate.  If AGENT is unsure use the more specific, #$surmises.  If AGENT is sure, use #$beliefs or a specialization thereof.")
(comment DefaultRootAccountFault "An operating system has this fault if its root password is set by default to something that can easily be guessed.")
(comment Pickle "#$Pickles are made by soaking cucumbers in a brine or vinegar solution. Varieties include dill and sweet pickles. #$Pickles are sometimes eaten alone, or chopped or sliced and used as a condiment.")
(comment WesternEquineEncephalitis "A viral infection whose symptoms range from mild fever and headache to high fever, headache, stupor, tremors, coma and spastic paralysis.")
(comment SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic "The collection of all #$PathSystems that are instances of both #$SimplePathSystem and #$Multigraph.  Each instance of #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic is a 'graph', as studied in graph theory, in which there are neither loops nor multiple links between the same pair of nodes.")
(comment FirefightersCoat "Heavy waterproof and heat-resistant coats worn by firefighters")
(comment activatePoweredDevice "(#$activatePoweredDevice AGENT DEVICE) means that AGENT activates DEVICE.")
(comment LegalCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture defined at least in part by the fact 
  that its core participants live under or work in the same or 
  very similar legal systems.  For example, there are instances 
  of #$LegalCulture associated with #$CommonLawSystem and 
  #$IslamicLawSystem.")
(comment geneticMaterial-GenInfo "(#$geneticMaterial-GenInfo BLO GI) means that the
#$GeneticInformation GI is a part of the genetic material of BLO, an
instance of #$BiologicalLivingObject.")
(disjointWith InformationRecordingProcess LocomotionEvent)
(comment preferredLanguageChoiceOfUIAUser "(#$preferredLanguageChoiceOfUIAUser USER LANGUAGE) says that LANGUAGE is the language that USER will almost certainly always choose for UIA knowledge-entry sessions.")
(comment FileCommandExecutionFault "A program has this fault if  it executes arbitrary code in response to invalid input in the form of a file.  Unlike other sorts of #$ArbitraryCommandExecutionFault, this fault is exploited not directly by sending a malformed string to the program but indirectly by sending a  file of some kind to that program, which results in the execution of code  when the file is read.  These faults are common in web browsers, allowing  a malicious web site to execute code by embedding a file in the site  (see, for example, #$CABFileExecutionFault). For cases where a program can be exploited to run executables already existing on a target machine, see #$FileExecutionFault-Local and #$FileExecutionFault-Remote.")
(comment PowassanEncephalitis "A viral infection. Symptoms range from mild fever and headache to high fever, stupor, tremors and coma. 4 to 10 days after apparent recovery there is a return of fever with encephalitis.")
(comment FoundationOfABuilding "The whole human-made sub-structure of a building -- the construction upon which the rest of the building stands.")
(comment Pants "#$Pants is a specialization of #$Clothing-Bottom.  Each instance of #$Pants is a clothing item worn on the lower torso and legs.  Notable specializations of #$Pants include #$ShortPants and #$LongPants.")
(comment Strong-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString, <strong>, used in instances of #$HTMLSource to mark certain text as being very important within the document.")
(comment InsecureUsernameFault "A program has this fault if a remote user could exploit the program in such a way that she could discover a valid username for the system.")
(comment (SubcollectionOfWithRelationToTypeFn GiftGiving objectOfPossessionTransfer Currency) "This non-atomic reified term denotes the sub-collection of #$GiftGiving events in which the #$objectOfPossessionTransfer is currency.")
(comment PathThroughWater "The collection of all designated or customary #$Path-Spatials that go entirely through water (underwater).   This would include designated undersea lanes for submarines, or corridors of fish migrations, etc.  An object following such a path is immersed in, and supported by, the water.  Thus it excludes a #$SolidSurfacePathThroughWater, and a #$WaterSurfacePath.  For arbitrary trajectories of motions through water, use #$TrajectoryThroughWater.")
(comment RuinFn "(#$RuinFn ?ART) indicates the collection of ruined artifacts of type ?ART.   Ruined means that it is no longer capable of its intended functions.  This can be  used to talk about ruined barns, junked out cars, etc.")
(comment Cardigan "A sweater which opens in front.")
(comment MartialArtist "The collection of individuals who practice the martial arts.")
(disjointWith Perceiving MakingSomething)
(disjointWith ExchangeOfUserRights GiftGiving)
(comment RibonucleotideSequence-GIS "An instance of #$StuffType and a subset of #$NucleicAcidSequence-GIS.  Each instance of #$RibonucleotideSequence-GIS is an abstract chemical structure consisting of a sequence of ribonucleotides; each such sequence is represented as an instance of #$List, each of whose members is an instance of #$Ribonucleotide-GIS.")
(comment queryBasicComparisonOnTerms "A #$QueryDedicatedPredicate used for comparing one CycL term with another.")
(comment BalconyLevelInAConstruction "#$BalconyLevelInAConstruction is a specialization of #$LevelOfAConstruction.  Each instance of #$BalconyLevelInAConstruction is a balcony in the style of those overhanging levels sometimes found in churches, theatres, etc.  Such balconies are often approximately one-third the size of the floor or level below them, and therefore can be considered legitimate levels themselves. They usually contain a mob of seats.  Note that this collection does _not_ include the kind of balcony that protrudes from a window or door on an already existing level. 

See also #$AboveGroundLevelInAConstruction and #$BasementLevelInAConstruction.")
(comment Warrant-Writ "The collection of all judicial writs authorizing (and possibly obliging) an agent of the court to make a search, seizure, or arrest.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureCreditCardAccountInformation "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a
#$InsecureCreditCardAccountInformationFault on it.")
(disjointWith MarkingOnASurface Synthesis-Generic)
(comment SymlinkFault-ProcessExploiting "A program has this fault if it allows a user to leverage a process run by another user (e.g., root) to launch a symlink attack.")
(comment FiberOpticTransmission "The collection of events in which #$FiberOpticCables are used to transmit            light signals.")
(disjointWith PathArtifactSystem Tool)
(comment PairingObjects "A subcollection of #$GroupingObjects (q.v.) each instance of which is a purposeful creation event in which two partially tangibles are grouped together (possibly in accordance with some general convention) in such a way as to thence constitute a #$PairOfObjects that did not exist before.  Such pairing events are common occurrences in, for example, cobblers' workshops, non-automated chopstick factories, and wedding chapels.  See also #$PairingThingsMentally.")
(comment VulnerableToUserRestrictionBypass "#$VulnerableToUserRestrictionBypass is a specialization of #$VulnerableToSecuritySoftwareBypass.  A computer has this fault if it is possible to circumvent restrictions that software running on it purports to make on the range of actions users are permitted to perform.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with a #$UserRestrictionBypassFault.  It is a #$LocalComputerVulnerabilityAttribute because it only applies when a machine runs software that restricts local users.")
(comment OlympicBoxingCompetition "The collection of #$BoxingCompetitions that are also #$OlympicCompetitions.")
(comment Mufti "A specialization of both #$Cleric and #$Judge.  Each instance of #$Mufti is a religious leader in #$Islam who deals with questions of jurisprudence.  A #$Mufti is the only type of religious leader who can issue a #$Fatwa, which gives him the power of handling cases where there is doubt among other authorities.  The Arabic root for 'mufti' and 'fatwa' is the same: f-t-w")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfUnderspecifiedPath "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with an #$UnderspecifiedPathFault on it.  Note that this vulnerability is exclusively a #$LocalComputerVulnerabilityAttribute.")
(comment ExploitationRemotenessFunction "This collection includes all functions that apply to  instances of #$ComputerVulnerabilityAttribute and return  instances of either #$LocalComputerVulnerabilityAttribute or #$RemoteComputerVulnerabilityAttribute.")
(comment VulnerableToJavascriptCommandExecution "A computer has this vulnerability if is has a program on it that has a #$JavascriptCommandExecutionFault.")
(comment keCommonQueryPredForSpecs-Inverse "A macro predicate for #$keCommonQueryForTerm.  (#$keCommonQueryPredForSpecs-Inverse COL PRED) means that for any specialiazation SPEC of COL, (#$keCommonQueryForTerm SPEC (PRED :WHAT SPEC).")
(comment ArbitraryContentArbitraryFileOverwriteFault "A program has an #$ArbitraryContentArbitraryFileOverwriteFault if it allows an unauthorized user to overwrite arbitrary files with arbitrary content.")
(comment ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Printer "A program has this fault if it allows a local user to acquire the privileges of the printer account.")
(comment removeProgram "(#$removeProgram AGENT COMPUTER PROGRAM) means that AGENT removes PROGRAM from COMPUTER.")
(comment SimplePathSystem "An instance of #$PathSystemType-Structural and the collection of #$PathSystems without loops or parallel links.  This collection includes #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic when there are no non-node points along links.")
(comment BusinessClothing "Things which are worn by business professionals when in the office environment - not the average Cyclist's daily attire!")
(comment contactInsiderAtOrganization "(#$contactInsiderAtOrganization AGENT INSIDER ORG) means that AGENT contacts INSIDER at ORG.")
(comment vaccinatedAgainst "This predicate relates an organism to types of diseases (#$AilmentCondition) against which it is is inoculated. (#$vaccinatedAgainst ORG AIL) means that at some point in the past ORG has been vaccinated against AIL.")
(disjointWith ElevatorCarMoving LocomotionEvent)
(comment DisposalTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections, a specialization of
#$CulturalTerrainFeatureType. Instances of #$DisposalTerrainFeatureType are
collections of constructed disposal sites or structures of significant
importance that are found in such sites. One way of partitioning further
this collection type could be to consider the nature of the waste.")
(comment Paralititan "One of the largest types of dinosaur, a 70-ton plant-eater, whose remains have been discovered in what is now Egypt.  It ate plants. It is a variety of long-neck, long-tailed herbivorous dinosaur.")
(comment mtOfDatabase "(#$mtOfDatabase MT DATABASE) means that the assertions in the #$Microtheory MT represent the information-content of the database represented by DATABASE.  Note that MT need not be an instance of #$PropositionalInformationThing ; MT may contain #$synonymousExternalConcept assertions linking CycL concepts to the database represented by DATABSE.")
(comment OropoucheVirus "The virus that causes #$Oropouche Virus Disease.")
(comment ConferenceRoom "The collection of rooms used for meetings.  Such rooms normally contain chairs and tables.")
(disjointWith Wig Clothing-Generic)
(comment DisplayLockScreenSaver "#$DisplayLockScreenSaver includes all instances of #$ScreenSaver that require authentication to cease displaying their animated images.")
(comment U-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to mark certain text as being underlined in the document generated by the #$HTMLSource.")
(comment sequenceCodesForSequence "(#$sequenceCodesForSequence NUCLEOTIDE-SEQ PEPTIDE-SEQ) means
that the sequence of nucleotides represented by the list
NUCLEOTIDE-SEQ codes for the sequence of #$AminoAcid types
PEPTIDE-SEQ, in the sense that if NUCLEOTIDE-SEQ appears in a
#$DNAMolecule, it can be translated into a #$ProteinMolecule with the
#$PeptideSequence PEPTIDE-SEQ.  Note that (#$sequenceCodesForSequence
NUCLEOTIDE-SEQ PEPTIDE-SEQ) does not entail that the
#$sequenceConnectivity of NUCLEOTIDE-SEQ be
#$CodingSequence-Uninterrupted: i.e., instances of #$Intron-GIS and
other noncoding sequences can be subsequences of NUCLEOTIDE-SEQ.  If
the stronger sense of 'uninterrupted coding' is intended, use the
specialization #$sequenceCodesForSequence-Continuous.")
(comment UnauthorizedSoftwareInstallationFault "A program has an #$UnauthorizedSoftwareInstallationFault if it is possible for an unauthorized remote user to cause software to be installed on the computer the program is running on.")
(comment ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-Root "#$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-Root is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has this fault when it allows unauthorized remote users access to a root account on the system.")
(comment RuinedArtifact "#$RuinedArtifact is the class of artifacts which have, either due to wear and tear over a long time, or due to destructive events, human-caused or otherwise, been degraded to the point that they can't serve their intended function.  If something is a #$RuinedArtifact, then it's usually so far gone that it can't be repaired. Specializations include ruined buildings, junked cars, smashed pottery, etc.")
(comment Parka "Short hip-length coats lined or padded , water-repellent with hoods.")
(disjointWith Polygon RoundObject)
(disjointWith Travel-TripEvent CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment complementaryNucleotide-GIS "(#$complementaryNucleotide-GIS NUCLEOTIDE1 NUCLEOTIDE2) means that that NUCLEOTIDE1 and NUCLEOTIDE2 are nucleotides that pair with each other.  The pairs are (#$Cytosine-GIS #$Guanine-GIS) (#$Adenine-GIS #$Thymine-GIS) and (#$Adenine-GIS #$Uracil-GIS) .")
(comment TranslocationAlongFn "(#$TranslocationAlongFn PATH) denotes the subcollection of #$Translation-LocationChange whose instances occur along PATH.")
(disjointWith AboveGroundLevelInAConstruction BasementLevelInAConstruction)
(comment Writ "The collection of all written orders by a court [#$Court-Judicial] ordering and authorizing a #$LegalAgent to whom it is addressed to perform or cease performing some specific act or type of act.")
(comment CapabilityPredicate-TypeLevel "This is the subcollection of those #$CapabilityPredicates whose first argument is a specialization of #$Individual.  These predicates are 'type-level' because they assert something about the capabilities of a type of thing, rather than an individual.  Contrast #$CapabilityPredicate-InstanceLevel.")
(disjointWith MarkingOnASurface ChangeInUserRights)
(comment POP2ServerProgram "#$POP2ServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement #$POP2Protocol. POP2 daemons  by default listen on TCP port 109, whereas #$POP3ServerProgram daemons run on port 110.")
(comment SpreadingBodyParts "The collection of all gestures in which an animal (person) spreads two or more like body parts apart to make a gesture, e.g., spreading fingers apart, spreading arms apart, etc.")
(comment RiflingInBarrel "Spinning while translating through a gun barrel due to grooves in the pipe.  Rotary motion is imparted to the moving object in this event.")
(comment CovertAgent "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent.  Each instance of #$CovertAgent is an individual or a formal or informal organization that plans and conducts a significant portion of its activities secretly.  Examples instances of #$CovertAgent include criminals and criminal organizations, terrorists, spies and espionage agencies, and military units working behind enemy lines.  Exposure of such an agent's activities, location, plans, and (if applicable) membership, to outside agents generally threatens its continued existence and effectiveness.")
(comment modifyLogProgramFileAccessTimeRecords "(#$modifyLogProgramFileAccessTimeRecords AGENT LOGPROG) means that AGENT modifies the time access records for the log files generated by LOGPROG.")
(disjointWith Device-OneTimeUse PathArtifactSystem)
(comment bodyPartTypeForClothingType "(#$bodyPartTypeForClothingType CLOTHINGTYPE BODYPARTTYPE) means that elements of CLOTHINGTYPE are typically worn on parts of the BODYPART belonging to BODYPARTTYPE.")
(comment VulnerableToDesktopSecuritySoftwareBypass "#$VulnerableToDesktopSecuritySoftwareBypass is a specialization of #$VulnerableToUserRestrictionBypass.  A computer has this fault if it is running a #$DesktopSecurityProgram with a #$DesktopSecuritySoftwareBypassFault.  It is a #$LocalComputerVulnerabilityAttribute because it only applies when a machine runs software that restricts local users.")
(comment OpeningTag "The collection of all tags that are the result of an application of #$OpenTagFn.  Instances of this collection are not reified.")
(disjointWith FloorInAConstruction WallOfAConstruction)
(comment InfrastructureProduct "The collection of products which add directly to the infrastructure of some place.")
(comment InstallationProgram "Software that installs another program when executed.")
(comment ElevatedPrivilegeFault-WebServer "#$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-WebServer is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-WebServer when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to create arbitrary files with the privileges of the web server.")
(comment Fatwa "A #$Fatwa is a legal pronouncement in #$Islam, issued by a religious lawyer called a #$Mufti, based upon standing precedent and the Qur'an.")
(comment Studio "A set of rooms where some type of activity is performed.")
(comment few-GenQuantRelnTo "(#$few-GenQuantRelnTo RELN COL THING) is true if
few of the instances X of COL are such that (RELN X THING) holds.")
(comment VulnerableToWINSFileDeletion "A computer has this vulnerability if has a program on it
that has a #$WINSFileDeletionFault.")
(comment PrimaryTranscript-ThreePrimeEnd "The collection of 3' ends of any primary transcript of an RNA molecule.")
(comment DeviceDriverCrashingFault "#$DeviceDriverCrashingFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program (usually an operating system or a device driver) has an #$DeviceDriverCrashingFault when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to send commands
 to copies of the program that cause it to crash and require rebooting to regain normal control of the devices it drives.")
(disjointWith Toy Weapon)
(comment itemCompared "'(#$itemCompared COMPARING ITEM)' means that ITEM is one of the things compared in the #$Comparing COMPARING.")
(comment CoolieHat "conical hat worn by field workers in Asia, usually made of straw.")
(comment copyFileFromTo "(#$copyFileFromTo AGENT FILE FROM_COMPUTER TO_COMPUTER) means that AGENT copies the #$ComputerFile-AIS from FROM_COMPUTER and creates a new copy on TO_COMPUTER.  Note that (#$copyFileFromTo AGENT FILE FROM_COMPUTER TO_COMPUTER) may be accomplished in a number of ways: by calling the cp function, by cutting-and-pasting, etc.")
(comment RegionalCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture whose participants live in a particular 
  geographic region, and which has developed around the 
  experiences of those participants.  For example, there are 
  instances of #$RegionalCulture associated with #$South-USRegion, 
  #$SouthernCalifornia, and the #$ArabianDesert.  See also
  #$RegionalTypeCulture.")
(comment allelicVariant-GenInfo "(#$allelicVariant-GenInfo GENE1 GENE2) means that GENE1 and GENE2 are alleles. Two genes are allelic or allelomorphic when they are instantiated in the same relative location in homologous chromosomes [see #$Chromosome] and produce alternative effects (i.e. phenotypical expression) in genetic processes and can mutate one to another.")
(comment pointInSystem "A binary predicate that relates #$PathSystems (q.v.) to the \"points\" in those systems.  (#$pointInSystem POINT SYSTEM) means that POINT is either a \"point\" on a path in, or a \"node\" in SYSTEM.  Each path system has at least one point.  Note that virtually any type of #$Thing can in principle serve as a point in some path-system (which is why the first argument-place of #$pointInSystem is not constrained to, e.g., instances of #$Individual).  The set of all _nodes_ in a given path-system is an important subset of the set of all _points_ in that system; see #$nodeInSystem for the difference between nodes and other (i.e. non-node) points. See also #$PointsInSystemFn.")
(comment FloorInAConstruction "#$FloorInAConstruction is a specialization of #$PartOfAnHSC and #$Wall-GenericBarrier.  Each instance of #$FloorInAConstruction is a physical floor in a building (typically made to walk upon), _not_ the level (the story composed of rooms or halls -- see #$LevelOfAConstruction).  The floor can include any floor in a building such as the floor of a room on the third floor as well as the floor of the entire first level of the building.  This includes just the horizontal surface -- not the subfloor.  It also does not include floor coverings like carpet or tile.")
(comment transportsTo "Agent A transports thing B to some place C.")
(comment PoliticalPartyMember "The collection of all #$PoliticalPartyMembers, includes the #$Republicans and #$Democrats, as well as other political parties.")
(comment TrojanDriveFault "A program has a #$TrojanDriveFault when a machine running it is susceptible to allowing an attacker to configure the system so a trojan drive masquerades as the standard drive.")
(comment IncreaseAction "The collection of #$Actions in which an agent acts to produce a increase in some quantity.")
(comment addedTogether "(#$addedTogether ADDING LIST) means that, in the instance of #$DoingAddition ADDING, the performer of ADDING added together the sequence of numbers in LIST.  If a particular event of #$DoingAddition is done properly, then the resulting number should be equal to that of (#$PlusFn N1, N2 ... Nn), where (N1, N2 ... Nn) is the sequence of numbers in LIST.  Note that duplicate digits are permissible in LIST: for instance, in the case of (#$addedTogether ADDING (#$TheList 5 2 5)), the performer of ADDING would add correctly if the result is 12, not 7.")
(comment Oropouche "A viral infection which emerged in 1961. Initial symptoms include fever, headache, malaise, joint and/or muscle pain, inflammation of the eyes with an intolerance to light. there may also be occasional nausea and vomiting. May progress to inflammation of the meninges and/or the brain.")
(comment no-GenQuantRelnToFromType "(#$no-GenQuantRelnToFromType RELN COL1 COL2) is true iff there is no

element INST1 of COL1 such that there is an element INST2 of COL2 for which

(RELN INST1 INST2) holds.")
(comment Ul-HTMLTag "The #$CharacterString used in instances of #$HTMLSource to indicate an unordered (i.e., unnumbered) list.")
(comment Leftist "Agents with this ideology advocate reform or overthrow of established order, usually in the name of the good of the common man.")
(comment objectProtected "(#$objectProtected PROTECT-EVENT OBJECT) means that during PROTECT-EVENT the agent responsible aims to protect OBJECT.  This is a stronger notion than the more general #$objectTakenCareOf since it is restricted to #$ProtectingSomething events.  Yet it also implies that one goes to relatively great lengths to protect OBJECT, including committing #$ViolentActions.")
(comment serverInitiatesServerProgramOn "A predicate relating instances of #$InternetServicesDaemon with
 instances of #$ServerProgram and instances of #$Computer.
 (#$serverInitiatesServerProgramOn DAEMON SERVER COMPUTER) means that DAEMON
 listens for connections on certain internet sockets for requests to
 SERVER on COMPUTER. If DAEMON receives a requests, it starts a process
 of SERVER.")
(comment SpoofedSourceFn "(#$SpoofedSourceFn DATA) denotes the collection of members of DATA
that come from spoofed sources.")
(comment TurnInPath "A portion of a #$Path-Generic which is curved.  Direction is a monotonic function of position.")
(comment StencilArtifact "The collection of artifacts that are the results of a
stenciling event.")
(comment WomensDressBoot "Formal shoes worn by women.")
(disjointWith SeparationEvent Constructing)
(comment queryDifferenceOnTerms "A #$QueryDedicatedPredicate used for querying for
differences between two terms.")
(comment BidirectionalCustomaryPath "The collection of all instances of #$Path-Customary with no customary direction.  They can be followed (in the customary system) in either direction.  See #$DirectedCustomaryPath for customary paths with a customary direction.")
(comment RealEstate "A specialization of #$Place-NonAgent.  Each instance of #$RealEstate is either a parcel of land or a land-based property that can be bought, sold, or rented.  Notable specializations of #$RealEstate include #$GroundsOfOrganization, #$Building, and #$ModernShelterConstruction.")
(comment MountRequestForwardingFault "A program has this fault if it is possible for an unauthorized remote user to send a mount request to that program, which will then be forwarded to the mount daemon. If the mount request is for a filesystem that is mountable, a valid filehandle will be returned. This in turn can be used to access a filesystem which would otherwise not be accessible.")
(comment TypewriterTyping "Typing on a typewriter (as opposed to, e.g. a terminal keyboard). Requires two hands.")
(comment InfluencingAnAgent "A collection of #$PurposefulActions.  In each instance of #$InfluencingAnAgent, one #$IntelligentAgent deliberately and successfully influences the actions of another (or at least the other's dispositions to act). This collection is restricted to \"influence\" through cognitive or emotional channels -- e.g. influencing someone through rational persuasion, through appeals to emotion, or by #$MakingAThreat. Affecting someone's behavior solely by the application of physical force -- e.g. twisting your arm to make you cry out -- is not influencing in the relevant sense.  Also, this collection does not include cases where an agent A influences the actions of B unknowingly -- e.g., by serving as a role model for B, or by unintentionally alienating B.  Borderline cases involve the influenced agent acting in a way the influencer did not envision -- e.g. my telling you to be more assertive in your personal relationships, and you responding to the advice (to my horror) by beating someone up.")
(comment ResponseTemplate "This template category covers a limited number of hard-to-characterize English words and phrases, such as \"Yes\", \"No\", and \"That is correct\".  See template assertions for more examples.")
(disjointWith PathArtifactSystem Projectile-Device)
(comment MensClothing "A specialization of #$Clothing-Generic.  Each specialization of #$MensClothing is a type of clothing item worn usually by men.  Specializations of #$MensClothing include #$Tuxedo and #$MensJockeyUnderwear.")
(comment VulnerableToDiskUsageManagementSoftwareBypass "#$VulnerableToDiskUsageManagementSoftwareBypass is a specialization of #$VulnerableToUserRestrictionBypass.  A computer has this fault if it is running a program with a #$DiskUsageManagementSoftwareBypassFault.  It is a #$LocalComputerVulnerabilityAttribute because it only applies when a machine runs software that restricts local users.")
(comment affordToHireType "(#$affordToHireType AGENT PROFESSIONTYPE) means that AGENT can financially afford to hire an instance of PROFESSIONTYPE.")
(comment IssuingAFatwa "The process of issuing a #$Fatwa.")
(comment subTranslations-SingleTrajectory "(#$subTranslations-SingleTrajectory MOVE1 MOVE2) means that MOVE2 is a subevent of MOVE1, both being #$Translation-SingleTrajectory, and that MOVE2 has as parts all parts of MOVE1 that are temporally subsumed by MOVE2.  That is to say, if MOVE1 is like a big rope, MOVE2 should be like a segment of the rope (rather than a thin thread in the rope).  Since there is only one OBJ in MOVE1 such that (#$objectMoving MOVE1 OBJ) holds, we can clarify the meaning of (#$subTranslations-SingleTrajectory MOVE1 MOVE2) by saying that MOVE2 is such a Translation-SingleTrajectroy that the MOVE2 is the movement of OBJ during an interval within the temporal extention of MOVE1")
(comment ChemistryLaboratory "A place equipped for research in chemistry.")
(comment few-GenQuantRelnFrom "(#$few-GenQuantRelnFrom RELN COL THING) is true if

few of the instances INST of COL are such that (RELN THING INST) holds.")
(comment mtImagePerspective "The visual image associated with the image mt ARG1 depicts the object ARG2 in the perspective attribute ARG3.")
(comment VulnerableToCacheBypass "A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a program with a #$CacheBypassFault.")
(comment DestinationNameFn "(#$DestinationNameFn COMPUTER_NAME_STRING) denotes the collection of #$Packet-Internets whose destination is the machine indicated by COMPUTER_NAME_STRING.  For example, (#$DestinationNameFn \"garm.cyc.com\") denotes the collection of all packets whose destination computer address is denoted by the name string \"garm.cyc.com\".")
(comment GeographicalArea-Intangible "The collection of two dimensional
intangible geographical things. For instance, the \"abstract\" (i.e. #$Intangible) area
circumscribed by the 25th and 65th north parallels and the 45th and 125th
west meridian (see #$GeographicalPlace-2D) - #$ContiguousUnitedStates is
located there; #$BattleZone is an example of specialization.")
(comment HyperlinkCommandExecutionFault "A program PROG has this fault if it is possible for a hostile web site operator to create a web page and a hyperlink such that a user running PROG who clicks on the hyperlink will inadvertently execute commands on his/her client machine. ")
(comment demarcates "(#$demarcates MARKER PLACE) means that MARKER is positioned so as to locate PLACE or a border or corner of PLACE.  Boundary markers, physical milestones, and markers which indicate an offset (``85 meters south of this spot'') all bear this relation with a place.")
(comment Sculpture "A specialization of #$ArtObject. Each instance of this collection is a tangible three-dimensional work of art. Buildings are not included, even though sculptural features of buildings (such as friezes) are. Types of #$Sculpture include stone statues, friezes, wood carvings, pipes welded into abstract art sculptures, etc. Example instances: the #$StatueOfLiberty, the #$MountRushmoreMonument, Michelangelo's David, the friezes on the #$Parthenon, the Buddhas at Longan. See also #$Sculptor.")
(comment FalconryGlove "The collection of gloves often worn by falconers while working with birds of prey.")
(comment doDenialOfServiceAttackOfType "(#$doDenialOfServiceAttackOfType AGENT MANNER DENIED ATTACK-TYPE) means that AGENT performs in MANNER a denial of service attack of ATTACK-TYPE to render DENIED incapable of performing basic services, such as responding to network requests.")
(comment RegionalTypeCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture whose participants live in the same 
  type of geographic region, and which has developed 
  around the experiences of those participants.  For example, 
  there are instances of #$RegionalTypeCulture associated with 
  #$Desert, #$Forest-Wild, and #$Seacoast.  See also 
  #$RegionalCulture.")
(comment PathArtifact "A specialization of both #$ConstructionArtifact and #$Path-Customary.  Each instance of #$PathArtifact is a spatial path made by humans or animals.  Instances of #$PathArtifact include #$ErieCanal, #$WellandShipCanal, #$ChampsElysee, #$WallStreet, and #$Highway101CA.  Note that each of these artifacts is a single, particular path; to refer to a whole system of #$PathArtifacts, use #$PathArtifactSystem.")
(disjointWith FoundationOfABuilding CeilingOfARoom)
(comment ProcessingIndustryTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections, a specialization of
#$CulturalTerrainFeatureType. Instances of
#$ProcessingIndustryTerrainFeatureType are collections of objects
participating in the industrial processing of some substance or
material. One way of partitioning further this collection type could be to
consider the nature of the substance processed.")
(comment GeographicalThing-Intangible-MovableLocation "The collection of all intangible things that have movable geographic locations, such as isotherms, isobars, isohyets or various kinds of 'lines' and 'zones' in battles (see #$LineOfMilitaryForces, #$BattleZone and #$ZoneOfMilitaryControl).  Another example would be the prohibited regions surrounding persons who have obtained court orders to keep other persons away from them.  Another example is tidal regions.  Contrast this with #$GeographicalThing-Intangible-FixedLocation.")
(comment UnauthorizedDLLUploadFault "A server program has this fault if it is possible for an unauthorized remote user to upload arbitrary DLL files onto the server.  These DLLs will run at the privilege level of the server program.")
(comment DecreaseAction "The collection of #$Actions in which an agent acts to produce a decrease in some quantity.")
(comment playPerformanceActorRole "(playPerformanceActorRole PLAY ROLE AGENT) means that in some particular #$PlayPerformance PLAY of a #$Play-CW, AGENT played the part of the #$NarrativeRole ROLE.")
(comment Onyong-Nyong-Virus "The virus that causes O'nyong-nyong disease (#$Onyong-Nyong).")
(comment TraversalFn "A function to obtain a traversal from a chain of points and paths.  For example, (#$TraversalFn CHAIN), with the #$PathChain CHAIN = (#$TheList X(1) Y(1) ... X(n) Y(n) X(n+1)), gives a #$Traversal that starts at point X(1), moves to point X(2) through path Y(1), ..., etc. and stops at point X(n+1).  Note that (#$TraversalFn CHAIN1) and (#$TraversalFn CHAIN2) may denote the same #$Traversal even when CHAIN1 is different from CHAIN2. This is due to the fact that the same path can be obtained by concatenating different path chains and that cycles can be obtained by concatenating paths in several combinations.")
(comment termStrings-GuessedFromName "(#$termStrings-GuessedFromName TERM PHRASE) indicates that PHRASE is inferred reference for TERM based on its name. This is a specialization of #$termStrings-Guessed intended for use mainly by a lexification utility.")
(comment SystemAccountFn "(#$SystemAccountFn COMPUTER) denotes a particular #$NonLoginAccount, namely, the instance of #$SystemAccountForNT on the instance of #$Computer COMPUTER, which runs the #$MSWindowsNT operating system on COMPUTER.")
(comment exampleArg2Strings "This predicate is used to make

 meta-assertions on binary instances of #$DocumentationConstant that

 take a #$SubLString in their arg2.  (#$exampleArg2Strings PRED EXAMPLE)

 says that EXAMPLE is a good example of the kind of string one should

 put in the arg2 of PRED.  This predicate is useful for documenting

 informal standards for use of predicates such as #$comment, #$cyclistNotes, etc.")
(comment OrigamiArtifact "The collection of artifacts that result from folding a piece
of paper into a recognizable ornamental shape.")
(comment BalletShoe "The special shoes worn by classical ballet dancers.")
(disjointWith MakingSomething Patrolling)
(comment entryPointOnPathToSystem "This predicate can be used to indicate when a point that lies 
on some path in an instance SYS of #$PathSystem is an 'access
point' to that system, i.e. is a point that allows direct external
access to SYS via some instance of #$Path-Simple.  More formally, 
(#$entryPointOnPathToSystem ENTRY_POINT PATH SYS) means four
things: (i) ENTRY_POINT is a point in the system SYS, i.e.
(#$pointInSystem ENTRY_POINT SYS), and ENTRY_POINT is on PATH, i.e.
(#$pointOnPath ENTRY_POINT PATH); there is some 
OUTSIDE_POINT such that (iia) (#$pointOnPath OUTSIDE_POINT PATH)
and (#$not (#$pointInSystem OUTSIDE_POINT SYS)), 
(iib) the relationship among PATH, OUTSIDE_POINT and
ENTRY_POINT is represented by
(#$pathConnects PATH OUTSIDE_POINT ENTRY_POINT), i.e.
PATH always allows 'travel' from OUTSIDE_POINT to 
ENTRY_POINT and often (but not always) from
ENTRY_POINT to OUTSIDE_POINT and (iic) if OTHER_POINT
is any #$pointInSystem SYS, then 
(#$not (#$betweenOnPath OTHER_POINT ENTRY_POINT OUTSIDE_POINT 
(#$SubPathBetweenFn PATH ENTRY_POINT OUTSIDE_POINT))),
in other words, ENTRY_POINT is the first point one would
'encounter' when 'travelling' along PATH from OUTSIDE_POINT into SYS.
This predicate is useful for, say, representing the 'access
points' to an instance of #$LocalAreaNetwork from the
#$Internet.")
(comment ModernHumanResidence "A specialization of both #$HumanResidence and #$ModernShelterConstruction.  Each instance of #$ModernHumanResidence is a humanly constructed shelter of a modern type in which people live.  Such residences are the typical dwellings in the developed world of the late 20th century and may be found in the more affluent regions of the developing world.  Examples include houses in suburban `developments', modern apartment buildings, `modular' homes, etc.")
(disjointWith SpermCell Egg)
(comment DecidingToDoSomething "This is the collection of mental acts of resolving to do a type of action.  #$PurposefulActions are preceded by such a decision, which is what makes them intentional.  One does not decide to do an action, since the action that one will do does not exist at the time of the decision; rather, one decides to do a type of act.")
(comment packetConformsToProtocol "(#$packetConformsToProtocol PACKET PROTOCOL) means that the #$Packet-Network PACKET carries information coded in accordance with the #$NetworkProtocol PROTOCOL.  If PACKET is a #$Packet-Internet, for example, (#$packetConformsToProtocol PACKET PROTOCOL) means either that PROTOCL is specified in PACKET's IP header or else PROTOCOL is the #$InternetProtocol.")
(comment SymlinkFault-BinGroupOnly "A program has this fault if it allows a  user in the \"bin\" group to launch a symlink attack.")
(comment PhysicalPathDisclosureFault "A program has a #$PhysicalPathDisclosureFault if it allows an attacker to determine full physical path name to a file, usually by providing malformed input to a process.")
(comment AircraftRepairOrganization "An organization which provides the service of repairing aircraft, and whose physical quarters is usually located at/near an airport or some other location where aircraft land, takeoff, refuel, etc.")
(disjointWith SupportColumn SheetOfSomeStuff)
(comment OxfordShirt "The collection of Oxford-style shirts, a front-buttoned style of collared shirt, typically long-sleeved with button-down collar and cuffs, and made of a smooth durable cloth.")
(comment VulnerableToDisplayLockBypass "#$VulnerableToDisplayLockBypass is a specialization of #$VulnerableToUserRestrictionBypass.  A computer has this vulnerabilty if it is possible for an attacker to unlock it without supplying the proper password.  That is, a computer has this vulnerability if it is running a program with a #$DisplayLockBypassFault.")
(comment ReligiousPerson "Any person who is a member of some Religion.  A believer by default.")
(comment CloseTagFn "For a particular instance of #$MarkupLanguageTag, (#$CloseTagFn TAG) returns the closing tag form of the #$MarkupLanguageTag TAG.  For example, the result of (#$CloseTagFn #$Caption-HTMLTag) is </caption>.  Closing tags are almost always indicated by a slash in front of the text comprising the opening tag form.")
(comment lengthOfPathTypeInRegion "(#$lengthOfPathTypeInRegion PLACE PATH-TYPE LENGTH) means that LENGTH (in miles or kilometers, for instance) is the total length of all pieces of PATH-TYPE in PLACE.")
(disjointWith Lingerie Clothing-Top)
(comment few-GenQuantRelnFrom "(#$few-GenQuantRelnFrom RELN THING COL) is true if
few of the instances INST of COL are such that (RELN THING INST) holds.")
(comment VulnerableToJavascriptSurveillance "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program that has a #$JavascriptSurveillanceFault.")
(comment SwitchCrashingFault "#$SwitchCrashingFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has an #$SwitchCrashingFault when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to send commands

to copies of the program that cause it to crash and require rebooting to regain normal control of the switch it drives.")
(comment PredictableCookieIDFault "A server program has this fault if it generates a predictable sequence of ID numbers for cookies saved on the machine of the user. For instance, it might generate a number from the user's UserID no.,  which would make it possible for a malicious user to locally edit the saved cookie, substituting the appropriate administrative cookie ID number for the one they were assigned.")
(comment doEscalatePrivilegeOnSystemSurreptitiously "(#$doEscalatePrivilegeOnSystemSurreptitiously AGENT LEVEL SYSTEM) means that AGENT raises his privileges on SYSTEM to LEVEL, in a manner likely to escape detection.  For instance, someone could load an executable root exploit, run it, and then remove it from the system.")
(disjointWith PoweredDevice TenderObject)
(comment DressShoe "DressShoes are usually worn with slacks or dresses.")
(comment doDecryptFile " (#$doDecryptFile AGENT AIS) means that AGENT takes steps to decrypt the #$ComputerFile-AIS AIS. See also #$decryptFile.")
(comment ReligiousCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance
  of which is a culture defined at least in part by the fact 
  that its core participants are followers of a particular 
  religion, sect, or religious cult and thus share various 
  religious beliefs and engage in various religious practices.
  For example, there are instances of #$ReligiousCulture
  associated with #$ProtestantReligion and #$SunniIslam.")
(comment GenomeOfBLOFn "(#$GenomeOfBLOFn BLO) denotes the instance of

#$GeneticInformation which is the genome of [see #$genomeOfBLO-GenInfo] the #$BiologicalLivingObject BLO.")
(comment PartOfAnHSC "#$PartOfAnHSC is a specialization of #$ConstructionArtifact and #$PhysicalPartOfObject.  Each instance of #$PartOfAnHSC is a \"built-in\" part of some #$HumanShelterConstruction; that is, each instance is built with the intention of remaining a part of the construction.  Notable specializations of #$PartOfAnHSC include #$FloorInAConstruction, #$PartOfBuilding, and #$WallOfAConstruction.")
(comment Anesthesia "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$DrugTherapy (q.v.).  In an instance of #$Anesthesia, a #$BiologicalLivingObject undergoes the effect of some instance of #$Anesthetic, the effect of which is to eliminate the perception of pain.  #$Anesthesia events occur in connection with other medical care events, so that a patient will not feel the pain or discomfort that would otherwise be associated with those medical procedures.  #$Anesthetics are of various chemical kinds, work in various ways, and can be administered in various ways.  They may topically numb an area, they may poison the central nervous system to the point where the animal loses consciousness, etc.  The resulting anesthetic therapies thus may differ, according to the type of anesthetic used; for example, the patient may or may not be conscious during an instance of #$Anesthesia.  See also #$AdministeringADrug.")
(comment CGICommandExecutionFault "A CGI program has this fault if it allows an unauthorized user to execute arbitrary code on the web server running the program.")
(comment Onyong-Nyong "A disease causing arthritis in wrist, knee, ankle and small joints of extremities. A rash may develop. May present hemorrhagic symptoms. Recovery may be prolonged.")
(comment traversalTo "(#$traversalTo TRAV POINT) means that POINT is an ending point of the #$Traversal TRAV along some paths.  Note that (#$traversalTo TRAV A) and (#$traversalTo TRAV B) may both be true even when A and B are different.  This can happen when, e.g., A is a part of B and a path goes to both.  This is why we did not call POINT, in the context above, THE ending point of TRAV.")
(comment ControlRoom "The collection of rooms, usually found in power plants, dams, and other similar large constructions, that contain crucial control devices.")
(comment no-GenQuantRelnFrom "(#$no-GenQuantRelnFrom RELN THING COL) is true iff there is no INST

such that INST is an element of COL and (RELN THING INST) holds.")
(comment challengee "'(#$challengee CHALLENGE AGENT)' means that AGENT is
challenged in the #$Challenging CHALLENGE.")
(comment onPath "(#$onPath THING PATH) means that THING is located along (on or adjacent to) the #$Path-Generic PATH.  THING could be a moving object, or it could be a stationary point (in the latter case, see the more specific predicate #$pointOnPath).  For example, Saint Louis, Missouri was #$onPath U.S. Route 66, as was Missouri, any car driving along Route 66, and any lamp-post alongside it.")
(comment EmbroideryArtifact "The collection of embroidered objects")
(comment RubberBoot "Boots made of rubber, protect from water and slush.")
(disjointWith Drying CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment Safeguard-Situation "This is the collection of situations which constitute the safeguarding of

something. Some of these are purposeful actions (#$ProtectingSomething); others are events

which are not purposeful actions (a security program running); still others are

more-or-less static situations (a lock's being in a door). While not all instances

of #$Safeguard-Situation are purposeful actions, all are a result of such. Note that the term `safeguard' may also

be used to denote artifacts such as locks and computer programs, even when they are not being used to safeguard. These things

are instances of #$Safeguard-Artifact. (#$SteveSchulz 4/11/2000)")
(comment codonCodesFor "(#$codonCodesFor CODON AMINO_ACID_TYPE) means that physical codons [#$Codon-MolecularSegment] in a #$MessengerRNA molecule which instantiate CODON (an instance of #$Codon-GIS) code for the placement of an instance of AMINO_ACID_TYPE being built into the corresponding position in a #$PeptideChain  generated from the #$MessengerRNA.  #$TransferRNA molecules with a complementary sequence [#$complementaryNucleicAcidSequences] bind to that type of #$AminoAcid.")
(comment querySimilarityOnTerms "A #$QueryDedicatedPredicate used for querying for
similarities between two terms.")
(comment entryPointToSystem "This predicate is a simpler, binary version of 
#$entryPointOnPathToSystem to be used only when simpler
representations of the entry points to a path system are useful.
(#$entryPointToSystem ENTRY_POINT SYS) means that
ENTRY_POINT lies on some instance PATH of #$Path-Simple
such that
(#$entryPointOnPathToSystem ENTRY_POINT PATH SYS) holds.
See also #$entryPathToSystem.")
(comment MS-DOSApplication "Programs that are made to run under #$MS-DOS.  Most of them are installed by default during a #$MSWindows or #$MSWindowsNT installation, but they must be run from the MS-DOS command line.")
(comment BuildingRow "A specialization of #$BuildingCluster each of whose 
instances is arranged in a row.  In densely-populated cites
it is not uncommon for a row of buildings to take up one 
side of an entire #$BlockOfStreet.")
(comment ArbitraryFileCopyFault "A program has this fault if it allows non-privileged users to copy any file on the system.")
(comment PaperTowelDispenser "A device for storing/dispensing paper towels.")
(comment MakingAPhoneCall "The collection of all actions wherein a phone call is made by inputting a multi-digit telephone number to a phone system.  It includes both cases where the phone call is 'successful' in the sense that the person whom the caller is trying to contact is contacted, and cases where the call is 'unsuccessful', insofar as the call does not succeed in reaching its intended recipient for any one of a variety of reasons.  The call must, however, actually be 'placed'--dialing must be successfully completed.  Cases where the full number is not dialed do not count as instances of #$MakingAPhoneCall.  The collection includes instances where the call is placed manually, by a human agent picking up a receiver and hitting buttons or dialing a rotary dial, and cases where the call is placed electronically, e.g., via a modem. In cases where an instance of #$MakingAPhoneCall is successful for the agent placing the call, the instance will figure as the initiating subevent in an instance of (#$CommunicatingByMeansOfFn #$Telephone).  As a rule, an instance of #$MakingAPhoneCall will consist of a complete 'dialing' and an instance of #$EstablishingAPhoneLink.  If the placer of the call is human, the instance will usually include an initial act of #$PickingUpATelephoneReceiver.")
(comment programRunningOnComputerHasFault "(#$programRunningOnComputerHasFault PROG COMP FAULT) means that the copy of PROG which is currently running on (#$programRunningOn, q.v.) COMP manifests FAULT.")
(comment VulnerableToVirusScanBypass "#$VulnerableToVirusScanBypass is a specialization of #$VulnerableToSecuritySoftwareBypass. A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a program with a #$VirusScanBypassFault.")
(comment affordToRent "(#$affordToRent AGENT OBJECT) means that AGENT can financially afford to rent OBJECT.")
(comment ExternalAccessToAccountsFault "#$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has this fault when it allows unauthorized remote users access to some account on the system.  The more specialized attributes, such as #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-Root or #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-User, should be used if possible.  However neither #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault nor any of its specializations should be used if some more precise attribute (e.g., #$BufferOverflowFault-CommandExecution, #$CommandExecutionFault) applies.")
(comment ComputerFile-Abstract "In some respects and in some domains (notably, #$ComputerSecurityMt) it is sometimes more convenient and more natural to represent computer files as instances of #$ConceptualWork.  This enables #$Cyclists to adapt existing, program-(#$ConceptualWork) oriented vocabulary to represent files.  On the other hand, in some respects (notably when dealing with encryption) it is sometimes more convenient and natural to represent computer files as instances of #$AbstractInformationStructure.  Thus we have two collections, #$ComputerFile-AIS and #$ComputerFile-CW.  This collection, #$ComputerFile-Abstract, serves as the union of these two collections in order that there might be some vocabulary which can apply to both collections (e.g., #$fileFoundOnComputer).")
(comment templateParsingRootMtForLanguage "(#$templateParsingRootMtForLanguage MT LANG) means that MT is the most general #$TemplateParsingMicrotheory which is specific to the #$NaturalLanguage, LANG.")
(comment few-GenQuantRelnToType "(#$few-GenQuantRelnToType RELN COL1 COL2) means that for few of the

instances X of COL1 there is an instance INST of COL2 such that (RELN X INST)

holds.")
(comment VulnerableToDirectoryTraversal "A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a server program with a #$DirectoryTraversalFault.")
(comment SourceNameFn "(#$SourceNameFn COMPUTER_NAME_STRING) denotes the collection of #$Packet-Internets whose source is the machine indicated by COMPUTER_NAME_STRING.  For example, (#$SourceNameFn \"garm.cyc.com\") denotes the collection of all packets whose source IP address is \"garm.cyc.com\".")
(comment DefaultWorldWritableExecutablesFault "A program has this fault if, either in its installation or
 execution, it creates executable files which are world writable
 (unless their permissions are subsequently changed).  A malicious user
 could potentially exploit a program with this fault by altering the
 executable files and waiting for the binary to be executed by some
 privileged user.")
(comment hasAsChiefExecutiveOfGovernment "(#$hasAsChiefExecutiveOfGovernment REGION HEAD) says that HEAD is the governmental figure with executive decision-making power.  In many cases the person who plays the role of #$hasAsChiefExecutiveOfGovernment will also be the one who plays the role of #$hasAsHeadOfGovernment.  In some cases, e.g., Russia, it is the person who plays role of #$headOfStateOf instead.")
(comment demarcatesPrecisely "(#$demarcatesPrecisely MARKER PLACE) means that MARKER is positioned exactly on PLACE or a border or corner of PLACE.  Boundary markers, lines painted across a sports track or on a roadway, and numbers painted on stairway doors all bear this relation with a place (e.g. a #$GeographicalRegion, #$LaneOfRoadway, or floor of a building [#$LevelOfAConstruction]).")
(comment Cross-FixedStructure "A specialization of #$FixedStructure.  Each instance of #$Cross-FixedStructure is a freestanding cross-shaped construction artifact.  A notable specialization is #$Cross-TortureDevice, instances of which are the crucifixes used by the Romans to crucify their victims (and a notable instance of which is #$CrossOfJesus).  #$Cross-FixedStructure also includes the crosses used by the Ku Klux Klan to terrorize their victims.")
(comment WingTipShoe "WingTips are mens lace-up dress shoes.  They have wings pattern stitched on the uppers.")
(comment PredictableEncryptionKeyFault "#$PredictableEncryptionKeyFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program (usually an encryption program) has this fault if the key it uses to encrypt data is not generated in a sufficiently random manner to prevent an attacker from guessing the key.")
(comment doGetAccessToData "(#$doGetAccessToData AGT DATA) means that AGT gets access to the bit of information DATA stored on a computational system.  Note that getting access to some data (say, a file) on a system does not necessarily involve opening the file on that system--it may involve simply being able to copy or write to the file.  See also #$doGetAccessToDataOfType.")
(comment SexualCulture "A specialization of #$HumanCulture, each instance of
  which is a culture whose core participants engage in certain 
  types of sexual practices, and which has developed around the 
  experiences of those core participants.  For example, there are 
  instances of #$SexualCulture associated with sado-masochism and 
  ''spouse-swapping''.")
(comment ProfessionalLicense-Document "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType. Each instance of #$ProfessionalLicense-Document is a document issued by some authority to a professional, certifying that the professional is licensed to practice his or her profession in a certain area (for instance, in a particular #$State-UnitedStates.")
(comment TwoStoryBuilding "#$TwoStoryBuilding is a specialization of #$Building.  Each instance is a building with exactly two stories.")
(comment AssociatedIndustrialTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections, a specialization of
#$CulturalTerrainFeatureType. Instances of
#$AssociatedIndustrialTerrainFeatureType are collections of objects,
structure or other large scale artifacts, that are found in industrial
sites.")
(comment WebServerCGICommandExecutionFault "A web server program has this fault if it contains CGI programs that allow an unauthorized user to execute arbitrary code.")
(comment Paramyxovirus1 "The virus that causes #$NewcastleDisease.")
(comment pointOnTraversal "(#$pointOnTraversal A TRAV) means that A is a point along a #$Traversal TRAV of some path or paths.  Let TRAV be (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X(1) PATH(1) ... X(n) PATH(n) X(n+1))), using a #$PathChain to describe the traversal.  Then (#$pointOnTraversal A TRAV) holds if and only if there is a k = 1, ..., n such that (#$pointOnPath-Generic A PATH(k)).  Note that each PATH(k) is an instance of #$Path-Generic. See also #$Traversal and #$TraversalFn.")
(comment BasementRoom "A room in the basement of a modern house, it is often the only room on the BasementLevel.")
(comment Competence "One of the most general attributes for describing the level of skill with which an agent performs some task.  Knowledge enterers will usually want to use some more specific attribute.")
(disjointWith Artifact-NonAgentive Agent-Generic)
(comment transportsVia "Agent A transports thing B via or along the #$Path-Spatial C.")
(comment CraftArtifact "The collection of objects that are the product of some
craft. Examples include #$Quilt, #$StencilArtifact, #$Woodwork, etc ...")
(comment Sandal "Light shoes worn in warm weather, with strapped upper, without a heel.")
(comment PlaneFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction for denoting the plane (abstract flat surface) which intersects the line segments ARG1-ARG2, ARG2-ARG3, and ARG1-ARG3.")
(disjointWith TemperatureControlledStorage CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment eMailReplyToAddress "A predicate for relating an email message to the character string that appears in its \"Reply To\" heading. (#$eMailReplyToAddress MSG TEXT) means that the #$EMailMessage, MSG, has TEXT, an instance of #$EMailAddress, as an entry in its \"Reply To\" field.")
(comment ThreeStoryBuilding "#$ThreeStoryBuilding is a specialization of #$Building. Each instance is a building with exactly three stories.")
(comment PreCutHome "The collection of all homes for which the building materials have been factory-cut to the size needed, and then transported to the home site and assembled.")
(disjointWith Cleaning InformationGathering)
(comment TCPChorusingFault "#$TCPChorusingFault is a fault of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  When \"pinged\" from another computer (ping or fping), hosts running software with this fault will issue one ACK for each stack loaded on the NIC. (ie: if five stacks are loaded, one ACK and four duplicate ACKs will be sent). The multiple ACKs create collisions on the subnet which may affect network functionality of other hosts on the subnet. With one offending host on the subnet, this TCP chorus may impact proper functioning of Samba hosts on the wire. With four TCP chorusers, an entire subnet may be rendered useless.")
(comment MedicalReferral-PIT "The collection of all mts which contain the propositional content of a medical referral.  Note that the referral communication medium (ibo) itself may be a note, a letter, a telephone conversation, etc., any sort of `text object', here taking `text' in its broadest sense.")
(comment DialingATelephoneNumber "The collection of events in which a phone number is completely or partially input to a phone system via an instance of #$Telephone. Events of this kind are more or less the definitive subevents in instances of #$MakingAPhoneCall, however normal instances of #$MakingAPhoneCall will also include additional subevents, e.g., picking up the phone receiver.  Note that we're including instances where the dialing is not completed, i.e., where the process is aborted for some reason.  Even inputting a single digit would count as an instance of #$DialingATelephoneNumber.  Such 'abortive' cases would not, however, figure as subevents in instances of #$MakingAPhoneCall.")
(comment AttackTypeByWeaponType "#$AttackTypeByWeaponType is a specialization of #$AttackType.  Each instances of  #$AttackTypeByWeaponType is a  collection of attacks, each instance of which is executed with a weapon of a certain type (e.g., one instance of #$AttackTypeByWeaponType is the collection of attacks executed with  biological weapons, another is the collection of attacks executed with computer programs, etc.).")
(comment growsByFactorToward-IntermedPredicate "Intermediate predicate: (growsByFactorToward-IntermedPredicate
THING UNIT DIR) expresses the fact that THING is the main agent in an instance
of #$BiologicalGrowthEvent in which THING grows by steps of UNIT at a time
in the direction DIR.")
(disjointWith NaturalTangibleStuff Weapon)
(comment PoloShirt "Polo shirts are knit shirts with collars and a few buttons.")
(comment VulnerableToStackProtectionBypass "#$VulnerableToStackProtectionBypass is a specialization of
 #$VulnerableToSecuritySoftwareBypass. A computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with a #$StackProtectionBypassFault.")
(comment PersonTypeByReligion "A collection of collections.  This collection exists to make it easier to refer to that dimension or facet of a person's behavior, attitudes, and beliefs (culture) which derives from, or is influenced by, the person's overarching `religious' beliefs, practices, and affiliations.  Note that `religion' and `religious' are understood here in a rather broad sense.  Many practicing Catholics do not believe in the Catholic Church's official teachings regarding Christian history or the significance of Jesus; many people who call themselves Jews do not observe any of Judaism's rituals.  But it is still useful to distinguish a `religious' mode of belief, activity, and group belonging, and to categorize people using these criteria.  (Jewishness is a notable special case, where the term may designate both an ethnic, kinship-based, primordial sense of identity and belonging, AND a set of religious beliefs and practices).")
(comment ClosingTag "The collection of all tags that are the result of an application of #$CloseTagFn.  Instances of this collection are not reified.")
(comment WindowsMachine "The collection of all #$Computers that run (#$runsOS) some version of #$MSWindows.")
(comment ExposingFilm "The collection of all situations in which the #$toLocation of some light is unexposed #$PhotographicFilm.  The result of this event is (a portion of) the film being partially or totally exposed.")
(disjointWith BeliefSystem ComputerFile-Abstract)
(comment TransportationLicense-Document "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$License-IBO.  Each instance of #$TransportationLicense-Document is a license issued by some governmental agency to a person that permits the person to operate some type(s) of vehicle. Notable specializations of #$TransportationLicense-Document include #$DriversLicense-Document and #$PilotsLicense-Document.")
(comment BlockedForFn "For any given movement type TYPE, (#$BlockedForFn TYPE) is the attribute of instances of #$Path-Customary that are blocked for movements of the type TYPE (from end to end).  For example, (#$holdsIn TIME (#$pathState PATH (#$BlockedForFn (#$TransportViaFn #$Truck)))) means that during TIME, PATH is blocked for transportation through PATH (from end to end) via trucks.  Note that when (#$pathState PATH (#$BlockedForFn (#$TransportViaFn #$Truck))) is true during TIME, it says nothing about whether, during TIME, PATH is blocked or open (see #$OpenForFn) for any other kind movement of transportation on PATH. Note also that (#$pathState PATH (#$BlockedForFn TYPE)) does not imply that no movement of the type TYPE is on PATH---it simply means that there is no movement of the type TYPE whose #$objectMoving can get one end from the other through the entire PATH.")
(comment PowerLineTower "towers constructed to hold up electric power lines")
(comment few-GenQuantRelnFromType "(#$few-GenQuantRelnFromType RELN COL2 COL1) means that for few of the

instances X of COL1 there is an instance INST of COL2 such that (RELN INST X)

holds.")
(comment VulnerableToFileUpload "A computer has this vulnerability if is running a server program with a #$UnauthorizedFileUploadFault.")
(comment browserInitiatesProgramOn "A predicate relating instances of #$WorldWideWebClientProgram with

instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW and instances of #$Computer.

(#$browserInitiatesProgramOn BROWSER PROGRAM COMPUTER) means that BROWSER

can start a process of PROGRAM on COMPUTER when it encounters data in PROGRAM format.  That is, PROGRAM is a plugin for BROWSER.")
(comment ActivityMonitoringFault "A program has this fault if it can be exploited by a malicious user to monitor activity on devices to which the program is linked.  Exploitation of this fault may allow a malicious user to sniff passwords, for example.")
(disjointWith InformationBearingThing DisplacementEvent)
(comment RainGear "The collection of clothes which are worn for protection from the elements.")
(comment doEnsureAbsenceFromPlaceOfWork "(#$doEnsureAbsenceFromPlaceOfWork AGENT ABSENTEE PLACE) means that AGENT ensures ABSENTEE is absent from PLACE.")
(comment SexualOrientationCulture "A specialization of #$SexualCulture, each instance of
  which is a culture whose core participants have a certain sexual 
  orientation, and which has developed around the experiences of 
  those core participants.  Examples include heterosexual culture, 
  lesbian culture, and bisexual culture.")
(comment genomeOfBLO-GenInfo "(#$genomeOfBLO-GenInfo BLO GENOME) means that the genome of the
#$BiologicalLivingObject BLO is GENOME, an instance of
#$Genome-GenInfo.")
(comment IndependentMoleculeFn "Where CHEMOBJTYPE is a spec of #$ChemicalObject that is

'agnostic' w.r.t. whether instances are #$Molecules or

#$MolecularComponents, (#$IndependentMoleculeFn CHEMOBJTYPE) returns

the collection of all instances of CHEMOBJTYPE that are #$Molecules.")
(comment LoopsInSystemFn "A function from path-systems to the set-or-collection of loops in those systems.  (#$LoopsInSystemFn SYSTEM) is the #$SetOrCollection (q.v.) of all loops (see #$loopInSystem) in the #$PathSystem (q.v.) SYSTEM.")
(comment DoorwayCovering "A specialization of #$PortalCovering.  Each instance of #$DoorwayCovering is a physical object used to cover some kind of portal, including but not limited to doorways in buildings.  This collection also includes doors of cars, buses, subways, elevators, garages, airplane hangars -- coverings over any doors that people (and perhaps vehicles) pass through.")
(comment UnaryCollectionDenotingFunctionForFn "#$UnaryCollectionDenotingFunctionForFn is an instance of #$EvaluatableFunction.  For any collection COL, if there is a single function FN such that (#$assertedSentence (#$resultGenl FN COL)), the expression (#$UnaryCollectionDenotingFunctionForFn COL) evaluates to FN. Otherwise, it is unevaluatable.")
(disjointWith DegenerationEvent TakingCareOfSomething)
(comment NewcastleDisease "A viral infection, hosted by birds. Symptoms include conjunctivitis with tearing and pain. May progress to a generalized illness with flu-like symptoms. Endemic in many countries of the world, though some European countries have been free of the disease for years.")
(disjointWith OfficialDocument SomethingToWear)
(comment no-GenQuantRelnTo "(#$no-GenQuantRelnTo RELN COL THING) is true iff there is no INST

such that INST is an element of COL and (RELN INST THING) holds.")
(comment Fractal "A collection of functions.  Each element of #$Fractal is a function which, when applied to data, can be displayed visually as an instance of #$FractalRepresentation.")
(disjointWith NaturalTangibleStuff ArtificialMaterial)
(comment JSPFileExecutionFault-Local "A program has this fault if a malicious user can exploit the program to run arbitrary java servlet pages (.jsp files) already existing on the machine running the program.")
(comment distanceAlongPath "(#$distanceAlongPath OBJ1 OBJ2 PATH DIST) means that the distance between OBJ1 and OBJ2, traveling along PATH, is DIST.  If PATH is not #$Straight, then DIST will be larger the length of the shortest straight line between OBJ1 and OBJ2.  See also #$distanceBetween which does not require reference to a pathway.")
(comment PoweredArtifact "The collection of artifacts (including devices) which are `powered', as opposed to inert.  Artifacts can be powered by kinetic energy, fuel, electricity, etc.")
(comment Handkerchief "A small piece of cloth used for personal purposes like blowing the nose or as an accessory on attire.")
(disjointWith BaseballFielding CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment correlatedStructures "This is a very general predicate that claims that the so-related items have structures that are somehow correlated, or reflect, one another.  (correlatedStructures THING1 THING2) means that THING1 and THING2 have somehow-correlated structures.  It makes no claim of causal influence; it does not say whether the structure of one influenced the structure of the other, or whether they both are affected by some common third thing, just that there is some correspondence.  (For a very general causal connection, see #$influencesStructure.) The correspondence can be exact or loose and indirect, for example that between written music and the dance motions of someone dancing to it, or between an ancient islamic art pattern and a recent, causally unrelated, wallpaper design.  Thus the truth of this predicate is often in the eye of the beholder, although there are many obvious cases for which almost everyone would agree to the correlation of the structures, e.g. (#$correlatedStructures #$EiffelTower #$TokyoTower).")
(comment eMailSubjectHeadingText "A predicate for relating an email message to the character string that appears in its subject heading. (#$eMailSubjectHeadingText MSG TEXT) means that the #$EMailMessage, MSG, has TEXT, instance of #$CharacterString, as its subject heading.")
(comment entryPathToSystem "This predicate is a simpler, binary version of 
#$entryPointOnPathToSystem to be used only when simpler
representations of 'entry paths' to path system are useful.
(#$entryPathToSystem ENTRY_PATH SYS) means that there is
a #$pointInSystem ENTRY_POINT such that
(#$entryPointOnPathToSystem ENTRY_POINT ENTRY_PATH SYS) holds.
See also #$entryPointToSystem.")
(comment suppliers "The predicate relates two generic agents. (#$suppliers SUPPLIER SUPPLIEE) means that SUPPLIER supplies some goods or services to SUPPLIEE, usually on an ongoing basis. When payment is returned for the supplying, consider using the inverse specialization #$customers.")
(comment AboveGroundLevelInAConstruction "#$AboveGroundLevelInAConstruction is a specialization of #$LevelOfAConstruction. Each instance of  #$AboveGroundLevelInAConstruction is at or above ground level.

See also #$BasementLevelInAConstruction and #$BalconyLevelInAConstruction.")
(comment PanelizedHome "The collection of all homes made with 'panels' - essentially factory-built walls including the frame, insulation, exterior, etc.")
(disjointWith LookingForSomething PhysicalDestructionEvent)
(comment TCP-IPParameterModificationFault "A program has this fault if it allows for a
 user to change the kernel TCP/IP parameters for its operating system, allowing a possible denial of service.")
(comment itemWorn "This is used to indicate that a particular article of clothing (or other wearable item) is worn in a particular situation.  (#$itemWorn WEARING ITEM) means that ITEM is worn during WEARING. To specify the wearer of an item in a situation, use the predicate #$wearer.")
(comment TheDisjunctiveCoordinationSet "A piece of NL-CycL scaffolding vocab, used to parse and coordinate 

reformulations of noun phrases that are disjunctive, e.g., 'Either Bob or Fred' in 'Either Bob or Fred is the culprit.'")
(comment AlterableEncryptionKeyFault "A program has this fault if it is possible for a user to tamper with cryptographic calculations on that machine, copying or modifying the encryption keys of other users.")
(comment programListeningOnComputerHasFault "(#$programListeningOnComputerHasFault PROG COMP FAULT) means that the copy of PROG which is currently listening on some port on COMP (#$programOnPort, q.v.) COMP manifests FAULT.")
(comment relatedToVia-Least "Like #$relatedToVia (#$relatedToVia-Least OBJ1 OBJ2 SET NUM) means that OBJ1 and OBJ2 are related via some sequence of NUM steps via the binary relations in the set SET. More precisely, (#$relatedToVia-Least OBJ1 OBJ2 SET NUM)

means that there is a sequence of objects of the length equal to NUM that OBJ1 is the first

element of the sequence, OBJ2 is the last element of the sequence, and each element of the sequence is

related to its successor (if any) by some predicate in SET, or by the inverse of some predicate in SET.  Unlike #$relatedToVia, #$relatedToVia-Least returns in the fourth argument the least number of steps by which OBJ1 and OBJ2 can be related using the relations in SET.")
(comment BoundedDirectedPathSystem "The collection of all those #$DirectedPathSystems each of which constains a unique node that is the source node in the system (see #$sourceNodeInSystem), and a unique node that is the sink node in the system (see #$sinkNodeInSystem).")
(comment DressSock "Dress socks are worn with DressShoes.")
(comment VulnerableToAutomaticHTMLAttachmentDownload "#$VulnerableToAutomaticHTMLAttachmentDownload is an attribute of some instances of #$Computer.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is running software with an #$AutomaticHTMLAttachmentDownloadFault.")
(comment literacyRate "The percentage of people of a certain group who are literate.")
(comment AutomaticAttachmentExecutionFault "A program has this fault if it will automatically execute an attachment to an email message if provided with the proper input in the message.")
(comment WindowsAccount "The collection of all #$ComputerAccounts on versions of #$MSWindows.  Microsoft did not start to incorporate computer accounts into their Windows technology properly until the advent of #$MSWindowsNT.  As a result, all programs (and users logged in) on a machine running #$MSWindows (95 or 98) run with the same privileges.")
(comment sendDataOfTypeToProgramOnSystem "(#$sendDataOfTypeToProgramOnSystem AGENT INFO PROG SYSTEM) means that AGENT sends INFO to the program PROG running on SYSTEM.")
(comment FuelCell "A fuel cell consists of two electrodes sandwiched around an electrolyte. Oxygen passes over one electrode and hydrogen over the other, generating

electricity, water and heat. Hydrogen fuel is fed into the \"anode\" of the fuel cell. Oxygen (or air) enters the fuel cell through the cathode. Encouraged by a catalyst, the hydrogen

atom splits into a proton and an electron, which take different paths to the cathode. The proton passes through the electrolyte. The electrons create a

separate current that can be utilized before they return to the cathode, to be reunited with the hydrogen and oxygen in a molecule of water.")
(comment SixtyNine "The collection of events involving simultaneous events of oral stimulation of male and female sexual organs by the two performers of the act.  See #$Fellatio and #$Cunnilingus.")
(disjointWith Microtheory ComputerFile-Abstract)
(comment DriversLicense-Document "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$TransportationLicense-Document.  Each instance of #$DriversLicense-Document is a license that permits its holder to operate some type(s) of road vehicle.")
(comment Pylon "a (usually steel) tower used for support")
(comment programInterpretsLanguage "#$programInterpretsLanguage is a binary predicate that relates a computer program to a computer language.  (#$programInterpretsLanguage PROG LANG) means that PROG, an instance of #$Interpreter-Computers, interprets programs written in LANG, an instance of #$ComputerLanguage.")
(comment interferesWithAction "'(#$interferesWithAction INTERFERE ACTION)' means that the #$Interfering INTERFERE interferes with the event ACTION.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureScriptSourceCode "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program on it with a #$InsecureScriptSourceCodeFault.")
(comment TheInstallationScriptFn "(#$TheInstallationScriptFn PROGRAM) denotes an archetypical code script that, when executed on a machine, installs PROGRAM on that machine.")
(comment FaultyThing "#$FaultyThing, an instance of #$ObjectType, is the collection of all things that are flawed in some way.")
(comment PhysicalCreationOrDestructionEvent "A specialization of #$CreationOrDestructionEvent.  During each instance of #$PhysicalCreationOrDestructionEvent, one or more physical objects (instances of #$PartiallyTangible) come into or go out of existence.  If the object created or destroyed in an event is not physical (e.g., if it is an agreement or a conceptual work), then the event should be an instance of the more general collection #$CreationOrDestructionEvent.")
(comment ExcavationSite "The collection of excavation sites. Instances of #$ExcavationSite
are geographical areas where some agent, typically human beings, conduct
excavation. In case of underground excavation, the corresponding excavation
site typically contains the main access to the excavation
[#$Excavation-Hole], that would be where a ground infrastructure, if any,
is located. Main types of excavation operations are that conducted for
industrial purpose such as for instance diamond mining and oil
drilling. Other types of excavations are scientific ones, geological or
archeological for instance, the place where these operations are conducted
are instances of specializations of #$ExcavationSite.")
(comment explosivePowerEquivalent-Type "(#$explosivePowerEquivalent-Type DEV-TYPE1 DEV-TYPE2 NUM) means that a single instance of DEV-TYPE1 has the same explosive force as NUM amount of DEV-TYPE2.  This predicate is useful for rating the explosive power of #$Bombs, etc., in terms of some common measure, such as pounds of TNT or numbers of #$Bomblet-M77s.")
(disjointWith BiologicalIntakeEvent DisplacementEvent)
(comment TortureDevice "A specialization of #$PhysicalDevice and #$DangerousThing.  Each instance of #$TortureDevice is a device designe to be used to torture people.  Significant specializations include #$IronMaiden and #$Cross-TortureDevice.")
(comment CasualShoe "CausalShoes are shoes worn with the least formal outfits.")
(comment doPhysicallyGetUserAccessToComputer "(#$doPhysicallyGetUserAccessToComputer AGENT COMP) means that AGENT physically logs in to COMP.")
(comment intentInPlan "(#$intentInPlan AGENT PLAN GOAL) means that one of the purposes which AGENT intends for the #$PlanningDomainMicrotheory PLAN to accomplish is GOAL.  This predicate is the plan-analog of #$purposeInEvent.")
(comment windowHasCovering "A predicate that relates a window to a physical covering used to seal it.  (#$windowHasCovering WINDOWCOVER) means that the instance WINDOW of #$WindowPortal has as a physical covering the instance COVER of #$PortalCovering.")
(comment PowerGenerationTerrainFeatureType "A collection of collections, a specialization of
#$CulturalTerrainFeatureType. Instances of
#$PowerGenerationTerrainFeatureType are collections of objects that
participate in the generation of energy. One way of partitioning further
this collection type could be to consider the nature of the energy
produced.")
(comment GeographicalPlace-0D "The subcollection of #$GeographicalThing-Intangible-FixedLocation whose instances are intangible points on the Earth's surface that have relatively fixed geographic locations.

Each geographical point is located on a unique #$LatitudeLine and on a unique #$LongitudeLine, and is itself the point of intersection of those two lines.")
(comment CABFileExecutionFault "A program has this fault if, when Active Scripting is enabled, a malicious user can create an executable file, compress it into a cab file, and rename it to have a file extension of any type automatically displayed by the client (e.g., .JPG, .GIF). He can then send this file as an attachment to the user of the faulty program as well as some active scripting (eg., JavaScript, VBscript). The active scripting can then execute the attachment on the target machine, using the Active Setup ActiveX control.")
(disjointWith Teaching ChangeInUserRights)
(comment CPOF-SpotReportMtFn "(#$CPOF-SpotReportMtFn NUM) is a microtheory which

corresponds to -- i.e., contains a #$CycL translation of --

a Block Party VI spot report.")
(comment MonkeypoxVirus "The virus that causes #$MonkeyPox (Orthopoxvirus Disease).")
(comment BankSpace "The space where a bank does business.")
(disjointWith HandTool SomethingToWear)
(comment challengesTo "'(#$challengesTo CHALLENGE ACT-TYPE ROLE)' means that the
#$Challenging CHALLENGE challenges the #$challengee to play ROLE in an
instance of the act-type ACT-TYPE.")
(comment keAssertedTermSentences "(#$keAssertedTermSentences TERM SENTENCE) means that a #$CycLAssertion of the form SENTENCE exists such that TERM is referred to as a term within that sentence, and that SENTENCE contains no #$keIrrelevantTerms.")
(comment nodeOfTypeInLAN "(#$nodeOfTypeInLAN COMPUTER COMPUTERTYPE LAN) means that COMPUTER is one of the computers that constitutes the #$LocalAreaNetwork LAN, and COMPUTER plays the role of COMPUTERTYPE in LAN. For instance, (#$nodeOfTypeInLAN Router001 #$Router-Network #$CycorpLAN) means that Router001 is a network router on the Cycorp LAN. See also the more specialized #$nodeOfTypeInAccountSystem.")
(comment nounSemTrans "(#$nounSemTrans NOUN INT FRAME TRANS) means that the translation of word sense number INT of noun NOUN in frame FRAME is TRANS.")
(comment eMailCompositionProgram "A predicate used to relate an instance of #$EMailClientProgram to an instance of #$EMailSending.  (#$eMailCompositionProgram SENDING MAIL_CLIENT) means that the program MAIL_CLIENT was used to compose the email sent in SENDING.")
(comment Angel "In popular (not necessarily orthodox) Jewish, Christian, and Islamic tradition, angels are the messengers who deliver information from God to humans.  The metaphor to think of is that of an oriental king sending messengers out to deliver news to his subjects.  The original Greek word means `messenger'.  They are supposed to have sort of semi-divine status.")
(comment RouterCrashingFault "An attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has an #$RouterCrashingFault when it allows a (authorized or unauthorized) user to send commands
 to copies of the program that cause a router to halt (for instance by attempting to make a looped connection from the router's IP address back to the same address) creating a denial of service.")
(comment Lingerie "Women's intimate apparel.")
(disjointWith RemovingSomething MakingAnAgreement)
(comment queryNegativeRolesInScript "A #$QueryDedicatedPredicate used for finding all of the scenes in a script with respect to which a specified actor type is not known to play a role.")
(comment SingleResidenceUnit "#$SingleResidenceUnit is a specialization of #$ModernHumanResidence.  Each instance of #$SingleResidenceUnit is either a modern-style detached house, an apartment, or another instance of #$ModernHumanResidence designed to accomodate either a single person or a single family (i.e., instance of #$FamilyCohabitationUnit (q.v.)).  Usually, each instance of #$SingleResidenceUnit has a unique mailing address.")
(comment decisionToDo "(#$decisionToDo DECIDING ACT-TYPE) means that the #$DecidingToDoSomething DECIDING is a decision to do an action of type ACT-TYPE.")
(comment InternetPacketTypeByTransportLayerProtocol "A collection of collections.  Every instance of #$InternetPacketTypeByTransportLayerProtocol is a collection of #$Packet-Internet grouped by the #$TransportLayerProtocol (i.e., UDP or TCP) to which they conform.")
(comment TownHouse "A single unit in a row of houses.")
(disjointWith CoveringSomething OpeningSomething)
(comment KerberosIDSpoofingFault "A program has this fault if it allows a user to imitate another user's Kerberos credentials.")
(comment InsecureMailStorageFault-System "A program has an #$InsecureMailStorageFault-System if specially-formed input to that program will yield access to the mail of the users of the email #$AccountSystem to an unauthorized user. See also #$InsecureMailStorageFault-Local, which yields access only to email files stored on the machine the user is accessing, and #$ReadableMailFault (which delivers mail of all users on the #$AccountSystem, but only to an already-authenticated user).")
(disjointWith NaturalTangibleStuff MechanicalDevice)
(comment Sock "Close-fitting covering for foot and ankle, and often the lower leg. It differs from stocking by what it covers: a sock doesn't cover the upper leg, whereas a stocking does.")
(comment ArbitraryInstance-NLAttr "The attribute value carried by utterances of the form \"an arbitrary XXX\".")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedWebServerAccess "A computer has this vulnerability if it allows an unauthorized user to access an httpd account.  When remotely exploitable, it is typically a consequence of an #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-WebServer.")
(comment Tribe "Social organization of people who are multiply affiliated by (some assortment of) kinship, beliefs, language, region, and activities.")
(comment Atheist "The collection of instances of #$Person who are athiests.")
(comment allows-AgentProp "This predicate relates agents to propositions (as represented by sentences that express them) that they allow to be, or let be, true. (#$allows-AgentProp AGENT SENT) means that AGENT  -- either by performing some action or (more saliently) refraining from performing an action that s/he might have done -- allows the proposition PROP expressed by SENT to become or remain true.  This relation is weaker than being a contributing cause (see e.g. #$enables-ThingProp), but the above formula entails that either (i) AGENT refrains from performing some type of action that s/he is capable of performing and which, were s/he to do it, would (ceteris paribus) prevent (or significantly reduce the likelihood of) PROP's being true or (ii) AGENT performs an action such that, were s/he not to do it (ceteris paribus) the likelihood of PROP's being true would at least be less than it actually was.  A further default assumption is that AGENT knows that her acting or failing to act, as the case may be, has the above consequences for PROP.  For example, if I do nothing to prevent a book's falling off the edge of my desk when I could have caught it, I allow it to be the case that the book falls off the desk.  If a parent answers a child's request for candy by saying \"Yes, you may\", s/he allows it to be true that the child has candy.")
(comment affordToRentType "(#$affordToRentType AGENT OBJECTTYPE) means that AGENT can financially afford to rent an instance of OBJECTTYPE.")
(comment ruleForOpenCyc "(#$ruleForOpenCyc RULE) means that rule is to be included in the OpenCyc release.")
(comment PilotsLicense-Document "An instances of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$TransportationLicense-Document.  Each instance of #$PilotsLicense-Document is a license that permits its holder to operate some type(s) of aircraft.")
(comment OpenForFn "For any given movement type TYPE, (#$OpenForFn TYPE) is the attribute of instances of #$Path-Customary that are open for movements of the type TYPE (from end to end).  For example, (#$holdsIn TIME (#$pathState PATH (#$OpenForFn (#$TransportViaFn #$Truck)))) means that during TIME, PATH is open for transportation through PATH (from end to end) via trucks.  Note that when (#$pathState PATH (#$OpenForFn (#$TransportViaFn #$Truck))) is true during TIME, it says nothing about whether, during TIME, PATH is blocked (see #$BlockedForFn) or open for any other kind movement of transportation on PATH.  Note also that (#$pathState PATH (#$OpenForFn TYPE)) is not implied by any movement of the type TYPE on PATH---it simply means that there are 'potential' movements of the type TYPE whose #$objectMoving can get one end from the other through the entire PATH.")
(comment RootAccountFn "(#$RootAccountFn COMPUTER) denotes the instance of #$RootAccount on the local account system on the instance of #$Computer COMPUTER, which runs a Unix operating system.")
(comment VulnerableToCertificateSpoofing "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program
that has a #$CertificateSourceValidationFault.")
(comment calendarSystemUsed "Different countries use different #$CalendarSystems.")
(comment PluggingInAPowerCord "The collection of events in which a #$PowerCord gets connected to an electrical outlet.")
(comment UkrainianPerson "This is the collection of people who are #$citizens of #$Ukraine, or participate in its #$NationalCulture.")
(disjointWith PhysicalCreationOrDestructionEvent StrictlyMentalEvent)
(comment uninstallProgramType "(#$uninstallProgramType AGENT PROGRAMTYPE COMPUTER) means that AGENT uninstalls, with or without permission, an instance of PROGRAMTYPE from COMPUTER.")
(comment SkiJacket "The collection of jackets designed for extended cold-weather activities, esp. skiing.")
(comment doEnsureInattentivenessToObjectForBriefPeriod "(#$doEnsureInattentivenessToObjectForBriefPeriod

AGENT DISTRACTED OBJECT) means that AGENT ensures that DISTRACTED does

not pay attention to OBJECT for a brief period of time.")
(comment keSalientPredicateUtility "(#$keSalientPredicateUtility PRED NUMBER) says that the #$keSalientPredicate PRED has a numeric utility of NUMBER, where larger values indicate higher utility.  If unprovided, the presumed value for this is assumed to be 0 by definition.")
(comment planningAgent "(#$planningAgent PLAN AGENT) means that AGENT
is directly responsible for devising and using the planning
context PLAN, and that AGENT has a direct stake and interest in a
successful execution of PLAN.")
(disjointWith ShelterConstruction CornerOnObject)
(comment DrugTherapy "A specialization of #$MedicalTreatmentEvent: a collection of medical care events in which drugs accomplish a medical purpose.  An instance of #$DrugTherapy is the result of an instance of #$AdministeringADrug (q.v.).  An instance of #$DrugTherapy is the event of the patient's body undergoing the physiological effects of the drug it was given.  
Note: #$DrugTherapy events do not include the administration of the drug; rather, they are the results of such administrations.  Cf. #$AdministeringADrug. For therapies with particular drugs, see #$DrugTherapyUseFn.")
(comment transportsFromToVia "Agent A transports thing B from location C to location D via or along the #$Path-Spatial E.")
(comment StackProtectionBypassFault "An execution stack protection program (e.g., #$StackGuard-TheProgram) has this fault if is possible to exploit a program with a #$BufferOverflowFault-CommandExecution in spite the protection program being run.")
(comment VulnerableToMaliciousCodeInstallationFn "(#$hasVulnerability COMP (#$VulnerableToMaliciousCodeInstallationFn MALWARE)) means that software on COMP  makes it possible for MALWARE to be installed on COMP.")
(disjointWith TakingCareOfSomething MakingAnEstimate)
(comment collectionIntersection2 "(#$collectionIntersection2 COL GENL1 GENL2) means that COL is the intersection of GENL1 and GENL2.  Every instance of COL is an instance of GENL1 and GENL2.  Each #$Collection that is a spec of both GENL1 and GENL2 is also a spec of COL.")
(comment Monkeypox "A disease found primarily in macaques. When humans are infected its clinical symptoms closely resemble those of small pox, including extreme fatigue, fever, muscular and back pain, with evolution of maculas progressing successively to papules, vesicles, pustules, and scabs. Also known as Orthopoxvirus Disease.")
(comment Skyscraper "Modern, urban buildings with many, many stories.  Often contain many offices.")
(disjointWith Water SomethingToWear)
(comment VulnerableToDigitalSignatureBypass "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$DigitalSignatureBypassFault on it.")
(comment nodeInLAN "A specialization of #$nodeInSystem; a binary predicate that relates instances of #$Computer to instances of #$LocalAreaNetwork.  (#$nodeInLAN NODE LAN) means that NODE is a computer on the local area network, LAN.")
(comment MicrosoftSoftwarePatchFn "A function that takes as an argument a string that is determined to refer to a #$MicrosoftSoftwarePatch, and denotes the patch to which the string refers.  For instance, (#$MicrosoftSoftwarePatchFn

\"Q252795\") denotes the #$MicrosoftSoftwarePatch referred to by the

string \"Q252795\".")
(comment StartupFileOverwriteFault "A program has this fault if it is possible for unauthorized users to overwrite/modify its startup file. This would allow attackers to modify the file and add malicious commands which could lead to a local root compromise.")
(comment God "The class of supernatural beings generally supposed to be (a) all-powerful (or more powerful than other classes of divinities within the same religious/folkloric tradition), and (b) immortal (or nearly so, for all practical purposes).")
(comment webServerInitiatesProgramOn "A predicate relating instances of #$WorldWideWebServerProgram with instances of #$LocalProgram and instances of #$Computer. (#$webServerInitiatesProgramOn WEBSERVER PROGRAM COMPUTER) means that WEBSERVER can invoke a process of PROGRAM in response to remote user requests.  In most cases, the second arg of this predicate will be filled by an instance of #$CGIScript.")
(comment Bikini "Two-part swimsuit worn by adult females.")
(disjointWith CircularRegion SemicircularRegion)
(disjointWith AccessingAnIBT MakingSomething)
(comment influencesStructure "This is a very general causal predicate that indicates that one thing influences the structure or pattern of another, directly or indirectly.  (influencesStructure THING1 THING2) means that the pattern or structure of THING1 somehow causally affects, or has affected, the pattern or structure of THING2, and that had THING1 been arranged differently in certain ways, THING2 would therefore have been arranged differently.  An example is where THING2 is a copy of THING1, or where THING1 is a computer program that controls the form of THING2.  Contrast this with a mere correlation between the two structures (see #$correlatedStructures).  Unlike the more specific #$sourcePatternFor predicate, #$influencesStructure does not require that any particular pattern in the source be preserved in the affected thing.")
(comment Doorway "#$Doorway is a specialization of #$Portal, #$CavityWithWalls, and #$Artifact-NonAgentive.  Each instance of #$Doorway is a portal in some instance of #$HumanOccupationConstruct (q.v.), suitable for people (and perhaps vehicles) to enter and exit.  Each instance of #$Doorway includes the frame, not merely the empty space within the doorway.  Instances of #$Doorway include doorways to houses, office buildings, elevators, automobiles, airplanes, and garages.")
(comment SafetyInspection "Events where an agent or agents evaluate the likelihood of harm to persons in the execution of some anticipated event or set of events.")
(comment ManufacturedHome "The collection of all homes that are largely or entirely built in a factory rather than at the home site. #$ManufacturedHomes include both #$ModularHomes and #$MobileHomes.")
(disjointWith Washing OpeningSomething)
(comment versionSeriesOfSoftware "A predicate relating an instance of #$UnversionedSoftwareObject with an instance of #$SoftwareVersionSeries.  (#$versionSeriesOfSoftware SOFTWARE SERIES) means that SERIES is a series of versions of SOFTWARE. In most cases SERIES will be a NART expressed using #$VersionsInclusiveFn.")
(comment softwareInstalledOnComputerHasFault "(#$softwareInstalledOnComputerHasFault SOFTWARE COMP FAULT) means that the copy of SOFTWARE installed on COMP manifests FAULT.")
(comment eliminateEvidenceOfIntrusionOnSystem "(#$eliminateEvidenceOfIntrusionOnSystem AGENT SYSTEM) means that AGENT removes all evidence of infiltrating SYSTEM.")
(disjointWith PhysicalDevice DrugSubstance)
(comment AcademicGown "The gown worn by participants in formal academic ceremonies (e.g, graduation).")
(comment LibraryVersionSeries "#$LibraryVersionSeries is the collection of all #$ConceptualWorkSeries consisting of versions of #$LibraryFiles.  An example instance of #$LibraryVersionSeries is (#$VersionsInclusiveFn #$Libc-TheLibrary \"4.0\" \"4.5\"), which is the series of all versions of #$Libc-TheLibrary between 4.0 and 4.5.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedPrinterAccountAccess "A computer has this vulnerability if it allows an unauthorized user to access a printer account. See also #$VulnerableToElevatedPrivilegePrinting, #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedDeviceAttachment.")
(comment HydrographicPathSystem "A subcollection of #$SpatialPathSystem. Instances of #$HydrographicPathSystem are system of streams. A path in such system is typically a portion of a stream (of a river for instance) between two points of confluence. This is a very general collection that admits system of natural streams only as well as systems including artificial paths (see #$PathArtifact).")
(comment ServerConnectionRequestInformationFn "(#$ServerConnectionRequestInformationFn PORT) denotes information

about connection requests to the network port PORT.")
(comment CensusGroupOfOtherDesignatedRaces "The catch-all collection for persons identified as having origins within ethnic groups not explicitly listed by the U.S. Census Bureau.")
(disjointWith CellPart-Structural Organelle)
(comment BoatingLicense-Document "An instance of #$OfficialDocumentType, and a specialization of #$TransportationLicense-Document.  Each instance of #$BoatingLicense-Document is a license that permits its holder to operate some type(s) of watercraft.")
(comment VulnerableToRouterBypass "A computer has this vulnerability if it is running a router program that has a #$RouterBypassFault.")
(comment CalendarSystem "A linguistic system for identifying days by means of unique dates.")
(comment FasteningSafetyBelt "The putting on of a safety belt in order to secure a passenger in a motor vehicle or similar device.")
(comment EstonianPerson "The collection of all #$EstonianPersons. This is a broad collection and includes #$citizens and #$EthnicGroupOfEstonians.")
(comment IRCClientProgram "#$IRCClientProgram is the collection of programs that can be used to engage in chatting sessions under the IRC protocol.")
(disjointWith EmittingAWave DisplacementEvent)
(disjointWith DrugSubstance BuildingMaterial)
(comment CapToeShoe "Cap-toed shoes are lace-up mens dress shoes.  Cap-toed shoes have a cap pattern stitched on the uppers.")
(comment doGetLoginInformationForAccount "(#$doGetLoginInformationForAccount AGENT ACCOUNT) means that AGENT acquires the password for ACCOUNT.")
(comment FleetOfMilitaryCraft "The collection of groups of naval ships and (sometimes) submarines that are in a relatively defined area and are under a single command.  See also #$NavalFleet-Organization.")
(comment keCommonQueryForTerm "This predicate is intended to express the relationship that
holds between a #$CycLReifiableDenotationalTerm and a query that may
be commonly or sensibly asked about it.  It is considered a
#$KEFacilitationPredicate, insofar as it can be used to prompt users
with queries that may be usefully asked.")
(comment Demanding-CommunicationAct "A collection of communication acts.  In each instance of #$Demanding-CommunicationAct, an agent presents to some other agent(s) an expectation that the latter do something that the first agent describes in the demand.  Making a demand differs from giving an order in that an ordering agent has some authoritative claim on the agent to whom the order is issued.  While a demanding agent may have reasons to expect that the demand will be fulfilled, there is no compelling authoritative claim on the agent to whom the demand is made.  See also #$Ordering-CommunicationAct.")
(comment SpaceInAFixedHOC "#$SpaceInAFixedHOC is a specialization of #$SpaceInAHOC and #$Place.  Each instance of #$SpaceInAFixedHOC is a space within some instance of a fixed (as opposed to moveable) #$HumanOccupationConstruct (q.v.).  Positive examples include rooms within #$Buildings, while negative examples include spaces within recreational vehicles.")
(disjointWith TransportationEvent DrugTherapy)
(comment vulnerableTo-Underspecified "(#$vulnerableTo-Underspecified THING HARMING-THING) means that THING is vulnerable to a threat involving HARMING-THING. This is a very general assertion in that HARMING-THING can either specify the event type of the attack or the object type of the attacking object, as well as a specific individual event or object. See #$vulnerableToAgent, #$vulnerableToAgentType and #$vulnerableToSituationType for specializations making the harm type more explicit.")
(disjointWith TendingAPlant ConstructionProject)
(comment UniversityDevelopmentDepartment "A specialization of #$UniversityDepartment. Each instance of this collection is a group of employees responsible for the development of a particular university.")
(comment PseudomonasPseudomallei "The bacterium that causes Melioidosis (#$Melioidosis-Infection).")
(comment hasHabitat "The predicate #$hasHabitat is used to relate an organism to the region where it lives.  (#$hasHabitat ORG REGION) means that the organism ORG lives in the #$EcologicalRegion REGION. Typically, REGION will belong to one of the subsets of #$EcologicalRegion which represent specific biomes (e.g., #$Desert, #$CoralReef).  See also #$residesInRegion.")
(comment SomethingToWear "#$SomethingToWear is a specialization of #$DurableGoods, #$Device-SingleUser, #$PersonalProduct, and #$PortableObject.  Each instance of #$SomethingToWear is an object that a mannequin or an animal (usually a person) wears on its body, i.e., in a #$WearingSomething event.  It is worth remarking that, in such an event, the wearer doesn't have to exert any intentional effort to continue wearing the object.  For example, shirts remain on people's torsos, hats stay on heads, rings on fingers; once in place, dog collars stay on dogs, saddles stay on horses.  By contrast, a hula hoop is NOT an example of #$SomethingToWear.  A borderline case is a #$Purse, which at first blush seems to be something to wear, yet requires carrying by the performer, hence is not a member of this collection.  Similarly, a briefcase is not an instance of #$SomethingToWear.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfReadableMail "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$ReadableMailFault on it.")
(comment DatabaseSoftwareFaultDataMicrotheory "The collection of all microtheories which store #$synonymousExternalConcept assertions pertaining to the computer vulnerability information of some computer vulnerability database (#$ComputerVulnerabilityDatabase, q.v.).")
(comment WeakPasswordResetFault "#$WeakPasswordResetFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this vulnerability if the method that the program uses to reset a lost/forgotten password is easily compromised or guessable.")
(comment EvilBeing "The collection of all #$SupernaturalBeings who are evil. Includes evil ghosts, wicked witches, evil sorcerers, and #$Satan.")
(comment TrojanAccommodatingFault "A program has this fault if it would be a relatively simple matter for a malicious user to manipulate the program in such a way that it executed a different program of the attacker's choice.")
(comment ThreeWayJunctionOfPaths "A collection of junctions of paths. A member of this collection exists where three #$SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPaths meet together, or where one #$SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPath joins the two ends of a #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPath that loops back to that junction.  If it is a three way junction in a specified #$PathSystem, use #$threeWayJunctionInSystem.  (Determining what constitutes a #$ThreeWayJunctionOfPaths depends on the #$PathTypes of the joined paths; if it is #$River then only a junction of rivers qualifies, not the place where a road joins a river.)")
(comment HikingBoot "Robust boots worn during hiking.")
(comment artifactsCreated "This predicate describes the relation between an #$Artifact-Generic (tangible or intangible) and the #$CreatingAnArtifact event which produced it.  (#$artifactsCreated EVENT THING) means that THING is intentionally created during EVENT.")
(comment PersonalAccount "An instance of #$AccountType, and a specialization of #$Account.  Each instance of #$PersonalAccount is an account in which the agent or agents holding the account (see the predicate #$accountHolder) are persons, rather than organizations.")
(comment PeptideSequence "The collection of all lists of instances of #$AminoAcidTypeByChemicalSpecies.")
(comment winner-First "(#$winner-First COMPETITN AGNT) means that AGNT is a first place winner of COMPETITN.  The #$arg2Format of this predicate is #$SetTheFormat to allow for the uncommon (but far from `very rare') case where there is a tie for first place and two or more agents are awarded that prize.  See also #$awardWinners, #$rankInCompetition, and #$competingAgents.")
(comment RoofOfAConstruction "#$RoofOfAConstruction is a specialization of #$TopSurface and #$PartOfBuilding.  Each instance of #$RoofOfAConstruction is a roof of a structure which is an instance of #$HumanShelterConstruction.  Like instances of #$Wall-Vertical, instances of #$RoofOfAConstruction may be considered as having one or two sides; the 'inner' side of a roof may or may not qualify as a #$CeilingOfARoom.  It is understood that one and only one side of a #$RoofOfAConstruction is 'exposed to the elements.'")
(comment programInstalledWithPackage "(#$programInstalledWithPackage PROG PACKAGE) means that PROG is one of the programs that is installed when PACKAGE is installed.")
(comment GroupingThingsMentally "A collection of purposeful acts of thinking.  Each instance of #$GroupingThingsMentally is a mental act in which the doer consciously considers two or more things together as members of the same group.  This neither entails nor precludes that the things in question actually are co-members of any #$Group, either before, during, or after the mental grouping. For example, a football coach who imagines his ideal \"dream team\" engages in this kind of activity.  See also #$GroupingObjects.")
(comment TransportLayerProtocolFn "(#$TransportLayerProtocolFn PROTOCOL) denotes the collection of all #$Packet-Internets in which the IP header specifies PROTOCOL as the packet's #$TransportLayerProtocol.")
(comment RadiatorTester "Stuff added to radiators that Cleans car.")
(disjointWith CoveringSomething UncoveringSomething)
(comment HelpFileCommandExecutionFault "A program has a #$HelpFileCommandExecutionFault if it allows an attacker who can construct a malicious help file and place it in a location accessible by the victim to cause this help file to be loaded and executed without interaction from the victim.")
(comment KineticEnergyPoweredDevice "A specialization of #$PoweredDevice.  Each instance of 
#$KineticEnergyPoweredDevice does not have any \"on-board\" 
energy source incorporated into it, at least not one supplying 
the bulk of the power requirements of the device.  Instead, 
its operating power is supplied by the kinetic energy from 
something else in motion -- such as animal muscle power 
(including human labor), wind energy, or hydraulic power.  
Specializations of this collection include #$Pulley and 
#$Piano-Acoustic.  (Cf. #$SelfPoweredDevice, which includes, 
e.g., electric organs.)")
(comment Caftan "The collection of loose fitting garments worn by either men or women--worn by men in the #$LevantRegion, or by women in imitation of this style.")
(comment IPPacketForwardingFault "A #$FirewallProgram has this fault if it will forward specially-fragmented IP packets to hosts on the internal network on supposedely \"blocked\" ports.  An attacker will need to know the IP address of the target machine to exploit this fault.  If this fault is propoerly exploited, the attacker may be able to carry out a denial of service attack on the target host.")
(comment TribeMember "Any member of a tribe.  By default, a person belongs only to one tribe (at a time).")
(comment fuelTankCapacity "(#$fuelTankCapacity VEHICLE VOL) says that VOL is the capacity of
the #$VehicleFuelTank of VEHICLE.")
(disjointWith RoomInAConstruction PathArtifactSystem)
(comment WindowsAccountFn "(#$WindowsAccountFn COMPUTER) denotes the #$WindowsAccount (there is only, I believe, one) on COMPUTER (which must be a #$WindowsMachine).")
(comment PasswordAuthenticationInformation "The collection of abstract information about attempts to log on to computers.")
(comment CellPart-Structural "The collection of all instances of #$CellPart that are

specifically concerned with helping a particular #$Cell maintain it's

physical integrity and structure.  Instances of #$CellPart-Structural

are different from the cellular 'micro-organs' known as

#$Organelles.")
(comment CentralAmericanPyramid "The stepped pyramids found in #$Mexico and other parts of Central America")
(comment FileSystemMountingProgram "All files accessible in a filesystem are arranged a large tree. These files can be spread out over several devices (hard disks, CD_ROM drives, floppy disks, etc.  File system mounting programs can attach and/or remove the file systems found on one device to/from the big file tree.")
(comment warner "'(#$warner WARNING WARNER)' means that WARNER issues the

warning in WARNING.  WARNER may be an automatic warning device, such as

a smoke alarm, or an animal emitting a warning signal.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecurePasswordFile "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program on it with a #$InsecurePasswordFileFault.")
(comment UnfasteningSafetyBelt "See english on #$FasteningSafetyBelt")
(comment CarEnthusiast "The collection of people who have a serious interest in cars.  Such people might collect cars of certain types or simply be fascinated with cars of certain types, going to car shows with some regularity, or subscribing to car \"fan\" magazines.  It is important to keep in mind that a person who is an enthusiast of car type A need not be an enthusiast of car type B, where (genls B A), since one can be a fan of, e.g., Ford Mustangs, yet disdain Ford Mustangs from 1997.")
(comment TCPPortDenialOfServiceFault "A program/OS has this fault if it can be forced into a state in which certain TCP ports are rendered useless.")
(disjointWith EnergyStuff BuildingMaterial)
(comment ShoeWithLaces "Shoes which have laces.")
(comment sendDataOfTypeToSystem "#$sendDataOfTypeToSystem is an #$ActionPredicate relating instances of #$IntelligentAgent with subcollections of #$InformationStore and instances of #$ComputationalSystem.  (#$sendDataOfTypeToSystem AGENT DATATYPE SYSTEM) means that AGENT remotely sends data of type DATATYPE to SYSTEM.")
(comment culturePrescribes-Hypothetical "(#$culturePrescribes-Hypothetical CULTURE COND ACTTYPE ROLE) 
  means that within CULTURE, when COND is true, it is considered good 
  or proper or right for one to play ROLE in an instance of ACTTYPE,
  and bad or improper or wrong not to do so.  For example, some cultures 
  expect one to help others in need when one is in a position to do so.  
  This predicate applies equally to moral rules, rules of conduct or 
  etiquette, and customs.  See also #$culturePrescribes-Categorical,
  #$cultureProscribes-Categorical, and
  #$cultureProscribes-Hypothetical.")
(comment geneOfBLO-GenInfo "(#$geneOfBLO-GenInfo BLO GENE) means that the

#$BiologicalLivingObject BLO has the #$GeneticInformation GENE in its

genetic material and that GENE is encoded by an instance of #$Gene-GIS and

instantiated in a corresponding instance of #$Gene-HereditaryUnit. Note

also that GENE is a #$subGeneticInformation of the BLO's genome [See #$genomeOfBLO-GenInfo].")
(comment ModernShelterConstruction "A specialization of both #$FixedStructure and #$HumanShelterConstruction.  Each instance of #$ModernShelterConstruction is a construction artifact that provides comfortable shelter for humans during some of their daily activities.  Instances of #$ModernShelterConstruction have the kinds of features found in modern-day buildings in Europe, the USA, and other technologically developed parts of the world, namely, amenities like doors, plumbing, electricity, and probably some kind of climate control system for maintaining humanly comfortable conditions indoors.  Examples include the #$NewYorkHiltonAtBroadway, the #$SydneyOperaHouse, and instances of the collection #$ModernHumanResidence (e.g., a newly built home in a suburban development or a renovated brownstone in New York City).")
(disjointWith DirectedTranslation DrugTherapy)
(disjointWith InformationTransferEvent TendingAPlant)
(comment ShoppingCart "#$ShoppingCart is the collection of handcarts that are designed to hold dry goods for shoppers.")
(comment occupiesFraction "This predicate indicates how much of one thing is occupied spatially by another. (#$occupiesFraction THING1 THING2 FRACTION) means that THING1 spatially occupies part of THING2 and takes up FRACTION fraction of the space in THING2.  In the special case where THING1 occupies all of THING2, the value of FRACTION would be 1.  (FRACTION is always greater than zero if this predicate holds.)  See also #$occupiesMostOf.")
(comment RickettsiaConorii "The pathogen that causes #$MediterraneanSpottedFever.")
(comment Habitat "The living environment of an organism.  On a descending scale, one can speak of biomes, vicinities, ambient environment, and contiguous environment.")
(comment traversalFromToInSystem "(#$traversalInSystem TRAV A B SYS) means that TRAV is a #$Traversal from A to B in the #$PathSystem SYS.  Let TRAV = (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X(1) PATH(1) ... X(n) PATH(n) X(n+1))).  To say that TRAV is a #$Traversal from A to B in SYS we mean that (i) TRAV is a #$Traversal in SYS, i.e., (#$traversalInSystem TRAV SYS) holds, and (ii) A = X(1) and B = X(n+1) (and thus both A and B are points in SYS and both (#$traversalFrom TRAV A) and (#$traversalTo TRAV B) hold).  So (#$traversalInSystem TRAV A B SYS) is actually an abbreviation of (#$and (#$traversalInSystem TRAV SYS) (#$pointInSystem A SYS) (#$pointInSystem B SYS) (#$traversalFrom TRAV A) (#$traversalTo TRAV B)).")
(disjointWith FurniturePiece SomethingToWear)
(comment VulnerableToFileCreation "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$FileCreationFault on it.")
(disjointWith TopographicalFeature InformationStore)
(comment Trotskyist "The collection of #$Person that subscribe to #$Trotskyism.")
(comment WeakPasswordResetFault-Administrator "#$WeakPasswordResetFault-Administrator is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.  A program has this vulnerability if the method that the program uses to reset a lost/forgotten administrator password is easily compromised or guessable.")
(comment opponentsInConflict "(#$opponentsInConflict AGT1 AGT2 CONF) means that AGT1 and AGT2 are instances of #$IntelligentAgent who participate, with conflicting purposes, in the #$ConflictEvent CONF.  Note that there could be more than two agents who participate in CONF with conflicting purposes, but there are at least two.  Accordingly, AGT1 and AGT2 must be distinct agents when (#$opponentsInConflict AGT1 AGT2 CONF) holds.")
(comment SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPath "The collection of all #$Path-Simples that do not have any branching points along them (except possibly at the ends) and such that each has its endpoints at two different locations, that is, it is not a loop from one place back to the same place.  (For contrast, see #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPath.)  When the segment is part of a specified #$PathSystem (as opposed to a mere #$CustomarySystemOfLinks), then the predicates #$pathInSystem or #$linkInSystem may relate it to the system.")
(comment ToyVersionFn "(#$ToyVersionFn OBJ) denotes the collection of toy versions of objects of type OBJ.  See also #$ModelFn.")
(comment NylonStocking "Not #$Pantyhose.  Stockings made of nylon worn by adult females.")
(comment Axis "A specialization of #$Line-Straight-Directed. Each instance of #$Axis is a straight line about which a three-dimensional figure is oriented or rotates.  The orientation is between specified sides or points of the object or according to the right-hand rule for a rotational axis. Examples include spatially localized objects, such as the Earth's axis of rotation, as well as abstract objects, such as the axis of rotation for some abstract three-dimensional figure.")
(comment queryRuleMacroRolesInEventType "A #$QueryDedicatedPredicate used for querying whether for any roles such that all instances of specified event type are known to have some instance of a specified actor type playing the role in question.")
(comment LouseBiting "The collection of instances in which a #$Louse performs an
#$InsectBiting. Not all lice bite humans, see #$SuckingLouse and
#$ChewingLouse.")
(comment CeilingOfARoom "#$CeilingOfARoom is a specialization of #$PartOfRoomInAConstruction. Each instance of #$CeilingOfARoom is a ceiling of some #$RoomInAConstruction.  Note that, unlike walls, ceilings are conventionally considered to be 'one-sided' objects.  The other side of a #$CeilingOfARoom may be a #$RoofOfAConstruction, or in a #$ModernShelterConstruction, more probably the #$FloorInAConstruction in another room.")
(comment Gargoyle-Sculpture "The collection of ornamental sculptures commonly known as gargoyles.")
(disjointWith Washing CuttingSomething)
(comment ran "'(#$ran RUN RUNNER)' means that RUNNER is the running animal in the #$Running RUN.")
(comment HoldingInMouth "An animal holding something, by using its jaws and/or teeth.")
(comment RegistryModificationFault "A program has this fault if it allows unauthorized users to edit #$RegistryKeys on the system.  Depending upon which #$RegistryKeys the user has access to, escalating to #$AdministratorAccount privileges can be trivial.")
(comment operatingSystemOnComputerHasFault "(#$operatingSystemOnComputerHasFault OS COMP FAULT) means that the copy of OS running on COMP (#$runsOS, q.v.) manifests FAULT.")
(comment Aba-Garment "#$Aba-Garment is the subset of #$OuterGarment whose instances are loose, sleeveless, made of (instances of) #$AbaCloth, and are worn by people from the #$ArabianPeninsula.")
(comment LibraryOnOSSeriesFn "(#$LibraryOnOSSeriesFn LIB OS-SERIES) denotes a library file LIB that runs on each of the operating systems in the #$ConceptualWorkSeries, OS-SERIES.  For example, (#$LibraryOnOSSeriesFn #$Libc-TheLibrary (#$VersionsInclusiveFn #$HP-UX \"1.0\" \"2.0\") denotes the libc installed with each of the HP/UX operating system versions 1.0 through 2.0. See also #$LibraryOnOSFn.")
(comment VulnerableToFileModification "#$VulnerableToFileModification is a specialization of #$ComputerVulnerability.  A computer has this vulnerability if it is it allows an unauthorized user either to overwrite, delete, or recover
 files.")
(comment ReligiousDenomination "The collection of all instances of #$Religion which are variations of a more general religion which adherents of the #$ReligiousDenomination regard as their #$Religion.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedRootAccess "A computer has this vulnerability if it allows an unauthorized user to access a root account.  When exploitable locally, it is typically a consequence of an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-Root.  When exploitable remotely, it is typically the consequence of an #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-Root. See also #$VulnerableToEscapeFromRestrictedShell.")
(disjointWith ReligiousPerson NonReligiousPerson)
(comment perceivesThat "(#$perceivesThat AGENT PROP) means that AGENT discerns that PROP is true, by the use of one of AGENT's sense modalities. 

For example, an agent may perceive (via seeing) that the water is boiling, or perceive (via smelling) that the roast is done. #$perceivesThat does not relate an agent to any proposition PROP which is not discerned 'directly' by the use of one of its sense modalities. For example, seeing that various events have occurred at various times and later deducing some proposition, PROP, from these observations is not a case or perceiving that PROP. For a practical guideline: It is typically necessary that some sentence of the form 'AGENT Xs that PROP' be true in order for (#$perceivesThat AGENT PROP) to be true, where Xs is a verb expressing the activity of a sense modality, such as 'sees', 'hears', etc. This condition is not satisfied only in cases where AGENT perceives that PROP by the use of some sense modality for which there is no corresponding sensory verb.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseAllowsAnonymousFTP "A computer has this vulnerability if it allows remote users
 of an instance of #$FTPServerProgram to log in to the service without authentication.
 In most cases, the user simply types in \"anonymous\" for the username
 and a (real or fictional) email address for the password.")
(comment deviceReliability "Although the `best' version of reliability might involve probability, we're going to start with it as being an interval.")
(comment latitudeMax "(#$latitudeMax OBJ LAT) means that the 

#$SpatialThing-Localized OBJ has its farthest north part(s) geographically 

located at LAT, where LAT denote a latitude line

[#$LatitudeLine] in the \"geographical universe\".")
(comment EnzymeComplementFn "The purpose of this function is to return the group of all
enzymes that are physical parts (#$internalParts) of a given cell
within the time frame of the context in which the NAT is reified.")
(disjointWith ListOfVertices (ListOfTypeFn Character-Abstract))
(comment CenterLineOfPathFn "(#$CenterLineOfPathFn PATH) denotes the centerline of PATH: the one-dimensional spatial object that is equidistant from, and roughly parallel to, the edges of PATH (see #$centerLineOfPath). In the

#$ModernMilitaryTacticsMt the centerline is a #$Traversal.")
(comment EgyptianPyramid "The giant pyramids found in Giza, #$Egypt and other places in #$Egypt")
(comment FileMovingProgram "The collection of programs that move a file in one location to another location.")
(comment ArbitraryPortPacketMishandlingFault "An operating system has this fault if a remote attacker can cause it to crash by sending it (malformed)  packets from a remote client.  Use this fault or a specialization of it if the entire range of ports are faulty -- if less than all are faulty, specify a port and a protocol by using #$PacketMishandlingFaultFn.")
(comment FerrySlip "The collection of docking facilities for a ferry. Usually
informations about instances of this collection include orientation wrt
true north, lenght, width and associated mode of transportation with the
feature.")
(comment PushingAButton "The event in which a button or a key is pressed with the finger.")
(comment FileCreationFault-RootOwnership "A program has a #$FileCreationFault-RootOwnership if it can be exploited to create a file with root ownership.")
(comment interArgGenl1-2 "(#$interArgGenl1-2 REL INDEPENDENT-COL DEPENDENT-COL) means that, when a spec of INDEPENDENT-COL appears as the first argument to REL, the second argument is constrained to be a spec of DEPENDENT-COL.")
(comment doGetLoginInformationForAccountSurreptitiously "(#$doGetLoginInformationForAccountSurreptitiously AGENT ACCOUNT) means that AGENT acquires the password for ACCOUNT in a manner likely to escape detection.")
(comment connectedInSystem "(#$connectedInSystem X Y SYS) means that there is a path PATH in the #$PathSystem SYS such that (#$pathBetweenInSystem PATH X Y SYS) holds, or else X and Y are the same point in SYS.  This predicate applies to a particular #$PathSystem, and the connectedness is an equivalence relation on that system, i.e., it is reflexive, transitive and symmetrical on that system.")
(disjointWith GaseousTangibleThing BuildingMaterial)
(comment SkiPants "Pants for extended cold-weather activities, esp. skiing.")
(comment setRegistryKeyToValueOnComputer "An instance of #$ActionPredicate.  (#$setRegistryKeyToValueOnComputer AGENT REG_KEY VALUE COMP) means that AGENT sets the #$RegistryKey REG_KEY on COMP to VALUE.  Note that, for some instances of #$RegistryKey, VALUE may be an instance of #$MaliciousComputerProgram set by an evil hacker who has access to COMP.  Or AGENT might be a friendly systems administrator trying to make his network #$CycSecure.")
(comment mutantOfGene-GIS "(#$mutantOfGene-GIS MUTANT GENE) means that MUTANT is the abstract

structure of a gene that mutated from a gene instantiating the structure in

GENE, i.e. MUTANT is a structure derived from GENE by recombination or

substitution of the nucleotidic sequence.")
(comment FleetOfSubmarines "The collection of all submarine fleets, i.e. groups of submarines that are in a relatively well-defined area and are under a single command.  See also #$SubmarineFleet-Organization")
(comment directionPreservingSubSystems "(#$directionPreservingSubSystems SYS SUBSYS) means that (i) both SYS and SUBSYS are semi-directed path systems (see #$Semi-DirectedPathSystem), (ii) SUBSYS is a subsystem of SYS (so that (#$subPathSystems SYS SUBSYS) holds), and (iii) SUBSYS preserves the directions of links, in the following sense: for each link LINK in SUBSYS, (#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SUBSYS) iff (#$linkFromToInSystem LINK X Y SYS).")
(comment interests-Prop "(#$interests-Prop AGENT PROP) means that in the context of the assertion, AGENT has a substantial stake in whether PROP is true or false.  The interest may be 'pro' or 'con'--i.e., AGENT may want PROP to be true or AGENT may want PROP to be false.  What is required is that agent care strongly about what the truth-value is.  AGENT may be justified in doing so or not.  #$interests-Prop is one of the weakest instances of #$PropositionalAttitudeSlot, and features several stronger predicates as specializations, notably #$biases, #$desires, #$intends, and #$goals.")
(disjointWith SpaceInAHOC Building)
(comment PhysicalQuartersFn "This function is used to denote the physical facilities (construction artifacts) an organization uses, like the store building occupied by a retail store.")
(comment GopherServerProgram "#$GopherServerProgram is the collection of #$ServerPrograms that implement the #$Gopher-InternetProtocol.")
(comment vulnerableToTangibleType "(#$vulnerableToTangibleType OBJECT THREAT-OBJECT-TYPE) means that OBJECT is vulnerable to some threat involving instances of THREAT-OBJECT-TYPE. For example, (#$vulnerableToTangibleType #$Superman #$Kryptonite) states that Superman is vulnerable to harm via kryptonite. This leaves open the type of harm, which can specified via #$vulnerableToType.")
(comment StateGovernor "Head of a political division of a country, generalization of #$USStateGovernor.")
(disjointWith OutOfControlCrowdEvent TakingCareOfSomething)
(comment MediterraneanSpottedFever "A mild to severe fever with a red rash usually on the palms of the hands and soles of the feet. When caused by a tick bite, there is usually a lesion at the site that may resemble a small ulcer with a black center surrounded by a red circle.")
(comment Cathedral "A Christian place of worship, usually several centuries old, e.g. Notre Dame in Paris. St. Patrick's Cathedral in NYCity.")
(disjointWith Box-Container SomethingToWear)
(comment challengesToDo "'(#$challengesToDo CHALLENGE ACT-TYPE)' means that the #$Challenging CHALLENGE challenges the #$challengee to perform (#$performedBy) an instance of the act-type ACT-TYPE.  See #$challengesTo.")
(comment VulnerableToFileCreation-RootOwnership "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$FileCreationFault-RootOwnership on it.")
(comment signifiesTo-Icon "This is a specialized representation (semiotic) predicate meaning representation due to resemblance, such as when a portrait represents the person depicted. (#$signifiesTo-Icon THING1 THING2 AGENT) means that, to AGENT, THING1 represents THING2 because THING1 resembles THING2.  This is called 'iconic' representation. Compare this with the predicates #$signifiesTo-Index and #$signifiesTo-Symbol.  It's possible for all three to apply to the same representation.  If the basis for the representation is unknown, use the more general predicate #$signifiesTo.")
(comment SystemMicrophoneFault "#$SystemMicrophoneFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$SystemMicrophoneFault if an unauthorized person can use the program to operate the system microphone.")
(comment SchemeCommandExecutionFault "#$SchemeCommandExecutionFault is an attribute of some instances of
 #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has a #$SchemeCommandExecutionFault if
 an unauthorized person can pass Scheme code to it and have it execute
 arbitrary commands.")
(comment adversarialResponseTo "(#$adversarialResponseTo ACT SIT) means that (#$inReactionTo ACT SIT) and that ACT is an adversarial or hostile response to  SIT.  Roughly speaking, ACT is an adversarial response if (i) the director or performer of ACT (AGENT1) intends ACT to either threaten or harm some interest of some doer of SIT (AGENT2), and (ii) AGENT1 acts with this intention towards AGENT2 *because of* AGENT2's participation in SIT.  A bit more formally: in the case of an adversarial response, AGENT1 has a goal GOAL1 and AGENT2 has a goal GOAL2 such that AGENT1 believes that AGENT2 is #$responsibleFor SIT and also believes that SIT decreases the likelihood that GOAL1 will be realized. This belief causes AGENT1 to perform the action ACT, which #$startsAfterStartingOf SIT.  AGENT1 believes that ACT decreases the likelihood that GOAL2 will be realized.")
(comment RidingBoot "A kind of shoe that one sometimes wears while riding horses.")
(disjointWith TwoDimensionalGeometricThing OneDimensionalGeometricThing)
(disjointWith MoleculeTypeByChemicalCompoundType PersonTypeByCulture)
(comment pathConcatenationOf-Cycle "(pathConcatenationOf-Simple CHAIN PATH) means that PATH is the #$Path-Cyclic obtained by 'path-concatenating' all of the links in CHAIN. See also #$JoinPathsIntoCycleFn .")
(comment PartOfBuilding "#$PartOfBuilding is a specialization of #$PartOfAnHSC.  Each instance of #$PartOfBuilding is a part of a building that is 'built-in', that is, built with the intention of remaining as part of the building.")
(comment threeToFivePrimeDirectionPred "The corresponding predicate of #$ThreeToFivePrimeDirectionFn.")
(comment ModularHome "The collection of all modular homes, constructed in sections at a factory and transported to the home site, where the sections are assembled into a finished house.")
(disjointWith Washing AttachmentEvent)
(comment RpcRequestForwardingFault "A program has this fault if it is possible for an unauthorized remote user to send an rpc request to that program, which will then be forwarded to an rpc service on the same network.")
(comment agentiveNounStrings "(#$agentiveNounStrings WORD STRING) states that STRING is one of the agentive noun strings for the word unit WORD in some microtheory.  In other words, some agentive #$SpeechPartPredicate is used on WORD to relate it to STRING.  This predicate is

#$notAssertible since it is concluded from the current state of the knowledge base.")
(comment ContinuousPhysicalContactSituation "A specialization of #$PhysicalContactSituation each instance of which involves two or more tangible objects touching (see #$touches) continuously throughout the entire duration of the situation.  Every #$PhysicalContactSituation has a #$ContinuousPhysicalContactSituation as a (proper or improper)

sub-situation (see #$subSituations).")
(comment Toga "The collection of mantles such as those worn by the Romans beginning around 400 BC.  The Roman #$Toga emerged as a modification of the earlier Etruscan mantles.  Instances of #$Toga were generally large squares of linen, folded and draped in complicated patterns, and sometimes colored or embroidered according to the social standing of the wearer.")
(comment LibraryOnOSFn "(#$LibraryOnOSFn PROG OS) denotes a library that is installed on the operating system OS.  For example, (#$LibraryOnOSFn #$Libc-TheLibrary #$HP-UX) denotes the libc installed on HP/UX.  See also #$LibraryOnOSSeriesFn.")
(comment UDPFragmentationMishandlingFault "A program with this fault, when running on a computer, makes that computer #$VulnerableToTearDropAttack (q.v.).")
(comment InfectionTypeBySymptomology "This type-level collection facets the class of #$Infections by characteristic symptom.  More specifically, if INFECTION-COL is an instance of #$InfectionTypeBySymptomology, then its instances will, under normal circumstances, feature a certain type of symptom which is characteristic of the infection-class as a whole.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedGroupAccess "A computer has his vulnerability if it allows an
 unauthorized user to access a group account.")
(comment NonReligiousPerson "The collection of instances of #$Person who are not religious in any way.")
(comment doOverrunLogFileTypeOfProgram "(#$doOverrunLogFileTypeOfProgram AGENT INFO PROG) means that AGENT
overruns the log file for PROG that contains INFO.")
(comment dislikesEvent "(#$dislikesEvent AGT EVENT) means that the sentient agent AGT dislikes EVENT in some way --- that is, (#$feelsEmotion AGT (#$MediumToVeryHighAmountFn #$Dislike)).  The kinds of interactions that produce displeasure depend largely on what kind of thing EVENT is.")
(comment AnimalPoweredDevice "A collection of physical devices.  An instance of #$AnimalPoweredDevice is a device that is powered by animal muscle power and not by any human user, although a human user may control the device and/or direct the animal.")
(comment AirControlTower "A specialization of #$ControlTower. Instances of
#$AirControlTower are located within airport traffic areas and house
persons and equipment used to control the flow of air traffic.")
(disjointWith ServerProgram LocalProgram)
(comment programCallsProgram "#$programCallsProgram is a binary predicate used to relate one instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW to another. (#$programCallsProgram PROG1 PROG2) means that PROG1 is written in such a way that when it runs, it calls PROG2. For example, if we consider the following shell code snippet \"for i `ls /bin`; do echo $i done\" to be Snippet-TheProgram, it is true that (#$programCallsProgram Snippet-TheProgram #$Echo-TheProgram).")
(comment warnee "'(#$warnee WARNING AGENT)' means that AGENT is warned in the
#$Warning WARNING.")
(comment SuperuserAccount "The collection of all superuser computer accounts, i.e. those accounts which have unfettered (or nearly so) access to the file system.  Notable specs are #$RootAccount and #$AdministratorAccount.")
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureFiles "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program on it with a #$InsecureFilesFault.")
(comment TheYearInCalendarFn "The year in a specified calendar.")
(comment HoldingAHandle "To hold the handle of some object, usually a tool, in the hand.")
(comment Excavation-Hole "The collection of holes or digging made by some agent, typically
human beings, for some working purpose. For example, a mine shaft, the
cavity resulting from an archeological excavation would be instances of
this collection or preferably some of its specialization.")
(comment exploitFaultOfProgramOnSystemWithInstrument "An #$ActionPredicate relating instances of #$IntelligentAgent with instances of  #$ProgramFaultAttribute, #$ComputerProgram-CW, and #$ComputationalSystem.  (#$exploitFaultOfProgramOnSystem AGENT FAULT PROGRAM SYSTEM) means that AGENT exploits the FAULT of PROGRAM when PROGRAM is running on SYSTEM.")
(comment eventOutcomes-Propositional "An intermediate predicate:  (#$eventOutcomes-Propositional PROP X) means that the fact that  PROP -- i.e., the fact that makes PROP true -- results in the situation X. Intended use: subordinate gerund phrases as in `RNA polymerase moves along, creating single strands'.")
(comment DeliveringMail "A subevent of #$SendingTangibleMail. #$DeliveringMail is the collection 
of all events of a #$ShippingOrganization delivering a #$MailableObject to its
intended destination. This may involve a direct #$TransferOfControl, such as 
handing the #$MailableObject to the recipient, or leaving the #$MailableObject in
a location where it can be collected by the recipient. See #$recipientOfPost-Intended
for further information.")
(comment subPathSystems "(#$subPathSystems SYS SUBSYS) means that the path system SUBSYS is a subsystem of the path system SYS.  Technically, this means the following: (i) Every point in SUBSYS is a point in SYS, (ii) every node in SUBSYS is a node in SYS, (iii) every link in SUBSYS is a link in SYS, and (iv) every loop in SUBSYS is a loop in SYS.  Some consequences of these conditions are as follows.  (a) Every point in SUBSYS that is a node in SYS is a node in SUBSYS.  (b) For any nodes X and Y in SUBSYS and each link LINK in SUBSYS, LINK is between X and Y in SYS iff it is between X and Y in SUBSYS.  (c) For each point X in SYS that is not a node in SYS, if X is on a link in SYS that is not in SUBSYS, X is not in SUBSYS.  (d) Isolated points and deadends in SUBSYS must be nodes in SYS.  (e) For each loop LOOP in SUBSYS, the only node in SYS on LOOP must be a node in SUBSYS.  (f) If SYS is a #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretic (or a #$Multigraph), all subsystems of SYS are #$SimpleGraph-GraphTheoretics (or #$Multigraphs).  Predicates concerning particular kinds of subsystems of path systems, i.e., predicates that take #$subPathSystems as #$genlPreds, include #$linkClosedSubSystems, #$pointClosedSubSystems, and #$maximalConnectedSubSystems, etc.  Predicates whose #$genlInverse are #$subPathSystems includes #$underlyingGraph.")
(comment SinglePurposeDevice "A collection of devices each of which has a single #$primaryFunction.   Each instance of #$SinglePurposeDevice may have more than one function, but will have only one _primary_ function.  For example, a car is a single purpose device because it has the primary function of providing transportation.  Of course, a car can provide shelter as well as transportation; but a convertible with a badly torn roof still functions as a car (because its primary function is transportation) even though it does not function as much of a shelter.  It is also possible for a #$SinglePurposeDevice to have other functions associated with it, even though they are not functions of that device per se.  For example, if a car has a cigarette lighter, a clock, etc., those parts have their own functions, which are performed in the car and enjoyed by the users of the car while they are using the car.  However, the functions of those devices (lighting cigarettes and telling time) are generally not considered to be the functions of the car itself.  If someone utters the sentence `Fred used his car today' we would guess that Fred drove/rode somewhere in the car, and would be surprised/amused/annoyed/confused if we later discover that the speaker meant only that Fred used the car's lighter and the clock but didn't travel somewhere by car.")
(comment SkiSuit "A suit for extended cold-weather activities, typically consisting of pants and jacket.")
(comment sniffAccountLoginInformation "#$sniffAccountLoginInformation is an instance of #$ActionPredicate that relates an instance of #$IntelligentAgent to an instance of #$UserAccount and an instance of #$Computer. (#$sniffAccountLoginInformation AGENT ACCOUNT COMPUTER) means that AGENT sniffs the password for ACCOUNT using a #$PasswordSnifferProgram on COMPUTER.")
(comment cultureProscribes-Categorical "(#$cultureProscribes-Categorical CULTURE ACTTYPE ROLE) 
  means that within CULTURE it is considered improper or immoral
  or wrong to play ROLE in instances of ACTTYPE.  For example, 
  most cultures consider it wrong to take a human life.  This does not 
  entail, however, that CULTURE has a (hypothetical) proscription 
  against playing ROLE in instances of ACTTYPE with respect to every 
  possible condition; i.e. there might exist exceptional situations in 
  which playing ROLE in an ACTTYPE is not proscribed (and might even 
  be prescribed) by CULTURE.  One might be required to take human life,
  for example, in wartime.  This predicate applies equally to moral 
  rules, rules of conduct or etiquette, and customs.  See also 
  #$cultureProscribes-Hypothetical,#$culturePrescribes-Categorical, 
  and #$culturePrescribes-Hypothetical.")
(comment sociallyCapableOf "'(#$sociallyCapableOf BEING SIT-TYPE ROLE)' means that BEING is able to play ROLE in social situations of type SIT-TYPE.  This notion of social capability is the weak one of conceivability; for instance, no man is socially capable of playing the role of wife in a family, but any woman is.  The relevant social group is one to which BEING belongs.")
(comment structuralSupport-FunctionalRole "(#$structuralSupport-FunctionalRole SYSTEM SUPPORT) means
that SYSTEM is expected to play the role of #$supportingObject in some
#$SupportingSomething in which the #$supportedObject is SYSTEM. It
entails the capability of playing the role of #$supportingObject in
#$SupportingSomethings.")
(comment pointOnCycle "(#$pointOnCycle POINT CYCLE) means that the #$Thing POINT is a stationary point (or place) on a #$Path-Cyclic CYCLE.")
(comment AnalogyAgentCaseFn "(#$AnalogyAgentCaseFn AGENT) denotes the #$AnalogyCase which is based on the given AGENT.  This function is primarily used with #$matchBetween to state that an #$AnalogyMatch exists between two cases which are based on two agents.")
(disjointWith SpaceInAHOC Tower)
(comment BoosterVaccinationEvent "#$BoosterVaccinationEvent is the collection of #$VaccinationEvents which occur after the initial #$Vaccine shots. Typically, a #$Vaccine will require that after the first shot or series of shots, the #$Vaccine has to be administered again after some #$TimeInterval for the #$Vaccine to maintain its effectiveness.")
(comment ZooGrounds "The grounds (compound, physical complex) of a zoo.")
(disjointWith StateGovernor Minister-Governmental)
(disjointWith StoringSomething Communicating)
(comment FormingOpinion "The collection of all #$Thinking events in which the doer ends up with #$beliefs that something is true.  The beliefs could be either #$opinions or knowledge [#$knows].")
(comment Ecosystem "This is the collection of ecosystems. An ecosystem is

a particular region in which organisms live, together with the interrelations

between these organisms and the relations between these organisms and their

physical environment.")
(comment SubSystemUnderTraversalFn "A function, when applied to a #$PathSystem SYS and a #$Traversal TRAV in SYS as in (#$SubSystemUnderTraversalFn SYS TRAV), returns the smallest point-closed subsystem SUB of SYS such that TRAV is a traversal in SUB (see #$smallestSubSystemUnderTraversal, #$traversalInSystem and #$pointClosedSubSystems).  Note that 'smallest' here means that no link LINK between X and Y in SYS is a link in SUB if neither (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList X LINK Y)) nor (#$TraversalFn (#$TheList Y LINK X)) is a #$subTraversals of TRAV.  Note also that since SUB is a point-closed subsystem of SYS, every point in SYS that is on TRAV (see #$pointOnTraversal) is a point in SUB.  Note finally that since SUB is the 'smallest' subsystem of SYS in which TRAV is a traversal, SUB must be a #$ConnectedPathSystem.")
(comment FastFoodRestaurantSpace "A typical fast food restaurant space.  Eventually we may wish to make a unit to refer to the single-story, roadside building.")
(disjointWith ConstructionArtifact SomethingToWear)
(comment VulnerableToSwitchCrashing "A switch computer has this vulnerability if it has a program
with a #$SwitchCrashingFault on it.")
(comment doLoginToAccountOn "(#$doLoginToAccountOn AGENT ACCT COMP) means that AGENT takes steps toward the goal of getting access to a login prompt on COMP.  Note that this will seldom (if ever) be an AGENT's goal if AGENT does not yet know the password and username for ACCT.  Note that this predicate is appropriate only for instances of #$LoginAccount, whereas #$doGetAccessToAccount is appropriate for all accounts.")
(comment VulnerableToEavesdropping "An attribute applying to instances of #$Computer. A computer system is #$VulnerableToEavesdropping if it can be used by anyone logged in to it to listen to audible events in its vicinity.")
(comment FourWayJunctionOfPaths "A collection of junctions of paths. A member of this collection exists where four #$SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPaths meet together, or where two #$SimpleUnloopedSegmentOfPaths join the two ends of a #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPath that loops back to that junction, or else where two #$SimpleLoopedSegmentOfPaths both loop to the same point abstractly forming a figure-eight pattern.  If there is a specified #$PathSystem, use #$fourWayJunctionInSystem instead.  (Determining what constitutes a #$FourWayJunctionOfPaths depends on the #$PathTypes of the joined paths; if it is #$River then only a junction of four segments of rivers qualifies (which is fairly rare), not a place where two roads joins a river.)")
(comment DemineralizedWater "#$Water without most metal ions")
(comment BoxingTrunks "The collection of shorts one normally wears while boxing.")
(comment queryForEventOutcomes "A #$QueryDedicatedPredicate used for querying about the outcomes of a specified event type.")
(comment ChewingLouse "The collection of all instances of #$Louse that have mouth
parts designed for chewing. These lice live on or near birds, and do
not infect humans. See #$SuckingLouse for the human parasite.")
(comment EntryPathsFn "An instance of #$Function-Denotational and #$UnaryFunction that takes an
instance of #$PathSystem as an argument and returns the
number of entry paths into that system.  
(#$EntryPathsFn PATH_SYS) denotes the subcollection of
#$Path-Simple that contains all the entry paths into PATH_SYS, i.e.
the collection of all paths PATH such that
(#$entryPathToSystem PATH PATH_SYS) holds.  See also
#$entryPointOnPathToSystem and #$entryPointToSystem.")
(comment WallOfAConstruction "#$WallOfAConstruction is a specialization of #$PartOfAnHSC and #$Wall-Vertical.  Each instance of #$WallOfAConstruction is a part of a #$HumanShelterConstruction.  This includes the walls on the outside of the building as well as those on the inside such as the wall separating two rooms in a house.")
(comment XDisplayManagerProgram "Any program that implements the #$XDisplayManagerControlProtocol.  The most familiar program of this sort is #$Xdm-TheProgram.")
(comment PairingThingsMentally "A collection of purposeful acts of thinking.  Each instance of #$PairingThingsMentally is a mental act in which the doer consciously considers two things together as members of the same two-member group.  This neither entails nor precludes that the things in question actually are co-members of any such #$Group, either before, during, or after the mental pairing.  For example, a lovestruck teenager who daydreams about being married to his love interest engages in this kind of activity.  See also #$PairingObjects.")
(comment CentralHeatDwelling "Dwelling has a heat-producing unit (Furnace, Heat pump, or whatever) from which hot fluids are distributed to ducts, radiators or whatever in the rooms where the heat is desired.  We need to create a genl of Furnace that includes these other things.")
(comment Writing "A specialization of both #$HumanActivity and #$VisualInformationGeneratingAct.  Each instance of #$Writing is an action in which some text is produced, either via writing by hand or writing with a machine, such as a typewriter or a computer.  An instance of #$Writing could be a single episode of writing, or a discontinuous series of episodes (as when one writes a letter over a few days).  #$Writing is not a specialization of #$Communicating, because in some instances of #$Writing there is not a successful transfer of information to another agent.")
(comment ClausalFrameType "This frame is used for words that take a clausal complement, possibly in addition to other complements.")
(comment HoldingOnShoulders "An animal holding something, by supporting the thing's weight on its shoulders.")
(comment PortscanProtectionBypassFault "A #$FirewallProgram has this fault if it allows remote attackers to conduct a port scan on the network without logging the attack.")
(comment MolecularComponentType "The collection of all collections whose instances are frequently #$physicalDecompositions of a #$Molecule.")
(comment VulnerableToFileOverwrite "#$VulnerableToFileOverwrite is a specialization of #$VulnerableToFileModification.  A computer has this vulnerability if it allows unauthorized users to overwrite certain files.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedUserAccess "A computer has his vulnerability if it allows an unauthorized user to access a user account.  When it is locally exploitable, it is typically the consequence of an #$ElevatedPrivilegeFault-User.  When it is remotely exploitable, it is typically the consequence of an #$ExternalAccessToAccountsFault-User.")
(disjointWith Atheist ReligiousAgnostic)
(comment Gnome-Mythical "Imaginary creatures.  Typically very small, old, male, bearded, wearing pointy hats.")
(comment seesThat "(#$seesThat AGENT PROP) means that AGENT perceives, by sense of sight, that PROP is true.")
(comment Device-UserPowered "A specialization of #$MusclePoweredDevice.  Each instance of #$Device-UserPowered is an artifact deliberately designed to perform a particular function, and one which depends upon the physical efforts of the user to perform that function in part or in whole.  A paradigm

example would be a bicycle.  However, the definition also leaves room

for some counterintuitive cases -- for example, combs and forks also qualify as user-powered devices.  Borderline cases would be devices which

require effort on the part of the user to perform part of the function,

but not all of it.  For example, many gas-powered lawnmowers have to be 

pushed by hand, but use an internal combustion engine to impart the necessary velocity to the cutting surfaces.")
(comment latitudeMin "(#$latitudeMin OBJ LAT) means that the 

#$SpatialThing-Localized OBJ has its most southern part(s) geographically 

located at LAT, where LAT denote a latitude line

[#$LatitudeLine] in the \"geographical universe\".")
(comment Econometrician "The collection of all econometricians.  The field of #$Econometrics is where #$Statistics and #$Economics come together.")
(comment UrbanArea "A subcollection of #$HumanResidenceArea.  Each instance of #$UrbanArea is a geographical region the whole of which (more or less) is characterized by typically \"urban\" features (such as streets, buildings, businesses, houses, schools, sidewalks, sewer systems, power lines, automobiles, pedestrians, and so on).  An urban area might be as small as an inner-city street corner or as large as the New York City Metropolitan Area.  By default, urbanness is a \"stuff-like\" property of human residence areas: (nearly) every subregion of an #$UrbanArea is itself an #$UrbanArea.  Examples include #$UTAustinCampus, #$ResearchTrianglePark, and the territorial extent of various cities (#$CityOfAustinTX, #$CityOfToulouseFrance, etc.).")
(comment Roofing "Building or repairing roofs (cf. #$RoofOfAConstruction).")
(comment PersonWithLatentParaphilia "The collection of #$PersonWithPsychologicalAilment who
suffer from paraphilic disorders, such as a
#$PersonWithLatentPedophilia. These are #$Persons that are not
currently engaging in activities that designate them as a
paraphilic person, but have desires or fantasies to do so. For
example, a #$PersonWithLatentPedophilia may have sexual fantasies
about children, but has not acted on those fantasies. When the
#$PersonWithLatentPedophilia does act on those desires, then they
become an instance of the collection #$ChildMolester.")
(comment BlockingTraffic "A collection of all events of blocking traffic.  Each             instance of #$BlockingTraffic is also a purposeful action              done by some agent with a purpose of stopping the traffic              on a certain path.  For any #$BlockingTraffic, there is              at least one #$objectActedOn which is a #$Path-Customary             (e.g., a bridge which is broken or a road which is blocked             to prevent vehicles or people from passing through it).")
(comment HumanWithDiabetesMellitus "The collection of all humans inflicted with #$DiabetesMellitus.")
(comment NetworkPropagation "Events in which information is transmitted over a computer network.  The #$transferredThing is an instance of #$ElectroMagneticIBT. An instance of #$ComputerNetwork is the #$instrument-Generic.")
(comment Cleats-Shoe "The collection of #$AthleticShoes which have cleats on the sole.")
(comment BlondeHairedHuman "The collection of all #$HomoSapiens with #$Blonde-HairColor evident on the head.  The color may be natural or dyed, and it may include woven hair.  Removable wigs are excluded from consideration in determining this class of people.")
(comment SoccerCleats-Shoe "The collection of shoes with cleats [#$Cleats-Shoe]  intended for use in playing soccer.")
(comment OccupationalSafetyAndHealthAdministration "A regulatory agency within the U.S. Department of Labor whose mission is to ensure safe and healthful workplaces in the United States.")
(comment LearningAnAbility "A specialization of #$Learning.  Each instance of #$LearningAnAbility is an event in which a new ability is acquired.  Some abilities are complex, and learning them involves learning one or more sub-abilities.  Thus, #$LearningAnAbility is an instance of #$TemporalStuffType (q.v.).")
(comment RedHairedHuman "The collection of all #$HomoSapiens with #$Red-HairColor evident on the head.  The color may be natural or dyed, and it may include woven hair.  Removable wigs are excluded from consideration in determining this class of people.")
(comment MakingAGesture "The collection of acts of #$IBOCreation done by an #$Animal (including #$Person) arranging its limbs or other body parts (and whatever objects the limbs might be holding) in some meaningful configuration (static or dynamic).  Vocal #$IBTGenerations are not considered to be gestures (see #$MakingAnOralSound for this), but they might be done in conjunction with gestures.   NB:  #$MakingAGesture is NOT a subcollection of #$NonVerbalCommunicating; at most, an instance of #$MakingAGesture is only half of a communication event. And someone can make a gesture while alone, without using it for communication. Thus, only some gestures are #$subEvents of #$NonVerbalCommunicating. (But note that #$MakingAGesture IS a subcollection of #$IBTGeneration-Original (q.v.), since every gesture encodes information, whether or not it is used for communication in a particular instance.)")
(comment HumanWithDwarfism "The collection of all humans afflicted with dwarfism. See also the more specific #$HumanWithProportionateDwarfism.")
(comment HumanWithProportionateDwarfism "A specialization of #$HumanWithDwarfism - the collection of all humans afflicted with  #$Dwarfism-Proportionate (whereby the dwarf's proportions are essentially the same as a non-dwarf's).")
(comment LightForce "The subcollection of #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable whose instances are equipped with lighter and less powerful weapons, fewer armored vehicles if any, and possibly lower troop strength than a typical unit of the same
specialty. Light units are suitable to tasks that require rapid movement and deployment, such as reconnaissance and, to a more limited extent, security operations.")
(comment BlackHairedHuman "The collection of all #$HomoSapiens with #$Black-HairColor evident on the head.  The color may be natural or dyed, and it may include woven hair.  Removable wigs are excluded from consideration in determining this class of people.")
(disjointWith LightForce HeavyForce)
(comment HeavyForce "The subcollection of #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable whose instances are equipped with heavier and more powerful weapons, more armored vehicles, and possibly higher troop strength than a typical unit of the same specialty. Heavy units are suitable to tasks that require high concentration of combat power, such as many offensive military tasks.")
(comment HumanWithCeliacDisease "The collection of all humans with #$CeliacDisease.")
(comment BrownHairedHuman "The collection of all #$HomoSapiens with #$Brown-HairColor evident on the head.  The color may be natural or dyed, and it may include woven hair.  Removable wigs are excluded from consideration in determining this class of people.")
(comment HumanWithMelanoma "The collection of humans afflicted with a #$Melanoma.")
(comment PersonWithAilmentCondition "The collection of all #$Persons afflicted by an #$AilmentCondition. This collection subsumes #$PersonWithPsychologicalAilment.")
(comment MilitaryUnitByLevelOfCombatForce "A collection of collections used to indicate the level of combat force of military units and, indirectly, the type of task for which they are suited.  Examples of such collections are #$LightForce and #$HeavyForce. Note: collections of this type are perforce generic quantities, since they are relative to the average of their unit type. For instance, a `light' cavalry unit might have considerable lower combat force than a `light' armored brigade, say.")
(comment Watch "A specialization of #$Clock.  Each instance of #$Watch is a clock that is designed to be easily transported (typically worn) by a person.")
(comment SystemVulnerableToAttackByComputerOperation "#$SystemVulnerableToAttackByComputerOperation is a specialization of #$ComputationalSystem and #$VulnerableThing. Each instance of #$SystemVulnerableToAttackByComputerOperation is a computational system vulnerable to instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation. Being an instance of #$SystemVulnerableToAttackByComputerOperation is a consequence of a #$ComputationalSystem's electronic configuration (e.g., its software, file permissions, protocols, etc.) rather than its physical configuration (e.g., its physical access points, location, etc.).")
(comment AuburnHairedHuman "The collection of all #$HomoSapiens with #$Auburn-HairColor evident on the head (see also the more specific #$RedHairedHuman). The color may be natural or dyed, and it may include woven hair.  Removable wigs are excluded from consideration in determining this class of people.")
(comment BrakingWithFoot "What happens when a driver puts the brakes on--the driver moves his/her leg to push the pedal until it bottoms out.")
(comment ComputerVulnerability "A specialization of #$SystemVulnerableToAttackByComputerOperation and #$Computer.  Each instance of #$ComputerVulnerability is a computer (not a computer network or a computer program copy) that is vulnerable to attack by computeroperation.  In many cases, however, a computer is an instance of #$ComputerVulnerability because it has a faulty program running on it.")
(comment NaturalHazard "A specialization of #$PhysicalEvent and #$DangerousSituation.  #$NaturalHazard is the collection of natural hazard events, such as #$HurricaneAsEvent, #$Mudslides, #$Earthquakes and the like. Each instance of this collection is an event that can inflict extensive property damage, injury, or death. Instances of #$NaturalHazard which actually cause significant damage are instances of #$NaturalDisaster.  If the hazards are caused by human action, they are not instances of #$NaturalHazard.")
(comment Device-SingleUser "#$Device-SingleUser is a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice.  Each instance of #$Device-SingleUser is a device that typically has exactly one (i.e., one and only one) \"user\" who is the only individual who derives the value of its single function at a single time.  A screwdriver (an instance of  #$Screwdriver) is a #$Device-SingleUser, but a grand piano (an instance of #$GrandPiano) is not.  A borderline non-example is a multiple-passenger car --- although only one person operates it, several can \"use\" it at once, i.e. derive the value of its primary function (transportation).  So a multiple-passenger car is not a #$Device-SingleUser. A borderline example is a telephone -- although it requires two or more users (each on telephones) for meaningful use, each phone generally has just one user at a time.  So a telephone is a #$Device-SingleUser, but a telephone-circuit is not.")
(comment ShapeChangeEvent "A specialization of #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent (q.v.) whose instances are events involving a physical object's changing shape.   A #$ShapeChangeEvent occurs when either (i) the  shape of some (usually more or less \"plastic\") object is changed in a fairly significant way, (ii) an object is created (see #$PhysicalCreationEvent) through a process in which a definite shape is imposed on some material, or (iii) an object is destroyed (see #$PhysicalDestructionEvent) through some process in which its shape is so radically altered that the it can no longer be said to exist.  Examples of these three respective cases include flattening an aluminum can with one's foot, fashioning a figure from clay, and steamrolling a birthday cake.  Shape changes are usually (though not necessarily always) the result of the shapee's being acted upon by another tangible thing (or things).  When a shape change of type (i) or (ii) occurs via the purposeful actions of some agent, the event is a #$ShapingSomething(q.v.).  Note that, in most contexts, very gradual changes in an object's shape -- such as instances of #$Growth-Physical or #$Erosion -- are not #$ShapeChangeEvents.")
(comment ExposureOfOrganismToHarmfulSubstance "The collection of all events in which an instance of #$Organism-Whole comes into 'contact' with an instance of #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance, where 'contact' is loosely construed as any positioning or action that would place the organism at risk of succumbing to a harmful action of the type usually associated with the #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance.  This connotation of 'exposure' is most often used in connection with the exposure of an individual or population to a disease-causing agent, but may also refer to exposure to other hazardous substances, e.g., radioactive material.")
(comment InfectingEvent "The collection of events in which some instance of #$Organism-Whole is infected. The infectious agent can be transmitted from any partially tangible thing. An important specialization of this collection is that of events in which the pathogen comes from an infected host, see #$InfectionTransmissionEvent.")
(comment ProjectileMotion "A specialization of #$Translation-LocationChange.  Each instance of #$ProjectileMotion is a movement event in which no forces other than gravity are acting on the moving object. Notable specializations of #$ProjectileMotion include #$FallingProcess and #$TumblingMotion.")
(comment DisabledPerson "The collection of #$Persons who have an #$AilmentCondition (whether physiological or psychological) that prevents them from functioning normally in the society of which they are a part.")
(comment PersonTypeByPhysiologicalConditionType "A collection of collections. Its members are subsets of #$Person such that all their members are afflicted by the same #$PhysiologicalConditionType. (Note that this may include psychological conditions).")
(comment Movement-Rotation "A specialization of #$MovementEvent.  In each instance of  #$Movement-Rotation the most salient moving object (see  #$primaryObjectMoving) rotates (see #$objectRotating). That is, the object rotates about an axis (see  #$axisOfRotation) that spatially intersects it (or goes  through a hole in it).  Examples include the daily  rotation of the Earth on its axis and the rotation of a  clock hand about its fastened end.  A non-example is the  orbiting of the Earth around the sun, as the axis of the  orbit does not spatially intersect the Earth.")
(comment objectsInMutualContact "The predicate #$objectsInMutualContact indicates that two different objects physically touch in a particular #$PhysicalContactSituation.  (#$objectsInMutualContact SIT OBJ-1 OBJ-2) means that OBJ-1 and OBJ-2 are in contact in the #$PhysicalContactSituation SIT.  For example, a #$ClothingItem and its #$wearer are #$objectsInMutualContact during the wearing.  A father and son in a #$CarryingPiggyback event are #$objectsInMutualContact.  (#$objectsInMutualContact SIT OBJ-1 OBJ-2) entails (#$holdsIn SIT (#$touches OBJ-1 OBJ-2)); #$touches covers both direct touching and touching indirectly (i.e., through a thin layer, e.g., through clothing).")
(comment AttackType "#$AttackType is a specialization of #$TemporalStuffType. Each instance of  #$AttackType is a collection of attacks that are intended to contribute to the weakening of an enemy.")
(comment PersonWithPhysiologicalCondition "The collection of all #$Persons with some kind of #$PhysiologicalCondition. This includes physical and mental conditions. See also #$PersonWithAilmentCondition")
(comment HumanTypeBySexualOrientation "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$PersonTypeByCulture.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of #$HomoSapiens all of whom share a particular sexual preference.")
(comment BorrowingSomething "A collection of events; a subcollection of #$TemporaryChangeOfUserRights.  In an instance of #$BorrowingSomething, an agent takes temporary control of something, usually with the permission of its owner(s).  Generally, the lending agent expects the borrowing agent to use the object for one of its normal functions (see #$intendedBehaviorCapable).")
(comment PreservingFood "A specialization of both #$ManipulatingFoodOrDrink and #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.  Each instance of #$PreservingFood is an event in which a single item of food or drink (an instance of the collection #$FoodOrDrink) is acted on to prevent it from spoiling (see the collection #$Spoiling).")
(comment PumpingGasEvent "The collection of events in which a discrete portion of gasoline is pumped *entirely* (see #$FluidFlow-Translation vs #$Translation-Complete) from a pump into the gas tank of a vehicle.  Every complete #$PumpingGasEvent has a #$subEvents in which #$PumpingFluid is occurring.  Also, every #$PumpingGasEvent has a number of sub-events in which a portion of gas is completely transmitted into a gas tank (see #$Translation-Complete).")
(comment LaneOfRoadway "The approximately one car-width wide part of a roadway designated for a car to stay in.")
(comment Warning "The collection of actions in which something (the #$warner) warns an agent (the #$warnee) about some danger (see #$warningOf).")
(comment placeInCity "(#$placeInCity PLACE CITY) means that the #$Place PLACE has the relationship #$inRegion to the territory of the #$City CITY.")
(comment Conveying-Stationary "A collection of events.  An instance of #$Conveying-Stationary is an event in which one object (in the role of            #$conveyor-Stationary) aids in the translational movement of one or more other objects (having the role(s) of #$transportees).  Note that by definition the  #$conveyor-Stationary does not move along with the #$transportees.")
(comment InterpretingProgramUserInput "The collection of all events in which an instance of #$SoftwareAgent converts information input by an interactive user into a form which can be reasoned with by the system.")
(comment objectField "This relation is intended to capture a subtle but important

feature of logical table schemas: namely, it picks out the logical

field in the schema (possibly corresponding to an 'implicit' field at

the physical level) whose value denotes the thing that the schema is

about. Thus, for example, suppose one had a logical table schema

SCHEMA such that any instantiation constituted a description of a

person in the context of the database. It would therefore be correct

to assert (#$objectField SCHEMA (#$The

#$Person)). In general, then, (#$objectField SCHEMA FIELD)

means that FIELD is the #$IndexicalConcept corresponding to the

instance that SCHEMA actually describes.")
(disjointWith TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType BeliefSystemType)
(comment longerThan "(#$longerThan LONG SHORT) says that the length of LONG is #$greaterThan the length of SHORT.")
(disjointWith ComputerMotherBoard ExpansionCard)
(disjointWith SingleBond TripleBond)
(comment doGetAccessToDataFrom "(#$doGetAccessToDataFrom AGT DATA COMP) means that, from COMP, AGT gets access to the information DATA.  Note that getting access to some data (say, a file) on a system does not necessarily involve opening the file on that system -- it may involve simply being able to copy or write to the file.  See also #$doGetAccessToData.")
(comment InvestmentBank "The collection of all banks that primarily exist to serve investors, rather than savers or borrowers.  In many cases, they do not serve such customers.")
(comment corruptFileOfTypeOn "(#$corruptFileOfTypeOn AGENT FILE-TYPE COMP) means that AGENT corrupts a file of type FILE-TYPE found on the computer COMP.")
(comment KEFacilitationPredicate-New "The collection of instances of #$KEFacilitationPredicate that allow the system to distinguish between a formula that should be known to hold of a term, and constraints on other terms that occur in the formula.")
(comment InterpretingTheUserInput "The collection of all events in which #$Cyc converts information input by an interactive user into a form which can be reasoned with by the system.")
(comment softwareVendorUpdateDownloadLink "(#$softwareVendorUpdateDownloadLink VENDOR URL)   means that the #$SoftwareVendor VENDOR provides a \"one-stop shopping\" web page for   all updates and downloads of its various software products, and the page may be found at URL.")
(comment PhilosophicalTheory "The collection of philosophical theories, broadly intended: a systematic, rationally supported view of some aspect of the world. #$ScientificTheory is a specialization of this, so we don't intend #$PhilosophicalTheory to capture just the extent of the academic discipline called `philosophy' in contemporary Western culture. Minimal criteria that

apply to this notion: an instance of

#$PhilosophicalTheory has to be internally or logically coherent, although many such theories are in fact about the very standards by which coherence is judged. It is not required that a #$PhilosophicalTheory be empirically testable or supported, or that it be formalized or formalizable.")
(comment TakingAGroupOfPeopleHostage "The collection of all events that consist in the taking-hostage of a group of people by some agent.  Once the hostages have been taken, their safety is often used by the hostage taker to bargain with in order to obtain some goal, often a political concession or relief from criminal prosecution.")
(comment DoubleBond "The collection of all #$CovalentBonds in which two pairs of electrons are shared.")
(comment Disappearance-SocialOccurrence "The collection of all incidents in which all or most existing contacts between a #$Person and the circle of their acquaintances (see #$acquaintedWith) are severed, so that the majority of their close friends, associates, colleagues, business partners, etc. do not know where they are or what is happening to them.  Instances should be considered to begin with the 'severing-of-ties' and extend for as long as the condition of general ignorance among affiliates persists.  Instances may or may not be carried out deliberately by the person who does the disappearing.")
(comment CommonVehicleEpidemic "A collection of #$Epidemics each of whose instances are such that the cases constituting the #$Epidemic result from exposure to the same source of the harmful agent. Although the time and place of the exposure need not be the same for all cases of illness that constitute the #$Epidemic, the cases  are caused by exposure to a common source. Harmful agents include drugs, chemical agents, biological toxins, and infectious agents. #$CommonVehicleEpidemics contrast with #$PropagatedEpidemics in which the cases of disease are spread from one case to another.")
(comment keStrongSuggestion-New "(#$keStrongSuggestion-New TERM CONSTRAINT FORMULA) states a strong suggestion that FORMULA should be known to be true about TERM, where FORMULA is an open formula containing one keyword, constraints on which are given in CONSTRAINT.  For example, (#$implies (#$isa ?X #$UnitedStatesPresident) (#$keStrongSuggestion-New ?X (#$isa #$TheUnknownTerm #$Person) (#$knowsAbout #$TheUnknownTerm ?X))) states a strong suggestion that for US Presidents, Cyc learn which things stand in the #$knowsAbout relation to them, where those things are constrainted to be instances of #$Person.")
(comment AcknowledgingUserInput "The collection of all events in which an instance of #$SoftwareAgent acknowledges input from an interactive user of an instance of #$ComputerProcessRunning.")
(disjointWith TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType TemporalObjectType)
(comment TransferringControlOfAnAnimal "In every instance of #$TransferringControlOfAnAnimal, control over some animal is transferred from one agent to another.  This collection is agnostic as to whether the agent that #$losesControl is the animal itself or some other agent.")
(disjointWith DoubleBond SingleBond)
(comment eMailRecipientProgram "A predicate used to relate an instance of #$EMailClientProgram to an instance of #$EMailReceiving.  (#$eMailRecipientProgram RECEIVING MAIL_CLIENT) means that the program MAIL_CLIENT was used to receive the email received in RECEIVING.")
(comment actionFulfillsContract "'(#$actionFulfillsContract ACT CONTRACT)' means that ACT is an #$Action which fulfills, implements, or carries out the contract formulated in the #$ContractingAService CONTRACT.")
(comment CommonVehicleInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic "A collection of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics each of whose instances are such that the cases constituting the #$Epidemic result from exposure to the same source of the infectious agent. The time and place of the exposure need not be the same. If the time and place of the exposure are the same, it is a #$PointSourceInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic. #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics which involve vector-borne transmission or person-person spread are not #$CommonVehicleInfectiousDiseaseEpidemics. #$CommonVehicleInfectiousDiseaseEpidemics typically are food-borne or water-borne. They are also called 'common-source' epidemics.")
(comment AcknowledgingTheUserInput "The collection of all events in which #$Cyc (or an agentive component of #$Cyc) acknowledges input from #$TheUser.")
(disjointWith TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType ProductType)
(comment KillingByMeansOfFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to a specialization of #$PhysicalDevice DEVICE, #$KillingByMeansOfFn returns the specialization of #$KillingByOrganism consisting of all and only those killings in which a device of type DEVICE is used to carry out the killing.")
(comment readFileOfTypeOn "(#$readFileOfTypeOn AGENT FILE-TYPE COMP) means that AGENT reads a file of type FILE-TYPE found on the computer COMP.")
(comment TrainingCamp "The collection of encampments used primarily for training.")
(comment PointSourceInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic "A collection of #$CommonVehicleInfectiousDiseaseEpidemics each of whose instances are such that the cases constituting the epidemic result from exposure to the same source of the infecting agent at about the same time, and usually at the same place. Thus all the cases develop symptoms within one incubation period of the #$Microorganism that causes the infection. For example, an outbreak of food poisoning which occurs after ingesting contaminated egg salad served at a picnic at Stewart Park, Ithaca NY on 7/20/2001 would be an instance of #$PointSourceInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic. Typically food-borne and water-borne transmission routes are involved in #$PointSourceInfectiousDiseaseEpidemics. If the date and time of exposure can be determined, one can calculate the incubation period of the pathogen causing the outbreak. The incubation period is the period of time that elapses from the time of exposure to the time of onset of symptoms.")
(comment SpecifyingAnAIS "The collection of all actions in which an agent [#$Agent-Generic] originally connects a ``meaning'' to an instance of #$AbstractInformationStructure (AIS).  The agent was not aware of a connection between the meaning and the AIS before the action and is so aware afterwards.  Such actions include the expression of propositions into words, an imagined tune into notes, a known fact into a new language or character set, etc.")
(disjointWith TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType HumanCapabilityType)
(comment closerToInSeries "(#$closerToInSeries START CLOSE FAR SERIES)

 says that in the #$Series SERIES, START is closer to CLOSE than it is to FAR.

The notion of \"closer to\" here is not that of #$closerTo, which is spatial.")
(comment Pick-TheTool "The collection of small #$HandTools called \"picks\" used for breaking or scraping away hard materials.  Types of picks include dental picks and fine tools used by archaeologists for carefully scraping the dirt away from a buried find.  A #$PickAxe is a different type of tool.")
(comment EMailCommunication "A specialization of (#$CommunicatingByMeansOfFn #$ComputerNetwork).  Each instance of #$EMailCommunication is an event in which an e-mail message is successfully sent and received.  Thus every instance of #$EMailCommunication has as sub-events both at least one instance of #$EMailSending and at least one instance of #$EMailReceiving. Important specializations include #$SingleEMailCommunication, #$MassEMailCommunication and #$EMailMailingListCommunication.")
(comment ProgramCrashingFault-MalformedSNMPPacket "A program has this fault if the program can be crashed by receiving a malformed SNMP packet.")
(comment SingleEMailCommunication "A specialization of #$EMailCommunication.  Each instance of #$SingleEMailCommunication is an event in which a single e-mail message is successfully sent by one person, and then later received by one other person.  Thus every instance of #$SingleEMailCommunication has as sub-events both exactly one instance of #$EMailSending and exactly one instance of #$EMailReceiving.")
(comment InsecureNetworkInformationFault "A program has this fault if a specially-formed input to it will yield network information for the computer, such as server and domain names, IP addresses etc.")
(disjointWith FourthOrderCollection ThirdOrderCollection)
(comment doGetTrojanProgramToExecuteAsOn "(#$doGetTrojanProgramToExecuteAsOn AGENT CODE ACCOUNT MACHINE) means that AGENT takes steps toward the goal of having CODE executed on MACHINE with the privilege-level of ACCOUNT, where it is understood that AGENT has previously inserted CODE into the filesystem on MACHINE in the appropriate location and under the appropriate name.")
(comment noNotableInstances "(#$noNotableInstances TYPE) says 

that data about particular instances of TYPE is typically less important or interesting (to normal instances of #$IntelligentAgent) than generalizations about TYPE.")
(comment ArrestingSomeone "The collection of all instances of #$TakingAPersonPrisoner
which constitute legally sanctioned arrests by law enforcement
officers.")
(comment locusOfCellularProcess-CellPart "(#$locusOfCellularProcess-CellPart PROCESS CELLPART) says that CELLPART is the instance of #$CellPart

 that plays the role of #$eventOccursAt in the #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel PROCESS.")
(comment ContractingFn "'(#$ContractingFn ACT-TYPE)' picks out the collection of all #$ContractingAService actions in which the type of action contracted for is ACT-TYPE.  For example, '(#$ContractingFn #$Murder)' is the collection of all contractings to commit murder.")
(comment SententialConstituentType "The collection of all subcollections, or types, of #$SententialConstituent. Any instance of this collection is itself a collection of #$SententialConstituents.")
(comment keSalientSpecPredicate "(#$keSalientSpecPredicate PRED) means that PRED stands in
the #$genlPreds relation to another predicate GEN-PRED that has
already been designated as a #$keSalientPredicate, but PRED is a
potentially valuable predicate, example uses for which might prove
useful to a SME. The more general #$keSalientPredicates will appear in an
example sentence for cloning in the Examples page of the UIA, and a
link there will allow a SME to access the example sentences for spec
preds marked as #$keSalientSpecPredicates.")
(disjointWith DoubleBond TripleBond)
(comment Disappearance-FoulPlaySuspected "The collection of all instances of #$Disappearance-SocialOccurrence that are such that one or more persons believe that the person who disappeared (the '#$doneBy' of the disappearance) was a #$maleficiary in the #$Disappearance.")
(comment doGetAccessToDataOfType "(#$doGetAccessToDataOfType AGT DATA-TYPE) means that AGT gets access to a bit of information DATA of type DATA-TYPE stored on a computational system.  Note that getting access to some data (say, a file) on a system does not necessarily involve opening the file on that system -- it may involve simply being able to copy or write to the file.  See also #$doGetAccessToData.")
(comment pathogenCausesEpidemicType "(#$pathogenCausesEpidemicType MICRO-TYPE EPI-TYPE) means every instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI-TYPE is caused by #$Microorganism MICRO-TYPE. This type-level statement can be cashed out as follows. Since every instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic is a group of #$Infections, for each #$Infection that is a member of an instance of EPI-TYPE, many instances of MICRO-TYPE play the role of #$infectionCausedByOrganism in that #$Infection.")
(comment aISSpecifyingSourceCW "(#$aISSpecifyingSourceCW SPECIFYING CW) means that in SPECIFYING [an instance of #$SpecifyingAnAIS], CW [an instance of #$ConceptualWork] was the concept for which an abstract structure [#$AbstractInformationStructure] was specified.")
(comment BinaryChemicalReaction "The collection of all instances of #$ChemicalReaction in which two instances of #$Molecule come together interacting to produce one or two different instances of #$Molecule.")
(comment EMailMessageTextCopy "A specialization of #$ComputerFileCopy. Each instance of #$EMailMessageTextCopy is an #$InformationBearingThing intended to be used in an #$EMailCommunication event.")
(comment BinaryOperatorInProgramFn "(#$BinaryOperatorInProgramFn OPERATOR TERM1 TERM2) refers to the program step

of using a binary operator with args TERM1 and TERM2.")
(comment infoStructureRepresentsSentence "(#$infoStructureRepresentsSentence AIS CYC_SENTENCE) means that using some #$CommunicationConvention, AIS represents the meaning of CYC_SENTENCE, a sentence in CycL [#$CycLSentence].")
(comment polynucleotideStrandsComplementaryBasePaired "(#$polynucleotideStrandsComplementaryBasePaired STRAND1 STRAND2) means that there are hydrogen bonds between paired nucleotides that are the respective components of #$PolynucleotideStrands STRAND1 and STRAND2 and that the nucleotides are complementary (see #$nucleotidesComplementaryBasePaired).")
(comment SimpleChemicalDecomposition "The collection of all instances of #$ChemicalReaction in which a single #$Molecule breaks down (due to incipient energy or catalysis) to produce two different instances of #$Molecule.  If more than two molecules are produced or if several molecules (even of the same type) must break down together, it is a different type of #$ChemicalDecomposition.")
(comment ProgramExpression "This is the collection of all 

   program steps that instantiate a value in some sense. For example,

   calling a function that returns a value can be considered an expression,

   since the value returned can \"stand in\" for the expression in the surrounding

   context of the program.")
(comment interArgResultIsa-Asserted "#$interArgResultIsa-Asserted is a quaternary instance of #$MetaRelation.  It is used to state that a certain complex and partly #$isa -based relationship holds between a given argument to a given function and the corresponding value that is returned when the function is applied to the argument.                                                                                       (#$interArgResultIsa-Asserted FUNC N INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL                                                                                             DEPENDENT-ARG-COL) means that, when a term that is asserted to be                                                                                    an instance of INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL appears as the Nth argument to FUNC,                                                                              then (regardless of what the other arguments to FUNC might be) the value                                                                             (if any) of that function for those arguments is an instance of                                                                                      DEPENDENT-ARG-COL. That is: if INST is asserted to be an instance of                                                                                 INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL and (FUNC ARG(1) ... ARG(N-1) INST ...) = VALUE, then                                                                            VALUE is an instance of DEPENDENT-ARG-COL.  Note that, unlike                                                                                        #$interArgResultIsa assertions, #$interArgResultIsa-Asserted assertions                                                                              will not support assertions of the form (isa VALUE DEPENDENT-ARG-COL)                                                                                unless it is asserted in the Cyc KB that (isa INST INDEPENDENT-ARG-COL).")
(comment SimplyCompoundLeaf "The collection of all leaves that have simple leaflets [#$Leaflet-Plant] all arising from the stem or sole rachis of the leaf.  Compare with #$DoublyCompoundLeaf.")
(comment Appraising "This is the collection of #$Events in which someone (usually an #$Appraiser) estimates the amount that would be paid for a certain object either (a) if it were sold in either a retail or a wholesale context, (b) if a new one had to be bought to replace it, or (c) if one in the same condition had to be bought to replace it.  For relating a #$Product to its appraised value, use #$appraisedValue.")
(comment Meitnerium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is a radioactive piece of #$Meitnerium (element 109).")
(disjointWith RegionTypeBySurfaceGrowth OutdoorLocationTypeByWeather)
(comment ProgramOperator "This is the collection of operators found in programming languages.")
(comment epidemicInfectionType "(#$epidemicInfectionType EPI INF-TYPE) means that every member of the #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI is an instance of the collection of #$Infections INF-TYPE. Thus, this predicate can be used to characterize an instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic by the type of #$Infection constituting each case of that #$Epidemic.")
(comment LeafTypeByStructure "The collection of leaf types by structure: #$SimpleLeaf, #$CompoundLeaf, #$DoublyCompoundLeaf.")
(comment chainEnd "This predicate relates a segmented cordlike object to its ends.")
(comment remoteLoginToAccountViaProgram "#$remoteLoginToAccountViaProgram AGENT COMPUTER ACCOUNT TARGET PROGRAM) means that AGENT uses COMPUTER to log in remotely to ACCOUNT on TARGET via PROGRAM, either with or without authorization.")
(comment hitContractor "'(#$hitContractor HIT AGENT)' means that AGENT contracted the #$MurderForHire HIT.")
(comment infoStructureRepresentsSentenceInCC "(#$infoStructureRepresentsSentenceInCC AIS CYC_SENTENCE CC) means that AIS uses the #$CommunicationConvention CC to represent the meaning of CYC_SENTENCE, a sentence in CycL [#$CycLSentence].")
(comment pathnamePermissions "(#$pathnamePermissions PATHNAME ACCT PERM) means that a user logged on to a #$Computer as ACCT has PERM access to the computer file specified by PATHNAME accessible to that #$Computer.")
(comment MakeFunctionCallInProgramFn "A variable-arity denotational function.

This function denotes program steps that call a previously defined instance of

#$ProgramFunction.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForRelationalNPTersification "This predicate is used to mark rules which clean-up (tersify) the translation of relational nouns.")
(comment ComplianceWithRequest "The collection of all #$PurposefulActions which one agent accepts and completes in compliance with a request from another agent.")
(comment CompoundLeaf "The collection of all leaves that have leaflets [#$Leaflet-Plant].  This includes both the collections #$SimplyCompoundLeaf and #$DoublyCompoundLeaf.")
(comment nodeInFileSharingSystem "A predicate relating instances of #$Computer with instances of #$FileSharingSystem.  (#$nodeInFileSharingSystem COMPUTER FILE-SHARING-SYSTEM) means that users of COMPUTER are can access files on other computers in FILE-SHARING-SYSTEM.")
(comment LiverCell "The collection of #$Cells that are the structural units of the #$Liver. In addition to producing #$BileTheSecretion and #$VitaminA, these cells extract harmful materials and waste products from the blood.")
(comment ProgramFunction "A specialization of #$ProgramStep. This is the collections of all named subroutines that can be

used in computer programs. This includes operators, functions, methods,

procedures, and macros.")
(comment NLQuantFn-3 "(#$NLQuantFn-3 TAG TERM POS-NUMBER) means that TERM appeared in a natural language utterance with the quantification denoted by TAG, in the argument place denoted by POS-NUMBER.  For example, (#$NLQuantFn-3 #$Some-NLAttr #$Dog 0) would mean that some word meaning #$Dog occurred with the quantifier \"some\" in the subject position of an English clause, as in \"Some dogs sleep all day.\" **Work in progress: quantproc overhaul.")
(comment InternallyQueryingKB "The collection of all events of a #$SoftwareAgent asking for some information from some #$KnowledgeBase.")
(comment DoublyCompoundLeaf "The collection of all leaves that have leaflets [#$Leaflet-Plant] which come off of secondary raches of the leaf.  Compare with #$SimplyCompoundLeaf.")
(disjointWith ConfigurationFile ComputerProgram-CW)
(comment DHCPProgram "#$DHCPProgram is the collection of programs that implement the #$DHCPProtocol, including #$DHCPServerPrograms and #$DHCPClientPrograms. Individual dhcp programs typically should be asserted to be instances of one or both of those more specialized collections.")
(comment runProgramOnAs "(#$runProgramOnAs AGENT TARGET PROGRAM ACCOUNT) means that AGENT runs PROGRAM on TARGET with the privileges of ACCOUNT.")
(comment ContentMtFn "This unary and reifiable function takes a structured knowledge source (#$StructuredKnowledgeSource) as its sole argument and denotes a content microtheory (#$SKSIContentMicrotheory) which \"sees\" the contents of the source. It is the function corresponding to the predicate #$contentMt with the canonical argument order.  See #$functionCorrespondingPredicate-Canonical for details.")
(comment SpecificHeat "Specific heat capacity.  (How many calories it takes to increase an object's temperature.)")
(comment epidemicInfectionCases "(#$epidemicInfectionCases EPI CASE) means that the #$Infection CASE is a member of the group of #$Infections constituting the #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI.")
(comment InternallyQueryingCycKB "The collection of all events of #$Cyc asking for some information from some #$CycKB.")
(disjointWith SimplyCompoundLeaf DoublyCompoundLeaf)
(disjointWith FileDirectory ConfigurationFile)
(comment neededUntilPredicateStrengthenerPatch "This predicate is used for documentation purposes, so that we can identify reformulator rules that were added as a work-around until #$DaveS and #$Hagen are able to patch their improvements to the predicate-strengthening code.")
(comment TakingControlOfAGroup "The collection of all instances of #$TransferOfControl in which the #$objectOfControlTransfer is a #$Group.")
(disjointWith HalogenElementType NobleGasElementType)
(comment NFn "A #$CollectionDenotingFunction for denoting the collection of all precisely numbered group of objects of a given type.  See #$GroupOfNFn for the function that creates a unique group of the given cardinality.")
(comment RequestingInformationFromComputerUser "The collection of all events in which some #$SoftwareAgent requests information from some #$ComputerUser.")
(comment collectionOverlapFraction "#$collectionOverlapFraction(COLL1 COLL2 N) states that the fraction of instances of COLL1 which are also instances of COLL2 is N.  Thus, you can state things like 52% of people are female as (#$collectionOverlapFraction #$HomoSapiens #$FemaleHuman 0.52)")
(comment PalmatelyCompoundLeaf "The collection of all leaves that have a set of simple leaflets [#$Leaflet-Plant] all arising from the same point.")
(disjointWith ConfigurationFile LibraryFile)
(comment SNMPProgram "#$SNMPProgram is the collection of programs that implement the #$SimpleNetworkManagementProtocol, including #$SNMPServerPrograms and #$SNMPClientPrograms. Individual snmp programs typically should be asserted to be instances of one or both of those more specialized collections.")
(comment SchemaFieldSetFn "This function defines a #$SKSSchema-Logical \"on the fly\"
in terms of its #$logicalFields.")
(comment HalogenElementType "A specialization of #$ElementStuffTypeByNumberOfProtons.  Each instance of #$HalogenElementType is a type of non-metallic element. The term \"halogen\" means \"salt-former\", and compounds containing instances of halogens are known as \"salts\".  Instances of halogens have 7 electrons in their outer shells. The five natural instances of #$HalogenElementType are are #$Iodine, #$Astatine, #$Bromine, #$Fluorine, and #$Chlorine.  Element 117 would also be an instance if it were created.")
(comment epidemicPathogenType "(#$epidemicPathogenType EPI MICRO-TYPE) means that every member of the #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI is an instance of #$Infection such that it is caused by pathogens of type MICRO-TYPE.")
(disjointWith RequestingInformationFromComputerUser ProgramAction-HumanInitiated)
(comment PinnatelyCompoundLeaf "The collection of all leaves that have pairs of simple leaflets [#$Leaflet-Plant] arising from different points along the rachis/raches of the leaf.")
(comment fileConfiguresSoftware "A binary predicate that relates instances of #$ConfigurationFile with the program, library or package that they configure.  (#$fileConfiguresSoftware FILE SOFTWARE) means that FILE contains configuration information (see #$SoftwareParameter) relevant to the way SOFTWARE executes.")
(comment InsideJob "The collection of criminal acts in which a person closely associated with the victim is either the perpetrator or an accessory.")
(comment Unununium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is #$RadioactiveStuff; typically,
these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment Pentium4 "A specialization of #$PentiumProcessor, #$Pentium4 is the collection of all Pentium4 processors developed by #$IntelCorporation.")
(comment NLDefinitenessFn-3 "(#$NLDefinitenessFn-3 TAG TERM POS-NUMBER) means that TERM appeared in a natural language utterance with the definiteness feature denoted by TAG, in the NP argument position corresponding to POS-NUMBER.  For example, (#$NLDefinitenessFn #$Indefinite-NLAttr #$Dog 0) would mean that some word meaning #$Dog occurred with an indefinite determiner (\"a\" or \"an\") in the first (i.e. subject) position, as in \"A dog barked.\" **This is work in progress for quantproc redesign 12.10.2001. (to self: the original examples are not correct wrt actual use.)")
(disjointWith PinnatelyCompoundLeaf PalmatelyCompoundLeaf)
(comment ExposureOfOrganismToHarmfulSubstanceFn "(#$ExposureOfOrganismToHarmfulSubstanceFn SUBSTANCETYPE) returns the collection of all instances of #$ExposureOfOrganismToHarmfulSubstance in which an #$Organism-Whole plays the role of #$organismExposedToHarmfulSubstance and an instance of SUBSTANCETYPE plays the role of #$harmfulSubstanceExposedTo.")
(comment fileSetsParameterToValueOnComputer "A predicate that relates an instance of #$ConfigurationFile to instances of #$SoftwareParameter, #$CharacterString, and #$ComputationalSystem. (#$fileSetsParameterToValueOnComputer FILE PARAM VALUE COMP) means that on COMP, when the program configured by FILE runs (see #$fileConfiguresSoftware), it runs with the value of PARAM set to VALUE.  For example, if on vega.cyc.com the file /etc/sendmail.cf sets AliasFile to /etc/aliases, it is true that (#$fileSetsParameterToValueOnComputer #$Sendmail-cf-TheConfigurationFile #$SendmailOption-AliasFile \"/etc/aliases\" #$Vega-Cyc-Com).")
(comment hasPartTypes "(#$hasPartTypes IND PART-TYPE) means that the object OBJ has at least one part of type PART-TYPE as a part. Use the predicate #$partTypes to state that every object of a given type has at least one part of PART-TYPE.")
(disjointWith InsideJob PhysiologicalProcess)
(comment FileSharingSystem "#$FileSharingSystem is a specialization of #$ComputationalSystem.  Every instance of #$FileSharingSystem is such that each node in it shares files with the other nodes in it.  See #$nodeInFileSharingSystem and #$Filesystem.")
(comment Ununbium "A collection of pieces of material. Each piece is #$RadioactiveStuff; typically,
these will be tightly bound into solid form.")
(comment ProgramBlockFn "The function is used to denote sequences of program actions.")
(comment PentiumProcessor "A specialization of #$Microprocessor, #$PentiumProcessor is the collection of all Pentium processors developed by #$IntelCorporation.")
(comment MoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies "A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection of #$Molecules characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules with exactly the same chemical formula and structure.")
(comment infectingPathogenType "(#$infectingPathogenType EVT MICRO-TYPE) means that during #$InfectingEvent EVT a #$Mob of #$Microorganisms is transmitted to and infects a new host and every member of that mob is an instance of #$Microorganism MICRO-TYPE. See #$infectingPathogen.")
(comment RequestingInformationFromTheUser "The collection of all events of #$Cyc asking for some information from #$TheUser.")
(comment organismExposedToHarmfulSubstance "(#$organismExposed EXPOSING ORG) means that ORG is an
organism exposed to the #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance that is the
#$harmfulSubstanceExposedTo in EXPOSING.")
(comment TransferringCustodyOfAPerson "The collection of all instances of #$TransferOfControl in which legal custody of a #$Person is transferred from one agent to another.")
(disjointWith InsideJob BiologicalEvent)
(comment FileSavingProgram "The collection of programs used in #$SavingAFile events.")
(comment KillingByDeviceType "#$KillingByDeviceType is a faceting of #$KillingByOrganism.  Each instance is a specialization of #$KillingByOrganism whose membership is defined in terms of the device used to carry out the killing.")
(comment AnglicanPerson "The collection of people who adhere to a faith in the #$AnglicanReligion.")
(comment OrganizationNamedFn "(#$OrganizationNamedFn NAME) denots the #$Organization whose name is the string NAME")
(disjointWith SoftwareParameter Microtheory)
(comment SimpleLeaf "The collection of all leaves that have no leaflets [#$Leaflet-Plant].")
(comment SendmailOption "A specialization of #$SoftwareParameter.  Instances of this collection are options that can be set in #$Sendmail-cf-TheConfigurationFile.")
(disjointWith InsideJob TranslationAlongInternalLivingStructure)
(comment NetworkManagementProgram "The collection of programs that are used to manage computer networks by monitoring network activity, managing network devices

and resources.")
(comment Cattle-DomesticatedTypeByBreed "A collection of collections. Each instance is a collection of cattle all belonging to the same breed.")
(comment SoftwareParameter "The collection of all parameters or variables used in computer systems, either by the operating system or by a program.  The value of an instance of #$SoftwareParameter may be set [#$SettingSoftwareParameter] or read [#$ReadingSoftwareParameter].  (#$softwareParameterValue SOFTWARE-PARAMETER VALUE) means that SOFTWARE-PARAMETER has the value VALUE in the current context. (#$softwareParameterValueInProgram SOFTWARE-PARAMETER VALUE COMPUTER-PROGRAM-RUNNING) means that SOFTWARE-PARAMETER currently has the value VALUE in the program COMPUTER-PROGRAM-RUNNING.")
(disjointWith CompoundLeaf SimpleLeaf)
(comment DatabaseProgram "A specialization of #$ApplicationProgram. Each instance of this collection is an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW which has something (where this is deliberately left vague) to do with database usage or maintenance. Its major specializations are #$DatabaseServerProgram and #$DatabaseClientProgram (though the odd case will not fit under either of these -- for example programs which repair fragmented databases). See also #$Database-Physical, #$Database-AbstractContent.")
(comment Stealing-InsideJob "The collection of thefts in which a person closely associated with the victim is either the thief or an accessory to the theft.")
(comment FileExecutionFault-Remote "A type of #$ProgramFault. A program  has this fault if a malicious user can exploit the program to run executables  existing on some machine other than the one running the program (for example, machines in a web client relationship with the machine running the program).")
(disjointWith SoftwareParameter BeliefSystem)
(comment Leaflet-Plant "The collection of all segments of compound leaves [#$CompoundLeaf].  Each leaflet has the shape of a leaf.")
(comment hydrogenBondBetweenCapable "(#$hydrogenBondBetweenCapable INS1 INS2) means that INS1 (an instance of #$ChemicalObject) can form a hydrogen bond with INS2, where 'can' means that it is chemically possible.  Instance-level version of #$typesHydrogenBondBetweenCapable.")
(comment softwareOfProcess "(#$softwareOfProcess COMPUTER_PROCESS SOFTWARE) means that COMPUTER_PROCESS is executing some instantiation of SOFTWARE. If the process is an instance of computer program running and the software is an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW, use the more specific predicate, #$programOfProcess.")
(comment Aurochs "The extinct single common ancestor of every breed of #$Cattle-Domestic.")
(comment PlaceNamedFn "(#$PlaceNamedFn NAME) denots the #$Place whose name is the string NAME")
(disjointWith MoleculeTypeByChemicalSpecies AminoAcidTypeByChemicalSpecies)
(comment SettingSoftwareParameter "The collection of all #$ProgramActions in which the value of an instance of #$SoftwareParameter is set.  This normally involves the value being changed, but it includes instances when the value is ``overwritten'' with its old value.")
(comment ReadingSoftwareParameter "The collection of all events in which the value of an instance of #$SoftwareParameter is read by a #$ComputerProcessRunning.")
(comment SpindlePole "The collection of the configuaration of centrosomes and
microtubules in a cell during mitosis. The pair of centrosomes radiate
microtubules to form the mitotic spindle during the prophase of
mitosis. The microtubules bind to the chromosomes and later guide the
chomosomes to the spindle poles during #$Anaphase.")
(comment runsKernel "(#$runsKernel COMPUTER KERNEL) means that the individual #$Computer COMPUTER is running an #$OperatingSystem built around the  #$OperatingSystemKernel KERNEL.")
(comment minimizeCollectionExtent "(#$minimizeCollectionExtent COLL)

 means that *negation-by-failure* should always be non-nil for queries

 of the form (isa ?X COLL).  This predicate is also used by the UIA to

 generate drop down lists that can be added to.")
(comment BinaryProgramOperator "This is the collection of operators found in programming languages.")
(comment IntegratedCircuit "A specialization of #$SemiconductorDevice.  Each instance of #$IntegratedCircuit is a device that contains more than one component and is fabricated on a silicon wafer.")
(comment InfectingEvent-DirectTransmission "The collection of #$InfectingEvents in which there is a direct and immediate transfer of an infectious agent or pathogen (see #$Microorganism) to a receptive portal (see #$infectingOccursAt) through which an #$Organism-Whole becomes infected.  Examples include transferring pathogens via touching, kissing, biting, sexual intercourse, projection of droplet spray into mucous membranes, direct exposure of tissue to agents in soil, and transplacental transmission. Contrast with #$InfectingEvent-IndirectTransmission.")
(disjointWith Line-Straight-Directed Line-Straight)
(comment InterArgIsaGenlPredicate "Those instances of both #$TernaryPredicate and #$ArgGenlPredicate used to specify the conditional #$genls requirement of one argument (the dependent argument) of a #$Relation given the #$isa of another argument (the independent argument).  The arg1 is the #$Relation.  The arg2 is the #$isa #$Collection of the independent argument; this defines the antecedent of the conditional constraint.  The arg3 is the #$genls #$Collection required of the dependent argument when the antecedent is satsifed (that is, when the independent argument has the arg2 #$Collection as an #$isa).")
(comment BuryingSomeoneAlive "This is the subcollection of #$BuryingSomething in which the thing buried is a living #$Person.")
(comment microprocessorArchitecture "(#$microprocessorArchitecture CHIP ARCHITECTURE) means that the microprocessor CHIP implements ARCHITECTURE.")
(comment InfectingEvent-IndirectTransmission "The collection of #$InfectingEvents in which there is an indirect transfer of an infectious agent or pathogen (see #$Microorganism) via some intermediary to a receptive portal (see #$infectingOccursAt) through which an #$Organism-Whole becomes infected. The intermediary can be inanimate or living, and if living may itself be infected or not. Contrast with #$InfectingEvent-DirectTransmission. The major subcollections are #$InfectingEvent-VehicleBorneTransmission, #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmission, and #$InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmission.")
(comment CreatingNewConceptInCyc "The collection of all actions in which a #$Cyclist (including #$Cyc) creates new terms in Cyc.")
(disjointWith Line-Straight-Directed LineSegment-Straight)
(comment MurderingSomeoneByDrowning "This is the subcollection of #$Murder in which the victim dies by #$Drowning.")
(comment InfectingEvent-VehicleBorneTransmission "The collection of #$InfectingEvent-IndirectTransmissions in which contaminated inanimate objects or substances serve as an intermediate means by which an infectious agent is transported to receptive portal (see #$infectingOccursAt) through which an #$Organism-Whole may become infected. The infectious agent may or may not have multiplied on or in the vehicle before being transmitted. Since the vehicle is inanimate, the vehicle cannot itself become infected. Potential vehicles of infection include toys, bedding, eating utensils and surgical instruments; substances such as food, water, milk; and biological products such as blood, plasma, tissue.")
(comment MadeForTVMovie "A collection of TV shows [#$TVShow-CW].  Instances of #$MadeForTVMovie are movies like those shown in a movie theater except that they are created instead for the purpose of #$TVTransmitting.")
(comment DeterminingTypeOfKnowledgeNeeded "The collection of all actions in which an agent determines the type of knowledge needed to complete a given task.  After such an act is complete, the agent is likely to attmept to determine facts that match the type of knowledge needed or to communicate the knowledge template to others so that they may solve the problem.")
(disjointWith Line-Straight-Directed Ray-Geometrical)
(comment constructStream "(#$constructStream AGENT STREAM) means that AGENT writes a STREAM.")
(disjointWith WordProcessingProgram DocumentViewerProgram)
(comment Line-Straight-Directed "The collection of all straight lines combined with an associated intrinsic direction.  #$Line-Straight-Directed is not a specialization of #$Line-Straight, since only one #$Line-Straight can pass through a given point and be parallel to another line in a Euclidean space.  Two instances of #$Line-Straight-Directed have this property.")
(disjointWith Arson CreatingAnArtifact)
(comment OpenCycDefinitionalPredicate "The collection of predicates considered \"definitional\" for the purposes of the review of #$PublicConstants being done in preparation for OpenCyc.  Where CONST is a #$PublicConstant, a \"definitional GAF\" for CONST is any asserted #$CycLClosedAtomicSentence (PRED CONST ARG2..ARGN) such that PRED is an #$OpenCycDefinitionalPredicate.  See also #$PublicConstant-DefinitionalGAFsOK.")
(disjointWith Arson TakingCareOfSomething)
(comment preservesIsaInArg "(#$preservesIsaInArg FUNC N) means that a non-atomic reified term (NART) created by means of FUNC is an instance of any collection that its Nth argument of FUNC.")
(comment infectingVehicle "(#$infectingVehicle INFECTING SOURCE) means that during the #$InfectingEvent-VehicleBorneTransmission INFECTING, SOURCE is the intermediary that serves as the means of transmission of the pathogen to the new host. The vehicle must be inanimate. If the source of the pathogen is an #$Organism-Whole, then the source is a vector (see #$InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmission).")
(comment undirectedLine "(#$undirectedLine DIRECTED_STRAIGHT_LINE STRAIGHT_LINE) means that STRAIGHT_LINE is the instance of #$Line-Straight that is combined with an orientation in DIRECTED_STRAIGHT_LINE, an instance of #$Line-Straight-Directed.")
(comment CycUIAUser "The collection of all users of the #$UIA-CycProgram")
(comment hitWeaponUsed "'(#$hitWeaponUsed HIT WEAPON)' means that WEAPON is a weapon used in the #$MurderForHire HIT.")
(comment SKSIContentMicrotheory "This is the collection of all content microtheories associated with structured knowledge sources integrated within Cyc.  Microtheories in this collection provide \"windows\" into the information withing a knowledge source.  That is, whenever a query is asked within a microtheory in this collection (or is asked in any microtheory that is a specialization of a microtheory in this collection) the inference engine has access to the content of the structured knowledge source associated with the content microtheory when answering the query.")
(comment CodonTypeByChemicalStructure "The collection of all types of codons [#$Codon-MolecularSegment] that are solely differentiated by their chemical structure.")
(comment WordProcessingProgram-Interactive "#$WordProcessingProgram-Interactive is a specialization of #$WordProcessingProgram. It is the collection of computer programs whose primary function is the production, manipulation, and editing of text under the interactive direction of the user of the program.  The most significant specialization of this collection is #$WordProcessingProgram-Visual.")
(comment BufferOverflowStringFn "This function takes an instance of a #$ComputerProgram-CW, PROG, as an argument and returns an instance of #$ComputerFile-CW which is designed to exploit the buffer overflow fault (#$BufferOverflowFault-CommandExecution or #$BufferOverflowFault-ProgramCrashing) of PROG.  This file contains a data string that is larger than the buffer for the program can handle, and is designed to be read as input to the program via a function in the program that does not perform bounds checking.  By inputting this file to the program, a hacker can push commands into the execution stack of the computer on which the program is running, and overwrite the return address so that it points back into the buffer.")
(disjointWith Arson Conveying-Generic)
(comment ConcealingInTypeFn "A collection-denoting function.  (#$ConcealingInTypeFn CONTAINER) returns

the collection of all events in which something is hidden in a container

of type CONTAINER, and, as a result, is completely concealed from view.")
(comment Line-Directed "The collection of all instances of #$Line (whether curved or not) combined with an associated intrinsic direction.")
(comment LoopTerminatingTransitivePredicate "The collection of all #$TransitiveBinaryPredicates such that there is always an arg2 for any arg1 such that that arg2 can be used in the arg1 position in a recursive manner and only in a recursive manner.  For example, #$temporallySubsumes (a #$TimePoint) and #$compatibleBloodTypes (#$BloodTypeO).")
(comment ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies "A type-level collection. Each instance is a collection of #$ChemicalObjects characterized by the fact that all of its instances are molecules with exactly the same chemical formula and structure.  If two chemical objects have the same chemical formula and structure they will be instances of the same instance of #$ChemicalObjectTypeByChemicalSpecies regardless of whether they differ in ionization level, or state of matter.")
(comment transitiveClosureForPredicate "(#$transitiveClosureForPredicate PRED THING) means that (PRED THING THING) and for any ARG1 for which (PRED ARG1 AG2) is true, (PRED ARG1 THING) is also true.")
(comment AgentTypeByEmotionalState "A collection of collections of #$IntelligentAgents. Instances are collections of agents characterized by being in certain emotional state. Examples include #$Angry, #$Excited, and #$Hopeful.")
(comment extConceptOverlapsColAndReln "(#$extConceptOverlapsColAndReln COL RELN SOURCE STRING) means
that the external structured data source SOURCE variously uses the term
named by STRING as a value that semantically maps to the Cyc #$Collection
COL, and as a slot that maps to the Cyc #$BinaryPredicate RELN.")
(comment SingleLevelTransitivePredicate "The collection of all #$TransitiveBinaryPredicates in whose extent the arg2s are related via the predicate only to themselves.  For example, #$x-Component, #$vectorDirection.")
(comment objectTaken "'(#$objectTaken TAKING OBJECT)' means that OBJECT is the #$PartiallyTangible thing taken in the #$TakingSomething TAKING.")
(comment hasAgentsIn "(#$hasAgentsIn GROUP ORG) means that at least one member
of ORG (see #$hasMembers) is also a #$groupMembers of GROUP, although
no formal association between GROUP and ORG exists.")
(comment programFunctionIdentifier "(#$programFunctionIdentifier FOO \"foo\") means that the name of the function FOO is \"foo\" in the
current context.")
(comment NonTerminatingTransitivePredicate "The collection of all antisymmetric #$TransitiveBinaryPredicates such that if (PRED ARG1 ARG2) there exists an ARG3 different from ARG1 and ARG2 such that (PRED ARG2 ARG3).")
(comment Mousse "A sweet dessert made with whipped cream, gelatin, and flavoring.")
(comment programFunctionBody "(#$programFunctionBody FOO BODY) means that the calls of the function FOO, will mean the program step(s) of BODY will be executed. Normally the function body is a sequence of steps rather than a single step.")
(comment Hopeful "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being hopeful. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment RecruitingActivity "The collection of all actions in which an #$IntelligentAgent attempts to persuade one or more #$IntelligentAgents to join an #$Organization or take part in an activity directed by some #$Organization.")
(comment feelsEmotion "(#$feelsEmotion AGENT FEELING) means that AGENT has the #$FeelingAttribute FEELING. For example (#$feelsEmotion AGENT (#$HighAmountFn #$Happiness)) means that AGENT is feeling a high amount of happiness.")
(disjointWith LoopTerminatingTransitivePredicate NonTerminatingTransitivePredicate)
(comment FaultVulnerabilityPredicate "A specialization of #$BinaryPredicate.  Each instance of #$FaultVulnerabilityPredicate is a predicate that relates an instance of #$ProgramFaultAttribute to an instance of #$ComputerVulnerabilityAttribute, where the fault in some circumstances creates the vulnerability.")
(comment infiltrates "A specialization of #$hasAgentsIn.  In addition to implying
that (#$hasAgentsIn GROUP ORG), (#$infiltrates GROUP ORG) implies that
any member of ORG (see #$hasMembers) who is not a #$groupMembers of
GROUP does not know (see #$knows) that (#$hasAgentsIn GROUP ORG).")
(comment VisualProgrammingLanguage "A specialization of #$AbstractProgrammingLanguage, #$VisualProgrammingLanguage is the collection of  programming languages that allow users to specify programs in a manner that uses two or more dimensions. Conventional textual languages are not considered two-dimensional -- #$Compilers or #$Interpreter-Computers process them as one-dimensional streams of characters. Visual programming languages allows programming with visual expressions, such as spatial arrangements of textual and graphical symbols.")
(comment typesChemicalBondBetweenCapable "(#$typesChemicalBondBetweenCapable COL1 COL2) means that it is chemically possible for instances of COL1 to form chemical bonds with instances of COL2.")
(comment Sad "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being sad. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment softwareParameterValue "(#$softwareParameterValue SOFTWARE-PARAMETER VALUE) means that SOFTWARE-PARAMETER has the value VALUE in the current context.  See #$softwareParameterValueInProgram for a #$TernaryPredicate that specifies the #$ComputerProcessRunning that determines the context.")
(comment agentRecruited "(#$agentRecruited RECRUITING RECRUIT) means that RECRUIT agrees to be recruited by the #$RecruitingActivity RECRUITING, with the agreement taking place at some point after RECRUITING has started. 'Agrees to be recruited' in this context means either agreeing, at a minimum, to be a #$deliberateActors in the #$enterpriseRecruitedFor or a member (#$hasMembers) of the #$recruitingOrganization.")
(disjointWith OrderingPredicate SingleLevelTransitivePredicate)
(comment ImmersionOfInFn "(#$ImmersionOfInFn SOLID_TYPE FLUID_TYPE) returns the collection of all instances of #$SolidEnteringFluid in which the #$entersFluid is an instance of SOLID_TYPE and the #$fluidTypeEntered is LIQUID_TYPE.")
(comment fileDoesNotSetParameterToValueOnComputer "A predicate that relates an instance of #$ConfigurationFile to instances of #$SoftwareParameter, #$CharacterString, and #$ComputationalSystem. (#$fileDoesNotSetParameterToValueOnComputer FILE PARAM VALUE COMP) means that on COMP, when the program configured by FILE runs (see #$fileConfiguresSoftware), it runs with the value of PARAM set by FILE to some value other than VALUE.  For example, if on vega.cyc.com the file /etc/sendmail.cf sets AliasFile to /etc/aliases, it is true that (#$fileDoesNotSetParameterToValueOnComputer #$Sendmail-cf-TheConfigurationFile #$SendmailOption-AliasFile \"/etc/mail/aliases\" #$Vega-Cyc-Com).")
(comment VisualProgrammingEnvironment "Programs that allow the use of visual expressions (such as graphics, drawings, animation or icons) in the process of programming. A notable example is #$MSVisualStudio.")
(comment programFunctionArity "(#$programFunctionArity FOO N) means that the function FOO takes N parameters or arguments.")
(comment Dissatisfied "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being dissatisfied. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment softwareParameterValueInProgram "(#$softwareParameterValueInProgram SOFTWARE-PARAMETER VALUE COMPUTER-PROCESS-RUNNING) means that SOFTWARE-PARAMETER has the value VALUE in the program COMPUTER-PROCESS-RUNNING.  See #$softwareParameterValue for a #$BinaryPredicate that uses a default context.")
(comment eMailPrecedence "A predicate for relating an email message to the character string that appears in its \"Precedence:\" header. (#$eMailPrecedence MSG PRECEDENCE) means that the #$EMailMessage, MSG, has PRECEDENCE, an instance of #$CharacterString, as as the entry in its \"Precedence:\" header.   The \"Precedence:\" header can be used as a crude control of message priority. It tweaks the sort order in the queue and can be configured to change the message timeout values.")
(comment DirectoryServerProgram "a type of #$ServerProgram which checks permissions and, where appropriate, delivers access to the files and data (whatever application they were created by) on a given network. Many such programs implement the popular #$LightweightDirectoryAccessProtocol.")
(comment programFunctionArg "(#$programFunctionArg FOO 3 X Char-theDataType) means that function FOO takes 
a character as its third argument.")
(comment hitTarget "'(#$hitTarget HIT VICTIM)' means that VICTIM is the person killed in the #$MurderForHire HIT.")
(comment Frustrated "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being frustrated. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment reformulatorTestCaseMicrotheory "(#$reformulatorTestCaseMicrotheory TESTCASE MT)
means that the #$ReformulatorTestCase TESTCASE has MT as the
microtheory in which its reformulation testing will be performed.")
(comment synonymousRelnArgs "(#$synonymousRelnArgs RELN SOURCE LIST) means that when it is known that (#$synonymousExternalConcept RELN SOURCE STRING) or (#$overlappingExternalConcept RELN SOURCE STRING) and STRING appears with an associated set of arguments in an output deriving from SOURCE, the appropriate argument order to observe on the corresponding Cyc relation RELN is given by LIST.  For example suppose (#$synonymousExternalConcept #$ethnicity #$SRATemplateExtractionOntology 'NATIONALITY') and suppose NATIONALITY appears in an #$SRATemplateExtractionOntology mediated output with the arguments 'Sudanese' 'Abu Doha' in that order and , where additional mapping info tells us that 'Abu Doha' corresponds to AbuDoha and 'Sudanese' to #$EthnicGroupOfSudaneseArabs.  (#$synonymousRelnArgs #$ethnicity #$SRATemplateExtractionOntology (TheList 2 1) means that AbuDoha (corresponding to the second argument associated with NATIONALITY) should appear as the first argument to #$ethnicity, and #$EthnicGroupOfSudaneseArabs (corresponding to the first argument shown with NATIONALITY) should appear as the second argument to #$ethnicity.")
(comment resultTypeGenlArg "(#$resultTypeGenlArg FUNC N) means that FUNC always returns a collection type TYPE such that (#$typeGenls TYPE COL), where COL is the Nth argument of FUNC. That is, the value of FUNC for any appropriate sequence of arguments is a collection of collections, each instance of which is a subcollection of the Nth item in that sequence. Symbolically, (typeGenls (FUNC ARG1..ARGN..) ARGN).")
(comment immersedInFluid "'(#$immersedInFluid THING TYPE)' means that THING is fully immersed in fluid of type TYPE.  This is a type-level--in its second argument--version of #$in-ImmersedFully.  Usually, we are not interested in the specific bit of water or air that we are immersed in, but we are intensely interested in the type of fluid.")
(comment PaymentThroughActionTypeFn "Where ACT_TYPE is a specialization of #$PurposefulAction, (#$PaymentThroughActionTypeFn ACT_TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$Paying that employ ACT_TYPE as the means by which payment is delivered.  Consequently, any instance of (#$PaymentThroughActionTypeFn ACT_TYPE) will include an instance of ACT_TYPE as a sub-event (see the predicate #$subEvents).")
(comment InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmission "The collection of #$InfectingEvent-IndirectTransmissions in which either a #$Vertebrate or #$Invertebrate animal serves as the intermediary (a vector) by which an infectious agent is carried to and infects a susceptible host.")
(comment Bored "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being bored. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment reformulatorTestCaseRequiresRecursion "This is a predicate to indicate that a test case
requires recursion, and thus should be run through the
Reformulator Hub, and not through the relevant #$RLModule
directly.  If the RL module applies to a subformula of
the input expression, and not the entire input expression,
label it with this predicate.")
(comment MilitantBeliefs "The collection of political ideologies that accept and advocate initiating violence as a legitimate solution to otherwise non-violent religious, cultural, and political disputes in which agression has not been threatened.  Examples include #$Trotskyism, #$Maoism, and #$GermanNaziIdeology.")
(comment NuclearFuel "A specialization of #$NuclearRelatedMaterial and #$EnergyStuff.  Each instance of #$NuclearFuel is some radioactive substance that can be used as an energy source in a nuclear reactor or a nuclear weapon.")
(comment XMLCommandExecutionFault "#$XMLCommandExecutionFault is an attribute of some instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW. A program has an #$XMLCommandExecutionFault if an unauthorized person can pass XML code to it and have it execute arbitrary commands.")
(disjointWith InfectingEvent-VehicleBorneTransmission InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmission)
(comment Disgusted "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being disgusted. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment reformulatorTestCaseSettings "(#$reformulatorTestCaseSettings TESTCASE SETTINGS)
means that the #$ReformulatorTestCase TESTCASE has SETTINGS as the
settings under which its reformulation testing will be performed.")
(comment ChiefTechnologyOfficer "A collection of people (a sub-collection of #$BusinessPerson). The #$ChiefTechnologyOfficer is the head of the technology development within a corporate organization (not necessarily a business, although Cyc's current representation tends to assume a business context).  See also, #$ChiefExecutiveOfficer, #$ChiefFinancialOfficer, and #$President-CorporateOfficer")
(disjointWith SolidEnteringFluid PuttingSomethingOnto)
(comment PaymentByDeliveryType "An instance of #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType.  Each instance of #$PaymentByDeliveryType is a sub-collection of #$Paying characterized by use of a specific type of delivery of payment, such as #$TransportationEvent (q.v.) or wire transfer of funds.")
(comment PoisoningTypeByAgentType "A #$CollectionType (collection of collections) and a covering on #$Poisoning.  Each instance is a collection of poisonings whose instances have the common feature of a particular type of substance being involved, e.g. poisoning by cyanide.")
(comment UnaryProgramOperator "This is the collection of unary operators found in programming languages.

For example, the \"++\" operator in the C language is an unary operator.")
(comment Restless "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being restless. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment ReformulatorTestCaseFn "(#$ReformulatorTestCaseFn NUM) denotes a

general #$ReformulatorTestCase.  For test cases which test a specific

#$RLModule, use #$RLModuleTestCaseFn instead.  NUM is a unique identifier to distinguish different reformulator tests.")
(comment Subcommittee-Organization "The collection of all subcommittees formally organized by their parent committees (instances of #$Committee-Organization), usually to accomplish tasks or address issues determined by their parent committees. Typically, subcommittees are formed in order to divide up large tasks or issues addressed by the parent committee into smaller tasks or issues to be addressed by the subcommittee and reported back to the parent committee. Instances of #$Subcommittee-Organization usually operate in accordance with rules or procedures inherited from or determined by their parent committees. Each instance of #$Subcommittee-Organization consists of at least two (and perhaps many) individual #$CommitteeMembers and may, in certain instances, include a #$CommitteeChairman. Note that since a subcommittee is itself a committee, the collection #$Subcommittee-Organization is a subcollection of #$Committee-Organization. However one salient difference between the two is that every instance of #$Subcommittee-Organization necessarily bears the relation #$subOrganizations with a unique instance of #$Committee-Organization, while not every committee must have subcommittees.")
(comment resultTypeGenl "(#$resultTypeGenl FUNCTION COLLECTION) means that the result of applying FUNCTION to a set of arguments is a collection each of whose elements is a spec of COLLECTION.  So (#$resultTypeGenl FUNCTION COLLECTION) entails for any set of arguments, ARGS, (#$typeGenls (FUNCTION . ARGS) COLLECTION).  FUNCTION is permitted to be an indexical function with no arguments (e.g. EndangeredSpeciesFn) if such are created.")
(disjointWith SolidEnteringFluid PedestrianSportsEvent)
(comment SendmailParameter "A specialization of #$SoftwareParameter.  Instances of this collection are options that can be set in #$Sendmail-cf-TheConfigurationFile.")
(comment fieldEncoding "This predicate defines how a logical field
in a logical schema is interpreted and given a physical value in a
corresponding physical schema.  The sentence (#$fieldEncoding
PHYSICAL-SCHEMA PF-INDEXICAL LOGICAL-SCHEMA ENCODING-EXPRESSION) is used
to state an ENCODING-EXPRESSION, which is one of the term-level
translation templates (encodings) from LOGICAL-SCHEMA into
PHYSICAL-SCHEMA. More precisely, ENCODING-EXPRESSION expresses a
translation in terms of some of the the logical fields of LOGICAL-SCHEMA
into a physically encoded term suitable for PF-INDEXICAL in
PHYSICAL-SCHEMA.")
(comment BiologicalAttackEpidemic "#$BiologicalAttackEpidemic is a collection of #$Epidemics, each instance of which is the result of an instance of #$BiologicalAttack.")
(comment ProgramArithmeticOperator "This is the collection of arithmetical operators found in programming languages.

For example, the \"++\" increment operator in the C programming language is arithmetical.")
(comment HiringAHitman "This is the scene in the #$MurderForHire script in which the #$hitContractor hires the #$hitman.")
(comment Surprised "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being surprised. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment RLModuleTestCaseFn "(#$RLModuleTestCaseFn RLMODULE NUM) denotes a

#$ReformulatorTestCase specifically designed to test the #$RLModule

RLMODULE.  For general reformulator tests which do not test a specific

#$RLModule, use #$ReformulatorTestCaseFn instead.  NUM is a unique identifier to distinguish different tests

for the same RL module.")
(comment LocalDeliveryAgent "Programs used on an e-mail recipient's local machine to filter and sort received e-mail before it is stored in the user's local directory and accessed by the user's #$EMailClientProgram.  A very popular local delivery agent is #$Procmail-TheProgram.")
(comment WireTransferOfFunds "The collection of all instances of #$InformationTransferEvent-Electronic in which funds are wired from one agent's account to another agent's account by electronic means, without any withdrawal or deposit of physical #$TenderObjects.")
(disjointWith SolidEnteringFluid WindProcess)
(comment DatabaseClientProgram "A specialization of #$DatabaseProgram. Each instance of this collection is some instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW which presents information taken from a database (or databases) to the user -- often mediating between the user and one or more #$DatabaseServerProgram.")
(comment SPECint "A function and an instance of #$UnitOfCPUCapacity. It is used to represent a unit (or \"benchmark\") of computer processor capacity, invented by the \"Standard Performance Evaluation Corporation\". The #$SPECint benchmark represents speed and efficiency in performing integer operations. See also #$SPECfp -- for floating point operations. It should be noted that different versions of this standard exist, not necessarily intertranslateable.")
(comment PlanningTheKilling "This is the scene in the #$MurderForHire script in which the #$hitman plans the crime, including choosing the #$hitWeaponUsed.")
(comment Resentful "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being resentful. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment reformulatorTestCaseModuleTested "(#$reformulatorTestCaseModuleTested TESTCASE RLMODULE)
means that TESTCASE is a test case for the #$RLModule RLMODULE.")
(comment InternetMailAccessServerProgram "Programs whose processes are initiated by an e-mail recipient's #$EMailClientProgram, and which retrieve mail for the recipient from the location in which it has been stored by an #$SMTPServerProgram.  Internet mail access servers are typically either #$POPServerPrograms or #$IMAPServerPrograms.")
(disjointWith SolidEnteringFluid MakingWrittenMaterial)
(comment registryKeyNotSetToValueOnComputer "(#$registryKeyNotSetToValueOnComputer KEY VALUE COMP) means that, on the #$Computer COMP, the #$RegistryKey KEY in the #$WindowsRegistry found on COMP is not set to VALUE, or such a key does not exist.  This relation is the negation of #$registryKeySetToValueOnComputer.")
(comment epidemicResultsFromAttack "(#$epidemicResultsFromAttack EPI ATTACK) means that the instance of #$BiologicalAttackEpidemic EPI is the result of the instance of #$BiologicalAttack ATTACK.")
(comment ContractMurder "This is the scene in the #$MurderForHire script in which the #$hitman carries out the #$Murder.")
(comment Nervous "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being nervous. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment reformulatorTestCaseOutputExpression "(#$reformulatorTestCaseOutputExpression TESTCASE EXPR)

means that the #$ReformulatorTestCase TESTCASE has EXPR as its

expected output #$CycLExpression.  EXPR will be compared against

the result returned by the reformulator.")
(comment BalloonMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements requiring a #$BalloonPayment at the end of their terms.")
(comment IntelligenceAgent "The collection consisting of every #$Professional-Adult
who is an #$employees of some #$GovernmentIntelligenceOrganization.")
(comment ProgramRelationalOperator "This is the collection of relational operators found in programming languages.

For example, the \">=\" operator in the C programming language is relational.")
(comment PayingTheHitman "This is the scene in the #$MurderForHire script in which the #$hitContractor pays the #$hitman.")
(comment infectingVector "(#$infectingVector INFECTING VECTOR) means that during the #$InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmission INFECTING, VECTOR is the animal vector that serves as the intermediate means of transmission of the pathogen to the new host. The vector may or may not itself be infected with the pathogen.")
(comment Happy "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being happy. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment reformulatorTestCaseInputExpression "(#$reformulatorTestCaseInputExpression TESTCASE EXPR)
means that the #$ReformulatorTestCase TESTCASE has EXPR as its
input #$CycLExpression.  EXPR is the input that will be provided
to the #$CycLReformulator when testing TESTCASE.")
(comment BiweeklyMortgage "The collection of #$MortgageAgreements that are fixed-rate and have a fixed payment schedule such that payments are expected every two weeks.  Ordinarily the biweekly payment is half the normal monthly payment, allowing the loan to be paid off much faster than the loan would have been had payments been made once a month.")
(comment entersFluid "'(#$entersFluid ENTRY SOLID)' means that the thing SOLID enters a type of fluid in the #$SolidEnteringFluid event ENTRY.")
(comment BiologicalToxinAttackEpidemic "#$BiologicalToxinAttackEpidemic is a collection of #$BiologicalAttackEpidemics, each instance of which is the result of an instance of #$BiologicalAttack in which a #$BiologicalToxin is deployed as a #$BiologicalWeapon.")
(comment SPECfp "A function and an instance of #$UnitOfCPUCapacity. It is used to represent a unit (or \"benchmark\") of computer processor speed invented by the \"Standard Performance Evaluation Corporation\". The #$SPECfp benchmark represents speed and efficiency in performing floating-point operations. See also #$SPECint -- for integer operations. It should be noted that different version of this standard exist, not necessarily intertranslateable.")
(comment Defenestration "The collection of all events in which some person or object is 

thrown out of a window.")
(comment Proud "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being proud. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment ReformulatorTestCase "The collection of test cases for the #$CycLReformulator.  Each test case consists of an input #$CycLExpression, an expected output #$CycLExpression, a #$Microtheory, and a list of settings for the reformulator.")
(comment CycLToELFn "(#$CycLToELFn CYCL-EXPR) denotes the EL version of CYCL-EXPR.  NARTs are unreified, #$CycLAssertions are converted to their EL forms, etc.. This is an extremely useful function to use in situations where an #$ELFormula is needed because of arg constraints, but you don't happen to have one handy. For example, since the #$arg3Isa of the function #$SubstituteFormulaFn is #$ELFormula, trying to get terms substituted within #$CycLNonAtomicTerms won't work since these are #$CycLFormulas. With this function, one can do a quick conversion, create the EL version of the NAT, and have the substitution take place on that like so: (#$SubstituteFormulaFn #$Emu #$Cat (#$CycLToELFn (#$JuvenileFn #$Cat))).")
(comment SelfConfident "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being self confident. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment notablePerformerOfMusicType "(#$notablePerformerOfMusicType ?PERFORMER ?TYPE) says that ?PERFORMER, an instance of #$MusicPerformanceAgent, is a notable, or noteworthy performer of ?TYPE, an instance of #$MusicTypeByGenre.")
(comment epidemicBiologicalToxinType "(#$epidemicBiologicalToxinType EPI TOXIN-TYPE) means that every member of the #$BiologicalToxinAttackEpidemic EPI is an instance of #$Poisoning such that it is caused by exposure to an instance of #$BiologicalToxin TOXIN-TYPE.")
(comment Fearful "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being fearful. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment positionPromotedTo "This predicate is used to specify the type of position that a person undergoing a promotion in some organization is promoted to.")
(comment BalloonPayment "The collection of all #$MoneyTransactions in which the remaining unpaid principle amount of a mortgage or other long-term loan is paid to the lender, extinguishing the debt.  This final payment is larger than the regular payments.")
(comment parameterOfProgram "#$parameterOfProgram is a binary predicate that relates instances of #$SoftwareParameter to instances of #$ComputerProgram-CW.")
(comment BiologicalAttackInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic "#$BiologicalAttackInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic is the collection of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics which are also #$BiologicalAttackEpidemics. Each instance of #$BiologicalAttackInfectiousDiseaseEpidemic is the result of an instance of #$BiologicalAttack in which a #$LivingBiologicalAgent is deployed as a #$BiologicalWeapon.")
(comment Contemptuous "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being contemptuous. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment positionPromotedFrom "This predicate is used to specify the type of position that a person undergoing a promotion in some organization is promoted from.")
(comment fileSetsParameter "#$fileSetsParameter is a binary predicate that relates instances of #$SoftwareParameter to instances of #$ConfigurationFile.  (#$fileSetsParameter FILE PARAM) means that PARAM is a software parameter that is set by copies of FILE.")
(comment MultiFunctionServerProgram "#$MultiFunctionServerProgram is a supecialization of #$ServerProgram.  Copies of #$MultiFunctionServerProgram function as a number of different types of server program.  Instances of this collection should also be asserted to be instances of as many other specializations of #$ServerProgram as is appropriate.")
(comment Lonely "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being lonely. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment ProgramStep "The collection of all linear steps that are part of some piece of software [#$SoftwareObject].  Instantiations of each #$ProgramStep operate as a serial process, although instantiations of multiple program steps for the same program may run in parallel or asynchronously.")
(comment TFTPClientProgram "#$TFTPServerProgram is the collection of #$ClientPrograms that implement the #$TrivialFileTransferProtocol (TFTP).")
(comment portNumberForSKS "(#$portNumberForSKS SOURCE PORT) means
that SOURCE can be accessed by the SKSI code via PORT.")
(comment Shameful "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being shameful. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment Convicting-Legal "The collection of all events in which a defendant is convicted of a criminal offense as part of a #$Trial-Criminal.  In Western legal systems, instances of #$Convicting-Legal are ordinarily performed by juries prior to the sentencing phase of the trial (see #$Sentencing-Legal).")
(comment fluidTypeEntered "'(#$fluidTypeEntered ENTRY TYPE)' means that the fluid entered in the #$SolidEnteringFluid event ENTRY is of type TYPE.")
(comment TFTPProgram "#$TFTPProgram is the collection of programs that implement the #$TrivialFileTransferProtocol, including #$TFTPServerPrograms and #$TFTPClientPrograms. Individual tftp programs typically should be asserted to be instances of one of those more specialized collections.")
(comment schemaFieldSet "This is the most general relation in the SKSI vocabulary for
linking an #$SKSSchema-LogicalOrPhysical with a set of fields
contained within it.")
(disjointWith University CollegeInUniversity-DegreeGranting)
(comment InfectingEvent-MechanicalVectorBorneTransmission "The collection of #$InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmissions in which the infectious agent is merely transported by a living #$Animal to a susceptible host (see #$infectingVector). For example, an insect vector may carry the infectious agent on its feet or proboscis as it flies and crawls or the infectious agent may pass through its gastrointestinal tract. Another example would be a rodent carrying fleas infected with the #$Plague-Bacterium. A rodent's transporting the fleas is an example of a #$InfectingEvent-MechanicalVectorBorneTransmission. In contrast, a biting by an infected flea would be an example of a #$InfectingEvent-BiologicalVectorBorneTransmission because the flea is infected by #$Plague-Bacterium and the latter undergoes part of its life cycle within the flea before the flea can transmit the infective form of #$Plague-Bacterium.")
(comment Grateful "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being grateful. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment ComputerAidedSoftwareEngineeringProgram "Programs used to implement the computer aided software engineering approach to helping with the phases of the software life-cycle, with particular emphasis on building and maintaining systems.")
(comment recruitingOrganization "(#$recruitingOrganization RECRUITING ORG) means that ORG is the #$Organization on whose behalf and at whose direction the #$RecruitingActivity RECRUITING is carried out.  This entails, among other things, that ORG is both the #$directingAgent and the #$intendedBeneficiary of RECRUITING.")
(comment MessagePiggyBackingFn "This function takes an instance of #$EMailMessage, MSSG, and a data type DATA-TYPE included with MSSG (such as #$EMailAttachment) as arguments and returns an instance of #$ComputerFile-CW which is the maliciously piggy-backed data of DATA-TYPE sent with MSSG.")
(comment ImmersingInLiquid "This is the collection of actions in which an agent immerses a solid object in a liquid.")
(comment TheFn "#$TheFn takes a #$Collection as its argument and returns an instance of #$IndexicalConcept that in the context functions as an indexical instance of the collection that can be used in certain kinds of general statements.")
(comment HTMLEditor-Dynamic "#$HTMLEditor-Dynamic is a subset of #$ScriptingProgram that allows web developers to create dynamically-generated web pages. (For HTML editing programs that edit pages non-dynamically, i.e. with word-processing functionality only, see #$HTMLEditor-Static.)")
(disjointWith University SchoolInUniversity-DegreeGranting)
(comment InfectingEvent-BiologicalVectorBorneTransmission "The collection of #$InfectingEvent-VectorBorneTransmissions in which the infectious agent infects a living #$Animal (see #$infectingVector) before developing into a form that can infect a #$Vertebrate host species. The pathogen must propagate (multiply), develop cyclically, or both inside the vector before the vector is capable of transmitting the pathogen in its infective form. The time period between the infection of the vector and the pathogen becoming infective to a different host species is the extrinsic incubation period for the infectious agent. The infectious agent may be transmitted to a #$Vertebrate host in several ways which include via saliva during biting, or by regurgitation or deposition of feces or other material on the skin which penetrates through the bite wound or through the abrasions caused by scratching.")
(comment Excited "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being excited. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment FTPProgram "#$FTPProgram is the collection of programs that implement the #$FileTransferProtocol, including #$FTPServerPrograms and #$FTPClientPrograms. Individual ftp programs typically should be asserted to be instances of one or both of those more specialized collections.")
(comment ApprovalOfLoan "A subset of #$ApprovingARequest. In each instance of #$ApprovalOfLoan, a loan request is approved by some financial institution.")
(comment EMailAttachment "A subcollection of #$ComputerAIS, #$EMailAttachment is the collection of all information structures sent as attachments to #$EMailMessages.")
(comment mostNotableIsaInContext "If (#$mostNotableIsaInContext X COL CNTXT), then X is an instance of (#$isa) COL, and in the #$Microtheory CNTXT, COL is the most important or most obvious collection of which X is an instance.  In other words, COL is what typically comes to mind in that context as an answer to the question, \"What is X?\" For example, in the context of human activities, a side of beef might be considered most notably food, whereas in the context of human vegetarian activities it might be considered most notably to be an animal carcass.")
(disjointWith ImmersingInLiquid Drying)
(comment InsecureSQLDataStorageFault "A program has an #$InsecureSQLDataStorageFault if it manages (saves to memory, caches, allows querying of) an SQL database in an insecure way. This is a specialization of #$InsecureDataStorageFault.")
(disjointWith University College)
(disjointWith InfectingEvent-MechanicalVectorBorneTransmission InfectingEvent-BiologicalVectorBorneTransmission)
(comment Satisfied "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being satisfied. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment EMailProgram "#$EMailProgram is the collection of programs that are related to e-mailing, such as programs used to process, send, or receive email, or to diagnose specific aspect's of a networks mail process. Individual email programs typically should be asserted to be instances of more specialized collections, such as #$SMTPServerProgram, #$InternetMailAccessServerProgram, #$EMailClientProgram, or #$LocalDeliveryAgent.")
(comment mostNotableGenlsInContext "If (#$mostNotableGenlsInContext COL1 COL2 CNTXT), then every instance of COL1 is an instance of COL2, and in the #$Microtheory CNTXT, COL2 is the most important or most obvious collection that is a generalization of COL1. In other words, COL2 is what typically comes to mind in that context as an answer to the question, \"What collection is COL1 a spec of?\". For example, every waterfall is a body of water, but in the context of river navigation, it is most notable that waterfalls are obstacles.")
(disjointWith ImmersingInLiquid Mounting-Installing)
(comment GregorianYear "The collection of all calendar years in the #$GregorianCalendar system.  Each year starts ten or eleven days after the #$DecemberSolsticeDay.  This is the normal year used since the middle of the 20th Century throughout the non-Islamic world.")
(comment VulnerableToLogFileOverwrite "A specialization of #$VulnerableToFileOverwrite. A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program with a #$LogFileOverwriteFault on it, or if for some other reason it allows people to overwrite log files on it. See also #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedSystemLogAccess, #$VulnerableBecauseNoActivityLogging.")
(comment (PartTypeEntirePortionFn Cell Cytoplasm) "The living part of the cell outside of the nucleus and within the plasma membrane in which the cisternal and membrane-bound organelles lie. ")
(comment HighSchool "the collection of high schools")
(comment VectorBorneEpidemic "A collection of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics whose instances are such that many (but not necessarily all) of the cases constituting the epidemic result from exposure to living #$Animals (see #$infectingVector) that either are contaminated with the infectious agent (see #$InfectingEvent-MechanicalVectorBorneTransmission) or are themselves infected by the infectious agent (see #$InfectingEvent-BiologicalVectorBorneTransmission).")
(comment Jealous "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being jealous. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment typeUsedWithCycModule "This instance of #$DocumentationPredicate links types of I-CycL terms to the Cyc modules defined for them.  For example, (#$typeUsedWithCycModule #$NLQuantAttribute #$QuantifierProcessingRLModule) says that the Quantifier Processor is a module used to process formulae containing instances of #$NLQuantAttribute.")
(comment SSHProgram "#$SSHProgram is the collection of programs that implement the secure shell protocol, including #$SSHServerPrograms and #$SSHClientPrograms. Individual ssh programs typically should be asserted to be instances of one or both of those more specialized collections")
(comment enterpriseRecruitedFor "(#$enterpriseRecruitedFor RECRUITING ACTIVITY) means that
ACTIVITY is the #$Action that recruits are being recruited to join in
in the #$RecruitingActivity RECRUITING.  The exact nature of the role
the recruit plays in ACTIVITY will depend in part on the type of
#$RecruitingActivity that is going on, and in part on other
exigencies: in general, however, (#$enterpriseRecruitedFor RECRUITING
ACTIVITY) implies that any #$agentRecruited will be a
#$deliberateActors in ACTIVITY at some point in the future.  We also
assume ACTIVITY will end some time after RECRUITING has ended, and
that if there is a #$recruitingOrganization in RECRUITING, this
organization is the #$directingAgent of ACTIVITY.")
(comment dataTypeExploitedBy "(#$dataTypeExploitedBy FAULT DATA-TYPE) means that to take advantage of the #$SoftwareFault,FAULT, one uses as an implement data that is of the type DATA-TYPE.  For example, (#$dataTypeExploitedBy #$AutomaticAttachmentExecutionFault #$EMailAttachment) means that to exploit an automatic attachment execution fault, one uses an e-mail attachment.")
(comment programTypicallyInstalledWith "(#$programTypicallyInstalledWith ASSOC-PROG PROG) means that the instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW, ASSOC-PROG, is usually installed with the program PROG.  Even if PROG is a software package, ASSOC-PROG need not be a part of that software package (see #$programInstalledWithPackage).  For example, (#$programTypicallyInstalledWith #$MsoHelp-TheProgram #$MSOffice) means that the help program, #$MsoHelp-TheProgram, is typically installed whenever #$MSOffice is installed.")
(disjointWith ImmersingInLiquid ComputerActivity)
(comment SchemaObjectIDFn "This function is used to specify #$fieldEncodings for schema fields for which code mappings exist--i.e., for cases where the values taken by a field are alphabetical or numeric tokens that code for something else.  (#$SchemaObjectIDFn ODS LOGICAL_FIELD) takes the value assumed by the indexical LOGICAL_FIELD and returns the code that corresponds to it in the physical encoding of the table, assumed to be as #$KSID.")
(comment AuthenticationProgram "A specialization of #$SecurityProgram. Each instance of #$AuthenticationProgram is a program whose running copies are used to ensure that the person accessing some resource (network accounts, files, programs, etc.) has legitimate access to that resource. A notable specialization is #$LoginProgram.")
(comment NonDegreeGrantingInstitution "Collection of higher education institutions not granting degrees, e.g. Trinity College, Cambridge. For those that do grant degrees, such as universities and community colleges, see specializations of #$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution.")
(comment epidemicVectorType "(#$epidemicVectorType EPI VEC-TYPE) means that the #$VectorBorneEpidemic is transmitted to susceptible hosts by means of animal vectors of type VEC-TYPE.")
(comment Disappointed "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being dissapointed. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(disjointWith ImmersingInLiquid EmittingAnObject)
(comment VocationalOrTechnicalSchool "The class of #$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution
that dispense exclusively #$Vocational-TechnicalDegrees.")
(comment PoisoningViaSubstanceFn "Where SUBSTANCE-TYPE is a specialization of #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance, (#$PoisoningViaSubstanceFn SUBSTANCE-TYPE) denotes the collection of all #$Poisonings in which the #$stuffUsed is an instance of SUBSTANCE-TYPE.")
(comment reviewReformulationRule "(#$reviewReformulationRule RULE) indicates

that RULE needs to be reviewed by those responsible for the maintenance of the reformulator code and OE. This predicate is useful to flag legacy reformulator rules that are not explicitly linked to any particular reformulator module.")
(comment OsteopathicMedicalSchool "Schools that give training in osteopathic medicine and grant D.O. degrees.")
(comment Relaxed "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being relaxed. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment Barometer "A device used for measuring atmospheric pressure.  Commonly used in weather forecasting.")
(comment NonLoginAccount "A non-login account is a computer account to which a user could not log in. These are accounts that have certain privileges, but do not have associated login information, such as a username/password combination.  Note that, of course, #$NonLoginAccount and #$LoginAccount partition #$ComputerAccount.")
(comment TrojanAccommodatingFault-Runtime "A program PROG on a computer COMP has this fault if it an attacker can exploit in the following way: first, the attacker places a malicious file on some computer, which is then executed with the privileges of PROG when PROG is subsequently run on COMP.  See the associated planner rule.")
(comment SolidExitingFluid "This is the collection of events in which a solid object exits a type of #$FluidTangibleThing in such a way that the solid is no longer immersed in the fluid.  A rocket going into space is an example, but so is an animal diving into water, since the animal exits the air as it enters the water.  It is not necessary for the solid object to move, though either it or the fluid does.")
(disjointWith VocationalOrTechnicalSchool University)
(comment favorableResponseTo "(#$favorableResponseTo ACT SIT) means that #$Action, ACT is #$inReactionTo the situation, SIT, and that ACT is an favorable response to  SIT.  Roughly  speaking,  ACT is a favorable response if (i) the director or performer of ACT (AGENT1) intends ACT to assist some interest of some doer of SIT (AGENT2), and (ii) AGENT1 acts with this intention towards AGENT2 *because of* AGENT2's participation in SIT.   A bit more  formally: in the case of  a favorable response, AGENT1 has a goal GOAL1 and believes AGENT2 has a goal GOAL2 such that AGENT1 believes that AGENT2 is #$responsibleFor SIT and also believes that SIT increases the likelihood  that GOAL1 will be realized. This belief causes AGENT1 to perform the action ACT, which #$startsAfterStartingOf  SIT.  AGENT1 believes that ACT increases the likelihood that GOAL2 will be realized.")
(comment MedicalSchool "Schools that grant medical degrees, whose students usually end up as medical doctors.")
(comment Calm "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being calm. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment Salinometer "A device that measures the concentration of salt in a solution.")
(disjointWith NonLoginAccount LoginAccount)
(comment WebPageCodeExecutionFault "A program PROG on a computer COMP has this fault if an attacker could exploit it to execute arbitrary code at the privilege level of PROG by luring the user to a malicious web page.  See the associated planner rule.")
(disjointWith SolidExitingFluid LookingForAThingOrTypeOfThing)
(comment registrySecurityZoneCode "A binary predicate which associates a Microsoft Windows registry key (#$RegistryKey) substring with a function which denotes the Internet Explorer (#$MSInternetExplorer) security zone type which (in the appropriate context) that substring is used to refer to. (#$registrySecurityZoneCode STRING ZONE) means that the #$SubLString STRING refers to the zone ZONE. The zones  in question may be found in the collection #$ComputerCapabilityQualifier. See also #$registryCapabilityCode.")
(comment FlightSchool "The class of #$VocationalOrTechnicalSchools where the type
of degree dispensed is a (#$VocationalDegreeForFn (#$TransportViaFn
#$Airplane)).  More generally, the class of schools that teach people
to fly #$Airplanes.  A certain number of hours of training at such an
institution is a prerequisite to receiving a pilot's license in every
State in the U.S.")
(comment Fermentation-Bacterium "A collection of events done by
#$Chemoorganotrophs in which the substrate is metabolized without the
involvement of an exogenous oxidizing agent.  It typically occurs in
#$AnaerobicBacterium, but not necessarily.  Other #$Chemoorganotrophs
use #$Respiration-Bacterium for their #$BiologicalMetabolismEvent.")
(comment MedicalSchool-General "The collection of all schools that offer medical training.  This includes schools of osteopathic medicine as well as those schools that grant M.D.s.")
(comment InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmission "The collection of #$InfectingEvent-IndirectTransmissions in which microbial aerosols (see #$AerosolStuff) are disseminated to a portal of entry, usually the respiratory tract. Microbial aerosols are suspensions in the air of #$Particles consisting partially or wholly of #$Microorganisms. #$Particles in the 1 to 5 #$Micron range are easily drawn into the alveoli of the lungs and may be retained there, causing #$Infection.")
(comment Listless "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being listless. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(disjointWith EndothermicReaction ExothermicReaction)
(comment PlannerAxiomatizedFault "This quoted collection is designed to gather all specializations of #$SoftwareFault that are mentioned in planner axioms written for the CycSecure AttackPlan Analyzer.")
(disjointWith SolidExitingFluid ChangeInUserRights)
(comment FlightSchool "The class of #$VocationalOrTechnicalSchools where the type
of degree dispensed is a (#$VocationalDegreeForFn #$AirplanePilot)).  More generally, the class of schools that teach people
to fly #$Airplanes.  A certain number of hours of training at such an
institution is a prerequisite to receiving a pilot's license in every
State in the U.S.")
(comment portNumberOnServer "(#$portNumberOnServer SERVER NUM PORT)
means that PORT is the #$NetworkPortNumber denoted by NUM on SERVER.")
(comment DoingAHomeworkAssignment "The collection of all educational #$Tasks assigned by a #$Teacher to a #$Student to be performed outside of school hours. Generally involves reading, writing, and/or solving problems.")
(comment AirborneEpidemic "A collection of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics whose instances are such that many (but not necessarily all) the cases constituting the epidemic result from exposure to an airborne pathogen. See #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmission.")
(comment Angry "A specialization of #$IntelligentAgent. Each instance is an agent in the emotional state of being angry. Use this constant with a #$GenericValueFunction to denote a collection of agents that are in this emotional state to some varying degree.")
(comment EndothermicReaction "A specialization of #$ChemicalReaction.  Each instance of #$EndothermicReaction is a chemical reaction in which the energy level of the product is higher than that of the reactants (so that heat is absorbed in the reaction).")
(disjointWith SolidExitingFluid TakingCareOfPeople)
(comment ThreateningToDoFn "Where ACTTYPE is a specialization of #$PurposefulAction, (#$ThreateningToDoFn ACTTYPE) is the collection of all instances of #$MakingAThreat such that a significant part of the content of the threat (see #$infoTransferred) is that the person making the threat (the #$senderOfInfo) will perform an action of type ACTTYPE some time after starting to make the threat, and that the intended recipient of the the threat (the #$recipientOfInfo-Intended) will be harmed by (the #$maleficiary of) this action.")
(comment VeteransAffairsMedicalCenter "The collection of all medical centers operated by or under the direction of the United States Department of Veterans Affairs.")
(comment PortNumberFn "(#$PortNumberFn SERVER NUM) denotes the
unique #$NetworkPortNumber denoted by NUM on SERVER. See the
corresponding predicate #$portNumberOnServer.")
(comment NucleicAcidType "A collection of collections.  Instances

 are acids (see #$AcidType) composed of chains of nucleotides (see #$PolynucleotideStrand).")
(comment logicalFields "(#$logicalFields SCHEMA FIELD) means that FIELD is a logical field in the logical schema, SCHEMA. This predicate is a #$typedGenlPreds of #$schemaFields.  See also #$physicalFields for a similar predicate relating physical fields to physical schemata.")
(comment College "Instances are educational institutions providing undergraduate education.  For colleges that are #$subOrganizations of universities use #$CollegeInUniversity-DegreeGranting")
(comment CollectionOrder "The collection of all #$FixedOrderCollections which include every collection of that same fixed order.  These include #$Individual (zero-order), #$FirstOrderCollection, #$SecondOrderCollection, #$ThirdOrderCollection, and #$FourthOrderCollection.  If higher order collections are defined, they will also be members of this collection.")
(comment patchForProgram "(#$patchForProgram PROGRAM PATCH) means that

PATCH is a software module written so that one may fix a #$SoftwareFault possessed by PROGRAM, by applying PATCH to PROGRAM.")
(comment synonymousListFields "In some cases where it is necessary to articulate a preliminary mapping of a distributed database schema, it is necessary to map CycL constants to entities represented in so-called list objects which have been created for purposes of streamlining the database.  In these cases, multiple fields in the list object jointly comprise a single term that must be mapped to some term in the CycL vocabulary.  #$synonymousListFields enables us to do this.  Where LIST_STRINGS is a list comprised of #$CharacterStrings, (#$synonymousListFields LIST_STRINGS INFO_SOURCE CYC_TERM) means that CYC_TERM is the meaning of the term denoted by the list of character strings that appear on one row of a list object in the database schema INFO_SOURCE.")
(disjointWith SolidExitingFluid MakingSomething)
(disjointWith Agent-Generic ExanimateObject)
(comment rowInSourceClaims "This predicate relates a structured knowledge source with a CycL sentence that expresses one or more of the physical field values which appear in some row of the knowledge source.  The sentence does not itself interpret logical meaning of the row, or of its field values, but only expresses the physical field values in Cyc.  More formally, let SOURCE denote an instance of #$StructuredKnowledgeSource and SENTENCE denotes an instance of #$ELSentence-Assertible, then (#$rowInSourceClaims SOURCE SENTENCE) is true precisely if SENTENCE is a CycL representation of one or more of the physical field values in some row of SOURCE. See also the predicate #$fieldValue, which is often used in SENTENCE to express the physical field values of a row in CycL.")
(comment AcidType "The collection of all acids. Instances are instances of #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies whose instances will react in certain chemically predictable ways with a base (see #$BaseType).")
(comment indexedFields "(#$indexedFields SCHEMA FIELD) means FIELD is a physical
field that is defined within SCHEMA, and that FIELD is indexed within
SCHEMA.")
(comment LiberalArtsCollege "A collection of #$EducationalOrganizations.  Instances of this collection generally focus on providing enrolled students with undergraduate educations, and - unlike instances of the collection #$University - they offer little or no graduate schooling.")
(comment InfectiousDiseaseEpidemicTypeByTransmissionType "A collection of collections. Each instance is a specialization of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic. All #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics that are instances of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemicTypeByTransmissionType are caused, in part, by the same type of transmission route. This collection is neither a #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType nor a #$DisjointCollectionType because some #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics have multiple means of infection transmission.")
(comment nextHigherOrder "(#$nextHigherOrder ORDER1 ORDER2) means that both ORDER1 and ORDER2 are instances of #$CollectionOrder and ORDER1 comprises every instance of ORDER2.  Thus, (#$nextHigherOrder #$Individual #$FirstOrderCollection), (#$nextHigherOrder #$FirstOrderCollection #$SecondOrderCollection), ...")
(comment provenanceOfMediaSeriesProduct "(#$provenanceOfMediaSeriesProduct SERIES CITY) means that individual series elements [episodes] are considered to originate within the environs of CITY, and that instantiations of those elements are by default produced in the same area. Some newspapers may have remote publishing plants & TV shows may broadcast from many stations around a far larger GeographicalRegion. By default the intended audience includes the residents of CITY (or a subset thereof) and information about CITY is one of the topics of any newspaper or news show.")
(disjointWith SolidExitingFluid PreparingFoodOrDrink)
(comment Spliceosome "Spliceosomes are particles that direct the RNA splicing process (See #$RNASplicingProcess).")
(comment College-4Year "Instances are schools which provide a four-year undergraduate program leading to a baccalaureate 
degree. Cf. #$College-2Year.")
(comment epidemicTransmissionType "(#$epidemicTransmissionType EPI TRANS-TYPE) means that #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI is an instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemicTypeByTransmissionType TRANS-TYPE.")
(comment AuPairService "The collection of events in which a #$Nanny takes care of an employer's children.")
(comment overlappingListFields "In some cases where it is necessary to articulate a preliminary mapping of a distributed database schema, it is necessary to map CycL constants to entities represented in so-called list objects which have been created for purposes of streamlining the database.  In these cases, multiple fields in the list object jointly comprise a single term that must be mapped to some term in the CycL vocabulary.  #$overlappingListFields enables us to do this.  Where LIST_STRINGS is a list comprised of #$CharacterStrings, (#$synonymousListFields LIST_STRINGS INFO_SOURCE CYC_TERM) means that CYC_TERM overlaps semantically with the term denoted by the list of character strings that appear on one row of a list object in the database schema INFO_SOURCE.")
(comment BusinessPartnershipAgreement "A specialization of #$LegalAgreement, according to which certain agreeing agents enter into a #$businessPartners relationship.")
(disjointWith SolidExitingFluid SportsPenalizing)
(comment registryKeyPath "A predicate which associates a Microsoft windows registry key with the \"path\" which uniquely identifies it. (#$registryKeyPath KEY PATH) means that the #$RegistryKey KEY corresponds to the #$Pathname PATH. Each path takes the form of an arbitrarily-sized series of character strings, separated by backslashes.")
(comment ComputerDataStructure "A specialization of #$ComputerAIS.  Each instance of #$ComputerDataStructure is data structured in such a way that when it is stored a computer can use it efficiently. Important specializations include #$Array-DataStructure and #$HashTable-DataStructure.")
(comment WaterPistol "The collection of toy pistols which squirt water, usually made of plastic.  Also called a 'squirt gun'.")
(comment GraduateSchool "The class of organizations in which graduate students are enrolled; the #$providerOfService for most graduate instances of #$CourseOfStudy.")
(disjointWith SolidExitingFluid InformationBearingThing)
(comment ImitationOfIndividual "#$ImitationOfIndividual a specialization of #$TemporalThing.  Each instance of #$ImitationOfIndividual is a temporal thing created in order to resemble distinct particular instances of #$TemporalThing.  Important specializations include the collection of forged copies of the Mona Lisa painting, and #$Imposter, which includes as instances anyone who pretends to be a           particular person he or she is not.  Compare this constant to          #$ImitationOfCollection.")
(disjointWith ComputerDataStructure ComputerCode)
(comment VulnerableBecauseOfInsecureMailSystemConfigurationData "A computer has this vulnerability if it has a program on it with a #$InsecureMailSystemConfigurationDataFault.")
(comment BaseType "The collection of all chemical bases. Instances are #$ChemicalCompoundTypeByChemicalSpecies whose instances will react with acids to form a salt. (see #$AcidType).")
(comment hasAlumni "The school has these individuals as alumni.")
(disjointWith SolidExitingFluid IBTGeneration)
(comment Array-DataStructure "A specialization of #$ComputerDataStructure.  Each instance of #$Array-DataStructure arranges a group of data elements in a continuous block of memory.   Individual elements are accessed by index using integers.")
(disjointWith Reading-Tactile Reading-Visual)
(comment fieldGenls "(#$fieldGenls FIELD COLLECTION) means that the values of FIELD

correspond in CycL to collections which are specializations of

COLLECTION.")
(comment CollegeInUniversity-DegreeGranting "Collection of colleges that are separate and named parts of universities. Some colleges offer professional degrees and some offer both undergraduate and graduate degrees. St.Jerome's College at the #$UniversityOfWaterloo is an example of such a college.")
(comment BusinessGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which 

have to do ultimately with the economic well-being of some particular

business or organization. The agent possessing such a goal can be 

the business itself, an employee or owner of the business, or someone 

else doing work on behalf of the business. #$BusinessGoal is not intended

to refer to a desire by, for example, a shareholder who cannot assist

in bringing about the intended state of affairs.")
(comment HashTable-DataStructure "A specialization of #$ComputerDataStructure.  Each instance of #$HashTable-DataStructure
is a data structure comprised of entries, where each entry associates a key with a value.")
(disjointWith ChemicallyAcidicSubstance ChemicallyBasicSubstance)
(comment College-2Year "Instances are schools which provide a two-year undergraduate program leading either to an 
associates degree or to transfer to a four-year institution. See #$College-4Year.")
(comment BusinessCommunication "A communication that occurs as partof the operation of a business.  Only one actor need be participating in a business capacity.")
(comment exitsFluid "'(#$exitsFluid EXIT SOLID)' means that the thing SOLID exits a type of fluid in the #$SolidExitingFluid event EXIT.")
(disjointWith FileDirectory ComputerProgram-CW)
(comment logicalSchemaKeys "(#$logicalSchemaKeys ODS SET) means that SET is a set of logical fields that collectively covary with instantiations of ODS:  i.e., any change in instantiation entails that at least one of the members of SET changes value, and vice versa.")
(comment LawSchool "Schools which prepare their students to become lawyers, and grant DoctorOfJurisprudence degrees.")
(disjointWith FileDirectory LibraryFile)
(comment GregorianMonth "The collection of all calendar months in the #$GregorianCalendar system.  The months are (in order) #$January, #$February, #$March, #$April, #$May, #$June, #$July, #$August, #$September, #$October, #$November, #$December.")
(comment outputProgramToken " (#$outputProgramToken PROGRAMMER FILE TOKEN) means that PROGRAMMER appends #$ProgramExpression TOKEN to the end of FILE, an instance of #$ComputerCode-Source.")
(comment UsingProgramFn "(#$UsingProgramFn PROGRAM) denotes the collection of instances of (#$UsingAFn #$Computer) in which the #$programUsed-Generic is PROGRAM.")
(comment DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution "#$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution is a specialization of #$HigherEducationInstitution.  Each instance of #$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution is a higher education institution that grants degrees. For those that do not grant degrees, such as colleges of universities, e.g. Trinity College, Cambridge, see specs of #$NonDegreeGrantingInstitution.")
(comment HackersMaliciousWebPage "A #$WorldWideWebPage-AIS maintained and created by #$HypotheticalHacker.  If you receive #$HackersMaliciousEMailMessage, do not follow any hyperlinks contained within it; they are links to #$HackersMaliciousWebPage, wherein #$HypotheticalHacker has embeded some malicious code.")
(comment PayingWithObjectTypeFn "Where OBJECT_TYPE is a specialization of #$SomethingExisting, (#$PayingWithObjectTypeFn OBJECT_TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$Paying such that the object offered in payment for goods or services rendered is an instance of OBJECT_TYPE.")
(comment FileDirectory "A specialization of #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource and #$ComputerFile-CW. Each instance of #$FileDirectory is a directory structure comprised of other directories, instances of #$ComputerFile-CW, symbolic links, or the logical names of devices. In #$MSWindowsOperatingSystem terminology, instances of this collection are called \"folders\". On a #$UnixOS, a directory is a list of names and inode (#$FileIndexNode) numbers.")
(comment IslamicYear "The collection of all calendar years in the #$IslamicLunarCalendar system.  There are 12 lunar months in the calendar, which means that the months [see #$IslamicMonth] and any events tied to specific days of the year slowly migrate through the seasons from year to year.")
(comment ProgramSyntaxObject "The collection of all \"chunks\" of computer code which have independent meaning to a programmer cognizant of the language in which they are written.")
(comment RegistryKeyFn "(#$RegistryKeyFn PATHNAME) denotes the instance of #$RegistryKey which is stored in the #$WindowsRegistry in the location specified by PATHNAME. All pathnames start with \"HKEY\" (which means \"handle to a key\"), and are divided into branches such as HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE (often contracted to \"HKLM\") and HKEY_CURRENT_USER (often contracted to \"HKCU\"). For substituting variable strings into pathnames, see #$RegistryKeyTemplateFn. See also the predicates #$registryKeySetToValueOnComputer and #$registryKeyNotSetToValueOnComputer.")
(comment ComputerUserInteraction-UIA "The collection of instances of #$ComputerUserInteraction that occur during a UIA-driven knowledge entry session.")
(comment exampleTuple "This predicate is used to illustrate examples of the  raw data which may appear in tuples defined by a physical schema.  That is, if SCHEMA is a physical schema (an instance of #$SKSSchema-Physical) and TUPLE is a tuple of data objects (an instance of #$Tuple) then (#$exampleTuple SCHEMA TUPLE) means that the elements of TUPLE satisfy the data type constraints of the physical fields of SCHEMA.  However, TUPLE may or may not correspond to an actual record in a database or knowledge source implementing SCHEMA.")
(disjointWith DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution NonDegreeGrantingInstitution)
(comment HackersMaliciousEMailMessage "#$HypotheticalHacker's malicious email.  If you receive it, DO NOT OPEN IT!  It may contain malicious code!  If you do happen to open it, whatever else you do, DO NOT OPEN ANY ATTACHMENTS!  They are surely malicious files, and not the innocuous documents they seem to be!  And, for God's sake, do not visit any websites mentioned in the email!  You'll rue the day, I assure you.")
(comment VersionedSoftwareObject "A specialization of #$SoftwareObject-Individual. Each instance of #$SoftwareObject is a computer program, software package or library that is versioned.  Positive examples include (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$NetscapeNavigator \"5\") and (#$SoftwareVersionFn #$Libc-TheLibrary \"2.0\").  Negative examples include #$Libc-TheLibrary (which is unversioned) and (#$VersionsInclusiveFn #$NetscapeNavigator \"3\" \"6\") (which is a version series, not an individual software object). #$VersionedSoftwareObject is disjoint with #$UnversionedSoftwareObject, and these collections partition #$SoftwareObject-Individual.")
(comment Filesystem "A specialization of #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource.  Each instance of #$Filesystem is an organization of one or more instances of #$ComputerFile-CW and one or more instances of #$FileDirectory.")
(comment IslamicMonth "The collection of all calendar months in the #$IslamicYear according to the #$IslamicLunarCalendar system.  The months are (in order) #$Muharram-IslamicMonth, #$Safar-IslamicMonth, #$RabiAlAwwal-IslamicMonth, #$RabiAlThani-IslamicMonth, #$JumadaAlAwwal-IslamicMonth, #$JumadaAlThani-IslamicMonth, #$Rajab-IslamicMonth, #$Shaban-IslamicMonth, #$Ramadan-IslamicMonth, #$Shawwal-IslamicMonth, #$DhuAlQidah-IslamicMonth, #$DhuAlHijjah-IslamicMonth.")
(comment doOutputStatementPart "A ternary complex action predicate. (#$doOutputStatementPart PROGRAMMER FILE SYNTAXOBJECT) means that PROGRAMMER appends to the end of FILE a string (or strings) which signify SYNTAXOBJECT in the current programming language, to determined by context.")
(comment computerInteractionUser "(#$computerInteractionUser INTERACTION USER) says that the computer user during INTERACTION, an instance of #$ComputerUserInteraction, is USER.")
(comment UnisexRestroom "A public restroom [#$PublicRestroom] for both men and women.  In most cases in the US around the year 2000, these are restrooms for a single person to use at a time.")
(disjointWith SchoolInstitution-KThrough12 HigherEducationInstitution)
(comment HackersEMailMessageText-Lure "#$HackersEMailMessageText-Lure is the subcollection of #$EMailMessageText consisting of messages that are designed to lure the recipient of any email containing the message text to a particular website.")
(comment AttributingResponsibility "This is the collection of actions in which one agent attributes at least causal responsibility, and perhaps moral responsibility, for an action to an agent.  This is a general collection which includes both accusations (see #$Accusing) and claims of responsibility (see #$ClaimingResponsibility).")
(comment IfStatement-StartIf "An instance of #$ProgramSyntaxObject. #$IfStatement-StartIf denotes for a contextually determined programming language
the sequence of tokens that would signal the start of an if statement.
For example, in #$Pascal-ProgrammingLanguage, #$IfStatement-StartIf would
denote the token \"if\".")
(comment PistolMakarov "The Makarov is a semi-automatic and self-loading pistol.  It was designed in the 1950s by Russian Nikolai Federovich Makarov as a

a simple and reliable medium-powered pistol intended as the sidearm of the Soviet Forces.")
(comment AnnualBusinessReport "The collection of documents that describe the business performance of an agent, usually put out annually.")
(comment fluidTypeExited "'(#$fluidTypeExited EXIT TYPE)' means that the fluid exited in the #$SolidExitingFluid event EXIT is of type TYPE.")
(comment ClaimingResponsibility "The subcollection of #$AttributingResponsibility in which the agent attributes responsibility to itself.  Cf. #$Accusing.")
(comment IfStatement-Then "An instance of #$ProgramSyntaxObject. #$IfStatement-Then denotes for a contextually determined programming language
the sequence of tokens that would signal the \"then\" part of an if statement.
For example, in #$Pascal-ProgrammingLanguage, #$IfStatement-Then would
denote the token \"then\".")
(comment SubmachineGun-Uzi "The Uzi is a type of submachine gun.")
(comment RNAStuff "The collection of all instances of RNA, the chemical compound composed of individual #$RNAMolecules.")
(comment AdmissionsDepartment "A specialization of #$UniversityDepartment. Each instance of this collection is a group of employees who determine which students will be admitted to an educational instutition.")
(comment ShootingSomeoneExecutionStyle "The collection of all events in which a person is murdered via an 'execution-style' shooting in which the victim is dispatched via a single shot to the back of the head.  If an instance of #$ShootingSomeoneExecutionStyle occurs, there is a strong presumption to the effect that a #$CriminalOrganization was the #$directingAgent and that the #$perpetrator is an agent in the employ of some #$CriminalOrganization.")
(disjointWith LegMovement BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel)
(comment performerOfRecordedMusicalCW "This predicate relates musical performers to audio conceptual works that they have recorded.   (#$performerOfRecordedMusicalCW MUSICIAN MUSIC) means that #$MusicPerformanceAgent MUSICIAN is a performer on a recording of #$AudioConceptualWork MUSIC.  Note that MUSICIAN need not have created (i.e., need not have originally authored) the work MUSIC -- the recording produced may be a \"cover\" of a work created by someone else.")
(comment BusinessTrip "A trip taken for business.")
(comment SolidPassingBetweenFluids "This is the collection of events in which a solid object exits a type of #$FluidTangibleThing and then immediately enters another type.  An animal diving into water is an example, since the animal exits the air and enters the water.  A rocket going into space is a non-example.  It is not necessary for the solid object to move, though either it or the fluids do.")
(comment IfStatement-Else "An instance of #$ProgramSyntaxObject. #$IfStatement-Else denotes for a contextually determined programming language
the sequence of tokens that would signal the \"else\" part of an if statement.
For example, in #$Pascal-ProgrammingLanguage, #$IfStatement-Else would
denote the token \"else\".")
(comment Bullet-9x19mmNATO "The collection of #$BulletAssembly that are a 9x19mm caliber and made for NATO.  Invented for the German military at the turn of the century, the wide distribution of the 9x19mm Parabellum/Luger cartridge made it the logical choice for the NATO standard pistol and SMG round.  While weaker than .40 S&W, it tends to have an advantage in weight and capacity. Fairly good against unarmored targets, but very weak against armor.")
(comment MRNAProcessingType "The collection of instances of #$CellularProcessType, each instance of which is a stage in mRNA production, in which prospective mRNA molecules are processed.")
(comment PhysicsDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Physics.")
(comment targetShape "(targetShape EVENT OBJ) asserts that OBJ exemplifies the target shape for some shape changing event EVENT.")
(disjointWith EmittingSound BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel)
(disjointWith GettingFreeFromControl BeingFreedFromControl)
(comment playsInstrumentInMusicalGroup "(#$playsInstrumentInMusicalGroup MUSICIAN INST GROUP) means that INST is one of the types of instruments that MUSICIAN plays in GROUP.")
(comment FinancialExchange "A collection of Organizations that provide or maintain marketplaces where securities, options, futures, or commodities can be traded. Examples of such organizations in the UnitedStates include the New York Stock Exchange, the American Stock Exchange, and NASDAQ, as well as the various bond exchanges.")
(comment DivingIntoWater "This is the subcollection of #$Diving in which the diver falls into water.")
(comment claimsResponsible "'(#$claimsResponsible CLAIM AGENT)' means that in the #$AttributingResponsibility action CLAIM, responsibility is attributed to AGENT.")
(comment BiologyDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Biology.")
(comment TakingAPersonPrisoner "The collection of all #$Events that consist in a person being taken prisoner:  i.e., the collection of all events in which a person enters a period of captivity or confinement in which their scope and freedom of action are deliberately restricted by the imprisoning agency.")
(comment leadSinger "(leadSinger GROUP SINGER) means that SINGER is the lead singer in GROUP.")
(comment ProgramObject "A specialization of #$ComputerAIS. #$ProgramObject is the collection of all data structures that are explicitly referenced in computer programs. All data types are considered to be specializations of this collection.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedFloppyDriveAccess "A specialization of #$AllowsSharedFloppyAccess and #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedAccess. A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible for its #$FloppyDiskDrive to be accessed by someone other than the currently logged on user.")
(comment kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Binary "(#$kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Binary BROADP NARROWP COL1

COL2) indicates that whenever [1] (BROADP INS1 INS2) is known and [2]

COL1, COL2 are respectively the 1st and 2nd argument type constraint on NARROWP and

[3] INS1, INS2 are instances of COL1, COL2 resp., then (NARROWP INS1

INS2) is likely to be true. This predicate is used to suggest plausible

specializations to ke'rs via the predicate strengthener. If one of the

#$Collection arguments is irrelevant to the suggested restriction, use

the arg type constraint for BROADP in that position. E.g.  if

(#$kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Binary BROADP NARROWP BROAD_COL1 COL2)

and (#$arg1Isa BROADP BROAD_COL1), then that collection is ignored by the

strengthener.")
(comment AnthropologyDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Anthropology.")
(comment epidemicTypeResultsFromTransmissionType "(#$epidemicTypeResultsFromTransmissionType EPI-TYPE INFECTING-TYPE) means that typically the type of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic EPI-TYPE is the result of #$InfectingEvents of type INFECTING-TYPE. This predicate is used to make type-level statements about the type of #$InfectingEvent that typically causes the #$Infections that constitute #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemics of a certain type. For example, (#$epidemicTypeResultsFromTransmissionType #$AirborneEpidemic #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmission) means that typically #$AirborneEpidemics are the result of #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmissions. However, it is possible for an instance of #$AirborneEpidemic to have some #$epidemicInfectionCases that result from a different type of #$InfectingEvent, for example, from #$InfectingEvent-DirectTransmissions.")
(comment SnipingAtSomeone "The collection of all events in which a #$Sniper-Professional aims (via a scope) a #$Gun-Portable at a human target at a distance and fires with the intent of killing or causing mortal harm.")
(comment InterArgNotIsaPredicate "The subcollection of both #$InterArgTypePredicate and #$ArgNotIsaPredicate (qq.v.) whose instances are used to put conditional #$isa based argument-type constraints on polyadic relations in regards to two of their argument-places.  Each instance of #$InterArgNotIsaPredicate specifies, with respect to a given #$Relation, that one of its arguments (the \"dependent\" one) must _not_ be an instance of (#$isa) a certain collection, contingent upon another of its argument's (the \"independent\" one's) being an instance of a certain (possibly different) collection.  An inter-argument-isa predicate PRED has argument-places for designating the relation and the two collections serving as argument-types; the (numerically-specified) identities of the relation's corresponding dependent and independent arguments is in most cases fixed (as in #$interArgNotIsa1-2), but is in some cases variable and specified via two additional argument-places of PRED's (as in #$interArgNotIsa). In cases of the former sort, where the relation's argument-places are fixed, PRED is a #$TernaryPredicate that takes as it first argument (or \"arg1\") a relation, as its arg2 the type specified for the relation's independent argument, and as its arg3 the type forbidden (contingently) for the dependent argument.")
(comment PaymentByActionTypeFn "Where ACT_TYPE is a specialization of #$PurposefulAction, (#$PaymentByActionTypeFn ACT_TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of ACT_TYPE that are undertaken as a form of payment for goods or services rendered.  For all intents and purposes this can be thought of as shorthand for (#$CollectionIntersectionFn (#$TheSet #$Transaction ACT_TYPE).")
(comment HomeBusiness "The collection of all small #$Businesses run out of #$HumanResidences.")
(comment FileServer-Network "A subcollection of #$Computer, whose instances function as file servers for instances of #$ComputerNetwork.")
(comment AgricultureDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Agriculture.")
(comment cellTypeInvolved "(#$cellTypeInvolved PROCESS TYPE) says that

 for any instance INS of the #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel PROCESS, some

 instance of TYPE is the cell that does INS [see #$doneBy, #$nonDeliberateActors].")
(comment ArgNotIsaPredicate "The collection of #$ArgTypePredicates (q.v.) that specify argument-types directly (by referencing certain collections) and impose constraints that _forbid_ a thing's being an instance of a collection thus specified.  More precisely, each instance of #$ArgNotIsaPredicate PRED takes a #$Relation RELN as its first argument (or \"arg1\"), and has at least one other argument-place (say the Mth) for specifying a forbidden argument-type for one of RELN's argument-places (say the Nth).  (The value of N might be fixed or might be given by yet another of PRED's arguments.)  Suppose M=2 and N=1.  PRED then takes a #$Collection as its second argument, and a closed atomic sentence (or \"GAF\") of the form (PRED RELN COL ..) puts a negative \"#$isa\" constraint on RELN's first argument-place that is based on COL.  If PRED is a \"single-argument\" constraint predicate, the GAF entails that a closed formula of the form (RELN ARG1 ..) is semantically well-formed only if ARG1 is _not_ an instance of (i.e. #$isa) COL.  If PRED is an \"inter-argument\" constraint predicate, the GAF expresses a slightly more complicated, conditional negative #$isa constraint on a pair of RELN's argument-places (see #$InterArgNotIsaPredicate).")
(comment EventQualifyingFunction "A specialization of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  Each instance of #$EventQualifyingFunction is a unary predicate that takes a specialization of #$Event as an argument and returns a distinct specialization of #$Event.  The collection returned by an event qualifier function is the collection of events that occur in a certain manner.")
(comment CapitalManagement "The collection of #$Management activities the goals of which involve maintaining or increasing the #$businessCapital or #$assets of a #$Person or an #$Organization.")
(comment IntegerObject "#$IntegerObject is the signed version of the integer

simple data type in C-like languages. Normally its size in memory is equal to the

word size of the particular implementation.")
(comment Bullet-9x18mmSoviet "The collection of #$BulletAssembly that are a 9x18mm caliber and made by the Soviets/Russians.  ")
(comment kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Inverse "(#$kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Inverse BROADP NARROWP COL1
COL2) indicates that whenever [1] (BROADP INS1 INS2) is known and [2] COL1, COL2
are respectively the 2nd and 1st arg constraint on NARROWP and [3] INS1,
INS2 are instances of, resp., COL1 and COL2, then (NARROWP
INS2 INS1) is likely to be true. This predicate is used to suggest
plausible specializations to ke'rs via the predicate strengthener. If one
of the #$Collection arguments is irrelevant to the suggested restriction,
use the arg constraint for BROADP in that position. E.g.  if
(#$kePrecisionSuggestionByTypeRestriction-Inverse BROADP NARROWP BROAD_COL1 COL2)
and (#$arg1Isa BROADP BROAD_COL1), then that collection is ignored by the
strengthener.")
(comment BotanyDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Botany.")
(comment musicTypeInfluencedBy "(#$musicTypeInfluencedBy MUSIC-TYPE THING) means that a particular thing THING influenced a particular type of music MUSIC-TYPE.")
(disjointWith ArgNotIsaPredicate ArgIsaPredicate)
(comment IndirectlyFn "The action qualifier which qualifies actions as indirect.")
(comment LinguisticsDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Linguistics.")
(comment InfectiousParticle "The collection of #$Particles which are contaminated with an infectious #$Microorganism. #$InfectiousParticles are capable of being the #$infectingSource in #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmissions because they are easily suspended in the air and are small enough to be inhaled.")
(comment VulnerableToUnauthorizedCDRomAccess "A specialization of #$AllowsSharedCDRomAccess and #$VulnerableToUnauthorizedAccess. A computer has this vulnerability if it is possible for its #$CD-ROMDrive to be accessed by someone other than the currently logged on user.")
(comment enumerableSchema "(#$enumerableSchema PHYSICAL_SCHEMA) means that it is possible/feasible to enumerate every column of
every row in the schema.")
(comment ChemistryDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Chemistry.")
(comment InfectiousDroplet "The collection of (#$ParticleFn #$LiquidTangibleThing) which contain infectious microorganisms. #$InfectiousDroplets can be projected from the mouth or nose during coughing, breathing, or sneezing or can be part of an animal's bodily fluids (blood, urine, etc.) that reach the environment. The evaporation of #$InfectiousDroplets result in #$InfectiousDropletNucleus. #$InfectiousDroplets are capable of being the vehicle of infection in #$InfectingEvent-DirectTransmissions and #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmissions.")
(comment actAttributed "'(#$actAttributed ATTRIBUTING ACT)' means that ACT is the action for which responsibility is attributed in the #$AttributingResponsibility ATTRIBUTING.")
(comment Pistol-Glock-17 "The collection of Glock 17 pistols, which are made in Austria.")
(comment schemaExampleSentence "(#$schemaExampleSentence SCHEMA SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE is an example of a sentence that could be generated in a CycL translation of a database description conforming to SCHEMA.")
(comment PhilosophyDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Philosophy.")
(comment InfectiousDustParticle "The collection of #$DustParticles which carry infectious #$Microorganisms. This collection includes particles of dust from contaminated inanimate objects such as bedding and clothing, the solid residues that result from the evaporation of #$InfectiousDroplets (see #$InfectiousDropletNucleus), naturally occurring dust particles from soil containing spores or other #$Microorganisms, and manufactured powders designed to carry spores or other bacterial agents.")
(comment musicTypeInfluencedByType "(#$musicTypeInfluencedByType MUSIC-TYPE THING-TYPE) means a particular type of music MUSIC-TYPE was influenced by a particular type of thing THING-TYPE.")
(comment fieldDecoding "(#$fieldDecoding LOGICAL_SCHEMA LOGICAL_FIELD
PHYSICAL_SCHEMA TERM) means either that TERM is the logical field
value that is conventionally denoted by the value taken by the
physical field in PHYSICAL_SCHEMA corresponding to the logical field
LOGICAL_FIELD in LOGICAL_SCHEMA, or that it simply is this value in
the case where the logical field value is itself a code string.")
(comment ComputerScienceDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$ComputerScience.")
(comment InfectiousDropletNucleus "The collection of #$InfectiousDustParticles resulting from the evaporation of #$InfectiousDroplets. Infectious droplet nuclei are easily aerosolized and aerosols containing them can serve as the intermediary vehicle for #$InfectingEvent-AirborneTransmissions.  For example, aerosols of #$InfectiousDropletNucleus have been implicated in the transmission of #$Tuberculosis and #$Hantaan.  See #$Aerosolizing.")
(comment complementaryPolynucleotideStrands "Two instances of #$PolynucleotideStrand stand in this relation to each other if their bases can be paired.")
(comment Investor "People who are involved in #$Investing.")
(comment CharacterObject "This is the character data type in C-like programming languages. Normally the
char is stored in memory as one byte (8 bits).")
(comment DateFromStringFn "(DateFromStringFn DATE-STRING) returns the instance of #$Date corresponding to DATE-STRING.")
(comment doInstallMaliciousProgramOfType "(#$doInstallMaliciousProgramOfType AGENT MALPROGRAMTYPE COMPUTER) means that AGENT installs, with or without permission, an instance of MALPROGRAMTYPE on COMPUTER.")
(comment relationMemberExists "(#$relationMemberExists PRED GROUP COLL) means that for every MEMBER such that (#$groupMembers GROUP MEMBER), there exists an instance INS of collection COLL such that (PRED MEMBER INS) is true. This predicate enables one to make claims about the members of a group without referencing the members.")
(comment predicateRoot "(#$predicateRoot PREDICATE ROOT) means that for every term, TERM, that fits the arg1 constraints of PREDICATE, (PREDICATE TERM ROOT) is true.")
(comment MathematicsDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$Mathematics.")
(comment CorrespondingCycCollectionFn "(#$CorrespondingCycCollectionFn PRED) denotes the specialization of #$Event which corresponds to the instance of #$SituationPredicate PRED.  (#$correspondingCycCollection PRED (#$CorrespondingCycCollectionFn PRED)) is true when PRED ranges over all instances of #$SituationPredicate.")
(comment Aerosolizing "The collection of #$DispersionOfStuff events which result in an aerosol (#$AerosolStuff), a mixture of either solid or liquid particles suspended in a gaseous medium. #$Aerosolizing can be done purposely or not.  Wind stirring up particles of soil aerosolizes them naturally . Since an #$Atomizer is designed to aerosolize the particles in the container, someone using an #$Atomizer aerosolizes these particles intentionally. In contrast, someone opening an envelope containing #$Powder aerosolizes the powder unintentionally.")
(comment locusOfCellularProcess-Cell "(#$locusOfCellularProcess-Cell PROCESS CELL) says that CELL is the instance of #$Cell

 that plays the role of #$doneBy and #$eventOccursAt in the #$BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel PROCESS.")
(comment ReleasingAPrisoner "The collection of all instances of #$BeingFreedFromControl that involve a prisoner (who may or may not be being held in accordance with legal precepts) being deliberately released from custody by the person, group, or institution that is holding him or her.")
(comment musicTypeInfluencedByEvent "(#$musicTypeInfluencedByEvent MUSIC-TYPE EVENT) means a particular type of music MUSIC-TYPE was influenced by a particular event EVENT.")
(comment DistributedDatabaseSystem "A specialization of #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource.  Each instance of

#$DistributedDatabaseSystem is a system that enable access to commonly replicated information from a central authority.  On computer networks a common in=mplementation of a distributed database is #$NetworkInformationSystem.")
(comment predicatesCycLGraphType "(#$predicatesCycLGraphType PRED GRAPH-TYPE) means that the #$BinaryPredicate, PRED, is interanally graphed in CycL by a graph of type GRAPH-TYPE), which is expressed in code as ``(list :link-style GRAPH-TYPE)''.")
(comment BusinessSchool "A specialization of #$SchoolInUniversity-DegreeGranting, instances of which conduct teaching and research in #$BusinessAdministration.")
(comment PayingWithObjectsOfTypeFn "Where OBJECT_TYPE is a specialization of #$SomethingExisting, (#$PayingWithObjectsOfTypeFn OBJECT_TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$Paying such that many objects of type OBJECT_TYPE are offered in payment for goods or services rendered.")
(comment BusinessInformation "A specialization of #$PropositionalInformationThing. Each instance of this collection is a set of facts / data / knowledge about #$Business and business transactions (cf. #$BusinessEvent, #$BusinessProcess).")
(comment ProgramIdentifier "This is the collection of all identifiers that can be found in computer programs.
Included are variables, named constants, function names, macro names.")
(comment SpoofableMailServerFault "A specialization of #$SpoofableProxyFault. A program has this fault if it is possible to send messages through it such that they appear to have originated from an arbitrary user. The program may be an #$EMailProgram or an #$InstantMessengerProgram.")
(comment ProspectiveMRNAMolecule "The collection of instances of #$PrimaryTranscript-RNAMolecule that undergo #$MRNAProcessing.")
(comment SchoolInUniversity-DegreeGranting "A specialization of #$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution. Each instance of this collection is a semi-autonomous (in contrast with #$AcademicDepartment) organization set up by a university to provide some kind of professional degree to students (such as Business or Nursing). A typical example of such an organization is Baylor Medical School.")
(comment KillingThroughEventType "This #$SiblingDisjointCollectionType is a faceting of #$KillingByOrganism.  Each instance is a specialization of #$KillingByOrganism whose instances are characterized by coming about through (and as part of) an action of a certain type.")
(comment NISServer-Network "A subcollection of #$Computer whose instances function as NIS servers for #$NISDomains. For NIS+, see #$NISPlusServer-Network.")
(comment Microkernel "A specialization of #$OperatingSystemKernel (q.v.).  Each instance of this collection is a kernel that does not include any instances of #$DeviceDriverProgram.  Operating systems that employ microkernels load and execute device drivers when needed. Cf. #$MonolithicKernel.")
(comment MIMECodeExecutionFault "'MIME' stands for Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions.  A program has this fault if it mishandles certain types of MIME headers and can be exploited to execute arbitrary code with the privileges of the faulty program.  This fault can be exploited via email if the faulty program is used to view HTML attachments and may also be exploited via #$HackersMaliciousWebPage.  It is therefore a spec-attribute of the #$ProgramFault-PlannerSpecifics  #$WebPageCodeExecutionFault and #$EMailCodeExecutionFault.")
(comment EngineeringAcademicDepartment "A specialization of both #$EngineeringDepartment and #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct teaching and research in engineering.  See also #$EngineeringField.")
(comment enterBogusLoginInformationAtComputer "A binary #$ActionPredicate. (#$enterLoginInformationForAccountAtComputer AGENT COMP) means that AGENT enters a bogus #$usernameForAccount and #$passwordForAccount for at thew login prompt on COMP.")
(comment infectingEventActor "(#$infectingEventActor EVT ACTOR) means that #$SomethingExisting ACTOR plays a role in the #$InfectingEvent EVT. This predicate is a generalization of those #$ActorSlots that relate an instance of #$SomethingExisting to an instance of #$InfectingEvent. It is useful for collecting and querying for facts about an #$InfectingEvent. When possible, use a specialization of #$infectingEventActor to make assertions about a particular #$InfectingEvent. ")
(comment SurreptitiouslyFn "The action qualifier which qualifies actions as surreptitious.")
(comment NISDomain "#$NISDomain is a specialization of #$UnixAccountSystem.  Every #$NISDomain is the group of hosts that participate in the centralized management of configuration and login information run by one #$NISMasterServer-Network.")
(comment MonolithicKernel "A specialization of #$OperatingSystemKernel (q.v.).  Instances of this  collection are kernels that include numerous #$DeviceDriverPrograms. Cf. #$Microkernel.")
(comment WikiWiki "#$WikiWiki is a specialization of #$DynamicIndexedInfoSource.  Each instance of #$WikiWiki consists of interlinked web pages, each of which can be edited collaboratively using a simple markup scheme.  The WikiWiki was named by its inventor, Ward Cunningham -- \"wiki wiki\" means \"quick\" in the Hawaiian language.")
(comment ZoologyDepartment "A specialization of #$AcademicDepartment, instances of which conduct research and teaching regarding the scientific study of #$Animals.")
(comment changeAccountOnSystem "(#$changeAccountOnSystem AGENT ACCOUNT1 ACCOUNT2 SYSTEM) means that AGENT, who currently has access to ACCOUNT1, gains access to ACCOUNT2, where ACCOUNT1 and ACCOUNT2 are in the same #$AccountSystem SYSTEM.  Usually this predicate is used to represent an escalation of privilege, e.g., when ACCOUNT1 is a user account and ACCOUNT2 isa root account. However, its use is not limited to this kind of case.")
(comment TradeableSecurity "The collection of #$Agreements (some of which are technically #$LoanAgreements) issued by #$Organizations (typical examples include #$LegalCorporations and #$LocalGovernmentOrganizations) and bought and sold by investors.  An instance of #$TradeableSecurity being issued means that, in effect, the #$Agreement is sold to an investor or to a a #$creditor (which could be an individual investor or another #$Organization) for funds that are then held by the issuer of the security for it own use and either repaid at an agreed upon rate (see #$yieldToMaturity), paid in the form of dividends, or are absorbed by the #$Organization in return for ownership.")
(comment NISMasterServer-Network "A subcollection of #$NISServer-Network whose instances function as NIS master servers for #$NISDomains.")
(comment TextEditorProgram "A specialization of #$FileWritingProgram and #$FileReadingProgram. Instances of this collection are used to 
edit text files.  Text editors that embed control characters or escape sequences to control formating are instances of the
more specialized collection, #$WordProcessingProgram.")
(comment relationExistsMember "(#$relationExistsMember PRED COLL GROUP) means that for every MEMBER such that (#$groupMembers GROUP MEMBER), there exists an instance INS of collection COLL such that (PRED INS MEMBER) is true. This predicate enables one to make claims about the members of a group without referencing the members.")
(comment WikiEngine "#$WikiEngine is a specialization of #$HTMLEditor-Dynamic.  Each instance of #$WikiEngine is a script that runs wiki sites (instances of #$WikiWiki).")
(comment PoliticalScandal "The collection of all political #$Scandals.")
(comment seriesEnd "(#$seriesEnd SERIES END) means that END is either the first or last item of the #$Series, SERIES.")
(comment useReformulationRuleWithSalientDescriptor "Use this predicate to tag reformulator rules that are to be used

 immediately after the SME responds to a salient descriptor suggestion, and prior to 

wff-checking the SME's resultant assertion.")
(comment musicTypeInfluencedByEventType "(#$musicTypeInfluencedByEvent MUSIC-TYPE EVENT-TYPE) means a particular type of music MUSIC-TYPE was influenced by a particular type of event EVENT-TYPE.")
(comment Protoplasm "The living part of the cell within the plasma membrane.  That within the nucleus is the #$Nucleoplasm, that without is the #$Cytoplasm.")
(comment KillingThroughEventTypeFn "Where EVT_TYPE is a specialization of #$Event and an instance of #$TemporalObjectType, (#$KillingThroughEventTypeFn EVT_TYPE) denotes the collection of all instances of #$KillingByOrganism that come about as the result of and as part of an instance of EVT_TYPE:  i.e., the collection of all instances of #$KillingByOrganism that are #$subEvents of instances of EVT_TYPE such that the instance of EVT_TYPE may be considered the proximal cause of the killing.")
(comment NISSlaveServer-Network "A subcollection of #$NISServer-Network whose instances function as NIS slave servers for #$NISDomains.")
(comment AuthenticationMethodDisclosureFault "A program has this fault if the authentication method of a program or server can be revealed to an attacker through some means (such as the inspection of returned error messages, or access to the \"scheme file\").")
(comment WikiFarm "#$WikiFarm is a specialization of #$ComputerServer.  Each instance of #$WikiFarm is a server that runs an instance of #$WikiEngine that is available for others to use to develop their own instances of #$WikiWiki without configuring a #$WikiEngine and a #$WorldWideWebServerProgram themselves.")
(comment nonDavidsonianPredReln "The #$functionCorrespondingPredicate of the function #$NonDavidsonianPredFn.")
(comment objectIDField "(#$objectIDField SCHEMA ID_FIELD) means that unique values

of ID_FIELD correspond to unique instantiations of SCHEMA and that

ID_FIELD is the explicit field of SCHEMA chosen by the DBA as a unique

reference to the instantiations of SCHEMA.")
(comment ElementarySchool "The collection of elementary schools -- schools that teach children in the first four to eight grades, with six being the most standard in the US.  A kindergarden is often included in such a school.  Also called \"grammar school\" and \"grade school\".")
(comment nthInSeries "(#$nthInSeries SERIES ITEM N) means that ITEM is the Nth item in the #$Series SERIES.")
(comment CytoplasmLayer "The collection of pieces of #$Cytoplasm which are the complete cytoplasm of a cell.")
(comment ProgramAssignmentOperator "This is the collection of assignment operators found in programming languages.")
(comment SchoolInstitution-KThrough12 "#$SchoolInstitution-KThrough12 is a specialization of #$AcademicOrganization.  Each instance of #$SchoolInstitution-KThrough12 is a school which provides instruction in all or some of the grades from kindergarten (K) through high school (12th-grade) education.  Notable specializations of #$SchoolInstitution-KThrough12 include #$ElementarySchool, #$MiddleSchool, and #$HighSchool.")
(comment Nucleoplasm "The collection of all #$Protoplasm within the nuclear membrane of #$EukaryoticCells.  That without the nucleus is the #$Cytoplasm.")
(comment HigherEducationInstitution "#$HigherEducationInstitution is a specialization of #$AcademicOrganization. Two important types of #$HigherEducationInstitution are #$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution and #$NonDegreeGrantingInstitution.  Specs of #$DegreeGrantingHigherEducationInstitution include #$University, #$College, and #$CollegeInUniversity-DegreeGranting while specs of #$NonDegreeGrantingInstitution include #$CollegeInUniversity-NonDegreeGranting.")
(comment AuditingFinancialRecords "The collection of #$BusinessEvents in which the accounts of some #$Person or #$CommercialOrganization are officially examined and verified for the purpose of providing accurate figures and adequate accounting controls.")
(disjointWith Nucleoplasm Cytoplasm)
(comment ProgramLogicalOperator "This is the collection of logical operators found in programming languages.")
(comment UserOptionsWRTProgramActionFn "(#$UserOptionsWRTProgramActionFn PROGRAM-ACTION) denotes the collection of all specializations of (#$UsingAFn #$Computer) that are options for the user to perform in response to PROGRAM-ACTION, a type of #$ProgramAction.")
(comment FieldSchool "Used in archaeology, field schools are sites where a long-term dig is progressing while students are receiving college or graduate level instruction together with first-hand experience.")
(comment DisjointSetOrCollectionType "A collection of mathematical sets and collections whose elements are themselves mathematical sets or collections.  A set or collection, SETORCOL, of sets or collections is an instance of #$DisjointSetOrCollectionType just in case the elements of SETORCOL are mutually disjoint -- that is, no two elements of SETORCOL have any elements in common.")
(comment ServerConnectionRequest "The collection of #$NetworkPacketTransfers in which a connection request is made to a server.")
(comment schemaKeys "This predicate relates a physical schema with a set of its physical fields that defines a key for the schema.  There may be more than one key for a schema, however if a key is chosen by the schema designers to be the canonical key for the schema, then the specialization, #$primaryKey holds as well.  Else, the specialization #$secondaryKeys holds.  See the #$SharedNoteAboutKeysInSKSI for a definition of a key.")
(comment OperatorFn "Denotes operators in programming languages. For Example: (#$OperatorFn \"=\") would

denote the assignment operator in a C programming context.")
(comment ContractingAService "This is the script for the generic event-type in which two agents come to an agreement for one to perform a service for the other in return for compensation.")
(comment UserOptionsWRTUIAActionFn "(#$UserOptionsWRTUIAActionFn PROGRAM-ACTION) denotes the collection of all specializations of (#$UsingProgramFn #$UIA-CycProgram) that are options for the user to perform in response to PROGRAM-ACTION, a type of #$UIAProgramAction.")
(disjointWith ClosingSomething FluidFlowEvent)
(comment ComputerTypeByBrand "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ComputerTypeByBrand is a collection of computers, where that collection is a #$ProductTypeByBrand.")
(comment taskEfficiencyOfType "(#$taskEfficiencyOfType EVENT-TYPE

 EFFIC-LEVEL) means that typically, every task TASK in the collection EVENT-TYPE

 is completed with efficiency level, EFFIC-LEVEL.   Efficiency presumably is based on measures of rate and/or amount of input compared to amount of output or success of output.")
(comment initiatePacketTransferOfTypeToProgramFromTo "(#$initiatePacketTransferOfTypeToProgramFromTo AGENT TRANSFER PROG SYSTEM1 SYSTEM2) means that from SYSTEM1 AGENT initiates TRANSFER to the program PROG running on SYSTEM2.")
(disjointWith ClosingSomething ShootingAProjectileWeapon)
(comment primaryKey "This functional predicate relates a physical schema with the unique set of physical fields with the following properties (i) the set defines a key for the schema (see #$schemaKeys for a definition of a key) and (ii) this key in particular was chosen by the schema designers to be the canonical reference to individual elements of the schema.  See also the sibling predicate #$secondaryKeys. Together, #$primaryKey and #$secondaryKeys partition #$schemaKeys. That is, if (#$schemaKeys SCHEMA KEY) is true, then either (#$primaryKey SCHEMA KEY) is true, or (#$secondaryKeys SCHEMA KEY) is true, but never both simultaneously.")
(comment modifiedForPasswordlessLogin "(#$modifiedForPasswordlessLogin AGENT PROGRAM ACCOUNT COMPUTER) means that AGENT has modified PROGRAM on COMPUTER so that users can login to ACCOUNT via PROGRAM without being prompted for a username or password.")
(comment infectionActor "(#$infectionActor INFECTION ACTOR) means that #$SomethingExisting ACTOR plays a role in the #$Infection INFECTION. This predicate is a generalization of those #$ActorSlots that relate an instance of #$SomethingExisting to an instance of #$Infection. It is useful for collecting and querying for facts about an #$Infection. When possible, use a specialization of #$infectionActor to make assertions about a particular #$Infection.")
(comment precedesInSeries "(#$precedesInSeries ITEM1 ITEM2 SERIES) means that ITEM1 comes before ITEM2 in the series, SERIES.")
(disjointWith Country EducationalOrganization)
(comment licenseAppliesToSoftware "#$licenseAppliesToSoftware is a binary predicate that relates instances of #$License-LegalAgreement to instances of  #$SoftwareObject.  (#$licenseAppliesToSoftware LICENSE PROG) means that the legimate uses of PROG are subject to the terms of LICENSE.")
(disjointWith ClosingSomething ProgrammingAComputer)
(comment Hijacker "People who have engaged in hijacking at some point.  Does not include those who are planning hijacking or are otherwise potential, but not yet actual hijackers.")
(comment chemicalBondBetween "(#$chemicalBondBetween CHEMICALBOND CHEMICALOBJECT1 CHEMICALOBJECT2) means that CHEMICALBOND, an instance of chemical bond, connects CHEMICALOBJECT1 and CHEMICALOBJECT2.")
(comment GregorianMonthType "A collection of #$Collections. Instances of #$GregorianMonthType are the canonical subsets of #$GregorianMonth in the #$GregorianCalendar system.")
(comment SegmentsFn "(#$SegmentsFn TANG) denotes the collection of proper segments of the #$SegmentedCordlikeObject TANG.  For example, (#$SegmentsFn Chain001) denotes the collection of chain links of Chain001.")
(comment DVDPlayer-Software "A specialization of #$MultimediaProgram. Each instance of this collection is a computer program designed to play DVDs. Not to be confused with #$DVDPlayer, the specialized piece of hardware.")
(comment leadGuitarist "(#$leadGuitarist GROUP GUITARIST) means that GUITARIST is the lead guitarist in GROUP.")
(comment IslamicMonthType "A collection of #$Collections. Instances of #$IslamicMonthType are the canonical subsets of #$IslamicMonth in the #$IslamicLunarCalendar system.")
(comment Country "A specialization of #$GeopoliticalEntity.  Each instance of #$Country is a nation-state having its own territory, population, and government, whether or not it is fully independent.  For example, #$Scotland is an instance of #$Country, even though it is a part of the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland.  See also the important specialization #$IndependentCountry.")
(comment secondaryKeys "This predicate relates a physical schema with one of its secondary keys.  That is, (#$secondaryKeys SCHEMA KEY) means that (i) KEY is a key for SCHEMA (see the generalization #$schemaKeys) and (ii) KEY is not the primary key for SCHEMA (see the sibling #$primaryKey).  For a definition of a key, see the #$SharedNoteAboutKeysInSKSI")
(comment bindingSite "(#$bindingSite MOLECULE SITE) means that SITE [an instance of #$MolecularComponent] is a #$molecularSubComponents of MOLECULE [an instance of #$ChemicalObject] at which instances of #$ChemicalObject of a very restricted type preferentially bond.")
(comment MP3Program "The collection of all computer programs whose function is to manipulate #$MP3Files.")
(disjointWith BeliefSystemFocusGroup GeopoliticalEntity)
(comment ChemicalBindingSite "The collection of parts of molecules that preferentially bind to other molecules of a limited set of chemical types.  An individual #$ChemicalBindingSite consists of the atoms which can bond with molecules of the restricted types as well as any atoms in between them that rigidly position the reactive atoms.")
(comment VideoProgram "The collection of all #$ComputerProgram-CWs designed to manipulate video computer files.")
(comment Songwriter "The collection of instances of #$Person who write songs.")
(comment AdministrationProgram "A specialization of #$UtilityProgram. Programs run by humans in order to manage services, processes, users, files, and other types of control such as booting and configuring other programs.")
(comment UninstallationProgram "Software that uninstalls another program (or programs) when executed.")
(disjointWith ResearchOrganization GeopoliticalEntity)
(comment InformingProgramUser "The collection of all events in which an instance of #$SoftwareAgent provides information to an interactive user of an instance of #$ComputerProcessRunning.")
(comment Sometimes-GenericFrequency "The most general of all instances of #$Frequency.  Every frequency #$genlAttributes up to this frequency, except #$Never, which is its #$negationAttribute.")
(disjointWith CapturingSomething Stealing)
(comment Business "A specialization of #$CommercialOrganization (q.v.).  Each instance of #$Business is an organization intended to make profits, i.e. to make money for agents who own them.  Note that not all #$CommercialOrganizations are #$Businesses.  For example, in a franchise #$Organization, while the parent company (see #$parentCompany) is regarded as a business, the sub-organizations  are commercial organizations but not businesses.  Also, #$Businesses are typically #$LegalAgents, while #$CommercialOrganizations need not be.")
(comment InformingTheUser "The collection of all events in which an instance of #$SoftwareAgent provides information to #$TheUser.")
(comment bindingSiteBetween "(#$bindingSiteBetween CHEMICAL CHEM_TYPE BINDING_SITE) means that chemicals of type CHEM_TYPE will preferentially bond to CHEMICAL at BINDING_SITE, which is a #$molecularSubComponents of CHEMICAL.")
(comment HitConceptualWork "The collection of all instances of #$ConceptualWork that are deemed highly successful, e.g. songs that make the top 40, plays that are performed on Broadway (and subsequently elsewhere), books that make best-seller lists, etc.")
(comment NormallyFn "An instance of #$EventQualifyingFunction.  #$NormallyFn takes a specialization of #$Event as an argument and returns the collection of events that are not qualified in any particular manner.  (#$NormallyFn EVENT) denotes the collection of instances of EVENT that are qualified as normal (i.e.,  unqualified).")
(comment editFileOfTypeOn "(#$editFileOfTypeOn AGENT FILE-TYPE COMP) means that AGENT edits a file of type FILE-TYPE found on the computer COMP.")
(comment ParsingText "#$ParsingText is the analysis of text to produce a
understanding of what is being said, especially in reference to
automating machine understanding of the text. Typically this involves
an analysis of the syntactic structure of the text and an
interpretation in terms of corresponding semantic structures.")
(comment AcceptingProgramUserCommunication "The collection of all events in which an instance of #$SoftwareAgent accepts information from an interactive user of an instance of #$ComputerProcessRunning.")
(comment softwareUpdateDownloadLink "(#$softwareUpdateDownloadLink 

PROGRAM URL) means that updates of PROGRAM are available for download on an 

ongoing basis from the website that URL points to. See also 

#$softwareVendorUpdateDownloadLink, which provides URLs for general update

pages maintained by specific vendors.")
(comment segmentOfChain-Individual "(#$segmentOfChain-Individual CHAIN LINK) says that LINK is a proper segment of CHAIN, a #$SegmentedCordlikeObject.")
(disjointWith HandingOverControlOfSomething Stealing)
(comment TripleBond "The collection of all #$CovalentBonds in which three pairs of electrons are shared.")
(comment hostages "'(#$hostages HOLDING PERSON)' means that PERSON is being held hostage in the #$HoldingHostages event HOLDING.")
(disjointWith AcceptingProgramUserCommunication PoweringADevice)
(disjointWith FixedOrderCollection VariedOrderCollection)
(disjointWith TotallyOrderedScalarIntervalType MatterTypeByPhysicalState)
(disjointWith CapturingSomething HandingOverControlOfSomething)
(comment SingleBond "The collection of all #$CovalentBonds in which a single pair of electrons is shared.")
(comment EmeticAgentStuff "Instances of #$EmeticAgentStuff are substances that, if inhaled or ingested, will induce vomiting.")
(comment SikkimPerson "The people who are #$citizens of #$Sikkim-StateIndia, or participate in its #$HumanCulture.")
(comment Antioxidant "#$Antioxidants reduce the risk of free radical health related problems, such as #$Cancer and #$Atherosclerosis, by preventing oxidation which could cause a change in the ways cells differentiate.")
(comment SuckingLouse "The collection of all instances of #$Louse that have mouth parts designed for sucking blood. These are the lice that attack humans and
are the transmitters of many human diseases.")
(comment LagerBeer "A light form of #$Beer (contrast with #$AleBeer and #$StoutBeer) that originated in #$Germany, containing carbon dioxide and a bitterness derived from hops. Golden-colored and refreshing, #$LagerBeer is a popular summer alternative to #$StoutBeer and an all-year-round favorite with #$Beer drinkers.")
(comment typeIngredientTypes "'(#$typeIngredientTypes TYPE1 TYPE2)' means that all instances of TYPE1 have some instances of TYPE2 as ingredients.  Thus, this is a type-level version of #$ingredients.")
(comment NuclearRelatedMaterial "The collection of all #$NuclearRelatedThings that are at least #$PartiallyTangible. The collection includes, for example, all #$Artifacts which are components in nuclear reactors, and also all kinds of #$NuclearFuel, as well as nonfissionable #$RadioactiveStuff.  #$NuclearServiceEvents are specifically excluded.")
(comment (ChemicalSubstanceFn HydrogenPeroxideMolecule) "The collection of samples of hydrogen peroxide; H2O2.")
(comment Refining "A specialization of #$SeparationEvent.  Each instance of #$Refining is an event in which some stuff is transformed from an impure or crude state into a fine or pure state.")
(comment muzzleVelocity "(#$muzzleVelocity GUN SPEED) states that when  #$ProjectileShellAssembly passes through the #$Muzzle-GunPart when fired from  GUN, it occurs on average at a certain SPEED.  The unit of SPEED to use is  #$MetersPerSecond.")
(comment USCashHealthCarePayer "The collection of #$UnitedStatesPersons who pay for health care goods and services out-of-pocket.")
(comment HealthCarePayerType "A collection of collections. Each #$HealthCarePayerType is a different type of agent who pays for health care services. See also #$USPersonByMedicalBenefitProvider.")
(comment AustralianAntarcticTerritoryPerson "A person who is a resident of the #$AustralianAntarcticTerritory.")
(comment PuttingSomethingSomewhere "A collection of events.  An instance of #$PuttingSomethingSomewhere is an event in which an #$Agent-Generic guides a moving object to a new location.  This #$Agent-Generic is often, but not always, the #$providerOfMotiveForce in the event.  The #$Agent-Generic, or some instrument under its control, must accompany the #$objectMoving along its #$motionPathway-Complete.  For example, someone lifting a crate, or steering a car, and placing it in some location (e.g., a garage), carries out an instance of #$PuttingSomethingSomewhere.  The #$providerOfMotiveForce and the #$objectMoving (the focal object moving) must be distinct.")
(comment deathToll "A ternary predicate that relates a given event to the number of deaths it caused within a specified population. (#$deathToll EVENT ORGTYPE N) means that N instances of ORGTYPE (some specialization of #$Organism-Whole) either died in the course of EVENT itself or died as an immediate and direct result of EVENT.  Thus, both (#$deathToll #$BombingOfNagasaki #$HomoSapiens 40000) and (#$deathToll IrradiationCausedByBombingOfNagasaki #$HomoSapiens 100000) are (at least approximately) true.")
(comment HumanOccupationConstructResident "Each specialization of #$HumanOccupationConstructResident is a type of creature that commonly resides in structures that house people (see the related constant #$HumanOccupationConstruct).")
(comment IncapacitatingAgentStuff "The collection of #$ToxicSubstances designed  to cause temporary disability in its target.")
(comment Deciding-Collectively "The collection of events in which a decision is reached by some group of agents (cf. #$Agent-Generic), and in which the relevant opinions of each of the agents are given due consideration in reaching that decision. This collection includes cases of informal collective decision-making (such as when a group of friends makes a collective decision to see a particular movie), as well as cases of formal collective decision-making (such as national #$Elections)")
(comment NuclearWeaponProductionFacility "The collection of facilities where    #$NuclearWeapons    are built.")
(comment WeightLossProgram "The collection of all 'programs' available for    one to follow in order to lose weight.  When following such a program, one is #$DietingForWeightLoss.  Instances include the Weight Watcher's program as well as the Atkins Diet.")
(comment CityNamedFn "The Cyc function #$CityNamedFn is an #$IndividualDenotingFunction.  (#$CityNamedFn STRING GEOPOL) applied to a (quoted) #$ProperNameString STRING which is the name of a city in region GEOPOL returns the #$City in that region with that name.  Examples: (#$CityNamedFn \"New York City\" #$NewYork-State); (#$CityNamedFn \"Columbus\" #$FranklinCountyOhio);  (#$CityNamedFn \"Taipei\" #$Taiwan-RepublicOfChina).  Note the assumption that there is only one so-named city as a #$geopoliticalSubdivision of the #$GeopoliticalEntity specified.")
(comment ProtectiveFiltrationMask "The collection of all #$Masks whose primary purpose is to protect the lung tissue and respiratory processes of the wearer by
filtering potentially harmful substances from the air.  Secondary purposes may also include protecting the eyes, facial skin, and nose and throat tissue of the user.")
(comment MetropolitanAreaFn "An #$IndividualDenotingFunction. (#$MetropolitanAreaFn
CITY) denotes the #$MetropolitanArea in and around CITY in which social
and economic activity are substantially interconnected.")
(comment casualtyCount "A ternary predicate that relates a given event to the number of deaths, injuries and other losses it caused within a specified population. (#$casualtyCount EVENT ORGTYPE N) means that N instances of ORGTYPE (some specialization of #$Organism-Whole) were injured, killed or lost as an immediate and direct result of EVENT. For injuries and killings considered separately, see #$injuryCount and #$deathToll respectively.")
(comment inboundLegOfRoundTrip "(#$inboundLegOfRoundTrip TRIP INBOUND) means that the translational movement INBOUND is the final portion of the round-trip translation event TRIP.  In other words, INBOUND is the `return trip' portion of TRIP.  During the INBOUND leg, the primary object moving in TRIP (see the predicate #$primaryObjectMoving) travels from the destination of TRIP (see the predicate #$destination-RoundTrip) back to its origin (see the predicate #$origin-RoundTrip).  Since the origin of TRIP is the ending point of INBOUND, it is related to INBOUND by #$toLocation (q.v.), and since the destination of TRIP is the starting point of INBOUND, it is related to INBOUND by #$fromLocation (q.v.).")
(comment injuryCount "A ternary predicate that relates a given event to the number of injuries it caused within a specified population. (#$injuryCount EVENT ORGTYPE N) means that N instances of ORGTYPE (some specialization of #$Organism-Whole) were injured as an immediate and direct result of EVENT. See also #$deathToll, #$casualtyCount.")
(comment effectiveBetweenDates "An instance of #$TernaryPredicate.  (effectiveBetweenDates STBMT DATE1 DATE2) means that the instance of #$SupposedToBeMicrotheory STBMT, went into effect on DATE1 and will remain in effect until DATE2.")
(comment DramaticPerformance "#$DramaticPerformance is the collection of instances of #$EntertainmentPerformance such that (#$PerformingFn #$DramaticPerformance) returns a collection of instances of #$DramaticActing - these may be subevents of instances of #$DancePerformance, Play-Dramatic, #$Play-Musical-CW or #$OperaPerformance, as in #$DramaticActing-Live, or they may be instances of #$DramaticActingForFilm.--Huffer, Dec. 2, 1998")
(comment TextileArtifact "#$TextileArtifact is a specialization of #$Artifact-NonAgentive, #$DurableGoods, #$SolidTangibleArtifact, and #$CommodityProduct.  Each instance of #$TextileArtifact is a product made by spinning, weaving, knitting, wrapping, pressing, or other processes used to form fibers into usable materials such as cloth or linen.  Notable specializations of #$TextileArtifact include #$Cloth, #$Cord-Textile, and #$Netting.")
(comment Plastic "#$Plastic is a specialization of #$ArtificialMaterial.  Each instance of #$Plastic is a piece of some type of plastic.  This collection includes plastics of all kinds: artificial, mostly polymeric, inedible, organic moldable hydrocarbons.  Some common types are #$Rayon, #$Nylon, polyethylene, etc.")
(comment Pigment "instances are pieces of a chemical compound that impart color.")
(comment countyOfAddress "(#$countyOfAddress LOC COUNTY) means that the  #$ContactLocation LOC is found in the territory of the #$County COUNTY. For example, as   #$CycorpHeadquarters is a #$ContactLocation for #$Cycorp, then  (#$countyOfAddress #$CycorpHeadquarters #$TravisCountyTexas) means that the  Cycorp Headquarters building is located in Travis County, Texas.  Note that  the arg-constraint on the first argument should be an instance of #$ContactLocation  which serves as a #$pointsOfContact for an agent and not the agent itself.")
(comment clothingTypeForSituationTypeAt "This predicate relates places and kinds of social occurrences to attire that is appropriate to wear to instances of the social occurrences that occur at the place. (#$clothingTypeForSituationTypeAt PLACE SOCOC-TYPE            ATTIRETYPE) means that participants in instances of SOCOC-TYPE that occur at PLACE are expected to wear instances of ATTIRETYPE during the event. ")
(comment Scale-AnimalBodyPart "Outer covering, analogous to skin, of reptiles and fish.  See also #$ScaledAnimal, the collection of animals covered with scales.")
(comment SolidFn "An instance of #$CollectionDenotingFunction.  When applied to an instance STUFF-TYPE of #$TangibleStuffCompositionType, #$SolidFn returns as its value all of the instances of STUFF-TYPE that are also instances of #$SolidTangibleThing (q.v.).  For example, (#$SolidFn #$Water-Fresh) is the collection of all instances of #$Water-Fresh that are also instances of #$SolidTangibleThing; thus, it would include as instances an ice cube, the layer of ice at the top of a frozen-over river, and so on.")
(comment WaterSportActivity "The collection of sports activities that are performed in/on water")
(comment CulturalThing "The collection of all temporal things, including both activities and objects, that are either created or adopted by any culture that has them, and thus can distinguish one culture or set of cultures from another.")
(comment economicInterestIn "(#$economicInterestIn AGENT OBJ) means that AGENT has an economic interest in OBJ.  Examples include trading partners, goods, and trade agreements.  It is important that this predicate not be used to express interest in everything that a particular interest requires.  For example, although one has a trade interest in one's business partners, it is difficult to see how one has a trade interest in a business partner's  health, although the latter is arguably related to sustaining the former.")
(comment Artist-Performer "A specialization of #$Artist and of #$Entertainer. Each instance of this collection is a person watched by the audience during some instance of #$EntertainmentPerformance. Note that this collection includes only individual performers and not, for instance, musical groups (for that, see #$MusicPerformanceAgent).")
(comment Musician "A specialization of #$Artist. Each instance of this collection is an artist whose medium is #$Sound. Notable specializations of this collection include #$MusicalComposer and #$MusicalPerformer.")
(comment MusicalPerformer "A specialization of #$Artist-Performer, #$Musician and #$MusicPerformanceAgent. Each instance of this collection is a an individual person performing music for an audience. For groups or bands, see #$MusicPerformanceAgent.")
(comment MusicPerformanceAgent "A collection of agents. Each instance of            #$MusicPerformanceAgent is either an instance of #$MusicPerformanceOrganization (if it is, say, a group or band), or an instance of #$MusicalPerformer (if it is an individual musician).  Each instance has as a main function or activity the playing/performing of music for some audience, either direct (live performance) or mediated through recordings or radio or TV broadcasts.")
(comment SunProtectionStuff "Goods that help protect people from ultraviolet rays while they are in the sun.")
(comment Trustworthy "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that are trustworthy, reliable.")
(comment Technophile "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent enamored of technology.  Such agents like gadgets and are typically interested in the newest advances in technology.")
(comment compatibleWithIn "(#$compatibleWithIn PROD1 PROD2 SCRIPT) states that instances of PROD1 are compatible with instances of PROD2 when used in scripts of type SCRIPT.  The roles that each object must play are stated as their primaryFunction assertions involving SCRIPT")
(comment RoadVehicleTypeByModel "A collection of collections, each element of #$RoadVehicleTypeByModel is a collection of road vehicle types categorized by model. For example, #$HondaCivicCar, the collection of Honda Civics, would be an element of this collection, as would be the collection of Harley Davidson Sportster motorcycles.")
(comment DiscStorageMedium "A spec of #$InformationStorageMedia, this is the collection of all disks used for storage of information.  This includes floppy disks as well as hard disks.")
(comment ManufacturedGoods "The collection of all #$Artifacts that are made or processed in large-scale industrial operations for distribution (normally sale) to agents outside the manufacturing organization.  This includes manufactured stuff, e.g. Finlandia vodka; refined ore, e.g. iron; otherwise procesed natural material, e.g. cut diamonds, as well as manufactured objects.  This collection excludes handicrafts; privately made stuff, e.g. moonshine; and other artifacts produced by one or a few people on a small scale.")
(comment hasPersonality "'(#$hasPersonality AGENT ALITY)' means that #$IntelligentAgent AGENT has the personality ALITY.")
(comment Animal "An instance of #$BiologicalKingdom, and a specialization of #$Organism-Whole.  Instances of #$Animal are typically motile, living, whole organisms; they are instances of #$Heterotroph (q.v.), and thus incapable of performing instances of #$Photosynthesis-Generic.  Animal cells contain cholesterol and lack cell walls made of cellulose.")
(comment typeInstancesHaveQuantity "(#$typeInstancesHaveQuantity COL QUANTITY) means that every instance of COL has the quantity of the property stated by QUANTITY.")
(comment CholinesteraseInhibitingSubstance "The collection of #$ToxicSubstances that can react with #$Acetylcholinesterase in an animal's #$NervousSystem.  In sufficient dosages, instance of this collection can induce #$AcetylcholinePoisoning.")
(comment VE-NerveAgent "A #$NerveAgentType which is extremely lethal when inhaled.")
(comment PersonalProduct "A specialization of #$Artifact.  Each instance of #$PersonalProduct is an object or substance designed for use on and the benefit of the physical body of a person, including personal care products (e.g., deodorant, hand soap), personal care devices (e.g., razors, heating pads), and cosmetics.  These are items which a person would seek out or apply to him/herself; i.e., it excludes products used on the body of a person by physicians (e.g., scalpels), dentists (e.g., dental drills), or morticians.")
(disjointWith ArtSupplies SomethingToWear)
(comment NonPersonAnimal "The collection of all instances of #$Animal that are not instances of #$Person, and thus incapable of participating in the activities and social roles characteristic of personhood. (For the more 'biological' concept of #$Animals that are not instances of #$HomoSapiens, see #$NonHumanAnimal).")
(comment MediaProduct "A specialization of #$InformationStore.  Each instance of #$MediaProduct is an information store created for the purposes of media distribution (see #$MediaTransferEvent).  Specializations of #$MediaProduct include #$RecordedVideoProduct, #$MediaSeriesProduct, #$WorldWideWebSite and #$NewsArticle.")
(comment MultipleUserComputer "The collection of instances of #$Computer designed to be used by multiple 
persons. (e.g. a VAX mainframe)")
(comment AdventurousPersonality "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that are disposed to try new or unknown things, especially those with an element of risk.  Instances of this collection often appreciate outdoor activities.")
(comment NuclearProduct "An instance of #$ProductType.  This collection comprises all #$NuclearRelatedThings that are for sale or in storage to be sold at some later point, i.e. are #$Products.")
(comment PleasantPersonality "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that have a pleasant personality, one that people view as comfortable or nice to be around.")
(comment Vicious "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that are vicious, meaning malicious and marked by deep ill will or deliberately and aggressively harmful.")
(comment ObjectionableSpeech "a quality of lexical senses or words that are considered socially objectionable.")
(comment TopicallyAppliedSubstance "This collection is intended to include substances that are used for medicinal purposes as well as those used for hygienic ones.  It only includes substances that are applied on the body's surface, and not those which are ingested, worn, or implanted.")
(comment RudeSpeech "a quality of lexical senses or words that are considered rude")
(comment Gentle "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent with a kindly, tender, and mild nature.")
(comment VulgarSpeech "a quality of lexical senses or words that are considered vulgar")
(comment Technophobe "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that are afraid of technology.  Agents who have this attribute  tend to be Luddites, opposing progress in technology; they are afraid to use new, high-tech tools.")
(comment GuerillaForce "The collection of all groups that engage in guerilla warfare.  These are often small defensive forces of irregular soldiers, usually volunteers, making surprise raids, especially behind the lines of the  invading enemy army.")
(comment SexyPersonality "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent  that project sex appeal, tending to arouse sexual desire.")
(comment Macho "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that project a tough, virile, masculine image.")
(comment LevelOfTouch "The collection of touch pressure quantities that describe the pressure of a touch.")
(comment FractiousPersonality "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that tend to be divisive, to argue and to cause bad feelings, etc.")
(comment SafetyConscious "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that are particularly concerned with their personal safety.")
(comment RuggedPersonality "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that are tough, capable of enduring hardship.")
(comment Charismatic "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that are attractive either physically or personally in a way that arouses popular enthusiasm and/or loyalty, as for a political leader or actor.")
(comment Diligent "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent marked by patiently persevering at carrying out tasks, especially with detail or exactness.")
(comment AnalRetentivePersonality "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that that are overly concerned with rules, order, or neatness.  Such agents are often viewed as stingy and too meticulous.  They tend to have a poor sense of humor.  Such agents have traits that are considered by Freudian #$Psychoanalysts to be typical of those who are fixated at the \"anal stage\" of psychosexual development.")
(comment Dependable-Personality "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent that are consistent and dependable.")
(comment PracticalPersonality "The collection of instances of #$IntelligentAgent concerned with actual use or practice, as opposed to theory.")
(comment SqueezingWithHand "The collection of instances of #$HoldingWithOneHand in which the hand is putting considerable pressure on the object being held.  The hand can be in any position.")
(comment HoldingWithHand "When #$HoldingWithHand, the object held is clasped, not just supported.  In order to hold something one must first grab it.  Also one never holds anything forever.  Thus it is redundant to state that a holding and a grabbing or releasing are all #$subEvents of some event.  #$HoldingWithHand is agnostic as to whether the performer is holding the object with one hand or both.")
(comment stateOfLegalResidence "(#$stateOfLegalResidence PERSON STATE)  means that the person PERSON is a legal resident of the #$State-Geopolitical STATE (where STATE can be an instance of #$State-UnitedStates or some other country subsidiary such as a province).   While different states have different criteria for legal residency, most have  criteria that require the person to demonstrate that he/she considers that state  his/her true, fixed, and permanent home.")
(comment FluidReservoir "A specialization of #$ContainerArtifact.  Each instance of #$FluidReservoir is a container designed to hold fluids.  Instances of #$FluidReservoir generally have an opening, which may be small and resealable (as in a #$Bottle) or large and open (as in a #$Tub).  Note a special negative case: natural `reservoirs', such as #$Lakes, are not #$ContainerArtifacts -- though the #$Dams that create some of them are artifacts, the reservoir water is contained in the natural landscape -- and hence such reservoirs are not instances of #$FluidReservoir.")
(comment CentralAmericanPerson "The collection of people who are citizens or subjects of a Central America #$GeopoliticalEntity.")
(comment SoundStructure "The collection of instances of #$ObjectTypeBySensibleFeature that are audible qualities of sounds.  For example, the feature a sound has when it the sequence of played notes D, A, and G occur in this order is a #$SoundStructure. There is no limit to how complex #$SoundStructures may be. For example, there is a single #$SoundStructure, SOUND, corresponding to the entirety of a given performance of a symphony, PERFORMANCE1. Any other performance which instantiates SOUND would sound exactly like PERFORMANCE1.")
(comment LiteraryWork-CW "The collection of all works of literature, broadly construed. Including articles, essays, as well as novels and poems.")
(comment AerialPerspective "The collection of instances of #$VisualImage that have a perspective looking down upon the subject.")
(comment ExpositoryArticle "The collection of all articles [#$Article-PCW] which, in the current #$Microtheory, meet the criteria for articles such that their most salient style is \"expository\". Such articles are written in a way so as to \"lay out the facts\", \"explain meanings\", \"describe the truth\".  Note that although the definition of #$ExpositoryArticle must meet certain stylistic criteria, the current #$Microtheory need not claim that the contents of #$ExpositoryArticles are factual, correct, etc..  Consider the following 4 examples which assume that one is in microtheory which defines \"expository\" as a \"20th Century Scientific Rationalist\" person would.  (1) Any professional scientific journal article would be a typical positive example of #$ExpositoryArticle.  (2) The writings of #$ThomasAquinas could qualify as a positive example of #$ExpositoryArticle even though the contents of his writings might not be considered factual.  (3) A _Reader's Digest_ article version of #$MobyDickNovel would be a negative example of #$ExpositoryArticle since its contents would be considered a narrative, and thus not in expository style. (Note that, even if said article contained expository tracts on whaling and ships, its most salient overall style would be narrative, and thus not expository.)  (4) An article from the \"Journal of Irreproducible Results\", although fictional, is a positive example because it is written expositorily. To be sure, note that membership in #$ExpositoryArticle may change as one moves to microtheories which posit different requirements for what is considered \"expository\".  For example, in a microtheory which defined \"expository\" as per around the time of #$TheRenaissance, an article-sized excerpt of #$GalileoGalilei's \"Dialogue Concerning the Two Chief World Systems, Ptolemaic & Copernican\" could arguably count as an #$ExpositoryArticle.  However, in a microtheory such as #$MainstreamAmericanCultureMt, it would be much more of a stretch to claim that something in the style of the previously mentioned dialogue would be an admissible element of #$ExpositoryArticle.")
(disjointWith WithoutHair SparselyHairy)
(comment ScholarlyArticle "The collection of all articles [#$Article-PCW] which present the results of a scientific investigation or a scientific explanation of how some part of reality works.")
(disjointWith PartiallyHairy SparselyHairy)
(disjointWith PartiallyHairy CoveredWithHair)
(comment areasOfOrigin "The predicate #$areasOfOrigin relates an ethnic group to a particular region in which its members originated.  (#$areasOfOrigin GROUP REGION) means that the #$PersonTypeByEthnicity GROUP originated in the #$GeographicalRegion REGION.  For example, to indicate that Circassians originated in Asia, we would say (#$areasOfOrigin #$EthnicGroupOfCircassians #$ContinentOfAsia).  Ethnic groups may have originated in several different areas; e.g., the #$EthnicGroupOfHutu is native to the territories of #$Rwanda, #$Burundi, #$Tanzania, and #$Uganda.")
(comment Cramping "The collection of conditions one is in when a muscle in some body part contracts with spasms.")
(comment FoodVessel "A specialization of #$ContainerArtifact.  Each instance of #$FoodVessel is a portable container designed for holding, storing, or preparing food or drink.  Specializations of #$FoodVessel include the collections #$CookingVessel, #$EatingVessel, and #$FoodStorageContainer.")
(comment HarmfulChemicalSubstance "A specialization of #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance (q.v.).  Each instance of #$HarmfulChemicalSubstance is a sample of some #$ChemicalSubstanceType or mixture thereof that can kill or incapacitate.")
(comment irrelevantAssertion "A #$CycInferenceHeuristicRelevancePredicate. (#$irrelevantAssertion ASSERTION) states that the #$CycLAssertion ASSERTION should be heuristically considered very unlikely to be relevant to inferences in the current #$Microtheory.  See also other instances of #$CycInferenceHeuristicRelevancePredicate.")
(comment irrelevantMt "A #$CycInferenceHeuristicRelevancePredicate. (#$irrelevantMt MT) means that all assertions made in the #$Microtheory MT should be heuristically considered very unlikely to be relevant to inferences done in the #$Microtheory MT-1 in which (#$irrelevantMt MT) is asserted (where MT-1 and MT need not be the same).  As a consequence, note that when (#$irrelevantMt MT) is asserted in a Microtheory MT-1, each of the assertions in MT will be an #$irrelevantAssertion (q.v.) for inferences done in MT-1.")
(comment irrelevantPredAssertion "(#$irrelevantPredAssertion PREDICATE ASSERTION) states that the given ASSERTION should be heuristically considered very unlikely to be relevant to inferences concluding uses of the given PREDICATE in the current mt.  See also other instances of #$CycInferenceHeuristicRelevancePredicate.")
(disjointWith ChangedActor UnchangedActor)
(disjointWith ShortPhysicalBuild TallPhysicalBuild)
(comment InhalationalAnthrax "Instances of #$InhalationalAnthrax are infections [see #$Infection] caused by a colony of B. Anthracis [see #$Anthrax-Bacterium] the original population of which entered the body of the host via the respiratory tract. Two major subcollections are #$InhalationalAnthrax-Natural, the 'naturally' occurring form of the disease and #$InhalationalAnthrax-BW.")
(comment Colorful "The collection of colorful things.  Something that is colorful is typically composed of 2 or more #$BrightColors")
(comment Monomer "The collection of all molecular structures that serve or can
serve as 'building blocks' of #$PolymerMolecules, which are long-chain
molecular structures.")
(comment FireExtinguisher "A device that produces a mixture of gas and liquid to extinguish fire.")
(comment AcademicBookReport "A kind of #$AcademicComposition in which the #$Student reports on a book [#$Book-CW] which he or she has (ostensibly) read.")
(comment ProseLiteraryWork-CW "The collection of all #$PropositionalConceptualWorks which are prose. Including all instances of #$Article-PCW, #$AcademicEssay, #$Novel-CW.")
(comment unitOfPolymerMolecule "(#$unitOfPolymerMolecule POLYMER-TYPE MONOMER-TYPE) means that instances of POLYMER-TYPE, a spec of #$PolymerMolecule, are sequences of instances of MONOMER-TYPE, a spec of #$ChemicalObject.")
(disjointWith Unshaved WithoutHair)
(comment Rust "The reddish-brown coating that forms on an object in a #$RustingProcess.")
(comment actsInCapacity-SupportFunction "(#$actsInCapacity-SupportFunction AGT ROLE EVT-TYPE) hold just in case AGT's role in events of type EVT-TYPE is of a supporting function (not as the main function).")
(comment BiologicalDestructionEvent "A specialization of both #$PhysicalDestructionEvent and #$BiologicalProcess.  In each instance  of #$BiologicalDestructionEvent, some instance(s) of  #$BiologicalLivingObject (q.v.) are destroyed.  Notable  specializations of #$BiologicalDestructionEvent include #$BiologicalCatabolismEvent, #$DigestionEvent, and #$BiologicalDecompositionEvent.")
(comment NonAmericanCar "A specialization of #$Automobile.  Each instance of #$NonAmericanCar is a car that was manufactured by a corporation headquarted somewhere other than the United States of America.  In the U.S., such cars are often called \"imported cars\"; however, in fact some cars manufactured by companies headquartered outside the U.S. are actually manufactured in the U.S.  Cf. #$AmericanAutomobile, with which #$NonAmericanCar is disjoint.")
(comment optimumGrowthTempForOrganismType "(#$optimumGrowthTempForOrganismType ORG TEMP) means that ORG, an instance of #$Oranism-Whole, grows optimally at the temperature TEMP.")
(comment PackagedProduct "A specialization of both #$ManufacturedGoods and #$PackagedObject.  Each instance of #$PackagedProduct is a complete packaged product, including everything the customer gets when the product is purchased, i.e. the main product itself (see #$mainProduct), along with any packaging materials, manuals, instructions, warranty cards, etc.")
(disjointWith Organism-Whole Secretion-Bodily)
(comment Bouncer "A person hired to remove disorderly people from nightclubs, etc.  In most real-world contexts most or all bouncers are men.")
(comment CapacityPredicate "A specialization of #$Predicate.  Each instance of #$CapacityPredicate is a predicate representing a specific capacity in which an agent does an action.  Instances include #$actsInCapacity-IntendedFunction, #$actsInCapacity-HobbyCapacity, etc..")
(comment actsInCapacity-IntendedFunction "An instance of #$CapacityPredicate (#$actsInCapacity-IntendedFunction AGENT ROLE EVENT-TYPE) holds just in case when AGENT is performing ROLE in events of type EVENT-TYPE the agent is performing the event as one of its intended functions.  For instance, if a stock broker is the buyer of stocks in some #$StockTrading, then (#$actsInCapacity-IntendedFunction Bob-TheStockBroker #$buyer #$StockTrading) holds.")
(comment actsInCapacity-HobbyCapacity "(#$actsInCapacity-HobbyCapacity AGENT SLOT EVENT-TYPE) holds just in case AGENT's role in events of type EVENT-TYPE is that of engaging in that role as a hobby.")
(disjointWith PurposefulAction BiologicalEvent)
(comment actsInCapacity-JobCapacity "(#$actsInCapacity-JobCapacity AGT ROLE EVT-TYPE) holds just in case AGT's ROLE in acts of EVT-TYPE is in the capacity of a job.")
(comment PublisherOfPublicationTypeFn "#$PublisherOfPublicationTypeFn takes as argument any spec of #$PublishedMaterial and returns the collection of agents who publish instances of that spec.  For example, (#$PublisherOfPublicationTypeFn #$JournalSeries) returns the collection of all journal publishers.")
(comment ColonialTerritory "The physical and functional sides of a Colony -- a geographic region which is controlled almost completely by a foreign power")
(comment Extraterrestrial "Each instance of this collection is a creature belonging to a species which did not arise on #$PlanetEarth. See also the more specific #$ExtraterrestrialPerson.")
(comment (VersusFn termOfUnit rewriteOf) "#$termOfUnit is used internally for connecting unreified NATs to reified NATs.  If you want to say something like (#$termOfUnit #$Apple (#$FruitFn #$AppleTree)),  don't.  That's ill-formed because the #$arg1Isa of #$termOfUnit requires  that it be a NAT.  But something like (#$rewriteOf #$Apple (#$FruitFn #$AppleTree))  would be permissible.")
(comment Meeting-SocialGathering "A specialization of #$SocialGathering.  Each instance of #$Meeting-SocialGathering is an event in which people (see #$meetingParticipants) gather intentionally for some common purpose: for example, to communicate with each other, share some experience, or transact some business.  Notable specializations of #$Meeting-SocialGathering include #$StaffMeeting, #$ClassMeeting, and #$BusinessMeeting.")
(comment SpecsWithQuantityFn "(#$SpecsWithQuantityFn COL ATT) is the collection
 of all specs of COL that have ATT.  For example,
 (#$SpecsWithQuantityFn #$Bird #$Indigenous) is the
 collection of all kinds of birds that are indigenous.
 It is important to keep in mind that 
(#$SpecsWithQuantityFn COL ATT) is always 
an instance of #$CollectionType, and though it is true that
 for every instance C of (#$SpecsWithQuantityFn COL ATT), there is an appropriate quantity slot, QUANTITY-SLOT, such that 
 (QUANTITY-SLOT C ATT), it does not follow that
 (QUANTITY-SLOT COL ATT), nor does it follow that
 there are any instances of COL such that 
 (QUANTITY-SLOT COL ATT).  In most cases, ATT will
 be an instance of #$TypeLevelQuantity; the reason
 the #$arg2Isa of this function is not #$TypeLevelQuantity is that there
 could be quantities that can apply meaningfully to both
#$Individuals and #$Collections.")
(comment pragmaticRequirement "A #$MetaKnowledgePredicate that is used to place a certain kind of pragmatic precondition on the use of a given asserted rule (see #$CycLRuleAssertion). (#$pragmaticRequirement SENTENCE RULE) means that SENTENCE expresses a necessary condition on RULE's being used in any proof carried out by the Cyc inference engine. The effect of asserting this is virtually the same as that of asserting (#$exceptWhen (#$unknownSentence SENTENCE) RULE): it blocks the use of RULE when SENTENCE is not currently \"known\" by the Cyc system to be true. SENTENCE should not contain disjuncts (or canonicalize into disjuncts). Upon assertion to the knowledge base, a #$pragmaticRequirement sentence is transformed by the canonicalizer into a rule involving #$pragmaticallyNormal (q.v.).")
(comment productTypeSoldAt "(#$productTypeSoldAt PRODTYPE LOCATION) the #$ProductType PRODTYPE can be obtained at LOCATION. LOCATION can be any instance of partially tangible, including a particular supermarket, vending machine, or trunk of someone's car.  The implication is that PRODTYPE can typically be purchased at LOCATION,  not just as a one-time sale.  See #$sellsProductType to relate a product type to an organization or person who sells it instead of a place where it is sold.")
(comment typeLessInQuantityByDegree "(#$typeLessInQuantityByDegree COL1 COL2 QUANT-TYPE PRED QUANT) means that instances of COL1 will typically differ from instances of COL2 in terms of the value of QUANT-TYPE to which they're respectively related by PRED.  Instances of COL1 are related to smaller instances of QUANT-TYPE than are instances of COL2.  QUANT gives some indication of the degree of difference.")
(comment hasPersonalQuantity "'(#$hasPersonalQuantity PERSON QUANTITY)' means that the #$Person PERSON has the #$Quantity QUANTITY, and that QUANTITY is one of the characteristics with which people are identified socially or have some level of control over.  For instance, #$LevelOfFitness is a personal quantity , but the degree to which they have some infection is not.")
(comment inTheVicinityOf-Geographical "(#$inTheVicinityOf-Geographical REGION AREA) means that the #$GeographicalRegion REGION is near AREA. While being a direct specialization of #$near, this relation is still rather general. Specialization could be conceived that record fine grain details of relative localization between a group of ants for instance and an ant trap placed in someone's cubicles or record the relative location between two cities, see #$inTheSuburbOf for additional considerations.")
(disjointWith ComputerHardwareItem HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject)
(comment typesDifferInQuantity "(#$typesDifferInQuantity COL1 COL2 QUANT-TYPE) means that
instances of COL1 will differ from instances of COL2 in terms of the
value of QUANT-TYPE that they respectively hold.")
(comment agentStaysViableInSubstanceFor-BCW "(#$agentStaysViableInSubstanceFor-BCW AGENTTYPE SUBSTANCETYPE DURATION) means that, other things being equal, if an instance of the #$BiochemicallyHarmfulSubstance type AGENTTYPE remains in an instance of SUBSTANCETYPE for a time interval with #$duration DURATION, it will retain its capacity to harm living organisms throughout that interval.")
(comment Cheddar-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of cheddar cheese.  Cheddar is originally English. It is a firm aged cheese which becomes sharper as it ages.  Though aged, it is not as hard as a grating cheese.")
(comment ProductType "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ProductType is a collection of #$Products (q.v.) -- i.e. a kind of substances, objects, or actions -- that are produced (or performed) and sold as products.  Examples of #$ProductType include #$GiftCertificate, #$HardDiskDrive, #$PlasticWrap, and #$ServiceEvent.  Non-examples include #$Bread, since not all bread is produced to be sold (think \"home-made\"); but its subcollection (#$ProductFn #$Bread) is a product-type.  On the other hand, there are some microtheoretic contexts whose domain assumptions are such that collections whose instances are _commonly_ (but not exclusively) sold as products (e.g. #$Bread, #$DairyProduct) count as #$ProductTypes in those contexts; #$BuyingMt and #$BrandNameProductGMt are two such contexts.  Note that #$ProductType is not a subcollection of either #$ObjectType or #$StuffType, because some product-types are of one but not the other of these kinds (e.g. #$Ketchup is a #$StuffType but not an #$ObjectType).  Also note that not every conceivable subcollection of #$Product constitutes a #$ProductType; only those subcollections that correspond (in some broad sense) to categories under which products are produced, bought, or sold should be product-types.  Product types that are specific to a single brand should be made instances of the specialization #$ProductTypeByBrand; those that are specified by both brand and version (e.g. Model-T Fords) should be made instances of the even more specialized #$ProductTypeByBrandVersion.")
(comment MusicSingle "A collection of IBOs.  Collection of musical $#RecordedSoundProducts that correspond to #$SingleRecording-CW.")
(comment typesDifferInQuantityRelatedTo "(#$typesDifferInQuantityRelatedTo COL1 COL2 QUANT-TYPE BINPRED)
means that instances of COL1 will be related to a different
instance(s) of QUANT-TYPE by BINPRED than will instances of COL2.  Note
that if QUANT-TYPE is ordered, the collection that will take on \"greater\"
instances of ATT-COLL is to appear in the first argument place. ")
(disjointWith Paper HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject)
(comment MiniPad "A smaller #$SanitaryNapkin than a #$MaxiPad.")
(comment differentInQuantityRelation "This predicate compares two things in terms of some #$QuantitySlot that relates them to different instances of a given specialization of Quantity. (#$differentInQuantityRelation T1 T2 SLOT) means that there are different #$Quantities QUANT-1 and QUANT-2, such that (SLOT T1 QUANT-1) and (BINPRED T2 QUANT-2).")
(disjointWith HumanlyOccupiedSpatialObject ExplosiveDevice)
(disjointWith HumanOccupationConstruct FurniturePiece)
(comment DataProjector "This is the collection of data projectors. A data projector is a projector designed to display computer pages on an ordinary screen or wall. Many data projectors use LCDs. ")
(comment Gouda-Cheese "This is the collection of all instances of Gouda, a firm Dutch cheese that comes encased in wax.")
(comment TakingApartAnArtifact "The collection of events in which one or more agents purposefully disassemble an #$Artifact into component pieces.  The #$Artifact goes out of existence by the end of the event, although generally it can be reconstituted from the pieces.  In this respect #$TakingApartAnArtifact differs from, say, #$ShatteringEvent.")
(comment PhysicalDestructionEvent "The collection of all #$DestructionEvents in which something #$PartiallyTangible is destroyed via physical means. Examples include natural disasters (cf. #$DisasterEvent), #$KillingByOrganisms, and dissassemblings (cf. #$TakingApartAnArtifact). For cases where at least some portion of the thing destroyed becomes incorporated into a new created thing, see the more specialized #$PhysicalTransformationEvent.  See also the reifiable functions #$PhysicalDestructionFn and #$PhysicalDestructionByMeansOfFn.")
(comment LogicallySoundSystem "This is a collection logical systems. A logical system is an instance of #$LogicallySoundSystem just in case a formula is derivable from the system only if the formula is entailed by the system.")
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion Wave-Liquid)
(comment quantityPartitionSet "(#$quantityPartitionSet PART SET) states that the quantity partition PART has SET as the set of quantities which constitute a mutually exclusive partition of some specific quantity.  See also #$quantityPartitionedBy and #$QuantityPartitionType.")
(comment QuantityPartitionType "Every instance of #$QuantityPartitionType is a collection of quantities which together form a mutually exclusive partition of some specific quantity (this, of course, entails that the quantity involved is a range and not a point value).  See also #$quantityPartitionSet, #$quantityPartitionedBy and #$QuantityPartitionFn.")
(comment quantityPartitionedBy "(#$quantityPartitionedBy QUANT PART) states that the #$Quantity QUANT is partitioned by the quantity partition PART.  In other words, anything which has the quantity ATT must also have one of the quantities in PART.  Furthermore, since PART is a partition of QUANT, anything having one of the quantites in PART will have QUANT as well, and nothing will have two different quantities in PART.  See also #$quantityPartitionSet and #$QuantityPartitionType.")
(comment QuantityPartitionFn "(#$QuantityPartitionFn SET) denotes an instance of #$QuantityPartitionType in which SET is the set of quantities which constitute a mutually exclusive partition of some specific quantity.  See also #$quantityPartitionSet, #$quantityPartitionedBy and #$QuantityPartitionType.")
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion SpaceInAFixedHOC)
(comment QuantityCoveringType "Every instance of #$QuantityCoveringType is a collection of quantities which together form a covering of some specific quantity.  See also #$quantityCoveringSet, #$quantityCoveredBy and #$QuantityCoveringFn.")
(comment LandBorderFn "(#$LandBorderFn ?ENT) returns those parts of the  border between ?ENT and another region which are not coastal. This includes borders formed by rivers. So, for example, the potion of the (#$BorderBetweenFn #$France #$Germany) formed by the #$RhineRiver would count as part of the (#$LandBorderFn #$France) and the (#$LandBorderFn #$Germany). However, the Atlantic coastline of France would not count.  Note that because many countries have some coastline, the instance of #$Border returned by this function is not necessarily #$SpatiallyContinuousThings.")
(comment JudicialAgent "A specialization of #$LegalAgent.  Each instance of #$JudicialAgent is a person or organization whose responsibility it is to judge or evaluate.  Instances of #$JudicialAgent include officials at sporting events (see the collection #$SportsOfficial), judges of various competitions, as well as judges in the legal sense (see the collection #$Judge).")
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion Device-SingleUser)
(disjointWith Place Device-OneTimeUse)
(comment Artifact-Agentive "The collection of all instances of #$Agent-Generic created by an agent or agents (i.e., by some instance(s) of #$Agent-Generic).  Since each instance of #$Artifact-Agentive is created by an agent, each instance is also an artifact (i.e., an instance of #$Artifact-Generic).  One important specialization of #$Artifact-Agentive is #$Organization (q.v.).  #$Artifact-Agentive is disjoint with #$Agent-NonArtifactual, the collection of all agents _not_ created by an agent.")
(disjointWith CohabitationUnit BranchOfMilitaryService)
(comment TravelingByClassFn "(#$TravelingByClassFn TRAVELBYTRANSPORTTYPE TRAVELCLASS)
returns the collection of all instances of TRAVELBYTRANSPORTTYPE where
the accomodations and service involved are considered to have the
#$TransportationAccommodationType TRAVELCLASS.  E.g., (#$TravelingByClassFn
(#$TravelingByMeansOfFn #$Train-TransportationDevice) #$FirstClass) returns the collection
of all instances of (#$TravelingByMeansOfFn #$Train-TransportationDevice) where the travel
and accomodations are #$FirstClass, or, more succinctly, the concept
of 'first-class train travel'.")
(comment quantityCoveredBy "(#$quantityCoveredBy QUANT COVER) states that the #$Quantity QUANT is covered by the quantity covering COVER.  In other words, anything which has all of the quantities in COVER also has the quantity QUANT.  See also #$quantityCoveringSet and #$QuantityCoveringType.")
(comment QuantityCoveringFn "(#$QuantityCoveringFn SET) denotes an instance of #$QuantityPartitionType in which SET is the set of quantities which constitute a covering of some specific quantity.  See also #$quantityCoveringSet, #$quantityCoveredBy and #$QuantityCoveringType.")
(comment quantityCoveringSet "(#$quantityCoveringSet COVER SET) states that the quantity covering COVER has SET as the set of quantities which constitute a covering of some specific instance of #$Quantity.  See also #$quantityCoveredBy and #$QuantityCoveringType.")
(comment (GaseousFn Chlorine) "A greenish-yellow, poisonous gas which is sometimes used as a chemical weapon.")
(comment TopAndBottomSidedObject "A #$TopAndBottomSidedObject is an object with an intrinsic #$TopSide and an intrinsic #$BottomSide.  By 'intrinsic' we mean simply that there exists an established convention according to which one side is considered 'top' and the other side is considered 'bottom'.  Usually the two sides in question can be reliably distinguished from one another.  For example, by convention, the 'top' of a #$Table-PieceOfFurniture is the side on which other objects usually rest, while the 'bottom' is the side which usually touches the floor.  Notice that a conventionally distinguishable bottom and top do not necessarily imply a left and right, or a front and back.  A plant is a good example of the case where they do not: top and bottom can be reliably distinguished but not, ordinarily, front and back or left and right.  Notice also--and this is crucial to the whole conception--that while a
#$TopAndBottomSidedObject may well have a preferred orientation, changing this orientation does not change what counts as 'top' and what counts as 'bottom': if a car flips over on the highway its top is now facing the pavement and its bottom--the undercarriage--is now up in the air.  If an entity does not obey this rule then it does not, generally speaking, count as having a distinguishable top and bottom--example: an hourglass or a book.  (see also #$NoteAboutSidedObject) ")
(comment CenterFn "(#$CenterFn OBJ) denotes the point at the spatial center of an object.  Formally, this can be defined as a point such that the average of the distances from this point to all points which are 'in' (see #$spatiallySubsumes) OBJ is minimized.  Note that for objects whose density is not homogeneous (#$CenterFn OBJ) may be different from the 'center of gravity' of the object.  Also, for objects which aren't spatially continuous (see #$SpatiallyContinuousThing), (#$CenterFn OBJ) is not necessarily 'in' (see #$spatiallySubsumes) OBJ.  For example, the centroid of a non-spatially-continuous object such as a flock of seagulls is not necessarily a point in one of the seagulls.")
(comment EuropeanCitizenOrSubject "The collection of people who are citizens of, or otherwise by status under the jurisdiction of, a country or other #$GeopoliticalEntity whose territory is located in the #$ContinentOfEurope.  A person native to an area of Europe not under the jurisdiction of any #$GeopoliticalEntity would also be an instance of #$EuropeanCitizenOrSubject.")
(comment Up-Partially "The direction #$Up-Partially is a unit vector interval which includes in its range all unit vectors that have a greater than zero upward component.  Different #$Up-Partially assertions in different #$FrameOfReference microtheories should not be considered equivalent by default.  An elevator ascending as well as an airplane on a very gradual ascent move in the #$Up-Partially direction.  See #$Up-Generally and #$Up-Directly for more directionally constrained versions of `up'.")
(comment objectSides "This predicate relates tangible objects to the sides that make up the outer sides of the object.  (#$objectSides OBJ SIDE) means that SIDE is one of the boundary defining surfaces of OBJ, which is an instance of #$PartiallyTangible.")
(comment SubregionByDirectionFn "(#$SubregionByDirectionFn REG DIR) denotes the subregion of REG whose location is indicated by the direction DIR.")
(comment AnatomicalDirection "The set of directions used to describe the orientation of objects in or near an object with an #$AnimalBodyShapeType.  Includes directions related to front and back (e.g., #$VentralDirection), central and peripheral (#$DistalDirection), center and sides, and head and toe.")
(comment SendingSomething "The collection of events in which an #$Agent-PartiallyTangible intends to have an object (other than itself) delivered to some other #$Agent-PartiallyTangible. This involves at least a temporary loss of some user rights to the object by the sender.  If successful, an instance of #$SendingSomething is also an instance of #$TransferringPossession.")
(comment resemblesInQuantity "(#$resemblesInQuantity THING1 THING2 QUANT-TYPE) means that the two things THING1 and THING2 resemble each other in their values of the specialization of #$Quantity QUANT-TYPE.  Here 'resembles' means has a 'close' or similar value in that dimension -- what this means, and what the standard of closeness or similarity is, depends on the context.  See also #$identicalInQuantity and #$differentInQuantity.")
(comment typesChemicalBondTypeBetweenCapable "(#$typesChemicalBondTypeBetweenCapable BOND-TYPE COL1 COL2) means
that instances of COL1 can form chemical bonds of type  BOND-TYPE with
instances of COL2, where 'can' means that it is chemically possible (or
maybe even likely).")
(comment EncounteringSomething "This is the collection of events in which an agent encounters an object or another agent.  To encounter something is to
become close enough to it to become aware of it.  One may encounter a bear by the bear approaching, so encountering does not require movement on the part of the encounterer (though the bear would also be an encounterer).  If both objects encountering each other are #$Agent-PartiallyTangibles, the #$doneBy slot would normally be filled by the moving agent, if only one moves.  See #$MeetingSomeone.")
(comment SituationIns-TypeFn "(#$SituationIns-TypeFn THING ATT) refers to the collection of situations in which THING is an instance of COL. For example, (#$SituationIns-TypeFn #$ElvisPresley-Musician #$Asleep) is collection of all situations in which Elvis Presley is asleep.")
(comment WestIndiesPerson "The set of people who are citizens or subjects of a government that exclusively rules territory in the West Indies.  E.g. a citizen or subject of #$PuertoRico is a #$WestIndiesPerson, but a citizen or subject of the colonial power ruling #$PuertoRico (#$Spain or #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica) who is a subject of that government some place other than the #$CaribbeanRegion is not a member of this collection.")
(comment PhysicalUrgeType "A collection of collections, and a specialization of #$SensoryReactionType.  Each instance of #$PhysicalUrgeType is a type of urge (to do something) that animals have.  Instances of #$PhysicalUrgeType include the collections #$UrgeToSneeze, #$UrgeToScratch, and #$UrgeToEat.")
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice OceanLiner)
(comment AsianCitizenOrSubject "The collection of people who are citizens of, or otherwise by status under the jurisdiction of, a country or other #$GeopoliticalEntity whose territory is located in the #$ContinentOfAsia.  A person native to an area of Asia not under the jurisdiction of any #$GeopoliticalEntity would also be an instance of #$AsianCitizenOrSubject.")
(comment Culture-Practice "A specialization of #$Action and #$SocialOccurrence each instance of which is a very extended, multi-doer event involving material and/or social modifications by #$IntelligentAgents to their environment, as well as a set of learned shared practices which are transmitted amongst all members of any given culture. A notable specialization of this collection is #$HumanCulture, but it also includes any nonhuman animal (e.g. chimpanzee) cultures, cultures created by #$Extraterrestrials and/or AIs. See also #$CulturalEvent.")
(disjointWith Country State-Geopolitical)
(comment PersonTypeByCultureFn "A function from cultures to the collections of persons in those cultures.  (#$PersonTypeByCultureFn CULTURE) denotes the collection of persons who are #$cultureParticipants in CULTURE.")
(comment PersonTypeByEthnicity "A collection of collections and a specialization of #$PersonTypeByCulture.  Each instance of #$PersonTypeByEthnicity is a collection of people who participate in a common #$HumanCulture defined on the basis of ethnic origin.  Instances of #$PersonTypeByEthnicity include #$EthnicGroupOfVietnamese, #$EthnicGroupOfNativeAmericansOfTheUS, and #$EthnicGroupOfHutu.")
(comment ArgGenlQuantityPredicate "The subcollection of #$ArgTypePredicate used to specify the required #$Quantity of an argument of a #$Relation.")
(comment phenotypeOfIndividual-Enumeration "(#$phenotypeOfIndividual-Enumeration ORG PHENO) means that ORG, an instance of
#$Organism-Whole, has the feature denoted by PHENO, an instance of
#$PhenotypeFeatureType. The phenotype of an individual is a purely descriptive
account of observable features of an organism. The phenotype is determined
by the genotype, but knowledge of the former doesn't give knowledge of the
later. See #$genotypeOfIndividual-Enumeration.")
(comment organismTypePhenotype-Enumeration "(#$organismTypePhenotype-Enumeration ORG-TYPE PHENO) means that PHENO, a
#$PhenotypeFeatureType, stands for a morphological character shared by most of
the instances of ORG-TYPE, an instance of #$OrganismClassificationType.")
(comment ArgGenlQuantityBinaryPredicate "Those instances of both #$ArgTypeBinaryPredicate and #$ArgGenlAttributePredicate used to specify the required quantity of an argument of #$Relation.  Each instance PRED of this collection is a binary predicate with the following properties: ARG1 is an instance of #$Relation, and ARG2 is an instance of #$Quantity.  (PRED ARG1 ARG2) means that some argument of ARG1 is constrained to be subsumed by (via #$quantitySubsumes) ARG2, where PRED determines the argument place in question.")
(comment RolePlayingCharacter "The collection of all characters played by human or computer participants in a #$RolePlayingGame. #$RolePlayingCharacter s are characterized by a set of statistics, such as hit points, stamina, morale, charisma, and so on, which affect, and are affected by, the development of the game.")
(comment LettucePlant "A plant order in the dicot subclass. See also #$Lettuce-Foodstuff.")
(comment Wizard "The collection of people who specialize in the #$Magic arts. In #$DungeonsAndDragonsMt, a class of #$RolePlayingCharacter with #$Magic using abilities.")
(comment LegalAgent "A specialization of #$SocialBeing.  Each instance of #$LegalAgent is an agent who has some status in a particular legal system.  At the very least, such an agent is recognized by some legal authority as having some kinds of rights and/or responsibilities as an agent (e.g., #$citizens of Germany), or as being subject to certain restrictions and penalties (e.g., a company that has been blacklisted by Iraq).  Thus, instances of #$LegalAgent include agents that may have property rights, may be taxed, may have a government identification number, may be sued, may have an address, or may buy or sell.  Note that membership in this collection is very much dependent upon context.  In some societies, only adult males and various kinds of state-run organizations would be included in #$LegalAgent.")
(comment most-GenQuantWithQuantityHaveQuant "(#$most-GenQuantWithQuantityHaveQuant SETORCOL QUANT1 QUANT2) is
true if and only if most elements of SETORCOL with the #$Quantity QUANT1 have
the #$Quantity QUANT2.  For instance, it might be true that all persons that are experiencing a low level of burning sensation are also experiencing a low level of pain.  We can express this dependency in the following way: (#$most-GenQuantWithQuantityHaveQuant #$Person (#$LowAmountFn #$LevelOfBurningSensation) (#$LowAmountFn #$LevelOfPain)).")
(comment asserted "(#$asserted AGENT SENTENCE) means that AGENT has made a #$DeclarativeUtterance whose content is expressed by SENTENCE.")
(comment alleged "(#$alleged AGENT SENTENCE) means that AGENT has alleged that the proposition expressed by the CycL formula FORMULA is true. An allegation remains in force as long as the alleger doesn't withdraw it and the allegation is not disproven. To allege something is to assert it without presently being able to prove it. It is similar to conjecturing, but alleging is essentially a public act and carries with it the implication that the alleger is under some obligation to attempt to prove what is alleged. The publicity of allegation also plays into when it is considered to be in force: an allegation that is not remembered by anyone is no longer in force. Note that \"allegations\" in the present sense are not typically about wrongdoing.")
(comment PlayerOfInstrumentFn "A function from types of instruments to the people who play them. (#$PlayerOfInstrumentFn #$Cello) denotes the collection of cellists.")
(disjointWith AnatomicalVessel Tumor)
(comment Identifying "A subcollection of #$PurposefulAction, instances of  #$Identifying are those actions in which  something is identified.  See also #$identifiedThing, #$IdentifyingObjectAsType, #$identifiedAsType and #$IdentifyingAsTypeFn.")
(comment AustralianCitizenOrSubject "The collection of people who are citizens of, or otherwise by status under the jurisdiction of, a country or other #$GeopoliticalEntity whose territory is located on the #$ContinentOfAustralia.  A person native to an area of Australia not under the jurisdiction of any #$GeopoliticalEntity would also be an instance of #$AustralianCitizenOrSubject.  Since 1901 such people are citizens, or by status under the jurisdiction, of the Commonwealth of #$Australia.")
(disjointWith Organism-Whole BloodCell)
(comment resultSubsumedBy "(#$resultSubsumedBy FUNCTION QUANT) means that the result of applying the function FUNCTION to a series of arguments ARG1 - ARGN results in an instance  
QUANT-SUB of #$Quantity such that (#$quantitySubsumes QUANT QUANT-SUB) holds.")
(disjointWith PublishedMaterial Conveyance)
(disjointWith ComputerHardwareItem PublishedMaterial)
(disjointWith PublishedMaterial SomethingToWear)
(comment ClassicalAgeGreekPerson "A Greek who lived between the times of the Persian War and the Macedonian conquest.")
(comment HellenisticAgeGreekPerson "The collection of Greeks who lived during the Hellenistic Age, which is dated from the Macedonian conquest of Greece to sometime around the end  of the Roman Republic.")
(comment NorthAmericanCitizenOrSubject "The collection of people who are citizens of, or otherwise by status under the jurisdiction of, a country or other #$GeopoliticalEntity whose territory is located in the #$ContinentOfNorthAmerica.  A person native to an area of North America not under the jurisdiction of any #$GeopoliticalEntity would also be an instance of #$NorthAmericanCitizenOrSubject.")
(disjointWith PublishedMaterial Weapon)
(disjointWith PublishedMaterial FurniturePiece)
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice Rowboat)
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice Raft)
(comment hasQuantityWithRespectTo "(#$hasQuantityWithRespectTo THING VAL RES) means that the
instance of the collection #$Thing, THING, has the quantity VAL, an
instance of the collection #$Quantity with respect to RES, an
instance of the collection #$Thing. For instance, (#$hasQuantityWithRespectTo #$Juggling #$Difficult Bob) means that juggling is difficult at least with respect to Bob.")
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice ModernFrigate)
(disjointWith LandTransportationDevice MineWarfareShip)
(comment SpecifiedFoodDishType "This is a collection of types. Each type is a collection of instances of a particular dish, such as Vichyssoise. Each such type is associated with a set of recipes which are considered variations rather than recipes for different dishes. Each type also has a name, and all recipes for the type bear this name or a translation of it. ")
(comment HumanFather "The collection of all human fathers")
(disjointWith ContinuousPhysicalContactSituation PhysicalContactMakingEvent)
(disjointWith PublishedMaterial FoodOrDrink)
(disjointWith StorageConstruct EatingVessel)
(disjointWith DrinkingGlass StorageConstruct)
(disjointWith DrinkingMug StorageConstruct)
(comment SafetyInspector "A specialization of #$Inspector-Professional. Each instance of this collection is a person who examines workplaces, products and other entities in order to determine whether they are hazardous (generally, whether they are hazardous to humans).")
(comment BaseballPlayerTypeByPosition "The collection of all types of #$BaseballPlayer faceted by position.")
(comment StorageConstruct "#$StorageConstruct is a specialization of #$ContainerArtifact.  Each instance of #$StorageConstruct is a container used primarily for storing something and includes such things as closets, trunks of cars, and attics.  Negative examples would be #$Sink, #$Sandbox, and #$SewerLine, since their primary purpose is something other than storing something.")
(comment ComputerTypeByPassiveCapability "A collection and a spec of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive. A collection of computers, which can be used to represent the property a computer has when it can be used to perform a certain action.")
(comment ThingTypeByCapability "A collection of collections. Each instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability is a collection that represents the degree to which something is capable of performing some function.")
(disjointWith ServingVessel StorageConstruct)
(disjointWith CookingVessel StorageConstruct)
(disjointWith MedicalTreatmentEvent MedicalTesting)
(comment NonFunctionalObject "A collection of non-functional things (a sub-collection of #$SomethingExisting) that represents that something is nonfunctional with respect to its being capable of performing the primary function of things of its kind (see #$typePrimaryFunction).")
(comment FunctionalObject "A collection of things that function ( a sub-collection of #$SomethingExisting) that represents that something is fully functional with respect to its being capable of performing the primary function of things of its kind (see #$typePrimaryFunction).")
(comment AlternativeMedicineSpecialistType "#$AlternativeMedicineSpecialistType is a collection of collections. Each element of #$AlternativeMedicineSpecialistType is a collection of #$AlternativeMedicinePractitioner s who practice the same type of #$AlternativeMedicine modality.  The forms of practice that are considered \"alternative\" vary by context.  Some example elements in #$ModernWesternMedicineMt include #$Acupuncturist and #$Homeopath.")
(comment PromptFirstFn "One of a series of functions which may be used to \"wrap\" a computer-related instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability, thereby allowing one to qualify the statement that a certain computer may perform (or, in the case of instances of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive, may be used to perform) a certain action. This function allows one to claim that before the action is performed the computer will prompt the user -- letting them know that the action is about to be performed and requesting permission to proceed.")
(comment Helmsman "The collection of all persons who steer ships or boats")
(comment hasPassiveCapability "(#$hasPassiveCapability THING CAP) means that THING has the capacity represented by the instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive CAP.")
(comment HumanTeenager "A specialization of #$YoungHuman. Each instance of this collection is a #$HomoSapiens whose age is greater than 12 years and less than 20 years. A notable specialization is #$HumanTeenager-LegallyAdult.")
(comment HumanTeenager-LegallyAdult "A specialization of #$HumanTeenager. This is the collection of all teenagers who are considered to be adult for legal purposes such as the right to vote, to fight wars, to buy cigarettes, to live outside parental control and to be depicted in pornography without sanction to the pornographer. The ages involved are usually 18 and 19.")
(comment Dominatrix "Individuals who are elements of this class engage in #$Bondage-Sexual activities for fun and (sometimes) profit.  The #$Dominatrix plays the dominant role (versus the submissive role) in role-playing.")
(disjointWith ConfigurationFile CommunicationConvention)
(comment networkHasSecurityEnvironment "(#$networkHasSecurityEnvironment NETWORK ENVIRON) means that the

instance of #$ComputerNetwork, NETWORK, has a security environment

described by ENVIRON.")
(comment Stripper "The collection of all dancers [#$Dancer-Performer] who remove all or most of their clothing during a performance.")
(disjointWith SimpleRepairing LawEnforcementActivity)
(disjointWith SoftwareParameter CommunicationConvention)
(comment AISTypeByEvaluationTone "A collection of collections.  Each element of #$AISTypeByEvaluationTone is an collection of assertions used to specify the general tone of some assertion, group of assertions, or presentation about some topic.  Examples of #$AISTypeByEvaluationTone: #$PositiveTone, #$NegativeTone, #$NeutralTone.")
(comment NeutralTone "A specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure and

an element of #$AISTypeByEvaluationTone.  The collection #$NeutralTone represents the attitude implied by judgments which neither seriously disparage nor seriously praise their subjects.")
(comment NegativeTone "A specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure and

an element of #$AISTypeByEvaluationTone.  The collection #$NegativeTone represents the attitude implied by judgments which are critical, derisive, disparaging, or insulting about their subjects.")
(comment PositiveTone "A specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure and

an element of #$AISTypeByEvaluationTone.  The collection #$PositiveTone represents the attitude implied by judgments which praise, commend, celebrate, or applaud their subjects.")
(disjointWith SelfPoweredDevice HollowCylindricalObject)
(disjointWith SimpleRepairing ScreeningAFriendlyForce)
(comment permeableTo "(#$permeableTo OBJECT STUFF) means that OBJECT allows intances of STUFF to pass through it unhindered and freely.")
(comment StudentByEducationalOrganizationLevel "A collection of collections. Each element of #$StudentByEducationalOrganizationLevel is a collection which classifies #$Students by the level of #$EducationalOrganization in which they are enrolled. An example is undergraduate students, denoted by (#$SubcollectionWithAttributeFn #$Student #$UndergraduateLevel). Use #$StudentByEducationalOrganizationLevel and #$educationLevel to make assertions about the educational level of instances of #$Person. In many cases, a coextensional collection can be created using #$PersonEnrolledInFn.")
(disjointWith SimpleRepairing BuildingCleaningChore)
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention ComputerAIS)
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention CharacterString)
(comment FirewallTypeByPacketTarget "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of firewall programs in a particular state with respect to how they assign attributes to packets.  The instances of

#$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget represent features or attributes that a firewall program F assigns to a

packet P that determine the fate of P when P arrives at the computer on

which F is running. The most common #$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget are

#$Accept-FirewallTarget, #$Deny-FirewallTarget,

#$Reject-FirewallTarget, #$Redirect-FirewallTarget, and

#$Masquerade-FirewallTarget.")
(comment LevelOfFlawedness "A collection of instances of #$Quantity which indicate the degree to which something is flawed.")
(comment CultureClassificationType "A collection of collections of instances of #$Culture-Practice. Each instance of #$CultureClassificationType is a collection of cultures; interesting instances correspond to noteworthy features that individual cultures can be classified in terms of, e.g. #$RegionalCulture and #$SexualCulture.")
(comment CulturalEvent "The collection of events having something to do with some particular #$Culture-Practice.  This includes museum displays, concerts, celebrations, etc. (each of which is a considered to be #$subEvents of the culture to which it belongs).")
(comment HumanCulture "A specialization of #$Culture-Practice and #$AnimalActivity each instance of which is a very extended, multi-performer activity involving social and material modifications by #$HomoSapiens to their environment. Human cultures are generally considered very important by their participants (see #$cultureParticipants). Humans tend to identify themselves largely in relation to the cultures in which they participate.  Exactly what sorts of events constitute a human culture is hard to specify (see the instances of #$CultureClassificationType for guidance here), but cultures generally can at least be said to involve the following sorts of activities on the part of many of their participants: (1) the expression of certain characteristic beliefs, (2) the following of certain characteristic practices, and (3) the use (and sometimes, production) of certain characteristic artifacts. See #$cultureBeliefs, #$culturePractices, #$cultureSpecialPractices, and #$cultureArtifacts.")
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention DiversionaryComputerProgram)
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention ProgramFault)
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention VisualWork)
(disjointWith FluidConduit Waterfall)
(disjointWith PhysiologicalProcess BiologicalProcess-CellularLevel)
(disjointWith BiologicalMaturationEvent PhysiologicalProcess)
(disjointWith FunctionalObject NonFunctionalObject)
(comment goalCategoryForAgent "(#$goalCategoryForAgent AGT CYCFORMULA GOALCAT) means that the  CYCFORMULA is a goal for AGT of GOALCAT. Each GOALCAT is a collection of goals in a particular category, such as #$ForeignPolicyGoal, LifePreservationGoal, etc. They specify what type of goal GOAL is for the agent.")
(comment hasBloodType "(#$hasBloodType BLOOD TYPE) means that BLOOD has the #$BloodType TYPE).  See also #$animalHasBloodType.")
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion Bridge-Military)
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention TextualPCW)
(disjointWith GeographicalRegion HumanShelterConstruction)
(disjointWith CommunicationConvention ComputerPatchProgram)
(comment AdultAnimal "An instance of #$AnimalTypeByMaturity (q.v.) and a specialization of #$Animal.  #$AdultAnimal is the collection of all animals  that are at least mature enough to bear offspring.  Cf.  #$JuvenileAnimal.")
(comment hasArgumentJustificationType "(#$hasArgumentJustificationType ARGUMENT JUST) means that ARGUMENT includes at least one support with justification of type JUST.")
(disjointWith NonNaturalThing NaturalThing)
(disjointWith ElectricalHouseholdAppliance FuelPoweredDevice)
(comment positionOfPersonInOrganization "The predicate #$positionOfPersonInOrganization is used to relate a particular person to his or her position in a particular organization.  (#$positionOfPersonInOrganization PERSON ORG POS-TYPE) means that the #$Person PERSON  is a member of the #$Organization ORG, and holds a position of type POS-TYPE.  Even in an employment situation, POS-TYPE may or may not specifically indicate PERSON 's occupational field or training; for example, one individual occupying a position of #$Manager may be a #$MarketingPerson, while another is an #$ElectricalEngineer.  In addition, POS-TYPE may or may not correspond to an official `Job Title' (cf. #$titleOfPersonInOrganization), or be the primary occupation of PERSON .  Note that assertions using #$positionOfPersonInOrganization should be properly time-constrained.")
(comment mtImageLighting "The visual image associated with the image mt ARG1 depicts the object ARG2 in lighting condition ARG3.")
(comment NaturalThing "The notoriously hard to define collection of \"natural\" things.  An individual

 is an instance of this collection if it is itself an individual

 or #$Situation that occurs in nature, i.e., not as

 a result of an #$IntelligentAgent's (or group thereof)

 intentions to modify the environment, or else is an

 individual that is the #$outputsCreated of an

   #$Event that is itself natural.")
(comment identifiedThing "This predicate allows one to specify an instance of #$Individual
identified in some instance of #$Identifying.
(#$identifiedThing IDENT IND) means that in the instance
IDENT of #$Identifying the instance IND of #$Individual
is identified.  For example, to partially represent in #$CycL, say,
a process of tree identification carried out by some biologists,
we might use the GAF, (#$identifiedThing IDENT002 OAK004),
if one of the biologists identified a particular tree as an
instance OAK004 of #$OakTree in some instance IDENT002 of
#$Identifying.  See also #$IdentifyingObjectAsType,
          #$identifiedAsType and #$IdentifyingAsTypeFn.")
(disjointWith HouseholdAttachment TransportationContainerProduct)
(comment lightSource "The predicate #$lightSource is used to indicate the source of an illumination falling on a particular object.  (#$lightSource OBJ SOURCE MODE) means that OBJ is illuminated by SOURCE with the type of illumination (see #$ObjectTypeByIlluminationMode) MODE.")
(disjointWith Gun-Portable Platform-Military)
(disjointWith Bracelet Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith ProjectileSlug-Bullet ProjectileLauncher)
(disjointWith Necklace Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Token-Physical Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith Ring-Jewelry Clothing-Generic)
(disjointWith FuelPoweredDevice BusinessMachine)
(disjointWith Clothing-Generic Eyewear)
(comment ObjectTypeTypeByStatusAfterEvent "A third order collection.  Each instance of #$ObjectTypeTypeByStatusAfterEvent is a collection that represents a feature of objects after their participation in events.  Each instance of an instance of #$ObjectTypeTypeByStatusAfterEvent is a collection of actors in some event that share some property relating to their participation in that event.")
(comment featureOfPathWRTVehicleClass "(#$featureOfPathWRTVehicleClass PATH FEATURE CLASS)

means that PATH has the structural feature FEATURE with respect to instances of

CLASS. This predicate is used to relate a path and the type of

transportation that it can accomodate to the degree indicated by an

instance of #$PathArtifactTypeByStructuralFeature.  For instance this predicate can be used to state that a certain road is an #$AllWeather-PathArtifact with respect to light duty vehicles.")
(disjointWith ProjectileShellAssembly ProjectileLauncher)
(comment ConversationTypeByFeature "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$ConversationTypeByFeature is a collection of conversations with a certain feature.")
(comment fullSiblings "'(#$fullSiblings SIBLING1 SIBLING2)' means that SIBLING1 and SIBLING2 have the same biological parents.")
(comment ProfessionalModel "The collection of individuals that work as models for visual artists [#$Artist-Visual] or fashion professionals.")
(comment IdentifyingObjectAsType "The subcollection of #$Identifying in which the #$identifiedThings are (correctly) identified as belonging to some type (represented in the #$CycKB as a collection).  For example identifying a tree as an Oak tree, i.e. as an instance of #$OakTree, is an example of an action in this collection. See #$identifiedAsType and #$IdentifyingAsTypeFn as well as #$identifiedThing. ")
(comment identifiedAsType "This predicate can be used to indicate a type
that an object is (correctly) identified as in some instance of 
#$IdentifyingObjectAsType.  (#$identifiedAsType IDENT
OBJ COL) means that in the instance IDENT of
#$IdentifyingObjectAsType, the instance OBJ of 
#$Individual is identified as being of the type
COL, a collection.  See also #$IdentifyingAsTypeFn as well
as #$Identifying and #$identifiedThing.")
(disjointWith InternalCombustionPoweredDevice Clock)
(comment SupportingReference "A collection of #$TextStrings.  Each instance of #$SupportingReference is a #$TextString that is a reference (see #$referenceInWorkTo) and that points to one or more instances of #$StructurallySpecificWork or #$IntelligentAgent for the purpose of citing authority for propositions stated in the #$StructurallySpecificWork within which the #$TextString is contained (see #$containsStructure-CW).  For example, footnotes often contain #$TextString citing works that support the proposition stated in the sentence to which the footnote mark is appended.")
(disjointWith ComputerHardwareItem FuelPoweredDevice)
(comment BibliographicReference "A collection of #$TextStrings.  This collection consists of the instance of #$TextString that are a reference (see #$referenceInWorkTo) and that set forth all the data necessary to identify a particular #$StructurallySpecificWork.  The instances of #$BibliographicReference usually include #$ProperNameStrings that identify, among other things, the author, editor, composer, and/or publisher of a #$StructurallySpecificWork, as well as #$CharacterStrings that identify the date of publication.")
(disjointWith Tumor Organ)
(disjointWith CombatSportsEvent CooperationEvent)
(disjointWith FuelPoweredDevice ComputationalSystem)
(disjointWith ElectronicDevice InternalCombustionPoweredDevice)
(comment HeadOfState "A collection of persons.  Each instance of #$HeadOfState is a person who holds a political position as the titular leader of some instance of #$Country.  Titles that such a person might hold include President, Premier, Chairman, Sultan, King or Queen, or Regent.  Examples of #$HeadOfState: #$BillClinton, #$QueenElizabethII, #$YassirArafat, #$Hirohito, #$JiangZemin.  See also the related constants #$titleOfPosition and #$HeadOfGovernment.")
(comment GroupUserRightsFn "Takes an Organization and returns an instance of #$SituationTypeByGroupUserRight.  For instance (#$GroupUserRightsFn #$Cycorp) returns the user rights to objects that members of the organization Cycorp have a right to use based on their membership in that group.  ")
(comment SportsCoachFn "#$SportsCoachFn takes instances of  #$SportsOrganization and returns the collection of all instances of  #$SportsCoach who are coaches in that  #$Organization.  So, for example,  (#$SportsCoachFn #$NationalBasketballAssociation) is the collection of all NBA coaches.   (#$SportsCoachFn #$MiamiHeat) is the collection of all coaches employed by the #$MiamiHeat.")
(disjointWith ComputationalSystem ProjectileLauncher)
(disjointWith Event CavityOrContainer)
(comment contains-Underspecified "(#$contains-Underspecified CONTAINER CONTENTS) states that the abstract container CONTAINER in some underspecified (possibily metaphoric or non-spatial) manner 'contains' the thing CONTENTS. For instance, we might say (#$contains-Underspecified #$Ireland-TheIsland #$Dublin-CountyIreland) or more figuratively, (#$contains-Underspecified #$Ireland-TheIsland #$Happiness).")
(comment tourOptions "(#$tourOptions TOUR CHARACTERISTIC) means that TOUR has

the attribute CHARACTERISTIC.")
(disjointWith FixedStructure TransportationContainerProduct)
(disjointWith MultiRoomUnit TransportationContainerProduct)
(comment vacationPackageOptions "(#$vacationPackageOptions PACKAGE-TYPE TOUR-TYPE) means that  vacation packages of PACKAGE-TYPE include

#$TravelTours of type TOUR-TYPE.")
(comment IdentifyingAsTypeFn "An instance of #$Function-Denotational that takes one argument, a collection, and returns the collection of all identifying  actions in which some object or group of objects is identified as belonging to that collection.  (#$IdentifyingAsTypeFn COL) denotes the subcollection of #$IdentifyingObjectAsType in which some object or group of objects is identified by some instance of #$IntelligentAgent as belonging to the collection COL. For example, (#$IdentifyingAsTypeFn #$Gecko) is the collection of all actions in which an instance of #$Reptile is identified as being a Gecko.  (#$IdentifyingAsTypeFn #$PineTree) denotes the collection of all actions in which either a single tree is identified as a Pine tree or all trees in a grove of trees are identified as being pine trees. See #$identifiedAsType as well as #$Identifying and #$identifiedThing for related constants.")
(disjointWith JetPropelledAircraft InternalCombustionPoweredDevice)
(disjointWith InternalCombustionPoweredDevice RocketPropelledTransportationDevice)
(comment ChildMolester "The collection of all #$Persons that engage in #$ChildMolestation.")
(comment IterationEventByType "A collection of collections. Instances of this collection are collections of #$IterativeEvents of a similar type understood in the most general way -- example: 'stepwise', 'one at a time' -- or units of specified

object types -- example: (#$IterationTypeFn #$StepOfStairs), which

would be used to describe the iteration of a motion up the stairs one step

at a time.")
(disjointWith RecordingOfWaveIBT ProjectileLauncher)
(comment ExhibitionistOffender "The collection of #$SexOffenders that are guilty of #$IndecentExposure.  Note that #$IndecentExposure may not be a crime in many cultures.")
(comment Rapist "The collection of people that have committed an act of #$Rape.  If the act occured in a location in which it was illegal, the #$Rapist is a #$SexOffender.")
(comment typesGreaterInQuantity "(#$typesGreaterInQuantity COL1 COL2 QUANT-TYPE) means
that instances of COL1 have more of QUANT-TYPE than instances of COL2.  This cashes out as meaning every instance of COL11 is related to a value of QUANT-TYPE that is greater than any value had by an instance of COL2.  So, for any VAL1, VAL2, if (QUANTITY-PRED INSTANCE-OF-COL1 VAL1) and (QUANTITY-PRED INSTANCE-OF-COL2 VAL2) and VAL1 and VAL2 are both instances of QUANT-TYPE, then (#$followingValue VAL2 VAL1).  Note: QUANTITY-PRED in the above explanation is supposed to be the canonical quantity attribution predicate for use with QUANT-TYPE.  
Example: (#$typesGreaterInQuantity #$Dog #$Cat #$IntelligenceLevel) means that dogs have higher levels of intelligence than cats.  This entails that any value for argument 2 in #$hasIntelligenceLevel when an instance of #$Dog is in argument 1 is higher than when an instance of #$Cat is in argument 1.")
(comment similarInQuantityRelation "This predicate relates two things in terms of some #$BinaryPredicate that relates them to similar instances of a given collection of #$Quantity[ies]. (#$similarInQuantityRelation T1 T2 BINPRED) means that there are similar instances of #$Quantity QUANT1 and QUANT2, such that (BINPRED T1 QUANT1) and (BINPRED T2 QUANT2). See also #$resemblesInQuantity.")
(comment Foreign "The collection of all things foreign to an agent.  If the agent is a country, then other countries and people and things belonging to them are #$Foreign to the reference country.  If the agent is a person, than countries other than that in which one has ones citizenship, and people and things belonging to that country are foreign to the agent.  If the person is an expatriate who has adopted the culture of the country in which s/he is living, that country and things belonging to it are not considered foreign.")
(comment AgentCapacityQuantity "A specialization of #$Quantity.  This is the collection of all capacities or abilities that can be had to different degrees by agents.  An agent's having a given capacity implies that it can perform certain tasks or play certain roles within a  community of agents.")
(disjointWith VideoConceptualWork VisualArtifact-CW)
(comment typesResembleInQuantity "This is a type level version of the predicate #$resemblesInQuantity.  (#$typesResembleInQuantity TYPE1 TYPE2 QUANT-TYPE) means that where INST1 and INST2 are any instances drawn, respectively, from TYPE1 and TYPE2, it will be the case that (#$resemblesInQuantity INST1 INST2 QUANT-TYPE).")
(comment indirectlyAcquaintedWith "X is indirectly acquainted with Y if X knows (is acquainted with) someone who works for Y, someone who has dealt with Y, etc.  E.g., X meets and chats with someone who works for company Y and they talk about company Y --- then, X can be assumed to have be #$indirectlyAcquaintedWith with company Y.  X may also be more directly acquainted with Y.")
(comment AnatomicalDirectionPredicate "A collection of predicates.  Each member of this collection is a #$TransitiveBinaryPredicate relating the location of two #$PartiallyTangibles (frequently but not necessarily #$AnimalBodyRegions) in terms of directions defined with respect to a object having an animal body shape [see #$AnimalBodyShapeType].")
(comment regionsSurfaceHasFeatures "states what features or properties the surface of this GeographicalRegion has.")
(comment Exotic-Foreign "The #$Collection of all non-person types of organism (#$Organism-Whole) that live in a #$GeographicalRegion [#$residesInRegion] which is non-native to their species.  Instances of #$BiologicalTaxon are specs of this collection only in geographically-restricted contexts.")
(comment pathStateAffectsTranslocationType "(#$pathStateAffectsTranslocationType STATE TRANSLOCATION) means that TRANSLOCATION is the type of movement that is affected when some instance of #$Path-Customary has #$PathViabilityState STATE.")
(comment hasAuthorityOver "(#$hasAuthorityOver PARENT KID) means that PARENT has authority over KID. This implies, among other things, that they are in a position to be #$GrantingPermission to KID. This can also be expressed as: (#$agentsRelationship PARENT KID #$hasAuthorityOver) ")
(comment alterEgoOfHero "This predicate is used to relate instances of   #$Superhero with their alter-egos, in   the #$FictionalContexts in which the     alter-ego relationship holds.    For example, (#$alterEgoOfHero    #$BruceWayne-MillionaireSocialite #$Batman)   says that Bruce Wayne is Batman's 'secret   identity,' and should be asserted in    those contexts in which this is held to    be true, e.g., (#$ContextOfPCWFn    #$Batman-The1960sTVShow).  Keep in mind    the importance of contexts here: Though   it's true in the above context that    (#$alterEgoOfHero #$DickGrayson-HeroAlterEgo       #$Robin-BatmanSidekick), the same   assertion is not always true in others, e.g.,   (#$ContextOfPCWFn #$BatmanTheAnimatedSeries-TheTVShow), where    Robin's secret identity is generally  #$TimDrake-HeroAlterEgo.")
(comment frequentlyInContactWith "(#$frequentlyInContactWith AGENT1 AGENT2) means that AGENT and AGENT2 run into each other at frequent, perhaps regular intervals in the indefinite present, possibly because they are coworkers, club co-members, or some other more or less regularized and frequent activity, or possibly due to spatial nearness (being next-door neighbors, etc.).  This is a #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate.")
(disjointWith VisualWork NewspaperIssue)
(comment normalityOfThing "A predicate to describe how normal a thing is to a 'typical observer'.  (#$normalityOfThing THING COL NORMALITY) means that, for an instance of COL, THING has the normality level NORMALITY for a typical observer. The notion of typical observer will, of course, be dependent on the microtheory in which the assertion is made.  Such assertions need to be asserted in sufficiently specific contexts.  Note that normality is different from but related to frequency (e.g. #$frequencyOfActionType, #$Frequency). For example, a mechanic sees broken cars every day, but those cars are still abnormal cars.  To assert the normality of thing for a particular observer, see #$normalityForAgent.")
(comment actsInOfficialCapacityForIn "(#$actsInOfficialCapacityForIn AGENT GOVERNMENT ACT) holds when AGENT acts in a official capacity for GOVERNMENT during ACT.")
(comment above-Higher "(#$above-Higher HIGH-OBJ LOW-OBJ) means that HIGH-OBJ is at a greater altitude (from some common reference point) than LOW-OBJ.  In terrestrial contexts (see #$TerrestrialFrameOfReferenceMt), (#$above-Higher HIGH-OBJ LOW-OBJ) typically means that HIGH-OBJ-A is at a greater altitude above sea level (see the predicate #$altitudeAboveSeaLevel) than LOW-OBJ.")
(disjointWith GameEvent Tournament)
(disjointWith OlympicGames GameEvent)
(comment acquaintances "(#$acquaintances PERSON AGENT ACQUAINTANCE-PRED) means that PERSON is acquainted with AGENT, at least in the way (and/or to the degree) specified by ACQUAINTANCE-PRED; i.e. (ACQUAINTANCE-PRED PERSON AGENT).  Note that AGENT must be an #$IntelligentAgent, so this is not the predicate to use to express the fact that Fred `is acquainted with' drag racing.  Note that, depending on the value for ACQUAINTANCE-PRED, there may or may not be some way in which one can conclude that AGENT is acquainted with PERSON.")
(comment actsInPesonalCapacityIn "(#$actsInPesonalCapacityIn AGENT ACT) holds when AGENT performs or otherwise plays some role in ACT in a personal (vs. official) capacity")
(comment normalityForAgent "The collection of all things by how normal a thing is to a particular agent.  (#$normalityForAgent OBJ COL AGT NORMALITY) means that for the observer AGT, OBJ has the 'normality level' NORMALITY for an element of collection COL. For example (#$normalityForAgent 'Piranha001' #$Fish Charles #$Exotic-Unusual) means that for Charles, the 'Piranha001' is an exotic fish. The COLL attribute is important here: 'Piranha001' could.  be a perfectly normal piranha, yet still be an exotic fish.  Normality is different from but related to frequency (e.g. #$frequencyOfActionType, #$Frequency). For example, a mechanic sees broken cars every day; such cars are common for the mechanic, but not for the general population.  To assert the normality of a thing for a normal observer, see #$normalityOfThing.")
(comment identicalInQuantity "(#$identicalInQuantity THING1 THING2 QUANT-TYPE) means that the two things THING1 and THING2 have the same values of the quantity type  QUANT-TYPE.  Here 'the same' means complete identity or very close resemblance -- what this means, and what the standard of closeness or identity is, depends on the context, but #$identicalInQuantity and #$differentInQuantity cannot both be correctly asserted of the same two things.  See also #$resemblesInQuantity.")
(comment intimatelyAcquaintedWith "(#$intimatelyAcquaintedWith X Y) means that X and Y are very closely acquainted and would probably know a lot about each other.  This does NOT mean that they have intimate relations.  This is the level of acquaintance we would expect for #$cohabitingFamilyMembers, #$spouses, very close friends, etc.  We would also expect X and Y to be in frequent contact in the indefinite present, but this is not necessarily true.  We can say, though, that if X and Y are now intimately acquainted, they probably spent a lot of time together at some (perhaps undetermined) time in the past.")
(comment Custom-Made "The collection of all things which are unique and made for one customer, possibly according to that customer's specifications; made to order.  Instances include tailored clothes, suspension bridges, skyscrapers, and some meals.  Tract houses, manufactured houses, and (most) mobile homes are not instances of this collection, although ")
(comment Normal-Usual "The collection of all things that are common, everyday, usual, unnoteworthy, etc. in the indicated (often highly-specific and unreified) context.  See #$normalityOfThing amd #$normalityForAgent for the means of specifying the context in which something is an instance of this collection.")
(comment onHorizon "(#$onHorizon LOC HORIZON-OBJ) means that HORIZON-OBJ appears to be \"on the horizon\" from location LOC.  This is always context dependent.  If the two objects are fixed relative to the same planet, then #$onHorizon can relate them for a long time.  Otherwise the context can be fleeting.")
(comment Exotic-Unusual "An instance of #$ThingByNormalityInContext.  The collections of all things that are intriguingly unusual and rare in the indicated (often highly restrictive) context.  Exotic things are often foreign, but need not be.  Spices were exotic to Europeans of the 15th century, but not to those of the 21st.")
(disjointWith Exotic-Unusual Normal-Usual)
(comment ExistenceAwareness "The the quantity of awareness of something which specifies that an agent is somehow aware of an object's existence.")
(comment AwarenessQuantity "The collection of degrees of awareness that describe the ways in which an agent is aware of some object.")
(comment fieldName-SKS "(#$fieldName-SKS FIELD STRING) means that STRING is the name string of FIELD.  Assertions using this predicate are inferred from forward rules.")
(comment SimpleExposureAwareness "The quantity of awareness which specifies that an agent X is aware of (knows something about) some individual object through having once (or very few times) been in it's physical presence, or in physical contact with it.  In the case of an agent X and a fax machine Y, for example, (#$exposedTo X Y SimplePhysicalPresenceAwareness) means that X has used Y at least once and could probably be expected to know some things about how a fax machine is used by virtue of limited exposure to one.")
(disjointWith MusicalPerformance GameEvent)
(disjointWith ProfessionalServicing GameEvent)
(comment differentInQuantity "(#$differentInQuantity THING1 THING2 QUANT-TYPE) means that the two things THING1 and THING2 do not have the same values of the quantity type QUANT-TYPE.  Here 'the same' could mean complete identity or close resemblance -- what this 'different' means, and what the standard of closeness or identity is, depends on the context, but #$differentInQuantity and #$identicalInQuantity cannot both be correctly asserted of the same two things.  See also #$resemblesInQuantity.")
(comment OccasionalExposureAwareness "The quantity of awareness which specifies that an agent X is aware of (knows something about) some individual object through having occasionally been in it's physical presence (been in contact with it, used it, etc.).  In the case of an agent X and a fax machine Y, for example, (#$exposedTo X Y OccasionalPhysicalPresenceAwareness) means that X has used Y several times and could probably be expected to know some things about how a fax machine is used by virtue of this exposure to one.")
(comment VisualAwareness "The degree of awareness which specifies that an agent X is aware of (knows something about) some individual object's physical appearance.")
(comment FrequentExposureAwareness "The degree of awareness which specifies that an agent X is aware of (knows something about) some individual object through having frequently been in it's physical presence (been in contact with it, used it, etc.).  In the case of an agent X and a fax machine Y, for example, (#$exposedTo X Y FrequentPhysicalPresenceAwareness) means that X has used Y many times and could probably be expected to have a good understanding of how a fax machine is used by virtue of this exposure to one.")
(comment DescriptionAwareness "The quantity of awareness which specifies that an agent X is aware of (knows something about) some individual object by virtue of having read or heard a description of it.  In the case of an agent X and a fax machine Y, for example, (#$exposedTo X Y #$DescriptionAwareness) could mean that X has heard some coworker describe Y's appearance or explain how to use Y, or has read the instructions for using Y, and could be expected to know some things about Y on the basis of the description/explanation/instructions.")
(comment imageFeature "The visual image ARG1 has the image feature ARG2.")
(comment AcquaintancePredicate "The collection of predicates that specify ways in which (and/or degrees to which) one person is acquainted with another agent [#$Agent-Generic].  Some instances of this collection are: #$famousPersonAcquaintance, #$trueFanAcquaintance, #$intimatelyAcquaintedWith, #$frequentlyInContactWith, etc.")
(comment hyphenString "(#$hyphenString STRINGS WORD PART TERM) means, just as with #$multiWordString, that the translation of the phrase or word containing STRINGS and WORD, with part of speech PART, is TERM. (See #$multiWordString for further usage notes). In addition, this predicate specifies that STRINGS and WORD may occur in THREE juxtapositions: they may be separated not only 1: by a space, but also 2: with a hyphen or 3: run together with no space at all. For example, (#$hyphenString (#$TheList \"time\") #$Zone-TheWord #$CountNoun #$TimeZone)denotes that \"time zone\", \"time-zone\", and \"timezone\" are all acceptable forms of the word.  In generation, by default, the hyphenated form will be used (e.g. \"time-zone\")")
(comment chiefPorts "The predicate #$chiefPorts relates an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity to an instance of #$PortCity which is a #$geopoliticalSubdivision of the polity. (#$chiefPorts POLITY CITY) means that the #$City CITY is one of the chief port cities controlled by POLITY.")
(comment contentMt "This predicate relates a structured knowledge source with a Cyc microtheory which \"sees\" its contents.  If (#$contentMt SKS MT) is true, then the inference engine has access to the knowledge in SKS when answering queries asked within MT (or any specialization of MT).  A #$contentMt assertion is typically inferred from a forward rule.")
(comment SubcollectionOccursAtFn "(#$SubcollectionOccursAtFn SCRIPTTYPE GEO-THING) is the collection of all instances of SCRIPTTYPE that occur [#$eventOccursAt] in the region of GEO-THING.  If GEO-THING is an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity, then its territory (see #$territoryOf and #$TerritoryFn) is referred to.  Thus (#$SubcollectionOccursAtFn #$PoliticalProtesting  #$CityOfWashingtonDC) is the collection of political protests in the US capital and (#$SubcollectionOccursAtFn #$EscapeCaptivity #$Alcatraz-TheIsland) is the collection of escapes from Alcatraz island.")
(comment Licensed-Professional "The collection of instances of #$PersonWithOccupation that are licensed professionals,
 e.g., doctors and lawyers.")
(comment ProductTypeByLicensingFeature "A collection of collections.  Each instance of this collection is a collection of instance of #$ProductTypes that
have a particular sort of license.")
(comment Licensed-ProductType "The collection of instances of products that are licensed by someone for use somewhere.")
(comment minorReligions "(#$minorReligions GEO REL) means that #$Religion REL is believed in and/or practiced by a relatively small percent of the population of the #$GeographicalThing, GEO.")
(comment SightseeingInFn "(#$SightseeingInFn GEO-THING) returns the collection of all instances of #$SightSeeing that take place in GEO-THING (or its territory if GEO-THING is an instance of #$GeopoliticalEntity).")
(comment contentSentenceOfSchema "(#$contentSentenceOfSchema SCHEMA
SENTENCE) means that SENTENCE expresses a logical feature, or domain
assumption, of SCHEMA.  For example, (#$contentSentenceOfSchema
#$TestLanguageSpoken-LS (#$completeExtentEnumerable #$languageSpoken))
means that the complete extent of #$languageSpoken is known in any
content microtheory which interprets data using the logical schema
#$TestLanguageSpoken-LS.  These SENTENCEs are valid from within or
below the 'content microtheory' associated with SOURCE via the
predicate #$contentMt.")
(comment schemaCompleteExtentKnown "(#$schemaCompleteExtentKnown SCHEMA PRED) entails that (#$completeExtentEnumerable PRED) is true in the context which SCHEMA is describing.  In practice, this means that the #$completeExtentEnumerable sentence will be asserted in the content microtheory of SCHEMA.")
(comment completeObjectSchema "This relation is the structured knowledge source analogue of #$completeExtentEnumerable.  (#$completeObjectSchema SCHEMA_LS) means that where (#$meaningSentenceOfSchema SCHEMA_LS TEMPLATE) is asserted, and SENTENCE is a CycL sentence that matches TEMPLATE in the sense of substituting appropriate CycL terms for the indexicals such that the terms in question denote individuals described in the database of which SCHEMA_LS is a logical schema, if SENTENCE cannot be proved by dynamic-access lookup from the database using the #$meaningSentenceOfSchema assertion in question, this is a strong argument that SENTENCE is false.")
(comment necConditionFor-Events "'(#$necConditionFor-Events EVENT1 EVENT2)' means that EVENT1 started before, and is part of the causal chain leading to EVENT2 in such a way that if EVENT1 had not happened then EVENT2 would not have happened.  This is logically weaker than #$preconditionFor-Events which requires that the precondition have ended before the conditioned event starts.")
(comment DesktopSecurityProgram "#$DesktopSecurityProgram is the collection of computer programs whose primary function is to supplement the operating system's function of controlling varying levels of user access to software and files.")
(comment Ethnic "A collection used to describe the artifacts, food, and customs of those ethnic groups that differ from the predominant local culture(s).")
(comment ImmunityPredicate "The collection of all #$BinaryPredicates specifying the type of immunity an organism [#$Organism-Whole] has to a type of pathogenic organisms.")
(comment EvaluativePropositionalAttitudePredicate "A subcollection of #$EvaluativePredicate (q.v.) whose instances, are used to attribute evaluatory relations or assessments to propositions.  More precisely, an instance of #$EvaluativePropositionalAttitudePredicate can be used to relate an agent to a sentence (specifically, an #$ELSentence-Assertible) in such a way that the agent is actually making a particular sort of evaluative assessment of the state of affairs or proposition that the sentence expresses, and thereby assumes a particular attitude or cognitive stance toward that proposition (see #$evaluates-Propositional).")
(comment passiveImmunity "(#$passiveImmunity ORGANISM PATHOGEN-TYPE) means that ORGANISM acquired immunity to organisms of type PATHOGEN-TYPE by transfer of antibodies or #$Lymphocytes from an immune donor.")
(comment innateImmunity "(#$innateImmunity ORGANISM PATHOGEN-TYPE) means that ORGANISM has an immunity to pathogens of PATHOGEN-TYPE due to ORGANISM's genetic constitution.")
(comment pathogenCausesConditionType "(#$pathogenCausesConditionType PATHOGENTYPE CONDITIONTYPE) means that under ordinary circumstances, organisms of PATHOGENTYPE are capable of causing a #$PhysiologicalCondition of the type CONDITIONTYPE in a host organism.")
(comment speciesImmunity "(#$speciesImmunity ORGANISM PATHOGEN-TYPE) means that ORGANISM belongs to a species not susceptible to diseases caused by given type of pathogen.")
(comment majorReligions "(#$majorReligions POLITY RELIGION) means that #$Religion RELIGION is believed in and/or practiced by a substantial percentage of the population of the #$GeopoliticalEntity, POLITY.")
(comment activeImmunityTo "(#$activeImmunityTo ORGANISM PATHOGEN-TYPE) means that ORGANISM has acquired immunity to diseases caused by pathogens of PATHOGEN-TYPE attributable to the presence of antibodies or of immune lymphoid cells formed in response to antigenic stimulus.")
(comment hasImmunityWithRespectToOrg "(#$hasImmunityWithRespectToOrg ORG IMM ORG-TYPE) means that ORG, an instance of #$Organism-Whole, has the type of immunity IMM, an #$ImmunityPredicate, with respect to organisms of the type ORG-TYPE, i.e. (IMM ORG ORG-TYPE). If ORG is immune with respect to ORG-TYPE, Org is also said insusceptible to diseases caused by organisms of the type ORG-TYPE, see #$immuneWithRespectToPathogen. Contrast with #$hasImmunityWithRespectToDisease and #$immuneWithRespectToDisease.")
(comment agentTypeCausesConditionType "(#$agentTypeCausesConditionType PATH-TYPE COND-TYPE) means that instances of PATH-TYPE would cause an ailment condition of the type COND-TYPE, if appropriate conditions of concentration or susceptibility of the possible victim  are met.")
(comment immuneWithRespectToDisease "(#$immuneWithRespectToDisease ORG DISEASE) means that the instance of #$Organism-Whole, ORG, is #$Immune to the infectious disease, DISEASE.")
(comment acquiredImmunity "(#$acquiredImmunity ORGANISM PATHOGEN-TYPE) means that ORGANISM acquired immunity to pathogens of PATHOGEN-TYPE do to the functioning of ORGANISM's immune system acquired by natural infection or vaccination, see #$activeImmunityTo, or transfer of antibodies or #$Lymphocytes from an immune donor, see #$passiveImmunity.")
(comment Territory "#$Territory is a specialization of #$ControlledLand.  Each instance of #$Territory is a geopolitical entity which is distinct from, but dependent on and controlled by, another geopolitical entity.  Instances of #$Territory include #$PuertoRico, #$BritishAntarcticTerritory, and #$RyukyuIslandsTerritory.")
(comment annualDeathRate "(#$annualDeathRate POLITY RATE) means that the #$GeographicalRegion which is the #$territoryOf POLITY has a death rate of RATE in number of deaths per 1000 population per year.")
(comment naturalImmunity "(#$naturalImmunity ORGANISM PATHOGEN-TYPE) means that ORGANISM has resistance to diseases caused by pathogens of PATHOGEN-TYPE mediated by cells capable of immune activity without being stimulated by immunization, or acquired through contact with an #$Antigen.  Natural immunity is non-specific and includes barriers to infectious agents, see #$Infection and #$LivingBiologicalAgent. For example, natural immunity activities are conducted by #$Skin, mucous membrane, #$NaturalKillerCells, phagocytosis, inflammation, interferon , and a variety of non-specific factors. Natural immunity may vary with age and with hormonal or metabolic activity.")
(disjointWith RegionType LifeStageType)
(comment holidayCelebratedInPolity "(#$holidayCelebratedInPolity HOLIDAY POLITY) means that POLITY is a #$GeopoliticalEntity in whose territory HOLIDAY is typically observed as a holiday.")
(disjointWith RegionType PersonTypeByActivity)
(comment premier "The #$HeadOfGovernment of a country with the title Premier or Prime Minister.")
(comment IllegalAction "The collection of actions that are illegal.  Since different things are legal/illegal in different areas this collection should only be used in a microtheory that specifies the area where the instances of this collection are illegal.")
(comment LegalAction "The collection of actions that are legal. Since different things are legal/illegal in different areas this collection should only be used in a microtheory that specifies the area where the instances of this collection are legal.")
(comment QuestionablyLegal "The collection of actions that are of questionable legality. Since different things are legal/illegal in different areas this collection should only be used in a microtheory that specifies the area where the instances of this collection have questionable legal status.")
(comment insIdenticalInQuantity "(#$insIdenticalInQuantity COL QUANT-TYPE) means that all instances of COL have the same values of the quantity type QUANT-TYPE.  Here 'the same' means complete identity or very close resemblance -- what this means, and what the standard of closeness or identity is, depends on the context.  See #$identicalInQuantity, #$differentInQuantity, and #$resemblesInQuantity.")
(comment simpleContactAcquaintances "The predicate which specifies that persons X and Y have met each other at least once, and probably would be able to recall this, and even recognize each other, if they meet again.  If X has met Y, then Y has met X, thus this is a #$SymmetricBinaryPredicate.  This assumes that there was a meeting event in which X and Y interacted, that both were minimally conscious, etc.")
(comment outputsCreated-TypeType "A type-level version of #$outputsCreated.    (#$outputsCreated-TypeType EVENT-TYPE TYPE)   says that among the outputs (see #$outputsCreated) for any  instance of EVENT-TYPE is at least one instance  of TYPE.  For example, (#$outputsCreated-TypeType  #$DiggingAHole #$Cavity) says that every instance  of #$DiggingAHole results in the creation of a  #$Cavity.")
(comment EvaluativePredicate "A collection of predicates whose instances are designed to predicate value judgements, in a broad sense of the  phrase that includes pragmatic, moral, and aesthetic assessments of a thing by an agent.    The salient example is that of evaluative
states: the subjective assessment of the value of an action is something
projected onto the world, i.e. not entirely objective, though not
necessarily dependent upon any one individual mind. An evaluative
assessment in this sense may, for instance, supervene on the attitudes of
many minds -- those of a military unit, say, or of a country, or perhaps of
a culture.  These predicate can be used on their own to attribute an evaluatory property to an action relative to an agent or, they can be used as argument places in predicates that are specifically
defined for them, e.g. #$evaluates-Propositional.")
(comment SoftwareDevelopment "A specialization of #$DevelopingAProduct and #$WritingAComputerProgram. The collection of events in which an instance of #$ComputerProgram-CW is developed. The development process may involve several rounds of producing prototypes and fixing bugs and extending features.")
(comment GoalTypeByCategory "A collection of collections.  Each element of #$GoalTypeByCategory is a collection of goals (sentences whose truth is intended to be acted towards by some agent) that represent a particular category of goals, e.g., #$ForeignPolicyGoal, #$NationalDefenseGoal, #$TradeGoal.  More precisely, elements of #$GoalTypeByCategory indicate the status of a goal when possessed by a particular #$Agent-Generic.  The qualification is important because goals may fall into different categories depending on who possesses them.  For example, improving the Russian economy might be a #$NationalEconomyGoal of #$Russia and a #$ForeignPolicyGoal of the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica.  Taking a closer look at the example, #$NationalEconomyGoal is the collection of goals that are national economy goals.  In other words, they are the collection of sentences such that someone's goal is to make them true to help improve or somehow affect their national economy.  So, \"improving the Russian economy\" is a national economy goal by virtue of #$Russia's attitude towards it.  To attribute a goal and category to an agent use #$goalCategoryForAgent.  ")
(comment evaluates-Propositional "This predicate can be used to describe propositional attitudes in terms of an agent attributing a certain type of evaluative attitude (q.v.) to a proposition. (#$evaluates-Propositional AGENT SENT EVAL-PRED) means that AGENT attributes to some action, ACT, described by SENT the 
attitude that would be expressed by (EVAL-PRED AGENT ACT).  Thus it represents a certain propositional attitude on the part of AGENT toward that action.    Such attitudes correspond in some case to stances that are largely based on emotion, and in other cases to reasoned evaluative judgments. Entities capable of taking evaluative stances are entities capable of manifesting interests in purposeful action, hence the restriction of the first argument to #$Agent-Generic.")
(comment EconomicGoal "The attribute characterizing goals which  have to do with economic ends. This can include personal goals, such  as gaining employment, or maximizing one's income, to national or  company goals, such as reducing one's national budget deficit or  maximizing profits.--Okeefe, June 24, 1998")
(comment RadiallySymmetricObject "A specialization of #$SpatialThing.  Each instance of #$RadiallySymmetricObject is a spatial thing whose spatial parts are regularly arranged about a central axis.  Instances of #$RadiallySymmetricObject include wheels and adult starfish.")
(comment polityHasTransportMeans "(#$polityHasTransportMeans POLITY TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE) means that the #$GeopoliticalEntity POLITY has regular, major use of or access to transport by means of instances of TRANSPORTMEANSTYPE. For example, the #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica has access to transport via #$Ships.")
(comment MetalPlating "A collection of events.  In each #$MetalPlating event, an object made of metal is coated with a very thin layer of a different metal.  The coating process is done in such a way as to permanently bond the two layers.")
(comment permanentlyEastOf "(#$permanentlyEastOf EAST WEST) means that the (territory of) #$GeographicalThing EAST is to the east of the (territory of) #$GeographicalThing WEST, when viewed in the terrestrial frame of reference.  Note that WEST is therefore west of EAST; thus, no distinct predicate is needed to represent `west of'.  Example: (#$permanentlyEastOf #$EasternUSATimeZone #$CentralUSATimeZone).  See also #$permanentlyNorthOf and #$directionBetweenObjects.  To express '(permanentlyWestOf x y)' all we need is to say (#$permanentlyEastOf y x).  In order to relate two instances of #$SpatialThing-Localized that are mobile or do not fit the argument restrictions of #$permanentlyEastOf, use the more general predicate, #$eastOf.")
(comment touchesAtEnd "(#$touchesAtEnd OBJ1 OBJ2) means that an end of OBJ1 #$touches OBJ2.  If the two objects are #$connectedTo each other at this point, the more specific #$Predicate, #$connectedAtEnd applies.")
(comment BackSide "A specialization of #$Side. Each instance of #$BackSide is the entire back side (as conventionally understood) of an object that has distinct sides, one of which faces backwards.")
(comment evidentialSupportForBelief "#$evidentialSupportForBelief AGENT INFO GEN-VAL-PRED) means that the evidence AGENT has bearing on the truth of INFO makes it reasonable to have degree represented by GEN-VAL-PRED of belief in INFO. Roughly, this is to say that there is some (possibly complex) proposition PROP such that (#$beliefs AGENT PROP) and (#$conditionalProbability INFO PROP NUMBER), where given the domain assumptions of the relevant Mt, NUMBER falls within the range determined by the #$GenericValuePredicate GEN-VAL-PRED.  What this means is if there were a quantity type called \"EvidentialSupport\" and GEN-VAL-PRED was, say, #$mediumAmountOf, then AGENT would have a (#$MediumAmountFn \"EvidentialSupport\") for the Information INFO.  (#$evidentialSupportForBelief AGENT INFO GEN-VAL-PRED) does not mean that AGENT in fact does have that degree of belief in INFO; that is, it does not entail (#$confidenceLevel AGENT INFO AMOUNT)) wher AMOUNT corresponds to the amount represented by GEN-VAL-PRED. arg3 is constrained to be an instance of #$GenericValuePredicate, rather than of #$Real0-1, in order to make use of this predicate feasible in practice (since we can often say of an agent that she has a low, medium or high amount of evidence for a given proposition, but can rarely or never say she has exactly N degree of evidence, for some particular instance N of Real0-1). This predicate's main use is in stating relations among propositional attitudes such as those expressed by #$beliefs, #$knows, #$goals and so on; there will probably be relatively few occasions to assert GAFs with #$evidentialSupportForBelief as arg zero.")
(comment unacceptablyCostly "(#$unacceptablyCostly AGT ACTION) holds just in case in AGT's considered opinion ACTION is too costly to perform.  The respect to which the action is considered too costly is undetermined, but meant to indicate an \"all things considered\" judgement.  Typically, this will be true when the agent judges that the cost of an action vastly exceeds the benefits of its
expected outcome, i.e., that the cost of the action is unacceptable with
respect to the goal of the agent. This is not to be understood merely as a
generically negative disposition or feeling toward the action.  Often this will be used as an argument place certain other predicates: e.g. #$costOfAction.")
(comment attitudeTowardsEvent "#$attitudeTowardsEvent(AGT EVT DEGREE-OF-EMOTYPE) means that the #$SentientAnimal AGT has the instance of #$FeelingAttribute DEGREE-OF-EMOTYPE about the #$Event EVT.  By `attitude' we mean a feeling which may be latent and/or long-lasting.  The third argument to this predicate is usually constructed by wrapping a specialization of #$FeelingAttribute in a generic value function such as #$HighAmountFn.  Please avoid using these functions with #$FeelingAttribute itself.  To refer to feelings that AGT experiences immediately and consciously towards EVT, use #$feelsTowardsEvent.")
(comment commensurateToBenefits "(#$commensurateToBenefits AGT ACTION) holds just in case in AGT's considered opinion the cost of performing ACTION is commensurate to its benefits.  This predicate can encode an agent's evaluative
judgment that the cost of an action does not exceed the benefits of its
expected outcome, i.e., that the cost of the action is acceptable with
respect to the goal of the agent. This is not to be understood as a
generically positive evaluative disposition or feeling toward the action.  This predicate is often used in the 4th argument place of #$costOfAction")
(comment anatomicalResourceRequired "#$anatomicalResourceRequired is an instance of #$ResourcePredicate. (#$anatomicalResourceRequired ACT BODYPARTTYPE NUM) means that the successful doer of ACT must have at least this many (NUM) of the #$AnimalBodyPartType BODYPARTTYPE. For example, if VOLANT is an instance of #$Flying-FlappingWings, then (#$anatomicalResourceRequired VOLANT #$Wing-AnimalBodyPart 2).")
(comment anatomicalPartTypeRequired "#$anatomicalPartTypeRequired is an instance of #$ResourcePredicate. '(#$anatomicalPartTypeRequired ACT-TYPE PART-TYPE ROLE)' means that the successful player of ROLE in an act of ACT-TYPE must have at least one physical part of type PART-TYPE.")
(comment NervousSystem "A specialization of both #$ConnectedPhysicalPathSystem  and #$AnimalBodyPart.  Each instance of #$NervousSystem is a bodily system composed of the brain, spinal cord, and nerves of an animal (see the collections #$Brain, #$SpinalCord, and #$Nerve).  This system enables the animal to receive, interpret, and respond to various stimuli.")
(comment anatomicalPartCountRequired "#$anatomicalPartCountRequired is an instance of #$ResourcePredicate. (#$anatomicalPartCountRequired ACT-TYPE PART-TYPE ROLE COUNT) means that the successful player of ROLE in an act of ACT-TYPE must have exactly COUNT many of #$anatomicalParts PART-TYPE.")
(comment typeRequiresToPlayRole "#$typeRequiresToPlayRole is an instance of #$ResourcePredicate. (#$typeRequiresToPlayRole OBJTYPE1 OBJTYPE2 EVENTTYPE ROLE) means that, in order to play ROLE in an event of EVENTTYPE, instances of OBJTYPE1 require some single instance of OBJTYPE2.  Note that this is neutral as to whether or not the instance of OBJTYPE1 desires to, needs to, or actually will play ROLE in an event of EVENTTYPE.  See also #$requiresToPlayRole.")
(comment requiresToPlayRole "#$requiresToPlayRole is an instance of #$ResourcePredicate. (#$requiresToPlayRole OBJ OBJTYPE EVENTTYPE ROLE) means that, in order to play ROLE in an event of EVENTTYPE, OBJ requires an instance of OBJTYPE.  Note that this is neutral as to whether or not OBJ desires to, needs to, or actually will play ROLE in such an event.  See also #$typeRequiresToPlayRole.")
(comment SkolemFuncN "#$SkolemFuncN is a collection of Cyc system-generated functions that partially implement existential quantifications in Cyc.  Whenever someone asserts to Cyc an expression that contains a '#$thereExistAtLeast', a '#$thereExistAtMost', or a '#$thereExistExactly' quantifier, Cyc automatically creates a new instance of #$SkolemFuncN and rewrites the assertion using this skolem function instead of that existential quantifier.  See also #$termOfUnit. At this time (3/98), skolem functions are automatically named by the Cyc system using the prefix 'SKF-' followed by a number.")
(comment percentOfTerritoryIs "(#$percentOfTerritoryIs ?POLITY ?TYPE ?PCT) means that ?PCT percent of the territory of ?POLITY is made up of ?TYPE.")
(comment levelOfMentalExertion "(#$levelOfMentalExertion AGNT ACT LEVEL) means that AGNT performs ACT, exerting a level of mental effort described by LEVEL.  E.g., (#$levelOfMentalExertion JohannesBrahms CreationOfBrahmsSymphonyNo1 (#$VeryHighAmountFn #$MentalEffortLevel)).")
(comment provenanceOfArtObject "(#$provenanceOfArtObject GEO OBJECT) means that OBJECT, an instance of #$ArtObject, has been made in (the territory of) GEO, an instance of #$GeographicalThing.")
(comment BottomSide "A specialization of #$Side.  Each instance of #$BottomSide is the entire bottom side (as conventionally understood) of an object that has distinct sides, one of which faces down.")
(comment zipCodeRangeOfState "A ternary predicate that relates a given US state to the range of five-digit zip codes available for use in that state.  (#$zipCodeRangeOfState STATE LOWZIP HIGHZIP) means that all the #$ZipCode-FiveDigits used in STATE are alphabetically between LOWZIP and HIGHZIP inclusive.")
(comment flowsInRegions "(#$flowsInRegions RIVER GEO) means that RIVER is a #$River that flows within or through the (territory of) GEO, a #$GeographicalRegion or #$GeopoliticalEntity.")
(comment GroupTransferOut "A subcollection of #$GroupTransfer. Instances of this collection are those actions in which there is necessarily something that ceases to be a #$groupMembers of some instance of #$Group. This is a very diverse subcollection of #$TransferOut, including transfers out of organizations, systems of physical devices, teams or anything represented as a subcollection of #$Group in the Cyc ontology.  For further clarification see the #$NoteAboutGroupTransfers.  Note that if the group has a #$groupMemberType assertion for it, then anything transferred out of it must be of that type.  See also #$GroupTransferIn, #$toGroup and #$fromGroup. You may also want to look at #$OrganizationalTransfer and constants closely related to it.")
(comment PostalCode "A specialization of #$ContactInfoString.  Each instance of #$PostalCode is a character string used by a postal service to designate a particular geographic area.  For example, the code used by the #$USPostalService for central downtown Austin, TX, is '78701'.  Important specializations of #$PostalCode include #$InternationalPostalCode and #$ZipCode.")
(comment GroupTransfer "A collection of #$Actions in which something changes membership with respect to some instance of #$Group, i.e. actions in which something becomes a #$groupMembers of some group, ceases to be a #$groupMembers of some group, or is moved from one group to another. This collection includes a wide variety of group transfers, including those among organizations, instances of #$SystemOfDevices,  (#$GroupFn #$ProfessionalSportsTeam) or #$Family-SocialEntity. For further clarification see the #$NoteAboutGroupTransfers.  Note that if a group has a #$groupMemberType assertion for it, then anything transferred out of it must be of that type.   See also #$GroupTransferIn, #$GroupTransferOut, #$toGroup and #$fromGroup. You may also want to look at #$OrganizationalTransfer and constants closely related to it.")
(comment FootballGoalPost-ScoringRegion "Elements are regions of space between the two parallel 'arms' of a football goalpost.  If one team kicks the football in play through the opposing team's #$FootballGoalPost-ScoringRegion, 1 or 3 points are scored depending on whether the kick happens immediately following a touchdown or as a field goal attempt.")
(comment Party-Celebration "A specialization of #$SocialGathering.  Each instance of #$Party-Celebration is a social gathering whose main purpose is the entertainment, amusement, or pleasure of those gathered.  Specializations of #$Party-Celebration include #$BirthdayParty, #$DinnerParty, and #$BabyShower.")
(disjointWith Party-Celebration BusinessMeeting)
(disjointWith Party-Celebration Lecturing)
(comment Perceiving-Involuntary "A specialization of #$Perceiving.  Each instance of #$Perceiving-Involuntary is a perceptual event in which an agent involuntarily perceives something (so that each instance of #$Perceiving-Involuntary is _not_ an instance of #$PurposefulAction).")
(comment UnintendedLossOfUserRights "A specialization of #$LosingUserRights and #$HarmingAnAgent (qq.v.) whose instances involve a loss of some #$SituationTypeByUserRights that was not deliberate or intended by the agent who loses the user-right in question.  For example, having something stolen appropriated is an instance of an unintendended loss of user rights.")
(disjointWith IndividualAgent Group)
(comment RobbingABank "This is the collection of thefts from a #$BankOrganization, excluding embezzlement.")
(comment olderThan "(#$olderThan OLD YOUNG) means that the #$age of OLD is #$greaterThan the #$age of YOUNG.  The purpose of this predicate is to allow one to make assertions about relative ages when exact ages are not known or not important.")
(comment SpeechPartPredicate "A specialization of #$NLSyntacticPredicate.  Instances of #$SpeechPartPredicate are used to state the forms which words can take.  The first argument of a #$SpeechPartPredicate must be an instance of #$EnglishWord, and the second must be an instance of #$CharacterString.  For example, (#$singular #$Dog-TheWord \"dog\") means that the singular (noun) form of #$Dog-TheWord is \"dog\".")
(comment physicalCopyOf "(#$physicalCopyOf COPY ORIGINAL) means that COPY  is a physical copy of ORIGINAL.  If they are information bearing objects, then they contained and conveyed the same information at the time COPY was made.")
(comment physicalCopiesOfTheSameObject "This predicate relates copies that have come from the same original. (#$physicalCopiesOfTheSameObject COPY1 COPY2) means that COPY1 and COPY2 are two (numerically distinct) tangible copies of (see #$physicalCopyOf) the same tangible thing ORIG (which is itself numerically distinct from either of these copies).  (Although of course ORIG might itself be a copy of something else, it is -- relative to COPY1 and COPY2 -- the \"original\" from whence they both came.")
(comment RelationshipTypeByArity "A collection of collections.  Each instance of #$RelationshipTypeByArity is a broad collection of relations defined primarily in terms of its instances' arity, and perhaps also in terms of whether its instances are all #$Predicates or all #$Function-Denotationals. Most instances of #$RelationshipTypeByArity are such that all of their instances have the same fixed arity, e.g.  #$UnaryFunction, #$BinaryPredicate, #$TernaryRelation.  A few instances of #$RelationshipTypeByArity, however, are defined in terms of whether their instances have fixed or variable arity, e.g. #$FixedArityFunction and #$VariableArityRelation.")
(comment consumedObject "(#$consumedObject EVENT THING) means that the entirety of THING is consumed during EVENT.")
(comment objectFound "(#$objectFound EVENT OBJECT) means that OBJECT is found in EVENT.")
(comment Shaft "A specialization of #$SolidTangibleArtifact.  Each instance of #$Shaft is an artifact that is long, straight, cylindrical, and rigid. Instances of #$Shaft are usually made of wood, metal, or plastic.")
(comment predominantLanguage "(#$predominantLanguage COUNTRY LANGUAGE) means that most of the population that lives in the territory of COUNTRY speak LANGUAGE.  I.e., (#$languagesSpokenHere (#$TerritoryFn COUNTRY) LANGUAGE).  In #$DualistGeopoliticalMt (and its specMts), (#$genlPreds #$predominantLanguage #$languagesSpokenHere), since a country and its territory are conflated.")
(comment objectProcessed "(#$objectProcessed EVT OBJ) says that OBJ is what gets processed in EVT, an instance of #$ProcessingEvent.")
(comment transformedInto "An instance of #$ObjectPredicate that relates two instances of #$SomethingExisting.  (#$transformedInto DESTROYED CREATED) means that CREATED is created immediately after DESTROYED is destroyed (so that (#$contiguousAfter CREATED DESTROYED) holds).  Moreover, the material that constituted DESTROYED consitutes much, if not all, of CREATED at the moment it is created.  See also the related collection #$PhysicalTransformationEvent.")
(comment ZipCodeToIntegerFn "A #$ScalarDenotingFunction that converts a #$ZipCode string into the corresponding #$Integer.  More precisely, (#$ZipCodeToIntegerFn ZIP) is the integer denoted by the (initial) five-digit numeric string (within) ZIP.  Note that if ZIP is a #$ZipCode-NineDigit, only ZIP's first five digits are used in the conversion.  Thus, for example, #$ZipCodeToIntegerFn maps both of the strings \"01122\" and \"01122-3344\" to the integer 1122.")
(comment productionAmount "(#$productionAmount PRODUCER PRODUCT-TYPE AMOUNT) means that the #$ScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE produced by the instance of #$SomethingExisting, PRODUCER.  PRODUCER might, for example, be a #$Country, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion. If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of production of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by PRODUCER. This predicate should be used when the time period of production is unknown. If the time period is known, use #$productionAmountDuring.")
(comment significanceOfSituation "(#$significanceOfSituation SITUATION GVP) indicates that
SITUATION has the degree of significance indicated by GVP. For example, 
(#$significanceOfSituation #$GettysburgAddress-Speech #$highAmountOf) indicates
that the Gettysburg address is considered significant.")
(comment productionAmountDuring "(#$productionAmountDuring PRODUCER PRODUCT-TYPE THING AMOUNT) means that the #$NonNegativeScalarInterval AMOUNT is a measure of the amount of instances of the #$ProductType PRODUCT-TYPE produced by the instance of #$SomethingExisting PRODUCER during the temporal extent of the #$TemporalThing THING.  PRODUCER might, for example, be a #$Country, a #$Business, or a #$GeographicalRegion.  THING will often be a calendar time interval; but it may also be, for instance, a particular #$Event.  If AMOUNT is a #$Rate, AMOUNT indicates the average rate of production of instances of PRODUCT-TYPE by PRODUCER during the temporal extent of THING.  See also #$productionAmount, which can be used when the time period is unknown.")
(comment physicalStructuralIntegrity "(#$physicalStructuralIntegrity SUBST DEGREE) means that the tangible object SUBST has DEGREE ability to maintain its physical structure intact in the face of various forces.  DEGREE is an instance of #$GenericValuePredicate.  The #$physicalStructuralIntegrity of an object may be inferred from some of its other physical attributes.")
(comment NumeralString "A specialization of #$NumberString (q.v.).  Each instance of #$NumeralString is a #$SubLString composed entirely of #$ArabicNumerals.  Examples include \"1\", \"9828\", and \"0037846\", but not \"3.14\" or \"78731-1234\". (But note that \"3.14\" _is_ a #$NumberString and \"78731-1234\" a #$NumericString (q.v.).)")
(comment residesInRegion "This predicate relates a person or other sort of animal to a geographical region in which or the geopoliticalEntity in whose territory s/he/it resides.  (#$residesInRegion RESIDENT GEO) means that RESIDENT lives or resides primarily in (the territory of) GEO.  This obviously does not entail that RESIDENT is physically in GEO at any particular time, since people are often away from their places of residence. Note that a given person/animal (even with respect to a particular time) is normally related by #$residesInRegion to many different regions, where each such region is a sub- or super-region of some of the others.  For example, Karen currently resides in Austin, in Texas, in the United States, in North America, and so on.  See also #$residesInDwelling, #$hasHabitat, and #$ethnicity.")
(disjointWith Person (CollectionDifferenceFn Mammal Person))
(disjointWith GeneticallyEngineeredOrganism (CollectionDifferenceFn BiologicalLivingObject GeneticallyEngineeredOrganism))
(comment termStrings "(#$termStrings THING STRING) means that THING is a denotation of STRING.")
(disjointWith Path-Customary (CollectionDifferenceFn Path-Spatial Path-Customary))
(disjointWith Person (CollectionDifferenceFn Animal Person))
(disjointWith Artifact (CollectionDifferenceFn (SubcollectionOfWithRelationFromTypeFn Basin-Topographical covers-Paintlike Asphalt) Artifact))
(disjointWith Monotreme (CollectionDifferenceFn Mammal Monotreme))
(disjointWith Stealing-InsideJob (CollectionDifferenceFn Stealing Stealing-InsideJob))
(comment powerInRegion-Economic "(#$powerInRegion-Economic AGENT REGION            GENERIC-VALUE-PRED) means that the economic power of the #$IntelligentAgent AGENT in region REGION is at the level given by GENERIC-VALUE-PRED. Intelligent Agents can have different amounts of economic power in different regions, e.g., (#$powerInRegion-Economic #$Mexico #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica #$mediumAmountOf) but (#$powerInRegion-Economic #$Mexico #$Cameroon #$lowToVeryLowAmountOf). The Intelligent Agent need not be a #$GeopoliticalEntity, but could be of the form (#$powerInRegion-Economic #$OPEC #$PersianGulfRegion #$highAmountOf).")
(comment connotes "(#$connotes OBJ-1 OBJ-2 DEGREE) means that as a consequence of perceiving or thinking about one thing (OBJ-1), a typical sane intelligent perceiving agent would likely think of another thing (OBJ-2) with a strength of association indicated by DEGREE.  E.g., (#$connotes #$GermanNaziParty #$Prejudice #$highAmountOf).  This predicate is sometimes symmetric, but often not.  See also #$typeConnotes.")
(comment ambientAtmosphericConcentration "(#$ambientAtmosphericConcentration PLACE STUFF CONCENTRATION) holds just in case the concentation of the substance type STUFF is CONCENTRATION in the ambient atmospere in PLACE.  For instance, (#$ambientAtmosphericConcentration MyOffice #$Cyanide ((#$PerFn #$Gram #$CubicCentimeter) .003)) holds just in case the ambient atmospheric concentration of #$Cyanide in MyOffice is .003 grams per cubit centimeter.")
(comment levelOfOutputOfType "(#$levelOfOutputOfType EVT TYPE AMOUNT) says that EVT produced
AMOUNT instances of TYPE.  For example (#$levelOfOutputOfType
CowMilking001 #$CowsMilk-Product #$veryLowAmountOf) says that CowMilking001
produced very little milk.")
(comment powerInRegion-Military "(#$powerInRegion-Military ORG REGION            GENERIC-VALUE-PRED) means that the military power of the #$Organization            ORG in region REGION is given by GENERIC-VALUE-PRED. Organizations can have different amounts of military power in different regions, e.g., (#$powerInRegion-Military #$RepublicOfSouthAfrica #$SubSaharanAfrica #$mediumAmountOf) but (#$powerInRegion-Military #$RepublicOfSouthAfrica #$ContinentOfEurope #$lowToVeryLowAmountOf).")
(comment importanceOfThingInSet "(#$importanceOfThingInSet THING SET GENERIC-VALUE-PRED) means
that of the elements of SET, THING is an important member by some measure of 'importance' that is legitimate in the current microtheory.  Assertions
about 'major', 'moderate', 'low' importance of THING should have
#$highAmountOf, #$mediumAmountOf, and #$lowAmountOf for GENERIC-VALUE-PRED. Importance is a highly
context dependent notion.  This context dependence may be determined
by the goals of the current conversation, or by the properties of the
#$Microtheory that a given #$importanceOfThingInSet assertion occurs
in, or by some implicit agent's judgements about what is important, or
some other factors.  Concluding importance is a heuristic matter,
i.e. there are often not hard and fast rules concluding
#$importanceOfThingInSet except in more narrowly defined contexts.
Thus, it would probably not be correct to write a rule such as 'If
?STATE is one of the 10 biggest U.S. states its importance is high.'
unless, for example, such an assertion were stated in a conversational
microtheory where conversational agents share the belief that 'the
bigger a thing is, the more important it is'.  On the other hand, a
rule such as 'If ?STATE is one of the 10 oldest U.S. states its
importance is high.'  might be of some worth in the 'HistoriansMt' in
which history experts would be identified as the aforementioned
implicit importance evaluating agents.  Finally, a rule such as 'If
?STATE is one of the 10 most populous U.S. state's then its importance
is high' is a rule that could be re-used in a wider variety of
applications.  The original motivation of this constant was to preserve the level of vagueness in a natural language statement such as 'Houston is 
an important oil port.'")
(comment typicalVolumeOfOutputOfTypeOverDuration "(#$typicalVolumeOfOutputOfTypeOverDuration EVTTYPE OBJTYPE AMOUNT
DURATION) says that typically, instances of EVTTYPE produce AMOUNT of
OBJTYPE as its #$outputsCreated over DURATION. For example,
(#$typicalVolumeOfOutputOfTypeOverDuration MilkingACowByHand #$CowsMilk-Product
#$lowAmountOf #$AFewMinutesDuration).  The 'Lowness' here is relative to some
 unspecified parent collection (say, MilkingACow) whose typical level of output  over #$AFewMinutesDuration is
relatively high.")
(comment evidentialSupportForPhenomena "(#$evidentialSupportForPhenomena AGT PHENOM GVP)
 allows us to say that AGT has
  level associated with GVP of evidence supporting AGT's belief in the existence of
  PHENOM, without requiring us to spell this out
 in terms of the propositional content of AGT's belief.
 For example, (#$evidentialSupportForPhenomena #$FoxMulder-FBIAgent 
  #AlienBeing #$highToVeryHighAmountOf) says that Fox Mulder
 has a great deal of evidence supporting his belief in AlienBeings.
  To say that someone has evidence for his or her
 belief *that* something is the case, see #$evidentialSupportForBelief.)
  #$evidentialSupportForPhenomena is useful for parsing English 
 sentences, which frequently omit references to
  the belief that the evidence supports, and often 
 contain only references to the object 
of the supported belief.  See also #$evidentialSupportForBelief.")
(comment levelOfCompatibility "(#$levelOfCompatibility ?OLD ?NEW ?LEVEL) means that ?NEW can do anything that ?OLD can do, with a degree of sureness specified by ?LEVEL.  This predicate should be used when two things are less than completely compatible.  See also #$compatibleWithIn and #$upwardCompatibleProgram.")
(comment powerInRegion-Geopolitical "(#$powerInRegion-Geopolitical AGENT REGION            GENERIC-VALUE-PRED) means that the geopolical            power or leadership potential of the #$IntelligentAgent            AGENT in region REGION is has the value indicated by GENERIC-VALUE-PRED. Intelligent Agents can have different amounts of geopolitical power in different regions, e.g., (#$powerInRegion-Geopolitical #$Nigeria #$SubSaharanAfrica #$mediumAmountOf) but (#$powerInRegion-Geopolitical #$Nigeria #$IrishRepublic #$lowToVeryLowAmountOf).")
(comment goalImportance "(#$goalImportance AGT G DEGREE) means that the #$IntelligentAgent AGT has the #$Goal G, and G has the degree of importance DEGREE for AGT. ")
(comment coversWithConformity "(#$coversWithConformity OBJ SHEET LEVEL) means that OBJ is covered by SHEET, and that the inner surface of SHEET conforms to the surface features of OBJ to the degree LEVEL.  SHEET may cover OBJ in either the sense of #$covers-Ruglike or #$covers-Baglike.  For example, hosiery covers legs with a #$highAmountOf conformity; sweat pants have #$lowAmountOf conformity to legs.  Level of conformity could probably based on the average of the distance between of lines going normal to the inside surface of OBJ to SHEET.  The lowness or highness of this number would be based on comparison to representative exemplars.  E.g. in a low conformity case, e.g. the average OBJ to SHEET distance for a pen in a grocery bag would be high relative to the dimensions of the pen.  Thus level would be #$lowAmountOf.  The analogous measure for a leg inside spandex pants would be very low compared to the dimensions of the leg.  In such a case LEVEL would be #$highAmountOf.")
(comment qualitativeContent "qualitative description of the amount present (or contained) of some type of stuff (e.g., (#$qualitativeContent(Leaf #$Chlorophyll #$veryHighAmountOf)).")
(comment durationAtIntensityLevel "(#$durationAtIntensityLevel COND DIS-LEV TIME) means that the agent experiencing (#$bodilyDoer) COND has experienced the level of discomfort DIS-LEV for the time period TIME.")
(comment levelOfPhysicalExertion "(#$levelOfPhysicalExertion AGNT ACT LEVEL) means that AGNT does ACT with a level of physical exertion LEVEL.  E.g., (#$levelOfPhysicalExertion DonovanBailey RunningMens100MRaceIn1996Olympics #$veryHighAmountOf).")
(comment genericallyEquivalentQuantity "(#$genericallyEquivalentQuantity COL SLOT QUANT GVP) <=> The #$GenericValuePredicate GVP's arg2 is equivalent to the quantity QUANT when it appears on SLOT in the context of instances of COL.  For example, (#$genericallyEquivalentQuantity #$Sprinter #$age (#$YearsDuration 14 17) #$lowAmountOf) holds just in case being age 14-17 is a low amount on the slot #$age with respect to instances of #$Sprinter.  In other words, it states that 14-17 is a low age for sprinters.  This is a way to relativize the values for #$lowAmountOf.  It is as if, in the context of sprinter's ages, (#$lowAmountOf #$Time-Quantity (#$YearsDuration 14 17)) holds.  Or, equivalently, in the context of sprinter's ages (#$LowAmountFn #$Time-Quantity) =   (#$YearsDuration 14 17).   ")
(comment relativeIntensityOfCondition "This predicate allows us to relativize a subject's
discomfort with respect to a particular symptom or ailment condition.
(#$relativeIntensityOfCondition COND BLO DIS-LEVEL) means that BLO has
the level of discomfort DIS-LEVEL as a result of
COND.  Note that (#$relativeIntensityOfCondition COND BLO DIS-LEVEL)
implies that the agent has the condition COND.")
(comment istMakesLikelihood "(#$istMakesLikelihood INDPROP DEPPROP PROB) means that the
truth of INDPROP in the context of the assertion makes the likelihood
that DEPROP is also true in the context of the assertion PROB.")
(comment JoinPathsIntoCycleFn "An instance of #$UnaryFunction.  When applied to a #$PathChain of the form (#$TheList POINT(1) PATH(1) ... POINT(n) PATH(n) POINT(n+1)) where the concatenation of all PATH(k)s results in a #$Path-Cyclic, #$JoinPathsIntoCycleFn returns as its value the #$Path-Cyclic obtained by that concatenation.  Note that #$JoinPathsIntoCycleFn is a partial function.  Note also that in order for (#$JoinPathsIntoCycleFn (#$TheList POINT(1) PATH(1) ... POINT(n) PATH(n) POINT(n+1))) to be defined, all PATH(k)s must be different instances of #$Path-Simple, and all POINT(k)s must be different, except POINT(1) = POINT(n+1).  Note, finally, that in a #$PathSystem, it is usually convenient to use nodes and links in the system as items in the list, as opposed to including non-node points along links.")
(comment wantsToRelnChange "`Change' here means change in cardinality.  (#$wantsToRelnChange AGT COL PRED GVP) means that AGT #$desires to be in the relation PRED with the amount suffested by GVP; more [#$highAmountOf] or fewer [#$lowAmountOf] instances of the collection COL.  PRED is a #$BinaryPredicate.")
(comment CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion "A specialization of both #$ActionOnObject and #$Movement-TranslationEvent.  In each instance of #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion, one object causes another object to undergo a translational motion.  The object causing the motion is related to the event by #$providerOfMotiveForce (q.v.), while the object which is caused to move is related by #$objectActedOn and #$objectMoving (qq.v.).  One way to cause another object's motion is to carry it along with oneself (see the specialization #$CarryingWhileLocomoting); other ways include throwing it, kicking it, or knocking it away.  Some instances  of #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion may also be instances of #$Translation-Complete (such as instances of #$CarryingWhileLocomoting), whereas others (such as instances of #$PumpingFluid) may be instances of #$FluidFlow-Translation.  Instances of #$CausingAnotherObjectsTranslationalMotion include a train transporting passengers, a person pushing a coin into a vending machine, the release of a bowstring which propels an arrow, and a magnet attracting a nail.")
(comment BaseballInning "#$BaseballInning is a specialization of #$Event-Organized and #$AthleticActivity.  Each instance of #$BaseballInning is a subevent of some instance of #$BaseballGame (q.v.), or of some attempt to complete an instance of #$BaseballGame.  In Major League Baseball a complete baseball game consists of nine innings, unless it is extended due to a tie score after the ninth, or shortened (1) because the home team needs none of its half of the ninth inning or only a fraction of it, or (2) because the umpire calls the game. (Note that National Association leagues may adopt a rule providing that one or both games of a doubleheader shall be seven innings in length. In such games, any of these rules applying to the ninth inning shall apply to the seventh inning.). If a game is called, it is a regulation game: (1) If five innings have been completed; (2) If the home team has scored more runs in four or four and a fraction half innings than the visiting team has scored in five completed half innings; (3) If the home team scores one or more runs in its half of the fifth inning to tie the score. (d) If each team has the same number of runs when the game ends, the umpire shall declare it a \"Tie Game.\" (e) If a game is called before it has become a regulation game, the umpire shall declare it \"No Game.\"  Each instance of #$BaseballInning consists of at least two instances of #$HalfInning (q.v). During each #$BaseballInning, each #$BaseballTeam takes its turn trying to score baseball runs.  A team's turn during an inning is called a #$HalfInning.  By tradition, between the two half innings of the seventh inning of a game, there occurs an instance of #$MassOrganizedStretch performed by the members of the game's audience.")
(comment helpfulActions "The predicate #$helpfulActions is used to indicate that an agent engaged in a particular effort would (normally) increase the chances of success in that effort by taking a certain role in events of a certain kind.  (#$helpfulActions ENDEAVOR SIT-TYPE ROLE DEGREE) means that the #$PurposefulAction ENDEAVOR would (normally) be helped along if its agent participated as described by ROLE in a situation of the type SIT-TYPE.  DEGREE is an instance of #$GenericValuePredicate used to suggest how helpful such an occurrence would be for succeeding in ENDEAVOR.  For example, for an agent trying to win in a football or soccer game, performing instances of #$InterceptingAPass contributes to a #$highToVeryHighAmountOf success in that game.")
(comment RelationAllExistsFn "An #$IndeterminateTermDenotingFunction (q.v.) that is closely related to #$relationAllExists.  If both (#$relationAllExists PRED INDEP-COL DEP-COL) and (#$isa INDEP-INS INDEP-COL) hold,  then (PRED INDEP-INS (#$RelationAllExistsFn INDEP-INS PRED INDEP-COL DEP-COL) also holds.  Thus the term '(#$RelationAllExistsFn INDEP-INS PRED INDEP-COL DEP-COL)' \"indeterminately denotes\" some instance of DEP-COL that is related to INDEP-INS by PRED.  For instance, since (#$relationAllExists #$citizens #$Country #$Person) and (#$isa #$Malaysia #$Country) both hold, so does (#$citizens #$Malaysia (#$RelationAllExistsFn #$Malaysia #$citizens #$Country #$Person)).")
(comment usefulActorAttribute "For the event Arg1, it is useful if any entry on Arg1's Arg2 slot has a value of Arg4 for its Arg3 slot.  Arg5 describes how useful.  (Note that if Arg5 is Low or #$veryLowAmountOf that does not just mean it is not useful, that means it is detrimental.)  For example:  (#$usefulActorAttribute Surgery #$objectActedOn constitutionLevel Strong #$highAmountOf) means its Highly useful for the #$objectActedOn in a Surgery event to have an Strong Constitution.")
(comment pathConcatenationOf-Simple "An instance of #$BinaryPredicate. (#$pathConcatenationOf-Simple CHAIN PATH) means that PATH is the #$Path-Simple obtained by 'path-concatenating' all of the instances of #$Path-Simple in the #$PathChain CHAIN. See also #$JoinPathsFn .")
(comment PurposefulActionFeature "A collection of collections.  Each instance of 
         #$PurposefulActionFeature is a collection of instances of #$PurposefulAction.  These collections can be used to meaningfully ascribe to purposeful actions various features; e.g. that they are successful or unsuccessful,
          well-planned or spontaneous, important or of no consequence, etc..")
(comment SuccessfulAction "The collection of purposeful actions that are considered \"successful\".  \"Success\" is a context dependent notion, but for the purposes of this constant can be thought to be relativized to the peformer of the action.  So, a purposeful action is an instance of this collection just in case the performer considered it successful given the reasons for (or the goals of) performing the action.")
(comment significantSubEvents "'(#$significantSubEvents RESULT-TYPE COMPONENT-TYPE PERF-QUANT-TYPE QUANTITY)' means that performing acts of type COMPONENT-TYPE with the quantity QUANTITY is required for the performance of RESULT-TYPE to have a high degree of PERF-QUANT-TYPE.  For example, '(#$significantSubEvents #$SpeedSkatingSportsEvent #$BodyMovementEvent #$Effectiveness (#$HighToVeryHighAmountFn #$Agility))' means that performing a speed skating sporting event with a high degree of effectiveness requires performing some body movement events with a high to very high amount of agility.")
(comment performanceLevel "This predicate relates performers to particular individual actions.  (#$performanceLevel OBJ EVT ROLE QUANT) means that the individual OBJ plays the role ROLE in the action EVT, and does so with the quantity indicated by QUANT.  Such an assertion expresses actual performance in a particular action; for example, (#$performanceLevel Joe DiggingHole54001 #$performedBy (#$LowAmountFn #$Strength)) means Joe exerted a low level of strength while digging that particular hole.  This does not imply much about Joe's potential to exert strength, about strength required in general for hole-digging, etc., it just talks about that one single event.  To talk about typical or expected performance, use #$skillLevel.")
(comment skillRequired "(#$skillRequired ACT-TYPE OTHER-TYPE PERF-LEVEL) means that if one is to successfully perform an instance of some kind of action (ACT-TYPE), then one must be capable of performing instances of another kind of action (OTHER-TYPE) with the performance attribute at a level at least equal to PERF-LEVEL .  For example, (#$skillRequired PlayingVolleyball ServingAVolleyball (#$LowAmountFn #$Competence)) holds just in case playing volleyball requires at least a low amount of competence in serving a volleyball.")
(comment DissidentGroup "The collection of groups of people which are openly opposed to some authority.  Since being a dissident is essentially a relationship, for any dissident group that relationship should be explicitly stated using #$hasDissidentStatusIn.  For example: (#$hasDissidentStatusIn #$CommitteeForDefenseOfLegitimateRights #$SaudiArabia).  Some instances of #$DissidentGroup will also be instances of #$Organizations, being instances of #$PoliticalOrganization, #$ReligiousOrganization, or both.  Some instances of #$DissidentGroup will not be instances of #$Organization.")
(comment TruckBomb-VehicleDelivered "A specialization of #$Bomb-RoadVehicleDelivered.  Each instance of #$TruckBomb-VehicleDelivered is a bomb contained in a truck.  Typically a truck containing a #$TruckBomb-VehicleDelivered is left near the intended target and detonated remotely or by a timer device.  Truck bombs are weapons with only terrorist applications.")
(comment Surveillance-InformationGatheringActivity "The collection of all information-gathering  activities in which the activities of an    agent or the activities in and around a place   are monitored with some regularity.  This   is a subtly different activity from     reconnaissance, which primarily involves     travelling to an area in order to gather    information about its usefulness as a     strategic resource, or travelling to an   enemy site to determine information about    the enemy that would prove strategic.  An example   of surveillance that is not reconnaissance:    a private eye covertly observing someone   through a window.  An example of  reconnaissance that is not surveillance:    that same private eye, earlier in the day,    looking around    the person's back yard for a    tree to climb, from which to get a good    view of the window.")
(comment MetersPerSecond "(#$MetersPerSecond NUMBER) is the rate or speed of NUMBER meters per second.  Notice that this result is not presently thought of as incorporating a vector, although it might be modified to do so at some point in the future if this should prove appropriate.")
(comment eyeColor "This predicate is used to state the eye-color of a human or other animal. (#$eyeColor ANIMAL COLOR) means that at least one of ANIMAL's eyes (specifically its irises, if it has them) has the color COLOR.  For example, (#$eyeColor #$AmyIrving #$PurpleColor) holds.  Since individual members of most species typically do not have eyes of different colors (Siamese cats being one exception), #$eyeColor behaves like a #$FunctionalSlot (q.v.) with respect to most, but not all, types of animals. See also #$HumanEyeColor.")
(comment HandGeometryScanner "#$HandGeometryScanner is a subset of #$BiometricAuthenticationDevice.  Individuals in the collection           #$HandGeometryScanner scan a streched hand and attempt to match the angles between fingers, the thicknesses of fingers, and the lengths of fingers with recorded representations of them.")
(comment monetaryUnitIssuedBy "(#$monetaryUnitIssuedBy UNIT GPE) means that
the #$UnitOfMoney UNIT is such that all currency representing it is issued by the #$GeopoliticalEntity GPE.  For example, (#$monetaryUnitIssuedBy #$Dinar-Bahrain #$Bahrain), (#$monetaryUnitIssuedBy #$Euro #$EuropeanUnion), (#$monetaryUnitIssuedBy #$MillionDollars #$UnitedStatesOfAmerica).")
(comment PhysicalEvent "A specialization of #$Event-Localized.  Each instance of #$PhysicalEvent is a spatially localized event involving one or more physical objects or stuffs.  #$PhysicalEvents typically involve interaction among #$PartiallyTangibles.  But note that a physical event might consist in the creation, destruction, movement, or a change in some physical feature of a single salient physical object.  (See #$PhysicalCreationEvent, #$PhysicalDestructionEvent, #$MovementEvent, and #$IntrinsicStateChangeEvent.)  For a contrasting (though not necessarily disjoint) collection, see #$StrictlyMentalEvent.  For events that have both physical and mental components, see the collection #$CompositePhysicalAndMentalEvent.")
(comment FixedArityFunction "A specialization of both  #$Function-Denotational and #$FixedArityRelation (qq.v.);  the collection of functions of fixed arity (see #$arity).  Each instance of #$FixedArityFunction is a function that  always takes a certain fixed number of arguments. Most  functions reified in the Cyc ontology are of fixed arity.  For example, #$GroupFn always takes a single argument and  #$BorderBetweenFn always takes two arguments. This  collection is disjoint with #$VariableArityFunction.")
(comment SlotTrendPredicate "Instances of #$SlotTrendPredicate are used to describe trends of some quantity. Some of them make explicit the cause of the trend.  Some make explicit the time period over which those trends occur.   #$SlotTrendPredicates, by definition, use the zeroth argument position to indicate the kind of change.  Net increases, decreases, or no net change are the only kinds of change currently (Feb '98) expressible with these constants.  For a net increase see predicates whose names begin with 'increase', for a net decrease see predicates whose names begin with 'decrease'.  For no net change see #$remainsStableImmediately.  See also #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates.  A negative exemplar of a #$SlotTrendPredicate is #$quantityChangeFunction.  Although this predicate is useful for representing trends in quantity changes, the kind of change occurring is referenced not by its zeroth argument but by its fourth argument (a specialization of #$Function-Denotational).")
(comment PathBlocked "A specialization of both #$ClosedObject  and #$Path-Customary.  Instances of this collection are paths that are blocked or closed, thus preventing any passage along it.")
(comment decreasesImmediatelyCausally "(#$decreasesImmediatelyCausally EVENT THING SLOT) means that the value for the predicate SLOT applied to THING (in the first argument position) is lower immediately after (#$STIF q.v.) EVENT than it was immediately before (#$STIB q.v.) EVENT.  In addition, it means EVENT is the cause of that decrease.  See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(comment TimePointDesignatingFunction "The collection of #$UnreifiableFunctions that serve to designate #$TimePoints.")
(comment increasesImmediatelyCausally "(#$increasesImmediatelyCausally EVENT THING SLOT) means that the value for the predicate SLOT applied to THING (in the first argument position) is greater immediately after (#$STIF q.v.) EVENT than it was immediately before (#$STIB q.v.) EVENT.  In addition, it means EVENT
is the cause of that increase.  For example, (#$increasesImmediatelyCausally HeatingEvent01 AirMass001 #$ambientTemperature) means that HeatingEvent01 immediately caused an increase in the ambient temprature of AirMass001.")
(disjointWith IsraeliPerson (CollectionDifferenceFn Tourist IsraeliPerson))
(comment MoneraKingdom "An instance of #$BiologicalKingdom, and a specialization of #$ProkaryoticCell.  Each instance of #$MoneraKingdom is a one-celled prokaryotic organism (so each instance lacks a nuclear membrane, as well as other internal organelles).  Specializations of #$MoneraKingdom include #$Bacterium, #$PseudomonasMallei, and #$EscherichiaColi.")
(comment promotesRisk "(#$promotesRisk EVENT AGENT RESULT-SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that if (#$doneBy EVENT AGENT), then EVENT contributes to AGENT being at risk for playing the role ROLE in a situation of type RESULT-SIT-TYPE as a result.  This predicate is intended to be used to express long-term risks, like getting cancer from smoking. See also #$immediateRisk for risks that would occur during the event rather than at some later time.")
(comment immediateRisk "(#$immediateRisk EVENT AGENT RESULT-SIT-TYPE ROLE) means that if (#$doneBy EVENT AGENT), then EVENT contributes to AGENT being at immediate risk for playing the role ROLE in a situation of type SIT-TYPE as a result.  See also #$promotesRisk for less immediate risks, like getting cancer.")
(comment doneViaDoing "This predicate relates two events #$doneBy the same agent such that s/he does the first by virtue of doing the  second.  (#$doneViaDoing EVENT1 EVENT2) means that some agent  fills the #$doneBy actor slot (or a specialization thereof)  with respect to EVENT2 and thereby fills the #$doneBy actor slot  (or a specialization thereof) with respect to EVENT1.  This can happen in at least three different ways.  (1) EVENT2 might  cause EVENT1.  For example, the statement \"John offended Peter  by dressing like Peter's mother\" could be true because of John's  doing a certain act of impersonation that causes an event of  Peter's being offended by John.  (2) EVENT2 might be a proper  subevent of EVENT1.  For example, the statement \"By pressing the  button, the President destroyed Moscow\" could be true and the  button-pressing itself a subevent of the destroying.  (3) EVENT1  and EVENT2 might actually be the _same_ event under different  descriptions, such that \"EVENT1\" is stated to be an instance  of a certain subcollection EVENTTYPE1 of #$Event and \"EVENT2\"  is stated to be an instance of a different (but not disjoint)  subcollection EVENTTYPE2 of #$Event.  EVENTTYPE1 will normally  be a \"broader\" collection that EVENTTYPE2; EVENTTYPE2 might  even be a subcollection of EVENTTYPE1.  For example, the statement  \"Joni communicated by talking\" could be true due to Joni's  performing a #$Talking event that is also a #$Communicating event.   (Although #$Talking is not a proper subcollection of #$Communicating  -- think of talking to oneself -- the latter is \"broader\" than the  former in that talking normally amounts to communicating, and is  but one of many standard ways of communicating.)  #$doneViaDoing is  indeterminate with respect to the distinctions among cases (1) -   (3) above; thus one may assert (#$doneViaDoing EVENT1 EVENT2) without settling the question as to whether EVENT2 causes, is a  subevent of, or is identical with EVENT1.")
(comment decreasesCausallyOverPeriod "(#$decreasesCausallyOverPeriod EVENT THING SLOT PERIOD) means that EVENT causes the value of the predicate SLOT applied to THING to be lower immediately after (#$STIF q.v.)  PERIOD than it was immediately before (#$STIB q.v.) PERIOD.  PERIOD must start no earlier than EVENT starts in order to prevent effects preceeding their causes.  If PERIOD ends before EVENT, it still must be the case that the value of SLOT applied to THING must be lower immediately following EVENT than it was immediately before EVENT.  Like with #$decreasesImmediately, the decrease need not be monotonic.  This predicate is agnostic as to whether the decrease occurs during EVENT or after it.  See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(comment increasesCausallyOverPeriod "(#$increasesCausallyOverPeriod EVENT THING SLOT PERIOD) means that EVENT causes the value of the predicate SLOT applied to THING to be greater immediately after (#$STIF q.v.)  PERIOD than it was immediately before (#$STIB q.v.) PERIOD.  PERIOD must start no earlier than EVENT starts in order to prevent effects preceeding their causes. If PERIOD ends before EVENT, it still must be the case that the value of SLOT applied to THING must be greater immediately following EVENT than it was immediately before EVENT.  Like with #$increasesImmediately, the increase need not be monotonic.  This predicate is agnostic as to whether the increase occurs during EVENT or after it.  See #$NoteAboutQuantityChangePredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(disjointWith Fin Limb-AnimalBodyPart)
(disjointWith Hand Fin)
(disjointWith (CitizenFn SriLanka) (CollectionDifferenceFn Person (CitizenFn SriLanka)))
(comment AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService "#$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService  is the collection of all instances of #$AttackByComputerOperation where the objective of the attack is to degrade the service of an instance of #$Computer.  Specializations of #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService include both #$AttackByComputerOperation-DataFlooding and  #$AttackByComputerOperation-OSCrashing.  Computers are vulnerable to #$AttackByComputerOperation-DenialOfService if they have the attribute #$VulnerableToDenialOfService.")
(comment Acre "An instance of #$UnitOfArea and #$FPSUnitOfMeasure, equal to 4,840 #$SquareYards.")
(comment Ampere "An instance of #$SIUnitOfMeasure-Base.  #$Ampere is the standard unit of #$ElectricalCurrentLevel, equivalent to a 1-#$Coulomb flow of current, or 1 #$Volt across a resistance of 1 #$Ohm.")
(comment InterAgentSupportQuantity "The collection of quantities that represent/measure the kind of support that one agent gives to another agent.  See also #$givesSupportToAgent.")
(comment CycLExpression-Assertible "A #$CycLExpressionType.  The collection  of all compound CycL expressions that either could themselves be asserted to the  Cyc Knowledge Base (see #$CycLSentence-Assertible) or could appear as denotational terms within sentences that could be so asserted (see #$CycLDenotationalTerm-Assertible).  More precisely, each instance of #$CycLExpression-Assertible is a CycL expression that is both syntactically and semantically well-formed.  By definition, any compound CycL expression is  syntactically well-formed.  To be semantically well-formed, a CycL expression  must be constructible via the syntax of CycL without violating any applicable arity or argument-type constraints (see #$arity and #$ArgTypePredicate).  A CycL expression must be semantically well-formed in order to be interpretable as having a \"semantic value\", such as a truth-value (if the expression is a sentence) or a denotation (if it's a #$CycLDenotationalTerm).  Note that being \"assertible\" in the present sense does not require an expression's actually being asserted in (or being a component of something asserted in) the KB.")
(comment PhysicalDBTable "Instances are particular tables that are part of some
#$Database-Physical.  Even if two #$PhysicalDBTables have the same physical schema and the same
information content, they are considered different tables if they have different 
access parameters.")
(comment useReformulationRuleForPredicateStrengthening "(#$useReformulationRuleForPredicateStrengthening RULE) indicates
that RULE is to be used for the purpose of replacing predicates in the input formula with more specialized ones (in the sense of #$typedGenlPreds).")
(comment Redirect-FirewallTarget "A #$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget.  If a firewall program F is configured on a machine M to assign #$Redirect-FirewallTarget to packets of type T, packets of type T that reach M are sent to a local port instead of wherever they were heading. This attibute can be assigned only to packets that conform  to #$TransmissionControlProtocol or #$UserDatagramProtocol. ")
(comment Model-Artifact "A collection of artifacts; a subset of #$VisualInformationBearingThing.  Each element of #$Model-Artifact is a tangible object designed to resemble and/or represent some other object, which may or may not exist tangibly.  For example, an architectural model for a proposed public building; a souvenir model of #$TheWhiteHouse; a scale model of a dinosaur skeleton; a miniature room and furnishings copying a real house.  The function, #$ModelFn, is used to designate the collection of models of a collection of objects.")
(comment BacteriumOfTypeInCultureFn "#$BacteriumOfTypeInCultureFn is a Cyc function that takes an instance of #$BiologicalSpecies and returns the collection of #$Bacterium grown with those cells.  Thus, (#$BacteriumOfTypeInCultureFn #$Anthrax-Bacterium) denotes the collection of #$Anthrax-Bacterium grown in culture.  Note this function denotes the objects created by the set of events.  See also #$CulturedGrowthFn for the function that denotes the set of events in which a culture is grown.")
(comment Masquerade-FirewallTarget "A #$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget that may apply only to outgoing packets.  If a firewall program F is configured on a machine M to assign #$Masquerade-FirewallTarget to packets of type T, packets of type T are forwarded by M with the IP address of M instead of the IP address of the originating machine.")
(comment TVMiniseries "A subset of #$TVSeriesProduct; each instance of #$TVMiniseries is a #$TVSeriesProduct broken into a series of (temporally) separate episodes that together tell a single story.")
(comment TornadoAsObject "A specialization of #$CycloneAsObject.  Each instance of #$TornadoAsObject is a tornado object (i.e., a swirling high-speed weather object).  See also #$TornadoAsEvent, for the collection of events in which a tornado object cuts a path through space and time.")
(comment Accept-FirewallTarget "A #$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget.  If a firewall program F is configured on a machine M to assign #$Accept-FirewallTarget to packets of type T, packets of type T that reach M are simply forwarded by M according to the protocol to which packets of type T conform.")
(comment Deny-FirewallTarget "A #$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget.  If a firewall program F is configured on a machine M to assign #$Deny-FirewallTarget to packets of type T, packets of type T that reach M are discarded as though M had never received them (though some log may be kept).")
(comment Reject-FirewallTarget "A #$FirewallTypeByPacketTarget, and a specialization of #$Deny-FirewallTarget.  If a firewall program F is configured on a machine M to assign #$Reject-FirewallTarget to packets of type T, packets of type T that reach M are discarded and the machine that sent them is notified.")
(comment LocallyExploitableFn "(#$hasVulnerability COMPUTER (#$LocallyExploitableFn VULNERABILITY)) means that COMPUTER is an instance of the #$ComputerTypeByVulnerability VULNERABILITY and, furthermore, this vulnerability is due to the presence of a faulty #$LocalProgram on COMPUTER.  Only users who are logged in on COMPUTER may directly exploit this kind of vulnerability.  For example, (#$hasVulnerability #$Crystal-Cyc-Com (#$LocallyExploitableFn #$VulnerableToOSCrashing)) means that a savvy hacker or incautious user who was logged in on #$Crystal-Cyc-Com could cause the #$OperatingSystem to crash.")
(comment RemotelyExploitableFn "(#$hasVulnerability COMPUTER (#$RemotelyExploitableFn VULNERABILITY)) means that COMPUTER is an instance of the #$ComputerTypeByVulnerability VULNERABILITY and, furthermore, this vulnerability is due to the presence of a faulty #$ServerProgram on COMPUTER.  This vulnerability therefore may be directly exploited by a remote attacker (i.e., one who is not logged in on COMPUTER).  For example, (#$hasVulnerability #$Crystal-Cyc-Com (#$RemotelyExploitableFn #$VulnerableToOSCrashing)) means that a savvy remote hacker could crash the #$OperatingSystem running on #$Crystal-Cyc-Com.")
(comment ProtectionGoal "An instance of #$Goal. This attribute characterizes relationships between Cyc formulas and agents when the formula depicts a state of affairs that the agent seeks to actualize in order to protect some one or thing from harm.")
(comment CalligraphyWriting "The collection of writing events of producing a
#$Calligraphy-ArtObject")
(comment preservesRelnInArg "(#$preservesRelnInArg FN BIN-PRED N) means that if NAT1 and NAT2 are non-atomic terms generated by means of FN, and (BINPRED ARG1 ARG2) is known to be true, and ARG1 appears as the Nth argument of NAT1 and ARG2 appears as then Nth argument of NAT2, then (BIN-PRED NAT1 NAT2).")
(comment AviationUnit-MilitarySpecialty "The collection of instances of #$ModernMilitaryUnit-Deployable that rely on the use of #$MilitaryAircraft for closing with and engaging the enemy. Instances of #$AviationUnit-MilitarySpecialty include attack, reconnaissance and transport units.")
(comment VariableArityRelation "A specialization of #$Relation.  Each instance of #$VariableArityRelation is a relation that can take a variable number of arguments. The degree of variability for a given such relation can be constrained using the predicates #$arityMin and #$arityMax. Examples of #$VariableArityRelations include the predicate #$different and the function #$PlusFn.  Thus the terms '(#$PlusFn 1 2)' and '(#$PlusFn 1 2 3)' are both well-formed. Cf. #$FixedArityRelation.")
(comment VulnerableThing "The most general collection of vulnerable things.  A thing is an instance of #$VulnerableThing if it is vulnerable to any threat whatsoever.  Whenever possible, a more specific collection should be used.")
(comment AnnouncingSomething "The public statement of something believed to be factual (therefore, it is disjoint with #$StoryTelling). It can be written or spoken, but is almost always verbal, not visual.  Announcing is a #$Communicating, since there are receiving agents.")
(comment ThingTypeByCapability-Passive "Each instance of #$ThingTypeByCapability-Passive is a collection of things with a certain passive capacity.  Instances of this collection represent a capability something has that enables it to play the role #$objectActedOn in certain events.")
(comment faultVulnerability-Remote "(#$faultVulnerability-Remote FAULT VULN) means that a #$ServerProgram with #$SoftwareObjectTypeByFault FAULT will lead to the existence of #$ComputerVulnerability VULN on a #$Computer on which that #$ServerProgram is running.")
(comment RAM "Random access memory. Cf. #$rAMSize.")
(comment faultVulnerability "(#$faultVulnerability FAULT VULN) means that #$SoftwareObjectTypeByFault FAULT creates #$ComputerVulnerability VULN under some circumstance. This predicate is not assertible due to this vagueness. All assertions should be made using a more specialized predicate.")
(comment faultVulnerability-OS "(#$faultVulnerability-OS FAULT VULN) means that an #$OperatingSystem with the #$SoftwareObjectTypeByFault FAULT will lead to the existence of the vulnerability VULN on computers on which it is installed.")
(comment faultVulnerability-Local "(#$faultVulnerability-Local FAULT VULN) means that #$LocalPrograms with #$SoftwareObjectTypeByFault FAULT lead to the existence of #$ComputerTypeByVulnerability-Local VULN on #$Computers on which the program is either installed or is running. This predicate is not assertible because of this vagueness. All assertions should be made using a specPred.")
(comment faultVulnerability-Installed "(#$faultVulnerability-Installed FAULT VULN) means that the installation of a #$LocalProgram with #$SoftwareObjectTypeByFault FAULT will lead to the existence of the #$ComputerVulnerability VULN on the #$Computer on which that #$LocalProgram is installed.")
(comment EnvironmentVariableFaultFn "(#$faultOfSoftwareObject-ReportIndexed (#$EnvironmentVariableFaultFn ENVIRON_VARIABLE) PROGRAM REPORT) means that according to REPORT, PROGRAM, when executed, runs with a significant level of privilege and takes the value of the #$EnvironmentVariable ENVIRON_VARIABLE as one of its inputs.  Faults of this kind can lead to a user's executing commands at a higher level of privilege than she ought to be able to.")
(comment Extremist "The collection of persons with extreme political, social, or religious views.")
(comment UserAccountFn "(#$UserAccountFn ACCOUNT_SYSTEM ID) denotes the #$UserAccount on ACCOUNT_SYSTEM (#$userAccountForSystem, q.v.) which is uniquely identified by the number ID.  For example, (#$UserAccountFn #$CycorpLANAccountSystem-Unix \"321\") denotes user account no. 321  on the Cycorp Unix #$AccountSystem. For account usernames, see #$accountName. User accounts for individual machines are covered by this function, since individual machines are also account systems.")
(comment FlowTerrain "A collection of topographical features.  Each element of #$FlowTerrain is a topographical region marked by the product of flowing matter, such as a volcanic flow.")
(comment WavePropagation "A specialization of #$Translocation (q.v.).  Each instance of #$WavePropagation is an event in which a wavelike disturbance propagates through space, with or without a medium.  A wave propagation is like  a translational movement (see #$Movement-TranslationEvent) in that it can have both a starting and an ending point (see #$fromLocation and #$toLocation), but differs from a translational motion in that there is no object moving (see #$objectMoving).  Notable specializations of #$WavePropagation include #$ElectromagneticRadiation and #$Sound.")
(comment PortScan "A specialization of #$PacketScanningAComputationalSystem. #$PortScan is the collection of all scans to determine which ports are open on a given machine or network, as performed by a #$PortScanningProgram.")
(comment ProbingAComputerNetwork "The collection of all activities of gathering information concerning the accessibility of a network by means of attempts to gain access that network.")
(comment informationArtifactAuthor "(#$informationArtifactAuthor INFO-ARTIFACT AUTHOR) means that AUTHOR is the creator of the #$InformationStore and #$Artifact-Generic INFO-ARTIFACT.")
(comment Cell-Organization "An instance of #$OrganizationTypeByStructuralCharacteristic, and a specialization of #$OrganizationOfPeopleOnly. Each instance of #$Cell-Organization is a sub-organization of some larger organization, where the larger organization is divided into many instances of #$Cell-Organization. Each instance of #$Cell-Organization is a small group of people who perform a set of tasks for the larger organization to which the cell belongs. Each cell within the larger organization is relatively isolated from all the other cells in that organization, so that members of one cell will generally not know members of the other cells, nor will they generally know what the other cells are doing for the larger organization. Organizations that structure themselves into cells usually do so because they wish to conceal their activities, and the extent of their membership, from others (so organizations that structure themselves into cells will usually be instances of #$CovertAgent, such as intelligence groups, criminal organizations, or terrorist groups). By organizing itself into independent cells, an organization ensures that its members will be able to divulge the identities and activities of only a few other members of that organization, if those members defect from the organization, or if they are captured by some agent interested in knowing about the organization's activities.")
(comment precedesInGraphicalStructure "(#$precedesInGraphicalStructure WHOLE PART1 PART2) means that, within the #$GraphicalStructure WHOLE, the #$GraphicalStructure PART1 comes before the #$GraphicalStructure PART2.  There are certain types of #$GraphicalStructure that always precede certain other types of #$GraphicalStructure within an inclusive #$GraphicalStructure.  For example, within a #$CWStructure, an instance of #$TableOfContents always #$precedesInGraphicalStructure an instance of #$TextString that it is an #$alphabeticalIndexTo.")
(comment divisionOfGraphicalStructure "(#$divisionOfGraphicalStructure STRUCTURE DIVISION) means that the #$GraphicalStructure DIVISION is one of the #$subStructures of the #$GraphicalStructure STRUCTURE.  DIVISION is not any arbitrarily selected sub-structure of STRUCTURE, however, but a coherent, self-contained division of STRUCTURE according to some existing convention or standard of practice.  In most contexts, chapters, sections, and subsections are regarded as divisions.  In various text classification systems, other parts of a document structure may be considered divisions.")
(comment highestDivisionOfGraphicalStructure "(#$highestDivisionOfGraphicalStructure STRUCTURE DIVISION) means that the #$GraphicalStructure DIVISION is at the highest level of division within the #$GraphicalStructure STRUCTURE.  Each DIVISION is a division of a #$GraphicalStructure according to some convention or standard practice (see #$divisionOfGraphicalStructure).  For example, if (#$highestDivisionOfGraphicalStructure CWSTRUCTURE DIVISION) is true, then there is no division of CWSTRUCTURE of which DIVISION is one of its #$subStructures.")
(comment hasHeading-TextString "'(#$hasHeading-TextString STRUCTURE HEADING) means that the #$GraphicalStructure STRUCTURE has the heading and is identified and named by the #$TextString HEADING.")
(comment textStringIsReferenceTypeInWork "(#$textStringIsReferenceTypeInWork WORK TEXT REFTYPE) means that the #$TextString TEXT, which is a reference to something external to WORK (see #$referenceInWorkTo), has the function or purpose characterized by REFTYPE, a instance of #$TextStringTypeByReferenceType.  For example, a #$TextString in a #$BookCopy that attributes a particular photograph reproduced in the #$BookCopy to an individual photographer would be an instance of  #$AttributiveReference.")
(comment CombineFn "A ternary #$FunctionDenotingFunction that \"combines\" (in a particular way) two unary functions and one binary (or variable-arity) function into one unary function.  (#$CombineFn BINARYFN UNARYFN1 UNARYFN2) is the unary  function COMB that maps a given argument ARG to a particular thing VALUE if and only if VALUE is the result of first applying both UNARYFN1 and UNARYFN2 to ARG, and then applying BINARYFN to the two results thus obtained.  Symbolically: (COMB ARG) = (BINARYFN (UNARYFN1 ARG) (UNARYFN2 ARG)).  The argument-constraints on UNARYFN1 and UNARYFN2 must not be disjoint, and their respective result-constraints must fall within BINARYFN's arg1 and arg2 constraints.  For example, (#$CombineFn #$PlusFn #$SquaredFn #$MinusFn) denotes the function that maps a given real number NUM to the result of subtracting NUM from its own square (e.g. it maps 5 to 20).  Cf. #$FunctionCompositionFn.")
(comment slotDefinition "#$slotDefinition(S F(X)) defines slot S as being equivalent to function F(X).  In other words, when given a unit U, the value on U.S = F(U).  So, for example, (#$slotDefinition #$physicalMemorySize (#$CombineFn #$PlusFn #$rAMSize #$rOMSize)).")
(comment slotDefinitionWRTObject "A contextual version of #$slotDefinition;  (#$slotDefinitionWRTObject OBJ SLOT FUNC) states that FUNC is the #$slotDefinition of SLOT just for object OBJ, i.e. (SLOT OBJ (FUNC OBJ)) holds.  Also, (#$slotDefinitionWRTObject OBJ SLOT FUNC) can be considered shorthand for (#$numericFluentValue OBJ (#$CombineFn #$QuotientFn SLOT FUNC) 1).  See also the similar predicate #$slotDefinition.")
(comment AtomicSymbol-Abstract "A specialization of #$AbstractInformationStructure (q.v.).  This is the collection of all abstract symbols that are not composed of further symbols.  By 'abstract symbol' we mean any abstract object whose concrete instantiations have meaning, broadly construed, according to some convention.  For example, the Roman letter 'A' is an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract, whereas concrete instantiations of it (see #$CharacterToken) are not.  The character string 'ABC' is not an #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract, because it is composed of more than one symbol.  An arbitrary #$AbstractStructure (such as the abstract structure of carbon dioxide) is not #$AtomicSymbol-Abstract unless its instantiations have a meaning, according to some convention.  Other examples include all instances of #$Character-Abstract, punctuation marks, words (but not their corresponding character strings), symbols of diagram types (e.g. the symbols used in schematic diagrams for electrical curcuits), and abstract individual sound structures (see e.g #$Phoneme).")
(comment partialInfoStructureOfCW "(#$partialInfoStructureOfCW WORK STRUCTURE) means that an #$AbstractStructure of WORK contains the information structure STRUCTURE. For example, #$MobyDickNovel (an instance of #$PropositionalConceptualWork) has as partial information structures the #$AbstractInformationStructure \"fish\" (used in English versions) and \"poisson\" (used in French versions), as well as the entire abstract sequences of characters that were used in the writing of any edition of #$MobyDickNovel. This predicate allows us to refer to information structures used in a particular work without reference to any instantiation of that work.")
(disjointWith GraphicalStructure Phoneme)
(comment Graph-AIS "The collection of all instances of #$GraphicalStructure that are graphs.")
(comment ProgramFunctionFn "This function is used to denote the particular instances of those functions which are found in programs. For example,  (#$ProgramFunctionFn \"abs\" (#$FileOnFn #$Beret-Cyc-Com \"abs.c\")) denotes the function \"int abs(int x)\" in the a C source file \"abs.c\" stored on  #$Beret-Cyc-Com.")
(comment List "A specialization of #$Tuple.  Each instance of #$List is a  finite sequence of things with a first and last member-position, with each member-position other than the last having a successor member-position.   As with tuples generally, lists allow for repetition of their members, so that the same item can appear at multiple member-positions in the same list.  A list can be represented formally as a function from a finite index set of counting numbers, beginning with one, into the domain of all #$Things (but note that #$Lists are _not_ explicitly represented as functions in the Cyc ontology).  Unlike an instance of #$Series (q.v.), a list is purely abstract (i.e. both aspatial and atemporal), and the only implied relation between an item and its successor in a list is the successor relation of the list itself.  Technically, #$List is more specific than #$Tuple only in that the index set (see #$tupleIndexSet) for a given list must be the counting numbers in their usual order (or some initial segment thereof), whereas the index set for a tuple, generally speaking, might be any set whatsoever.")
(comment PositionsOfSublistInListFn "An instance of both #$BinaryFunction and #$EvaluatableFunction.  When applied to two lists, LIST1 and LIST2, #$PositionsOfSublistInListFn finds every occurrence of LIST1 as a sublist of LIST2, and returns a list of all the positions in LIST2 (i.e. a list of #$PositiveIntegers) where a copy of LIST1 starts. For any instances LIST1 and LIST2 of #$List, (#$PositionsOfSublistInListFn LIST1 LIST2) is the list LIST* of #$PositiveIntegers defined below.  Let L be the length of LIST1.  The first member of LIST*, if there is any, is the smallest positive integer N1 such that LIST1 = (#$SublistFromToFn LIST2 N1 N1+L).  The second member of LIST*, if there is any, is the second smallest positive integer N2 such that LIST1 = (#$SublistFromToFn LIST2 N2 N2+L).  ...  The last member of LIST* is the greatest positive integer N such that LIST1 = (#$SublistFromToFn LIST2 N N+L).  Note that if LIST1 is not a sublist of LIST2 or LIST2 is #$TheEmptyList, then (#$PositionsOfSublistInListFn LIST1 LIST2) is #$TheEmptyList.  Note also that if LIST1 is #$TheEmptyList while LIST2 is not, then (#$PositionsOfSublistInListFn LIST1 LIST2) returns a list of _all_ the positions in LIST2 (e.g. if LIST2 = (#$TheList A B C), (#$PositionsOfSublistInListFn #$TheEmptyList LIST2) = (#$TheList 1 2 3)).")
(comment PositionOfItemInListFn "A binary #$ScalarDenotingFunction that takes a non-repeating list and any one of its members to the position of the latter within the former.  Where ITEM is a member (see #$memberOfList) of the #$ListWithoutRepetition LIST, (#$PositionOfItemInListFn ITEM LIST) is the integer corresponding to the position of ITEM in LIST (starting from 1).  For example, (#$PositionOfItemInListFn George (#$TheList John Paul George Ringo)) is 3.  Note that if ITEM were _not_ a member of LIST, then an expression of the form (#$PositionOfItemInListFn ITEM LIST) would not semantically well-formed; see the #$interArgReln assertion on the function.  Also note that ITEM cannot appear more than once in LIST, as the latter is constrained to be a #$ListWithoutRepetition.  See also #$PositionsOfSublistInListFn.")
(comment Isomorphism "A subcollection of #$Function-Denotational.  A function is an instance of #$Isomorphism if and only if it is a homomorphism that is a #$OneToOneFunction and whose inverse (see #$inverseFunctions) is also a homomorphism.  A homomorphism is a structure-preserving mapping from one structure to another.  A structure consists of a domain of ojects together with a function specifying interpretations, with respect to that domain, of the relation symbols, function symbols, and individual symbols of given language.")
(comment MassEMailCommunication "A specialization of #$EMailCommunication.  Each instance of #$MassEMailCommunication is an event in which an email message is successfully sent, and then later received by dozens to thousands of recipients.  Thus every instance of #$MassEMailCommunication has as sub-events both an instance of #$MassEMailSending and many instances of #$EMailReceiving.  Compare this collection with #$SingleEMailCommunication.")
(comment SkilledActivityType "This is the collection of collections of activities which require some specialized skill to perform--i.e., to play any role which is a specPred of #$doneBy.  So, all skilled activities are learned, but not all learned activities are skilled.  For instance, #$WalkingOnTwoLegs is an instance of #$LearnedActivityType but not an instance of #$SkilledActivityType.  Since every normal person learns to walk, it requires no special skill.  In contrast, #$Juggling is an instance of #$SkilledActivityType, for most people do not know how to juggle.")
(comment causes-SitSit "(#$causes-SitSit CAUSE EFFECT)  says that the situation CAUSE caused the situation EFFECT.    See #$NoteAboutCausationPredicates for a map of related predicates.")
(comment VernalEquinoxDay "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an instance of #$AnnualTemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$VernalEquinoxDay is a calendar-day during which the sun crosses the equator, making daytime (see #$DaytimeHours) and nighttime (see #$Night) of equal duration on all parts of the earth, but where daytimes are lengthening and nighttimes shortening in the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region.  A vernal equinox occurs about March 21 each year and marks the end of the #$CalendarWinter and beginning of the #$CalendarSpring in the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region, and the end of #$CalendarSummer and the beginning of #$CalendarAutumn in the #$SouthernHemisphere-Region.")
(comment AutumnalEquinoxDay "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an instance of #$AnnualTemporalObjectType.  Each instance of #$AutumnalEquinoxDay is a calendar-day during which the sun crosses the equator from north to south, making daytime (see #$DaytimeHours) and nighttime (see #$Night) of equal duration on all parts of the earth, but where daytimes are shortening and nighttimes lengthening in the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region.  An autumnal equinox marks the beginning of the #$CalendarAutumn in the #$NorthernHemisphere-Region and the beginning of #$CalendarSpring in the #$SouthernHemisphere-Region.  Instances occur about September 22 of each year.")
(comment RegionalGovernment "A specialization of #$LegalGovernmentOrganization.  Each instance of #$RegionalGovernment is a government organization that controls a particular geopolitical region (e.g. a country, state, city, or county).  Governmental organizations focused on a single type of control, e.g., a border patrol, are not instances of this collection.  Specializations of #$RegionalGovernment include #$CountyGovernment and #$GovernmentOfCountry.")
(comment ResourcePredicate "#$ResourcePredicate is an instance of #$PredicateTypeByTopic.  It is the collection of predicates that state of some individual or collection THING what its resource requirements are, or what resources it has available to it.")
(comment EMailMailingListCommunication "A specialization of #$EMailCommunication.  Each instance of #$EMailMailingListCommunication is an event in which an email message is successfully sent to a central list manager, and then is forwarded by the list manager to those who are members of the list.")
(comment Thursday "A collection of #$CalendarDays and an  instance of #$DayOfWeekType.  #$Thursday is the collection of all  (and only) thursdays.")
(comment HighlighterPen "The collection highlighters. These are a specific kind of #$Marker-WritingImplement with a wide tip and ink which is transparent and in very bright colors. The intended purpose of a highlighter is not writing but highlighting passages by running the pen over them. One can, of course, also write with it.")
(comment CycLSentence-Askable "The collection of #$CycLSentences that are askable as queries to the Cyc system.  More precisely, each  instance of #$CycLSentence-Askable is a CycL sentence that is  constructible via the syntax of CycL without violating any applicable  arity constraints (see #$arity).  Note that askable CycL sentences do  not necessarily obey other semantic constraints beyond arity, such as  argument-type constraints (see #$ArgTypePredicate); thus they are  not always semantically well-formed in the fullest sense (cf.  #$CycLSentence-Assertible).  The idea behind this criterion of  \"askability\" is that such a sentence, even if it isn't true or false (which it can't be unless it also obeys all argument-type  constraints), at least \"makes enough sense\" to be asked as a query  to the Cyc system.")
(comment InternationalTerritorialDispute "A collection of events, a subset of #$ConflictEvent and #$InternationalConflict. In each instance, there are at least two instances of #$Country, who both claim legal control over some place, in such a way that their claims come into conflict. The dispute between the #$UnitedKingdomOfGreatBritainAndNorthernIreland and #$Argentina over who controlled the #$FalklandIslands would be an instance.  While both the #$CityOfAustinTX and #$Texas-State claiming control over parts of Travis County would not, since the claims are not in conflict and the dispute is not at the international level.")
(comment MassEMailSending "A specialization of #$EMailSending. Each instance of this collection is an event in which somebody or something sends copies of an #$EMailMessage to many -- dozens to thousands -- of #$EMailAddresses. Cf. #$MassEMailCommunication.")
(comment SubstituteFromListFn "(#$SubstituteFromListFn EXP (#$TheList (#$TheList NEW1 OLD1) ... (#$TheList NEWN OLDN))) returns a #$CycLFormula which is derived from EXP by substituting NEW1 for OLD1, NEW2 for OLD2, and so on for each pair that is an element of the second argument.")
(comment BindingList "A special type of #$List containing #$Lists as elements.  In a #$BindingList, the list elements are lists which are all exactly two elements long.  Each pair represents a binding, in which the first element can be substituted for the second element.")
(comment frontLineOfTroops "(#$frontLineOfTroops MILITARYFORCE
LINE) means that the ModernMilitaryOrganization MILITARYFORCE has
deployed troops in a Battle, a campaign, or in a defensive position,
and those troops have an outermost line LINE in which troops are
located at the edge of the maximal area controlled by
MILITARYFORCE. The LINE has a geographical location determined by
those maximally forward troops. The front line of one force may
coincide with or overlap the enemy's front line, or there may be a
'no-man's land' area separating them. It is not necessary that every
force deployment have a #$frontLineOfTroops. In certain formations,
especially in high-speed, cavalry, guerilla or commando operations,
there is often no identifiable zone that could be called the
#$frontLineOfTroops of the force.")
(comment LineOfMilitaryForces "A collection of individual line-like
terrain objects.  Each #$LineOfMilitaryForces is a
#$TacticalLine determined by the deployment or position of a
group of military units, vessels or installations. The line is longer
than it is wide, may be curved or straight, and may be either a rank
or file or other linear formation. It may be the front line of troops
of some military force (the forward edge of the main force -- see
#$frontLineOfTroops). It may be a linear flotilla of ships, a convoy
arrangement, or a closed perimeter.")
(disjointWith Person ConsumableProduct)
(comment argsIsa "A binary #$ArgIsaPredicate (q.v.) that is used to put a specified #$isa based argument-type constraint on all of a given relation's argument-places at once.  (#$argsIsa RELN COL) means that semantic well-formedness requires that each argument to which RELN is applied (regardless of argument-place) be an instance of COL.  For example, '(#$argsIsa #$PlusFn #$ScalarInterval)' means that the function #$PlusFn must only be applied to scalar intervals.   #$argsIsa is particularly useful for constraining (any and all of) the arguments to a #$VariableArityRelation (the preceding example being a case in point); though #$argsIsa may be applied to fixed-arity relations as well.  For an explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its immediate specializations.  See also #$argsGenl.")
(comment MKSUnitOfMeasure "A specialization of #$SIUnitOfMeasure and an instance of #$UnitOfMeasureTypeBySystem-Coherent.  Each instance of #$MKSUnitOfMeasure is a #$UnitOfMeasure which is part of the MKS system of measurement.  As its name suggests, MKS has three base units (see #$MKSUnitOfMeasure-Base): #$Meter, #$Kilogram, and #$SecondsDuration.  Derived units are those that can be defined algebraically from the base units or obtained by adding a #$MetricUnitPrefix to a non-prefixed MKS unit. Some instances of #$MKSUnitOfMeasure are #$CubicMeter, #$Joule, and #$KiloWatt.  Some notable non-instances are #$MetricTon, #$HoursDuration, and #$Liter.")
(comment ParaphraseDataMicrotheory "The collection of all microtheories containing assertions that specify a way to paraphrase an individual CycL expression or type of CycL expression. The body of assertions visible from a given
#$ParaphraseDataMicrotheory constitutes a theory for paraphrasing CycL
within certain parameters, such as a single natural language or
a specific application.")
(comment TimeOfDay-AM "A specialization of #$TimeOfDay.  Each instance of #$TimeOfDay-AM is the smallest (continuous) time interval including the first second (minute/hour) after midnight and the last second (minute/hour) before noon on a particular calendar day (see the collection #$CalendarDay).")
(disjointWith Water LandStuff)
(disjointWith PhysicalDevice GeopoliticalRegion)
(disjointWith GeographicalHemisphere Artifact-Generic)
(disjointWith PhysicalDevice TimeZone)
(comment CalendarSeason "A specialization of #$Date and an instance of #$CalendarCoveringType and #$ConventionallyClassifiedTimeIntervalSeries-CoveringAndDisjoint (qq.v.).  Each instance of #$CalendarSeason is a time interval that is thought of by a significant group of people (often an entire culture -- see #$CalendarSeasonTypeByCulture) as significantly intersecting the instances of #$SeasonOfYear to which those people are typically exposed.  For example, one specialization of #$CalendarSeason (#$CalendarWinter-US) is the collection of time intervals that people in mainstream U.S. culture consider to be co-temporal with the cold winter season (each of these intervals begins on the December solstice of a given year and ends on the Vernal equinox of that year).  For more on the difference between #$CalendarSeason and #$SeasonOfYear see the #$SharedNoteOnHemispheresAndCalendars.  Important specializations of #$CalendarSeason include #$CalendarWinter, #$CalendarSpring, #$CalendarSummer, and #$CalendarAutumn.")
(disjointWith PhysicalDevice LanguageArea)
(comment PropositionalAttitudeSlot "A specialization of #$CognitiveAttitudePredicate (q.v.).  A propositional attitude slot is a binary predicate that relates an agent to a proposition to which the agent bears a certain \"de dicto\" attitude (e.g. belief, doubt, knowledge).  More precisely, each #$PropositionalAttitudeSlot takes as arguments an #$IntelligentAgent (and/or in some cases a #$PerceptualAgent) and a #$CycLPropositionalSentence (that is also an #$ELSentence-Assertible), and is used to state that the agent has a certain cognitive attitude toward the propositional content of the sentence.   A defining characeristic of such a predicate -- what makes it de dicto -- is that its second argument-place is \"opaque\" (see #$opaqueArgument): a sentence appearing in that place may _not_ be freely replaced by others that are extensionally (or even logically) equivalent to it.  From the fact that a person believes (de dicto) that Mark Twain wrote \"Tom Sawyer\", for example, it cannot be inferred that s/he believes that Samuel Clemens wrote that book.  Instances of #$PropositionalAttitudeSlot include #$goals, #$beliefs, #$knows, and #$expects.  Cf. #$DeReAttitudePredicate.")
