(comment relationHoldsAmong "A #$MetaRelation predicate that relates an instance of #$Relation to any sequence of things among which it holds. (#$relationHoldsAmong RELATION LIST) means that LIST is an element of the #$relationExtension (q.v.) of RELATION.  That is, where the #$relationalArity (q.v.) of RELATION is N, LIST is an N-length instance of #$List such that RELATION holds among the members of LIST (taken in the order of their occurrence in LIST).  For example, the binary predicate #$mother stands in the relation #$relationHoldsAmong to (#$TheList #$ChelseaClinton #$HillaryClinton).  Note that if RELATION is a #$VariableArityRelation (q.v.) there will be no particular length N shared by each of the sequences it holds among.")
