(comment Epidemic "A specialization of (#$GroupFn #$AilmentCondition) and #$PhysicalEvent. Each instance of #$Epidemics is a group of many ailments of the same type that occur during some specific block of time, in a specific region (which may be quite large, even world-wide).  Often, all of the ailment instances that make up an epidemic are caused by a single event or by a closely related collection of events.  Also, during an epidemic of a disease, the incidence rate for that disease increases dramatically.")
(comment InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic "#$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic is a specialization of #$Epidemic and (#$GroupFn #$Infection).  In each instance of #$InfectiousDiseaseEpidemic, an infection is spread through a large population (see #$InfectionTransmissionEvent).  Not all epidemics are infectious disease epidemics.  Any group of #$AilmentConditions in excess of the norm for some location might be considered an #$Epidemic. For example, there could be an epidemic of (#$CancerFn #$Throat) in the #$CityOfIzmirTurkey.  See also #$InfectionEpidemicFn.")
(comment Exhibitionism-TheAction "An instance of #$SexualBehaviorType and a specialization of #$DisplayingSomething.  Each instance of #$Exhibitionism-TheAction is an #$Action in which a #$Person deliberately exposes his or her #$ExternalSexOrgans in public.  #$Persons who compulsively engage in instances of #$Exhibitionism-TheAction are said to be afflicted with #$Exhibitionism-TheCondition (q.v.).")
