(comment spits "(#$spits AGT SPIT SOURCE) holds just in case AFT spit the instance of #$PartiallyTangible, SPIT, from SOURCE.  Usually, the arg3 of this predicate will be an instance of #$Mouth or some other thing capable of being the source of spitting.  For instance, when brushing one's teeth the following usually holds for a short time after the brushing (#$spits AGT SOME-TOOTHPASTE AGT-MOUTH).")
(comment ArgTypePredicate "The collection of #$ArgConstraintPredicates used to put semantic well-formedness constraints on the type of argument(s) appropriate for a given argument-place (or -places) of a given relation.  A \"type\" of argument can be specified in terms of #$isa or #$genls; see the various specializations of #$ArgTypePredicate for more detail. Violation of such a constraint results in an expression that is semantically malformed.  For a general explanation of semantic well-formedness, see #$CycLExpression-Assertible and its specializations.")
(disjointWith Milk FruitOrVegetableFood)
(disjointWith Stealing Buying)
