without median or have their divided roadbeds separated by a distance

smaller than 75 meters.")
(comment Peritrichous "A collection of #$Bacterium that have many flagella uniformly distributed around the cell.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-ExperimentalGenre "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are
considered \"experimental\" in nature.                             ")
(comment SkunkOdor "A very foul odor characteristic of skunk spray.  Detectable at far ranges.")
(disjointWith LightDuty-PathArtifact HeavyDuty-PathArtifact)
(disjointWith MediumDuty-PathArtifact HeavyDuty-PathArtifact)
(comment AvailableForDating "Every unit should have an english.")
(comment Dormant "The collection of instances of #$Plant that have completed their flower/fruit producting stages and are no longer active.  Positive example: a deciduous tree (one that loses its leaves) in winter.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-DramaGenre "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are of the 
drama genre.  A very broad genre which includes instances of #$SoapOpera as well as
instances of #$DramaticMovie.  The underlying similarity is that the stories in this 
genre all revolve around conflict driven interactions between people.    ")
(comment SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema "A page numbering schema for instances of
#$SpecifiedInformationBearingThingType that are specifications of
#$TextualMaterial.  A text that has the
#$SequentialWithPriviledgedSubsectionsSchema exhibits sequential
numbering by increments of one throughout most of its main body:
however, there are one or more 'priviledged' subsections exhibiting
separate and internal sequential numbering schemas.  This arrangement
is often to be observed in texts with introductions and appendices,
which exhibit their own internal numbering separate from the rest of
the text.")
(disjointWith NonEndangered-OrganismTypeByExistentialThreatLevel Endangered-OrganismTypeByExistentialThreatLevel)
(disjointWith ImprovedSurface-PathArtifact UnimprovedSurface-PathArtifact)
(comment UnimprovedSurface-PathArtifact "This is the collection of instances of #$PathArtifact that can

accomodate only light loads in dry weather. They are without surface

improvement and are seldom maintained. Included are abandoned roads, fire

roads, and lumber roads. Source: US Army Field Manual, FM 21-31.")
(comment BachelorLevel "The collection of individuals who have a bachelor's degree as their highest educational degree earned (see #$highestEducationLevel).  To state that someone has at least a bachelor's level use #$educationLevel.")
(disjointWith NotHungry Hungry)
(disjointWith Starving Hungry)
(comment OpenForBusiness "The collection of instances of #$LocalOrganization which are open for business.  Uses of this collection should be temporally qualified.")
(comment Pinkish "The attribute of containing at least a tinge of #$PinkColor.")
(comment ArticulateOrEloquent "Having a natural facility eloquence or fluency with written or spoken words particularly with one's native language (see #$nativeLanguage).  Good writers are often #$ArticulateOrEloquent.")
(comment Quadriplegic "The attribute of having all four limbs paralyzed.")
(comment Bluish "The attribute of containing at least a tinge of #$BlueColor.")
(comment ForSaleOnline "An attribute for #$Buying events. (salesAttribute BUYING ForSaleOnline) means that BUYING is accomplished by means of online communication between the #$buyingAgent and the #$sellingAgent.")
(comment ArtNouveauArchitecturalStyle "The #$ArtNouveauArchitecturalStyle is a style of building and furniture design that became popular in Europe and the United States of America the late 19th Century and early 20th Century.  It is characterized by curved lines and forms, organic or biological-appearing ornament, and use of varied materials, colors and textures.")
(disjointWith CanopyClosure-Moderate CanopyClosure-Sparse)
(disjointWith CanopyClosure-Open CanopyClosure-Sparse)
(comment Congenital "The state of being congenitally afflicted by some type of ailment.")
(comment Capricorn-TheSign "The tenth sign of the zodiac. Named after the #$Constellation Capricorn, or The Goat. Ruled by the #$PlanetSaturn. #$Persons born between December 22 and January 19 have this sign.")
(comment PalladianStyle "The #$PalladianStyle is a style of neoclassic architecture first popularized by the architect Andrea Palladio in the 17th Century.  It became popular in Italy, England, and in derived form in the works of #$ThomasJefferson in America.  See also #$NeoclassicArchitecturalStyle.")
(disjointWith NonPoliticalAction PoliticalAction)
(comment RuggedClothingStyle "The collection of instances of #$SomethingToWear that project a \"rugged\" image.")
(comment DramaticMode "The collection of instances of #$CWInstantiating that present instances of #$Narratives in a way or mode that arouse deep emotions and            greatly stimulate the imagination.")
(comment MusicalComposition-Electronica "The Collection of instances of #$MusicalComposition that are in the \"electronica\" style or genre.")
(comment Restored-ExistentialStatus "This instance of #$ConstructionArtifactTypeByExistentialStatus describes

instances of #$ConstructionArtifact that have been restored, i.e., they

have been brought back to a former or more desirable condition. This

attribute could be specialized according to the importance of the

restoration achieved.")
(disjointWith Secret Confidential)
(disjointWith HighlyConfidential Confidential)
(comment NC-17Rating "A #$NC-17Rating is a rating applied to #$Movie-CWs by the #$MotionPictureAssociationOfAmerica that means no children age 17 and under admitted. The rating #$XRating used to apply to such films intended for adult audiences, but was dropped by the #$MotionPictureAssociationOfAmerica after 'X-Rated' came to be used to indicate obscene or pornographic content. The #$MotionPictureAssociationOfAmerica did not want to be in the business of judging whether #$Movie-CWs have pornographic content. #$XRating is still applied to #$Movie-CWs by parties other than the #$MotionPictureAssociationOfAmerica because it helps sell #$Movie-CWs with pornographic content.")
(comment StandingOnAllLegsPosture "the upright posture such that all legs are supporting body weight.  Usually animals are standing still when they are in this posture.  However, the important exceptions are those moments during walking  when all feet are on the ground.  Incidentally, there are no such moments during running.")
(comment MusicalComposition-Progressive "The Collection of instances of #$MusicalComposition that are in the progressive style or genre.")
(comment Repairable "The device is non- or poorly-functioning, but can be restored to functionality through repair.")
(comment Shiny "Shiny")
(disjointWith Mirrorlike Shiny)
(disjointWith Dull-NotShiny Shiny)
(comment CyanColor "The color cyan, also known as blue-green or green-blue.")
(comment FixedWorkingHours "The attribute of the type of profession, in which the employer determines when the worker must work.")
(disjointWith AssociateLevel CollegeSophomoreLevel)
(comment CollegeSophomoreLevel "college sophomore level")
(comment ConstructionLoan "A #$LoanAgreement is a #$ConstructionLoan (#$loanDedication LOAN #$ConstructionLoan) when it is a #$ShortTermLoan used to finance real estate construction.  Such a loan is generally followed, upon completion of construction, by long term financing such as a 'take out' loan (such as a #$PermanentMortgage).")
(disjointWith RecliningPosture SittingPosture)
(disjointWith UprightPosture SittingPosture)
(comment SittingPosture "The attribute that describes, most generically, an #$Animal in a seated position.  The exact nature of the position depends upon the typical body structure of the animal's species.")
(comment MusicalComposition-Reggae "The Collection of instances of #$MusicalComposition that are in the reggae style or genre.")
(disjointWith CellularTangibleThing Twisted)
(comment BeigeColor "The color beige")
(disjointWith ParentalGuidanceRating ParentalGuidance13Rating)
(comment EverydayLifeAnthropacity "(#$mtAnthropacity MT #$EverydayLifeAnthropacity) means that MT assumes people are `around', sane, and engaged in behavior that is ordinary -- `typical daily life' -- for the time and place.")
(comment CurvaceousPhysicalBuild "An attractively curved body shape.")
(comment MusicalComposition-Gospel "The Collection of instances of #$MusicalComposition that are in the gospel style or genre.")
(disjointWith Unfolded Folded)
(comment PhysicalUniverseAnthropacity "(#$mtAnthropacity MT #$PhysicalUniverseAnthropacity) means that MT assumes the existence of a physical universe (of some sort).")
(comment FrontLighting "light is shining on the side of the objects facing the viewer.")
(comment ConsolidationLoan "A #$LoanAgreement is a #$ConsolidationLoan (#$loanDedication LOAN #$ConsolidationLoan) just when the loan is one that allows the #$borrower to repay, or to consolidate, two or more other outstanding debts.  Usually the result of a #$ConsolidationLoan is that the #$borrower pays less interest or makes lower payments than he would be without it.")
(disjointWith HasDisjunctiveBranching LinearlyOrderedByStarts)
(disjointWith ContainsIncomparableScenes LinearlyOrderedByStarts)
