(comment Extended "the body part is exteded, stretched out.  the flexor muscles are relaxed, and the extensors are contracting.  SOme axioms that come to mind to be stated at a later date are, when a body part is in the Extended state, it's length is greater than in its Flexed state. In the Extended state, a body part comes closer to being planar or linear than when it is Flexed.")
(comment Bug-Software "The collection of instances of #$ComputerProgramCopy that possess some flaw from the perspective of either the software's designer(s) or user(s).  The notion of \"flaw\" in this context, as in others, is highly subjective. See also #$DebuggingAComputerProgram.")
