(comment Monotrichous "A collection of bacteria that have only one #$Flagellum-Prokaryotic. See #$Peritrichous, #$Amphitrichous, Bacterium-Lophotrichous for bacteria with more that one flagellum.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-BiblicalEpicGenre "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are of the 
biblical epic genre.  The movie #$TheTenCommandments-TheMovie is a prime example of something 
in this genre.      ")
(comment LowEarthOrbit "Satellites in #$LowEarthOrbit (LEO) have a period of about 90 minutes, because they
must travel at a speed of about 17,000 miles per hour so that they will 
avoid the downward vector of the 
Earth's gravitational pull. Satellites in #$LowEarthOrbit circle the Earth with an
altitude of 200 - 500 miles. Satellites in Low Earth Orbit are useful for taking
clear and detailed images of the Earth's surface.  Most #$WeatherSatellites and
#$EarthRemoteSensingSatellites circle the Earth in Low Earth Orbit. Also, most
satellites are originally released into space from a #$GroundToOrbitVehicle
in Low Earth Orbit.  From there, their own power sources drive them into their
proper orbit.")
(disjointWith OneLaneRoadway TwoLanesOrWiderRoadway)
(comment Flexed "the body part is flexed, curled up.  cf Extended.  The flexor muscles are activated, and the extensor muscles are relaxed. ")
(comment InDefault "The state of being in financial default, of not being able to (or being unwilling to) pay your debts.")
(comment PropositionalConceptualWork-AdventureGenre "The collection of instances of #$PropositionalConceptualWork that are of the
adventure genre.  These are works that portray people in dangerous exciting situations, often
in far-off lands.  Famous authors that write in this genre include #$HRiderHaggard and 
#$EdgarRiceBurroughs.       ")
