(comment ArtDecoArchitecturalStyle "The #$ArtDecoArchitecturalStyle is a style of building and furniture design that became popular in Europe and the United States of America in the early 20th Century.  It is characterized by repeated parallel geometric lines, arcs and forms, triangular ornaments, and use of artificial materials and colors and smooth, hard and often metallic textures.  There was a concscious effort to appear 'modern' and 'streamlined'.")
